प्रो(प्रौ)ष्ठः<BR>—1 A bull, an ox.<BR>—2 A bench, stool.<BR>—3 A kind of fish (ष्ठी also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रोष्ठपदः, प्रोष्ठपाद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठः|प्रौष्ठ
प्रो(प्रौ)ष्ठः<BR>—1 A bull, an ox.<BR>—2 A bench, stool.<BR>—3 A kind of fish (ष्ठी also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रोष्ठपदः, प्रोष्ठपाद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपदः|प्रोष्ठपद
प्रोष्ठः + -पदः the month भाद्रपद; कुर्यादापरपक्षीयं मासि प्रौष्ठपदे<BR> द्विजः । श्राद्धं पित्रोर्यथावित्तं तद्बन्धूनां च वित्तवान् Bhāg. 7. 14. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपदा
प्रोष्ठः + -पदः + .({@-दा@}) the 25th and 26th lunar mansions; पूर्वाभाद्रपदा and<BR> उत्तराभाद्रपदा; these are double stars. ‘चत्वार एकमभिकर्म देवाः प्रौष्ठपदास इति यान् वदन्ति’ Ts.;<BR> गुणवन्तोऽनुरूपाश्च रुच्या प्रौष्ठपदोपमाः<BR> Rām. 1. 18. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपदी
प्रोष्ठः + -पदः + .({@-दी@}) The full-moon of भाद्रपद; प्रौष्टपद्यां प्रौर्णमास्यां<BR> हेमसिंहसमन्वितम् । ददाति यो भागवतं स याति परमां गतिम् ॥ Bhāg. 12. 13. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ठपाद|प्रोष्ठपादः
प्रोष्ठः + -पाद <i>a.</i> born under the above Nakṣatra; P. VII. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोष्ण
प्रोष्ण <i>a.</i> Burning hot, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोह|प्रोहः
प्रो(प्रौ)ह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A reasoner, disputant.<BR>—2 Skilful, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौह|प्रौहः
प्रो(प्रौ)ह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A reasoner, disputant.<BR>—2 Skilful, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोहः|प्रोह
प्रो(प्रौ)ह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 Reasoning, logic.<BR>—2 An elephantʼs foot or ankle; आकुञ्चितप्रोहनिरूपितक्रमं करेणुरारोहयते<BR> निषादिनम् Śi. 12. 5.<BR>—3 A knot, joint.<BR>—4 A part of the elephantʼs body especially between the shoulders;<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 5, 8, 12, 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढ
प्रो(प्रौ)ढ <i>a.</i> [प्र + वह्-क्त वा वृद्धिः]<BR>—1 Full-grown, fully developed, matured, ripened, perfected, full, (as<BR> moon &c.); प्रौढपुष्पैः कदम्बैः Me. 25; प्रौढताली-विपाण्डु &c.<BR> Māl. 8. 1, 9. 28.<BR>—2 Adult, old, grown up; वर्तते हि मन्मथप्रौढसुहृदो निशीथस्य यौवनश्रीः<BR> Māl. 8; Śi. 11. 39;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">Page1142-1</a>]<BR> Mv. 6. 4.<BR>—3 Thick, dense, pitchy; प्रौढं तमः कुरु कृतज्ञतयैव भद्रम् Māl. 7. 3;<BR> Śi. 4. 62.<BR>—4 Grand, mighty, strong, magnificent; प्रौढं विकान्तमासीद् वन इव<BR> भवतां शूरशून्ये रणेऽस्मिन् Ve. 5. 37.<BR>—5 Violent, impetuous.<BR>—7 Proud; अस्त्रदानाद्भुतं काले प्रौढेन मुनिना कृतम् Mv. 2. 3.<BR>—8 Luxuriant.<BR>—9 Married.<BR>—10 Full of, filled with (at the end of comp).<BR>—11 Raised or lifted up.<BR>—12 Controverted, discussed.<BR>—13 Large, great.<BR>—14 Occupied, engaged; कान्तया सपदि कोऽप्युपगूढः प्रौढपाणिरपनेतुमियेष Śi. 10. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढ|प्रौढं
प्रो(प्रौ)ढ <i>a.</i> [प्र + वह्-क्त वा वृद्धिः]<BR>—1 Full-grown, fully developed, matured, ripened, perfected, full, (as<BR> moon &c.); प्रौढपुष्पैः कदम्बैः Me. 25; प्रौढताली-विपाण्डु &c.<BR> Māl. 8. 1, 9. 28.<BR>—2 Adult, old, grown up; वर्तते हि मन्मथप्रौढसुहृदो निशीथस्य यौवनश्रीः<BR> Māl. 8; Śi. 11. 39;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">Page1142-1</a>]<BR> Mv. 6. 4.<BR>—3 Thick, dense, pitchy; प्रौढं तमः कुरु कृतज्ञतयैव भद्रम् Māl. 7. 3;<BR> Śi. 4. 62.<BR>—4 Grand, mighty, strong, magnificent; प्रौढं विकान्तमासीद् वन इव<BR> भवतां शूरशून्ये रणेऽस्मिन् Ve. 5. 37.<BR>—5 Violent, impetuous.<BR>—7 Proud; अस्त्रदानाद्भुतं काले प्रौढेन मुनिना कृतम् Mv. 2. 3.<BR>—8 Luxuriant.<BR>—9 Married.<BR>—10 Full of, filled with (at the end of comp).<BR>—11 Raised or lifted up.<BR>—12 Controverted, discussed.<BR>—13 Large, great.<BR>—14 Occupied, engaged; कान्तया सपदि कोऽप्युपगूढः प्रौढपाणिरपनेतुमियेष Śi. 10. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढा
प्रो(प्रौ)ढ + .{@-ढा@} A bold and grown-up woman, no longer bashful or timid in the<BR> presence of her lord, one of the four principal female characters in poetic<BR> compositions; आषोडशाद्भवेद्बाला त्रिंशता तरुणी मता । पञ्चपञ्चशता<BR> प्रौढा भवेद् वृद्धा ततः परम् ॥ Ratimañjarī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रोढाङ्गना, प्रोढाचाराः, प्रोढोक्तिः, प्रोढजलदः, प्रोढदोर्दण्डः, प्रोढपाद, प्रोढपुष्प, प्रोढप्रताप, प्रोढप्रिया, प्रोढब्राह्मणम्, प्रोढमनोरमा, प्रोढयौवन, प्रोढवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1141-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढाङ्गना|प्रोढांगना
प्रोढ + -अङ्गना a bold woman; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढाचाराः
प्रोढ + -आचाराः bold or confident behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढोक्तिः|प्रोढोक्ति
प्रोढ + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> a bold or pompous assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढजलदः
प्रोढ + -जलदः a dense cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढदोर्दण्डः
प्रोढ + -दोर्दण्डः a strong and long arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढपाद
प्रोढ + -पाद <i>a.</i> one whose feet are raised on a bench; शयानः प्रौढपादश्च<BR> (नाधीयीत) Ms. 4. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढपुष्प
प्रोढ + -पुष्प <i>a.</i> having full-grown blossoms; त्वत्संपर्कात् पुलकितमिव<BR> प्रौढपुष्पैः कदम्बैः Me. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढप्रताप
प्रोढ + -प्रताप <i>a.</i> of great or mighty valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढप्रिया
प्रोढ + -प्रिया a bold or confident mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढब्राह्मणम्
प्रोढ + -ब्राह्मणम् = ताण्ड्यब्राह्मणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढमनोरमा
प्रोढ + -मनोरमा N. of a commentary on सिद्धान्तकौमुदी and other works.<BR> ˚कुचमर्दनम् a com. on this work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढयौवन
प्रोढ + -यौवन <i>a.</i> advanced in youth, in the prime or bloom of youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढवादः
प्रोढ + -वादः an arrogant or bold assertion, defiant speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढत्वम्
प्रौढ(ढि)त्वम्<BR>—1 Sublimity or felicity; यत्प्रौढित्वमुदारता च वचसां यच्चार्थतो<BR> गौरवम् Māl. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Confidence.<BR>—3 Arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढित्वम्
प्रौढ(ढि)त्वम्<BR>—1 Sublimity or felicity; यत्प्रौढित्वमुदारता च वचसां यच्चार्थतो<BR> गौरवम् Māl. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Confidence.<BR>—3 Arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढिः|प्रौढि
प्रौ(प्रो)ढिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Full growth or development, maturity, perfection; एवं वीक्ष्य तवाविवेकमपि<BR> च प्रौढिं परामुन्नतेः Jag.<BR>—2 Growth, increase.<BR>—3 Greatness, grandeur, elevation, dignity; प्रौढिप्रकर्षेण पुराणरीतिव्यतिक्रमः<BR> श्लाघ्यतमः पदानाम् Vikr. 1. 15.<BR>—4 Boldness, audacity; प्रासपाशधनुर्बाणधारिणः प्रौढिकारिणः Śiva B. 26. 30.<BR>—5 Pride, arrogance, self-confidence.<BR>—6 Controversy, discussion.<BR>—7 Zeal, exertion, enterprize.<BR>—8 Earnestness, profundity (of character); हास्यप्रौढिमजानन्त्याः करुणः<BR> सोऽन्वकम्पत Bhāg. 10. 60. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रौढिवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढिः|प्रोढि
प्रौ(प्रो)ढिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Full growth or development, maturity, perfection; एवं वीक्ष्य तवाविवेकमपि<BR> च प्रौढिं परामुन्नतेः Jag.<BR>—2 Growth, increase.<BR>—3 Greatness, grandeur, elevation, dignity; प्रौढिप्रकर्षेण पुराणरीतिव्यतिक्रमः<BR> श्लाघ्यतमः पदानाम् Vikr. 1. 15.<BR>—4 Boldness, audacity; प्रासपाशधनुर्बाणधारिणः प्रौढिकारिणः Śiva B. 26. 30.<BR>—5 Pride, arrogance, self-confidence.<BR>—6 Controversy, discussion.<BR>—7 Zeal, exertion, enterprize.<BR>—8 Earnestness, profundity (of character); हास्यप्रौढिमजानन्त्याः करुणः<BR> सोऽन्वकम्पत Bhāg. 10. 60. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्रौढिवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढिवादः|प्रौढिवाद
प्रौढिः + -वादः<BR>—1 a grandiloquent or pompous speech.<BR>—2 a bold assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौढीभू
प्रौढीभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To become matured, ripen, be developed, grow up.<BR>—2 To increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौण|प्रौणः
प्रौण <i>a.</i> Clever, learned, skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौक्त
प्रौक्त <i>a.</i> Having the sense of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रौष्ठपदः|प्रौष्ठपद
प्रौष्ठपदः = प्रोष्ठपद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लकः|प्लक
प्लकः Ved. Pudendum muliebre (अधोङ्गभेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्ष्
प्लक्ष् €1 U. To eat, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्षः|प्लक्ष
प्लक्षः [प्लक्ष्यते कीटैः प्लक्ष्-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 The Indian figtree; प्लक्षप्ररोह इव सौधतलं विभेद R. 8. 93, 13. 71;<BR> कपित्थैः; किंशुकैः प्लक्षैः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-2" target="_blank">Page1142-2</a>]<BR> Parṇāl. 4. 62.<BR>—2 One of the seven Dvīpas or continents of the world; प्लक्षो जम्बूप्रमाणो<BR> द्वीपः ख्यातिकरो हिरण्मय उत्थितो यत्राग्निरुपास्ते सप्तजिह्वः Purāṇam.<BR>—3 A side or back-door, a private entrance.<BR>—4 The space at the side of a door.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: प्लक्षजाता, प्लक्षसमुद्रवाचका, प्लक्षतीर्थम्, प्लक्षप्रस्रवणम्, प्लक्षराज्, प्लक्षद्वारम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्षजाता
प्लक्षः + -जाता, -समुद्रवाचका an epithet of the river Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्लक्षसमुद्रवाचका
प्लक्षः + -जाता, -समुद्रवाचका an epithet of the river Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1142-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

