फेनि(न)ल <i>a.</i> Foamy, frothy; फेनिलमम्बुराशिम् R. 13. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेनिलः|फेनिल|फेनिलं
फेनि(न)ल + .{@-लः@} A kind of tree (Mar. रिठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरः|फेर
फेरः, फेरण्डः A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरण्डः|फेरण्ड|फेरंड|फेरंडः
फेरः, फेरण्डः A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरवः|फेरव
फेरवः<BR>—1 A jackal; कन्दत्फेरवचण्डडात्कृति &c. Māl. 5. 19.<BR>—2 A rogue, rascal, cheat.<BR>—3 A demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेरुः|फेरु
फेरुः A jackal; गृहेषु येष्वतिथयो नार्चिताः सलिलैरपि । यदि निर्यान्ति<BR> ते नूनं फेरुराजगृहोपमाः ॥ Bhāg. 8. 16. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेल्
फेल् €1 P. (फेलति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलम्
फेलम्, फेला, फेलिका, फेली (alos फेलकः, फेलिः according<BR> to L. D. B.) Remnants of food, leavings of a meal, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेला
फेलम्, फेला, फेलिका, फेली (alos फेलकः, फेलिः according<BR> to L. D. B.) Remnants of food, leavings of a meal, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलिका
फेलम्, फेला, फेलिका, फेली (alos फेलकः, फेलिः according<BR> to L. D. B.) Remnants of food, leavings of a meal, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेली
फेलम्, फेला, फेलिका, फेली (alos फेलकः, फेलिः according<BR> to L. D. B.) Remnants of food, leavings of a meal, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेला
फेला <i>f.</i> (or छेला) The vault of a foundation pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

फेलुकः|फेलुक
फेलुकः The scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1148-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बः|ब
बः<BR>—1 N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 A water-jar; (the meanings of this letter are given in the following<BR> verse; बः पुमान् वरुणे सिन्धौ भगे तोये गते तु वा । गन्धने तन्तुसंताने<BR> पुंस्येव वपने स्मृतः ॥) Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंह्
बंह् €1 Ā. (बंहते, बंहित) To increase, grow. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To increase.<BR>—2 To strengthen, make firm, fix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिमन्
बंहिमन् <i>m.</i> Abundance, multitude; P. VI. 4. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहिष्ठ|बंहिष्ठः
बंहिष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Most abundant, very great, excessive; (superl. of बहुल q. v.).<BR>—2 Very low or deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बंहीयस्
बंहीयस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 More numerous or abundant, much more, exceeding; (compar. of बहुल q. v.).<BR>—2 Very stout or fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकः|बक
बकः<BR>—1 The Indian crane; न प्रयत्नशतेनापि शुकवत् पाठ्यते बकः H.<BR>—2 A cheat, rogue, hypocrite (the crane being a very cunning bird that<BR> knows well how to draw others into its clutches).<BR>—3 N. of a demon killed by Bhīma.<BR>—4 N. of another demon killed by Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—5 N. of Kubera. —6 An apparatus for subliming metals or minerals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकी
बकः + .{@-की@} = पूतना q. v. अहो बकी यं स्तनकालकूटं जिघांसयापाययदप्यसाध्वी<BR> Bhāg. 3. 2. 23.<BR>—2 A female crane.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बकचरः, बकवृत्तिः, बकव्रतचरः, बकव्रतिकः, बकव्रतिन्, बकचिञ्चिका, बकचिञ्ची, बकजित्, बकधूपः, बकपञ्चकम्, बकयन्त्रम्, बकव्रतम्, बकसहवासिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकचरः|बकचर
बकः + -चरः, -वृत्तिः, -व्रतचरः, -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> ‘acting like a crane’<BR>, a false devotee, religious hypocrite; अधोदृष्टिर्नैष्कृतिकः<BR> स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः । शठो मिथ्याविनीतश्च बकव्रतचरो द्विजः ॥ Ms. 4. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकवृत्तिः|बकवृत्ति
बकः + -चरः, -वृत्तिः, -व्रतचरः, -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> ‘acting like a crane’<BR>, a false devotee, religious hypocrite; अधोदृष्टिर्नैष्कृतिकः<BR> स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः । शठो मिथ्याविनीतश्च बकव्रतचरो द्विजः ॥ Ms. 4. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकव्रतचरः|बकव्रतचर
बकः + -चरः, -वृत्तिः, -व्रतचरः, -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> ‘acting like a crane’<BR>, a false devotee, religious hypocrite; अधोदृष्टिर्नैष्कृतिकः<BR> स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः । शठो मिथ्याविनीतश्च बकव्रतचरो द्विजः ॥ Ms. 4. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकव्रतिकः|बकव्रतिक
बकः + -चरः, -वृत्तिः, -व्रतचरः, -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> ‘acting like a crane’<BR>, a false devotee, religious hypocrite; अधोदृष्टिर्नैष्कृतिकः<BR> स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः । शठो मिथ्याविनीतश्च बकव्रतचरो द्विजः ॥ Ms. 4. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकव्रतिन्
बकः + -चरः, -वृत्तिः, -व्रतचरः, -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> ‘acting like a crane’<BR>, a false devotee, religious hypocrite; अधोदृष्टिर्नैष्कृतिकः<BR> स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः । शठो मिथ्याविनीतश्च बकव्रतचरो द्विजः ॥ Ms. 4. 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकचिञ्चिका
बकः + -चिञ्चिका, -चिञ्ची a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकचिञ्ची
बकः + -चिञ्चिका, -चिञ्ची a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकजित्
बकः + -जित् <i>m.</i>, {@-निषूदनः@}<BR> epithets of<BR>—1 Bhīma.<BR>—2 of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकधूपः|बकधूप
बकः + -धूपः a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकपञ्चकम्
बकः + -पञ्चकम् the last five days of the bright half of the month of<BR> Kārtika (during which even the heron eats no fish).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकयन्त्रम्
बकः + -यन्त्रम् a kind of retort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकव्रतम्
बकः + -व्रतम् ‘crane-like conduct’, hypocrisy; ये बकव्रतिनो विप्राः<BR> Ms. 4. 197; see also 196 (बकव्रतचर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकसहवासिन्
बकः + -सहवासिन् a lotus flower; Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकबकाय
बकबकाय Den. Ā. To croak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकाची
बकाची A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकाय
बकाय Denom. P. To act like बक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुर|बकुरः
बकुर <i>a.</i> Horrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुरः|बकुर
बकुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Lightning; thunderbolt.<BR>—2 A wind instrument used in battle; अभि दस्युं बकुरेणा धमन्ता Rv. 1. 117. 21.<BR> (Naighaṇṭuka gives the first meaning.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुलः|बकुल
बकुलः<BR>—1 A kind of tree, Mimusops Elengi, (said according to the convention<BR> of poets to put forth blossoms when sprinkled by young women with mouthfuls<BR> of wine); काङ्क्षत्यन्यो (केसरः or बकुलः) वदनमादिरां<BR> दोहदच्छद्यनाऽस्याः Me. 80; बकुलः सीधुगण्डूषसेकात् (विकसति);<BR> तव निश्वसितानुकारिर्भिर्बकुलैरर्धचितां समं मया R. 8. 64; (for<BR> similar conventions about other trees see the quotation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">Page1149-2</a>]<BR> under अशोक).<BR>—2 A kind of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुलम्
बकुलः + .{@-लम्@} The fragrant flower of this tree; कृती मालाकारो बकुलमपि<BR> कुत्रापि निदधे Bv. 1. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकुली
बकुलः + .{@-ली@} A kind of drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकूलः|बकूल
बकूलः The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकेरुका
बकेरुका<BR>—1 A small crane.<BR>—2 The branch of a tree bent by the wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बकोटः|बकोट
बकोटः A crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बटुः|बटु
बटुः<BR>—1 A boy, lad, chap, often used as a depreciatory term or to show contempt;<BR> चाणक्यबटुः &c.; see वटु.<BR>—2 A young Brahmachārin; अव्रता वटवोऽशौचाः Bhāg. 12. 3. 33.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बटुमात्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बटुमात्रः|बटुमात्र
बटुः + -मात्रः a mere boy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बटुकः|बटुक
बटुकः<BR>—1 A boy, lad; see वटु.<BR>—2 A stupid fellow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बटुकभैरवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बटुकभैरवः|बटुकभैरव
बटुकः + -भैरवः a form of Bhairava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बटूकरणम्
बटूकरणम् Investiture with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बट्टलोहकम्
बट्टलोहकम् Damasked steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बडिशम्
बडि(लि)शम् (-शः, -शा, -शी)<BR>—1 A fish-hook; स मीनोऽप्यज्ञानाद् बडिशयुतमश्नातु पिशितम् Bh. 3. 21;<BR> तांस्ते भक्षयतः कण्ठे यस्तप्तबडिशायते Bm. 1. 122. गरीयसेऽपकाराय<BR> तिमीनां बडिशं यथा Śiva B. 26. 45.<BR>—2 A surgical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिशम्
बडि(लि)शम् (-शः, -शा, -शी)<BR>—1 A fish-hook; स मीनोऽप्यज्ञानाद् बडिशयुतमश्नातु पिशितम् Bh. 3. 21;<BR> तांस्ते भक्षयतः कण्ठे यस्तप्तबडिशायते Bm. 1. 122. गरीयसेऽपकाराय<BR> तिमीनां बडिशं यथा Śiva B. 26. 45.<BR>—2 A surgical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बत
बत <i>ind.</i> A particle expressing:−<BR>—1 Sorrow, regret (alas!); वयं बत विदूरतः कमगता पशोः कन्यका<BR> Māl. 3. 18; अहो बत महत् पापं कर्तुं व्यवसिता वयम् Bg. 1. 45.<BR>—2 Pity or compassion; क्व बत हरिणकानां जीवितं चातिलोलम् Ś. 1. 10.<BR>—3 Addressing, calling; बत वितरत तोयं तोयवाहा नितान्तम् G. M.; R. 9. 47.<BR>—4 Joy or satisfaction; अपि बत मधुपुर्यामार्यपुत्रोऽधुनास्ते Bhāg. 10. 47. 21;<BR> अहो बतासि स्पृहणीयवीर्यः Ku. 3. 20.<BR>—5 Wonder or surprise; वनजे नेति बलं बतास्ति सत्त्वे Ki. 13. 8;<BR> अहो बत महच्चित्रम् K. 154.<BR>—6 Censure.<BR>—7 Truth (सत्यार्थ); कल्याणी बत गाथेयं लौकिकी प्रतिभाति माम्<BR> Rām. 5. 34. 6. For the meanings of बत with अहो see under अहो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्
बद् €1 P. To be steady or firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरः|बदर|बदरं
बदरः [बद् स्थैर्ये अरच्]<BR>—1 The jujube tree.<BR>—2 The kernel of the fruit of the cotton-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरा
बदरः + .{@-रा@} The cotton shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरम्
बदरः + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The fruit of jujube; करबदरसदृशमखिलं भुवनतलं यत् प्रसादतः<BR> कवयः । पश्यन्ति सूक्ष्ममतयः सा जयति सरखती देवी Vās. 1; बदरामलकाम्रदाडिमानामपहृत्य<BR> श्रियमुन्नतां क्रमेण Bv. 2. 8.<BR>—2 The pod of the cotton shrub.<BR>—3 The berry used as a weight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बदरकुणः, बदरपाचनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरकुणः|बदरकुण
बदरः + -कुणः the time when the fruit of the jujube becomes ripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरपाचनम्
बदरः + -पाचनम् N. of a sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिका
बदरिका<BR>—1 The jujube tree or its fruit; अन्ये बदरिकाकारा बहिरेव मनोहराः H. 1. 90.<BR>—2 N. of one of the many sources of the Ganges and of the neighbouring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">Page1150-1</a>]<BR> hermitage of the sages Nara and Nārāyaṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बदरिकाश्रमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1149-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिकाश्रमः|बदरिकाश्रम
बदरिका + -आश्रमः the hermitage at Badarikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरिः|बदरि
बदरिः <i>f.</i> The jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरी
बदरी<BR>—1 The jujube tree; see बादरायण.<BR>—2 = बदरिका (2) above.<BR>—3 The cotton shrub.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बदरीच्छदः, बदरीतपोवनम्, बदरीनाथः, बदरीनारायणः, बदरीपत्रम्, बदरीफलम्, बदरीवनम्, बदरीवासा, बदरीशैलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीच्छदः|बदरीच्छद
बदरी + -छदः a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीतपोवनम्
बदरी + -तपोवनम् the penance grove at Badarī; बदरीतपोवननिवासनिरतमवगात<BR> मान्यथा Ki. 12. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीनाथः|बदरीनाथ
बदरी + -नाथः N. of a temple at Badarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीनारायणः|बदरीनारायण
बदरी + -नारायणः N. of a sacred place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीपत्रम्
बदरी + -पत्रम् a kind of perfume (नखरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीफलम्
बदरी + -फलम् a fruit of the jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीवनम्
बदरी + -वनम् + ({@-णम्@})<BR> a wood or thicket of jujube trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीवणम्
बदरी + -वनम् + ({@-णम्@})<BR> a wood or thicket of jujube trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीवासा
बदरी + -वासा an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बदरीशैलः|बदरीशैल
बदरी + -शैलः a rocky eminence at Badarī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्वम्
बद्वम् A large number (according to Sāyaṇa 100 kotis, others 10,000<BR> millions; 13084 according to Bhāg. 9. 20. 26 com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बध्
बध् €1 Ā. (बीभत्सते; strictly the desiderative base of बध्<BR> used in a primitive sense) To abhor, loathe, detest, shrink from, be disgusted<BR> with (with abl.); येभ्यो बीभत्समानाः U. 1. ━II. €10 P. (बाधयति)<BR> To bind, check, restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिर|बधिरः
बधिर <i>a.</i> Deaf; ध्वनिभिर्जनस्य बधिरीकृतश्रुतेः Śi. 13. 3; Ms. 7. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरयति
बधिरयति Den. P., बधिरीकृ €8 U. To deafen (fig. also); बधिरिताशेषदिगन्तरालम् K.; Mv. 6. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरित
बधिरित <i>a.</i> Made deaf, deafened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बधिरिमन्
बधिरिमन् <i>m.</i> Deafness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्द्|बंद्
बन्द् €1 P. To divide; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिन्
बन्दिन् See वन्दिन्. A bard, herald; धर्मच्छेदात् पटुतरगिरो<BR> बन्दिनो नीलकण्ठाः V. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिः|बन्दि|बंदि|बंदिः
बन्दिः, -न्दी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Bondage, confinement.<BR>—2 A prisoner, captive; मोक्ष्यते सुरबन्दीनां वेणीर्वीर्यविभूतिभिः Ku. 2. 61.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्दिग्रहः, बन्दिग्राहः, बन्दिपालः, बन्दिशूला, बन्दिस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दी
बन्दिः, -न्दी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Bondage, confinement.<BR>—2 A prisoner, captive; मोक्ष्यते सुरबन्दीनां वेणीर्वीर्यविभूतिभिः Ku. 2. 61.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्दिग्रहः, बन्दिग्राहः, बन्दिपालः, बन्दिशूला, बन्दिस्थित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिग्रहः|बन्दिग्रह
बन्दिः + -ग्रहः taking prisoner, capture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिग्राहः|बन्दिग्राह
बन्दिः + -ग्राहः a house breaker, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिपालः
बन्दिः + -पालः a jailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिशूला
बन्दिः + -शूला a harlot, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्दिस्थित
बन्दिः + -स्थित <i>a.</i> imprisoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्|बंध्
बन्ध् €9 P. (बध्नाति, बबन्ध, अभांत्सीत्, भंत्स्यति, बन्द्धुम्, बद्ध;<BR> <i>pass.</i> बध्यते)<BR>—1 To bind, tie, fasten; बन्द्धुं न संभावित एव तावत् करेण रुद्धोऽपि<BR> च केशपाशः Ku. 7. 57, 25; R. 7. 9; Bk. 9. 75.<BR>—2 To catch, capture, imprison, ensnare, make captive; कर्मभिर्न स<BR> बध्यते Bg. 4. 14; बलिर्बबन्धे Bk. 2. 39, 14. 56.<BR>—3 To chain, fetter.<BR>—4 To check, stop, suppress; as in बद्धकोप, बद्धकोष्ठ &c.<BR>—5 To put on, wear; न हि चूडामणिः पादे प्रभवामीति बध्यते Pt. 1. 72;<BR> बबन्धुरङ्गुलित्राणि Bk. 14. 7.<BR>—6 To attract, arrest (as eyes &c.); बबन्ध चक्षूंषि यवप्ररोहः<BR> Ku. 7. 17; or बध्नाति मे चक्षुः (चित्रिकूटः) R. 13. 47.<BR>—7 To fix or set upon, direct towards (as the eyes or mind), cast upon<BR> (with loc.); दृष्टिं लक्ष्येषु बध्नन् Mu. 1. 2; R. 3. 4, 6. 36; Bk. 20. 22.<BR>—8 To bind or fasten together (as hair); पूर्णप्रतिज्ञेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-2" target="_blank">Page1150-2</a>]<BR> मया केवल बध्यते शिखा Mu. 7. 17.<BR>—9 To build, construct, form, arrange; बद्धोर्मिनाकवनितापरिभुक्तमुक्तम्<BR> Ki. 8. 57; छायाबद्धकदम्बकं मृगकुलम् Ś. 2. 6; तस्याञ्जलिं बन्धुमतो<BR> बबन्ध R. 16. 5, 4. 38, 11. 35, 78; Ku. 2. 47, 5. 30; Bk. 7. 77.<BR>—10 To put together, compose, construct (a poem, verse &c.); तुष्टैर्बद्धं<BR> तदलघु रघुस्वामिनः सच्चरित्रम् Vikr. 18. 107; श्लोक एवास्त्वयं<BR> बद्धः Rām. 1. 2. 31.<BR>—11 To form, produce, bear (as fruit &c.); काले खलु समारब्धाः फलं<BR> बध्नन्ति नीतयः R. 12. 69;<BR> Ku. 5. 60 (v. l.) Ś. 6. 3.<BR>—12 To have, possess, entertain, cherish, feel.<BR>—13 To punish, chastise.<BR>—14 To offer, sacrifice (as an animal).<BR>—15 To shut, close, stop.<BR>—16 To oppress, overpower.<BR>—17 To join, unite.<BR>—18 To produce, cause, effect.<BR>—19 To strike (as root).<BR>—20 To display, exhibit, show. (The senses of बन्ध् are variously modified<BR> according to the noun with which it is connected; <i>e. g.</i> भ्रुकुटिं<BR> बन्ध् to knit or bend the eyebrows, to frown; मुष्टिं बन्ध् to clench<BR> the fist; अञ्जलिं बन्ध् to fold the hands together in supplication;<BR> चित्तं, धियं, मनः, हृदयं बन्ध् to set the heart on; प्रीतिं,<BR> भावं, रागं बन्ध् to fall in love with, be enamoured of; सेतुं बन्ध्<BR> to construct or build a bridge; वैरं बन्ध् to conceive hatred, contract<BR> enmity; सख्यं, सौहृदं बन्ध् to form friendship; गोलं बन्ध् to<BR> form a globe; मण्डलं बन्ध् to form a circle, sit or stand in a circle;<BR> मौनं बन्ध् to maintain silence; परिकरं, कक्षां बन्ध् to gird<BR> up oneʼs loins, prepare oneself for any thing; see the compounds under<BR> बद्ध also). ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to bind, form, construct, build<BR> &c.; स सेतुं बन्धयामास प्लवगैर्लवणाम्भसि R. 12. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्ध|बद्धं
बद्ध <i>p. p.</i> [बन्ध्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Bound, tied, fastened.<BR>—2 Chained, fettered.<BR>—3 Captured, caught.<BR>—4 Confined, imprisoned.<BR>—5 Put or girt on.<BR>—6 Restrained, suppressed, withheld.<BR>—7 Formed, built; शरबद्धभिवाभाति द्वितीयं भास्वदम्बरम् Rām. 6. 107. 24.<BR>—8 Cherished, entertained.<BR>—9 Combined, united.<BR>—10 Firmly rooted, firm.<BR>—11 Shut, stopped, closed.<BR>—12 Inlaid, studded.<BR>—13 Composed (as verses).<BR>—14 Formed, contracted; असूत सा नागवधूपभोग्यं मैनाकमम्भोनिधिबद्धसख्यम् Ku. 1. 20.<BR>—15 Manifested, displayed.<BR>—16 Entangled, involved.<BR>—17 Congealed, clotted (as blood).<BR>—18 Effected, caused, formed, produced; बद्धं जालकम् Ś. 1. 29, 2. 6;<BR> U. 6. 17; Māl. 3. 7.<BR>—19 Possessed, preserved; बद्धं सन्तं मन्यते लब्धमर्थम् Mb. 5. 92. 23.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बद्धाङ्गुलित्र, बद्धाङ्गुलित्राण, बद्धाञ्जलि, बद्धानुराग, बद्धानुशय, बद्धाम्बु, बद्धावस्थिति, बद्धादर, बद्धानन्द, बद्धायुध, बद्धाशङ्क, बद्धोत्सव, बद्धोद्यम, बद्धकक्ष, बद्धकक्ष्य, बद्धकदम्बक, बद्धकलापिन्, बद्धकेसर, बद्धकोप, बद्धमन्यु, बद्धरोष, बद्धगुदम्, बद्धग्रह, बद्धचित्त, बद्धमनस्, बद्धजिह्व, बद्धतूणीर, बद्धदृष्टि, बद्धनेत्र, बद्धलोचन, बद्धधार, बद्धनिश्चय, बद्धनेपथ्य, बद्धपरिकर, बद्धपुरीष, बद्धप्रतिज्ञ, बद्धप्रतिश्रुत्, बद्धभाव, बद्धभूः, बद्धमण्डल, बद्धमुष्टि, बद्धमूत्र, बद्धमूल, बद्धमौन, बद्धराग, बद्धवसति, बद्धवाच्, बद्धवेपथु, बद्धवैर, बद्धशिख, बद्धसूतः, बद्धस्नेह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1150-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

