बद्ध + -वैर <i>a.</i> one who has conceived bitter hatred or contracted<BR> confirmed hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धशिख|बद्धशिखः
बद्ध + -शिख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one whose hair is tied up (into a knot on the crown of the head).<BR>—2 one who is still in childhood, young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धसूतः|बद्धसूत
बद्ध + -सूतः a particular preparation of quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बद्धस्नेह
बद्ध + -स्नेह <i>a.</i> forming an attachment, conceiving affection for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धः|बन्ध|बंध|बंधः
बन्धः [बन्ध्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A tie, bond (in general) (आशाबन्ध &c.).<BR>—2 A hair-band, fillet; रतिविगलितबन्धे केशहस्ते सुकेश्याः (सति)<BR> V. 4. 22; Ś. 1. 29.<BR>—3 A chain, fetter.<BR>—4 Fettering, confining, imprisoning, confinement, imprisonment; बन्धं<BR> चानिच्छता घोरं त्वयासौ पुरुषर्षभ Rām. 5. 21. 19; अधार्मिकं त्रिभिर्न्यायैर्निगृह्णीयात्<BR> प्रयत्नतः । निरोधनेन बन्धेन विविधेन वधेन च ॥ Ms. 8. 310.<BR>—5 Catching, capturing, catching hold of; गजबन्ध R. 16. 2.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Forming, constructing, arranging; सर्गबन्धो महाकाव्यम् S. D. 6.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Building, erecting.<BR>—7 Feeling, conceiving, cherishing;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">Page1151-2</a>]<BR> हे राजानस्त्यजत सुकविप्रेमबन्धे विरोधम् Vikr. 18. 107; R. 6. 81.<BR>—8 Connection, union, intercourse.<BR>—9 Joining or folding together, combining; प्रासादवातायनदृश्यबन्धैः<BR> साकेतनार्योऽञ्जलिभिः प्रणेमुः R. 14. 13; अञ्जलिबन्धः &c.<BR>—10 A bandage, ligature.<BR>—11 Agreement, harmony.<BR>—12 Manifestation, display, exhibition; मनसिजतरुपुष्पं रागबन्धप्रवालम्<BR> (यौवनम्) R. 18. 52.<BR>—13 Bondage, confinement to this world (opp. मुक्ति which is ‘complete emancipation from the trammels of the world’<BR>); बन्धं मोक्षं च या वेत्ति<BR> बुद्धिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी Bg. 18. 30; बन्धोन्मुक्त्यै खलु मखमुखान् कुर्वते<BR> कर्मपाशान् Bv. 4. 21; R. 13. 58, 18. 7.<BR>—14 Result, consequence.<BR>—15 A position, posture in general; आसनबन्धधीरः R. 2. 6; पर्यङ्कबन्धस्थिरपूर्वकायम् Ku. 3. 45, 59.<BR>—16 A particular position in sexual intercourse, or a particular mode<BR> of sexual enjoyment (these are said in Ratimañjarī to be 16,<BR> but other writers increase the number to 84).<BR>—17 A border, frame-work.<BR>—18 Arrangement of a stanza in a particular shape; <i>e. g.</i> खड्गबन्ध,<BR> पद्मबन्ध, मुरजबन्ध (<i>vide</i> K. P. 9 <i>ad loc.</i>).<BR>—19 A sinew, tendon.<BR>—20 The body.<BR>—21 A deposit, pledge.<BR>—22 An embankment, throwing a bridge across (a river).<BR>—23 A disease in which the eyelids cannot he wholly closed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्धकरणम्, बन्धकर्तृ, बन्धतन्त्रम्, बन्धनृत्यम्, बन्धपारुष्यम्, बन्धमुद्रा, बन्धस्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धकरणम्
बन्धः + -करणम् fettering, imprisoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धकर्तृ
बन्धः + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> a binder, fetterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धतन्त्रम्
बन्धः + -तन्त्रम् a complete army containing the four necessary elements,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> elephants, horses, chariots and footmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनृत्यम्
बन्धः + -नृत्यम् a kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धपारुष्यम्
बन्धः + -पारुष्यम् forced or unnatural construction of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धमुद्रा
बन्धः + -मुद्रा impression or mark of fetters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धस्तम्भः|बन्धस्तम्भ|बंधस्तंभ
बन्धः + -स्तम्भः a post to which an animal (<i>e. g.</i> an elephant) is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धकः|बन्धक|बंधक|बन्धकं|बंधकः
बन्धकः<BR>—1 One who binds or catches, a binder.<BR>—2 A catcher.<BR>—3 A band, tie, rope, tether.<BR>—4 A dike, bank, dam.<BR>—5 A pledge, deposit.<BR>—6 A posture of the body.<BR>—7 Barter, exchange.<BR>—8 A violator, ravisher.<BR>—9 A promise.<BR>—10 A city.<BR>—11 A part or portion (at the end of num. compounds); ऋणं सदशबन्धकम् Y. 2. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धकम्
बन्धकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Binding, confinement.<BR>—2 Pawn, mortgage; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धकी|बंधकी
बन्धकः + .{@-की@}<BR>—1 An unchaste woman; न मे त्वया कौमारबन्धक्या प्रयोजनम् Māl. 7; Ve. 2.<BR>—2 A harlot, courtezan; अतः परं स्वैरिणी स्याद्बन्धकी पञ्चमे भवेत्<BR> Mb. 1. 123. 77; बलात् धृतोऽसि मयेति बन्धकीधाष्टर्पम् K. 237; वैयात्यं<BR> प्रथयति बन्धकीव योषा Rām. Ch. 7. 58.<BR>—3 A female elephant.<BR>—4 A barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धन|बंधन|बन्धनं
बन्धन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Binding, fettering.<BR>—2 Checking, stopping.<BR>—3 (At the end of comp.) Dependent upon; cf. निबन्धन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनम्
बन्धन + .{@-नम्@} [बन्ध्-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of binding, fastening, tying; स्मरसि स्मर मेखलागुणैरुत<BR> गोत्रस्खलितेषु बन्धनम् Ku. 4. 8.<BR>—2 Binding on or round, throwing round, clasping; विनम्रशाखाभुजबन्धनानि<BR> Ku. 3. 39; Pt. 5. 21; घटय भुजबन्धनम् Gīt. 10; R. 19. 17.<BR>—3 A bond, tie (fig. also); R. 12. 76; आशाबन्धनम् &c.<BR>—4 Fettering, chaining, confining. गजभुजङ्गमयोरपि बन्धनम् Bh. 2. 91.<BR>—5 A chain, fetter, tether, halter &c.<BR>—6 Capturing, catching.<BR>—7 Bondage, confinement, imprisonment, captivity; as in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">Page1152-1</a>]<BR> बन्धनागार.<BR>—8 A place of confinement, prison, jail; वसुदेवस्य देवक्यां जातो भोजेन्द्रबन्धने<BR> Bhāg. 3. 2. 25; त्वां कारयामि कमलोदरबन्धनस्थम् Ś. 6. 20; द्विगुणं<BR> त्रिगुणं पश्चाद्यावज्जीवं तु बन्धनम् Śukra. 4. 80; Ms. 9. 288.<BR>—9 Forming, building, construction; सेतुबन्धनम् Ku. 4. 6.<BR>—10 Connecting, uniting, joining.<BR>—11 Hurting, injuring.<BR>—12 A stalk, stem, peduncle (of a flower); कृतं न कर्णार्पितबन्धनं<BR> सखे Ś. 6. 18; U. 2. 9; Ku. 4. 14.<BR>—13 A sinew, muscle; संधिन्नसंधिः प्रविकीर्णबन्धनो हतः क्षितौ वायुसुतेन<BR> राक्षसः Rām. 5. 47. 36, 5. 24. 40.<BR>—14 A bandage.<BR>—15 A bar, barrier.<BR>—16 Alloyage, mixing.<BR>—17 An embankment, a bridge.<BR>—18 A conjunction, connection.<BR>—19 (In phil.) Mundane bondage (opp. to liberation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनम्
बन्धन + .{@-नम्, -नी@}<BR>—1 A bond, tie.<BR>—2 A rope, cord.<BR>—3 A string, thread.<BR>—4 A chain, fetter.<BR>—5 A bondage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्धनागारः, बन्धनागारः, बन्धनागारम्, बन्धनालयः, बन्धनग्रन्थिः, बन्धनपालकः, बन्धनरक्षिन्, बन्धनवेश्मन्, बन्धनस्थः, बन्धनस्तम्भः, बन्धनस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनी
बन्धन + .{@-नम्, -नी@}<BR>—1 A bond, tie.<BR>—2 A rope, cord.<BR>—3 A string, thread.<BR>—4 A chain, fetter.<BR>—5 A bondage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्धनागारः, बन्धनागारः, बन्धनागारम्, बन्धनालयः, बन्धनग्रन्थिः, बन्धनपालकः, बन्धनरक्षिन्, बन्धनवेश्मन्, बन्धनस्थः, बन्धनस्तम्भः, बन्धनस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1151-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनागारः|बन्धनागार|बंधनागार
बन्धन + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -आलयः a prison, jail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनागारः|बन्धनागार|बंधनागार
बन्धन + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -आलयः a prison, jail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनागारम्
बन्धन + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -आलयः a prison, jail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनालयः|बन्धनालय|बंधनालय
बन्धन + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -आलयः a prison, jail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनग्रन्थिः|बन्धनग्रन्थि|बंधनग्रंथि
बन्धन + -ग्रन्थिः<BR>—1 the knot of a bandage.<BR>—2 a noose.<BR>—3 a rope for tying cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनपालकः|बन्धनपालक|बंधनपालक
बन्धन + -पालकः, -रक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a jailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनरक्षिन्
बन्धन + -पालकः, -रक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a jailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनवेश्मन्|बंधनवेश्मन्
बन्धन + -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a prison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनस्थः|बन्धनस्थ|बंधनस्थ
बन्धन + -स्थः a captive, prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनस्तम्भः|बन्धनस्तम्भ
बन्धन + -स्तम्भः a tying-post, a post to which an animal (<i>e. g.</i> an<BR> elephant) is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनस्थानम्
बन्धन + -स्थानम् a stable, stall (for horses &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धनिकः|बन्धनिक
बन्धनिकः A jailor, turnkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धयितृ
बन्धयितृ A binder; cf. Kull. on Ms. 8. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धित|बंधित
बन्धित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bound, fastened.<BR>—2 Confined, imprisoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धित्रः|बन्धित्र|बन्धित्रं|बंधित्रः
बन्धित्रः [बन्ध-इत्र]<BR>—1 The god of love.<BR>—2 A leathern fan (चर्मव्यजन).<BR>—3 A spot, mole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुः|बन्धु|बंधु|बंधुः
बन्धुः [बध्नाति मनः स्नेहादिना बन्ध्-उ]<BR>—1 A relation, kinsman, relative in general; यत्र द्रुमा अपि मृगा अपि<BR> बन्धवो मे U. 3. 8; मातृबन्धुनिवासिनम् R. 12. 12; Ś. 6. 23; Bg. 6. 9;<BR> Ms. 2. 136.<BR>—2 Any one connected or associated with another, a brother; प्रवासबन्धुः<BR> a brother-traveller; धर्मबन्धुः a spiritual brother; अनुमतगमना<BR> शकुन्तला तरुभिरियं वनवासबन्धुभिः Ś. 4. 10.<BR>—3 (In law) A cognate kinsman, oneʼs own kindred or kinsmen generally;<BR> (three kinds are enumerated:− आत्म˚ personal, पितृ˚ paternal,<BR> and मातृ˚ maternal; see these three words).<BR>—4 A friend (in general); as in बन्धुकृत्य below; oft. at the end<BR> of comp.; मकरन्दगन्धबन्धो Māl. 1. 38 ‘a friend of, (<i>i. e.</i>) charged with fragrance’<BR> &c., 9. 13.<BR>—5 A husband; वैदेहिबन्धोर्हृदयं विदद्रे R. 14. 33.<BR>—6 A father.<BR>—7 A mother.<BR>—8 A brother.<BR>—9 The tree called बन्धुजीव q. v.<BR>—10 One who belongs to or is connected with any tribe or profession only<BR> nominally; <i>i. e.</i> one who belongs to it, but does not do the duties<BR> pertaining thereto (often used by way of contempt); स्वयमेव ब्रह्मबन्धुनोद्भिन्नो<BR> दुर्गप्रयोगः M. 4; cf. क्षत्रबन्धु.<BR>—11 Connection, relationship, association in general; समुद्र एवास्य<BR> बन्धुः Bṛ. Up. 1. 1. 2; B. R. 3. 89.<BR>—12 A controller, governor; (नमः) गुणत्रयाभासनिमित्तबन्धवे<BR> Bhāg. 6. 4. 23.<BR>—13 (In astrol.) N. of the 3rd mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्धुकाम, बन्धुकृत्यम्, बन्धुजनः, बन्धुजीवः, बन्धुजीवकः, बन्धुदग्धः, बन्धुदत्तम्, बन्धुदायादः, बन्धुप्रिय, बन्धुप्रीतिः, बन्धुभावः, बन्धुवर्गः, बन्धुहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुकाम
बन्धुः + -काम<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">Page1152-2</a>]<BR> <i>a.</i> affectionate towards kinsmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुकृत्यम्
बन्धुः + -कृत्यम्<BR>—1 the duty of a kinsman; त्वयि तु परिसमाप्तं बन्धुकृत्यं प्रजानाम् Ś. 5. 8.<BR>—2 the business of a friend, a friendly or kind act or service; काच्चित्<BR> सौम्य व्यवसितमिदं बन्धुकृत्यं त्वया मे Me. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजनः|बन्धुजन|बंधुजन
बन्धुः + -जनः<BR>—1 a relative, kinsman.<BR>—2 kindred, kinsmen taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजीवः|बन्धुजीव|बंधुजीव
बन्धुः + -जीवः, -जीवकः N. of a tree; दृश्यन्ते बन्धुजीवाश्च श्यामाश्च<BR> गिरिसानुषु Rām. 4. 30. 62; बन्धुजीवमधुराधरपल्लवमुल्लसितस्मितशोभम्<BR> Gīt. 2; R. 11. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुजीवकः|बन्धुजीवक|बंधुजीवक
बन्धुः + -जीवः, -जीवकः N. of a tree; दृश्यन्ते बन्धुजीवाश्च श्यामाश्च<BR> गिरिसानुषु Rām. 4. 30. 62; बन्धुजीवमधुराधरपल्लवमुल्लसितस्मितशोभम्<BR> Gīt. 2; R. 11. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुदग्धः|बन्धुदग्ध
बन्धुः + -दग्धः an abandoned wretch (हतक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुदत्तम्
बन्धुः + -दत्तम् a kind of Strīdhana or womanʼs property, the property<BR> given to a girl by her relatives at the time of marriage; बन्धुदत्तं<BR> तथा शुल्कमन्वाधेयकमेव च Y. 2. 144; बान्धवा भ्रातरो बन्धुदत्तप्रदेन<BR> कन्यादशायां यत् पितृभ्यां दत्तं तदुच्यते Dāy. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुदायादः|बन्धुदायाद
बन्धुः + -दायादः kinsman and heir; Ms. 9. 158. ━<i>a.</i> entitled to inheritance<BR> by relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुप्रिय
बन्धुः + -प्रिय <i>a.</i> dear to friends or relations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुप्रीतिः|बन्धुप्रीति|बंधुप्रीति
बन्धुः + -प्रीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 love of a relative; बन्धुप्रीत्या Me. 51 (v. l.).<BR>—2 love for a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुभावः|बन्धुभाव|बंधुभाव
बन्धुः + -भावः<BR>—1 friendship.<BR>—2 relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुवर्गः|बन्धुवर्ग|बंधुवर्ग
बन्धुः + -वर्गः kinsmen, kindred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुहीन|बंधुहीन
बन्धुः + -हीन <i>a.</i> destitute of relatives or friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुकः|बन्धुक|बंधुक|बंधुकः
बन्धुकः<BR>—1 The tree called बन्धुजीव.<BR>—2 A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुका|बंधुका
बन्धुकः + .{@-का, -की@} An unchaste woman (see बन्धकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुकी|बंधुकी
बन्धुकः + .{@-का, -की@} An unchaste woman (see बन्धकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुता|बंधुता
बन्धुता<BR>—1 Relatives, kinsmen, kindred (taken collectively); प्रेयो मित्रं बन्धुता<BR> वा समग्रा Māl. 6. 18, 9. 21; Ki. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Relationship, affinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुत्वम्
बन्धुत्वम् Relationship, brotherhood, affinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुदा|बंधुदा
बन्धुदा An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुमत्|बन्धुमन्त्
बन्धुमत् <i>a.</i> Having relations or kinsmen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुर|बंधुर|बन्धुरं|बन्धुरः
बन्धुर <i>a.</i> [बन्ध्-उरच्]<BR>—1 Undulating, wavy, uneven; प्रसकलकुचबन्धुरोद्धुरोरः Śi. 7. 34;<BR> Ku. 1. 42; U. 6. 25; अयं रक्षोनाथः क्षितिधरशिरोबन्धुरतरे<BR> (रथे तिष्ठन्) Mv. 6. 30.<BR>—2 Bent, inclined, bowed; बन्धुरगात्रि R. 13. 47; (= सन्नताङ्गि).<BR>—3 Crooked, curved.<BR>—4 Pleasing, handsome, beautiful, lovely; कथं नु तं बन्धुरकोमलाङ्गुलिम्<BR> Ś. 6. 12 (where it may mean ‘undulating’ also); समस्तशास्त्रस्मृतिबन्धुरे<BR> मुखे K. 3; बन्धुरा लावण्यधरा कन्धरा Dk. 1. 1.<BR>—5 Deaf.<BR>—6 Injurious, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुरः|बन्धुर|बंधुर|बन्धुरं
बन्धुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A goose.<BR>—2 A crane.<BR>—3 A drug.<BR>—4 An oil-cake.<BR>—5 The vulva.<BR>—6 The बन्धुजीव tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुराः
बन्धुर + .{@-राः@} ━<i>m.</i> (pl.) Parched corn or meal thereof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुरा|बंधुरा
बन्धुर + .{@-रा@} An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुरम्
बन्धुर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A diadem.<BR>—2 A band, rope; पञ्चबन्धुरम् (रथम्) Bhāg. 4. 26. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुरित
बन्धुरित <i>a.</i> Inclined, bent, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुल|बंधुल|बन्धुलः
बन्धुल <i>a.</i> [बन्ध्-उलच्]<BR>—1 Bent, curved, inclined.<BR>—2 Pleasing, delightful, attractive, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धुलः|बन्धुल|बंधुल
बन्धुल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A bastard; परगृहललिताः परान्नपुष्टाः परपुरुषैर्जनिताः पराङ्गनासु ।<BR> परधननिरता गुणेष्ववाच्या गजकलभा इव बन्धुला ललामः Mk. 4. 28<BR> (which is an answer given by the <i>bandhulas</i> themselves to the Vidūṣakaʼs<BR> question भोः के यूयं बन्धुला नाम).<BR>—2 An attendant in a harlotʼs chamber.<BR>—3 The tree called बन्धूक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1152-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूकः|बन्धूक|बंधूक|बंधूकः
बन्धूकः [बन्ध्-ऊक] N. of a tree; तवकरनिकरेण स्पष्टबन्धूकसूनस्तबकरचितमेते<BR> शेखरं बिभ्रतीव Śi. 11. 46; Ṛs. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूकम्
बन्धूकः + .{@-कम्@} A flower of this tree; बन्धूकद्युतिबान्धवोऽयमधरः<BR> Gīt. 10; Ṛs. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूकृ
बन्धूकृ<BR>—1 To make a friend of.<BR>—2 To bring into connection with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूर|बंधूर|बन्धूरः
बन्धूर <i>a.</i> [बन्ध्-ऊरच्]<BR>—1 Undulating, uneven.<BR>—2 Bent, inclined, bowed.<BR>—3 Pleasing, delightful, lovely; cf. बन्धुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूरम्
बन्धूर + .{@-रम्@} A hole, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्धूलिः|बन्धूलि|बंधूलि|बंधूलिः
बन्धूलिः [बन्ध्-ऊलि] The बन्धुजीव. tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्य|बंध्य|बन्ध्यः
बन्ध्य [बन्ध्-यत्]<BR>—1 To be bound or fettered, to be confined or imprisoned; अबन्ध्यं यश्च<BR> बध्नाति बद्धं यश्च प्रमुञ्चति Y. 2. 243.<BR>—2 To be joined or bound together.<BR>—3 To be formed, built or constructed.<BR>—4 Detained, under arrest.<BR>—5 (= वन्ध्य) Barren, unproductive, fruitless, useless (said of persons<BR> or things); बन्ध्यश्रमास्ते R. 16. 75; अबन्ध्ययत्नाश्च बभूवुरत्र<BR> ते 3. 29; Ki. 1. 33.<BR>—6 Not having the menses or menstrual discharge.<BR>—7 (At the end of comp.) Deprived or destitute of.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्ध्यफल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्यफल|बंध्यफल
बन्ध्य + -फल <i>a.</i> useless, vain, idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्या
बन्ध्या (= वन्ध्या)<BR>—1 A barren woman; न हि बन्ध्या विजानाति गुर्वी प्रसववेदनाम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 A barren cow.<BR>—3 A kind of perfume (बाल).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बन्ध्यातनयः, बन्ध्यापुत्रः, बन्ध्यासुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्यातनयः|बन्ध्यातनय
बन्ध्या + -तनयः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः, or {@-दुहिता, -सुता@} &c. the son<BR> or daughter of a barren woman; <i>i. e.</i> a wild impossibility, anything<BR> that does not and cannot exist; एष बन्ध्यासुतो याति खपुष्पकृतशेखरः;<BR> see खपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्यापुत्रः|बन्ध्यापुत्र
बन्ध्या + -तनयः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः, or {@-दुहिता, -सुता@} &c. the son<BR> or daughter of a barren woman; <i>i. e.</i> a wild impossibility, anything<BR> that does not and cannot exist; एष बन्ध्यासुतो याति खपुष्पकृतशेखरः;<BR> see खपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्यासुतः|बन्ध्यासुत
बन्ध्या + -तनयः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः, or {@-दुहिता, -सुता@} &c. the son<BR> or daughter of a barren woman; <i>i. e.</i> a wild impossibility, anything<BR> that does not and cannot exist; एष बन्ध्यासुतो याति खपुष्पकृतशेखरः;<BR> see खपुष्प.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बन्ध्रम्
