बर्ह्
बर्ह् I. €1 Ā. (बर्हते)<BR>—1 To speak.<BR>—2 To give.<BR>—3 To cover.<BR>—4 To hurt, kill, destroy.<BR>—5 To spread.<BR>—6 To be pre-eminent or excellent. ━II. €10 U. (बर्हयति-ते) To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">Page1154-1</a>]<BR> hurt, injure.<BR>—2 To speak. ━<i>With</i> {@नि@} to kill, destroy; निबर्हयन्तश्चान्योन्यं<BR> ते राक्षसवनौकसः Rām. 6. 90. 3; विलोकनेनैव तवामुना मुने कृतः<BR> कृतार्थोऽस्मि निबर्हिंतांहसा Śi. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1153-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हः|बर्ह|बर्हं
बर्हः, -हम्<BR> [बर्ह्-अच्]<BR>—1 A peacockʼs tail; दवोल्काहतशोषबर्हाः R. 16. 14; (केशपाशे)<BR> सति कुसुमसनाथे कं हरेदेष बर्हः V. 4. 10 (v. l.).<BR>—2 The tail of a bird.<BR>—3 A tail-feather (especially of a peacock); ज्योतिर्लेखावलयि गलितं यस्य बर्हम् Me. 46; Ku. 1. 15; Śi. 8. 11.<BR>—4 A leaf; आपाण्डुरं केतकबर्हमन्यः R. 6. 17.<BR>—5 A train, retinue.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बर्हचन्द्रकः, बर्हनेत्रम्, बर्हभारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हम्
