बर्हिष्ठ
बर्हिष्ठ <i>a.</i> (superl. of बृहत्) Largest, strongest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिष्ठम्
बर्हिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@} A kind of fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिस्
बर्हिस् <i>m., n.</i> [बर्ह् कर्मणि इसि]<BR>—1 Kuśa grass; प्राक् कूले बर्हिष्यासीनो गङ्गाकुल उदङ्मुखः Bhāg. 12. 6. 10;<BR> नियमविधिजलानां बर्हिषां चोपनेत्री Ku. 1. 60.<BR>—2 A bed or layer of Kuśa grass.<BR>—3 A sacrifice, oblation; ये बर्हिषो भागभाजं परादुः Bhāg. 4. 6. 5. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 Light, splendour. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Sacrifice.<BR>—3 Ether.<BR>—4 A kind of perfume.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बर्हिरुत्थः, बर्हिष्केशः, बर्हिर्ज्योतिस्, बर्हिर्मुखः, बर्हिःशुष्मन्, बर्हिःसद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिरुत्थः|बर्हिरुत्थ
बर्हिस् + -उत्थः, -केशः, -ज्योतिस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिष्केशः|बर्हिष्केश
बर्हिस् + -उत्थः, -केशः, -ज्योतिस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिर्ज्योतिस्
बर्हिस् + -उत्थः, -केशः, -ज्योतिस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिर्मुखः|बर्हिर्मुख
बर्हिस् + -मुखः (बर्हिर्मुखः)<BR>—1 an epithet of fire.<BR>—2 a god (whose mouth is fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिःशुष्मन्
बर्हिस् + -शुष्मन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिःसद्
बर्हिस् + -सद् (बर्हिषद्) <i>a.</i> seated on a layer of Kuśa grass. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the manes (pl.); Ms. 3. 199.<BR>—2 a Pitṛ or deified progenitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिष्क
बर्हिष्क <i>a.</i> Formed of or covered with, sacrificial grass; Mb. 13. 139. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिष्कम्
बर्हिष्क + .{@-ष्कम्@} A sacrificial grass or its seat; बर्हिष्कान्तरिते नित्यं<BR> शयानोऽमिगृहे सदा Mb. 13. 143. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बर्हिष्मत्|बर्हिष्मन्त्
बर्हिष्मत् <i>m.</i> A worshipper, sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बल्
बल् I. €1 P. (बलति)<BR>—1 To breathe or live.<BR>—2 To hoard grain. ━II. €1 U. (बलति-ते)<BR>—1 To give.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, kill.<BR>—3 To speak.<BR>—4 To see, mark. ━III. €10 U. (बलयति-ते) To live. ━IV. €10 Ā.<BR> (बालयते) To describe. ━<i>Caus.</i> (बालयति-ते) To nourish, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलम्
बलम् [बल्-अच्]<BR>—1 Strength, power, might, vigour; क्षत्त्रियाणां बलं युद्धम् Brav. P.<BR>—2 Force, violence; as in बलात् q. v.<BR>—3 An army, host, forces, troops; भवेदभीष्ममद्रोणं धृतराष्ट्रबलं<BR> कथम् Ve. 3. 24, 43; बलं भीष्मा (भीमा) भिरक्षितम् Bg. 1. 10; R. 16. 37.<BR>—4 Bulkiness, stoutness (of the body).<BR>—5 Body, figure, shape.<BR>—6 Semen virile.<BR>—7 Blood,<BR>—8 Gum myrrh.<BR>—9 A shoot, sprout.<BR>—10 Force or power of articulalion; वर्णः स्वरः । मात्रा बलम् । साम<BR> संतानः । इत्युक्तः शीक्षाध्यायः T. Up. 1. 2. 1.<BR>—11 The deity of power (such as Indra); नमो बलप्रमथनाय Mb. 12. 284. 94.<BR>—12 The hand; कान्ते विष्णुर्बले शक्रः कोष्ठेऽग्निर्भोक्तुमिच्छति Mb. 12. 239. 8.<BR>—13 Effort (यत्न); विधिः शुकं बलं चेति त्रय एते गुणाः परे<BR> Mb. 12. 320. 110 (com. बलं वासनाविषयप्राप्त्यनुकूलो यत्नः). (बलेन<BR> means ‘on the strength of’, ‘by means or virtue of’; बाहुबलेन जितः,<BR> वीर्यबलेन &c.; बलात् ‘perforce’, ‘forcibly’, ‘violently’, ‘against oneʼs will’<BR>; बलान्निद्रा समायाता Pt. 1; हृदयमदये तस्मिन्नेवं<BR> पुनर्वलते बलात् Gīt. 7.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलः|बल|बलं
बलम् + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A crow; Rām. 6. 54. 9.<BR>—2 N. of the elder brother of Kṛṣṇa; see बलराम below.<BR>—3 N. of a demon killed by Indra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बलाग्रम्, बलाङ्गकः, बलाञ्चिता, बलाटः, बलाधिक, बलाधिकरणम्, बलाध्यक्षः, बलानुजः, बलान्वित, बलाबलम्, बलाभ्रः, बलारातिः, बलार्थिन्, बलावलेपः, बलाशः, बलासः, बलाड्यः, बलात्मिका, बलालयः, बलाहः, बलोत्कट, बलोपपन्न, बलोपेत, बलोपादानम्, बलौघः, बलकर, बलकृत्, बलकृत, बलक्षोभः, बलचक्रम्, बलज, बलतापनः, बलदः, बलदर्पः, बलदेवः, बलदेवा, बलदेवी, बलद्विष्, बलनिग्रह, बलपतिः, बलपुच्छकः, बलपृष्ठकः, बलप्रद, बलप्रमथनी, बलप्रसूः, बलभद्र, बलभिद्, बलभृत्, बलमुख्यः, बलरामः, बलवर्जित, बलवर्णिन्, बलवर्धन, बलविन्यासः, बलव्यसनम्, बलव्यापद्, बलशालिन्, बलसमुत्थानम्, बलसूदनः, बलसेना, बलस्थ, बलस्थितिः, बलहन्, बलहन्तृ, बलहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाग्रम्
बलम् + -अग्रम् excessive strength or force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाग्रः|बलाग्र
बलम् + -अग्रम् + .({@-ग्रः@}) the head of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाङ्गकः|बलाङ्गक|बलांगक
बलम् + -अङ्गकः the spring; ‘वसन्त इष्यः सुरभिः पुष्पकालो बलाङ्गकः’ Hc. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाञ्चिता|बलांचिता
बलम् + -अञ्चिता the lute of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाटः|बलाट
बलम् + -अटः a kind of beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाधिक
बलम् + -अधिक <i>a.</i> surpassing in strength, of superior strengh or force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाधिकरणम्
बलम् + -अधिकरणम् the affairs of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाध्यक्षः|बलाध्यक्ष
बलम् + -अध्यक्षः<BR>—1 a general or commander of an army; सेनापतिबलाध्यक्षौ सर्वदिक्षु<BR> निवेशयेत् Ms. 7. 189.<BR>—2 a war-minister.<BR>—3 An officer in charge of infantry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलानुजः|बलानुज
बलम् + -अनुजः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलान्वित
बलम् + -अन्वित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 endowed with strength, mighty, powerful.<BR>—2 leading an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाबलम्
बलम् + -अबलम्<BR>—1 comparative strength and want of strength, relative strength and weakness;<BR> परात्मनोः परिच्छिद्य शक्त्यादीनां बलाबलम् R. 17. 59.<BR>—2 relative significance and insignificance, comparative importance and<BR> unimportance; समय एव करोति बलाबलम् Śi. 6. 44. ˚अधिकरणम्<BR> a kind of न्यायभेद according to Jaimini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाभ्रः|बलाभ्र
बलम् + -अभ्रः an army in the form of a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलारातिः|बलाराति
बलम् + -अरातिः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलार्थिन्
बलम् + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> desirous of power; राज्ञो बलार्थिनः षष्ठे (वर्षे<BR> उपनयनं कार्यम्) Ms. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलावलेपः|बलावलेप
बलम् + -अवलेपः pride of strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाशः|बलाश
बलम् + -अशः, -असः<BR>—1 consumption.<BR>—2 the phlegmatic humour (कफ).<BR>—3 a swelling in the throat (which stops the passages of food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलासः|बलास
बलम् + -अशः, -असः<BR>—1 consumption.<BR>—2 the phlegmatic humour (कफ).<BR>—3 a swelling in the throat (which stops the passages of food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाड्यः
बलम् + -आड्यः a bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्मिका
बलम् + -आत्मिका a kind of sun-flower (हस्तिशुण्डी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलालयः
बलम् + -आलयः a military camp; पूज्यमानो हरिगणैराजगाम बलालयम्<BR> Rām. 6. 112. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाहः|बलाह|बलाहं
बलम् + -आहः water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोत्कट
बलम् + -उत्कट <i>a.</i> of mighty strength; न बध्यते ह्यविश्वस्तो दुर्बलोऽपि<BR> बलोत्कटैः Pt. 2. 44, 3. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपपन्न
बलम् + -उपपन्न, -उपेत <i>a.</i> endowed with strength, strong, powerful;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">Page1155-1</a>]<BR> एतां रामबलोपेतां रक्षां यः सुकृती पठेत् Rāmarakṣā 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपेत
बलम् + -उपपन्न, -उपेत <i>a.</i> endowed with strength, strong, powerful;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">Page1155-1</a>]<BR> एतां रामबलोपेतां रक्षां यः सुकृती पठेत् Rāmarakṣā 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1154-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलोपादानम्
बलम् + -उपादानम् Recruitment of the army; Kau. A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलौघः|बलौघ
बलम् + -ओघः a multitude of troops, numerous army; लक्ष्मीं दधत् प्रतिगिरेरलघुर्बलौघः Śi. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलकर
बलम् + -कर, -कृत् <i>a.</i> strengthening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलकृत्
बलम् + -कर, -कृत् <i>a.</i> strengthening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलकृत
बलम् + -कृत done by force or against free consent; सर्वान् बलकृतानर्थानकृतान्<BR> मनुरब्रवीत् Ms. 8. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्षोभः|बलक्षोभ
बलम् + -क्षोभः disturbance in the army, mutiny, revolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलचक्रम्
बलम् + -चक्रम्<BR>—1 dominion, sovereignty.<BR>—2 an army, a host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलज|बलजं
बलम् + -ज <i>a.</i> produced by power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलजम्
बलम् + -ज + .({@-जम्@})<BR>—1 a city-gate, gate.<BR>—2 a field.<BR>—3 grain, a heap of grain; त्वं समीरण इव प्रतीक्षितः कर्षकेण बलजान्<BR> पुपूषता Śi. 14. 7.<BR>—4 war, battle<BR>—5 marrow, pith.<BR>—6 a pretty figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलजा
बलम् + -ज + .({@-जा@})<BR>—1 the earth.<BR>—2 a handsome woman.<BR>—3 a kind of jasmine (Arabian).<BR>—4 a rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलतापनः
बलम् + -तापनः an epithet of Indra; अभिषिषेच मरन्दरसामृतैर्नवलतावलतापनरत्नभम्<BR> (अलिनम्) Rām. Ch. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदः|बलद
बलम् + -दः an ox, a bullock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदर्पः|बलदर्प
बलम् + -दर्पः pride of strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेवः|बलदेव
बलम् + -देवः<BR>—1 air, wind.<BR>—2 N. of the elder brother of Kṛṣṇa; see बलराम below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेवा
बलम् + -देवा, -देवी <i>f.</i> N. of a medicinal herb which is<BR> also called त्रायमाण. It grows in the forests on the slopes of the<BR> Himālayas and in Persia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलदेवी
बलम् + -देवा, -देवी <i>f.</i> N. of a medicinal herb which is<BR> also called त्रायमाण. It grows in the forests on the slopes of the<BR> Himālayas and in Persia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलद्विष्
बलम् + -द्विष् <i>m.</i>, {@-निषूदनः@}<BR> epithets of Indra; बलनिषूदनमर्थपतिं च तम् R. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलनिग्रह
बलम् + -निग्रह <i>a.</i> weakening, enervating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलपतिः|बलपति
बलम् + -पतिः<BR>—1 a general, commander.<BR>—2 an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलपुच्छकः
बलम् + -पुच्छकः a crow; Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलपृष्ठकः
बलम् + -पृष्ठकः a kind of deer (Mar. रोहें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलप्रद
बलम् + -प्रद <i>a.</i> giving strength, invigorating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलप्रमथनी
बलम् + -प्रमथनी N. of a form of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलप्रसूः
बलम् + -प्रसूः N. of Rohiṇi, mother of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्र|बलभद्रः
बलम् + -भद्र <i>a.</i> strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्रः|बलभद्र
बलम् + -भद्र + .({@-द्रः@})<BR>—1 a strong or powerful man.<BR>—2 a kind of ox.<BR>—3 N. of Balarāma, q. v. below.<BR>—4 the tree called लोध्र.<BR>—5 N. of Ananta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभद्रा
बलम् + -भद्र + .({@-द्रा@}) a maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभिद्
बलम् + -भिद् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Indra; Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलभृत्
बलम् + -भृत् <i>a.</i> strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलमुख्यः|बलमुख्य
बलम् + -मुख्यः the chief of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलरामः|बलराम
बलम् + -रामः ‘the strong Rāma’, N. of the elder brother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR> [He was the seventh son of Vasudava and Devakī; but transferred to the<BR> womb of Rohiṇī to save him from falling a prey to the cruelty of Kaṃsa.<BR> He and his brother Kṛṣṇa were brought up by Nanda in Gokula. When<BR> quite young, he killed the powerful demons Dhenuka and Pralamba, and performed,<BR> like his brother, many feats of surprising strength. On one occasion Balarāma<BR> under the influence of wine, of which he was very fond, called upon the<BR> Yamunā river to come to him that he might bathe; and on his command being<BR> unheeded, he plunged his plough-share into the river and dragged the waters<BR> after him, until the river assumed a human form and asked his forgiveness.<BR> On another occasion he dragged towards himself the whole city of Hastināpura<BR> along with its walls. As Kṛṣṇa was a friend and admirer of the Pāṇḍavas,<BR> so Balarāma was of the Kauravas, as was seen in his desire of giving<BR> his sister Subhadrā to Duryodhana rather than to Arjuna; yet he declined<BR> to take any part in the great Bhāratī war either with the Pāṇḍavas<BR> or the Kauravas. He is represented as dressed in blue clothes, and armed<BR> with a ploughshare which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">Page1155-2</a>]<BR> was his most effective weapon. His wife was Revatī. He is sometimes regarded<BR> as an incarnation of the serpent Śeṣa and sometimes as the eighth incarnation<BR> of Viṣṇu; see the quotation under हल].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्जित
बलम् + -वर्जित <i>a.</i> infirm, weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्णिन्
बलम् + -वर्णिन् <i>a.</i> strong and looking well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवर्धन
बलम् + -वर्धन <i>a.</i> invigorating, strengthening. ━<i>m.</i> N. of स्थण्डिलाग्नि<BR> in उत्सर्जन or उपाकर्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलविन्यासः|बलविन्यास
बलम् + -विन्यासः array or arrangement of troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलव्यसनम्
बलम् + -व्यसनम् the defeat of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलव्यापद्
बलम् + -व्यापद् <i>f.</i> decrease of strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलशालिन्
बलम् + -शालिन् <i>a.</i> strong; बलशालितया यथा तथा वा धियमुच्छेदपरामयं<BR> दधानः Ki. 13. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलसमुत्थानम्
बलम् + -समुत्थानम् Recruiting a strong army; Kau. A. 1. 16; तमभियोक्तुं<BR> बलसमुत्थानमकरोत् Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलसूदनः|बलसूदन
बलम् + -सूदनः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलसेना
बलम् + -सेना a strong army, an army, host.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलस्थ|बलस्थः
बलम् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलस्थः|बलस्थ
बलम् + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः@}) a warrior, soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलस्थितिः|बलस्थिति
बलम् + -स्थितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a camp; an encampment.<BR>—2 a royal camp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहन्
बलम् + -हन्, -हन्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Indra; पाण्डुः स्मरति ते नित्यं बलहन्तुः समीपगः<BR> Mb. 15. 20. 17.<BR>—2 of Balarāma.<BR>—3 phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहन्तृ
बलम् + -हन्, -हन्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Indra; पाण्डुः स्मरति ते नित्यं बलहन्तुः समीपगः<BR> Mb. 15. 20. 17.<BR>—2 of Balarāma.<BR>—3 phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलहीन
बलम् + -हीन <i>a.</i> destitute of strength, weak, feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलकः|बलक
बलकः A dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलकम्
बलकः + .{@-कम्@} A mixture of treacle and milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्ष|बलक्षः
बलक्ष <i>a.</i> [बलं क्षायत्यस्मात् क्षै-क] White; द्विरददन्तवलक्षमलक्ष्यत<BR> स्फुरितभृङ्गमृगच्छवि केतकम् Śi. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्षः|बलक्ष
बलक्ष + .{@-क्षः@} The white colour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बलक्षगुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलक्षगुः|बलक्षगु
बलक्ष + -गुः (for गो ‘a ray’) the moon; यथानत्यर्जुनाब्जन्मसदृक्षाङ्को<BR> बलक्षगुः Kāv. 1. 46 (given as an instance of the प्रसाद quality<BR> of the Gauḍīyas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलनम्
बलनम् Making strong, invigorating, strengthening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलयति
बलयति Den. P. To strengthen, invigorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलायते
बलायते Den. Ā. To put forth strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बललः|बलल
बललः<BR>—1 An epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्|बलवन्त्
बलवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strong, powerful, mighty; विधिरहो बलवानिति मे मतिः Bh. 2. 91.<BR>—2 Stout, robust; बलवानपि निस्तेजाः कस्य नाभिभवास्पदम् H. 2. 132.<BR>—3 Dense, thick (as darkness, &c.)<BR>—4 Getting the upper hand, predominant, prevailing; बलवानिन्द्रियग्रामो<BR> विद्वांसमपि कर्षति Ms. 2. 215.<BR>—5 More important, of greater weight; लोकापवादो बलवान् मतो मे R. 14. 40.<BR>—6 Accompained by an army. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of the 8th Muhūrta.<BR>—2 Phlegm; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवती
बलवत् + .{@-ती@} Small cardamoms. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Strongly, powerfully, forcibly; पुनर्वशित्वाद्बलवन्निगृह्य Ku. 3. 69.<BR>—2 Very much, excessively, in a high degree; बलवत्तर्पितश्चाहं बलवान्<BR> भगवंस्त्वया Rām. 2. 92. 5; बलवदपि शिक्षितानामात्मन्यप्रत्ययं<BR> चेतः Ś. 1. 2; शीतार्ति बलवदुपेयुषेव नीरैः Śi. 8. 62; Ś. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलवत्ता
बलवत्ता<BR>—1 Powerfulness, strength.<BR>—2 Superiority, excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बला
बला<BR>—1 N. of a powerful lore or incantation (taught by Viśvāmitra to Rāma<BR> and Lakṣmaṇa); तौ बलातिबलयोः प्रभावतः R. 11. 9. (For some<BR> description see the quotation under अतिबला).<BR>—2 N. of medicinal herbs नागवेल and जयन्ती.<BR>—3 The earth; Gīrvāṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बलापञ्चकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलापञ्चकम्
बला + -पञ्चकम् A pentad of the five medicinal herbs: बला,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">Page1156-1</a>]<BR> महाबला, नागबला, अतिबला and राजबला. The Bhāvaprakāśa<BR> however, mentions बलाचतुष्टय; बलाचतुष्टयं शीतं मधुरं बलकान्तिकृत् ।<BR> स्रिग्धं ग्राहि समीरास्रपित्तास्रक्षतनाशनम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1155-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलती
बलती A turret at the top of a palace; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाकः|बलाक
बलाकः, -का<BR> [Uṇ. 4. 14] A crane; सेविष्यन्ते नयनसुभगं खे भवन्तं<BR> बलाकाः Me. 9; Mk. 5. 18, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाका
बलाकः, -का<BR> [Uṇ. 4. 14] A crane; सेविष्यन्ते नयनसुभगं खे भवन्तं<BR> बलाकाः Me. 9; Mk. 5. 18, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाका
बलाकः, -का + .{@-का@} A mistress, beloved woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाकिका
बलाकिका A small kind of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाकिन्
बलाकिन् <i>a.</i> Abounding in cranes; कालिकेव निबिडा बलाकिनी<BR> R. 11. 15; Ku. 7. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्कारः|बलात्कार
बलात्कारः<BR>—1 Using violence, employing force.<BR>—2 Outrage, violence, force, oppression, exaction; शापयन्त्रितपौलस्त्यबलात्कारकचग्रहैः<BR> (अदूषितान्) R. 10. 47; बलात्कारेण निर्वर्त्य &c.<BR>—3 Injustice.<BR>—4 (In law) Detention of the person of a debtor by the creditor and the<BR> employment of forcible means to recover the debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलात्कृत
बलात्कृत <i>a.</i> Forced, overcome; चिन्ताशोकबलात्कृतम् Rām. 4. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलायः|बलाय
बलायः Crataeva Roxburghii (Mar. बायवर्णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलासः|बलास
बलासः<BR>—1 A kind of disease.<BR>—2 Consumption, phthisis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलासकः|बलासक
बलासकः A yellow spot in the white of the eye (caused by disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलासिन्
बलासिन् <i>a.</i> Consumptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाहम्
बलाहम् Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलाहकः|बलाहक
बलाहकः<BR>—1 A cloud; बलाहकच्छेदविभक्तरागामकालसंध्यामिव धातुमत्ताम् Ku. 1. 4.<BR>—2 A kind of crane.<BR>—3 A mountain.<BR>—4 N. of one of the seven clouds appearing at the destruction of the world.<BR>—5 One of the four horses of Viṣṇu. —6 A kind of snake; अथ कम्बलाऽश्वतर-धृतराष्ट्रबलाहकाः ।<BR> इत्यादयोऽपरे नागास्तत्तत्कुलसमुद्भवाः ॥ Abh. Cin. 1311.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिः|बलि
बलिः [बल्-इन्]<BR>—1 An oblation, a gift or offering (usually religious); नीवारबलिं<BR> विलोकयतः Ś. 4. 21; U. 1. 50.<BR>—2 The offering of a portion of the daily meal of rice, grain, ghee &c.<BR> to all creatures, (also called भूतयज्ञ), one of the five daily Yajñas<BR> to be performed by a householder; see Ms. 3. 67, 91; it is usually performed<BR> by throwing up into the air, near the house-door, portions of the daily<BR> meal before partaking of it; यासां बलिः सपदि मद्गृहदेहलीनां हंसैश्च<BR> सारसगणैश्च विलुप्तपूर्वः Mk. 1. 9.<BR>—3 Worship, adoration; Rām. 2. 3. 8; अवचितबलिपुष्पा वेदिसंमार्गदक्षा<BR> Ku. 1. 60; Me. 57; अवचितानि बलिकर्मपर्याप्तानि पुष्पाणि Ś. 4.<BR>—4 Fragments of food left at a meal.<BR>—5 A victim offered to a deity.<BR>—6 A tax, tribute, impost; also ‘religious tax’; (cf. सीता, भागो, बलिः,<BR> करो … … च राष्ट्रम्); Kau. A. 2. 6. 24; प्रजानामेव भूत्यर्थं<BR> स ताभ्यो बलिमग्रहीत् R. 1. 18; Ms. 7. 80, 8. 307;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">Page1156-2</a>]<BR> प्रजिघाय बलिं तथा Śiva B. 29. 42; न चाजिहीर्षींद् बलिमप्रवृत्तम् Bu. C. 2. 44.<BR>—7 The handle of a <i>chowrie</i>.<BR>—8 N. of a celebrated demon; येन बद्धो बली राजा दानवेन्द्रो महाबलः<BR> Rakṣābandhanamantra. [He was a son of Virochana, the son of Prahlāda.<BR> He was a very powerful demon and oppressed the gods very much. They, therefore,<BR> prayed to Viṣṇu for succour, who descended on earth as a son of Kaśyapa<BR> and Aditi in the form of a dwarf. He assumed the dress of a mendicant,<BR> and having gone to Bali prayed him to give him as much earth as he could<BR> cover in three steps. Bali, who was noted for his liberality, unhesitatingly<BR> acceded to this apparently simple request. But the dwarf soon assumed<BR> a mighty form, and began to measure the three steps. The first step covered<BR> the earth, the second the heavens; and not knowing where to place the<BR> third, he planted it on the head of Bali and sent him and all his legions<BR> to the Pātāla and allowed him to be its ruler. Thus the universe was<BR> once more restored to the rule of Indra; cf. छलयसि विकमणे बलिमद्भुतवामन<BR> Gīt. 1; R. 7. 35; Me. 59. Viṣṇu is said to still guard his door in<BR> Pātāla. He is one of the seven <i>Chirajivins</i>; cf. चिरजीविन्].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिः|बलि
बलिः + .{@-लिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A fold, wrinkle &c. (usually written वलि q. v.).<BR>—2 The fold of skin in stout persons or females.<BR>—3 The ridge of a thatched roof.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बलिकर^1, बलिकरम्भः, बलिकर्मन्, बलिक्रिया, बलिदानम्, बलिद्विष्, बलिध्वंसिन्, बलिनन्दनः, बलिपुत्रः, बलिसुतः, बलिपुष्टः, बलिप्रियः, बलिबन्धनः, बलिभुज्, बलिभृत्, बलिभोजः, बलिभोजनः, बलिमन्दिरम्, बलिवेश्मन्, बलिसद्मन्, बलिमुखः, बलिविधानम्, बलिव्याकुल, बलिषड्भागः, बलिहन्, बलिहरणम्, बलिहोमः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकर
बलिः + -कर^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 paying tribute.<BR>—2 offering sacrifices.<BR>—3 producing wrinkles.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकरम्भः|बलिकरम्भ
बलिः + -करम्भः a sacrificial cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिकर्मन्|बलिकर्म्मन्
बलिः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 offering oblations to all creatures.<BR>—2 the act of worshipping.<BR>—3 payment of tribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिक्रिया
बलिः + -क्रिया a line on the forehead; नतभ्रुवो मण्डयति स्म विग्रहे<BR> बलिक्रिया चातिलकं तदास्पदम् Ki. 8. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिदानम्
बलिः + -दानम्<BR>—1 presentation of an offering to a deity.<BR>—2 offering oblations to all creatures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिद्विष्
बलिः + -द्विष्, -ध्वंसिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिध्वंसिन्
बलिः + -द्विष्, -ध्वंसिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिनन्दनः|बलिनन्दन|बलिनंदन
बलिः + -नन्दनः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः epithets of Bāṇa, the son of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिपुत्रः|बलिपुत्र
बलिः + -नन्दनः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः epithets of Bāṇa, the son of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिसुतः|बलिसुत
बलिः + -नन्दनः, -पुत्रः, -सुतः epithets of Bāṇa, the son of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिपुष्टः|बलिपुष्ट
बलिः + -पुष्टः a crow; भ्रमेण द्रष्टुं बलिपुष्टलोकः समापतत्याशु<BR> तमिस्ररूपः Rām. Ch. 6. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिप्रियः|बलिप्रिय
बलिः + -प्रियः the <i>Lodhra</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिबन्धनः|बलिबन्धन|बलिबंधन
बलिः + -बन्धनः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभुज्
बलिः + -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a crow; अहो अधर्मः पालानां पीव्नां बलिभुजामिव Bhāg. 1. 18. 33.<BR>—2 a sparrow.<BR>—3 a crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभृत्
बलिः + -भृत् <i>a.</i> tributary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभोजः|बलिभोज
बलिः + -भोजः, -भोजनः a crow; द्वितीयो बलिभोजानां (पन्थाः)<BR> Rām. 4. 58. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिभोजनः|बलिभोजन
बलिः + -भोजः, -भोजनः a crow; द्वितीयो बलिभोजानां (पन्थाः)<BR> Rām. 4. 58. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमन्दिरम्
बलिः + -मन्दिरम्, -वेश्मन्, -सद्मन् <i>n.</i> the lower regions, the abode of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिवेश्मन्
बलिः + -मन्दिरम्, -वेश्मन्, -सद्मन् <i>n.</i> the lower regions, the abode of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिसद्मन्
बलिः + -मन्दिरम्, -वेश्मन्, -सद्मन् <i>n.</i> the lower regions, the abode of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिमुखः|बलिमुख
बलिः + -मुखः a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिविधानम्
बलिः + -विधानम् the offering of an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिव्याकुल
बलिः + -व्याकुल <i>a.</i> engaged in worship or in offering oblations to<BR> all creatures; आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला वा Me. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिषड्भागः|बलिषड्भाग
बलिः + -षड्भागः the sixth part as a tribute; अरक्षितारं राजानं बलिषड्भागहारिणम् Ms. 8. 308.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिहन्
बलिः + -हन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिहरणम्
बलिः + -हरणम् an offering of oblations to all creatures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिहोमः|बलिहोम
बलिः + -होमः the offering of oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिक
बलिक <i>a.</i> One who takes his food every sixth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बलिन्
बलिन् <i>a.</i> [बलमस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Strong, powerful, mighty; कुलध्वजस्तानि चलध्वजानि निवेशयामास<BR> बली बलानि R. 16. 37; Ms. 7. 174.<BR>—2 Stout, robust. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A buffalo.<BR>—2 A hog.<BR>—3 A camel.<BR>—4 A bull.<BR>—5 A soldier.<BR>—6 A kind<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1157-1" target="_blank">Page1157-1</a>]<BR> of jasmine.<BR>—7 The phlegmatic humour.<BR>—8 An epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1156-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

