बादरम्
बादर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 The jujube.<BR>—2 Silk.<BR>—3 Water.<BR>—4 A garment of cotton.<BR>—5 A conch-shell winding from left to right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरा
बादर + .{@-रा@} The cotton shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरायणः|बादरायण
बादरायणः [बदर्यां भवः फक्] N. of a sage said to be the<BR> author of the Śārīraka Sūtras of the Vedānta philosophy (generally<BR> identified with Vyāsa).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बादरायणसूत्रम्, बादरायणसंबन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरायणसूत्रम्
बादरायणः + -सूत्रम् the Vedānta aphorisms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरायणसंबन्धः|बादरायणसम्बन्ध
बादरायणः + -संबन्धः (a modern formation) an imaginary or far-fetched relation;<BR> अस्माकं बदरीचक्रं युष्माकं बदरीतरुः । बादरायणसंबन्धो यूयं<BR> यूयं वयं वयम् ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरायणिः|बादरायणि
बादरायणिः N. of Śuka, son of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरिः|बादरि
बादरिः N. of a philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बादरिक
बादरिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> One who gathers jujube fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्
बाध् €1 Ā. (बाधते, बाधित)<BR>—1 To harass, oppress, torment, press hard, annoy, trouble, disturb, vex,<BR> pain (persons or things); ऊनं न सत्त्वेष्वधिको बबाधे R. 2. 14; भूरिभारभराक्रान्तः<BR> स्कन्ध एष नु बाधति । न तथा बाधते स्कन्धो यथा बाधति बाधते Subhāṣ.;<BR> Me. 55; Ms. 9. 226, 10. 129; Bk. 14. 45.<BR>—2 To resist, oppose, thwart, check, obstruct, arrest, interfere with;<BR> गुणानुरागादिव सख्यमीयिवान् न बाधतेऽस्य त्रिगणः परस्परम् Ki. 1. 11;<BR> U. 5. 19.<BR>—3 To attack, assault, assail; स तदा लब्धतीर्थोऽपि न बबाधे निरायुधम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 19. 4.<BR>—4 To wrong, violate.<BR>—5 To hurt, injure.<BR>—6 To drive away, repel, remove; उष्णेन बाध्यते शीतं शीतेनोष्णं प्रबाध्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 16. 12.<BR>—7 To suspend, set aside, annul, annihilate, abolish (as a rule &c.);<BR> न धर्ममर्थकामाभ्यां बबाधे न च तेन तौ R. 17. 57. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To oppress, torment, harass &c.<BR>—2 To subdue, conquer. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि@}<BR>—1 to hurt, injure.<BR>—2 to vex, harass, torment.<BR>━{@आ@} to vex, torment, injure.<BR>━{@परि@} to trouble, afflict; मोहान्मया सुतनु पूर्वमुपेक्षितस्ते<BR> यो बाष्पबिन्दुरधरं परिबाधमानः Ś. 7. 25.<BR>━{@सम्@} to trouble, torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधः|बाध
बाधः, -धा<BR> [बाध्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Pain, suffering, affliction, torment; रजन्या सह जृम्भते मदनबाधा V. 3.<BR>—2 Disturbance, molestation, annoyance; इति भ्रमरबाधां निरूपयति Ś. 1.<BR>—3 Harm, injury, damage, hurt; चरणस्य बाधा M. 4; न निषेध्योऽल्पबाधस्तु<BR> सेतुः कल्याणकारकः Y. 2. 156.<BR>—4 Danger, peril; नैवासौ वेद संहारं प्राणबाध उपस्थिते Bhāg. 1. 7. 27.<BR>—5 Resistance, opposition.<BR>—6 An objection.<BR>—7 Contradiction, refutation.<BR>—8 Suspension, annulment.<BR>—9 A flaw in a syllogism, one of the five forms of हेत्वाभास or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">Page1162-1</a>]<BR> fallacious middle term; see बाधित below.<BR>—10 Violation, infraction.<BR>—11 Sublation; बाधो नाम यदेवेदमिति निश्चितं विज्ञानं कारणान्तरेण<BR> मिथ्येति कथ्यते ŚB. on MS. 10. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधा
बाधः, -धा<BR> [बाध्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Pain, suffering, affliction, torment; रजन्या सह जृम्भते मदनबाधा V. 3.<BR>—2 Disturbance, molestation, annoyance; इति भ्रमरबाधां निरूपयति Ś. 1.<BR>—3 Harm, injury, damage, hurt; चरणस्य बाधा M. 4; न निषेध्योऽल्पबाधस्तु<BR> सेतुः कल्याणकारकः Y. 2. 156.<BR>—4 Danger, peril; नैवासौ वेद संहारं प्राणबाध उपस्थिते Bhāg. 1. 7. 27.<BR>—5 Resistance, opposition.<BR>—6 An objection.<BR>—7 Contradiction, refutation.<BR>—8 Suspension, annulment.<BR>—9 A flaw in a syllogism, one of the five forms of हेत्वाभास or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">Page1162-1</a>]<BR> fallacious middle term; see बाधित below.<BR>—10 Violation, infraction.<BR>—11 Sublation; बाधो नाम यदेवेदमिति निश्चितं विज्ञानं कारणान्तरेण<BR> मिथ्येति कथ्यते ŚB. on MS. 10. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधा
बाधः, -धा + .{@-धा@} Refutation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बाधापवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1161-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधापवादः|बाधापवाद
बाधः + -अपवादः denial of an exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधक|बाधकः
बाधक <i>a.</i> (-धिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बाध् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Troubling, tormenting, oppressing.<BR>—2 Vexing, annoying.<BR>—3 Annulling.<BR>—4 Suspending, contradicting, invalidating (as a rule &c.).<BR>—5 Hindering.<BR>—6 That which sublates; तद्धि बाधकं भवति यदबाधमानमप्रयोजनं<BR> भवति ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधकः|बाधक
बाधक + .{@-कः@} A particular disease of women; (ऋतुकाले प्रजाजननशक्तिप्रतिरोधकः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधन|बाधनं
बाधन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Harassing, opposing. —2 Refuting, controverting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधनम्
बाधन + .{@-नम्@} [बाध्-भावे ल्युट्] —1 Harassing, oppression, annoyance, disturbance, pain; Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Annulment.<BR>—3 Removal, suspension.<BR>—4 Refutation, contradiction.<BR>—5 Opposing, hindering.<BR>—6 Precluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधना
बाधन + .{@-ना@} Pain, trouble, anxiety, disturbance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधयितृ
बाधयितृ, -बाधितृ <i>m.</i><BR> An injurer, opposer, annoyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधितृ
बाधयितृ, -बाधितृ <i>m.</i><BR> An injurer, opposer, annoyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधित|बाधितः
बाधित <i>p. p.</i> [बाध्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Harassed, oppressed, annoyed.<BR>—2 Pained, troubled, afflicted.<BR>—3 Opposed, obstructed.<BR>—4 Checked, arrested.<BR>—5 Set aside, suspended.<BR>—6 Refuted.<BR>—7 (In logic) Contradicted, contradictory; inconsistent (and hence futile);<BR> साध्याभाववत् पक्षको बाधितः; <i>e. g.</i> वह्निरनुष्णः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्य|बाध्यं
बाध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be pained or troubled.<BR>—2 Fit to be opposed or objected to, objectionable, exceptionable.<BR>—3 To be annulled.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बाध्यबाधकता, बाध्यरेतस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्यबाधकता
बाध्य + -बाधकता the condition of oppressed and oppressor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्यरेतस्
बाध्य + -रेतस् <i>a.</i> impotent; Kull. on Ms. 9. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्यत्वम्
बाध्यत्वम्, बाध्यमानत्वम् Suspension, annulment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाध्यमानत्वम्
बाध्यत्वम्, बाध्यमानत्वम् Suspension, annulment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाधिर्यम्
बाधिर्यम् Deafness; बाधिंर्यं प्राणमन्दत्वं यः पश्यति स मुच्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 288. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धकिनेयः|बान्धकिनेय|बांधकिनेय|बांधकिनेयः
बान्धकिनेयः A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धवः|बान्धव|बांधव|बांधवः
बान्धवः [बन्धु स्वार्थे इदमर्थे वाऽण्]<BR>—1 A relation, kinsman (in general); बान्धवाः कुलमिच्छन्ति Subhāṣ.;<BR> यस्यार्थास्तस्य बान्धवाः H. 1; Ms. 5. 74, 101, 4. 179.<BR>—2 A maternal relation; Ms. 4. 179.<BR>—3 A friend; धनेभ्यः परो बान्धवो नास्ति लोके Subhāṣ.<BR>—4 A brother.<BR>—5 Friendly service (बन्धुकृत्य); पैतृष्वस्रेयप्रीत्यर्थं तद्रोत्रस्यात्तबान्धवः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 19. 35.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बान्धवजनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धवजनः|बान्धवजन|बांधवजन
बान्धवः + -जनः relatives, kinsmen (taken collectively); दारिद्यात् पुरुषस्य<BR> बान्धवजनो वाक्ये न संतिष्ठते Mk. 1. 36; Pt. 4. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बान्धव्यम्
बान्धव्यम् Consanguinity, relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाभ्रव
बाभ्रव <i>a.</i> Belonging or relating to बभ्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाभ्रवी
बाभ्रवी An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाभ्रुक
बाभ्रुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Brown, brownish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्बटीरः|बार्बटीर|बार्ब्बटीर|बार्ब्बटीरः
बार्बटीरः<BR>—1 The kernel of the mango-fruit.<BR>—2 Tin.<BR>—3 A young shoot.<BR>—4 The son of a harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्ह
बार्ह <i>a.</i> (-र्ही <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बर्ह-अण्] Made of the feathers of a peacockʼs tail; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हद्रथः|बार्हद्रथ
बार्हद्रथः, बार्हद्रथिः A patronymic of king Jarāsandha, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हद्रथिः|बार्हद्रथि
बार्हद्रथः, बार्हद्रथिः A patronymic of king Jarāsandha, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत|बार्हस्पतं
बार्हस्पत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बृहस्पति-अण्] Related to, descended from or<BR> sacred to, Bṛhaspati. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a year; अद्य बार्हस्पतः श्रीमान्<BR> युक्तः पुष्येण राघव । प्रोच्यते ब्राह्मणैः प्राज्ञैः केन त्वमसि दुर्मनाः ॥ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत्य|बार्हस्पत्यः
बार्हस्पत्य <i>a.</i> [बृहस्पति-यक्] Relating to Bṛhaspti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत्यः|बार्हस्पत्य
बार्हस्पत्य + .{@-त्यः@}<BR>—1 A pupil of Bṛhaspati; Bhāg. 11. 23. 2.<BR>—2 A follower of Bṛhaspati who taught the rankest form of materialism, a materialist.<BR>—3 An epithet of Agni.<BR>—4 An infidel, materialist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत्यम्
बार्हस्पत्य + .{@-त्यम्@}<BR>—1 The constellation Puṣya.<BR>—2 Morality, ethics; the अर्थशास्त्र of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हस्पत्त्याः
बार्हस्पत्य + .{@-त्याः@} N. of a school of the writers on the science of Government<BR> mentioned by Kauṭilya; Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बार्हिण
बार्हिण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बर्हिन्-अण्] Derived from or relating to a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाल|बालं|बालः
बाल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Young, infantine, not full-grown or developed (of persons or things);<BR> बालेन स्थविरेण वा Ms. 8. 70; बालाशोकमुपोढरागसुभगं भेदोन्मुखं<BR> तिष्ठति V. 2. 7; so बालमन्दारवृक्षः Me. 77; R. 2. 45, 13. 24.<BR>—2 Newly risen, young (as the sun or its rays); बालार्कप्रतिमेवाप्सु<BR> वीचिभिन्ना पतिष्यतः R. 12. 100.<BR>—3 New, waxing (as the moon); पुपोष वृद्धिं हरिदश्वदीधितेरनुप्रवेशादिव<BR> बालचन्द्रमाः R. 3. 22; Ku. 3. 29.<BR>—4 Puerile.<BR>—5 Ignorant, unwise; अनर्थकुशला ह्येते बालाः पण्डितमानिनः Rām. 2. 100. 38.<BR>—6 Pure (as an animal fit for sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बालः|बाल|बालं
बाल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A child, an infant; बालादपि सुभाषितम् (ग्राह्यम्); Ms. 2. 239.<BR>—2 A boy, youth, young person.<BR>—3 A minor (under 16 years of age); बाल आषोडशाद्वर्षात् Nārada.<BR>—4 A colt, foal.<BR>—5 A fool, simpleton; नीरसायां रसं बालो बालिकायां विकल्पयेत् Pt. 4. 91.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A tail.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) An elephantʼs or a horseʼs tail.<BR>—7 Hair; तं केशपाशं प्रसमीक्ष्य कुर्युर्बालप्रियत्वं शिथिलं चमर्यः Ku. 1. 48.<BR>—8 An elephant five years old; ‘पञ्चवर्षो गजो बालः पोतस्तु दशवार्षिकः’<BR> Vaijayantī. According to Mātaṅga L. (5. 2.) however it means an elephant<BR> in the first year.<BR>—9 A kind of perfume.<BR>—10 The cocoa-nut.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बालाग्रम्, बालाध्यापकः, बालापत्यम्, बालाभ्यासः, बालारुण, बालार्कः, बालावबोधः, बालावबोधनम्, बालावस्थ, बालावस्था, बालातपः, बालामयः, बालेन्दुः, बालेष्टः, बालोपचारः, बालोपचरणम्, बालोपवीतम्, बालकदली, बालकाण्डम्, बालकुन्दः, बालकुन्दम्, बालकृमिः, बालकृष्णः, बालकेलिः, बालकेली, बालक्रीडनम्, बालक्रीडनकम्, बालक्रीडा, बालखिल्यः, बालगर्भिणी, बालगोपालः, बालग्रहः, बालघ्नः, बालचन्द्रः, बालचन्द्रमस्, बालचरितम्, बालचर्यः, बालचुम्बालः, बालचूतः, बालज, बालजातीय, बालतनयः, बालतन्त्रम्, बालतृणम्, बालदलकः, बालधनम्, बालधिः, बालनेत्र, बालपत्रः, बालपत्रकः, बालपाश्या, बालपुष्टिका, बालपुष्टी, बालपुष्पी, बालबोधः, बालभद्रकः, बालभारः, बालभावः, बालभृत्यः, बालभैषज्यम्, बालभोज्यः, बालमनोरमा, बालमरणम्, बालमित्रः, बालमृगः, बालमूलम्, बालमूषिका, बालमृणालः, बालयज्ञोपवीतकम्, बालराजम्, बालरोगः, बाललता, बाललीला, बालवत्सः, बालवायजम्, बालवासस्, बालवाह्यः, बालविधवा, बालवैधव्यम्, बालव्यजनम्, बालव्रतः, बालसखि, बालसंध्या, बालसात्म्यम्, बालसुहृद्, बालसूर्यह्, बालसूर्यकः, बालस्थानम्, बालहत्या, बालहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1162-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

