बिभित्सु
बिभित्सु <i>a.</i> Desirous of piercing or penetrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीतकः|बिभीतक
बिभीतकः Terminalia Bellerica (Mar. बेहडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीषक
बिभीषक <i>a.</i> Frightening, terrifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीषण|बिभीषणः
बिभीषण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Terrifying, frightening, intimidating.<BR>—2 Formidable, terrible.<BR>—3 Bullying or blustering (as language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीषणम्
बिभीषण + .{@-णम्, -णा@}<BR>—1 Terrifying.<BR>—2 A means of terrifying, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीषणा
बिभीषण + .{@-णम्, -णा@}<BR>—1 Terrifying.<BR>—2 A means of terrifying, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीषणः|बिभीषण
बिभीषण + .{@-णः@} N. of a demon and brother of Rāvaṇa. [Though a demon by<BR> birth, he was extremely sorry for the abduction of Sītā by Rāvaṇa,<BR> and severely reprimanded him for his wicked act. He several times advised<BR> Rāvaṇa to restore Sītā to Rāma if he cared to live; but the proud<BR> demon turned a deaf ear to his warnings. At last seeing that the ruin<BR> of his brother was inevitable, he repaired to Rāma and became his staunch<BR> friend. After the death of Rāvaṇa, Rāma installed him on the throne<BR> of Laṅkā. He is believed to be one of the seven Chirajīvins; see चिरजीविन्.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभीषिका
बिभीषिका<BR>—1 Threatening, terror.<BR>—2 That which threatens or scares away; यदि ते सन्ति सन्त्वेव केयमन्या<BR> बिभीषिका U. 4. 29. See विभीषिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रक्षु|बिभ्रक्षुः
बिभ्रक्षु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing to roast or fry.<BR>—2 Desirous of scorching up.<BR>—3 Wishing to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रक्षुः|बिभ्रक्षु
बिभ्रक्षु + .{@-क्षुः@} Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1166-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रज्जिषु|बिभ्रज्जिषुः
बिभ्रज्जिषु <i>a.</i> Wishing to fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिभ्रज्जिषुः|बिभ्रज्जिषु
बिभ्रज्जिषु + .{@-षुः@} Fire; रुषा बिभ्रज्जिषुप्रख्यं कपिं बाणैरवाकिरत् Bk. 9. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बः|बिम्ब|बिंब|बिंबं|बिम्बं|बिंबः
बिम्बः, -म्बम्<BR>—1 The disc of the sun or moon; वदनेन निर्जितं तव निलीयते चन्द्रबिम्बमम्बुधरे<BR> Subhāṣ.; so सूर्य˚, रवि˚ &c.<BR>—2 Any round or disc-like surface; as in नितम्बबिम्बः &c.<BR>—3 An image, shadow, reflection; बिम्बादिवोत्थितौ बिम्बौ रामदेहात्तथापरौ<BR> Rām. 1. 4. 11; प्रभवति शुचिर्बिम्बग्राहे मणिर्न मृदां चयः U. 2. 4.<BR>—4 A mirror.<BR>—5 A jar.<BR>—6 An object compared (opp. प्रतिबिम्ब to which it is compared).<BR>—7 A statue, figure, idol; हेमबिम्बनिभा सौम्या मायेव मयनिर्मिता<BR> Rām. 6. 12. 14.<BR>—8 A mould, matrix; यथा लोहस्य निःस्यन्दो निषिक्तो बिम्बविग्रहम् (उपैति) Mb. 14. 18. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बम्
बिम्बः, -म्बम्<BR>—1 The disc of the sun or moon; वदनेन निर्जितं तव निलीयते चन्द्रबिम्बमम्बुधरे<BR> Subhāṣ.; so सूर्य˚, रवि˚ &c.<BR>—2 Any round or disc-like surface; as in नितम्बबिम्बः &c.<BR>—3 An image, shadow, reflection; बिम्बादिवोत्थितौ बिम्बौ रामदेहात्तथापरौ<BR> Rām. 1. 4. 11; प्रभवति शुचिर्बिम्बग्राहे मणिर्न मृदां चयः U. 2. 4.<BR>—4 A mirror.<BR>—5 A jar.<BR>—6 An object compared (opp. प्रतिबिम्ब to which it is compared).<BR>—7 A statue, figure, idol; हेमबिम्बनिभा सौम्या मायेव मयनिर्मिता<BR> Rām. 6. 12. 14.<BR>—8 A mould, matrix; यथा लोहस्य निःस्यन्दो निषिक्तो बिम्बविग्रहम् (उपैति) Mb. 14. 18. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बः|बिम्ब|बिंब|बिंबं|बिम्बं|बिंबः
बिम्बः, -म्बम् + .{@-म्बः@} A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बम्
बिम्बः, -म्बम् + .{@-म्बम्@} The fruit of a tree (which, when ripe, is ruddy and to which<BR> the lips of young women are often compared); रक्ताशोकरुचा विशोषितगुणो<BR> बिम्बाधरालक्तकः M. 3. 5; पक्वबिम्बाधरोष्ठी Me. 84; cf. N. 2. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बिम्बौष्ठ, बिम्बफल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बौष्ठ|बिंबौष्ठ|बिम्बौष्ठः
बिम्बः + -ओष्ठ <i>a.</i> (बिम्बो(म्बौ)ष्ठ) having lips as ruddy or cherry<BR> as the Bimba fruit; दाक्षिण्यं नाम बिम्बोष्ठि बैम्बिकानां कुलव्रतम् M. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बौष्ठः|बिम्बौष्ठ|बिंबौष्ठ
बिम्बः + -ओष्ठ + .({@-ष्ठः@}) a lip like the Bimba fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बफल|बिंबफल
बिम्बः + -फल the Bimba fruit; उमामुखे बिम्बफलाधरोष्ठे Ku. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बकम्
बिम्बकम्<BR>—1 The disc of the sun or moon.<BR>—2 The Bimba fruit.<BR>—3 A round form, roundness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बटः|बिम्बट|बिंबटः
बिम्बटः The mustard plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बिका
बिम्बिका<BR>—1 The disc of the sun or moon.<BR>—2 The Bimba plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बित|बिंबित
बिम्बित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Reflected, shadowed.<BR>—2 Pictured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बिनी
बिम्बिनी The pupil of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बिसारः|बिम्बिसार
बिम्बिसारः N. of a king of Magadha, a contemporary of गौतमबुद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिम्बुः|बिम्बु
बिम्बुः The betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिरुदः|बिरुद
बिरुदः<BR>—1 A token worn on the arm or hand etc. indicating excellence; बिरुदैश्च<BR> ध्वजैरुच्चैः कोषेणापि च भूयसा Śiva B. 10. 26.<BR>—2 A panegyric; पेठुश्च प्रथितामुच्चैर्वन्दिनो बिरुदावलिम् Śiva B. 1. 82;<BR> see विरुद.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बिरुदघण्टा, बिरुदवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिरुदघण्टा
बिरुदः + -घण्टा, -वादः a proclamation; अद्वैतश्रीजयबिरुदघण्टाघणघणः<BR> Śāṅkaradigvijaya 4. 78; हनुमानिति कस्यचित् कपेरुपरि लोकस्य बिरुदवादबहुमानः<BR> Saugandhikā-haraṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिरुदवादः
बिरुदः + -घण्टा, -वादः a proclamation; अद्वैतश्रीजयबिरुदघण्टाघणघणः<BR> Śāṅkaradigvijaya 4. 78; हनुमानिति कस्यचित् कपेरुपरि लोकस्य बिरुदवादबहुमानः<BR> Saugandhikā-haraṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्
बिल् €6 P., €10 U. (बिलति, बेलयति-ते) To split, cleave, break, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलम्
बिलम् —1 A hole, cavity, burrow; खनन्नाखुबिलं सिंहः … प्राप्नोति<BR> नखभङ्गं हि Pt. 3. 17; R. 12. 5; Ms. 10. 49.<BR>—2 A gap, pit, chasm.<BR>—3 An aperture, opening, outlet.<BR>—4 A cave, hollow.<BR>—5 The hollow of a dish.<BR>—6 The vagina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलः|बिल|बिलं
बिलम् + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 N. of उच्चैःश्रवस्, the horse of Indra.<BR>—2 A sort of cane.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बिलायनम्, बिलौकस्, बिलकारिन्, बिलयोनि, बिलवासः, बिलवासिन्, बिलशायिन्, बिलस्वर्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलायनम्
बिलम् + -अयनम् a subterranean cave or cavern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलौकस्
बिलम् + -ओकस् <i>m.</i> any animal that lives in holes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलकारिन्
बिलम् + -कारिन् <i>m.</i> a mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलयोनि
बिलम् + -योनि <i>a.</i> of the breed of उच्चैःश्रवस्; यत्राश्वा बिलयोनयः Ku. 6. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलवासः|बिलवास
बिलम् + -वासः a pole-cat.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-2" target="_blank">Page1167-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिलवासिन्
