बिलेशयः|बिलेशय
बिलेशयः<BR>—1 A snake; बिलेशयाधीशशरीरशायिनः Viṣṇumahimna 34; Abh. Cin. 1303.<BR>—2 A mouse, rat; यत्र दन्दशूकाः पञ्चमुखाः सप्तमुखा उपसृत्य ग्रसन्ति<BR> यथा बिलेशयान् Bhāg. 5. 26. 33.<BR>—3 Any animal living in burrows.<BR>—4 A hare; बिलेशया वातहरा मधुरा रसपाकयोः Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्मम्
बिल्मम् Ved.<BR>—1 A (broken) helmet.<BR>—2 A slip, bit, chip; सं सानु मार्ज्मि दिधिषामि बिल्मैः Rv. 2. 35. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बिल्मग्रहणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्मग्रहणम्
बिल्मम् + -ग्रहणम् understanding by degrees; Nir. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्लम्
बिल्लम्<BR>—1 A pit.<BR>—2 Particularly, a basin for water round the foot of a tree (आलवाल).<BR>—3 The plant Asa Foetida.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बिल्लसूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्लसूः
बिल्लम् + -सूः a mother of ten children; बिल्लसूर्दशपुत्रा स्यात् Śabdaratnākara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1167-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्वः|बिल्व|बिल्वं
