बुद् €1 U. (बोदति-ते) See बुन्द्.<BR>—1 To perceive, see, apprehend, discern.<BR>—2 To understand, know.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्बुदः|बुद्बुद
बुद्बुदः<BR>—1 A bubble; सततं जातविनष्टाः पयसामिव बुद्बुदाः पयसि Pt. 5. 7.<BR>—2 A type of anything very transitory. —3 Embryo five days old; कललं<BR> त्वेकरात्रेण पञ्चरात्रेण बुद्बुदम् Bhāg. 3. 31. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुध्
बुध् €1 U., €4 Ā. (बोधति-ते, बुध्यते, बुद्ध)<BR>—1 To know, understand, comprehend; क्रमादमुं नारद इत्यबोधि सः<BR> Śi. 1. 3, 9. 24; नाबुद्ध कल्पद्रुमतां विहाय जातं तमात्मन्यसिपत्रवृक्षम्<BR> R. 14. 48; यदि बुध्यते हरिशिशुः स्तनंधयः Bv. 1. 53.<BR>—2 To perceive, notice, recognise, mark; हिरण्मयं हंसमबोधि नैषधः<BR> N. 1. 117; अपि लङ्घितमध्वानं वुवुधे न बुधोपमः R. 1. 47, 12. 39.<BR>—3 To deem, regard, consider, esteem &c.<BR>—4 To heed, attend to.<BR>—5 To think, reflect.<BR>—6 To wake up, awake, rise from sleep; दददपि गिरमन्तर्बुध्यते नो<BR> मनुष्यः Śi. 11. 4; ते च प्रापुरुदन्वन्तं बुबुधे चादिपूरुषः R. 10. 6.<BR>—7 To regain consciousness, to come to oneʼs senses; शनैरबोधि सुग्रीवः<BR> सोऽलुञ्चीत्कर्णनासिकम् Bk. 15. 57.<BR>—8 To advise, admonish. ━<i>Caus.</i> (बोधयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to know, make known, inform, acquaint with.<BR>—2 To teach, communicate, impart.<BR>—3 To advise, admonish; बोधयन्तं हिताहितम् Bk. 8. 82;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">Page1169-2</a>]<BR> मच्चित्ता मद्गतप्राणा बोधयन्तः परस्परम् Bg. 10. 9.<BR>—4 To revive, restore to life, bring to senses or consciousness.<BR>—5 To remind, put in mind of; स्मरिष्यति त्वां न स बोधितोऽपि सन् Ś. 4. 1.<BR>—6 To wake up, rouse, excite (fig.); अकाले बोधितो भ्रात्रा R. 12. 81, 5. 75.<BR>—7 To revive the scent (of a perfume).<BR>—8 To cause to expand, open; मधुरया मधुबोधितमाधवी Śi. 6. 20;<BR> सविता बोधयति पङ्कजान्येव Ś. 5. 28.<BR>—9 To signify, convey, indicate. ━<i>Desid.</i> (बुबु(बो)धिषति-ते,<BR> बुभुत्सते) To wish to know &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध|बुद्धः
बुद्ध <i>p. p.</i> [बुध्-क्त]<BR>—1 Known, understood, perceived.<BR>—2 Awakened, awake.<BR>—3 Observed.<BR>—4 Enlightened, wise; एवमेव मनुष्येन्द्र धर्मं त्यक्त्वाल्पकं नरः ।<BR> बृहन्तं धर्ममाप्नोति स बुद्ध इति निश्चितम् ॥ Mb. 3. 33. 67; (see वुध्).<BR>—5 Expanded (विकसित); सरःसु बुद्धाम्बुजभूषणेषु विक्षोभ्य विक्षोभ्य<BR> जलं पिबन्ति Rām. 4. 30. 41, 5. 14. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धः|बुद्ध
बुद्ध + .{@-द्धः@}<BR>—1 A wise or learned man, a sage.<BR>—2 (With Buddhists) A wise or enlightened person who, by perfect knowledge<BR> of the truth, is absolved from all existence, and who reveals to the world<BR> the method of obtaining the Nirvāṇa or final emancipation before obtaining it himself;<BR>—3 ‘The enlightened’, N. of Śākyasimha, the celebrated founder of the<BR> Bauddha religion; (he is said to have been born at Kapilavastu and to<BR> have died in 543 B. C.; he is sometimes regarded as the ninth incarnation<BR> of Viṣṇu; thus Jayadeva says:− निन्दसि यज्ञविधेरहह श्रुतिजातं<BR> सदयहृदय दर्शितपशुघातं केशव धृतबुद्धशरीर जय जगदीश हरे<BR> Gīt. 1); क्वचिद्बुद्धः कल्किर्विहरसि कुभारापहतये Viṣṇumahimna 4;<BR> ततः कलौ संप्रवृत्ते संमोहाय सुरद्विषाम् । बुद्धो नाम्नाञ्जनसुतः<BR> कीकटेषु भविष्यति Bhāg.<BR>—4 The Supreme Soul (परमात्मा); अथ बुद्धमथाबुद्धमिमं गुणविधिं<BR> शृणु Mb. 12. 308. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धम्
बुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} Knowledge.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बुद्धान्तः, बुद्धागमः, बुद्धोपासकः, बुद्धगया, बुद्धगुरुः, बुद्धमार्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धान्तः|बुद्धान्त
बुद्ध + -अन्तः waking condition, the being awake; स वा एष एतस्मिन्<BR> बुद्धान्ते रत्वा Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धागमः|बुद्धागम
बुद्ध + -आगमः the doctrines and tenets of the Bauddha religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धोपासकः|बुद्धोपासक
बुद्ध + -उपासकः a worshipper of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धगया
बुद्ध + -गया N. of a sacred place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धगुरुः|बुद्धगुरु
बुद्ध + -गुरुः a Buddhist spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धमार्गः|बुद्धमार्ग
बुद्ध + -मार्गः the doctrines and tenets of Buddha, Buddhism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिः|बुद्धि
बुद्धिः <i>f.</i> [बुध्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Perception, comprehension.<BR>—2 Intellect, understanding, intelligence, talent; तीक्ष्णा नारुंतुदा<BR> बुद्धिः Śi. 2. 109; शास्त्रेष्वकुण्ठिता बुद्धिः R. 1. 19.<BR>—3 Information, knowledge; बुद्धिर्यस्य बलं तस्य H. 2. 122 ‘knowledge is power’<BR>; P. I. 4. 52.<BR>—4 Discrimination, judgment, discernment; विदेशेष्वपि विज्ञाताः सर्वतो<BR> बुद्धिनिश्चयाः Rām. 1. 7. 17.<BR>—5 Mind; मूढः परप्रत्ययनेयबुद्धिः M. 1. 2; so कृपण˚, पाप˚ &c.<BR>—6 Presence of mind, readiness of wit.<BR>—7 An impression, opinion, belief, idea, feeling; दूरात्तमवलोक्य व्याघ्रबुद्धया<BR> पलायन्ते H. 3; अनया बुद्धया Mu. 1 ‘in this belief’; अनुक्रोशबुद्धपा Me. 117.<BR>—8 Intention, purpose, design; मन्दीचकार मरणव्यवसायबुद्धिम् Ku. 4. 45.<BR> (बुद्ध्या ‘intentionally’, ‘purposely’, ‘deliberately’).<BR>—9 Returning to consciousness, recovery from a swoon; Māl. 4. 10.<BR>—10 (In Sāṅ. phil.) Intellect, the second of the 25 elements of the<BR> Sāṅkhyas; एषा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">Page1170-1</a>]<BR> तेऽभिहिता सांख्ये बुद्धिर्योगे त्विमां शृणु Bg. 2. 39.<BR>—11 Nature (प्रकृति); Bhāg. 3. 27. 18.<BR>—12 A means, way (उपाय); किं करिष्याम भद्रं ते बुद्धिरत्र विचार्यताम्<BR> Rām. 1. 40. 9.<BR>—13 N. of the 5th astrological mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बुद्ध्यतीत, बुद्ध्यधिक, बुद्ध्यवज्ञानम्, बुद्धीन्द्रियम्, बुद्धिकृत्, बुद्धिकृत, बुद्धिगम्य, बुद्धिग्राह्य, बुद्धिचिन्तक, बुद्धिच्छाया, बुद्धिजन्मन्, बुद्धिजीविन्, बुद्धितत्त्वम्, बुद्धिद्यूतम्, बुद्धिपूर्व, बुद्धिपूर्वम्, बुद्धिपूर्वकम्, बुद्धिपुरःसरम्, बुद्धिप्रागल्भी, बुद्धिबलम्, बुद्धिभेदः, बुद्धिभ्रमः, बुद्धिमोहः, बुद्धियुक्त, बुद्धियोगः, बुद्धिलक्षणम्, बुद्धिलाघवम्, बुद्धिवर्जित, बुद्धिविध्वंसक, बुद्धिविलासः, बुद्धिविषयः, बुद्धिवृद्धिः, बुद्धिवैभवम्, बुद्धिशक्तिः, बुद्धिशस्त्र, बुद्धिशालिन्, बुद्धिसंपन्न, बुद्धिशुद्ध, बुद्धिसंकीर्णम्, बुद्धिसखः, बुद्धिसहायः, बुद्धिहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1169-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यतीत
बुद्धिः + -अतीत <i>a.</i> beyond the range or reach of the intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यधिक
बुद्धिः + -अधिक <i>a.</i> superior in intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्ध्यवज्ञानम्
बुद्धिः + -अवज्ञानम् contempt or low opinion for oneʼs understanding; अप्राप्तकालं<BR> वचनं बृहस्पतिरपि ब्रुवन् । प्राप्नोति बुद्ध्यवज्ञानमपमानं च पुष्कलम् ॥<BR> Pt. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धीन्द्रियम्
बुद्धिः + -इन्द्रियम् an organ of perception (opp. कर्मेन्द्रिय); (these<BR> are five:− the ear, skin, eye, tongue, and nose; श्रोत्रं त्वक् चक्षुषी<BR> जिह्वा नासिका चैव पञ्चमी; to these sometimes मनस् is added).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिकृत्
बुद्धिः + -कृत् <i>a.</i> supposing, conjecturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिकृत
बुद्धिः + -कृत <i>a.</i> acted wisely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिगम्य
बुद्धिः + -गम्य, -ग्राह्य <i>a.</i> within the reach of, or attainable to,<BR> intellect, intelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिग्राह्य
बुद्धिः + -गम्य, -ग्राह्य <i>a.</i> within the reach of, or attainable to,<BR> intellect, intelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिचिन्तक
बुद्धिः + -चिन्तक <i>a.</i> one who thinks wisely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिच्छाया
बुद्धिः + -च्छाया reflex action of the understanding on the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिजन्मन्
बुद्धिः + -जन्मन् a perception that arises; सत्संप्रयोगे पुरुषस्येन्द्रियाणां<BR> बुद्धिजन्म तत् प्रत्यक्षम् MS. 1. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिजीविन्
बुद्धिः + -जीविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 employing the reason, rational.<BR>—2 Subsisting by intelligence; भूतानां प्राणिनः श्रेष्ठाः प्राणिनां बुद्धिजीविनः Ms. 1. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धितत्त्वम्
बुद्धिः + -तत्त्वम् the second element of the Sāṅkhya philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिद्यूतम्
बुद्धिः + -द्यूतम् game at chess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्व
बुद्धिः + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> purposed, intentional, wanton, wilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्वम्
बुद्धिः + -पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम्, -पुरःसरम् <i>ind.</i> intentionally, purposely, wilfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपूर्वकम्
बुद्धिः + -पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम्, -पुरःसरम् <i>ind.</i> intentionally, purposely, wilfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिपुरःसरम्
बुद्धिः + -पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम्, -पुरःसरम् <i>ind.</i> intentionally, purposely, wilfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिप्रागल्भी
बुद्धिः + -प्रागल्भी soundness of judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिबलम्
बुद्धिः + -बलम् a kind of play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिभेदः|बुद्धिभेद
बुद्धिः + -भेदः, -भ्रमः distraction or aberration of mind; न बुद्धिभेदं<BR> जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम् Bg. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिभ्रमः|बुद्धिभ्रम
बुद्धिः + -भेदः, -भ्रमः distraction or aberration of mind; न बुद्धिभेदं<BR> जनयेदज्ञानां कर्मसङ्गिनाम् Bg. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धिमोहः|बुद्धिमोह
बुद्धिः + -मोहः confusion of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1170-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुद्धियुक्त
