बुषम्
बुसम् (-षम्)<BR>—1 Chaff.<BR>—2 Rubbish, refuse.<BR>—3 Dry cowdung.<BR>—4 Wealth.<BR>—5 The thick part of sour curds.<BR>—6 Water (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुसा
बुसम् (-षम्) + .{@-सा@} (In drama) A young sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्त्
बुस्त् €10 U. (बुस्तयति-ते)<BR>—1 To honour, respect.<BR>—2 To disrespect, treat with disrespect or contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बुस्तम्
बुस्तम्<BR>—1 The burnt crust of roast meat.<BR>—2 The shell of fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1171-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

