बृहतिका
बृहतिका An upper garment, a mantle, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पतिः|बृहस्पति
बृहस्पतिः [बृहतः वाचः पतिः पारस्करादि˚]<BR>—1 N. of the preceptor of the gods; सन्त्यन्येऽपि बृहस्पतिप्रभृतयः<BR> संभाविताः पञ्चषाः Bh. 1. 34; (for the abduction of his wife Tārā<BR> by the moon, see under तारा and सोम).<BR>—2 The planet Jupiter; बुधबृहस्पतियोगदृश्यः R. 18. 76.<BR>—3 N. of the author of a Smṛti; Y. 1. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बृहस्पतिचक्रम्, बृहस्पतिपुरोहितः, बृहस्पतिवारः, बृहस्पतिवासरः, बृहस्पतिसवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पतिचक्रम्
बृहस्पतिः + -चक्रम्<BR>—1 a period of sixty saṃvatsaras.<BR>—2 an astrological diagram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पतिपुरोहितः|बृहस्पतिपुरोहित
बृहस्पतिः + -पुरोहितः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पतिवारः|बृहस्पतिवार
बृहस्पतिः + -वारः, -वासरः Thursday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पतिवासरः|बृहस्पतिवासर
बृहस्पतिः + -वारः, -वासरः Thursday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बृहस्पतिसवः|बृहस्पतिसव
बृहस्पतिः + -सवः N. of a sacrifice offered to Bṛhaspati; बृहस्पतिसवं<BR> नाम समारेभे क्रतूत्तमम् Bhāg. 4. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बेकनाटः|बेकनाट
बेकनाटः Ved. A usurer (कुसीदिन्); इन्द्रो विश्वान् बेकनाटाँ अहर्दृशः Rv. 8. 66. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बेटी
बेटी A courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बेडा
बेडा A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बेह्
बेह् €1 Ā. (बेहते) To endeavour, strive, attempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैजिक|बैजिकं|बैजिकः
बैजिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बीजेन निर्वृत्तं ठक्]<BR>—1 Seminal; बैजिकं गार्भिकं चैनो द्विजानामपमृज्यते Ms. 2. 27.<BR>—2 Original.<BR>—3 Relating to conception.<BR>—4 Relating to sexual union; बैजिकादभिसंबन्धादनुरुन्ध्यादघं त्र्यहम् Ms. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैजिकः|बैजिक|बैजिकं
बैजिक + .{@-कः@} A sprout, young shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैजिकम्
बैजिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Cause, source, origin.<BR>—2 The spiritual cause of existence, soul, spirit.<BR>—3 Oil of the शिग्रु plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैडाल
बैडाल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बिडालस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a cat.<BR>—2 Peculiar to cats.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बैडालव्रतम्, बैडालव्रतिः, बैडालव्रतिकः, बैडालव्रतिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैडालव्रतम्
बैडाल + -व्रतम् ‘a cat-like observance’, concealing oneʼs malice or evil<BR> designs under the garb of piety or virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैडालव्रतिः|बैडालव्रति
बैडाल + -व्रतिः one who leads a chaste life simply from want of female<BR> company (and not because he has controlled his senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैडालव्रतिकः|बैडालव्रतिक
बैडाल + -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> a religious hypocrite, an impostor;<BR> बैडालव्रतिकाञ्छठान् … वाङ्मात्रेणापि नार्चयेत् Ms. 4. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैडालव्रतिन्
बैडाल + -व्रतिकः, -व्रतिन् <i>m.</i> a religious hypocrite, an impostor;<BR> बैडालव्रतिकाञ्छठान् … वाङ्मात्रेणापि नार्चयेत् Ms. 4. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैदल
बैदल See वैदल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैम्बिकः|बैम्बिक|बैंबिक|बैंबिकः
बैम्बिकः A man who is assiduous in his attentions to ladies, a gallant,<BR> lover; दाक्षिण्यं नाम बिम्बोष्ठि बैम्बिकानां कुलव्रतम् M. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैल
बैल <i>a.</i> Living in holes (as a mouse); relating to animals in<BR> holes; और्णान् बैलान … … काम्बोजः प्रददौ बहून् Mb. 1. 51. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैल्व
बैल्व <i>a.</i> (-ल्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बिल्वस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to or made of the Bilva tree or its wood; ततो यूपोच्छ्रये<BR> प्राप्ते षड् बैल्वान् भरतर्षभ Mb. 14. 88. 27.<BR>—2 Covered with Bilva trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैल्वम्
बैल्व + .{@-ल्वम्@} The fruit of the Bilva tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बैष्कम्
बैष्कम् Flesh of an hunted animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोक्काणः|बोक्काण
बोक्काणः A horseʼs nose-bag (which contains his food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध|बोधः
बोध <i>a.</i> Knowing, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधः|बोध
बोध + .{@-धः@} [बुध्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Perception, knowledge, apprehension, observation, conception; बालानां<BR> सुखबोधाय T. S.<BR>—2 Idea, thought.<BR>—3 Understanding, intellect, intelligence, wisdom.<BR>—4 Waking up, becoming awake, a waking state, consciousness.<BR>—5 Opening, blooming, expanding.<BR>—6 Instruction, advice, admonition.<BR>—7 Awakening, rousing.<BR>—8 An epithet, designation.<BR>—9 N. of a district.<BR>—10 Exciting (a perfume).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बोधातीत, बोधकर, बोधगम्य, बोधपूर्व, बोधपूर्वम्, बोधवासरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधातीत
बोध + -अतीत <i>a.</i> unknowable, incomprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधकर|बोधकरः
बोध + -कर <i>a.</i> one who teaches or informs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधकरः|बोधकर
बोध + -कर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a bard or minstrel who wakes up his master by singing appropriate songs<BR> in the morning.<BR>—2 an instructor, a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधगम्य
बोध + -गम्य <i>a.</i> intelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधपूर्व
बोध + -पूर्व <i>a.</i> intentional, conscious; cf. अबोधपूर्व Ś. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधपूर्वम्
बोध + -पूर्वम् <i>ind.</i> knowingly, consciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधवासरः|बोधवासर
बोध + -वासरः the eleventh day in the bright half of Kārtika when<BR> Viṣṇu is supposed to rise from his four monthsʼ sleep; see Me. 112, and प्रबोधिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधक|बोधकः
बोधक <i>a.</i> (-धिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बुध्-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Informing, apprising.<BR>—2 Instructing, teaching.<BR>—3 Indicative of.<BR>—4 Awakening, rousing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधकः|बोधक
बोधक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A spy.<BR>—2 A teacher, instructor.<BR>—3 A minstrel, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधतस्
बोधतस् <i>ind.</i> Through wisdom or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधन|बोधनं|बोधनः
बोधन <i>a.</i> [बुध्-णिच् ल्यु-ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Informing, acquainting.<BR>—2 Explaining, indicating.<BR>—3 Arousing, waking.<BR>—4 Kindling, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधनः|बोधन|बोधनं
बोधन + .{@-नः@} The planet Mercury (बुधः); बुध इव शिशिरांशोर्बोधनस्येव<BR> देवः V. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधनम्
बोधन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Informing, teaching, instruction, giving a knowledge of; भयरुषोश्च<BR> तदिङ्गितबोधनम् R. 9. 49.<BR>—2 Denoting, signifying.<BR>—3 Arousing, awakening; समयेन तेन चिरसुप्तमनोभवबोधनं सममबोधिषत Śi. 9. 24.<BR>—4 Observing, perceiving.<BR>—5 Waking, being awake.<BR>—6 Making attentive.<BR>—7 Burning incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधनी
बोधन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 The eleventh day in the bright half of Kārtika when Viṣṇu rises<BR> from his four monthsʼ sleep; शयनीबोधनीमध्ये या कृष्णैकादशी भवेत् ।<BR> सैवोपोष्या गृहस्थेन नान्या कृष्णा कदाचन Tithyādi.<BR>—2 Long pepper.<BR>—3 Understanding, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधनीय|बोधनीयः
बोधनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be admonished.<BR>—2 To be known or understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधयितृ
बोधयितृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A teacher, preceptor.<BR>—2 A waker; श्वानं वस्तो बोधयितारमब्रवीत् Rv. 1. 161. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधान|बोधानः
बोधान <i>a.</i> [बुध्-आनच्] Wise, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधानः|बोधान
बोधान + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A wise man.<BR>—2 An epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधायनः|बोधायन
बोधायनः N. of a teacher and author of ब्रह्मसूत्रवृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिः|बोधि
बोधिः [बुध्-इन्]<BR>—1 Perfect wisdom or enlightenment; इत्यभिहितो बोधौ जिनः पातु वः<BR> Nāg. 1. 1. स रतिमुपसिषेवे बोधिमापन्न यावत् Bu. C. 2. 56.<BR>—2 The enlightened intellect of a Buddha.<BR>—3 The sacred fig-tree.<BR>—4 A cock.<BR>—5 An epithet of Buddha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बोध्यङ्गम्, बोधितरुः, बोधिद्रुमः, बोधिवृक्षः, बोधिदः, बोधिमण्डलम्, बोधिसत्त्वः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध्यङ्गम्
बोधिः + -अङ्गम् a requisite<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">Page1173-1</a>]<BR> for attaining perfect knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1172-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधितरुः|बोधितरु
बोधिः + -तरुः, -द्रुमः, -वृक्षः the sacred fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिद्रुमः|बोधिद्रुम
बोधिः + -तरुः, -द्रुमः, -वृक्षः the sacred fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिवृक्षः|बोधिवृक्ष
बोधिः + -तरुः, -द्रुमः, -वृक्षः the sacred fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिदः|बोधिद
बोधिः + -दः an <i>arhat</i> (of the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिमण्डलम्
बोधिः + -मण्डलम् N. of the place where Gautama Buddha attained to perfect wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिसत्त्वः|बोधिसत्त्व|बोधिसत्त्वं
बोधिः + -सत्त्वः<BR>—1 a Buddhist saint, one who is on the way to the attainment of perfect<BR> knowledge and has only a certain number of births to undergo before attaining<BR> to the state of a Supreme Buddha and complete annihilation (this position<BR> could be attained by a long series of pious and virtuous deeds); एवंविधैर्विलसितैरतिबोधिसत्त्वैः<BR> Māl. 10. 21; उद्योतयन्नुत्तमबोधिसत्त्वः Bu. C. 1. 16.<BR>—2 N. of the principal Buddha of the present era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधित|बोधितं
बोधित <i>p. p.</i> [बुध्-णिच् क्त]<BR>—1 Made known, informed, apprised.<BR>—2 Reminded.<BR>—3 Advised, instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोधिन्
बोधिन् <i>a.</i> [बुध्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Knowing, familiar with.<BR>—2 Acquainting, informing, making known.<BR>—3 Teaching, explaining.<BR>—4 Arousing, awakening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोध्य
बोध्य, बोद्धव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be known or understood; उत्थायोत्थाय बोद्धव्यं महद्भयमुपस्थितम् H.<BR>—2 Intelligible, perceivable.<BR>—3 To be informed, instructed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बोद्धव्य
बोध्य, बोद्धव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be known or understood; उत्थायोत्थाय बोद्धव्यं महद्भयमुपस्थितम् H.<BR>—2 Intelligible, perceivable.<BR>—3 To be informed, instructed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्ध|बौद्धं|बौद्धः
बौद्ध <i>a.</i> (-द्धी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [बुद्ध-द्धि अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to <i>Buddhi</i> or understanding; mental.<BR>—2 Relating to Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्धः|बौद्ध|बौद्धं
बौद्ध + .{@-द्धः@} A follower of the religion taught by Buddha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: बौद्धदर्शनम्, बौद्धमतम्, बौद्धशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्धदर्शनम्
बौद्ध + -दर्शनम्, -मतम्, -शास्त्रम् Buddhist doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्धमतम्
बौद्ध + -दर्शनम्, -मतम्, -शास्त्रम् Buddhist doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौद्धशास्त्रम्
बौद्ध + -दर्शनम्, -मतम्, -शास्त्रम् Buddhist doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौधः|बौध
बौधः [बुध्-अण्] ‘Buddhaʼs son’, an epithet of Purūravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बौधायनः|बौधायन
बौधायनः Patronymic name of an ancient writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्नः|ब्रध्न
ब्रध्नः<BR>—1 The sun; अथ पुत्रस्य पौत्रेण ब्रध्नस्याप्नोति विष्टपम् Ms. 9. 137, 4. 231.<BR>—2 The root of a tree.<BR>—3 A day.<BR>—4 The <i>arka</i> plant.<BR>—5 Lead (<i>m.</i> ?).<BR>—6 A horse.<BR>—7 An epithet of Śiva or Brahmā.<BR>—8 The point of an arrow.<BR>—9 N. of a disease; अभ्यभिष्यन्दिगुर्वामसेवनान्निचयं गतः । करोति<BR> ग्रन्थिवच्छोथं दोषो वङ्क्षणसन्धिषु । ज्वरशूलाङ्गसादाद्यं तं ब्रध्नमिति<BR> निर्दिशेत् । Mādh. N.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्रध्नचक्रम्, ब्रध्नबिम्बम्, ब्रध्नमण्डलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्नचक्रम्
ब्रध्नः + -चक्रम् the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्नबिम्बम्
ब्रध्नः + -बिम्बम्, -मण्डलम् the disc of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रध्नमण्डलम्
ब्रध्नः + -बिम्बम्, -मण्डलम् the disc of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मन्
ब्रह्मन् <i>n.</i> [बृंह्-मनिन् नकारस्याकारे ऋतो रत्वम्; cf. Uṇ. 4. 145.]<BR>—1 The Supreme Being, regarded as impersonal and divested of all<BR> quality and action; (according to the Vedāntins, Brahman is both the<BR> efficient and the material cause of the visible universe, the all-pervading<BR> soul and spirit of the universe, the essence from which all created things<BR> are produced and into which they are absorbed; अस्ति तावन्नित्यशुद्धबुद्धमुक्तस्वभावं<BR> सर्वज्ञं सर्वशक्तिसमन्वितं ब्रह्म Ś. B.); … यत्प्रयन्त्यभिसंविशन्ति ।<BR> तद् विजिज्ञासस्व । तद् ब्रह्मेति T. Up. 3. 1; समीभूता दृष्टिस्त्रिभुवनमपि<BR> ब्रह्म मनुते Bh. 3. 84; Ku. 3. 15; दर्शनं तस्य लाभः स्यात् त्वं<BR> हि ब्रह्ममयो निधिः Mb.<BR>—2 A hymn of praise.<BR>—3 A sacred text; मैवं स्याद् ब्रह्मविक्रिया Bhāg. 9. 1. 17.<BR>—4 The Vedas; ब्रह्मणः प्रणवं कुर्यात् Ms. 2. 74; यद् ब्रह्म सम्यगाम्नातम्<BR> Ku. 6. 16; U. 1. 15;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1173-2" target="_blank">Page1173-2</a>]<BR> समस्तवदनोद्गीतब्रह्मणे ब्रह्मणे नमः Bm. 1. 1; Bg. 3. 15.<BR>—5 The sacred and mystic syllable <i>om</i>; एकाक्षरं परं ब्रह्म Ms. 2. 83.<BR>—6 The priestly or Brahmanical class (collectively); तदेतद् ब्रह्म<BR> क्षत्रं विट् शूद्रः Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 15; ब्रह्मैव संनियन्तृ स्यात् क्षत्रं<BR> हि ब्रह्मसंभवम् Ms. 9. 320.<BR>—7 The power or energy of a Brāhmaṇa; पवनाग्निसमागमो ह्ययं सहितं<BR> ब्रह्म यदस्त्रतेजसा R. 8. 4.<BR>—8 Religious penance or austerities.<BR>—9 Celibacy, chastity; शाश्वते ब्रह्मणि वर्तते Ś. 1.<BR>—10 Final emancipation or beatitude.<BR>—11 Theology, sacred learning, religious knowledge.<BR>—12 The Brāhmaṇa portion of the Veda.<BR>—13 Wealth.<BR>—14 Food.<BR>—15 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—16 Truth.<BR>—17 The Brāhmaṇahood (ब्राह्मणत्व); येन विप्लावितं ब्रह्म वृषल्यां<BR> जायतात्मना Bhāg. 6. 2. 26.<BR>—18 The soul (आत्मा); एतदेषां ब्रह्म Bṛ. Up. 1. 6. 1-3.<BR>—19 See ब्रह्मास्त्र. अब्राह्मणे न हि ब्रह्म ध्रुवं तिष्ठेत् कदाचन Mb. 12. 3. 31.<BR>—20 The गायत्री mantra; उभे सन्ध्ये च यतवाग्जपन् ब्रह्म<BR> समाहितः Bhāg. 7. 12. 2. ━<i>m.</i> —1 The Supreme Being, the Creator,<BR> the first deity of the sacred Hindu Trinity, to whom is entrusted the<BR> work of creating the world. [The accounts of the creation of the world<BR> differ in many respects; but, according to Manu Smṛti, the universe was<BR> enveloped in darkness, and the self-existent Lord manifested himself dispelling<BR> the gloom. He first created the waters and deposited in them a seed. This<BR> seed became a golden egg, in which he himself was born as Brahmā −the<BR> progenitor of all the worlds. Then the Lord divided the egg into two parts,<BR> with which he constructed heaven and earth. He then created the ten Prajāpatis<BR> or mind-born sons who completed the work of creation. According to another<BR> account (Rāmāyaṇa) Brahmā sprang from ether; from him was descended<BR> Marīci, and his son was Kaśyapa. From Kaśyapa sprang Vivasvata, and<BR> Manu sprang from him. Thus Manu was the procreator of all human beings.<BR> According to a third account, the Supreme deity, after dividing the golden<BR> egg, separated himself into two parts, male and female, from which sprang<BR> Virāj and from him Manu; cf. Ku. 2. 7 and Ms. 1. 32 <i>et seq.</i> Mythologically<BR> Brahman is represented as being born in a lotus which sprang from the<BR> navel of Viṣṇu, and as creating the world by an illicit connection with<BR> his own daughter Sarasvatī. Brahman had originally five heads, but one<BR> of them was cut down by Śiva with the ring-finger or burnt down by the<BR> fire from his third eye. His vehicle is a swan. He has numerous epithets,<BR> most of which have reference to his birth, in a lotus.]<BR>—2 A Brāhmaṇa; Ś. 4. 4.<BR>—3 A devout man.<BR>—4 One of the four <i>Ṛtvijas</i> or priests employed at a Soma sacrifice.<BR>—5 One conversant with sacred knowledge.<BR>—6 The sun.<BR>—7 Intellect.<BR>—8 An epithet of the seven Prajāpatis:− मरीचि, अत्रि, अङ्गिरस्, पुलस्त्य,<BR> पुलह, कतु and वसिष्ठ.<BR>—9 An epithet of Bṛhaspati; ब्रह्मन्नध्ययनस्य नैष समयस्तूष्णीं<BR> बहिः स्थीयताम् Hanumannāṭaka.<BR>—10 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1174-1" target="_blank">Page1174-1</a>]<BR> planet Jupiter; ब्रह्मराशिं समावृत्य लोहिताङ्गो व्यवस्थितः Mb. 3. 6. 18.<BR>—11 The world of Brahmā (ब्रह्मलोक); दमस्त्यागोऽप्रमादश्च ते त्रयो<BR> ब्रह्मणो हयाः Mb. 11. 7. 23.<BR>—10 Of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्रह्माक्षरम्, ब्रह्माङ्गभूः, ब्रह्माञ्जलिः, ब्रह्माण्डम्, ब्रह्मादिजाता, ब्रह्माद्रिजाता, ब्रह्माधिगमः, ब्रह्माधिगमनम्, ब्रह्माम्भस्, ब्रह्माभ्यासः, ब्रह्मायणः, ब्रह्मायनः, ब्रह्मारण्यम्, ब्रह्मार्पणम्, ब्रह्मास्त्रम्, ब्रह्मात्मभूः, ब्रह्मानन्दः, ब्रह्मारम्भः, ब्रह्मावर्तः, ब्रह्माश्रमः, ब्रह्मासनम्, ब्रह्माहुतिः, ब्रह्मोज्झता, ब्रह्मोत्तर, ब्रह्मोद्यम्, ब्रह्मोपदेशः, ब्रह्मर्षिः, ब्रह्मौदनः, ब्रह्मौदनम्, ब्रह्मकन्यका, ब्रह्मकरः, ब्रह्मकर्मन्, ब्रह्मकला, ब्रह्मकल्पः, ब्रह्मकाण्डम्, ब्रह्मकाष्ठः, ब्रह्मकिल्बिषम्, ब्रह्मकूटः, ब्रह्मकूर्चम्, ब्रह्मकृत्, ब्रह्मकोशः, ब्रह्मगायत्री, ब्रह्मगिरिः, ब्रह्मगीता, ब्रह्मगुप्तः, ब्रह्मगोलः, ब्रह्मगौरवम्, ब्रह्मग्रन्थिः, ब्रह्मग्रहः, ब्रह्मपिशाचः, ब्रह्मपुरुषः, ब्रह्मरक्षस्, ब्रह्मग्राहिन्, ब्रह्मघातकः, ब्रह्मघातिन्, ब्रह्मघातिनी, ब्रह्मघोषः, ब्रह्मघ्नः, ब्रह्मचक्रम्, ब्रह्मचर्यम्, ब्रह्मचारिकम्, ब्रह्मचारिन्, ब्रह्मचारिणी, ब्रह्मजः, ब्रह्मजन्मन्, ब्रह्मजारः, ब्रह्मजिज्ञासा, ब्रह्मजीविन्, ब्रह्मज्ञानम्, ब्रह्मज्ञ, ब्रह्मज्ञानिन्, ब्रह्मज्ञानम्, ब्रह्मज्येष्ठः, ब्रह्मज्योतिस्, ब्रह्मतत्त्वम्, ब्रह्मतन्त्रम्, ब्रह्मतालः, ब्रह्मतेजस्, ब्रह्मदः, ब्रह्मदण्डः, ब्रह्मदर्भा, ब्रह्मदानम्, ब्रह्मदायः, ब्रह्मदायादः, ब्रह्मदारुः, ब्रह्मदिनम्, ब्रह्मदूषक, ब्रह्मदेय, ब्रह्मदैत्यः, ब्रह्मद्वारम्, ब्रह्मद्विष्, ब्रह्मद्वेषिन्, ब्रह्मद्वेषः, ब्रह्मधर, ब्रह्मनदी, ब्रह्मनाभः, ब्रह्मनिर्वाणम्, ब्रह्मनिष्ठ, ब्रह्मनीडम्, ब्रह्मपदम्, ब्रह्मपवित्रः, ब्रह्मपरिषद्, ब्रह्मपादपः, ब्रह्मपत्रः, ब्रह्मपारः, ब्रह्मपारायणम्, ब्रह्मपाशः, ब्रह्मपितृ, ब्रह्मपुत्रः, ब्रह्मपुरम्, ब्रह्मपुरम्, ब्रह्मपुरी, ब्रह्मपुराणम्, ब्रह्मपुरुषः, ब्रह्मप्रलयः, ब्रह्मप्राप्तिः, ब्रह्मबलम्, ब्र