ब्रह्मन् + -सूः<BR>—1 N. of Aniruddha.<BR>—2 N. of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूत्रम्
ब्रह्मन् + -सूत्रम्<BR>—1 the sacred thread worn by the Brāhmaṇas or the twice-born (द्विज)<BR> over the shoulder; Bhāg. 10. 39. 51.<BR>—2 the aphorisms of the Vedānta philosophy by Bādarāyaṇa; ब्रह्मसूत्रपदैश्चैव<BR> हेतुमद्भिर्विनिश्चितैः Bg. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसूत्रिन्
ब्रह्मन् + -सूत्रिन् <i>a.</i> invested with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसृज्
ब्रह्मन् + -सृज् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्तम्बः|ब्रह्मस्तम्ब
ब्रह्मन् + -स्तम्बः the world, universe; ब्रह्मस्तम्बनिकुञ्जपुञ्जितघनज्याघोषघोरं<BR> धनुः Mv. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्तेयम्
ब्रह्मन् + -स्तेयम् acquiring holy knowledge by unlawful means; स ब्रह्मस्तेयसंयुक्तो<BR> नरकं प्रतिपद्यते Ms. 2. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्थली
ब्रह्मन् + -स्थली a place for learning the Veda (पाठशाला); … … ब्रह्मस्थलीषु<BR> च । सरीसृपाणि दृश्यन्ते … Rām. 6. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्थानः|ब्रह्मस्थान
ब्रह्मन् + -स्थानः the mulberry tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्वम्
ब्रह्मन् + -स्वम् the property or possessions of a Brāhmaṇa;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">Page1177-1</a>]<BR> परस्य योषितं हृत्वा ब्रह्मस्वमपहृत्य च । अरण्ये निर्जले देशे भवति<BR> ब्रह्मराक्षसः ॥ Y. 3. 212. ˚हारिन् <i>a.</i> stealing a Brāhmaṇaʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1176-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मस्वरूप
ब्रह्मन् + -स्वरूप <i>a.</i> of the nature of the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महत्या
ब्रह्मन् + -हत्या, -वधः Brahmanicide, killing a Brāhmaṇa; ब्रह्महत्यां<BR> वा एते ध्नन्ति Trisuparṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवधः|ब्रह्मवध
ब्रह्मन् + -हत्या, -वधः Brahmanicide, killing a Brāhmaṇa; ब्रह्महत्यां<BR> वा एते ध्नन्ति Trisuparṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महन्
ब्रह्मन् + -हन् <i>a.</i> murderer of a Brāhmaṇa; ब्रह्महा द्वादश समाः<BR> कुटीं कृत्वा वने वसेत् Ms. 11. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महुतम्
ब्रह्मन् + -हुतम् one of the five daily Yajñas or sacrifices, which consists<BR> in offering the rites of hospitality to guests; cf. Ms. 3. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महृदयः|ब्रह्महृदय
ब्रह्मन् + -हृदयः, -हृदयम् N. of a star (Capella).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्महृदयम्
ब्रह्मन् + -हृदयः, -हृदयम् N. of a star (Capella).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मम्
ब्रह्मम् The Supreme Spirit, the Absolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्य|ब्रह्मण्यः
ब्रह्मण्य <i>a.</i> [ब्रह्मणे हितः]<BR>—1 Relating to Brahma.<BR>—2 Relating to Brahman or the creator.<BR>—3 Relating to the acquisition of sacred knowledge, holy, pious.<BR>—4 Fit for a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—5 Friendly or hospitable to a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्यः|ब्रह्मण्य
ब्रह्मण्य + .{@-ण्यः@}<BR>—1 One well-versed in the Veda; त्वं ब्रह्मण्यः किल परिणतश्चासि धर्मेण<BR> युक्तः Mv. 3. 26.<BR>—2 The mulberry tree.<BR>—3 The palm tree.<BR>—4 Muñja grass.<BR>—5 The planet Saturn.<BR>—6 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 Of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्या
ब्रह्मण्य + .{@-ण्या@} An epithet of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्रह्मण्यदेवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्यदेवः|ब्रह्मण्यदेव
ब्रह्मण्य + -देवः an epithet of Viṣṇu; नमो ब्रह्मण्यदेवाय गोब्राह्मणहिताय च Stotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्यता
ब्रह्मण्यता<BR>—1 Friendliness towards Brāhmaṇas.<BR>—2 Piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मण्वत्|ब्रह्मण्वन्त्
ब्रह्मण्वत् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मता
ब्रह्मता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Absorption into the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 Divine nature.<BR>—3 Godhead.<BR>—4 The state of a Brāhmaṇa, Brāhmaṇahood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मत्वम्
ब्रह्मता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Absorption into the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 Divine nature.<BR>—3 Godhead.<BR>—4 The state of a Brāhmaṇa, Brāhmaṇahood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्ममय
ब्रह्ममय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Consisting of or derived from, the Veda, belonging to the Veda or spiritual<BR> pre-eminence; ज्वलन्निव ब्रह्ममयेन तेजसा Ku. 5. 30.<BR>—2 Fit for a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्ममयम्
ब्रह्ममय + .{@-यम्@} A missile presided over by Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मवत्|ब्रह्मवन्त्
ब्रह्मवत् <i>a.</i> Possessed of spiritual knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मसात्
ब्रह्मसात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 To the state of Brahma or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 To the care of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्माणी
ब्रह्माणी<BR>—1 The wife of Brahman.<BR>—2 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—3 A kind of perfume (= रेणुका).<BR>—4 A kind of brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मिन्
ब्रह्मिन् <i>a.</i> Relating to Brahma. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मिष्ठ
ब्रह्मिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Thoroughly proficient in the Vedas, very learned<BR> or pious; इष्ट्वा स वाजपेयेन ब्रह्मिष्ठानभिभूय च Bhāg. 4. 3. 3;<BR> ब्रह्मिष्ठमाधाय निजेऽधिकारे ब्रह्मिष्ठमेव स्वतनुप्रसूतम् R. 18. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मिष्ठा
ब्रह्मिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठा@} An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मी
ब्रह्मी<BR>—1 N. of a medicinal plant.<BR>—2 A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मीभूतः|ब्रह्मीभूत
ब्रह्मीभूतः N. of Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मीयस्
ब्रह्मीयस् <i>m.</i> A pious and learned Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रह्मेशयः|ब्रह्मेशय
ब्रह्मेशयः<BR>—1 An epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>—2 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं|ब्राह्मः
ब्राह्म <i>a.</i> (-ह्मी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ब्रह्मण इदं तेन प्रोक्तं वा अण् टिलोपः]<BR>—1 Relating to Brahman or the creator, or to the Supreme Spirit; R. 13. 60;<BR> Ms. 2. 40; एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति Bg. 2. 72.<BR>—2 Brahmanical, belonging to Brāhmaṇas; ब्राह्मं रथवरं युक्तमास्थाय<BR> सुधृतव्रतः Rām. 2. 5. 4; न विशेषोऽस्ति वर्णानां सर्वं ब्राह्ममिदं<BR> जगत् Mb. 12. 188. 10.<BR>—3 Relating to sacred knowledge or study; ब्राह्मं वेदमधीयाना वेदाङ्गानि<BR> च सर्वशः Mb. 1. 156. 5.<BR>—4 Prescribed by the Vedas, Vedic; scriptural; ब्राह्मस्य जन्मनः कर्ता Ms. 2. 150.<BR>—5 Holy, sacred, divine.<BR>—6 Presided over by Brahman as a मुहूर्त (see ब्राह्ममुहूर्त), or a missile.<BR>—7 Fit for a divine state or godhead. —8 Belonging to the ब्रह्मलोक;<BR> ददर्शाप्सरसं ब्राह्मीं पञ्चचूडामनिन्दिताम् Mb. 13. 38. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मः|ब्राह्म|ब्राह्मं
ब्राह्म + .{@-ह्मः@}<BR>—1 One of the eight forms of marriage in Hindu law, in which the bride<BR> decorated with ornaments is given away to the bridegroom, without requiring<BR> any gift or present from him (this is the best of the 8 forms); ब्राह्मो<BR> विवाह आहूय दीयते शक्त्यलंकृता Y. 1. 58; Ms. 3. 21, 27.<BR>—2 N. of Nārada.<BR>—3 Quicksilver.<BR>—4 The duty or prescribed course of conduct of a king; आवृत्तानां गुरुकुलात्<BR> विप्राणां पूज्यको भवेत् । नृपाणामक्षयो ह्येष ब्राह्मो धर्मो विधीयते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मम्
ब्राह्म + .{@-ह्मम्@}<BR>—1 The part of the hand under the root of the thumb; अङ्गुष्ठमूलस्य<BR> तले ब्राह्मं तीर्थं प्रचक्षते Ms. 2. 59.<BR>—2 Holy or sacred study.<BR>—3 N. of a Purāṇa.<BR>—4 N. of the constellation Rohiṇī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्राह्माहोरात्रः, ब्राह्मदेया, ब्राह्मनिधिः, ब्राह्ममुहूर्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्माहोरात्रः|ब्राह्माहोरात्र
ब्राह्म + -अहोरात्रः a day and night of Brahman (a period of 2 Kalpas of mortals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मदेया
ब्राह्म + -देया a girl to be married according to the Brāhma form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मनिधिः
ब्राह्म + -निधिः <i>m.</i> money bestowed on the sacerdotal class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्ममुहूर्तः|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्त|ब्राह्ममुहूर्त्तः
ब्राह्म + -मुहूर्तः a particular period of the day, the early part of the<BR> day (रात्रेश्च पश्चिमे यामे मुहूर्तो ब्राह्म उच्यते); cf. ब्राह्मे मुहूर्ते<BR> किल तस्य देवी कुमारकल्पं सुषुवे कुमारम् R. 5. 36; ब्राह्मे मुहूर्ते<BR> बुध्येत Ms. 4. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं|ब्राह्मणः
ब्राह्मण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ब्रह्म वेदं शुद्धं चैतन्यं वा वेत्त्वधीते वा अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—2 Befitting a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 Given by a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—4 Relating to religious worship. —5 One who knows Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणः|ब्राह्मण|ब्राह्मणं
ब्राह्मण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A man belonging to the first of the four original castes of the Hindus,<BR> a Brāhmaṇa (born from the mouth of the <i>Puruṣa</i>); ब्राह्मणोऽस्य<BR> मुखमासीत् Rv. 10. 90. 12; Ms. 1. 31, 96; (जन्मना ब्राह्मणो ज्ञेयः<BR> संस्कारैर्द्विंज उच्यते । विद्यया याति विप्रत्वं त्रिभिः श्रोत्रिय उच्यते ॥<BR> or जात्या कुलेन वृत्तेन स्वाध्यायेन श्रुतेन च । एभिर्युक्तो हि यस्तिष्ठोन्नित्यं<BR> स द्विज उच्यते ॥).<BR>—2 A priest, theologian.<BR>—3 An epithet of Agni.<BR>—4 N. of the twenty eighth Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणम्
ब्राह्मण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 An assemblage or society of Brāhmaṇas.<BR>—2 That portion of the Veda which states rules for the employment of the<BR> hymns at the various sacrifices, their origin and detailed explanation,<BR> with sometimes lengthy illustrations in the shape of legends or stories.<BR> It is distinct from the <i>Mantra</i> portion of the Veda.<BR>—3 N. of that<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">Page1178-1</a>]<BR> class of the Vedic works which contain the Brāhmaṇa portion (regarded<BR> as Śruti or part of the revelation like the hymns themselves). Each of<BR> the four Vedas has its own Brāhmaṇa or Brāhmaṇas:− ऐतरेय or<BR> आश्वलायन and कौषीतकी or सांख्यायन belonging to the Ṛgveda;<BR> शतपथ to the Yajurveda; पञ्चविंश and षड्विंश and six<BR> more to the Sāmaveda, and गोपथ to the Atharvaveda.<BR>—4 The Soma vessel of the Brahman priest.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्राह्मणातिक्रमः, ब्राह्मणादर्शनम्, ब्राह्मणापाश्रयः, ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तिः, ब्राह्मणात्मक, ब्राह्मणघ्नः, ब्राह्मणचाण्डालः, ब्राह्मणजातम्, ब्राह्मणजातिः, ब्राह्मणजीविका, ब्राह्मणद्रव्यम्, ब्राह्मणस्वम्, ब्राह्मणनिन्दकः, ब्राह्मणप्रसंगः, ब्राह्मणप्रातिवेश्यः, ब्राह्मणप्रियः, ब्राह्मणब्रुवः, ब्राह्मणभावः, ब्राह्मणभूयिष्ठ, ब्राह्मणयष्टिका, ब्राह्मणयष्टी, ब्राह्मणवधः, ब्राह्मणवाचनम्, ब्राह्मणसंतर्पणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1177-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणातिक्रमः|ब्राह्मणातिक्रम
ब्राह्मण + -अतिक्रमः offensive or disrespectful conduct towards Brāhmaṇas,<BR> insult to Brāhmaṇas; ब्राह्मणातिक्रमत्यागो भवतामेव भूतये Mv. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणादर्शनम्
ब्राह्मण + -अदर्शनम् absence of Brahmanical instruction or guidance; वृषलत्वं<BR> गता लोके ब्राह्मणादर्शनेन च Ms. 10. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणापाश्रयः
ब्राह्मण + -अपाश्रयः seeking shelter with Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तिः|ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्ति
ब्राह्मण + -अभ्युपपत्तिः <i>f.</i> protection or preservation of, or kindness<BR> shown to, a Brāhmaṇa; ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तौ च शपथे नास्ति पातकम् Ms. 8. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणात्मक
ब्राह्मण + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> belonging to Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणघ्नः|ब्राह्मणघ्न
ब्राह्मण + -घ्नः the slayer of a Brāhmaṇa; स्त्रीबालब्राह्मणघ्नांश्च हन्याद्<BR> द्विट्सेविनस्तथा Ms. 9. 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणचाण्डालः|ब्राह्मणचाण्डाल|ब्राह्मणचांडाल
ब्राह्मण + -चाण्डालः<BR>—1 a degraded or outcast Brāhmaṇa; यथा ब्राह्मणचाण्डालः पूर्वदृष्टस्तथैव<BR> सः Ms. 9. 87.<BR>—2 the son of a Śūdra father by a Brāhmaṇa woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजातम्
ब्राह्मण + -जातम्, -जातिः <i>f.</i> the Brāhmaṇa caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजातिः|ब्राह्मणजाति
ब्राह्मण + -जातम्, -जातिः <i>f.</i> the Brāhmaṇa caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणजीविका
ब्राह्मण + -जीविका the occupation or means of livelihood prescribed for a<BR> Brāhmaṇa; अध्यापनमध्ययनं यजनं याजनं तथा । दानं प्रतिग्रहश्चैव<BR> षट्कर्माण्यग्रजन्मनः ॥ षण्णां तु कर्मणामस्य त्रीणि कर्माणि जीविका ।<BR> याजनाध्यापने चैव विशुद्धाच्च प्रतिग्रहः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणद्रव्यम्
ब्राह्मण + -द्रव्यम्, -स्वम् a Brāhmaṇaʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणस्वम्
ब्राह्मण + -द्रव्यम्, -स्वम् a Brāhmaṇaʼs property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणनिन्दकः|ब्राह्मणनिन्दक|ब्राह्मणनिंदक
ब्राह्मण + -निन्दकः a blasphemer or reviler of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणप्रसंगः|ब्राह्मणप्रसङ्ग
ब्राह्मण + -प्रसंगः the applicability of the term Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणप्रातिवेश्यः|ब्राह्मणप्रातिवेश्य
ब्राह्मण + -प्रातिवेश्यः a neighbouring Brāhmaṇa; ब्राह्मणप्रातिवेश्यानामेतदेवानिमन्त्रणे Y. 2. 263.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणप्रियः|ब्राह्मणप्रिय
ब्राह्मण + -प्रियः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणब्रुवः|ब्राह्मणब्रुव
ब्राह्मण + -ब्रुवः one who pretends to be a Brāhmaṇa, one who is a Brāhmaṇa<BR> only in name and neglects the duties of his caste; बहवो ब्राह्मणब्रुवा<BR> निवसन्ति Dk.; सममब्राह्मणे दानं द्विगुणं ब्राह्मणब्रुवे Ms. 7. 85, 8. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणभावः|ब्राह्मणभाव
ब्राह्मण + -भावः the rank or condition of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणभूयिष्ठ
ब्राह्मण + -भूयिष्ठ <i>a.</i> consisting for the most part of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणयष्टिका
ब्राह्मण + -यष्टिका, -यष्टी Clerodendrum Siphonantus (Mar. भारंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणयष्टी
ब्राह्मण + -यष्टिका, -यष्टी Clerodendrum Siphonantus (Mar. भारंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणवधः|ब्राह्मणवध
ब्राह्मण + -वधः the murder of a Brāhmaṇa, Brahmanicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणवाचनम्
ब्राह्मण + -वाचनम् the recitation of benedictions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणसंतर्पणम्
ब्राह्मण + -संतर्पणम् feeding or satisfying Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणकः|ब्राह्मणक
ब्राह्मणकः<BR>—1 A bad or unworthy Brāhmaṇa (only in name); एवं युक्तो ब्राह्मणः<BR> स्यादन्यो ब्राह्मणको भवेत् Mb. 12. 270. 27.<BR>—2 A family of such a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 N. of a country inhabited by warlike Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणता
ब्राह्मणता, -त्वम्<BR> The state or rank of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणत्वम्
ब्राह्मणता, -त्वम्<BR> The state or rank of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणत्रा
ब्राह्मणत्रा <i>ind.</i> Among Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणसात्
ब्राह्मणसात् <i>ind.</i> In the possession of Brāhmaṇas, as in ब्राह्मणसात्<BR> भवति धनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणाच्छंसिन्
ब्राह्मणाच्छंसिन् <i>m.</i> N. of a priest, the assistant of the priest<BR> called <i>Brahman</i> q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणायनः|ब्राह्मणायन
ब्राह्मणायनः A Brāhmaṇa descended from learned and holy progenitors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणी
ब्राह्मणी<BR>—1 A woman of the Brāhmaṇa caste.<BR>—2 The wife of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 Intellect; (बुद्धि according to नीलकण्ठ).<BR>—4 A kind of lizard; हृष्टः पश्यति तस्यान्तं ब्राह्मणी करकादिव Rām. 3. 29. 5.<BR>—5 A kind of wasp.<BR>—6 A kind of brass (Mar. सोनपितळ).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्राह्मणीगामिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मणीगामिन्
ब्राह्मणी + -गामिन् <i>m.</i> the paramour of a Brāhmaṇa woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण्य|ब्राह्मण्यः
ब्राह्मण्य <i>a.</i> Befitting a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण्यः|ब्राह्मण्य
ब्राह्मण्य + .{@-ण्यः@} An epithet of the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मण्यम्
ब्राह्मण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@}<BR>—1 The station or rank of a Brāhmaṇa, priestly or sacerdotal character;<BR> सत्यं शपे ब्राह्मण्येन Mk. 5; Pt. 1. 66; Ms. 3. 17, 7. 42.<BR>—2 A collection of Brāhmaṇas; ब्राह्मण्यं कृत्स्नमेतत्त्वां ब्रह्मण्यमनुगच्छति<BR> Rām. 2. 45. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मी
ब्राह्मी<BR>—1 The personified female energy of Brahman.<BR>—2 Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech.<BR>—3 Speech; संस्कारोपगतां ब्राह्मीं नानाशास्त्रोपबृंहिताम् Mb. 1. 1. 19.<BR>—4 A tale or narrative.<BR>—5 A pious usage or custom, Vedic rituals; ब्राह्मपा संवर्तयामासू राङ्कवास्तरणावृताम्<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 113.<BR>—6 N. of the constellation Rohiṇī.<BR>—7 N. of Durgā.<BR>—8 A woman married according to the <i>Brāhma</i> form of marriage.<BR>—9 The wife of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—10 A kind of medicinal plant; ब्राह्मी हिमा सरा तिक्ता लघुर्मेध्या च<BR> शीतला । कषाया मधुरा स्वादुपाकायुष्या रसायनी । स्वर्या स्मृतिपदा कुष्ठपाण्डुमेहाश्रकासजित् ॥<BR> Bhāva P.; बभूव तेषां रजनी ब्राह्मीव प्रींतिवर्धिनी Mb. 15. 18. 23.<BR>—11 A kind of brass.<BR>—12 N. of a river.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्राह्मीकन्दः, ब्राह्मीपुत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मीकन्दः|ब्राह्मीकन्द
ब्राह्मी + -कन्दः a species of bulbous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्मीपुत्रः|ब्राह्मीपुत्र
ब्राह्मी + -पुत्रः the son of a Brāhmī, see above; दश पूर्वान् परान्<BR> वंश्यानात्मानं चैकविंशकम् । ब्राह्मीपुत्रः सुकृतकृन्मोचयेदेनसः पितॄन् ॥<BR> Ms. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्य|ब्राह्म्यं
ब्राह्म्य <i>a.</i> (-ह्मयी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [ब्रह्मण इदं ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Relating to Brahman, the creator.<BR>—2 Relating to the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—3 Relating to the Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्यम्
ब्राह्म्य + .{@-ह्म्यम्@}<BR>—1 Wonder, astonishment (विस्मय).<BR>—2 Worship of the Brāhmaṇas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ब्राह्म्यमुहूर्त, ब्राह्म्यहुतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्यमुहूर्त|ब्राह्म्यमुहूर्त्त
ब्राह्म्य + -मुहूर्त = ब्राह्ममुहूर्त q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्राह्म्यहुतम्
ब्राह्म्य + -हुतम् hospitality to guests; see ब्रह्मयज्ञ; cf. Ms. 3. 74;<BR> ब्राह्म्यहुतशब्देन मनुष्ययज्ञाख्यो ब्राह्मणश्रेष्ठस्यार्चा Kull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रू
ब्रू €2 U. (ब्रवीति, ब्रूते or आह; this root is defective in<BR> the non-conjugational tenses, its forms being made up from वच्).<BR>—1 To say, tell, speak (with two acc.); तां.. … ब्रूया एवम्<BR> Me. 103; रामं यथास्थितं सर्वं भ्राता ब्रूते स्म विह्वलः Bk. 6. 8;<BR> or माणवकं धर्मं ब्रूते Sk.; किं त्वां प्रति ब्रूमहे Bv. 1. 46.<BR>—2 To say or speak about, refer to (a person or thing); अहं तु शकुन्तलामधिकृत्य<BR> ब्रवीमि Ś. 2.<BR>—3 To declare, proclaim, publish, prove, indicate; ब्रुवते हि फलेन<BR> साधवो न तु कण्ठेन निजोपयोगिताम् N. 2. 48; स्तनयुगपरिणाहं मण्डलाभ्यां<BR> ब्रवीति Ratn. 2. 12.<BR>—4 To name, call, designate; छन्दसि दक्षा ये कवयस्तन्मणिमध्यं ते<BR> ब्रुवते Śrut. 15.<BR>—5 To answer; ब्रूहि मे प्रश्नान्.<BR>—6 To call or profess oneself to be. ━<i>With</i> {@अति@}<BR>—1 to insult, abuse; Mb. 3.<BR>—2 to argue, dispute; परस्परं केचिदुपाश्रयन्ति परस्परं केचिदतिब्रुवन्ति<BR> Rām. 5. 61. 17.<BR>━{@अनु@} to say, speak, declare; अथ यदनुब्रूते तेन ऋषीणाम् Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 16.<BR>━{@निस्@} to explain, derive.<BR>━{@प्र@} to say, speak, tell; पापानुवासितं सीता रावणं प्राब्रवीद्वचः Bk. 8. 85.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-1" target="_blank">Page1179-1</a>]<BR>━{@प्रति@} to speak in reply; प्रत्यब्रवीच्चैनम् R. 2. 42.<BR>━{@वि@}<BR>—1 to say, speak.<BR>—2 to speak falsely or wrongly; अब्रुवन् विब्रुवन् वापि नरो भवति किल्बिषी<BR> Ms. 8. 13; अब्रुवन् विब्रुवन्नज्ञो नरः किल्बिषमश्रुते Bhāg. 10. 44. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1178-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रुव
ब्रुव, ब्रुवाण <i>a.</i> Professing or pretending to be, calling<BR> oneself by a name to which he has no real title (at the end of comp.),<BR> as in ब्राह्मणब्रुव, क्षत्रियब्रुव &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्रुवाण|ब्रुवाणः
ब्रुव, ब्रुवाण <i>a.</i> Professing or pretending to be, calling<BR> oneself by a name to which he has no real title (at the end of comp.),<BR> as in ब्राह्मणब्रुव, क्षत्रियब्रुव &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ब्लेष्कम्
ब्लेष्कम् A snare, net, noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भः|भ|भं
भः<BR>—1 N. of the planet Venus.<BR>—2 Error, delusion, mere semblance.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śukra.<BR>—4 N. given to the base of nouns before the vowel terminations beginning<BR> with accusative plural; cf. अङ्ग and पद.<BR>—5 A bee. {@भम्@}<BR>—1 A star; ननु भन्यमूनि Rām. Ch. 6. 33; भगणो भाति यद्भयात्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 29. 4.<BR>—2 A lunar mansion or asterism.<BR>—3 A planet.<BR>—4 A sign of the zodiac.<BR>—5 The number twenty-seven.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भेनः, भेशः, भकक्षा, भगणः, भवर्गः, भगमः, भगोलः, भचक्रम्, भपञ्जरः, भमण्डलम्, भप, भपतिः, भभ्रमः, भलता, भवासरः, भसन्धिः, भसूचकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेनः|भेन
भः + -ईनः, -ईशः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the regent of an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेशः|भेश
भः + -ईनः, -ईशः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the regent of an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भकक्षा
भः + -कक्षा the path of the asterisms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगणः|भगण
भः + -गणः, -वर्गः<BR>—1 the group of stars or asterisms.<BR>—2 the zodiac.<BR>—3 revolution of the planets in the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवर्गः|भवर्ग
भः + -गणः, -वर्गः<BR>—1 the group of stars or asterisms.<BR>—2 the zodiac.<BR>—3 revolution of the planets in the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगमः|भगम
भः + -गमः the revolution of a planet; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगोलः|भगोल
भः + -गोलः the starry sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भचक्रम्
भः + -चक्रम्, -पञ्जरः, -मण्डलम् the zodiac. {@˚नाभिः@} the centre of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भपञ्जरः|भपञ्जर|भपञ्जरं
भः + -चक्रम्, -पञ्जरः, -मण्डलम् the zodiac. {@˚नाभिः@} the centre of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भमण्डलम्
भः + -चक्रम्, -पञ्जरः, -मण्डलम् the zodiac. {@˚नाभिः@} the centre of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भप
भः + -प <i>a.</i> the regent of an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भपतिः|भपति
भः + -पतिः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भभ्रमः|भभ्रम
भः + -भ्रमः a sidereal day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भलता
भः + -लता Paederia Foetida (Mar. हरणबेल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवासरः|भवासर
भः + -वासरः a sidereal day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसन्धिः|भसन्धि
भः + -सन्धिः N. of the last quarters of the asterisms, आश्लेषा, ज्येष्ठा<BR> and रेवती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भसूचकः|भसूचक
भः + -सूचकः an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्किका
भक्किका A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्त|भक्तं|भक्तः
भक्त <i>p. p.</i> [भज्-क्त]<BR>—1 Distributed, allotted, assigned; वामहस्ताहृतं चान्नं भक्तं पर्युषितं<BR> च यत् Mb. 12. 36. 31.<BR>—2 Divided.<BR>—3 Served, worshipped.<BR>—4 Engaged in, attentive to.<BR>—5 Attached or devoted to, loyal, faithful; मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी<BR> मां नमस्कुरु Bg. 9. 34.<BR>—6 Dressed, cooked (as food).<BR>—7 Forming a part of, belonging to.<BR>—8 Loved, liked (at the end of comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तः|भक्त|भक्तं
भक्त + .{@-क्तः@} A worshipper, adorer, devotee, votary, faithful attendant;<BR> भक्तोऽसि मे सखा चेति Bg. 4. 3, 7. 23, 9. 31; भक्तानां त्रिविधानां<BR> च लक्षणं श्रूयतामिति । तृणशय्यारतो भक्तो मन्नामगुणकीर्तिषु । मनो<BR> निवेशयेत् त्यक्त्वा संसारसुखकारणम् ॥ Brav. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तम्
भक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 A share, portion.<BR>—2 Food; वन्यं सुविहितं नित्यं भक्तमश्नाति पञ्चमम् Rām. 5. 36. 41;<BR> भक्तं भुक्तं ततः किम् Bh. 3. 74; also meal; तथैव सप्तमे<BR> भक्ते भक्तानि षडनश्नता Ms. 11. 16; चतुर्थभक्तक्षपणं वैश्ये शूद्रे<BR> विधीयते Mb. 13. 106.<BR>—3 Boiled rice; गन्धेन स्फुरता मनागनुसृतो भक्तस्य सर्पिष्मतः U. 4. 1.<BR>—4 Any eatable grain boiled with water.<BR>—5 Adoration, worship.<BR>—6 The grain; यस्य त्रैवार्षिकं भक्तं पर्याप्तं भृत्यवृत्तये Ms. 11. 7;<BR> Mb. 12. 165. 5 (भक्तम् एकाहपर्याप्तं धान्यम् Nīlakaṇṭha).<BR>—7 The wages, remuneration (वेतन); Mb. 13. 23. 70.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भक्ताग्रः, भक्ताग्रम्, भक्ताभिलाषः, भक्तोद्भवः, भक्तोपसाधकः, भक्तकंसः, भक्तकरः, भक्तकारः, भक्तकृत्यम्, भक्तच्छन्दम्, भक्तजा, भक्ततूर्यम्, भक्तद, भक्तदातृ, भक्तदायक, भक्तदासः, भक्तद्वेषः, भक्तपुलाकः, भक्तमण्डः, भक्तरुचिः, भक्तरोचन, भक्तवत्सल, भक्तशाला, भक्तसाधनम्, भक्तसिक्थम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ताग्रः|भक्ताग्र
भक्त + -अग्रः, -अग्रम् a refectory; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ताग्रम्
भक्त + -अग्रः, -अग्रम् a refectory; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ताभिलाषः|भक्ताभिलाष
भक्त + -अभिलाषः desire of food, appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तोद्भवः
भक्त + -उद्भवः gruel<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">Page1179-a2</a>]<BR> (Mar. पेज).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तोपसाधकः|भक्तोपसाधक
भक्त + -उपसाधकः a cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकंसः|भक्तकंस
भक्त + -कंसः a dish of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकरः|भक्तकर
भक्त + -करः incense prepared from various fragrant resins and perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तकारः|भक्तकार
भक्त + -कारः a cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

