भक्त + -द, -दातृ, -दायक <i>a.</i> supporter, maintainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदातृ
भक्त + -द, -दातृ, -दायक <i>a.</i> supporter, maintainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदायक
भक्त + -द, -दातृ, -दायक <i>a.</i> supporter, maintainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तदासः|भक्तदास
भक्त + -दासः a slave who agrees to serve another for maintenance, or<BR> who receives his meals as a return for his services; Ms. 8. 415 भक्तलोभाद्युपगतदास्यो<BR> भक्तदासः Kull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तद्वेषः|भक्तद्वेष
भक्त + -द्वेषः dislike of food, loss of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तपुलाकः|भक्तपुलाक
भक्त + -पुलाकः a mouthful of rice kneaded into a lump or ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तमण्डः|भक्तमण्ड|भक्तमंड
भक्त + -मण्डः the scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तरुचिः|भक्तरुचि
भक्त + -रुचिः <i>f.</i> appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तरोचन
भक्त + -रोचन <i>a.</i> stimulating appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तवत्सल|भक्तवत्सलः
भक्त + -वत्सल <i>a.</i> kind to worshippers or devotees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तवत्सलः|भक्तवत्सल
भक्त + -वत्सल + .({@-लः@}) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तशाला
भक्त + -शाला<BR>—1 an audience chamber (to admit petitioners and hear them).<BR>—2 a dining-hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तसाधनम्
भक्त + -साधनम् a dish of pulse (Mar. बरण); Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तसिक्थम्
भक्त + -सिक्थम् = भक्तमण्ड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिः|भक्ति
भक्तिः <i>f.</i> [भज्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Separation, partition, division.<BR>—2 A division, portion, share.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Devotion, attachment, loyalty, faithfulness; तद्भक्तिसंक्षिप्तबृहत्प्रमाणमारुह्य<BR> कैलासमिव प्रतस्थे Ku. 7. 37; R. 2. 63; Mu. 1. 15.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Faith, belief, pious faith.<BR>—4 Reverence, service, worship, homage.<BR>—5 Texture, arrangement; भवति विरलभक्तिर्म्लानपुष्पोपहारः R. 5. 74;<BR> मणिमरीचिरचितेन्द्रचापभक्तयः विद्याधरपतयः Nāg. 5.<BR>—6 Decoration, ornament, embellishment; सुकृतेहामृगाकीर्णं सूत्कीर्णं<BR> भक्तिभिस्तथा Rām. 2. 15. 35; आबद्धमुक्ताफलभक्तिचित्रे Ku. 7. 10, 94;<BR> R. 13. 55, 75, 15. 30. अधिरुह्य स वज्रभक्तिचित्रम् (आसनम्) Bu. C. 5. 44.<BR>—7 An attribute.<BR>—8 The being part of, belonging to.<BR>—9 A figurative sense, secondary sense; भक्त्या निष्कयवादः स्यात् MS. 4. 4. 28<BR> (भक्त्या here seems to have been used as an indeclinable);<BR> cf. also MS. 8. 3. 22.<BR>—10 Predisposition (of body to any disease).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भक्तिगम्य, भक्तिगन्धि, भक्तिच्छेदः, भक्तिज्ञ, भक्तिनम्र, भक्तिपूर्वम्, भक्तिपूर्वकम्, भक्तिभाज्, भक्तिमार्गः, भक्तियोगः, भक्तिरसः, भक्तिरागः, भक्तिवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिगम्य
भक्तिः + -गम्य <i>a.</i> accessible by devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिगन्धि
भक्तिः + -गन्धि <i>a.</i> one who has only a small measure of devotion; बह्वाश्चर्यं<BR> भक्तिचित्रं ब्रह्मणा परिनिर्मितम् Rām. 7. 15. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिच्छेदः|भक्तिच्छेद
भक्तिः + -छेदः<BR>—1 a coloured streak, lines of painting or decoration; भक्तिच्छेदैरिव<BR> विरचितां भूतिमङ्गे गजस्य Me. 19.<BR>—2 distinguishing marks of devotion to Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिज्ञ
भक्तिः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> faithfully attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिनम्र
भक्तिः + -नम्र <i>a.</i> making a humble obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिपूर्वम्
भक्तिः + -पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> devoutly, reverentially.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">Page1180-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिपूर्वकम्
भक्तिः + -पूर्वम्, -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> devoutly, reverentially.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">Page1180-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1179-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिभाज्
भक्तिः + -भाज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 devout, fervid.<BR>—2 firmly attached or devoted, faithful, loyal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिमार्गः|भक्तिमार्ग
भक्तिः + -मार्गः the way of devotion; <i>i. e.</i> devotion to god, regarded<BR> as the way to the attainment of final emancipation and eternal bliss (opp.<BR> to कर्ममार्ग and ज्ञानमार्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तियोगः|भक्तियोग
भक्तिः + -योगः loving faith, loyal devotion; स स्थाणुः स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो<BR> निःश्रेयसायास्तु वः Vikr. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिरसः|भक्तिरस
भक्तिः + -रसः<BR>—1 a sense of devotion.<BR>—2 a sentiment of devotion; भक्तिरसस्यैव हास्यशृङ्गारकरुणरौद्रभयानकबीभत्सशान्ताद्भुतवीररूपेणानुभवाद्<BR> व्यासादिभिर्वर्णितस्य विष्णोर्विष्णुभक्तानां वा चरितस्य नवरसात्मकस्य<BR> श्रवणादिना जनितश्चमत्कारो हि भक्तिरसः Muktā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिरागः|भक्तिराग
भक्तिः + -रागः affection, deep devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिवादः|भक्तिवाद
भक्तिः + -वादः assurance of attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिक
भक्तिक <i>a.</i> Relating to worship or devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिमत्|भक्तिमन्त्
भक्तिमत्^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Devout, having pious faith.<BR>—2 Loyally devoted or attached, faithful, loyal.<BR>—3 Religious, pious.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: virAma missing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तिल|भक्तिलः
भक्तिल <i>a.</i> Faithful, trusty (as a horse.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्तृ
भक्तृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 An adorer, a worshipper.<BR>—2 Devoutly attached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्
भक्ष् €10 U. (भक्षयति-ते, भक्षित)<BR>—1 To eat, devour; यथामिषं जले मत्स्यैर्भक्ष्यते श्वापदैर्भुवि Pt. 1.<BR>—2 To use up, consume.<BR>—3 To waste, destroy.<BR>—4 To bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षः|भक्ष
भक्षः<BR>—1 Eating.<BR>—2 Food, eatables; ममेप्सितः । भक्षः (त्वं) प्रीणय मे देहं चिरमाहारवर्जितम्<BR> Rām. 5. 58. 40, 7. 69. 15; यद्ययं क्रियते भक्षस्तर्हि मां खाद पूर्वतः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 9. 33.<BR>—3 Drink, drinking (Ved.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भक्षकारः, भक्षपत्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षकारः|भक्षकार
भक्षः + -कारः a cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षपत्री
भक्षः + -पत्री betel pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षक|भक्षकः
भक्षक <i>a.</i> (-क्षिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भक्ष्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 One who eats or lives upon.<BR>—2 Gluttonous, voracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षकः|भक्षक
भक्षक + .{@-कः@} Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षण|भक्षणं
भक्षण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Eating, one who eats or devours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षणम्
भक्षण + .{@-णम्@} [भक्ष्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Eating, feeding or living upon.<BR>—2 Ved. A drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षणीय|भक्षणीयं
भक्षणीय <i>a.</i> Eatable, edible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षिका
भक्षिका<BR>—1 A meal.<BR>—2 Eating (at the end of comp.); भवानिक्षुभक्षिकामर्हति ऋणे इक्षुभक्षिकां<BR> मे धारयति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षित|भक्षितं
भक्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Eaten, devoured.<BR>—2 Slurred over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षितम्
भक्षित + .{@-तम्@} Food.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भक्षितशेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्षितशेषः|भक्षितशेष
भक्षित + -शेषः leavings, remnants of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्य|भक्ष्यं
भक्ष्य <i>a.</i> [भक्ष्-कर्मणि ण्यत्] Eatable, fit for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यम्
भक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यम्@}<BR>—1 Anything eatable, an article of food, food (fig. also); भक्ष्यभक्षकयोः<BR> प्रीतिर्विपत्तेरेव कारणम् H. 1. 55; Ms. 1. 113.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भक्ष्याभक्ष्यम्, भक्ष्यकारः, भक्ष्यभोज्यमय, भक्ष्यवस्तु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्याभक्ष्यम्
भक्ष्य + -अभक्ष्यम् food allowed and prohibited; एतदुक्तं द्विजातीनां<BR> भक्ष्याभक्ष्यमशेषतः Ms. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यकारः|भक्ष्यकार
भक्ष्य + -कारः (also भक्ष्यंकारः) a baker, cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यभोज्यमय
भक्ष्य + -भोज्यमय <i>a.</i> Consisting of food of all kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भक्ष्यवस्तु
भक्ष्य + -वस्तु <i>n.</i> eatables, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगः|भग|भगं
भगः (also भगम्) [भज्-घ]<BR>—1 One of the twelve forms of the sun; the sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 A form of Śiva.<BR>—4 Good fortune, luck, happy lot, happiness;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">Page1180-2</a>]<BR> आस्ते भग आसीनस्य Ait. Br.; भगमिन्द्रश्च वायुश्च भगं सप्तर्षयो<BR> ददुः Y. 1. 282.<BR>—5 Affluence, prosperity; ‘ओश्वर्यस्य समग्रस्य वीर्यस्य यशसः श्रियः । ज्ञानवैराग्ययोश्चैव षण्णां भग इतीरणा ॥’;<BR> शमो दमो भगश्चेति यत्सङ्गाद्याति<BR> संक्षयम् Bhāg. 3. 31. 33.<BR>—6 Dignity, distinction.<BR>—7 Fame, glory.<BR>—8 Loveliness, beauty.<BR>—9 Excellence, distinction.<BR>—10 Love, affection.<BR>—11 Amorous dalliance or sport, pleasure.<BR>—12 The pudendum muliebre; Y. 3. 88; गुरुतल्पे भगः कार्यः Ms. 9. 237.<BR>—13 Virtue, morality, religious merit (धर्म).<BR>—14 Effort, exertion.<BR>—15 Absence of desire, indifference to worldly objects.<BR>—16 Final beatitude.<BR>—17 Strength.<BR>—18 Omnipotence; (said to be <i>n.</i> also in the last 15 senses).<BR>—19 N. of an Āditya presiding over love and marriage; Mb. 1. 227. 36.<BR>—20 Knowledge.<BR>—21 Desire, wish.<BR>—22 The superhuman power of becoming as small as an atom, one of the eight<BR> <i>Siddhis</i> or powers of Śiva; see अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगम्
भगः (also भगम्) [भज्-घ]<BR>—1 One of the twelve forms of the sun; the sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 A form of Śiva.<BR>—4 Good fortune, luck, happy lot, happiness;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">Page1180-2</a>]<BR> आस्ते भग आसीनस्य Ait. Br.; भगमिन्द्रश्च वायुश्च भगं सप्तर्षयो<BR> ददुः Y. 1. 282.<BR>—5 Affluence, prosperity; ‘ओश्वर्यस्य समग्रस्य वीर्यस्य यशसः श्रियः । ज्ञानवैराग्ययोश्चैव षण्णां भग इतीरणा ॥’;<BR> शमो दमो भगश्चेति यत्सङ्गाद्याति<BR> संक्षयम् Bhāg. 3. 31. 33.<BR>—6 Dignity, distinction.<BR>—7 Fame, glory.<BR>—8 Loveliness, beauty.<BR>—9 Excellence, distinction.<BR>—10 Love, affection.<BR>—11 Amorous dalliance or sport, pleasure.<BR>—12 The pudendum muliebre; Y. 3. 88; गुरुतल्पे भगः कार्यः Ms. 9. 237.<BR>—13 Virtue, morality, religious merit (धर्म).<BR>—14 Effort, exertion.<BR>—15 Absence of desire, indifference to worldly objects.<BR>—16 Final beatitude.<BR>—17 Strength.<BR>—18 Omnipotence; (said to be <i>n.</i> also in the last 15 senses).<BR>—19 N. of an Āditya presiding over love and marriage; Mb. 1. 227. 36.<BR>—20 Knowledge.<BR>—21 Desire, wish.<BR>—22 The superhuman power of becoming as small as an atom, one of the eight<BR> <i>Siddhis</i> or powers of Śiva; see अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगा
भगः (also भगम्) + .{@-गा@}<BR>—1 (in comp.). Dignity, majesty; भूः कालभर्जितभगापि यदङ्घ्रिपद्मस्पर्शोत्थशक्तिरभिवर्षति<BR> नोऽखिलार्थान् Bhāg. 10. 82. 30.<BR>—2 The female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगम्
भगः (also भगम्) + .{@-गम्@}<BR>—1 The asterism called उत्तराफल्गुनी; भगं नक्षत्रमाकम्य सूर्यपुत्रेण<BR> पीड्यते Mb. 6. 3. 14.<BR>—2 The perinaeum of males.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भगाङ्कुरः, भगाधानम्, भगेशः, भगकाम, भगघ्नः, भगदारणम्, भगदेवः, भगदेवता, भगदैवत, भगनन्दनः, भगनेत्रघ्नः, भगनेत्रहरः, भगपुरम्, भगभक्षकः, भगवृत्ति, भगवेदनम्, भगशास्त्रम्, भगहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाङ्कुरः|भगाङ्कुर|भगांकुर
भगः + -अङ्कुरः (in medicine) clitoris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगाधानम्
भगः + -आधानम् granting matrimonial happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगेशः|भगेश
भगः + -ईशः the lord of fortune or prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगकाम
भगः + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of sexual pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगघ्नः|भगघ्न
भगः + -घ्नः an epithet of Śiva; नमस्ते त्रिपुरघ्नाय भगध्नाय नमो नमः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदारणम्
भगः + -दारणम् = भगंदरः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदेवः|भगदेव
भगः + -देवः a thorough libertine; भगदेवानुयातानां सर्वासां वामलोचना<BR> Mb. 14. 43. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदेवता
भगः + -देवता the deity presiding over marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदैवत|भगदैवतं
भगः + -दैवत <i>a.</i> conferring conjugal felicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगदैवतम्
भगः + -दैवत + .({@-तम्@}) the constellation उत्तराफल्गुनी; विवाहं स्थापयित्वाऽग्रे<BR> नक्षत्रे भगदैवते Mb. 1. 8. 16. ˚मासः the month Phālguna; भगदैवतमासं<BR> तु एकभक्तेन यः क्षिपेत् Mb. 13. 106. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगनन्दनः|भगनन्दन
भगः + -नन्दनः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगनेत्रघ्नः|भगनेत्रघ्न
भगः + -नेत्रघ्नः, -नेत्रहरः an epithet of Śiva. वर्जयित्वा विरूपाक्षं<BR> भगनेत्रहरं हरम् Mb. 1. 221. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगनेत्रहरः|भगनेत्रहर
भगः + -नेत्रघ्नः, -नेत्रहरः an epithet of Śiva. वर्जयित्वा विरूपाक्षं<BR> भगनेत्रहरं हरम् Mb. 1. 221. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगपुरम्
भगः + -पुरम् N. of the city, Multān.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगभक्षकः|भगभक्षक
भगः + -भक्षकः a pander, procurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवृत्ति
भगः + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> subsisting by the vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवेदनम्
भगः + -वेदनम् proclaiming matrimonial felicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगशास्त्रम्
भगः + -शास्त्रम् (= कामशास्त्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगहन्
भगः + -हन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu (originally of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगंदरः|भगन्दर|भगंदर|भगन्दरः
भगंदरः A fistula in the anus or pudendum; कटीकपालयोस्तोददाहकण्डूरुजादयः ।<BR> भवन्ति पूर्वरूपाणि भविष्यति भगन्दरे ॥ Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवत्|भगवन्त्
भगवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Glorious, illustrious.<BR>—2 Revered, venerable, divine, holy (an epithet applied to gods, demigods<BR> and other holy or respectable personages); स्वर्गप्रकाशो भगवान् प्रदोषः<BR> Rām. 5. 5. 8; अथ भगवान् कुशली काश्यपः Ś. 5; भगवन् परवानयं<BR> जनः R. 8. 81; so भगवान् वासुदेवः &c.; उत्पत्तिं च विनाशं<BR> च भूतानामागतिं गतिम् । वेत्ति विद्यामविद्यां च स वाच्यो भगवानिति ॥<BR>—3 Fortunate (Ved.). ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A god, deity.<BR>—2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR>—4 Of Jina.<BR>—5 Of Buddha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भगवद्गीता, भगवद्दृश, भगवत्पदी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवद्गीता
भगवत् + -गीता N. of a celebrated sacred work; (it is an episode of the<BR> great Bhārata and purports to be a dialogue between Kṛṣṇa and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">Page1181-1</a>]<BR> Arjuna).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1180-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवद्दृश
भगवत् + -दृश <i>a.</i> resembling the Supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवत्पदी
भगवत् + -पदी N. of the source of Gaṅgā; साक्षाद्भगवत्पदीत्यनुपलक्षितवचः<BR> Bhāg. 5. 17. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवती
भगवती<BR>—1 N. of Durgā.<BR>—2 Of Lakṣmī.<BR>—3 Any venerable woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगवदीयः|भगवदीय
भगवदीयः A worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगालम्
भगालम् A skull; P. VI. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगालिन्
भगालिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिन्
भगिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Prosperous, happy, fortunate.<BR>—2 Grand, splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनिका
भगिनिका A little sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनी
भगिनी [भगं यत्नः अंशो वा पित्रादीनां द्रव्यादानेऽस्त्यस्याः इनि ङीप्]<BR>—1 A sister.<BR>—2 A fortunate woman.<BR>—3 A woman in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भगिनीपतिः, भगिनीभर्तृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनीपतिः|भगिनीपति
भगिनी + -पतिः, -भर्तृ <i>m.</i> a sisterʼs husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनीभर्तृ
भगिनी + -पतिः, -भर्तृ <i>m.</i> a sisterʼs husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगिनीयः|भगिनीय
भगिनीयः A sisterʼs son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथः|भगीरथ
भगीरथः N. of an ancient king of the solar dynasty, the great-grandson<BR> of Sagara, who brought down, by practising the most austere penance, the<BR> celestial river Gaṅgā from heaven to the earth and from earth to the<BR> lower regions to purify the ashes of his 60,000 ancestors, the sons of Sagara.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भगीरथपथः, भगीरथप्रयत्नः, भगीरथसुता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथपथः|भगीरथपथ
भगीरथः + -पथः, -प्रयत्नः the path or effort of Bhagīratha, used figuratively<BR> to denote any great or Herculean effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथप्रयत्नः|भगीरथप्रयत्न
भगीरथः + -पथः, -प्रयत्नः the path or effort of Bhagīratha, used figuratively<BR> to denote any great or Herculean effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगीरथसुता
भगीरथः + -सुता an epithet of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भगोस्
भगोस् Voc. A term of address like भगवन्, भगवस्; यन्नु म इयं<BR> भगोः सर्वा पृथिवी वित्तेन पूर्णा स्यात् Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्न|भग्नं
भग्न <i>p. p.</i> [भञ्ज्-क्त]<BR>—1 Broken, fractured, shattered, torn; रथोद्वहनखिन्नाश्च भग्ना मे<BR> रथवाजिनः Rām. 6. 104. 16.<BR>—2 Frustrated, foiled, disappointed.<BR>—3 Checked, arrested, suspended.<BR>—4 Marred, impaired.<BR>—5 Routed, completely defeated or vanquished; त्वर तेन महाबाहो भग्न<BR> एष न संशयः Rām. 6. 88. 40; U. 5.<BR>—6 Demolished, destroyed. (See भञ्ज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नम्
भग्न + .{@-ग्नम्@} Fracture of the leg.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भग्नास्थि, भग्नात्मन्, भग्नापद्, भग्नाश, भग्नोत्साह, भग्नोद्यम, भग्नक्रमः, भग्नचेष्ट, भग्नतालः, भग्नदंष्ट्र, भग्नदर्प, भग्ननिद्र, भग्नपरिणाम, भग्नपादर्क्षम्, भग्नपार्श्व, भग्नपृष्ठ, भग्नप्रकमः, भग्नप्रतिज्ञ, भग्नमनस्, भग्नमनोरथ, भग्नमान, भग्नव्रत, भग्नसंकल्प, भग्नसंधिकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नास्थि
भग्न + -अस्थि <i>a.</i> one whose bones are broken. ˚बन्धः a splint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नात्मन्
भग्न + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नापद्
भग्न + -आपद् <i>a.</i> one who has surmounted difficulties or misfortunes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नाश|भग्नाशः
भग्न + -आश <i>a.</i> disappointed; भग्नाशस्य करण्डपीडिततनोर्म्लानेन्द्रियस्य<BR> क्षुधा Bh. 2. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नोत्साह
भग्न + -उत्साह <i>a.</i> broken in energy, depressed in spirits, discouraged, damped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नोद्यम
भग्न + -उद्यम <i>a.</i> foiled in oneʼs endeavours, disappointed, baffled;<BR> मन्ये दुर्जनचित्तवृत्तिहरणे धाताऽपि भग्नोद्यमः H. 2. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नक्रमः|भग्नक्रम
भग्न + -क्रमः violation of symmetry in construction or expression; see<BR> प्रकमभङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नचेष्ट
भग्न + -चेष्ट <i>a.</i> disappointed, frustrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नतालः|भग्नताल
भग्न + -तालः (in music) a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नदंष्ट्र
भग्न + -दंष्ट्र <i>a.</i> having the fangs broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नदर्प
भग्न + -दर्प <i>a.</i> humbled, crest-fallen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्ननिद्र
भग्न + -निद्र <i>a.</i> whose sleep is interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नपरिणाम
भग्न + -परिणाम <i>a.</i> preventing from finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नपादर्क्षम्
भग्न + -पादर्क्षम् N. of six नक्षत्रs collectively (<i>viz.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">Page1181-2</a>]<BR> पुनर्वसू, उत्तराषाढा, कृत्तिका, उत्तराफल्गुनी, पूर्वभाद्रपदा and विशाखा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नपार्श्व
भग्न + -पार्श्व <i>a.</i> suffering from a pain in the sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नपृष्ठ|भग्नपृष्ठः
भग्न + -पृष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having a broken back.<BR>—2 coming in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नप्रकमः
भग्न + -प्रकमः<BR>—1 disorder, confusion.<BR>—2 absence of regularity or symmetry; see प्रक्रमभङ्गः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नप्रतिज्ञ
भग्न + -प्रतिज्ञ <i>a.</i> one who has broken his promises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नमनस्
भग्न + -मनस् <i>a.</i> discouraged, disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नमनोरथ
भग्न + -मनोरथ <i>a.</i> disappointed in expectations; तथा समक्षं<BR> दहता मनोभवं पिनाकिना भग्नमनोरथा सती Ku. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नमान
भग्न + -मान <i>a.</i> disgraced, dishonoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नव्रत
भग्न + -व्रत <i>a.</i> faithless in oneʼs vows; Pt. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नसंकल्प
भग्न + -संकल्प <i>a.</i> one whose designs are frustrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नसंधिकम्
भग्न + -संधिकम् butter-milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भग्नी
भग्नी A sister; आनयैतान्नरान् भग्नि … … Bm. 1. 765.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्कारी|भंकारी
भङ्का(ङ्गा)री A gad-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गारी|भंगारी
भङ्का(ङ्गा)री A gad-fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्क्तिः|भङ्क्ति|भंक्ति|भंक्तिः
भङ्क्तिः <i>f.</i> Breaking, fracture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग|भंग|भंगः|भङ्गः
भङ्ग [भञ्ज्-भावादौ घञ्]<BR>—1 Breaking, breaking down, shattering, tearing down, splitting, dividing;<BR> भङ्गः स जिष्णोर्धृतिमुन्ममाथ Ki. 17. 29. वार्यर्गलाभङ्ग इव प्रवृत्तः R. 5. 45.<BR>—2 A break, fracture, breach.<BR>—3 Plucking off, lopping; आम्रकलिकाभङ्ग Ś. 6.<BR>—4 Separation, analysis.<BR>—5 A portion, bit, fragment, detached portion; पुष्पोच्चयः पल्लवभङ्गभिन्नः<BR> Ku. 3. 61; R. 16. 16.<BR>—6 Fall, downfall, decay, destruction, ruin; as in राज्य˚, सत्त्व˚ &c.<BR>—7 Breaking up, dispersion; यात्राभङ्ग Māl. 1.<BR>—8 Defeat, overthrow, discomfiture, rout; भग्ने भग्नमवाप्नुयात् Pt. 4. 41;<BR> प्रसभं भङ्गमभङ्गुरोदयः (नयति) Śi. 16. 72.<BR>—9 Failure, disappointment, frustration; तत्पूर्वभङ्गे वितथप्रयत्नः<BR> R. 2. 42 (v. l.); आशाभङ्ग &c.<BR>—10 Rejection, refusal; अभ्यर्थनाभङ्गभयेन स्पधुर्माध्यस्थमिष्टेऽप्यवलम्बतेऽर्थे Ku. 1. 52.<BR>—11 A chasm, fissure.<BR>—12 Interruption, obstacle, disturbance; निद्रा˚, गति˚ Ki. 17. 29.<BR>—13 Non-performance, suspension, stoppage.<BR>—14 Taking to flight, flight.<BR>—15<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A bend, fold.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A wave; क्षौमे भङ्गवती तरङ्गतरले फेनाम्बुतुल्ये वहन्<BR> Nāg. 5. 2; ज्वालाभङ्गैः (= Wavelike flames) Nāg. 5. 21.<BR>—16 Contraction, bending, knitting; ग्रीवाभङ्गाभिरामम् Ś. 1. 7; so<BR> भ्रूभङ्ग U. 5. 36.<BR>—17 Going, motion.<BR>—18 Paralysis.<BR>—19 Fraud, deceit.<BR>—20 A canal, water-course.<BR>—21 A circumlocutory or round-about way of speaking or acting; see भङ्गि.<BR>—22 Hemp.<BR>—23 (With Buddhists) The constant decay taking place in the universe;<BR> constant change.<BR>—24 (With Jainas) A dialectical formula beginning with स्यात्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भङ्गनयः, भङ्गवासा, भङ्गसार्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गनयः|भङ्गनय|भंगनय
भङ्ग + -नयः removal of obstacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गवासा|भंगवासा
भङ्ग + -वासा turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गसार्थ|भंगसार्थ|भङ्गसार्थः
भङ्ग + -सार्थ <i>a.</i> dishonest, fraudulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गा
भङ्गा<BR>—1 Hemp.<BR>—2 An intoxicating drink prepared from hemp.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भङ्गाकटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गाकटम्
भङ्गा + -कटम् the pollen of hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गानः|भङ्गान
भङ्गानः A kind of fish; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिः|भङ्गि|भंगि|भंगिः
भङ्गिः, -ङ्गी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Breaking, fracture, breach, division.<BR>—2 Undulation.<BR>—3 Bending, contracting; दृग्भङ्गीभिः प्रथममथुरासंगमे चुम्बितोऽस्मि Ud. S. 13.<BR>—4 A wave.<BR>—5 A flood, current.<BR>—6 A crooked path, tortuous or winding course.<BR>—7 A circumlocutory or round-about way of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">Page1182-1</a>]<BR> speaking or acting, periphrasis; भङ्ग्यन्तरेण कथनात् K. P. 10; इति<BR> भङ्ग्या व्यज्यते-कथ्यते &c.; बहुभङ्गिविशारदः Dk.<BR>—8 A pretext, disguise, semblance; यः पाञ्चजन्यप्रतिबिम्बभङ्ग्या धाराम्भसः<BR> फेनमिव व्यनक्ति Vikr. 1. 1.<BR>—9 Trick, fraud, deceit.<BR>—10 Irony.<BR>—11 Repartee, wit.<BR>—12 A step; यानादवातरददूरमहीतलेन मार्गेण भङ्गिरचितस्फटिकेन<BR> रामः R. 13. 69.<BR>—13 An interval.<BR>—14 Modesty.<BR>—15 A fashion or mode; नानाश्रमलतापुष्पभङ्गीरचितकुन्तलाम् Bm. 1. 233;<BR> भङ्ग्यन्तरेण <i>ind.</i> in an indirect manner; in another manner.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भङ्गिभक्तिः, भङ्गिभाषणम्, भङ्गिभूत, भङ्गिविकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गी
भङ्गिः, -ङ्गी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Breaking, fracture, breach, division.<BR>—2 Undulation.<BR>—3 Bending, contracting; दृग्भङ्गीभिः प्रथममथुरासंगमे चुम्बितोऽस्मि Ud. S. 13.<BR>—4 A wave.<BR>—5 A flood, current.<BR>—6 A crooked path, tortuous or winding course.<BR>—7 A circumlocutory or round-about way of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">Page1182-1</a>]<BR> speaking or acting, periphrasis; भङ्ग्यन्तरेण कथनात् K. P. 10; इति<BR> भङ्ग्या व्यज्यते-कथ्यते &c.; बहुभङ्गिविशारदः Dk.<BR>—8 A pretext, disguise, semblance; यः पाञ्चजन्यप्रतिबिम्बभङ्ग्या धाराम्भसः<BR> फेनमिव व्यनक्ति Vikr. 1. 1.<BR>—9 Trick, fraud, deceit.<BR>—10 Irony.<BR>—11 Repartee, wit.<BR>—12 A step; यानादवातरददूरमहीतलेन मार्गेण भङ्गिरचितस्फटिकेन<BR> रामः R. 13. 69.<BR>—13 An interval.<BR>—14 Modesty.<BR>—15 A fashion or mode; नानाश्रमलतापुष्पभङ्गीरचितकुन्तलाम् Bm. 1. 233;<BR> भङ्ग्यन्तरेण <i>ind.</i> in an indirect manner; in another manner.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भङ्गिभक्तिः, भङ्गिभाषणम्, भङ्गिभूत, भङ्गिविकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1181-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिभक्तिः|भङ्गिभक्ति
भङ्गिः + -भक्तिः <i>f.</i> division into a series of waves or wave-like steps,<BR> a wavy staircase; cf. Me. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिभाषणम्
भङ्गिः + -भाषणम् crooked speeches (with hidden meaning); पांसुलजनभङ्गिभाषणरतः Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिभूत
भङ्गिः + -भूत <i>a.</i> resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिविकारः|भङ्गिविकार
भङ्गिः + -विकारः distortion of the features; a wry face, grimace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिन्|भंगिन्
भङ्गिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Frail, fragile, transient; तदपि तत्क्षणभङ्गि करोति चेत् Bh. 2. 92;<BR> Hence भङ्गित्व means ‘evanescence’; स च व्यापारो न तदात्वे<BR> सुखफलो भवति, नापि आयत्याम् । भङ्गित्वात् ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 10.<BR>—2 Cast in a suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिनी|भंगिनी
भङ्गिनी A river; आत्ममौलिमणिकान्तिभङ्गिनीं तत्पदारुणसरोजसङ्गिनीम् N. 18. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिमत्|भङ्गिमन्त्
भङ्गिमत् <i>a.</i> Wavy, crisped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिमन्|भंगिमन्
भङ्गिमन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Fracture, breach.<BR>—2 Bending, undulation.<BR>—3 Curliness.<BR>—4 Disguise, deceit.<BR>—5 Wit, irony.<BR>—6 Perversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गिलम्
भङ्गिलम् A defect in the organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुर|भंगुर|भङ्गुरः
भङ्गुर <i>a.</i> [भञ्ज्-घुरच्]<BR>—1 Apt to break, fragile, brittle.<BR>—2 Frail, transitory, transient, perishable; आमरणान्ताः प्रणयाः कोपास्तत्क्षणभङ्गुराः;<BR> सर्वमुत्पादि भङ्गुरम् H. 1. 181; Śi. 16. 72.<BR>—3 Changeful, variable.<BR>—4 Crooked, bent.<BR>—5 Curved, curled; शशिमुखि तव भाति भङ्गुरभ्रूः Gīt. 10.<BR>—6 Fraudulent, dishonest, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुरः|भङ्गुर|भंगुर
भङ्गुर + .{@-रः@} The bend of a river.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भङ्गुरनिश्चय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुरनिश्चय
भङ्गुर + -निश्चय <i>a.</i> vacillating, unsettled in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुरयति
भङ्गुरयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To break to pieces, destroy.<BR>—2 To curl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्गुरीकरणम्
भङ्गुरीकरणम् Making fragile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भङ्ग्यम्
भङ्ग्यम् A field of hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भज्
भज् I. €1 U. (भजति-ते but usually Ātm. only; बभाज, भेजे,<BR> अभाक्षीत्, अभक्त, भक्ष्यति-ते, भक्त)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To share, distribute, divide; भजेरन् पैतृकं रिक्थम् Ms. 9. 104;<BR> न तत्पुत्रैर्भजेत् सार्धम् 209, 119.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To assign, allot, apportion; गायत्रीमग्नयेऽभजत् Ait. Br.<BR>—2 To obtain for oneself, share in, partake of; पित्र्यं वा भजते शीलम् Ms. 10. 59.<BR>—3 To accept, receive; चामुण्डे भगवति मन्त्रसाधनादावुद्दिष्टामुपनिहितां<BR> भजस्व पूजाम् Māl. 5. 25.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To resort to, betake oneself to, have recourse to; शिलातलं<BR> भेजे K. 179; मातर्लक्ष्मि भजस्व कंचिदपरम् Bh. 3. 64; न कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोऽपि<BR> भजते Ś. 5. 10; Bv. 1. 83; R. 17. 28.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To practise, follow, cultivate, observe; तृष्णां छिन्धि भज क्षमाम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">Page1182-2</a>]<BR> Bh. 2. 77; भेजे धर्ममनातुरः R. 1. 21; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>—5 To enjoy, possess, have, suffer, experience, entertain; विधुरपि<BR> भजतेतरां कलङ्कम् Bv. 1. 74; न भेजिरे भीमविषेण भीतिम् Bh. 2. 80;<BR> व्यक्तिं भजन्त्यापगाः Ś. 7. 8; अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं भजते<BR> कैव कथा शरीरिषु R. 8. 43; Māl. 3. 9; U. 1. 35.<BR>—6 To wait or attend upon, serve; (दोग्ध्रीं) भेजे भुजोच्छिन्नरिपुर्निषण्णाम्<BR> R. 2. 23; Pt. 1. 181; Mk. 1. 32.<BR>—7 To adore, honour, worship (as a god).<BR>—8 To choose, select, prefer, accept; सन्तः परीक्ष्यान्यतरद्भजन्ते M. 1. 2.<BR>—9 To enjoy carnally; वसोर्वीर्योत्पन्नामभजत मुनिर्मत्स्यतनयाम् Pt. 4. 50.<BR>—10 To be attached or devoted to; आसन्नमेव नृपतिर्भजते मनुष्यं<BR> विद्याविहीनमकुलीनमसंस्कृतं वा Pt. 1. 35.<BR>—11 To take possession of.<BR>—12 To fall to the lot of any one.<BR>—13 To grant, bestow.<BR>—14 To supply, furnish (Ved.).<BR>—15 To favour; ये यथा मां प्रपद्यन्ते तांस्तथैव भजाम्यहम् Bg. 4. 11.<BR>—16 To decide in favour of, declare for.<BR>—17 To love, court (affection).<BR>—18 To apply oneself to, be engaged in.<BR>—19 To cook, dress (food).<BR>—20 To employ, engage. (The meanings of this root are variously modified<BR> according to the noun with which it is connected:− <i>e. g.</i> निद्रां<BR> भज् to go to sleep; मूर्छां भज् to swoon; भावं भज् to show love<BR> for &c. &c.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To divide.<BR>—2 To put to flight, pursue.<BR>—3 To cook, dress. ━II. €10 U. (भाजयति-ते, regarded by some as the<BR> <i>caus.</i> of भज् I)<BR>—1 To cook.<BR>—2 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजकः|भजक
भजकः [भज्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A divider, distributer.<BR>—2 A worshipper, votary, devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजनम्
भजनम् [भज्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sharing, dividing.<BR>—2 Possession.<BR>—3 Service, adoration, worship.<BR>—4 Waiting or attending upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भजमान|भजमानः
भजमान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dividing.<BR>—2 Enjoying.<BR>—3 Fit, right, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्ज्|भंज्
भञ्ज् I. €7 P. (भनक्ति, बभञ्ज, अभाङ्क्षीत्, भङ्क्ष्यति, भङ्क्तुम्, भग्न;<BR> <i>desid.</i> बिभङ्क्षति) —1 To break, tear down, shatter, shiver<BR> or break to pieces, split; भनज्मि सर्वमर्यादाः Bk. 6. 38; भङ्क्त्वा<BR> भुजौ 4. 3; बभञ्जुर्वलयानि च 3. 22; धनुरभाजि यत्त्वया R. 11. 76.<BR>—2 To devastate, destroy by pulling down; भनक्त्युपवनं कपिः Bk. 9. 2.<BR>—3 To make a breach (in a fortress).<BR>—4 To frustrate, foil, disappoint, baffle; पिनाकिना भग्नमनोरथा सती Ku. 5. 1.<BR>—5 To arrest, check, interrupt, suspend; as in भग्ननिद्रः.<BR>—6 To defeat, vanquish; क्षत्राणि रामः परिभूय रामात् क्षत्राद्यथाऽभज्यत<BR> स द्विजेन्द्रः N. 22. 133; नृपा भीष्मादयो भग्नाः Pañc. 2. 41. ━<i>With</i> {@अव@}<BR> to break down, shatter; वनस्पतिं वज्र इवावभज्य Ku. 3. 74.<BR>━{@प्र@}<BR>—1 To break down, shatter, splinter.<BR>—2 to stop, arrest, suspend.<BR>—3 to frustrate, disappoint. ━II. €10 U. (भञ्जयति-ते)<BR>—1 To brighten, illuminate.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जक|भंजक|भञ्जकः
भञ्जक <i>a.</i> (-ञ्जिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भञ्ज्-ण्वुल्] Breaking, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जन|भंजन|भञ्जनं|भञ्जनः
भञ्जन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भञ्ज्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Breaking, splitting.<BR>—2 Arresting, checking.<BR>—3 Frustrating.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">Page1183-1</a>]<BR>—4 Causing violent pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जनम्
भञ्जन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Breaking down, shattering, destroying.<BR>—2 Removing, dispelling, driving away; तदुदितभयभञ्जनाय यूनाम् Gīt. 10.<BR>—3 Routing, vanquishing.<BR>—4 Frustrating.<BR>—5 Checking, interrupting, disturbing.<BR>—6 Afflicting, paining.<BR>—7 Smoothing (of hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जनः|भञ्जन|भंजन|भञ्जनं
भञ्जन + .{@-नः@} Decay of the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जना
भञ्जन + .{@-ना@} Explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1182-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जनकः|भञ्जनक|भंजनक|भंजनकः
भञ्जनकः A particular disease of the mouth which consists in the<BR> decay of the teeth attended with contortion of the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जरुः|भञ्जरु|भंजरु|भंजरुः
भञ्जरुः A tree growing near a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भञ्जा|भंजा
भञ्जा N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्
भट् I. €1 P. (भटति, भटित)<BR>—1 To nourish, foster, maintain.<BR>—2 To hire.<BR>—3 To receive wages. ━II. €10 U. (भटयति-ते) To speak, converse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटः|भट
भटः [भट्-अच्]<BR>—1 A warrior, soldier, combatant; दीनपरिजनकृताश्रुजलो न भटीजनः<BR> स्थिरमना विचक्लमे Śi. 15. 93; तद्भटचातुरीतुरी N. 1. 12; वादित्रसृष्टिर्घटते<BR> भटस्य 22. 22; Bk. 14. 101.<BR>—2 A mercenary, hired soldier, hireling.<BR>—3 An outcast, a barbarian.<BR>—4 A demon.<BR>—5 N. of a degraded tribe.<BR>—6 A servant, slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटा
भटः + .{@-टा@} Coloquintida (इंद्रवारुणी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भटपेटकम्, भटबलाग्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटपेटकम्
भटः + -पेटकम् a troop of soldiers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटबलाग्रः|भटबलाग्र
भटः + -बलाग्रः a hero; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटबलाग्रम्
भटः + -बलाग्रः + .({@-ग्रम्@}) an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भटित्र|भटित्रं
भटित्र^1 <i>a.</i> Roasted on a spit.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टः|भट्ट
भट्टः [भट्-तन्]<BR>—1 A lord, master (used as a title of respect in addressing princes).<BR>—2 A title used with the names of learned Brāhmaṇas; भट्टगोपालस्य<BR> पौत्रः Māl. 1; so कुमारिलभट्टः &c.<BR>—3 Any learned man or philosopher.<BR>—4 A kind of mixed caste, whose occupation is that of bards or panegyrists;<BR> क्षत्रियाद्विप्रकन्यायां भट्टो जातोऽनुवाचकः । वैश्यायां शूद्रवीर्येण<BR> पुमानेको बभूव ह । स भट्टो वावदूकश्च सर्वेषां स्तुतिपाठकः ॥ Brav. P.<BR>—5 A bard, panegyrist.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भट्टाचार्यः, भट्टनारायणः, भट्टप्रयागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टाचार्यः|भट्टाचार्य|भट्टाचार्य्य|भट्टाचार्य्यः
भट्टः + -आचार्यः<BR>—1 a title given to a learned man or any celebrated teacher (esp. कुमारिलभट्ट).<BR>—2 a great doctor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टनारायणः|भट्टनारायण
भट्टः + -नारायणः N. of the author of वेणीसंहारम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टप्रयागः|भट्टप्रयाग
भट्टः + -प्रयागः = प्रयाग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टार|भट्टारः
भट्टार <i>a.</i> [भट्टं स्वामित्वमृच्छति, ऋ-अण्]<BR>—1 Revered, worshipful.<BR>—2 A title of respect or distinction used with proper names; as in भट्टारहरिचन्द्रस्थ<BR> पद्मबन्धो नृपायते Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारः|भट्टार
भट्टार + .{@-रः@} A noble lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारक|भट्टारकः
भट्टारक <i>a.</i> (-रिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> Venerable, worshipful &c.; see भट्टार above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारकः|भट्टारक
भट्टारक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A sage, saint.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 A god, deity.<BR>—4 (In dramas) A king.<BR>—5 An epithet applied to great and learned men.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भट्टारकवारः, भट्टारकवासरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारकवारः|भट्टारकवार
भट्टारक + -वारः, -वासरः Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टारकवासरः
भट्टारक + -वारः, -वासरः Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1183-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

