भद्र + -एला large cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकपिलः|भद्रकपिल
भद्र + -कपिलः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकल्पः|भद्रकल्प
भद्र + -कल्पः N. of the present age; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकान्तः|भद्रकान्त
भद्र + -कान्तः a beautiful lover or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकारक
भद्र + -कारक <i>a.</i> propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकाली
भद्र + -काली N. of Durgā; जयन्ती मङ्गला काली भद्रकाली कपालिनी<BR> Durgāpūjāmantra; भद्रकाल्यै पुरुषपशुमालभतापत्यकामः Bhāg. 5. 9. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकाष्ठम्
भद्र + -काष्ठम् the tree called Devadāru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकुम्भः|भद्रकुम्भ|भद्रकुंभ
भद्र + -कुम्भः a golden jar filled with water from a holy place, particularly<BR> from the Ganges (esp. used at the consecration of a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रगणितम्
भद्र + -गणितम् the construction of magical diagrams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रगौरः|भद्रगौर
भद्र + -गौरः N. of a mountain; Mārk. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रघटः|भद्रघट
भद्र + -घटः, -घटकः a vessel from which a lottery is drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रघटकः|भद्रघटक
भद्र + -घटः, -घटकः a vessel from which a lottery is drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रदारु
भद्र + -दारु <i>m., n.</i> a sort of pine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रनामन्
भद्र + -नामन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a wag-tail.<BR>—2 the wood-pecker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रनिधिः|भद्रनिधि
भद्र + -निधिः certain vessels of copper etc. fashioned for gifts; एवं<BR> तु तं भद्रनिधिं सुविद्वान् कृत्वासने प्रावरणोपयुक्ते Vāmana P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रनृपतिः
भद्र + -नृपतिः a gracious king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रपीठम्
भद्र + -पीठम्<BR>—1 a splendid seat, chair of state, throne; औदुम्बरं भद्रपीठमभिषेकार्थमाहृतम्<BR> Rām. 2. 14. 34; उपतस्थुः प्रकृतयो भद्रपीठोपवेशितम् R. 17. 10.<BR>—2 a kind of winged insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रबलनः|भद्रबलन
भद्र + -बलनः an epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुख
भद्र + -मुख <i>a.</i> ‘of an auspicious face’, used as a polite address,<BR> ‘good sir’, ‘gentle sir’; Ś. 7; ततो भद्रमुखात्राहं स्थास्ये स्थाणुरिवाचलः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">Page1184-2</a>]<BR> Mārk. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुखी
भद्र + -मुख + .({@-खी@}) good lady; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुस्तकः|भद्रमुस्तक
भद्र + -मुस्तकः + ({@-मुस्ता@})<BR> Cyperus Rotunda (Mar. नागरमोथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमुस्ता
भद्र + -मुस्तकः + ({@-मुस्ता@})<BR> Cyperus Rotunda (Mar. नागरमोथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रमृगः|भद्रमृग
भद्र + -मृगः an epithet of a particular kind of elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्ररेणुः|भद्ररेणु
भद्र + -रेणुः N. of Indraʼs elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवर्मन्|भद्रवर्म्मन्
भद्र + -वर्मन् <i>m.</i> a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवाच्
भद्र + -वाच् <i>f.</i> a kind or friendly speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रविराज्
भद्र + -विराज् N. of a metre; ओजे तपरौ जरौ गुरुश्चेन् म्सौ ज्गौ भद्रविराट् V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रशाखः|भद्रशाख
भद्र + -शाखः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्रयम्
भद्र + -श्रयम्, -श्रियम् sandalwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्रियम्
भद्र + -श्रयम्, -श्रियम् sandalwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रश्रीः
भद्र + -श्रीः <i>f.</i> the sandal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रसोमा
भद्र + -सोमा an epithet of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रक|भद्रकं|भद्रकः
भद्रक <i>a.</i> (-द्रिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Good, auspicious.<BR>—2 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>—3 Virtuous (सज्जन); विकर्मक्रियया नित्यं बाधन्ते भद्रिकाः प्रजाः Ms. 9. 226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकः|भद्रक|भद्रकं
भद्रक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The Devadāru tree.<BR>—2 A kind of bean; शालिवाहसहस्रं च द्वे शते भद्रकांस्तथा Rām. 2. 32. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रकम्
भद्रक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 N. of a metre of 22 syllables; भ्रौ नरनारनावथ गुरुर्दिगर्कविरसं<BR> हि भद्रकमिदम् V. Ratn.<BR>—2 Cyperus Rotunda (Mar. नागरमोथा).<BR>—3 A particular posture in sitting.<BR>—4 A particular mystic sign.<BR>—5 A harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रंकर|भद्रङ्कर|भद्रङ्करः
भद्रंकर <i>a.</i> One who confers prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवत्|भद्रवन्त्
भद्रवत् <i>a.</i> Auspicious. ━<i>n.</i> The Devadāru tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रवती
भद्रवत् + .{@-ती@} A wanton woman, courtezan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रा
भद्रा<BR>—1 A cow.<BR>—2 N. of the second, seventh, and twelfth days of a lunar fortnight.<BR>—3 The celestial Ganges.<BR>—4 N. of various plants such as अनन्ता, अपरिजाता, कृष्णा, जीवन्ती,<BR> नीली, रास्ना etc.<BR>—5 N. of several goddesses and rivers.<BR>—6 N. of Subhadrā, sister of Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma; पार्थश्चैकोऽहरद्भद्राम्<BR> Mb. 8. 31. 2, 1. 121. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भद्राकरणम्, भद्राश्रयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राकरणम्
भद्रा + -करणम् tonsure, the act of shaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्राश्रयम्
भद्रा + -श्रयम् sandalwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भद्रिका
भद्रिका<BR>—1 An amulet.<BR>—2 = भद्रा (2) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्
भन् €1 P. (भनति)<BR>—1 To worship.<BR>—2 To cry, shout, resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्द्|भंद्
भन्द् I. €1 Ā. (भन्दते)<BR>—1 To tell a good news.<BR>—2 To be glad.<BR>—3 To be fortunate.<BR>—4 To be excellent.<BR>—5 To honour, worship.<BR>—6 To shine. ━II. €10 U. (भन्दयतिते)<BR>—1 To do an auspicious act.<BR>—2 To cause to thrive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दम्
भन्दम्<BR>—1 Prosperity; L. D. B.<BR>—2 Happiness; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भन्दिलम्
भन्दिलम्<BR>—1 Prosperity, good fortune.<BR>—2 Tremulous motion.<BR>—3 A messenger (<i>m.</i> ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभः|भम्भ|भंभ|भम्भः
भंभः<BR>—1 A fly.<BR>—2 Smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभः|भम्भ|भंभ|भम्भः
भंभः + .{@-भः, -भम्@} The mouth of an oven or stove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभम्
भंभः + .{@-भः, -भम्@} The mouth of an oven or stove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभा|भम्भा
भंभः + .{@-भा@} A kettle-drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभरालिका|भम्भरालिका
भंभरालिका, -भंभराली<BR>—1 A gadfly.<BR>—2 A gnat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभराली|भम्भराली
भंभरालिका, -भंभराली<BR>—1 A gadfly.<BR>—2 A gnat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भंभारवः|भम्भारव|भंभारव
भंभारवः The lowing of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयम्
भयम् [बिभेत्यस्मात्, भी-अपादाने अच्]<BR>—1 Fear, alarm, dread, apprehension, (oft. with abl.); भोगे रोगभयं<BR> कुले च्युतिभयं वित्ते नृपालाद्भयम् Bh. 3. 35; यदि समरमपास्य नास्ति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">Page1185-1</a>]<BR> मृत्योर्भयम् Ve. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Fright, terror; जगद्भयम् &c.<BR>—3 A danger, risk, hazard; तावद्भयस्य भेतव्यं यावद्भयमनागतम् ।<BR> आगतं तु भयं वीक्ष्य नरः कुर्याद्यथोचितम् H. 1. 54.<BR>—4 The sentiment of fear; see भयानक below; रौद्रशक्त्या तु जनितं<BR> चित्तवैकल्यजं भयम् S. D. 6.<BR>—5 The blossom of Trapa Bispinosa (Mar. शिंगाडा)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयः|भय|भयं
भयम् + .{@-यः@} Sickness, disease.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भयान्वित, भयाक्रान्त, भयापह, भयातुर, भयार्त, भयावह, भयोत्तर, भयैकप्रवण, भयकम्पः, भयकर, भयडिण्डिमः, भयत्रातृ, भयदर्शिन्, भयद्रुत, भयनाशन, भयप्रतीकारः, भयप्रद, भयप्रस्तावः, भयब्राह्मणः, भयभ्रष्ट, भयविप्लुत, भयव्यूहः, भयशील, भयस्थानम्, भयहेतुः, भयहर्तृ, भयहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1184-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयान्वित
भयम् + -अन्वित, -आक्रान्त <i>a.</i> overcome with fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयाक्रान्त|भयाक्रांत
भयम् + -अन्वित, -आक्रान्त <i>a.</i> overcome with fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयापह|भयापहः
भयम् + -अपह <i>a.</i> warding off or removing fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयापहः|भयापह
भयम् + -अपह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयातुर
भयम् + -आतुर, -आर्त <i>a.</i> afraid, alarmed, frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयार्त|भयार्त्त
भयम् + -आतुर, -आर्त <i>a.</i> afraid, alarmed, frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयावह|भयावहः
भयम् + -आवह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 causing fear, formidable.<BR>—2 risky; स्वघर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः Bg. 3. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयोत्तर
भयम् + -उत्तर <i>a.</i> attended with or succeeded by fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयैकप्रवण
भयम् + -एकप्रवण <i>a.</i> wholly overpowered by fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयकम्पः|भयकम्प
भयम् + -कम्पः tremour of fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयकर
भयम् + -कर (also भयंकर) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 frightening, terrible, fearful.<BR>—2 dangerous, perilous; so भयकारक, -भयकृत्. {@-कृत्@} <i>m.</i><BR> N. of Viṣṇu; भयकृद् भयनाशनः V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयडिण्डिमः|भयडिण्डिम|भयडिंडिम
भयम् + -डिण्डिमः a drum used in battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयत्रातृ
भयम् + -त्रातृ <i>a.</i> a deliverer from fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयदर्शिन्
भयम् + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fearful.<BR>—2 intimidating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयद्रुत|भयद्रुतः
भयम् + -द्रुत <i>a.</i> fleeing from fear, routed, put to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयनाशन|भयनाशनः
भयम् + -नाशन removing fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयनाशनः|भयनाशन
भयम् + -नाशन + .({@-नः@}) N. of Viṣṇu; भयकृद् भयनाशनः V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रतीकारः|भयप्रतीकार
भयम् + -प्रतीकारः warding off or removal of fears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रद
भयम् + -प्रद <i>a.</i> inspiring fear, fearful, terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयप्रस्तावः|भयप्रस्ताव
भयम् + -प्रस्तावः an occasion of fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयब्राह्मणः|भयब्राह्मण
भयम् + -ब्राह्मणः a timid Brāhmaṇa, a Brāhmaṇa who, to save himself<BR> from danger, declares his caste relying on the inviolability of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयभ्रष्ट|भयभ्रष्टः
भयम् + -भ्रष्ट <i>a.</i> put to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयविप्लुत
भयम् + -विप्लुत <i>a.</i> panic-struck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयव्यूहः|भयव्यूह
भयम् + -व्यूहः a particular array of troops when they are threatened<BR> with danger; सर्वतः सर्वतोभद्रं भयव्यूहं प्रकल्पयेत् Kām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयशील
भयम् + -शील <i>a.</i> timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयस्थानम्
भयम् + -स्थानम्, -हेतुः a cause of fear; हर्षस्थानसहस्राणि भयस्थानशतानि<BR> च Mb. 18. 5. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहेतुः|भयहेतु
भयम् + -स्थानम्, -हेतुः a cause of fear; हर्षस्थानसहस्राणि भयस्थानशतानि<BR> च Mb. 18. 5. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहर्तृ
भयम् + -हर्तृ, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> removing fear, dispelling alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयहारिन्
भयम् + -हर्तृ, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> removing fear, dispelling alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयनम्
भयनम् Fear, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयंकर|भयङ्कर|भयङ्करं|भयंकरः
भयंकर <i>a.</i> = भयकर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयंकरः|भयङ्कर|भयंकर|भयङ्करं
भयंकर + .({@-रः@}) A kind of owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानक|भयानकः
भयानक <i>a.</i> [बिभेत्यस्मात्, भी-आन्क्; Uṇ. 3. 82] Fearful, horrible,<BR> terrible, frightful; किमतः परं भयानकं स्यात् U. 2; Śi. 17. 20;<BR> दंष्ट्राकरालानि भयानकानि Bg. 11. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानकः|भयानक
भयानक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A tiger.<BR>—2 N. of Rāhu.<BR>—3 The sentiment of terror, one of the eight or nine sentiments in poetry;<BR> भयानको भयस्थायिभावः कालाधिदैवतः S. D.; see under रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयानकम्
भयानक + .{@-कम्@} Terror, fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भयालु
भयालु <i>a.</i> Timid, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर|भरः
भर <i>a.</i> [भृ-अप्] Bearing, granting, supporting, &c. (at the end of comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरः|भर
भर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A burden, load, weight; खुरत्रये भरं कृत्वा Pt. ‘supporting himself on his three hoofs’<BR>; फलभरपरिणामश्यामजम्बू &c. U. 2. 20; भरव्यथा<BR> Mu. 2. 18; Ki. 11. 5.<BR>—2 A great number, large quantity, collection, multitude; धत्ते भरं<BR> कुसुमपत्रफलावलीनाम् Bv. 1. 94, 54; Śi. 9. 47.<BR>—3 Bulk, mass.<BR>—4 Excess; ततो भक्तिश्रद्धाभरगुरुगृणद्भ्यां गिरिश यत् Śivamahimna 10;<BR> निर्व्यूढसौहृदभरेति गुणोज्ज्वलेति Māl. 6. 17; शोभाभरैः संभृताः<BR> Bv. 1. 103; कोपभरेण Gīt. 3.<BR>—5 A particular measure of weight.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">Page1185-2</a>]<BR>—6 Theft, taking away.<BR>—7 Attacking, a battle (Ved.).<BR>—8 A hymn or song of praise.<BR>—9 Pre-eminence, excellence; न खलु वयसा जात्यैवायं स्वकार्यसहो<BR> भरः V. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरेण
भरेण, भरात् <i>ind.</i> In full measure, with all oneʼs might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरात्
भरेण, भरात् <i>ind.</i> In full measure, with all oneʼs might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरटः|भरट
भरटः [भृ-अटन्]<BR>—1 A potter.<BR>—2 A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण|भरणं|भरणः
भरण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भृ-ल्यु, ल्युट् वा] Bearing, maintaining, supporting, nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणम्
भरण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The act of nourishing, maintaining or supporting; प्रजानां विनयाधानाद्रक्षणाद्भरणादपि<BR> (स पिता) R. 1. 24; पुनर्यास्यत्याख्यां भरत इति लोकस्य भरणात् Ś. 7. 33.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The act of bearing or carrying.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Wearing, putting on; भरणे हि भवान् शक्तः फलानां महतामपि<BR> Rām. 7. 76. 32.<BR>—3 Bringing or procuring.<BR>—4 Nutriment.<BR>—5 Hire, wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणः|भरण|भरणं
भरण + .{@-णः@} The constellation Bharaṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणी
भरणी N. of the second constellation containing three stars.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भरणीभूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरणीभूः
भरणी + -भूः an epithet of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्डः|भरण्ड|भरंड|भरंडः
भरण्डः [भृ-अण्डन्]<BR>—1 A master, lord.<BR>—2 A prince, king.<BR>—3 An ox, a bull.<BR>—4 A worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्यम्
भरण्यम्<BR>—1 Cherishing, supporting, maintaining.<BR>—2 Wages, hire.<BR>—3 The lunar mansion Bharaṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्या
भरण्यम् + .{@-ण्या@}<BR>—1 Wages, hire.<BR>—2 A woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भरण्यभुज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्यभुज्
भरण्यम् + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a hired servant, hireling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरण्युः|भरण्यु
भरण्युः<BR>—1 A master.<BR>—2 A protector.<BR>—3 A friend.<BR>—4 Fire.<BR>—5 The moon.<BR>—6 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतः|भरत
भरतः [भरं तनोति तन्-ड]<BR>—1 N. of the son of Duṣyanta and Śakuntalā, who became a universal<BR> monarch (चक्रवर्तिन्), India being called <i>Bharatavarṣa</i> after<BR> him. He was one of the remote ancestors of the Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas; cf. Ś. 7. 33.<BR>—2 N. of a brother of Rāma, son of Kaikeyī, the youngest wife of Daśaratha.<BR> He was very pious and righteous, and was so much devoted to Rāma that<BR> when the latter prepared to go to the forest in accordance with the wicked<BR> demand of Kaikeyī, he was very much grieved to find that his own mother<BR> had sent his brother into exile, and refusing the sovereignty that was<BR> his own, ruled the kingdom in the name of Rāma (by bringing from him<BR> his two sandals and making them the ‘regents’ of the realm) till he returned<BR> after his fourteen yearsʼ exile. भरतो नाम कैकेय्यां जज्ञे सत्यपराक्रमः ।<BR> साक्षाद्विष्णोश्चतुर्भागः सर्वैः समुदितो गुणैः ॥ Rām. 1. 18. 13.<BR>—3 N. of an ancient sage who is supposed to have been the founder of the<BR> science of music and dramaturgy.<BR>—4 An actor, a stage-player; तत्किमित्युदासते भरताः Māl. 1.<BR>—5 A hired soldier, mercenary.<BR>—6 A barbarian, mountaineer.<BR>—7 An epithet of Agni.<BR>—8 A weaver.<BR>—9 N. of the sage Jaḍabharata.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भरताग्रजः, भरतर्षभः, भरतर्षभः, भरतशार्दूलः, भरतश्रेष्ठः, भरतखण्डम्, भरतज्ञ, भरतपुत्रः, भरतपुत्रकः, भरतवर्षः, भरतवाक्यम्, भरतशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरताग्रजः|भरताग्रज
भरतः + -अग्रजः ‘the elder brother of Bharata’, an epithet of Rāma;<BR> अस्त्येव मन्युर्भरताग्रजे मे R. 14. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतर्षभः|भरतर्षभ
भरतः + -ऋषभः N. of Viśvāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतर्षभः|भरतर्षभ
भरतः + -ऋषभः, -शार्दूलः, -श्रेष्ठः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">Page1186-1</a>]<BR> the best or most distinguished of the descendants of Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतशार्दूलः|भरतशार्दूल
भरतः + -ऋषभः, -शार्दूलः, -श्रेष्ठः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">Page1186-1</a>]<BR> the best or most distinguished of the descendants of Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतश्रेष्ठः|भरतश्रेष्ठ
भरतः + -ऋषभः, -शार्दूलः, -श्रेष्ठः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">Page1186-1</a>]<BR> the best or most distinguished of the descendants of Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1185-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतखण्डम्
भरतः + -खण्डम् N. of a part of India; भरतवर्षे भरतखण्डे जम्बुद्वीपे<BR> दण्डकारण्ये.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतज्ञ
भरतः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the science of Bharata or the dramatic science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतपुत्रः|भरतपुत्र
भरतः + -पुत्रः, -पुत्रकः an actor; a mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतपुत्रकः|भरतपुत्रक|भरतपुत्त्रकः
भरतः + -पुत्रः, -पुत्रकः an actor; a mime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतवर्षः|भरतवर्ष
भरतः + -वर्षः ‘the country of Bharata’, <i>i. e.</i> India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतवाक्यम्
भरतः + -वाक्यम् the last verse or verses in a drama, a sort of benediction<BR> (said to be in honour of Bharata, the founder of the dramatic science);<BR> तथापीदमस्तु भरतवाक्यम् (occurring in every play); cf. Nāg. 5 (<i>end</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरतशास्त्रम्
भरतः + -शास्त्रम् = नाठ्यशास्त्रम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरथः|भरथ
भरथः<BR>—1 A sovereign, king.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 A deity presiding over one of the regions of the world (लोकपाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरद्वाजः|भरद्वाज
भरद्वाजः<BR>—1 N. of one of the seven sages; भरे सुतान् भरे शिष्यान् भरे देवान् भरे<BR> द्विजान् । भरे भार्यां भरद्वाजां भरद्वाजोऽस्मि शोभने ॥ Mb.<BR>—2 A sky-lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरि
भरि <i>a.</i> Bearing, possessing, maintaining, supporting (at the<BR> end of comp.), as in उदरंभरि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिणी
भरिणी Green colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित|भरितः
भरित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Nourished, maintained.<BR>—2 Filled with, full of; जगज्जालं कर्ता कुसुमभरसौरभ्यभरितम् Bv. 1. 54, 33.<BR>—3 Weighted; उत्कम्पोऽल्पोऽपि पीनस्तनभरितमुरः क्षिप्तहारं दुनोति Ve. 2. 22.<BR>—4 Green.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरितः|भरित
भरित + .{@-तः@} The green colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरित्रम्
भरित्रम् Ved. The arm; अंशुं दुहन्ति हस्तिनो भरित्रैः Rv. 3. 36. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरिमन्
भरिमन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Supporting, nourishing.<BR>—2 A family.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुः|भरु
भरुः<BR>—1 A husband.<BR>—2 A lord.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR>—4 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 Gold; Mb. 2.<BR>—6 The sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुकच्छः|भरुकच्छ
भरुकच्छः N. of a country (v. l. मरुकच्छ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुजः|भरुज
भरुजः (-जा or -जी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 A jackal.<BR>—2 Roasted barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भरुटकम्
भरुटकम् Fried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्गः|भर्ग
भर्गः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 Of Brahman.<BR>—3 Radiance, lustre; आदित्यान्तर्गतं वर्चो भर्गाख्यं तन्मुमुक्षुभिः<BR> Yogiyājñavalkya.<BR>—4 Roasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्गस्
भर्गस् <i>n.</i> Radiance, lustre; देवस्य भर्गो मनसेदं जजान<BR> Bhāg. 5. 7. 14; ॐ तत् सवितुर्वरेण्यं भर्गो देवस्य धीमहि Gāyatrīmantra; Rv. 3. 62. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्ग्यः|भर्ग्य
भर्ग्यः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्जन|भर्जनं|भर्ज्जन
भर्जन <i>a.</i> [भ्रस्ज् ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Roasting, frying, baking.<BR>—2 Annihilating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्जनम्
भर्जन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The act of roasting or frying; भर्जनं भवबीजानामर्जनं सुखसंपदाम्<BR> Rāmarakṣā 36.<BR>—2 A frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तव्य|भर्त्तव्य|भर्त्तव्यं
भर्तव्य^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be borne or carried.<BR>—2 To be hired or kept.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृ|भर्त्तृ
भर्तृ <i>m.</i> [भृ-तृच्]<BR>—1 A husband; यद्भर्तुरेव हितमिच्छति तत् कलत्रम् Bh. 2. 8; स्त्रीणां<BR> भर्ता धर्मदाराश्च पुंसाम् Māl. 6. 18.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">Page1186-2</a>]<BR>—2 A lord, master, superior; भर्तुः शापेन Me. 1; गण˚, भूत˚ &c.<BR>—3 A leader, commander, chief; स्वभर्तृनामग्रहणाद्बभूव सान्द्रे रजस्यात्मपरावबोधः R. 7. 41.<BR>—4 A supporter, bearer, protector; भर्ता स्वानां श्रेष्ठः पुर एता भवति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 18.<BR>—5 The creator.<BR>—6 N. of Viṣṇu; सवनो भावनो भर्ता V. Sah.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भर्तृगुणः, भर्तृघ्नी, भर्तृचित्त, भर्तृदारकः, भर्तृदारिका, भर्तृदेवता, भर्तृदैवता, भर्तृप्रिय, भर्तृभक्त, भर्तृलोकः, भर्तृव्रतम्, भर्तृशोकः, भर्तृहरिः, भर्तृहार्यधन, भर्तृहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृगुणः|भर्तृगुण
भर्तृ + -गुणः the excellence or virtue of a husband; उत्कर्षं योषितः<BR> प्राप्ताः स्वैः स्वैर्भर्तृगुणैः शुभैः Ms. 9. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृघ्नी|भर्त्तृघ्नी
भर्तृ + -घ्नी a woman who murders her husband; पाषण्ड्यानाश्रितास्तेना भर्तृघ्न्यः<BR> कामगादिकाः Y. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृचित्त
भर्तृ + -चित्त <i>a.</i> thinking of a husband; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृदारकः|भर्तृदारक|भर्त्तृदारक|भर्त्तृदारकः
भर्तृ + -दारकः a crown-prince, prince royal, young prince, an heir-apparent<BR> (a term of address chiefly used in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृदारिका|भर्त्तृदारिका
भर्तृ + -दारिका a young princess (a term of address in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृदेवता
भर्तृ + -देवता, -दैवता idolizing a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृदैवता
भर्तृ + -देवता, -दैवता idolizing a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृप्रिय
भर्तृ + -प्रिय, -भक्त <i>a.</i> devoted to oneʼs master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृभक्त
भर्तृ + -प्रिय, -भक्त <i>a.</i> devoted to oneʼs master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृलोकः|भर्तृलोक
भर्तृ + -लोकः the husbandʼs world; पतिं या नाभिचरति मनोवाग्देहसंयता ।<BR> सा भर्तृलोकमाप्नोति Ms. 5. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृव्रतम्
भर्तृ + -व्रतम् fidelity or devotion to a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृव्रता
भर्तृ + -व्रतम् + .({@-ता@}) a virtuous and devoted wife; cf. पतिव्रता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृशोकः|भर्तृशोक
भर्तृ + -शोकः grief for the death of the husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृहरिः|भर्तृहरि|भर्त्तृहरि|भर्त्तृहरिः
भर्तृ + -हरिः N. of a celebrated author to whom are ascribed the three<BR> Śatakas (शृङ्गार, नीति and वैराग्य) and also वाक्यपदीय<BR> and भट्टिकाव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृहार्यधन
भर्तृ + -हार्यधन <i>a.</i> (a slave) whose possessions may be taken by<BR> his master; न हि तस्यास्ति किंचित् स्वं भर्तृहार्यधनो हि सः Ms. 8. 417.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृहीन
भर्तृ + -हीन <i>a.</i> abandoned by a master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृत्वम्
भर्तृत्वम्<BR>—1 Masterhood.<BR>—2 Husbandship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृमती
भर्तृमती A married woman whose husband is living; जनोऽन्यथा भर्तृमतीं<BR> विशङ्कते Ś. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृसात्
भर्तृसात् <i>ind.</i> In the possession of a husband; ˚कृता married; Y.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्री
भर्त्री<BR>—1 A mother.<BR>—2 A female supporter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्स्
भर्त्स् €10 Ā. (भर्त्सयते; P. also sometimes)<BR>—1 To menace, threaten.<BR>—2 To revile, reproach, abuse.<BR>—3 To deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सकः|भर्त्सक
भर्त्सकः [भर्त्स्-ण्वुल्] A threatener, reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सनम्
भर्त्सनम्, -भर्त्सना<BR> [भर्त्स् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Threatening, reviling.<BR>—2 A threat, menace.<BR>—3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>—4 A curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सना
भर्त्सनम्, -भर्त्सना<BR> [भर्त्स् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Threatening, reviling.<BR>—2 A threat, menace.<BR>—3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>—4 A curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सित
भर्त्सित <i>p. p.</i> Reviled, reproached, abused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्त्सितम्
भर्त्सित + .{@-तम्@} Reviling &c. See भर्त्सन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्मम्
भर्मम्<BR>—1 Wages, hire.<BR>—2 Gold.<BR>—3 The navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्मण्या|भर्म्मण्या
भर्मण्या Wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्म्
भर्म्(र्व्) €1 P. To kill, to hurt; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्व्
भर्म्(र्व्) €1 P. To kill, to hurt; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्मन्|भर्म्मन्
भर्मन् <i>n.</i> [भृ-मनिन्]<BR>—1 Support, maintenance, nourishment; कुमारभृत्याकुशलैरनुष्ठिते भिषग्भिराप्तैरथ<BR> गर्भभर्मणि R. 3. 12.<BR>—2 Wages, hire.<BR>—3 Gold.<BR>—4 Gold coin.<BR>—5 The navel.<BR>—6 A burden, load.<BR>—7 A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्
भल् I. €10 Ā. (भालयते, भालित) To see, behold. ━II. €1 Ā.<BR>—1 See भल्ल्.<BR>—2 To expound, explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल
भल <i>ind.</i> (Vedic) Certainly, indeed; cf. Mar. भलें.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1186-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल्
भल्ल् €1 Ā. (भल्लते, भल्लित)<BR>—1 To describe, narrate, tell.<BR>—2 To wound, hurt, kill. —3 To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ल|भल्लं|भल्लः
भल्ल <i>a.</i> Auspicious, favourable.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भल्लाक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लाक्षः|भल्लाक्ष
भल्ल + -अक्षः = भद्राक्षः a term used for addressing a flamingo; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लः|भल्ल|भल्लं
भल्लः, -ल्ली, -ल्लम्<BR> [भल्ल्-अच्] A kind of crescent-shaped missile or<BR> arrow; क्षुरार्धचन्द्रोत्तमकर्णभल्लैः शरांश्च चिच्छेद Rām. 6. 59. 99;<BR> क्वचिदाकर्णविकृष्टभल्लवर्षी R. 9. 66, 4. 63, 7. 58.<BR>—2 A particular part of an arrow; विष्णुं सोमं हुताशं च तस्येषुं समकल्पयन् ।<BR> शृङ्गमग्निर्बभूवास्य भल्लः सोमो विशांपते ॥ Mb. 8. 34. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्ली
भल्लः, -ल्ली, -ल्लम्<BR> [भल्ल्-अच्] A kind of crescent-shaped missile or<BR> arrow; क्षुरार्धचन्द्रोत्तमकर्णभल्लैः शरांश्च चिच्छेद Rām. 6. 59. 99;<BR> क्वचिदाकर्णविकृष्टभल्लवर्षी R. 9. 66, 4. 63, 7. 58.<BR>—2 A particular part of an arrow; विष्णुं सोमं हुताशं च तस्येषुं समकल्पयन् ।<BR> शृङ्गमग्निर्बभूवास्य भल्लः सोमो विशांपते ॥ Mb. 8. 34. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लम्
भल्लः, -ल्ली, -ल्लम्<BR> [भल्ल्-अच्] A kind of crescent-shaped missile or<BR> arrow; क्षुरार्धचन्द्रोत्तमकर्णभल्लैः शरांश्च चिच्छेद Rām. 6. 59. 99;<BR> क्वचिदाकर्णविकृष्टभल्लवर्षी R. 9. 66, 4. 63, 7. 58.<BR>—2 A particular part of an arrow; विष्णुं सोमं हुताशं च तस्येषुं समकल्पयन् ।<BR> शृङ्गमग्निर्बभूवास्य भल्लः सोमो विशांपते ॥ Mb. 8. 34. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लः|भल्ल|भल्लं
भल्लः, -ल्ली, -ल्लम् + .{@-ल्लः@}<BR>—1 A bear.<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 The marking-nut-plant (भल्ली also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लकः|भल्लक
भल्लकः, भल्लाटः A bear; Bhāg. 3. 10. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लाटः|भल्लाट|भल्लाटं
भल्लकः, भल्लाटः A bear; Bhāg. 3. 10. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातः|भल्लात
भल्लातः, भल्लातकः The marking-nut-plant. (Mar. बिब्बा);<BR> भल्लातकं फलं पक्वं स्वादुपाकरसं लघु । कषायं पाचनं स्निग्धं<BR> तीक्ष्णोष्णं छेदि भेदनम् । मेध्यं वह्निकरं हन्ति कफवातव्रणोदरम्<BR> Bhāva P.; Bhāg. 8. 2. 14; (also <i>n.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लातकः|भल्लातक
भल्लातः, भल्लातकः The marking-nut-plant. (Mar. बिब्बा);<BR> भल्लातकं फलं पक्वं स्वादुपाकरसं लघु । कषायं पाचनं स्निग्धं<BR> तीक्ष्णोष्णं छेदि भेदनम् । मेध्यं वह्निकरं हन्ति कफवातव्रणोदरम्<BR> Bhāva P.; Bhāg. 8. 2. 14; (also <i>n.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लुकः|भल्लुक
भल्लुकः<BR>—1 A bear.<BR>—2 A monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भल्लूकः|भल्लूक
भल्लूकः<BR>—1 A bear; दधति कुहरभाजामत्र भल्लूकयूनाम् U. 2. 21;<BR>—2 A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव|भवं|भवः
भव <i>a.</i> [भवत्यस्मात्, भू-अपादाने अप्] (At the end of comp.)<BR> Arising or produced from, originating in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवः|भव|भवं
भव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Being, state of being, existence, (सत्ता); तथाप्यहं योषिदतत्त्वविच्च<BR> ते दीना दिदृक्षे भव मे भवक्षितिम् Bhāg. 4. 3. 11.<BR>—2 Birth, production; भवो हि लोकाभ्युदयाय तादृशाम् R. 3. 14; Ś. 7. 27.<BR>—3 Source, origin.<BR>—4 Wordly existence; mundane or worldly life, life; as in भवार्णव,<BR> भवसागर &c.; कर्मबन्धच्छिदं धर्मं भवस्येव मुमुक्षवः Ku. 2. 51;<BR> भवोच्छेदकरः पिता ते R. 14. 74; Śi. 1. 35.<BR>—5 The world.<BR>—6 Well-being, health, prosperity; भवाय युष्मच्चरणानुवर्तिनाम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 27. 9; कालेनानुगृहीतैस्तैर्यावद्वो भव आत्मनः Bhāg. 8. 6. 19;<BR> Rām. 5. 27. 6.<BR>—7 Excellence, superiority.<BR>—8 N. of Śiva; तमब्रवीद् भवोऽसीति तद्यदस्य तन्नामाकरोत पार्जन्यं<BR> तद्रूपमभवत् पर्जन्यो वै भवः Śat. Br.; दक्षस्य कन्या भवपूर्वपत्नी<BR> Ku. 1. 21, 3. 72.<BR>—9 A god, deity.<BR>—10 Acquisition (प्राप्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवौ
भव + .{@-वौ@} (dual) Śiva and Bhavānī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भवाग्रम्, भवातिग, भवान्तकृत्, भवान्तरम्, भवाब्धिः, भवार्णवः, भवसमुद्रः, भवसागरः, भवसिन्धुः, भवाभवौ, भवाभीष्टम्, भवायना, भवायनी, भवारण्यम्, भवात्मजः, भवार्त, भवेशः, भवोच्छेदः, भवक्षितिः, भवघस्मरः, भवच्छिद्, भवच्छेदः, भवजलम्, भवदारु, भवनाशिनी, भवप्रतिसंधिः, भवबन्धेशः, भवभङ्गः, भवभाज्, भवभावन, भवभीरु, भवभूतम्, भवभूतिः, भवभोगः, भवमन्युः, भवमोचनः, भवरुद्, भववीतिः, भवव्ययः, भवशेखरः, भवसंगिन्, भवसंततिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाग्रम्
भव + -अग्रम् the farthest end of the world; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवातिग
भव + -अतिग <i>a.</i> overcoming worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवान्तकृत्|भवांतकृत्
भव + -अन्तकृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of Buddha.<BR>—2 an epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवान्तरम्
भव + -अन्तरम् another existence (previous or future); शुभाशुभफलं<BR> सद्यो नृपाद्देवाद्भवान्तरे Pt. 1. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाब्धिः|भवाब्धि
भव + -अब्धिः, -अर्णवः, -समुद्रः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः the ocean of worldly life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवार्णवः|भवार्णव
भव + -अब्धिः, -अर्णवः, -समुद्रः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः the ocean of worldly life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवसमुद्रः|भवसमुद्र
भव + -अब्धिः, -अर्णवः, -समुद्रः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः the ocean of worldly life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवसागरः|भवसागर
भव + -अब्धिः, -अर्णवः, -समुद्रः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः the ocean of worldly life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवसिन्धुः|भवसिन्धु|भवसिंधु
भव + -अब्धिः, -अर्णवः, -समुद्रः, -सागरः, -सिन्धुः the ocean of worldly life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाभवौ
भव + -अभवौ (<i>m.</i> dual)<BR>—1 existence.<BR>—2 prosperity and adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवाभीष्टम्
भव + -अभीष्टम् bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवायना
भव + -अयना, -अयनी the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवायनी
भव + -अयना, -अयनी the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवारण्यम्
भव + -अरण्यम् ‘a forest of worldly life’, a dreary world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवात्मजः|भवात्मज
भव + -आत्मजः an epithet of Gaṇeśa or Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवार्त
भव + -आर्त <i>a.</i> sick of the world, disgusted with worldly cares and troubles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवेशः|भवेश
भव + -ईशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवोच्छेदः|भवोच्छेद
भव + -उच्छेदः destruction of worldly existence; सतां भवोच्छेदकरः<BR> पिता ते R. 14. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवक्षितिः|भवक्षिति
भव + -क्षितिः <i>f.</i> the place of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवघस्मरः|भवघस्मर
भव + -घस्मरः a forest-conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवच्छिद्
भव + -छिद् <i>a.</i> cutting the (bonds of) wordly life, preventing recurrence of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">Page1187-2</a>]<BR> birth; भवच्छिदस्त्र्यम्बकपादपांशवः K. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवच्छेदः|भवच्छेद
भव + -छेदः prevention of recurring birth; मनुष्यजन्मापि सुरासुरान्<BR> गुणैर्भवान् भवच्छेदकरैः करोत्यधः Śi. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवजलम्
भव + -जलम् the water (or ocean) of worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदारु
भव + -दारु <i>n.</i> the <i>devadāru</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनाशिनी
भव + -नाशिनी N. of the river Sarayū.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवप्रतिसंधिः|भवप्रतिसन्धि
भव + -प्रतिसंधिः coming into being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवबन्धेशः|भवबन्धेश
भव + -बन्धेशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभङ्गः|भवभङ्ग
भव + -भङ्गः delivery from births or transmigration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभाज्
भव + -भाज् <i>a.</i> living in the world of mortals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभावन
भव + -भावन <i>a.</i> conferring welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभीरु
भव + -भीरु <i>a.</i> afraid of worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभूतम्
भव + -भूतम् the source of all beings, <i>i. e.</i> the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभूतिः|भवभूति
भव + -भूतिः N. of a celebrated poet (see App. II.); भवभूतेः संबन्धाद्<BR> भूधरभूरेव भारती भाति । एतत्कृतकारुण्ये किमन्यथा रोदिति ग्रावा ॥<BR> Āryā. S. 36. ━(<i>f.</i>) welfare, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभोगः|भवभोग
भव + -भोगः the enjoyment or pleasure of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवमन्युः|भवमन्यु
भव + -मन्युः the resentment against the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवमोचनः|भवमोचन
भव + -मोचनः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवरुद्
भव + -रुद् <i>m.</i> a drum beaten at funeral ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भववीतिः|भववीति
भव + -वीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 liberation from worldly existence; भववीतये हतबृहत्तमसामवबोधवारि<BR> रजसः शमनम् Ki. 6. 41.<BR>—2 end of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवव्ययः|भवव्यय
भव + -व्ययः (du.) birth and dissolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवशेखरः|भवशेखर
भव + -शेखरः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवसंगिन्|भवसङ्गिन्
भव + -संगिन् <i>a.</i> attached to worldly existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवसंततिः|भवसन्तति
भव + -संततिः an uninterrupted series of births and transmigrations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवक|भवकः
भवक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living, existing.<BR>—2 Giving a blessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवत्|भवन्त्
भवत् <i>a.</i> (-न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Being, becoming, happening.<BR>—2 Present; समतीतं च भवच्च भावि च R. 8. 78. ━<i>pron. a.</i><BR>.(-ती <i>f.</i>) A respectful or honorific pronoun, translated by<BR> ‘your honour’, ‘your lordship, worship or highness’; (oft. used in the<BR> sense of the second personal pronoun, but with the third person of the<BR> verb); अथवा कथं भवान् मन्यते M. 1; भवन्त एव जानन्ति रघूणां<BR> च कुलस्थितिम् U. 5. 23; R. 2. 40, 3. 48, 5. 16. It is often joined to<BR> अत्र or तत्र (see the words), and sometimes to स also; यन्मां<BR> विधेयविषये सभवान्नियुङ्क्ते Māl. 1. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भवद्भूतभव्ये, भवद्वसु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवद्भूतभव्ये
भवत् + -भूतभव्ये <i>ind.</i> in present, past and future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवद्वसु
भवत् + -वसु <i>a.</i> wealthy, opulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवती
भवती<BR>—1 Your ladyship, lady.<BR>—2 A poisoned arrow.<BR>—3 Shining; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनम्
भवनम् [भू-आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Being, existence.<BR>—2 Production, birth.<BR>—3 An abode, residence, dwelling, mansion; अथवा भवनप्रत्ययात् प्रविष्टोऽस्मि<BR> Mk. 3; Me. 34; Rām. 7. 11. 50.<BR>—4 A site, abode, receptacle; as in अविनयभवनम् Pt. 1. 191.<BR>—5 A building.<BR>—6 A field; स शालिभवनं रम्यं सर्वसस्यसमाचितम् Mb. 5. 84. 15.<BR>—7 Nature.<BR>—8 Horoscope, natal star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनः|भवन|भवनं
भवनम् + .{@-नः@} A dog.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भवनोदरम्, भवनद्वारम्, भवनपतिः, भवनस्वामिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनोदरम्
भवनम् + -उदरम् the interior of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनद्वारम्
भवनम् + -द्वारम् a palace-gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनपतिः|भवनपति
भवनम् + -पतिः, -स्वामिन् <i>m.</i> the lord of the house, a <i>pater familias</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनस्वामिन्
भवनम् + -पतिः, -स्वामिन् <i>m.</i> the lord of the house, a <i>pater familias</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवनीय|भवनीयं
भवनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be about to take place.<BR>—2 Impending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्तः|भवन्त|भवंत|भवंतः
भवन्तः, -न्तिः<BR> The time being, present time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्तिः|भवन्ति|भवंति|भवंतिः
भवन्तः, -न्तिः<BR> The time being, present time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवन्ती
भवन्ती<BR>—1 A virtuous wife.<BR>—2 Time being, present time; Uṇ. 3. 50.<BR>—3 (In gram.) A technical term for the present tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1187-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानी
भवानी N. of Pārvatī, wife of Śiva; आलम्बताग्रकरमत्र भवो<BR> भवान्याः Ki. 5. 29; Ku. 7. 84; Me. 38, 46; भवानि स्तोतुं त्वां प्रभवति<BR> चतुर्भिर्न वदनैः । प्रजानामीशानस्त्रिपुरमथनः पञ्चभिरपि ॥ Ānandalaharī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भवानीगुरुः, भवानीपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानीगुरुः|भवानीगुरु
भवानी + -गुरुः an epithet of the mountain Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवानीपतिः|भवानीपति
भवानी + -पतिः an epithet of Śiva; अधिवसति सदा यदेनं जनैरविदितविभवो<BR> भवानीपतिः Ki. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृक्ष|भवादृक्षः
भवादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), भवादृश् <i>a.</i>, भवादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Like your honour, like you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृक्षी
भवादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), भवादृश् <i>a.</i>, भवादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Like your honour, like you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृश्
भवादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), भवादृश् <i>a.</i>, भवादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Like your honour, like you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृश|भवादृशः
भवादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), भवादृश् <i>a.</i>, भवादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Like your honour, like you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवादृशी
भवादृक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), भवादृश् <i>a.</i>, भवादृश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Like your honour, like you.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविक|भविकं
भविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Beneficial, suitable, useful.<BR>—2 Happy, prosperous.<BR>—3 Righteous, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविकम्
भविक + .{@-कम्@} Prosperity, welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्य|भवितव्यं
भवितव्य <i>pot. p.</i> About to take place, about to happen, likely<BR> to be, often used like भाव्य impersonally, <i>i. e.</i> in the neuter<BR> gender and singular number, with the instrumental of the subject and the<BR> predicative word; त्वया मम सहायेन भवितव्यम् Ś. 2; गुरुणा कारणेन<BR> भवितव्यम् Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्यम्
भवितव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} What is destined to happen; भवितव्यं भवत्येव यद्विधेर्मनसि<BR> स्थितम् Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितव्यता
भवितव्यता Inevitable necessity, necessary consequence, fate, destiny;<BR> भवितव्यता बलवती Ś. 6; सर्वंकषा भगवती भवितव्यतैव Māl. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवितृ
भवितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भू-तृच्]<BR>—1 About to become, future; सा व्यत्यगादन्यवधूर्भवित्री R. 6. 52;<BR> समादिदेशैकवधूं भवित्रीम् Ku. 1. 50.<BR>—2 Imminent, impending.<BR>—3 Being or faring well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविन्
भविन् <i>a.</i> Living, being. ━<i>m.</i> A living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविनः|भविन
भविनः A poet; also भविनिन् <i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविल|भविलः
भविल <i>a.</i> [भू-भविष्यति इलच्]<BR>—1 Being, living.<BR>—2 Future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविलः|भविल
भविल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A paramour.<BR>—2 A sensualist, voluptuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविलम्
भविल + .{@-लम्@} A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्णु|भविष्णुः
भविष्णु [भू-इष्णुच्]<BR>—1 To be about to become or take place.<BR>—2 Future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्य|भविष्यः
भविष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Future; नैतदन्ये करिष्यन्ति भविष्या वसुधाधिपाः Mb. 14. 87. 21.<BR>—2 Imminent, impending; श्रुत्वा सांग्रामिकीं वार्तां भविष्यां स्वामिनं<BR> प्रति Pt. 1. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यम्
भविष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} The future, futurity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भविष्यकालः, भविष्यज्ञानम्, भविष्यपुराणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यकालः|भविष्यकाल
भविष्य + -कालः the future tense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यज्ञानम्
भविष्य + -ज्ञानम् knowledge of futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यपुराणम्
भविष्य + -पुराणम् N. of one of the 18 Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यत्|भविष्यन्त्
भविष्यत् <i>a.</i> (-ती or -न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> About to be, become or come to pass, future. ━<i>n.</i><BR> The future time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भविष्यदाक्षेपः, भविष्यत्कालः, भविष्यद्वक्तृ, भविष्यद्वादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यदाक्षेपः|भविष्यदाक्षेप
भविष्यत् + -आक्षेपः<BR>—1 denying the occurrence of a possible future event.<BR>—2 a kind of Alaṅkāra or figure of speech; सोऽयं भविष्यदाक्षेपः<BR> प्रागेवातिमनस्विनी । कदाचिदपराधोऽस्य भावीत्येवमरुन्द्ध यत् ॥ Kāv. 2. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यत्कालः|भविष्यत्काल
भविष्यत् + -कालः futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यद्वक्तृ
भविष्यत् + -वक्तृ, -वादिन् <i>a.</i> predicting future events, prophesying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भविष्यद्वादिन्
भविष्यत् + -वक्तृ, -वादिन् <i>a.</i> predicting future events, prophesying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्य|भव्यं|भव्यः
भव्य <i>a.</i> [भू-कर्तरि नि˚ यत्] ‘भव्यं सुखे शुभे चापि भेद्यवद्योग्यभाविनोः’ Viśva.<BR>—1 Existing, being, being present.<BR>—2 Future, about to be; ईशानं भूतभव्यस्य न ततो विजुगुप्सते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-2" target="_blank">Page1188-2</a>]<BR> Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 15.<BR>—3 Likely to become.<BR>—4 Suitable, proper, fit, worthy; इति त्याज्ये भवे भव्यो मुक्तावुत्तिष्ठते<BR> जनः Ki. 11. 13; यत्पादपद्ममभवाय भजन्ति भव्याः Bhāg. 1. 15. 17.<BR>—5 Good, nice, excellent.<BR>—6 Auspicious, fortunate, happy; समाधिमत्यामुदपादि भव्या Ku. 1. 22;<BR> अनुग्रहायेह चरन्ति नूनं भूतानि भव्यानि जनार्दनस्य Bhāg. 3. 5. 3;<BR> Ki. 3. 12, 10. 51.<BR>—7 Handsome, lovely, beautiful; मृदुश्च स्थिरचित्तश्च सदाभव्योऽनसूयकः<BR> Rām. 2. 2. 32.<BR>—8 Calm, tranquil, placid; भव्यो भवन्नपि मुनेरिह शासनेन (क्षात्रे<BR> स्थितः पथि) Ki. 5. 49.<BR>—9 True.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्या
भव्य + .{@-व्या@} N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्यम्
भव्य + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 Existence.<BR>—2 Future time.<BR>—3 Result, fruit.<BR>—4 Good result, prosperity; R. 17. 53.<BR>—5 A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्यः|भव्य|भव्यं
भव्य + .{@-व्यः, -व्यम्@} one division of the poetical Rasas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भव्यमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्यम्
भव्य + .{@-व्यः, -व्यम्@} one division of the poetical Rasas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भव्यमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भव्यमनस्
भव्य + -मनस् <i>a.</i> well-meaning, benevolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवदीय|भवदीयं
भवदीय <i>a.</i> Your honourʼs, your, thine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्क|भावत्कः
भावत्क <i>a.</i> Belonging to your honour; भावत्कौरिव धवलैर्यशःप्रवाहैः<BR> केषां नो जनयति चेतसि प्रमोदम् Rām. Ch. 7. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भष्
भष् €1 P. (भषति)<BR>—1 To bark, growl, bark at; नैषादिं श्वा समालक्ष्य भषंस्तस्थौ तदन्तिके<BR> Mb. 1. 132. 39.<BR>—2 To abuse, reproach, revile, rail at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1188-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

