भाद्री
भाद्रपदी, भाद्री The day of full moon in the month of Bhādrapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाद्रमातुरः|भाद्रमातुर
भाद्रमातुरः The son of a virtuous or good mother (भद्रमातुरपत्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानम्
भानम् [भा-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Appearing, being visible.<BR>—2 Light, lustre.<BR>—3 Perception, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानतस्
भानतस् <i>ind.</i> In consequence of the appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानव
भानव <i>a.</i> Peculiar to the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानवी
भानव + .{@-वी@} A kind of pace (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानवीयम्
भानवीयम् The right eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुः|भानु
भानुः [भा-नु Uṇ. 3. 32]<BR>—1 Light, lustre, brightness.<BR>—2 A ray of light; मण्डिताखिलदिक्प्रान्ताश्चण्डांशोः पान्तु भानवः Bv. 1. 129;<BR> Śi. 2. 53; Ms. 8. 132.<BR>—3 The sun; भानुः सकृद्युक्ततुरङ्ग एव Ś. 5. 4; भीमभानौ निदाघे Bv. 1. 30.<BR>—4 Beauty.<BR>—5 A day.<BR>—6 A king, prince, sovereign.<BR>—7 An epithet of Śiva or Viṣṇu; अमृतांशूद्भवो भानुः V. Sah. ━<i>f.</i><BR> A handsome woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भानुकेशरः, भानुकेसरः, भानुजः, भानुदिनम्, भानुवारः, भानुफला, भानुभूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुकेशरः|भानुकेशर
भानुः + -केशरः, -केसरः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुकेसरः|भानुकेसर
भानुः + -केशरः, -केसरः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुजः|भानुज
भानुः + -जः the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुदिनम्
भानुः + -दिनम्, -वारः Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुवारः|भानुवार
भानुः + -दिनम्, -वारः Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुफला
भानुः + -फला Musa Sapientum (Mar. केळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुभूः
भानुः + -भूः daughter of the sun, the Yamunā river; अह्नि भानुभुवि दाशदारिकाम् N. 18. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1191-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुमत्|भानुमन्त्
भानुमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Luminous, bright, splendid.<BR>—2 Beautiful, handsome. ━<i>m.</i> The sun; तुल्येऽपराधे स्वर्भानुर्भानुमन्तं<BR> चिरेण यत् Śi. 2. 49; Ku. 3. 65; R. 6. 36; Ṛs. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भानुमती
भानुमत् + .{@-ती@} N. of the wife of Duryodhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाम्
भाम् €1 Ā. (भामते) To be angry; (also €10 P. according to L. D. B.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामः|भाम
भामः [भाम्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Brightness, lustre, splendour.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 Passion, wrath, anger.<BR>—4 A sisterʼs husband; अहो भगिन्यहो भाम मया वां बत पाप्मना । पुरुषाद<BR> इवापत्यं बहवो हिंसिताः सुताः ॥ Bhāg. 10. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामा
भामः + .{@-मा@}<BR>—1 A passionate woman.<BR>—2 N. of one of the wives of Kṛṣṇa, usually called सत्यभामा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भामनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामनी
भामः + -नी <i>m.</i> the Supreme Being; एष उ एव भामनीरेष हि सर्वेषु<BR> लोकेषु भाति य एवं वेद Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिन्
भामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Passionate, angry.<BR>—2 Shining.<BR>—3 Handsome, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिनी
भामिनी<BR>—1 A beautiful young woman; (कामिनी); क्षितिरिन्दुमती च भामिनी पतिमासाद्य<BR> तमग्ग्यपौरुषम् R. 8. 28.<BR>—2 A passionate woman (often used like चण्डी as a term of endearment);<BR> उपचीयत एव कापि शोभा परितो भामिनि ते मुखस्य नित्यम् Bv. 2. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भामिनीविलासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामिनीविलासः|भामिनीविलास
भामिनी + -विलासः N. of a poem by Jagannātha Paṇḍita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामकः|भामक
भामकः A sisterʼs husband; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भामहः|भामह
भामहः N. of the author of अलङ्कारशास्त्र and प्राकृतमनोरमा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारः|भार
भारः [भृ-घञ्]<BR>—1 A load, burden, weight (fig. also); कुचभारानमिता न योषितः Bh. 3. 27;<BR> so श्रोणीभार Me. 84; भारः कायो जीवितं वज्रकीलम् Māl. 9. 37.<BR>—2 Brunt, thickest part (as of a battle); N. 5. 5.<BR>—3 Excess, pitch; सा मुक्तकण्ठं व्यसनातिभाराच्चक्रन्द R. 14. 68.<BR>—4 Labour, toil, trouble.<BR>—5 A mass, large quantity; विष्वग्वृत्तिर्जटानां प्रचलति निबिडग्रन्थिबद्धोऽपि<BR> भारः Māl. 5. 4. कुच˚, जटा˚.<BR>—6 A particular weight equal to 2000 <i>palas</i> of gold; कृतं भारसहस्रस्य<BR> शूलं कालायसं महत् Rām. 6. 67. 63.<BR>—7 A yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>—8 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—9 Task imposed on anyone; आनुकूल्येन कार्याणामन्तरं संविधीयते ।<BR> भारं हि रथकारस्य न व्यवस्यन्ति पण्डिताः ॥ Mb. 4. 49. 4.<BR>—10 A particular manner of beating a drum.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भारावतरण, भारावतारणम्, भाराक्रान्त, भाराक्रान्ता, भारोद्धरणम्, भारोद्वहः, भारोपजीवनम्, भारोढिः, भारगः, भारभृत्, भारयष्टिः, भारवाह, भारवाहः, भारवाहनः, भारवाहिकः, भारसह, भारसाह, भारसाहः, भारसाधन, भारहरः, भारहारः, भारहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारावतरण
भारः + -अवतरण, -अवतारणम् the removal of a load from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारावतारणम्
भारः + -अवतरण, -अवतारणम् the removal of a load from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाराक्रान्त|भाराक्रांत
भारः + -आक्रान्त <i>a.</i> heavily laden, over-burdened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाराक्रान्ता
भारः + -आक्रान्ता N. of a metre; भाराक्रान्ता मभनरसना गुरुः श्रुतिरसहयैः Chand. M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोद्धरणम्
भारः + -उद्धरणम् The lifting of a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोद्वहः|भारोद्वह
भारः + -उद्वहः a porter, burden-carrier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोपजीवनम्
भारः + -उपजीवनम् living by carrying burdens, a porterʼs life; वरं<BR> भारोपजीवनम् Pt. 1. 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारोढिः|भारोढि
भारः + -ऊढिः <i>f.</i> the bearing of a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारगः|भारग
भारः + -गः a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारभृत्
भारः + -भृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu; भारभृत् कथितो योगी V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारयष्टिः|भारयष्टि
भारः + -यष्टिः a pole for carrying burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारयष्टिधरः
भारः + -यष्टिः + ˚धरः one who carries<BR> loads suspended at the two ends of a pole borne on the shoulder (Mar.<BR> काबडधारी); भारयष्टिधरैश्चापि पुरुषैर्विष्टिकारिभिः Śiva B. 30. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाह|भारवाहः
भारः + -वाह <i>a.</i> (भारौही <i>f.</i>)<BR> bearer of burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहः|भारवाह
भारः + -वाहः a burden-carrier, porter; भारवाहस्य पन्थाः Mb. 3. 133. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाही
भारः + -वाहः + .({@-ही@})<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">Page1192-2</a>]<BR> indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहनः|भारवाहन
भारः + -वाहनः a beast of burden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहनम्
भारः + -वाहनः + .({@-नम्@}) a cart, waggon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवाहिकः|भारवाहिक
भारः + -वाहिकः a porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारसह
भारः + -सह, -साह <i>a.</i> ‘able to carry a great load’, very strong<BR> or powerful; विकृष्य चापं समरे भारसाहमनुत्तमम् Mb. 6. 74. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारसाह|भारसाहः
भारः + -सह, -साह <i>a.</i> ‘able to carry a great load’, very strong<BR> or powerful; विकृष्य चापं समरे भारसाहमनुत्तमम् Mb. 6. 74. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारसाहः|भारसाह
भारः + -साहः an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारसाधन
भारः + -साधन <i>a.</i> effecting arduous works, accomplishing great objects;<BR> कार्मुकैर्भारसाधनैः Mb. 2. 99. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहरः|भारहर
भारः + -हरः, -हारः a burden-bearer, porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहारः|भारहार
भारः + -हरः, -हारः a burden-bearer, porter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारहारिन्
भारः + -हारिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारक|भारकः
भारक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Loaded with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारकः|भारक
भारक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A load, burden, weight.<BR>—2 A particular weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारायते
भारायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To become a burden, form a load.<BR>—2 To be like a load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिक|भारिकः
भारिक, भारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bearing or carrying a load.<BR>—2 Heavy. ━<i>m.</i> A burden-carrier, porter; Ms. 2. 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिन्
भारिक, भारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bearing or carrying a load.<BR>—2 Heavy. ━<i>m.</i> A burden-carrier, porter; Ms. 2. 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिका
भारिका A heap, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारङ्गी|भारंगी
भारङ्गी<BR>—1 A female supporter.<BR>—2 Clerodendrum Siphonantus (Mar. भारंगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारण्डः|भारण्ड|भारंड|भारंडः
भारण्डः A kind of fabulous bird. (Also भारुण्ड); एकोदराः<BR> पृथग्ग्रीवा अन्योन्यफलभक्षिणः । असंहता विनश्यन्ति भारण्डा इव पक्षिणः Pt. 5. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारत|भारतं|भारतः
भारत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भरतस्येदम्, भारतान् भरतवंश्यानधिकृत्य कृतो<BR> ग्रन्थः अण्] Belonging to or descended from Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतः|भारत|भारतं
भारत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A descendant of Bharata; (such as विदुर; सञ्जातहर्षो मुनिमाह भारतः<BR> Mb. 3. 20. 8; also धृतराष्ट्र, अर्जुन in Bg.).<BR>—2 An inhabitant of <i>Bharatavarṣa</i> or India.<BR>—3 An actor.<BR>—4 An epithet of the sun shining on the south of Meru.<BR>—5 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतम्
भारत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 India, the country of Bharata; एतदूढगुरुभार भारतं वर्षमद्य<BR> मम वर्तते वशे Śi. 14. 5.<BR>—2 N. of the most celebrated epic poem in Sanskrit which gives the history<BR> of the descendants of Bharata with innumerable episodes. (It is attributed<BR> to Vyāsa or कृष्णद्वैपायन, but the work, as we have it at present,<BR> is evidently the production of many hands); श्रवणाञ्जलिपुटपेयं विरचितवान्<BR> भारताख्यममृतं यः । तमहमरागमकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं वन्दे ॥<BR> Ve. 1. 4; व्यासगिरां निर्यासं सारं विश्वस्य भारतं वन्दे । भूषणतयैव<BR> संज्ञां यदङ्कितां भारती वहति ॥ Āryā. S. 31.<BR>—3 The science of music and dramaturgy founded by Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारती
भारत + .{@-ती@} Speech, voice, words, eloquence; भारतीनिर्धोषः U. 3;<BR> तमर्थमिव भारत्या सुतया योक्तुमर्हसि Ku. 6. 79; नवरसरुचिरां<BR> निर्मितिमादधती भारती कवेर्जयति K. P. 1.<BR>—2 The goddess of speech, Sarasvatī; कीरानने स्फुरसि भारति का रतिस्ते Govindarāja.<BR>—3 N. of a particular kind of style; भारती संस्कृतप्रायो वाग्व्यापारो<BR> नटाश्रयः S. D. 285.<BR>—4 A quail.<BR>—5 The dramatic art in general.<BR>—6 The Sanskṛt speech of an actor.<BR>—7 One of the 10 orders (दशनाम) of Gosāvins, mendicants (Mar.<BR> दसनाम गोसावी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भारताख्यानम्, भारतेतिहासः, भारतकथा, भारतजः, भारतमण्डलम्, भारतवर्षम्, भारतसावित्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारताख्यानम्
भारत + -आख्यानम्, -इतिहासः, -कथा the story of the Bhāratas (महाभारत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतेतिहासः
भारत + -आख्यानम्, -इतिहासः, -कथा the story of the Bhāratas (महाभारत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतकथा
भारत + -आख्यानम्, -इतिहासः, -कथा the story of the Bhāratas (महाभारत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतजः
भारत + -जः Indian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतमण्डलम्
भारत + -मण्डलम्, -वर्षम् India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतवर्षम्
भारत + -मण्डलम्, -वर्षम् India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारतसावित्री
भारत + -सावित्री N. of a stotra; इमां भारतसावित्रीं प्रातरुत्थाय यः<BR> पठेत् Mb. 18. 5. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजः|भारद्वाज|भारद्वाजं
भारद्वाजः [भरद्वाजस्यापत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 N. of Droṇa, the military preceptor of the Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">Page1193-1</a>]<BR> यदाश्रौषं व्यूहमभेद्यमन्यैर्भारद्वाजेनात्तशस्त्रेण गुप्तम् Mb. 1. 1. 190.<BR>—2 Of Agastya.<BR>—3 The planet Mars.<BR>—4 One of the seven Ṛṣis.<BR>—5 A sky-lark.<BR>—6 N. of the author on the science of Government mentioned by Kauṭilya; Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजम्
भारद्वाजः + .{@-जम्@} A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजी
भारद्वाजः + .{@-जी@} The wild cotton shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजाः
भारद्वाजः + .{@-जाः@} One of the अर्थशास्त्र schools mentioned by Kauṭilya<BR> in connection with राजपुत्ररक्षण; Kau. A. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1192-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारद्वाजकी
भारद्वाजकी A sky-lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारयः|भारय
भारयः A sky-lark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवम्
भारवम् A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवी
भारवम् + .{@-वी@} The sacred basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारविः|भारवि
भारविः N. of the author of the Kirātārjunīya; तावद् भा भारवेर्भाति<BR> यावन्माघस्य नोदयः । उदिते च पुनर्माघे भारवेर्भा रवेरिव ॥; भारवेरर्थगौरवम्<BR> Udb.; कविताश्रितकालिदासभारविकीर्तिः Samudragupta inscription.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिः|भारि
भारिः A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारिटः|भारिट
भारिटः A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारुषः|भारुष
भारुषः<BR>—1 The son of a वैश्यव्रात्य and an unmarried वैश्या.<BR>—2 A kind of Śakti worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गः|भार्ग
भार्गः A king of the Bhargas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवः|भार्गव
भार्गवः [मृगोरपत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 N. of Śukra, regent of the planet Venus and preceptor of the Asuras.<BR>—2 N. of Paraśurāma; भार्गवः प्रददौ यस्मै परमास्त्रं महाहवे<BR> Mb. 8. 2. 13; see परशुराम.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—4 An archer.<BR>—5 An elephant.<BR>—6 An epithet of Jamadagni.<BR>—7 Of Mārkaṇḍeya; तावच्छिशोर्वै श्वसितेन भर्गवः सोऽन्तः शरीरं<BR> मशको यथाविशत् Bhāg. 12. 9. 27.<BR>—8 N. of an eastern country; ब्रह्मोत्तरा प्रविजया भार्गवाज्ञेयमल्लकाः Mārk. P.<BR>—9 An astrologer, fortune-teller; ‘भार्गवो शुक्रदैवज्ञौ’ Vaijayantī;<BR> भार्गवो नाम भृत्वा भिक्षानिभेन तद्गृहं प्रविश्य Dk. 2. 6.<BR>—10 A potter; ब्राह्मणैः प्राविशत् तत्र जिष्णुर्भार्गववेश्म तत् Mb. 1. 190. 47;<BR> भार्गवकर्मशाला 1. 91. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवम्
भार्गवम्, भार्गवकम्, भार्गवप्रियः<BR> A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवकम्
भार्गवम्, भार्गवकम्, भार्गवप्रियः<BR> A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवप्रियः|भार्गवप्रिय
भार्गवम्, भार्गवकम्, भार्गवप्रियः<BR> A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्गवी
भार्गवी<BR>—1 The Dūrvā grass.<BR>—2 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—3 Of Pārvatī.<BR>—4 Of Devayānī; सर्वत्र सङ्गमुत्सृज्य स्वप्नौपम्येन भार्गवी Bhāg. 9. 19. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्य|भार्यः|भार्य्य
भार्य <i>a.</i> [भृ-ण्यत्] To be supported or cherished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यः|भार्य|भार्य्य
भार्य + .{@-र्यः@}<BR>—1 A servant, a dependant (to be supported); स हैवालं भार्येभ्यो भवति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 18.<BR>—2 A mercenary, soldier; P. III. 1. 112 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्या|भार्य्या
भार्या [भर्तुं योग्या]<BR>—1 A lawful wife; सा भार्या या गृहे दक्षा सा भार्या या प्रजावती । सा<BR> भार्या या पतिप्राणा सा भार्या या पतिव्रता ॥ H. 1. 196.<BR>—2 The female of an animal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भार्याट, भार्योढ, भार्याजितः, भार्याटिकः, भार्यापतित्वम्, भार्यावृक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्याट|भार्य्याट|भार्य्याटः
भार्या + -आट <i>a.</i> living by the prostitution of his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्योढ|भार्य्योढ
भार्या + -ऊढ <i>a.</i> married (as a man); भार्योढं तमवज्ञाय Bk. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्याजितः|भार्याजित
भार्या + -जितः, -आटिकः<BR>—1 a hen-pecked husband.<BR>—2 a kind of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्याटिकः|भार्याटिक|भार्य्याटिक|भार्य्याटिकः
भार्या + -जितः, -आटिकः<BR>—1 a hen-pecked husband.<BR>—2 a kind of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यापतित्वम्
भार्या + -पतित्वम् wedlock, matrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यावृक्षः|भार्यावृक्ष|भार्य्यावृक्ष|भार्य्यावृक्षः
भार्या + -वृक्षः Caesalpina Sappan (Mar. पतंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्यारुः|भार्यारु|भार्य्यारु|भार्य्यारुः
भार्यारुः<BR>—1 A kind of deer.<BR>—2 The father of a child by another manʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भार्श्यम्
भार्श्यम्<BR>—1 Violence, vehemence.<BR>—2 Excessiveness, intensity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालम्
भालम् [भा-लच्]<BR>—1 The forehead, brow; यद्धात्रा निजभालपट्टलिखितं स्तोकं महद्वा<BR> धनम् Bh. 2. 49; (स्मरस्य) वपुः सद्यो भालानलभसितजालस्पदमभूत्<BR> Bv. 1. 84; स्वामिन् भङ्गुरयालकं सतिलकं भालं विलासिन् कुरु S. D.<BR>—2 Light.<BR>—3 Darkness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भालाङ्कः, भालचन्द्रः, भालदर्शनः, भालदर्शनम्, भालदर्शिन्, भालदृश्, भालपट्टः, भालपट्टम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालाङ्कः|भालाङ्क|भालांक
भालम् + -अङ्कः<BR>—1 a man born with lucky lines on his forehead.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 a saw.<BR>—4 a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालचन्द्रः|भालचन्द्र|भालचंद्र
भालम् + -चन्द्रः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालचन्द्रा
भालम् + -चन्द्रः + .({@-द्रा@}) N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदर्शनः|भालदर्शन|भालदर्शनं
भालम् + -दर्शनः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदर्शनम्
भालम् + -दर्शनम् red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदर्शिन्
भालम् + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> ‘looking at or watching the brow’, said of a servant<BR> who is attentive to his masterʼs wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालदृश्
भालम् + -दृश् <i>m.</i>, {@-लोचनः@}<BR> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालपट्टः|भालपट्ट
भालम् + -पट्टः, -पट्टम् the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालपट्टम्
भालम् + -पट्टः, -पट्टम् the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालुः|भालु
भालुः The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालुकः|भालुक
भालु(लू)कः, भाल्लु(ल्लू)कः A bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भालूकः|भालूक
भालु(लू)कः, भाल्लु(ल्लू)कः A bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लुकः|भाल्लुक
भालु(लू)कः, भाल्लु(ल्लू)कः A bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लूकः|भाल्लूक
भालु(लू)कः, भाल्लु(ल्लू)कः A bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाल्लविः|भाल्लवि
भाल्लविः <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A branch of Sāmaveda.<BR>—2 Those who belong to this branch of Sāmaveda; तामेतां भाल्लवय उपासते Tāṇḍya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावः|भाव
भावः [भू-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Being, existing, existence; नासतो विद्यते भावः Bg. 2. 16.<BR>—2 Becoming, occurring, taking place.<BR>—3 State, condition, state of being; लताभावेन परिणतमस्या रूपम्<BR> V. 4; U. 6. 23; so कातरभावः, विवर्णभावः &c.<BR>—4 Manner, mode.<BR>—5 Rank, station, position, capacity; देवीभावं गमिता K. P. 10; so<BR> प्रेष्यभावम्, किंकरभावम् &c.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) True condition or state, truth, reality; परं भावमजानन्तः<BR> Bg. 7. 24; इति मत्वा भजन्ते मां बुधा भावसमन्विताः 10. 8.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Sincerity, devotion; त्वयि मे भावनिबन्धना रतिः R. 8. 52, 2. 26.<BR>—7 Innate property, disposition, nature, temperament; स तस्य स्वो भावः<BR> प्रकृतिनियतत्वादकृतकः U. 6. 14.<BR>—8 Inclination or disposition of mind, idea, thought, opinion, supposition;<BR> हृदयनिहितभावा गूढमन्त्रप्रचाराः किमपि विगणयन्तो बुद्धिमन्तः सहन्ते<BR> Pt. 3. 43; Ms. 8. 25, 4. 65; निकृष्टोत्कृष्टयोर्भावं यास्तु गृह्णन्ति ताः<BR> स्त्रियः Bu. C. 4. 23.<BR>—9 Feeling, emotion, sentiment; एको भावः Pt. 3. 66; Ku. 6. 95; निर्विकारात्मके<BR> चित्ते भावः प्रथमविक्रिया S. D. (In the dramatic science or in poetic<BR> compositions generally, <i>Bhāvas</i> are either स्थायिन् primary,<BR> or व्यभिचारिन् subordinate. The former are eight or nine, according<BR> as the <i>Rasas</i> are taken to be 8 or 9, each <i>rasa</i> having<BR> its own स्थायिभाव. The latter are thirty-three or thirty four in number,<BR> and serve to develop and strengthen the prevailing sentiment; for definition<BR> and enumeration of the several kinds, see R. G. first <i>anana</i>, or K. P. 4).<BR>—10 Love, affection, attachment; द्वन्द्वानि भावं क्रियया विवव्रुः Ku. 3. 35;<BR> कुमुद्वती भानुमतीव भावं (बबन्ध) R. 6. 36.<BR>—11 Purport, drift, gist, substance; इति भावः (often used by commentators);<BR> जनकोऽप्युत्स्मयन् राजा भावमस्या विशेषयन् । प्रतिजग्राह भावेन भावमस्या<BR> नृपोत्तम Mb. 12. 320. 18.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">Page1194-1</a>]<BR>—12 Meaning, intention, sense, import; अन्योन्यभावचतुरेण सखीजनेन मुक्तास्तदा<BR> स्मितसुधामधुराः कटाक्षाः Māl. 1. 25.<BR>—13 Resolution, determination.<BR>—14 The heart, soul, mind; तयोर्विवृतभावत्वात् Māl. 1. 12; भावसंशुद्धिरित्येतत्<BR> तपो मानसमुच्यते Bg. 17. 16; स्व एव भावे विनिगृह्य मन्मथम् Bu. C. 4. 101.<BR>—15 Any existing thing, an object, a thing, substance; पश्यन्ती विविधान्<BR> भावान् Rām. 2. 94. 18; जगति जयिनस्ते ते भावा नवेन्दुकलादयः<BR> Māl. 1. 17, 36; R. 3. 41; U. 3. 32.<BR>—16 A being, living creature.<BR>—17 Abstract meditation, contemplation (= भावना q. v.).<BR>—18 Conduct, movement.<BR>—19<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Gesture, behaviour; अहिंसा समता .. भवन्ति भावा भूतानाम् Bg. 10. 5.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Amorous gesture or expression of sentiment, gesture of love;<BR> कामं प्रिया न सुलभा मनस्तु तद्भावदर्शनाश्वासि Ś. 2. 1.<BR>—20 Birth; तवाहं पूर्वके भावे पुत्रः परपुरंजय Rām. 7. 104. 2.<BR>—21 The world, universe.<BR>—22 The womb.<BR>—23 Will; घोरैर्विव्यधतुर्बाणैः कृतभावावुभौ जये Rām. 6. 90. 38.<BR>—24 Superhuman power; मिथो घ्नतं न पश्यन्ति भावैर्भावं पृथग्दृशः Bhāg. 10. 4. 27.<BR>—25 Advice, instruction.<BR>—26 (In dramas) A learned or venerable man, worthy man, (a term of address);<BR> भाव अयमस्मि V. 1; (तां खलु भावेन तथैव सर्वे वर्ग्याः पाठिताः) Māl. 1.<BR>—27 (In gram.) The sense of an abstract noun, abstract idea conveyed by<BR> a word; भावे क्तः.<BR>—28 A term for an impersonal passive or neuter verb.<BR>—29 (In astr.) An astronomical house.<BR>—30 A lunar mansion.<BR>—31 An organ of sense.<BR>—32 Welfare (कल्याण); भावमिच्छति सर्वस्य नाभावे कुरुते मनः Mb. 5. 36. 16.<BR>—33 Protection; द्रोणस्याभावभावे तु प्रसक्तानां यथाऽभवत् Mb. 7. 25. 64.<BR>—34 Fate, destiny (प्रारब्ध); नातिप्रहीणरश्मिः स्यात्तथा भावविपर्यये Mb. 5. 77. 14.<BR>—35 Consciousness of past perceptions (वासना); येभ्यः सृजति भूतानि<BR> काले भावप्रचोदितः । महाभूतानि पञ्चेति तान्याहुर्भूतचिन्तिकाः ॥ Mb. 12. 275. 4.<BR>—36 Lordship (प्रभुत्व); तेऽपि भावाय कल्पन्ते राजदण्डनिपीडिताः<BR> Rām. 2. 67. 32.<BR>—37 The six states (अवस्थाषट्क); A. Rām. 1. 7. 31.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भावानुग, भावान्तरम्, भावाद्वैतम्, भावार्थः, भावाकूतम्, भावाख्यः, भावात्मक, भावाभासः, भावालीना, भावैकरस, भावकर्तृकः, भावगतिः, भावगम्भीरम्, भावगम्य, भावग्राहिन्, भावग्राह्य, भावचेष्टितम्, भावजः, भावज्ञ, भावविद्, भावदर्शिन्, भावनिर्वृत्तिः, भावनेरिः, भावबन्धन, भावबोधक, भावमिश्रः, भावरूप, भाववचनम्, भाववाचकम्, भावविकारः, भाववृत्तः, भावशबलत्वम्, भावशुद्धिः, भावशून्य, भावसंधिः, भावसमाहित, भावसर्गः, भावस्थ, भावस्थिर, भावस्निग्ध, भावंगम<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1193-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावानुग
भावः + -अनुग <i>a.</i> not forced, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावानुगा
भावः + -अनुग + .({@-गा@}) a shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावान्तरम्
भावः + -अन्तरम् a different state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाद्वैतम्
भावः + -अद्वैतम्<BR>—1 a natural cause.<BR>—2 material cause (as thread of a cloth).<BR>—3 identity of conception, oneness of view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावार्थः|भावार्थ
भावः + -अर्थः<BR>—1 the obvious meaning or import (of a word, phrase &c.).<BR>—2 the subject matter; सर्वेषामपि वस्तूनां भावार्थो भवति स्थितः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 14. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाकूतम्
भावः + -आकूतम् (secret) thoughts of the mind; हृदयनिहितं भावाकूतं<BR> वमद्भिरिवेक्षणैः Amaru. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाख्यः
भावः + -आख्यः One of the two types of creation according to the Sāṅkhya<BR> philosophy; लिङ्गाख्यो भावाख्यस्तस्माद् द्विविधः प्रवर्तते सर्गः Sāṅ. K. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावात्मक
भावः + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> real, actual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाभासः|भावाभास
भावः + -आभासः simulation of a feeling, a feigned or false emotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावालीना
भावः + -आलीना a shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावैकरस
भावः + -एकरस <i>a.</i> influenced solely by the sentiment of (sincere)<BR> love; ममात्र भावैकरसं मनः स्थितम् Ku. 5. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावकर्तृकः|भावकर्तृक
भावः + -कर्तृकः an impersonal verb; Kāśi. on P. II. 3. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावगतिः
भावः + -गतिः <i>f.</i> power to convey human feelings; भावगतिराकृतीनाम् Pratimā 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावगम्भीरम्|भावगंभीरम्
भावः + -गम्भीरम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 heartily, from the bottom of the heart.<BR>—2 deeply, gravely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावगम्य
भावः + -गम्य <i>a.</i> conceived by the mind; मत्सादृश्यं विरहतनु<BR> वा भावगम्यं लिखन्ती Me. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावग्राहिन्
भावः + -ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 understanding the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">Page1194-2</a>]<BR> sense.<BR>—2 appreciating the sentiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावग्राह्य
भावः + -ग्राह्य <i>a.</i> to be conceived with the heart; भावग्राह्यमनीडाख्यं<BR> भावाभावकरं शिवम् Śvet. Up. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावचेष्टितम्
भावः + -चेष्टितम् amorous gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावजः|भावज
भावः + -जः<BR>—1 love.<BR>—2 the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावज्ञ
भावः + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i> knowing the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावविद्
भावः + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i> knowing the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावदर्शिन्
भावः + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> see भालदर्शिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनिर्वृत्तिः
भावः + -निर्वृत्तिः the material creation (Sāṅ. phil.); न विना लिङ्गेन<BR> भावनिर्वृत्तिः Sāṅ. K. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनेरिः|भावनेरि
भावः + -नेरिः a kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावबन्धन|भावबंधन
भावः + -बन्धन <i>a.</i> enchanting or fettering the heart, linking together<BR> the hearts; रथाङ्गनाम्नोरिव भावबन्धनं बभूव यत्प्रेम परस्पराश्रयम् R. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावबोधक|भावबोधकः
भावः + -बोधक <i>a.</i> indicating or revealing any feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावमिश्रः|भावमिश्र
भावः + -मिश्रः a worthy person, a gentleman (used in dramas); प्रसीदन्तु<BR> भावमिश्राः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावरूप
भावः + -रूप <i>a.</i> real, actual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाववचनम्
भावः + -वचनम् denoting an abstract idea, conveying the abstract notion of a verb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाववाचकम्
भावः + -वाचकम् an abstract noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावविकारः|भावविकार
भावः + -विकारः a property of a being; षड् भावविकारा भवन्तीति वार्ष्यायणिः ।<BR> जायतेऽस्ति विपरिणमते वर्धतेऽपक्षीयते नश्यति ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाववृत्तः|भाववृत्त
भावः + -वृत्तः an epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशबलत्वम्
भावः + -शबलत्वम् a mixture of various emotions (भावानां बाध्यबाधकभावमापन्नानामुदासीनानां<BR> वा व्यामिश्रणम् R. G., <i>vide</i> examples given <i>ad loc.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशुद्धिः|भावशुद्धि
भावः + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> purity of mind, honesty, sincerity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावशून्य
भावः + -शून्य <i>a.</i> devoid of real love; उपचारविधिर्मनस्विनीनां<BR> न तु पूर्वाभ्यधिकोऽपि भावशून्यः M. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसंधिः|भावसन्धि|भावसंधि
भावः + -संधिः the union or co-existence of two emotions (भावसंधिरन्योन्यानभिभूतयोरन्योन्याभिभावनयोग्ययोः<BR> सामानाधिकरण्यम् R. G., see the examples there given).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसमाहित
भावः + -समाहित <i>a.</i> abstracted in mind, devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावसर्गः|भावसर्ग
भावः + -सर्गः the mental or intellectual creation; <i>i. e.</i> the creation<BR> of the faculties of the human mind and their affections (opp. भौतिकसर्ग<BR> or material creation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावस्थ
भावः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> attached; devoted (to one); न वेत्सि भावस्थमिमं<BR> कथं जनम् Ku. 5. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावस्थिर
भावः + -स्थिर <i>a.</i> firmly rooted in the heart; Ś. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावस्निग्ध
भावः + -स्निग्ध <i>a.</i> affectionately disposed, sincerely attached; भावस्निग्धैरुपकृतमपि<BR> द्वेष्यतां याति किंचित् Pt. 1. 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावंगम
भावः + भावंगम <i>a.</i> charming, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावक|भावकः
भावक <i>a.</i> [भाव-स्वार्थे क]<BR>—1 Effecting, bringing about.<BR>—2 Promoting any oneʼs welfare; नैते भूतस्य भावकाः Mb. 12. 88. 24.<BR>—3 Fancying, imagining.<BR>—4 Having a taste for the sublime and beautiful, having a poetic taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावकः|भावक
भावक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A feeling, sentiment.<BR>—2 The external manifestation of oneʼs sentiments (especially of love).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावन|भावनं|भावनः
भावन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भू-णिच्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Effecting &c.; भूतभव्यभविष्याणां<BR> भावानां भुवि भावनाः Mb. 14. 37. 15; यत् पृच्छसे भागवतान् धर्मांस्त्वं<BR> विश्वभावनान् Bhāg. 11. 2. 11, 8. 1. 16; see भावक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनः|भावन|भावनं
भावन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 An efficient cause.<BR>—2 A creator; जय देव भुवनभावन Māl. 9. 4.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—4 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनम्
भावन + .{@-नम्, -ना@}<BR>—1 Creating, manifesting; भावनं ब्रह्मणः स्थानम् Bhāg. 3. 26. 46.<BR>—2 Promoting any oneʼs interests.<BR>—3 Conception, imagination, fancy, thought, idea; मधुरिपुरहमिति भावनशीला<BR> Gīt. 6; or भावनया त्वयि लीना 4; Pt. 3. 162.<BR>—4 Feeling of devotion, faith; नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना<BR> Bg. 2. 66; यादृशी भावना यस्य सिद्धिर्भवति तादृशी Pt. 5. 105.<BR>—5 Meditation, contemplation, abstract meditation.<BR>—6 A supposition, hypothesis.<BR>—7 Observing, investigating.<BR>—8 Settling, determining;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">Page1195-1</a>]<BR> विभागभावना ज्ञेया Y. 2. 149.<BR>—9 Remembering, recollection.<BR>—10 Direct knowledge, perception or cognition.<BR>—11 The cause of memory which arises from direct perception (in logic);<BR> see भावना and स्मृति in T. S.; भावनाख्यस्तु संस्कारो जीववृत्तिरतीन्द्रियः Bhāṣā P.<BR>—12 Proof, demonstration, argument.<BR>—13 Steeping, infusion, saturating a dry powder with fluid; द्रवेण<BR> यावन्मानेन चूर्णं सर्वं प्लुतं भवेत् । भावनायाः प्रमाणस्तु चूर्णे प्रोक्तं<BR> भिषग्वरैः Bhāva P.<BR>—14 Scenting; decorating with flowers and perfumes.<BR>—15 (In arith.) Finding by combination or composition.<BR>—16 Nature, essence (at the end of comp.).<BR>—17 Reason, cause; परावरेशं प्रकृतिमस्योत्पत्त्यन्तभावनम् Bhāg. 3. 32. 7.<BR>—18 Growth, prosperity (वर्धन); तस्यैषा निष्कृतिः कृत्स्ना भूतानां<BR> भावनं पुनः Mb. 12. 97. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावना
भावन + .{@-नम्, -ना@}<BR>—1 Creating, manifesting; भावनं ब्रह्मणः स्थानम् Bhāg. 3. 26. 46.<BR>—2 Promoting any oneʼs interests.<BR>—3 Conception, imagination, fancy, thought, idea; मधुरिपुरहमिति भावनशीला<BR> Gīt. 6; or भावनया त्वयि लीना 4; Pt. 3. 162.<BR>—4 Feeling of devotion, faith; नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य न चायुक्तस्य भावना<BR> Bg. 2. 66; यादृशी भावना यस्य सिद्धिर्भवति तादृशी Pt. 5. 105.<BR>—5 Meditation, contemplation, abstract meditation.<BR>—6 A supposition, hypothesis.<BR>—7 Observing, investigating.<BR>—8 Settling, determining;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">Page1195-1</a>]<BR> विभागभावना ज्ञेया Y. 2. 149.<BR>—9 Remembering, recollection.<BR>—10 Direct knowledge, perception or cognition.<BR>—11 The cause of memory which arises from direct perception (in logic);<BR> see भावना and स्मृति in T. S.; भावनाख्यस्तु संस्कारो जीववृत्तिरतीन्द्रियः Bhāṣā P.<BR>—12 Proof, demonstration, argument.<BR>—13 Steeping, infusion, saturating a dry powder with fluid; द्रवेण<BR> यावन्मानेन चूर्णं सर्वं प्लुतं भवेत् । भावनायाः प्रमाणस्तु चूर्णे प्रोक्तं<BR> भिषग्वरैः Bhāva P.<BR>—14 Scenting; decorating with flowers and perfumes.<BR>—15 (In arith.) Finding by combination or composition.<BR>—16 Nature, essence (at the end of comp.).<BR>—17 Reason, cause; परावरेशं प्रकृतिमस्योत्पत्त्यन्तभावनम् Bhāg. 3. 32. 7.<BR>—18 Growth, prosperity (वर्धन); तस्यैषा निष्कृतिः कृत्स्ना भूतानां<BR> भावनं पुनः Mb. 12. 97. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावना
भावन + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 A crow.<BR>—2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनम्
भावन + .{@-नम्@} Apprehension, perception.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भावनाश्रयः, भावनमय, भावनयुक्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1194-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनाश्रयः|भावनाश्रय
भावन + -आश्रयः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनमय
भावन + -मय <i>a.</i> imaginary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावनयुक्त
भावन + -युक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 thoughtful<BR>—2 anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावयितृ
भावयितृ <i>a.</i> A protector, promoter; क्रोधो हन्ता मनुष्याणां क्रोधो<BR> भावयिता पुनः Mb. 3. 29. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाटः|भावाट
भावाटः [भावं भावेन वा अटति, अट्-अण् अच् वा]<BR>—1 Emotion, passion, sentiment.<BR>—2 The external indication of the feeling of love.<BR>—3 A pious or holy man.<BR>—4 An amorous man.<BR>—5 An actor.<BR>—6 Decoration, dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविक|भाविकः
भाविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भावेन निर्वृत्तं ठक्]<BR>—1 Natural, real, inherent, innate.<BR>—2 Sentimental, pervaded by a feeling or sentiment; विभावितभाविकस्फुटरसमृशाभ्यक्ता<BR> वैतालिकैर्जगिरे गिरः N. 19. 1; Śi. 4. 33.<BR>—3 Future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविकः|भाविक
भाविक + .{@-कः@} An equation involving the products of unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविकम्
भाविक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Language full of love or passion.<BR>—2 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech which consists in describing the past<BR> or future so vividly that it appears to be actually present. It is thus<BR> defined by Mammaṭa; प्रत्यक्षा इव यद्भावाः क्रियन्ते भूतभाविनः । तद्<BR> भाविकम् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित|भावितः
भावित <i>p. p.</i> [भू-णिच् कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>—1 Created, produced; obtained, got.<BR>—2 Manifested, displayed, exhibited; भावितविषवेगविक्रियः Dk.; (भजे)<BR> भक्तेष्वलं भावितभूतभावनम् Bhāg. 5. 17. 18.<BR>—3 Cherished, fostered; तेषां दृष्ट्वा भावितानीङ्गितानि प्रोवाच राजा जनमेजयोऽथ Mb. 1. 55. 17.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Conceived, imagined, supposed, presented to the imagination;<BR> तं तमेवैति कौन्तेय सदा तद्भावभावितः Bg. 8. 6.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Known, recognized, acknowledged.<BR>—5 Thought of, meditated upon.<BR>—6 Made to become, transformed into.<BR>—7 Sanctified by meditation; अनन्यभावे निजधर्मभाविते मनस्यवस्थाप्य<BR> भजस्व पूरुषम् Bhāg. 4. 8. 22; see भावितात्मन्.<BR>—8 Proved, established.<BR>—9 Pervaded by, filled or saturated with, inspired by.<BR>—10 Soaked, steeped, infused in; किञ्चित् स्निग्धं यथा च स्याच्छुष्कचूर्णमभावितम्<BR> Mb. 12. 195. 18.<BR>—11 Perfumed, scented.<BR>—12 Mixed with.<BR>—13 (In math.). Involving the products of unknown quantities.<BR>—14 Directed towards, fixed upon; यदीश्वरे भगवति कर्म ब्रह्मणि<BR> भावितम् Bhāg. 1. 5. 32.<BR>—15 Possessed, captured (वशीकृत); ततोऽन्ये च यथाकामं दुदुहुः<BR> पृथुभाविताम् Bhāg. 4. 18. 13.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">Page1195-2</a>]<BR>—16 Engrossed, filled; रथाङ्गपाणेरनुभावभावितम् Bhāg. 12. 10. 42.<BR>—17 Pleased, gladdened; इष्टान् भोगान् हि वो देवा दास्यन्ते यज्ञभाविताः Bg. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितम्
भावित + .{@-तम्@} Product obtained by multiplication, a factum.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भावितात्मन्, भावितबुद्धि, भावितभावन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितात्मन्
भावित + -आत्मन्, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one whose soul is purified by meditating on the Supreme Spirit, one<BR> who has perceived the Supreme Soul; तस्य देवप्रभावस्य तपसा भावितात्मनः Rām. 3. 5. 4.<BR>—2 pure, devout, holy; एको भावः सदा शस्तो यतीनां भावितात्मनाम् Pt. 3. 65.<BR>—3 thoughtful, meditative; भावितात्मा भुवो भर्तुरथैनं प्रत्यबोधयत् R. 1. 74.<BR>—4 engaged in, occupied with; स्वगोत्रसंकीर्तनभावितात्मनः Śi. 12. 38.<BR>━(<i>m.</i>) a sage, saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितबुद्धि
भावित + -आत्मन्, -बुद्धि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one whose soul is purified by meditating on the Supreme Spirit, one<BR> who has perceived the Supreme Soul; तस्य देवप्रभावस्य तपसा भावितात्मनः Rām. 3. 5. 4.<BR>—2 pure, devout, holy; एको भावः सदा शस्तो यतीनां भावितात्मनाम् Pt. 3. 65.<BR>—3 thoughtful, meditative; भावितात्मा भुवो भर्तुरथैनं प्रत्यबोधयत् R. 1. 74.<BR>—4 engaged in, occupied with; स्वगोत्रसंकीर्तनभावितात्मनः Śi. 12. 38.<BR>━(<i>m.</i>) a sage, saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितभावन
भावित + -भावन <i>a.</i> being oneʼs self furthered and furthering others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावितकम्
भावितकम् The product of a multiplication, a factum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित्रम्
भावित्रम् [भू-णि त्रन्] The three worlds (heaven, earth, and lower<BR> regions); Uṇ. 4. 179.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविता
भाविता<BR>—1 The state of being or becoming.<BR>—2 Futurity.<BR>—3 Predestination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावित्वम्
भावित्वम् Inevitableness, necessity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविन्
भाविन् [भू-भविष्यति णिनि]<BR>—1 Being, becoming; भृत्यभावि R. 11. 49.<BR>—2 To be or to come to pass in future, what will take place; लोकेन<BR> भावी पितुरेव तुल्यः R. 18. 38; प्रस्थानं ते कथमपि सखे लम्बमानस्य भावि Me. 43.<BR>—3 Future; समतीतं च भवच्च भावि च R. 8. 78; प्रत्यक्षा इव<BR> यद्भावाः क्रियन्ते भूतभाविनः K. P. 10; N. 3. 11.<BR>—4 Capable of taking place.<BR>—5 What must take place or is destined to happen, predestined; यदभावि<BR> न तद्भावि भावि चेन्न तदन्यथा H. 1.<BR>—6 Noble, beautiful, illustrious.<BR>—7 Attached or devoted to; खाद्वै निवर्तन्ति न भाविनस्ते Mb. 12. 202. 2.<BR>—8 Possessed of (at the end of comp.).<BR>━<i>m.</i> N. given to every vowel except अ and आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाविनी
भाविन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A handsome woman; Mb. 1. 6. 9.<BR>—2 A noble or virtuous lady; अनेन धर्मः सविशेषमद्य मे त्रिवर्गसारः<BR> प्रतिभाति भाविनि Ku. 5. 38.<BR>—3 A wanton woman.<BR>—4 A particular musical composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुक|भावुकं|भावुकः
भावुक <i>a.</i> [भू-उकञ्]<BR>—1 About to be or happen.<BR>—2 Becoming.<BR>—3 Prosperous, happy.<BR>—4 Auspicious, blessed.<BR>—5 Having a poetic taste, appreciative; मुहुरहो रसिका भुवि भावुकाः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुकः|भावुक|भावुकं
भावुक + .{@-कः@} A sisterʼs husband (used chiefly in dramas); स्वकुटुम्बवियोगेन<BR> क्लिश्यते तव भावुकः Gaṇeśa P. (The story of Pāṭaliputra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावुकम्
भावुक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Happiness, welfare, prosperity; स रातु वो दुश्च्यवनो भावुकानां परंपराम्<BR> K. P. 7 (given as an instance of the fault of composition called अप्रयुक्तत्व).<BR>—2 Language full of love and passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्य|भाव्यं
भाव्य <i>a.</i> [भू-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 About to be or happen; मनुस्त्रयोदशो भाव्यः Bhāg. 8. 13. 30;<BR> oft. used impersonally like भवितव्यम् q. v.; किं तैर्भाव्यं मम<BR> सुदिवसैः Bh. 3. 41.<BR>—2 Future.<BR>—3 To be performed or accomplished.<BR>—4 To be conceived or imagined.<BR>—5 To be proved or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">Page1196-1</a>]<BR> demonstrated.<BR>—6 To be determined or investigated.<BR>—7 To be convicted; त्र्यवरैः साक्षिभिर्भाव्यो नृपब्राह्मणसंनिधौ Ms. 8. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्यम्
भाव्य + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 What is destined or sure to happen in the future; it is to be; सदा<BR> प्रहृष्टया भाव्यं गृहकार्येषु दक्षया Ms. 5. 150.<BR>—2 Futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1195-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाव्यता
भाव्यता Futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत|भावतः
भावत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>), भावत्क <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Your honourʼs, your (respectfully); भावत्कं दृष्टवत्स्वेतदस्मास्वधि<BR> सुजीवितम् Bk. 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावती
भावत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>), भावत्क <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Your honourʼs, your (respectfully); भावत्कं दृष्टवत्स्वेतदस्मास्वधि<BR> सुजीवितम् Bk. 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्क|भावत्कः
भावत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>), भावत्क <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Your honourʼs, your (respectfully); भावत्कं दृष्टवत्स्वेतदस्मास्वधि<BR> सुजीवितम् Bk. 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावत्की
भावत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>), भावत्क <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Your honourʼs, your (respectfully); भावत्कं दृष्टवत्स्वेतदस्मास्वधि<BR> सुजीवितम् Bk. 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भावाव
भावाव <i>a.</i> Delicate, tender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्
भाष् €1 Ā. (भाषते, भाषित)<BR>—1 To say, speak, utter; त्वयैकमीशं प्रति साधु भाषितम् Ku. 5. 81;<BR> oft. with two acc.; भीतां प्रियामेत्य वचो बभाषे R. 7. 66; आखण्डलः<BR> काममिदं बभाषे Ku. 3. 11; Bk. 9. 122.<BR>—2 To speak to, address; किंचिद्विहस्यार्थपतिं बभाषे R. 2. 46, 3. 51.<BR>—3 To tell, announce, declare; क्षितिपालमुच्चैः प्रीत्या तमेवार्थमभाषतेव R. 2. 51.<BR>—4 To speak or talk about.<BR>—5 To name, call.<BR>—6 To describe. ━<i>With</i> {@अनु@}<BR>—1 to speak, say.<BR>—2 to communicate, announce; यथा यथा नरोऽधर्मं स्वयं कृत्वानुभाषते Ms. 11. 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषक
भाषक <i>a.</i> [भाष्-ण्वुल्] (At the end of comp.) Speaking, talking about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषणम्
भाषणम् [भाष्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Speaking, talking, saying.<BR>—2 Speech, words, talk.<BR>—3 Kind words.<BR>—4 (In drama) Expression of satisfaction after the attainment of an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषणी
भाषणम् + .{@-णी@} Resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषा
भाषा [भाष्-अ]<BR>—1 Speech, talk; as in चारुभाषः.<BR>—2 Language, tongue; सत्या न भाषा भवति यद्यपि स्यात् प्रतिष्ठिता Ms. 8. 164.<BR>—3 A common or vernacular dialect;<BR>——(<i>a</i>) the <i>spoken</i> Sanskṛt language (opp. छन्दस् or वेद);<BR> विभाषा भाषायाम् P. VI. 1. 181;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) any Prākṛta dialect (opp. संस्कृत); भाषाश्च विविधा<BR> नृणाम् Ms. 9. 332; see प्राकृत.<BR>—4 Definition, description; स्थितप्रज्ञस्य का भाषा Bg. 2. 54.<BR>—5 An epithet of Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech.<BR>—6 (In law) The first of the four stages of a law-suit; the plaint, charge<BR> or accusation; यदावेदयते राज्ञे तद्भाषेत्यभिधीयते Y.<BR>—7 (In music) N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भाषान्तरम्, भाषाचित्रकम्, भाषापत्रम्, भाषापादः, भाषासमः, भाषासमितिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषान्तरम्
भाषा + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 another dialect or language.<BR>—2 translation (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषाचित्रकम्
भाषा + -चित्रकम् a play on words, conundrum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषापत्रम्
भाषा + -पत्रम् application (Mar. अर्ज); भाषापत्रं तु तज्ज्ञेयमथवावेदनार्थकम्<BR> Śukra. 2. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषापादः|भाषापाद
भाषा + -पादः a charge, plaint; see भाषा (6) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषासमः|भाषासम
भाषा + -समः a figure of speech, which consists in so arranging the<BR> words of a sentence that it may be considered and read either as Sanskṛt<BR> or Prākṛta (one or more of its varieties); <i>e. g.</i> मञ्जुलमणिमञ्जीरे<BR> कलगम्भीरे विहारसरसीतीरे । विरसासि केलिकीरे किमालि धीरे च गन्धसारसमीरे ॥<BR> S. D. 642 (एष श्लोकः संस्कृतप्राकृतशौरसेनीप्राच्यावन्तीनागरापभ्रंशेष्वेकविध<BR> एव); किं त्वां भणामि विच्छेददारुणायासकारिणि । कामं कुरु वरारोहे<BR> देहि मे परिरम्भणम् Māl. 6. 11 (which is in Sanskṛt or Śaurasenī); so 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषासमितिः|भाषासमिति
भाषा + -समितिः <i>f.</i> (with Jaiṇas) moderation in speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिक
भाषिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to common or vernacular speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिकम्
भाषिक + .{@-कम्@} General rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिका
भाषिका Speech, language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषित|भाषितं
भाषित <i>p. p.</i> [भाष्-कर्मणि-क्त] Spoken, said, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितम्
भाषित + .{@-तम्@} Speech, utterance, words, language; आकारैरिङ्गितैर्गत्या<BR> चेष्टया भाषितेन च । नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च गृह्यतेऽन्तर्गतं मनः ॥ Ms. 8. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भाषितेशा, भाषितपुंस्क<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितेशा
भाषित + -ईशा Sarasvatī; N. 11. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितपुंस्क
भाषित + -पुंस्क = उक्तपुंस्क q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषितृ
भाषितृ <i>a.</i> A speaker, talker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाषिन्
भाषिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 (At the end of comp.) Speaking, talking; as in अल्प˚ &c.<BR>—2 Loquacious, talkative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यम्
भाष्यम् [भाष्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 Speaking, talking.<BR>—2 Any work in the common or vernacular language.<BR>—3 Exposition, gloss, commentary; as in वेदभाष्य.<BR>—4 Especially, a commentary which explains <i>Sūtras</i> or aphorisms<BR> word by word with comments of its own; (सूत्रार्थो वर्ण्यते यत्र पदैः<BR> सूत्रानुसारिभिः । स्वपदानि च वर्ण्यन्ते भाष्यं भाष्यविदो विदुः ॥);<BR> संक्षिप्तस्याप्यतोऽस्यैव वाक्यस्यार्थगरीयसः । सुविस्तरतरा वाचो भाष्यभूता<BR> भवन्तु मे Śi. 2. 24; फणिभाषितभाष्यफक्किका N. 2. 95.<BR>—5 N. of the great commentary of Patañjali on Pāṇiniʼs Sūtras.<BR>—6 A sort of house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भाष्यकरः, भाष्यकारः, भाष्यकृत्, भाष्यभूत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकरः|भाष्यकर
भाष्यम् + -करः, -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a commentator, scholiast.<BR>—2 N. of Patañjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकारः|भाष्यकार
भाष्यम् + -करः, -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a commentator, scholiast.<BR>—2 N. of Patañjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यकृत्
भाष्यम् + -करः, -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a commentator, scholiast.<BR>—2 N. of Patañjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भाष्यभूत
भाष्यम् + -भूत <i>a.</i> serving as a commentary; सुविस्तरतरा वाचो भाष्यभूता<BR> भवन्तु मे Śi. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् €1 Ā. (भासते-भासित)<BR>—1 To shine, glitter, be bright; तावत् कामनृपातपत्रसुषमं बिम्बं<BR> बभासे विधोः Bv. 2. 74, 4. 18; Ku. 6. 11; Bk. 10. 61.<BR>—2 To become clear or evident, come into the mind; त्वदङ्गमार्दवे दृष्टे<BR> कस्य चित्ते न भासते । मालतीशशभृल्लेखाकदलीनां कठोरता Candr. 5. 42.<BR>—3 To appear. ━<i>Caus.</i> (भासयति-ते)<BR>—1 To brighten, irradiate, illuminate; अधिवसंस्तनुमध्वरदीक्षितामसमभासमभासयदीश्वरः<BR> R. 9. 21; न तद् भासयते सूर्यो न शशाङ्को न पावकः Bg. 15. 6.<BR>—2 To show, make clear or evident, manifest; अवभासन् स्वकाः शक्तीः Bk. 15. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्
भास् <i>f.</i> [भास्-भावे-क्विप्]<BR>—1 Light, lustre, brightness; यदि भाः सदृशी सा स्याद् भासस्तस्य महात्मनः<BR> Bg. 11. 12; दृशा निशेन्दीवरचारुभासा N. 22. 43; R. 9. 21; Ku. 7. 3.<BR>—2 A ray of light; रविकरसंवलिताः फलन्ति भासः Ki. 5. 38, 46, 9. 6;<BR> अस्तापास्तसमस्तभासि नभसः पारं प्रयाते रवौ Ratn. 1. 24, 4. 16.<BR>—3 A reflection, an image.<BR>—4 Majesty, glory, splendour.<BR>—5 Wish, desire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भास्करः, भास्करम्, भास्कराध्वन्, भास्करावर्तः, भास्करद्युतिः, भास्करप्रियः, भास्करलवणम्, भास्करसप्तमी, भास्करिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करः|भास्कर|भास्करं
भास् + -करः<BR>—1 the sun; परिणतमदिराभं भास्करेणांशुबाणैः Śi. 11. 49; R. 11. 7, 12. 25;<BR> Ku. 6. 49; स स्तौति भास्करं भक्त्या नौति पापहरं हरम् ।<BR>—2 a hero.<BR>—3 fire.<BR>—4 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—5 N. of a celebrated Hindu astronomer who is said to have flourished<BR> in the eleventh or twelfth century A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करम्
भास् + -करः + -रम्<BR>—1 gold.<BR>—2 a kind of breach (made by thieves in a wall); पद्मव्याकोशं भास्करं<BR> बालचन्द्रम् … … तत्कस्मिन् देशे दर्शयाम्यात्मशिल्पम् Mk. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्कराध्वन्
भास् + -करः + ˚अध्वन् the sky; स भास्कराध्वानमनुप्रपन्नः Rām. 6. 74. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करावर्तः|भास्करावर्त|भास्करावर्त्त
भास् + -करः + ˚आवर्तः N. of a disease of the head (Mar. अर्धशिशी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करद्युतिः|भास्करद्युति
भास् + -करः + ˚द्युतिः<BR> N. of Viṣṇu; चन्द्रांशुर्भास्करद्युतिः V. Sah.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">Page1197-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करप्रियः|भास्करप्रिय
भास् + -करः + ˚प्रियः a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करलवणम्
भास् + -करः + ˚लवणम् a kind of salt or mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करसप्तमी
भास् + -करः + ˚सप्तमी<BR> the seventh day in the bright half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1196-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्करिः|भास्करि
भास् + -करिः<BR>—1 the planet Saturn.<BR>—2 Vaivasvata Manu.<BR>—3 Karṇa.<BR>—4 N. of Sugrīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासः|भास
भासः [भास्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Brightness, light, lustre.<BR>—2 Fancy.<BR>—3 A cock; Mb. 12. 36. 23; Bhāg. 8. 10. 10.<BR>—4 A vulture.<BR>—5 A cow-shed (गोष्ठ).<BR>—6 N. of a poet; भासो हासः कविकुलगुरुः कालिदासो विलासः P. R. 1 22; M. 1.<BR>—7 A kind of bird; कृत्रिमं भासमारोप्य वृक्षाग्रे शिल्पिभिः कृतम् Mb. 1. 132. 68<BR> (com. भासं नीलपक्षं पक्षिणं शकुन्तमित्यन्ये गृध्रमित्यपरे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासक|भासकः
भासक <i>a.</i> (-सिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भास्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Enlightening, brightening, illuminating.<BR>—2 Showing, making evident.<BR>—3 Making intelligible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासकः|भासक
भासक + .{@-कः@} N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासता
भासता Vulturous nature, rapacity; स याति भासतां विप्रः Ms. 11. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासनम्
भासनम् [भास्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Shining, glittering.<BR>—2 Illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्त|भासंत|भासन्तः
भासन्त <i>a.</i> (-न्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Shining.<BR>—2 Beautiful, handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्तः|भासन्त|भासंत
भासन्त + .{@-न्तः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 An asterism, a star.<BR>—4 The bird भास q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासन्ती|भासंती
भासन्त + .{@-न्ती@} An asterism (नक्षत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासस्
भासस् <i>n.</i> Brightness, light; भासांसि वस्ते सूर्यो न शुकः Rv. 6. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुः|भासु
भासुः The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुर|भासुरं|भासुरः
भासुर <i>a.</i> [भास्-घुरच्]<BR>—1 Shining, bright, splendid; मणिमयूखचयांशुकभासुराः Ki. 5. 5;<BR> तं भूपतिर्भासुरहेमराशिं (दिदेश) R. 5. 30.<BR>—2 Terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भासुरः|भासुर|भासुरं
भासुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A hero.<BR>—2 A crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वत्|भास्वन्त्
भास्वत् <i>a.</i> Bright, shining, luminous, resplendent; भास्वन्ति<BR> रत्नानि महौषधीश्च पृथूपदिष्टां दुदुहुर्धरित्रीम् Ku. 1. 2, 6. 60. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sun; भास्वानुदेष्यति हसिष्यति चक्रवालम् Subhāṣ.; R. 16. 44.<BR>—2 Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>—3 A hero.<BR>—4 Ved. Dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वती
भास्वत् + .{@-ती@} The city of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वर|भास्वरं|भास्वरः
भास्वर <i>a.</i> [भास्-वरच्] Shining, bright, radiant, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्वरः|भास्वर|भास्वरं
भास्वर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 A day.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास्मन
भास्मन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भस्मनो विकारोऽण्] Consisting or made of ashes,<BR> ashy; अहिपरिकरभाजो भास्मनैरङ्गरागैः Śi. 4. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्ष्
भिक्ष् €1 Ā. (भिक्षते, भिक्षित)<BR>—1 To ask, beg or ask for (with two acc.); भिक्षमाणो वनं प्रियाम् Bk. 6. 9.<BR>—2 To beg (as alms); न यज्ञार्थं धनं शूद्राद्विप्रो भिक्षेत कर्हिचित्<BR> Ms. 11. 24, 25.<BR>—3 To ask without obtaining.<BR>—4 To be weary or distressed.<BR>—5 To obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षणम्
भिक्षणम् [भिक्ष्-ल्युट्] Begging, begging alms, mendicancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षा
भिक्षा [भिक्ष्-अ]<BR>—1 Asking, begging, soliciting; वृत्ते शरावसंपाते भिक्षां नित्यं यतिश्चरेत् Ms. 6. 56.<BR>—2 Anything given as alms, alms; भवति भिक्षां देहि.<BR>—3 Wages, hire.<BR>—4 Service.<BR>—5 A means of subsistence; अपेतक्लमसंतापाः सुभिक्षाः सुप्रतिश्रयाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">Page1197-2</a>]<BR> Rām. 2. 92. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भिक्षाटनम्, भिक्षान्नम्, भिक्षायनम्, भिक्षार्थिन्, भिक्षार्ह, भिक्षाशनम्, भिक्षाशिन्, भिक्षाहारः, भिक्षोपजीविन्, भिक्षाकरणम्, भिक्षाचरः, भिक्षाचारः, भिक्षाचरणम्, भिक्षाचर्यम्, भिक्षाचर्या, भिक्षापात्रम्, भिक्षाभुज्, भिक्षामाणवः, भिक्षावासस्, भिक्षावृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाटनम्
भिक्षा + -अटनम् wandering about begging for alms; रुद्रो येन कपालपाणिपुटके<BR> भिक्षाटनं कारितः Bh. 2. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाटनः|भिक्षाटन|भिक्षाटनं
भिक्षा + -अटनम् + .({@-नः@}) a beggar, mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षान्नम्
भिक्षा + -अन्नम् food obtained by begging, alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षायनम्
भिक्षा + -अयनम् ({@णम्@}) = भिक्षाटन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षार्थिन्
भिक्षा + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> begging for alms or charity. ━(<i>m.</i>) a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षार्ह
भिक्षा + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> worthy of alms, a fit object of charity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाशनम्
भिक्षा + -अशनम् the food obtained by begging; भिक्षाशनं तदपि नीरसमेकवारम् Bh. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाशिन्
भिक्षा + -आशिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 living on alms; भिक्षाशी जनमध्यसंगरहितः Bh. 3. 86.<BR>—2 dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाहारः|भिक्षाहार
भिक्षा + -आहारः begged food; Bh. 3. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षोपजीविन्
भिक्षा + -उपजीविन् <i>a.</i> living on alms, a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाकरणम्
भिक्षा + -करणम् asking alms, begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचरः|भिक्षाचर
भिक्षा + -चरः, -चारः a beggar or mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचारः|भिक्षाचार
भिक्षा + -चरः, -चारः a beggar or mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचरणम्
भिक्षा + -चरणम्, -चर्यम्, -चर्या wandering about begging for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचर्यम्
भिक्षा + -चरणम्, -चर्यम्, -चर्या wandering about begging for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाचर्या
भिक्षा + -चरणम्, -चर्यम्, -चर्या wandering about begging for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षापात्रम्
भिक्षा + -पात्रम् a begging-bowl, an alms-dish; so भिक्षाभाण्डम्, भिक्षाभाजनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाभुज्
भिक्षा + -भुज् <i>a.</i> living on alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षामाणवः|भिक्षामाणव
भिक्षा + -माणवः a young beggar (used as a term of contempt); P. VI. 2. 69 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षावासस्
भिक्षा + -वासस् <i>n.</i> a beggarʼs dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षावृत्तिः|भिक्षावृत्ति
भिक्षा + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> living by begging, a mendicantʼs life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षाकः|भिक्षाक
भिक्षाकः (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> A beggar, mendicant; P. III. 2. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षित
भिक्षित <i>p. p.</i> Begged, asked, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुः|भिक्षु
भिक्षुः [भिक्ष्-उन्]<BR>—1 A beggar, mendicant in general; भिक्षां च भिक्षवे दद्यात् Ms. 3. 94.<BR>—2 A religious mendicant, a Brāhmaṇa in the fourth order of his religious<BR> life (when he quits his house and family and lives only on alms), a <i>Sannyāsin</i>.<BR>—3 The fourth order or stage in the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa (संन्यास).<BR>—4 A Buddhist mendicant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भिक्षुचर्या, भिक्षुभावः, भिक्षुसङ्घः, भिक्षुसङ्घाती, भिक्षुसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुचर्या
भिक्षुः + -चर्या begging, a mendicantʼs life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुभावः|भिक्षुभाव
भिक्षुः + -भावः monk-hood, priest-hood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुसङ्घः|भिक्षुसङ्घ
भिक्षुः + -सङ्घः a society of Buddhist mendicants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुसङ्घाती|भिक्षुसंघाती
भिक्षुः + -सङ्घाती old or tattered clothes (चीवर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुसूत्रम्
भिक्षुः + -सूत्रम् a collection of rules for mendicants; P. IV. 3. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुकः|भिक्षुक
भिक्षुकः [भिक्ष्-उक] A beggar, mendicant; आकीर्णं भिक्षुकैर्वान्यैरगारमुपसंव्रजेत् Ms. 6. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिक्षुकी
भिक्षुकः + .{@-की@} A female mendicant; cf. भिक्षुणी A Buddhist nun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिङ्गिसी
भिङ्गिसी A variety of कम्बल; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिण्डः|भिण्ड
भिण्डः, भिण्डकः, भिण्डा Abelmoschus Esculentus (Mar. भेंडा);<BR> एरण्डभिण्डार्कनलैः प्रभूतैरपि संचितैः । दारुकृत्यं यथा नास्ति तथैवाज्ञैः<BR> प्रयोजनम् Pt. 1. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिण्डकः|भिण्डक
भिण्डः, भिण्डकः, भिण्डा Abelmoschus Esculentus (Mar. भेंडा);<BR> एरण्डभिण्डार्कनलैः प्रभूतैरपि संचितैः । दारुकृत्यं यथा नास्ति तथैवाज्ञैः<BR> प्रयोजनम् Pt. 1. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिण्डा
भिण्डः, भिण्डकः, भिण्डा Abelmoschus Esculentus (Mar. भेंडा);<BR> एरण्डभिण्डार्कनलैः प्रभूतैरपि संचितैः । दारुकृत्यं यथा नास्ति तथैवाज्ञैः<BR> प्रयोजनम् Pt. 1. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद् I. €1 P. (भिन्दति)<BR> To divide or cut into parts. ━II. €7 U. (भिनत्ति,<BR> भिन्त्ते, बिभेद, बिभिदे, अभैत्सीत्, अभिनत्, अभिन्त्त, भेत्स्यति-ते, भेत्तुम्<BR> भिन्न) —1 To break, cleave, split, cut asunder, rend, pierce, break through<BR> or down; अतिशीतलमप्यम्भः किं भिनत्ति न भूभृतः H. 3. 38; तेषां<BR> कथं नु हृदयं न भिनत्ति लज्जा Mu. 3. 34; Śi. 8. 39; Ms. 3. 33;<BR> R. 8. 93, 12. 77.<BR>—2 To dig or tear up, excavate; U. 1. 23.<BR>—3 To pass through; यदि रोहिण्याः शकटं भिनत्ति रविनन्दनो गगनवीथ्याम्<BR> Pt. 1. 211, 212.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To divide, separate; द्विधा भिन्ना शिखण्डिभिः R. 1. 39.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To displace; आनन्दजः शोकजमश्रु बाष्पस्तयोरशीतं शिशिरो<BR> बिभेद R. 14. 3.<BR>—5 To violate, break, infringe; समयं लक्ष्मणोऽभिनत् R. 15. 94;<BR> निहतश्च स्थितिं भिन्दन् दानवोऽसौ बलद्विषा Bk. 7. 68.<BR>—6 To remove, take away; धैर्यमभिनदुदितं शिशुना Śi. 15. 87.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">Page1198-1</a>]<BR>—7 To disturb, interrupt; as in समाधिभेदिन्; असिपत्रवने चैव भिद्यमानानधार्मिकान्<BR> Rām. 7. 21. 15.<BR>—8 To change, alter; (न) भिन्दन्ति मन्दां गतिमश्वमुख्यः Ku. 1. 11;<BR> or विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः शब्दं सहन्ते मृगाः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—9 To expand, cause to open or blossom, open; सूर्यांशुभिर्भिन्नमिवारविन्दम्<BR> Ku. 1. 32; नवोषसा भिन्नमिवैकपङ्कजम् Ś. 7. 16; Me. 109.<BR>—10 To disperse, scatter, scare away; भिन्नसारङ्गयूथः Ś. 1. 32; V. 1. 16.<BR>—11 To disjoin, disunite, set at variance; भेत्स्यामि स्वमतेन भेदकुशलो<BR> ह्येष प्रतीपं द्विषः Mu. 3. 13.<BR>—12 To loosen, relax, dissolve; पर्यङ्कबन्धं निबिडं बिभेद Ku. 3. 59.<BR>—13 To disclose, divulge.<BR>—14 To perplex, distract.<BR>—15 To distinguish, discriminate.<BR>—16 To explain or to understand; वचांसि योगग्रथितानि साधो न नः क्षमन्ते<BR> मनसापि भेत्तुम् Bhāg. 5. 10. 18. ━<i>Pass.</i> (भिद्यते)<BR>—1 To be split, rent or shivered; धरा धारापातैर्मणिमयशरैर्भिद्यत<BR> इव Mk. 5. 22.<BR>—2 To be divided or separated.<BR>—3 To expand, blossom, open.<BR>—4 To be loose or relaxed; प्रस्थानभिन्नां न बबन्ध नीविम् R. 7. 9, 66.<BR>—5 To be different from (with abl.); न कारणात् स्वाद् बिभिदे कुमारः<BR> प्रवर्तितो दीप इव प्रदीपात् R. 5. 37; U. 4.<BR>—6 To be destroyed.<BR>—7 To be divulged or betrayed, get abroad; षट्कर्णो भिद्यते मन्त्रः &c. Pt. 1. 99.<BR>—8 To be harassed, pained or afflicted.<BR>—9 To be frightened or alarmed; अम्भसा भिद्यते सेतुस्तथा मन्त्रोऽप्यरक्षितः ।<BR> पैशुन्याद् भिद्यते स्नेहो वाचा भिद्येत कातरः ॥ Pt. 1. 102.<BR>—10 To separate oneself from, keep aloof from. ━<i>Caus.</i> (भेदयति-ते)<BR>—1 To split, cleave, divide, tear &c.<BR>—2 To destroy, dissolve.<BR>—3 To disunite, set at variance.<BR>—4 To perplex.<BR>—5 To seduce. ━<i>Desid.</i> (बिभित्सति-ते) To wish to break &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1197-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तम्
भित्तम् (भिद्-क्त नि˚ तस्य न नः)<BR>—1 A part, portion; गृहाः शशभृद्भित्तनिरङ्कभित्तयः N. 2. 74.<BR>—2 A fragment, bit.<BR>—3 A wall, partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्ति|भित्तिः
भित्ति <i>f.</i> [भिद्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Breaking, splitting; dividing.<BR>—2 A wall, partition; समया सौधभित्तिम् Dk.; Śi. 4. 67 fort-wall;<BR> इष्टकोपलमृद्भित्तिप्राकारं पारिघं स्मृतम् Śukra. 4. 849.<BR>—3 (Hence) Any place, spot or ground (आश्रय) to work anything upon;<BR> चित्रकर्मरचना भित्तिं विना वर्तते Mu. 2. 4.<BR>—4 A fragment, bit, piece, portion.<BR>—5 Anything broken.<BR>—6 A rent, fissure.<BR>—7 A mat (made of split reeds).<BR>—8 A flaw, defect.<BR>—9 An opportunity.<BR>—10 A wall-like surface; कपोलभित्ति, गण्डभित्ति &c.; सिंहः शिशुरपि<BR> निपतति मदमलिनकपोलभित्तिषु गजेषु Bh. 1. 38.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भित्तिखातनः, भित्तिचौरः, भित्तिपातनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिखातनः|भित्तिखातन
भित्ति + -खातनः a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिचौरः|भित्तिचौर
भित्ति + -चौरः a house-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिपातनः|भित्तिपातन
भित्ति + -पातनः<BR>—1 a kind of rat.<BR>—2 a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भित्तिका
भित्तिका<BR>—1 A wall, partition.<BR>—2 A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्
भिद् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Breaking, splitting; destroying<BR> &c.; तुरगविचयव्यग्रानुर्वींभिदः U. 1. 23. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Breaking, splitting, dividing.<BR>—2 Difference.<BR>—3 A sort, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदकः|भिदक|भिदकं
भिदकः [भिद्-क्वुन्] A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदकम्
भिदकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A diamond.<BR>—2 Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदा
भिदा [भिद्-भावे अङ्]<BR>—1 Breaking, bursting, rending, tearing; विरहिणां हृदयस्य भिदाभृतः<BR> कपिशितं पिशितं मदनाग्निना Śi. 6. 5.<BR>—2 Separation.<BR>—3 Difference.<BR>—4 Kind, species, sort.<BR>—5 Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदापनम्
भिदापनम् Causing to break or trample on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदिः|भिदि
भिदिः, भिदिरम्, भिदुः Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदिरम्
भिदिः, भिदिरम्, भिदुः Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुः|भिदु
भिदिः, भिदिरम्, भिदुः Indraʼs thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुर|भिदुरं|भिदुरः
भिदुर <i>a.</i> [भिद्-कुरच्]<BR>—1 Breaking, bursting, splitting,<BR>—2 Fragile, brittle.<BR>—3 Blended, variegated, mixed, mingled; नीलाश्मद्युतिभिदुराम्भसोऽपरत्र<BR> Śi. 4. 26, 19. 58, 20. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुरः|भिदुर|भिदुरं
भिदुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The <i>Plakṣa</i> tree.<BR>—2 A chain for an elephantʼs feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदुरम्
भिदुर + .{@-रम्@} A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिदेलिम
भिदेलिम <i>a.</i> Fragile, brittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्यः|भिद्य
भिद्यः<BR>—1 A rushing river.<BR>—2 N. of a particular river; तोयदागम इवोद्धपभिद्ययोर्नामधेयसदृशं<BR> विचेष्टितम् R. 11. 8; (see Malli.); Kīr. K. 4. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्यम्
भिद्यः + .{@-द्यम्@} Splitting, breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिद्रम्
भिद्रम् A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दपालः|भिन्दपाल|भिंदपाल|भिंदपालः
भिन्द(न्दि)पालः<BR>—1 A small javelin thrown from the hand; वानरान् भिन्दिपालैश्च शूलैश्चैव<BR> व्यदारयन् Rām. 6. 42. 45.<BR>—2 A sling, an instrument like a sling for throwing stones; उल्काबाणैश्च<BR> शतशः भिन्दिपालैश्च भूरिशः Śiva B. 14. 20; भिन्दिपालासिपट्टिशैः<BR> Parṇāl. 4. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दिपालः|भिन्दिपाल|भिंदिपाल|भिंदिपालः
भिन्द(न्दि)पालः<BR>—1 A small javelin thrown from the hand; वानरान् भिन्दिपालैश्च शूलैश्चैव<BR> व्यदारयन् Rām. 6. 42. 45.<BR>—2 A sling, an instrument like a sling for throwing stones; उल्काबाणैश्च<BR> शतशः भिन्दिपालैश्च भूरिशः Śiva B. 14. 20; भिन्दिपालासिपट्टिशैः<BR> Parṇāl. 4. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दु|भिंदु|भिन्दुः
भिन्दु <i>a.</i> Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्दुः|भिन्दु|भिंदु
भिन्दु + .{@-न्दुः@}<BR>—1 A breaker, destroyer; पुरां भिन्दुर्युवा कविरमितौजा अजायत Rv. 1. 11. 4.<BR>—2 A drop; cf. बिन्दु. {@-न्दुः@} <i>f.</i> A woman bringing<BR> forth a dead child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्न|भिन्नः
भिन्न <i>p. p.</i> [भिद्-क्त]<BR>—1 Broken, torn, split, rent; संछिन्नभिन्नसर्वाङ्गाः सर्त्विक्सभ्या भयाकुलाः ।<BR> स्वयंभुवे नमस्कृत्य Bhāg. 4. 6. 2.<BR>—2 Divided, separated.<BR>—3 Detached, disunited, disjoined; scattered; भिन्नं च वानरानीकम्<BR> Rām. 6. 67. 80.<BR>—4 Expanded, blown, opened; भिन्नैलासुरभिमुवाह गन्धवाहः Ki. 7. 38.<BR>—5 Different from, other than (with abl.); तस्मादयं भिन्नः.<BR>—6 Different, varied; भिन्नरुचिर्हि लोकः R. 6. 30.<BR>—7 Loosened.<BR>—8 Mingled, mixed, blended; एकत्र स्फटिकतटांशुभिन्ननीरा नीलाश्मद्युतिभिदुराम्भसोऽपरत्र Śi. 4. 26.<BR>—9 Deviating from.<BR>—10 Changed.<BR>—11 Furious; दुरुक्तैर्भिन्नमात्मानं यः समाधातुमीश्वरः Bhāg. 11. 23. 2.<BR>—12 Without, deprived of.<BR>—13 Undutiful, vicious; भिन्नवृत्तिता Ms. 12. 33; नैतत् खलायोपदिशेत् … … न<BR> भिन्नाय Bhāg. 3. 32. 39.<BR>—14 Stood up (as hair); खरोष्ट्राश्वतरा राजन् भिन्नरोमाः स्रवन्ति च<BR> Rām. 6. 10. 18.<BR>—15 Seduced, bribed; H. (See भिद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नः|भिन्न
भिन्न + .{@-न्नः@} A defect or flaw in a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नम्
भिन्न + .{@-न्नम्@}<BR>—1 A bit, fragment, part.<BR>—2 A blossom.<BR>—3 A wound, stab; शक्तिकुन्तेषुखड्गाग्रविषाणैराशयो हतः । यत् किंचित्<BR> प्रसवेत् तद्धि भिन्नमित्यभिधीयते Bhāva P.<BR>—4 A fraction.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भिन्नाञ्जनम्, भिन्नार्थ, भिन्नोदरः, भिन्नकट, भिन्नकरटः, भिन्नकरट,^1 भिन्नकुम्भः, भिन्नकूट, भिन्नक्रम, भिन्नगति, भिन्नगर्भ, भिन्नगात्रिका, भिन्नगुणनम्, भिन्नघनः, भिन्नदर्शिन्, भिन्नदेश, भिन्नदेह, भिन्ननौ, भिन्नपरिकर्मन्, भिन्नप्रकार, भिन्नभागहरः, भिन्नभाजनम्, भिन्नमन्त्र, भिन्नमर्मन्, भिन्नमर्याद, भिन्नरुचि, भिन्नलिङ्गम्, भिन्नवचनम्, भिन्नवर्गः, भिन्नवर्चस्, भिन्नवर्चस्क, भिन्नवर्ण, भिन्नवृत्त, भिन्नवृत्ति, भिन्नव्यवकलितम्, भिन्नसंहति, भिन्नसंकलनम्, भिन्नसंकलितम्, भिन्नस्वर, भिन्नहृतिः, भिन्नहृदय<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नाञ्जनम्
भिन्न + -अञ्जनम् a kind of mixed collyrium, made of many pounded ingredients;<BR> प्रयान्ति … … भिन्नाञ्जनवर्णतां घनाः Śi. 12. 68; Me. 61; Ṛs. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नार्थ
भिन्न + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> clear, evident, intelligible; स्फुटभिन्नार्थमुदाहरद्<BR> वचः Śi. 16. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नार्थम्
भिन्न + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थम्@}) <i>ind.</i> clearly, distinctly, unenigmatically; न खल्ववगच्छामि<BR> भिन्नार्थमभिधीयताम् Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नोदरः|भिन्नोदर
भिन्न + -उदरः ‘born of a different womb or mother’,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">Page1199-1</a>]<BR> a half-brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1198-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नकट
भिन्न + -कट <i>a.</i> furious, in rut; भेजे भिन्नकटैर्नागैरन्यानुपरुरोध<BR> यैः R. 4. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नकरटः|भिन्नकरट
भिन्न + -करटः an elephant in rut (from whose temples ichor exudes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नकरट|भिन्नकरटः
भिन्न + -करट^1 <i>a.</i> having divided ears (said of particular animals); P. VI. 3. 115.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नकुम्भः|भिन्नकुम्भ
भिन्न + -कुम्भः a person who has regained his liberty by redeeming his pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नकूट
भिन्न + -कूट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 deprived of a leader (as an army).<BR>—2 employing a different stratagem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नक्रम
भिन्न + -क्रम <i>a.</i> out of order, disordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगति
भिन्न + -गति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going with broken steps.<BR>—2 going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगर्भ
भिन्न + -गर्भ <i>a.</i> broken up (in the centre), disorganized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगात्रिका
भिन्न + -गात्रिका Cucumis Usitatissimus (Mar. चिबूड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नगुणनम्
भिन्न + -गुणनम् multiplication of fractions; अंशाहतिश्छेदवधेन भक्ता<BR> लब्धं विभिन्ने गुणने फलं स्यात् Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नघनः|भिन्नघन
भिन्न + -घनः the cube of a fraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नदर्शिन्
भिन्न + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> making or seeing a difference, partial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नदेश
भिन्न + -देश <i>a.</i> belonging to different places; कृत्ययोर्भिन्नदेशत्वाद्<BR> द्वैधीभवति मे मनः । Ś. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नदेह
भिन्न + -देह <i>a.</i> wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्ननौ
भिन्न + -नौ <i>a.</i> ship-wrecked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नपरिकर्मन्|भिन्नपरिकर्म्मन्
भिन्न + -परिकर्मन् <i>n.</i> any one of the arithmetical operations with fractions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नप्रकार
भिन्न + -प्रकार <i>a.</i> of a different kind or sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभागहरः|भिन्नभागहर
भिन्न + -भागहरः division of fractions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नभाजनम्
भिन्न + -भाजनम् a potsherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमन्त्र
भिन्न + -मन्त्र <i>a.</i> one who has betrayed a plan; Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमर्मन्|भिन्नमर्म्मन्
भिन्न + -मर्मन् <i>a.</i> wounded in vital parts, mortally wounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नमर्याद
भिन्न + -मर्याद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has transgressed the due limits, disrespectful; आः, तातापवादभिन्नमर्याद U. 5.<BR>—2 unrestrained, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नरुचि
भिन्न + -रुचि <i>a.</i> having different tastes; भिन्नरुचिर्हि लोकः R. 6. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नलिङ्गम्
भिन्न + -लिङ्गम्, -वचनम् incongruity of gender or number in a composition; see K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवचनम्
भिन्न + -लिङ्गम्, -वचनम् incongruity of gender or number in a composition; see K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्गः|भिन्नवर्ग
भिन्न + -वर्गः the square of a fraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्चस्
भिन्न + -वर्चस्, -वर्चस्क <i>a.</i> voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्चस्क
भिन्न + -वर्चस्, -वर्चस्क <i>a.</i> voiding excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवर्ण
भिन्न + -वर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 discoloured, pale.<BR>—2 of a different caste or tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवृत्त
भिन्न + -वृत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 leading a bad life, abandoned.<BR>—2 containing a metrical fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नवृत्ति
भिन्न + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 leading a bad life, following evil courses; तदन्तःपुरेषु चामी भिन्नवृत्तेषु<BR> मन्दत्रसा बहुसुखैरवर्तन्त Dk. 2. 8.<BR>—2 having different feelings or tastes or emotions.<BR>—3 having different occupations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1199-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भिन्नव्यवकलितम्
