भीष्म|भीष्मं|भीष्मः
भीष्म <i>a.</i> [भी-णिच्-सुक्-अपादाने मक्] Terrible, dreadful, frightful,<BR> fearful; भीष्मो हि देवः सहसः सहीयान् Bhāg. 11. 23. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मः|भीष्म|भीष्मं
भीष्म + .{@-ष्मः@}<BR>—1 The sentiment of terror (in rhetoric); see भयानक.<BR>—2 A demon, an imp, a fiend, goblin.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—4 N. of the son of Śantanu by Gangā; हृते भीष्मे हते द्रोणे शल्ये<BR> च निधनं गते Mb. [He was the youngest of the eight sons of Śantanu<BR> by Gangā; but all the others having died, he remained the sole heir to<BR> the throne after his father. On one occasion while Śantanu was walking<BR> by the side of a river, he beheld a charming young damsel named Satyavatī,<BR> the daughter of a fisherman, and, though bowed down<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">Page1201-1</a>]<BR> with age, conceived a passion for her, and sent his son to negotiate the<BR> marriage. But the parents of the girl said that if their daughter bore<BR> sons to the king, they would not succeed to the throne, for after his<BR> death Śāntanava, being the rightful heir, would be the king. But Śāntanava,<BR> to please his father, made a vow to the parents that he would never accept<BR> the kingdom or marry a wife or become the father of children by any woman,<BR> so that if their daughter bore a son to Śantanu, he would be the king.<BR> This dreadful vow soon became known abroad, and thenceforth he was called<BR> <i>Bhiṣma</i>. He remained single, and, after the death of his father,<BR> he installed Vicitravīrya, the son of Śatyavatī, on the throne, got<BR> him married to the two daughters of king Kāśirāja (see Ambikā), and<BR> became the guardian of his sons and grandsons, the Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas.<BR> In the great war he fought on the side of the Kauravas, but was wounded<BR> by Arjuna with the assistance of Śikhanḍin and was lodged in a ‘cage of darts’<BR>. But having got from his father the power of choosing his own<BR> time for death, he waited till the sun had crossed the vernal equinox,<BR> and then gave up his soul. He was remarkable for his continence, wisdom,<BR> firmness of resolve, and unflinching devotion to God].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मम्
भीष्म + .{@-ष्मम्@} Horror, horribleness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भीष्माष्टमी, भीष्मजननी, भीष्मपञ्चकम्, भीष्मपर्वन्, भीष्मसूः, भीष्मस्तवराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1200-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्माष्टमी
भीष्म + -अष्टमी the eighth day in the light half of Māgha (when Bhīṣma died).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मजननी
भीष्म + -जननी an epithet of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मपञ्चकम्
भीष्म + -पञ्चकम् N. of the five days from the eleventh to the fifteenth<BR> of the bright balf of Kārtika (said to be sacred to Bhīṣma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मपर्वन्
भीष्म + -पर्वन् N. of the 6th Book of the Mahā-Bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मसूः
भीष्म + -सूः <i>f.</i> an epithet of the river Ganges; हरशिरसि पतन्ती<BR> भीष्मसूर्वः पुनातु Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मस्तवराजः|भीष्मस्तवराज
भीष्म + -स्तवराजः N. of the 47th Chapter of शान्तिपर्व in Mahābhāraṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भीष्मकः|भीष्मक
भीष्मकः<BR>—1 N. of a son of Śantanu by Gangā.<BR>—2 N. of a king of the Vidarbhas, whose daughter Rukmiṇī was carried<BR> off by Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
भुज् I. €6 P. (भुजति, भुग्न)<BR>—1 To bend.<BR>—2 To curve, make crooked. ━II. €7 U. (भुनक्ति-भुङ्क्ते, भुक्त)<BR>—1 To eat, devour, consume (Ātm.); शयनस्थो न भुञ्जीत Ms. 4. 74, 3. 146;<BR> Bk. 14. 92; हत्वार्थकामांस्तु गुरूनिहैव भुञ्जीय भोगान् रुधिरप्रदिग्धान् Bg. 2. 5.<BR>—2 To enjoy, use, possess (property, land &c.); संप्रीत्या भुज्यमानानि<BR> न नश्यन्ति कदाचन Ms. 8. 146; Y. 2. 24.<BR>—3 To enjoy carnally (Ātm.); सदयं बुभुजे महाभुजः R. 8. 7, 4. 7, 15. 1, 18. 4;<BR> सुरूपं वा कुरूपं वा पुमानित्येव भुञ्जते Ms. 9. 14.<BR>—4 To rule, govern, protect, guard (Paras.); राज्यं न्यासमिवाभुनक्<BR> R. 12. 18; एकः कृत्स्नां (धरित्रीं) नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति Ś. 2. 16.<BR>—5 To suffer, endure, experience; वृद्धो नरो दुःखशतानि भुङ्क्ते Sk.<BR>—6 To pass, live through (as time).<BR>—7 (In astr.) To pass through, fulfil. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be enjoyed or eaten.<BR>—2 To be possessed.<BR>—3 To be brought under the influence of. ━<i>Caus.</i> (भोजयति-ते)<BR> To cause to eat, feed with. ━<i>Desid.</i> (बुभुक्षति-ते) To wish to eat &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्त|भुक्तं
भुक्त <i>p. p.</i> [भुज्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Eaten.<BR>—2 Enjoyed, used; भोगा न भुक्ता वयमेव भुक्ताः Bh. 3. 12; न तद्<BR> भुक्तं न तत् पीतं न तत् सुप्तं न तद्गतम् Udb.<BR>—3 Suffered, experienced.<BR>—4 Possessed, occupied (in law).<BR>—5 Passed (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तम्
भुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 The act of eating or enjoying.<BR>—2 That which is eaten, food.<BR>—3 The place where any one has eaten.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भुक्तोच्छिष्टम्, भुक्तशेषः, भुक्तसमुज्झितम्, भुक्तपीत, भुक्तभोग, भुक्तमात्रे, भुक्तवृद्धिः, भुक्तसुप्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तोच्छिष्टम्
भुक्त + -उच्छिष्टम्, -शेषः, -समुज्झितम् remnants of the food eaten, leavings of food, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तशेषः|भुक्तशेष
भुक्त + -उच्छिष्टम्, -शेषः, -समुज्झितम् remnants of the food eaten, leavings of food, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तसमुज्झितम्
भुक्त + -उच्छिष्टम्, -शेषः, -समुज्झितम् remnants of the food eaten, leavings of food, orts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तपीत
भुक्त + -पीत <i>a.</i> one who has eaten and drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तभोग
भुक्त + -भोग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 one who has enjoyed or suffered (anything).<BR>—2 that which has been used, enjoyed, or employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तमात्रे
भुक्त + -मात्रे <i>ind.</i> immediately on having eaten; Ms. 4. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तवृद्धिः|भुक्तवृद्धि
भुक्त + -वृद्धिः <i>f.</i> the swelling of food (in the stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तसुप्त
भुक्त + -सुप्त <i>a.</i> sleeping after a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तिः|भुक्ति
भुक्तिः <i>f.</i> [भुज्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Eating, enjoyment; भुक्तिं मुक्तिं च विन्दति Rāmarakṣā 12.<BR>—2 (In law) Possession, fruition; प्रमाणं लिखितं भुक्तिः साक्षिणश्चेति<BR> कीर्तितम् Y. 2. 22; Pt. 3. 94.<BR>—3 Food.<BR>—4 The daily motion of a planet.<BR>—5 A limit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भुक्तिपात्रम्, भुक्तिप्रदः, भुक्तिवर्जित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तिपात्रम्
भुक्तिः + -पात्रम् a food-dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तिप्रदः|भुक्तिप्रद
भुक्तिः + -प्रदः a kind of plant (मुद्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुक्तिवर्जित
भुक्तिः + -वर्जित <i>a.</i> not allowed to be enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुगुभुगुः
भुगुभुगुः The sound of fire (अग्निध्वनि); अनुष्णाशीतसंस्पर्शो<BR> वह्नौ भुगुभुगुध्वनिः Pañcadaśī 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुग्न|भुग्नः
भुग्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bent, bowed, stooping; as in वायुभुग्न, रुजाभुग्न &c.; आस्ते कृत्वा<BR> शिरः कुक्षौ भुग्नपृष्ठशिरोधरः Bhāg. 3. 31. 8; भरभुग्नविततबाहुषु गोपेषु Vās.<BR>—2 Crooked, curved; पीनो भटस्योरसि वीक्ष्य भुग्नांस्तनुत्वचः पाणिरुहान्<BR> सुमध्या Bk. 11. 8; V. 4. 32.<BR>—3 Broken (for भग्न); स शेते निहतो भूमौ वातभुग्न इव द्रुमः Mb. 6. 14. 16.<BR>—4 Cowed down, disheartened; किमनेनातिभुग्नेन वाग्भिः काष्ठसधर्मणा Mb. 9. 61. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुज्
भुज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 (At the end of comp.) Eating, enjoying, suffering, ruling, governing;<BR> स्वधाभुज्, हुतभुज्, पाप˚, क्षिति˚, मही˚ &c.<BR>—2 Useful, serviceable. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Enjoyment.<BR>—2 Profit, advantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजः|भुज
भुजः [भुज्यतेऽनेन, भुज्-घञर्थे करणे क]<BR>—1 The arm; ज्ञास्यसि कियद् भुजो मे रक्षति मौर्वीकिणाङ्क इति Ś. 1. 13;<BR> R. 1. 34, 2. 7, 3. 55.<BR>—2 The hand; यावन्तो रजनीचराः प्रहरणोद्भूर्णद्भुजाकेतवः Mv. 6. 59.<BR>—3 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>—4 A bend, curve.<BR>—5 The side of a mathematical figure; as in त्रिभुजः ‘a triangle’;<BR> तथायते तद्भुजकोटिघातः Līlā.<BR>—6 The base of a triangle.<BR>—7 A branch (of a tree.).<BR>—8 (In astr.) The base of a shadow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भुजाङ्कः, भुजाग्रम्, भुजान्तरम्, भुजान्तरालम्, भुजार्पणम्, भुजाकम्बुः, भुजापीडः, भुजकोटरः, भुजच्छाया, भुजज्या, भुजदण्डः, भुजदलः, भुजदलम्, भुजप्रतिभुजम्, भुजफलम्, भुजबन्धनम्, भुजबलम्, भुजवीर्यम्, भुजमध्यम्, भुजमूलम्, भुजलता, भुजविनिष्पेषः, भुजवीर्य, भुजशालिन्, भुजशिखरम्, भुजशिरस्, भुजसूत्रम्, भुजस्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजाङ्कः|भुजाङ्क
भुजः + -अङ्कः an embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजाग्रम्
भुजः + -अग्रम्<BR>—1 the hand.<BR>—2 the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजान्तरम्
भुजः + -अन्तरम्, -अन्तरालम् the bosom, breast; दिलीपसूनोः स बृहद्भुजान्तरम्<BR> R. 3. 54, 19. 32; M. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजान्तरालम्
भुजः + -अन्तरम्, -अन्तरालम् the bosom, breast; दिलीपसूनोः स बृहद्भुजान्तरम्<BR> R. 3. 54, 19. 32; M. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजार्पणम्
भुजः + -अर्पणम् the paying for subsistence; वाचा दण्डो ब्राह्मणानां<BR> क्षत्रियाणां भुजार्पणम् Mb. 12. 15. 9 (com. वेतनप्रदानम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजाकम्बुः
भुजः + -आकम्बुः a conch, a bracelet; त्रुटद्भुजाकम्बुमृणालहारिणी N. 12. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजापीडः|भुजापीड
भुजः + -आपीडः clasping or folding in the arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजकोटरः|भुजकोटर
भुजः + -कोटरः the arm-pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजच्छाया
भुजः + -छाया secure shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजज्या
भुजः + -ज्या the base sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजदण्डः|भुजदण्ड
भुजः + -दण्डः a staff-like arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजदलः|भुजदल
भुजः + -दलः, -दलम् the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1201-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भुजदलम्
