भूफलः|भूफल
भूः + -पलः, -फलः a kind of rat (Mar. घूस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपवित्रम्
भूः + -पवित्रम् cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपालः|भूपाल
भूः + -पालः<BR>—1 a king, sovereign; भूपालसिंहं निजगाद सिंहः.<BR>—2 an epithet of king Bhoja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपालनम्
भूः + -पालनम् sovereignty, dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपुत्रः|भूपुत्र
भूः + -पुत्रः, -सुतः<BR>—1 the planet Mars.<BR>—2 N. of the demon Naraka; q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूसुतः|भूसुत
भूः + -पुत्रः, -सुतः<BR>—1 the planet Mars.<BR>—2 N. of the demon Naraka; q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूपुत्री
भूः + -पुत्री, -सुता ‘daughter of the earth’, an epithet of Sītā; भूपुत्री<BR> यस्य पत्नी स भवति कथं भूपती रामचन्द्रः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूसुता
भूः + -पुत्री, -सुता ‘daughter of the earth’, an epithet of Sītā; भूपुत्री<BR> यस्य पत्नी स भवति कथं भूपती रामचन्द्रः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूप्रकम्पः|भूप्रकम्प|भूप्रकंप
भूः + -प्रकम्पः an earthquake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूप्रदानम्
भूः + -प्रदानम् a gift of land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूफलः|भूफल
भूः + -फलः a kind of rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूबिम्बः|भूबिम्ब|भूबिंब
भूः + -बिम्बः, -बिम्बम् the terrestrial globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूबिम्बम्
भूः + -बिम्बः, -बिम्बम् the terrestrial globe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभर्तृ
भूः + -भर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a king, sovereign.<BR>—2 a mountain; भूभर्तुः शिरसि नभोनदीव रेजे Ki. 7. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभा
भूः + -भा the shadow of the earth on the moon (in an eclipse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभागः|भूभाग
भूः + -भागः a region, place, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभुज्
भूः + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a king; निवासाय प्रशस्यन्ते भूभुजां भूतिमिच्छताम् Kām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूभृत्
भूः + -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a mountain; दाता मे भूभृतां नाथः प्रमाणीक्रियतामिति Ku. 6. 1; R. 17. 78.<BR>—2 a king, sovereign; निष्प्रभश्च रिपुरास भूभृताम् R. 11. 81.<BR>—3 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 a term for the number ‘seven’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमणिः
भूः + -मणिः the king; अतस्तिष्ठामि भूत्वाहं कृपाणी भूमणे तव Śiva B. 20. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमण्डलम्
भूः + -मण्डलम्<BR>—1 the earth, (terrestrial globe).<BR>—2 the circumference of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयुक्ता
भूः + -युक्ता a kind of palm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुण्डी
भूः + -रुण्डी a kind of sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुह्
भूः + -रुह् <i>m.</i>, {@-रुहः@}<BR> a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरुहम्
भूः + -रुह् + ({@-हम्@}) a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलता
भूः + -लता a worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलिङ्गशकुनः|भूलिङ्गशकुन
भूः + -लिङ्गशकुनः a species of bird; भूलिङ्गशकुनाश्चान्ये सामुद्राः<BR> पर्वतोद्भवाः Mb. 12. 169. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूलोकः|भूलोक
भूः + -लोकः (भूर्लोकः)<BR>—1 the terrestrial globe.<BR>—2 the country on the southern part of the equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूवलयम्
भूः + -वलयम् = भूमण्डलम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूवल्लभः|भूवल्लभ
भूः + -वल्लभः a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूवल्लूरम्
भूः + -वल्लूरम् a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूवृत्तम्
भूः + -वृत्तम् the equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशक्रः|भूशक्र
भूः + -शक्रः ‘Indra on earth’, a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशमी
भूः + -शमी a kind of Acacia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशयः|भूशय
भूः + -शयः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 any animal lying on the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशय्या
भूः + -शय्या lying on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूशुद्धिः|भूशुद्धि
भूः + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> purification of the ground by sweeping &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूश्रवस्
भूः + -श्रवस् <i>m.</i> an ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूश्वभ्रम्
भूः + -श्वभ्रम् a hole in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूसुरः|भूसुर
भूः + -सुरः a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्थः|भूस्थ
भूः + -स्थः a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्पृश्
भूः + -स्पृश् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a man.<BR>—2 mankind.<BR>—3 a Vaiśya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्फोटः|भूस्फोट
भूः + -स्फोटः a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वर्गः|भूस्वर्ग
भूः + -स्वर्गः an epithet of the mountain Meru; भूस्वर्गायते to<BR> become a heaven on earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूस्वामिन्
भूः + -स्वामिन् <i>m.</i> a landlord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकः|भूक|भूकं
भूकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A cavity, hole, chasm.<BR>—2 The spring.<BR>—3 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकम्
भूकः, -कम्<BR>—1 A cavity, hole, chasm.<BR>—2 The spring.<BR>—3 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकः|भूक|भूकं
भूकः, -कम् + .{@-कः@} Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूकलः|भूकल
भूकलः A restive horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत|भूतं|भूतः
भूत <i>p. p.</i> [भू-क्त]<BR>—1 Become, being, existing.<BR>—2 Produced, formed.<BR>—3 Actually being, really happened, true; भूताश्चार्था विरुद्धपन्ति देशकालविरोधिताः<BR> Rām. 5. 30. 37.<BR>—4 Right, proper, fit; अभूतेनापवादेन कीर्तिं निपतितामिव Rām. 5. 15. 34;<BR> भूतार्थव्याहृतिः सा हि न स्तुतिः परमेष्ठिनः R. 10. 33.<BR>—5 Past, gone.<BR>—6 Obtained.<BR>—7 Mixed or joined with.<BR>—8 Being like, similar, (see भू); मग्नां द्विषच्छद्मनि पङ्कभूते Ki. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतः|भूत|भूतं
भूत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A son, child.<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 The fourteenth day of the dark half of a lunar month (also भूता).<BR>—4 A great devotee.<BR>—5 N. of a priest of the gods.<BR>—6 The dark fortnight of a month (कृष्णपक्ष).<BR>—7 see भूतगण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतम्
भूत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Any being (human, divine or even inanimate); इत्थं रतेः किमपि भूतमदृश्यरूपं<BR> मन्दीचकार मरणव्यवसायबुद्धिम् Ku. 4. 45; Pt. 2. 87.<BR>—2 A living being, an animal, a creature; क्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर<BR> उच्यते Bg. 15. 16; भूतेषु किं च करुणां बहुलीकरोति Bv. 1. 122; U. 4. 6.<BR>—3 A spirit, ghost, an imp, a devil (<i>m.</i> also in these senses); ततो<BR> रक्षां महातेजः कुरु भूतविनाशिनीम् Rām. 7. 66. 3.<BR>—4 An element; (they are five, <i>i. e.</i> पृथ्वी, अप्, तेजस्, वायु, and<BR> आकाश); तं वेधा विदधे नूनं महाभूतसमाधिना R. 1. 29.<BR>—5 An actual occurrence, a fact, a matter of fact.<BR>—6 The past, past time.<BR>—7 The world.<BR>—8 Well-being, welfare.<BR>—9 A symbolical expression for the number ‘five’.<BR>—10 Fitness, propriety.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूतानुकम्पा, भूतानुवादः, भूतान्तकः, भूताभिषङ्गः, भूतारिः, भूतार्थः, भूतावमानिन्, भूतात्मक, भूतात्मन्, भूतादिः, भूतार्त, भूतावासः, भूताविष्ट, भूतावेशः, भूतेज्यम्, भूतेज्या, भूतेन्द्रियजयिन्, भूतेष्टा, भूतेशः, भूतेश्वरः, भूतोन्मादः, भूतोपदेशः, भूतोपसृष्ट, भूतोपहत, भूतौदनः, भूतकर्तृ, भूतकृत्, भूतकला, भूतकालः, भूतकेशी, भूतकोटिः, भूतक्रान्तिः, भूतगणः, भूतगत्या, भूतगुणः, भूतग्रस्त, भूतग्रामः, भूतघ्नः, भूतचतुर्दशी, भूतचारिन्, भूतचिन्तकः, भूतचिन्तनिकः, भूतचिन्ता, भूतचैतन्यम्, भूतजननी, भूतजयः, भूततन्त्रम्, भूततन्मात्रम्, भूतदया, भूतद्रुमः, भूतद्रुह्, भूतध्रुक्, भूतधरा, भूतधात्री, भूतधारिणी, भूतधात्री, भूतनाथः, भूतनायिका, भूतनाशनः, भूतनिचयः, भूतपक्षः, भूतपतिः, भूतपत्री, भूतपालः, भूतपूर्णिमा, भूतपूर्वम्, भूतप्रकृतिः, भूतबलिः, भूतब्रह्मन्, भूतभर्तृ, भूतभव, भूतभव्यम्, भूतभावनः, भूतभाविन्, भूतभाषा, भूतभाषितम्, भूतभृत्, भूतभौतिक, भूतमहेश्वरः, भूतमातृ, भूतमातृका, भूतमात्रम्, भूतमात्रा, भूतमात्रा, भूतयज्ञः, भूतयोनिः, भूतरयाः, भूतराज्, भूतलिपिः, भूतवर्गः, भूतवादिन्, भूतवासः, भूतवाहनः, भूतविक्रिया, भूतविज्ञान, भूतविद्या, भूतविनायकः, भूतविभुः, भूतवृक्षः, भूतवेशी, भूतशुद्धिः, भूतसंसारः, भूतसंघः, भूतसंचारः, भूतसंचारिन्, भूतसंप्लवः, भूतसमागमः, भूतसर्गः, भूतसाक्षिन्, भूतसाधनी, भूतसूक्ष्मम्, भूतसृज्, भूतसृष्टिः, भूतस्थानम्, भूतहत्या, भूतहन्त्री, भूतहरः, भूतहासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतानुकम्पा|भूतानुकंपा
भूत + -अनुकम्पा compassion for all beings; भूतानुकम्पा तव चेत् R. 2. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतानुवादः
भूत + -अनुवादः a mention of established facts, a variety of अर्थवाद<BR> (q. v.); भूतानुवादमात्रमनर्थकम् ŚB. on MS. 1. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतान्तकः|भूतान्तक|भूतांतक
भूत + -अन्तकः the god of death, Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूताभिषङ्गः|भूताभिषङ्ग
भूत + -अभिषङ्गः possession by evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतारिः|भूतारि
भूत + -अरिः Asa Foetida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्थः|भूतार्थ
भूत + -अर्थः<BR>—1 the fact, real fact, true state, truth, reality; आर्ये कथयामि ते<BR> भूतार्थम् Ś. 1; भूतार्थशोभाह्रियमाणनेत्रा Ku. 7. 13; कः श्रद्धास्यति<BR> भूतार्थं सर्वो मां तुलयिष्यति Mk. 3. 24.<BR>—2 an element of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्थकथनम्
भूत + -अर्थः + ˚कथनम्, ˚व्याहृतिः <i>f.</i> a statement of facts;<BR> भूतार्थव्याहृतिः सा हि न स्तुतिः परमेष्ठिनः R. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्थव्यवहृतिः
भूत + -अर्थः + ˚कथनम्, ˚व्याहृतिः <i>f.</i> a statement of facts;<BR> भूतार्थव्याहृतिः सा हि न स्तुतिः परमेष्ठिनः R. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावमानिन्
भूत + -अवमानिन् <i>m.</i> despiser of all; भूतावमानी हैहयश्चार्जुनः Kau. A. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतात्मक
भूत + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> consisting or composed of the elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतात्मन्
भूत + -आत्मन्<BR>—1 one whose soul is purified.<BR>—2 composed of the five elements (as the body); cf. Ms. 12. 12. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the individual (as opposed to the Supreme Soul); विद्यातपोभ्यां भूतात्मा<BR> बुद्धिर्ज्ञानेन शुद्ध्यति Ms. 5. 109; विधमिष्यति ते देहे भूतात्मानं<BR> चिरोषितम् Rām. 6. 59. 55.<BR>—2 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—3 of Śiva.<BR>—4 of Viṣṇu; भूतात्मा भूतभावनः V. Sah.<BR>—5 an elementary substance.<BR>—6 the body.<BR>—7 war, conflict.<BR>—8 the elementary or vital principle.<BR>—9 a soul which clings to the elements, a carnal mind; भूतात्मनस्तपोविद्ये<BR> बुद्धेर्ज्ञानं विशोधनम् Y. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतादिः|भूतादि
भूत + -आदिः<BR>—1 the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 an epithet of <i>Ahamkāra</i> (in Sāṅkhya phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतार्त|भूतार्त्त|भूतार्त्तः
भूत + -आर्त <i>a.</i> possessed by a devil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावासः|भूतावास
भूत + -आवासः<BR>—1 the body.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 of Viṣṇu; वसन्ति त्वयि भूतानि भूतावासस्ततो हरिः Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूताविष्ट|भूताविष्टः
भूत + -आविष्ट <i>a.</i> possessed by a devil or evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतावेशः|भूतावेश
भूत + -आवेशः demoniac possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेज्यम्
भूत + -इज्यम्, -इज्या making oblations to the Bhūtas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेज्या
भूत + -इज्यम्, -इज्या making oblations to the Bhūtas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेन्द्रियजयिन्
भूत + -इन्द्रियजयिन् <i>m.</i> a kind of ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेष्टा
भूत + -इष्टा the fourteenth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेशः|भूतेश
भूत + -ईशः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">Page1205-1</a>]<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 of Śiva; भूतेशस्य भुजङ्गवल्लिवलयस्रङ्नद्धजूटा जटाः Māl. 1. 2;<BR> भूतेशप्रीतिहेतोः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1204-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतेश्वरः|भूतेश्वर
भूत + -ईश्वरः an epithet of Śiva; भूयः स भूतेश्वरपार्श्ववर्ती R. 2. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतोन्मादः|भूतोन्माद
भूत + -उन्मादः demoniac possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतोपदेशः|भूतोपदेश
भूत + -उपदेशः a reference to past things or such as already exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतोपसृष्ट
भूत + -उपसृष्ट, -उपहत <i>a.</i> possessed by a devil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतोपहत
भूत + -उपसृष्ट, -उपहत <i>a.</i> possessed by a devil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतौदनः
भूत + -ओदनः a dish of rice (eaten to counteract the influence of demons).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकर्तृ
भूत + -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman; सर्वलोकप्रभुर्ब्रह्मा<BR> भूतकर्तृ तथर्षयः Rām. 2. 25. 25; ततस्तानाह भूतकृत् 7. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकृत्
भूत + -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman; सर्वलोकप्रभुर्ब्रह्मा<BR> भूतकर्तृ तथर्षयः Rām. 2. 25. 25; ततस्तानाह भूतकृत् 7. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकला
भूत + -कला <i>f.</i> a power which produces the five elements; धरादिपञ्चभूतानां<BR> निवृत्त्याद्याः कलाः स्मृताः Śāradātilakam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकालः|भूतकाल
भूत + -कालः<BR>—1 past time.<BR>—2 (in gram.) the past or preterite time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकेशी
भूत + -केशी the holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतकोटिः|भूतकोटि
भूत + -कोटिः absolute non-entity; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतक्रान्तिः|भूतक्रान्ति|भूतक्रांति
भूत + -क्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> possession by a devil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगणः|भूतगण
भूत + -गणः<BR>—1 the collection of created beings.<BR>—2 the whole class of spirits or devils; प्रेतान् भूतागणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते<BR> तामसा जनाः Bg. 17. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगत्या
भूत + -गत्या truthfully; तदखिलमिह भूतं भूतगत्या … … अभिलषति<BR> स्म N. 9. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतगुणः|भूतगुण
भूत + -गुणः a quality of the elements; शब्दस्पर्शरूपरसगन्धा भूतगुणाः<BR> स्मृताः Śāradātilakam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतग्रस्त
भूत + -ग्रस्त possessed by a devil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतग्रामः|भूतग्राम
भूत + -ग्रामः<BR>—1 the whole multitude or aggregate of living beings; U. 7; भूतग्रामः<BR> स एवायं भूत्वा भूत्वा प्रलीयते Bg. 8. 19.<BR>—2 a multitude of spirits.<BR>—3 the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतघ्नः|भूतघ्न
भूत + -घ्नः<BR>—1 a kind of birch tree.<BR>—2 a camel.<BR>—3 garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतघ्नी
भूत + -घ्नः + .({@-घ्नी@}) the holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचतुर्दशी|भूतचतुर्द्दशी
भूत + -चतुर्दशी the fourteenth day of the dark half of Kārtika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचारिन्
भूत + -चारिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचिन्तकः
भूत + -चिन्तकः = स्वभाववादिन् q. v.; दैवमित्यपरे विप्राः स्वभावं<BR> भूतचिन्तकाः Mb. 12. 232. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचिन्तनिकः
भूत + -चिन्तनिकः an adherent to the doctrine that the mind or intellect<BR> is produced from material elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचिन्ता
भूत + -चिन्ता an enquiry into the elements, investigation into their nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतचैतन्यम्
भूत + -चैतन्यम् intellectuality of matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतजननी
भूत + -जननी the mother of all beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतजयः|भूतजय
भूत + -जयः victory over the elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूततन्त्रम्
भूत + -तन्त्रम् the doctrine of spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूततन्मात्रम्
भूत + -तन्मात्रम् a subtle element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतदया
भूत + -दया compassion towards all beings, universal benevolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतद्रुमः|भूतद्रुम
भूत + -द्रुमः Cordia Latifolia (Mar. भोंकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतद्रुह्
भूत + -द्रुह्, -ध्रुक् <i>a.</i> injurious, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतध्रुक्
भूत + -द्रुह्, -ध्रुक् <i>a.</i> injurious, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतधरा
भूत + -धरा, -धात्री, -धारिणी the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतधात्री
भूत + -धरा, -धात्री, -धारिणी the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतधारिणी
भूत + -धरा, -धात्री, -धारिणी the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतधात्री
भूत + -धात्री sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाथः|भूतनाथ
भूत + -नाथः an epithet of Śiva; तद् भूतनाथानुग नार्हसि त्वम् R. 2. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनायिका
भूत + -नायिका an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाशनः|भूतनाशन|भूतनाशनं
भूत + -नाशनः<BR>—1 the marking-nut plant.<BR>—2 mustard.<BR>—3 pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनाशनम्
भूत + -नाशनः + ({@-नम्@})<BR>—1 Asa Foetida.<BR>—2 a bead used for rosaries (रुद्राक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतनिचयः|भूतनिचय
भूत + -निचयः the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपक्षः|भूतपक्ष
भूत + -पक्षः the dark fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपतिः|भूतपति
भूत + -पतिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva; ध्यानास्पदं भूतपतेर्विवेश Ku. 3. 43, 74.<BR>—2 of Agni.<BR>—3 the sacred basil.<BR>—4 the sky; ज्वलसि यन्निशि भूतपतिं श्रितः N. 4. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपत्री
भूत + -पत्री the holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपालः|भूतपाल
भूत + -पालः the guardian of living beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्णिमा
भूत + -पूर्णिमा the day of full-moon in the month of Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतपूर्वम्|भूतपूर्व्वम्
भूत + -पूर्वम् <i>ind.</i> formerly. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 former, ancient, old; पश्यामि च जनस्थानं भूतपूर्वखरालयम् U. 2. 17.<BR>—2 deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतप्रकृतिः|भूतप्रकृति
भूत + -प्रकृतिः <i>f.</i> the origin of all beings; यामाहुः सर्वभूतप्रकृतिरिति<BR> Ś. 1. 1 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतबलिः|भूतबलि
भूत + -बलिः = भूतयज्ञ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतब्रह्मन्
भूत + -ब्रह्मन् <i>m.</i> a low Brāhmaṇa who maintains himself with the<BR> offerings made to an idol; see देवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभर्तृ|भूतभर्त्तृ
भूत + -भर्तृ <i>a.</i> sustaining all beings; भूतभर्तृ च तज्ज्ञेयं<BR> ग्रसिष्णु प्रभविष्णु च Bg. 13. 16. ━<i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभव
भूत + -भव <i>a.</i> existing in all beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभव्यम्
भूत + -भव्यम् past and future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभावनः|भूतभावन
भूत + -भावनः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">Page1205-2</a>]<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभाविन्
भूत + -भाविन् <i>a.</i> creating living beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभाषा
भूत + -भाषा, -भाषितम् the language of devils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभाषितम्
भूत + -भाषा, -भाषितम् the language of devils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभृत्
भूत + -भृत् <i>a.</i> sustaining the elements or creatures; भूतभृन्न<BR> च भूतस्थो ममात्मा भूतभावनः Bg. 9. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतभौतिक
भूत + -भौतिक <i>a.</i> consisting of the elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमहेश्वरः|भूतमहेश्वर
भूत + -महेश्वरः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमातृ
भूत + -मातृ <i>f.</i> an epithet of Gaurī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमातृका
भूत + -मातृका the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमात्रम्
भूत + -मात्रम्, -मात्रा the rudiment of an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमात्रा
भूत + -मात्रम्, -मात्रा the rudiment of an element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमात्रा
भूत + -मात्रा <i>f.</i> pl. the coarse and subtile elements; तास्वेव भूतमात्रासु<BR> प्रलीयन्ते विभागशः Ms. 12. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतयज्ञः|भूतयज्ञ
भूत + -यज्ञः an oblation or offering to all created beings, one of<BR> the five daily Yajñas to be performed by a householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतयोनिः|भूतयोनि
भूत + -योनिः the origin of all created beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतरयाः
भूत + -रयाः a class of gods under the 5th Manu; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतराज्
भूत + -राज् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतलिपिः|भूतलिपि
भूत + -लिपिः a particular magic formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवर्गः|भूतवर्ग
भूत + -वर्गः the whole class of spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवादिन्
भूत + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> telling the real fact or truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवासः|भूतवास
भूत + -वासः the Bibhītaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवाहनः|भूतवाहन
भूत + -वाहनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविक्रिया
भूत + -विक्रिया<BR>—1 epilepsy.<BR>—2 possession by a devil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविज्ञान
भूत + -विज्ञान, -विद्या demonology (भूतविद्या); Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविद्या
भूत + -विज्ञान, -विद्या demonology (भूतविद्या); Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविनायकः|भूतविनायक
भूत + -विनायकः a leader of evil beings; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतविभुः
भूत + -विभुः a king; शाहभूविभुः Śāhendra. 2. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवृक्षः|भूतवृक्ष
भूत + -वृक्षः the Bibhītaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतवेशी
भूत + -वेशी a white flowering Vitex Negundo (Mar. निर्गुडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतशुद्धिः|भूतशुद्धि
भूत + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> purification of the elements (of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंसारः|भूतसंसार
भूत + -संसारः<BR>—1 the world of mortals.<BR>—2 the course of existence; घोरेऽस्मिन् भूतसंसारे नित्यं सततयायिनि Ms. 1. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंघः|भूतसङ्घ
भूत + -संघः the totality of beings or of the elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंचारः|भूतसञ्चार|भूतसंचार|भूतसञ्चारः
भूत + -संचारः demoniac possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंचारिन्
भूत + -संचारिन् <i>m.</i> a forest conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसंप्लवः|भूतसम्प्लव|भूतसंप्लव
भूत + -संप्लवः universal deluge or destruction; आभूतसंप्लवस्थानममृतत्वं हि भाषते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसमागमः|भूतसमागम
भूत + -समागमः the meeting of mortals; यथा काष्ठं च … समेत्य<BR> च व्यपेयातां तद्वद् भूतसमागमः Mb. 12. 28. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसर्गः|भूतसर्ग
भूत + -सर्गः<BR>—1 the creation of the world, the class or order of created beings.<BR>—2 creation of the elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसाक्षिन्
भूत + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i> ‘all-seeing’, an eye-witness of created beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसाधनी
भूत + -साधनी the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसूक्ष्मम्
भूत + -सूक्ष्मम् a subtle element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसृज्
भूत + -सृज् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman; बहुधा गतां जगति भूतसृजा<BR> कमनीयतां समभिहृत्य पुरा Ki. 6. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतसृष्टिः|भूतसृष्टि
भूत + -सृष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the illusion effected by the power of Bhūtas.<BR>—2 the whole class of Bhūtas taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतस्थानम्
भूत + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 the abode of living beings.<BR>—2 the abode of demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतहत्या
भूत + -हत्या destruction of living beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतहन्त्री
भूत + -हन्त्री a species of Dūrvā grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतहरः|भूतहर
भूत + -हरः bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतहासः|भूतहास
भूत + -हासः a kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतमय
भूतमय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Including all beings.<BR>—2 Formed out of the elements or created beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूति|भूतिः
भूति <i>f.</i> [भू-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Being, existence.<BR>—2 Birth, production.<BR>—3 Well-being, welfare, happiness, prosperity; प्रजानामेव भूत्यर्थं<BR> स ताभ्यो बलिमग्रहीत् R. 1. 18; नरपतिकुलभूत्यै 2. 75; स वोऽस्तु<BR> भूत्यै भगवान् मुकुन्दः Vikr. 1. 2.<BR>—4 Success, good fortune.<BR>—5 Wealth, riches, fortune; विपत्प्रतीकारपरेण मङ्गलं निषेव्यते<BR> भूतिसमुत्सुकेन वा Ku. 5. 76.<BR>—6 Grandeur, dignity, majesty.<BR>—7 Ashes; भृतभूतिरहीनभोगभाक् Śi. 16. 71 (where भूति means<BR> ‘riches’ also); स्फुटोपमं भूतिसितेन शंभुना 1. 4.<BR>—8 Decoration of elephants with coloured stripes; भक्तिच्छेदैरिव विरचितां<BR> भूतिमङ्गे गजस्य Me. 19.<BR>—9 The superhuman power attainable by the practice of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">Page1206-1</a>]<BR> penance or magical rites; सूक्ष्मात् सूक्ष्मतमोऽणीयान् शीघ्रत्वं लघिमागुणः ।<BR> महिमाशेषपूज्यत्वात् प्राप्तिर्नाप्राप्यमस्य यत् ॥ प्राकाम्यस्य व्यापित्वादीशित्वं<BR> चेश्वरो यतः । वशित्वाद्वशिमा नाम योगिनः सप्तमो गुणः ॥ यत्रेच्छा<BR> स्थानमप्युक्तं यत्र कामावसायिता ॥ Mārk. P. 40. 31-33.<BR>—10 Fried meat.<BR>—11 The rutting of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिः|भूति
भूति + .{@-तिः@} <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Of a class of Manes.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूत्यर्थम्, भूतिकर्मन्, भूतिकाम, भूतिकालः, भूतिकीलः, भूतिकृत्, भूतिकृत्यम्, भूतिगर्भः, भूतिदः, भूतिविधानम्, भूतिभूषणः, भूतिवाहनः, भूतिसृज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1205-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूत्यर्थम्
भूति + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i> for the sake of prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकर्मन्
भूति + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> any auspicious or festive rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकाम|भूतिकामः
भूति + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकामः|भूतिकाम
भूति + -काम + .({@-मः@})<BR>—1 a minister of state.<BR>—2 an epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकालः|भूतिकाल
भूति + -कालः a happy or auspicious hour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकीलः|भूतिकील
भूति + -कीलः<BR>—1 a hole, pit.<BR>—2 a meat.<BR>—3 a cellar, an underground room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकृत्
भूति + -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 a class of Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकृत्यम्
भूति + -कृत्यम् see भूतिकर्मन्; श्रोत्रियः श्रोत्रियं साधुं भूतिकृत्येष्वभोजयन् Ms. 8. 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिगर्भः|भूतिगर्भ
भूति + -गर्भः an epithet of Bhavabhūti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिदः|भूतिद
भूति + -दः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिविधानम्
भूति + -विधानम् the lunar mansion called धनिष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिभूषणः|भूतिभूषण
भूति + -भूषणः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिवाहनः|भूतिवाहन
भूति + -वाहनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिसृज्
भूति + -सृज् <i>a.</i> creating welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूतिकम्
भूतिकम्<BR>—1 Camphor.<BR>—2 Sandal-wood. —3 N. of a medicinal plant (Mar. कायफळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमत्|भूमन्त्
भूमत् <i>a.</i> Possessed of land or earth. ━<i>m.</i> A king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमन्
भूमन् <i>m.</i> [बहोर्भावः बहु इमनिच् इलोपे भ्वादेशः Tv.]<BR>—1 A great quantity, abundance, plenty, large number; भूम्ना रसानां<BR> गहनाः प्रयोगाः Māl. 1. 4; संभूयेव सुखानि चेतसि परं भूमानमातन्वते 5. 9;<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 5. 4.<BR>—2 Wealth.<BR>—3 Virāṭ Puruṣa, the Supreme Being (ब्रह्मन्); यो वै भूमा तत्<BR> सुखम् Ch. Up. 7. 23. 1; Bhāg. 5. 18. 30. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 A territory, district, piece of ground.<BR>—3 A being, creature.<BR>—4 Plurality (of number); आपः स्त्रीभूम्नि Ak.; cf. पुंभूमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमय
भूमय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>) Earthen, earthly, made of or produced from earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमयति
भूमयति Den. P. To augment, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिः|भूमि
भूमिः <i>f.</i> [भवन्त्यस्मिन् भूतानि, भू-मि किच्च वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 The earth (opp. स्वर्ग, गगन or पाताल); द्यौर्भूमिरापो हृदयं<BR> यमश्च Pt. 1. 182; R. 2. 74.<BR>—2 Soil, ground; उत्खातिनी भूमिः Ś. 1; विदूरभूमिः Ku. 1. 24.<BR>—3 A territory, district, country, land; विदर्भभूमिः.<BR>—4 A place, spot, ground, plot of ground; प्रमदवनभूमयः Ś. 6;<BR> अधित्यकाभूमिः N. 22. 41; R. 1. 52, 3. 61; Ku. 3. 58.<BR>—5 A site, situation.<BR>—6 Land, landed property.<BR>—7 A story, the floor of a house; as in सप्तभूमिकः प्रासादः; प्रासादैर्नैकभूमिभिः<BR> Rām. 4. 33. 8.<BR>—8 Attitude, posture.<BR>—9 A character or part (in a play); cf. भूमिका.<BR>—10 Subject, object, receptacle; विश्वासभूमि, स्नेहभूमि &c.; मात्राणि<BR> कर्मणि पुरं च तासां वदन्ति हैकादशवीर भूमीः Bhāg. 5. 11. 9.<BR>—11 Degree, extent, limit; प्रकुपितमभिसारणेऽनुनेतुं प्रियमियती<BR> ह्यबलाजनस्य भूमिः Ki. 10. 58.<BR>—12 The tongue.<BR>—13 The number ‘one’.<BR>—14 The area.<BR>—15 The base of any geometrical figure.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूम्यनन्तरः, भूम्यनृतम्, भूम्यामलकी, भूम्याली, भूमीच्छा, भूमीन्द्रः, भूमीश्वरः, भूमिकदम्बः, भूमिकम्पः, भूमिकूश्मण्डः, भूमिखर्जूरिका, भूमिखर्जूरी, भूमिगत, भूमिगर्तः, भूमिगुहा, भूमिगृहम्, भूमिगोचरः, भूमिचलः, भूमिचलनम्, भूमिच्छत्रम्, भूमिज, भूमिजीविन्, भूमितनयः, भूमितलम्, भूमिदानम्, भूमिदुन्दुभिः, भूमिदेवः, भूमिधरः, भूमिनाथः, भूमिपः, भूमिपतिः, भूमिपालः, भूमिभुज्, भूमिपक्षः, भूमिपरिमाणम्, भूमिपिशाचम्, भूमिपुत्रः, भूमिपुरंदरः, भूमिप्र, भूमिबुध्न, भूमिभागः, भूमिभृत्, भूमिमण्डा, भूमिरक्षकः, भूमिरथिकः, भूमिरुहः, भूमिलाभः, भूमिलेपनम्, भूमिवर्धनः, भूमिवर्धनम्, भूमिशय, भूमिशयनम्, भूमिशय्या, भूमिसत्रम्, भूमिसमीकृत, भूमिसंनिवेशः, भूमिसंभवः, भूमिसुतः, भूमिस्थ, भूमिस्नुः, भूमिस्पृश्, भूमिस्फोटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम्यनन्तरः|भूम्यनन्तर
भूमिः + -अनन्तरः a king of an adjacent district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम्यनृतम्
भूमिः + -अनृतम् false evidence concerning land; सर्वं भूम्यनृते हन्ति<BR> मा स्म भूम्यनृतं वदीः Ms. 8. 99.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">Page1206-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूम्यामलकी
