भूमिः + -सत्रम् an offering of land; अक्षयान् लभते लोकान् भूमिसत्रं<BR> हि तस्य तत् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसमीकृत
भूमिः + -समीकृत <i>a.</i> thrown to the ground, floored (Mar. जमीनदोस्त);<BR> वानरै राक्षसाश्चापि द्रुमैर्भूमिसमीकृताः Rām. 6. 52. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसंनिवेशः|भूमिसन्निवेश
भूमिः + -संनिवेशः the general appearance of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसंभवः|भूमिसम्भव|भूमिसंभव
भूमिः + -संभवः, -सुतः<BR>—1 the planet Mars.<BR>—2 an epithet of the demon Naraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसुतः|भूमिसुत
भूमिः + -संभवः, -सुतः<BR>—1 the planet Mars.<BR>—2 an epithet of the demon Naraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसंभवा|भूमिसम्भवा
भूमिः + -संभवः, -सुतः + ({@-वा, -ता@}) an epithet of Sītā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिसंभवता
भूमिः + -संभवः, -सुतः + ({@-वा, -ता@}) an epithet of Sītā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्थ
भूमिः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> being, standing on the ground; भूमिष्ठं नोत्सहे<BR> योद्धुं भवन्तं रथमास्थितः Mb. 5. 179. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्नुः|भूमिस्नु
भूमिः + -स्नुः an earth-worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्पृश्
भूमिः + -स्पृश् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 blind.<BR>—2 lame, cripple. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a man.<BR>—2 mankind.<BR>—3 a Vaiśya,<BR>—4 a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिस्फोटः
भूमिः + -स्फोटः a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1206-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिका
भूमिका<BR>—1 Earth, ground, soil.<BR>—2 A place, region, spot (of ground).<BR>—3 A story, floor (of a house); गृहोपरि˚ the flat roof of a house.<BR>—4 Step, degree; मधुमतीसंज्ञां भूमिकां साक्षात्कुर्वतः Yoga S.;<BR> or नैयायिकादिभिरात्मा प्रथमभूमिकायामवतारितः Sāṅkhyapravachanabhāṣya.<BR>—5 A tablet or board, as for writing; see अक्षरभूमिका.<BR>—6 A part or character in a play; या यस्य युज्यते भूमिका तां खलु तथैव<BR> भावेन सर्वे वर्ग्या पाठिताः; कामन्दक्याः प्रथमां भूमिकां भाव एवाधीते<BR> Māl. 1; or लक्ष्मीभूमिकायां वर्तमानोर्वशी वारुणीभूमिकायां वर्तमानया<BR> मेनकया पृष्टा V. 3; Śi. 1. 69; (अन्यरूपैर्यदन्यस्य प्रवेशः स<BR> तु भूमिका Bharata).<BR>—7 Theatrical dress, an actorʼs costume.<BR>—8 Decoration (as of an image).<BR>—9 A preface or introduction to a book.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूमिकाभागः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमिकाभागः|भूमिकाभाग
भूमिका + -भागः a floor, threshold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमी
भूमी The earth; see भूमि.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूमीकदम्बः, भूमीध्रः, भूमीपतिः, भूमीभुज्, भूमीरुह्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीकदम्बः|भूमीकदम्ब
भूमी + -कदम्बः = भूमिकदम्बः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीध्रः
भूमी + -ध्रः A mountain; आरामप्रायभूमीध्रं तीर्थप्रायनदीनदं (देशं)<BR> Śiva B. 29. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीपतिः|भूमीपति
भूमी + -पतिः, -भुज् <i>m.</i> a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीभुज्
भूमी + -पतिः, -भुज् <i>m.</i> a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूमीरुह्
भूमी + -रुह् <i>m.</i>, {@-रुहः@}<BR> a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयम्
भूयम् The state of being or becoming; as in ब्रह्मभूयम्; दाशरथिभूयम् Śi. 14. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयशस्
भूयशस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Mostly, generally, commonly, as a general rule; द्वेष्यो भवति भूयशः Mb. 10. 2. 17.<BR>—2 Exceedingly, in a high degree.<BR>—3 Again, more further.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्
भूयस् <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>) [अतिशयेन बहु ईयसुन्]<BR>—1 More, more numerous or abundant.<BR>—2 Greater, larger; तद्दर्शनादभूच्छंभोर्भूयान् दारार्थमादरः Ku. 6. 13.<BR>—3 More important.<BR>—4 Very great or large, much, many, numerous; भवति च पुनर्भूयान् भेदः<BR> फलं प्रति तद्यथा U. 2. 4; भद्रं भद्रं वितर भगवन् भूयसे मङ्गलाय<BR> Māl. 1. 3; U. 3. 48; R. 17. 41; U. 2. 3.<BR>—5 Rich or abounding in; एवंप्रायगुणभूयसीं स्वकृतिम् Māl. 1.<BR>—6 Vehement, severe. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Much, very much, exceedingly, largely, greatly.<BR>—2 More, again, further more, moreover; पाथेयमुत्सृज बिसं ग्रहणाय<BR> भूयः V. 4. 15; R. 2. 46; भूयश्चाह त्वमसि शयने कण्ठलग्ना पुरा<BR> मे Me. 113. 3 Repeatedly, frequently; पूर्वं भूयः first, in the<BR> first place -next, in the next place. (The form भूयसा is often used<BR> adverbially in the sense of<BR>—1 very much, in a high degree, exceedingly, beyond measure, for the greater<BR> part; न खरो न च भूयसा मृदुः R. 8. 9; कुसुमपुरभुवो भूयसा<BR> दुःखयन्ति Mu. 6. 9; पश्चार्धेन प्रविष्टः शरपतनभयाद् भूयसा पूर्वकायम् Ś. 1. 7.<BR>—2 generally, as a general rule; भूयसा जीविधर्म एषः U. 5).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूयःकर, भूयस्काम, भूयोदर्शनम्, भूयोभावः, भूयोभूयस्, भूयोमात्रम्, भूयोविद्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयःकर
भूयस् + -कर <i>a.</i> augmenting, increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्काम
भूयस् + -काम <i>a.</i> very desirous of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयोदर्शनम्
भूयस् + -दर्शनम्<BR>—1 frequent observation; भूयोभूयोदर्शनेन यत्र यत्र धूमस्तत्र तत्राग्निरिति<BR> व्याप्तिं गृहीत्वा T. S.<BR>—2 an inference based on frequent and wide observation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयोभावः|भूयोभाव
भूयस् + -भावः increase, growth, progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयोभूयस्
भूयस् + -भूयस् <i>ind.</i> again and again, repeatedly; भूयोभूयः सविधनगरीरथ्यया<BR> पर्यटन्तम् Māl. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयोमात्रम्
भूयस् + -मात्रम् the greatest part, most of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयोविद्य
भूयस् + -विद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 more learned.<BR>—2 very learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयस्त्वम्
भूयस्त्वम्<BR>—1 Abundance, plentifulness; क्लेदनं पिण्डनं तृप्तिः प्राणनाप्यायनोन्दनम् ।<BR> तापापनोदो भूयस्त्वमम्भसो वृत्तयस्त्विमाः ॥ Bhāg. 3. 26. 43.<BR>—2 Majority, preponderance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठ|भूयिष्ठं
भूयिष्ठ <i>a.</i> [अतिशयेन बहु इष्ठन् भ्वादेशे युक् च]<BR>—1 Most, most numerous or abundant.<BR>—2 Most important, principal, chief.<BR>—3 Very great or large, very much, much, many, numerous.<BR>—4 Chiefly or for the most part composed of, mostly composed or consisting<BR> of, chiefly filled with or characterized by (at the end of com.); अभिरूपभूयिष्ठा<BR> परिषद् Ś. 1; शूल्यमांसभूयिष्ठ आहारोऽश्यते Ś. 2; राष्ट्रेषु कतमत्सुपुरुषभूयिष्ठम्<BR> Dk.; शिल्पदारिकाभूयिष्ठं परिजनम् M. 5; R. 4. 70.<BR>—5 Almost, mostly, nearly all (usually after a past passive participle); अये अदितभूयिष्ठ<BR> एष तपनः Māl. 1; निर्वाणभूयिष्ठमथास्य वीर्यम् Ku. 3. 52; V. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूयिष्ठम्
भूयिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 For the most part, mostly; भूयिष्ठमन्यविषया न तु दृष्टिरस्याः Ś. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Exceedingly, very much, in the highest degree; भूयिष्ठं भव दक्षिणा<BR> परिजने Ś. 4. 18; R. 6. 4, 13. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्
भूर् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 One of the three Vyāhṛtis.<BR>—2 The lowest of the seven lower worlds.<BR>—3 A spiritual son of Brahman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूर्भुवः, भूर्लोकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्भुवः|भूर्भुव
भूर् + -भुवः N. of one of the mind-born sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्लोकः|भूर्लोक
भूर् + -लोकः<BR>—1 the terrestrial world, earth. —2 the country south of the equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरि|भूरिः
भूरि <i>a.</i> [भू-क्रिन् Uṇ. 4. 65] Much, abundant, numerous, copious;<BR> प्रेङ्खद्भूरिमयूख … Māl. 6. 5. भूरिभारभराक्रान्तो बाधति स्कन्ध<BR> एष ते । न तथा बाधते स्कन्धो यथा बाधति बाधते ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Great, large. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Of Brahman.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR>—4 Of Indra. ━<i>f.</i> Reason, intellect. ━<i>n.</i> Gold. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Very much, exceedingly; नवाम्बुभिर्भूरि विलम्बिनो घनाः Ś. 5. 12.<BR>—2 Frequently, often, repeatedly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूरिकालम्, भूरिकृत्वस्, भूरिगन्धा, भूरिगमः, भूरिगुण, भूरितेजस, भूरिद, भूरिदक्षिण, भूरिदक्षिणः, भूरिदानम्, भूरिधन, भूरिधामन्, भूरिप्रयोग, भूरिप्रेमन्, भूरिफेना, भूरिभाग, भूरिभोज, भूरिमायः, भूरिरसः, भूरिरामः, भूरिलाभः, भूरिविक्रम, भूरिदृष्टिः, भूरिव्यय, भूरिश्रवस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिकालम्
भूरि + -कालम् <i>ind.</i> for a long time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिकृत्वस्
भूरि + -कृत्वस् <i>ind.</i> many times, repeatedly; मर्मृज्मा ते तन्वं<BR> भूरि कृत्वः Rv. 3. 18. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिगन्धा
भूरि + -गन्धा a particular perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिगमः|भूरिगम
भूरि + -गमः an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिगुण
भूरि + -गुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 multiplying greatly.<BR>—2 bearing manifold fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरितेजस
भूरि + -तेजस + ({@-स्@})<BR> <i>a.</i> possessed of great lustre. ━(<i>m.</i>) fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरितेजस्
भूरि + -तेजस + ({@-स्@})<BR> <i>a.</i> possessed of great lustre. ━(<i>m.</i>) fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिद
भूरि + -द <i>a.</i> liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिदक्षिण|भूरिदक्षिणः
भूरि + -दक्षिण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 attended with rich presents or rewards.<BR>—2 giving liberal rewards, munificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिदक्षिणः|भूरिदक्षिण
भूरि + -दक्षिणः N. of Viṣṇu; कपीन्द्रो भूरिदक्षिणः V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिदानम्
भूरि + -दानम् liberality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिधन
भूरि + -धन <i>a.</i> wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिधामन्
भूरि + -धामन् <i>a.</i> possessed of great lustre or energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिप्रयोग
भूरि + -प्रयोग <i>a.</i> frequently used, in common use (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिप्रेमन्
भूरि + -प्रेमन् <i>m.</i> the ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिफेना
भूरि + -फेना a species of plant, सप्तला (Mar. शिकेकाई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिभाग
भूरि + -भाग <i>a.</i> wealthy, prosperous; अद्येश नो वसतयः खलु भूरिभाग ।<BR> यः सर्वदेवपितृभूतनृदेवमूर्तिः Bhāg. 10. 48. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिभोज
भूरि + -भोज <i>a.</i> having many enjoyments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिमायः|भूरिमाय
भूरि + -मायः a jackal or fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिरसः|भूरिरस
भूरि + -रसः the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिरामः|भूरिराम
भूरि + -रामः a donkey, ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिलाभः|भूरिलाभ
भूरि + -लाभः a great gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिविक्रम
भूरि + -विक्रम <i>a.</i> very brave, a great warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिदृष्टिः
भूरि + -दृष्टिः <i>f.</i> a heavy rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिव्यय
भूरि + -व्यय <i>a.</i> spending much; lavish in expenditure; भूरिव्यया<BR> प्रचुरवित्तसमागमा च वेश्याङ्गनेव नृपनीतिरनेकरूपा Pt. 1. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिश्रवस्
भूरि + -श्रवस् <i>m.</i> N. of a warrior on the Kaurava side slain by Sātyaki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिज्
भूरिज् <i>f.</i> The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूरिशस्
भूरिशस् <i>ind.</i> manifoldly, variously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1207-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्जः|भूर्ज|भूर्ज्ज
भूर्जः The birch-tree; भूर्जगतोऽक्षरविन्यासः V. 2; Ku. 1. 7;<BR> ‘भूर्जः कटुः कषायोष्णो भूतरक्षाकरः परः’ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्जम्
भूर्जः + .{@-र्जम्@}<BR>—1 A leaf made of birch-bark for writing on.<BR>—2 A written deed, document.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूर्जकण्टकः, भूर्जपत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्जकण्टकः|भूर्जकण्टक|भूर्जकंटक
भूर्जः + -कण्टकः a man of one of the mixed tribes, the offspring of an<BR> outcast Brāhmaṇa by a woman of the same class; व्रात्यात्तु जायते विप्रात्<BR> पापात्मा भूर्जकण्टकः Ms. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्जपत्रः|भूर्जपत्र|भूर्ज्जपत्र|भूर्ज्जपत्रः
भूर्जः + -पत्रः the birch-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूर्णिः|भूर्णि
भूर्णिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 A desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्
भूष् €1 P., €10 U. (भूषति, भूषयति-ते, भूषित)<BR>—1 To adorn, deck, decorate; शुचि भूषयति श्रुतं वपुः Bk. 20. 15.<BR>—2 To decorate oneself (Ātm.); भूषयते कन्या स्वयमेव<BR>—3 To spread or strew with, overspread; नखप्रभाभूषितकङ्कपत्रे<BR> R. 2. 31. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि@} to adorn, grace, give beauty to; अहरत<BR> सुतरामतोऽस्य चेतः स्फुटमभिभूषयति स्त्रियस्त्रपैव Śi. 7. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषणम्
भूषणम् [भूष्यतेऽनेन भूष्-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Ornamenting, decoration.<BR>—2 An ornament, decoration, an article of decoration; क्षीयन्ते खलु<BR> भूषणानि सततं वाग्भूषणं भूषणम् Bh. 2. 19; R. 3. 2, 13. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषणः|भूषण|भूषणं
भूषणम् + .{@-णः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भूषणवासस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषणवासस्
भूषणम् + -वासस् <i>n.</i> pl. clothes and ornaments; Ms. 8. 357.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषा
भूषा [भूष्-भावे अ]<BR>—1 Decorating, adorning.<BR>—2 An ornament, decoration; as in कर्णभूषा q. v.; दम्पत्योः पर्यदात्<BR> प्रीत्या भूषावासः परिच्छदान् Bhāg. 3. 22. 23.<BR>—3 A jewel; नभोभूषा पूषा कमलवनभूषा मधुकरः … … सकलगुणभूषा<BR> च विनयः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषाय
भूषाय Den. Ā. To serve as an ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूषित|भूषितः
भूषित <i>p. p.</i> [भूष्-क्त] Decorated, ornamented; मणिना भूषितः<BR> सर्पः किमसौ न भयंकरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भूष्णु|भूष्णुः
भूष्णु <i>a.</i> [भू-ग्ष्णु]<BR>—1 Being, becoming; as in अलंभूष्णु q. v.<BR>—2 Wishing for wealth or prosperity; क्षत्रियं चैव सर्पं च ब्राह्मणं<BR> च बहुश्रुतम् । नावमन्येत वै भूष्णुः कृशानपि कदाचन ॥ Ms. 4. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृ
भृ €1. €3 U. (भरति-ते; बिभर्ति-बिभृते, बभार-बभ्रे, बिभरांचकार-चक्रे,<BR> अभार्षित्-अभृत, भरिष्यति-ते, भर्तुम्, भृत; <i>pass.</i> भ्रियते,<BR> <i>desid.</i> बिभरिषति-ते or बुभूर्षति-ते)<BR>—1 To fill; जठरं को न बिभर्ति केवलम् Pt. 1. 22.<BR>—2 To fill, pervade, fill with; अभार्षीद् ध्वनिना लोकान् Bk. 15. 24.<BR>—3 To bear, support, uphold, bear up; धुरं धरित्र्या बिभरांबभूव<BR> R. 18. 45; कूर्मो बिभर्ति धरणीं खलु पृष्ठकेन C. P. 50; Bk. 17. 16.<BR>—4 To maintain, foster, cherish, protect, take care of, nourish; भरस्व<BR> पुत्रं दुष्यन्त Bhāg. 9. 20. 21; दरिद्रान् भर कौन्तेय मा प्रयच्छेश्वरे<BR> धनम् H. 1. 14.<BR>—5 To bear, have, possess; सिन्धोर्बभार सलिलं शयनीयलक्ष्मीम् Ki. 8. 57;<BR> पिशुनजनं खलु बिभ्रति क्षितीन्द्राः Bv. 1. 74; वलित्रयं<BR> चारु बभार बाला Ku. 1. 39; इन्दोर्दैन्यं त्वदनुसरणक्लिष्टकान्तेर्बिभर्ति<BR> Me. 86; Ś. 2. 4.<BR>—6 To wear; बिभ्रज्जटामण्डलम् Ś. 7. 11, 6. 5; विवाहकौतुकं ललितं<BR> बिभ्रत एव (तस्य) R. 8. 1, 10. 10; जटाश्च बिभृयान्नित्यम् Ms. 6. 6.<BR>—7 To feel, experience, suffer, endure (joy, sorrow &c.); भावशुद्धिसहितैर्मुदं<BR> जनो नाटकैरिव बभार भोजनैः Śi. 14. 50; संत्रासमविभः शक्रः<BR> Bk. 17. 108; Ś. 7. 21.<BR>—8 To confer, bestow, give, produce; यौवने सदलंकाराः शोभां बिभ्रति<BR> सुभ्रवः Subhāṣ.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">Page1208-2</a>]<BR>—9 To keep, hold, retain (as in memory).<BR>—10 To hire; Ms. 11. 62; Y. 3. 235.<BR>—11 To bring or carry.<BR>—12 To take away, transport.<BR>—13 Ved. To acquire, gain.<BR>—14 To balance, hold in equipoise (as a pair of scales). (गर्भं भृ<BR> to become pregnant, conceive; क्षितिं भृ to rule the earth; जटां<BR> भृ to wear matted hair &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्
भृत् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Bearing, carrying.<BR>—2 Supporting, nourishing.<BR>—3 Possessing, having; प्रथमे मानभृतां न वृष्णयः Ki. 2. 44.<BR>—4 Bringing, procuring, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत|भृतः
भृत <i>p. p.</i> [भृ-क्त]<BR>—1 Borne.<BR>—2 Supported, maintained, cherished, fostered.<BR>—3 Possessed, endowed or furnished with.<BR>—4 Full of, filled with.<BR>—5 Hired; नानुग्रहभृतः कश्चित् Mb. 3. 15. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतः|भृत
भृत + .{@-तः@} A hired servant; hireling, mercenary; कालातिक्रमणे ह्येव<BR> भक्तवेतनयोर्भृताः Rām. 2. 100. 33; उत्तमस्त्वायुधीयो यो मध्यमस्तु<BR> कृषीवलः । अधमो भारवाही स्यादित्येवं त्रिविधो भृतः Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतक|भृतकः
भृतक <i>a.</i> [भृतं भरणं वेतनमुपजीवति कन्]<BR>—1 Nourished; कैकेय्या न वयं राज्ये भृतका हि वसेमहि Rām. 2. 48. 23.<BR>—2 Hired, paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकः|भृतक
भृतक + .{@-कः@} A hired servant; … … द्वादशमंशं भृतकः Kau. A. 2. 8. 26;<BR> रक्षेत भृतकोऽरण्ये यथा गास्तादृगेव सः Mb. 3. 33. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भृतकाध्यापकः, भृतकाध्यापनम्, भृतकाध्यापित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापकः|भृतकाध्यापक
भृतक + -अध्यापकः a hired teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापनम्
भृतक + -अध्यापनम् instruction given by a hired teacher; भृतादध्ययनादानं<BR> भृतकाध्यापनं तथा Y. 3. 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापित|भृतकाध्यापितः
भृतक + -अध्यापित <i>a.</i> taught by a paid teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतकाध्यापितः|भृतकाध्यापित
भृतक + -अध्यापित + ({@-तः@}) a student<BR> who pays his teacher for his labour (= ‘a paying student’ of the modern<BR> days); मृतकाध्यापको यश्च भृतकाध्यापितस्तथा Ms. 3. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतिः|भृति
भृतिः <i>f.</i> [भृ-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Bearing, upholding, supporting.<BR>—2 Cherishing, maintaining.<BR>—3 Bringing, leading to.<BR>—4 Nourishment, support, maintenance.<BR>—5 Food.<BR>—6 Wages, hire; त्रिभिः प्रकारैर्भृतिर्भवति व्यापारतः फलतो वचनत<BR> इति ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 45; भृतिश्च कर्मकरेभ्य आनत्यर्थं यद्दीयते<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 27; cf. also कालमानं त्रिधा ज्ञेयं चान्द्रं सौरं<BR> च सावनम् । भृतिदाने सदा सौरं चान्द्रं कौसीदबुद्धिषु ॥ Śukra. See<BR> also Śukra. 3. 266.<BR>—7 Service for hire.<BR>—8 Capital, principal.<BR>—9 Wages, hire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भृत्यध्यापनम्, भृत्यर्थम्, भृतिभुज्, भृतिरूपम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यध्यापनम्
भृतिः + -अध्यापनम् teaching (especially the Vedas) for hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यर्थम्
भृतिः + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i> on account of the maintenance; प्रजानामेव भृत्यर्थं<BR> (v. l. for भूत्यर्थं) स ताभ्यो बलिमग्रहीत् R. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतिभुज्
भृतिः + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a hired servant, a hireling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृतिरूपम्
भृतिः + -रूपम् a reward in place of the wages due, but not to be paid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्य|भृत्यः
भृत्य <i>a.</i> [भृ क्यप् तक् च] To be nourished or maintained &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यः|भृत्य
भृत्य + .{@-त्यः@}<BR>—1 Any one requiring to be supported.<BR>—2 A servant, dependant, slave.<BR>—3 A kingʼs servant, minister of state; भृत्यप्रणाशो मरणं नृपाणाम् H. 2. 136.<BR>—4 A subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्या
भृत्य + .{@-त्या@}<BR>—1 Rearing, fostering, nourishing, taking care of; as in कुमारभृत्या q. v.<BR>—2 Maintenance, support.<BR>—3 A means of sustenance, food.<BR>—4 Wages.<BR>—5 Service.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भृत्याध्यापनम्, भृत्यजनः, भृत्यभर्तृ, भृत्यवर्गः, भृत्यवात्सल्यम्, भृत्यवृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्याध्यापनम्
भृत्य + -अध्यापनम् teaching the Veda for hire; Ms. 11. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यजनः|भृत्यजन
भृत्य + -जनः<BR>—1 a servant, dependant. —2 servants taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यभर्तृ|भृत्यभर्त्तृ
भृत्य + -भर्तृ <i>m.</i> the master of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">Page1209-1</a>]<BR> a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1208-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवर्गः|भृत्यवर्ग
भृत्य + -वर्गः the body of servants, household; यथावद् भृत्यवर्गस्य<BR> चिकीर्षेत् कर्म आदितः Mb. 12. 292. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवात्सल्यम्
भृत्य + -वात्सल्यम् kindness to servants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यवृत्तिः|भृत्यवृत्ति
भृत्य + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> maintenance of servants; यस्य त्रैवार्षिकं भक्तं<BR> पर्याप्तं भृत्यवृत्तये Ms. 11. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यता
भृत्यता, -त्वम्, भृत्यभावः<BR> Service, dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यत्वम्
भृत्यता, -त्वम्, भृत्यभावः<BR> Service, dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यभावः|भृत्यभाव
भृत्यता, -त्वम्, भृत्यभावः<BR> Service, dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यायते
भृत्यायते Den. Ā. To behave like a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्यीभू
भृत्यीभू €1 P. To become a servant, accept service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृत्रिम
भृत्रिम <i>a.</i> Supported, nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुंशः|भृकुंश
भृकुंशः(सः) A male actor in female attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुंसः|भृकुंस
भृकुंशः(सः) A male actor in female attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुटिः|भृकुटि
भृकुटिः, -टी<BR> See भ्रु(भ्रू)कुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृकुटी
भृकुटिः, -टी<BR> See भ्रु(भ्रू)कुटि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृग्
भृग् <i>ind.</i> An onomatopoetic word expressive of the crackling sound<BR> of fire. ━<i>f.</i> A flame; मृगित्येव भृगुः पूर्वमङ्गारेभ्योऽङ्गिराऽभवत् Mb. 13. 85. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुः|भृगु
भृगुः —1 N. of a sage, regarded as the ancestor of the family of<BR> the Bhṛgus, and described in Ms. 1. 35 as one of the ten patriarchs<BR> created by the first Manu; (said to be so called because he was produced<BR> along with flames; सह ज्वालाभिरुत्पन्नो भृगुस्तस्माद् मृगुः स्मृतः ।).<BR> [On one occasion when the sages could not agree as to which of the three<BR> gods, Brahman, Viṣṇu and Śiva, was best entitled to the worship of<BR> Brāhmaṇas, the sage Bhṛgu was sent to test the character of the three<BR> gods. He first went to the abode of Brahman, and, on approaching him,<BR> purposely omitted an obeisance. Upon this the god reprehended him severely,<BR> but was pacified by apologies. Next he entered the abode of Śiva in Kailāsa,<BR> and omitted, as before, all tokens of adoration. The vindictive deity<BR> was enraged and would have destroyed him, had he not conciliated him by<BR> mild words. (According to another account, Bhṛgu was coldly received<BR> by Brahman, and he, therefore, cursed him that he would receive no worship<BR> or adoration; and condemned Śiva to take the form of a <i>Liṅga</i>,<BR> as he got no access to the deity who was engaged in private with his wife).<BR> Lastly he went to Viṣṇu, and finding him asleep, he boldly gave the<BR> god a kick on his breast which at once awoke him. Instead of showing anger,<BR> however, the God arose, and on seeing Bhṛgu, inquired tenderly whether<BR> his foot was hurt, and then began to rub it gently. ‘This’, said Bhṛgu,<BR> ‘is the mightiest god. He overtops all by the most potent of all weapons −kindness and generosity’<BR>. Viṣṇu was therefore, declared to be the<BR> god who was best entitled to the worship of all.]<BR>—2 N. of the sage Jamadagni.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śukra.<BR>—4 The planet Venus.<BR>—5 A cliff, precipice; कृत्वा पुंवत्पातमुच्चैर्भृगुभ्यः Śi. 4. 23;<BR> भृगुपतनकारणमपृच्छम् Dk.<BR>—6 Table-land, the level summit of a mountain.<BR>—7 N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—8 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—9 Friday.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भृगूद्वहः, भृगुकच्छः, भृगुकच्छम्, भृगुजः, भृगुतनयः, भृगुनन्दनः, भृगुपतनम्, भृगुपतिः, भृगुपातः, भृगुवंशः, भृगुवारः, भृगुवासरः, भृगुशार्दूलः, भृगुश्रेष्ठः, भृगुसत्तमः, भृगुसुतः, भृगुसूनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगूद्वहः|भृगूद्वह
भृगुः + -उद्वहः an epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुकच्छः|भृगुकच्छ
भृगुः + -कच्छः, -कच्छम् N. of a place on the north bank of the Narmadā<BR> (modern Broach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुकच्छम्
भृगुः + -कच्छः, -कच्छम् N. of a place on the north bank of the Narmadā<BR> (modern Broach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुजः|भृगुज
भृगुः + -जः, -तनयः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śukra.<BR>—2 the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुतनयः|भृगुतनय
भृगुः + -जः, -तनयः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śukra.<BR>—2 the planet Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुनन्दनः|भृगुनन्दन|भृगुनंदन
भृगुः + -नन्दनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Paraśurāma; वीरो न यस्य भगवान् भृगुनन्दनोऽपि U. 5. 34.<BR>—2 of Śukra.<BR>—3 of Śaunaka; एवं निशम्य भृगुनन्दनसाधुवादम् Bhāg. 10. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुपतनम्
भृगुः + -पतनम् a fall from a precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भृगुपतिः|भृगुपति
भृगुः + -पतिः an epithet of Paraśurāma; भृगुपतियशोवर्त्म यत् क्रौञ्चरन्ध्रम्<BR> Me. 59; so भृगूणांपतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1209-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

