भेषज <i>a.</i> [भेषं रोगमयं जयति जि-ड Tv.] Making well<BR> or healthy, curative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजम्
भेषज + .{@-जम्@}<BR>—1 A medicine, medicament, or drug; नरानम्ब त्रातुं त्वमिह परमं<BR> भेषजमसि G. L. 15; अतिवीर्यवतीव भेषजे बहुरल्पीयसि दृश्यते<BR> गुणः Ki. 2. 4; व्याधिर्मेषजसंग्रहैश्च Bh. 1. 11.<BR>—2 A remedy or cure in general.<BR>—3 A kind of fennel.<BR>—4 Any spell against diseases.<BR>—5 Water (Ved.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भेषजागारः, भेषजागारः, भेषजागारम्, भेषजाङ्गम्, भेषजकरणम्, भेषजकृत, भेषजवीर्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजागारः|भेषजागार
भेषज + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् an apothecaryʼs shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजागारः|भेषजागार
भेषज + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् an apothecaryʼs shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजागारम्
भेषज + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् an apothecaryʼs shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजाङ्गम्
भेषज + -अङ्गम् anything taken after medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजकरणम्
भेषज + -करणम् preparation of drugs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजकृत
भेषज + -कृत <i>a.</i> healed, cured; भेषजकृतो ह वा एष यज्ञः Ch. Up. 4. 17. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषजवीर्यम्
भेषज + -वीर्यम् the healing power of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भेषज्य
भेषज्य <i>a.</i> Curative, having healing properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष|भैक्षं
भैक्ष <i>a.</i> (-क्षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भिक्षैव तत्समूहो वा अण्] Living on alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षम्
भैक्ष + .{@-क्षम्@}<BR>—1 Begging, mendicancy; भवत्पूर्वं चरेद् भैक्षमुपनीतो द्विजोत्तमः<BR> Ms. 2. 49; एककालं चरेद् भैक्षं न प्रसज्जेत विस्तरे Ms. 6. 55; Y. 3. 42.<BR>—2 Anything got by begging, alms, charity; भैक्षेण वर्तयेन्नित्यम्<BR> Ms. 2. 188, 4. 5; गोरक्षणे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">Page1211-2</a>]<BR> संनियुक्तो गुरुणा भैक्षभोजनः Bm. 1. 32.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भैक्षान्नम्, भैक्षाशिन्, भैक्षाहारः, भैक्षकालः, भैक्षचरणम्, भैक्षचर्यम्, भैक्षचर्या, भैक्षजीविका, भैक्षवृत्तिः, भैक्षभुज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षान्नम्
भैक्ष + -अन्नम् alms, food obtained by begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षाशिन्
भैक्ष + -आशिन् <i>a.</i> eating food obtained by begging. ━(<i>m.</i>) a beggar,<BR> mendicant; Ms. 11. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षाहारः|भैक्षाहार
भैक्ष + -आहारः a beggar; भैक्षाहारो विशुद्ध्यति Ms. 11. 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षकालः|भैक्षकाल
भैक्ष + -कालः the time for begging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचरणम्
भैक्ष + -चरणम्, -चर्यम्, -चर्या going about begging, begging, collecting alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचर्यम्
भैक्ष + -चरणम्, -चर्यम्, -चर्या going about begging, begging, collecting alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षचर्या|भैक्षचर्य्या
भैक्ष + -चरणम्, -चर्यम्, -चर्या going about begging, begging, collecting alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षजीविका
भैक्ष + -जीविका, -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> mendicancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षवृत्तिः|भैक्षवृत्ति
भैक्ष + -जीविका, -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> mendicancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षभुज्
भैक्ष + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a beggar, mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षव|भैक्षवं
भैक्षव <i>a.</i> Belonging to a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षवम्
भैक्षवम्, भैक्षुकम् [भिक्षूणां समूहः अञ्] A number of beggars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षुकम्
भैक्षवम्, भैक्षुकम् [भिक्षूणां समूहः अञ्] A number of beggars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्षुकः|भैक्षुक|भैक्षुकं
भैक्षुकः<BR>—1 The life of a religious mendicant.<BR>—2 संन्यास q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष्यम्
भैक्ष्यम् [भिक्षा-ष्यञ्] Food got by begging, alms, charity; see<BR> भैक्ष; अयाचितं तु तद् भैक्ष्यं भोक्तव्यं मनुरब्रवीत् Uśanāh Dharmaśāstra;<BR> गुरूनहत्वा हि महानुभावान् श्रेयो भोक्तुं भैक्ष्यमपीह लोके Bg. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैक्ष्याश्रमः
भैक्ष्यम् + .{@-आश्रमः@}<BR>—1 संन्यास q. v.; समदर्शिनश्च भूतेषु भैक्ष्याश्रमपदं भवेत् Mb. 12. 66. 5.<BR>—2 ब्रह्मचर्य q. v. Mb. 12. 66. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैम
भैम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>) [भीमस्य नृपस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to Bhīma.<BR>—2 Doing valorous deeds (भीमकर्मकर्तारः); Mb. 3. 120. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमी
भैम + .{@-मी@}<BR>—1 ‘The daughter of Bhīma’, a patronymic of Damayantī, wife of Nala.<BR>—2 The eleventh day of the bright half of Māgha or a festival performed on that day.<BR>—3 A descendant of Bhīma; आत्तायुधं मामिह रौहिणेय पश्यन्तु भैमा युधि<BR> जातहर्षाः Mb. 3. 120. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमसेनिः|भैमसेनि
भैमसेनिः, -न्यः<BR> A son of Bhīmasena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैमसेन्यः|भैमसेन्य
भैमसेनिः, -न्यः<BR> A son of Bhīmasena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरव|भैरवं|भैरवः
भैरव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भीरोरिदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Terrible, frightful, horrible, formidable; वेल्लद्भैरवरुण्डमुण्डनिकरैर्वीरो<BR> विधत्ते भुवम् U. 5. 6.<BR>—2 Miserable.<BR>—3 Relating to Bhairava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवः|भैरव|भैरवं
भैरव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A form of Śiva (of which 8 kinds are enumerated).<BR>—2 The sentiment of terror (भयानक).<BR>—3 Fear, terror.<BR>—4 N. of a musical mode (राग) calculated to excite emotions of fear or terror.<BR>—5 A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवी
भैरव + .{@-वी@}<BR>—1 A form of the goddess Durgā. ˚चक्रम् a disc of the goddess भैरवी;<BR> प्रवृत्ते भैरवीचक्रे सर्वे वर्णा द्विजोत्तमाः । निवृत्ते भैरवीचक्रे सर्वे<BR> वर्णाः पृथक् पृथक् ॥ Utpattitantra.<BR>—2 N. of a Rāgiṇī in the Hindu musical system.<BR>—3 A girl of 12 or a young girl representing the goddess Durgā at the<BR> Durgā festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवम्
भैरव + .{@-वम्@} Terror, horror.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भैरवेशः, भैरवयातना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवेशः|भैरवेश
भैरव + -ईशः an epithet of Viṣṇu (or Śiva ?); so भैरवतर्जकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैरवयातना
भैरव + -यातना a sort of purificatory torment inflicted by Bhairava of<BR> Benares on those who die there, to make their spirits fit for absorption<BR> into the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषजम्
भैषजम् [भेषजमेव स्वार्थे अण्] A medicine, drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषजः|भैषज|भैषजं
भैषजम् + .{@-जः@} The bird called लावक or quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैषज्यम्
भैषज्यम् [भिषजः कर्म, भेषज-स्वार्थे वा ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Administering medicines, medical treatment.<BR>—2 A medicament,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">Page1212-1</a>]<BR> medicine, drug; सर्वस्नेहधान्यक्षारलवणभैषज्य … … … Kau. A. 2. 4. 22.<BR>—3 Healing power, curativeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1211-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भैष्मकी
भैष्मकी A patronymic of Rukmiṇī, daughter of Bhīṣmaka of Vidarbha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृ
भोक्तृ <i>a.</i> [भुज् तृच्]<BR>—1 One who enjoys or eats.<BR>—2 Possessing.<BR>—3 Enjoying or making use of.<BR>—4 Feeling, enduring, experiencing.<BR>—5 Protecting, ruling, governing. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A possessor, enjoyer, user; पुरुषोऽस्ति भोक्तृभावात् कैवल्यार्थप्रवृत्तेश्च Sāṅ. K. 17.<BR>—2 A husband.<BR>—3 A king, ruler.<BR>—4 A lover.<BR>—5 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोक्तृत्वम्
भोक्तृत्वम्<BR>—1 Being a possessor.<BR>—2 Enjoyment, possession.<BR>—3 Perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगः|भोग
भोगः [भुज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Eating, consuming.<BR>—2 Enjoyment, fruition.<BR>—3 Possession.<BR>—4 Utility, advantage.<BR>—5 Ruling, governing, government.<BR>—6 Use, application (as of a deposit).<BR>—7 Suffering, enduring, experiencing.<BR>—8 Feeling, perception.<BR>—9 Enjoyment of women, sexual enjoyment, carnal pleasure.<BR>—10 An enjoyment, an object of enjoyment or pleasure; भोगे रोगभयम्<BR> Bh. 3. 35; भोगा मेघवितानमध्यविलसत्सौदामिनीचञ्चलाः Bh. 3. 54;<BR> भोगो विभवभेदश्च निष्कृतिर्मुक्तिरेव च Brav. P.; Bg. 1. 32.<BR>—11 A repast, feast, banquet.<BR>—12 Food.<BR>—13 Food offered to an idol.<BR>—14 Profit, gain.<BR>—15 Income, revenue.<BR>—16 Wealth; भोगान् भोगानिवाहेयानध्यास्यापन्न दुर्लभा Ki. 11. 23.<BR>—17 The wages of prostitutes.<BR>—18 A curve, coil, winding.<BR>—19 The (expanded) hood of a snake; श्वसदसितभुजङ्गभोगाङ्गदग्रन्थि<BR> &c. Māl. 5. 23; R. 10. 7, 11. 59.<BR>—20 A snake.<BR>—21 The body.<BR>—22 An army in column.<BR>—23 The passing (of an asterism).<BR>—24 The part of the ecliptic occupied by each of the 27 Nakṣatras.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोगार्ह, भोगार्ह्यम्, भोगाधिः, भोगावली, भोगावासः, भोगकर,^1 भोगगुच्छम्, भोगगृहम्, भोगतृष्णा, भोगदेहः, भोगधरः, भोगनाथः, भोगपतिः, भोगपत्रम्, भोगपालः, भोगपिशाचिका, भोगभुज्, भोगभूमिः, भोगभृतकः, भोगलाभः, भोगवस्तु, भोगसद्मन्, भोगस्थानम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगार्ह
भोगः + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> fit to be enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगार्हम्
भोगः + -अर्ह + ({@-र्हम्@}) property, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगार्ह्यम्
भोगः + -अर्ह्यम् corn, grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगाधिः|भोगाधि
भोगः + -आधिः a pledge which may be used until redeemed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगावली
भोगः + -आवली the panegyric of a professional encomiast; नग्नः स्तुतिव्रतस्तस्य<BR> ग्रन्थो भोगावली भवेत्; Abh. Cin. 795; भोगावलीः कलगिरोऽवसरेषु पेठुः Śi. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगावासः|भोगावास
भोगः + -आवासः the apartments of women, harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगकर
भोगः + -कर^1 <i>a.</i> affording enjoyment or pleasure.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगगुच्छम्
भोगः + -गुच्छम् wages paid to prostitutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगगृहम्
भोगः + -गृहम् the womenʼs apartments, harem, zenana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगतृष्णा
भोगः + -तृष्णा desire of worldly enjoyments; तदुपस्थितमग्रहीदजः<BR> पितुराज्ञेति न भोगतृष्णया R. 8. 2; selfish enjoyment; Māl. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगदेहः|भोगदेह
भोगः + -देहः ‘the body of suffering’, the subtle body which a dead person<BR> is supposed to carry with him, and with which he experiences happiness<BR> or misery according to his good or bad actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगधरः|भोगधर
भोगः + -धरः a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगनाथः|भोगनाथ
भोगः + -नाथः a nourisher, supporter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपतिः|भोगपति
भोगः + -पतिः the governor or ruler of a district or province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपत्रम्
भोगः + -पत्रम् an Inām deed; Śukra. 2. 295.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपालः|भोगपाल
भोगः + -पालः a groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगपिशाचिका
भोगः + -पिशाचिका hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभुज्
भोगः + -भुज् <i>a.</i> enjoying pleasures. ━<i>m.</i> a wealthy man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभूमिः|भोगभूमि
भोगः + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> ‘the land of enjoyment’, heaven, paradise (where<BR> persons are said to enjoy the fruit of their actions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगभृतकः|भोगभृतक
भोगः + -भृतकः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">Page1212-2</a>]<BR> servant who works only for livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगलाभः|भोगलाभ
भोगः + -लाभः<BR>—1 acquisition of enjoyment or profit.<BR>—2 well-being, welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगवस्तु
भोगः + -वस्तु <i>n.</i> an object of enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगसद्मन्
भोगः + -सद्मन् <i>n.</i> = भोगावास q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगस्थानम्
भोगः + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 the body, as the seat of enjoyment.<BR>—2 womenʼs apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगवत्|भोगवन्त्
भोगवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Giving pleasure or delight, delightful.<BR>—2 Happy, prosperous.<BR>—3 Having curves, ringed, coiled. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A snake.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 Dancing, acting, and singing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगवती
भोगवत् + ({@-ती@}) ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of the Ganges of Pātāla or the lower world (पातालगङ्गा);<BR> भोगवती च पाताले स्वर्गे मन्दाकिनी तथा Purāṇam; A. Rām. 6. 9. 8.<BR>—2 A female snake-demon; Mb. 1. 171. 38.<BR>—3 N. of the city of the snake-demons in the lower world; आत्मतुल्यबलैर्गुप्तां<BR> नागैर्भोगवतीमिव Bhāg. 1. 11. 11.<BR>—4 The night of the second day of a lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिकः|भोगिक
भोगिकः [भोग-ठन्] A groom, horse-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिन्
भोगिन् <i>a.</i> [भोग-इनि]<BR>—1 Eating.<BR>—2 Enjoying.<BR>—3 Suffering, experiencing, enduring.<BR>—4 Using, possessing (at the end of comp. in these four senses.)<BR>—5 Having curves, having large body; अभवन् पन्नगास्त्रस्ता भोगिनस्तत्रवासिनः<BR> Rām. 6. 50. 35 (com.).<BR>—6 Having hoods.<BR>—7 Devoted to enjoyment, indulging in sensual pleasures; भोगिनः कञ्चुकाविष्टाः<BR> कुटिलाः क्रूरचेष्टिताः । सुदुष्टा मन्त्रसाध्याश्च राजानः पन्नगा इव ॥<BR> Pt. 1. 65 (where it has sense 6 also).<BR>—8 Rich, opulent. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A snake; गजाजिनालम्बि पिनद्धभोगि वा Ku. 5. 78; R. 2. 32, 4. 48, 10. 7, 11. 59.<BR>—2 A king.<BR>—3 A voluptuary.<BR>—4 A barber.<BR>—5 The headman of a village.<BR>—6 The lunar mansion आश्लेषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिनी
भोगिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A woman belonging to the kingʼs harem, but not consecrated with him,<BR> the concubine of a king.<BR>—2 A kind of heroine.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोगीन्द्रः, भोगीशः, भोगिकान्तः, भोगिभुज्, भोगिराज्, भोगिवल्लभम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगीन्द्रः|भोगीन्द्र|भोगींद्र
भोगिन् + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः Śeṣa or Vāsuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगीशः|भोगीश
भोगिन् + -इन्द्रः, -ईशः Śeṣa or Vāsuki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिकान्तः|भोगिकान्त|भोगिकांत
भोगिन् + -कान्तः wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिभुज्
भोगिन् + -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an ichneumon.<BR>—2 a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिराज्
भोगिन् + -राज् <i>m.</i> Śeṣa, the lord of snakes; भुजे भोगिराजो गले कालिमा च.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोगिवल्लभम्
भोगिन् + -वल्लभम् sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्य|भोग्यं
भोग्य <i>a.</i> [भुज् ण्यत् कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 To be enjoyed or turned to oneʼs account; समुपास्यत पुत्रभोग्यया<BR> स्नुषयेवाविकृतेन्द्रियः श्रिया R. 8. 14; Pt. 1. 117.<BR>—2 To be suffered or endured; Me. 1; स पुनर्द्विविधः प्रोक्तो गोप्यो भोग्यस्तथैव च Nārada.<BR>—3 Profitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्यम्
भोग्य + .{@-ग्यम्@}<BR>—1 Any object of enjoyment.<BR>—2 Wealth, property, possessions.<BR>—3 Corn, grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्या
भोग्य + .{@-ग्या@} A harlot, courtezan.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोग्यवस्तु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोग्यवस्तु
भोग्य + -वस्तु articles of luxury; अस्त्यत्र भोग्यवस्तु वर्षशतोपभोगेनाप्यक्षय्यम् Dk. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज|भोजः
भोज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bestowing enjoyment; राजा भोजो विराट् सम्राट् क्षत्रियो भूपतिर्नृपः<BR> Mb. 12. 68. 54.<BR>—2 Leading a life of enjoyment, enjoying; देवासुरमनुष्येषु ये भजन्त्यशिवं शिवम् । प्रायस्ते धनिनो भोजाः Bhāg. 10. 88. 1.<BR>—3 Liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजः|भोज
भोजः [भुज्-अच्] N. of a celebrated king of Mālvā (or Dhārā);<BR> (supposed to have flourished about the end of the tenth or the beginning<BR> of the eleventh century, and to have been a great patron of Sanskrit<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">Page1213-1</a>]<BR> learning; he is also supposed to have been the author of several learned<BR> works, such as सरस्वतीकण्ठाभरण &c.).<BR>—2 N. of a country.<BR>—3 N. of a king of the Vidarbhas; भोजेन दूतो रघवे विसृष्टः R. 5. 39, 7. 18, 29, 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजाः
भोजः + .{@-जाः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) N. of a people.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोजाधिपः, भोजेन्द्रः, भोजकटम्, भोजकुलम्, भोजदेवः, भोजराजः, भोजपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1212-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजाधिपः|भोजाधिप
भोजः + -अधिपः an epithet of<BR>—1 Kamsa.<BR>—2 Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजेन्द्रः|भोजेन्द्र|भोजेंद्र
भोजः + -इन्द्रः a king of the Bhojas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजकटम्
भोजः + -कटम् N. of a town founded by Rukmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजकुलम्
भोजः + -कुलम् the dynasty of the Bhojas who ruled over the country of<BR> Vidarbha or Berar; अभोजयद् भोजकुलाङ्कुरः क्वचित् N. 16. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजदेवः|भोजदेव
भोजः + -देवः, -राजः king Bhoja; धन्यः श्रीभोजराजस्त्रिभुवनविजयी<BR> Udb.; see (1) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजराजः|भोजराज
भोजः + -देवः, -राजः king Bhoja; धन्यः श्रीभोजराजस्त्रिभुवनविजयी<BR> Udb.; see (1) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजपतिः|भोजपति
भोजः + -पतिः<BR>—1 king Bhoja.<BR>—2 an epithet of Kamsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजक
भोजक <i>a.</i> [भुज् णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Causing to eat, feeding, nourishing; दैवे पित्र्ये च भोजकः Y. 2. 35.<BR>—2 An eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजन|भोजनं|भोजनः
भोजन <i>a.</i> [भुज्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Feeding, nourishing, giving to eat.<BR>—2 Voracious; (राक्षसी) अङ्गारकेति विख्याता छायामाक्षिप्य भोजनी<BR> Rām. 4. 41. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनः|भोजन|भोजनं
भोजन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनम्
भोजन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Eating, eating food; taking oneʼs meals; अजीर्णे भोजनं विषम्.<BR>—2 Food.<BR>—3 Giving (food) to eat, feeding.<BR>—4 Using, enjoying.<BR>—5 Any object of enjoyment.<BR>—6 That which is enjoyed; सहानुजैः प्रत्यवरुद्धभोजनः Bhāg. 1. 10. 1.<BR>—7 Property, wealth, possessions.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोजनाधिकारः, भोजनाच्छादनम्, भोजनकालः, भोजनवेला, भोजनसमयः, भोजनत्यागः, भोजनभाण्डम्, भोजनभूमिः, भोजनविशेषः, भोजनवृत्तिः, भोजनव्यग्र, भोजनव्ययः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनाधिकारः|भोजनाधिकार
भोजन + -अधिकारः charge of provender, superintendence over food or provisions, stewardship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनाच्छादनम्
भोजन + -आच्छादनम् food and raiment; भोजनाच्छादने दद्यादृतुकाले च<BR> संगमम् Pt. 5. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनकालः|भोजनकाल
भोजन + -कालः, -वेला, -समयः meal-time, dinner or supper time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनवेला
भोजन + -कालः, -वेला, -समयः meal-time, dinner or supper time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनसमयः|भोजनसमय
भोजन + -कालः, -वेला, -समयः meal-time, dinner or supper time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनत्यागः|भोजनत्याग
भोजन + -त्यागः abstaining from food, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनभाण्डम्
भोजन + -भाण्डम् a dish of meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनभूमिः|भोजनभूमि
भोजन + -भूमिः <i>f.</i> a dining-hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनविशेषः|भोजनविशेष
भोजन + -विशेषः a dainty, delicacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनवृत्तिः|भोजनवृत्ति
भोजन + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> a meal, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनव्यग्र
भोजन + -व्यग्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 engaged in eating.<BR>—2 straitened for want of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनव्ययः|भोजनव्यय
भोजन + -व्ययः expense for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनीय
भोजनीय <i>a.</i> [भुज् अनीयर्]<BR>—1 Eatable, edible.<BR>—2 To be fed, nourished (dependants).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजनीयम्
भोजनीय + .{@-यम्@} Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजयितृ
भोजयितृ <i>a.</i> [भुज्-णिच्-तृच्] One who feeds, a feeder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोजिन्
भोजिन् <i>a.</i> [भुज्-णिनि] (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Eating, enjoying; using, possessing &c.<BR>—2 Feeding, nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्य|भोज्यं
भोज्य <i>pot. p.</i> [भुज्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be eaten.<BR>—2 To be enjoyed or possessed.<BR>—3 To be suffered or experienced.<BR>—4 To be enjoyed carnally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यम्
भोज्य + .{@-ज्यम्@}<BR>—1 Food, meal; त्वं भोक्ता अहं च भोज्यभूतः Pt. 2; Ku. 2. 15; Ms. 3. 240;<BR> भोज्यं भोजनशक्तिश्च रतिशक्तिर्नराः स्त्रियः Cāṇ.<BR>—2 A store of provisions, eatables; वर्धयेद्बाहुयुद्धार्थं भोज्यैः शारीरकेवलम्<BR> Śukra. 4. 877.<BR>—3 A dainty.<BR>—4 Enjoyment.<BR>—5 Advantage, profit.<BR>—6 Food given to the Manes.<BR>—7 Wounding the mortal spot (मर्मभेद); भोज्ये पांसुविकर्षणे<BR> Mb. 5. 169. 12 (com. भोज्ये कौटिल्ये मर्मपीडने).<BR>—8 A festive dinner, feast.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोज्यान्न, भोज्योष्ण, भोज्यकालः, भोज्यसंभवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यान्न
भोज्य + -अन्न <i>a.</i> one whose food may be eaten; एते शूद्रेषु भोज्यान्नाः Ms. 4. 253.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्योष्ण
भोज्य + -उष्ण <i>a.</i> too hot to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यकालः|भोज्यकाल
भोज्य + -कालः meal-time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्यसंभवः|भोज्यसम्भव|भोज्यसंभव|भोज्यसम्भवः
भोज्य + -संभवः chyme, the primary juice of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोज्या
भोज्या<BR>—1 A princess of the Bhojas; पूर्वानुशिष्टां निजगाद भोज्याम् R. 6. 59, 7. 2, 13.<BR>—2 A procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटः|भोट
भोटः N. of a country (said to be the same as Tibet).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोटाङ्गः, भोटगो<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटाङ्गः|भोटाङ्ग|भोटांग
भोटः + -अङ्गः the country called Bhootāna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटगो
भोटः + -गो Bos Vacus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोटीय
भोटीय <i>a.</i> Tibetan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोमीरा
भोमीरा Coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलः|भोल
भोलः The son of a Vaiśya and a Naṭī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलानाथः|भोलानाथ
भोलानाथः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोलिः|भोलि
भोलिः A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोस्
भोस् <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle used in addressing persons, and<BR> translatable by ‘o’, ‘sir’, ‘oh’, ‘halloo’, {sic} ‘ah’; (it drops its<BR> final <i>visarga</i> before vowels and soft consonants); कः कोऽत्र<BR> भोः Ś. 2; अयि भो महर्षिपुत्र Ś. 7; it is sometimes repeated; भो<BR> भोः शंकरगृहाधिवासिनो जानपदाः Māl. 3; भो भोः पण्डिताः श्रूयताम्<BR> H. भोस् is said to have, in addition, the senses of ‘sorrow’ and ‘interrogation’.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भोःकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भोःकारः
भोस् + -कारः rules of address.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजङ्ग|भौजंग
भौजङ्ग <i>a.</i> (-ङ्गी <i>f.</i>) [भुजङ्ग-अण्] Serpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजङ्गम्
भौजङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गम्@} The lunar mansion called आश्लेषा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौजिष्यम्
भौजिष्यम् Slavery, servitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौज्यम्
भौज्यम्<BR>—1 A kind of sovereignty; cf. वैराज्य, स्वाराज्य &c.<BR>—2 A royal rank (ऐश्वर्य); न वयं साध्वि साम्राज्यं स्वाराज्यं भौज्यमप्युत ।<BR> वैराज्यं पारमेष्ठपं च आनन्त्यं वा हरेः पदम् ॥ Bhāg. 10. 83. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौट्टः|भौट्ट
भौट्टः A Tibetan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौत|भौतः
भौत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>) [भूतानि प्राणिनोऽधिकृत्य प्रवृत्तः,<BR> तानि देवता वा अस्य अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to living beings.<BR>—2 Elemental, material.<BR>—3 Demoniacal.<BR>—4 Mad, crazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतः|भौत
भौत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A worshipper of demons and spirits.<BR>—2 An attendant upon an idol (देवल).<BR>—3 One of the five daily Yajñas to be performed by a householder (also<BR> called भूतयज्ञ, q. v.); होमो दैवो बलिर्भौतो नृयज्ञोऽतिथिपूजनम् Ms. 3. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतम्
भौत + .{@-तम्@} A collection of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौती
भौत + .{@-ती@} Night.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भौततुल्य, भौतप्रिय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौततुल्य
भौत + -तुल्य, -प्रिय <i>a.</i> imbecile, deranged, like an idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतप्रिय
भौत + -तुल्य, -प्रिय <i>a.</i> imbecile, deranged, like an idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतक
भौतक <i>a.</i> Possessed by evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिक|भौतिकं|भौतिकः
भौतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [भूत-ठक्]<BR>—1 Belonging to created or living beings; प्रहुतो भौतिको बलिः Ms. 3. 74;<BR> आहंकारिकत्वश्रुतेर्न भौतिकानि Sāṅ. S.<BR>—2 Formed of coarse elements, elemental, material; वृक्षाणां नास्ति भौतिकम्<BR> Bhāg. 12. 184. 9; पिण्डेष्वनास्था खलु भौतिकेषु R. 2. 57.<BR>—3 Relating to evil spirits.<BR>—4 Possessed by evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिकः|भौतिक|भौतिकं
भौतिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 A being, animal (जीव); कालस्य ते किमुत तत्कृतभौतिकानाम्<BR> Bhāg. 12. 8. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिकम्
भौतिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A pearl.<BR>—2 Anything elemental.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भौतिकमठः, भौतिकविद्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिकमठः
भौतिक + -मठः a monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौतिकविद्या
भौतिक + -विद्या sorcery, witch-craft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1213-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौपालः|भौपाल
भौपालः A prince, son of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम|भौमः
भौम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>) [भूमेरपत्यं तस्या इदं वा अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the earth; संस्तूयन्ते विप्रकर्षाद्भौमा नोपाधयः स्फुटम् Mv. 7. 22.<BR>—2 Being on the earth, earthly, terrestrial; भौमो मुनेः स्थानपरिग्रहोऽयम्<BR> R. 13. 36, 15. 59.<BR>—3 Earthy, made of earth; Ms. 11. 155.<BR>—4 Relating to Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमः|भौम
भौम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 The planet Mars.<BR>—2 An epithet of the demon Naraka; त्वयि भौमं गते जेतुमरौत्सीत् स<BR> पुरीमिमाम् Śi. 2. 39; भौमं हत्वा तन्निरोधादाहृताश्चारुदर्शनाः Bhāg. 10. 58. 58.<BR>—3 Water.<BR>—4 Light.<BR>—5 Sky, atmosphere.<BR>—6 N. of Atri.<BR>—7 A red-flowering पुनर्नवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमम्
भौम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Corn, grain.<BR>—2 An elemental thing; किमात्मनश्चात्र ह भौमयोस्तत् Bhāg. 11. 23. 51.<BR>—3 Floor; हैमराजतभौमेषु Rām. 2. 88. 5.<BR>—4 Story; सप्तभौमाष्टभौमैश्च स ददर्श महापुरीम् Rām. 5. 2. 50.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भौमदिनम्, भौमवारः, भौमवासरः, भौमब्रह्मन्, भौमरत्नम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमदिनम्
भौम + -दिनम्, -वारः, -वासरः Tuesday; भौमदिनमभिदधत्यथवा भृशमप्रशस्तमपि<BR> मङ्गलं जनाः Śi. 15. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमवारः|भौमवार
भौम + -दिनम्, -वारः, -वासरः Tuesday; भौमदिनमभिदधत्यथवा भृशमप्रशस्तमपि<BR> मङ्गलं जनाः Śi. 15. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमवासरः|भौमवासर
भौम + -दिनम्, -वारः, -वासरः Tuesday; भौमदिनमभिदधत्यथवा भृशमप्रशस्तमपि<BR> मङ्गलं जनाः Śi. 15. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमब्रह्मन्
भौम + -ब्रह्मन् (भौमब्रह्मन्) Vedas, Brāhmaṇas and sacrifices;<BR> भौमस्य ब्रह्मणो गुप्त्यै दीपमग्निमिवारणिः Mb. 12. 47. 29 (com. भौमं<BR> ब्रह्म वेदा ब्राह्मणा यज्ञाश्च).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमरत्नम्
भौम + -रत्नम् coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमकः|भौमक
भौमकः Any animal living in the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमनः|भौमन
भौमनः N. of Viśvakarman, architect of the gods; Mb. 1. 32. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमिक|भौमिकः
भौमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौम्य
भौमिक + .{@-भौम्य@} <i>a.</i> [भूमि-ठक् यत् वा] Earthly, terrestrial, living<BR> or existing on the earth; भौमिकैस्ते समा ज्ञेया न तैराप्रयतो भवेत् Ms. 5. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौमी
भौमी <i>f.</i> An epithet of Sītā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौरिकः|भौरिक
भौरिकः [भूरि सुवर्णमधिकरोति ठक्] The superintendent of gold<BR> in a royal treasury, a treasury-officer, a treasurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौली
भौली N. of a Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवनः|भौवन
भौवनः See भौमन; निहत्य विश्वकर्माणं भौवनं सोमरक्षणे Bm. 1. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भौवादिक
भौवादिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Belonging to the class of roots<BR> which begin with भू, <i>i. e.</i> to the first conjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्यस्
भ्यस् €1 Ā. (भ्यसते) To fear. ━<i>Caus.</i> To frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंश्
भ्रंश् €1 Ā., €4 P. (भ्रंशते, भ्रश्यति, भ्रष्ट; with abl. in most cases)<BR>—1 To fall or drop down, tumble; हस्ताद् भ्रष्टमिदं बिसाभरणम् Ś. 3. 25;<BR> Pt. 1. 130; Śi. 18. 21.<BR>—2 To fall from, deviate or swerve from, stray from; यूथाद् भ्रष्टः<BR> H. 4; R. 14. 16.<BR>—3 To be deprived of, lose; बभ्रंशेऽसौ धृतेस्ततः Bk. 14. 71; Pt. 2. 108, 4. 37.<BR>—4 To escape, flee from; संग्रामाद् बभ्रशुः केचित् Bk. 14. 105, 15. 59.<BR>—5 To decline, decay, decrease; विवर्णवदनश्चासीत् किंचिदभ्रश्यत<BR> स्वनः Rām. 6. 95. 45.<BR>—6 To disappear, vanish, depart; द्रवति हृदयमन्तर्भ्रश्यतीवान्तरात्मा<BR> Māl. 8. 12. ━<i>Caus.</i> (भ्रंशयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to fall, throw or cast down.<BR>—2 To deprive of.<BR>—3 To ruin, overturn.<BR>—4 To cause to disappear or vanish.<BR>—5 To expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशः|भ्रंश
भ्रंशः, -सः<BR> [भ्रंश् भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Falling off, dropping down, fall, slipping or falling down; सेहेऽस्य<BR> न भ्रंशमतो न लोभात् R. 16. 74; कनकवलयभ्रंशरिक्तप्रकोष्ठः Me. 2.<BR>—2 Decline, decrease, decay.<BR>—3 Fall, destruction, ruin, overthrow.<BR>—4 Running away.<BR>—5 Disappearance.<BR>—6 Losing, loss, deprivation; स्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशः Bg. 2. 63; so<BR> जातिभ्रंश, स्वार्थभ्रंश.<BR>—7 Straying, swerving, or deviating from.<BR>—8 Abandoning, deserting.<BR>—9 (In drama) A slip of the tongue (due to excitement).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंसः|भ्रंस
भ्रंशः, -सः<BR> [भ्रंश् भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Falling off, dropping down, fall, slipping or falling down; सेहेऽस्य<BR> न भ्रंशमतो न लोभात् R. 16. 74; कनकवलयभ्रंशरिक्तप्रकोष्ठः Me. 2.<BR>—2 Decline, decrease, decay.<BR>—3 Fall, destruction, ruin, overthrow.<BR>—4 Running away.<BR>—5 Disappearance.<BR>—6 Losing, loss, deprivation; स्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशः Bg. 2. 63; so<BR> जातिभ्रंश, स्वार्थभ्रंश.<BR>—7 Straying, swerving, or deviating from.<BR>—8 Abandoning, deserting.<BR>—9 (In drama) A slip of the tongue (due to excitement).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशथुः|भ्रंशथु
भ्रंशथुः See प्रभ्रंशथुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशन
भ्रंश(स)न <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भ्रंश्-ल्यु, ल्युट् वा] Throwing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंसन
भ्रंश(स)न <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भ्रंश्-ल्यु, ल्युट् वा] Throwing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशनम्
भ्रंश(स)न + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The act of dropping down.<BR>—2 Falling from, being deprived of, losing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशित
भ्रंशित <i>a.</i> Thrown or cast down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंशिन्
भ्रंशिन् <i>a.</i> [भ्रंश्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Falling off or down, falling from.<BR>—2 Decaying.<BR>—3 Straying away from.<BR>—4 Ruining, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्ट|भ्रष्टं
भ्रष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen, dropped.<BR>—2 Decayed, ruined.<BR>—3 Fled, escaped.<BR>—4 Depraved, vicious.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रष्टाधिकार, भ्रष्टक्रिय, भ्रष्टगुद, भ्रष्टयोग, भ्रष्टश्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टाधिकार
भ्रष्ट + -अधिकार <i>a.</i> dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टक्रिय
भ्रष्ट + -क्रिय <i>a.</i> one who has omitted prescribed acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टगुद
भ्रष्ट + -गुद <i>a.</i> suffering from prolapsus ani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टयोग
भ्रष्ट + -योग <i>a.</i> fallen from devotion; back-slider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रष्टश्री
भ्रष्ट + -श्री <i>a.</i> unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रंस्
भ्रंस् = भ्रंश् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुंशः|भ्रकुंश
भ्रकुंशः An actor in female dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रकुटि|भ्रकुटिः
भ्रकुटि = भ्रुकुटि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रक्ष्
भ्रक्ष् €1 U. (भ्रक्षति-ते) To eat, devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रज्जनम्
भ्रज्जनम् [भ्रस्ज् ल्युट्] The act of frying, roasting, or parching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रण्
भ्रण् €1 P. (भ्रणति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रभङ्गः|भ्रभङ्ग|भ्रभंग|भ्रभंगः
भ्रभङ्गः = भ्रूभङ्गः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रम्
भ्रम् €1. €4 P. (भ्रमति, भ्रम्यति, भ्राम्यति, बभ्राम, अभ्रमत्, अभ्रमीत्,<BR> भ्रमिष्यति, भ्रमितुम्, भ्रान्त) —1 To roam or wander about, move or go<BR> about, rove, ramble (fig. also); भ्रमति भुवने कन्दर्पाज्ञा Māl. 1. 17;<BR> मनो निष्ठाशून्यं भ्रमति च किमप्यालिखति च 31; oft. with acc.<BR> of place; भुवं बभ्राम Dk.; दिग्मण्डलं भ्रमसि मानस चापलेन<BR> Bh. 3. 77; so भिक्षां भ्रम् ‘to go about begging’.<BR>—2 To turn or whirl round, revolve, move round or in a circle; सूर्यो<BR> भ्राम्यति नित्यमेव गगने Bh. 2. 95; भ्रमता भ्रमरेण Gīt. 3.<BR>—3 To go astray, stray, swerve, deviate.<BR>—4 To spread, prevail, be current or afloat; अभ्रमच्च पौरजानपदेष्वियं वार्ता Dk.<BR>—5 To totter, reel, stagger, be in doubt or suspense, waver; अन्तर्भिन्नं<BR> भ्रमति हृदयम् Māl. 5. 20.<BR>—6 To err, be in error or mistake, be mistaken; आभरणकारस्तु तालव्य इति बभ्राम.<BR>—7 To flicker, flutter, quiver, move unsteadily; चक्षुर्भ्राम्यति Pt. 4. 78.<BR>—8 To surround.<BR>—9 To waver, be perplexed, doubt; तैरश्वैर्भ्राम्यते भ्रान्तैः सुमाली राक्षसेश्वरः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">Page1215-1</a>]<BR> Rām. 7. 7. 30. ━<i>Caus.</i> (भ्रमयति-ते or भ्रामयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to rove or wander, cause to revolve or turn round, whirl round;<BR> भ्रमय जलदानम्भोगर्भान् Māl. 9. 41.<BR>—2 To cause to err, delude, mislead, perplex, confuse, embarrass, cause<BR> to reel or stagger; विकारश्चैतन्यं भ्रमयति च संमीलयति च U. 1. 36.<BR>—3 To wave, brandish, vibrate; लीलारविन्दं भ्रमयांचकार R. 6. 13.<BR>—4 To proclaim by beat of drum.<BR>—5 To disarrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1214-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमः|भ्रम
भ्रमः [भ्रम्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Moving or roaming about, roving.<BR>—2 Turning round, whirling, revolving.<BR>—3 Circular motion, rotation.<BR>—4 Straying, deviating.<BR>—5 An error, a mistake, misapprehension, delusion; शुक्तौ रजतमिति<BR> ज्ञानं भ्रमः; भ्रमं संमोहमावर्तमभ्यासाद्विनिवर्तयेत् Mb. 12. 274. 7;<BR> भ्रमो द्विविधः विपर्यासः संशयश्च T. S.<BR>—6 Confusion, perplexity, embarrassment.<BR>—7 An eddy, a whirlpool.<BR>—8 A potterʼs wheel.<BR>—9 A grind-stone.<BR>—10 A lathe.<BR>—11 Giddiness.<BR>—12 A fountain, water-course; भ्रमागतैरम्बुभिरम्बुराशिः Śi. 3. 38.<BR>—13 An umbrella.<BR>—14 A circle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रमाकुल, भ्रमासक्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमाकुल
भ्रमः + -आकुल <i>a.</i> confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमासक्तः|भ्रमासक्त
भ्रमः + -आसक्तः a sword-cleaner, an armourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमणम्
भ्रमणम्^1 [भ्रम्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Moving or roving about, roaming about.<BR>—2 Turning round, revolution.<BR>—3 Deviation, swerving.<BR>—4 Shaking, tottering, unsteadiness, staggering.<BR>—5 Erring.<BR>—6 Giddiness, dizziness.<BR>—7 A tour, excursion.<BR>—8 The orbit of a planet<BR>—9 A cupola.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: neuter noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमणी
भ्रमणम् + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 A kind of game.<BR>—2 A leech.<BR>—3 N. of one of the 5 धारणाs. ˚विलासः a pleasure trip; विधेः<BR> कदाचिद्भ्रमणीविलासे N. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्
भ्रमत् <i>a.</i> Wandering, roving &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रमत्कुटी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमत्कुटी
भ्रमत् + -कुटी a kind of umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमर|भ्रमरः
भ्रमर [भ्रम्-करन्]<BR>—1 A bee, large black bee; मलिनेऽपि रागपूर्णां विकसितवदनामनल्पकल्पेऽपि ।<BR> त्वयि चपलेऽपि च सरसां भ्रमर कथं वा सरोजिनीं त्यजसि ॥ Bv. 1. 100<BR> (where the next meaning is also suggested).<BR>—2 A lover, gallant, libertine.<BR>—3 A potterʼs wheel.<BR>—4 A young man.<BR>—5 A top; अभ्रामयदहो दारुभ्रमरं स कदाचन Śiva B. 7. 32.<BR>—6 A particular position of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरी
भ्रमर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A bee; अमरीकबरीभारभ्रमरीमुखरीकृतम् Kuval.<BR>—2 Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरम्
भ्रमर + .{@-रम्@} Giddiness, vertigo.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रमरातिथिः, भ्रमराभिलीन, भ्रमरालकः, भ्रमरानन्दः, भ्रमरेष्टः, भ्रमरोत्सवा, भ्रमरकरण्डकः, भ्रमरकीटः, भ्रमरनिकरः, भ्रमरपदम्, भ्रमरप्रियः, भ्रमरबाधा, भ्रमरमण्डलम्, भ्रमरविलसितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरातिथिः|भ्रमरातिथि
भ्रमर + -अतिथिः the Champaka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमराभिलीन
भ्रमर + -अभिलीन <i>a.</i> with bees clung or attached to; तिरश्चकार<BR> भ्रमराभिलीनयोः सुजातयोः पङ्कजकोशयोः श्रियम् R. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरालकः|भ्रमरालक
भ्रमर + -अलकः a curl on the forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरानन्दः|भ्रमरानन्द
भ्रमर + -आनन्दः<BR>—1 the Bakula tree.<BR>—2 the Atimukta creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरेष्टः|भ्रमरेष्ट
भ्रमर + -इष्टः the tree called श्योनाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरोत्सवा
भ्रमर + -उत्सवा the Mādhavī creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकरण्डकः|भ्रमरकरण्डक|भ्रमरकरंडक
भ्रमर + -करण्डकः a small box containing bees (carried by thieves to<BR> extinguish light in a house by letting the bees escape); Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकीटः|भ्रमरकीट
भ्रमर + -कीटः a species of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरनिकरः|भ्रमरनिकर
भ्रमर + -निकरः a multitude of bees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरपदम्
भ्रमर + -पदम् a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरप्रियः|भ्रमरप्रिय
भ्रमर + -प्रियः a kind of Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरबाधा
भ्रमर + -बाधा molestation by a bee; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरमण्डलम्
भ्रमर + -मण्डलम् a swarm of bees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरविलसितम्
भ्रमर + -विलसितम्<BR>—1 the sporting of bees.<BR>—2 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकः|भ्रमरक
भ्रमरकः [भ्रमर स्वार्थे क]<BR>—1 A bee.<BR>—2 A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकः|भ्रमरक
भ्रमरकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A lock of hair or curl hanging down on the forehead.<BR>—2 A ball for playing with.<BR>—3 A humming top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरकम्
भ्रमरकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A lock of hair or curl hanging down on the forehead.<BR>—2 A ball for playing with.<BR>—3 A humming top.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरिका
भ्रमरिका Roving in all directions. ˚दृष्टिः a wandering glance;<BR> यथा भ्रमरिकादृष्ट्या भ्राम्यतीव महीयते Bhāg. 10. 46. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरित
भ्रमरित <i>a.</i> Turned blue; यदतिविमलनीलवेश्मरश्मिभ्रमरितभाः<BR> शुचिसौधवस्त्रवल्लिः N. 2. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमरायते
भ्रमरायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To begin turning round or revolving.<BR>—2 To act like a bee, <i>i. e.</i> to be unsteady in oneʼs attachments to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमिः|भ्रमि
भ्रमिः <i>f.</i> [भ्रम्-इ]<BR>—1 Whirling or turning round, circular movement; moving about or round,<BR> revolution; भ्रमिषु कृतपुटान्तर्मण्डलावृत्तिचक्षुः U. 3. 19, 6. 3; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>—2 A potterʼs wheel.<BR>—3 A turnerʼs lathe.<BR>—4 A whirlpool.<BR>—5 A whirlwind.<BR>—6 A circular arrangement of troops.<BR>—7 An error, a mistake.<BR>—8 Swoon, fainting (मूर्च्छा); A. Rām. 6. 11. 73. ━<i>a.</i> Turning round,<BR> revolving; क्षौरपव्यं स्वयंभ्रमिम् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमित
भ्रमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Made to go round, whirled.<BR>—2 Falsely taken for, confounded with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रमिन्
भ्रमिन् <i>a.</i> [भ्रम्-णिनि] Turning or moving round, revolving, whirling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रश्
भ्रश् See भ्रंश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रशिमन्
भ्रशिमन् <i>m.</i> Violence, excessiveness, impetuosity, vehemence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रस्ज्
भ्रस्ज् €6 U. (भृज्जति, भृष्ट; <i>caus.</i> भर्जयति-ते, भ्रज्जयति-ते;<BR> <i>desid.</i> बिभर्क्षति-बिभ्रक्षति, बिभर्जिषति-बिभ्रज्जिषति) To<BR> fry, roast, parch, broil; (fig. also); बभ्रज्ज निहते तस्मिन् शोको रावणमग्निवत् Bk. 14. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राज्
भ्राज् €1 Ā. (भ्रजते) To shine, gleam, flash, glitter; रुरुजुर्भ्रेजिरे<BR> फेणुर्बहुधा हरिराक्षसाः Bk. 14. 78, 15. 24. ━<i>Caus.</i> To illuminate,<BR> irradiate. ━<i>With</i> {@वि@} to shine brilliantly or intensely; विभ्राजसे<BR> मकरकेतनमर्चयन्ती Ratn. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजः|भ्राज
भ्राजः N. of one of the seven suns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजम्
भ्राजः + .{@-जम्@} N. of a Sāman; भ्राजा भ्राजे पवमानमुखे भवतो सुखत<BR> एवास्य ताभ्यां तमोऽपघ्नन्ति Tāṇḍya Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजक|भ्राजकं
भ्राजक <i>a.</i> (-जिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [भ्रज्-ण्वुल्] Illuminating, irradiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजकम्
भ्राजक + .{@-कम्@} Bile, gall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजथुः|भ्राजथु
भ्राजथुः Splendour, lustre, brilliance, beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजनम्
भ्राजनम् [भ्राज्-ल्युट्] Illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिन्
भ्राजिन् <i>a.</i> Shining, glittering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्णु|भ्राजिष्णुः
भ्राजिष्णु <i>a.</i> [भ्राज्-इष्णुच्] Shining, resplendent, bright, radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राजिष्णुः|भ्राजिष्णु
भ्राजिष्णु + .{@-ष्णुः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 Of Viṣṇu. भ्राजिष्णुर्भोजनं भोक्ता V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1215-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृ
भ्रातृ <i>m.</i> [भ्राज्-तृच् पृषो˚; cf. Uṇ. 2. 96.]<BR>—1 A brother.<BR>—2 An intimate friend or relation.<BR>—3 A near relative in general.<BR>—4 A term of friendly address (my good friend); भ्रातः कष्टमहो Bh. 3. 37, 2. 34;<BR> तत्त्वं चिन्तय तदिदं भ्रातः Moha M. 3. ━<i>Dual</i><BR> A brother and sister [cf. L. <i>frater</i>; Zend. <i>bratar</i>, Eng.<BR> <i>brother</i>.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रातृगन्धि, भ्रातृगन्धिक, भ्रातृगन्धिकः, भ्रातृगन्धिन्, भ्रातृजः, भ्रातृजाया, भ्रातृदत्तम्, भ्रातृद्वितीया, भ्रातृपुत्रः, भ्रातृवधूः, भ्रातृभगिन्यौ, भ्रातृश्वशुरः, भ्रातृहत्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृगन्धि|भ्रातृगंधि
भ्रातृ + -गन्धि, -गन्धिक <i>a.</i> having only the name of a brother, a brother in mere name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृगन्धिक|भ्रातृगंधिक|भ्रातृगन्धिकः
भ्रातृ + -गन्धि, -गन्धिक <i>a.</i> having only the name of a brother, a brother in mere name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृगन्धिकः|भ्रातृगन्धिक|भ्रातृगंधिक
भ्रातृ + -गन्धिकः, -गन्धिन् <i>m.</i> a brother in mere name; गत्वा चाह्वय<BR> सुग्रीव वालिनं भ्रातृगन्धिनम् Rām. 4. 12. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृगन्धिन्
भ्रातृ + -गन्धिकः, -गन्धिन् <i>m.</i> a brother in mere name; गत्वा चाह्वय<BR> सुग्रीव वालिनं भ्रातृगन्धिनम् Rām. 4. 12. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृजः|भ्रातृज
भ्रातृ + -जः a brotherʼs son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृजाया
भ्रातृ + -जाया (also भ्रातुर्जाया) a brotherʼs wife, a sister-in-law;<BR> अव्यापन्नामविहतगतिर्द्रक्ष्यसि भ्रातृजायाम् Me. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृदत्तम्
भ्रातृ + -दत्तम् property given by a brother to a sister at the time of<BR> her marriage; मातृकं भ्रातृदत्तं वा स्तेना स्याद्यदि तं हरेत् Ms. 9. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृद्वितीया
भ्रातृ + -द्वितीया the second day of the bright half of Kārtika (when sisters<BR> invite their brothers to their houses and entertain them, who in their<BR> turn give them presents; the day seems to have been so called on account<BR> of Yamunā having entertained her brother Yama on that day; cf. यमद्वितीया).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृपुत्रः|भ्रातृपुत्र
भ्रातृ + -पुत्रः (also भ्रातुष्पुत्रः) a brotherʼs son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृपुत्री
भ्रातृ + -पुत्रः + .({@-त्री@}) a niece.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृवधूः
भ्रातृ + -वधूः a brotherʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृभगिन्यौ
भ्रातृ + -भगिन्यौ a brother and sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृश्वशुरः|भ्रातृश्वशुर
भ्रातृ + -श्वशुरः elder brother of the husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृहत्या
भ्रातृ + -हत्या fratricide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृक|भ्रातृकः
भ्रातृक <i>a.</i> Relating to a brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृव्यः|भ्रातृव्य
भ्रातृव्यः [भ्रातुः पुत्रः व्यत्]<BR>—1 A brotherʼs son, nephew.<BR>—2 An enemy, adversary; आत्मना परास्य द्विषन् भ्रातृव्या भवति Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 7;<BR> तस्माद्भयं नो भूयिष्ठं भ्रातृव्याच्च वृकोदरात् Mb. 7. 24. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृत्वम्
भ्रातृत्वम् Brotherhood, fraternity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रातृवल
भ्रातृवल <i>a.</i> Having a brother or brothers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रीय|भ्रात्रीयः
भ्रात्रीय, भ्रात्रेय <i>a.</i> Fraternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रेय
भ्रात्रीय, भ्रात्रेय <i>a.</i> Fraternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्रीयः|भ्रात्रीय
भ्रात्रीय, भ्रात्रेय + .{@-यः@} A brotherʼs son, nephew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रात्र्यम्
भ्रात्र्यम् Fraternity, brotherhood; यातितः स मया पूर्वं भ्रात्र्यं<BR> ज्ञापयितुं तव Mb. 12. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रादिनी
भ्रादिनी A particular Śruti (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्त|भ्रांत|भ्रान्तः
भ्रान्त <i>p. p.</i> [भ्रम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Wandered or roamed about.<BR>—2 Turned round, whirled, revolved.<BR>—3 Erred, mistaken, gone astray.<BR>—4 Perplexed, confused.<BR>—5 Moving about, moving to and fro, wheeling.<BR>—6 Whirling or turning round, roaming or wandering about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तः|भ्रान्त|भ्रांत
भ्रान्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 An elephant in rut.<BR>—2 A kind of thorn-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तम्
भ्रान्त + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Roaming, moving about; वरं पर्वतदुर्गेषु भ्रान्तं वनचरैः सह Bh. 2. 14.<BR>—2 A mistake, an error.<BR>—3 A particular mode of fighting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रान्तबुद्धि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तबुद्धि
भ्रान्त + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> confused or perplexed in mind, puzzled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिः|भ्रान्ति|भ्रांति|भ्रांतिः
भ्रान्तिः [भ्रम्-क्तिन्] <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Moving or wandering about.<BR>—2 Turning round, rolling.<BR>—3 A revolution, circular or rotatory movement; चक्रभ्रान्तिररान्तरेषु<BR> वितनोत्यन्यामिवारावलीम् V. 1. 5.<BR>—4 An error, a mistake, delusion, wrong<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">Page1216-2</a>]<BR> notion, false idea or impression; श्रितासि चन्दनभ्रान्त्या दुर्विपाकं<BR> विषद्रुमम् U. 1. 47; षाण्मासिके तु संप्राप्ते भ्रान्तिः संजायते नृणाम् ।<BR> धात्राक्षराणि सृष्टानि पत्रारूढान्यतः पुरा ॥ Jyotistattvam.<BR>—5 Confusion, perplexity.<BR>—6 Doubt, uncertainty, suspense.<BR>—7 Unsteadiness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: भ्रान्तिकर, भ्रान्तिनाशनः, भ्रान्तिहर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिकर
भ्रान्तिः + -कर <i>a.</i> confounding, causing delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिनाशनः|भ्रान्तिनाशन|भ्रांतिनाशन
भ्रान्तिः + -नाशनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिहर|भ्रांतिहर|भ्रान्तिहरः
भ्रान्तिः + -हर <i>a.</i> removing doubt or error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिहरः|भ्रान्तिहर|भ्रांतिहर
भ्रान्तिः + -हर + ({@-रः@}) a counsellor, minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रान्तिमत्|भ्रांतिमत्|भ्रान्तिमन्त्
भ्रान्तिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Revolving, turning round; भ्रान्तिमद्वारियन्त्रम् M. 2. 18.<BR>—2 Erring, mistaking, being under a delusion. ━<i>m.</i> A figure of speech<BR> in which one thing is represented as being mistaken for another on account<BR> of the close resemblance between the two; भान्तिमानन्यसंवित्तत्तुल्यदर्शने<BR> K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i> कपाले मार्जारः पय इति करान् लेढि शशिनः &c.;<BR> see V. 3. 2; Māl. 1. 2 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामः|भ्राम
भ्रामः [भ्रम्-अण्]<BR>—1 Roaming about.<BR>—2 Delusion, error, mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामक|भ्रामकः
भ्रामक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>). [भ्रामयति-भ्र णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Causing to move or whirl.<BR>—2 Perplexing, deluding, misleading.<BR>—3 Deceptive, false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामकः|भ्रामक
भ्रामक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A sun-flower.<BR>—2 A kind of loadstone.<BR>—3 A deceiver, rogue, cheat.<BR>—4 A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामणम्
भ्रामणम् [भ्रम्-णिच् ल्युट्] Swinging or turning round, causing to revolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामर|भ्रामरं|भ्रामरः
भ्रामर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>) [भ्रमरेण संभृतं भ्रमरस्येदं<BR> वा अण्] Relating to a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरः|भ्रामर|भ्रामरं
भ्रामर + .{@-रः, -रम्@} A kind of loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरम्
भ्रामर + .{@-रः, -रम्@} A kind of loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरम्
भ्रामर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Whirling round.<BR>—2 Giddiness.<BR>—3 Epilepsy.<BR>—4 Honey; निर्मलं स्फटिकाभं यत् तन्मधु भ्रामरं स्मृतम् Bhāva P.<BR>—5 A kind of coitus or mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR>—6 A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरी
भ्रामर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>—2 Going round, walking round from left to right; (= प्रदक्षिणा q. v.);<BR> as in दीयतां भ्रामर्यः Karpūr. 4; Vb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामरिन्
भ्रामरिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Revolving.<BR>—2 Having epilepsy, epileptic; भ्रामरी गण्डमाली च Ms. 3. 161.<BR>—3 Made of honey.<BR>—4 Giddy, dizzy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रामिन्
भ्रामिन् <i>a.</i> Confused, perplexed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राश्
भ्रा(भ्ला)श् €1. €4 Ā. (भ्राशते, भ्राश्यते, भ्लाशते, भ्लाश्यते) To<BR> shine, glitter, blaze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लाश्
भ्रा(भ्ला)श् €1. €4 Ā. (भ्राशते, भ्राश्यते, भ्लाशते, भ्लाश्यते) To<BR> shine, glitter, blaze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रः|भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं
भ्राष्ट्रः, -ष्ट्रम्<BR> A frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रम्
भ्राष्ट्रः, -ष्ट्रम्<BR> A frying-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रः|भ्राष्ट्र|भ्राष्ट्रं
भ्राष्ट्रः, -ष्ट्रम् + .{@-ष्ट्रः@}<BR>—1 Light.<BR>—2 Ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रकम्
भ्राष्ट्रकम्, -कः<BR> A frying-pan; उत्पतितोऽपि हि चणकः शक्तः किं भ्राष्ट्रकं<BR> भङ्क्तुम् Pt. 1. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रकः|भ्राष्ट्रक|भ्राष्ट्रकं
भ्राष्ट्रकम्, -कः<BR> A frying-pan; उत्पतितोऽपि हि चणकः शक्तः किं भ्राष्ट्रकं<BR> भङ्क्तुम् Pt. 1. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्राष्ट्रमिन्ध
भ्राष्ट्रमिन्ध <i>a.</i> One who fries or roasts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रास्
भ्रा(भ्ला)स् See भ्रा(भ्ला)श्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्लास्
भ्रा(भ्ला)स् See भ्रा(भ्ला)श्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रुकुंशः|भ्रुकुंश
भ्रु(भ्रू)कुंशः (सः) A male actor in female attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1216-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भ्रूकुंशः|भ्रूकुंश
