मङ्गलम्
मङ्गल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Auspiciousness, propitiousness; जनकानां रघूणां च यत् कृत्स्नं<BR> गोत्रमङ्गलम् U. 6. 42; R. 6. 9, 10. 67.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Happiness, good luck or fortune, bliss, felicity; भद्रं भद्रं<BR> वितर भगवन् भूयसे मङ्गलाय Māl. 1. 3; U. 3. 48.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Wellbeing, welfare, good; सङ्गः सतां किमु न मङ्गलमातनोति<BR> Bv. 1. 122; (also <i>m.</i> in these senses).<BR>—2 A good omen, anything tending to an auspicious issue.<BR>—3 A blessing, benediction.<BR>—4 An auspicious or lucky object.<BR>—5 An auspicious occasion or event, a festivity.<BR>—6 Any solemn or auspicious ceremony or rite (such as marriage).<BR>—7 Any ancient custom.<BR>—8 Turmeric.<BR>—9 (In music) A particular composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1219-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

