मत्कुणी
मत्कुणः + .{@-णी@} Pudendum (of a young girl, अजातलोमा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मत्कुणारिः, मत्कुणगन्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुणारिः|मत्कुणारि
मत्कुणः + -अरिः hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कुणगन्ध
मत्कुणः + -गन्ध <i>a.</i> having the smell of a bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्कोटकः|मत्कोटक
मत्कोटकः A termite (Mar. वाळवी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्त|मत्तः
मत्त <i>p. p.</i> [मद्-क्त]<BR>—1 Intoxicated, drunk, inebriated (fig. also); Ms. 11. 96; मत्तं प्रमत्तमुन्मत्तं<BR> … … न रिपुं हन्ति धर्मवित् Bhāg. 1. 7. 36; ज्योत्स्नापानमदालसेन<BR> वपुषा मत्ताश्चकोराङ्गनाः Vb. 1. 11; प्रभामत्तश्चन्द्रो जगदिदमहो<BR> विभ्रमयति K. P. 10; so ऐश्वर्य˚, धन˚, बल˚ &c.<BR>—2 Mad, insane.<BR>—3 In rut, furious (as an elephant); जयश्रीरन्तरा वेदिर्मत्तवारणयोरिव R. 12. 93.<BR>—4 Proud, arrogant.<BR>—5 Delighted, overjoyed, excited with joy.<BR>—6 Amorous, sportive, wanton.<BR>—7 Excited by sexual desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तः|मत्त
मत्त + .{@-त्तः@}<BR>—1 A drunkard.<BR>—2 A mad man.<BR>—3 An elephant in rut.<BR>—4 A cuckoo.<BR>—5 A buffalo.<BR>—6 The thorn-apple or Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्ता
मत्त + .{@-त्ता@} Spirituous or vinous liquor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मत्ताक्रीडा, मत्ताम्लबः, मत्तेभः, मत्तकाशिनी, मत्तकासिनी, मत्तकीशः, मत्तगमिनी, मत्तदन्तिन्, मत्तपालकः, मत्तमयूरः, मत्तवारणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्ताक्रीडा
मत्त + -आक्रीडा N. of a metre; मत्ताक्रीडा म्नौ त्नौ नौ नल्गिति भवति<BR> वसुशरदशयनियुता V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्ताम्लबः
मत्त + -आम्लबः a fence round a large building (as of a rich man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तेभः|मत्तेभ
मत्त + -इभः an elephant in rut. ˚गमना a woman having the gait<BR> of an elephant in rut, <i>e. g.</i> with a lounging gait. ˚विक्रीडितम्<BR> N. of a metre; सभरा न्मौ यलगास्त्रयोदशयतिर्मत्तेभविक्रीडितम् V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकाशिनी
मत्त + -काशिनी, -कासिनी a handsome and very fascinating<BR> woman; दर्शितोऽसौ चित्रपटस्तस्यै मत्तकाशिन्यै Dk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकासिनी
मत्त + -काशिनी, -कासिनी a handsome and very fascinating<BR> woman; दर्शितोऽसौ चित्रपटस्तस्यै मत्तकाशिन्यै Dk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तकीशः|मत्तकीश
मत्त + -कीशः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तगमिनी
मत्त + -गमिनी =<BR>—1 मत्तेभगमना above.<BR>—2 a bewitching or wanton woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तदन्तिन्|मत्तदंतिन्
मत्त + -दन्तिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-नागः@}<BR> an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तपालकः
मत्त + -पालकः a drunken wretch; दास्याः पुत्र मत्तपालक कुतोऽत्र<BR> नवमालिका Nāg. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तमयूरः|मत्तमयूर
मत्त + -मयूरः a wild or amorous peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तमयूरम्
मत्त + -मयूरः + .({@-रम्@}) a kind of metre; वेदैरन्ध्रैर्मत्तौ यसगा मत्तमयूरम् V. Ratn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तवारणः|मत्तवारण|मत्तवारणं
मत्त + -वारणः an elephant in rut; R. 12. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तवारणः|मत्तवारण|मत्तवारणं
मत्त + -वारणः + ({@-णः, -णम्@})<BR>—1 a fence round a large building or mansion.<BR>—2 a turret or small room on the top of a large building.<BR>—3 a veranda.<BR>—4 a pavilion.<BR>—5 a peg or bracket.<BR>—6 a bed-stead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तवारणम्
मत्त + -वारणः + ({@-णः, -णम्@})<BR>—1 a fence round a large building or mansion.<BR>—2 a turret or small room on the top of a large building.<BR>—3 a veranda.<BR>—4 a pavilion.<BR>—5 a peg or bracket.<BR>—6 a bed-stead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तवारणम्
मत्त + -वारणः + ({@-णम्@}) pounded betel-nuts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्तक
मत्तक <i>a.</i> Somewhat drunk, intoxicated, or proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्यम्
मत्यम् [मते समीकरणे साधु यत् Tv.]<BR>—1 A harrow.<BR>—2 The means of acquiring knowledge.<BR>—3 The exercise of knowledge.<BR>—4 Harrowing, making even or level (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सः|मत्स
मत्सः<BR>—1 A fish.<BR>—2 A lord of the Matsyas.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मत्सगण्टः, मत्सगण्ठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सगण्टः|मत्सगण्ट
मत्सः + -गण्टः, -गण्ठः a kind of fish-curry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सगण्ठः|मत्सगण्ठ
मत्सः + -गण्टः, -गण्ठः a kind of fish-curry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सर|मत्सरः
मत्सर <i>a.</i> [मद्-सरन्; Uṇ. 3. 73]<BR>—1 Jealous, envious.<BR>—2 Insatiate, greedy, covetous.<BR>—3 Niggardly.<BR>—4 Wicked.<BR>—5 Selfish, self-interested.<BR>—6 Ved. Satisfying.<BR>—7 Intoxicating (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरः|मत्सर
मत्सर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Envy, jealousy; अदत्तावकाशो मत्सरस्य K. 45; परवृद्धिषु बद्धमत्सराणाम्<BR> Ki. 13. 7; Śi. 9. 63; Ku. 5. 17; निन्दन्ति मां सदा लोका धिगस्तु मम<BR> जीवनम् । इत्यात्मनि भवेद्यस्तु धिक्कारः स च मत्सरः Kriyāyogasāra.<BR>—2 Hostility, enmity; स चापमुत्सृज्य विवृद्धमत्सरः R. 3. 60.<BR>—3 Pride; इति धौतपुरंध्रिमत्सरान् सरसि मज्जनेन Śi. 8. 71.<BR>—4 Covetousness, greediness.<BR>—5 Anger, passion.<BR>—6 The Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरः|मत्सर
मत्सर + .{@-रः, -रा@} A gnat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरा
मत्सर + .{@-रः, -रा@} A gnat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरी
मत्सर + .{@-री@} (In music) a particular मूर्च्छना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सरिन्
मत्सरिन् <i>a.</i> [मत्सर-इनि]<BR>—1 Envious, jealous; परवृद्धिमत्सरि मनो हि मानिनाम् Śi. 15. 1, 2. 115;<BR> दुष्टात्मा परगुणमत्सरी मनुष्यः Mk. 9. 37; R. 18. 19.<BR>—2 Hostile, inimical.<BR>—3 Greedy of, selfishly addicted to (with loc.).<BR>—4 Wicked.<BR>—5 Ved. Intoxicating.<BR>—6 Satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्सिन्
मत्सिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Containing fish.<BR>—2 Marked by water (as a boundary).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यः|मत्स्य
मत्स्यः [मद्-स्यन्; Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>—1 A fish; शूले मत्स्यानिवापक्ष्यन् दुर्बलान् बलवत्तराः Ms. 7. 20.<BR>—2 A particular variety of fish.<BR>—3 A king of the Matsyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यौ
मत्स्यः + .{@-त्स्यौ@} (dual) The sign <i>Pisces</i> of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्त्स्याः
मत्स्यः + .{@-त्स्याः@} (pl.) N. of a country and its inhabitants, the country<BR> of Virāṭa q. v.; Ms. 2. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मत्स्याक्षका, मत्स्याक्षी, मत्स्याद्, मत्स्यादन, मत्स्याद, मत्स्यावतारः, मत्स्याशनः, मत्स्याशिक, मत्स्यासुरः, मत्स्याधानी, मत्स्यधानी, मत्स्योदरिन्, मत्स्योदरी, मत्स्योदरीयः, मत्स्योद्वर्तनम्, मत्स्योपजीविन्, मत्स्यकरण्डिका, मत्स्यकीशः, मत्स्यगन्ध, मत्स्यघण्टः, मत्स्यघातः, मत्स्यघातिन्, मत्स्यजीवत्, मत्स्यजीविन्, मत्स्यजालम्, मत्स्यदेशः, मत्स्यद्वादशी, मत्स्यनारी, मत्स्यनाशकः, मत्स्यनाशनः, मत्स्यपुराणम्, मत्स्यपित्ता, मत्स्यबन्धः, मत्स्यबन्धिन्, मत्स्यबन्धनम्, मत्स्यबन्धनी, मत्स्यबन्धिनी, मत्स्यमांसम्, मत्स्यरङ्कः, मत्स्यरङ्गः, मत्स्यरङ्गकः, मत्स्यराजः, मत्स्यवेधनम्, मत्स्यवेधनी, मत्स्यवेधनी, मत्स्यव्रतिन्, मत्स्यसंघातः, मत्स्यसन्तानिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1225-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

