मत्स्यः + -सन्तानिकः fish cooked with sauce; दग्धोङ्गारे सलवणो वेशवारैरुपस्कृतः ।<BR> सार्द्रकः कटुतैलेन मत्स्यसन्तानिको भवेत् Śabdachandrikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यण्डिका|मत्स्यंडिका
मत्स्यण्डिका, मत्स्यण्डी Coarse or unrefined sugar; हीही<BR> इयं सीधुपानोद्वेजितस्य मत्स्यण्डिकोपनता M. 3; इक्षो रसो यः संपक्वो<BR> घनः किंचिद् द्रवान्वितः । मदवत् स्यन्दते यस्मान्मत्स्यण्डीति निगद्यते Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यण्डी|मत्स्यंडी
मत्स्यण्डिका, मत्स्यण्डी Coarse or unrefined sugar; हीही<BR> इयं सीधुपानोद्वेजितस्य मत्स्यण्डिकोपनता M. 3; इक्षो रसो यः संपक्वो<BR> घनः किंचिद् द्रवान्वितः । मदवत् स्यन्दते यस्मान्मत्स्यण्डीति निगद्यते Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्यलम्
मत्स्यलम् A kind of fish-curry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्
मथ् See मन्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ
मथ = माथ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन्
मथन् (मथ्ना instr. form) A piece of wood for producing fire by attrition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथन|मथनं|मथनः
मथन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>) [मथ् ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Churning, stirring up.<BR>—2 Hurting, injuring.<BR>—3 Killing, destroying, a destroyer; मुग्धे मधुमथनमनुगतमनुसर<BR> राधिके Gīt. 2.<BR>—4 Rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथनः|मथन|मथनं
मथन + .{@-नः@} N. of a tree (गणिकारिका, used in producing fire by attrition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथनम्
मथन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Churning, stirring round, agitating.<BR>—2 Rubbing, friction.<BR>—3 Injury, hurting, destruction.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मथनाचलः, मथनपर्वतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथनाचलः|मथनाचल
मथन + -अचलः, -पर्वतः the mountain Mandara used as a churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथनपर्वतः
मथन + -अचलः, -पर्वतः the mountain Mandara used as a churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथिः|मथि
मथिः [मथ् इ] A churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथित|मथितं
मथित <i>p. p.</i> [मथ्-क्त]<BR>—1 Churned, stirred round, agitated, shaken about.<BR>—2 Crushed, ground, pinched.<BR>—3 Afflicted, distressed, oppressed.<BR>—4 Killed, destroyed.<BR>—5 Dislocated; (see मन्थ्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथितम्
मथित + .{@-तम्@} Pure butter-milk (without water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथिन्
मथिन् <i>m.</i> [मथ्-इनि] (Nom. sing. मन्थाः, acc. pl. मथः)<BR>—1 A churning-stick; मुहुः प्रणुन्नेषु मथां विवर्तनैर्नदत्सु कुम्भेषु<BR> मृदङ्गमन्थरम् Ki. 4. 16; N. 11. 62, 22. 44.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR>—3 A thunderbolt.<BR>—4 The penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथ्य
मथ्य <i>a.</i> To be extracted or produced from; अमृतममरवर्या<BR> नाशयत्सिन्धुमथ्यम् Bhāg. 8. 12. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरा
मथु(थू)रा [मथ्-उ(ऊ)रच्] N. of an ancient town situated on the<BR> right bank of the Yamunā, the birth-place of Kṛṣṇa and the scene<BR> of his amours and exploits; it is one of the seven sacred cities in India<BR> (see अवन्ति), and is, to this day, the favourite resort of thousands<BR> of devotees. It is said to have been founded by Śatrughna; निर्ममे<BR> निर्ममोऽर्थेषु मथुरां मधुराकृतिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">Page1226-2</a>]<BR> R. 15. 28; कलिन्दकन्या मथुरां गताऽपि गङ्गोर्मिसंसक्तजलेव भाति 6. 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मथुरेशः, मथुरानाथः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथूरा
मथु(थू)रा [मथ्-उ(ऊ)रच्] N. of an ancient town situated on the<BR> right bank of the Yamunā, the birth-place of Kṛṣṇa and the scene<BR> of his amours and exploits; it is one of the seven sacred cities in India<BR> (see अवन्ति), and is, to this day, the favourite resort of thousands<BR> of devotees. It is said to have been founded by Śatrughna; निर्ममे<BR> निर्ममोऽर्थेषु मथुरां मधुराकृतिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">Page1226-2</a>]<BR> R. 15. 28; कलिन्दकन्या मथुरां गताऽपि गङ्गोर्मिसंसक्तजलेव भाति 6. 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मथुरेशः, मथुरानाथः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरेशः|मथुरेश
मथुरा + -ईशः, -नाथः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मथुरानाथः|मथुरानाथ
मथुरा + -ईशः, -नाथः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
मद् A form of the first personal pronoun in the singular number used<BR> chiefly at the beginning of comps.; as मदर्थे ‘for me’, ‘for my sake’;<BR> मच्चित्त ‘thinking of me’; मद्वचनम्, मत्संदेशः, मत्प्रियम्<BR> &c. &c.; मन्मना भव मद्भक्तो मद्याजी मां नमस्कुरु Bg. 18. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मद्
मद् I. €4 P. (माद्यति, मत्त)<BR>—1 To be drunk or intoxicated; वीक्ष्य मद्यमितरा तु ममाद Śi. 10. 27.<BR>—2 To be mad.<BR>—3 To revel or delight in.<BR>—4 To be glad or rejoiced.<BR>—5 Ved. To satisfy, delight, gladden.<BR>—6 To enjoy supreme felicity. ━<i>Caus.</i> (मादयति)<BR>—1 To intoxicate; inebriate, madden.<BR>—2 (मदयति) To exhilarate, gladden, delight; मायूरी मदयति मार्जना<BR> मनांसि M. 1. 21; प्रकृतिमधुराः सन्त्येवान्ये मनो मदयन्ति ये Māl. 1. 36;<BR> Śi. 13. 38; Ki. 5. 26.<BR>—3 To inflame with passion; मदयति हृदयम् Māl. 3. 6.<BR>—4 (Ātm.) To be glad, rejoice, be pleased. ━II. €10 Ā. (मादयते)<BR> To please, gratify. ━III. €1 P. (मदति)<BR>—1 To be proud.<BR>—2 To be poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदः|मद
मदः [मद्-अच्]<BR>—1 Intoxication, drunkenness, inebriety; मदेनास्पृश्ये Dk.; मदविकाराणां<BR> दर्शकः K. 45; see comps. below.<BR>—2 Madness, insanity.<BR>—3 Ardent passion, wanton or lustful passion, lasciviousness, lust; इति<BR> मदमदनाभ्यां रागिणः स्पष्टरागान् Śi. 10. 91.<BR>—4 Rut, ichor, or the juice that exudes from the temples of an elephant<BR> in rut; मदेन भाति कलभः प्रतापेन महीपतिः Candr. 5. 45; so<BR> मदकलः, मदोन्मत्त; Me. 20; R. 2. 7, 12. 102.<BR>—5 Love, desire, ardour.<BR>—6 Pride, arrogance, conceit; तं मोहाच्छ्रयते मदः स च मदाद्दास्येन<BR> निर्विद्यते Pt. 1. 240.<BR>—7 Rapture, excessive delight.<BR>—8 Spirituous liquor; पाययित्वा मदं सम्यक् Śukra. 4. 1171.<BR>—9 Honey.<BR>—10 Musk.<BR>—11 Semen virile.<BR>—12 Soma.<BR>—13 Any beautiful object.<BR>—14 A river (नद.)<BR>—15 Beauty; नीलारविन्दमदभङ्गिमदैः कटाक्षैः Bv. 3. 4.<BR>—16 N. of the 7th astrological mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदी
मदः + .{@-दी@}<BR>—1 A drinking-cup.<BR>—2 Any agricultural implement (such as a plough &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मदात्ययः, मदातङ्कः, मदान्ध, मदापनयम्, मदाम्बरः, मदालस, मदालसा, मदावस्था, मदाकुल, मदाढ्य, मदाम्नातः, मदालापिन्, मदाह्वः, मदोत्कट, मदोत्सवः, मदोद्भवः, मदोदग्र, मदोन्मत्त, मदोदग्रा, मदोद्धत, मदोल्लापिन्, मदोर्जित, मदकटः, मदकर, मदकरिन्, मदकल, मदकोहलः, मदखेल, मदगन्धा, मदगमनः, मदच्युत्, मदजलम्, मदवारि, मदज्वरः, मदद्रुः, मदद्विपः, मदप्रयोगः, मदप्रसेकः, मदप्रस्रवणम्, मदस्रावः, मदस्रुतिः, मदप्रसेकः, मदभङ्गः, मदभञ्जिनी, मदमत्ता, मदमुच्, मदमोहित, मदरक्त, मदरागः, मदलेखा, मदविक्षिप्त, मदविह्वल, मदवीर्यम्, मदवृन्दः, मदशौण्डः, मदशौण्डकम्, मदसारः, मदस्थलम्, मदस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदात्ययः|मदात्यय
मदः + -अत्ययः, -आतङ्कः any distemper (such as headache) resulting<BR> from drunkenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदातङ्कः|मदातङ्क|मदातंक
मदः + -अत्ययः, -आतङ्कः any distemper (such as headache) resulting<BR> from drunkenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदान्ध|मदांध
मदः + -अन्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 blinded by intoxication, dead drunk, drunk with passion; अधरमिव<BR> मदान्धा पातुमेषा प्रवृत्ता V. 4. 13; यदा किंचिज्ज्ञोऽहं द्विप इव मदान्धः<BR> समभवम् Bh. 2. 7.<BR>—2 blinded by passion or pride, arrogant, infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदापनयम्
मदः + -अपनयम् removal of intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्बरः|मदाम्बर|मदांबर
मदः + -अम्बरः<BR>—1 an elephant in rut.<BR>—2 N. of Airāvata, the elephant of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालस
मदः + -अलस <i>a.</i> languid with passion or intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालसा
मदः + -अलसा N. of the daughter of Viśvaketu, the lord of Gandharvas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदावस्था
मदः + -अवस्था<BR>—1 a state of drunkenness.<BR>—2 wantonness, lustfulness.<BR>—3 rut, being in rut; अन्तर्मदावस्थ इव द्विपेन्द्रः R. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाकुल
मदः + -आकुल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 furious with rut.<BR>—2 full of lust, overpowered by passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाढ्य|मदाढ्यः
मदः + -आढ्य <i>a.</i> drunk, intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाढ्यः|मदाढ्य
मदः + -आढ्य + ({@-ढ्यः@}) the palm tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाम्नातः|मदाम्नात
मदः + -आम्नातः a kettle-drum carried on the back of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदालापिन्
मदः + -आलापिन् <i>m.</i> a cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदाह्वः|मदाह्व
मदः + -आह्वः musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोत्कट|मदोत्कटः
मदः + -उत्कट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 intoxicated, excited by drink.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">Page1227-1</a>]<BR>—2 furious with passion, lustful.<BR>—3 arrogant, proud, haughty.<BR>—4 ruttish, under the influence of rut; मदोत्कटे रेचितपुष्पवृक्षा गन्धद्विपे<BR> वन्य इव द्विरेफाः R. 6. 7; हस्तिनं कमलनालतन्तुना बद्धुमिच्छति<BR> वने मदोत्कटम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोत्कटः|मदोत्कट
मदः + -उत्कट + ({@-टः@})<BR>—1 an elephant in rut.<BR>—2 a dove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोत्कटा
मदः + -उत्कट + .({@-टा@}) spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1226-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोत्सवः
मदः + -उत्सवः, -उद्भवः mango<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोद्भवः
मदः + -उत्सवः, -उद्भवः mango<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोदग्र
मदः + -उदग्र, -उन्मत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 drunk, intoxicated.<BR>—2 furious, drunk with passion: मदोदग्राः ककुद्मन्तः सरितां कूलमुद्रुजाः R. 4. 22.<BR>—3 arrogant, proud, haughty; मदोन्मत्तस्य भूपस्य कुञ्जरस्य च गच्छतः<BR> उन्मार्गं वाच्यतां यान्ति महामात्राः समीपगाः Pt. 1. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोन्मत्त
मदः + -उदग्र, -उन्मत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 drunk, intoxicated.<BR>—2 furious, drunk with passion: मदोदग्राः ककुद्मन्तः सरितां कूलमुद्रुजाः R. 4. 22.<BR>—3 arrogant, proud, haughty; मदोन्मत्तस्य भूपस्य कुञ्जरस्य च गच्छतः<BR> उन्मार्गं वाच्यतां यान्ति महामात्राः समीपगाः Pt. 1. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोदग्रा
मदः + -उदग्रा <i>f.</i> A woman; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोद्धत|मदोद्धतः
मदः + -उद्धत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 drunk with passion; मदोद्धताः प्रत्यनिलं विचेरुः Ku. 3 31; सत्पक्षा मधुरगिरः प्रसाधिताशा मदोद्धतारम्भाः Ve. 1. 6.<BR>—2 inflated with pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोल्लापिन्
मदः + -उल्लापिन् <i>m.</i> the cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदोर्जित
मदः + -ऊर्जित <i>a.</i> swollen with pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकटः|मदकट
मदः + -कटः a eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकर
मदः + -कर <i>a.</i> intoxicating, causing intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकरिन्
मदः + -करिन् <i>m.</i> an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकल|मदकलः
मदः + -कल <i>a.</i> speaking softly or inarticulately, speaking indistinctly;<BR> मदकलोदकलोलविहंगमाः R. 9. 37; मदकलमदिराक्षीनीविमोक्षो<BR> हि मोक्षः Udb.<BR>—2 uttering low sounds of love.<BR>—3 drunk with passion; एतस्मिन् मदकलमल्लिकाक्षपक्ष … U. 1. 31; Māl. 9. 14.<BR>—4 indistinct yet sweet; मदकलं कूजितं सारसानाम् Me. 31.<BR>—5 ruttish, furious, under the influence of rut; V. 4. 46.<BR>—6 furious, mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकलः|मदकल
मदः + -कल + .({@-लः@}) an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदकोहलः|मदकोहल
मदः + -कोहलः a bull set at liberty (to roam at will).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदखेल
मदः + -खेल <i>a.</i> stately or sportive through passion; मदखेलपदं<BR> कथं नु तस्याः V. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदगन्धा|मदगंधा
मदः + -गन्धा<BR>—1 an intoxicating drink.<BR>—2 hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदगमनः|मदगमन
मदः + -गमनः a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदच्युत्
मदः + -च्युत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 distilling rut (as an elephant).<BR>—2 lustful, wanton, drunk.<BR>—3 gladdening, exhilarating. ━(<i>m.</i>) an epithet of Indra. ━(<i>m.</i> dual)<BR> an epithet of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदजलम्
मदः + -जलम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> rutting juice, ichor exuding from the temples<BR> of a ruttish elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदवारि
मदः + -जलम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> rutting juice, ichor exuding from the temples<BR> of a ruttish elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदज्वरः|मदज्वर
मदः + -ज्वरः fever of pride or passion; कतिपयपुरस्वाम्ये पुंसां<BR> क एष मदज्वरः Bh. 3. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदद्रुः
मदः + -द्रुः a cocoa-nut tree (Mar. माड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मदद्विपः|मदद्विप
मदः + -द्विपः a furious elephant, an elephant in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1227-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

