मद्गुः|मद्गु
मद्गुः [मस्ज्-उ न्यङ्क्वा˚; cf. Uṇ. 1. 7]<BR>—1 A kind of aquatic bird, a cormorant or diver; मांसं गृध्रो वपां<BR> मद्गुः (भवति) Ms. 12. 63.<BR>—2 A kind of snake.<BR>—3 A kind of wild animal.<BR>—4 A kind of galley or vessel of war; कोऽपि मद्गुरभ्यधावत् Dk.<BR>—5 N. of a degraded mixed tribe, the offspring of a Brāhmaṇa by a woman<BR> of the bard class; see Ms. 10. 48.<BR>—6 An outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1228-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

