मधुहन्
मधु + -हन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a destroyer or collector of honey; सर्वथा संहतैरेव दुर्बलैर्बलवानपि ।<BR> अमित्रः शक्यते हन्तुं मधुहा भ्रमरैरिव ॥ Mb. 3. 33. 70; Bhāg. 11. 7. 34.<BR>—2 a kind of bird of prey.<BR>—3 a sooth-sayer.<BR>—4 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुक|मधुकं|मधुकः
मधुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sweet.<BR>—2 Sweet-speaking, melodious.<BR>—3 Of the colour of honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकः|मधुक|मधुकं
मधुक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of a tree (= मधूक q. v.).<BR>—2 The Aśoka tree.<BR>—3 A kind of bird.<BR>—4 The liquorice root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकम्
मधुक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Tin.<BR>—2 Liquorice.<BR>—3 The palm-liquor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मधुकाश्रयम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुकाश्रयम्
मधुक + -आश्रयम् wax; Nigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुतम
मधुतम <i>a.</i> Very intoxicating, sweetest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमत्|मधुमन्त्
मधुमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sweet.<BR>—2 Pleasant, agreeable.<BR>—3 Mixed with honey, honied.<BR>—4 Rich in honey (as a flower); मघुमत् पार्थिवं रजः Rv. 1. 90. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुमती
मधुमती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 N. of a river.<BR>—2 N. of a creeper, Clematis triloba (Mar. मोरवेल).<BR>—3 A mental stage in Yogaśāstra.<BR>—4 the 3 Ṛks (मधु वाता ऋतायते &c.); Bṛ. Up. 6. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुर|मधुरं|मधुरः
मधुर <i>a.</i> [मधु-माधुर्यं राति रा-क, मधु-अस्त्यर्थे र वा]<BR>—1 Sweet; यथा प्रकृत्या मधुरं गवां पयः H.<BR>—2 Honied, mellifluous.<BR>—3 Pleasant, charming, attractive, agreeable; अहो मधुरमासां दर्शनम्<BR> Ś. 1; Ku. 5. 9; Māl. 2. 11; किमिव हि मधुराणां मण्डनं नाकृतीनाम्<BR> Ś. 1. 20; मधुरया मधुबोधितमाधवी … Śi. 6. 20.<BR>—4 Melodious (as a sound); पुंस्कोकिलोऽयं मधुरं चुकूज Ku. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरः|मधुर|मधुरं
मधुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The red sugar-cane.<BR>—2 Rice.<BR>—3 A kind of sugar, molasses (गुड).<BR>—4 A kind of mango.<BR>—5 Cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरा
मधुर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 Liquorice.<BR>—2 Sour rice-water.<BR>—3 N. of the city Mathurā.<BR>—4 N. of plants like काकोली, शतावण,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">Page1230-2</a>]<BR> बृहज्जीवन्ती.<BR>—5 Sweet fennel (Mar. बडीशेप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरी
मधुर + .{@-री@} A kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरम्
मधुर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Sweetness.<BR>—2 A sweet drink, syrup.<BR>—3 Poison.<BR>—4 Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरम्
मधुर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Sweetly, pleasantly, agreeably. (मधुरेण <i>ind.</i><BR> in a kindly or friendly manner; नहि दुर्योधनो राज्यं मधुरेण प्रदास्यति Mb. 5. 4. 1.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मधुराक्षर, मधुराङ्गकः, मधुराम्लः, मधुराम्लकः, मधुराष्टकम्, मधुरालाप, मधुरोपन्यासः, मधुरकण्टकः, मधुरजम्बीरम्, मधुरत्रयम्, मधुरफलः, मधुरभाषिन्, मधुरवाच्, मधुरमिशिः, मधुरलता, मधुरविपाक, मधुरस्रवा, मधुरस्वनः, मधुरस्वर, मधुरस्वन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराक्षर
मधुर + -अक्षर <i>a.</i> sounding sweetly, uttering sweet sounds, melodious;<BR> कूजन्तं रामरामेति मधुरं मधुराक्षरम् Rām. Stotra 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराङ्गकः|मधुराङ्गक
मधुर + -अङ्गकः astringent taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराम्लः|मधुराम्ल
मधुर + -अम्लः<BR>—1 the orange.<BR>—2 the pomegranate.<BR>—3 some sour plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराम्लकः|मधुराम्लक
मधुर + -अम्लकः the hog-plum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुराष्टकम्
मधुर + -अष्टकम् N. of a collection of 8 verses by Vallabhācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरालाप|मधुरालापः
मधुर + -आलाप <i>a.</i> uttering sweet sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरालापः|मधुरालाप
मधुर + -आलाप + ({@-पः@}) sweet or melodious<BR> notes; मधुरालापनिसर्गपण्डिताम् Ku. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरालापा
मधुर + -आलाप + ({@-पा@}) a kind of thrush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरोपन्यासः|मधुरोपन्यास
मधुर + -उपन्यासः kind address or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरकण्टकः|मधुरकण्टक|मधुरकंटक
मधुर + -कण्टकः a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरजम्बीरम्
मधुर + -जम्बीरम् a species of lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरत्रयम्
मधुर + -त्रयम् = मधुत्रयम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरफलः|मधुरफल
मधुर + -फलः a sort of jujube tree (राजबदर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरभाषिन्
मधुर + -भाषिन्, -वाच् <i>a.</i> sweet-speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरवाच्
मधुर + -भाषिन्, -वाच् <i>a.</i> sweet-speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरमिशिः
मधुर + -मिशिः <i>f.</i> sweet fennel (Mar. बडीशेप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरलता
मधुर + -लता a kind of liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरविपाक
मधुर + -विपाक <i>a.</i> sweet after digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरस्रवा
मधुर + -स्रवा a kind of date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरस्वनः|मधुरस्वन
मधुर + -स्वनः a conch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरस्वर
मधुर + -स्वर, -स्वन <i>a.</i> warbling sweetly, sweet-voiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरस्वन|मधुरस्वनः
मधुर + -स्वर, -स्वन <i>a.</i> warbling sweetly, sweet-voiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरक|मधुरकः
मधुरक <i>a.</i> Sweet, pleasant, agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिका
मधुरिका sweet fennel (Mar. बडीशेप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरता
मधुरता, -त्वम्<BR> Sweetness, pleasantness, agreeableness, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरत्वम्
मधुरता, -त्वम्<BR> Sweetness, pleasantness, agreeableness, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरयति
मधुरयति Den. P. To sweeten, render sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरित
मधुरित <i>a.</i> Sweetened, made sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुरिमन्
मधुरिमन् <i>m.</i> Sweetness, agreeableness; मधुरिमातिशयेन वचोऽमृतम् Bv. 1. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुल|मधुलं
मधुल <i>a.</i> Sweet &c.; see मधुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलम्
मधुल + .{@-लम्@} An intoxicating drink, spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुलिका
मधुलिका<BR>—1 Black mustard.<BR>—2 A kind of bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधुस्यति
मधुस्यति Den. P. To wish or long for honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूकः|मधूक|मधूकं
मधूकः<BR>—1 A bee.<BR>—2 N. of a tree; अङ्गैर्मुग्धमधूकपुष्परुचिभिर्लांवण्यसारैरयम् Mv. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूकम्
मधूकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A flower of the Madhūka tree; दूर्वावता पाण्डुमधूकदाम्ना Ku. 7. 14;<BR> स्निग्धो मधूकच्छविर्गण्डः Gīt. 10; R. 6. 25.<BR>—2 Liquorice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूलः|मधूल
मधूलः [मधु लाति ला-क पृषो˚] A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूली
मधूलः + .{@-ली@}<BR>—1 The mango tree.<BR>—2 Liquorice.<BR>—3 A kind of citron.<BR>—4 Pollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूलम्
मधूलः + .{@-लम्@} Honey. ━<i>a.</i> Astringent, bitter, and sweet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मधूलिका
मधूलिका A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्य|मध्यं|मध्यः
मध्य <i>a.</i> [मन्-यत् नस्य धः Tv.]<BR>—1 Middle, central, being in the middle or centre; एकं मुक्तागुणमिव<BR> भुवः स्थूलमध्येन्द्रनीलम् Me. 48; Ms. 2. 21.<BR>—2 Intervening, intermediate.<BR>—3 Middling, moderate, of a middling size or quality, mediocre; अग्र्यो<BR> मध्यो जघन्यश्च तं प्रवेक्ष्याम्यशेषतः Ms. 12. 30; प्रारभ्य विध्नविहता<BR> विरमन्ति मध्याः Bh. 2. 27.<BR>—4 Neutral, impartial.<BR>—5 Just, right. —6 Mean (in astr.).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">Page1231-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यः|मध्य|मध्यं
मध्य + .{@-ध्यः, -ध्यम्@} —1 The middle, centre, middle or central part; अह्नः<BR> मध्यम् mid-day; सहस्रदीधितिरलंकरोति मध्यमह्नः Māl.<BR>—1 ‘the sun is on the meridian’ or ‘right over-head’; सरति सहसा<BR> बाह्वोर्मध्यं गताप्यबला सती M. 4. 11 (v. l.); व्योममध्ये V. 2. 1.<BR>—2 The middle of the body, the waist; मध्ये क्षाम Me. 84; वेदिविलग्नमध्या<BR> Ku. 1. 39; विशालवक्षास्तनुवृत्तमध्यः R. 6. 32; दधाना बलिभं<BR> मध्यं कर्णजाहविलोचना Bk. 4. 16.<BR>—3 The belly, abdomen; मध्येन … वलित्रयं चारु बभार बाला Ku. 1. 39.<BR>—4 The inside or interior of anything.<BR>—5 A middle state or condition.<BR>—6 The flank of a horse.<BR>—7 Mean time in music.<BR>—8 The middle term of a progression.<BR>—9 Cessation, pause, interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यम्
मध्य + .{@-ध्यः, -ध्यम्@} —1 The middle, centre, middle or central part; अह्नः<BR> मध्यम् mid-day; सहस्रदीधितिरलंकरोति मध्यमह्नः Māl.<BR>—1 ‘the sun is on the meridian’ or ‘right over-head’; सरति सहसा<BR> बाह्वोर्मध्यं गताप्यबला सती M. 4. 11 (v. l.); व्योममध्ये V. 2. 1.<BR>—2 The middle of the body, the waist; मध्ये क्षाम Me. 84; वेदिविलग्नमध्या<BR> Ku. 1. 39; विशालवक्षास्तनुवृत्तमध्यः R. 6. 32; दधाना बलिभं<BR> मध्यं कर्णजाहविलोचना Bk. 4. 16.<BR>—3 The belly, abdomen; मध्येन … वलित्रयं चारु बभार बाला Ku. 1. 39.<BR>—4 The inside or interior of anything.<BR>—5 A middle state or condition.<BR>—6 The flank of a horse.<BR>—7 Mean time in music.<BR>—8 The middle term of a progression.<BR>—9 Cessation, pause, interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्या
मध्य + .{@-ध्या@}<BR>—1 The middle finger.<BR>—2 A young woman, one arrived at puberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यम्
मध्य + .{@-ध्यम्@} Ten thousand trillions. [The acc., instr., abl. and loc.<BR> singulars of मध्य are used adverbially.<BR>——(<i>a</i>) मध्यम् into the midst of, into.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) मध्येन through or between.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) मध्यात् out of, from among, from the midst (with gen.); तेषां<BR> मध्यात् काकः प्रोवाच Pt. 1.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) मध्ये<BR>—1 in the middle, between, among, in the midst; स जहार तयोर्मध्ये<BR> मैथिलीं लोकशोषणः R. 12. 29.<BR>—2 in, into, within, inside, oft, as the first member of adverbial compounds;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> मध्येगङ्गम् into the Ganges; मध्येजठरम् in the belly;<BR> Bv. 1. 61; मध्येनगरम् inside the city; मध्येनदि in the middle<BR> of the river; मध्येपृष्ठम् on the back; मध्येभक्तम् a medicine<BR> taken in the middle of oneʼs meals; मध्येरणम् in the battle; Bv. 1. 128;<BR> मध्येसभम् in or before an assembly; N. 6. 76; मध्येसमुद्रम्<BR> in the midst of the sea; Śi. 3. 33.].<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मध्याङ्गुलिः, मध्याङ्गुला, मध्याह्नः, मध्यादित्यः, मध्योदात्त, मध्यकर्णः, मध्यक्षामा, मध्यग, मध्यगत, मध्यगन्धः, मध्यग्रहणम्, मध्यच्छाया, मध्यजिह्वम्, मध्यज्या, मध्यतमस्, मध्यतापिनी, मध्यदन्तः, मध्यदिनम्, मध्यदीपकम्, मध्यदेशः, मध्यदेहः, मध्यनिहित, मध्यपदम्, मध्यपरिमाणम्, मध्यपातः, मध्यप्रविष्ट, मध्यभः, मध्यभागः, मध्यभावः, मध्यमणिः, मध्ययवः, मध्ययोगिन्, मध्यरात्रः, मध्यरात्रिः, मध्यरेखा, मध्यलग्नम्, मध्यलोकः, मध्यवयस्, मध्यवर्तिन्, मध्यवृत्तम्, मध्यशरीर, मध्यसूत्रम्, मध्यस्थ, मध्यस्थता, मध्यस्थलम्, मध्यस्थली, मध्यस्थानम्, मध्यस्थित, मध्यता, मध्यस्वरित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1230-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्याङ्गुलिः|मध्याङ्गुलि|मध्यांगुलि
मध्य + -अङ्गुलिः, -अङ्गुला <i>f.</i> the middle finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्याङ्गुला
मध्य + -अङ्गुलिः, -अङ्गुला <i>f.</i> the middle finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्याह्नः|मध्याह्न
मध्य + -अह्नः (for अहन्) mid-day, noon; प्रातःकालो मुहूर्तांस्त्रीन्<BR> संगवस्तावदेव तु । मध्याह्नस्त्रिमुहूर्तं स्यात् … … Dakṣasaṃhitā.<BR> ˚कृत्यम्, ˚क्रिया a mid-day rite or observance. ˚कालः, ˚वेला, ˚समयः<BR> noon-time, mid-day. ˚स्नानम् mid-day ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यादित्यः|मध्यादित्य
मध्य + -आदित्यः the mid-day sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्योदात्त
मध्य + -उदात्त <i>a.</i> having the उदात्त accent on the middle syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यकर्णः|मध्यकर्ण
मध्य + -कर्णः a radius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यक्षामा
मध्य + -क्षामा N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यग
मध्य + -ग <i>a.</i> being or going in the middle or among.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यगत
मध्य + -गत <i>a.</i> central, middle, being in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यगन्धः|मध्यगन्ध|मध्यगंध
मध्य + -गन्धः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यग्रहणम्
मध्य + -ग्रहणम् the middle of an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यच्छाया
मध्य + -छाया mean or middle shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यजिह्वम्
मध्य + -जिह्वम् the organ of the palatals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यज्या
मध्य + -ज्या the sign of the meridian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यतमस्
मध्य + -तमस् <i>n.</i> circular or annular darkness, central darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यतापिनी
मध्य + -तापिनी N. of an Upaniṣad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदन्तः|मध्यदन्त
मध्य + -दन्तः a front tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदिनम्
मध्य + -दिनम् (also मध्यंदिनम्); मध्यंदिनेऽर्धरात्रे च Ms. 7. 151.<BR>—1 mid-day, noon.<BR>—2 a mid-day offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदीपकम्
मध्य + -दीपकम् a variety of the figure called Dīpaka, in which the<BR> common attribute that throws light on the whole description is placed in<BR> the middle; <i>e. g.</i> गरुडानिलतिग्मरश्मयः पततां यद्यपि संमता<BR> जवे । अचिरेण कृतार्थमागतं तममन्यन्त तथाप्यतीव ते ॥ Bk. 10. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदेशः|मध्यदेश
मध्य + -देशः<BR>—1 the middle region or space, the middle part of anything.<BR>—2 the waist.<BR>—3 the belly.<BR>—4 the meridian.<BR>—5 the central region, the country lying between the Himālaya and Vindhya<BR> mountains; हिमवद्विन्ध्ययोर्मध्यं यत्प्राग्विनशनादपि । प्रत्यगेव प्रयागाच्च<BR> मध्यदेशः स कीर्तितः ॥ Ms. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यदेहः|मध्यदेह
मध्य + -देहः the trunk of the body, the belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यनिहित
मध्य + -निहित <i>a.</i> inserted, fixed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">Page1231-2</a>]<BR> into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यपदम्
मध्य + -पदम् the middle word. ˚लोपिन् see मध्यमपदलोपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यपरिमाणम्
मध्य + -परिमाणम् the middle measure (between an atom and infinitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यपातः|मध्यपात
मध्य + -पातः<BR>—1 communion, intercourse.<BR>—2 (in astr.) the mean occurrence of the aspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यप्रविष्ट
मध्य + -प्रविष्ट <i>a.</i> one who has stolen into anotherʼs confidence; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यभः|मध्यभ
मध्य + -भः (in astr.) the meridian ecliptic point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यभागः|मध्यभाग
मध्य + -भागः<BR>—1 the middle part.<BR>—2 the waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यभावः|मध्यभाव
मध्य + -भावः<BR>—1 middle state, mediocrity.<BR>—2 a middling or moderate distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमणिः|मध्यमणि
मध्य + -मणिः the principle or central gem of a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्ययवः|मध्ययव
मध्य + -यवः a weight of six white mustard-seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्ययोगिन्
मध्य + -योगिन् <i>a.</i> being in the middle of a conjunction, completely obscured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यरात्रः|मध्यरात्र
मध्य + -रात्रः, -रात्रिः <i>f.</i> midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यरात्रिः|मध्यरात्रि
मध्य + -रात्रः, -रात्रिः <i>f.</i> midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यरेखा
मध्य + -रेखा the central or first meridian; (the line supposed to be<BR> drawn through लङ्का, उज्जयिनी, कुरुक्षेत्र and other places to the mount मेरु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यलग्नम्
मध्य + -लग्नम् the point of the ecliptic situated on the meridian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यलोकः|मध्यलोक
मध्य + -लोकः the middle of the three worlds; <i>i. e.</i> the earth or<BR> world of mortals. ˚ईशः, ˚ईश्वरः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवयस्
मध्य + -वयस् <i>a.</i> middle-aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवर्तिन्|मध्यवर्त्तिन्
मध्य + -वर्तिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 middle, central.<BR>—2 being among or in the middle. ━(<i>m.</i>) an arbitrator, a mediator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यवृत्तम्
मध्य + -वृत्तम् the navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यशरीर
मध्य + -शरीर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having a middle-sized body.<BR>—2 one of moderately full habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यसूत्रम्
मध्य + -सूत्रम् = मध्यरेखा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थ|मध्यस्थः
मध्य + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being or standing in the middle, central.<BR>—2 intermediate, intervening.<BR>—3 middling.<BR>—4 mediating, acting as umpire between two parties.<BR>—5 impartial, neutral; सुहृन्मित्रार्युदासीनमध्यस्थद्वेष्यबन्धुषु …<BR> समबुद्धिर्विशिष्यते Bg. 6. 9.<BR>—6 indifferent, unconcerned; अन्या मध्यस्थचिन्ता तु विमर्दाभ्यधिकोदया<BR> Rām. 2. 2. 16; मध्यस्थो देशबन्धुषु Pt. 4. 60; वयमत्र मध्यस्थाः<BR> Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थः|मध्यस्थ
मध्य + -स्थ + ({@-स्थः@})<BR>—1 an umpire, arbitrator, a mediator.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थता
मध्य + -स्थता<BR>—1 intermediate position.<BR>—2 middle state or character.<BR>—3 mediocrity.<BR>—4 arbitration, mediatorship.<BR>—5 impartiality; मध्यस्थतां गृहीत्वा भण M. 3 ‘say impartially’;<BR> मध्यस्थतानैकतरोपहासः N.<BR>—6 indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थलम्
मध्य + -स्थलम्, -स्थली<BR>—1 the middle or centre.<BR>—2 the middle space or region.<BR>—3 the waist.<BR>—4 the hip; कुचौ मरिचसंनिभौ मुरजमध्यमध्यस्थली Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थली
मध्य + -स्थलम्, -स्थली<BR>—1 the middle or centre.<BR>—2 the middle space or region.<BR>—3 the waist.<BR>—4 the hip; कुचौ मरिचसंनिभौ मुरजमध्यमध्यस्थली Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थानम्
मध्य + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 the middle station.<BR>—2 the middle space; <i>i. e.</i> air.<BR>—3 a neutral region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्थित
मध्य + -स्थित <i>a.</i> central, intermediate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यता
मध्य + -ता indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यस्वरित
मध्य + -स्वरित <i>a.</i> having the स्वरित accent on the middle syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यकम्
मध्यकम् A common property, common belonging; मध्यकं हीदं दम्पत्योर्धनम्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 17; मध्यकं स्यात् कृत्स्नं फलम् इति ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यतस्
मध्यतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From the middle or midst, out of.<BR>—2 Among, between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यंदिन|मध्यन्दिन|मध्यन्दिनः
मध्यंदिन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Middle, central.<BR>—2 Meridional, belonging to noon (also मध्यंदिनीय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यंदिनम्
मध्यंदिन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The mid-day (the third division of the day out of five); अथ यत्<BR> संप्रति मध्यंदिने Ch. Up. 2. 9. 5.<BR>—2 The time of the day between 16 to 20 Ghaṭakās; मध्यंदिने विष्णुररीन्द्रपाणिः<BR> Bhāg. 6. 8. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यन्य
मध्यन्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Occupying a middle station.<BR>—2 Having a middle rank or position (in any caste &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1231-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यम|मध्यमं|मध्यमः
मध्यम <i>a.</i> [मध्ये भवः म]<BR>—1 Being or standing in the middle, middle, central; पितुः पदं मध्यममुत्पतन्ती<BR> V. 1. 19; मध्यमोपलम् Ki. 9. 2; so मध्यमलोकपालः, मध्यमपदम्,<BR> मध्यमरेखा qq. vv.<BR>—2 Intermediate, intervening; नाप्नोद्योऽयं मध्यमः प्राणस्तानि ज्ञातुं<BR> दध्रिरे Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 21.<BR>—3 Middling condition or quality, mediocre; as in उत्तमाधममध्यम.<BR>—4 Middling, moderate; तेन मध्यमशक्तीनि मित्राणि स्थापितान्यतः R. 17. 58.<BR>—5 Middle-sized.<BR>—6 Neither youngest nor oldest, the middle-born (as a brother); प्रणमति<BR> पितरौ वां मध्यमः पाण्डवोऽयम् Ve. 5. 26; ततोऽर्धं मध्यमस्य स्यात्<BR> तुरीयं तु यवीयसः Ms. 9. 112.<BR>—7 Impartial, neutral.<BR>—8 Mean (in astr.).<BR>—9 Belonging to the meridian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमः|मध्यम|मध्यमं
मध्यम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 The fifth note in music.<BR>—2 A particular musical mode.<BR>—3 The mid-land country; see मध्यदेश.<BR>—4 The second person (in grammar).<BR>—5 A neutral sovereign; धर्मोत्तरं मध्यममाश्रयन्ते R. 13. 7.<BR>—6 the middle-most prince; मध्यमस्य प्रचारं च विजिगीषोश्च चेष्टितम् Ms. 7. 155.<BR>—7 the middle character in plays.<BR>—8 The governor of a province.<BR>—9 An epithet of Bhīma; (cf. मध्यमव्यायोग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमा
मध्यम + .{@-मा@}<BR>—1 The middle finger.<BR>—2 A marriageable girl, one arrived at the age of puberty.<BR>—3 The pericarp of a lotus.<BR>—4 One of the classes of heroines (Nāyikās) in poetic compositions,<BR> a woman in the middle of her youth; cf. S. D. 100.<BR>—5 A central blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमम्
मध्यम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 The middle.<BR>—2 The waist; तदैव यन्न दग्धस्त्वं धर्षयंस्तनुमध्यमाम् Rām. 6. 111. 24.<BR>—3 The defectiveness.<BR>—4 (In astr.) The meridian ecliptic point.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मध्यमाङ्गुलिः, मध्यमागमः, मध्यमाहरणम्, मध्यमोत्खातः, मध्यमोपलः, मध्यमकक्षा, मध्यमखण्डम्, मध्यमगतिः, मध्यमग्रामः, मध्यमजात, मध्यमपदम्, मध्यमपाण्डवः, मध्यमपुरुषः, मध्यमपूरुषः, मध्यमभृतकः, मध्यमयानम्, मध्यमरात्रः, मध्यमराष्ट्रकम्, मध्यमरेखा, मध्यमलोकः, मध्यमवयस्, मध्यमवयस्क, मध्यमसंग्रहः, मध्यमसाहसः, मध्यमस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमाङ्गुलिः|मध्यमाङ्गुलि|मध्यमांगुलि
मध्यम + -अङ्गुलिः the middle finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमागमः|मध्यमागम
मध्यम + -आगमः one of the four Āgamas; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमाहरणम्
मध्यम + -आहरणम् (in alg.) elimination of the middle term in an equation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमोत्खातः|मध्यमोत्खात
मध्यम + -उत्खातः a particular division of time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमोपलः
मध्यम + -उपलः = मध्यमणिः q. v.; मध्यमोपलनिभे लसदंशौ Ki. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमकक्षा
मध्यम + -कक्षा the middle courtyard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमखण्डम्
मध्यम + -खण्डम् the middle term of an equation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमगतिः|मध्यमगति
मध्यम + -गतिः (in astr.) the mean motion of a planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमग्रामः|मध्यमग्राम
मध्यम + -ग्रामः (in music) the middle scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमजात
मध्यम + -जात <i>a.</i> middle-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपदम्
मध्यम + -पदम् the middle member (of a compound). ˚लोपिन् <i>m.</i> a<BR> subdivision of the Tatpuruṣa compound in which the middle word is omitted<BR> in composition; the usual instance given is शाकपार्थिवः which is<BR> dissolved as शाकप्रियः पार्थिवः; here the middle word प्रिय is<BR> omitted; so छायातरुः, गुडधानाः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपाण्डवः|मध्यमपाण्डव|मध्यमपांडव
मध्यम + -पाण्डवः an epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपुरुषः|मध्यमपुरुष
मध्यम + -पुरुषः the second person (in grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमपूरुषः|मध्यमपूरुष
मध्यम + -पूरुषः a mediocre person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमभृतकः|मध्यमभृतक
मध्यम + -भृतकः a husbandman or cultivator (who works both for himself<BR> and his master or landlord).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमयानम्
मध्यम + -यानम् the middle way to salvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमरात्रः|मध्यमरात्र
मध्यम + -रात्रः midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमराष्ट्रकम्
मध्यम + -राष्ट्रकम् a variety of diamonds; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमरेखा
मध्यम + -रेखा the central meridian of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमलोकः|मध्यमलोक
मध्यम + -लोकः the middle world, the earth. ˚पालः a king; तां … … अन्वग्ययौ<BR> मध्यमलोकपालः R. 2. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमवयस्
मध्यम + -वयस् <i>n.</i> middle age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमवयस्क
मध्यम + -वयस्क <i>a.</i> middle-aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसंग्रहः|मध्यमसङ्ग्रह
मध्यम + -संग्रहः intrigue of a middling character, such as sending presents<BR> of flowers &c. to anotherʼs wife; it is thus defined by Vyāsa:− प्रेषणं<BR> गन्धमाल्यानां धूपभूषणवाससाम् । प्रलोभनं चान्नपानैर्मध्यमः संग्रहः स्मृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसाहसः|मध्यमसाहस|मध्यमसाहसं
मध्यम + -साहसः the second of the three penalties or modes of punishment; see Ms. 8. 138.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">Page1232-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसाहसः|मध्यमसाहस|मध्यमसाहसं
मध्यम + -साहसः + .({@-सः, -सम्@}) an outrage or offence of the middle class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमसाहसम्
मध्यम + -साहसः + .({@-सः, -सम्@}) an outrage or offence of the middle class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमस्थ
मध्यम + -स्थ <i>a.</i> being in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमक
मध्यमक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Middle, middle-most.<BR>—2 Common (property &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमकम्
मध्यमक + .{@-कम्@} The interior of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमिका
मध्यमिका A girl arrived at puberty, a marriageable woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्यमीय|मध्यमीयं
मध्यमीय <i>a.</i> Middle, central.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्ये
मध्ये See under मध्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वः|मध्व
मध्वः N. of a celebrated preceptor and author, the founder of the<BR> sect of Vaiṣṇavas, and author of a Bhāṣya on the Vedānta Sūtras.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मध्वमतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वमतम्
मध्वः + -मतम् the doctrine of Madhva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वकः|मध्वक
मध्वकः A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्वला
मध्वला A drinking bout; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मध्विजा
मध्विजा Any intoxicating drink, spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्
मन् I. €1 P. (मनति)<BR>—1 To be proud.<BR>—2 To worship. ━II. €10 Ā. (मानयते)<BR>—1 To be proud.<BR>—2 To stop, to obstruct; L. D. B. ━III. €4. €8 Ā. (मन्यते, मनुते,<BR> मेने, अमंस्त, मंस्यते, मन्तुम्, मत)<BR>—1 To think, believe, suppose, imagine, fancy, conceive; अङ्कं केऽपि<BR> शशङ्किरे जलनिधेः पङ्कं परे मेनिरे Subhāṣ.; वत्स मन्ये कुमारेणानेन<BR> जृम्भकास्त्रमामन्त्रितम् U. 5; कथं भवान् मन्यते ‘what is your opinion’?<BR>—2 To consider, regard, deem, look upon, take (one) for, take to be; समीभूता<BR> दृष्टिस्त्रिभुवनमपि त्रह्म मनुते Bh. 3. 84; अमंस्त चानेन परार्ध्यजन्मना<BR> स्थितेरभेत्ता स्थितिमन्तमन्वयम् R. 3. 27, 1. 32, 6. 84; नित्यं वा<BR> मन्यसे मृतम् Bg. 2. 26, 35; Bk. 9. 117; स्तनविनिहितमपि हारमुदारम् ।<BR> सा मनुते कृशतनुरिव भारम् Gīt. 4.<BR>—3 To honour, respect, value, esteem, think highly of, prize; यस्यानुषङ्गिण<BR> इमे भुवनाधिपत्यभोगादयः कृपणलोकमता भवन्ति Bh. 3. 76.<BR>—4 To know, understand, perceive, observe, have regard to; मत्वा देवं<BR> धनपतिसखं यत्र साक्षाद्वसन्तम् Me. 75.<BR>—5 To agree or consent to, act up to; तन्मन्यस्व मम वचनम् Mk. 8.<BR>—6 To think or reflect upon.<BR>—7 To intend, wish or hope for; स्त्रियः कस्माद्वधं वीर मन्यसे राक्षसेश्वर<BR> Rām. 6. 92. 60.<BR>—8 To set the heart or mind on.<BR>—9 To mention, declare.<BR>—10 To think out, devise, invent.<BR>—11 To be considered or regarded as, seem, appear like.<BR>—12 To accept, agree; कालपाशमहं मन्ये त्वमपि द्रष्टुमर्हसि Mb. 17. 1. 3.<BR> (The senses of मन् are variously modified according to the<BR> word with which it is used; <i>e. g.</i> बहु मन् to think highly or<BR> much of, value greatly, prize, esteem; बहु मनुते ननु ते तनुसंगतपवनचलितमपि<BR> रेणुम् Gīt. 5; see under बहु also; लघु मन् to think lightly<BR> of, despise, slight; प्रथमोपकृतं मरुत्वतः प्रतिपत्त्या लघु मन्यते<BR> भवान् Ś. 7. 1; अन्यथा मन् to think otherwise; doubt; साधु मन्<BR> to think well of, approve, consider satisfactory; आ परितोषाद्विदुषां<BR> न साधु मन्ये प्रयोगविज्ञानम् Ś. 1. 2; असाधु मन् to disapprove;<BR> तृणाय मन् or तृणवत् मन् to value at a straw, value lightly,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">Page1233-1</a>]<BR> make light of; हरिमप्यमंसत तृणाय Śi. 15. 61; न मन् to<BR> disregard, not to mind). ━<i>Caus.</i> (मानयति-ते) To honour, esteem,<BR> respect, pay respect to, value; मान्यान् मानय Bh. 2. 77; (Ātm.) to<BR> esteem one-self highly, prize highly. ━<i>Desid.</i> (मीमांसते)<BR>—1 To reflect upon, examine, investigate, inquire into.<BR>—2 To doubt, call in question (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1232-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनन|मननं
मनन <i>a.</i> [मन्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Thoughtful, careful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मननम्
मनन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Thinking, reflection, meditation, cogitation; युक्त्या संभावितत्वानुसंधानं<BR> मननं तु तत् Pañcadaśī 1. 53; मननान्मुनिरेवासि Hariv.<BR>—2 Intelligence, understanding.<BR>—3 An inference arrived at by reasoning.<BR>—4 A guess, conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तव्य|मंतव्य|मन्तव्यं
मन्तव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be thought, considered, or regarded.<BR>—2 Imaginable, conceivable.<BR>—3 To be maintained.<BR>—4 To be approved or sanctioned; see मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तुः|मन्तु|मंतु|मंतुः
मन्तुः<BR>—1 A fault, an offence; मुधैव मन्तुं परिकल्प्य Bv. 2. 13; अनेन<BR> हेतुना ह्यस्य मन्तवः शतशो मया (क्षान्ताः) Śiva B. 15. 12; भवता<BR> शिवभूपस्य बहवो मन्तवः कृताः Śiva B. 31. 6; N. 6. 110.<BR>—2 Man, mankind.<BR>—3 Lord of men (प्रजापति).<BR>—4 Ved. An adviser.<BR>—5 A manager, director.<BR>—6 Advice, counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तुः|मन्तु|मंतु|मंतुः
मन्तुः + .{@-न्तुः@} <i>f.</i> Understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तूयति
मन्तूयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To offend, transgress against.<BR>—2 To be angry.<BR>—3 To be jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्तृ|मंतृ
मन्तृ <i>m.</i> A sage, wise man, an adviser or counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्
मनस् <i>n.</i> [मन्यतेऽनेन मन् करणे असुन्]<BR>—1 The mind, heart, understanding, perception, intelligence; as in सुमनस्, दुमर्नस् &c.<BR>—2 (In phil.) The mind or internal organ of perception and cognition,<BR> the instrument by which objects of sense affect the soul; (in Nyāya phil.<BR> मनस् is regarded as a Dravya or substance, and is distinct from आत्मन्<BR> or the soul); तदेव सुखदुःखाद्युपलब्धिसाधनमिन्द्रियं प्रतिजीवं<BR> भिन्नमणु नित्यं च Tarka K.<BR>—3 Conscience, the faculty of discrimination or judgment.<BR>—4 Thought, idea, fancy, imagination, conception; पश्यन्नदूरान्मनसाप्यधृष्यम्<BR> Ku. 3. 51; R. 2. 27; कायेन वाचा मनसापि शश्वत् 5. 5; मनसापि<BR> न विप्रियं मया (कृतपूर्वम्) 8. 52.<BR>—5 Design, purpose, intention.<BR>—6 Will, wish, desire, inclination; in this sense मनस् is frequently<BR> used with the infinitive form with the final म् dropped, and forms<BR> adjectives; अयं जनः प्रष्टुमनास्तपोधने Ku. 5. 40; cf. काम.<BR>—7 Reflection (ध्यान); मनसा जपैः प्रणतिभिः प्रयतः समुपेयिवानधिपतिं<BR> स दिवः Ki. 6. 22.<BR>—8 Disposition, temper, mood.<BR>—9 Spirit, energy, mettle; मनोवीर्यवरोत्सिक्तमसृण्यमकुतोभयम् Bhāg. 3. 17. 22.<BR>—10 N. of the lake called Mānasa.<BR>—11 Breath or living soul.<BR>—12 Desire, longing after. (मनसा गम् &c. to think of, contemplate,<BR> remember; जगाम मनसा रामं धर्मज्ञो धर्मकाङ्क्षया Rām. 2. 82. 9;<BR> (अगमत्) मनसा कार्यसंसिद्धौ त्वरादिगुणरंहसा Ku. 2. 63;<BR> मनः कृ to fix the mind upon, direct the thoughts towards, with dat.<BR> or loc.; मनो बन्ध् to fix the heart or affection upon; (अभिलाषे) मनो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">Page1233-2</a>]<BR> बबन्धान्यरसान् विलङ्घ्य सा R. 3. 4; मनः समाधा to collect oneself;<BR> मनसि उद्भू to cross the mind; मनसि कृ to think, to bear in<BR> mind; to resolve, determine, think of.) (<i>N. B.</i> In comp. मनस् is<BR> changed to मनो before अ and soft consonants, as मनोऽनुग,<BR> मनोज्ञ, मनोहर &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मनोधिनाथः, मनोनवस्थानम्, मनोनुग, मनोपहारिन्, मनोभिनिवेशः, मनोभिराम, मनोभिलाषः, मनआप, मनःकान्त, मनःकारः, मनःक्षेपः, मनोगत, मनोगतिः, मनोगवी, मनोगुप्त, मनोग्रहणम्, मनोग्रहिन्, मनोग्राह्य, मनोग्राह्यम्, मनोग्लानिः, मनोज, मनोजन्मन्, मनोजल्पः, मनोजव, मनोजवस, मनोजवा, मनोजात, मनोजिघ्र, मनोज्ञ, मनस्तापः, मनःपीडा, मनस्तालः, मनस्तुष्टिः, मनस्तोका, मनोदण्डः, मनोदत्त, मनोदाहः, मनोदुःखम्, मनोदाहिन्, मनोदुष्ट, मनोधारणम्, मनोनाशः, मनोनीत, मनःपतिः, मनःपर्यायः, मनःपूत, मनःप्रणीत, मनःप्रसादः, मनःप्रिय, मनःप्रियः, मनःप्रीतिः, मनोभव, मनोभवः, मनोभूः, मनोमथनः, मनोमय, मनोयायिन्, मनोयोगः, मनोयोनिः, मनोरञ्जनम्, मनोरथः, मनोरम, मनोरागः, मनोराज्यम्, मनोरुज्, मनोलयः, मनोलौल्यम्, मनोवल्लभा, मनोवहा, मनोवाक्कर्मन्, मनोवाञ्छा, मनोवाञ्छितम्, मनोविकारः, मनोविकृतिः, मनोविनयनम्, मनोविरुद्ध, मनोवृत्तिः, मनोवेगः, मनोव्यथा, मनःशल्य, मनःशिलः, मनःशिला, मनःशीघ्र, मनःसंकल्पः, मनःसंगः, मनःसंचेतनाहारः, मनःसंतापः, मनःसमृद्धिः, मनःसंवरः, मनःसुख, मनःस्थ, मनःस्थैर्यम्, मनोहत, मनोहर, मनोहर्तृ, मनोहारिन्, मनोहारी, मनोह्लादः, मनोह्वा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोधिनाथः|मनोधिनाथ
मनस् + -अधिनाथः a lover, husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोनवस्थानम्
मनस् + -अनवस्थानम् inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोनुग
मनस् + -अनुग <i>a.</i> suiting the mind, agreeable; ततस्तदग्र्यं वचनं<BR> मनोनुगं समस्तमाज्ञाय ततो हि हेतुमत् Mb. 12. 167. 49; Rām. 7. 72. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोपहारिन्
मनस् + -अपहारिन् <i>a.</i> captivating the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभिनिवेशः|मनोभिनिवेश
मनस् + -अभिनिवेशः close application of mind, firmness of purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभिराम
मनस् + -अभिराम <i>a.</i> pleasing the mind, gratifying to the heart; मनोभिरामाः<BR> (केकाः) R. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभिलाषः|मनोभिलाष
मनस् + -अभिलाषः the desire or longing of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनआप|मनआपः
मनस् + -आप <i>a.</i> gaining the heart, attractive, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःकान्त|मनःकांत
मनस् + -कान्त <i>a.</i> (मनस्कान्त or मनःकान्त) dear to the mind,<BR> pleasant, agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःकारः
मनस् + -कारः perfect perception, full consciousness (of pleasure or<BR> pain), mental concentration, resolution; भवन्मनस्कारलवोद्गमेन क्रमेलकानां<BR> निलयः पुरेव N. 14. 84. (cf. मनसः ऐकाग्र्यकरणं मनस्कारः<BR> Nārāyaṇa com. on N.) दिदृक्षादत्तदृष्टीनां मनस्कारमनीषयोः । सप्रीतिरससन्तोषं<BR> दिशन्तौ देहकान्तितः ॥ Yādavābhyudaya 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःक्षेपः|मनःक्षेप
मनस् + -क्षेपः (मनःक्षेपः) distraction of the mind, mental confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगत
मनस् + -गत <i>a.</i> —1 existing or passing in the mind, concealed in the<BR> breast, internal, inward, secret; नेयं न वक्ष्यति मनोगतमाधिहेतुम् Ś. 3. 11.<BR>—2 affecting the mind, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगतम्
मनस् + -गत + ({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 a wish, desire; मनोगतं सा न शशाक शंसितुम् Ku. 5. 51.<BR>—2 an idea, thought, notion, opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगतिः|मनोगति
मनस् + -गतिः <i>f.</i> desire of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगवी
मनस् + -गवी wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगुप्त
मनस् + -गुप्त <i>a.</i> hidden in the mind, thought secretly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोगुप्ता
मनस् + -गुप्त + ({@-प्ता@}) red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोग्रहणम्
मनस् + -ग्रहणम् captivating the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोग्रहिन्
मनस् + -ग्रहिन् <i>a.</i> captivating or fascinating the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोग्राह्य
मनस् + -ग्राह्य <i>a.</i> to be grasped by the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोग्राह्यम्
मनस् + -ग्राह्यम् the pleasures of sense; यो वृणीते मनोग्राह्यमसत्त्वात्<BR> कुमनीष्यसौ Bhāg. 10. 48. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोग्लानिः|मनोग्लानि
मनस् + -ग्लानिः depression of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज
मनस् + -ज, -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> mind-born. ━(<i>m.</i>) the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजन्मन्
मनस् + -ज, -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> mind-born. ━(<i>m.</i>) the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजल्पः|मनोजल्प
मनस् + -जल्पः imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजव|मनोजवः
मनस् + -जव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 quick or swift as thought; मनोजवं मारुततुल्यवेगम् Rāmarakṣā 33.<BR>—2 quick in thought or conception.<BR>—3 fatherly, paternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजवस|मनोजवसः
मनस् + -जवस <i>a.</i> resembling a father, fatherly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजवा
मनस् + -जवा<BR>—1 N. of one of the tongues of Agni.<BR>—2 N. of one of the शक्तिs of Durgā; ‘काली कराली च मनोजवा च’ Śruti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजात
मनस् + -जात <i>a.</i> mind-born, arisen or produced in the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोजिघ्र
मनस् + -जिघ्र <i>a.</i> scenting out, <i>i. e.</i> guessing the thoughts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज्ञ|मनोज्ञं|मनोज्ञः
मनस् + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> pleasing, lovely, agreeable, beautiful, charming;<BR> इयमधिकमनोज्ञा वल्कलेनापि तन्वी Ś. 1. 20; R. 3. 7, 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज्ञः|मनोज्ञ|मनोज्ञं
मनस् + -ज्ञ + ({@-ज्ञः@})<BR> N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोज्ञा
मनस् + -ज्ञ + .({@-ज्ञा@})<BR>—1 red arsenic.<BR>—2 an intoxicating drink.<BR>—3 a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्तापः|मनस्ताप
मनस् + -तापः, -पीडा —1 mental pain or agony, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःपीडा
मनस् + -ज्ञ + .({@-ज्ञा@})<BR>—1 red arsenic.<BR>—2 an intoxicating drink.<BR>—3 a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्तालः|मनस्ताल
मनस् + -तालः the lion of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्तुष्टिः|मनस्तुष्टि
मनस् + -तुष्टिः <i>f.</i> satisfaction of the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्तोका
मनस् + -तोका an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदण्डः|मनोदण्ड|मनोदंड
मनस् + -दण्डः complete control over the mind or thoughts; Ms. 12. 10;<BR> cf. त्रिदण्डिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदत्त
मनस् + -दत्त <i>a.</i> devoted in thought, mentally dedicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदाहः|मनोदाह
मनस् + -दाहः, -दुःखम् mental distress or torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदुःखम्
मनस् + -दाहः, -दुःखम् mental distress or torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदाहिन्
मनस् + -दाहिन् the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोदुष्ट
मनस् + -दुष्ट <i>a.</i> depraved in mind; रजसा स्त्री मनोदुष्टा संन्यासेन<BR> द्विजोत्तम (शुद्धपति) Ms. 5. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोधारणम्
मनस् + -धारणम् conciliating the favour of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोनाशः|मनोनाश
मनस् + -नाशः loss of the mind or understanding, dementedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोनीत
मनस् + -नीत <i>a.</i> approved, chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःपतिः|मनःपति
मनस् + -पतिः (मनःपतिः)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">Page1234-1</a>]<BR> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1233-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःपर्यायः|मनःपर्याय
मनस् + -पर्यायः (with Jainas) N. of the last but one stage in the perception of truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःपूत
मनस् + -पूत <i>a.</i> (मनःपूत)<BR>—1 considered pure by the mind, approved by oneʼs conscience; मनःपूतं<BR> समाचरेत् Ms. 6. 46.<BR>—2 of a pure mind, conscientious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःप्रणीत
मनस् + -प्रणीत <i>a.</i> (मनःप्रणीत) agreeable or pleasing to the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःप्रसादः|मनःप्रसाद
मनस् + -प्रसादः (मनः-प्रसादः) composure of mind, mental calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःप्रिय|मनःप्रियः
मनस् + -प्रिय <i>a.</i> dear to the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःप्रियः|मनःप्रिय
मनस् + -प्रियः cinammon (Mar. दालचिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःप्रीतिः|मनःप्रीति
मनस् + -प्रीतिः <i>f.</i> (मनःप्रीतिः) mental satisfaction, joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभव|मनोभवः
मनस् + -भव <i>a.</i> mind-born, created by fancy; दृश्यमाना विनार्थेन<BR> न दृश्यन्ते मनोभवाः Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभवः|मनोभव
मनस् + -भवः, -भूः<BR>—1 the god of love, Cupid; रे रे मनो मम मनोभवशासनस्य पादाम्बुजद्वयमनारतमानमन्तम्<BR> Bv. 4. 32; Ku. 3. 27; R. 7. 22; श्यामा शुशुभे शशिना तया मनोभूः Kalāvilāsa.<BR>—2 love, passion, lust; अत्यारूढो हि नारीणामकालज्ञो मनोभवः R. 12. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोभूः
मनस् + -भवः, -भूः<BR>—1 the god of love, Cupid; रे रे मनो मम मनोभवशासनस्य पादाम्बुजद्वयमनारतमानमन्तम्<BR> Bv. 4. 32; Ku. 3. 27; R. 7. 22; श्यामा शुशुभे शशिना तया मनोभूः Kalāvilāsa.<BR>—2 love, passion, lust; अत्यारूढो हि नारीणामकालज्ञो मनोभवः R. 12. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोमथनः|मनोमथन
मनस् + -मथनः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोमय
मनस् + -मय see separately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयायिन्
मनस् + -यायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 going at will or pleasure.<BR>—2 swift, quick as thought; उत्पत्य खं दशग्रीवो मनोयायी शितास्त्रभृत् Bk. 5. 30.<BR>—3 keen desire; अहं हि तस्याद्य मनोभवेन संपीडिता तद्गतसर्वभावा<BR> Rām. 5. 32. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयोगः|मनोयोग
मनस् + -योगः close application of the mind, close attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोयोनिः|मनोयोनि
मनस् + -योनिः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरञ्जनम्
मनस् + -रञ्जनम्<BR>—1 pleasing the mind.<BR>—2 pleasantness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरथः|मनोरथ
मनस् + -रथः<BR>—1 ‘the car of the mind’, a wish, desire; अवतरतः सिद्धिपथं शब्दः<BR> स्वमनोरथस्येव M. 1. 22; मनोरथानामगतिर्न विद्यते Ku. 5. 64;<BR> R. 2. 72, 12. 59; उत्पद्यन्ते विलीयन्ते दरिद्राणां मनोरथाः Udb.;<BR> आशा नाम नदी मनोरथजला Bh. 3. 45.<BR>—2 a desired object; मनोरथाय नाशंसे Ś. 7. 13.<BR>—3 (in dramas) a hint, a wish expressed indirectly or covertly. ˚तृतीया<BR> N. of the third day in the bright half of Chaitra. ˚दायक <i>a.</i><BR> fulfilling oneʼs expectations. (-कः) N. of a Kalpa-taru. ˚द्रुमः<BR> the god of love. ˚बन्धः cherishing or entertaining of desire. ˚बन्धुः<BR> the friend of (who satisfies) desires; तस्या भवानपि मनोरथबन्धबन्धुः<BR> Māl. 1. 34. ˚सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> fulfilment of oneʼs desires. ˚सृष्टिः<BR> <i>f.</i> a creation of the fancy, a castle in the air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरम|मनोरमं
मनस् + -रम <i>a.</i> attractive, pleasing, agreeable, lovely, beautiful;<BR> अरुणनखमनोरमासु तस्याः (अङ्गुलीषु) Ś. 6. 11; पुरस्ताद्विमले<BR> पात्रे सुविस्तीर्णे मनोरमे Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरमा
मनस् + -रम + .({@-मा@})<BR>—1 a lovely woman.<BR>—2 a kind of pigment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरागः|मनोराग
मनस् + -रागः affection, passion (of the heart).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोराज्यम्
मनस् + -राज्यम् ‘kingdom of the fancy’, a castle in the air; मनोराज्यविजृम्भणमेतत्<BR> ‘this is building castles in the air’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोरुज्
मनस् + -रुज् <i>f.</i> pain or grief of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोलयः|मनोलय
मनस् + -लयः loss of consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोलौल्यम्
मनस् + -लौल्यम् freak, caprice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवल्लभा
मनस् + -वल्लभा a beloved woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवहा
मनस् + -वहा N. of a particular artery; (‘अश्वत्थपत्रनाडीव द्विसप्ततिशताधिका । नाडी मनोवहेत्युक्तं योगशास्त्रविशारदैः’);<BR> मध्ये च हृदयस्यैका<BR> शिरा तत्र मनोवहा । शुक्रं संकल्पजं नॄणां सर्वगात्रैर्विमुञ्चति ॥<BR> Mb. 12. 214. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवाक्कर्मन्
मनस् + -वाक्कर्मन् <i>n.</i> pl. thoughts, words and deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवाञ्छा|मनोवांछा
मनस् + -वाञ्छा, -वाञ्छितम् a wish of the heart, a desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवाञ्छितम्
मनस् + -वाञ्छा, -वाञ्छितम् a wish of the heart, a desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोविकारः|मनोविकार
मनस् + -विकारः, -विकृतिः <i>f.</i> emotion of the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोविकृतिः
मनस् + -विकारः, -विकृतिः <i>f.</i> emotion of the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोविनयनम्
मनस् + -विनयनम् mental discipline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोविरुद्ध
मनस् + -विरुद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 incomprehensible.<BR>—2 against the dictates of mind or conscience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवृत्तिः|मनोवृत्ति
मनस् + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 working of the mind, volition.<BR>—2 disposition, temper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोवेगः|मनोवेग
मनस् + -वेगः quickness of thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोव्यथा
मनस् + -व्यथा mental pain or anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशल्य
मनस् + -शल्य <i>a.</i> rankling in the mind; (बाहुः) कुबेरस्य मनःशल्यं शंसतीव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">Page1234-2</a>]<BR> पराभवम् Ku. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशिलः|मनःशिल
मनस् + -शिलः, -शिला red arsenic; मनःशिलाविच्छुरिता निषेदुः Ku. 1. 55;<BR> R. 12. 80; टङ्कैर्मनःशिलगुहैरवदीर्यमाणा Mk.; गन्धाश्मानं<BR> मनःशिलाम् Śiva B. 30. 19; मनःशिलापङ्कलिखितेन च विद्योतितललाटपट्टाम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशिला
मनस् + -शिलः, -शिला red arsenic; मनःशिलाविच्छुरिता निषेदुः Ku. 1. 55;<BR> R. 12. 80; टङ्कैर्मनःशिलगुहैरवदीर्यमाणा Mk.; गन्धाश्मानं<BR> मनःशिलाम् Śiva B. 30. 19; मनःशिलापङ्कलिखितेन च विद्योतितललाटपट्टाम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःशीघ्र
मनस् + -शीघ्र <i>a.</i> quick as thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसंकल्पः|मनःसङ्कल्प
मनस् + -संकल्पः desire of the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसंगः|मनःसङ्ग|मनःसंग
मनस् + -संगः attachment of the mind (to anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसंचेतनाहारः|मनःसञ्चेतनाहार
मनस् + -संचेतनाहारः (with Buddhists) one of the four kinds of food<BR> (in a material and spiritual sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसंतापः|मनःसन्ताप
मनस् + -संतापः anguish of the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसमृद्धिः|मनःसमृद्धि
मनस् + -समृद्धिः heartʼs content; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसंवरः|मनःसंवर
मनस् + -संवरः coercion of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःसुख
मनस् + -सुख <i>a.</i> agreeable to the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःस्थ
मनस् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> being in the heart, mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनःस्थैर्यम्
मनस् + -स्थैर्यम् firmness of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहत|मनोहतः
मनस् + -हत <i>a.</i> disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहर|मनोहरं|मनोहरः
मनस् + -हर <i>a.</i> pleasing, charming, attractive, fascinating, lovely;<BR> अव्याजमनोहरं वपुः Ś. 1. 18; Ku. 3. 39; R. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहरः|मनोहर|मनोहरं
मनस् + -हर + ({@-रः@})<BR> a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहरम्
मनस् + -हर + .({@-रम्@}) gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहर्तृ
मनस् + -हर्तृ, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> heart-stealing, captivating, agreeable,<BR> pleasing; हितं मनोहारि च दुर्लभं वचः Ki. 1. 4; गाङ्गं वारि<BR> मनोहारि मुरारिचरणच्युतम् Gaṅgāṣṭaka by Vālmīki 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहारिन्
मनस् + -हर्तृ, -हारिन् <i>a.</i> heart-stealing, captivating, agreeable,<BR> pleasing; हितं मनोहारि च दुर्लभं वचः Ki. 1. 4; गाङ्गं वारि<BR> मनोहारि मुरारिचरणच्युतम् Gaṅgāṣṭaka by Vālmīki 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोहारी
मनस् + -हारी an unchaste or unfaithful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोह्लादः|मनोह्लाद
मनस् + -ह्लादः gladness of heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोह्वा
मनस् + -ह्वा red arsenic; मनःशिला मनोगुप्ता मनोह्वा नागजिह्विका Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसा
मनसा N. of a daughter of Kaśyapa, sister of the serpent king,<BR> Ananta, wife of the sage जरत्कारु and mother of the sage अस्तिक;<BR> so मनसादेवी.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मनसापञ्चमी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसापञ्चमी
मनसा + -पञ्चमी the fifth day in the dark half of Āṣāḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिज|मनसिजः
मनसिज <i>a.</i> [मनसि जायते जन्-ड अलुक्˚] Mind-born, mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिजः|मनसिज
मनसिज + .{@-जः@}<BR>—1 The god of love; मनसिजतरुपुष्पम् R. 18. 52.<BR>—2 Love, passion; मनसिजरुजं सा वा दिव्या ममालमपोहितुम् V. 3. 10;<BR> समस्तापः कामं मनसिजनिदाघप्रसरयोः Ś. 3. 9.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनसिशयः|मनसिशय
मनसिशयः<BR>—1 The god of love; मनसिशयमहास्त्रमन्यथामी न कुसुमपञ्चकमप्यलं<BR> विसोढुम् Śi. 7. 2.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्तः
मनस्तः <i>ind.</i> From the mind or heart; R. 14. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्यति
मनस्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To intend, design.<BR>—2 To think, reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विन्
मनस्विन् <i>a.</i> [प्रशस्तं मनः अस्त्यस्य विनि]<BR>—1 Wise, intelligent, clever, high-souled, high-minded; तया मेने मनस्विन्या<BR> लक्ष्म्या च वसुधाधिपः R. 1. 32; Pt. 2. 120; विपक्त्रिमज्ञानगतिर्मनस्वी Bk. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Attentive. —3 Steady-minded, resolute, determined; Ku. 5. 6; मनस्वी<BR> कार्यार्थी न गणयति दुःखं न च सुखम् Bh. 2. 81. ━<i>m.</i> The fabulous<BR> animal called Śarabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विनी
मनस्विन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A high-minded or proud woman; मनस्विनीमानविघातदक्षम् Ku. 3. 32;<BR> M. 1. 20; V. 3. 5.<BR>—2 A wise or virtuous woman.<BR>—3 N. of Durgā.<BR>—4 N. of the mother of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनस्विता
मनस्विता<BR>—1 Intelligence.<BR>—2 Magnanimity, high-mindedness.<BR>—3 Hope, expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनित|मनितं
मनित <i>p. p.</i> Known, understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीकृ
मनीकृ P. To take to heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोमय
मनोमय <i>a.</i> Mental, spiritual; मनोमयः प्राणशरीरनेता प्रतिष्ठितोऽन्ने<BR> हृदयं संनिधाय Muṇḍ. 2. 2. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मनोमयकोशः, मनोमयकोषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोमयकोशः|मनोमयकोश
मनोमय + -कोशः, -कोषः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">Page1235-1</a>]<BR> the second of the five vestures or sheaths which are supposed<BR> to enshrine the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोमयकोषः
मनोमय + -कोशः, -कोषः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">Page1235-1</a>]<BR> the second of the five vestures or sheaths which are supposed<BR> to enshrine the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1234-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्
मनाक् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A little, slightly, in a small degree; न मनाक् ‘not at all’; न<BR> मनागपि राहुरोषशङ्का Bv. 2. 1; रे पान्थ विह्वलमना न मनागपि स्याः<BR> 1. 37, 111.<BR>—2 Slowly, tardily.<BR>—3 Only, merely.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मनाक्कर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्कर|मनाक्करं
मनाक् + -कर <i>a.</i> doing little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाक्करम्
मनाक् + -कर + ({@-रम्@}) a kind of fragrant aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनाका
मनाका A female elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनायी
मनायी(वी) The wife of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनावी
मनायी(वी) The wife of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीकम्
मनीकम् Collyrium, eye-salve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीष्
मनीष् <i>f.</i> Intelligence; हृदा मनीषा मनसाभिकॢप्तो य एतद्विदुरमृतास्ते<BR> भवन्ति Kaṭh. 2. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषा
मनीषा [ईष्-अङ् ईष; मनस ईषा शकं˚]<BR>—1 Desire, wish; यो दुर्जनं वशयितुं तनुते मनीषाम् Bv. 1. 95.<BR>—2 Intelligence, understanding; अतः साधोऽत्र यत् सारं समुद्धृत्य मनीषया<BR> Bhāg. 1. 1. 11; प्रविभज्य पृथङ्मनीषया स्वगुणं यत्किल तत्करिष्यसि Śi. 16. 42.<BR>—3 A thought, idea.<BR>—4 Ved. Hymn, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषिका
मनीषिका<BR>—1 Understanding, intelligence.<BR>—2 Expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषित
मनीषित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wished for, desired, liked, loved, dear; मनीषिताः सन्ति गृहेषु देवताः Ku. 5. 4.<BR>—2 Agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषितम्
मनीषित + .{@-तम्@} A wish, desire, desired object; मनीषितं विजानाति केशवो<BR> न तु तस्य ते Mb. 12. 347. 92; मनीषितं द्यौरपि येन दुग्धा R. 5. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषिता
मनीषिता Wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनीषिन्
मनीषिन् <i>a.</i> [मनीषा-इनि]<BR>—1 Wise, learned, intelligent, clever, thoughtful, prudent; अप्यर्थकामौ तस्यास्तां धर्म एव मनीषिणः R. 1. 25.<BR>—2 Ved. Praying, praising. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A wise or learned person, a sage, a paṇḍita; माननीयो मनीषिणाम्<BR> R. 1. 11; संस्कारवत्येव गिरा मनीषी Ku. 1. 28, 5. 39; R. 3. 44.<BR>—2 Ved. A singer, praiser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनु|मनुः
मनु <i>a.</i> Thinking, wise, intelligent, sage; सलोकपाला मुनयो<BR> मनूनामाद्यं मनुं प्राञ्जलयः प्रणेमुः Bhāg. 4. 6. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुः|मनु
मनुः [मन्-उ Uṇ. 1. 10]<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated personage regarded as the representative man and<BR> father of the human race (sometimes regarded as one of the divine beings).<BR>—2 Particularly, the fourteen successive progenitors or sovereigns of<BR> the earth mentioned in Ms. 1. 63. (The first Manu called स्वायंभुवमनु<BR> is supposed to be a sort of secondary creator, who produced the ten <i>Prajāpatis</i><BR> or <i>Maharṣis</i> and to whom the code of laws known as <i>Manusmṛti</i><BR> is ascribed. The seventh Manu called वैवस्वतमनु, being supposed<BR> to be born from the sun, is regarded as the progenitor of the present<BR> race of living beings and was saved from a great flood by Viṣṇu in the<BR> form of a fish; cf. मत्स्यावतार; he is also regarded as the founder<BR> of the solar race of kings who ruled at Ayodhyā; see U. 6. 18; R. 1. 11;<BR> विवस्वान् मनवे प्राह मनुरिक्ष्वाकवेऽब्रवीत् Bg. 4. 1. The names<BR> of the fourteen<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">Page1235-2</a>]<BR> Manus in order are:− 1 स्वायंभुव, 2 स्वारोचिष, 3 औत्तमि,<BR> 4 तामस, 5 रैवत, 6 चाक्षुष, 7 वैवस्वत, 8 सावर्णि,<BR> 9 दक्षसावर्णि, 10 ब्रह्मसावर्णि, 11 धर्मसावर्णि, 12 रुद्रसावर्णि,<BR> 13 रौच्य-दैवसावर्णि and 14 इंद्रसावर्णि).<BR>—3 A symbolical expression for the number ‘fourteen’.<BR>—4 A man, mankind (opp. evil spirits); मनवे शासदव्रतान् Rv. 1. 130. 8.<BR>—5 Thought, thinking or mental faculty (Ved.).<BR>—6 A prayer, sacred text or spell (मन्त्र); मनुं साधयतो राज्यं<BR> नाकपृष्ठमनाशके Mb. 13. 7. 18.<BR>—7 (pl.) Mental powers; देहोऽसवोऽक्षा मनवो भूतमात्रा नात्मानमन्यं<BR> च विदुः परं यत् Bhāg. 6. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुः|मनु
मनुः + .{@-नुः@} <i>f.</i> The wife of Manu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्वन्तरम्, मनुजः, मनुजा, मनुजातः, मनुज्येष्ठः, मनुप्रणीत, मनुभूः, मनुराज्, मनुश्रेष्ठः, मनुसंहिता, मनुस्मृतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्वन्तरम्
मनुः + -अन्तरम् the period or age of a Manu; (this period, according<BR> to Ms. 1. 79, comprises 4,320,000 human years or ¹⁄₁₄th day of Brahmā,<BR> the fourteen <i>Manvantaras</i> making up one whole day; each of these<BR> fourteen periods is supposed to be presided over by its own Manu; six<BR> such periods have already passed away; we are at present living in the<BR> seventh, and seven more are yet to come); मन्वन्तरं तु दिव्यानां युगानामेकसप्ततिः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुजः|मनुज
मनुः + -जः a man, mankind. ˚अधिपः, ˚अधिपतिः, ˚ईश्वरः, ˚पतिः, ˚राजः<BR> a king, sovereign. ˚लोकः the world of men; <i>i. e.</i> the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुजा
मनुः + -जा a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुजातः|मनुजात
मनुः + -जातः a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुज्येष्ठः|मनुज्येष्ठ
मनुः + -ज्येष्ठः a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुप्रणीत
मनुः + -प्रणीत <i>a.</i> taught or expounded by Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुभूः
मनुः + -भूः a man, mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुराज्
मनुः + -राज् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुश्रेष्ठः|मनुश्रेष्ठ
मनुः + -श्रेष्ठः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुसंहिता
मनुः + -संहिता, -स्मृतिः the code of laws ascribed to the first Manu,<BR> the institutes of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुस्मृतिः|मनुस्मृति
मनुः + -संहिता, -स्मृतिः the code of laws ascribed to the first Manu,<BR> the institutes of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुषी
मनुषी A female, a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्य|मनुष्यः
मनुष्य <i>a.</i> [मनोरपत्यं यत् सुक् च] Friendly or useful to man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यः|मनुष्य
मनुष्य + .{@-ष्यः@}<BR>—1 A man, human being, mortal.<BR>—2 A mate.<BR>—3 Ved. A class of manes.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मनुष्येन्द्रः, मनुष्येश्वरः, मनुष्यकारः, मनुष्यगन्धर्वः,^1 मनुष्यजन्मन्, मनुष्यजातम्, मनुष्यजातिः, मनुष्यदेवः, मनुष्यधर्मः, मनुष्यधर्मन्, मनुष्यपोतः, मनुष्यमात्र, मनुष्यमारणम्, मनुष्ययज्ञः, मनुष्ययानम्, मनुष्यलोकः, मनुष्यविश्, मनुष्यविशा, मनुष्यशृङ्गम्, मनुष्यशोणितम्, मनुष्यसभा<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्येन्द्रः|मनुष्येन्द्र|मनुष्येंद्र
मनुष्य + -इन्द्रः, -ईश्वरः a king, sovereign; मार्गं मनुष्येश्वरधर्मपत्नी<BR> श्रुतेरिवार्थं स्मृतिरन्वगच्छत् R. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्येश्वरः|मनुष्येश्वर
मनुष्य + -इन्द्रः, -ईश्वरः a king, sovereign; मार्गं मनुष्येश्वरधर्मपत्नी<BR> श्रुतेरिवार्थं स्मृतिरन्वगच्छत् R. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यकारः|मनुष्यकार
मनुष्य + -कारः human exertion or effort; cf. पुरुषकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यगन्धर्वः|मनुष्यगन्धर्व
मनुष्य + -गन्धर्वः^1 <i>m.</i> (pl.) the human गन्धर्वs (as distinguished<BR> from देवगन्धर्वs).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यजन्मन्
मनुष्य + -जन्मन् <i>a.</i> begotten by a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यजातम्
मनुष्य + -जातम्, -जातिः <i>f.</i> mankind, human race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यजातिः|मनुष्यजाति
मनुष्य + -जातम्, -जातिः <i>f.</i> mankind, human race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यदेवः|मनुष्यदेव
मनुष्य + -देवः<BR>—1 a king; निशम्य देवानुचरस्य वाचं मनुष्यदेवः पुनरप्युवाच R. 2. 52.<BR>—2 a god among men, a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यधर्मः|मनुष्यधर्म
मनुष्य + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the duty of man.<BR>—2 the character of man, human character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यधर्मन्|मनुष्यधर्म्मन्
मनुष्य + -धर्मन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यपोतः|मनुष्यपोत
मनुष्य + -पोतः a little boy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यमात्र
मनुष्य + -मात्र <i>a.</i> only a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यमारणम्
मनुष्य + -मारणम् homicide; मनुष्यमारणे क्षिप्रं चौरवत् किल्बिषं भवेत् Ms. 8. 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्ययज्ञः|मनुष्ययज्ञ
मनुष्य + -यज्ञः hospitality, hospitable reception of guests, one of the<BR> five daily acts of a house-holder; see नृयज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्ययानम्
मनुष्य + -यानम् a litter, palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यलोकः|मनुष्यलोक
मनुष्य + -लोकः the world of mortals, the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यविश्
मनुष्य + -विश्, -विशा <i>f.</i>, {@-विशम्@}<BR> human race, mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यविशा
मनुष्य + -विश्, -विशा <i>f.</i>, {@-विशम्@}<BR> human race, mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यशृङ्गम्
मनुष्य + -शृङ्गम् impossibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यशोणितम्
मनुष्य + -शोणितम् human blood; (पपौ) कुतूहलेनेव मनुष्यशोणितम् R. 3. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यसभा
मनुष्य + -सभा<BR>—1 an assembly of men.<BR>—2 a crowd, multitude.<BR>—3 a place of meeting, assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यता
मनुष्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Manhood.<BR>—2 Humanity; दुर्लभं त्रयमेवैतद् देवानुग्रहहेतुकम् । मनुष्यत्वं<BR> मुमुक्षत्वं महापुरुषसंश्रयः ॥ Vivekacūḍāmaṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनुष्यत्वम्
मनुष्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Manhood.<BR>—2 Humanity; दुर्लभं त्रयमेवैतद् देवानुग्रहहेतुकम् । मनुष्यत्वं<BR> मुमुक्षत्वं महापुरुषसंश्रयः ॥ Vivekacūḍāmaṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1235-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोतृ
मनोतृ <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 An inventor.<BR>—2 A manager; धिया मनोता प्रथमो मनीषी Rv. 9. 91. 1.<BR>—3 An honourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मनोन्मनी
मनोन्मनी A form of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्र्|मंत्र्
मन्त्र् €10 Ā. (मन्त्रयते, but sometimes मन्त्रयति also, मन्त्रित)<BR>—1 To consult, deliberate, ponder over, hold consultation, take counsel;<BR> एतान् सर्वान् समानीय मन्त्रयित्वा च लक्ष्मण Rām. 7. 91. 3; न<BR> हि स्त्रीभिः सह मन्त्रयितुं युज्यते Pt. 5; Ms. 7. 146.<BR>—2 To advise, counsel, give advice; युद्धे विक्रमतश्चैव हितं मन्त्रयतस्तथा<BR> Rām. 6. 115. 8; अतीतलाभस्य च रक्षणार्थं … … यन्मन्त्र्यतेऽसौ<BR> परमो हि मन्त्रः Pt. 2. 182.<BR>—3 To consecrate with sacred texts, enchant with spells or charms.<BR>—4 To say, speak, talk, mutter; किमपि हृदये कृत्वा मन्त्रयेथे Ś. 1;<BR> किमेकाकिनी मन्त्रयसि Ś. 6; हला संगीतशालापरिसरेऽवलोकिताद्वितीया<BR> त्वं किं मन्त्रयन्त्यासीः Māl. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रः|मन्त्र|मंत्र|मंत्रः
मन्त्रः [मन्त्र्-अच्]<BR>—1 A Vedic hymn or sacred prayer (addressed to any deity), a sacred text;<BR> (it is of three kinds:− it is called ऋच् if metrical and intended<BR> to be loudly recited; यजुस् if in prose and muttered in a low tone;<BR> and सामन् if, being metrical, it is intended for chanting).<BR>—2 The portion of the Veda including the Samhitā and distinguished from<BR> the <i>Brāhmaṇa</i>; q. v.<BR>—3 A charm, spell, an incantation; सोऽहमस्मि मन्त्रसिद्धः Dk. 54;<BR> न हि जीवन्ति जना मनागमन्त्राः Bv. 1. 111; अचिन्त्यो हि मणिमन्त्रौषधीनां<BR> प्रभावः Ratn. 2; R. 2. 32, 5. 57.<BR>—4 A formula (of prayer) sacred to any deity, as ॐ नमः शिवाय &c.<BR>—5 Consultation, deliberation, counsel, advice, resolution, plan; तस्य<BR> संवृतमन्त्रस्य R. 1. 20; मन्त्रः प्रतिदिनं तस्य बभूव सह मन्त्रिभिः 17. 50;<BR> Pt. 2. 182; Ms. 7. 58; मन्त्रपूर्वाः सर्वारम्भाः Kau. A. 1. 15;<BR> also पञ्चाङ्गो मन्त्रः.<BR>—6 Secret plan or consultation, a secret; मन्त्रो योध इवाधीरः सर्वाङ्गैः<BR> संवृतैरपि Śi. 2. 29.<BR>—7 Policy, statesmanship.<BR>—8 A means, contrivance; किं तु मन्त्रं प्रदास्यामि यो वै तान् निहनिष्यति<BR> Rām. 7. 6. 10.<BR>—9 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—10 of Śiva.<BR>—11 (In astrol.) The fifth mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्त्राक्षरम्, मन्त्राधिकारः, मन्त्राधिराजः, मन्त्राराधनम्, मन्त्रोक्त, मन्त्रोदकम्, मन्त्रजलम्, मन्त्रतोयम्, मन्त्रवारि, मन्त्रोपष्टम्भः, मन्त्रकरणम्, मन्त्रकर्कश, मन्त्रकारः, मन्त्रकार्यम्, मन्त्रकालः, मन्त्रकुशल,^1 मन्त्रकृत्, मन्त्रकृत, मन्त्रगण्डकः, मन्त्रगुप्तिः, मन्त्रगूढः, मन्त्रगृहम्, मन्त्रग्रहः, मन्त्रजा, मन्त्रजागरः, मन्त्रजिह्वः, मन्त्रझ, मन्त्रतत्त्वम्, मन्त्रतन्त्र, मन्त्रदः, मन्त्रदातृ, मन्त्रदर्शिन्, मन्त्रदीधितिः, मन्त्रदृश्, मन्त्रदेवता, मन्त्रधरः, मन्त्रधारिन्, मन्त्रनिर्णयः, मन्त्रपदम्, मन्त्रपूत, मन्त्रप्रचारः, मन्त्रप्रभावः, मन्त्रप्रयोगः, मन्त्रयुक्तिः, मन्त्रबीजम्, मन्त्रवीजम्, मन्त्रभेदः, मन्त्रमूर्तिः, मन्त्रमूलम्, मन्त्रयन्त्रम्, मन्त्रयुक्तिः, मन्त्रयोगः, मन्त्ररक्षा, मन्त्रवर्जम्, मन्त्रवहः, मन्त्रवादः, मन्त्रवादिन्, मन्त्रविद्, मन्त्रविद्या, मन्त्रशक्तिः, मन्त्रश्रुतिः, मन्त्रसंस्कारः, मन्त्रसंस्क्रिया, मन्त्रसंवरणम्, मन्त्रसंहिता, मन्त्रसाधकः, मन्त्रसाधनम्, मन्त्रसाध्य, मन्त्रसिद्ध, मन्त्रसिद्धिः, मन्त्रसूत्रम्, मन्त्रस्नानम्, मन्त्रस्पृश्, मन्त्रहीन<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्राक्षरम्
मन्त्रः + -अक्षरम् a syllable in a spell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्राधिकारः
मन्त्रः + -अधिकारः business of council meetings; Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्राधिराजः|मन्त्राधिराज
मन्त्रः + -अधिराजः supreme over all spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्राराधनम्
मन्त्रः + -आराधनम् endeavouring to obtain by spells or incantations; मन्त्राराधनतत्परेण<BR> मनसा नीताः श्मशाने निशाः Bh. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रोक्त
मन्त्रः + -उक्त <i>a.</i> mentioned in a hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रोदकम्
मन्त्रः + -उदकम्, -जलम्, -तोयम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> water consecrated by means<BR> of spells, charmed water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रजलम्
मन्त्रः + -उदकम्, -जलम्, -तोयम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> water consecrated by means<BR> of spells, charmed water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतोयम्
मन्त्रः + -उदकम्, -जलम्, -तोयम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> water consecrated by means<BR> of spells, charmed water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवारि
मन्त्रः + -उदकम्, -जलम्, -तोयम्, -वारि <i>n.</i> water consecrated by means<BR> of spells, charmed water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रोपष्टम्भः|मन्त्रोपष्टम्भ|मंत्रोपष्टंभ
मन्त्रः + -उपष्टम्भः backing up by advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकरणम्
मन्त्रः + -करणम्<BR>—1 Vedic texts.<BR>—2 composing or reciting sacred texts; P. I. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकर्कश
मन्त्रः + -कर्कश <i>a.</i> advocating a stern policy; येऽपि मन्त्रकर्कशाः<BR> शास्त्रतन्त्रकाराः Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकारः|मन्त्रकार|मंत्रकार
मन्त्रः + -कारः the author of Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकार्यम्
मन्त्रः + -कार्यम् subject of consultation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकालः|मन्त्रकाल|मंत्रकाल
मन्त्रः + -कालः time of consultation or deliberation; स्त्रीम्लेच्छव्याधितव्यङ्गान्<BR> मन्त्रकालेऽपसारयेत् Ms. 7. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकुशल|मंत्रकुशल
मन्त्रः + -कुशल^1 <i>a.</i> skilled in giving advice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकृत्|मंत्रकृत्
मन्त्रः + -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an author or composer of Vedic hymns; अप्यग्रणीर्मन्त्रकृतामृषीणां<BR> कुशाग्रबुद्धे कुशली गुरुस्ते R. 5. 4, 1. 61, 15. 31.<BR>—2 one who recites a sacred text.<BR>—3 a counsellor, an adviser.<BR>—4 an ambassador; यद्वा अयं मन्त्रकृद्वो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">Page1236-2</a>]<BR> भगवानखिलेश्वरः Bhāg. 3. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रकृत
मन्त्रः + -कृत <i>a.</i> Consecrated by mantras; यस्ते मन्त्रकृतः पाणिरग्नौ<BR> पापे मया धृतः Rām. 2. 14. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगण्डकः|मन्त्रगण्डक|मंत्रगंडक
मन्त्रः + -गण्डकः knowledge, science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगुप्तिः|मन्त्रगुप्ति|मंत्रगुप्ति
मन्त्रः + -गुप्तिः <i>f.</i> secret counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगूढः|मन्त्रगूढ|मंत्रगूढ
मन्त्रः + -गूढः a spy, a secret emissary or agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रगृहम्
मन्त्रः + -गृहम् a council-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रग्रहः
मन्त्रः + -ग्रहः listening to the counsels of ministers; सप्तमे तु मन्त्रग्रहो<BR> दूतभिप्रेषणानि च Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रजा
मन्त्रः + -जा the power of spells; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रजागरः|मन्त्रजागर
मन्त्रः + -जागरः recital of Vedic texts at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रजिह्वः|मन्त्रजिह्व|मंत्रजिह्व
मन्त्रः + -जिह्वः fire; अमृतं नाम यत् सन्तो मन्त्रनिह्वेषु जुह्वति Śi. 2. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रझ|मन्त्रझः
मन्त्रः + -झ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing sacred texts.<BR>—2 skilled in counsel.<BR>—3 skilled in spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रझः|मन्त्रझ
मन्त्रः + -झ + ({@-झः@})<BR>—1 a counsellor, adviser.<BR>—2 a learned Brāhmaṇa; मन्त्रज्ञैर्मन्त्रिभिश्चैव विनीतः प्रविशेत् सभाम् Ms.<BR>—3 a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतत्त्वम्
मन्त्रः + -तत्त्वम् the essence of counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतन्त्र
मन्त्रः + -तन्त्र see अमन्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदः|मन्त्रद|मंत्रद
मन्त्रः + -दः, -दातृ <i>m.</i> a spiritual preceptor or teacher; पिता भवति<BR> मन्त्रदः Ms. 2. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदातृ|मंत्रदातृ
मन्त्रः + -दः, -दातृ <i>m.</i> a spiritual preceptor or teacher; पिता भवति<BR> मन्त्रदः Ms. 2. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदर्शिन्|मंत्रदर्शिन्
मन्त्रः + -दर्शिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a seer of Vedic hymns.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa versed in the Vedas; यो ह्यग्निः स द्विजो विप्रैर्मन्त्रदर्शिभिरुच्यते Ms. 3. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदीधितिः|मन्त्रदीधिति|मंत्रदीधिति
मन्त्रः + -दीधितिः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदृश्|मंत्रदृश्
मन्त्रः + -दृश् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing sacred texts.<BR>—2 skilled in counsel or spells. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a seer of Vedic hymns<BR>—2 an adviser, a counsellor; अथाह तन्मन्त्रदृशां वरीयान् यन्मन्त्रिणो<BR> वैदुरिकं वदन्ति Bhāg. 3. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रदेवता|मंत्रदेवता
मन्त्रः + -देवता the deity invoked in a sacred text or <i>mantra</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रधरः|मन्त्रधर
मन्त्रः + -धरः, -धारिन् <i>m.</i> a counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रधारिन्
मन्त्रः + -धरः, -धारिन् <i>m.</i> a counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रनिर्णयः|मन्त्रनिर्णय|मंत्रनिर्णय
मन्त्रः + -निर्णयः final decision after deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रपदम्
मन्त्रः + -पदम् the words of a sacred text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रपूत|मंत्रपूत|मन्त्रपूतः
मन्त्रः + -पूत <i>a.</i> purified by <i>mantras</i>. ˚आत्मन् <i>m.</i> an<BR> epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रप्रचारः
मन्त्रः + -प्रचारः the course of counsel or procedure; Pt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रप्रभावः|मन्त्रप्रभाव
मन्त्रः + -प्रभावः the power of a spell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रप्रयोगः|मन्त्रप्रयोग|मंत्रप्रयोग
मन्त्रः + -प्रयोगः, -युक्तिः <i>f.</i> application of spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयुक्तिः|मन्त्रयुक्ति
मन्त्रः + -प्रयोगः, -युक्तिः <i>f.</i> application of spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रबीजम्
मन्त्रः + -बीजम्, -वीजम् the first syllable of a spell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवीजम्
मन्त्रः + -बीजम्, -वीजम् the first syllable of a spell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रभेदः|मन्त्रभेद|मंत्रभेद
मन्त्रः + -भेदः breach or betrayal of counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रमूर्तिः|मन्त्रमूर्ति|मंत्रमूर्ति|मन्त्रमूर्त्ति
मन्त्रः + -मूर्तिः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रमूलम्
मन्त्रः + -मूलम् magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयन्त्रम्
मन्त्रः + -यन्त्रम् a mystical diagram with a magical formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयुक्तिः|मन्त्रयुक्ति
मन्त्रः + -युक्तिः application of spells; magical means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रयोगः|मन्त्रयोग|मंत्रयोग
मन्त्रः + -योगः<BR>—1 employment or application of spells.<BR>—2 magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्ररक्षा
मन्त्रः + -रक्षा not disclosing, keeping a secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवर्जम्|मंत्रवर्जम्
मन्त्रः + -वर्जम् <i>ind.</i> without the use of spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवहः|मन्त्रवह
मन्त्रः + -वहः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवादः|मन्त्रवाद
मन्त्रः + -वादः the substance of sacred texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवादिन्
मन्त्रः + -वादिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a reciter of sacred texts.<BR>—2 an enchanter, a conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रविद्|मंत्रविद्
मन्त्रः + -विद् see मन्त्रज्ञ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रविद्या|मंत्रविद्या
मन्त्रः + -विद्या the science of spells, magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रशक्तिः|मन्त्रशक्ति
मन्त्रः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> the power of spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रश्रुतिः|मन्त्रश्रुति
मन्त्रः + -श्रुतिः a consultation overheard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसंस्कारः|मन्त्रसंस्कार|मंत्रसंस्कार
मन्त्रः + -संस्कारः any Saṃskāra or rite performed with sacred texts;<BR> अनृतावृतुकाले च मन्त्रसंस्कारकृत् पतिः Ms. 5. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसंस्क्रिया
मन्त्रः + -संस्क्रिया any magical rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसंवरणम्
मन्त्रः + -संवरणम् concealment of a design; मन्त्रसंवरणेनास्मि कुन्त्या<BR> दुःखेन योजितः Mb. 12. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसंहिता|मंत्रसंहिता
मन्त्रः + -संहिता the whole body of Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसाधकः|मन्त्रसाधक|मंत्रसाधक
मन्त्रः + -साधकः a magician, conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसाधनम्
मन्त्रः + -साधनम्<BR>—1 effecting or subduing by magic.<BR>—2 a spell, an incantation. —3 attainment of supernatural or magical powers<BR> (by muttering spells); चामुण्डे भगवति मन्त्रसाधनादावुद्दिष्टामुपनिहितां<BR> भजस्व पूजाम् Māl. 5. 25; K. 37, 40, 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसाध्य|मंत्रसाध्य
मन्त्रः + -साध्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 to be effected or subdued by magic or spells; Pt. 1. 65.<BR>—2 attainable by consultation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसिद्ध
मन्त्रः + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> possessing the power of spells, rendered efficacious;<BR> सोऽस्म्यहं मन्त्रसिद्धः Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसिद्धिः|मन्त्रसिद्धि|मंत्रसिद्धि
मन्त्रः + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the working or accomplishment of a spell.<BR>—2 the power which the possession or knowledge of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">Page1237-1</a>]<BR> a spell gives to a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1236-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रसूत्रम्
मन्त्रः + -सूत्रम् a charm fastened on a string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रस्नानम्
मन्त्रः + -स्नानम् the recitation of particular texts as a substitute for ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रस्पृश्
मन्त्रः + -स्पृश् <i>a.</i> obtaining (anything) by means of spells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रहीन|मंत्रहीन
मन्त्रः + -हीन <i>a.</i> destitute of or contrary to sacred hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रणम्
मन्त्रणम्, -णा<BR> [मन्त्र् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Deliberation, consultation; न तेऽस्त्यकार्यं मतिपूर्वमन्त्रणे Rām. 5. 48. 5.<BR>—2 Advising, counselling; ‘गर्र्वी खर्व … … मन्त्रणायन्त्रितः’ Stotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रणा
मन्त्रणम्, -णा<BR> [मन्त्र् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Deliberation, consultation; न तेऽस्त्यकार्यं मतिपूर्वमन्त्रणे Rām. 5. 48. 5.<BR>—2 Advising, counselling; ‘गर्र्वी खर्व … … मन्त्रणायन्त्रितः’ Stotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रणकम्
मन्त्रणकम् Invitation; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रतः|मन्त्रत
मन्त्रतः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With respect or according to the sacred texts.<BR>—2 Deliberately, advisedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रवत्|मंत्रवत्|मन्त्रवन्त्
मन्त्रवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attended with spells or incantations; अशिक्षतास्त्रं पितुरेव मन्त्रवत् R. 3. 31.<BR>—2 Initjated. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to sacred texts.<BR>—2 According to the rules of consultation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिः|मन्त्रि|मंत्रि|मंत्रिः
मन्त्रिः = मन्त्रिन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रित|मंत्रित|मन्त्रितः
मन्त्रित <i>p. p.</i> [मन्त्र्-क्त]<BR>—1 Consulted.<BR>—2 Counselled, advised; कच्चित् ते मन्त्रितो मन्त्रो राष्ट्रं न परिधावति<BR> Rām. 2. 100. 18.<BR>—3 Said, spoken.<BR>—4 Charmed, consecrated by <i>mantras</i>.<BR>—5 Settled, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रितम्
मन्त्रित + .{@-तम्@} Advice, counsel; सुयुद्धं वानराणां च सुग्रीवस्य च मन्त्रितम्<BR> Rām. 6. 112. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिन्|मंत्रिन्
मन्त्रिन् <i>a.</i> [मन्त्रयते मन्त्र् णिनि]<BR>—1 Wise, clever in counsel.<BR>—2 Familiar with sacred texts or spells. —3 Ved. Eloquent. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A minister, counsellor, a kingʼs minister; अजिताधिगमाय मन्त्रिभिर्युयुजे<BR> नीतिविशारदैरजः R. 8. 17; Ms. 8. 1.<BR>—2 A conjurer, an enchanter.<BR>—3 (In chess) The queen.<BR>—4 (In astrol.) The 12th mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्त्रिधुर, मन्त्रिपतिः, मन्त्रिप्रधानः, मन्त्रिप्रमुखः, मन्त्रिमुख्यः, मन्त्रिवरः, मन्त्रिश्रेष्ठः, मन्त्रिपरिषद्, मन्त्रिप्रकाण्डः, मन्त्रिश्रोत्रियः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिधुर|मंत्रिधुर
मन्त्रिन् + -धुर <i>a.</i> able to bear the burden of a ministerʼs office; सुसंवृतो<BR> मन्त्रिधुरैरमात्यैः शास्त्रकोविदैः Rām. 2. 100. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिपतिः|मन्त्रिपति|मंत्रिपति
मन्त्रिन् + -पतिः, -प्रधानः, -प्रमुखः, -मुख्यः, -वरः, -श्रेष्ठः the prime<BR> minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिप्रधानः|मन्त्रिप्रधान|मंत्रिप्रधान
मन्त्रिन् + -पतिः, -प्रधानः, -प्रमुखः, -मुख्यः, -वरः, -श्रेष्ठः the prime<BR> minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिप्रमुखः|मन्त्रिप्रमुख
मन्त्रिन् + -पतिः, -प्रधानः, -प्रमुखः, -मुख्यः, -वरः, -श्रेष्ठः the prime<BR> minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिमुख्यः|मन्त्रिमुख्य|मंत्रिमुख्य
मन्त्रिन् + -पतिः, -प्रधानः, -प्रमुखः, -मुख्यः, -वरः, -श्रेष्ठः the prime<BR> minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिवरः|मन्त्रिवर|मंत्रिवर
मन्त्रिन् + -पतिः, -प्रधानः, -प्रमुखः, -मुख्यः, -वरः, -श्रेष्ठः the prime<BR> minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिश्रेष्ठः|मन्त्रिश्रेष्ठ|मंत्रिश्रेष्ठ
मन्त्रिन् + -पतिः, -प्रधानः, -प्रमुखः, -मुख्यः, -वरः, -श्रेष्ठः the prime<BR> minister, premier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिपरिषद्
मन्त्रिन् + -परिषद् a council of ministers; इन्द्रस्य हि मन्त्रिपरिषद् ऋषीणां<BR> सहस्रम् Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिप्रकाण्डः|मन्त्रिप्रकाण्ड|मंत्रिप्रकांड
मन्त्रिन् + -प्रकाण्डः an excellent or eminent minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1237-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्त्रिश्रोत्रियः|मन्त्रिश्रोत्रिय|मंत्रिश्रोत्रिय
