मन्दोदरी|मंदोदरी
मन्द + -उदरी N. of the wife of Rāvaṇa, regarded as one of the five<BR> very chaste women; cf. अहल्या. She advised her husband to deliver<BR> Sītā to Rāma and thus save himself from certain ruin, but he did not<BR> heed her; मन्दोदरीकुटिलकोमलकेशपाशमन्दारदाममकरन्दरसं पिबन्तः P. R. 1. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोष्ण|मंदोष्ण|मन्दोष्णं
मन्द + -उष्ण <i>a.</i> tepid, lukewarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दोष्णम्
मन्द + -उष्ण + .({@-ष्णम्@}) gentle heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दौत्सुक्य|मंदौत्सुक्य
मन्द + -औत्सुक्य <i>a.</i> slackened in eagerness, cast down, disinclined;<BR> मन्दौत्सुक्योऽस्मि नगरगमनं प्रति Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

