मन्दता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Slowness, inactivity.<BR>—2 Dulness.<BR>—3 Foolishness, stupidity, simplicity; उच्चैरस्यति मन्दतामरसताम्<BR> Candr. 1. 1.<BR>—4 Weakness.<BR>—5 Littleness, smallness; मन्दत्वमापन्नः Pt. 2. 167 ‘became less, subsided’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दयति
मन्दयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To weaken, slacken, diminish.<BR>—2 To retard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दायते
मन्दायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To go slowly, tarry, lag behind, loiter, delay; मन्दायन्ते न खलु<BR> सुहृदामभ्युपेतार्थकृत्याः Me. 40; V. 3. 15.<BR>—2 To be weak or faint, grow dim; दिशि मन्दायते तेजो दक्षिणस्यां रवेरपि R. 4. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दीकृ|मंदीकृ
मन्दीकृ €8 U. To weaken, diminish, relax, slacken; रथस्य मन्दीकृतो<BR> वेगः Ś. 1; मन्दीचकार मरणव्यवसायबुद्धिम् Ku. 4. 45; Ve. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दीभू
मन्दीभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To become weak, be relaxed or slackened.<BR>—2 To grow less, diminish, subside, abate; अपि कालविप्रकर्षान्मन्दीभूतः<BR> पितृमरणशोकः Mv. 5; मन्दीभूतशोकः K. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दटः|मन्दट|मंदट|मंदटः
मन्दटः The coral tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दनम्
मन्दनम्<BR>—1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>—2 Chatter of husband and wife (variant of मन्मनः); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दयन्ती
मन्दयन्ती An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दर|मंदर|मन्दरः
मन्दर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Slow, tardy, dull.<BR>—2 Thick, dense; firm.<BR>—3 Large, bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दरः|मन्दर|मंदर
मन्दर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 N. of a mountain (used by the gods and demons as a churning stick when<BR> they churned the ocean for nectar); पृषतैर्मन्दरोद्धूतैः क्षीरोर्मय<BR> इवाच्युतम् R. 4. 27; अभिनवजलसुन्दर धृतमन्दर ए Gīt. 1; शोभैव<BR> मन्दरक्षुब्धक्षुभिताम्भोधिवर्णना Śi. 2. 107; Ki. 5. 30.<BR>—2 A necklace of pearls (of 8 or 16 strings).<BR>—3 Heaven.<BR>—4 A mirror.<BR>—5 One of the five trees in Indraʼs<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">Page1239-1</a>]<BR> paradise; see मन्दार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दरम्
मन्दर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Slowly, sluggishly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्दरावासा, मन्दरवासिनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1238-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दरावासा|मंदरावासा
मन्दर + -आवासा, -वासिनी Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दरवासिनी|मंदरवासिनी
मन्दर + -आवासा, -वासिनी Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दसानः|मन्दसान|मंदसानः
मन्दसानः<BR>—1 N. of fire.<BR>—2 Life.<BR>—3 Sleep; (also written मन्दसानु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाकः|मन्दाक|मंदाक|मन्दाकं|मंदाकः
मन्दाकः<BR>—1 A current, stream.<BR>—2 Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दाकिनी|मंदाकिनी
मन्दाकिनी [मन्दमकति अक्-णिनि]<BR>—1 The river Ganges; मन्दाकिनी भाति नगोपकण्ठे मुक्तावली कण्ठगतेव<BR> भूमेः R. 13. 48; Ku. 1. 29.<BR>—2 The river of heaven, celestial Ganges (मन्दाकिनी वियद्गङ्गा); मन्दाकिन्याः<BR> सलिलशिशिरैः सेव्यमाना मरुद्भिः Me. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दामणिः
मन्दामणिः A big jar, earthern water vessel; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारः|मन्दार|मंदार|मंदारः
मन्दारः [मन्द्-आरक्]<BR>—1 The coral tree, one of the five trees in Indraʼs paradise; हस्तप्राप्यस्तबकनमितो<BR> बालमन्दारवृक्षः Me. 77, 69; V. 4. 35; वृन्दारकारिविजये सुरलोकलब्धमन्दारमाल्यमधुवासितवासभूमिः Rām. Ch.<BR>—2 The plant called Arka, Calotropis Gigantea<BR>—3 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>—4 Heaven.<BR>—5 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारम्
मन्दारः + .{@-रम्@} A flower of the coral tree; विनिद्रमन्दाररजोरुणाङ्गुली<BR> Ku. 5. 80; R. 6. 23.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्दारमाला, मन्दारषष्ठी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारमाला|मंदारमाला
मन्दारः + -माला a garland of Mandāra flowers; मन्दारमाला हरिणा पिनद्धा Ś. 7. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारषष्ठी
मन्दारः + -षष्ठी and {@-सप्तमी@}<BR> the sixth and seventh days in the bright half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारकः|मन्दारक|मंदारक|मंदारकः
मन्दारकः, मन्दारवः, मन्दारुः<BR> The coral tree; see मन्दार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारवः|मन्दारव|मंदारव|मंदारवः
मन्दारकः, मन्दारवः, मन्दारुः<BR> The coral tree; see मन्दार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दारुः|मन्दारु|मंदारु|मंदारुः
मन्दारकः, मन्दारवः, मन्दारुः<BR> The coral tree; see मन्दार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिकुकुरः|मन्दिकुकुर
मन्दिकुकुरः A kind of fish (also read as मल्लिकुकुडः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिमन्|मंदिमन्
मन्दिमन् <i>m.</i> [मन्द-इमनिच्]<BR>—1 Slowness, tardiness.<BR>—2 Dulness, stupidity, folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरम्
मन्दिरम् [मन्द्यतेऽत्र मन्द् किरच्] A dwelling house, habitation,<BR> place, mansion; प्रावेशयन्मन्दिरमृद्धमेनम् Ku. 7. 55; Bk. 8. 96;<BR> R. 12. 83; मणिमयमन्दिरमध्ये पश्यति पिपीलिका छिद्रम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 An abode, a dwelling in general; as in क्षीराब्धिमन्दिरः.<BR>—3 A town; विनिक्षिप्य बलं सर्वं बहिरन्तश्च मन्दिरे Rām. 6. 12. 3.<BR>—4 A camp.<BR>—5 A temple.<BR>—6 The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरः|मन्दिर|मंदिर|मंदिरं|मन्दिरं
मन्दिरम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The sea.<BR>—2 The hollow of the knee, ham.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्दिरपशुः, मन्दिरमणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरपशुः|मन्दिरपशु|मंदिरपशु
मन्दिरम् + -पशुः a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरमणिः|मन्दिरमणि
मन्दिरम् + -मणिः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दिरा
मन्दिरा A stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरकम्
मन्दुरकम् A kind of mat; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरा|मंदुरा
मन्दुरा [मन्द् उरच् Uṇ. 1. 38]<BR>—1 A stable for horses, a stable in general; प्रभ्रष्टोऽयं प्लवङ्गः<BR> प्रविशति नृपतेर्मन्दिरं मन्दुरायाः Ratn. 2. 2; R. 16. 41; क्षुराञ्चलैः<BR> क्षोभितमन्दुरोदरम् N.; मन्दुरायां निरुद्धोऽपि विद्रुतोऽभूद्धरिर्हरेः ।<BR> Śiva B. 21. 74.<BR>—2 A bed, mattress.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्दुरापतिः, मन्दुरापालः, मन्दुराभूषणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरापतिः|मन्दुरापति
मन्दुरा + -पतिः, -पालः the manager of a stable; a groom; शुश्राव … …<BR> असौ परस्परालापं मन्दुरायामपालयोः Dharmābhyudayamahākāvya 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुरापालः|मन्दुरापाल
मन्दुरा + -पतिः, -पालः the manager of a stable; a groom; शुश्राव … …<BR> असौ परस्परालापं मन्दुरायामपालयोः Dharmābhyudayamahākāvya 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्दुराभूषणम्
मन्दुरा + -भूषणम् a species of monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द्र|मंद्र|मन्द्रः
मन्द्र <i>a.</i> [मन्द् रक् Uṇ. 2. 13] Low, deep, grave, hollow,<BR> rumbling (as sound); पयोदमन्द्रध्वनिना धरित्री<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">Page1239-2</a>]<BR> Ki. 16. 3, 7. 22; Me. 101; R. 6. 56.<BR>—2 Ved. Delightful, pleasing, pleasant; एवं ब्रुवाणे वैकुण्ठे भृगुस्तन्मन्द्रया<BR> गिरा Bhāg. 10. 89. 13.<BR>—3 Praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्द्रः|मन्द्र|मंद्र
मन्द्र + .{@-न्द्रः@}<BR>—1 A deep sound, low tone.<BR>—2 A kind of drum.<BR>—3 A kind of elephant; ‘भद्रा मन्द्रा मृगाश्चेति विज्ञेयास्त्रिविधा गजाः’;<BR> cf. Rām. 1. 6. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्धातृ|मंधातृ
मन्धातृ <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 An intelligent man.<BR>—2 A devout or pious man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथः|मन्मथ
मन्मथः<BR>—1 Cupid, the god of love; मन्मथो मां मथ्नन्निजनाम सान्वयं करोति<BR> Dk. 1; Me. 75; न मन्मथस्त्वं स हि नास्तिमूर्तिः N. 8. 29.<BR>—2 Love, passion; प्रबोध्यते सुप्त इवाद्य मन्मथः Ṛs. 1. 8; so परोक्षमन्मथः<BR> जनः Ś. 2. 19.<BR>—3 The wood apple.<BR>—4 N. of a संवत्सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथा
मन्मथः + .{@-था@} N. of Dākṣāyaṇī. ━<i>a.</i> Enchanting, attractive; साक्षान्मन्मथमन्मथः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 32. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्मथानन्दः, मन्मथालयः, मन्मथकर, मन्मथबन्धुः, मन्मथयुद्धम्, मन्मथलेखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथानन्दः|मन्मथानन्द|मन्मथानंद
मन्मथः + -आनन्दः a kind of mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथालयः|मन्मथालय
मन्मथः + -आलयः<BR>—1 the mango tree.<BR>—2 pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथकर
मन्मथः + -कर <i>a.</i> exciting love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथबन्धुः|मन्मथबन्धु
मन्मथः + -बन्धुः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथयुद्धम्
मन्मथः + -युद्धम् amorous strife, sexual union, copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथलेखः|मन्मथलेख
मन्मथः + -लेखः a love letter; क्लान्तो मन्मथलेख एष नलिनीपत्रे नखैरर्पितः Ś. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मथिन्
मन्मथिन् <i>a.</i> Amorous, enamoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मन्
मन्मन् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Wish, desire.<BR>—2 Hymn, prayer &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मनः|मन्मन
मन्मनः<BR>—1 Confidential whispering (दंपत्योर्जल्पितं मन्दम्); करोति सहकारस्य<BR> कलिकोत्कलिकोत्तरं । मन्मनो मन्मनोऽप्येष मत्तकोकिलनिस्वनः Kāv. 3. 11.<BR>—2 The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्मनत्वम्
मन्मनत्वम् A particular defect of the organs of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्य
मन्य <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Thinking oneself to be, as in पण्डितंमन्य.<BR>—2 Appearing as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्या
मन्या [मन्यतेऽनया मन्या गलपार्श्वशिरा P. III. 3. 59. Sk.]<BR>—1 The nape or back of the neck; दोषास्तु दुष्टास्त्रय एव मन्या Suśr.<BR> (also मन्याका).<BR>—2 Knowledge.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्याग्रहः, मन्यास्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्याग्रहः|मन्याग्रह
मन्या + -ग्रहः Contraction of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्यास्तम्भः|मन्यास्तम्भ
मन्या + -स्तम्भः Stiffness of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्युः|मन्यु
मन्युः [मन्-युच् Uṇ. 3. 20]<BR>—1 Anger, wrath, resentment, indignation, rage; बाहुप्रतिष्टम्भविवृद्धमन्युः<BR> R. 2. 32, 49, 11. 46; नियमितमनोमन्युर्दृष्टा मया रुदती प्रिया Nāg. 2. 6.<BR>—2 Grief, sorrow, affliction, distress; निकृन्तन्मर्माणि क्रकच इव<BR> मन्युर्विरमति U. 4. 3; Ki. 1. 35; यास्यन् सुतस्तप्स्यति मां सुमन्युम्<BR> Bk. 1. 23; also 3. 49.<BR>—3 Wretched or miserable state, meanness.<BR>—4 A sacrifice; प्रसहेत रणे तवानुजान् द्विषतां कः शतमन्युतेजसः Ki. 2. 23.<BR>—5 Spirit, mettle, courage (as of horses).<BR>—6 Ardour, zeal.<BR>—7 Pride.<BR>—8 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—9 Of Agni.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मन्युसूक्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्युसूक्तम्
मन्युः + -सूक्तम् the hymns of Manyu (Rv. 10. 83 and 84).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मन्युमत्|मन्युमन्त्
मन्युमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Angry, wrathful.<BR>—2 Sorrowful, distressed.<BR>—3 Spirited, energetic; यशस्विनी मन्युमती कुले जाता विभावरी Mb. 5. 133. 2.<BR>—4 Vehement, passionate. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपष्टः|मपष्ट
मप(पु)ष्टः, -ष्टकः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपुष्टः|मपुष्ट
मप(पु)ष्टः, -ष्टकः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मपष्टकः|मपष्टक
मप(पु)ष्टः, -ष्टकः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1239-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मभ्र्
मभ्र् €1 P. (मभ्रति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मम
मम (Gen. sing. of अस्मद् the first personal pronoun) My, mine.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ममकारः, ममकृत्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममकारः|ममकार
मम + -कारः, -कृत्यम् interesting oneself about anything, self-interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममकृत्यम्
मम + -कारः, -कृत्यम् interesting oneself about anything, self-interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममता
ममता [मम भावः तल्]<BR>—1 The feeling of <i>‘meum’</i>, the sense of ownership, self-interest, selfishness.<BR>—2 Pride, arrogance, self-sufficiency.<BR>—3 Individuality.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: ममतायुक्त, ममताशून्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममतायुक्त|ममतायुक्तः
ममता + -युक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 a miser.<BR>—2 an egoist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममताशून्य
ममता + -शून्य <i>a.</i> devoid of interest (for us).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममत्वम्
ममत्वम्<BR>—1 Regarding as ‘mine’ or oneʼs own, sense of ownership.<BR>—2 Affectionate regard, attachment to, regard for; क्षुद्रेऽपि नूनं शरणं<BR> प्रपन्ने ममत्वमुच्चैःशिरसां सतीव Ku. 1. 12.<BR>—3 Arrogance, pride; ममत्वं कृ<BR>—1 To be attached to.<BR>—2 To envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ममापतालः|ममापताल
ममापतालः An object of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मब्
मब् €1 P. To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मम्मटः|मम्मट
मम्मटः N. of the author of the Kāvyaprakāśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय्
मय् €1 Ā. (मयते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मय|मयः
मय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>) An affix used to indicate ‘made of’<BR>, ‘consisting or composed of’, ‘full of’; कनकमय, काष्ठमय, तेजोमय, जलमय &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयः|मय
मय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 N. of a demon, the architect of the demons. (He built the ‘three cities’<BR> for the demons; cf. त्रिपुर. He is also said to have built a splendid<BR> hall for the Pāṇḍavas); सानन्दं देवताभिर्मयपुरदहने धूर्जटिः<BR> पातु युष्मान् Ve. 1. 3.<BR>—2 A horse.<BR>—3 A camel.<BR>—4 A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मया
मय + .{@-या@} Medical treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयी
मय + .{@-यी@} A mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयटः|मयट
मयटः A hut of grass or leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयष्टः|मयष्ट
मय(यु)ष्टः, -ष्टकः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुष्टः
मय(यु)ष्टः, -ष्टकः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयष्टकः|मयष्टक
मय(यु)ष्टः, -ष्टकः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयस्
मयस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Pleasure, delight, satisfaction; सरस्वती नः<BR> सुभगा मयस्करत् Rv. 1. 89. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मयोभव, मयोभुव, मयोभु, मयोभू<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयोभव
मयस् + -भव, -भुव, -भु, -भू <i>a.</i> causing pleasure,<BR> delighting; आपो हि ष्ठा मयोभुवः Rv. 10. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयोभुव
मयस् + -भव, -भुव, -भु, -भू <i>a.</i> causing pleasure,<BR> delighting; आपो हि ष्ठा मयोभुवः Rv. 10. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयोभु
मयस् + -भव, -भुव, -भु, -भू <i>a.</i> causing pleasure,<BR> delighting; आपो हि ष्ठा मयोभुवः Rv. 10. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयोभू
मयस् + -भव, -भुव, -भु, -भू <i>a.</i> causing pleasure,<BR> delighting; आपो हि ष्ठा मयोभुवः Rv. 10. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयिवसु
मयिवसु <i>a.</i> Good in me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुः|मयु
मयुः<BR>—1 A <i>Kinnara</i>, a celestial musician.<BR>—2 A deer, an antelope.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मयुराजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयुराजः|मयुराज
मयुः + -राजः an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूखः|मयूख
मयूखः [मा ऊख मयादेशः Uṇ. 5. 25]<BR>—1 A ray of light, beam, ray, lustre, brightness; विसृजति हिमगर्भैरग्निमिन्दुर्मयूखैः<BR> Ś. 3. 4; R. 2. 46; Śi. 4. 56; Ki. 5. 5, 8.<BR>—2 Beauty.<BR>—3 A flame.<BR>—4 The pin of a sun-dial.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मयूखेशः, मयूखमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूखेशः|मयूखेश
मयूखः + -ईशः, -मालिन् the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूखमालिन्
मयूखः + -ईशः, -मालिन् the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूखिन्
मयूखिन् <i>a.</i> Radiant, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरः|मयूर
मयूरः [मी ऊरन् Uṇ. 1. 67]<BR>—1 A peacock; स्मरति गिरिमयूरे एष देव्याः U. 3. 20; फणी मयूरस्य<BR> तले निषीदति Ṛs. 1. 13.<BR>—2 A kind of flower.<BR>—3 N. of a poet (author of the सूर्यशतक); यस्याश्चोरश्चिकुरनिकरः<BR> कर्णपूरो मयूरः P. R. 1. 22.<BR>—4 A kind of instrument for measuring time.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">Page1240-2</a>]<BR>—5 (In music) A kind of gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरी
मयूरः + .{@-री@} A pea-hen; (Proverb:− वरं तत्कालोपनता तित्तिरी न पुनर्दिवसान्तरिता<BR> मयूरी Vb. 1., or वरमद्य कपोतो न श्वो मयूरः ‘a bird in the hand is worth two in the bush’<BR>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरम्
मयूरः + .{@-रम्@} A particular posture in sitting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मयूरारिः, मयूरोल्लासकः, मयूरकेतुः, मयूरगतिः, मयूरग्रीवकम्, मयूरघृतम्, मयूरचटकः, मयूरचूडा, मयूरतुत्थम्, मयूरनृत्यम्, मयूरपत्रिन्, मयूरपदकम्, मयूरपिच्छम्, मयूररथः, मयूरव्यंसकः, मयूरशिखा, मयूरसारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरारिः|मयूरारि
मयूरः + -अरिः a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरोल्लासकः|मयूरोल्लासक
मयूरः + -उल्लासकः the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरकेतुः|मयूरकेतु
मयूरः + -केतुः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरगतिः|मयूरगति
मयूरः + -गतिः N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरग्रीवकम्
मयूरः + -ग्रीवकम् blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरघृतम्
मयूरः + -घृतम् a kind of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरचटकः|मयूरचटक
मयूरः + -चटकः the domestic cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरचूडा
मयूरः + -चूडा<BR>—1 a peacockʼs crest.<BR>—2 = मयूरीशिखा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरतुत्थम्
मयूरः + -तुत्थम् blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरनृत्यम्
मयूरः + -नृत्यम् the dance of a peacock; a position comparable to it; तदेतन्मथूरनृत्यमापद्यते ।<BR> तद्यथा मयूरस्य नृत्यतोऽन्यदपाव्रियतेऽन्यत् संव्रियते । एवमिहापि<BR> इदं संव्रियते तदपाव्रियते । ŚB. on MS. 7. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरपत्रिन्
मयूरः + -पत्रिन् <i>a.</i> feathered with peacockʼs feathers (as an arrow);<BR> जहार चान्येन मयूरपत्रिणा शरेण शक्रस्य महाशनिध्वजम् R. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरपदकम्
मयूरः + -पदकम् a scratch in the form of a peacockʼs foot (made with<BR> the fingernails).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरपिच्छम्
मयूरः + -पिच्छम् a peacockʼs tail or feather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूररथः|मयूररथ
मयूरः + -रथः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरव्यंसकः|मयूरव्यंसक
मयूरः + -व्यंसकः a cunning peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरशिखा
मयूरः + -शिखा<BR>—1 a peacockʼs crest.<BR>—2 a cockʼs comb.<BR>—3 N. of a medicinal plant, Celosia Cristata; cf. नीलकण्ठशिखा लघ्वी<BR> पित्तश्लेष्मातिसारजित् Bhāva P.; Mātaṅga L. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरसारिन्
मयूरः + -सारिन् <i>a.</i> strutting like a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरकः|मयूरक|मयूरकं
मयूरकः<BR>—1 A peacock.<BR>—2 A cockʼs comb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरकः|मयूरक|मयूरकं
मयूरकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@} Blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरकम्
मयूरकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@} Blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूरिका
मयूरिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A nose-ring; मनोज्ञनासिकान्यस्तचित्ररत्नमयूरिकाम् Śiva B. 20. 5.<BR>—2 A kind of venomous insect.<BR>—3 Hibiscus Cannabinus (Mar. भेंडी, अंबाडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरः|मर
मरः Ved.<BR>—1 Death.<BR>—2 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकः|मरक
मरकः [मृ-वुन्] A plague, murrain, pestilential disease, an epidemic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकतम्
मरकतम् [मरकं तरत्यनेन तॄ-ड] An emerald; वापी चास्मिन्<BR> मरकतशिलाबद्धसोपानमार्गा Me. 78; Śi. 4. 56; Ṛs. 3. 21; (sometimes<BR> written मरक्त.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मरकतमणिः, मरकतशिला, मरकतश्याम<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकतमणिः|मरकतमणि
मरकतम् + -मणिः <i>m., f.</i> an emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकतशिला
मरकतम् + -शिला an emerald slab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरकतश्याम
मरकतम् + -श्याम <i>a.</i> dark or green as an emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणम्
मरणम् [मृ-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Dying, death; मरणं प्रकृतिः शरीरिणाम् R. 8. 87; or संभावितस्य<BR> चाकीर्तिर्मरणादतिरिच्यते Bg. 2. 34.<BR>—2 A kind of poison.<BR>—3 Passing away, cessation (as of rain).<BR>—4 (In astrol.) The 8th mansion.<BR>—5 A refuge, asylum.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मरणान्त, मरणान्तक, मरणाभिमुख, मरणोन्मुख, मरणात्मक, मरणदशा, मरणधर्मः, मरणधर्मन्, मरणनिश्चय, मरणमण्डनम्, मरणशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणान्त|मरणांत
मरणम् + -अन्त, -अन्तक <i>a.</i> ending in death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणान्तक
मरणम् + -अन्त, -अन्तक <i>a.</i> ending in death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणाभिमुख
मरणम् + -अभिमुख, -उन्मुख <i>a.</i> on the point of death, near death, moribund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणोन्मुख
मरणम् + -अभिमुख, -उन्मुख <i>a.</i> on the point of death, near death, moribund.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणात्मक
मरणम् + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> causing death, fatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणदशा
मरणम् + -दशा the time or hour of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणधर्मः|मरणधर्म
मरणम् + -धर्मः the law of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणधर्मन्
मरणम् + -धर्मन् <i>a.</i> mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणनिश्चय
मरणम् + -निश्चय <i>a.</i> determined to die; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणमण्डनम्
मरणम् + -मण्डनम् Wearing dress and ornamants as a Satī usually wears;<BR> अथ मदम्बा मरणमण्डनमनुष्ठाय Dk. 2. 10. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणशील
मरणम् + -शील <i>a.</i> mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरतः|मरत
मरतः Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरणीय
मरणीय, -मरिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR> Mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिष्णु
मरणीय, -मरिष्णु <i>a.</i><BR> Mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरिमन्
मरिमन् <i>m.</i> Death, dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1240-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरन्द|मरंद|मरंदः|मरन्दः
मरन्द, -न्दकः<BR> The juice of flowers; अयि दलदरविन्द स्यन्दमानं<BR> मरन्दं तव किमपि लिहन्तो मञ्जु गुञ्जन्तु भृङ्गाः Bv. 1. 5, 10, 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मरन्दौकस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मरन्दकः|मरन्दक|मरंदकः
मरन्द, -न्दकः<BR> The juice of flowers; अयि दलदरविन्द स्यन्दमानं<BR> मरन्दं तव किमपि लिहन्तो मञ्जु गुञ्जन्तु भृङ्गाः Bv. 1. 5, 10, 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मरन्दौकस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1241-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

