महा + -अनसम् + .({@-सः, -सम्@}) a kitchen; सूपानस्य करिष्यामि कुशलोऽस्मि महानसे Mb. 4. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानसम्
महा + -अनसम् + .({@-सः, -सम्@}) a kitchen; सूपानस्य करिष्यामि कुशलोऽस्मि महानसे Mb. 4. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानिलः|महानिल
महा + -अनिलः a whirlwind; महानिलेनेव निदाघजं रजः Ki. 14. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानुभाव|महानुभावः
महा + -अनुभाव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of great prowess, dignified, noble, glorious, magnanimous,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">Page1248-1</a>]<BR> exalted, illustrious; ग्रहीतुमार्यान् परिचर्यया मुहुर्महानुभावा हि<BR> नितान्तमर्थिनः Śi. 1. 17; Ś. 3.<BR>—2 virtuous, righteous, just.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानुभावः|महानुभाव
महा + -अनुभाव + .({@-वः@})<BR>—1 a worthy or respectable person.<BR>—2 (pl.) people of a religious sect in Mahārāṣtra founded by Cakradhara<BR> in the 13th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1247-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महान्तकः|महान्तक
महा + -अन्तकः<BR>—1 death.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महान्धकारः|महान्धकार
महा + -अन्धकारः<BR>—1 thick darkness.<BR>—2 gross (spiritual) ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महान्ध्राः
महा + -अन्ध्राः (pl.) N. of a people and their country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महान्वय|महान्वयः
महा + -अन्वय, -अभिजन <i>a.</i> nobly-born, of noble birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभिजन|महाभिजनः
महा + -अन्वय, -अभिजन <i>a.</i> nobly-born, of noble birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महान्वयः|महान्वय
महा + -अन्वय, -अभिजन + .({@-यः, -नः@}) noble birth, high descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभिजनः|महाभिजन
महा + -अन्वय, -अभिजन + .({@-यः, -नः@}) noble birth, high descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाभिषवः|महाभिषव
महा + -अभिषवः the great extraction of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महामात्यः|महामात्य
महा + -अमात्यः the chief or prime minister (of a king).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाम्बुकः|महाम्बुक|महांबुक
महा + -अम्बुकः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाम्बुजम्
महा + -अम्बुजम् a trillion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाम्ल|महाम्लं
महा + -अम्ल <i>a.</i> very sour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाम्लम्
महा + -अम्ल + .({@-म्लम्@}) the fruit of the tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारण्यम्
महा + -अरण्यम् a great (dreary) forest, large forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्घ|महार्घं|महार्घः
महा + -अर्घ <i>a.</i> very costly, costing a high price; महार्घस्तीर्थानामिव<BR> हि महतां कोऽप्यतिशयः U. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्घः|महार्घ|महार्घं
महा + -अर्घ + .({@-र्घः@}) a kind of quail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्घ्य
महा + -अर्घ्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 valuable, precious.<BR>—2 invaluable; inestimable; see महार्ह below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्चिस्
महा + -अर्चिस् <i>a.</i> flaming high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्णवः|महार्णव
महा + -अर्णवः<BR>—1 the great ocean.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्थ
महा + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 rich.<BR>—2 great, noble, dignified.<BR>—3 important, weighty.<BR>—4 significant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्बुदम्
महा + -अर्बुदम् one thousand millions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्ह|महार्हं
महा + -अर्ह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 very valuable, very costly; महार्हशय्यापरिवर्तनच्युतैः स्वकेशपुष्पैरपि<BR> या स्म दूयते Ku. 5. 12.<BR>—2 invaluable, inestimable; महार्हशयनोपेत किं शेषे निहतो भुवि<BR> Rām. 6. 109. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महार्हम्
महा + -अर्ह + .({@-र्हम्@}) white sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महावरोहः|महावरोह
महा + -अवरोहः the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशनिध्वजः|महाशनिध्वज
महा + -अशनिध्वजः a great banner in the form of the thunderbolt; जहार<BR> चान्येन मयूरपत्रिणा शरेण शक्रस्य महाशनिध्वजम् R. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशन
महा + -अशन <i>a.</i> voracious, gluttonous; Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाश्मन्
महा + -अश्मन् <i>m.</i> a precious stone, ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाष्टमी
महा + -अष्टमी the eighth day in the bright half of Āśvina sacred to<BR> Durgā; आश्विने शुक्लपक्षस्य भवेद् या तिथिरष्टमी । महाष्टमीति सा प्रोक्ता … …<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासिः|महासि
महा + -असिः a large sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महासुरी
महा + -असुरी N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाह्नः|महाह्न
महा + -अह्नः the afternoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकार
महा + -आकार <i>a.</i> extensive, large, great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाचार्यः|महाचार्य
महा + -आचार्यः<BR>—1 a great teacher. —2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाढ्य|महाढ्यः
महा + -आढ्य <i>a.</i> wealthy, very rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाढ्यः|महाढ्य
महा + -आढ्य + .({@-ढ्यः@}) the Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महात्मन्
महा + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> —1 high-souled, high-minded, magnanimous, noble;<BR> अयं दुरात्मा अथवा महात्मा कौटिल्यः Mu. 7; द्विषन्ति मन्दाश्चरितं<BR> महात्मनाम् Ku. 5. 75; U. 1. 49; प्रकृतिसिद्धमिदं हि महात्मनाम् Bh. 1. 63.<BR>—2 illustrious, distinguished, exalted, eminent; किमाचाराः किमाहाराः क्व च वासो महात्मनाम् Mb. 3. 1. 4.<BR>—3 mighty (महाबल); अथायमस्यां कृतवान् महात्मा लङ्केश्वरः कष्टमनार्यकर्म Rām. 5. 9. 74.<BR>━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the Supreme Spirit; युगपत्तु प्रलीयन्ते यदा तस्मिन् महात्मनि Ms. 1. 54.<BR>—2 the great principle, <i>i. e.</i> intellect of the Sāṅkhyas. (महात्मवत्<BR> means the same as महात्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानकः|महानक
महा + -आनकः a kind of large drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानन्दः|महानन्द|महानंद
महा + -आनन्दः, -नन्दः<BR>—1 great joy or bliss.<BR>—2 especially, the great bliss of final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानन्दा|महानंदा
महा + -आनन्दः, -नन्दः + .({@-न्दा@})<BR>—1 spirituous liquor.<BR>—2 a festival on the ninth day in the bright half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महानन्दः|महानन्द|महानंद
महा + -आनन्दः, -नन्दः<BR>—1 great joy or bliss.<BR>—2 especially, the great bliss of final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महापगा
महा + -आपगा a great river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महायुधः|महायुध
महा + -आयुधः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारम्भ|महारंभ|महारम्भं|महारम्भः
महा + -आरम्भ <i>a.</i> undertaking great works, enterprizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महारम्भः|महारम्भ|महारंभ|महारम्भं
महा + -आरम्भ + .({@-म्भः@}) any great enterprize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालयः|महालय
महा + -आलयः<BR>—1 a temple in general.<BR>—2 a sanctuary, an asylum.<BR>—3 a great dwelling.<BR>—4 a place of pilgrimage.<BR>—5 the world of Brahman.<BR>—6 the Supreme Spirit.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">Page1248-2</a>]<BR>—7 a tree &c. sacred to a deity.<BR>—8 N. of a particular dark fortnight. —9 पितृश्राद्ध in the month of Bhādrapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महालया
महा + -आलयः + .({@-या@}) N. of a particular deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशय|महाशयः
महा + -आशय <i>a.</i> high-souled, noble-minded, magnanimous, noble; दैवात्<BR> प्रबुद्धः शुश्राव वराहो हि महाशयः Ks.; राजा हिरण्यगर्भो महाशयः<BR> H. 4; see महात्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाशयः|महाशय
महा + -आशय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 a noble-minded or magnanimous person; महाशयचक्रवर्ती Bv. 1. 70.<BR>—2 the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महास्पद
महा + -आस्पद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 occupying a great position.<BR>—2 mighty, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाहवः|महाहव
महा + -आहवः a great or tumultuous fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेच्छ|महेच्छः|महेछ
महा + -इच्छ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 magnanimous, noble-minded, high-souled, noble; महीं महेच्छः परिकीर्य<BR> सूनौ R. 18. 33.<BR>—2 having lofty aims or aspirations, ambitious; विद्यावतां महेच्छानां<BR> … … नाश्रयः पार्थिवं विना Pt. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेन्द्रः|महेन्द्र|महेंद्र
महा + -इन्द्रः<BR>—1 ‘the great Indra’, N. of Indra; इयं महेन्द्रप्रभृतीनधिश्रियः<BR> Ku. 5. 53; R. 13. 20; Ms. 7. 7.<BR>—2 a chief or leader in general.<BR>—3 N. of a mountain range; पतिर्महेन्द्रस्य महोदधेश्च R. 6. 54, 4. 39, 43.<BR> ˚चापः rain-bow. ˚नगरी N. of Amarāvatī, the capital<BR> of Indra. ˚मन्त्रिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Bṛhaspati. ˚वाहः the<BR> elephant Airāvata; महेन्द्रवाहप्रतिमो महात्मा Mb. 9. 17. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेभ्य
महा + -इभ्य <i>a.</i> very rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेषुः|महेषु
महा + -इषुः a great archer; अधिरोहति गाण्डीवं महेषौ Ki. 13. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेष्वासः|महेष्वास
महा + -इष्वासः a great archer, a great warrior; अत्र शूरा महेष्वासा<BR> भीमार्जुनसमा युधि Bg. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेशः|महेश
महा + -ईशः, -ईशानः N. of Śiva; महेशस्त्वां धत्ते शिरसि रसराजस्य<BR> जयिनीम् Udb. ˚बन्धुः the Bilva tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेशानः|महेशान
महा + -ईशः, -ईशानः N. of Śiva; महेशस्त्वां धत्ते शिरसि रसराजस्य<BR> जयिनीम् Udb. ˚बन्धुः the Bilva tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेशानी
महा + -ईशानी N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश्वरः|महेश्वर
महा + -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a great lord, sovereign; महेश्वरस्त्र्यम्बक एव नापरः R.; गोप्तारं<BR> न निधीनां कथयन्ति महेश्वरं विबुधाः Pt. 2. 74.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 a god (opp. प्रकृति).<BR>—5 the Supreme Being (परमात्मा); मायां तु प्रकृतिं विद्यान्मायिनं<BR> तु महेश्वरम् Śvet. Up. 4. 10. ˚सखः N. of Kubera; यया कैलासभवने<BR> महेश्वरसखं बली Mb. 9. 11. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेश्वरी
महा + -ईश्वरः + .({@-री@})<BR>—1 N. of Durgā. —2 a kind of bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोक्षः|महोक्ष
महा + -उक्षः (for उक्षन्) a large bull; a full grown or strong bull;<BR> महोक्षतां वत्सतरः स्पृशन्निव R. 3. 32, 4. 22, 6. 72; Śi. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्पलम्
महा + -उत्पलम् a large blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्पलः|महोत्पल|महोत्पलं
महा + -उत्पलम् + .({@-लः@}) the Sārasa bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्सवः|महोत्सव
महा + -उत्सवः —1 a great festival or occasion of joy; नयनविषयं<BR> जन्मन्येकः स एव महोत्सवः Māl. 1. 36.<BR>—2 the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्साह|महोत्साहः
महा + -उत्साह <i>a.</i> possessed of great energy, energetic, perservering;<BR> अहं च कर्णं जानामि … … सत्यसंधं महोत्साहं … … Mb. 3. 91. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोत्साहः|महोत्साह
महा + -उत्साह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 perseverance.<BR>—2 great pride; ये जात्यादिमहोत्साहान्नरेन्द्रान्नोपयान्ति च । तेषामामरणं<BR> भिक्षा प्रायश्चितं विनिर्मितम् ॥ Pt. 1. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदधिः|महोदधि
महा + -उदधिः<BR>—1 the great ocean; महोदधेः पूर इवेन्दुदर्शनात् R. 3. 17.<BR>—2 an epithet of Indra. ˚जः a conchshell, shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदय|महोदयं|महोदयः
महा + -उदय <i>a.</i> very prosperous or lucky, very glorious or splendid,<BR> of great prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदयः|महोदय|महोदयं
महा + -उदय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) great elevation or rise, greatness, prosperity; नन्दस्त्वतीन्द्रियं<BR> दृष्ट्वा लोकपालमहोदयम् Bhāg. 10. 28. 10; अपवर्गमहोदयार्थयोर्भुवमंशाविव<BR> धर्मयोर्गतौ R. 8. 16.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) great fortune or good luck.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) greatness, pre-eminence.<BR>—2 final beatitude.<BR>—3 a lord, master.<BR>—4 N. of the district called Kānyakubja or Kanouja; see App.<BR>—5 N. of the capital of Kanouja.<BR>—6 sour milk mixed with honey.<BR>—7 = महात्मन् q. v.; संसक्तौ किमसुलभं महोदयानाम् Ki. 7. 27.<BR> ˚पर्वन् a time of union of the middle of श्रवण नक्षत्र and<BR> the end of व्यतिपात (generally in the month<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">Page1249-1</a>]<BR> of माघ or पौष at the beginning of अमावास्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1248-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदर
महा + -उदर <i>a.</i> big-bellied, corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदरम्
महा + -उदर + .({@-रम्@})<BR>—1 a big belly.<BR>—2 dropsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदार
महा + -उदार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 very generous or magnanimous.<BR>—2 mighty, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोद्यम|महोद्यमः
महा + -उद्यम <i>a.</i> = महोत्साह q. v.; महोद्यमाः कर्म समारभन्ते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोद्योग
महा + -उद्योग <i>a.</i> very industrious or diligent, hard-working.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोद्रेकः|महोद्रेक
महा + -उद्रेकः a particular measure (= 4 प्रस्थs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्नत|महोन्नतः
महा + -उन्नत <i>a.</i> exceedingly lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्नतः|महोन्नत
महा + -उन्नत + .({@-तः@}) the palmyra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोन्नतिः|महोन्नति
महा + -उन्नतिः <i>f.</i> great rise or elevation (fig. also), high rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोपकारः|महोपकार
महा + -उपकारः a great obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोपाध्यायः|महोपाध्याय
महा + -उपाध्यायः a great preceptor, a learned teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोरगः|महोरग|महोरगं
महा + -उरगः a great serpent; वपुर्महोरगस्येव करालफणमण्डलम् R. 12. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोरस्क
महा + -उरस्क <i>a.</i> broad-chested. ({@स्कः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोर्मिन्
महा + -उर्मिन् <i>m.</i> the ocean; ततः सागरमासाद्य कुक्षौ तस्य महोर्मिणः Mb. 3. 20. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोल्का
महा + -उल्का<BR>—1 a great meteor. —2 a great fire-brand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्त्विज्
महा + -ऋत्विज् <i>m.</i> ‘great priest’, N. of the four chief sacrificial priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्द्धि
महा + -ऋद्धि <i>a.</i> very prosperous, opulent. ━(<i>f.</i>) great prosperity or affluence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्षभः|महर्षभ
महा + -ऋषभः a great bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महर्षिः|महर्षि
महा + -ऋषिः —1 a great sage or saint; यस्मादृषिः परत्वेन महांस्तस्मान्महर्षयः;<BR> (the term is applied in Ms. 1. 34 to the ten <i>Prajāpatis</i> or patriarchs<BR> of mankind, but it is also used in the general sense of ‘a great sage’).<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौघ|महौघः
महा + -ओघ <i>a.</i> having a strong current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौघः|महौघ
महा + -ओघः a very large number; शतं खर्वसहस्राणां समुद्रमभिधीयते ।<BR> शतं समुद्रसाहस्रं महौघमिति विश्रुतम् ॥ Rām. 6. 28. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौष्ठ|महौष्ठः
महा + -ओष्ठ (महोष्ठ) <i>a.</i> having large lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौष्ठः|महौष्ठ
महा + -ओष्ठ + .({@-ष्ठः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजस्
महा + -ओजस् <i>a.</i> very mighty or powerful, possessed of great splendour<BR> or glory; महौजसा मानधना धनार्चिताः Ki. 1. 19. ━(<i>m.</i>) a great<BR> hero or warrior, a champion. ━(<i>n.</i>) great vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजसम्
महा + -ओजसम् the discus of Viṣṇu (सुदर्शन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौजसी
महा + -ओजसम् + .({@-सी@}) N. of a plant (Mar. कांगणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौदनी
महा + -ओदनी Asparagus Racemosus (Mar. शतावरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषधिः|महौषधि
महा + -ओषधिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a very efficacious medicinal plant, a sovereign drug.<BR>—2 the Dūrvā grass.<BR>—3 N. of various plants ब्राह्मी, श्वेतकण्टकारी, कटुका, अतिविष &c.<BR> ˚गणः a collection of great or medicinal herbs:− पृश्निपर्णी श्यामलता<BR> भृङ्गराजः शतावरी । गुडूचा सहदेवी च महौषधिगणः स्मृतः ॥ cf.<BR> also सहदेवी तथा व्याघ्री बला चातिबला त्वचा । शङ्खपुष्पी तथा सिंही<BR> अष्टमी च सुवर्चला ॥ महौषध्यष्टकं प्रोक्तं ….<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महौषधम्
महा + -औषधम्<BR>—1 a sovereign remedy, panacea.<BR>—2 ginger.<BR>—3 garlic.<BR>—4 a kind of poison (वत्सनाभ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकच्छः|महाकच्छ
महा + -कच्छः<BR>—1 the sea.<BR>—2 N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—3 a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकन्दः|महाकन्द|महाकंद
महा + -कन्दः garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकपर्दः|महाकपर्द
महा + -कपर्दः a kind of shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकपित्थः|महाकपित्थ
महा + -कपित्थः<BR>—1 the Bilva tree.<BR>—2 red garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकम्बु|महाकंबु|महाकम्बुः
महा + -कम्बु <i>a.</i> stark naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकम्बुः|महाकम्बु|महाकंबु
महा + -कम्बु + .({@-म्बुः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकर
महा + -कर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 large-handed.<BR>—2 having a large revenue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकर्णः|महाकर्ण
महा + -कर्णः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकर्मन्
महा + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i> doing great works. ━(<i>m.</i>) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकला
महा + -कला the night of the new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकल्पः|महाकल्प
महा + -कल्पः a great cycle of time (100 years of Brahman); Bhāg. 7. 15. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकविः|महाकवि
महा + -कविः<BR>—1 a great poet, a classical poet, such as कालिदास, भवभूति, बाण, भारवि &c.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śukra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकषायः
महा + -कषायः N. of a plant (Mar. कायफळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकान्तः|महाकान्त
महा + -कान्तः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकान्ता|महाकांता
महा + -कान्तः + .({@-ता@}) the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाय|महाकायः
महा + -काय <i>a.</i> big-bodied, big, gigantic, bulky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकायः|महाकाय
महा + -काय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 an elephant.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">Page1249-2</a>]<BR> being attending on Śiva (= नन्दि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकारुणिक
महा + -कारुणिक <i>a.</i> exceedingly compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकार्तिकी|महाकार्त्तिकी
महा + -कार्तिकी the night of full-moon in the month of Kārtika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकालः|महाकाल
महा + -कालः<BR>—1 a form of Śiva in his character as the destroyer of the world; महाकालं<BR> यजेद्देव्या दक्षिणे धूम्रवर्णकम् Kālītantram.<BR>—2 N. of a celebrated shrine or temple of Śiva (Mahākāla) (one of the 12<BR> celebrated Jyotirliṅgas) established at Ujjayinī (immortalized by<BR> Kālidāsa in his Meghadūta, which gives a very beautiful description<BR> of the god, his temple, worship &c., together with a graphic picture of<BR> the city; cf. Me. 30-38; also R. 6. 34); महाकालनिवासिनं कालीविलासिनमनश्वरं<BR> महेश्वरं समाराध्य Dk. 1. 1.<BR>—3 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 N. of a kind of gourd.<BR>—5 N. of Śivaʼs servant (नन्दि). ˚पुरम् the city of Ujjayinī.<BR> ˚फलम् a red fruit with black seeds; पक्वं महाकालफलं किलासीत् N. 22. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाली
महा + -काली an epithet of Durgā in her terrific form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकाव्यम्
महा + -काव्यम् a great or classical poem; (for a full description of<BR> its nature, contents &c., according to Rhetoricians see S. D. 559). (The<BR> number of Mahākāvyas is usually said to be five:− रघुवंश, कुमारसंभव,<BR> किरातार्जुनीय, शिशुपालवध and नैषधचरित or six, if. मेघदूत ━a ▪ very<BR>small poem or खण्डकाव्य━ be added to the list. But this enumeration<BR> is apparently only traditional, as there are several other poems, such<BR> as the भट्टिकाव्य, विक्रमाङ्कदेवचरित, हरविजय &c. which have<BR> an equal claim to be considered as Mahākāvyas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकीर्तनम्
महा + -कीर्तनम् a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुमारः|महाकुमार
महा + -कुमारः the eldest son of a reigning prince, heir-apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुल|महाकुलः
महा + -कुल, -कुलीन <i>a.</i> of noble birth or descent, sprung from a<BR> noble family, nobly born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुलम्
महा + -कुल, -कुलीन + .({@-लम्@}) a noble birth or family, high descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुलीन|महाकुलीनः
महा + -कुल, -कुलीन <i>a.</i> of noble birth or descent, sprung from a<BR> noble family, nobly born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकुहः|महाकुह
महा + -कुहः a species of parasitical worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकृच्छ्रम्
महा + -कृच्छ्रम् a great penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकेतुः|महाकेतु
महा + -केतुः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकेशः|महाकेश
महा + -केशः, -कोशः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 a large sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाकोशः|महाकोश
महा + -केशः, -कोशः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 a large sheath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाक्रतुः|महाक्रतु
महा + -क्रतुः a great sacrifice; <i>e. g.</i> a horse-sacrifice; तदङ्गमग्र्यं<BR> मघवन् महाक्रतोरमुं तुरङ्गं प्रतिमोक्तुमर्हसि R. 3. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1249-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महाक्रमः|महाक्रम
