माधव|माधवः
माधव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मधु-अण्]<BR>—1 Honey-like, sweet.<BR>—2 Made of honey.<BR>—3 Vernal, relating to the spring; सावज्ञेव मुखप्रसाधनविधौ श्रीमाधवी<BR> योषिताम् M. 3. 5.<BR>—4 Relating to the descendants of Madhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवः|माधव
माधव + .{@-वः@} [माया लक्ष्म्या धवः]<BR>—1 N. of Kṛṣṇa; राधामाधवयोर्जयन्ति यमुनाकूले रहःकेलयः Gīt. 1;<BR> माधवे मा कुरु मानिनि मानमये 9.<BR>—2 The spring season, a friend of Cupid; स्मर पर्युत्सुक एष माधवः<BR> Ku. 4. 28; स माधवेनाभिमतेन सख्या (अनुप्रयातः) 3. 23; माधवप्रथमे<BR> मासि बलस्य प्रथमे पुनः Caraka-sūtrasthāna.<BR>—3 The month called Vaiśākha; जगाम माधवे मासि रैभ्याश्रमपदं प्रति<BR> Mb. 3. 136. 1; भास्करस्य मधुमाधवाविव R. 11. 7.<BR>—4 N. of Indra.<BR>—5 of Paraśurāma.<BR>—6 N. of the Yādavas (pl.); प्रहितः प्रधनाय माधवान् Śi. 16. 52.<BR>—7 N. of a celebrated author, son of Māyaṇa and brother of Sāyaṇa<BR> and Bhoganātha, and suppossed to have lived in the fifteenth century.<BR> He was a very reputed scholar, numerous important works being ascribed<BR> to him; he and Sāyaṇa are suppossed to have jointly written the commentary<BR> on the Ṛgveda; श्रुतिस्मृतिसदाचारपालको माधवो बुधः । स्मार्तं व्याख्याय<BR> सर्वार्थं द्विजार्थं श्रौत उद्यतः ॥ J. N. V.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: माधवोचितम्, माधवद्रुमः, माधवनिदानम्, माधववल्ली, माधवश्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवोचितम्
माधव + -उचितम् a kind of perfume (कक्कोल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवद्रुमः|माधवद्रुम
माधव + -द्रुमः Spondias Mangifera (Mar. अंबाडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवनिदानम्
माधव + -निदानम् N. of a medical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधववल्ली
माधव + -वल्ली = माधवी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवश्री
माधव + -श्री vernal beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवकः|माधवक
माधवकः A kind of intoxicating liquor (produced from honey).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधविका
माधविका N. of a creeper; माधविकापरिमलललिते Gīt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवी
माधवी<BR>—1 Candied sugar.<BR>—2 A kind of drink made from honey.<BR>—3 The spring-creeper (वासन्ती), with white fragrant flowers; पत्राणामिव<BR> शोषणेन मरुता स्पृष्टा लता माधवी Ś. 3. 9; Me. 80.<BR>—4 The sacred basil.<BR>—5 The earth (also with देवी); तथा मे माधवी देवी विवरं दातुमर्हति<BR> Rām. 7. 97. 14-16.<BR>—6 A procuress, bawd.<BR>—7 Affluence in cattle.<BR>—8 (In music) A particular Rāginī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: माधवीमण्डपः, माधवीमण्डपम्, माधवीलता, माधवीवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीमण्डपः|माधवीमण्डप
माधवी + -मण्डपः, -मण्डपम् a bower formed of spring flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीमण्डपम्
माधवी + -मण्डपः, -मण्डपम् a bower formed of spring flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीलता
माधवी + -लता the spring creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीवनम्
माधवी + -वनम् a grove of Mādhavī creepers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीय
माधवीय <i>a.</i> Relating to Mādhava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकर
माधुकर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मधुकर-अण्] Relating to or resembling a bee;<BR> as in माधुकरी वृत्तिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकरी
माधुकर + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 Collecting alms by begging from door to door, as a bee collects honey<BR> by moving from flower to flower.<BR>—2 Alms obtained from five different places; पञ्चस्विहास्याङ्घ्निकरेष्वभिख्याभिक्षाधुना<BR> माधुकरसिदृक्षा N. 7. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुपर्किक
माधुपर्किक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Offered to a guest as a token of respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुमताः
माधुमताः (pl.) The province of Kashmir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुरम्
माधुरम् [मधुर-अण्] The flower of the Mallikā creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुरी
माधुरी<BR>—1 Sweetness, sweet or savoury taste; वदने तव यत्र माधुरी सा<BR> Bv. 2. 161; कामालसस्वर्वामाधरमाधुरीमधरयन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">Page1260-2</a>]<BR> वाचां विपाको मम 4. 42, 37, 43; वाङ्माधुरीविरसीकृतकलकण्ठा<BR> Dk.; यैर्माकन्दवने मनोज्ञपवने सद्यः स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधौतधामनि<BR> धराधीशत्वमालम्ब्यते Udb.<BR>—2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—3 Mead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर्यम्
माधुर्यम् [मधुरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Sweetness; माधुर्यमीष्टे हरिणान् ग्रहीतुम् R. 18. 13; माधुर्यं<BR> मधुबिन्दुना रचयितुं क्षाराम्बुधेरीहते Bh. 2. 6.<BR>—2 Attractive beauty, exquisite beauty; रूपं किमप्यनिर्वाच्यं तनोर्माधुर्यमुच्यते.<BR>—3 (In Rhet.) Sweetness, one of the three (according to Mammaṭa) chief<BR> Guṇas in poetic compositions; चित्तद्रवी भावमयो ह्लादो माधुर्यमुच्यते<BR> S. D. 606; see K. P. 8 also.<BR>—4 Kindness, amiability.<BR>—5 (With Vaiṣṇavas) A feeling of tender affection for Kṛṣṇa (like<BR> that of a woman for her lover); Dk. 2. 2. ━<i>a.</i> Sweetly speaking; स्वच्छप्रकृतितः<BR> स्निग्धो माधुर्यस्तीर्थभूर्नृणाम् Bhāg. 11. 7. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूक
माधूक <i>a.</i> Sweet-speaking, amiable; मैत्रेयकं तु वैदेहो माधूकं<BR> संप्रसूयते Ms. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्य
माध्य <i>a.</i> [मध्य-अण्] Central, middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यंदिन|माध्यन्दिन|माध्यन्दिनं|माध्यंदिनः
माध्यंदिन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Mid-day, meridional.<BR>—2 Middle, central.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यंदिनः|माध्यन्दिन|माध्यंदिन|माध्यन्दिनं
माध्यंदिन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 N. of a branch of Vājasaneyins.<BR>—2 N. of an astronomical school which fixed the starting point of planetary<BR> movements at noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यंदिनम्
माध्यंदिन + .{@-नम्@} A branch of the शुक्ल or white Yajurveda (followed by<BR> the Mādhyandinas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यम|माध्यमं
माध्यम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मध्यम-अण्] Belonging to the middle portion,<BR> central, middle, middle-most.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमक
माध्यमक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माध्यमिक@} <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Middle, central.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमिका
माध्यमक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माध्यमिक@} <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Middle, central.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमिक
माध्यमक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माध्यमिक@} <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Middle, central.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमिकी
माध्यमक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माध्यमिक@} <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Middle, central.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमकाः
माध्यमक + .{@-काः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.)<BR>—1 N. of a people or their country in the central part of India.<BR>—2 N. of a Buddhist school; भगवत्पूज्यपादाश्च शुष्कतर्कपटूनमून् ।<BR> आहुर्माध्यमिकान् भ्रान्तानचिन्त्येऽस्मिन् सदात्मनि ॥ Pañcadaśī 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ|माध्यस्थं
माध्यस्थ^1 <i>a.</i> Indifferent, impartial, neutral.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थम्
माध्यस्थम्, माध्यस्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Impartiality; निर्माध्यस्थ्याच्च हर्षाच्च बभाषे दुर्वचं वचः Rām. 2. 11. 11.<BR>—2 Indifference, unconcern; अभ्यर्थनाभङ्गभयेन साधुर्माध्यस्थ्यमिष्टेऽप्यवलम्बतेऽर्थे<BR> Ku. 1. 52; कैवल्यं माध्यस्थ्यम् Sāṅ. K. 19.<BR>—3 Intercession, mediation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ्यम्
माध्यस्थम्, माध्यस्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Impartiality; निर्माध्यस्थ्याच्च हर्षाच्च बभाषे दुर्वचं वचः Rām. 2. 11. 11.<BR>—2 Indifference, unconcern; अभ्यर्थनाभङ्गभयेन साधुर्माध्यस्थ्यमिष्टेऽप्यवलम्बतेऽर्थे<BR> Ku. 1. 52; कैवल्यं माध्यस्थ्यम् Sāṅ. K. 19.<BR>—3 Intercession, mediation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्याह्निक
माध्याह्निक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्व|माध्वः
माध्व <i>a.</i> (-ध्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sweet; वदन्ति चाटुकान् मूढा यथा माध्व्या गिरोत्सुकाः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वः|माध्व
माध्व + .{@-ध्वः@} A follower of Madhva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वी
माध्व + .{@-ध्वी@}<BR>—1 A kind of liquor (made from honey).<BR>—2 The creeper called Mādhavī.<BR>—3 A kind of date tree (Mar. मधुखजूरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वकम्
माध्वकम् An intoxicating drink prepared from honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्विकः|माध्विक
माध्विकः A person who collects honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीकम्
माध्वीकम् [मधुना मधूकपुष्पेण निर्वृत्तम् ईकक्]<BR>—1 A kind of spirituous liquor distilled from the flowers of the tree<BR> called Madhūka; गौडी पेष्टी च माध्वी च विज्ञेया त्रिविधा सुरा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">Page1261-1</a>]<BR> Ms. 11. 94; चचाम मधु माध्वीकम् Bk. 14. 94.<BR>—2 Wine distilled from grapes; साध्वी माध्वीक चिन्ता न भवति भवतः<BR> Gīt. 12. (= मधो; Com.).<BR>—3 A grape.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: माध्वीकफलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1260-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीकफलम्
माध्वीकम् + -फलम् a kind of sweet cocoa-nut (Mar. मोहाचा नारळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीका
माध्वीका <i>f.</i> A kind of red pulse (Mar. तांबडा पावटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्
मान् I. €1 Ā. (मीमांसते = desid. of मन् q. v.)<BR>━II. €1 P., €10 U. = <i>Caus.</i> of मन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानः|मान|मानं
मानः [मन्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Respect, honour, regard, respectful consideration; दारिद्र्यस्य परा<BR> मूर्तिर्यन्मानद्रविणाल्पता Pt. 2. 159; Bg. 6. 7; so मानधन &c.<BR>—2 Pride (in a good sense), self-reliance, self-respect; जन्मिनो मानहीनस्य<BR> तृणस्य च समा गतिः Pt. 1. 106; R. 19. 81.<BR>—3 Haughtiness, pride, conceit, self-confidence, vanity; मानाद् रावणः<BR> परदारान् अप्रयच्छन् (विननाश) Kau. A. 1. 6.<BR>—4 A wounded sense of honour.<BR>—5 Jealous anger, anger excited by jealousy (especially in women); anger<BR> in general; मुञ्च मयि मानमनिदानम् Gīt. 10; माधवे मा कुरु मानिनि<BR> मानमये 9; त्यजत मानमलं वत विग्रहैः R. 9. 47; Śi. 9. 84;<BR> Bv. 2. 56; Dk. 2. 3.<BR>—6 Opinion, conception.<BR>—7 Ved. Object, purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानम्
मानः + .{@-नम्@} [मा-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Measuring.<BR>—2 A measure, standard; मानाधीना मेयसिद्धिः Mīmāṃsā; निराकृतत्वाच्छ्रुतियुक्तिमानतः<BR> A. Rām. 7. 5. 57.<BR>—3 Dimension, computation.<BR>—4 A standard of measure, measuring rod, rule; परिमाणं पात्रमानं<BR> संख्यैकद्यादिसंज्ञिका Śukra. 2. 344.<BR>—5 Proof, authority, means of proof or demonstration; येऽमी माधुर्यौजः<BR> प्रसादा रसमात्रधर्मतयोक्तास्तेषां रसधर्मत्वे किं मानम् R. G.; मानाभावात्<BR> (frequently occuring in controversial language) Pad. D. 4. 3.<BR>—6 Likeness, resemblance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मानान्ध, मानार्ह, मानावभङ्गः, मानासक्त, मानोत्साहः, मानोन्नतिः, मानोन्मादः, मानकलहः, मानकलिः, मानक्षतिः, मानग्रन्थिः, मानग्रहणम्, मानद, मानदण्डः, मानधन, मानधानिका, मानध्मात, मानपरिखण्डनम्, मानभङ्गः, मानभाज्, मानभृत्, मानपर, मानमहत्, मानयोगः, मानरन्ध्रा, मानवर्जित, मानवर्धनम्, मानविषमः, मानसारः, मानसारम्, मानसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानान्ध
मानः + -अन्ध <i>a.</i> blinded by pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानार्ह
मानः + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> worthy of honour; Ms. 2. 137.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानावभङ्गः|मानावभङ्ग
मानः + -अवभङ्गः destruction of pride or anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानासक्त
मानः + -आसक्त <i>a.</i> given to pride, haughty, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोत्साहः|मानोत्साह
मानः + -उत्साहः energy arising from self-confidence; Pt. 1. 226.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोन्नतिः|मानोन्नति
मानः + -उन्नतिः <i>f.</i> great respect or honour; (सत्संगतिः) मानोन्नतिं<BR> दिशति पापमपाकरोति Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोन्मादः|मानोन्माद
मानः + -उन्मादः infatuation of pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानकलहः|मानकलह
मानः + -कलहः, -कलिः a quarrel caused by jealous anger; Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानकलिः|मानकलि
मानः + -कलहः, -कलिः a quarrel caused by jealous anger; Amaru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानक्षतिः|मानक्षति
मानः + -क्षतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-भङ्गः, -हानिः@} <i>f.</i><BR> injury to reputation or honour, humiliation,<BR> mortification, insult, indignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानग्रन्थिः|मानग्रन्थि|मानग्रंथि
मानः + -ग्रन्थिः<BR>—1 injury to honour or pride.<BR>—2 violent anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानग्रहणम्
मानः + -ग्रहणम् fit of sulkiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानद|मानदः
मानः + -द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 showing respect.<BR>—2 proud; इत्थं मानद नातिदूरमुभयोरप्यावयोरन्तरम् Bh. 3. 24.<BR>—3 destroying pride.<BR>—4 a giver of honour (a mode of addressing lovers &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानदः|मानद
मानः + -द + .({@-दः@}) a mystical name for the letter आ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानदा
मानः + -द + .({@-दा@}) N. of the second digit of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानदण्डः|मानदण्ड|मानदंड
मानः + -दण्डः a measuring-rod; स्थितः पृथिव्या इव मानदण्डः Ku. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानधन
मानः + -धन <i>a.</i> rich in honour; महौजसो मानधना धनार्चिताः Ki. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानधानिका
मानः + -धानिका a cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानध्मात
मानः + -ध्मात <i>a.</i> puffed up with pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानपरिखण्डनम्
मानः + -परिखण्डनम् mortification, humiliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानभङ्गः|मानभङ्ग|मानभंग
मानः + -भङ्गः see मानक्षति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानभाज्
मानः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> receiving honour from; राजस्नातकयोश्चैव स्नातको<BR> नृपमानभाक् Ms. 2. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानभृत्
मानः + -भृत्, -पर <i>a.</i> possessing pride, extremely proud; प्रथमे<BR> मानभृतां न वृष्णयः Ki. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानपर
मानः + -भृत्, -पर <i>a.</i> possessing pride, extremely proud; प्रथमे<BR> मानभृतां न वृष्णयः Ki. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानमहत्|मानमहन्त्
मानः + -महत् <i>a.</i> rich or great in pride, greatly proud; किं जीर्णं<BR> तृणमत्ति मानमहतामग्रेसरः केसरी Bh. 2. 29.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">Page1261-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानयोगः|मानयोग
मानः + -योगः the correct mode of measuring or weighing; मानयोगं<BR> च जानीयात्तुलायोगांश्च सर्वशः Ms. 9. 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानरन्ध्रा|मानरंध्रा
मानः + -रन्ध्रा a sort of clepsydra, a perforated water-vessel, which,<BR> placed in water and gradually filling, serves to measure time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवर्जित|मानवर्जितः|मानवर्ज्जित
मानः + -वर्जित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 disgraced, dishonoured.<BR>—2 humble, lowly.<BR>—3 slanderous, libellous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवर्धनम्
मानः + -वर्धनम् indicating, increasing respect; यत्किंचिदेव देयं<BR> तु ज्यायसे मानवर्धनम् Ms. 9. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानविषमः
मानः + -विषमः one of the ways of embezzlement namely making use of<BR> false weights and measures; Kau. A. 2. 8. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसारः|मानसार
मानः + -सारः, -सारम् a high degree of pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसारम्
मानः + -सारः, -सारम् a high degree of pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसूत्रम्
मानः + -सूत्रम्<BR>—1 a measuring-cord; Dk. 2. 2.<BR>—2 a chain (of gold &c.) worn round the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानयितृ
मानयितृ <i>m.</i> One who honours, honourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननम्
माननम्, -ना<BR>—1 Honouring, respecting; अश्विनोर्माननार्थं हि सर्वलोकपितामहः Rām. 5. 60. 2.<BR>—2 Killing; भवतोऽभिमनाः समीहते सरुषः कर्तुमुपेत्य माननाम् Śi. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानना
माननम्, -ना<BR>—1 Honouring, respecting; अश्विनोर्माननार्थं हि सर्वलोकपितामहः Rām. 5. 60. 2.<BR>—2 Killing; भवतोऽभिमनाः समीहते सरुषः कर्तुमुपेत्य माननाम् Śi. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननीय|माननीयं
माननीय <i>a.</i> Fit to be honoured, worthy of honour, deserving to<BR> be honoured (with gen.); मेनां मुनीनामपि माननीयाम् Ku. 1. 18; R. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवत्|मानवन्त्
मानवत् <i>a.</i> Proud, arrogant, haughty or high-spirited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवती
मानवत् + .{@-ती@} A haughty or high-spirited woman angry through-jealous pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानित
मानित <i>p. p.</i> [मन् णिच् क्त] Honoured, respected, esteemed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानितम्
मानित + .{@-तम्@} Showing honour or respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन् <i>a.</i> [मान-इनि, मन्-णिनि वा]<BR>—1 Fancying, considering, regarding (at the end of comp.); as in पण्डितमानिन्,<BR> अनूचानमानी Bṛ. Up. 6. 1. 2.<BR>—2 Honouring, respecting (at the end of comp.).<BR>—3 Haughty, proud, possessed of self-respect; पराभवोऽप्युत्सव एव<BR> मानिनाम् Ki. 1. 41; परवृद्धिमत्सरि मनो हि मानिनाम् Śi. 15. 1.<BR>—4 Entitled, to respect, highly honoured; मानिनो मानयेः काले Bk. 19. 24.<BR>—5 Disdainful, angry, sulky.<BR>—6 Being regarded or considered as. ━<i>m.</i> A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिनी
मानिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A woman possessed of self-respect, a strong-minded, resolute, or proud<BR> woman (in a good sense); चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य मानिनी Ku. 5. 53; R. 13. 38.<BR>—2 An angry woman, or one offended with her husband (through jealous pride);<BR> माधवे मा कुरु मानिनि मानमये Gīt. 9; Ki. 9. 36.<BR>—3 A kind of odoriferous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिता
मानिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Haughtiness, pride.<BR>—2 Honouring, respect.<BR>—3 Being respected or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानित्वम्
मानिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Haughtiness, pride.<BR>—2 Honouring, respect.<BR>—3 Being respected or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानःशिल
मानःशिल <i>a.</i> Consisting of red arsenic (मनःशिला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव|मानवः
मानव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मनोरपत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to or descended from Manu; मानवस्य राजर्षिवंशस्य प्रसवितारं<BR> सवितारम् U. 3; Ms. 12. 107.<BR>—2 Human.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवः|मानव
मानव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A man, human being; मनोर्वंशो मानवानां ततोऽयं प्रथितोऽभवत् ।<BR> ब्रह्मक्षत्रादयस्तस्मान्मनोर्जातास्तु मानवाः Mb.; Ms. 2. 9, 5. 35.<BR>—2 A lad, boy.<BR>—3 Mankind (pl.).<BR>—4 The subjects of a kind (pl.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवाः
मानव + .{@-वाः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) N. of a school on Arthaśāstra; तेषामानुपूर्व्या<BR> यावानर्थोपघातस्तावानेकोत्तरो दण्डः इति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">Page1262-1</a>]<BR> मानवाः Kau. A. 2. 7. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवी
मानव + .{@-वी@}<BR>—1 A woman.<BR>—2 N. of the daughter of स्वयंभू मनु; यथा ससर्ज भूतानि लब्ध्वा भार्यां<BR> च मानवीम् Bhāg. 3. 21. 5.<BR>—3 N. of a Jain शासनदेवता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवम्
मानव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 A particular fine, penance.<BR>—2 A manʼs length (as a measure).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मानवेन्द्रः, मानवदेवः, मानवपतिः, मानवधर्मशास्त्रम्, मानवराक्षसः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1261-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवेन्द्रः|मानवेन्द्र|मानवेंद्र
मानव + -इन्द्रः, -देवः, -पतिः a lord of men, king, sovereign; अन्यत्र<BR> रक्षोभवनोषितायाः परिग्रहान्मानवदेव देव्याः R. 14. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवदेवः|मानवदेव
मानव + -इन्द्रः, -देवः, -पतिः a lord of men, king, sovereign; अन्यत्र<BR> रक्षोभवनोषितायाः परिग्रहान्मानवदेव देव्याः R. 14. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवपतिः|मानवपति
मानव + -इन्द्रः, -देवः, -पतिः a lord of men, king, sovereign; अन्यत्र<BR> रक्षोभवनोषितायाः परिग्रहान्मानवदेव देव्याः R. 14. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवधर्मशास्त्रम्
मानव + -धर्मशास्त्रम् the institutes of Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवराक्षसः|मानवराक्षस
मानव + -राक्षसः a demon or fiend in the form of a man; तेऽमी मानवराक्षसाः<BR> परहितं स्वार्थाय निघ्नन्ति ये Bh. 2. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवीय
मानवीय <i>a.</i> Descended or derived from Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवीयम्
मानवीय + .{@-यम्@} A particular fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव्यम्
मानव्यम् A number of boys or youths (माणव्यम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मन एव, मनस इदं वा अण्]<BR>—1 Pertaining to the mind, mental, spiritual (opp. शारीर).<BR>—2 Produced from the mind, sprung at will; ब्रह्मणो मानसपुत्राः; किं<BR> मानसी सृष्टिः Ś. 4; Ku. 1. 18; मद्भावा मानसा जाता Bg. 10. 6.<BR>—3 Only to be conceived in the mind, conceivable; अहिंसा सत्यमस्तेयं<BR> ब्रह्मचर्यमलुब्धता । एतानि मानसानि स्युर्व्रतानि …<BR>—4 Tacit, implied.<BR>—5 Dwelling on the lake Mānasa; न रमते मरालस्य मानसं मानसं विना Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसः|मानस|मानसं
मानस + .{@-सः@} A form of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसम्
मानस + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 The mind, heart, soul; सपदि मदनानलो दहति मम मानसम् Gīt. 10;<BR> अपि च मानसमम्बुनिधिः Bv. 1. 113; मानसं विषयैर्विना (भाति) 116.<BR>—2 N. of a sacred lake on the mountain Kailāsa; कैलासशिखरे राम मनसा<BR> निर्मितं सरः । ब्रह्मणा प्रागिदं यस्मात्तदभून्मानसं सरः ॥ Rām.;<BR> (it is said to be the native place of swans, who are described as migrating<BR> to its shores every year at the commencement of the breeding season or<BR> the monsoons); मेघश्यामा दिशो दृष्ट्वा मानसोत्सुकचेतसाम् । कूजितं राजहंसानां<BR> नेदं नूपुरशिञ्जितम् V. 4. 14, 15; यस्यास्तोये कृतवसतयो मानसं<BR> संनिकृष्टं नाध्यास्यन्ति व्यपगतशुचस्त्वामपि प्रेक्ष्य हंसाः Me. 78;<BR> (see Me. 11; Ghaṭ. 9 also); R. 6. 26; Me. 64; Bv. 1. 3.<BR>—3 (In law) Tacit or implied consent.<BR>—4 A kind of salt.<BR>—5 The mental powers.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मानसालयः, मानसोत्क, मानसौकस्, मानसचारिन्, मानसजन्मन्, मानसपूजा, मानसशुच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसालयः|मानसालय
मानस + -आलयः a swan, goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसोत्क
मानस + -उत्क <i>a.</i> eager to go to Mānasa; तच्छ्रुत्वा ते श्रवणसुभगं<BR> गर्जितं मानसोत्काः Me. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसौकस्
मानस + -ओकस्, -चारिन् <i>m.</i> a swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसचारिन्
मानस + -ओकस्, -चारिन् <i>m.</i> a swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसजन्मन्
मानस + -जन्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the god of love.<BR>—2 a swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसपूजा
मानस + -पूजा mental or spiritual devotion (opp. मूर्तिपूजा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसशुच्
मानस + -शुच् <i>f.</i> mental sorrow, grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसिक|मानसिकं|मानसिकः
मानसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Mental, spiritual.<BR>—2 Imaginary.<BR>—3 Committed in thought (as a sin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसिकः|मानसिक|मानसिकं
मानसिक + .{@-कः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानाप्यम्
मानाप्यम् A temporary degradation of a monk; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिका
मानिका<BR>—1 A kind of spirituous liquor.<BR>—2 A kind of weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष|मानुषः
मानुष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मनोरयम् अण् सुक् च]<BR>—1 Human; मानुषी तनुः, मानुषी वाक् &c.; R. 1. 60, 16. 22; मानुषे<BR> लोके Bg. 4. 12; अवजानन्ति मां मूढा मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितम् 9. 11; Ms. 4. 124.<BR>—2 Humane, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषः|मानुष
मानुष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 A man, human being.<BR>—2 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">Page1262-2</a>]<BR> epithet of the three signs of the zodiac, Gemini, Virgo, and Libra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषी
मानुष + .{@-षी@}<BR>—1 A woman.<BR>—2 A branch of medicine, administering drugs and herbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषम्
मानुष + .{@-षम्@}<BR>—1 Humanity.<BR>—2 Human effort or action; मानुषं च स्वाध्यायप्रवचने च T. Up. 1. 9. 1.<BR>—3 Manhood; श्रीरेषा द्रौपदीरूपा त्वदर्थे मानुषं गता Mb. 18. 4. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मानुषोपेत, मानुषराक्षसः, मानुषलौकिक, मानुषसम्भव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषोपेत
मानुष + -उपेत <i>a.</i> joined with human effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषराक्षसः|मानुषराक्षस
मानुष + -राक्षसः a fiend in human form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषलौकिक
मानुष + -लौकिक <i>a.</i> belonging to the world of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषसम्भव
मानुष + -सम्भव <i>a.</i> coming from or produced by man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषक
मानुषक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Human, mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषता
मानुषता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Humanity.<BR>—2 State or condition of man, human nature; मानुषतासुलभो लघिमा K.<BR>—3 Manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषत्वम्
मानुषता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Humanity.<BR>—2 State or condition of man, human nature; मानुषतासुलभो लघिमा K.<BR>—3 Manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यम्
मानुष्यम्, मानुष्यकम्<BR>—1 Human nature, humanity; असारमिव मानुष्यम् Mb. 12. 288. 45; किं<BR> पुनर्मानुष्यं विडम्ब्यते V. 2; यावन्मानुष्यके शक्यमुपपादयितुं तावत्सर्वमुपपाद्यताम् K. 62.<BR>—2 A mortal frame, human body; प्राप्यापि मानुष्यकमनेकसाधारणीभव Dk.<BR>—3 Mankind, the race of human beings.<BR>—4 A collection of men; अश्वीयैरौक्षकैर्मानुष्यकै रथ्याभिरौष्ट्रकैः । धनश्चचाल<BR> वैपुल्यं वसुधाया विलोपयन् ॥ Dharmābhyudayamahākāvya.<BR>—5 = मनुष्यलोक; मानुष्ये चिन्तयामास जन्मभूमिमथात्मनः Rām. 1. 16. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यकम्
मानुष्यम्, मानुष्यकम्<BR>—1 Human nature, humanity; असारमिव मानुष्यम् Mb. 12. 288. 45; किं<BR> पुनर्मानुष्यं विडम्ब्यते V. 2; यावन्मानुष्यके शक्यमुपपादयितुं तावत्सर्वमुपपाद्यताम् K. 62.<BR>—2 A mortal frame, human body; प्राप्यापि मानुष्यकमनेकसाधारणीभव Dk.<BR>—3 Mankind, the race of human beings.<BR>—4 A collection of men; अश्वीयैरौक्षकैर्मानुष्यकै रथ्याभिरौष्ट्रकैः । धनश्चचाल<BR> वैपुल्यं वसुधाया विलोपयन् ॥ Dharmābhyudayamahākāvya.<BR>—5 = मनुष्यलोक; मानुष्ये चिन्तयामास जन्मभूमिमथात्मनः Rām. 1. 16. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोज्ञकम्
मानोज्ञकम् Beauty, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्र
मान्त्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proper or peculiar to Veda.<BR>—2 Pertaining to magic or magical texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्त्रिकः|मान्त्रिक|मांत्रिक|मांत्रिकः
मान्त्रिकः One who is conversant with charms or spells, a conjurer, sorcerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थ्|मांथ्
मान्थ् €1 P. (मान्थति) To hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्थर्यम्
मान्थर्यम्<BR>—1 Slowness, dulness, tardiness.<BR>—2 Weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्दारः|मान्दार|मांदार|मांदारः
मान्दारः, मान्दारवः A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्दारवः|मान्दारव|मांदारव|मांदारवः
मान्दारः, मान्दारवः A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्दुरिकः|मान्दुरिक
मान्दुरिकः An ostler, groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्यम्
मान्द्यम् [मन्द-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Dulness, laziness, slowness; प्रवचने मान्द्यम् Pt. 1. 190.<BR>—2 Stupidity.<BR>—3 Weakness, feeble state; अग्निमान्द्यम्.<BR>—4 Apathy.<BR>—5 Sickness, illness, indisposition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मान्द्यव्याजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्द्यव्याजः|मान्द्यव्याज
मान्द्यम् + -व्याजः simulation of illness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धातृ|मांधातृ
मान्धातृ <i>m.</i> N. of a king of the solar race, son of Yuvanāśva<BR> (being born from his own belly). As soon as he came out of the belly,<BR> the sages said ‘कम् एष धास्यति’; whereupon Indra came down and said<BR> ‘मां धास्यति’; the boy was, therefore, called Māndhātṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धालः|मान्धाल
मान्धालः, मान्धीरः, मान्धीलवः A bat, flying fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धीरः|मान्धीर
मान्धालः, मान्धीरः, मान्धीलवः A bat, flying fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्धीलवः|मान्धीलव
मान्धालः, मान्धीरः, मान्धीलवः A bat, flying fox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्मथ
मान्मथ <i>a.</i> (-थी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मन्मथ-अण] Relating to or caused by love;<BR> आचार्यकं विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 16, 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्य|मान्यः
मान्य <i>pot. p.</i> [मान् अर्चायां कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be revered or respected; अहमपि तव मान्या हेतुभिस्तैश्च तैश्च Māl. 6. 26.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">Page1263-1</a>]<BR>—2 Respectable, honourable, venerable; मान्यः स मे स्थावरजङ्गमानां<BR> सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारहेतुः R. 2. 44; Y. 1. 111.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मान्यस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1262-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्यस्थानम्
मान्य + -स्थानम् a title to respect; एतानि मान्यस्थानानि Ms. 2. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापनम्
मापनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Measuring; यस्मिन् देशे च काले च मापनेयं प्रवर्तिता Mb. 1. 51. 16.<BR>—2 Forming, making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापना
मापनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Measuring; यस्मिन् देशे च काले च मापनेयं प्रवर्तिता Mb. 1. 51. 16.<BR>—2 Forming, making.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापनः|मापन|मापनं
मापनम्, -ना + .{@-नः@} A balance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मापनविषमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापनविषमः
मापनम् + -विषमः one of the ways of embezzlement namely deception in counting<BR> articles; Kau. A. 2. 8. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापत्यः|मापत्य
मापत्यः The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माम
माम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 My, mine.<BR>—2 Dear friend. —3 Uncle (used in voc.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मामकेसरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकेसरः|मामकेसर
माम + -केसरः a maternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामक|मामकं|मामकः
मामक <i>a.</i> (-मिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 My, mine, belonging to my side; मामकाः पाण्डवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत<BR> संजय Bg. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Selfish, covetous, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकः|मामक|मामकं
मामक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A miser.<BR>—2 A maternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकीन|मामकीनं
मामकीन <i>a.</i> My, mine; यो मामकीनस्य मनसो द्वितीयं निबन्धनम्<BR> Māl. 2; सा मामकीनकवितेव मनोभिरामा Bv. 3. 6, 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय|मायः
माय <i>a.</i> Possessing magical power; नमो विश्वाय मायाय चिन्त्याचिन्त्याय<BR> वै नमः Mb. 13. 14. 316.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायः|माय
माय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 A conjurer, juggler.<BR>—2 A demon, an evil spirit.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu; L. D. B. 4 A garment; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माया
माया [मा-यः बा˚ नेत्वम्]<BR>—1 Deceit, fraud, trick, trickery; a device, an artifice; रथचर्यास्त्रमायाभिर्मोहयित्वा<BR> परंतप Mb. 7. 46. 24; यो मायां कुरुते मूढः प्राणत्यागे धनादिके Pt. 1. 359.<BR>—2 Jugglery, witchercraft, enchantment, an illusion of magic; स्वप्नो<BR> नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु Ś. 6. 10; मायायोगविदां चैव न स्वयं कोपकारणात् Kau. A. 1. 19.<BR>—3 (Hence) An unreal or illusory image, a phantom, illusion, unreal apparition;<BR> मायां मयोद्भाव्य परीक्षितोऽसि R. 2. 62; विकृतिः किं नु भवेदियं<BR> नु माया Ki. 13. 4; R. 12. 74; oft. as the first member of comp. in the<BR> sense of ‘false’, ‘phantom’, ‘illusory’; <i>e. g.</i> मायावचनम् false<BR> words; मायामृग &c.<BR>—4 A political trick or artifice, diplomatic feat.<BR>—5 (In Vedānta phil.) Unreality, the illusion by virtue of which one<BR> considers the unreal universe as really existent and as distinct from the<BR> Supreme Spirit; मायां तु प्रकृतिं विद्यान्मायिनं तु महेश्वरम् Śvet. Up.<BR>—6 (In Sāṅ. phil.) The Pradhāna or Prakṛti.<BR>—7 Wickedness.<BR>—8 Pity, compassion.<BR>—9 N. of the mother of Buddha.<BR>—10 Ved. Extraordinary power, wisdom (प्रज्ञा).<BR>—11 (With Śaivas) One of the four snares (पाश) which entangle the soul.<BR>—12 N. of the city Gayā.<BR>—13 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>—14 N. of Durgā; देवीं मायां तु श्रीकामः Bhāg. 2. 3. 3.<BR>—15 Skill, art; दधारैको रणे राजन् वृषसेनोऽस्त्रमायया Mb. 7. 16. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मायाचार, मायात्मक, मायोपजीविन्, मायाकारः, मायाकृत्, मायाजीविन्, मायाचण, मायाजलम्, मायादः, मायादेवी, मायाधर, मायापटु, मायाप्रयोगः, मायाफलम्, मायामृगः, मायायन्त्रम्, मायायोगः, मायायोधिन्, मायारसिक, मायावसिक, मायावचनम्, मायावादः, मायाविद्, मायासुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाचार
माया + -आचार <i>a.</i> acting deceitfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायात्मक
माया + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> false, illusory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायोपजीविन्
माया + -उपजीविन् <i>a.</i> living by fraud; बहवः पण्डिताः क्षुद्राः<BR> सर्वे मायोपजीविनः Pt. 1. 288.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकारः|मायाकार
माया + -कारः, -कृत्, -जीविन् <i>m.</i> a conjurer, juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाकृत्
माया + -कारः, -कृत्, -जीविन् <i>m.</i> a conjurer, juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाजीविन्
माया + -कारः, -कृत्, -जीविन् <i>m.</i> a conjurer, juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाचण
माया + -चण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 noted for juggling.<BR>—2 deceptive.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">Page1263-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाजलम्
माया + -जलम् artificial water; स्निग्धत्वमायाजललेपलोपसयत्नरत्नांशुमृजांशुकाभाम् N. 10. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायादः|मायाद
माया + -दः a crocodile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायादेवी
माया + -देवी N. of the mother of Buddha. ˚सुतः Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाधर
माया + -धर <i>a.</i> deceitful, illusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायापटु
माया + -पटु <i>a.</i> skilled in deception, fraudulent, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाप्रयोगः|मायाप्रयोग
माया + -प्रयोगः<BR>—1 deceitfulness, employment of tricks or fraud; मायाप्रयोगः प्रिये Pt. 1. 190.<BR>—2 employment of magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाफलम्
माया + -फलम् a gall-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामृगः|मायामृग
माया + -मृगः a phantom deer, an illusory or false deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायायन्त्रम्
माया + -यन्त्रम् an enchantment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायायोगः|मायायोग
माया + -योगः employment of magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायायोधिन्
माया + -योधिन् <i>a.</i> fighting deceitfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायारसिक
माया + -रसिक, -वसिक <i>a.</i> deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावसिक|मायावसिकः
माया + -रसिक, -वसिक <i>a.</i> deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावचनम्
माया + -वचनम् false or deceitful words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावादः|मायावाद
माया + -वादः the doctrine of illusion, (a term applied to Buddhism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाविद्
माया + -विद् <i>a.</i> skilled in deception or magical arts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायासुतः|मायासुत
माया + -सुतः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामय
मायामय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Illusive, illusory, deceitful.<BR>—2 False, unreal.<BR>—3 Magical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावत्|मायावन्त्
मायावत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deceitful, fraudulent.<BR>—2 Illusory, unreal, deceptive.<BR>—3 Skilled in magical arts, employing magical powers. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Kamsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावती
मायावत् + .{@-ती@} N. of the wife of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाविन्
मायाविन् <i>a.</i> [माया-अस्त्यर्थे विनि]<BR>—1 Using deceit or tricks, employing stratagems, deceitful, fraudulent;<BR> व्रजन्ति ते मूढधियः पराभवं भवन्ति मायाविषु ये न मायिनः Ki. 1. 30;<BR> R. 10. 45.<BR>—2 Skilled in magic.<BR>—3 Unreal, illusory. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A magician, conjurer.<BR>—2 A cat. ━<i>n.</i> A gall-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक <i>a.</i> [माया-ठन्]<BR>—1 Deceitful, fraudulent.<BR>—2 Illusory, unreal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिकः|मायिक|मायिकं
मायिक + .{@-कः@} A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिकम्
मायिक + .{@-कम्@} A gall-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिन्
मायिन् [माया-इनि] See मायाविन्. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A conjurer.<BR>—2 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—3 A deceitful or treacherous person; जातवेदोमुखान्मायी मिषतामाच्छिनत्ति<BR> नः Ku. 2. 46.<BR>—4 N. of Brahman.<BR>—5 Of Kāma.<BR>—6 Of Agni.<BR>—7 Śiva; मायां तु प्रकृतिं विद्यान्मायिनं तु महेश्वरम् Śvet. Up. 4. 10.<BR>━<i>n.</i> Magic, magical art.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायातिः|मायाति
मायातिः The sacrifice to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुः|मायु
मायुः<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 Bile, bilious humour; (<i>n.</i> also in this sense).<BR>—3 Sorcery, bad art.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुराजः|मायुराज
मायुराजः Son of Kubera; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूर|मायूरं
मायूर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मयूर-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to or arising from a peacock; मायूरी मदयति मार्जना मनांसि<BR> M. 1. 21; Rām. 2. 91. 70.<BR>—2 Made of the feathers of a peacock.<BR>—3 Drawn by a peacock (as a car).<BR>—4 Dear to a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरम्
मायूर + .{@-रम्@} A flock of peacocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरी
मायूर + .{@-री@} N. of a plant (अजमोदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरकः|मायूरक
मायूरकः, -मायूरिकः<BR>—1 A peacock-catcher.<BR>—2 One who makes various articles with peacock feathers; Rām. 2. 83. 13<BR> (com. मायूरका लीलामयूरग्राहिणः यद्वा मयूरपिच्छैश्छत्रादिव्यजनकारिणः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरिकः|मायूरिक
मायूरकः, -मायूरिकः<BR>—1 A peacock-catcher.<BR>—2 One who makes various articles with peacock feathers; Rām. 2. 83. 13<BR> (com. मायूरका लीलामयूरग्राहिणः यद्वा मयूरपिच्छैश्छत्रादिव्यजनकारिणः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारः|मार
मारः [मृ-घञ्]<BR>—1 Killing, slaughter, slaying; अशेषप्राणिनामासीदमारो दश वत्सरान्<BR> Rāj. T. 5. 64.<BR>—2 An obstacle, hindrance, opposition.<BR>—3 The god of love; श्यामात्मा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">Page1264-1</a>]<BR> कुटिलः करोतु कबरीभारोपि मारोद्यमम् Gīt. 3; (where मार primarily<BR> means ‘killing’); Nāg. 1. 1.<BR>—4 Love, passion.<BR>—5 The thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR>—6 An evil one, a destroyer; the tempter (according to Buddhists); सेर्ष्यं मारवधूभिरित्यभिहितो बोधौ जिनः पातु वः Nāg. 1. 1; Pt. 5. 14.<BR>—7 Death.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: माराङ्क, माराभिभूः, मारारिः, माररिपुः, मारात्मक, मारजातकः, मारजित्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1263-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माराङ्क|मारांक
मारः + -अङ्क <i>a.</i> ‘marked by love’, displaying signs of love; माराङ्के<BR> रतिकेलिसंकुलरणारम्भे Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माराभिभूः
मारः + -अभिभूः (भुः ?) an epithet of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारारिः|मारारि
मारः + -अरिः, -रिपुः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माररिपुः|माररिपु
मारः + -अरिः, -रिपुः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारात्मक
मारः + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> murderous; कथं मारात्मके त्वयि विश्वासः कर्तव्यः H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजातकः|मारजातक
मारः + -जातकः a cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारजित्
मारः + -जित् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारक|मारकः
मारक <i>a.</i> [मृ-णिच् ण्वुल्] (At the end of comp.) Killing, destroying, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकः|मारक
मारक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Any pestilential disease, plague, epidemic.<BR>—2 The god of love.<BR>—3 A murderer, destroyer in general.<BR>—4 A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकम्
मारक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Death of all creatures at the dissolution of the universe.<BR>—2 Vermilion (Mar. हिंगूळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारणम्
मारणम् [मृ-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Killing, slaying, slaughter, destruction; पशुमारणकर्मदारुणः Ś. 6. 1.<BR>—2 A magical ceremony performed for the purpose of destroying an enemy.<BR>—3 Calcination.<BR>—4 A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिः|मारि
मारिः <i>f.</i> [मृ-णिच्-इनि]<BR>—1 A pestilence, plague; दुर्भिक्षमार्यरिष्टानि Bhāg. 10. 56. 11.<BR>—2 Killing, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिका
मारिका A plague, pestilence; विबुध्य तां बालकमारिकाग्रहम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारित|मारितः
मारित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Slain, killed.<BR>—2 Destroyed, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिन्
मारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Dying.<BR>—2 Killing, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारी
मारी<BR>—1 Plague, pestilence, an epidemic.<BR>—2 Pestilence personified (the goddess presiding over plagues and identified with Durgā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकत
मारकत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to an emerald; यत्र विद्रुमसोपाना महामारकता<BR> भुवः Bhāg. 7. 4. 9; काचः काञ्चनसंसर्गाद्धत्ते मारकतीं द्युतिम् H. Pr. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारव
मारव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Desert, belonging to a wilderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारवी
मारव + .{@-वी@} N. of a particular musical scale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिच
मारिच <i>a.</i> (-ची <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिचिक|मारिचिकं
मारिचिक <i>a.</i> Peppered, seasoned with pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिषः|मारिष
मारिषः<BR>—1 A respectable, worthy or venerable man, (used in dramas in the voc.<BR> as a respectful mode of address by the Sūtradhāra to one of the principal<BR> actors; see U. 1; Māl. 1.); शूरो मातामहः कच्चित् स्वस्त्यास्ते वाऽथ<BR> मारिषः Bhāg. 1. 14. 26.<BR>—2 Amaranthus Oleraceus (Mar. तांदुळजा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच|मारीचः
मारीच <i>a.</i> (-ची <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to or composed by Marīci.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीचः|मारीच
मारीच + .{@-चः@}<BR>—1 N. of a demon, son of Sunda and Tāḍakā. He assumed the form of a<BR> golden deer, and thus enticed Rāma to a considerable distance from Sītā,<BR> so that Rāvaṇa found a good opportunity to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">Page1264-2</a>]<BR> carry her off.<BR>—2 A large or royal elephant.<BR>—3 A kind of plant (Mar. कंकोळ).<BR>—4 N. of the sage Kaśyapa; cf. स्वायंभुवान्मरीचेर्यः प्रबभूव प्रजापतिः Ś. 7. 9.<BR>—5 A sacrificing priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीची
मारीच + .{@-ची@}<BR>—1 N. of the mother of Śākyamuni.<BR>—2 N. of a Buddhist goddess.<BR>—3 N. of an Apsaras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीचम्
मारीच + .{@-चम्@} A collection of pepper shrubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुङ्गः|मारुङ्ग
मारुङ्गः Softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुण्डः|मारुण्ड|मारुंड|मारुंडः
मारुण्डः<BR>—1 A serpentʼs egg.<BR>—2 Cow-dung.<BR>—3 A way, road.<BR>—4 A place covered with cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुत|मारुतः
मारुत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मरुतः इदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to or arising from the Maruts; व्रतमेतद्धि मारुतम् Ms. 9. 306.<BR>—2 Relating to wind, aerial, windy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतः|मारुत
मारुत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Wind; स कीचकैर्मारुतपूर्णरन्ध्रैः R. 2. 12, 34, 4. 55; Ms. 4. 122.<BR>—2 The god of wind, the deity presiding over wind; मनोजवं मारुततुल्यवेगम्<BR> Rāmarakṣā. 33<BR>—3 Breathing.<BR>—4 Vital air, one of the three essential humours of the body; प्रविश्य<BR> सर्वभूतानि यथा चरति मारुतः Ms. 9. 306.<BR>—5 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>—6 Ved. A son of the Maruts.<BR>—7 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—8 Of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुती
मारुत + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 The north-west quarter.<BR>—2 The daughter of the Maruts or gods; उतथ्यस्य च भार्यायां ममतायां<BR> महातपाः । मारुत्यां जनयामास भरद्वाजं बृहस्पतिः ॥ Bu. C. 4. 74;<BR> cf. V. P. 4. 19. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतम्
मारुत + .{@-तम्@} The lunar mansion called Svāti.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मारुतायनम्, मारुताशनः, मारुतात्मजः, मारुतसुतः, मारुतसूनुः, मारुतव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतायनम्
मारुत + -अयनम् a (round) window; केलीमन्दिरमारुतायनमुखे विन्यस्तवक्त्राम्बुजा Bv. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुताशनः|मारुताशन
मारुत + -अशनः a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतात्मजः|मारुतात्मज
मारुत + -आत्मजः, -सुतः, -सूनुः<BR>—1 epithets of Hanumat.<BR>—2 of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतसुतः|मारुतसुत
मारुत + -आत्मजः, -सुतः, -सूनुः<BR>—1 epithets of Hanumat.<BR>—2 of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतसूनुः|मारुतसूनु
मारुत + -आत्मजः, -सुतः, -सूनुः<BR>—1 epithets of Hanumat.<BR>—2 of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतव्रतम्
मारुत + -व्रतम् ‘penetrating everywhere’, one of the duties of a king<BR> (who is able to penetrate everywhere by means of spies); cf. प्रविश्य<BR> सर्वभूतानि यथा चरति मारुतः । तथा चरैः प्रवेष्टव्यं व्रतमेतद्धि<BR> मारुतम् ॥ Ms. 9. 306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतिः|मारुति
मारुतिः [मरुतोऽपत्यम् इञ्]<BR>—1 An epithet of Hanumat; मारुतिः सागरं तीर्णः संसारमिव निर्ममः R. 12. 60.<BR>—2 Of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कट
मार्कट <i>a.</i> Apish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मार्कटपिपीलिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कटपिपीलिका
मार्कट + -पिपीलिका a small black ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डः|मार्कण्ड|मार्कंड|मार्कंडः
मार्कण्डः, -मार्कण्डेयः<BR> [मृकण्डोरपत्यम् अण् ढक्] N. of an ancient sage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मार्कण्डपुराणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डेयः|मार्कण्डेय|मार्कंडेय|मार्कंडेयः
मार्कण्डः, -मार्कण्डेयः<BR> [मृकण्डोरपत्यम् अण् ढक्] N. of an ancient sage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मार्कण्डपुराणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कण्डपुराणम्
मार्कण्डः + -पुराणम् N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas (composed by this<BR> sage); यः शृणोति नरो भक्त्या पुराणमिदमादरात् । मार्कण्डेयाभिधं वत्स<BR> स लभेत परां गतिम् ॥ Nārada P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्
मार्ग् I. €1 P., €10 U. (मार्गति, मार्गयति-ते)<BR>—1 To seek, seek for; हृतदारः सह भ्रात्रा पत्नीं मार्गन् स राघवः<BR> Mb. 3. 148. 1.<BR>—2 To hunt after, chase.<BR>—3 To strive to attain, strive after; आत्मोत्कर्षं न मार्गेत परेषां<BR> परिनिन्दया । स्वगुणैरेव मार्गेत विप्रकर्षं पृथग्जनात् Subhāṣ.<BR>—4 To solicit, beg, ask for; वरं वरेण्यो नृपतेरमार्गीत् Bk. 1. 12; Y. 2. 66.<BR>—5 To ask in marriage.<BR>—6 To seek through, trace out. ━II. €10 U. (मार्गयति-ते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To decorate, adorn. ━<i>With</i> {@परि@} to seek, look out for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गः|मार्ग
मार्गः [मृज्-शुद्धौ, मार्ग्-अन्वेषणे घञ् वा]<BR>—1 A way, road, path (fig. also); मार्गो दशकरः प्रोक्तो ग्रामेषु नगरेषु च Śukra. 1. 261;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1265-1" target="_blank">Page1265-1</a>]<BR> अग्निशरणमार्गमादेशय Ś. 5; so विचारमार्गप्रहितेन<BR> चेतसा Ku. 5. 42; R. 2. 72; U. 3. 37.<BR>—2 A course, passage, the tract passed over; वायोरिमं परिवहस्य वदन्ति<BR> मार्गम् Ś. 7. 6.<BR>—3 Reach, range; मार्गातीतायेन्द्रियाणां नमस्ते Ki. 18. 40.<BR>—4 A scar, mark (left by a wound &c.); भोगिवेष्टनमार्गेषु R. 4. 48;<BR> ते पुत्रयोर्नैरृतशस्त्रमार्गानार्द्रानिवाङ्गे सदयं स्पृशन्त्यौ 14. 4.<BR>—5 The path or course of a planet.<BR>—6 Search, inquiry, investigation.<BR>—7 A canal, channel, passage.<BR>—8 A means, way.<BR>—9 The right way or course, proper course; सुमार्ग, अमार्ग.<BR>—10 Mode, manner, method, course; शान्ति˚ R. 7. 71.<BR>—11 Style, direction; इति वैदर्भमार्गस्य प्राणा दश गुणाः स्मृताः<BR> Kāv. 1. 42; वाचां विचित्रमार्गाणाम् 1. 9.<BR>—12 Custom, usage, practice; कुल˚, शास्त्र˚, घर्म˚ &c.<BR>—13 Hunting or tracing out game.<BR>—14 A title or head in law, ground for litigation; अष्टादशसु मार्गेषु<BR> निबद्धानि पूथक् पृथक् Ms. 8. 3.<BR>—15 A high style of acting, dancing and singing; अगायतां मार्गविधानसंपदा<BR> Rām. 1. 4. 36 (com. गानं द्विविधम् । मार्गो देशी चेति । तत्र प्राकृतावलम्बि<BR> गानं देशी । संस्कृतावलम्बि तु गानं मार्गः).<BR>—16 (In dramaturgy) Hinting or indicating how anything is to happen.<BR>—17 (In geom.) A section.<BR>—18 The anus.<BR>—19 Musk.<BR>—20 The constellation called मृगशिरस्.<BR>—21 The month called मार्गशीर्ष.<BR>—22 N. of Viṣṇu (as the way to final emancipation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गम्
मार्गः + .{@-र्गम्@} A herd of deer; मार्गमदन्या बीथ्या नागवनं प्रयातो भर्ता<BR> Pratijñā. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मार्गागतः, मार्गाख्यायिन्, मार्गायातः, मार्गारब्ध, मार्गाली, मार्गोपदेशकः, मार्गतालः, मार्गतोरणम्, मार्गदर्शकः, मार्गद्रङ्गः, मार्गद्रुमः, मार्गधेनुः, मार्गधेनुकम्, मार्गपतिः, मार्गपरिणायकः, मार्गपाली, मार्गबन्धनम्, मार्गरक्षकः, मार्गवटी, मार्गविनोदनम्, मार्गशोधकः, मार्गसंस्करणम्, मार्गस्थ, मार्गहर्म्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1264-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

