मार्दलिकः A drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दवम्
मार्दवम् [मृदोर्भावः अण्]<BR>—1 Softness (lit. and fig.), pliancy, weakness; अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं<BR> भजते कैव कथा शरीरिषु R. 8. 43 ‘becomes soft’; स्वशरीरमार्दवम् Ku. 5. 18.<BR>—2 Mildness, indulgence, gentleness, leniency; Bg. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्वीक
मार्द्वीक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of grapes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्वीकम्
मार्द्वीक + .{@-कम्@} Wine; मार्द्वीकं प्रियतमसंनिधानमासन् नारीणामिति जलकेलिसाधनानि Śi. 8. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्मिक
मार्मिक <i>a.</i> [मर्म जानाति ठञ्] Having a deep insight into,<BR> fully conversant with the essence, beauty &c.; (= मर्मज्ञ q. v.);<BR> मार्मिकः को मरन्दानामन्तरेण मधुव्रतम् Bv. 1. 117; परिणतमकरन्दमार्मिकास्ते<BR> जगति भवन्तु चिरायुषो मिलिन्दाः 1. 8, 4. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्षः|मार्ष
मार्षः, -मार्षकः<BR> See मारिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्षकः|मार्षक
मार्षः, -मार्षकः<BR> See मारिष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष्टिः|मार्ष्टि
मार्ष्टिः <i>f.</i> [मृज्-क्तिन्] Cleansing, scouring, purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालः|माल|मालं
मालः<BR>—1 N. of a district in the west or south-west of Bengal.<BR>—2 N. of a tribe of barbarians, a mountaineer.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालम्
मालः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A field.<BR>—2 A high ground, rising or elevated ground (मालमुन्नतभूतलम्);<BR> क्षेत्रमारुह्य मालम् Me. 16 (शैलप्रायमुन्नतस्थलम् Malli.).<BR>—3 A wood near a village.<BR>—4 Fraud, deceit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मालचक्रकम्, मालजातकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालचक्रकम्
मालः + -चक्रकम् the hip-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालजातकम्
मालः + -जातकम् a civet-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालकः|मालक|मालकं
मालकः<BR>—1 The <i>Nimba</i> tree.<BR>—2 A wood near a village.<BR>—3 A pot made of a cocoa-nut shell.<BR>—4 An arbour,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">Page1266-2</a>]<BR> bower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालका
मालकः + .{@-का, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A garland.<BR>—2 The land-growing lotus; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालकम्
मालकः + .{@-का, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A garland.<BR>—2 The land-growing lotus; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाका
मालाका <i>f.</i> A garland; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालकौशः|मालकौश
मालकौशः N. of a Rāga or musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिः|मालति
मालतिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of jasmine (with fragrant white flowers); तन्मन्ये क्वचिदङ्ग<BR> भृङ्गतरुणेनास्वादिता मालती G. M.; जालकैर्मालतीनाम् Me. 100; Ki. 10. 20.<BR>—2 A flower of this jasmine; शिरसि बकुलमालां मालतीभिः समेताम् Ṛs. 2. 24.<BR>—3 A bud, blossom (in general).<BR>—4 A virgin, young woman.<BR>—5 Night.<BR>—6 Moonlight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मालतिक्षारकः, मालतीरजम्, मालतिपत्रिका, मालतिफलम्, मालतिमाधवम्, मालतिमाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालती
मालतिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of jasmine (with fragrant white flowers); तन्मन्ये क्वचिदङ्ग<BR> भृङ्गतरुणेनास्वादिता मालती G. M.; जालकैर्मालतीनाम् Me. 100; Ki. 10. 20.<BR>—2 A flower of this jasmine; शिरसि बकुलमालां मालतीभिः समेताम् Ṛs. 2. 24.<BR>—3 A bud, blossom (in general).<BR>—4 A virgin, young woman.<BR>—5 Night.<BR>—6 Moonlight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मालतिक्षारकः, मालतीरजम्, मालतिपत्रिका, मालतिफलम्, मालतिमाधवम्, मालतिमाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिक्षारकः|मालतिक्षारक
मालतिः + -क्षारकः, मालतीरजम् borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतीरजम्
मालतिः + -क्षारकः, मालतीरजम् borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिपत्रिका
मालतिः + -पत्रिका the shell of a nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिफलम्
मालतिः + -फलम् nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिमाधवम्
मालतिः + -माधवम् N. of a celebrated drama by Bhavabhūti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालतिमाला
मालतिः + -माला<BR>—1 a garland of jasmine flowers.<BR>—2 a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालय|मालयः
मालय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मलये भवः अण्] Coming from the Malaya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालयः|मालय
मालय + .{@-यः@} Sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालयम्
मालय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 caravansary.<BR>—2 the unguent prepared from sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवः|मालव
मालवः<BR>—1 N. of a country, the modern Mālvā in central India.<BR>—2 N. of a Rāga or musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवाः
मालवः + .{@-वाः@} (pl.) The people of Mālvā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मालवाधीशः, मालवेन्द्रः, मालवनृपतिः, मालवगौडः, मालवदेशः, मालवविषयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवाधीशः|मालवाधीश
मालवः + -अधीशः, -इन्द्रः, -नृपतिः a king of Mālvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवेन्द्रः|मालवेन्द्र|मालवेंद्र
मालवः + -अधीशः, -इन्द्रः, -नृपतिः a king of Mālvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवनृपतिः|मालवनृपति
मालवः + -अधीशः, -इन्द्रः, -नृपतिः a king of Mālvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवगौडः|मालवगौड
मालवः + -गौडः (in music) a particular Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवदेशः|मालवदेश
मालवः + -देशः, -विषयः the country of Mālvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवविषयः|मालवविषय
मालवः + -देशः, -विषयः the country of Mālvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालवकः|मालवक
मालवकः<BR>—1 The country of the Mālavas.<BR>—2 An inhabitant of Mālvā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालविका
मालविका<BR>—1 N. of the heroine of Kālidāsaʼs Mālavikāgnimitra.<BR>—2 N. of a plant निशोत्तर, Ipomoea Turpethum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालसी
मालसी<BR>—1 N. of a plant (केशपुष्ट).<BR>—2 N. of a Rāgiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माला
माला [मल् संज्ञायां कर्तरि घञ्]<BR>—1 A garland, wreath, chaplet; अनधिगतपरिमलापि हि हरति दृशं मालतीमाला Vās.<BR>—2 A row, line, series, succession; गण्डोड्डीनालिमाला Māl. 1. 1; आबद्धमालाः Me. 9.<BR>—3 A group, cluster, collection.<BR>—4 A string, necklace; as in रत्नमाला.<BR>—5 A rosary, chain; as in अक्षमाला.<BR>—6 A streak; as in तडिन्माला, विद्युन्माला.<BR>—7 A series of epithets.<BR>—8 (In dramas) The offering of several things to obtain a wish. —9 A vocabulary, dictionary.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मालोपमा, मालाकण्टः, मालाकरः, मालाकारः, मालागुणः, मालागुणा, मालातृणम्, मालादीपकम्, मालाधर, मालाधरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालोपमा
माला + -उपमा a variety of Upamā or simile, in which one <i>Upameya</i><BR> is compared to several <i>Upamānas</i>; <i>e. g.</i> अनयेनेव राज्यश्रीर्दैन्येनेव<BR> मनस्विता । मम्लौ साथ विषादेन पद्मिनीव हिमाम्भसा K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाकण्टः|मालाकण्ट
माला + -कण्टः N. of a plant (अपामार्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाकरः|मालाकर
माला + -करः, -कारः<BR>—1 a garland-maker, florist, gardener; कृती मालाकारो बकुलमपि कुत्रापि<BR> निदधे Bv. 1. 54; Pt. 1. 220.<BR>—2 the tribe of gardeners.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाकारः|मालाकार
माला + -करः, -कारः<BR>—1 a garland-maker, florist, gardener; कृती मालाकारो बकुलमपि कुत्रापि<BR> निदधे Bv. 1. 54; Pt. 1. 220.<BR>—2 the tribe of gardeners.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालागुणः|मालागुण
माला + -गुणः a necklace. ˚परिक्षिप्ता a marriageable woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालागुणा
माला + -गुणा a species of venomous spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालातृणम्
माला + -तृणम् a kind of fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालादीपकम्
माला + -दीपकम् a variety of दीपक; Mammaṭa thus defines it:−<BR> मालादीपकमाद्यं चेद्यथोत्तरगुणावहम् K. P. 10; see the example given <i>ad loc.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाधर
माला + -धर <i>a.</i> wearing a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालाधरम्
माला + -धरम् a kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1266-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिकः|मालिक
मालिकः [माला तन्निर्माणं शिल्पमस्य ठन्]<BR>—1 A florist, gardener.<BR>—2 A dyer, painter.<BR>—3 A garland-maker.<BR>—4 A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिका
मालिका [मालैव कन् अत इत्वम्]<BR>—1 A garland; पाशाक्षमालिकाम्भोज Lakṣmīdhyānam.<BR>—2 A row, line, series.<BR>—3 A string, necklace.<BR>—4 A variety of jasmine.<BR>—5 Linseed.<BR>—6 A daughter.<BR>—7 A palace.<BR>—8 A kind of bird.<BR>—9 An intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालित
मालित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Garlanded, crowned.<BR>—2 Surrounded by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्
मालिन् <i>a.</i> [माला अस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Wearing a garland.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Crowned or wreathed with, encircled by; समुद्रमालिनी<BR> पृथ्वी; so अंशुमालिन्, मरीचिमालिन्, ऊर्मिमालिन् &c.; व्यराजतादित्य<BR> इवार्चिमाली Rām. 5. 54. 48; युवतिषु कोमलमाल्यमालिनीषु Śi. 7. 61. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A gardener.<BR>—2 A garland-maker, florist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिनी
मालिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A female florist, the wife of a garland-maker.<BR>—2 N. of the city of Champā.<BR>—3 A girl seven years old representing Durgā at the Durgā festival.<BR>—4 N. of Durgā.<BR>—5 The celestial Ganges.<BR>—6 N. of a metre; see App. ननमयययुतेयं मालिनी भोगिलोकैः V. Ratn.<BR>—7 N. of the mother of Bibhīṣaṇa.<BR>—8 N. assumed by Draupadī while residing at the Court of Virāta.<BR>—9 N. of a river; Ś. 3. 7.<BR>—10 (In music) A particular श्रुति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालेयः|मालेय
मालेयः A garland-maker, florist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्य|माल्यं
माल्य <i>a.</i> [मालायै हितं यत्] Proper for or relating to a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यम्
माल्य + .{@-ल्यम्@}<BR>—1 A garland, wreath; माल्येन तां निर्वचनं जघान Ku. 7. 19; Ki. 1. 21.<BR>—2 A flower; दिव्यमाल्याम्बरधरम् Bg. 11. 11; Ms. 4. 72.<BR>—3 A chaplet or garland worn on the head.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: माल्यापणः, माल्यजीवकः, माल्यधारय, माल्यपुष्पः, माल्यवृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यापणः|माल्यापण
माल्य + -आपणः a flower-market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यजीवकः|माल्यजीवक
माल्य + -जीवकः a florist, garland-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यधारय
माल्य + -धारय <i>a.</i> one who wears a garland; नृजग्धो माल्यधारयः Bk. 5. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यपुष्पः|माल्यपुष्प
माल्य + -पुष्पः a kind of hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यवृत्तिः|माल्यवृत्ति
माल्य + -वृत्तिः a florist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्यवत्|माल्यवन्त्
माल्यवत् <i>a.</i> Wreathed, crowned. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of a mountain or mountain range; सोऽयं शैलः ककुभसुरभिर्माल्यवान्नाम<BR> U. 1. 33; R. 13. 26.<BR>—2 N. of a demon, son of Suketu. [He was the maternal uncle and minister<BR> of Rāvaṇa and aided him in many of his schemes. In early times he propitiated<BR> the god Brahman by his austere penance, as a reward of which the splendid<BR> island of Laṅkā was caused to be built for him. He lived there with<BR> his brothers for some years, but afterwards left it, which was then occupied<BR> by Kubera. Afterwards when Rāvaṇa ousted Kubera from the island, Mālyavat<BR> returned with his relatives and lived with him for a long time.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालिन्यम्
मालिन्यम् [मलिनस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Dirtiness, foulness, impurity.<BR>—2 Pollution, defilement.<BR>—3 Sinfulness.<BR>—4 Blackness.<BR>—5 Trouble, affliction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुः|मालु
मालुः, -माल्लः<BR> N. of a particular mixed tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्लः|माल्ल
मालुः, -माल्लः<BR> N. of a particular mixed tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुः|मालु
मालुः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A kind of creeper.<BR>—2 A woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मालुधानः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुधानः|मालुधान
मालुः + -धानः a kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालुकाच्छदः|मालुकाच्छद
मालुकाच्छदः A species of tree (Mar. आपटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूकः|मालूक
मालूकः Ocimum Sanctum (Mar. काळी तुळस).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूरः|मालूर
मालूरः<BR>—1 The <i>Bilva</i> tree.<BR>—2 The <i>Kapittha</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालूरम्
मालूरः + .{@-रम्@} A Bilva fruit; ददर्श मालूरफले पचेलिमम् N. 1. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मालेया
मालेया Large cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माल्लवी
माल्लवी A wrestling or boxing match (also माल्लयात्रा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषः|माष
माषः [मष् संज्ञायां कर्तरि घञ्]<BR>—1 A bean; (the sing. being used for the plant and the pl. for the fruit<BR> or seed); तिलेभ्यः प्रति यच्छति माषान् Sk.; मुद्गाभावे माषाद्याः<BR> प्रतिनिधित्वमर्हन्ति J. N. V.<BR>—2 A particular weight of gold; पञ्चकृष्णलको माषस्ते सुवर्णस्तु षोडश<BR> Ms. 8. 134; माषो विंशतिमो भागः पणस्य परिकीर्तितः or गुञ्जाभिरष्टभिर्माषः<BR>—3 A fool, blockhead.<BR>—4 A kind of pulse.<BR>—5 A cutaneous eruption resembling beans.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: माषादः, माषादः, माषाज्यम्, माषाशः, माषोन, माषपर्णी, माषपिष्टम्, माषपेशम्, माषयोनिः, माषवर्धकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषादः|माषाद
माषः + -अदः, -आदः a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषादः|माषाद
माषः + -अदः, -आदः a tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषाज्यम्
माषः + -आज्यम् a dish of beans cooked with ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषाशः|माषाश
माषः + -आशः a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषोन
माषः + -ऊन <i>a.</i> less by a Māṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषपर्णी
माषः + -पर्णी Glycine Debilis (Mar. रानौडीद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषपिष्टम्
माषः + -पिष्टम् a kind of sauce prepared from the flour of Māṣa (Mar.<BR> डांगर ?) Gaṇeśa P. 49. 47-51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषपेशम्
माषः + -पेशम् <i>ind.</i> as if beans were ground; Mk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषयोनिः
माषः + -योनिः a thin cake (पर्पट) made of Māṣa flour; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषवर्धकः|माषवर्धक|माषवर्द्धकः
माषः + -वर्धकः a goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषकः|माषक
माषकः<BR>—1 A bean.<BR>—2 A kind of weight of gold; द्वे कृष्णले समधृते विज्ञेयो रौप्यमाषकः Ms. 8. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषिक
माषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Worth a Māṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषीण|माषीणं
माषीण <i>a.</i> [माषाणां भवनं क्षेत्रं खञ्] Sown with beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माषीणम्
माषीण + .{@-णम्@} A field of beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष्य|माष्यं
माष्य <i>a.</i> [माष-यत्]<BR>—1 Fit for beans.<BR>—2 Worth a particular number of Māṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माष्यम्
माष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} A field of beans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्
मास् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 = मास q. v.; चतुर्थे मासि कर्तव्यं शिशोर्निष्क्रमणं गृहात्<BR> Ms. 2. 34. (This word has no forms for the first five inflections and<BR> is optionally substituted for मास after acc. dual.)<BR>—2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासः|मास|मासं
मासः, -सम्<BR> [मा एव अण्]<BR>—1 A month, (it may be चान्द्र, सौर, सावन, नाक्षत्र or बार्हस्पत्य);<BR> न मासे प्रतिपत्तासे मां चेन्मर्तासि मैथिलि Bk. 8. 95.<BR>—2 The moon (Ved.).<BR>—3 The number ‘twelve’.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मासाधिपः, मासाधिपतिः, मासानुमासिक, मासान्तः, मासावधिक, मासाहार, मासोपवासिनी, मासर्क्षम्, मासकालिक, मासचारिक, मासजात, मासज्ञः, मासदेय, मासपाक, मासप्रमितः, मासप्रवेशः, मासभुक्तिः, मासमानः, माससंचयिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासम्
मासः, -सम्<BR> [मा एव अण्]<BR>—1 A month, (it may be चान्द्र, सौर, सावन, नाक्षत्र or बार्हस्पत्य);<BR> न मासे प्रतिपत्तासे मां चेन्मर्तासि मैथिलि Bk. 8. 95.<BR>—2 The moon (Ved.).<BR>—3 The number ‘twelve’.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मासाधिपः, मासाधिपतिः, मासानुमासिक, मासान्तः, मासावधिक, मासाहार, मासोपवासिनी, मासर्क्षम्, मासकालिक, मासचारिक, मासजात, मासज्ञः, मासदेय, मासपाक, मासप्रमितः, मासप्रवेशः, मासभुक्तिः, मासमानः, माससंचयिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासाधिपः|मासाधिप
मासः + -अधिपः, -अधिपतिः the planet presiding over a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासाधिपतिः|मासाधिपति
मासः + -अधिपः, -अधिपतिः the planet presiding over a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासानुमासिक
मासः + -अनुमासिक <i>a.</i> monthly; पिण्डान्वाहार्यकं श्राद्धं कुर्यान्मासानुमासिकम् Ms. 3. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासान्तः|मासान्त|मासांत
मासः + -अन्तः the day of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासावधिक
मासः + -अवधिक <i>a.</i> lasting for or occurring in a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासाहार
मासः + -आहार <i>a.</i> eating only once a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासोपवासिनी
मासः + -उपवासिनी<BR>—1 a woman who fasts for a whole month.<BR>—2 a procuress, a lascivious or lewd woman (ironically.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासर्क्षम्
मासः + -ॠक्षम् the constellation after which a month (like चैत्र, वैशाख)<BR> is named; माघे च सितसप्तम्यां मघाराकासमागमे । राकया चानुमत्वा<BR> वा मासार्क्षाणि युतान्यपि ॥ Bhāg. 7. 14. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासकालिक
मासः + -कालिक <i>a.</i> monthly, lasting for a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासचारिक
मासः + -चारिक <i>a.</i> practising (any thing) for a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासजात
मासः + -जात <i>a.</i> a month old, born a month ago.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासज्ञः|मासज्ञ
मासः + -ज्ञः a kind of gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासदेय
मासः + -देय <i>a.</i> to be paid in a month.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">Page1268-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1267-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासपाक
मासः + -पाक <i>a.</i> maturing in a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासप्रमितः|मासप्रमित
मासः + -प्रमितः the new-moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासप्रवेशः|मासप्रवेश
मासः + -प्रवेशः the beginning of a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासभुक्तिः|मासभुक्ति
मासः + -भुक्तिः (the sunʼs) monthly course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासमानः|मासमान
मासः + -मानः a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माससंचयिक
मासः + -संचयिक <i>a.</i> having provisions for a month; सद्यःप्रक्षालको<BR> वा स्यान्माससंचयिकोऽपि वा Ms. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासकः|मासक
मासकः A month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासिक|मासिकं|मासिकः
मासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मासे भवः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Relating to a month.<BR>—2 Happening every month, monthly.<BR>—3 Lasting for a month.<BR>—4 Payable in a month.<BR>—5 Engaged for a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासिकम्
मासिक + .{@-कम्@} A funeral rite or Śrāddha performed every newmoon (during<BR> the first year of a manʼs death); पितॄणां मासिकं श्राद्धमन्वाहार्यं<BR> विदुर्बुधाः; मासिकान्नं तु योऽश्नीयात् Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासीन
मासीन <i>a.</i> [मास-खञ्]<BR>—1 One month old.<BR>—2 Monthly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मास्य
मास्य <i>a.</i> [मास-यत्] (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Continuing for a month.<BR>—2 A month old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासरः|मासर
मासरः<BR>—1 The scum of boiled rice, rice-gruel.<BR>—2 The meal of parched barley mixed with sour milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासलः|मासल
मासलः A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासुरी
मासुरी A beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मासूर
मासूर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Lentil-shaped.<BR>—2 Made of pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माह्
माह् €1 U. (माहति-ते) To measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहनः|माहन
माहनः [मा + हन्] A Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहा
माहा A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुल|माहाकुलः
माहाकुल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>), माहाकुलीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nobly born, of noble family, of illustrious descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुली
माहाकुल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>), माहाकुलीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nobly born, of noble family, of illustrious descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुलीन|माहाकुलीनः
माहाकुल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>), माहाकुलीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nobly born, of noble family, of illustrious descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाकुलीनी
माहाकुल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>), माहाकुलीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Nobly born, of noble family, of illustrious descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनिक
माहाजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माहाजनीन@} <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Fit for merchants.<BR>—2 Fit for great persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनिकी
माहाजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माहाजनीन@} <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Fit for merchants.<BR>—2 Fit for great persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनीन
माहाजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माहाजनीन@} <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Fit for merchants.<BR>—2 Fit for great persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाजनीनी
माहाजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>{@माहाजनीन@} <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Fit for merchants.<BR>—2 Fit for great persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्मिक
माहात्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> High-minded, magnanimous, noble, dignified, glorious;<BR> राज्ञो माहात्मिके स्थाने सद्यः शौचं विधीयते Ms. 5. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहात्म्यम्
माहात्म्यम् [महात्मनो भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Magnanimity, noble-mindedness, greatness; गङ्गा च यस्या विदुर्माहात्म्यम् U. 4. 5.<BR>—2 Majesty, dignity, exalted position; अजानन्माहात्म्यं पततु शलभो<BR> दीपदहने Bh.<BR>—3 The peculiar virtue of any divinity or sacred shrine; or a work giving<BR> an account of the merits of such divinities or shrines; as देवीमाहात्म्य,<BR> शनिमाहात्म्य &c.<BR>—4 Largeness, hugeness; ते दृष्ट्वा देहमाहात्म्यं कुम्भकर्णोऽयमुत्थितः ।<BR> भयार्ता वानराः Rām. 6. 71. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहानस
माहानस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to a large carriage.<BR>—2 Relating to a kitchen. Hence माहानसिक = A superintendent of the<BR> kitchen; चिकित्सक-माहानसिक-मौहूर्तिकांश्च पश्येत् Kau. A. 1. 19. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाप्राण
माहाप्राण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Having the aspirate or hard breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाभाग्यम्
माहाभाग्यम् Great prosperity, good luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहायानिक
माहायानिक <i>a.</i> That which propounds the view of the followers<BR> of the Mahāyāna school of Buddhism; यद्येवं प्रत्युक्तः स माहायानिकः<BR> पक्षः । ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराजिक
माहाराजिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Fit for a great king, imperial, royal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराज्यम्
माहाराज्यम् Sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाराष्ट्री
माहाराष्ट्री See महाराष्ट्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहाव्रती
माहाव्रती The doctrine of the Pāśupatas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिन|माहिनं
माहिन <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Joyous, joyful.<BR>—2 Great, exalted.<BR>—3 Giving delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिनम्
माहिन + .{@-नम्@} Sovereignty, power, dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिरः|माहिर
माहिरः An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष
माहिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [महिष्या इदम् अण्] Coming or derived from a buffalo<BR> or a buffalo-cow; as माहिषं दधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषम्
माहिष + .{@-षम्@} The female apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषकः|माहिषक
माहिषकः A buffalo-keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषिकः|माहिषिक
माहिषिकः<BR>—1 A buffalo-keeper, a herdsman.<BR>—2 The paramour of an unchaste woman; (महिषीत्युच्यते नारी या च स्याद्<BR> व्यभिचारिणी । तां दृष्टां कामयति यः स वै माहिषिकः स्मृतः ॥) Kālikā P.<BR>—3 One who lives by the prostitution of his wife; महिषीत्युच्यते नार्या<BR> भगेनोपार्जितं धनम् । उपजीवति यस्तस्याः स वै माहिषिकः स्मतः ॥<BR> Śrīdhara on V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिषेय
माहिषेय A son of the first wife of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्मती
माहिष्मती N. of a city, the hereditary capital of the Haihaya kings;<BR> माहिष्मतीवप्रनितम्बकाञ्चीम् (रेवाम्) R. 6. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्यः|माहिष्य
माहिष्यः A mixed caste sprung from a Kṣatriya father and Vaiśya mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्र|माहेंद्र|माहेन्द्रः
माहेन्द्र <i>a.</i> (-न्द्री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to or fit for Indra; माहेन्द्रमम्भः प्रथमं पृथिव्या Ku. 7. 84;<BR> R. 12. 86.<BR>—2 Eastern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्रम्
माहेन्द्र + .{@-द्रम्@} A kind of pearl; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेन्द्री|माहेंद्री
माहेन्द्र + .{@-द्री@}<BR>—1 The east.<BR>—2 A cow.<BR>—3 N. of Indrāṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेय|माहेयः
माहेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Terrestrial.<BR>—2 Made of earth, earthen; शातकुम्भमयैः कुम्भैर्माहेयैश्चाभिमन्त्रितैः Mb. 8. 10. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेयः|माहेय
माहेय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 The planet Mars.<BR>—2 The demon Naraka.<BR>—3 Coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेयी
माहेयी A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेश्वर|माहेश्वरः
माहेश्वर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to a great lord or to Śiva; अनेन च महाराज माहेश्वरमनुत्तमम् ।<BR> इष्ट्वा यज्ञं … Rām. 6. 7. 19.<BR>—2 Worshipping Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेश्वरः|माहेश्वर
माहेश्वर + .{@-रः@} A worshipper of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहेश्वरी
माहेश्वर + .{@-री@} N. of Pārvatī or Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मि
मि €5 U. (मिनोति, मिनुते; rarely used in classical literature)<BR>—1 To throw, cast, scatter.<BR>—2 To build, erect.<BR>—3 To measure.<BR>—4 To establish.<BR>—5 To observe, perceive.<BR>—6 Ved. To fix in the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1268-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिच्छ्|मिछ्
मिच्छ् €6 P. (मिच्छति)<BR>—1 To hinder, obstruct.<BR>—2 To annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिण्मिण
मिण्मिण <i>a.</i> Speaking indistinctly through the nose. See मिन्मिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्
मित् <i>f.</i> Ved. A column, post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित|मितः
मित <i>p. p.</i> [मि मा-वा-क्त]<BR>—1 Measured, meted or measured out.<BR>—2 Measured off, bounded, defined.<BR>—3 Limited, measured, moderate, little, scanty, sparing, brief (words<BR> &c.); पृष्टः सत्यं मितं ब्रूते स भृत्योऽर्हो महीभुजाम् Pt. 1. 87; R. 9. 34.<BR>—4 Measuring, of the measure of (at the end of comp.), as in ग्रहवसुकरिचन्द्रमिते<BR> वर्षे <i>i. e.</i> in 1889.<BR>—5 Investigated, examined.<BR>—6 Cast, thrown away.<BR>—7 Built.<BR>—8 Established, founded.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिताक्षर, मितार्थ, मितार्थकः, मिताहार, मितद्रुः, मितभाषिन्, मितवाच्, मितभुक्त, मितमति, मितव्ययिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताक्षर
मित + -अक्षर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 brief, measured, short, concise; कथंचिदद्रेस्तनया मिताक्षरं चिरव्यवस्थापितवागभाषत Ku. 5. 63.<BR>—2 composed in verse, metrical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताक्षरा
मित + -अक्षर + .({@-रा@}) N. of a celebrated commentary by Vijñāneśvara on Yājñavalkyaʼs Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितार्थ
मित + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> of measured meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितार्थकः|मितार्थक
मित + -अर्थकः a cautious envoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताहार|मिताहारः
मित + -आहार <i>a.</i> sparing in diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिताहारः|मिताहार
मित + -आहार + .({@-रः@}) moderation in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितद्रुः|मितद्रु
मित + -द्रुः the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितभाषिन्
मित + -भाषिन्, -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking little or measured words; महीयांसः<BR> प्रकृत्या मितभाषिणः Śi. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितवाच्
मित + -भाषिन्, -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking little or measured words; महीयांसः<BR> प्रकृत्या मितभाषिणः Śi. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितभुक्त
मित + -भुक्त <i>a.</i> moderate in diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितमति
मित + -मति <i>a.</i> narrow-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितव्ययिन्
मित + -व्ययिन् <i>a.</i> frugal, economical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितंगम|मितङ्गम|मितंगमः|मितङ्गमः
मितंगम <i>a.</i> Going slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितंगमः|मितङ्गम|मितंगम|मितङ्गमः
मितंगम + .{@-मः@} An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितंपच|मितम्पच|मितम्पचः
मितंपच <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Cooking a measured portion, cooking little; P. III. 2. 34.<BR>—2 Small-sized (utensils).<BR>—3 Sparing, niggardly, stingy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मितिः|मिति
मितिः <i>f.</i> [मा-मि-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Measuring, a measure, weight.<BR>—2 Accurate knowledge.<BR>—3 Proof, evidence.<BR>—4 Determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रः|मित्र|मित्त्रं|मित्रं
मित्रः [मिद्यति स्निह्यति, मिद्-त्र, मि-त्र वा]<BR>—1 The sun; तद्दिनं दुर्दिनं मन्ये यत्र मित्रागमो हि ना Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 N. of an Āditya and usually associated with Varuṇa; cf. Rv. 3. 59.<BR>—3 The deity presiding over the part of rectum (गुदस्थान); गुदं<BR> पुंसो विनिर्भिन्नं मित्रो लोकेश आविशत् Bhāg. 3. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रम्
मित्रः + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 A friend; तन्मित्रमापदि सुखे च समक्रियं यत् Bh. 2. 68; Me. 17.<BR>—2 An ally, the next neighbour of a king; cf. मण्डल.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मित्रानुग्रहणम्, मित्रामित्रम्, मित्राचारः, मित्रोदयः, मित्रोपस्थानम्, मित्रकर्मन्, मित्रकार्यम्, मित्रकृत्यम्, मित्रघ्न, मित्रद्रुह्, मित्रद्रोहिन्, मित्रभम्, मित्रभावः, मित्रभेदः, मित्रयुद्धम्, मित्रलाभः, मित्रवत्सल, मित्रविन्दः, मित्रविषयः, मित्रसप्तमी, मित्रसाह, मित्रहत्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रानुग्रहणम्
मित्रः + -अनुग्रहणम् the act of favouring friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रामित्रम्
मित्रः + -अमित्रम् friend and foe; मित्राऽमित्रस्य चार्जनम् Ms. 12. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्राचारः|मित्राचार
मित्रः + -आचारः conduct towards a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रोदयः|मित्रोदय
मित्रः + -उदयः<BR>—1 sun-rise.<BR>—2 the welfare or prosperity of a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रोपस्थानम्
मित्रः + -उपस्थानम् worship of the sun (part of the morning संध्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रकर्मन्
मित्रः + -कर्मन्, -कार्यम्, -कृत्यम् the business of a friend, a friendly<BR> act or service; मित्रकृत्यमपदिश्य पार्श्वतः (प्रस्थितम्) R. 19. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रकार्यम्
मित्रः + -कर्मन्, -कार्यम्, -कृत्यम् the business of a friend, a friendly<BR> act or service; मित्रकृत्यमपदिश्य पार्श्वतः (प्रस्थितम्) R. 19. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रकृत्यम्
मित्रः + -कर्मन्, -कार्यम्, -कृत्यम् the business of a friend, a friendly<BR> act or service; मित्रकृत्यमपदिश्य पार्श्वतः (प्रस्थितम्) R. 19. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रघ्न
मित्रः + -घ्न <i>a.</i> treacherous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रद्रुह्
मित्रः + -द्रुह्, -द्रोहिन् <i>a.</i> hating a friend, treacherous to a friend,<BR> a false or treacherous friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रद्रोहिन्
मित्रः + -द्रुह्, -द्रोहिन् <i>a.</i> hating a friend, treacherous to a friend,<BR> a false or treacherous friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रभम्
मित्रः + -भम् the अनुराधा constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रभावः|मित्रभाव
मित्रः + -भावः friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रभेदः|मित्रभेद
मित्रः + -भेदः breach of friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयुद्धम्
मित्रः + -युद्धम् a contest between friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रलाभः|मित्रलाभ
मित्रः + -लाभः<BR>—1 acquisition of friends, contracting of friendship.<BR>—2 N. of the first book of the Hitopadeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रवत्सल|मित्रवत्सलः
मित्रः + -वत्सल <i>a.</i> kind to friends, of winning manners.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रविन्दः|मित्रविन्द
मित्रः + -विन्दः an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">Page1269-2</a>]<BR> epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रविषयः|मित्रविषय
मित्रः + -विषयः friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रसप्तमी
मित्रः + -सप्तमी N. of the seventh day in the bright half of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रसाह
मित्रः + -साह <i>a.</i> kind or indulgent to friends; स्वैर्दौहित्रैस्तारितो<BR> मित्रसाहः Mb. 1. 93. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रहत्या
मित्रः + -हत्या the murder of a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रता
मित्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Friendship, friendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रत्वम्
मित्रता, -त्वम्<BR> Friendship, friendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रति
मित्रति Den. P. To be friendly, behave in a friendly manner, act<BR> as a friend towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयु|मित्रयुः
मित्रयु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Friendly-minded.<BR>—2 Winning friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रयुः|मित्रयु
मित्रयु + .{@-युः@} A friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रायते
मित्रायते Den. Ā. To act as a friend, be friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीकृ
मित्रीकृ €8 U. To make a friend of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीभू
मित्रीभू €1 P. To become a friend, make friends with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रीयति
मित्रीयति Den. P. To treat (one) as a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रावरुणौ
मित्रावरुणौ Mitra and Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मित्रिय
मित्रिय <i>a.</i> Friendly, relating to a friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्
मिथ् €1 U. (मेथति-ते)<BR>—1 To associate with.<BR>—2 To unite, pair, copulate.<BR>—3 To hurt, injure, strike, kill.<BR>—4 To understand, perceive, know.<BR>—5 To wrangle, contradict.<BR>—6 To grasp, seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथस्
मिथस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Mutually, reciprocally, to each other; कामान्माता पिता चैनं यदुत्पादयतो<BR> मिथः Ms. 2. 147; oft. in comp. मिथःप्रस्थाने Ś. 2; मिथःसमयात् Ś. 5.<BR>—2 In secret or private, secretly, privately; भर्तुः प्रसादं प्रतिनन्द्य<BR> मूर्ध्ना वक्तुं मिथः प्राक्रमतैवमेनम् Ku. 3. 2, 6. 1; R. 13. 1.<BR>—3 Alternately, by turns.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिथोसम्बन्धन्यायः, मिथःकृत्यम्, मिथःसमयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथोसम्बन्धन्यायः
मिथस् + -असम्बन्धन्यायः a rule of interpretation according to which subsidiary<BR> portions (of a sentence) cannot be connected with one another. This rule<BR> is discussed by Jaimini and Śabara in ‘गुणानां च परार्थत्वादसम्बन्धः समत्वात् स्यात्’ MS. 3. 1. 22 and भाष्य thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथःकृत्यम्
मिथस् + -कृत्यम् mutual obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथःसमयः|मिथःसमय
मिथस् + -समयः mutual agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिलः|मिथिल
मिथिलः N. of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिलाः
मिथिलः + .{@-लाः@} (pl.) N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिला
मिथिलः + .{@-ला@} [मथ्यन्तेऽत्र रिपवः इति मिथिला Uṇ. 1. 57] N. of a city,<BR> capital of the country called Videha, q. v.; मिथिला वदत्ययोध्यां त्वं<BR> स्त्री परपुरुषानुरक्तासि Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथु|मिथुः
मिथु, मिथुः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Ved. Falsely, wrongly.<BR>—2 Alternately.<BR>—3 Together, mutually (मिथः); ब्रह्मादयस्तनुमृतो मिथुरर्द्यमानाः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुः|मिथु
मिथु, मिथुः <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Ved. Falsely, wrongly.<BR>—2 Alternately.<BR>—3 Together, mutually (मिथः); ब्रह्मादयस्तनुमृतो मिथुरर्द्यमानाः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुन|मिथुनं|मिथुनः
मिथुन <i>a.</i> [मिथ्-उनन् किच्च Uṇ. 3. 55] Paired, forming a pair, or couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनः|मिथुन|मिथुनं
मिथुन + .{@-नः@} Ved. A pair, couple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनम्
मिथुन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A pair, couple; मिथुनं परिकल्पितं त्वया सहकारः फलिनी च नन्विमौ<BR> R. 8. 61; Me. 18; U. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Twins.<BR>—3 Union, junction.<BR>—4 Sexual union, copulation, cohabitation<BR>—5 The third sign of the zodiac, <i>Gemini</i>.<BR>—6 (In gram.) A root compounded with a preposition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिथुनभावः, मिथुनयमकम्, मिथुनव्रतिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनभावः|मिथुनभाव
मिथुन + -भावः<BR>—1 forming a couple, state of being a pair.<BR>—2 copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनयमकम्
मिथुन + -यमकम् a particular kind of यमक; cf. Bk. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनव्रतिन्
मिथुन + -व्रतिन् <i>a.</i> practising cohabitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1269-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनायते
मिथुनायते Den. Ā. To copulate, cohabit (sexually).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनिन्
मिथुनिन् <i>m.</i> A wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनीकृ
मिथुनीकृ €8 U. To cause to couple, unite together (the sexes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनीभू
मिथुनीभू €1 Ā. To pair, to be joined or arranged in couples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनीभावः|मिथुनीभाव
मिथुनीभावः Cohabitation, sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथुनेचरः|मिथुनेचर
मिथुनेचरः The ruddy goose (चक्रवाक); cf. द्वन्द्वचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्या
मिथ्या <i>ind.</i> [मिथ्-क्यप्]<BR>—1 Falsely, deceitfully, wrongly, incorrectly; oft. with the force of<BR> an adjective; मणौ महानील इति प्रभावादल्पप्रमाणेऽपि यथा न मिथ्या<BR> R. 18. 42; यदुवाच न तन्मिथ्या 17. 42; मिथ्यैव व्यसनं वदन्ति<BR> मृगयामीदृग्विनोदः कुतः Ś. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Invertedly, contrarily.<BR>—3 To no purpose, in vain, fruitlessly; मिथ्या कारयते चारैर्धोषणां<BR> राक्षसाधिपः Bk. 8. 44; मिथ्यैष व्यवसायस्ते प्रकृतिस्त्वां नियोक्ष्यति<BR> Bg. 18. 59. (मिथ्या वद्-वच् to tell a falsehood, lie. मिथ्या कृ<BR>—1 to falsify.<BR>—2 to contradict. मिथ्या भू to turn out false, be false. मिथ्या ग्रह्<BR> to misunderstand, mistake.) At the beginning of comp. मिथ्या may be<BR> translated by ‘false, untrue, unreal, sham, pretended, feigned’ &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिथ्याध्यवसितिः, मिथ्यापवादः, मिथ्याभिधानम्, मिथ्याभियोगः, मिथ्याभिशंसनम्, मिथ्याभिशापः, मिथ्याचार, मिथ्याहारः, मिथ्योत्तरम्, मिथ्योपचारः, मिथ्याकर्मन्, मिथ्याकारुणिक, मिथ्याकोपः, मिथ्याक्रोधः, मिथ्याक्रयः, मिथ्याग्रहः, मिथ्याग्रहः, मिथ्याग्रहणम्, मिथ्याचतुर्विधम्, मिथ्याचर्या, मिथ्याजल्पितम्, मिथ्याज्ञानम्, मिथ्यादर्शनम्, मिथ्यादृष्टिः, मिथ्यानिरसनम्, मिथ्यापण्डित, मिथ्यापुरुषः, मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञ, मिथ्याप्रत्ययः, मिथ्याफलम्, मिथ्यामतिः, मिथ्यायोगः, मिथ्यालिङ्गधर, मिथ्यावचनम्, मिथ्यावाक्यम्, मिथ्यावादः, मिथ्यावाक्, मिथ्यावादिन्, मिथ्यावार्ता, मिथ्याव्यापारः, मिथ्यावृत्त, मिथ्यासाक्षिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याध्यवसितिः|मिथ्याध्यवसिति
मिथ्या + -अध्यवसितिः <i>f.</i> a figure of speech, an expression of the impossibility<BR> of a thing by making it depend upon an impossible contingency; किंचिन्मिथ्यात्वसिद्धपर्थं<BR> मिथ्यार्थान्तरकल्पनम् । मिथ्याध्यवसितिर्वेश्यां वशयेत् खस्रजं वहन् ॥ Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यापवादः|मिथ्यापवाद
मिथ्या + -अपवादः a false charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिधानम्
मिथ्या + -अभिधानम् a false assertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभियोगः|मिथ्याभियोग
मिथ्या + -अभियोगः a false or groundless charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिशंसनम्
मिथ्या + -अभिशंसनम् calumny, false accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याभिशापः|मिथ्याभिशाप
मिथ्या + -अभिशापः<BR>—1 a false prediction.<BR>—2 a false or unjust claim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचार|मिथ्याचारः
मिथ्या + -आचार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 acting falsely.<BR>—2 hypocritical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचारः|मिथ्याचार
मिथ्या + -आचार + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 wrong treatment (in medic.).<BR>—2 wrong or improper conduct.<BR>—3 a rogue, hypocrite; इन्द्रियार्थान् विमूढात्मा मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते Bg. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याहारः|मिथ्याहार
मिथ्या + -आहारः wrong diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्योत्तरम्
मिथ्या + -उत्तरम् a false or prevaricating reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्योपचारः|मिथ्योपचार
मिथ्या + -उपचारः<BR>—1 pretended kindness or service; मिथ्योपचारैश्च वशीकृतानां किमर्थिनां<BR> वञ्चयितव्यमस्ति H.<BR>—2 (in medic.) a wrong treatment of a malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याकर्मन्
मिथ्या + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> a false act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याकारुणिक
मिथ्या + -कारुणिक <i>a.</i> pretending to be kind; मिथ्याकारुणिकोऽसि निर्घृणतरस्त्त्वत्तः<BR> कुतोऽन्यः पुमान् Pt. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याकोपः|मिथ्याकोप
मिथ्या + -कोपः, -क्रोधः feigned anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याक्रोधः|मिथ्याक्रोध
मिथ्या + -कोपः, -क्रोधः feigned anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याक्रयः|मिथ्याक्रय
मिथ्या + -क्रयः a false price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याग्रहः|मिथ्याग्रह
मिथ्या + -ग्रहः useless obstinacy or persistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याग्रहः|मिथ्याग्रह
मिथ्या + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम् misconception, misunderstanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याग्रहणम्
मिथ्या + -ग्रहः, -ग्रहणम् misconception, misunderstanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचतुर्विधम्
मिथ्या + -चतुर्विधम् four types of lying; मिथ्यैतन्नाभिजानामि तदा तत्र<BR> न संनिधिः । अजातश्चास्मि तत्काले इति मिथ्याचतुर्विधम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याचर्या
मिथ्या + -चर्या hypocrisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याजल्पितम्
मिथ्या + -जल्पितम् a false report or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याज्ञानम्
मिथ्या + -ज्ञानम् a mistake, error, misapprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यादर्शनम्
मिथ्या + -दर्शनम् heresy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यादृष्टिः|मिथ्यादृष्टि
मिथ्या + -दृष्टिः <i>f.</i> heresy, holding heretic or atheistic doctrines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यानिरसनम्
मिथ्या + -निरसनम् denial by oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यापण्डित
मिथ्या + -पण्डित <i>a.</i> educated or learned only in appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यापुरुषः|मिथ्यापुरुष
मिथ्या + -पुरुषः a man only in appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञ
मिथ्या + -प्रतिज्ञ <i>a.</i> false to oneʼs promise, perfidious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याप्रत्ययः|मिथ्याप्रत्यय
मिथ्या + -प्रत्ययः an erroneous perception; यो हि जनित्वा प्रध्वंसते<BR> नैतदेवमिति स मिथ्याप्रत्ययः ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याफलम्
मिथ्या + -फलम् an imaginary advantage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यामतिः|मिथ्यामति
मिथ्या + -मतिः <i>f.</i> delusion, mistake, error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यायोगः|मिथ्यायोग
मिथ्या + -योगः wrong use<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">Page1270-2</a>]<BR> or application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यालिङ्गधर
मिथ्या + -लिङ्गधर <i>a.</i> being anything only in appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावचनम्
मिथ्या + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम्, -वादः an untrue speech, a falsehood, lie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावाक्यम्
मिथ्या + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम्, -वादः an untrue speech, a falsehood, lie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावादः|मिथ्यावाद
मिथ्या + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम्, -वादः an untrue speech, a falsehood, lie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावाक्
मिथ्या + -वाक्, -वादिन् <i>a.</i> lying, false, untruthful; मिथ्यावादिनि दूति … … K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावादिन्
मिथ्या + -वाक्, -वादिन् <i>a.</i> lying, false, untruthful; मिथ्यावादिनि दूति … … K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावार्ता|मिथ्यावार्त्ता
मिथ्या + -वार्ता a false report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्याव्यापारः|मिथ्याव्यापार
मिथ्या + -व्यापारः meddling with anotherʼs affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यावृत्त
मिथ्या + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> of vicious conduct; उद्योगं तव संप्रेक्ष्य मिथ्यावृत्तं<BR> च रावणम् Rām. 6. 17. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यासाक्षिन्
मिथ्या + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a false witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथ्यात्वम्
मिथ्यात्वम्<BR>—1 Falsity, unreality.<BR>—2 Illusion, error.<BR>—3 Inversion.<BR>—4 Perversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्
मिद् I. €1 Ā., €4. €10 U. (मेदते, मेद्यति-ते, मेदयति-ते)<BR>—1 To be unctuous or greasy.<BR>—2 To melt.<BR>—3 To be fat.<BR>—4 To love, feel affection. ━II. €1 U. (मेदति-ते); see मिथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्न
मिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fat; P. VII. 2. 16.<BR>—2 Unctuous, greasy.<BR>—3 Affectionately inclined towards (one).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिद्धम्
मिद्धम्<BR>—1 Sloth, indolence.<BR>—2 Torpor, sleepiness, dulness (of spirits also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्द्|मिंद्
मिन्द् €1. €10 U. (मिन्दति, मिन्दयति-ते). See मिद् II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्मिन|मिन्मिनः
मिन्मिन(ल) <i>a.</i> One who speaks with nasal utterance;<BR> a snuffler; आवृत्य वायुः सकफो धमनीः शब्दवाहिनीः । नरान् करोत्यक्रियकान्<BR> मूकमिन्मिलगद्गदान् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्मिल
मिन्मिन(ल) <i>a.</i> One who speaks with nasal utterance;<BR> a snuffler; आवृत्य वायुः सकफो धमनीः शब्दवाहिनीः । नरान् करोत्यक्रियकान्<BR> मूकमिन्मिलगद्गदान् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिन्व्
मिन्व् €1 P. (मिन्वति)<BR>—1 To sprinkle, moisten.<BR>—2 To honour, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमंक्षा|मिमङ्क्षा
मिमंक्षा A desire to take bath or to sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिमन्थिषा
मिमन्थिषा A desire to churn or to destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मियेधः|मियेध
मियेधः A sacrificial offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मियेध्य
मियेध्य <i>a.</i> Partaking of sacrificial offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिल्
मिल् €6 U. (मिलति-ते, generally मिलति; मिलित)<BR>—1 To join, be united with, accompany; रुमण्वतो मिलितः Ratn. 4.<BR>—2 To come or meet together, meet, gather, assemble; ये चान्ये सुहृदः<BR> समृद्धिसमये द्रव्याभिलाषाकुलास्ते सर्वत्र मिलन्ति H. 1. 183; याताः<BR> किं न मिलन्ति Amaru. 10; मिलितशिलीमुख &c. Gīt. 1; स पात्रेसमितोऽन्यत्र<BR> भोजनान्मिलितो न यः Trik.<BR>—3 To be mixed or united with, come in contact with; मिलति तव तोयैर्मृगमदः G. L. 7.<BR>—4 To meet or encounter (as in fighting); close, close with.<BR>—5 To come to pass, happen.<BR>—6 To embrace, clasp.<BR>—7 To concur.<BR>—8 To find, fall in with. ━<i>Caus.</i> (मेलयति-ते) To bring together,<BR> assemble, convene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलत्
मिलत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Meeting, joining.<BR>—2 Happening, occurring.<BR>—3 Joined, connected.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिलद्व्याध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलद्व्याध
मिलत् + -व्याध <i>a.</i> surrounded or joined by huntsmen; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलनम्
मिलनम् [मिल् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Joining, meeting, assembling together.<BR>—2 Encountering.<BR>—3 Contact, being mixed with, coming in contact with; व्यालनिलयमिलनेन<BR> गरलमिव कलयति मलयसमीरम् Gīt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलित|मिलितः
मिलित <i>p. p.</i> [मिल्-क्त]<BR>—1 Come together, assembled, encountered, combined.<BR>—2 Met, encountered.<BR>—3 Mixed.<BR>—4 Put together, taken in all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1270-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलपत्रः
मिलपत्रः N. of a plant (Mar. आपटा); Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलिन्दः|मिलिन्द|मिलिंदः
मिलिन्दः A bee; परिणतमकरन्दमार्मिकास्ते जगति भवन्तु चिरायुषो<BR> मिलिन्दाः Bv. 1. 8, 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिलिन्दप्रश्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलिन्दप्रश्नः|मिलिन्दप्रश्न
मिलिन्दः + -प्रश्नः N. of a Pāli work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलिन्दकः|मिलिन्दक|मिलिंदक|मिलिंदकः
मिलिन्दकः A kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिलीमिलिन्
मिलीमिलिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्
मिश् €1 P. (मेशति)<BR>—1 To make a sound or noise.<BR>—2 To be angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिशिः|मिशि
मिशिः(षिः, -सिः) <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Anise.<BR>—2 Spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषिः|मिषि
मिशिः(षिः, -सिः) <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Anise.<BR>—2 Spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिसिः|मिसि
मिशिः(षिः, -सिः) <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Anise.<BR>—2 Spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र्
मिश्र् €10 U. (मिश्रयति-ते; strictly a denom. from मिश्र)<BR>—1 To mix, mingle, unite, blend, combine, add; वाचं न मिश्रयति यद्यपि<BR> मे वचोभिः Ś. 1. 30; न मिश्रयति लोचने Bv. 2. 140.<BR>—2 To add to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्र|मिश्रं|मिश्रः
मिश्र <i>a.</i> [मिश्र्-अच्]<BR>—1 Mixed, blended, mingled, combined; गद्यं पद्यं च मिश्रं च तत्<BR> त्रिधैव व्यवस्थितम् Kāv. 1. 11, 31, 32; R. 16. 32; (स राजा) अहन्यहन्यर्थगजाश्वमिश्रैर्वृद्धिं<BR> ययौ सिन्धुरिवाम्बुवेगैः Bu. C. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Associated, connected.<BR>—3 Manifold, diverse; प्रसूतिमिश्राः स्त्रिय उद्विग्नचित्ता ऊचुर्विपाको वृजिनस्यैष<BR> तस्य Bhāg. 4. 5. 9.<BR>—4 Tangled, intertwined.<BR>—5 (At the end of comp.) Having a mixture of, consisting for the most part of.<BR>—6 Mixing, adulterating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रः|मिश्र|मिश्रं
मिश्र + .{@-श्रः@}<BR>—1 A respectable or worthy person; usually affixed to the names of great<BR> men and scholars; आर्यमिश्राः प्रमाणम् M. 1; वसिष्ठमिश्रः; मण्डनमिश्रः &c.<BR>—2 A kind of elephant.<BR>—3 The group of the constellations कृत्तिका and विशाखा.<BR>—4 (In music) A kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रम्
मिश्र + .{@-श्रम्@}<BR>—1 A mixture.<BR>—2 A kind of radish.<BR>—3 (with धन) Principal and interest.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिश्रौदनः, मिश्रचोरः, मिश्रचौरः, मिश्रजः, मिश्रजाति, मिश्रधान्यम्, मिश्रवर्ण, मिश्रवृत्तम्, मिश्रव्यवहारः, मिश्रशब्दः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रौदनः
मिश्र + -ओदनः a food of rice and pulse boiled (Mar. खिचडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रचोरः|मिश्रचोर
मिश्र + -चोरः, -चौरः an adulterator of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रचौरः|मिश्रचौर
मिश्र + -चोरः, -चौरः an adulterator of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रजः|मिश्रज
मिश्र + -जः a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रजाति
मिश्र + -जाति <i>a.</i> of mixed breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रधान्यम्
मिश्र + -धान्यम् mixed grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रवर्ण|मिश्रवर्णं
मिश्र + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> of a mixed colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रवर्णम्
मिश्र + -वर्ण + .({@-र्णम्@})<BR>—1 a kind of black aloe-wood.<BR>—2 a species of sugar-cane.<BR>—3 (in music) a kind of measure. ˚फला Solanum Melongena (Mar. डोरली वांगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रवृत्तम्
मिश्र + -वृत्तम् a mixed story (partly popular and partly supernatural).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रव्यवहारः|मिश्रव्यवहार
मिश्र + -व्यवहारः (in arith.) investigation of composition (of principal and interest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रशब्दः|मिश्रशब्द
मिश्र + -शब्दः a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रक|मिश्रकं|मिश्रकः
मिश्रक <i>a.</i> [मिश्र्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Mixed, mingled.<BR>—2 Mixing, adulterating.<BR>—3 Miscellaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रकः|मिश्रक|मिश्रकं
मिश्रक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A compounder.<BR>—2 An adulterator of mercantile goods; आतिरेक्यं तु मिश्रकः Ms. 11. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रकम्
मिश्रक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Salt produced from salt soil.<BR>—2 The garden of Indra, (also मिश्रकावणम्).<BR>—3 Singing out of tune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रणम्
मिश्रणम् [मिश्र्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Mixing, blending, combining.<BR>—2 (In arith.) Addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रित|मिश्रितं
मिश्रित <i>p. p.</i> [मिश्र्-क्त]<BR>—1 Mixed, blended, combined.<BR>—2 Added.<BR>—3 Respectable.<BR>—4 Promiscuous, miscellaneous (as taste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रीकरणम्
मिश्रीकरणम्<BR>—1 The act of mixing, seasoning.<BR>—2 An ingredient; P. II. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिश्रेया
मिश्रेया Anise (Mar. बडिशेप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्
मिष् I. €6 P. (मिषति)<BR>—1 To open the eyes, wink.<BR>—2 To look at, look helplessly; जातवेदोमुखान्मायी मिषतामाच्छिनत्ति<BR> नः Ku. 2. 46; येनार्ध्यं नृपमण्डलस्य मिषतो भीष्माग्रहस्ताद् धृतम्<BR> Dūtavākyam 1. 41.<BR>—3 To rival, contend, emulate. ━II. €1 P. (मेषति) To wet, moisten, sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषः|मिष|मिषं
मिषः [मिष्-क]<BR>—1 Emulation, rivalry.<BR>—2 The son of a Kṣatriya and a low woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषम्
मिषः + .{@-षम्@} Pretext, disguise, deceit, trick, fraud, false or outward<BR> appearance; बालमेनमेकेन मिषेणानीय Dk. (often used like छल<BR> q. v., to indicate an उत्प्रेक्षा); न रोमकूपौघमिषाज्जगत्कृता कृताश्च<BR> किं दूषणशून्यबिन्दवः N. 1. 21; वदने विनिवेशिता भुजङ्गी पिशुनानां<BR> रसनामिषेण धात्रा Bv. 1. 111; अस्वस्थतामिषेण Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषमिषायते
मिषमिषायते Den. Ā. To crackle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिषिका
मिषिका Nardostachys Jatāmānsī (जटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्ट|मिष्टं|मिष्टः
मिष्ट <i>a.</i> [मिष्-क्त]<BR>—1 Sweet.<BR>—2 Dainty, savoury; किं मिष्टमन्नं खरसूकराणाम्; cf. ‘why cast pearls before swine’.<BR>—3 Moistened, wetted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टम्
मिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 A sweetmeat.<BR>—2 A dainty or savoury dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टा
मिष्ट + .{@-ष्टा@} Sweetness. ˚निम्बू sweet citron.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिष्टान्नम्, मिष्टकर्तृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टान्नम्
मिष्ट + -अन्नम् sweet or savoury food, dainty, sweets; कन्या वरयते<BR> रूपं … … मिष्टान्नमितरेजनाः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिष्टकर्तृ|मिष्टकर्त्तृ
मिष्ट + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> a skilful cook (maker of dainties; Mar. हलवाई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिह्
मिह् €1 P. (मेहति, मीढ)<BR>—1 To make water.<BR>—2 To wet, moisten, sprinkle.<BR>—3 To emit semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ|मीढं|मीढः
मीढ <i>p. p.</i> [मिह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Urined, watered.<BR>—2 Passed (as urine)<BR>—3 Begotten (from oneʼs semen); cf. देवमीढ (= god-begotten); Bhāg. 10. 20. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढम्
मीढ + .{@-ढम्@} Ved.<BR>—1 A battle.<BR>—2 Prize, reward.<BR>—3 Faeces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढः|मीढ|मीढं
मीढ + .{@-ढः@} A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिका
मिहिका<BR>—1 Mist, snow; भूपांसवः खे मिहिका द्युभासः Bhāg. 10. 14. 7.<BR>—2 Camphor; अथ चन्द्रमृणालचन्द्रिकामिहिकाचन्दनचम्पकादिभिः Śiva B. 32. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिहिकारुच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिकारुच्
मिहिका + -रुच् the moon; रात्रीमुचं मिहिकारुचम् N. 19. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिरः|मिहिर
मिहिरः [मिह्-किरच् Uṇ. 1. 51]<BR>—1 The sun; मयि तावन्मिहिरोऽपि निर्दयोऽभूत् Bv. 2. 34; याते मय्यचिरान्निदाघमिहिरज्वालाशतैः<BR> शुष्कताम् 1. 16; N. 2. 36, 13. 54.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR>—4 Wind, air.<BR>—5 An old man.<BR>—6 The <i>Arka</i> plant<BR>—7 An epithet of Buddha; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मिहिरापद्, मिहिरकुलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिरापद्
मिहिरः + -आपद् <i>f.</i> eclipse of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिरकुलः|मिहिरकुल
मिहिरः + -कुलः N. of a prince; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिहिराणः|मिहिराण
मिहिराणः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मी
मी I. €9 U. (मीनाति मीनीते; seldom used in classical literature)<BR>—1 To kill, destroy, hurt, injure.<BR>—2 To lessen, diminish.<BR>—3 To change, alter.<BR>—4 To transgress, violate.<BR>—5 To disappear, be lost.<BR>—6 To stray, go astray. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (मयति, माययति-ते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To know, understand (गतिमत्योः). ━III. €4 Ā. (मीयते) To<BR> die, perish; see प्रमी; जन्तोः प्रमीयमाणस्य जीवो नैवोपलभ्यते Mb. 12. 186. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1271-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीडम्
मीडम् Ved. In a low tone, softly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढुष्टमः|मीढुष्टम
मीढुष्टमः<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva; तदा सर्वाणि भूतानि श्रुत्वा मीढुष्टमोदितम् Bhāg. 4. 7. 6.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीढ्वस्
मीढ्वस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bountiful, liberal; निशम्य कर्म तच्छम्भोर्देवदेवस्य मीढुषः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 7. 46.<BR>—2 Discharging semen; पीवानं श्मश्रुलं प्रेष्ठं मीढ्वांसं याभकोविदम्<BR> Bhāg. 9. 19. 5. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Śiva; ललाटाक्षाय शर्वाय मीढुषे<BR> शूलपाणये (नमः) Mb. 3. 39. 77; Bhāg. 4. 7. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनः|मीन
मीनः [मी-नक्]<BR>—1 A fish; सुप्तमीन इव ह्रदः R. 1. 73; मीनो नु हन्त कतमां<BR> गतिमभ्युपैतु Bv. 1. 17.<BR>—2 The twelfth sign of the zodiac (<i>Pisces</i>).<BR>—3 The first incarnation of Viṣṇu; see मत्स्यावतार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीना
मीनः + .{@-ना@} A stick.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मीनाक्षी, मीनाण्डम्, मीनाघातिन्, मीनघातिन्, मीनालयः, मीनकेतनः, मीनध्वजः, मीनगन्धा, मीनगन्धिका, मीनघातिन्, मीनरङ्कः, मीनरङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाक्षी
मीनः + -अक्षी N. of a deity (worshipped in Madurā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाण्डम्
मीनः + -अण्डम् roe, fish-spawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाण्डा
मीनः + -अण्डम् + .({@-ण्डा@}) moist sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाघातिन्
मीनः + -आघातिन्, -घातिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a fisherman.<BR>—2 a crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनघातिन्
मीनः + -आघातिन्, -घातिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a fisherman.<BR>—2 a crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनालयः|मीनालय
मीनः + -आलयः the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनकेतनः|मीनकेतन
मीनः + -केतनः, -ध्वजः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनध्वजः|मीनध्वज
मीनः + -केतनः, -ध्वजः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनगन्धा|मीनगंधा
मीनः + -गन्धा an epithet of Satyavatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनगन्धिका|मीनगंधिका
मीनः + -गन्धिका a pond, pool of water (v. l. गोधिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनघातिन्
मीनः + -घातिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a crane.<BR>—2 a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनरङ्कः|मीनरङ्क|मीनरंक
मीनः + -रङ्कः, -रङ्गः a kingfisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनरङ्गः|मीनरङ्ग|मीनरंग
मीनः + -रङ्कः, -रङ्गः a kingfisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनरः|मीनर
मीनरः The sea-monster called <i>Makara</i>, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीनाम्रीणः|मीनाम्रीण
मीनाम्रीणः<BR>—1 A fish-sauce.<BR>—2 A wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीम्
मीम् €1 P. (मीमति)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसकः|मीमांसक
मीमांसकः [मान् विचारे स्वार्थे सन् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 One who investigates or inquires into, an investigator, examiner.<BR>—2 A follower of the system of philosophy called मीमांसा, q. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसनम्
मीमांसनम् Investigation, examination, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसनः|मीमांसन|मीमांसनं
मीमांसनम् + .{@-नः@} An investigator, inquirer, examiner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसिका
मीमांसिका The Mīmāṃsā system.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसा
मीमांसा [मान्-विचारे स्वार्थे सन् अ]<BR>—1 Deep reflection, inquiry, examination, investigation; अथातो व्रतमीमांसा<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 21; रसगङ्गाधरनाम्नीं करोति कुतुकेन काव्यमीमांसाम्<BR> R. G.; सैषा आनन्दस्य मीमांसा भवति T. Up.; so दत्तक˚, अलंकार˚ &c.<BR>—2 N. of one of the six chief <i>darśanas</i> or systems of Indian philosophy.<BR> (It was originally divided into two systems:− the पूर्वमीमांसा or<BR> कर्ममीमांसा founded by Jaimini, and the उत्तरमीमांसा or ब्रह्ममीमांसा<BR> ascribed to Bādarāyaṇa; but the two systems have very little in common<BR> between them, the first concerning itself chiefly with the correct interpretation<BR> of the ritual of the Veda and the settlement of dubious points in regard<BR> to Vedic texts; and the latter dealing chiefly with the nature of Brahman<BR> or the Supreme Spirit. The पूर्वमीमांसा is, therefore, usually, styled<BR> only मीमांसा or <i>the</i> Mīmāṃsā, and the उत्तरमीमांसा,<BR> वेदान्त which, being hardly a sequel of Jaiminiʼs system, is now considered<BR> and ranked separately.) मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं जैमिनिम् Pt. 2. 34.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मीमांसाकारः, मीमांसाकृत्, मीमांसामांसल, मीमांसामांसलप्रज्ञः, मीमांसासूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसाकारः
मीमांसा + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i> N. of Jaimini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसाकृत्
मीमांसा + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i> N. of Jaimini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसामांसल
मीमांसा + -मांसल <i>a.</i> fat with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">Page1272-2</a>]<BR> Mīmāṃsā (a satirical term meaning ‘dull’); अहो मन्दस्य मीमांसाश्रमहानिर्विजृम्भते ।<BR> मीमांसामांसलं चेतः कथमित्थं प्रमाद्यति ॥ Āgama Pr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसामांसलप्रज्ञः
मीमांसा + -मांसलप्रज्ञः one whose intellect is fattened on the Mīmāṃsā<BR> philosophy (a term of ridicule); ब्रूथ च स्वयं, मीमांसामांसलप्रज्ञाः,<BR> ताम् N. 17. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसासूत्रम्
मीमांसा + -सूत्रम् N. of the 12 books of aphorisms by Jaimini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांसितव्य
मीमांसितव्य, मीमांस्य <i>a.</i> To be examined, thought over,<BR> reflected; श्रुतिस्तु वेदो विज्ञेयो धर्मशास्त्रं तु वै स्मृतिः । ते सर्वार्थेष्वमीमांस्ये<BR> ताभ्यां धर्मो हि निर्बभौ ॥ Ms. 2. 10; मीमांस्यमेव ते मन्ये विदितम् Ken. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीमांस्य
मीमांसितव्य, मीमांस्य <i>a.</i> To be examined, thought over,<BR> reflected; श्रुतिस्तु वेदो विज्ञेयो धर्मशास्त्रं तु वै स्मृतिः । ते सर्वार्थेष्वमीमांस्ये<BR> ताभ्यां धर्मो हि निर्बभौ ॥ Ms. 2. 10; मीमांस्यमेव ते मन्ये विदितम् Ken. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीरः|मीर
मीरः<BR>—1 The ocean.<BR>—2 A limit, boundary.<BR>—3 A drink, beverage.<BR>—4 A particular part of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मील्
मील् €1 P. (मीलति, मीलित)<BR>—1 To close (as the eyes), close or contract the eye-lids, wink, twinkle;<BR> पत्रे बिभ्यति मीलति क्षणमपि क्षिप्रं तदालोकनात् Gīt. 10.<BR>—2 To close, be closed or shut (as eyes or flowers); नयनयुगममीलत्<BR> Śi. 11. 2; तस्या मिमीलतुर्नेत्रे Bk. 14. 54.<BR>—3 To fade, disappear, vanish; कालेन मीलितधियामवमृश्य नॄणाम् Bhāg. 2. 7. 36.<BR>—4 To meet or be collected (for मिल्). ━<i>Caus.</i> (मीलयति-ते)<BR> To cause to shut, close, shut (eyes, flowers &c.); न लोचनं मीलयितुं<BR> विषेहे Ki. 3. 36; शेषान् मासान् गमय चतुरो लोचने मीलयित्वा Me. 112 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलनम्
मीलनम् [मील् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Closing of the eyes, winking, twinkling.<BR>—2 Closing the eyes.<BR>—3 The closing of a flower.<BR>—4 (In Rhet.) A concealed simile; see मीलित below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलित|मीलितं
मीलित <i>p. p.</i> [मील्-क्त]<BR>—1 Shut, closed.<BR>—2 Twinkled.<BR>—3 Half-opened, unblown.<BR>—4 Vanished, disappeared.<BR>—5 Assembled, gathered (for मिलित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीलितम्
मीलित + .{@-तम्@} (In Rhet.) A figure of speech in which the difference or<BR> distinction between two objects is shown to be completely obscured on account<BR> of their similarity, whether natural or artificial, in some respects;<BR> it is thus defined by Mammaṭa:− समेन लक्ष्मणा वस्तु वस्तुना यन्निगूह्यते ।<BR> निजेनागन्तुना वापि तन्मीलितमिति स्मृतम् ॥ K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीव्
मीव् €1 P. (मीवति)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To grow fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवन्
मीवन् <i>m.</i> Wind; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवर|मीवरः
मीवर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hurtful, injurious.<BR>—2 Respectable, venerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवरः|मीवर
मीवर + .{@-रः@} The leader of an army, a general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मीवा
मीवा<BR>—1 The tape-worm.<BR>—2 Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुः|मु
मुः<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 Bondage, confinement.<BR>—3 Final emancipation.<BR>—4 A funeral pile.<BR>—5 A reddish-brown or tawny colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकः|मुक
मुकः The smell of cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकन्दकः|मुकन्दक|मुकंदक|मुकंदकः
मुकन्दकः An onion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुः|मुकु
मुकुः Liberation, deliverance; especially, final emancipation; also<BR> मुकुम् <i>ind.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1272-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुटम्
मुकुटम्<BR>—1 A crown, tiara, diadem; मुकुटरत्नमरीचिभिरस्पृशत् R. 9. 13.<BR> [मुकुट is crescent-shaped, the किरीट is pointed and the मौलि<BR> has three points.]<BR>—2 A crest.<BR>—3 A peak, point.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुकुटोत्पलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुटोत्पलः
मुकुटम् + -उत्पलः a crest-gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुटी
मुकुटी Cracking or snapping the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दः|मुकुन्द|मुकुंद|मुकुंदः
मुकुन्दः [मुकुम् दाति दा-क पृषो˚ मुम्]<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—2 Quicksilver.<BR>—3 A kind of precious stone.<BR>—4 N. of one of the nine treasures of Kubera.<BR>—5 A kind of drum.<BR>—6 A kind of grain.<BR>—7 (In music) A kind of measure.<BR>—8 The resin of the गुग्गुल or कुरुन्द tree (Boswellia Thurifera);<BR> also मुकुन्दुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दकः|मुकुन्दक|मुकुंदकः
मुकुन्दकः<BR>—1 A kind of grain (कुधान्य).<BR>—2 An onion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुन्दा
मुकुन्दा <i>f.</i> A kind of drum; वीणामुकुन्दामुरजादिभिश्च Bu. C. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुरः|मुकुर
मुकुरः<BR>—1 A mirror, looking-glass; गुणिनामपि निजरूपप्रतिपत्तिः परत एव<BR> संभवति । स्वमहिमदर्शनमक्ष्णोर्मुकुरतले जायते यस्मात् Vās.; Śi. 9. 73;<BR> N. 22. 43.<BR>—2 A bud; see मुकुलः.<BR>—3 The handle of a potterʼs wheel.<BR>—4 The Bakula tree.<BR>—5 The Mallikā creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुरायते
मुकुरायते Den. Ā. To become a mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलः|मुकुल|मुकुलं
मुकुलः, -लम्<BR>—1 A bud; आविर्भूतप्रथममुकुलाः कन्दलीश्चानुकच्छम् Me. 21; R. 9. 31, 15. 99.<BR>—2 Anything like a bud; आलक्ष्यदन्तमुकुलान् (तनयान्) Ś. 7. 17.<BR>—3 The body.<BR>—4 The soul or spirit<BR>—5 A bud-like junction of the fingers. (मुकुलीकृ means ‘to close in the form of a bud’<BR>; अथाग्रहस्ते मुकुलीकृताङ्गुलौ Ku. 5. 63.). ━<i>a.</i><BR> Closed (as eyes).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुकुलाग्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलम्
मुकुलः, -लम्<BR>—1 A bud; आविर्भूतप्रथममुकुलाः कन्दलीश्चानुकच्छम् Me. 21; R. 9. 31, 15. 99.<BR>—2 Anything like a bud; आलक्ष्यदन्तमुकुलान् (तनयान्) Ś. 7. 17.<BR>—3 The body.<BR>—4 The soul or spirit<BR>—5 A bud-like junction of the fingers. (मुकुलीकृ means ‘to close in the form of a bud’<BR>; अथाग्रहस्ते मुकुलीकृताङ्गुलौ Ku. 5. 63.). ━<i>a.</i><BR> Closed (as eyes).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुकुलाग्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलाग्रम्
मुकुलः + -अग्रम् a surgical instrument with a bud-like point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलयति
मुकुलयति Den. P. To cause to close or shut, close; मुकुलयति<BR> च नेत्रे सर्वथा सुभ्रु खेदः Māl. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलायित
मुकुलायित = मुकुलित q. v.; Kāv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुलित
मुकुलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having buds, budded, blossoming.<BR>—2 Half-closed, half-shut; दरमुकुलितनयनसरोजम् Gīt. 2; Ku. 3. 76;<BR> Māl. 1. 27; बाले लीलामुकुलितममी मन्थरा दृष्टिपाताः, किं क्षिप्यन्ते … …<BR> Bh. 1. 62.<BR>—3 Closed, shut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुष्ठः|मुकुष्ठ
मुकुष्ठः, मुकुष्ठकः A kind of bean (Mar. मटकी ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुकुष्ठकः|मुकुष्ठक
मुकुष्ठः, मुकुष्ठकः A kind of bean (Mar. मटकी ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्त|मुक्तः
मुक्त <i>p. p.</i> [मुच्-क्त]<BR>—1 Loosened, relaxed, slackened.<BR>—2 Set free, liberated, relaxed.<BR>—3 Abandoned, left, given up, set aside, taken off.<BR>—4 Thrown, cast, discharged, hurled.<BR>—5 Fallen down, dropped down from; विदन्ति मार्गं नखरन्ध्रमुक्तैर्मुक्ताफलैः Ku. 1. 6.<BR>—6 Drooping, unnerved; मुक्तैरवयवैरशयिषि Dk.<BR>—7 Given, bestowed.<BR>—8 Sent forth, emitted.<BR>—9 Finally saved or emancipated.<BR>—10 Ejected, spit out.<BR>—11 Deprived.<BR>—12 Absolved or emancipated (from sin or worldly existence); see मुच् also.<BR>—13 Opened, blown (as a flower); मुक्तपुष्पावकीर्णेन (शोभिता) Rām. 5. 1. 8.<BR>—14 Set up, established (प्रवर्तित); स दण्डो विधिवन्मुक्तः Rām. 7. 79. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तः|मुक्त
मुक्त + .{@-क्तः@} One who is finally emancipated from the bonds<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">Page1273-2</a>]<BR> of worldly existence, one who has renounced all worldly attachments and<BR> secured final beatitude, an absolved saint; सुभाषितेन गीतेन युवतीनां<BR> च लीलया । मनो न भिद्यते यस्य स वै मुक्तोऽथवा पशुः ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तम्
मुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} The spirit released from worldly existence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुक्ताम्बरः, मुक्तात्मन्, मुक्तासन, मुक्तकच्छः, मुक्तकञ्चुकः, मुक्तकण्ठ, मुक्तकर, मुक्तहस्त, मुक्तकेश, मुक्तचक्षुस्, मुक्तचेतस्, मुक्तप्रपाङ्गम्, मुक्तबन्धन, मुक्तलज्ज, मुक्तवसनः, मुक्तशैशव, मुक्तसंग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्ताम्बरः|मुक्ताम्बर|मुक्तांबर
मुक्त + -अम्बरः a Jaina mendicant of the <i>digambara</i> class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तात्मन्
मुक्त + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> finally saved or emancipated. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 the soul absolved from sins or from worldly matter.<BR>—2 a person whose soul is absolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तासन
मुक्त + -आसन <i>a.</i> rising from a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तासनम्
मुक्त + -आसन + .({@-नम्@}) a particular position of ascetics (सिद्धासन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकच्छः|मुक्तकच्छ
मुक्त + -कच्छः a Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकञ्चुकः|मुक्तकञ्चुक|मुक्तकंचुक
मुक्त + -कञ्चुकः a snake that has cast off its slough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकण्ठ
मुक्त + -कण्ठ <i>a.</i> raising a cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकण्ठम्
मुक्त + -कण्ठ + .({@-ण्ठम्@}) <i>ind.</i> bitterly, loudly, aloud; सा मुक्तकण्ठं व्यसनातिभाराच्चक्रन्द<BR> विग्ना कुररीव भूयः R. 14. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकर
मुक्त + -कर, -हस्त <i>a.</i> open-handed, liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तहस्त
मुक्त + -कर, -हस्त <i>a.</i> open-handed, liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तकेश
मुक्त + -केश <i>a.</i> letting the hair hang down, having the hair dishevelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तचक्षुस्
मुक्त + -चक्षुस् <i>m.</i> a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तचेतस्
मुक्त + -चेतस् <i>a.</i> absolved, emancipated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तप्रपाङ्गम्
मुक्त + -प्रपाङ्गम् an open court-yard connected with a tank; मुक्तप्रपाङ्गमपि<BR> दारुशिलेष्टकाद्यैः । रत्नैरनेकबहुलोहविशेषकैश्च ॥ Māna. 47. 31-32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तबन्धन
मुक्त + -बन्धन <i>a.</i> free from bondage; पश्य मूषिकमात्रेण कपोता<BR> मुक्तबन्धनाः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुक्तलज्ज
मुक्त + -लज्ज <i>a.</i> shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1273-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

