मुद्गः + -पर्णी Phaseolus Trilobus (Mar. रानमूग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गमोदकः|मुद्गमोदक
मुद्गः + -मोदकः a kind of sweetmeat; Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गभुज्
मुद्गः + -भुज्, -भोजिन् <i>m.</i> a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गभोजिन्
मुद्गः + -भुज्, -भोजिन् <i>m.</i> a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गरः|मुद्गर|मुद्गरं
मुद्गरः [मुदं गिरति गॄ-अच्]<BR>—1 A hammer, mallet, as in मोहमुद्गरः (a small poem by Śaṅkarācārya);<BR> समधूच्छिष्टमुद्गराः Mb. 5. 155; शिलानिष्पिष्टमुद्गरः R. 12. 73.<BR>—2 A club, mace.<BR>—3 A staff for breaking clods of earth.<BR>—4 A kind of dumb-bell.<BR>—5 A bud.<BR>—6 A kind of jasmine (said to be <i>n.</i> also in this sense).<BR>—7 A particular posture in sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गरकः|मुद्गरक
मुद्गरकः A hammer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गलः|मुद्गल|मुद्गलं
मुद्गलः N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गलम्
मुद्गलः + .{@-लम्@} A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्गष्टः|मुद्गष्ट
मुद्गष्टः A kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्ग|मुद्गः
मुद्ग <i>a.</i> (मुदं राति इति) Giver of joy; बभौ मरुत्वान् विकृतः<BR> स मुद्रः Bk. 10. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रा
मुद्रा [मुद्-रक्]<BR>—1 A seal, an instrument for sealing or stamping; especially a seal-ring,<BR> signet-ring; अनया मुद्रया मुद्रयैनम् Mu. 1; नाममुद्राक्षराण्यनुवाच्य<BR> परस्परमवलोकयतः Ś. 1; बभौ मरुत्वान् विकृतः स-मुद्रः Bk. 10. 19<BR> (fig. also); इति प्रायो भावाः स्फुरदवधिमुद्रामुकुलिताः Bh. 2. 114.<BR>—2 A stamp, print, mark, impression; चतुःसमुद्रमुद्रः K. 191; सिन्दूरमुद्राङ्कितः<BR> (बाहुः) Gīt. 4.<BR>—3 A pass, passport (as given by a seal-ring); अगृहीतमुद्रः कटकान्निष्क्रामसि<BR> Mu. 5; गृहीतमुद्रः सलेखः पुरुषो गृहीतः Mu. 5; शाहसूनोः शिवस्यैषा<BR> मुद्रा भद्राय राजते (wording on Śivājeeʼs seal).<BR>—4 A stamped coin, coin, piece of money.<BR>—5 A medal.<BR>—6 An image, a sign, badge, token.<BR>—7 Shutting, closing, sealing; सैवौष्ठमुद्रा स च कर्णपाशः U. 6. 27;<BR> क्षिपन्निद्रामुद्रां मदनकलहच्छेदसुलभाम् Māl. 2. 12 ‘removing the seal of sleep’<BR> &c.<BR>—8 A mystery.<BR>—9 (In Rhet.) The expression of things by their right names.<BR>—10 N. of certain positions of the fingers practised in devotion or religious<BR> worship; योजनात् सर्वदेवानां द्रावणात् पापसंहतेः । तस्मान्मुद्रेति<BR> सा ख्याता सर्वकामार्थसाधनी Tantrasāra; Dk. 2. 2.<BR>—11 A particular branch of education (reckoning by the fingers).<BR>—12 A dance accordant with tradition.<BR>—13 A lock, stopper.<BR>—14 A nymph; बभौ मरुत्वान् विकृतः समुद्रः Bk. 10. 19.<BR>—15 “Parched grain” in the form of rice, paddy etc. (Yoginī Tantra, Ch. VI quoted in Woodroffe, Śakti and Śākta, 571).<BR>—16 Particular lines, marks; माता पुत्रः पिता भ्राता भार्या मित्रजनस्तथा ।<BR> अष्टापदपदस्थाने दक्ष मुद्रेव लक्ष्यते ॥ Mb. 12. 298. 40.<BR>—17 Type or block for printing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुद्राक्षरम्, मुद्राङ्क, मुद्राङ्कित, मुद्राधिपः, मुद्राध्यक्षः, मुद्राकारः, मुद्रामार्गः, मुद्रायन्त्रम्, मुद्रारक्षकः, मुद्राराक्षसम्, मुद्रालिपिः, मुद्रास्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राक्षरम्
मुद्रा + -अक्षरम्<BR>—1 a letter of the seal.<BR>—2 a type (a modern use).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राङ्क
मुद्रा + -अङ्क, -अङ्कित <i>a.</i> stamped with a seal, sealed, stamped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राङ्कित|मुद्राङ्कितः
मुद्रा + -अङ्क, -अङ्कित <i>a.</i> stamped with a seal, sealed, stamped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राधिपः
मुद्रा + -अधिपः the keeper of the seal; the officer in charge of the fort;<BR> ततो मुद्राधिपो मुख्यः कौक्षेयकसहायवान् Parṇāl. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राध्यक्षः|मुद्राध्यक्ष
मुद्रा + -अध्यक्षः superintendent of pass-ports; Kau. A. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राकारः
मुद्रा + -कारः a maker of seals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रामार्गः|मुद्रामार्ग
मुद्रा + -मार्गः an opening believed to exist in the crown of the head<BR> through which the soul is said to escape at death; cf. ब्रह्मरन्ध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रायन्त्रम्
मुद्रा + -यन्त्रम् a press, a printing-press (a modern formation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रारक्षकः|मुद्रारक्षक
मुद्रा + -रक्षकः the keeper of the seals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्राराक्षसम्
मुद्रा + -राक्षसम् N. of a drama by Viśākha-datta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रालिपिः|मुद्रालिपि
मुद्रा + -लिपिः an alphabet of written characters; मुद्रालिपिः शिल्पलिपिर्लिपिर्लेखनिसंभवा ।<BR> गुण्डिका घुणसंभूता लिपयः पञ्चधा मताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रास्थानम्
मुद्रा + -स्थानम् the place (on the finger) for a seal-ring; Ś.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रणम्
मुद्रणम्<BR>—1 Sealing, stamping, printing, marking.<BR>—2 Closing, shutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रणीपत्रम्
मुद्रणीपत्रम् A proof-sheet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1277-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रयति
मुद्रयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To seal; वादिनश्चिह्नितं साक्ष्यं कृत्वा राजादि मुद्रयेत् Śukra. 4. 608;<BR> अनया मुद्रया मुद्रयैनम् Mu. 1.<BR>—2 To stamp, mark, impress.<BR>—3 To cover, close up (fig.); विवराणि मुद्रयन् द्रागूर्णायुरिव सज्जनो<BR> जयति Bv. 1. 90.<BR>—4 To print (as a book).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रिका
मुद्रिका<BR>—1 A little seal.<BR>—2 A seal-ring.<BR>—3 A stamp or impression.<BR>—4 A stamped coin, coin.<BR>—5 A signed or sealed paper.<BR>—6 A particular surgical instrument.<BR>—7 = मुद्रा (10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुद्रित|मुद्रितं
मुद्रित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sealed, marked, impressed, stamped; त्यागः सप्तसमुद्रमुद्रितमहीनिर्व्याजदानावधिः<BR> Mv. 2. 36; काश्मीरमुद्रितमुरो मधुसूदनस्य Gīt. 1; स्वयं सिन्दूरेण<BR> द्विपरणमुदा मुद्रित इव 11.<BR>—2 Closed, sealed up.<BR>—3 Unblown.<BR>—4 Printed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुधा
मुधा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In vain, to no purpose, uselessly, unprofitably; यत्किंचिदपि संवीक्ष्य<BR> कुरुते हसितं मुधा S. D.<BR>—2 Wrongly, falsely; रात्रिः सैव पुनः स एव दिवसो मत्वा मुधा जन्तवः<BR> Bh. 3. 78 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिः|मुनि
मुनिः [मन्-इन् उच्च Uṇ. 4. 122]<BR>—1 A sage, a holy man, saint, devotee, an ascetic; मुनीनामप्यहं व्यासः<BR> Bg. 10. 37; दुःखेष्वनुद्विग्नमनाः सुखेषु विगतस्पृहः । वीतरागभयक्रोधः<BR> स्थितधीर्मुनिरुच्यते ॥ 2. 56; पुण्यः शब्दो मुनिरिति मुहुः केवलं<BR> राजपूर्वः Ś. 2. 15; R. 1. 8, 3. 49.<BR>—2 N. of the sage Agastya.<BR>—3 Of Vyāsa; Mb. 6. 119. 40.<BR>—4 Of Buddha.<BR>—5 of Pāṇini.<BR>—6 N. of several plants (पियालु, पराशर and दमनक).<BR>—7 The internal conscience (according to Kull. on Ms. 8. 91 ‘the Supreme Spirit’).<BR>—8 The mango-tree.<BR>—9 The number ‘seven’. ━<i>pl.</i> The seven sages.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुन्यन्नम्, मुनीन्द्रः, मुनीशः, मुनीश्वरः, मुनिच्छदः, मुनित्रयम्, मुनिदारकः, मुनिकुमारः, मुनिद्रुमः, मुनिधान्यम्, मुनिपरंपरा, मुनिपित्तलम्, मुनिपुङ्गवः, मुनिपुत्रकः, मुनिप्रियः, मुनिभेषजम्, मुनिवृत्ति, मुनिव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुन्यन्नम्
मुनिः + -अन्नम् (pl.) the food of ascetics, (कन्दफलादि); देशे काले<BR> च संप्राप्ते मुन्यन्नं हरिदैवतम् Bhāg. 7. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनीन्द्रः|मुनीन्द्र|मुनींद्र
मुनिः + -इन्द्रः<BR>—1 ‘the lord of the sages’, a great sage.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śākyamuni.<BR>—3 of Bharata.<BR>—4 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनीशः|मुनीश
मुनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a great sage.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनीश्वरः|मुनीश्वर
मुनिः + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 a great sage.<BR>—2 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिच्छदः|मुनिच्छद
मुनिः + -च्छदः Alstonia Scholaris (Mar. सातवीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनित्रयम्
मुनिः + -त्रयम् ‘the triad of sages’, <i>i. e.</i> Pāṇini, Kātyāyana,<BR> and Patañjali (who are considered to be inspired saints); मुनित्रयं<BR> नमस्कृत्य, or त्रिमुनि व्याकरणम् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिदारकः|मुनिदारक
मुनिः + -दारकः, -कुमारः a young sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिकुमारः|मुनिकुमार
मुनिः + -दारकः, -कुमारः a young sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिद्रुमः|मुनिद्रुम
मुनिः + -द्रुमः the Śyonāka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिधान्यम्
मुनिः + -धान्यम् a kind of wild grain (Mar. देवभात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपरंपरा|मुनिपरम्परा
मुनिः + -परंपरा uninterrupted tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपित्तलम्
मुनिः + -पित्तलम् copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुङ्गवः|मुनिपुङ्गव|मुनिपुंगव
मुनिः + -पुङ्गवः a great or eminent sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिपुत्रकः|मुनिपुत्रक|मुनिपुत्त्रकः
मुनिः + -पुत्रकः<BR>—1 a wagtail.<BR>—2 the <i>damanaka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिप्रियः|मुनिप्रिय
मुनिः + -प्रियः Panicum Miliaceum (Mar. नीवार, काङ्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिभेषजम्
मुनिः + -भेषजम्<BR>—1 the fruit of the yellow myrobalan.<BR>—2 fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिवृत्ति
मुनिः + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> leading an ascetic life; वार्द्धके मुनिवृत्तीनाम् R. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिव्रतम्
मुनिः + -व्रतम् an ascetic vow; keeping silence; मुनिव्रतैस्त्वामतिमात्रकर्शिताम्<BR> Ku. 5. 48; मुनिव्रतमथ त्यक्त्वा निश्चक्रामाम्बिकागृहात् Bhāg. 10. 53. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनिता
मुनिता, -त्वम्<BR> The state or character of a muni (वानप्रस्थत्व); कथं<BR> वादीयतामर्वाङ्मुनिता धर्मरोधिनी Ki. 11. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुनित्वम्
मुनिता, -त्वम्<BR> The state or character of a muni (वानप्रस्थत्व); कथं<BR> वादीयतामर्वाङ्मुनिता धर्मरोधिनी Ki. 11. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुन्थ्
मुन्थ् €1 P. (मुन्थति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षा
मुमुक्षा Desire of liberation or of final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षु|मुमुक्षुः
मुमुक्षु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desirous of releasing or liberating.<BR>—2 Wishing to discharge.<BR>—3 About to shoot (arrows &c.); तस्यापरेष्वपि मृगेषु शरान् मुमुक्षोः R. 9. 58.<BR>—4 Wishing to be free from worldly existence, striving after final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुक्षुः|मुमुक्षु
मुमुक्षु + .{@-क्षुः@} A sage striving after final emancipation or beatitude; अन्तर्यश्च<BR> मुमुक्षुभिर्नियमितप्राणादिभिर्मृग्यते V. 1. 1; Ku. 2. 51; एवं ज्ञात्वा<BR> कृतं कर्म पूर्वैरपि मुमुक्षुभिः Bg. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुचानः|मुमुचान
मुमुचानः A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमुषिषुः|मुमुषिषु
मुमुषिषुः A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षा
मुमूर्षा Desire of death; राममायान् मुमूर्षया Bk. 5. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुमूर्षु|मुमूर्षुः
मुमूर्षु <i>a.</i> Being on the point of death, about to die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्
मुर् €6 P. (मुरति) To encircle, surround, encompass, entwine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरम्
मुरम् Encompassing, surrounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरः|मुर|मुरं
मुरः N. of a demon slain by Kṛṣṇa; पार्थेनाथ द्विषन्मुरम् Śi. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरा
मुरः + .{@-रा@} N. of a fragrant plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरम्
मुरः + .{@-रम्@} Encompassing, surrounding.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुरारिः, मुरजित्, मुरद्विष्, मुरभिद्, मुरमर्दन, मुररिपु, मुरवैरिन्, मुरहन्, मुरदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरारिः|मुरारि
मुरः + -अरिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kṛṣṇa; मुरारिमारादुपदर्शयन्त्यसौ Gīt. 1; सकृदपि<BR> यस्य मुरारिसमर्चा तस्य यमः किं कुरुते चर्चाम् and इह संसारे<BR> भवदुस्तारे कृपयापारे पाहि मुरारे Śaṅkara.<BR>—2 N. of the author of Anargharāghava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजित्
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरद्विष्
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरभिद्
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरमर्दन|मुरमर्द्दनः
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुररिपु|मुररिपुः
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरवैरिन्
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरहन्
मुरः + -जित्, -द्विष्, -भिद्, -मर्दन, -रिपु, -वैरिन्, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets<BR> of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu; प्रकीर्णासृग्बिन्दुर्जयति भुजदण्डो मुरजितः<BR> Gīt. 1; मुरवैरिणो राधिकामधि वचनजातम् 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरदः|मुरद
मुरः + -दः the discus of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरगण्डः|मुरगण्ड|मुरगंडः
मुरगण्डः An eruption on the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजः|मुरज
मुरजः [मुरात् वेष्टनात् जायते जन्-ड]<BR>—1 A kind of drum or tabor; सानन्दं नन्दिहस्ताहतमुरजरव &c.<BR> Māl. 1. 1; संगीताय प्रहतमुरजाः Me. 66, 58; M. 1. 22; Ku. 6. 40.<BR>—2 A stanza artificially arranged in the form of a drum; also called मुरजबन्ध,<BR> see K. P. 9 <i>ad loc.</i><BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुरजफलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजफलः|मुरजफल
मुरजः + -फलः the jackfruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरजा
मुरजा<BR>—1 A large drum.<BR>—2 N. of Kuberaʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरण्डाः
मुरण्डाः <i>m.</i> pl. A country to the north-west of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरन्दला|मुरंदला
मुरन्दला N. of a river (supposed to be the same as Narmadā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलः|मुरल
मुरलः<BR>—1 A kind of fresh-water fish.<BR>—2 A king of the Muralas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलाः
मुरलः + .{@-लाः@} pl. N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरला
मुरला N. of a river rising in the country of the Keralas; (mentioned<BR> in U. 3 along with तमसा); मुरलामारुतोद्धूतमगमत् कैतकं रजः R. 4. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरली
मुरली A flute, pipe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मुरलीधरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरलीधरः|मुरलीधर
मुरली + -धरः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्छ्
मुर्छ् €1 P. (मूर्छति, मूर्छित or मूर्त; the word is written<BR> as मूर्छ् or मूर्च्छ्)<BR>—1 To settle into a solid from, coagulate, congeal.<BR>—2 To faint, swoon, faint away; lose consciousness,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">Page1279-1</a>]<BR> become senseless; पतत्युद्याति मूर्च्छत्यपि Gīt. 4; क्रीडानिर्जितविश्वमूर्च्छितजनाघातेन<BR> किं पौरुषम् Gīt. 3; Bk. 15. 55.<BR>—3 To grow, increase, become strong or powerful; मुमूर्च्छ सहजं तेजो<BR> हविषेव हविर्भुजः R. 10. 79; मुमूर्च्छ सख्यं रामस्य 12. 57; मूर्च्छन्त्यमी<BR> विकाराः प्रायेणैश्वर्यमत्तेषु Ś. 5. 18; Ki. 16. 8, 59.<BR>—4 To gather strength, thicken, become dense, prevail; तमसां निशि<BR> मूर्च्छताम् V. 3. 7.<BR>—5 (a) To take effect on; छाया न मूर्च्छति मलोपहतप्रसादे शुद्धे तु<BR> दर्पणतले सुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32; हर्म्येषु मूर्छन्ति न चन्द्रपादाः<BR> R. 16. 18 ‘are not reflected’ &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To prevail against, have power against; न पादपोन्मूलनशक्ति<BR> रंहः शिलोच्चये मूर्छति मारुतस्य R. 2. 34.<BR>—6 To fill, pervade, penetrate, spead over; Ku. 6. 59; R. 6. 9.<BR>—7 To be a match for.<BR>—8 To be frequent. —9 To cause to sound loudly. ━<i>Caus.</i> (मूर्छयति-ते)<BR>—1 To stupefy, cause to faint; म्लेच्छान् मूर्छयते Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 To strengthen, increase.<BR>—3 To excite, stir up.<BR>—4 To cause to sound loudly, play on (as musical instrument); इमास्तन्त्रीः<BR> सुमधुराः … … मूर्च्छयित्वा सुमधुरं गायतां विगतज्वरौ Rām. 7. 93. 13;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 6. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1278-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्मिणी
मुर्मिणी A small fire-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्मुरः|मुर्मुर
मुर्मुरः [मुर् क पृषो˚ द्वित्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A fire made of chaff, chaff-fire; स्मरहुताशनमुर्मुरचूर्णतां दधुरिवाम्रवणस्य<BR> रजःकणाः Śi. 6. 6.<BR>—2 The god of love.<BR>—3 N. of one of the horses of the sun.<BR>—4 The smell of the urine of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुर्व्
मुर्व् €1 P. (मुर्वति) To bind, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुल्
मुल् €10 U. (मोलयति-ते) To plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशटी
मुशटी A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशलम्
मुशलम् A staff, stick; मुशलशब्दश्च दण्डे प्रसिद्धः ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुशली
मुश(स)ली A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुसली
मुश(स)ली A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
मुष् I. €9 P. (मुष्णाति, मुषित; <i>desid.</i> मुमुषिषति)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To steal, filch, rob, plunder, carry off (said to govern two<BR> acc.; देवदत्तं शतं मुष्णाति, but very rarely used in classical literature);<BR> मुषाण रत्नानि Śi. 1. 51, 3. 38; क्षत्रस्य मुष्णन् वसु जैत्रमोजः<BR> Ki. 3. 41; Śi. 3. 38.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To ravish, seduce, abduct, carry off; राघवस्यामुषः कान्तामाप्तैरुक्तो<BR> न चार्पिपः Bk. 15. 16.<BR>—2 To dispel, remove, drive off; घनतिमिरमुषि ज्योतिषि Śi. 4. 67; Ratn. 3. 19.<BR>—3 (Fig.) To ruin, undo; न वेत्सि मुषितमात्मानम् K. 164; Ratn. 4. 3.<BR>—4 To eclipse, cover, envelop, conceal; सैन्यरेणुमुषितार्कदीधितिः R. 11. 51.<BR>—5 To captivate, enrapture, ravish; व्रीडास्फुटस्मितविसृष्टकटाक्षमुष्टः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 12. 22.<BR>—6 To surpass, excel; मुष्णञ् श्रियमशोकानां रक्तैः परिजनाम्बरैः ।<BR> गीतैर्वराङ्गनानां च कोकिलभ्रमरध्वनिम् ॥ Ks. 55. 113; Ratn. 1. 24;<BR> Bk. 9. 92; Me. 49.<BR>—7 To deceive; मुषितोऽस्मि महात्मभिः Bhāg. 1. 13. 26. ━II. €1 P.<BR> (मोषति) —1 To hurt, injure, kill. ━III. €4 P. (मुष्यति)<BR>—1 To steal.<BR>—2 To break, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुष्
मुष्<BR>—1 Stealing, removing, destroying.<BR>—2 Surpassing, excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1279-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

