मुस्रम्
मुस्रम्<BR>—1 A pestle.<BR>—2 A tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह्
मुह् €4 P. (मुह्यति, मुग्ध or मूढ)<BR>—1 To faint, swoon, lose consciousness, become senseless; इहाहं द्रष्टुमाह्वं<BR> तां स्मरन्नेवं मुमोह सः Bk. 6. 21, 1. 20, 15. 16.<BR>—2 To be perplexed or bewildered, to be disturbed in mind, be at a loss;<BR> आपस्त्वपि न मुह्यन्ति नराः पण्डितबुद्धयः H. 1. 145; Ki. 18. 9.<BR>—3 To be foolish, stupid, or infatuated.<BR>—4 To fail. —5 To err, mistake. ━<i>Caus.</i> (मोहयति-ते)<BR>—1 To stupefy, infatuate; मा मूमुहत् खलु भवन्तमनन्यजन्मा Māl. 1. 32.<BR>—2 To confound, bewilder, perplex; व्यामिश्रेणेव वाक्येन बुद्धिं मोहयसीव<BR> मे Bg. 3. 2, 4. 16.<BR>—3 To throw into confusion.<BR>—4 To cause to err or mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढ|मूढः
मूढ <i>p. p.</i> [मुह्-क्त]<BR>—1 Stupefied, infatuated; मूढाः शोणितगन्धेन निपेतुर्धरणीतले Rām. 6. 52. 15;<BR> प्रत्यासन्नविपत्तिमूढमनसां प्रायो मतिः क्षीयते Pt. 2. 4.<BR>—2 Perplexed, bewildered, confounded, at a loss; किंकर्तव्यतामूढः<BR> ‘being at a loss what to do’; so ह्रीमूढ Me. 70.<BR>—3 Foolish, silly, dull, stupid, ignorant; अल्पस्य हेतोर्बहु हातुमिच्छन्<BR> विचारमूढः प्रतिभासि मे त्वम् R. 2. 47.<BR>—4 Mistaken, erring, deceived, gone astray.<BR>—5 Abortive.<BR>—6 Confounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढः|मूढ
मूढ + .{@-ढः@} A fool, blockhead, dolt, an ignorant person; मूढः परप्रत्ययनेयबुद्धिः M. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढाः
मूढ + .{@-ढाः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) An epithet of the elements in the Sāṅkhya philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढम्
मूढ + .{@-ढम्@} confusion of mind.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मूढात्मन्, मूढगर्भः, मूढग्राहः, मूढचेतन, मूढचेतस्, मूढधी, मूढबुद्धि, मूढमति, मूढप्रभुः, मूढश्रेष्ठः, मूढवात, मूढसत्त्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढात्मन्
मूढ + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 stupefied in mind.<BR>—2 foolish, stupid, silly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढगर्भः|मूढगर्भ
मूढ + -गर्भः<BR>—1 a dead foetus.<BR>—2 difficult delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढग्राहः|मूढग्राह
मूढ + -ग्राहः<BR>—1 a wrong notion, misconception, misapprehension; मूढग्राहेणात्मनो<BR> यत् पीडया क्रियते तपः Bg. 17. 19.<BR>—2 infatuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढचेतन
मूढ + -चेतन, -चेतस् <i>a.</i> foolish, silly, ignorant; अवगच्छति<BR> मूढचेतनः प्रियनाशं हृदि शल्यमर्पितम् R. 8. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढचेतस्
मूढ + -चेतन, -चेतस् <i>a.</i> foolish, silly, ignorant; अवगच्छति<BR> मूढचेतनः प्रियनाशं हृदि शल्यमर्पितम् R. 8. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढधी
मूढ + -धी, -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i> foolish, stupid, silly, simple; व्रजन्ति<BR> ते मूढधियः पराभवम् Ki. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढबुद्धि
मूढ + -धी, -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i> foolish, stupid, silly, simple; व्रजन्ति<BR> ते मूढधियः पराभवम् Ki. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढमति
मूढ + -धी, -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i> foolish, stupid, silly, simple; व्रजन्ति<BR> ते मूढधियः पराभवम् Ki. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढप्रभुः|मूढप्रभु
मूढ + -प्रभुः, -श्रेष्ठः the greatest block-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढश्रेष्ठः|मूढश्रेष्ठ
मूढ + -प्रभुः, -श्रेष्ठः the greatest block-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढवात
मूढ + -वात <i>a.</i> caught in a storm; महार्णवे नौरिव मूढवाता Rām. 5. 28. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढसत्त्व
मूढ + -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> infatuated, insane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढता
मूढता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Confusion, bewilderment.<BR>—2 Folly, stupidity.<BR>—3 The gathering or drawing (of a tumour); Suśr.<BR>—4 Morbid condition (of शरीरस्थवात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1280-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढत्वम्
