मूर्खता
मूर्खता, -त्वम्, मूर्खिमन् <i>m.</i><BR> Stupidity, folly, silliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खत्वम्
मूर्खता, -त्वम्, मूर्खिमन् <i>m.</i><BR> Stupidity, folly, silliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खिमन्
मूर्खता, -त्वम्, मूर्खिमन् <i>m.</i><BR> Stupidity, folly, silliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छ्
मूर्च्छ् €1 P. To increase; सुखस्य रूपान्तरमेव मूर्च्छतः चिरस्य<BR> निद्रामथ गच्छतः स्म तौ Rām. Ch. 2. 90; मूर्च्छन्मोहमहर्षिहर्षविहित … …<BR> K. P.; see मुर्च्छ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खलिका
मूर्खलिका An arrow in the form of a birdʼs heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छन
मूर्च्छन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Stupefying, producing insensibility or stupor (an epithet applied to<BR> one of the five arrows of Cupid).<BR>—2 Increasing, augmenting, strengthening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छनम्
मूर्च्छन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} [मुर्च्छ्-युच्]<BR>—1 Fainting, swooning.<BR>—2 Prevalence, growth, increase (usually <i>n.</i> in this sense); अनुकर्षं<BR> च निष्कर्षं व्याधिपावकमूर्च्छनम् Mb. 2. 13. 13.<BR>—3 A process in metallic preparation, calcining quicksilver with sulphur;<BR> cf. मूर्च्छा (3) also.<BR>—4 (In music) The rising of sounds, an intonation, a duly regulated rise<BR> and fall of sounds conducting the air and the harmony through the keys<BR> in a pleasing manner, changing the key or passing from the key to another;<BR> modulation, melody; स्फुटीभवद्ग्रामविशेषमूर्च्छनाम् Śi. 1. 10; भूयो<BR> भूयः स्वयमपि कृतां मूर्च्छनां विस्मरन्ती Me. 88; वर्णानामपि मूर्च्छनान्तरगतं<BR> तारं विरामे मृदु Mk. 3. 5; सप्त स्वरास्त्रयो ग्रामा मूर्च्छनाश्चैकविंशतिः<BR> Pt. 5. 54; (मूर्च्छा or मूर्च्छना is thus defined:− क्रमात् स्वराणां<BR> सप्तानामारोहश्चावरोहणम् । सा मूर्च्छेत्युच्यते ग्रामस्था एताः सप्त सप्त<BR> च ॥ see Malli. on Śi. 1. 10 for further information); ‘यत्रैव स्युः स्वराः पूर्णा मूर्च्छना सेत्युदाहृता’ com. on Rām. 1. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छना
मूर्च्छन + .{@-नम्, -ना@} [मुर्च्छ्-युच्]<BR>—1 Fainting, swooning.<BR>—2 Prevalence, growth, increase (usually <i>n.</i> in this sense); अनुकर्षं<BR> च निष्कर्षं व्याधिपावकमूर्च्छनम् Mb. 2. 13. 13.<BR>—3 A process in metallic preparation, calcining quicksilver with sulphur;<BR> cf. मूर्च्छा (3) also.<BR>—4 (In music) The rising of sounds, an intonation, a duly regulated rise<BR> and fall of sounds conducting the air and the harmony through the keys<BR> in a pleasing manner, changing the key or passing from the key to another;<BR> modulation, melody; स्फुटीभवद्ग्रामविशेषमूर्च्छनाम् Śi. 1. 10; भूयो<BR> भूयः स्वयमपि कृतां मूर्च्छनां विस्मरन्ती Me. 88; वर्णानामपि मूर्च्छनान्तरगतं<BR> तारं विरामे मृदु Mk. 3. 5; सप्त स्वरास्त्रयो ग्रामा मूर्च्छनाश्चैकविंशतिः<BR> Pt. 5. 54; (मूर्च्छा or मूर्च्छना is thus defined:− क्रमात् स्वराणां<BR> सप्तानामारोहश्चावरोहणम् । सा मूर्च्छेत्युच्यते ग्रामस्था एताः सप्त सप्त<BR> च ॥ see Malli. on Śi. 1. 10 for further information); ‘यत्रैव स्युः स्वराः पूर्णा मूर्च्छना सेत्युदाहृता’ com. on Rām. 1. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छा
मूर्च्छा [मुर्च्छ्-भावे अङ्]<BR>—1 Fainting, swooning; प्रहारमूर्च्छापगमे R. 7. 44.<BR>—2 Spiritual ignorance or delusion.<BR>—3 A process in calcining metals; मूर्च्छां गतो मृतो वा निदर्शनं पारदोऽत्र<BR> रसः Bv. 1. 82.<BR>—4 The rising of sounds &c.; see मूर्च्छन (4) above.<BR>—5 Growth, increase.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मूर्च्छापगमः, मूर्च्छाक्षेपः, मूर्च्छापरिप्लुत, मूर्च्छापरीत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छापगमः
मूर्च्छा + -अपगमः the passing off of fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छाक्षेपः
मूर्च्छा + -आक्षेपः (in Rhet.) expressing strong dissent by a swoon; इति<BR> तत्कालसम्भूतमूर्च्छयाक्षिप्यते गतिः । कान्तस्य कातराक्ष्या यन्मूर्च्छाक्षेपः<BR> स ईदृशः ॥ Kāv. 2. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छापरिप्लुत
मूर्च्छा + -परिप्लुत, -परीत <i>a.</i> unconscious, fainted away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छापरीत
मूर्च्छा + -परिप्लुत, -परीत <i>a.</i> unconscious, fainted away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छाल
मूर्च्छाल <i>a.</i> Fainted, insensible, senseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छित
मूर्च्छित <i>p. p.</i> [मूर्च्छा जाता अस्य तार˚ इतच्, मूर्च्छ्-क्त-वा]<BR>—1 Fainted, swooning, insensible; मुग्धा कान्तस्य यात्रोक्ति-<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">Page1282-1</a>]<BR> श्रवणादेव मूर्च्छिता Kāv. 2. 153.<BR>—2 Foolish, stupid, silly.<BR>—3 Increased, augmented; जयारवक्ष्वेडितनादमूर्च्छितः Ki. 14. 29.<BR>—4 Made violent, intensified.<BR>—5 Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>—6 Filled; वारुणीमदगन्धश्च माल्यगन्धश्च मूर्च्छितः Rām. 2. 114. 20, 6. 56. 2.<BR>—7 Calcined.<BR>—8 Rising upwards, lofty.<BR>—9 Reflected; Śataślokī 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छितम्
मूर्च्छित + .{@-तम्@} A kind of song or air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1281-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ण|मूर्णः
मूर्ण <i>a.</i> Bound, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त|मूर्त्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त <i>a.</i> [मूर्च्छ्-क्त]<BR>—1 Fainted, insensible.<BR>—2 Stupid, foolish.<BR>—3 Embodied, incarnate; मूर्तो विध्नस्तपस इव नो भिन्नसारङ्गयूथः<BR> Ś. 1. 32; प्रसाद इव मूर्तस्ते स्पर्शः स्नेहार्द्रशीतलः U. 3. 14;<BR> R. 2. 69, 7. 70; Ku. 7. 42; Pt. 2. 99.<BR>—4 Material, corporeal.<BR>—5 Solid, hard.<BR>—6 Real.<BR>—7 Thickened, coagulated (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तत्वम्
मूर्तत्वम्<BR>—1 Embodiment, materiality.<BR>—2 (In phil.) Having a finite or fixed measure or motion; परिच्छिन्नपरिमाणवत्त्वं<BR> क्रियावत्त्वं वा मूर्तत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिः|मूर्ति|मूर्त्ति|मूर्त्तिः
मूर्तिः <i>f.</i> [मूर्च्छ्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Anything which has definite shape and limits, material element, matter,<BR> substance; एतत् सर्वं यन्मूर्तं चामूर्तं च तस्मान्मूर्तिरेव रयिः<BR> Praśna. Up. 1. 5.<BR>—2 A form, visible shape, body, figure; कौटिल्यधीरज्जुनिबद्धमूर्तिं<BR> मन्ये स्थिरां मौर्यनृपस्य लक्ष्मीम् Mu. 2. 2; R. 3. 27, 14. 54.<BR>—3 An embodiment, incarnation, personification, manifestation; करुणस्य<BR> मूर्तिः U. 3. 4; Pt. 2. 159.<BR>—4 An image, idol, a statue.<BR>—5 Beauty.<BR>—6 Solidity, hardness.<BR>—7 Body (कलेवर); विशिखसंहतितापितमूर्तिभिः Ki. 14. 64; Ms. 1. 17, 19.<BR>—8 A limb of the body (शरीरावयव); नहि मे तप्यमानस्य क्षयं<BR> यास्यन्ति मूर्तयः Rām. 1. 64. 20.<BR>—9 (In phil.) The mind and the four elements -earth, air, fire and water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मूर्तिधर, मूर्तिसंचर, मूर्तिपः, मूर्तिपूजा, मूर्तिसेवनम्, मूर्तिभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिधर
मूर्तिः + -धर, -संचर <i>a.</i> embodied, incarnate; धर्मो वा मूर्तिसंचरः<BR> Mv. 1. 10; U. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिसंचर
मूर्तिः + -धर, -संचर <i>a.</i> embodied, incarnate; धर्मो वा मूर्तिसंचरः<BR> Mv. 1. 10; U. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिपः|मूर्तिप
मूर्तिः + -पः a worshipper of an image, one who is in charge of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिपूजा
मूर्तिः + -पूजा, -सेवनम् adoration of images, idolatry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिसेवनम्
मूर्तिः + -पूजा, -सेवनम् adoration of images, idolatry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिभावः|मूर्तिभाव
मूर्तिः + -भावः materiality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तित्वम्
मूर्तित्वम्<BR>—1 Embodiment, materiality, incarnation.<BR>—2 (In phil.) The having a finite measure or motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिमत्|मूर्तिमन्त्|मूर्त्तिमत्
मूर्तिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Material, corporeal.<BR>—2 Embodied, incarnate, personified; शकुन्तला मूर्तिमती च सत्क्रिया<BR> Ś. 5. 15; तव मूर्तिमानिव महोत्सवः करः U. 1. 18; R. 12. 64; Māl. 9. 9.<BR>—3 Hard, solid. ━<i>m.</i> The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्
मूर्धन् <i>m.</i> [मुह्यत्यस्मिन्नाहते इति मूर्धा, cf. Uṇ. 1. 156]<BR>—1 The forehead, brow.<BR>—2 The head in general; नतेन मूर्ध्ना हरिरग्रहीदपः Śi. 1. 18;<BR> R. 16. 81; नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः कुसुमस्य सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि स्थितिर्न चरणैरवताडनानि<BR> U. 1. 14; Ku. 3. 22.<BR>—3 The highest or most prominent part, top, summit, peak, head; अतिष्ठन्मनुजेन्द्राणां<BR> मूर्ध्नि देवपतिर्यथा Mb. ‘stood at the head of all kings’ &c.; उत्तमे<BR> शिखरे जाते भूम्यां पर्वतमूर्धनि Sandhyā Mantra; Ś. 5. 7; Me. 17.<BR>—4 (Hence) A leader, head, chief, foremost, prominent.<BR>—5 Front, van, forepart; स किल संयुगमूर्ध्नि सहायतां मघवतः प्रतिपद्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">Page1282-2</a>]<BR> महारथः R. 9. 19.<BR>—6 (In geom.) The base.<BR>—7 (In gram.) The roof of the palate.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मूर्धान्तः, मूर्धाभिषिक्त, मूर्धाभिषेकः, मूर्धावसिक्तः, मूर्धकर्णी, मूर्धकर्परी, मूर्धग, मूर्धजः, मूर्धज्योतिस्, मूर्धपातः, मूर्धपिण्डः, मूर्धपुष्पः, मूर्धरसः, मूर्धवेष्टनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धान्तः|मूर्धान्त|मूर्धांत
मूर्धन् + -अन्तः the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धाभिषिक्त|मूर्द्धाभिषिक्तः|मूर्धाभिषिक्तः
मूर्धन् + -अभिषिक्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 consecrated, crowned, inaugurated; मूर्धाभिषिक्तं कुमुदो बभाषे R. 16. 81.<BR>—2 common, stock (as an instance); उत्कृत्योत्कृत्य कृत्तिम् इति बीभत्सस्य<BR> मूर्धाभिषिक्तमुदाहरणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धाभिषिक्तः|मूर्धाभिषिक्त|मूर्द्धाभिषिक्तः
मूर्धन् + -अभिषिक्त + .({@-क्तः@})<BR>—1 a consecrated king; पश्य मूर्धाभिषिक्तानामाचार्य कदनं महत् Mb. 7. 150. 12.<BR>—2 a man of the Kṣatriya caste.<BR>—3 a minister.<BR>—4 = मूर्धावसिक्त (1) q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धाभिषेकः|मूर्धाभिषेक
मूर्धन् + -अभिषेकः consecration, inauguration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धावसिक्तः|मूर्धावसिक्त
मूर्धन् + -अवसिक्तः<BR>—1 N. of a particular mixed tribe sprung from a Brāhmaṇa father and<BR> Kṣatriya mother.<BR>—2 a consecrated king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धकर्णी
मूर्धन् + -कर्णी, -कर्परी <i>f.</i> an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धकर्परी
मूर्धन् + -कर्णी, -कर्परी <i>f.</i> an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धग
मूर्धन् + -ग <i>a.</i> sitting down on the head; स्यन्दनैः स्यन्दनगता<BR> गजैश्च गजमूर्धगाः Rām. 7. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धजः|मूर्धज|मूर्द्धजः
मूर्धन् + -जः<BR>—1 the hair (of the head); पर्याकुला मूर्धजाः Ś. 1. 30; विललाप<BR> विकीर्णमूर्धजा Ku. 4. 4 ‘she tore her hair for grief’.<BR>—2 the mane.<BR>—3 a crown, helmet; विमुक्तमूर्धजा ये च ये चापि हतवाहनाः Mb. 10. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धज्योतिस्
मूर्धन् + -ज्योतिस् <i>n.</i> see ब्रह्मरन्ध्र or मुद्रामार्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धपातः|मूर्धपात
मूर्धन् + -पातः splitting of the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धपिण्डः|मूर्धपिण्ड
मूर्धन् + -पिण्डः a lump upon the head (of an elephant in rut).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धपुष्पः|मूर्धपुष्प|मूर्द्धपुष्पः
मूर्धन् + -पुष्पः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धरसः|मूर्धरस|मूर्द्धरसः
मूर्धन् + -रसः the scum of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धवेष्टनम्
मूर्धन् + -वेष्टनम् a turban, diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्य|मूर्द्धन्यः
मूर्धन्य <i>a.</i> [मूर्ध्नि भवः यत्]<BR>—1 Being in or on the head; मणिं जहार मूर्धन्यं द्विजस्य सहमूर्धजम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 7. 55.<BR>—2 Cerebral or lingual, a term applied to the letters ऋ, ॠ, ट्, ठ्, ड्,<BR> ढ्, ण्, र्, and ष्; ऋटुरषाणां मूर्धा.<BR>—3 Chief, pre-eminent, most excellent; सन्नद्धान् पत्तिमूर्धन्यान् Śiva B. 28. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ध्वन्
मूर्ध्वन् See मूर्धन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्वा|मूर्व्वा
मूर्वा, -र्वी, मूर्विका<BR> A kind of creeper (from the fibres of which bow-strings<BR> and the girdle of Kṣatriyas are made).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्वी
मूर्वा, -र्वी, मूर्विका<BR> A kind of creeper (from the fibres of which bow-strings<BR> and the girdle of Kṣatriyas are made).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्विका
मूर्वा, -र्वी, मूर्विका<BR> A kind of creeper (from the fibres of which bow-strings<BR> and the girdle of Kṣatriyas are made).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्
मूल् I. €1 U. (मूलति-ते) To take or strike root, be firm, stand<BR> fast. ━II. €10 U. (मूलयति-ते, मूलित)<BR>—1 To plant, cause to grow, rear.<BR>—2 To grow, sprout, germinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलम्
मूलम् [मूल्-क]<BR>—1 A root (fig. also); तरुमूलानि गृहीभवन्ति तेषाम् Ś. 7. 20; or<BR> शाखिनो धौतमूलाः 1. 15; मूलं बन्ध् to take or strike root; बद्धमूलस्य<BR> मूलं हि महद्वैरतरोः स्त्रियः Śi. 2. 38.<BR>—2 The root, lowest edge or extremity of anything; कस्याश्चिदासीद्रशना<BR> तदानीमङ्गुष्ठमूलार्पितसूत्रशेषा R. 7. 10; so प्राचीमूले Me. 91.<BR>—3 The lower part or end, base, the end of anything by which it is joined<BR> to something else; बाह्वोर्मूलम् Śi. 7. 32; so पादमूलम्, कर्णमूलम्, ऊरुमूलम् &c.<BR>—4 Beginning, commencement; आमूलाच्छ्रोतुमिच्छामि Ś. 1.<BR>—5 Basis, foundation, source, origin, cause; सर्वे गार्हस्थ्यमूलकाः<BR> Mb.; रक्षोगृहे स्थितिर्मूलम् U. 1. 6; इति केनाप्युक्तं तत्र मूलं<BR> मृग्यम् ‘the source or authority should be found out’; पुष्पं पुष्पं<BR> विचिन्वीत मूलच्छेदं न कारयेत् Mb. 5. 34. 18; समूलघातमध्नन्तः<BR> परान्नोद्यन्ति मानवाः Śi. 2. 33.<BR>—6 The foot or bottom of anything; पर्वतमूलम्, गिरिमूलम् &c.<BR>—7 The text, or original passage (as distinguished from the commentary or gloss).<BR>—8 Vicinity, neighbourhood;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">Page1283-1</a>]<BR> सा कन्दुकेनारमतास्य मूले विभज्यमाना फलिता लतेव Mb. 3. 112. 16.<BR>—9 Capital, principal, stock; मूलं भागो व्याजी परिघः कॢप्तं रूपिकमत्यश्चायमुखम्<BR> Kau. A. 2. 6. 24.<BR>—10 A hereditary servant.<BR>—11 A square root.<BR>—12 A kingʼs own territory; स गुप्तमूलमत्यन्तम् R. 4. 26; Ms. 7. 184.<BR>—13 A vendor who is not the true owner; Ms. 8. 202 (अस्वामिविक्रेता Kull.).<BR>—14 The nineteenth lunar mansion containing<BR>—11 stars.<BR>—15 A thicket, copse.<BR>—16 The root of long pepper.<BR>—17 A particular position of the fingers.<BR>—18 A chief or capital city.<BR>—19 An aboriginal inhabitant.<BR>—20 A bower, an arbour (निकुञ्ज).<BR>—21 N. of several roots पिप्पली, पुष्कर, शूरण &c.<BR>—22 A tail; मूलो मूलवता स्पृष्टो धूप्यते धूमकेतुना Rām. 6. 4. 51.<BR> (In comp. मूल may be translated by ‘first, prime, original, chief, principal’<BR> <i>e. g.</i> मूलकारणम् ‘prime cause’, &c. &c.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मूलाधारम्, मूलाभम्, मूलायतनम्, मूलाशिन्, मूलाह्वम्, मूलोच्छेदः, मूलकर्मन्, मूलकारः, मूलकारणम्, मूलकारिका, मूलकृच्छ्रः, मूलकृच्छ्रम्, मूलकेशरः, मूलखानकः, मूलगुणः, मूलग्रन्थः, मूलघातिन्, मूलच्छिन्न, मूलच्छेदः, मूलज, मूलत्रिकोणम्, मूलदेवः, मूलद्रव्यम्, मूलधनम्, मूलधातुः, मूलनिकृन्तन, मूलपुरुषः, मूलप्रकृतिः, मूलप्रतीकारः, मूलफलदः, मूलबन्धः, मूलबर्हणम्, मूलबलम्, मूलभद्रः, मूलभृत्यः, मूलमन्त्रः, मूलराशिः, मूलवचनम्, मूलवापः, मूलवित्तम्, मूलविद्या, मूलविभुजः, मूलव्यसनवृत्तिः, मूलव्रतिन्, मूलशकुनः, मूलशाकटः, मूलशाकिनम्, मूलसंघः, मूलसाधनम्, मूलस्थानम्, मूलस्थायिन्, मूलस्रोतस्, मूलहर, मूलहरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1282-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलाधारम्
मूलम् + -आधारम्<BR>—1 the navel.<BR>—2 a mystical circle above the organs of generation; मूलाधारे त्रिकोणाख्ये<BR> इच्छाज्ञानक्रियात्मके.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलाभम्
मूलम् + -आभम् a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलायतनम्
मूलम् + -आयतनम् the original abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलाशिन्
मूलम् + -आशिन् <i>a.</i> living upon roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलाह्वम्
मूलम् + -आह्वम् a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलोच्छेदः|मूलोच्छेद
मूलम् + -उच्छेदः utter destruction, total eradication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकर्मन्|मूलकर्म्मन्
मूलम् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> magic; Ms. 9. 290.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकारः|मूलकार
मूलम् + -कारः the author of an original work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकारणम्
मूलम् + -कारणम् the original or prime cause; क्रियाणां खलु धर्म्याणां<BR> सत्पत्न्यो मूलकारणम् Ku. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकारिका
मूलम् + -कारिका a furnace, an oven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकृच्छ्रः|मूलकृच्छ्र
मूलम् + -कृच्छ्रः, -कृच्छ्रम् a kind of penance, living only upon roots; मूलकृच्छ्रः स्मृतो मूलैः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकृच्छ्रम्
मूलम् + -कृच्छ्रः, -कृच्छ्रम् a kind of penance, living only upon roots; मूलकृच्छ्रः स्मृतो मूलैः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलकेशरः|मूलकेशर
मूलम् + -केशरः a citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलखानकः|मूलखानक
मूलम् + -खानकः one who lives upon root-digging (मूलोत्पाटनजीवी); Ms. 8. 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलगुणः|मूलगुण
मूलम् + -गुणः the co-efficient of a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलग्रन्थः|मूलग्रन्थ
मूलम् + -ग्रन्थः<BR>—1 an original text.<BR>—2 the very words uttered by Śākyamuni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलघातिन्
मूलम् + -घातिन् <i>a.</i> destroying completely; (नहि … कर्मसु)<BR> मूलघातिषु सज्जन्ते बुद्धिमन्तो भवद्विधाः Rām. 5. 51. 18; see मूलहर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलच्छिन्न
मूलम् + -छिन्न <i>a.</i> nipped in the bud; साऽद्य मूलच्छिन्ना Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलच्छेदः|मूलच्छेद
मूलम् + -छेदः uprooting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलज|मूलजं|मूलजः
मूलम् + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 radical.<BR>—2 growing at the roots of trees (as an ant-hill).<BR>—3 born under the constellation Mūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलजः|मूलज|मूलजं
मूलम् + -ज + .({@-जः@}) plant growing from a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलजम्
मूलम् + -ज + .({@-जम्@}) green ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलत्रिकोणम्
मूलम् + -त्रिकोणम् the third astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलदेवः|मूलदेव
मूलम् + -देवः an epithet of Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलद्रव्यम्
मूलम् + -द्रव्यम्, -धनम् principal, stock, capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलधनम्
मूलम् + -द्रव्यम्, -धनम् principal, stock, capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलधातुः|मूलधातु
मूलम् + -धातुः lymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलनिकृन्तन
मूलम् + -निकृन्तन <i>a.</i> destroying root and branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलपुरुषः|मूलपुरुष
मूलम् + -पुरुषः ‘the stock-man’, the male representative of a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलप्रकृतिः|मूलप्रकृति
मूलम् + -प्रकृतिः <i>f.</i> the Prakṛti or Pradhāna of the Sāṅkhyas<BR> (q. v.); मूलप्रकृतिरविकृतिः Sāṅ. K. 3. (pl.) the four principal<BR> sovereigns to be considered at the time of war (विजिगीषु, अरि, मध्यम,<BR> and उदासीन); see Ms. 7. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1283-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलप्रतीकारः
