मृधस् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 War; दैत्यराजस्य च ब्रह्मन् कस्माद् हेतोरभून्मृधः Bhāg. 3. 14. 3.<BR>—2 Contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृधम्
मृधम् War, battle, fight; सत्त्वविहितमतुलं भुजयोर्बलमस्य<BR> पश्यत मृधेऽधिकुप्यतः Ki. 12. 39; हत्वा निवृत्ताय मृधे खरादीन्<BR> R. 13. 65; Mv. 5. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मृधभू<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृधभू
मृधम् + -भू <i>f.</i> a field of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृश्
मृश् €6 P. (मृशति, मृष्ट)<BR>—1 To touch, handle.<BR>—2 To rub, stroke.<BR>—3 To consider, reflect, deliberate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्
मृष् I. €1 P. (मर्षति) To sprinkle. ━II. €1 U. (मर्षति-ते)<BR>—1 To bear, endure &c. (usually €4 U.).<BR>—2 To sprinkle. ━III. €4. €10 U. (मृष्यति-ते, मर्षयति-ते, मर्षित)<BR>—1 To suffer, bear, endure, put up with; न मर्षयन्ति चात्मानं संभावयितुमात्मना<BR> Rām. 6. 65. 4; तत्किमिदमकार्यमनुष्ठितं देवेन-लोको न<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">Page1288-1</a>]<BR> मृष्यतीति U. 3; R. 9. 62.<BR>—2 To allow, permit.<BR>—3 To pardon, forgive, excuse, forbear; मृष्यन्तु लवस्य बालिशतां तातपादाः<BR> U. 6; प्रथममिति प्रेक्ष्य दुहितृजनस्यैकोऽपराधो भगवता मर्षयितव्यः<BR> Ś. 4; आर्य मर्षय मर्षय Ve. 1; महाब्राह्मण मर्षय Mk. 1.<BR>—4 To forget, neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1287-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषा
मृषा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Falsely, wrongly, untruly, lyingly; यद् वक्त्रं मुहुरीक्षसे न धनिनां<BR> ब्रूषे न चाटुं मृषा Bh. 3. 147; मृषाभाषासिन्धो Bv. 2. 21.<BR>—2 In vain, to no purpose, uselessly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मृषाध्यायिन्, मृषार्थक, मृषोद्यम्, मृषाज्ञानम्, मृषादानम्, मृषाभाषिन्, मृषावादिन्, मृषावाच्, मृषावादः, मृषासाक्षिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषाध्यायिन्
मृषा + -अध्यायिन् <i>m.</i> a kind of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषार्थक|मृषार्थकं
मृषा + -अर्थक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 untrue.<BR>—2 absurd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषार्थकम्
मृषा + -अर्थक + .({@-कम्@}) an absurdity, an impossibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषोद्यम्
मृषा + -उद्यम् falsehood, lying, a false statement; तत् किं मन्यसे<BR> राजपुत्रि मृषोद्यं तदिति U. 4; मृषोद्यं प्रवदन्तीं ताम् Bk. 5. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषाज्ञानम्
मृषा + -ज्ञानम् ignorance, error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषादानम्
मृषा + -दानम् insincere promise of a gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषाभाषिन्
मृषा + -भाषिन्, -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a liar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावादिन्
मृषा + -भाषिन्, -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a liar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावाच्
मृषा + -वाच् <i>f.</i> an untrue or satirical speech, satire, irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषावादः|मृषावाद
मृषा + -वादः<BR>—1 an untrue speech; a lie, falsehood.<BR>—2 insincere speech, flattery.<BR>—3 irony, satire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषासाक्षिन्
मृषा + -साक्षिन् false witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषायते
मृषायते Den. Ā. To be mistaken, to err.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृषालकः|मृषालक
मृषालकः The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्ट|मृष्टं|मृष्टः
मृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [मृज् मृश् वा-क्त]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Cleansed, purified; शरच्छशिकरैर्मृष्टं मानयन् रजनीमुखम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 2. 34.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Pure, clean; भक्षयित्वा फलान्यथ । मूलानि च सुमृष्टानि …<BR> Rām. 7. 93. 8.<BR>—2 Besmeared.<BR>—3 Dressed, cooked.<BR>—4 Touched; स्थितपतितं च करोति मृष्टमन्नम् Bṛ. S.<BR>—5 Considered, deliberated.<BR>—6 Savoury, agreeable; मांसानि च सुमृष्टानि Rām. 7. 39. 26; ग्रासं<BR> सुमृष्टं विरसं महान्तं स्तोकमेव वा । यदृच्छयैवापतितं ग्रसेदाजगरोऽक्रियः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 11. 8. 2.<BR>—7 Sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टम्
मृष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Pepper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मृष्टकुण्डल, मृष्टगन्धः, मृष्टयशस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टकुण्डल
मृष्ट + -कुण्डल <i>a.</i> wearing bright earrings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टगन्धः|मृष्टगन्ध|मृष्टगंध
मृष्ट + -गन्धः a savoury or agreeable smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टयशस्
मृष्ट + -यशस् <i>a.</i> of pure glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टिः|मृष्टि
मृष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cleansing, cleaning, purifying.<BR>—2 Cooking, dressing, preparation.<BR>—3 Touch, contact.<BR>—4 Sprinkling.<BR>—5 A savoury repast; सृष्टिर्मृष्टिर्द्विजाश्चाग्र्याः श्राद्धकर्मसु संपदः Ms. 3. 255.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृष्टेरुक|मृष्टेरुकः
मृष्टेरुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Eating dainties, luxurious.<BR>—2 Selfish.<BR>—3 Liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मॄ
मॄ €9 P. (मृणाति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मे
मे €1 Ā. (मयते, मित; <i>desid.</i> मित्सते) To exchange<BR> or barter. ━<i>With</i> {@नि@} or {@विनि@} to exchange or barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकः|मेक
मेकः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलः|मेकल
मेकलः<BR>—1 N. of a mountain; (also मेखल).<BR>—2 A goat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मेकलाद्रिजा, मेकलकन्यका, मेकलकन्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलाद्रिजा
मेकलः + -अद्रिजा, -कन्यका, -कन्या epithets of the river Narmadā; रेवेन्दुजा<BR> पूर्वगङ्गा नर्मदा मेकलाद्रिजा Abh. Cin. 1083.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलकन्यका
मेकलः + -अद्रिजा, -कन्यका, -कन्या epithets of the river Narmadā; रेवेन्दुजा<BR> पूर्वगङ्गा नर्मदा मेकलाद्रिजा Abh. Cin. 1083.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकलकन्या
मेकलः + -अद्रिजा, -कन्यका, -कन्या epithets of the river Narmadā; रेवेन्दुजा<BR> पूर्वगङ्गा नर्मदा मेकलाद्रिजा Abh. Cin. 1083.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेक्षणम्
मेक्षणम् A wooden spoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखला
मेखला<BR>—1 A belt, girdle, waist-band, zone in general (fig. also); anything which<BR> girds or surrounds; मही<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">Page1288-2</a>]<BR> सागरमेखला ‘the sea-girt earth’; रत्नानुविद्धार्णवमेखलाया दिशः<BR> सपत्नी भव दक्षिणस्याः R. 6. 63; Ṛs. 6. 3.<BR>—2 Particularly, the girdle or zone of a woman; नितम्बबिम्बैः सदुकूलमेखलैः<BR> Ṛs. 1. 4, 6; R. 8. 64; मेखलागुणैरुत गोत्रस्खलितेषु बन्धनम् Ku. 4. 8.<BR>—3 The triple girdle worn by the first three castes; मौञ्जी त्रिवृत् समा<BR> श्लक्ष्णा कार्या विप्रस्य मेखला । क्षत्रियस्य तु मौर्वी ज्या वैश्यस्य शणतान्तवी ॥<BR> Ms. 2. 42.<BR>—4 The slope of a mountain (नितम्ब); आमेखलं संचरतां घनानाम्<BR> Ku. 1. 5; Me. 12.<BR>—5 The hips.<BR>—6 A sword-belt.<BR>—7 A sword-knot or string fastened to the hilt.<BR>—8 The girth of a horse.<BR>—9 N. of the river Narmadā.<BR>—10 The cords or lines drawn round an alter; विधिना विहिते कुण्डे मेखलागर्तवेदिभिः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 27. 36.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मेखलापदम्, मेखलाबन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलापदम्
मेखला + -पदम् the hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलाबन्धः|मेखलाबन्ध|मेखलाबंध
मेखला + -बन्धः investiture with the girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलिन्
मेखलिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 A religious student, a Brahmachārin, q. v.; मेखलीनां महासङ्घः<BR> कौसल्यां समुपस्थितः Rām. 2. 32. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेखलालः|मेखलाल
मेखलालः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघः|मेघ
मेघः [मेहति वर्षति जलम्, मिह्-घञ् कुत्वम्]<BR>—1 A cloud; कुर्वन्नञ्जनमेचका इव दिशो मेघः समुत्तिष्ठते Mk. 5. 23, 2, 3 &c.<BR>—2 A mass, multitude.<BR>—3 N. of one of the six Rāgas (in music).<BR>—4 A fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघम्
मेघः + .{@-घम्@} Talc.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मेघाध्वन्, मेघान्तः, मेघारिः, मेघास्थि, मेघाख्यम्, मेघागमः, मेघाच्छादित, मेघाटोपः, मेघाडम्बरः, मेघानन्दा, मेघालोकः, मेघास्पदम्, मेघोदकम्, मेघोदयः, मेघकफः, मेघकालः, मेघगर्जनम्, मेघगर्जना, मेघचिन्तकः, मेघजः, मेघजालम्, मेघजीवकः, मेघजीवनः, मेघज्योतिस्, मेघडम्बरः, मेघदीपः, मेघदूतम्, मेघद्वारम्, मेघनादः, मेघनामन्, मेघनिर्घोषः, मेघपङ्क्तिः, मेघमाला, मेघराजिः, मेघपथः, मेघपुष्पम्, मेघप्रसरः, मेघप्रसवः, मेघभूतिः, मेघमण्डलम्, मेघमाल, मेघमालिन्, मेघमोदिनी, मेघयोनिः, मेघरवः, मेघरावः, मेघरेखा, मेघलेखा, मेघवर्णा, मेघवर्त्मन्, मेघवह्निः, मेघवाहनः, मेघविस्फूर्जितम्, मेघवेश्मन्, मेघश्याम, मेघसंघातः, मेघसारः, मेघसुहृद्, मेघस्कन्दिन्, मेघस्तनितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1288-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेघाध्वन्
