मोटनम्, -मोटनकम् + .{@-नः@} Wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोट्टायितम्
मोट्टायितम् Silent involuntary expression of affection towards an<BR> absent lover, as when a woman, her mind being taken up by her lover, scratches<BR> the ear &c. when he is remembered or talked of; it is thus defined by<BR> उज्ज्वलमणि:− कान्तस्मरणवार्तादौ हृदि तद्भावभावतः । प्राकठ्यसभिलाषस्य<BR> मोट्टायितमुदीर्यते; see S. D. 141 also; सद्यो मोट्टायितमधुरिमोल्लासभङ्गीविधाता Ud. S. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1292-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोणः|मोण
मोणः<BR>—1 A dried fruit.<BR>—2 A basket for keeping snakes.<BR>—3 A kind of fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदः|मोद
मोदः [मुद्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Delight, pleasure, joy, gladness; यत्रानन्दाश्च मोदाश्च U. 2. 12;<BR> R. 5. 15; अनुपदनिगदितमधुरिपुमोदम् Gīt.<BR>—2 Perfume, fragrance; अश्विनोरोषधीनां च घ्राणो मोदप्रमोदयोः Bhāg. 2. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदा
मोदः + .{@-दा@} A species of plant (अजमोदा); also मोदाढ्या.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मोदाख्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदाख्यः|मोदाख्य
मोदः + -आख्यः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदक|मोदकः
मोदक <i>a.</i> (-का, -की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मोदयति-मुद् णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Pleasing, delighting, gladdening. —2 Glad, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदकः|मोदक
मोदक + .{@-कः, -कम्@} —1 A sweetmeat in general; Y. 1. 289 (com. मोदकाः लड्डुकाः).<BR>—2 A kind of pill (in medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदकम्
मोदक + .{@-कः, -कम्@} —1 A sweetmeat in general; Y. 1. 289 (com. मोदकाः लड्डुकाः).<BR>—2 A kind of pill (in medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदकः|मोदक
मोदक + .{@-कः@} N. of a mixed tribe (sprung from a Kṣatriya father and a<BR> Śūdra mother).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मोदककारः, मोदकवल्लभः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदककारः|मोदककार
मोदक + -कारः a confectioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदकवल्लभः|मोदकवल्लभ
मोदक + -वल्लभः N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदकिका
मोदकिका A sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदनम्
मोदनम् [मुद्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Joy, pleasure.<BR>—2 The act of pleasing.<BR>—3 Wax. ━<i>a.</i> Gladdening, delighting; निशामुखे वृकबलगृध्रमोदनं<BR> महात्मनां नृपवरयुद्धमद् भुतम् Mb. 7. 155. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदयन्तिका|मोदयंतिका
मोदयन्तिका, -मोदयन्ती<BR> A kind of jasmine (Arabian).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदयन्ती
मोदयन्तिका, -मोदयन्ती<BR> A kind of jasmine (Arabian).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदित|मोदितः
मोदित <i>a.</i> Glad, pleased, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदितम्
मोदित + .{@-तम्@} Pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदिन्
मोदिन् <i>a.</i> [मुद्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Glad, pleased, cheerful.<BR>—2 Gladdening, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोदिनी
मोदिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 N. of various plants (अजमोदा, मल्लिका, यूथिका).<BR>—2 Musk.<BR>—3 An intoxicating or spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरः|मोर
मोरः A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरकम्
मोरकम्<BR>—1 A kind of steel.<BR>—2 The milk of cow seven days after calving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरटः|मोरट|मोरटं
मोरटः [मुर्-अटन्]<BR>—1 A kind of plant with sweet juice.<BR>—2 The milk of a cow seven days after calving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरटम्
मोरटः + .{@-टम्@}<BR>—1 The root of the sugarcane.<BR>—2 The flower of the Ankoṭa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरटा
मोरटः + .{@-टा@} Hemp used for bow-strings (मूर्वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरणः|मोरण
मोरणः Sour butter-milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोरिका
मोरिका A side-door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषः|मोष
मोषः [मुष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A thief, robber; पथि मोषाभिदर्शने शक्तितो नाभिधावन्तः Ms. 9. 274.<BR>—2 Theft, robbery.<BR>—3 Plundering, stealing, taking away, removing (fig. also); न पुष्पमोषमर्हत्युद्यानलता<BR> Mk. 1; दृष्टिमोषे प्रदोषे Gīt. 11.<BR>—4 Stolen property; संनिधातॄंश्च मोषस्य हन्याच्चौरमिवेश्वरः Ms. 9. 278.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मोषकृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषकृत्
मोषः + -कृत् <i>m.</i> a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषकः|मोषक
मोषकः [मुष्-ण्वुल्] A robber, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषणम्
मोषणम् [मुष्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Robbing, plundering, stealing, defrauding; Kull. on Ms. 8. 400.<BR>—2 Cutting.<BR>—3 Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषयित्नुः|मोषयित्नु
मोषयित्नुः<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—2 The cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोषा
मोषा Theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोष्टृ
मोष्टृ <i>m.</i> A thief, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहः|मोह|मोहं
मोहः [मुह् घञ्]<BR>—1 Loss of consciousness, fainting, a swoon, insensibility; मोहेनान्तर्वरतनुरियं<BR> लक्ष्यते मुच्यमाना V. 1. 8; मोहादभूत् कष्टतरः प्रबोधः R. 14. 56;<BR> Ku. 3. 73; कतिचन पेतुरुपेत्य मोहमुद्राम् Śiva B. 28. 88.<BR>—2 Perplexity, delusion, embarrassment, confusion; यज्ज्ञात्वा न पुनर्मोहमेवं<BR> यास्यसि पाण्डव Bg. 4. 35.<BR>—3 Folly, ignorance, infatuation; तितीर्षुर्दुस्तरं मोहादुडुपेनास्मि सागरम्<BR> R. 1. 2; Ś. 7. 25.<BR>—4 Error, mistake.<BR>—5 Wonder, astonishment.<BR>—6 Affliction, pain.<BR>—7 A magical art employed to confound an enemy.<BR>—8 (In phil.) Delusion of mind which prevents one from discerning the<BR> truth (makes one believe in the reality of worldly objects and to be addicted<BR> to the gratification of sensual pleasures); महामोहं च मोहं च तमश्चाज्ञानवृत्तयः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 12. 2.<BR>—9 Illusion of attachment or love; स्वगृहोद्यानगतेऽपि स्निग्धैः पापं<BR> विशङ्क्यते मोहात् Pt. 2. 171.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मोहोपमा, मोहकलिलम्, मोहजालम्, मोहनिद्रा, मोहमन्त्रः, मोहरात्रिः, मोहशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहोपमा
मोहः + -उपमा (in Rhet.) a figure of speech in which the उपमान<BR> and उपमेय are confounded; शशीत्युत्प्रेक्ष्य तन्वङ्गि त्वन्मुखं त्वन्मुखाशया ।<BR> इन्दुमप्यनुधावामीत्येषा मोहोपमा स्मृता ॥ Kāv. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहकलिलम्
मोहः + -कलिलम्<BR>—1 the thick net or snare of delusion.<BR>—2 spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहजालम्
मोहः + -जालम् mundane fascination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनिद्रा
मोहः + -निद्रा over-weening confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहमन्त्रः|मोहमन्त्र|मोहमंत्र
मोहः + -मन्त्रः a deluding spell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहरात्रिः|मोहरात्रि
मोहः + -रात्रिः <i>f.</i> the night when the whole universe will be destroyed;<BR> कालरात्रिर्महारात्रिर्मोहरात्रिश्च Caṇḍīpāṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहशास्त्रम्
मोहः + -शास्त्रम् a false doctrine or precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहक
मोहक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Infatuating.<BR>—2 Causing ignorance or folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहन|मोहनं|मोहनः
मोहन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मुह्-णिच्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Stupefying.<BR>—2 Bewildering, perplexing, puzzling; तमस्त्वज्ञानजं विद्धि मोहनं<BR> सर्वदेहिनाम् Bg. 14. 8.<BR>—3 Deluding, infatuating.<BR>—4 Fascinating, enrapturing; सकलेन्द्रियमोहनानि U. 1. 36; Māl. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनः|मोहन|मोहनं
मोहन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 N. of one of the five arrows of Cupid.<BR>—3 The Thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनी
मोहन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A particular illusion.<BR>—2 A particular incantation.<BR>—3 One of the nine शक्तिs of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनम्
मोहन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Stupefying.<BR>—2 Bewildering, perplexing, puzzling.<BR>—3 Stupor; loss of sensation.<BR>—4 Infatuation, delusion, mistake.<BR>—5 A seduction, temptation.<BR>—6 Sexual intercourse; योषितः पतितकाञ्चनकाञ्चौ मोहनातिरभसेन नितम्बे<BR> Śi. 10. 85; Māl. 4.<BR>—7 A means employed in perplexing others.<BR>—8 A magical charm employed to bewilder an enemy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मोहनास्त्रम्, मोहनगृहम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनास्त्रम्
मोहन + -अस्त्रम् a missile which fascinates or bewitches the person against<BR> whom it is used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनगृहम्
मोहन + -गृहम् a delusive chamber; गूढभित्तिसंचारं मोहनगृहं तन्मध्ये<BR> वा वासगृहम् Kau. A. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनकः|मोहनक
मोहनकः The month of Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1293-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहनीय
मोहनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to or causing swoon, delusion &c.<BR>—2 Perplexing, puzzling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहित
मोहित <i>p. p.</i> [मुह्-णिच् क्त]<BR>—1 Stupefied.<BR>—2 Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>—3 Deluded, fascinated, infatuated, beguiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिन्
मोहिन् <i>a.</i> [मुह्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Stupefying.<BR>—2 Perplexing, bewildering, fallacious.<BR>—3 Fascinating, enrapturing, enchanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मोहिनी
मोहिनी<BR>—1 N. of an <i>Apsaras</i>.<BR>—2 A fascinating woman (the form assumed by Viṣṇu at the time of cheating<BR> the demons of nectar.)<BR>—3 The flower of a kind of jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकलिः|मौकलि
मौक(कु)लिः A crow; स्तम्बाडम्बरमूकमौकुलिकुलः क्रौञ्चावतोऽयं<BR> गिरिः U. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकुलिः|मौकुलि
मौक(कु)लिः A crow; स्तम्बाडम्बरमूकमौकुलिकुलः क्रौञ्चावतोऽयं<BR> गिरिः U. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौकल्यः|मौकल्य
मौकल्यः A वैदेहक who sews and dyes clothes (रामक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकम्
मौक्तिकम् [मुक्तैव स्वार्थे ठक्] A pearl; गारुत्मतं च माणिक्यं<BR> मौक्तिकं श्रेष्ठमेव हि Śukra. 4. 162; मोक्तिकं न गजे गजे Subhāṣ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मौक्तिकावली, मौक्तिकगुम्फिका, मौक्तिकतण्डुलः, मौक्तिकदामन्, मौक्तिकप्रसवा, मौक्तिकशुक्तिः, मौक्तिकसरः, मौक्तिकस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकावली
मौक्तिकम् + -आवली a string of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकगुम्फिका|मौक्तिकगुंफिका
मौक्तिकम् + -गुम्फिका a female who prepares pearl-necklaces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकतण्डुलः|मौक्तिकतण्डुल
मौक्तिकम् + -तण्डुलः a kind of white यावनाल (Mar. जोंधळा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकदामन्
मौक्तिकम् + -दामन् <i>n.</i> a string of pearls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकप्रसवा
मौक्तिकम् + -प्रसवा a pearl-muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकशुक्तिः|मौक्तिकशुक्ति
मौक्तिकम् + -शुक्तिः <i>f.</i> a pearl-oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकसरः|मौक्तिकसर
मौक्तिकम् + -सरः a necklace or string of pearls; अयं कण्ठे बाहुः शिशिरमसृणो<BR> मौक्तिकसरः U. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्तिकस्थानम्
मौक्तिकम् + -स्थानम्<BR>—1 a conch, shell.<BR>—2 an elephant, frog or hog (?).<BR>—3 the bamboo tree; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौक्यम्
मौक्यम् [मूकस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Dumbness, muteness, speechlessness;<BR> अन्नहर्तामयावित्वं मौक्यं वागपहारकः Ms. 11. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख|मौखं
मौख <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Oral.<BR>—2 Relating to the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौख्यम्
मौख्यम् Precedence, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखरिः|मौखरि
मौखरिः N. of a family; पदे पदे मौखरिभिः कृतार्चनम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौखर्यम्
मौखर्यम् [मुखरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Talkativeness, garrulity.<BR>—2 Abuse, defamation, calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौग्ध्यम्
मौग्ध्यम् [मुग्ध-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Silliness, foolishness.<BR>—2 Artlessness, simplicity, innocence.<BR>—3 Charm, beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौघ्यम्
मौघ्यम् Uselessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौचम्
मौचम् The fruit of the plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्ज|मौंज
मौञ्ज <i>a.</i> (-ञ्जी <i>f.</i>) [मुञ्ज-अण्] Made of Munja grass<BR> (also मौञ्जक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जी|मौंजी
मौञ्जी The girdle of a Brāhmaṇa made of a triple string of Munja<BR> grass; व्रताय मौञ्जीं त्रिगुणां बभार याम् Ku. 5. 10; Ms. 2. 42; पिशङ्गमौञ्जीयुजमर्जुनच्छविम् Śi. 1. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मौञ्जीनिबन्धनम्, मौञ्जीबन्धनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जीनिबन्धनम्
मौञ्जी + -निबन्धनम्, -बन्धनम् binding on the Munja grass<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">Page1294-2</a>]<BR> girdle, investiture with the sacred thread; Ms. 2. 27; मातुरप्रेऽधिजननं<BR> द्वितीयं मौञ्जिबन्धने 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौञ्जीबन्धनम्
मौञ्जी + -निबन्धनम्, -बन्धनम् binding on the Munja grass<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">Page1294-2</a>]<BR> girdle, investiture with the sacred thread; Ms. 2. 27; मातुरप्रेऽधिजननं<BR> द्वितीयं मौञ्जिबन्धने 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौढ्यम्
मौढ्यम्<BR>—1 Ignorance, stupidity, folly; हित्वार्चां भजते मौढ्याद् भस्मन्येव जुहोति सः Bhāg.<BR>—2 Childishness.<BR>—3 Spiritual folly.<BR>—4 Swoon, stupor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौण्ड्यम्
मौण्ड्यम्<BR>—1 Shaving of the head, tonsure; मौण्ड्यं प्राणान्तिको दण्डो ब्राह्मणस्य<BR> विधीयते Ms. 8. 379.<BR>—2 Baldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौत्रम्
मौत्रम् A quantity of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदक
मौदक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to sweetmeats.<BR>—2 Dealing in sweetmeats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौदकिकः|मौदकिक
मौदकिकः A confectioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गलायनः|मौद्गलायन
मौद्गलायनः N. of a pupil of गौतमबुद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गलिः|मौद्गलि
मौद्गलिः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौद्गीन|मौद्गीनं
मौद्गीन <i>a.</i> [मुद्गानां भवनं क्षेत्रं खञ्] Fit for being sown<BR> with beans, or sown with beans (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनम्
मौनम् [मुनेर्भावः अण्]<BR>—1 Silence, taciturnity; विभूषणं मौनमपण्डितानाम् Bh. 2. 7; मौनं<BR> सर्वार्थसाधनम्; मौनं त्यज ‘open your lips’; मौनं समाचर ‘hold your tongue’.<BR>—2 The unblooming state (अप्रफुल्लीभाव); गुञ्जति मञ्जु मिलिन्दे मा<BR> मालति मौनमुपयासीः Bv. 1. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मौनमुद्रा, मौनव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनमुद्रा
मौनम् + -मुद्रा the attitude of silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनव्रतम्
मौनम् + -व्रतम् a vow of silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौनिन्
मौनिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मौनमस्यास्ति इनि] Observing a vow of silence,<BR> silent, taciturn; तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिर्मौनी संतुष्टो येनकेनचित् Bg. 12. 19.<BR>━<i>m.</i> A holy sage, an ascetic, a hermit; also मौनिः; एवं ब्रुवति<BR> मौनीश आगताश्चापवाहकाः A. Rām. 1. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरजिकः|मौरजिक
मौरजिकः [मुरजवादनं शिल्पमस्य ठक्] A drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौरव
मौरव <i>a.</i> Made from the Muru iron; also मौर्व्य; मौर्व्याभिजध्ने<BR> गदया विभावरीम् Bhāg. 3. 17. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्ख्यम्
मौर्ख्यम् [मूर्ख-ष्यञ्] Folly, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्यः|मौर्य
मौर्यः [मुर-ण्य] N. of a dynasty of kings beginning with Chandragupta;<BR> मौर्ये नवे राजनि Mu. 4. 15; मौर्यौर्हिरण्यार्थिभिरर्चाः प्रकल्पिताः<BR> Mbh.; (there is a difference of opinion among scholars as to the meaning<BR> of the word मौर्य in this passage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्व
मौर्व <i>a.</i> (-र्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Made of Mūrvā plant; मौर्व्या मेखलया नियन्त्रितमधोवासश्च<BR> माञ्जिष्ठकम् U. 4. 20; Mv. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौर्वी|मौर्व्वी
मौर्वी [मूर्वालता तत्तन्तुना निर्वृत्ता अण्]<BR>—1 A bow-string; मौर्वीकिणाङ्को भुजः Ś. 1. 13; मौर्वी धनुषि चातता<BR> R. 1. 19, 18. 48; Ku. 3. 55; धनुः पौष्पं मौर्वी मधुकरमयी पञ्च विशिखाः<BR> Saundaryalaharī 6.<BR>—2 A girdle made of Mūrvā grass (to be worn by a Kṣatriya); क्षत्रियस्य<BR> तु मौर्वी ज्या Ms. 2. 42.<BR>—3 (In geom.) The sine of an arc; (also मौर्विका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1294-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल|मौलः
मौल <i>a.</i> (-ला, -ली <i>f.</i>) [मूलं वेत्ति मूलादागतो वा अण्]<BR>—1 Radical, original.<BR>—2 Ancient, old, of long standing (as a custom); aboriginal, indigenous<BR> (as people); सामन्तानामभावे तु मौलानां सीम्नि साक्षिणाम् Ms. 8. 259.<BR>—3 Nobly born, of a good family.<BR>—4 Brought up in the service of a king for generations, holding office<BR> from ancient times, hereditary; मौलाञ्छास्त्रविदः Ms. 7. 54; R. 19. 57;<BR> अभावेन च मौलानाम् Śiva B. 8. 56.<BR>—5 Monetary; आददीत बलं राजा मौलं मित्रबलं तथा Mb. 15. 7. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलः|मौल
मौल + .{@-लः@} An old or hereditary minister; (प्रकृतयः) मौलैरानाययामासुर्भरतं<BR> स्तम्भिताश्रुभिः R. 12. 12, 14. 10, 18. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलि|मौलिः
मौलि <i>a.</i> [मूलस्यादूरभवः इञ्] Head, foremost, best; अखिलपरिमलानां<BR> मौलिना सौरभेण Bv. 1. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिः|मौलि
मौलि + .{@-लिः@}<BR>—1 The head, the crown of the head; मौलौ वा रचयाञ्जलिम् Ve. 3. 40;<BR> R. 13. 59; Ku. 5. 79.<BR>—2 The head or top of anything, top-most point; U. 2. 30; देव्यग्रदीपमालाया<BR> मौलिदीपतुलां दधौ Parṇāl. 3 The Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिः|मौलि
मौलि + .{@-लिः@} (<i>m., f.</i>)<BR>—1 A crown, diadem, tiara; अलब्धशाणोत्कषणा नृपाणां न जातु मौलौ मणयो<BR> वसन्ति Bv. 1. 73.<BR>—2 Hair on the crown of the head, tuft or lock of hair; जटामौलि Ku. 2. 26<BR> (जटाजूट Malli.); पुष्पितलतान्तनियमितंविलम्बिमौलिना Ki. 12. 41.<BR>—3 Braided hair, hair braided and ornamented; दुःशासनेन कचकर्षणभिन्नमौलिः Ve. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिः|मौलि
मौलि + .{@-लिः, -ली@} <i>f.</i> The earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मौलिकफः, मौलिपृष्ठम्, मौलिबन्धः, मौलिमणिः, मौलिरत्नम्, मौलिमण्डनम्, मौलिमुकुटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौली
मौलि + .{@-लिः, -ली@} <i>f.</i> The earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: मौलिकफः, मौलिपृष्ठम्, मौलिबन्धः, मौलिमणिः, मौलिरत्नम्, मौलिमण्डनम्, मौलिमुकुटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिकफः|मौलिकफ
मौलि + -कफः the phlegm secreted in the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिपृष्ठम्
मौलि + -पृष्ठम् the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिबन्धः|मौलिबन्ध
मौलि + -बन्धः a diadem for the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिमणिः|मौलिमणि
मौलि + -मणिः, -रत्नम् a crest-jewel, a jewel worn in the crown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिरत्नम्
मौलि + -मणिः, -रत्नम् a crest-jewel, a jewel worn in the crown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिमण्डनम्
मौलि + -मण्डनम् a head-ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिमुकुटम्
मौलि + -मुकुटम् a crown, tiara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिक|मौलिकः
मौलिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Radical.<BR>—2 Chief, principal, prime; संजीवनोपायस्तु मौलिक एव रामभद्रस्याद्य<BR> संनिहितः U. 3.<BR>—3 Inferior, of low origin (opp. to कुलीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिकः|मौलिक
मौलिक + .{@-कः@} A dealer in or digger of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलिन्
मौलिन् <i>a.</i> Having a crown, crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौलेयकः|मौलेयक
मौलेयकः A variety of gems; Kau. A. 2. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौल्यम्
मौल्यम् Price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौषल|मौषलं
मौषल <i>a.</i> A bath in which one remains steady like a pestle in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौषिकारः|मौषिकार
मौषिकारः A male mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टा
मौष्टा Playing at fisticuffs, a boxing or pugilistic encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौष्टिकः|मौष्टिक
मौष्टिकः<BR>—1 A rogue, cheat, sharper.<BR>—2 A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसल|मौसलः
मौसल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मुसल-अण्]<BR>—1 Formed like a club, club-shaped.<BR>—2 Fought with clubs (as a battle).<BR>—3 Relating to the battle with clubs (as a <i>parvan</i>; in this <i>parvan</i><BR> (Mb. 16th) is narrated the death of Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma, and the self-destruction<BR> of Kṛṣṇaʼs family through the curse of Brāhmaṇas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसलः|मौसल
मौसल + .{@-लः@} A kind of <i>madhuparka</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौसलम्
मौसल + .{@-लम्@} The destruction of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">Page1295-2</a>]<BR> Yādavas in the battle with clubs; वज्रस्तस्याभवद्यस्तु मौसलादवशेषितः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 90. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्तः|मौहूर्त|मौहूर्त्त|मौहूर्त्तः
मौहूर्तः [मुहूर्त-अण्] An astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्तिक|मौहूर्तिकः|मौहूर्त्तिक|मौहूर्त्तिकः
मौहूर्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [मुहूर्त-ठक्]<BR>—1 Momentary, transient.<BR>—2 Relating to a particular time.<BR>—3 Skilled in astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मौहूर्तिकः|मौहूर्तिक|मौहूर्त्तिक|मौहूर्त्तिकः
मौहूर्तिक + .{@-कः@} An astrologer; मौहूर्तिकैः संवाद्यताम्; चिकित्सकमाहानसिकमौहूर्तिकांश्च<BR> पश्येत् Kau. A. 1. 19. 16; अथ मौहूर्तिकादिष्टे विध्युक्तेऽहनि शोभने<BR> Śiva B. 1. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्ना
म्ना €1 P. (मनति, म्नात)<BR>—1 To repeat (in the mind).<BR>—2 To learn diligently.<BR>—3 To remember.<BR>—4 To praise (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्नात
म्नात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Repeated.<BR>—2 Learnt, studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्ष्
म्रक्ष् I. €1 P. (म्रक्षति)<BR>—1 To rub; मृक्षा शीर्षा चतुर्णाम् Rv. 8. 74. 13.<BR>—2 To heap, collect, accumulate.<BR>—3 To strike, hurt, kill. ━II. €10 U. (म्रक्षयति-ते)<BR>—1 To heap, accumulate.<BR>—2 To smear, rub, anoint.<BR>—3 To mix, combine.<BR>—4 To speak indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्षः|म्रक्ष
म्रक्षः Hypocrisy, dissimulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रक्षणम्
म्रक्षणम्^1 [म्रक्ष्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Smearing the body with unguents.<BR>—2 Anointing, smearing in general.<BR>—3 Accumulating, heaping up.<BR>—4 Oil, ointment.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: virAma missing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रञ्च्
म्रञ्च् See मृञ्च् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रद्
म्रद् €1 Ā. (म्रदते, <i>caus.</i> म्रदयति-ते) To pound,<BR> grind, crush, trample upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमन्
म्रदिमन् <i>m.</i> [मृदोर्भावः इमनिच्]<BR>—1 Tenderness, softness; लसत्फुल्लाम्भोजम्रदिमहरणः कोऽपि चरणः<BR> Lakṣmīlaharī 6.<BR>—2 Mildness, weakness; (स्वर्भानुः) हिमांशुमाशु ग्रसते तन्म्रदिम्नः<BR> स्फुटं फलम् Śi. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रदिमान्वित
म्रदिमान्वित <i>a.</i> Mild, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रातनम्
म्रातनम् Cyperus Rotundus (Mar. बिंवली नागरमोथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रुच्
म्रुच् €1 P. (म्रोचति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

