म्रेट्
म्रेट्(ड्) €1 P. (म्रेट(ड)ति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्रेड्
म्रेट्(ड्) €1 P. (म्रेट(ड)ति) To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लक्ष्
म्लक्ष् €10 U. (म्लक्षयति-ते) To cut or divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्ट|म्लिष्टं|म्लिष्टः
म्लिष्ट <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spoken indistinctly (as by barbarians), indistinct; P. VII. 2. 18;<BR> म्लिष्टमस्फुटम् Abh. Cin. 266.<BR>—2 Barbarous.<BR>—3 Withered, faded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लिष्टम्
म्लिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 An indistinct or barbarous speech.<BR>—2 A foreign language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुच्
म्लुच्, -म्लुञ्च्<BR>—1 See म्रच्, म्रुञ्च्.<BR>—2 To set; म्लोचन्ति ह्यन्या देवता न वायुः Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लुञ्च्|म्लुंच्
म्लुच्, -म्लुञ्च्<BR>—1 See म्रच्, म्रुञ्च्.<BR>—2 To set; म्लोचन्ति ह्यन्या देवता न वायुः Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छ्|म्लेछ्
म्लेच्छ् or म्लेछ् €1 P., €10 U. (म्लेच्छति, म्लेच्छयति-ते, म्लिष्ट, म्लेच्छित)<BR>—1 To speak confusedly, indistinctly, or barbarously.<BR>—2 To speak distinctly (व्यक्तायां वाचि); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेछ्|म्लेच्छ्
म्लेच्छ् or म्लेछ् €1 P., €10 U. (म्लेच्छति, म्लेच्छयति-ते, म्लिष्ट, म्लेच्छित)<BR>—1 To speak confusedly, indistinctly, or barbarously.<BR>—2 To speak distinctly (व्यक्तायां वाचि); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1295-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छः|म्लेच्छ|म्लेच्छं|म्लेछ
म्लेच्छः [म्लेच्छ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A barbarian, a non-Aryan (one not speaking the Sanskṛt language,<BR> or not conforming to Hindu or Āryan institutions), a foreigner in general;<BR> ग्राह्या म्लेच्छप्रसिद्धिस्तु विरोधादर्शने सति J. N. V.; म्लेच्छान् मूर्छयते;<BR> or म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालम् Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 An outcast, a very low man; (Baudhāyana thus defines the word:− गोमांसखादको<BR> यस्तु विरुद्धं बहु भाषते । सर्वाचारविहीनश्च म्लेच्छ इत्यभिधीयते ॥).<BR>—3 A sinner, wicked person.<BR>—4 Foreign or barbarous speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छम्
म्लेच्छः + .{@-च्छम्@}<BR>—1 Copper.<BR>—2 Vermilion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: म्लेच्छाख्यम्, म्लेच्छाशः, म्लेच्छास्यम्, म्लेच्छमुखम्, म्लेच्छकन्दः, म्लेच्छजातिः, म्लेच्छदेशः, म्लेच्छमण्डलम्, म्लेच्छद्विष्टः, म्लेच्छभाषा, म्लेच्छभोजनः, म्लेच्छवाच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छाख्यम्
म्लेच्छः + -आख्यम् copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छाशः|म्लेच्छाश
म्लेच्छः + -आशः wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छास्यम्
म्लेच्छः + -आस्यम्, -मुखम् copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमुखम्
म्लेच्छः + -आस्यम्, -मुखम् copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छकन्दः|म्लेच्छकन्द|म्लेच्छकंद
म्लेच्छः + -कन्दः garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छजातिः|म्लेच्छजाति
म्लेच्छः + -जातिः <i>f.</i> a savage or barbarian race, a mountaineer; पुलिन्दा<BR> नाहला निष्टपाः शबरा वरुटा भटाः । माला भिल्लाः किराताश्च सर्वेऽपि म्लेच्छजातयः ॥<BR> Abh. Cin. 934.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छदेशः|म्लेच्छदेश
म्लेच्छः + -देशः, -मण्डलम् a country inhabited by non-Āryans or barbarians,<BR> a foreign or barbarous country; कृष्णसारस्तु चरति मृगो यत्र स्वभावतः ।<BR> स ज्ञेयो यज्ञियो देशो म्लेच्छदेशस्त्वतः परः ॥ Ms. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छमण्डलम्
म्लेच्छः + -देशः, -मण्डलम् a country inhabited by non-Āryans or barbarians,<BR> a foreign or barbarous country; कृष्णसारस्तु चरति मृगो यत्र स्वभावतः ।<BR> स ज्ञेयो यज्ञियो देशो म्लेच्छदेशस्त्वतः परः ॥ Ms. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छद्विष्टः|म्लेच्छद्विष्ट
म्लेच्छः + -द्विष्टः bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभाषा
म्लेच्छः + -भाषा a foreign language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभोजनः|म्लेच्छभोजन|म्लेच्छभोजनं
म्लेच्छः + -भोजनः wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छभोजनम्
म्लेच्छः + -भोजनः + .({@-नम्@}) barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छवाच्
म्लेच्छः + -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking a barbarous or foreign language; म्लेच्छवाचश्चार्यवाचः<BR> सर्वे ते दस्यवः स्मृताः Ms. 10. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छनम्
म्लेच्छनम्<BR>—1 Speaking indistinctly or confusedly.<BR>—2 Speaking in a barbarous tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छित|म्लेच्छितं
म्लेच्छित <i>p. p.</i> Spoken indistinctly or barbarously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छितम्
म्लेच्छित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A foreign tongue.<BR>—2 An ungrammatical word or speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेच्छितकम्
म्लेच्छितकम् Foreign or barbarous speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेट्
म्लेट्, -म्लेड् (म्लेट(ड)ति)<BR> To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेड्
म्लेट्, -म्लेड् (म्लेट(ड)ति)<BR> To be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लेव्
म्लेव् €1 Ā. (म्लेवते) To worship, serve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लै
म्लै €1 P. (म्लायति, मम्लौ, अम्लासीत्, म्लास्यति, म्लान)<BR>—1 To fade, wither; म्लायतां भूरुहाणाम् Bv. 1. 36; Śi. 5. 43; बभ्रमुश्चस्खलुश्चान्ये<BR> पेतुर्मम्लुस्तथाऽपरे Mb. 7. 115. 29; माने म्लायति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">Page1296-2</a>]<BR> Bh. 3. 33.<BR>—2 To grow weary or languid; to be fatigued or exhausted; पथि..मम्लतुर्न<BR> मणिकुट्टिमोचितौ R. 11. 9; Bk. 14. 6; वनविहरणखेदम्लानम् Śi. 7. 75.<BR>—3 To be sad or dejected, be downcast or dispirited; मम्लौ साथ विषादेन<BR> K. P. 10; म्लायते मे मनो हीदम् Mb.<BR>—4 To become thin or emaciated.<BR>—5 To disappear, vanish.<BR>—5 To decline, become less; वनविहरणखेदम्लानमम्लानशोभाः Śi. 7. 75.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> (म्लापयति)<BR>—1 To cause to fade, wither up.<BR>—2 To make languid or dispirited, emaciate, enfeeble.<BR>—3 To crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लात
म्लात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Faded, withered.<BR>—2 Made white by tanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लान|म्लानं
म्लान <i>p. p.</i> [म्लै-क्त तस्य नः]<BR>—1 Faded, withered.<BR>—2 Wearied, weary, languid.<BR>—3 Enfeebled, weak, feeble, faint.<BR>—4 Sad, dejected, melancholy.<BR>—5 Black.<BR>—6 Foul, dirty.<BR>—7 Ignominous; कः कुर्वीत शिरः प्रणाममलिनं म्लानं मनस्वी जनः Bh. 1. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानम्
म्लान + .{@-नम्@} Withering, fading.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: म्लानाङ्ग, म्लानमनस्, म्लानमुख, म्लानवक्त्र, म्लानव्रीड<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानाङ्ग
म्लान + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> weak-bodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानाङ्गी|म्लानांगी
म्लान + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गी@}) a woman during her menses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानमनस्
म्लान + -मनस् <i>a.</i> depressed in mind, dispirited, disheartened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानमुख
म्लान + -मुख <i>a.</i> sad, dejected; see म्लानवक्त्र; द्राक्षा म्लानमुखी<BR> जाता शर्करा चाश्मतां गता । सुभाषितरसस्याग्रे सुधा भीता दिवं गता ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानवक्त्र
म्लान + -वक्त्र <i>a.</i> having a blackened countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानव्रीड
म्लान + -व्रीड <i>a.</i> shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानिः|म्लानि
म्लानिः <i>f.</i> [म्लै-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Fading, withering, decay.<BR>—2 Languor, lassitude, weariness.<BR>—3 Sadness, dejection.<BR>—4 Foulness.<BR>—5 Disappearance.<BR>—6 Blackness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लानिमन्
म्लानिमन् <i>m.</i> Withered or faded condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लायत्
म्लायत्, -म्लायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Withering, growing thin or emaciated.<BR>—2 Declining, growing less.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: म्लायद्वक्त्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लायिन्
म्लायत्, -म्लायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Withering, growing thin or emaciated.<BR>—2 Declining, growing less.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: म्लायद्वक्त्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लायद्वक्त्र
म्लायत् + -वक्त्र <i>a.</i> having a sorrowful or haggard face; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

म्लास्नु
म्लास्नु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Becoming faded or withered.<BR>—2 Growing thin or emaciated.<BR>—3 Growing languid or weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1296-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यः|य|यं
यः<BR>—1 One who goes or moves, a goer, mover.<BR>—2 A carriage.<BR>—3 Wind, air.<BR>—4 Union.<BR>—5 Fame.<BR>—6 Barley.<BR>—7 Restraint.<BR>—8 Light.<BR>—9 A bandoning.<BR>—10 One of the eight syllabic feet (गण) consisting of one short<BR> syllable followed by two long ones.<BR>—11 N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

या
यः + .{@-या@}<BR>—1 Going.<BR>—2 A carriage.<BR>—3 Restraining.<BR>—4 Religious meditation (ध्यान).<BR>—5 Obtaining.<BR>—6 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—7 Pudendum muliebre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकन्
यकन् <i>n.</i> The liver. (This word has no forms for the first five<BR> inflections, and is optionally substituted for यकृत् after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्
यकृत् <i>n.</i> [यं संयमं करोति कृ क्विप् तुक् च Tv.] The liver<BR> or any affection of it; सिन्धवो गुदा यकृच्च क्लोमानश्च पर्वताः Bṛ. Up. 1. 1. 1;<BR> Mv. 3. 32.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यकृदात्मिका, यकृदुदरम्, यकृत्कोषः, यकृद्वैरिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृदात्मिका
यकृत् + -आत्मिका a kind of cockroach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृदुदरम्
यकृत् + -उदरम् enlargement of the liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृत्कोषः|यकृत्कोष
यकृत् + -कोषः the membrane enveloping the liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यकृद्वैरिन्
यकृत् + -वैरिन् <i>m.</i> N. of a plant (Mar. रक्तरोहिडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्
यक्ष् I. €10 Ā. (यक्षयते) To honour, worship, adore; रक्षाम<BR> इति तत्रान्यैर्यक्षाम इति चापरैः Rām. 7. 4. 12. ━II. €1 P. (यक्षति) To stir, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षः|यक्ष
यक्षः [यक्ष्यते, यक्ष्-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 N. of a class of demigods who are described as attendants of Kubera,<BR> the god of riches, and employed in guarding his gardens and treasures;<BR> यक्षोत्तमा यक्षपतिं धनेशं रक्षन्ति वै प्रासगदादिहस्ताः Hariv.;<BR> Me. 68; Bg. 10. 23, 11. 22.<BR>—2 A kind of ghost or spirit; तन्न व्यजानन्त किमिदं यक्षमिति Ken. 3. 2.<BR>—3 N. of the palace of Indra.<BR>—4 N. of Kubera.<BR>—5 Worship.<BR>—6 A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षम्
यक्षः + .{@-क्षम्@}<BR>—1 A ghost.<BR>—2 Sacrifice.<BR>—3 Anything honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षी
यक्षः + .{@-क्षी@}<BR>—1 A female Yakṣa.<BR>—2 N. of Kuberaʼs wife.<BR>—3 The Yakṣa class; अल्पवीर्या यदा यक्षी श्रूयते मुनिपुंगव Rām. 1. 25. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यक्षाधिपः, यक्षाधिपतिः, यक्षेन्द्रः, यक्षामलकम्, यक्षावासः, यक्षकर्दमः, यक्षग्रहः, यक्षतरुः, यक्षधूपः, यक्षबलिः, यक्षरसः, यक्षराज्, यक्षराजः, यक्षरात्रिः, यक्षवित्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षाधिपः|यक्षाधिप
यक्षः + -अधिपः, -अधिपतिः, -इन्द्रः Kubera, the lord of Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षाधिपतिः|यक्षाधिपति
यक्षः + -अधिपः, -अधिपतिः, -इन्द्रः Kubera, the lord of Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षेन्द्रः|यक्षेन्द्र
यक्षः + -अधिपः, -अधिपतिः, -इन्द्रः Kubera, the lord of Yakṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षामलकम्
यक्षः + -आमलकम् the fruit of the पिण्डखर्जूर tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षावासः|यक्षावास
यक्षः + -आवासः the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षकर्दमः|यक्षकर्दम|यक्षकर्द्दम|यक्षकर्द्दमः
यक्षः + -कर्दमः an ointment consisting of camphor, agallochum, musk<BR> and Kakkola (according to others, also sandal and saffron) mixed in equal<BR> proportions; यक्षकर्दममृदून्मृदिताङ्गं … सिषिचुरुच्चकुचास्तम्<BR> N. 21. 7; (कर्पूरागुरुकस्तुरीकक्कोलैर्यक्षकर्दमः Ak.; कुङ्कुमागुरुकस्तूरी<BR> कर्पूरं चन्दनं तथा । महासुगन्धमित्युक्तं नामतो यक्षकर्दमः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षग्रहः|यक्षग्रह
यक्षः + -ग्रहः the being possessed by Yakṣas or evil spirits; a kind of insanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षतरुः|यक्षतरु
यक्षः + -तरुः the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षधूपः|यक्षधूप
यक्षः + -धूपः resin, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षबलिः|यक्षबलि
यक्षः + -बलिः a particular nuptial ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरसः|यक्षरस
यक्षः + -रसः a kind of intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराज्
यक्षः + -राज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of Kubera; प्रतिसिञ्चन् विचिक्रीडे यक्षीभिर्यक्षराडिव Bhāg. 10. 90. 9.<BR>—2 a place prepared for wrestling and boxing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षराजः|यक्षराज
यक्षः + -राजः N. of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षरात्रिः|यक्षरात्रि
यक्षः + -रात्रिः <i>f.</i> the festival called Dīpāli, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षवित्तः|यक्षवित्त
यक्षः + -वित्तः one who is like a Yakṣa, <i>i. e.</i> the guardian of wealth,<BR> but who never uses it; तस्यैवं यक्षवित्तस्य च्युतस्योभयलोकतः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 23. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिन्
यक्षिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Living, existing.<BR>—2 Adorable, fit to be honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्षिणी
यक्षिणी<BR>—1 A female Yakṣa.<BR>—2 N. of the wife of Kubera.<BR>—3 A certain female fiend in the service of Durgā.<BR>—4 A sylph or fairy (holding intercourse with mortals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मः|यक्ष्म
यक्ष्मः, -यक्ष्मन् <i>m.</i><BR> [यक्ष्-मनिन्] Pulmonary disease in general;<BR> वेगरोधात् क्षयाच्चैव साहसाद् विषमाशनात् । त्रिदोषो जायते यक्ष्मा गदो<BR> हेतुचतुष्टयात् ॥ Caraka.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यक्ष्मग्रहः, यक्ष्मग्रस्त, यक्ष्मघ्नी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मन्
यक्ष्मः, -यक्ष्मन् <i>m.</i><BR> [यक्ष्-मनिन्] Pulmonary disease in general;<BR> वेगरोधात् क्षयाच्चैव साहसाद् विषमाशनात् । त्रिदोषो जायते यक्ष्मा गदो<BR> हेतुचतुष्टयात् ॥ Caraka.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यक्ष्मग्रहः, यक्ष्मग्रस्त, यक्ष्मघ्नी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मग्रहः|यक्ष्मग्रह
यक्ष्मः + -ग्रहः an attack of consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मग्रस्त
यक्ष्मः + -ग्रस्त <i>a.</i> consumptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मघ्नी
यक्ष्मः + -घ्नी grapes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यक्ष्मिन्
यक्ष्मिन् <i>a.</i> One who is affected by or suffers from consumption;<BR> यक्ष्मी च पशुपालश्च परिवेत्ता निराकृतिः Ms. 3. 154; Mb. 13. 90. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्
यङ् A term for the sign of the Frequentative.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यङ्ङन्तम्, यङ्लुक्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्ङन्तम्
यङ् + -अन्तम् a term for the Ātm. frequentative; <i>e. g.</i> बोभूयते from भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यङ्लुक्
यङ् + -लुक् the omission of यङ् <i>i. e.</i> the Paras. frequentative;<BR> <i>e. g.</i> बोभवीति from भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्
यज् €1 U. (यजति-ते, इयाज, ईजे; अयाक्षीत्-अयष्ट, यक्ष्यति-ते, यष्टुम्,<BR> इष्ट) <i>pass.</i> इज्यते; <i>desid.</i> (यियक्षति-ते)<BR>—1 To sacrifice, worship with sacrifices (often with instr. of words meaning<BR> ‘a sacrifice’); यजेत राजा कतुभिः Ms. 7. 79, 5. 53, 6. 36, 11. 40;<BR> Bk. 14. 90; so अश्वमेधेनेजे, पाकयज्ञेनेजे &c.<BR>—2 To make an oblation to (with acc. of the deity and instr. of the means<BR> of sacrifice or oblation); पशुना रुद्रं यजते Sk.; यस्तिलैर्यजते<BR> पितॄन् Mb.; Ms. 8. 105, 11. 119.<BR>—3 To worship, adore, honour, revere.<BR>—4 To consecrate, dedicate.<BR>—5 To give, bestow. ━<i>Caus.</i> (याजयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to sacrifice.<BR>—2 To assist at a sacrifice.<BR>—3 To perform the office of the sacrificing priest; स वेदो याजयितुं<BR> ययौ Bm. 1. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजः|यज
यजः<BR>—1 A sacrifice.<BR>—2 Fire. See यजुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत|यजतः
यजत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Holy, divine.<BR>—2 Adorable.<BR>—3 Dignified, sublime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजतः|यजत
यजत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 An officiating priest (at a sacrifice).<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजतिः|यजति
यजतिः<BR>—1 A technical name for those sacrificial ceremonies to which the verb<BR> यजति is applied; (see जुहोति for further information).<BR>—2 The act of offering something with reference to some deity; द्रव्यदवताक्रियार्थस्य<BR> यजतिशब्देन प्रत्यायनं क्रियते । ŚB. on MS. 4. 2. 27.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यजतिदेशः, यजतिस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजतिदेशः|यजतिदेश
यजतिः + -देशः, -स्थानम् a place south of the sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजतिस्थानम्
यजतिः + -देशः, -स्थानम् a place south of the sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्रः|यजत्र
यजत्रः [यज्-अत्र] A Brāhmaṇa who maintains the sacred fire<BR> (अग्निहोत्रिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजत्रम्
यजत्रः + .{@-त्रम्@} Maintenance of the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1297-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजनम्
यजनम् [यज्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of sacrificing.<BR>—2 A sacrifice; देवयजनसंभवे देवि सीते U. 4.<BR>—3 A place of sacrifice; उत्पत्तिर्देवयजनाद् ब्रह्मवादी नृपः पिता ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमान|यजमानः
यजमान <i>a.</i> [यज्-शानच्] Sacrificing, worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमानः|यजमान
यजमान + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A person who performs a regular sacrifice and pays its expenses; जगाम<BR> यज्वा यजमानलोकम् R. 18. 12; ततः प्रविशति कुशानादाय यजमानशिष्यः Ś.<BR>—2 A person who employs a priest or priests to sacrifice for him.<BR>—3 (Hence) A host, patron, rich man.<BR>—4 The head of a family.<BR>—5 The head of a tribe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यजमानशिष्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमानशिष्यः|यजमानशिष्य
यजमान + -शिष्यः the pupil of a sacrificing Brāhmaṇa (of one who himself<BR> performs a sacrifice); Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजमानकः|यजमानक
यजमानकः = यजमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजस्
यजस् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Worship; इन्द्राग्नी यजसा गिरा Rv. 8. 40. 4.<BR>—2 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजाक|यजाकः
यजाक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Liberal.<BR>—2 Worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजिः|यजि
यजिः [यज्-इन्]<BR>—1 A sacrificer.<BR>—2 The act of sacrificing.<BR>—3 A sacrifice; दानमध्ययनं यजिः Ms. 10. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजिन्
यजिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 A worshipper, sacrificer.<BR>—2 Honouring, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुस्
यजुस् <i>n.</i> [यज्-उसि]<BR>—1 A sacrificial prayer or formula; तां कामयानां भगवानुवाह यजुषां<BR> पतिः Bhāg. 4. 1. 6.<BR>—2 A text of the Yajurveda, or the body of sacred <i>mantras</i> in prose<BR> muttered at sacrifices; वृत्तगीतिवजिंतत्वेन प्रश्लिष्टपठिता मन्त्रा<BR> यजूंषि Sāyaṇa; cf. मन्त्र.<BR>—3 N. of the Yajurveda.<BR>—4 Ved. Worship, oblation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यजुरुदरः, यजुष्पतिः, यजुर्विद्, यजुर्वेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुरुदरः
यजुस् + -उदरः Ved. an epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुष्पतिः|यजुष्पति
यजुस् + -पतिः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुर्विद्
यजुस् + -विद् <i>a.</i> knowing the sacrificial formulae.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यजुर्वेदः|यजुर्वेद|यजुर्व्वेदः
यजुस् + -वेदः the second of the three (or four, including the Atharvaveda)<BR> principal Vedas, which is a collection of sacred texts in prose relating<BR> to sacrifices; it has two chief branches or recensions:− the तैत्तिरीय<BR> or कृष्णयजुर्वेद and वाजसनेयी or शुक्लयजुर्वेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञः|यज्ञ
यज्ञः [यज्-भावे न]<BR>—1 A sacrifice, sacrificial rite; any offering or oblation; यज्ञेन<BR> यज्ञमयजन्त देवाः; तस्माद्यज्ञात् सर्वहुतः &c.; यज्ञाद् भवति पर्जन्यो<BR> यज्ञः कर्मसमुद्भवः Bg. 3. 14.<BR>—2 An act of worship, any pious or devotional act. (Every householder,<BR> but particularly a Brāhmaṇa, has to perform five such devotional acts<BR> every day; their names are:− भूतयज्ञ, मनुष्ययज्ञ, पितृयज्ञ, देवयज्ञ,<BR> and ब्रह्मयज्ञ, which are collectively called the five ‘great sacrifices’;<BR> see महायज्ञ, and the five words separately.)<BR>—3 N. of Agni.<BR>—4 Of Viṣṇu; ऋषयो यैः पराभाव्य यज्ञध्नान् यज्ञमीजिरे Bhāg. 3. 22. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: यज्ञांशः, यज्ञागारः, यज्ञागारः, यज्ञागारम्, यज्ञाङ्गम्, यज्ञान्तः, यज्ञारिः, यज्ञार्ह, यज्ञावयवः, यज्ञाशनः, यज्ञात्मन्, यज्ञायुधम्, यज्ञेशः, यज्ञेष्टम्, यज्ञोपकरणम्, यज्ञोपवीतम्, यज्ञोपासक, यज्ञकर्मन्, यज्ञकल्प, यज्ञकालः, यज्ञकीलकः, यज्ञकुण्डम्, यज्ञकृत्, यज्ञक्रतुः, यज्ञक्रिया, यज्ञगम्य, यज्ञगुह्यः, यज्ञघ्नः, यज्ञत्रातृ, यज्ञदक्षिणा, यज्ञदीक्षा, यज्ञद्रव्यम्, यज्ञद्रुह्, यज्ञधीर, यज्ञपतिः, यज्ञपत्नी, यज्ञपशुः, यज्ञपात्रम्, यज्ञभाण्डम्, यज्ञपुंस्, यज्ञपुमान्, यज्ञपुरुषः, यज्ञफलदः, यज्ञबाहुः, यज्ञभागः, यज्ञभावनः, यज्ञभावित, यज्ञभुज्, यज्ञभूमिः, यज्ञभूषणः, यज्ञभृत्, यज्ञभोक्तृ, यज्ञमहोत्सवः, यज्ञयोगः, यज्ञरसः, यज्ञरेतस्, यज्ञवराहः, यज्ञवल्लिः, यज्ञवल्ली, यज्ञवाटः, यज्ञवाह, यज्ञवाहनः, यज्ञवीर्यः, यज्ञवृक्षः, यज्ञवेदिः, यज्ञवेदी, यज्ञशरणम्, यज्ञशाला, यज्ञशिष्टम्, यज्ञशेषः, यज्ञशेषम्, यज्ञशील, यज्ञश्रेष्ठा, यज्ञसंस्तरः, यज्ञसदस्, यज्ञसंभारः, यज्ञसारः, यज्ञसिद्धिः, यज्ञसूत्रम्, यज्ञसेनः, यज्ञस्थाणुः, यज्ञहन्, यज्ञहुत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञांशः|यज्ञांश
यज्ञः + -अंशः a share of sacrifice ˚भुज् <i>m.</i> a deity, god; निबोध<BR> यज्ञांशभुजामिदानीम् Ku. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञागारः|यज्ञागार
यज्ञः + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् a sacrificial hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञागारः|यज्ञागार
यज्ञः + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् a sacrificial hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञागारम्
यज्ञः + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम् a sacrificial hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञाङ्गम्
यज्ञः + -अङ्गम्<BR>—1 a part of a sacrifice.<BR>—2 any sacrificial requisite, a means of a sacrifice; यज्ञाङ्गयोनित्वमवेक्ष्य<BR> यस्य Ku. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञाङ्गः|यज्ञाङ्ग|यज्ञांग
यज्ञः + -अङ्गम् + .({@-गः@})<BR>—1 the glomerous figtree (उदुम्बर).<BR>—2 the Khadira tree.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 the black-spotted antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञान्तः|यज्ञान्त
यज्ञः + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the completion of a sacrifice.<BR>—2 an ablution at the end<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">Page1298-2</a>]<BR> of a sacrifice for purification.<BR>—3 a supplementary sacrifice. ˚कृत् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञारिः|यज्ञारि
यज्ञः + -अरिः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञार्ह
यज्ञः + -अर्ह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 deserving sacrifice.<BR>—2 fit for a sacrifice. ━(<i>m.</i> dual) an epithet of the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञावयवः|यज्ञावयव
यज्ञः + -अवयवः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञाशनः|यज्ञाशन
यज्ञः + -अशनः a god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञात्मन्
यज्ञः + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i><BR> {@-ईश्वरः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञायुधम्
यज्ञः + -आयुधम् an implement of a sacrifice. These are said to be ten<BR> in number; स्फ्यश्च कपालानि च अग्निहोत्रहवणी च शूर्पं च कृष्णाजिनं<BR> च शम्या चोलूखलं च मुसलं च दृषच्चोपला एतानि वै दश यज्ञायुधानीति<BR> (quoted in ŚB. on MS. 4. 7.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञेशः|यज्ञेश
यज्ञः + -ईशः<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञेष्टम्
यज्ञः + -इष्टम् a kind of grass (दीर्घरोहिततृण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपकरणम्
यज्ञः + -उपकरणम् any utensil or implement necessary for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपवीतम्
यज्ञः + -उपवीतम् the sacred thread worn by members of the first three<BR> classes (and now even of other lower castes) over the left shoulder and<BR> under the right arm; see Ms. 2. 63; वामांसावलम्बिना यज्ञोपवीतेनोद्भासमानः<BR> K.; कौशं सूत्रं त्रिस्त्रिवृतं यज्ञोपवीतम् … … Baudhāyana; (originally<BR> यज्ञोपवीत was the ceremony of investiture with the sacred thread).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञोपासक
यज्ञः + -उपासक <i>a.</i> performing sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकर्मन्|यज्ञकर्म्मन्
यज्ञः + -कर्मन् <i>a.</i> engaged in a sacrifice. ━(<i>n.</i>) a sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकल्प
यज्ञः + -कल्प <i>a.</i> of the nature of a sacrifice or sacrificial offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकालः|यज्ञकाल
यज्ञः + -कालः the last lunar day of every fortnight (full-moon and newmoon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकीलकः|यज्ञकीलक
यज्ञः + -कीलकः a post to which the sacrificial victim is fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकुण्डम्
यज्ञः + -कुण्डम् a hole in the ground made for receiving the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञकृत्
यज्ञः + -कृत् <i>a.</i> performing a sacrifice. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a priest conducting a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञक्रतुः|यज्ञक्रतु
यज्ञः + -क्रतुः<BR>—1 a sacrificial rite; Ait. Br. 7. 15.<BR>—2 a complete rite or chief ceremony.<BR>—3 an epithet of Viṣṇu; ईजे च भगवन्तं यज्ञक्रतुरूपम् Bhāg. 5. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञक्रिया
यज्ञः + -क्रिया a sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञगम्य
यज्ञः + -गम्य <i>a.</i> accessible by sacrifice (Viṣṇu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञगुह्यः|यज्ञगुह्य
यज्ञः + -गुह्यः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञघ्नः|यज्ञघ्न
यज्ञः + -घ्नः a demon who interrupts a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञत्रातृ
यज्ञः + -त्रातृ <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञदक्षिणा
यज्ञः + -दक्षिणा a sacrificial gift, the fee given to the priests who<BR> perform a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञदीक्षा
यज्ञः + -दीक्षा<BR>—1 admission or initiation to a sacrificial rite.<BR>—2 performance of a sacrifice; (जननम्) तृतीयं यज्ञदीक्षायां द्विजस्य<BR> श्रुतिचोदनात् Ms. 2. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञद्रव्यम्
यज्ञः + -द्रव्यम् anything (<i>e. g.</i> a vessel) used for a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञद्रुह्
यज्ञः + -द्रुह् <i>m.</i> an evil spirit, a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञधीर
यज्ञः + -धीर <i>a.</i> conversant with worship or sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपतिः|यज्ञपति
यज्ञः + -पतिः<BR>—1 one who institutes a sacrifice. See यजमान.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपत्नी
यज्ञः + -पत्नी the wife of the institutor of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपशुः|यज्ञपशु
यज्ञः + -पशुः<BR>—1 an animal for sacrifice, a sacrificial victim.<BR>—2 a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपात्रम्
यज्ञः + -पात्रम्, -भाण्डम् a sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभाण्डम्
यज्ञः + -पात्रम्, -भाण्डम् a sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपुंस्
यज्ञः + -पुंस्, -पुमान् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपुमान्
यज्ञः + -पुंस्, -पुमान् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञपुरुषः|यज्ञपुरुष
यज्ञः + -पुरुषः, -फलदः epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञफलदः|यज्ञफलद
यज्ञः + -पुरुषः, -फलदः epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञबाहुः|यज्ञबाहु
यज्ञः + -बाहुः N. of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभागः|यज्ञभाग
यज्ञः + -भागः<BR>—1 a portion of a sacrifice, a share in the sacrificial offerings.<BR>—2 a god, deity. ˚ईश्वरः N. of Indra. ˚भुज् <i>m.</i> a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभावनः|यज्ञभावन
यज्ञः + -भावनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1298-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

यज्ञभावित
