रससरोरुहम्
रसः + -सरोरुहम् a red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्ध
रसः + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 accomplished in poetry, conversant with sentiments; जयन्ति ते सुकृतिनो<BR> रससिद्धाः कवीश्वराः Bh. 2. 24.<BR>—2 skilled in alchemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिद्धिः|रससिद्धि
रसः + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> skill in alchemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रससिन्दूरम्
रसः + -सिन्दूरम् a cinnabar made of zinc, mercury, blue vitriol and nitre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसस्थानम्
रसः + -स्थानम् vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसकम्
रसकम् Soup made from meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनम्
रसनम् [रस्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Crying, screaming, roaring, sounding, tinkling, noise or sound in general.<BR>—2 Thunder, rumbling or muttering of clouds.<BR>—3 Taste, flavour.<BR>—4 The organ of taste, the tongue; इन्द्रियं रसग्राहकं रसनं जिह्वाग्रवर्ति<BR> T. S.; Bg. 15. 9; न जयेद्रसनं यावज्जितं सर्वं जिते रसे Bhāg. 11. 8. 21.<BR>—5 Perception, appreciation, sense; सर्वेऽपि रसनाद्रसाः S. D. 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनः|रसन|रसनं
रसनम् + .{@-नः@} Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसना
रसना See रशना.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रसनामलम्, रसनामूलम्, रसनारदः, रसनालिह्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनामलम्
रसना + -मलम् any impurity on the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनामूलम्
रसना + -मूलम् the root of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनारदः|रसनारद
रसना + -रदः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसनालिह्
रसना + -लिह् <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसमय|रसमयः
रसमय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Consisting of juice or flavour.<BR>—2 Juicy, liquid.<BR>—3 Savoury.<BR>—4 Charming, elegant, graceful.<BR>—5 Proceeding from love; U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसयतिः|रसयति
रसयतिः <i>f.</i> Taste, flavour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवत्|रसवन्त्
रसवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Juicy, succulent.<BR>—2 Tasteful, savoury, sapid, well-flavoured; यदेवोपनतं दुःखात्सुखं<BR> तद्रसवत्तरम् V. 3. 21; संसारसुखवृक्षस्य द्वे एव रसवत्फले ।<BR> काव्यामृतरसास्वादः संपर्कः सज्जनैः सह ॥<BR>—3 Moist, well-watered.<BR>—4 Charming, graceful, elegant.<BR>—5 Full of feeling or sentiment, impassioned.<BR>—6 Full of affection, possessed of love.<BR>—7 Spirited, witty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवती
रसवत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 A kitchen.<BR>—2 A meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसवत्ता
रसवत्ता<BR>—1 Tastefulness.<BR>—2 Beauty, elegance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसा
रसा<BR>—1 The lower or infernal regions, hell.<BR>—2 The earth, ground, soil; यद् ग्रावेव रसातलं पुनरसौ यातो गजग्रामणीः<BR> Bv. 1. 59; रसादिपञ्चीकृतभूतसंभवम् A. Rām. 7. 5. 28; स्मरस्य<BR> युद्धरङ्गतां रसाऽऽर सारसारसा Nalod. 2. 10.<BR>—3 The tongue.<BR>—4 A vine or grapes.<BR>—5 Ved. Moisture.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रसौकस्, रसाखनः, रसातलम्, रसापायिन्, रसापुष्पः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसौकस्
रसा + -ओकस् <i>m.</i> an inhabitant of the lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाखनः|रसाखन
रसा + -खनः a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसातलम्
रसा + -तलम्<BR>—1 N. of one of the seven (अतल, वितल, सुतल, रसातल, तलातल,<BR> महातल and पाताल) regions below the earth; see पाताल.<BR>—2 the lower world or hell in general; राज्यं यातु रसातलं पुनरिदं<BR> न प्राणितुं कामये Bv. 2. 63; or जातिर्यातु रसातलम् Bh. 2. 39.<BR>—3 = रसा (2).<BR>—4 the fourth astrological mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसापायिन्
रसा + -पायिन् <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसापुष्पः
रसा + -पुष्पः a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालः|रसाल|रसालं
रसालः [रसमालाति आ-ला-क, ष˚ त˚]<BR>—1 The mango tree; भृङ्गा रसालकुसुमानि समाश्रयन्ते Bv. 1. 10.<BR>—2 The olibanum tree.<BR>—3 The bread-fruit tree.<BR>—4 Wheat.<BR>—5 The sugarcane.<BR>—6 A kind of mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाला
रसालः + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 The tongue.<BR>—2 Curds mixed with sugar and spices; रसालाकर्दमा नद्यो बभू वुर्भरतर्षभ<BR> Mb. 14. 89. 40.<BR>—3 Dūrvā grass.<BR>—4 A vine or grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालम्
रसालः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Gum-myrrh.<BR>—2 Frankincense.<BR>—3 A preparation of butter-milk (तक्रविशेष); ह्रदाः पूर्णाः रसालस्य<BR> दध्नः श्वेतस्य चापरे Rām. 2. 91. 73.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रसालवनी, रसालसालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालवनी
रसालः + -वनी <i>f.</i> a mango grove; रसालवन्या मधुपानुविद्धम् N. 3. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालसालः
रसालः + -सालः a mango tree; रसालसालः समदृश्यतामुना N. 1. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसालसा
रसालसा<BR>—1 A tubular vessel of the body.<BR>—2 A vein.<BR>—3 A nerve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसाली
रसाली Sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिक|रसिकः
रसिक <i>a.</i> [रसोऽस्त्यस्य ठन्]<BR>—1 Savoury, sapid, tasteful.<BR>—2 Graceful, elegant, beautiful.<BR>—3 Impassioned.<BR>—4 Apprehending flavour or excellence, possessed of taste, appreciative,<BR> discriminating; तद् वृत्तं प्रवदन्ति काव्यरसिकाः शार्दूलविक्रीडितम् Śrut. 40.<BR>—5 Finding pleasure or taking delight in, delighting in, devoted to (usually<BR> in comp.); इयं मालती भगवता सदृशसंयोगरसिकेन वेधसा मन्मथेन<BR> मया च तुभ्यं दीयते Māl. 6; so कामरसिकः Bh. 3. 112; परोपकाररसिकस्य Mk. 6. 19.<BR>—6 Humorous, witty.<BR>—7 Fanciful.<BR>—8 Lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिकः|रसिक
रसिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A man of taste or feeling, an appreciator of excellence or beauty;<BR> cf. अरसिक.<BR>—2 A libertine.<BR>—3 An elephant.<BR>—4 A horse.<BR>—5 The Sārasa bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिका
रसिक + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 The juice of sugar-cane, molasses.<BR>—2 The tongue.<BR>—3 A womanʼs girdle; see रसाला also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिकता
रसिकता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Taste, feeling.<BR>—2 Tastefulness.<BR>—3 Appreciative power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिकत्वम्
रसिकता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Taste, feeling.<BR>—2 Tastefulness.<BR>—3 Appreciative power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसित|रसितं
रसित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Tasted.<BR>—2 Having flavour or sentiment.<BR>—3 Gilded.<BR>—4 Sounded, making indistinct sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसितम्
रसित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Wine or liquor.<BR>—2 A cry, roar, roaring noise, sound or noise in general; हेरम्बकण्ठरसितप्रतिमानमेति Māl. 9. 3.<BR>—3 Thunder; जीमूतजालरसितानुकृतिर्निनादः Māl. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसिन्
रसिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Juicy, liquid.<BR>—2 Impassioned, full of feeling.<BR>—3 Tasteful, savoury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1332-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसोनः|रसोन
र(सु)सोनः A kind of garlic; cf. लसोन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रसुनः|रसुन
र(सु)सोनः A kind of garlic; cf. लसोन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्य|रस्यं
रस्य <i>a.</i> Juicy, savoury, sapid, palatable; रस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा<BR> हृद्या आहाराः सात्त्विकप्रियाः Bg. 17. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्यम्
रस्य + .{@-स्यम्@} Blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्नम्
रस्नम् A thing, object. ━<i>m.</i> [रसेः नित् कित् Uṇ. 3. 12] A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रस्ना
रस्नम् + .{@-स्ना@} A tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रह्
रह् €1 P., €10 U. (रहति, रहयति-ते, रहित) To quit, leave,<BR> abandon, forsake, desert; रहयत्यापदुपेतमायतिः Ki. 2. 14, 9. 16;<BR> रहयति नृपं स्वार्थपरता Mu. 3. 4; Māl. 9. 8; Mv. 1. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहणम्
रहणम् [रह्-ल्युट्] Desertion, quitting, separation; सहकारवृते<BR> समये सहका रहणस्य के न सस्मार पदम् Nalod. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्
रहस् <i>n.</i> [रह्-असुन् Uṇ. 4. 222]<BR>—1 Solitude, privacy, loneliness, retirement, secrecy; अथ राजा दशरथः<BR> कदाचिद्रहसि स्थितः A. Rām. 2. 2. 1; रहसि रमते Māl. 2. 2;<BR> R. 3. 3, 15. 92; Pt. 1. 138.<BR>—2 A deserted or lonely place, hiding-place.<BR>—3 A secret, mystery; कथ्यतां न रहो यदि Bhāg. 9. 9. 19.<BR>—4 Copulation, coition.<BR>—5 Truth.<BR>—6 Swiftness.<BR>—7 A privity. ━<i>ind.</i> Secretly, clandestinely, privately, in private<BR> or secret; अतः परीक्ष्य कर्तव्यं विशेषात्संगतं रहः Ś. 5. 24;<BR> oft. in comp.; वृत्तं रहःप्रणयमप्रतिपद्यमाने 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्य|रहस्यं
रहस्य <i>a.</i> [रहसि-भवः यत्]<BR>—1 Secret, private, clandestine; रहस्यं च प्रकाशं च यद् वृत्तं<BR> तस्य धीमतः (कथय) Rām. 1. 2. 33; रोमाणि च रहस्यानि सर्वाण्येव<BR> विवर्जयेत् Ms. 4. 144.<BR>—2 Mysterious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यम्
रहस्य + .{@-स्यम्@}<BR>—1 A secret (fig. also); स्वयं रहस्यभेदः कृतः V. 2.<BR>—2 A mystic spell or incantation, the mystery (of a missile); सरहस्यानि<BR> जृम्भकास्त्राणि U. 1.<BR>—3 The mystery or secret of conduct, mystery; रहस्यं साधूनामनुपधि<BR> विशुद्धं विजयते U. 2. 2; सरहस्यो धनुर्वेदः Bhāg. 1. 7. 44.<BR>—4 A secret or esoteric teaching, a mystic doctrine; भक्तोऽसि मे सखा<BR> चेति रहस्यं ह्येतदुत्तमम् Bg. 4. 3; साङ्गोपाङ्गोपनिषदः सरहस्यः<BR> प्रदीयताम् Rām. 1. 55. 16.<BR>—5 An Upaniṣad; चतुर्भ्यः सरहस्येभ्यो वेदेभ्यो ह्यधिकं यदा Mb. 1. 1. 272;<BR> Ms. 2. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यम्
रहस्य + .{@-स्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Secretly, privately; अनभिख्यातदोषस्तु रहस्यं<BR> व्रतमाचरेत् Y. 3. 300 (where it may be taken as an adj. also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रहस्याख्यायिन्, रहस्यत्रयम्, रहस्यभेदः, रहस्यविभेदः, रहस्यव्रतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्याख्यायिन्
रहस्य + -आख्यायिन् <i>a.</i> telling a secret; रहस्याख्यायीव स्वनसि मृदु<BR> कर्णान्तिकचरः Ś. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यत्रयम्
रहस्य + -त्रयम् the three categories of Rāmānuja school -ईश्वर, चित्<BR> and अचित् composing the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यभेदः|रहस्यभेद
रहस्य + -भेदः, -विभेदः disclosure of a secret or mystery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यविभेदः|रहस्यविभेद
रहस्य + -भेदः, -विभेदः disclosure of a secret or mystery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहस्यव्रतम्
रहस्य + -व्रतम्<BR>—1 a secret vow or penance.<BR>—2 the mystic science of obtaining command over magical weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहित|रहितं
रहित <i>p. p.</i> [रह्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Quitted, left, abandoned, deserted.<BR>—2 Separated from, free from, deprived or destitute of, without (with<BR> instr. or at the end of comp.); रहिते भिक्षुभिर्ग्रामे Y. 3. 59; गुणरहितः;<BR> सत्त्वरहितः &c.<BR>—3 Lonely, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहितम्
रहित + .{@-तम्@} Secrecy, privacy; नोपासितव्यौ रहिते कदाचित् Mb. 3. 234. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रहितासुर, रहितात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहितासुर
रहित + -असुर <i>a.</i> destitute of divinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहितात्मन्
रहित + -आत्मन् one without आत्मा (<i>i. e.</i> शून्यात्मा); शंसन्तु<BR> कृष्णपदवीं रहितात्मनां नः Bhāg. 10. 30. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहीभूत
रहीभूत <i>a.</i> In privacy with; दृष्ट्वा दयितया सार्धं रहीभूतं<BR> दशाननम् Bk. 8. 55 ‘retired’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रहाटः|रहाट
रहाटः<BR>—1 A minister.<BR>—2 A spring.<BR>—3 A ghost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रा
रा €2 P. (राति, रात) To give, grant, bestow; वयं ते अद्य<BR> ररिमा हि कामम् Rv. 3. 14. 5; स रातु वो दुश्च्यवनो भावुकानां परंपराम्<BR> K. P. 7; Bhāg. 8. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राका
राका [रा-क तस्य नेत्वम् Uṇ. 3. 40]<BR>—1 The full-moon day, particularly the night; दारिद्र्यं भजते कलानिधिरयं<BR> राकाधुना म्लायति Bv. 2. 72, 94, 165, 175, 3. 11; राकायामकलङ्कं<BR> चेदमृतांशोर्भवेद्वपुः K. P.<BR>—2 The goddess presiding over the full-moon day.<BR>—3 A girl in whom menstruation has just commenced.<BR>—4 Itch, scab.<BR>—5 N. of the mother of खर and शूर्पणखा.<BR>—6 N. of a river; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राकेशः, राकाचन्द्रः, राकापतिः, राकारमणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राकेशः|राकेश
राका + -ईशः<BR>—1 full moon; दृष्टं वनं कुमुदितं राकेशकररञ्जितम् Bhāg. 10. 29. 21.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राकाचन्द्रः|राकाचन्द्र
राका + -चन्द्रः, -पतिः, -रमणः full moon; राकापतिर्जेष्यति Bv. 2. 54;<BR> राकारमणस्य हन्त साम्राज्यम् 2. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राकापतिः|राकापति
राका + -चन्द्रः, -पतिः, -रमणः full moon; राकापतिर्जेष्यति Bv. 2. 54;<BR> राकारमणस्य हन्त साम्राज्यम् 2. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राकारमणः|राकारमण
राका + -चन्द्रः, -पतिः, -रमणः full moon; राकापतिर्जेष्यति Bv. 2. 54;<BR> राकारमणस्य हन्त साम्राज्यम् 2. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षस|राक्षसः
राक्षस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [रक्षस इदम् अण्] Belonging to or like an evil<BR> spirit, demoniacal, partaking of a demonʼs nature; मुनयो राक्षसीमाहुर्वाचमुन्मत्तदृप्तयोः<BR> U. 5. 30; ततस्तद्राक्षसं सैन्यम् Rām. 3. 22. 17; राक्षसीमासुरीं<BR> चैव प्रकृतिं मोहिनीं श्रिताः Bg. 9. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसः|राक्षस
राक्षस + .{@-सः@}<BR>—1 A demon, an evil spirit, a goblin, fiend, imp.<BR>—2 One of the eight forms of marriage in Hindu Law, in which a girl is<BR> forcibly seized and carried away after the defeat or destruction of her<BR> relatives in battle; हत्वा छित्त्वा च भित्त्वा च क्रोशन्तीं रुदतीं गृहात् ।<BR> प्रसह्य कन्याहरणं राक्षसो विधिरुच्यते ॥ Ms. 3. 33; राक्षसो<BR> युद्धहरणात् Y. 1. 61. (Kṛṣṇa carried away Rukmīṇī in this manner.)<BR>—3 One of the astronomical <i>Yogas</i>.<BR>—4 N. of a minister of Nanda, an important character in the Mudrārākṣasa.<BR>—5 A king of the Rākṣasas.<BR>—6 N. of the 30th Muhūrta.<BR>—7 N. of a संवत्सर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसी
राक्षस + .{@-सी@}<BR>—1 A female demon.<BR>—2 Laṅkā or Ceylon.<BR>—3 Night.<BR>—4 A larger tooth, tusk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राक्षसेन्द्रः, राक्षसग्रहः, राक्षसघ्नः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसेन्द्रः|राक्षसेन्द्र
राक्षस + -इन्द्रः N. of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसग्रहः|राक्षसग्रह
राक्षस + -ग्रहः N. of a particular insanity or seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षसघ्नः|राक्षसघ्न
राक्षस + -घ्नः N. of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राक्षा
राक्षा See लाक्षा; (perhaps an incorrect form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राख्
राख् €1 P. (राखति)<BR>—1 To be dry.<BR>—2 To adorn.<BR>—3 To prevent, ward off.<BR>—4 To be able. —5 To suffice, be competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राखडी
राखडी A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागः|राग
रागः [रञ्ज्-भावे घञ् नि˚ नलोपकुत्वे]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Colouring, dyeing, tinging.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Colour, hue, dye; वचस्तत्र प्रयोक्तव्यं यत्रोक्तं लभते<BR> फलम् । स्थायीभवति चात्यन्तं रागः शुक्लपटे यथा ॥ Pt. 1. 33.<BR>—2 Red colour, redness; अधरः किसलयरागः Ś. 1. 21; Śi. 8. 15; Ki. 16. 46.<BR>—3 Red dye, red lac; रागेण बालारुणकोमलेन चूतप्रवालोष्ठमलंचकार<BR> Ku. 3. 30, 5. 11.<BR>—4 Love, passion, affection, amorous or sexual feeling; मलिनेऽपि रागपूर्णाम्<BR> Bv. 1. 100 (where it means ‘redness’ also); Śi. 17. 2; अथ भवन्तमन्तरेण<BR> कीदृशोऽस्या दृष्टिरागः Ś. 2;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">Page1334-1</a>]<BR> see चक्षूराग also; चरणयुगलादिव हृदयमविशद्रगः K. 142.<BR>—5 Feeling, emotion, sympathy, interest.<BR>—6 Joy, pleasure.<BR>—7 Anger, wrath; निध्वनज्जवहारीभा भेजे रागरसात्तमः Śi. 19. 34.<BR>—8 Loveliness, beauty.<BR>—9 A musical mode or order of sound; (there are six primary <i>Rāgas</i>;<BR> भैरवः कौशिकश्चैव हिन्दोलो दीपकस्तथा । श्रीरागो मेघरागश्च रागाः<BR> षडिति कीर्तिताः Bharata; other writers give different names. Each <i>rāga</i><BR> has six <i>rāgiṇīs</i> regarded as its consorts, and their union gives<BR> rise to several musical modes).<BR>—10 Musical harmony, melody; तवास्मि गीतरागेण हारिणा प्रसभं हृतः<BR> Ś. 1. 5; अहो रागपरिवाहिणी गीतिः Ś. 5.<BR>—11 Regret, sorrow.<BR>—12 Greediness, envy; ‘रागस्तु मात्सर्ये लोहितादिषु’ Med.; राजकामस्य<BR> मूढस्य रागोपहतचेतसः Mb. 7. 85. 54.<BR>—13 The quality called Rajas q. v.<BR>—14 Nasalization.<BR>—15 A process in the preparation of quicksilver.<BR>—16 A king, prince.<BR>—17 The sun.<BR>—18 The moon.<BR>—19 Inflammation.<BR>—20 Seasoning, condiment; Mb. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रागाङ्गी, रागाढ्या, रागाशनिः, रागात्मक, रागायातम्, रागोद्रेकः, रागखाडव, रागखाण्डव, रागचूर्णः, रागच्छन्नः, रागद्रव्यम्, रागदा, रागदालिः, रागदृश्, रागपट्टः, रागपुष्पः, रागप्रसवः, रागबन्धः, रागयुज्, रागरज्जुः, रागलता, रागलेखा, रागवर्धनः, रागवृन्तः, रागषाडवः, रागसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1333-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागाङ्गी
रागः + -अङ्गी, -आढ्या Rubia Munjiṣṭa (Mar. मञ्जिष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागाढ्या
रागः + -अङ्गी, -आढ्या Rubia Munjiṣṭa (Mar. मञ्जिष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागाशनिः|रागाशनि
रागः + -अशनिः a Buddha or Jina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागात्मक
रागः + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> impassioned; रजो रागात्मकं विद्धि Bg. 14. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागायातम्
रागः + -आयातम्, -उद्रेकः excess of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागोद्रेकः|रागोद्रेक
रागः + -आयातम्, -उद्रेकः excess of passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागखाडव
रागः + -खाडव, -खाण्डव See रागषाडव; a kind of sweet rice preparation;<BR> रागखाण्डवभोज्यैश्च मत्ताः पतिषु शेरते Mb. 7. 61. 8 (com. रागखाण्डवं<BR> गुडोदनं पर्पटिकेति वैदर्भाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागखाण्डव
रागः + -खाडव, -खाण्डव See रागषाडव; a kind of sweet rice preparation;<BR> रागखाण्डवभोज्यैश्च मत्ताः पतिषु शेरते Mb. 7. 61. 8 (com. रागखाण्डवं<BR> गुडोदनं पर्पटिकेति वैदर्भाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागचूर्णः|रागचूर्ण
रागः + -चूर्णः Mb. 7. Acasia Catechu or Khadira tree.<BR>—2 red lead.<BR>—3 lac.<BR>—4 red powder thrown by people over one another at the festival called <i>holi</i>.<BR>—5 the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागच्छन्नः|रागच्छन्न|रागछन्न
रागः + -छन्नः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागद्रव्यम्
रागः + -द्रव्यम् a colouring substance, a paint, dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागदा
रागः + -दा crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागदालिः|रागदालि
रागः + -दालिः a kind of pulse (मसूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागदृश्
रागः + -दृश् a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागपट्टः|रागपट्ट
रागः + -पट्टः a kind of precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागपट्टी
रागः + -पट्टः + .({@-ट्टी@}) the chinese rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागपुष्पः|रागपुष्प
रागः + -पुष्पः, -प्रसवः the red globe-amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागप्रसवः|रागप्रसव
रागः + -पुष्पः, -प्रसवः the red globe-amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागबन्धः|रागबन्ध
रागः + -बन्धः manifestation of feeling, interest created by a proper<BR> representation (of various emotions); भावो भावं नुदति विषयाद्रागबन्धः<BR> स एव M. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागयुज्
रागः + -युज् <i>m.</i> a ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागरज्जुः|रागरज्जु
रागः + -रज्जुः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागलता
रागः + -लता N. of Rati, wife of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागलेखा
रागः + -लेखा a streak or mark of paint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवर्धनः|रागवर्धन
रागः + -वर्धनः (in music) a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवृन्तः|रागवृन्त
रागः + -वृन्तः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागषाडवः|रागषाडव
रागः + -षाडवः a kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागसूत्रम्
रागः + -सूत्रम्<BR>—1 any coloured thread.<BR>—2 a silk-thread.<BR>—3 the string of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागमय
रागमय, -रागवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Red, coloured.<BR>—2 Dear, beloved.<BR>—3 Impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागवत्|रागवन्त्
रागमय, -रागवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Red, coloured.<BR>—2 Dear, beloved.<BR>—3 Impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागा
रागा, -गी<BR> A sort of grain (Mar. नाचणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागी
रागा, -गी<BR> A sort of grain (Mar. नाचणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागारु|रागारुः
रागारु <i>a.</i> One who raises hopes of a gift, but does not fulfil them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिता
रागिता<BR>—1 The state of being coloured.<BR>—2 Being impassioned.<BR>—3 Fondness or desire for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिन्
रागिन् <i>a.</i> [राग-इनि]<BR>—1 Coloured, dyed.<BR>—2 Colouring, painting.<BR>—3 Red.<BR>—4 Full of passion or feeling, impassioned; रागिणापि विहिता तव भक्त्या Ki. 18. 27.<BR>—5 Full of love, subject to love.<BR>—6 Passionately fond of, devotedly attached to, desirous of, yearning<BR> after (at the end of comp.); रागी कर्मफलप्रेप्सुः Bg. 18. 27.<BR>—7 Delighting,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">Page1334-2</a>]<BR> rejoicing. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A painter.<BR>—2 A lover; एको रागिषु राजते प्रियतमादेहार्धहारी हरः Bh. 3. 121.<BR>—3 A libertine, sensualist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रागिणी
रागिन् + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 A modification of a musical mode (राग), of which 30 or 36 kinds<BR> are enumerated.<BR>—2 A wanton and intriguing woman, a lustful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ्
राघ् €1 Ā. To be able, to suffice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघ्
राघ् <i>m.</i> An able or efficient person; ननु हो मथना राघो घोरा<BR> नाथमहो नु न Ki. 15. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघवः|राघव
राघवः [रघोर्गोत्रापत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 A descendant of Raghu, especially Rāma.<BR>—2 A kind of large fish; क्रोडे क्रीडतु कस्य केलिकलहत्यक्तार्णवो राघवः Bv. 1. 55.<BR>—3 Sea, ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघवायणम्
राघवायणम् The Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राघवीयम्
राघवीयम् The poem composed by Rāghava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कलः|राङ्कल|रांकलः
राङ्कलः A thorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कव|रांकव|राङ्कवं
राङ्कव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [रङ्कोरयं विकारो वा तल्लोमजातत्वात् अण्] Belonging<BR> to the species of deer called <i>raṅku</i>, or made from its hair; woollen;<BR> ताः कस्तूरीपरिमलमुचः पट्टिका राङ्कवाणाम् Vikr. 18. 31; राङ्कवाणि<BR> तथौर्णानि Śiva B. 30. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कवम्
राङ्कव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 A woollen cloth made of deerʼs hair, a woollen garment; Mb. 12. 171. 20.<BR>—2 A blanket.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राङ्कवाजिनम्, राङ्कवास्तरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कवाजिनम्
राङ्कव + -अजिनम् <i>n.</i> woollen skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राङ्कवास्तरणम्
राङ्कव + -आस्तरणम् a woollen coverlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
राज् €1 U. (राजति-ते, राजित)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To shine, glitter, appear splendid or beautiful, be eminent;<BR> रेजे ग्रहमयीव सा Bh. 1. 17; तस्याः प्रविष्टा नतनाभिरन्ध्रं रराज<BR> तन्वी नवलोमराजिः Ku. 1. 38; राजन् राजति वीरवैरिवनितावैधव्यदस्ते<BR> भुजः K. P. 10; R. 3. 7; Ki. 4. 24, 11. 6.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To appear or look (like), shine (like); तोयान्तर्भास्करालीव<BR> रेजे मुनिपरंपरा Ku. 6. 49.<BR>—2 To rule, govern.<BR>—3 To direct, regulate.<BR>—4 To be the first or chief, be at the head. ━<i>Caus.</i> (राजयति-ते)<BR> To cause to shine, illuminate, brighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्
राज् <i>m.</i>, राजः<BR>—1 A king, chief, prince.<BR>—2 Anything best of its kind; सोऽम्बुजो हरिणाध्मातः सर्वप्राणेन शङ्खराट्<BR> Rām. 7. 7. 10; (adjective also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजः|राज
राज् <i>m.</i>, राजः<BR>—1 A king, chief, prince.<BR>—2 Anything best of its kind; सोऽम्बुजो हरिणाध्मातः सर्वप्राणेन शङ्खराट्<BR> Rām. 7. 7. 10; (adjective also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकः|राजक|राजकं
राजकः A little king, a petty prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकम्
राजकः + .{@-कम्@} A number of kings or princes, a collection of sovereigns;<BR> सहते न जनोऽप्यधःक्रियां किमु लोकाधिकधाम राजकम् Ki. 2. 47; राजकाय<BR> विषया विभेजिरे Śi. 14. 43; यत्पादौ मुकुटज्योत्स्नाजलैर्नेनेक्ति राजकम् Śabda C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकीय|राजकीयः
राजकीय <i>a.</i> Kingly, royal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत|राजतं
राजत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [रजत इदम् अण्] Silvery, made of silver; लीलां<BR> दधौ राजतगण्डशैलः Śi. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतम्
राजत + .{@-तम्@} Silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1334-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्
राजन् <i>m.</i> [राज्-कनिन् रञ्जयति रञ्ज्-कनिन् नि˚ वा Uṇ. 1. 145]<BR> A king, ruler, prince, chief (changed to राजः at the end of Tat. comp.);<BR> वङ्गराजः, महाराजः &c.; तथैव सोऽभूदन्वर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरञ्जनात्<BR> R. 4. 12; पित्रा न रञ्जितास्तस्य प्रजास्तेनानुरञ्जिताः । अनुरागात्ततस्तस्य<BR> नाम राजेत्यभाषत ॥ V. P.<BR>—2 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">Page1335-1</a>]<BR> man of the military caste; a Kṣatriya; Śi. 14. 14.<BR>—3 N. of Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR>—4 N. of Indra.<BR>—5 The moon; राजप्रियाः कैरविण्यो रमन्ते मधुपैःसह Bv. 1. 126.<BR>—6 Lord, master.<BR>—7 N. of Pṛthu.<BR>—8 A Yakṣa; तं राजराजानुचरोऽस्य साक्षात् Ki. 3. 30.<BR>—9 The Soma plant; ऐन्द्रश्च विधिवद्दत्तो राजा चाभिषुतोऽनधः Rām. 1. 14. 6;<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राजाग्निः, राजाङ्गनम्, राजादनः, राजाधिकारिन्, राजाधिकृतः, राजाधिराजः, राजेन्द्रः, राजाधिष्ठानम्, राजाध्वन्, राजानकः, राजान्नम्, राजापसदः, राजाभिषेकः, राजाम्लः, राजार्कः, राजार्हम्, राजार्हणम्, राजाहिः, राजाज्ञा, राजाभरणम्, राजाम्रः, राजावर्तः, राजावलिः, राजावली, राजासनम्, राजासन्दी, राजेन्दुः, राजेष्टः, राजोपकरणम्, राजोपसेवा, राजर्षिः, राजकन्या, राजकन्यका, राजकरः, राजकरणम्, राजकर्णः, राजकर्तृ, राजकर्मन्, राजकला, राजकलिः, राजकार्यम्, राजकृत्यम्, राजकुमारः, राजकुलम्, राजकोशनिघण्टुः, राजक्षवकः, राजगामिन्, राजगिरिः, राजगुरुः, राजगुह्यम्, राजगृहम्, राजग्रीवः, राजघ, राजचिह्नम्, राजचिह्नकम्, राजजक्ष्मन्, राजतरङ्गिणी, राजतरुः, राजतालः, राजताली, राजदण्डः, राजदन्तः, राजदूतः, राजदृशद्, राजदेयम्, राजभागम्, राजदौवारिकः, राजद्रोहः, राजद्रोहिन्, राजद्वार्, राजद्वारिकः, राजधर्मः, राजधानम्, राजधानकम्, राजधानिका, राजधानी, राजधान्यम्, राजधामन्, राजधुर्, राजनयः, राजनीतिः, राजनामन्, राजनारायणः, राजनिघण्टुः, राजनीलम्, राजपट्टः, राजपट्टिका, राजपदम्, राजपथः, राजपद्धतिः, राजपिण्डः, राजपिण्डा, राजपुंस्, राजपुत्रः, राजपुत्रिका, राजपुत्री, राजपुरम्, राजपुरुषः, राजपुष्पः, राजपूगः, राजपौरुषिकः, राजप्रकृतिः, राजप्रसादः, राजप्रेष्यः, राजफणिज्झकः, राजबदरम्, राजबीजिन्, राजवंश्य, राजभट्टिका, राजभृतः, राजभृत्यः, राजभोगः, राजभोग्यम