राजाग्निः|राजाग्नि
राजन् + -अग्निः wrath of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाङ्गनम्
राजन् + -अङ्गनम् a royal court, the court-yard of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजादनः|राजादन|राजादनं
राजन् + -अदनः<BR>—1 the Piyāla tree.<BR>—2 The seed of the tree Chirongia Sapida; राजादनं कन्दरालम् Śiva B. 30. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाधिकारिन्
राजन् + -अधिकारिन्, -अधिकृतः<BR>—1 a government officer or official.<BR>—2 a judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाधिकृतः|राजाधिकृत
राजन् + -अधिकारिन्, -अधिकृतः<BR>—1 a government officer or official.<BR>—2 a judge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाधिराजः|राजाधिराज
राजन् + -अधिराजः, -इन्द्रः a king of kings, a supreme king, paramount<BR> sovereign, an emperor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेन्द्रः|राजेन्द्र|राजेंद्र
राजन् + -अधिराजः, -इन्द्रः a king of kings, a supreme king, paramount<BR> sovereign, an emperor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाधिष्ठानम्
राजन् + -अधिष्ठानम् the capital of a king, metropolis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाध्वन्
राजन् + -अध्वन् <i>m.</i> a principal or royal road, main street, highway.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजानकः|राजानक
राजन् + -अनकः<BR>—1 an inferior king, a petty prince.<BR>—2 a title of respect formerly given to distinguished scholars and poets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजान्नम्
राजन् + -अन्नम्<BR>—1 rice grown in Āndhra.<BR>—2 food obtained from a king; राजान्नं तेज आदत्ते Ms. 4. 218.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजापसदः|राजापसद
राजन् + -अपसदः an unworthy or degraded king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाभिषेकः|राजाभिषेक
राजन् + -अभिषेकः coronation of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाम्लः|राजाम्ल
राजन् + -अम्लः a kind of vegetable plant: Rumex Vesicarius (Mar. चुका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्कः|राजार्क
राजन् + -अर्कः Calotropis Gigantea (मन्दार; Mar. रुई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्हम्
राजन् + -अर्हम्<BR>—1 aloe-wood, a species of sandal. —2 a kind of rice (राजान्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजार्हणम्
राजन् + -अर्हणम् a royal gift of honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाहिः|राजाहि
राजन् + -अहिः a large snake (having two mouths).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाज्ञा
राजन् + -आज्ञा a kingʼs edict, an ordinance, a royal decree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाभरणम्
राजन् + -आभरणम् a kingʼs ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजाम्रः|राजाम्र
राजन् + -आम्रः a superior kind of mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावर्तः|राजावर्त|राजावर्त्त|राजावर्त्तः
राजन् + -आवर्तः a diamond of an inferior quality.<BR>—2 a diamond from Virāṭa country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावलिः|राजावलि
राजन् + -आवलिः, -आवली a royal dynasty or genealogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजावली
राजन् + -आवलिः, -आवली a royal dynasty or genealogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजासनम्
राजन् + -आसनम् a throne.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजासन्दी
राजन् + -आसन्दी Ved. a stand on which the Soma is placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेन्दुः
राजन् + -इन्दुः an excellent king; दिलीप इति राजेन्दुरिन्दुः क्षीरनिधाविव R. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेष्टः|राजेष्ट
राजन् + -इष्टः a kind of onion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजेष्टम्
राजन् + -इष्टः + .({@-ष्टम्@}) = राजान्न q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजोपकरणम्
राजन् + -उपकरणम् (pl.) the paraphernalia of a king, the insignia of royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजोपसेवा
राजन् + -उपसेवा royal service; Ms. 3. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजर्षिः|राजर्षि
राजन् + -ऋषिः (राजॠषिः or राजर्षिः) a royal sage, a saint-like<BR> prince, a man of the Kṣatriya caste who, by his pious life and austere<BR> devotion, comes to be regarded as a sage or <i>ṛṣi</i>; <i>e. g.</i> पुरूरवस्,<BR> जनक, विश्वामित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकन्या
राजन् + -कन्या, -कन्यका a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकन्यका
राजन् + -कन्या, -कन्यका a princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकरः|राजकर
राजन् + -करः a tax or tribute paid to the king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकरणम्
राजन् + -करणम् a law-court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकर्णः|राजकर्ण
राजन् + -कर्णः an elephantʼs tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकर्तृ
राजन् + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> a person who assists at a coronation; समेत्य<BR> राजकर्तारः सभामीयुर्द्विजातयः Rām. 2. 67. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकर्मन्
राजन् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 the duty of a king.<BR>—2 royal service; cf. Ms. 7. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकला
राजन् + -कला a crescent of the moon (the 16th part of the moonʼs disc).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकलिः|राजकलि
राजन् + -कलिः a bad king; cf. अशरण्यः प्रजानां यः स राजा कलिरुच्यते<BR> Mb. 12. 12. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकार्यम्
राजन् + -कार्यम्, -कृत्यम्<BR>—1 state-affairs.<BR>—2 royal command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकृत्यम्
राजन् + -कार्यम्, -कृत्यम्<BR>—1 state-affairs.<BR>—2 royal command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुमारः|राजकुमार
राजन् + -कुमारः a prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकुलम्
राजन् + -कुलम्<BR>—1 a royal family, a kingʼs family; अग्निरापः स्त्रियो मूर्खः सर्पो राजकुलानि<BR> च H.; नदीनां शस्त्रपाणीनां नखिनां शृङ्गिणां तथा । विश्वासो नैव<BR> कर्तव्यः स्त्रीषु राजकुलेषु च ॥ <i>ibid.</i><BR>—2 the court of a king; आ दास्याः पुत्रि राजकुलं खल्वेतत् Nāg. 3. 12/13.<BR>—3 a court of justice; (राजकुले कथ्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">Page1335-2</a>]<BR> or निविद् <i>caus.</i> means ‘to sue one in a court of law, lodge a complaint against’<BR>).<BR>—4 a royal palace.<BR>—5 a king, master (as a respectful mode of speaking).<BR>—6 a royal servant; बध्नन्ति घ्नन्ति लुम्पन्ति दृप्तं राजकुलानि वै<BR> Bhāg. 10. 41. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजकोशनिघण्टुः|राजकोशनिघण्टु
राजन् + -कोशनिघण्टुः also<BR> {@-व्यवहारकोशः@} N. of a dictionary in Shivajiʼs time compiled<BR> by his minister Raghunātha Paṇḍita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजक्षवकः|राजक्षवक
राजन् + -क्षवकः a kind of mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगामिन्
राजन् + -गामिन्<BR>—1 <i>a.</i> escheating to the sovereign (as the property of a person having no heir).<BR>—2 brought before the king (as slander); Ms. 11. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगिरिः|राजगिरि
राजन् + -गिरिः N. of a mountain in Magadha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगुरुः|राजगुरु
राजन् + -गुरुः a royal counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगुह्यम्
राजन् + -गुह्यम् a royal mystery; राजविद्या राजगुह्यं पवित्रमिदमुत्तमम् Bg. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजगृहम्
राजन् + -गृहम्<BR>—1 a royal dwelling, royal palace.<BR>—2 N. of a chief city in Magadha (about 75 or 80 miles from Pāṭaliputra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजग्रीवः|राजग्रीव
राजन् + -ग्रीवः a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजघ|राजघः
राजन् + -घ <i>a.</i> sharp, hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजघः|राजघ
राजन् + -घ + .({@-घः@}) a king-killer, regicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजचिह्नम्
राजन् + -चिह्नम्<BR>—1 insignia of royalty, regalia.<BR>—2 the stamp on a coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजचिह्नकम्
राजन् + -चिह्नकम् the organ of generation (उपस्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजजक्ष्मन्
राजन् + -जक्ष्मन् = राजयक्ष्मन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतरङ्गिणी|राजतरंगिणी
राजन् + -तरङ्गिणी N. of a celebrated historical poem treating of the<BR> kings of Kāśmīra by Kalhaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतरुः|राजतरु
राजन् + -तरुः the कर्णिकार tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजतालः|राजताल
राजन् + -तालः, -ताली the betel-nut tree; राजतालीवनध्वनिः R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजताली
राजन् + -तालः, -ताली the betel-nut tree; राजतालीवनध्वनिः R.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदण्डः|राजदण्ड
राजन् + -दण्डः<BR>—1 a kingʼs sceptre.<BR>—2 royal authority.<BR>—3 punishment inflicted by a king.<BR>—4 fine payable to a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदन्तः|राजदन्त
राजन् + -दन्तः (for दन्तानां राजा) the front tooth; राजौ द्विजानामिह<BR> राजदन्ताः N. 7. 46; ‘राजन्ते सुतनोर्मनोरमतमास्ते राजदन्ताः पुरः’<BR> (शृङ्गारधनदशतकम् 67).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1335-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजदूतः|राजदूत
