राजन् + -मार्तण्डः, -मृगाङ्कः (in music) a kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमाषः|राजमाष
राजन् + -माषः a kind of bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमुद्रा
राजन् + -मुद्रा the royal seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयक्ष्मः|राजयक्ष्म
राजन् + -यक्ष्मः, -यक्ष्मन् <i>m.</i> ‘consumption of the moon’, pulmonary<BR> consumption, consumption in general; राजयक्ष्मपरिहानिराययौ कामयानसमवस्थया<BR> तुलाम् R. 19. 50; राजयक्ष्मेव रोगाणां समूहः स महीभृताम् Śi. 2. 96;<BR> (for explanation of the word see Malli. thereon, as well as on Śi. 13. 29).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयक्ष्मन्
राजन् + -यक्ष्मः, -यक्ष्मन् <i>m.</i> ‘consumption of the moon’, pulmonary<BR> consumption, consumption in general; राजयक्ष्मपरिहानिराययौ कामयानसमवस्थया<BR> तुलाम् R. 19. 50; राजयक्ष्मेव रोगाणां समूहः स महीभृताम् Śi. 2. 96;<BR> (for explanation of the word see Malli. thereon, as well as on Śi. 13. 29).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयानम्
राजन् + -यानम् a royal vehicle, a palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयुध्वन्
राजन् + -युध्वन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a kingʼs soldier.<BR>—2 one who fights with a king; P. III. 2. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजयोगः|राजयोग
राजन् + -योगः<BR>—1 a configuration of planets, asterisms &c. at the birth of a man which<BR> indicates that he is destined to be a king.<BR>—2 an easy mode of religious meditation (fit for kings to practise), as<BR> distinguished from the more rigorous one called हठयोग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजरङ्गम्
राजन् + -रङ्गम् silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराक्षसः|राजराक्षस
राजन् + -राक्षसः a bad king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराज्
राजन् + -राज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a supreme king.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराजः|राजराज
राजन् + -राजः<BR>—1 a supreme king, sovereign lord, an emperor.<BR>—2 N. of Kubera; अन्तर्बाष्पश्चिरमनुचरो राजराजस्य दध्यौ Me. 3.<BR>—3 the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजराज्यम्
राजन् + -राज्यम् the state or dignity of Kubera; स्वर्लोके राजराज्येन<BR> सोऽभिषिच्येत भार्गव Mb. 13. 85. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजरीतिः|राजरीति
राजन् + -रीतिः <i>f.</i> bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्षणम्
राजन् + -लक्षणम् —1 any mark on a manʼs body indicating future royalty.<BR> royal insignia, regalia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्ष्मन्
राजन् + -लक्ष्मन् <i>n.</i> royal insignia. ━(<i>m.</i>) N. of Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलक्ष्मीः
राजन् + -लक्ष्मीः, -श्रीः <i>f.</i> the fortune or prosperity of a king (personified<BR> as a goddess), the glory or majesty of a king; स न्यस्तचिह्नामपि राजलक्ष्मीम् R. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजश्रीः
राजन् + -लक्ष्मीः, -श्रीः <i>f.</i> the fortune or prosperity of a king (personified<BR> as a goddess), the glory or majesty of a king; स न्यस्तचिह्नामपि राजलक्ष्मीम् R. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलिङ्गम्
राजन् + -लिङ्गम् a kingly mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलेखः|राजलेख
राजन् + -लेखः a royal edict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजलोकः|राजलोक
राजन् + -लोकः a collection of princes or kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवंशः|राजवंश
राजन् + -वंशः a dynasty of kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवंशावली
राजन् + -वंशावली genealogy of kings, royal pedigree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवर्चसम्
राजन् + -वर्चसम् kingly rank or dignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवर्तः|राजवर्त
राजन् + -वर्तः cloth of various colours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवल्लभः|राजवल्लभ
राजन् + -वल्लभः<BR>—1 a kingʼs favourite.<BR>—2 a kind of mango.<BR>—3 a kind of Jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवसतिः|राजवसति
राजन् + -वसतिः<BR>—1 dwelling in a kingʼs court. —2 a royal palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाहः|राजवाह
राजन् + -वाहः a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवाह्यः|राजवाह्य
राजन् + -वाह्यः a royal elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजविः|राजवि
राजन् + -विः the blue-jay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजविजयः|राजविजय
राजन् + -विजयः (in music) a kind of Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजविद्या
राजन् + -विद्या ‘royal policy’, king-craft, state-policy, statesmanship;<BR> Bg. 9. 2; (cf. राजनय);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">Page1336-2</a>]<BR> so राजशास्त्रम्; वीराश्च नियतोत्साहा राजशास्त्रमनुष्ठिताः Rām. 1. 7. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजविहारः|राजविहार
राजन् + -विहारः a royal convent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवृक्षः|राजवृक्ष
राजन् + -वृक्षः the tree Cassia Fistula; गुच्छैः कृतच्छविरराजत राजवृक्षः<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवृत्तम्
राजन् + -वृत्तम् the conduct or occupation of a king; (कच्चित्) प्रजाः<BR> पालयसे राजन् राजवृत्तेन धार्मिक Rām. 1. 52. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजवृत्तिः|राजवृत्ति
राजन् + -वृत्तिः the works of a king; प्रत्यक्षाप्रत्यक्षानुमेया हि राजवृत्तिः Kau. A. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशफरः|राजशफर
राजन् + -शफरः a Hilsā fish; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशासनम्
राजन् + -शासनम् a royal edict; दिवा चरेयुः कार्यार्थं चिह्निता राजशासनैः Ms. 10. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशृङ्गम्
राजन् + -शृङ्गम् a royal umbrella with a golden handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशेखरः|राजशेखर
राजन् + -शेखरः N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसंसद्
राजन् + -संसद् <i>f.</i>, {@-सभा@} <i>f.</i><BR> a court of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसदनम्
राजन् + -सदनम् a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्पः|राजसर्प
राजन् + -सर्पः a kind of snake-devouring snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसर्षपः|राजसर्षप
राजन् + -सर्षपः black mustard (the seed used as a weight; त्रसरेणवोऽष्टौ<BR> विज्ञेया लिक्षैका परिमाणतः । ता राजसर्षपस्तिस्रस्ते त्रयो गौरसर्षपः ॥<BR> Ms. 8. 133).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसायुज्यम्
राजन् + -सायुज्यम् sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसारसः|राजसारस
राजन् + -सारसः a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूयः|राजसूय
राजन् + -सूयः, -सूयम् —1 a great sacrifice performed by a universal monarch<BR> (in which the tributary princes also took part) at the time of his coronation<BR> as a mark of his undisputed sovereignty; राजा वै राजसूयेनेष्ट्वा भवति<BR> Śat. Br.; cf. सम्राट् also; राजा तत्र सूयते तस्माद् राजसूयः ।<BR> राज्ञो वा यज्ञो राजसूयः ŚB. on MS. 4. 4. 1.<BR>—2 a lotus.<BR>—3 a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसूयम्
राजन् + -सूयः, -सूयम् —1 a great sacrifice performed by a universal monarch<BR> (in which the tributary princes also took part) at the time of his coronation<BR> as a mark of his undisputed sovereignty; राजा वै राजसूयेनेष्ट्वा भवति<BR> Śat. Br.; cf. सम्राट् also; राजा तत्र सूयते तस्माद् राजसूयः ।<BR> राज्ञो वा यज्ञो राजसूयः ŚB. on MS. 4. 4. 1.<BR>—2 a lotus.<BR>—3 a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसौधः|राजसौध
राजन् + -सौधः a kingʼs palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्कन्धः|राजस्कन्ध
राजन् + -स्कन्धः a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्थानाधिकारः|राजस्थानाधिकार
राजन् + -स्थानाधिकारः Viceroyalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्थानीयः|राजस्थानीय
राजन् + -स्थानीयः a viceroy, governor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्वम्
राजन् + -स्वम्<BR>—1 royal property; राजस्वं श्रोत्रियस्वं च न भोगेन प्रणश्यति Ms. 8. 149.<BR>—2 tribute, revenue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्वर्णः|राजस्वर्ण
राजन् + -स्वर्णः a kind of thorn-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस्वामिन्
राजन् + -स्वामिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहंसः|राजहंस
राजन् + -हंसः a flamingo (a sort of white goose with red legs and bill);<BR> संपत्स्यन्ते नभसि भवतो राजहंसाः सहायाः Me. 11; कूजितं राजहंसानां<BR> नेदं नूपुरशिञ्जितम् V.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहत्या
राजन् + -हत्या regicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहस्तिन्
राजन् + -हस्तिन् <i>m.</i> a royal elephant, <i>i. e.</i> a lordly and handsome elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजहासकः|राजहासक
राजन् + -हासकः a kind of fish; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजता
राजता, -त्वम्<BR> Royalty, sovereignty, royal rank or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजत्वम्
राजता, -त्वम्<BR> Royalty, sovereignty, royal rank or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजनम्
राजनम् A particular Sāma; एतद् राजनं देवतासु प्रोतम्<BR> Ch. Up. 2. 20. 1; Bhāg. 11. 27. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्य|राजन्यः
राजन्य <i>a.</i> [राजन्-यत् नलोपः] Royal, kingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यः|राजन्य
राजन्य + .{@-न्यः@}<BR>—1 A man of the Kṣatriya caste, royal personage; राजन्यान् स्वपुरनिवृत्तयेऽनुमेने<BR> R. 4. 87; संप्रति करणीयो राजन्येऽपि प्रश्रयः U. 6; R. 3. 48; Me. 50.<BR>—2 N. of Agni.<BR>—3 A noble or distinguished personage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्या
राजन्य + .{@-न्या@} A lady of royal rank.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राजन्यबन्धुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यबन्धुः|राजन्यबन्धु
राजन्य + -बन्धुः Kṣatriya; राजन्यबन्धोर्द्वाविंशे (केशान्तः विधीयते) Ms. 2. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्यकम्
राजन्यकम् A collection of warriors or Kṣatriyas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजन्वत्|राजन्वन्त्
राजन्वत् <i>a.</i> Governed by a just or good king (as a country, as<BR> distinguished from राजवत् which simply means ‘having a ruler’); (सुराज्ञि<BR> देशे राजन्वान् स्यात् ततोऽन्यत्र राजवान् Ak.); राजन्वतीमाहुरनेन भूमिम्<BR> R. 6. 22; Kāv. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजमान
राजमान <i>a.</i> Shining, radiant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजायते
राजायते Den. Ā. To act like a king, consider oneself a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1336-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजसात्
राजसात् <i>ind.</i> To the state or in the possession of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजित
राजित <i>a.</i> Illuminated, brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्ञी
राज्ञी<BR>—1 A queen, the wife of a king.<BR>—2 Yellowish-red brass.<BR>—3 N. of the wife of the sun. —4 N. of the western quarter; राज्ञी नाम<BR> प्रतीची Ch. Up. 3. 15. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यम्
राज्यम् [राज्ञो भावः कर्म वा, राजन्-यत् नलोपः]<BR>—1 Royalty, sovereignty, royal authority; राज्येन किं तद् विपरीतवृत्तेः<BR> R. 2. 53, 4. 1.<BR>—2 A kingdom, country, an empire; R. 1. 58.<BR>—3 Rule, reign, government, administration of a kingdom.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राज्याङ्गम्, राज्याधिकारः, राज्याधिदेवता, राज्यापहरणम्, राज्याभिषेकः, राज्याश्रममुनिः, राज्योपकरणम्, राज्यकरः, राज्यकर्तृ, राज्यखण्डम्, राज्यच्युत, राज्यतन्त्रम्, राज्यद्रव्यम्, राज्यधुरा, राज्यभारः, राज्यपरिक्रिया, राज्यभाज्, राज्यभङ्गः, राज्यभोगः, राज्यभ्रंशः, राज्यलक्ष्मीः, राज्यश्रीः, राज्यलोभः, राज्यविभूतिः, राज्यव्यवहारः, राज्यसुखम्, राज्यस्थितिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याङ्गम्
राज्यम् + -अङ्गम् a constituent member of the state, a requisite of regal<BR> administration; (these are usually said to be seven:− स्वाम्यमात्यसुहृत्कोषराष्ट्रदुर्गबलानि च Ak.)<BR>—2 a stronghold.<BR>—3 an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याधिकारः|राज्याधिकार
राज्यम् + -अधिकारः<BR>—1 authority over a kingdom.<BR>—2 a right to sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याधिदेवता
राज्यम् + -अधिदेवता the tutelary deity of a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यापहरणम्
राज्यम् + -अपहरणम् usurpation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याभिषेकः|राज्याभिषेक
राज्यम् + -अभिषेकः inauguration or coronation of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्याश्रममुनिः|राज्याश्रममुनि
राज्यम् + -आश्रममुनिः a pious king, the sage living in the hermitage in<BR> the form of the kingdom; पप्रच्छ कुशलं राज्ये राज्याश्रममुनिं मुनिः R. 1. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्योपकरणम्
राज्यम् + -उपकरणम् (pl.) the paraphernalia of government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यकरः|राज्यकर
राज्यम् + -करः the tribute paid by a tributary prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यकर्तृ
राज्यम् + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an administrator or officer of government.<BR>—2 a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यखण्डम्
राज्यम् + -खण्डम् a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यच्युत
राज्यम् + -च्युत <i>a.</i> deposed or dethroned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यतन्त्रम्
राज्यम् + -तन्त्रम् the science of government, system of administration,<BR> the government or administration of a kingdom; Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यद्रव्यम्
राज्यम् + -द्रव्यम् a requisite of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यधुरा
राज्यम् + -धुरा, -भारः the yoke or burden of government, the responsibility<BR> or administration of government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभारः|राज्यभार
राज्यम् + -धुरा, -भारः the yoke or burden of government, the responsibility<BR> or administration of government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यपरिक्रिया
राज्यम् + -परिक्रिया administration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभाज्
राज्यम् + -भाज् a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभङ्गः|राज्यभङ्ग|राज्यभंग
राज्यम् + -भङ्गः subversion of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभोगः|राज्यभोग
राज्यम् + -भोगः the possession of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यभ्रंशः|राज्यभ्रंश
राज्यम् + -भ्रंशः deposition from kingdom, loss of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यलक्ष्मीः
राज्यम् + -लक्ष्मीः, -श्रीः the glory of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यश्रीः
राज्यम् + -लक्ष्मीः, -श्रीः the glory of sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यलोभः|राज्यलोभ
राज्यम् + -लोभः greed of dominion, desire of territorial aggrandizement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यविभूतिः|राज्यविभूति
राज्यम् + -विभूतिः power of royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यव्यवहारः|राज्यव्यवहार
राज्यम् + -व्यवहारः administration, government business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यसुखम्
राज्यम् + -सुखम् the sweets of royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राज्यस्थितिः|राज्यस्थिति
राज्यम् + -स्थितिः government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजस|राजसः
राजस <i>a.</i> (-सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [रजसा निर्मितम् अण्] Relating to or influenced<BR> by the quality <i>rajas</i>, endowed with the quality <i>rajas</i> or<BR> passion; ऊर्ध्वं गच्छन्ति सत्त्वस्था मध्ये तिष्ठन्ति राजसाः Bg. 14. 18, 7. 12, 17. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिः|राजि
राजिः, -जी <i>f.</i><BR> [राज्-इन् वा ङीप् Uṇ. 4. 136]<BR>—1 A streak, line, row, range; सर्वं पण्डितराजराजितिलकेनाकारि लोकोत्तरम्<BR> Bv. 4. 44; दानराजिः R. 2. 7; राजीवराजीवशलोलभृङ्गम् Śi. 4. 9; Ki. 5. 4.<BR>—2 Black mustard.<BR>—3 The soft palate, uvula.<BR>—4 A striped snake.<BR>—5 A field.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राजिफला, राजिफली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजी
राजिः, -जी <i>f.</i><BR> [राज्-इन् वा ङीप् Uṇ. 4. 136]<BR>—1 A streak, line, row, range; सर्वं पण्डितराजराजितिलकेनाकारि लोकोत्तरम्<BR> Bv. 4. 44; दानराजिः R. 2. 7; राजीवराजीवशलोलभृङ्गम् Śi. 4. 9; Ki. 5. 4.<BR>—2 Black mustard.<BR>—3 The soft palate, uvula.<BR>—4 A striped snake.<BR>—5 A field.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राजिफला, राजिफली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिफला
राजिः + राजिफला, राजिफली<BR> a kind of cucumber (Mar. टरकाकडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिफली
राजिः + राजिफला, राजिफली<BR> a kind of cucumber (Mar. टरकाकडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीफलः|राजीफल
राजीफलः Trichosanthes Dioeca (Mar. पडवळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिका
राजिका<BR>—1 A line, row, range.<BR>—2 A field.<BR>—3 Black mustard; न राजिकाराद्धमभोजि तत्र N. 16. 73.<BR>—4 Mustard (used as a weight).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजिलः|राजिल
राजिलः [राज्-इलच्]<BR>—1 A species of innocent and poisonless snakes; किं महोरगविसर्पिविक्रमो<BR> राजिलेषु गरुडः प्रवर्तते R. 11. 27; cf. डुण्डुभ.<BR>—2 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीवः|राजीव|राजीवं
राजीवः [राजी दलराजी अस्त्यस्य व]<BR>—1 A kind of deer.<BR>—2 A crane.<BR>—3 An elephant.<BR>—4 A species of fish; Ms. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीवम्
राजीवः + .{@-वम्@} A blue lotus, Nymphea lotus; प्रफुल्लराजीवमिवाङ्कमध्ये Ku. 3. 45.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राजीवाक्ष, राजीवनेत्र, राजीवलोचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीवाक्ष
राजीवः + -अक्ष, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> lotus-eyed; ऊनषोडशवर्षो मे रामो<BR> राजीवलोचनः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीवनेत्र
राजीवः + -अक्ष, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> lotus-eyed; ऊनषोडशवर्षो मे रामो<BR> राजीवलोचनः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीवलोचन
राजीवः + -अक्ष, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> lotus-eyed; ऊनषोडशवर्षो मे रामो<BR> राजीवलोचनः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजीविनी
राजीविनी<BR>—1 The lotus plant.<BR>—2 A group of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राटिः|राटि
राटिः A bird. ━<i>f.</i> War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राडिः|राडि
राडिः A kind of bird; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राढा
राढा<BR>—1 Lustre.<BR>—2 N. of a district in Bengal, as also of its capital; गौडं राष्ट्रमनुत्तमं<BR> निरुपमा तत्रापि राढापुरी Prab. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणम्
राणम्<BR>—1 A leaf.<BR>—2 A peacockʼs tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणायनीयः|राणायनीय
राणायनीयः N. of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणायनीयाः
राणायनीयः + .{@-याः@} The school of राणायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राणिका
राणिका A bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राण्डीरः|राण्डीर
राण्डीरः = रण्डापुत्रः; Hc. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात
रात <i>a.</i> Given, bestowed; रातो वोऽनुग्रहार्थाय विष्णुना प्रभविष्णुना<BR> Bhāg. 1. 12. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रातन्ती|रातंती
रातन्ती A festival on the fourteenth day of the second half of Pauṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राति|रातिः
राति <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Liberal, favourable, generous.<BR>—2 Ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रातिः|राति
राति + .{@-तिः@} A friend (opp. to अरातिः). ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Giving, bestowing, presentation.<BR>—2 Wealth; विज्ञानमानन्दं ब्रह्म रातिर्दातुः परायणम् Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28;<BR> Bhāg. 5. 5. 3.<BR>—3 A favour.<BR>—4 A gift, present.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रातिसाच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रातिसाच्
राति + -साच् <i>a.</i> (-षाच्)<BR> bestowing gifts, liberal, bountiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिः|रात्रि
रात्रिः, -त्री <i>f.</i><BR> [राति सुखं भयं वा रा-त्रिप् वा ङी प् Uṇ. 4. 69]<BR>—1 Night; रात्रिर्गता मतिमतां वर मुञ्च शय्याम् R. 5. 66; दिवा<BR> काकरवाद् भीता रात्रौ तरति नर्मदाम्.<BR>—2 The darkness of night.<BR>—3 Turmeric; Mb. 13. 136. 25.<BR>—4 One of the four forms or bodies of Brahmā.<BR>—5 Day and night; अहःशब्दोऽपि अहोरात्रवचनः । रात्रिशब्दोऽपि Ś. B. on MS. 8. 1. 16<BR> यां रात्रिं जायते जीवो यां रात्रिं च विनश्यति Mb. 13. 9. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रात्र्यटः, रात्र्यन्ध,^1 रात्र्यागमः, रात्र्युपायः, रात्रिकरः, रात्रिचरः, रात्रिचर्या, रात्रिजम्, रात्रिजलम्, रात्रिजागरः, रात्रितरा, रात्रितिथिः, रात्रिद्विष्, रात्रिनाथः, रात्रिनाशनः, रात्रिपर्युषित, रात्रिपुष्पम्, रात्रिबलः, रात्रिभुजङ्गः, रात्रिमणिः, रात्रियोगः, रात्रिरक्षः, रात्रिरक्षकः, रात्रिरागः, रात्रिवासस्, रात्रिविगमः, रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन्, रात्रिवेदः, रात्रिवेदिन्, रात्रिसत्रन्यायः, रात्रिहासः, रात्रिहिण्डकः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्री
रात्रिः, -त्री <i>f.</i><BR> [राति सुखं भयं वा रा-त्रिप् वा ङी प् Uṇ. 4. 69]<BR>—1 Night; रात्रिर्गता मतिमतां वर मुञ्च शय्याम् R. 5. 66; दिवा<BR> काकरवाद् भीता रात्रौ तरति नर्मदाम्.<BR>—2 The darkness of night.<BR>—3 Turmeric; Mb. 13. 136. 25.<BR>—4 One of the four forms or bodies of Brahmā.<BR>—5 Day and night; अहःशब्दोऽपि अहोरात्रवचनः । रात्रिशब्दोऽपि Ś. B. on MS. 8. 1. 16<BR> यां रात्रिं जायते जीवो यां रात्रिं च विनश्यति Mb. 13. 9. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रात्र्यटः, रात्र्यन्ध,^1 रात्र्यागमः, रात्र्युपायः, रात्रिकरः, रात्रिचरः, रात्रिचर्या, रात्रिजम्, रात्रिजलम्, रात्रिजागरः, रात्रितरा, रात्रितिथिः, रात्रिद्विष्, रात्रिनाथः, रात्रिनाशनः, रात्रिपर्युषित, रात्रिपुष्पम्, रात्रिबलः, रात्रिभुजङ्गः, रात्रिमणिः, रात्रियोगः, रात्रिरक्षः, रात्रिरक्षकः, रात्रिरागः, रात्रिवासस्, रात्रिविगमः, रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन्, रात्रिवेदः, रात्रिवेदिन्, रात्रिसत्रन्यायः, रात्रिहासः, रात्रिहिण्डकः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्यटः|रात्र्यट
रात्रिः + -अटः<BR>—1 a goblin, demon, ghost.<BR>—2 a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्यन्ध|रात्र्यंध|रात्र्यन्धः
रात्रिः + -अन्ध^1 <i>a.</i> night-blind.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्यागमः|रात्र्यागम
रात्रिः + -आगमः, -उपायः the approach of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्युपायः|रात्र्युपाय
रात्रिः + -आगमः, -उपायः the approach of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिकरः|रात्रिकर
रात्रिः + -करः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिचरः|रात्रिचर
रात्रिः + -चरः (also {@रात्रिंचर@})<BR>.(-री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 ‘a night-rover’, robber, thief.<BR>—2 a watchman, patrol, guard.<BR>—3 a demon, ghost, evil spirit; (तं) यान्तं वने रात्रिचरी डुढौके Bk. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिचर्या
रात्रिः + -चर्या<BR>—1 night-roving.<BR>—2 a nightly act or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजम्
रात्रिः + -जम् a star, constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजलम्
रात्रिः + -जलम् dew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिजागरः|रात्रिजागर
रात्रिः + -जागरः<BR>—1 night-watching, wakefulness or sitting up at night; आरुरोह कुमुदाकरोपमां<BR> रात्रिजागरपरो दिवाशयः R. 19. 34.<BR>—2 a dog. ˚दः a gnat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रितरा
रात्रिः + -तरा the dead of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रितिथिः|रात्रितिथि
रात्रिः + -तिथिः <i>f.</i> a lunar night.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">Page1338-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1337-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिद्विष्
रात्रिः + -द्विष् the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिनाथः|रात्रिनाथ
रात्रिः + -नाथः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिनाशनः|रात्रिनाशन
रात्रिः + -नाशनः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिपर्युषित
रात्रिः + -पर्युषित <i>a.</i> stale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिपुष्पम्
रात्रिः + -पुष्पम् a lotus-flower opening at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिबलः|रात्रिबल
रात्रिः + -बलः a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिभुजङ्गः|रात्रिभुजङ्ग
रात्रिः + -भुजङ्गः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिमणिः|रात्रिमणि
रात्रिः + -मणिः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रियोगः|रात्रियोग
रात्रिः + -योगः night-fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिरक्षः
रात्रिः + -रक्षः, -रक्षकः a watchman, guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिरक्षकः|रात्रिरक्षक
रात्रिः + -रक्षः, -रक्षकः a watchman, guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिरागः|रात्रिराग
रात्रिः + -रागः darkness, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवासस्
रात्रिः + -वासस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 night-dress.<BR>—2 darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिविगमः|रात्रिविगम
रात्रिः + -विगमः ‘end of night’, break of day, dawn, day-light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिविश्लेषगामिन्
रात्रिः + -विश्लेषगामिन् <i>m.</i> the ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवेदः|रात्रिवेद
रात्रिः + -वेदः, -वेदिन् <i>m.</i> a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिवेदिन्
रात्रिः + -वेदः, -वेदिन् <i>m.</i> a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिसत्रन्यायः
रात्रिः + -सत्रन्यायः the rule according to which an act, for which no<BR> fruit is stated directly in the injunctive text, should be held as yielding<BR> the result spoken of in the अर्थवाद text connected with it. This<BR> rule is discussed and established by Jaimini and Śabara in MS. 4. 3. 17-19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहासः|रात्रिहास
रात्रिः + -हासः the white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिहिण्डकः|रात्रिहिण्डक
रात्रिः + -हिण्डकः<BR>—1 a guard of the womenʼs apartments.<BR>—2 a night-stalker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रक|रात्रकं|रात्रकः
रात्रक <i>a.</i> Nocturnal, nightly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रकः|रात्रक|रात्रकं
रात्रक + .{@-कः@} A man who takes up his abode in a harlotʼs house for one year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रकम्
रात्रक + .{@-कम्@} A period of five nights taken collectively (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिक
रात्रिक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Lasting or sufficient for a<BR> certain number of nights, as पञ्चरात्रिक उत्सवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिका
रात्रिक + .{@-का@} Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिंदिवम्
रात्रिंदिवम्, -रात्रिंदिवा <i>ind.</i><BR> By night and day, constantly, ceaselessly;<BR> रात्रिंदिवं गन्धवहः प्रयाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिंदिवा
रात्रिंदिवम्, -रात्रिंदिवा <i>ind.</i><BR> By night and day, constantly, ceaselessly;<BR> रात्रिंदिवं गन्धवहः प्रयाति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिमटः|रात्रिमट
रात्रिमटः A night-rover; a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रिंमन्य|रात्रिम्मन्य
रात्रिंमन्य <i>a.</i> Looking like night (as a cloudy or dark day);<BR> cf. रजनिंमन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रीण
रात्रीण <i>a.</i> Lasting for a certain number of nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रौ
रात्रौ, -रात्र्याम् <i>ind.</i><BR> At night, by night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्र्याम्
रात्रौ, -रात्र्याम् <i>ind.</i><BR> At night, by night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रात्रौशयनम्
रात्रौ शयनम् A festival on the 11th day of the first half<BR> of आषाढ, regarded as the night of the gods, beginning with the summer solstice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राध्
राध् I. €5 P. (राध्नोति, राद्ध; <i>desid.</i> रिरात्सति, but<BR> रित्सति to ‘wish to kill’)<BR>—1 To propitiate, conciliate, please.<BR>—2 To accomplish, effect, complete, perform, achieve.<BR>—3 To prepare, make ready.<BR>—4 To fall to the lot of any one (also €4 P.).<BR>—5 To injure, destroy, kill, exterminate; वानरा भूधरान् रेधुः Bk. 14. 19.<BR>━II. €4 P. (राध्यति, राद्ध)<BR>—1 To be favourable or merciful.<BR>—2 To be accomplished or finished.<BR>—3 To propitiate, look to the welfare of (any one, with dat.); कृष्णाय<BR> राध्यति गर्गः Sk. (<i>i. e.</i> पृष्टो गर्गः शुभाशुभं पर्यालोचयति).<BR>—4 To be successful, to succeed, prosper.<BR>—5 To be ready.<BR>—6 To kill, destroy. ━<i>Caus.</i> (राधयति-ते)<BR>—1 To propitiate.<BR>—2 To accomplish, complete.<BR>—3 To make ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्ध|राद्धं
राद्ध <i>p. p.</i> [राध्-कर्तरि कर्मणि वा क्त]<BR>—1 Propitiated, pleased, conciliated.<BR>—2 Effected, accomplished, achieved, performed; राद्धं निःश्रेयसं पुंसाम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 9. 41.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">Page1338-2</a>]<BR>—3 Dressed, cooked (as food).<BR>—4 Prepared; equipped; स यो मनुष्याणां राद्धः समृद्धो भवति Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 33.<BR>—5 Obtained, got.<BR>—6 Successful, fortunate, happy.<BR>—7 Perfect in magical power.<BR>—8 Fallen to the lot of.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राद्धान्तः, राद्धान्तित, राद्धान्नम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धान्तः|राद्धान्त|राद्धांत
राद्ध + -अन्तः a proved or established fact, a demonstrated conclusion<BR> or truth, an ultimate conclusion, doctrine; dogma; सर्ववैनाशिकराद्धान्तो<BR> नितरामनपेक्षितव्य इतीदानीमुपपादयामः Ś. B.; समस्ततन्त्रराद्धान्ते<BR> भवान् भागवततत्त्ववित् Bhāg. 12. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धान्तित|राद्धांतित
राद्ध + -अन्तित <i>a.</i> demonstrated, established by proof, logically proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धान्नम्
राद्ध + -अन्नम् dressed food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राद्धिः|राद्धि
राद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Accomplishment, perfection.<BR>—2 Success, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधः|राध
राधः The month called Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधः|राध
राधः + .{@-धः, -धम्@}<BR>—1 Favour, kindness.<BR>—2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधम्
राधः + .{@-धः, -धम्@}<BR>—1 Favour, kindness.<BR>—2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधी
राधः + .{@-धी@} The day of full moon in the month of Vaiśākha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राधरङ्कः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधरङ्कः|राधरङ्क
राधः + -रङ्कः<BR>—1 a plough.<BR>—2 thin rain.<BR>—3 hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधनम्
राधनम् [राध्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Propitiating, conciliating.<BR>—2 Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>—3 Accomplishing, effecting, completion.<BR>—4 Acquisition, going.<BR>—5 The means of accomplishing anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधना
राधनम् + .{@-ना@} Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधनी
राधनम् + .{@-नी@} Worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधस्
राधस् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Food.<BR>—2 Kindness, favour.<BR>—3 A gift, present.<BR>—4 Liberality.<BR>—5 Wealth, riches.<BR>—6 Accomplishment of oneʼs wishes, success; तस्मा अप्यनुभावेन स्वेनैवावाप्तराधसे<BR> Bhāg. 4. 7. 57.<BR>—7 Desire; ईश्वरालम्बनं चित्तं कुर्वतोऽनन्यराधसः Bhāg. 9. 21. 17.<BR>—8 Power, sovereignty; निरस्तसाम्यातिशयेन राधसा Bhāg. 2. 4. 14.<BR>—9 Device, proper application; बुद्ध्या वा किं निपुणया बलेनेन्द्रियराधसा<BR> Bhāg. 4. 31. 11.<BR>—10 Maintaining, keeping (पालनम्); आत्मारामोऽपि यस्त्वस्य लोककल्पस्य<BR> राधसे Bhāg. 4. 24. 18.<BR>—10 The sensual pleasure; कृष्णे कमलपत्राक्षे संन्यस्ताखिलराधसः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 65. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधा
राधा<BR>—1 Prosperity, success.<BR>—2 N. of a celebrated Gopī or cowherdess loved by Kṛṣṇa (whose amours<BR> have been immortalized by Jayadeva in his Gītagovinda); तदिमं राधे<BR> गृहं प्रापय Gīt. 1.<BR>—3 N. of the wife of Adhiratha and foster-mother of Karṇa.<BR>—4 The lunar mansion called विशाखा.<BR>—5 Lightning.<BR>—6 An attitude in shooting.<BR>—7 Emblic Myrobalan.<BR>—8 The full-moon day in the month of Vaiśākha.<BR>—9 Devotedness.<BR>—10 N. of a plant (Clytoria Ternatea; Mar. विष्णुक्रान्ता).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राधाकान्तः, राधापतिः, राधारमणः, राधाभेदिन्, राधावेधिन्, राधासुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधाकान्तः|राधाकान्त
राधा + -कान्तः, -पतिः, -रमणः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधापतिः
राधा + -कान्तः, -पतिः, -रमणः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधारमणः|राधारमण
राधा + -कान्तः, -पतिः, -रमणः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधाभेदिन्
राधा + -भेदिन्, -वेधिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधावेधिन्
राधा + -भेदिन्, -वेधिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधासुतः|राधासुत
राधा + -सुतः N. of Karṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधिका
राधिका See राधा above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राधेयः|राधेय
राधेयः An epithet of Karṇa; पुत्रस्य मे सुहृत् प्रेयान् राधेयः<BR> सोऽप्ययं हतः Ve. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राभस्यम्
राभस्यम्<BR>—1 Delight, joy.<BR>—2 Impetuosity.<BR>—3 Violence, force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम|रामं|रामः
राम <i>a.</i> [रम् कर्तरि घञ् ण वा]<BR>—1 Pleasing, delighting, rejoicing.<BR>—2 Beautiful, lovely, charming.<BR>—3 Obscure;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-1" target="_blank">Page1339-1</a>]<BR> dark-coloured, black. —4 White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामः|राम|रामं
राम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 N. of three celebrated personages;<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Paraśurāma, son of Jamadagni;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Balarāma, son of Vasudeva and brother of Kṛṣṇa, qq. vv.;<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Rāmachandra or Sītārāma, son of Daśaratha and Kausalyā<BR> and the hero of the Rāmāyaṇa; (the word is thus derived in Purāṇas:−<BR> राशब्दो विश्ववचनो मश्चापीश्वरवाचकः । विश्वाधीनेश्वरो यो हि तेन<BR> रामः प्रकीर्तितः ॥) cf. also राकारोच्चारमात्रेण मुखान्निर्याति पातकम् ।<BR> पुनः प्रवेशशङ्कायां मकारोऽस्ति कपाटवत् ॥ [When quite a boy, he<BR> with his brother was taken by Viśvāmitra, with the permission of Daśaratha,<BR> to his hermitage to protect his sacrifices from the demons that obstructed<BR> them. Rāma killed them all with perfect ease, and received from the sage<BR> several miraculous missiles as a reward. He then accompanied Viśvāmitra<BR> to the capital of Janaka where he married Sītā having performed the<BR> wonderful feat of bending Śivaʼs bow, and then returned to Ayodhyā. Daśaratha,<BR> seeing that Rāma was growing fitter and fitter to rule the kingdom, resolved<BR> to install him as heir-apparent. But, on the eve of the day of coronation,<BR> his favourite wife Kaikeyī, at the instigation of her wicked nurse Mantharā,<BR> asked him to fulfil the two boons he had formerly promised to her, by<BR> one of which she demanded the exile of Rāma for fourteen years and by<BR> the other the installation of her own son Bharata as Yuvarāja. The king<BR> was terribly shocked, and tried his best to dissuade her from her wicked<BR> demands, but was at last obliged to yield. The dutiful son immediately<BR> prepared to go into exile accompanied by his beautiful young wife Sītā<BR> and his devoted brother Lakṣmaṇa. The period of his exile was eventful,<BR> and the two brothers killed several powerful demons and at last roused<BR> the jealousy of Rāvaṇa himself. The wicked demon resolved to try Rāma<BR> by carrying off his beauteous wife for whom he had conceived an ardent<BR> passion, and accomplished his purpose being assisted by Mārīcha. After<BR> several fruitless inquiries as to her whereabouts, Hanumat ascertained<BR> that she was in Laṅkā and persuaded Rāma to invade the island and kill<BR> the ravisher. The monkeys built a bridge across the ocean over which Rāma<BR> with his numerous troops passed, conquered Laṅkā, and killed Rāvaṇa<BR> along with his whole host of demons. Rāma, attended by his wife and friends<BR> in battle, triumphantly returned to Ayodhyā where he was crowned king<BR> by Vasiṣṭha. He reigned long and righteously and was succeeded by his<BR> son Kuśa. Rāma is said to be the seventh incarnation of Viṣṇu; cf.<BR> Jayadeva:− वितरसि दिक्षु रणे दिक्पतिकमनीयं दशमुखमौलिवलिं रमणीयम् ।<BR> केशव धृतरघुपतिरूप जय जगदीश हरे Gīt.].<BR>—2 A kind of deer.<BR>—3 N. of Aruṇa.<BR>—4 A lover; cf. Śi. 4. 59.<BR>—5 A horse.<BR>—6 Pleasure, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामम्
राम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Darkness.<BR>—2 Leprosy (कुष्ठम्).<BR>—3 A tamāla leaf.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रामानुजः, रामायणम्, रामेश्वरः, रामकाण्डः, रामकिल्बिषम्, रामकृत्, रामक्री, रामगिरिः, रामचन्द्रः, रामभद्रः, रामजन्मन्, रामतापन, रामतापनी, रामतापनीय, रामदूतः, रामनवमी, रामपूगः, रामलीला, रामवल्लभः, रामशरः, रामसखः, रामसेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1338-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामानुजः|रामानुज
राम + -अनुजः N. of a celebrated<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">Page1339-2</a>]<BR> reformer, founder of a Vedāntic sect and author of several works. He<BR> was a Vaiṣṇava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामायणम्
राम + -अयनम् + .({@-णम्@})<BR>—1 the adventures of Rāma.<BR>—2 N. of a celebrated epic by Vālmīki which contains about 24000 verses<BR> in seven Kāṇḍas or books.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामेश्वरः|रामेश्वर
राम + -ईश्वरः N. of a sacred place of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकाण्डः|रामकाण्ड
राम + -काण्डः a species of cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकिल्बिषम्
राम + -किल्बिषम् an offence against Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकृत्
राम + -कृत् (in music) N. of a Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामक्री
राम + -क्री N. of a Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामगिरिः|रामगिरि
राम + -गिरिः N. of a mountain; (चक्रे) स्निग्धच्छायातरुषु वसतिं<BR> रामगिर्या श्रमेषु Me. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामचन्द्रः|रामचन्द्र|रामचंद्र
राम + -चन्द्रः, -भद्रः N. of Rāma, son of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामभद्रः|रामभद्र
राम + -चन्द्रः, -भद्रः N. of Rāma, son of Daśaratha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामजन्मन्
राम + -जन्मन् <i>n.</i> the birth or birth-day of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामतापन
राम + -तापन, -तापनी, -तापनीय {@उपनिषद्@} N. of a well-known उपनिषद्<BR> (belonging to the अथर्ववेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामतापनी
राम + -तापन, -तापनी, -तापनीय {@उपनिषद्@} N. of a well-known उपनिषद्<BR> (belonging to the अथर्ववेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामतापनीय
राम + -तापन, -तापनी, -तापनीय {@उपनिषद्@} N. of a well-known उपनिषद्<BR> (belonging to the अथर्ववेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामदूतः|रामदूत
राम + -दूतः<BR>—1 N. of Hanumat.<BR>—2 a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामदूती
राम + -दूतः + .({@-ती@}) a kind of basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामनवमी
राम + -नवमी the ninth day in the bright half of Chaitra, the anniversary<BR> of the birth of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामपूगः|रामपूग
राम + -पूगः a kind of betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामलीला
राम + -लीला N. of a dramatic performance, on the story of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामवल्लभः|रामवल्लभ|रामवल्लभं
राम + -वल्लभः the birchtree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामवल्लभम्
राम + -वल्लभः + .({@-भम्@}) cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामशरः|रामशर
राम + -शरः a kind of sugar cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसखः|रामसख
राम + -सखः N. of Sugrīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामसेतुः|रामसेतु
राम + -सेतुः ‘the bridge of Rāma’, a bridge of sand between the Indian<BR> peninsula and Ceylon, now called Adamʼs bridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामक|रामकः
रामक <i>a.</i> Delighting, gratifying, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामकः|रामक
रामक + .{@-कः@} a particular form of a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामठः|रामठ|रामठं
रामठः, -ठम्<BR> Asa Foetida (हिङ्गु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामठम्
रामठः, -ठम्<BR> Asa Foetida (हिङ्गु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणीयक|रामणीयकं
रामणीयक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Lovely, beautiful, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामणीयकम्
रामणीयक + .{@-कम्@} Loveliness, beauty; सर्वत्र दयिताधीनं सुव्यक्तं रामणीयकम्<BR> Bk. 6. 75; सा रामणीयकनिधेरधिदेवता वा Māl. 1. 21, 9. 47; तरुणीस्तन<BR> एव शोभते मणिहारावलिरामणीयकम् N. 2. 44; Ki. 1. 39, 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामण्यकम्
रामण्यकम् Loveliness, beauty; वनरामण्यकं यत्र जलरामण्यकं<BR> तथा Rām. 3. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामा
रामा [रमतेऽनया रम् करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 A beautiful woman, a charming young woman; अथ रामा विकसन्मुखी बभूव<BR> Bv. 2. 16, 3. 6.<BR>—2 A beloved, wife, mistress; रामो रामावबोधितः R. 12. 23; पप्रच्छ<BR> रामां रमणोऽभिलाषम् 14. 27.<BR>—3 A woman in general; रामा हरन्ति हृदयं प्रसभं नराणाम् Ṛs. 6. 25.<BR>—4 A woman of origin.<BR>—5 Vermilion.<BR>—6 Aśa Foetida.<BR>—7 A kind of pigment (गोरोचना).<BR>—8 Ruddle.<BR>—9 A river.<BR>—10 An accomplished woman (versed in fine arts).<BR>—11 A kind of metre.<BR>—12 (In music) A kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रामिलः|रामिल
रामिलः<BR>—1 A lover; husband.<BR>—2 The god of love.<BR>—3 N. of a poet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राम्भः|राम्भ|रांभ|रांभः
राम्भः A bamboo-staff carried by a religious student or ascetic;<BR> यतिहस्तस्थितैस्तस्य राम्भैरारम्भि तर्जना N. 17. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायः|राय
रायः A king, prince (often at the beginning or end of proper names;<BR> it is a corruption of राजन्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रायरङ्गालम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायरङ्गालम्
रायः + -रङ्गालम् a kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायणम्
रायणम्<BR>—1 Sounding, making noise.<BR>—2 Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1339-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रायभाटी
रायभाटी The stream of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रालः|राल
रालः The resin of the Sāla tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रालकार्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रालकार्यः|रालकार्य|रालकार्य्य|रालकार्य्यः
रालः + -कार्यः the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावः|राव
रावः [रु-घञ्]<BR>—1 A cry, scream, shriek, roar, the cry of any animal.<BR>—2 Sound in general; मुरजवाद्यरावः; मधुरिपुरावम् Gīt. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावण|रावणः
रावण <i>a.</i> [रु-णिच् ल्यु] Crying, screaming, roaring, bewailing;<BR> इत्युक्त्वा परुषं वाक्यं रावणः शत्रुरावणः Rām. 3. 56. 26 (com.<BR> शत्रून् रावयति क्रोशयति शत्ररावणः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणः|रावण
रावण + .{@-णः@} N. of a celebrated demon, king of Laṅkā and the chief of<BR> the Rākṣhasas; स रावणो नाम निकामभीषणं बभूव रक्षः क्षतरक्षणं<BR> दिवः Śi. 1. 48. [He was the son of Viśravas by Keśinī or Kaikaśī<BR> and so half-brother of Kuber. He is called <i>Paulastya</i> as being<BR> a grandson of the sage Pulastya. Laṅkā was originally occupied by Kubera,<BR> but Rāvaṇa ousted him from it and made it his own capital. He had ten<BR> heads (and hence his names Daśagrīva, Daśavadana &c.) and twenty arms,<BR> and according to some, four legs (cf. R. 12. 88 and Malli.). He is represented<BR> to have practised the most austere penance for ten thousand years in order<BR> to propitiate the god Brahman, and to have offered one head at the end<BR> of each one thousand years. Thus he offered nine of his heads and was<BR> going to offer the tenth when the God was pleased and granted him immunity<BR> from death by either god or man. On the strength of this boon he grew<BR> very tyrannical and oppressed all beings. His power became so great that<BR> even the gods are said to have acted as his domestic servants. He conquered<BR> almost all the kings of the day, but is said to have been imprisoned by<BR> Kārtavīrya for some time when he went to attack his territory. On one<BR> occasion he tried to uplift the Kailāsa mountain, but Śiva pressed it<BR> down so as to crush his fingers under it. He, therefore, hymned Śiva<BR> for one thousand years so loudly that the God gave him the name <i>Rāvaṇa</i><BR> and freed him from his painful position. But though he was so powerful<BR> and invincible, the day of retribution drew near. While Rāma −who was<BR> Viṣṇu descended on earth for the destruction of this very demon− was<BR> passing his years of exile in the forest, Rāvaṇa carried off his wife<BR> Sītā and urged her to become his wife but she persistently refused and<BR> remained loyal to her husband. At last Rāma assisted by his monkey-troops<BR> invaded Laṅkā, annihilated Rāvaṇaʼs troops and killed the demon himself.<BR> He was a worthy opponent of Rāma, and hence the expression:− रामरावणयोर्युद्धं<BR> रामरावणयोरिव ।].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणम्
रावण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The act of screaming.<BR>—2 N. of a Muhūrta.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रावणारिः, रावणगङ्गा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणारिः|रावणारि
रावण + -अरिः N. of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणगङ्गा
रावण + -गङ्गा N. of a river in Laṅkā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावणिः|रावणि
रावणिः [रावणस्यापत्यम् इञ्]<BR>—1 N. of Indrajit; रावणिश्चाव्यथो योद्धुमारब्ध च महीं गतः Bk. 15. 78, 89.<BR>—2 Any son of Rāvaṇa; प्रादुद्रुवंस्ततः क्रुद्धाः सर्वे रावणयोऽङ्गदम्<BR> Bk. 15. 79-80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रावितम्
रावितम् Sound, noise; स्यन्दनेभ्यश्च्युता वीराः शङ्खरावितदुर्बलाः<BR> Rām. 7. 7. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिः|राशि
राशिः <i>m., f.</i> [अश्नुते व्याप्नोति, अश्-इञ् धातोरुडागमश्च; cf. Uṇ. 4. 132]<BR>—1 A heap, mass, collection, quantity, multitude; मृदुनि मृगशरीरे<BR> तूलराशाविवाग्निः Ś. 1; धनराशिः, तोयराशिः, यशोराशिः &c.<BR>—2 The numbers or figures put down for any arithmetical operation (such<BR> as adding, multiplying &c.)<BR>—3 A sign of the zodiac.<BR>—4 Mathematics; Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2.<BR>—5 One-twelfth part of the ecliptic.<BR>—6 An astrological house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राश्यधिपः, राशिगत, राशिचक्रम्, राशित्रयम्, राशिनामन्, राशिपः, राशिभागः, राशिभेदः, राशिभोगः, राशिमण्डलम्, राशिवर्धन, राशिव्यवहारः, राशिस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राश्यधिपः|राश्यधिप
राशिः + -अधिपः the regent of an astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिगत
राशिः + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 heaped, piled up.<BR>—2 summed up.<BR>—3 algebraical or arithmetical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिचक्रम्
राशिः + -चक्रम् the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशित्रयम्
राशिः + -त्रयम् the rule of three.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिनामन्
राशिः + -नामन् <i>n.</i> a name given to a child taken from the Rāśi under<BR> which he is born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिपः|राशिप
राशिः + -पः the regent of an astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभागः|राशिभाग
राशिः + -भागः a fraction. ˚अनुबन्धः the addition of fractions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभेदः|राशिभेद
राशिः + -भेदः a division of a zodiacal sign or astrological house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिभोगः|राशिभोग
राशिः + -भोगः the passage of the sun, moon, or any planet through a sign of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिमण्डलम्
राशिः + -मण्डलम् (= -चक्रम् above).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिवर्धन
राशिः + -वर्धन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 adding to the number (संख्यापूरक).<BR>—2 (fig.) useless; राशिवर्धनमात्रं स नैव स्त्री न पुनः पुमान् Mb. 5. 133. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिव्यवहारः|राशिव्यवहार
राशिः + -व्यवहारः (in Arith.) the method for finding the quantity contained in a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशिस्थ
राशिः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकृ
राशीकृ €8 U. To pile up, heap together, accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीकृत
राशीकृत, -भूत<BR> Heaped together, accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राशीभूत
राशीकृत, -भूत<BR> Heaped together, accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रम्
राष्ट्रम् [राज् ष्ट्रन् Uṇ. 4. 167]<BR>—1 A kingdom, realm, empire; राष्ट्रदुर्गबलानि च Ak.; सामदण्डौ<BR> प्रशंसन्ति नित्यं राष्ट्राभिवृद्धये Ms. 7. 109, 10. 61.<BR>—2 A district, territory, country, region; as in महाराष्ट्रः नगराणि<BR> च राष्ट्राणि धनधान्ययुतानि च Rām. 1. 1. 93; स्वराष्ट्रे न्यायवृत्तः<BR> स्यात् Ms. 7. 32.<BR>—3 The people, nation, subjects; तस्य प्रक्षुभ्यते राष्ट्रम् Ms. 9. 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रः|राष्ट्र|राष्ट्रं
राष्ट्रम् + .{@-ष्ट्रः, -ष्ट्रम्@} Any national or public calamity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राष्ट्राभिवृद्धिः, राष्ट्रकर्षणम्, राष्ट्रतन्त्रम्, राष्ट्रपतिः, राष्ट्रपालः, राष्ट्रभेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रम्
राष्ट्रम् + .{@-ष्ट्रः, -ष्ट्रम्@} Any national or public calamity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राष्ट्राभिवृद्धिः, राष्ट्रकर्षणम्, राष्ट्रतन्त्रम्, राष्ट्रपतिः, राष्ट्रपालः, राष्ट्रभेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्राभिवृद्धिः|राष्ट्राभिवृद्धि
राष्ट्रम् + -अभिवृद्धिः increase of a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रकर्षणम्
राष्ट्रम् + -कर्षणम् distressing a kingdom; तथा राज्ञामपि प्राणाः क्षीयन्ते<BR> राष्ट्रकर्षणात् Ms. 7. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रतन्त्रम्
राष्ट्रम् + -तन्त्रम् administration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रपतिः|राष्ट्रपति
राष्ट्रम् + -पतिः, -पालः a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रपालः|राष्ट्रपाल
राष्ट्रम् + -पतिः, -पालः a sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रभेदः|राष्ट्रभेद
राष्ट्रम् + -भेदः division of a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रकः|राष्ट्रक
राष्ट्रकः = राष्ट्रिकः q. v.; निरीक्ष्य तावुत्तमपूरुषौ जना<BR> मञ्चस्थिता नागरराष्ट्रका नृप Bhāg. 10. 43. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिः|राष्ट्रि
राष्ट्रिः <i>f.</i>, -ष्ट्री<BR>—1 A female ruler.<BR>—2 Proprietress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्री
राष्ट्रिः <i>f.</i>, -ष्ट्री<BR>—1 A female ruler.<BR>—2 Proprietress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिकः|राष्ट्रिक
राष्ट्रिकः<BR>—1 An inhabitant of a kingdom or country, a subject; राष्ट्रिकैः सह<BR> तद्राष्ट्रं क्षिप्रमेव विनश्यति Ms. 10. 61.<BR>—2 The ruler of a kingdom, governor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रिय|राष्ट्रियः
राष्ट्रिय, -राष्ट्रीय <i>a.</i><BR> [राष्ट्रे भवः घ] Belonging to a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रीय|राष्ट्रीयः
राष्ट्रिय, -राष्ट्रीय <i>a.</i><BR> [राष्ट्रे भवः घ] Belonging to a kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राष्ट्रियः|राष्ट्रिय
राष्ट्रिय, -राष्ट्रीय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 The ruler of a kingdom, king; as in राष्ट्रियश्यालः Mk. 9.<BR>—2 The brother-in-law of a king (queenʼs brother); श्रुतं राष्ट्रियमुखाद्<BR> यावदङ्गुलीयकदर्शनम् Ś. 6.<BR>—3 An heir-apparent.<BR>—4 An officer in the kingdom; ततः संप्रेषयेद् राष्ट्रे राष्ट्रीयाय च<BR> दर्शयेत् Mb. 12. 85. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1340-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्
रास् €1 Ā. (रासते) To cry, scream, yell, sound, howl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासः|रास
रासः<BR>—1 An uproar, a din, confused noise.<BR>—2 A sound in general.<BR>—3 Speech.<BR>—4 A kind of dance practised by Kṛṣṇa and the cowherds but particularly<BR> the <i>gopis</i> or cowherdesses of Vṛndāvana; तत्रारभत गोविन्दो<BR> रासक्रीडामनुव्रतैः । स्त्रीरत्नैरन्वितः प्रीतैरन्योन्याबद्धबाहुभिः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 10. 33. 2; उत्सृज्य रासे रसं गच्छन्तीम् Ve. 1. 2; रासे हरिमिह<BR> विहितविलासं स्मरति मनो मम कृतपरिहासम् Gīt. 2; also Gīt. 1.<BR>—5 A chain.<BR>—6 A sport, play.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: रासेश्वरी, रासोत्सवः, रासक्रीडा, रासमण्डलम्, रासगोष्ठी, रासयात्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेश्वरी
रासः + -ईश्वरी N. of Rādhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासोत्सवः
रासः + -उत्सवः, -क्रीडा, -मण्डलम् a sportive dance, the circular dance<BR> of Kṛṣṇa and the cowherdesses of Vrindāvana; रासोत्सवः संप्रवृत्तो<BR> गोपीमण्डलमण्डितः Bhāg. 10. 33. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासक्रीडा
रासः + -उत्सवः, -क्रीडा, -मण्डलम् a sportive dance, the circular dance<BR> of Kṛṣṇa and the cowherdesses of Vrindāvana; रासोत्सवः संप्रवृत्तो<BR> गोपीमण्डलमण्डितः Bhāg. 10. 33. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासमण्डलम्
रासः + -उत्सवः, -क्रीडा, -मण्डलम् a sportive dance, the circular dance<BR> of Kṛṣṇa and the cowherdesses of Vrindāvana; रासोत्सवः संप्रवृत्तो<BR> गोपीमण्डलमण्डितः Bhāg. 10. 33. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासगोष्ठी
रासः + -गोष्ठी = रासक्रीडा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासयात्रा
रासः + -यात्रा <i>f.</i> a festival in honour of Kṛṣṇa on the Kārtikī Paurṇimā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासकम्
रासकम् A kind of minor drama; see S. D. 548.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेरसः|रासेरस
रासेरसः, रासेवासः<BR>—1 The Rāsa dance.<BR>—2 Pastime, sport.<BR>—3 A company, party, assembly.<BR>—4 The love sentiment (शृङ्गार).<BR>—5 The sixth night after delivery (षष्ठीजागर).<BR>—6 Jesting, joking.<BR>—7 Skill in alchemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासेवासः|रासेवास
रासेरसः, रासेवासः<BR>—1 The Rāsa dance.<BR>—2 Pastime, sport.<BR>—3 A company, party, assembly.<BR>—4 The love sentiment (शृङ्गार).<BR>—5 The sixth night after delivery (षष्ठीजागर).<BR>—6 Jesting, joking.<BR>—7 Skill in alchemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासन
रासन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the tongue.<BR>—2 Savoury, palatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासभः|रासभ
रासभः [रासेः अभच् Uṇ. 3. 124] An ass, a donkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासायन
रासायन, रासायनिक Relating to रसायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रासायनिक
रासायन, रासायनिक Relating to रसायन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रास्ना
रास्ना [Uṇ. 3. 15]<BR>—1 N. of a plant; नाकुली सुरसा रास्ना … … Bhāva P.<BR>—2 A rope.<BR>—3 Ved. A girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहडी
राहडी (In music) A kind of composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहित्यम्
राहित्यम् Being without any thing, destitution; destituteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुः|राहु
राहुः [रह्-उण् Uṇ. 1. 3]<BR>—1 N. of a demon, son of Viprachitti and Siṃhikā and hence often called<BR> <i>Saimhikeya</i>; ग्रसते हि तमोपहं मुहुर्ननु राह्वाह्वमहर्पतिं<BR> तमः Śi. 16. 57; विधुरपि विधियोगाद् ग्रस्यते राहुणासौ H. [When<BR> the nectar, that was churned out of the ocean, was being served to the<BR> gods, Rāhu disguised himself and attempted to drink it along with them.<BR> But he was detected by the sun and the moon who informed Viṣṇu of the<BR> fraud. Viṣṇu, thereupon, severed his head from the body; but as he had<BR> tasted a little quantity of nectar the head became immortal, and is supposed<BR> to wreak its vengeance on the sun and moon at the time of conjunction<BR> and opposition; cf. Bh. 2. 34. In astronomy Rāhu is regarded, like Ketu,<BR> as one of the nine planets, or only as the ascending node of the moon.]<BR>—2 An eclipse, or rather the moment of occultation.<BR>—3 Abandoning.<BR>—4 One who abandons.<BR>—5 The regent of the south-west quarter.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: राहूच्छिष्टम्, राहूत्सृष्टम्, राहुगत,^1 राहुग्रसनम्, राहुग्रासः, राहुदर्शनम्, राहुपीडा, राहुसंस्पर्शः, राहुच्छत्रम्, राहुपीडा, राहुभेदिन्, राहुरत्नम्, राहुशत्रुः, राहुसूतकम्, राहुहन्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूच्छिष्टम्
राहुः + -उच्छिष्टम्, -उत्सृष्टम् = लशुन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहूत्सृष्टम्
राहुः + -उच्छिष्टम्, -उत्सृष्टम् = लशुन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राहुगत
राहुः + -गत^1 <i>a.</i> darkened, eclipsed; also राहुग्रस्त.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1341-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

