लीला + -अगारः, -आगारः, -आगारम्, -गृहम्, -वेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a pleasure-house;<BR> लीलागारेष्वरमत पुनर्नन्दनाभ्यन्तरेषु R. 8. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाङ्ग|लीलांग
लीला + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> having graceful limbs; वयोपपन्नं लीलाङ्गं सर्वरत्नसमन्वितम्<BR> Mb. 13. 79. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाञ्चित
लीला + -अञ्चित <i>a.</i> sportively handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लीलाब्जम्
लीला + -अब्जम्, -अम्बुजम्, -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -तामरसम्, -पद्मम् &c.<BR> ‘toy-lotus’, a lotus-flower held in the hand as a play-thing; लीलारविन्दं<BR> भ्रमयाञ्चकार R. 6. 13; हस्ते लीलाकमलमलके बालकुन्दानुविद्धम्<BR> Me. 67; Ku. 6. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1368-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

