लोकाधिपः|लोकाधिप
लोकः + -अधिपः<BR>—1 a king.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">Page1372-2</a>]<BR>—2 a god or deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाधिपतिः|लोकाधिपति
लोकः + -अधिपतिः a lord of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकानुग्रहः|लोकानुग्रह
लोकः + -अनुग्रहः prosperity of mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकानुरागः|लोकानुराग
लोकः + -अनुरागः ‘love of mankind’, universal love, general benevolence, philanthropy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकानुवृत्तम्
लोकः + -अनुवृत्तम् obedience of the people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तरम्
लोकः + -अन्तरम् ‘another world’, the next world, future life; लोकान्तरसुखं<BR> पुण्यं तपोदानसमुद्भवम् R. 1. 69, 6. 45; लोकान्तरं गम्-प्राप् &c. ‘to die’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकान्तरित
लोकः + -अन्तरित <i>a.</i> dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकापवादः|लोकापवाद
लोकः + -अपवादः public scandal, popular censure; लोकापवादो बलवान्<BR> मतो मे R. 14. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाभिभाविन्
लोकः + -अभिभाविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 overcoming the world.<BR>—2 pervading the whole world (as light).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाभिलक्षित
लोकः + -अभिलक्षित <i>a.</i> generally liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाभ्युदयः|लोकाभ्युदय
लोकः + -अभ्युदयः public weal or welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायनः|लोकायन
लोकः + -अयनः N. of Nārāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकालोकः|लोकालोक
लोकः + -अलोकः N. of a mythical mountain that encircles the earth and<BR> is situated beyond the sea of fresh water which surrounds the last of<BR> the seven continents; beyond लोकालोक there is complete darkness, and<BR> to this side of it there is light; it thus divides the visible world from<BR> the regions of darkness; प्रकाशश्चाप्रकाशश्च लोकालोक इवाचलः R. 1. 68;<BR> लोकालोकव्याहतं धर्मराशेः शालीनं वा धाम नालं प्रसर्तुम्<BR> Śi. 16. 83; Mv. 5. 10, 45; ऊर्ध्वमालोकयामासुः लोकालोकमिवोच्छ्रितम्<BR> Parṇāl. 3. 30; (for further explanation see Dr. Bhāṇḍārkarʼs note on <i>l.</i> 79 of Māl. 10th Act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकालोकौ
लोकः + -अलोकः + .({@-कौ@}) the visible and the invisible world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाकाशः|लोकाकाश
लोकः + -आकाशः<BR>—1 space, sky.<BR>—2 (with Jains) a worldly region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकाचारः|लोकाचार
लोकः + -आचारः common practice, popular or general custom, ways of the<BR> world; अपि शास्त्रेषु कुशला लोकाचारविवर्जिताः Pt. 5. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकात्मन्
लोकः + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the soul of the universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकादिः|लोकादि
लोकः + -आदिः<BR>—1 the beginning of the world.<BR>—2 the creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायत|लोकायतं|लोकायतः
लोकः + -आयत <i>a.</i> atheistical, materialistic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायतः|लोकायत|लोकायतं
लोकः + -आयत + .({@-तः@}) a materialist, an atheist, a follower of Cārvāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायतम्
लोकः + -आयत + .({@-तम्@}) materialism, atheism; (for some account see the first chapter<BR> of the Sarvadarśanasaṃgraha).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकायतिकः|लोकायतिक
लोकः + -आयतिकः an atheist, a materialist; कच्चिन्न लोकायतिकान् ब्राह्मणांस्तात<BR> सेवसे Rām. 2. 100. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकेशः|लोकेश
लोकः + -ईशः<BR>—1 a king (lord of the world).<BR>—2 Brahman.<BR>—3 quick-silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकोक्तिः|लोकोक्ति
लोकः + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a proverb, popular saying; लोके ख्यातिमुपागतात्र सकले लोकोक्तिरेषा यतो दग्धानां किल वह्निना हितकरः सेकोऽपि तस्योद्भवः Pt. 1. 371.<BR>—2 common talk, public opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकोत्तर|लोकोत्तरः
लोकः + -उत्तर <i>a.</i> extraordinary, uncommon, unusual; लोकोत्तरा च<BR> कृतिः Bv. 1. 69, 70; U. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकोत्तरः|लोकोत्तर
लोकः + -उत्तर + .({@-रः@}) a king. ˚वादिन् <i>m.</i> pl. N. of a Buddhist school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकोपक्रोशनम्
लोकः + -उपक्रोशनम् circulating evil reports among the people; असारस्य<BR> वाक्संतक्षणैर्लोकोपक्रोशनैः … अपवाहनम् Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकैकबन्धुः|लोकैकबन्धु
लोकः + -एकबन्धुः an epithet of Śākyamuni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकैषणा
लोकः + -एषणा<BR>—1 desire for heaven; या वित्तैषणा सा लोकैषणोभे ह्येते एषणे एव भवतः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 3. 5. 1.<BR>—2 desire for the good opinion of the public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककण्टकः|लोककण्टक|लोककंटक
लोकः + -कण्टकः<BR>—1 a troublesome or wicked man, the curse of mankind.<BR>—2 an epithet of Rāvaṇa; see कण्टक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककथा
लोकः + -कथा a popular legend, folk-tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककर्तृ
लोकः + -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककृत्
लोकः + -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककल्प|लोककल्पः
लोकः + -कल्प <i>a.</i><BR>—1 resembling the world.<BR>—2 regarded by the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककल्पः|लोककल्प
लोकः + -कल्प + .({@-ल्पः@}) a period or age of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककान्त
लोकः + -कान्त <i>a.</i> liked by the people, popular; भव पितुरनुरूपस्त्वं<BR> गुणैर्लोककान्तैः V. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककान्ता
लोकः + -कान्त + .({@-न्ता@}) a kind of medical herb (Mar. मुरुडशेंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोककारणकारणः
लोकः + -कारणकारणः an epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">Page1373-1</a>]<BR> of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1372-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकक्षित्
लोकः + -क्षित् <i>a.</i> inhabiting heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकगतिः|लोकगति
लोकः + -गतिः <i>f.</i> actions of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकगाथा
लोकः + -गाथा a song handed down among people, folk-song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकचक्षुस्
लोकः + -चक्षुस् <i>n.</i> the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकचारित्रम्
लोकः + -चारित्रम् the ways of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकजननी
लोकः + -जननी an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकजित्
लोकः + -जित् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Buddha.<BR>—2 any conqueror of the world.<BR>—3 a sage. ━<i>a.</i> winning heaven; तद्धैतल्लोकजिदेव Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकज्ञ
लोकः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकज्येष्ठः|लोकज्येष्ठ
लोकः + -ज्येष्ठः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकतत्त्वम्
लोकः + -तत्त्वम् knowledge of mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकतन्त्रम्
लोकः + -तन्त्रम् course of the world; निर्मितो लोकतन्त्रोऽयं लोकेषु<BR> परिवर्तते Bhāg. 12. 11. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकतुषारः|लोकतुषार
लोकः + -तुषारः camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकत्रयम्
लोकः + -त्रयम्, -त्रयी the three worlds taken collectively; उत्खातलोकत्रयकण्टकेऽपि R. 14. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकत्रयी
लोकः + -त्रयम्, -त्रयी the three worlds taken collectively; उत्खातलोकत्रयकण्टकेऽपि R. 14. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकदम्भक
लोकः + -दम्भक <i>a.</i> cheating mankind; Ms. 4. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकद्वारम्
लोकः + -द्वारम् the gate of heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकधर्मः|लोकधर्म
लोकः + -धर्मः<BR>—1 a worldly matter.<BR>—2 (with Buddhists) worldly condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकधातुः|लोकधातु
लोकः + -धातुः a particular division of the world (जम्बुद्वीप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकधातृ
लोकः + -धातृ <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकधारिणी
लोकः + -धारिणी N. of the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनाथः|लोकनाथ
लोकः + -नाथः<BR>—1 Brahman.<BR>—2 Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Śiva.<BR>—4 a king, sovereign.<BR>—5 a Buddha<BR>—6 the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनेतृ
लोकः + -नेतृ <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपः|लोकप
लोकः + -पः, -पालः<BR>—1 a regent or guardian of a quarter of the world; ललिताभिनयं तमद्य<BR> भर्ता मरुतां द्रष्टुमनाः सलोकपालः V. 2. 18; R. 2. 75, 12. 89, 17. 78;<BR> (the <i>lokapālas</i> are eight; see अष्टदिक्पाल).<BR>—2 a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपालः|लोकपाल
लोकः + -पः, -पालः<BR>—1 a regent or guardian of a quarter of the world; ललिताभिनयं तमद्य<BR> भर्ता मरुतां द्रष्टुमनाः सलोकपालः V. 2. 18; R. 2. 75, 12. 89, 17. 78;<BR> (the <i>lokapālas</i> are eight; see अष्टदिक्पाल).<BR>—2 a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपक्तिः|लोकपक्ति
लोकः + -पक्तिः <i>f.</i> esteem of mankind, general respectability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपतिः|लोकपति
लोकः + -पतिः<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपथः|लोकपथ
लोकः + -पथः, -पद्धतिः <i>f.</i> the general or usual way, the universally accepted way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपद्धतिः|लोकपद्धति
लोकः + -पथः, -पद्धतिः <i>f.</i> the general or usual way, the universally accepted way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपरोक्ष
लोकः + -परोक्ष <i>a.</i> hidden from the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकपितामहः|लोकपितामह
लोकः + -पितामहः an epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रकाशनः|लोकप्रकाशन
लोकः + -प्रकाशनः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रत्ययः|लोकप्रत्यय
लोकः + -प्रत्ययः universal prevalence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रवादः|लोकप्रवाद
लोकः + -प्रवादः general rumour, current report, popular talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकप्रसिद्ध
लोकः + -प्रसिद्ध <i>a.</i> well-known, universally known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकबन्धुः|लोकबन्धु|लोकबंधु
लोकः + -बन्धुः, -बान्धवः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकबान्धवः|लोकबान्धव|लोकबांधव
लोकः + -बन्धुः, -बान्धवः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकबाह्य|लोकबाह्यः
लोकः + -बाह्य, -वाह्य<BR>—1 excluded from society, excommunicated.<BR>—2 differing from the world, eccentric, singular; उन्मादवन्नृत्यति लोकबाह्यः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 2. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकबाह्यः|लोकबाह्य
लोकः + -बाह्य, -वाह्य + .({@-ह्यः@}) an outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवाह्य
लोकः + -बाह्य, -वाह्य<BR>—1 excluded from society, excommunicated.<BR>—2 differing from the world, eccentric, singular; उन्मादवन्नृत्यति लोकबाह्यः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 2. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकभर्तृ
लोकः + -भर्तृ <i>a.</i> supporter of the people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकभावन
लोकः + -भावन, -भाविन् <i>a.</i> promoting the welfare of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकभाविन्
लोकः + -भावन, -भाविन् <i>a.</i> promoting the welfare of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकमर्यादा|लोकमर्य्यादा
लोकः + -मर्यादा an established or current custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकमातृ
लोकः + -मातृ <i>f.</i> an epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकमार्गः|लोकमार्ग
लोकः + -मार्गः an established custom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकयज्ञः|लोकयज्ञ
लोकः + -यज्ञः desire for the good opinion of the people (लोकैषणा);<BR> Mb. 10. 18. 5 (com. लोकयज्ञो लोकैषणा सर्वो मां साधुमेव जानात्विति वासनारूपः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकयात्रा
लोकः + -यात्रा<BR>—1 worldly affairs, the course of worldly life, business of the world;<BR> तस्माल्लोकयात्रार्थी नित्यमुद्यतदण्डः स्यात् Kau. A. 1. 4; Mb. 3. 150. 31;<BR> Dk. 2. 8; एवं किलेयं लोकयात्रा Mv. 7; यावदयं संसारस्तावत्<BR> प्रसिद्धैवेयं लोकयात्रा Ve. 3.<BR>—2 a popular usage or custom; एषोदिता लोकयात्रा नित्यं स्त्रीपुंसयोः<BR> शुभा Ms. 9. 25.<BR>—3 worldly existence, career in life; Māl. 4, 6.<BR>—4 support of life, maintenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरक्षः|लोकरक्ष
लोकः + -रक्षः a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरञ्जनम्
लोकः + -रञ्जनम् pleasing the world, popularity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरवः|लोकरव
लोकः + -रवः popular talk or report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकरावण
लोकः + -रावण <i>a.</i> tormentor of the people; रावणं लोकरावणम्<BR> Rām. 3. 33. 1; Mb. 3. 148. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकलेखः|लोकलेख
लोकः + -लेखः<BR>—1 a public document.<BR>—2 an ordinary letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकलोचनम्
लोकः + -लोचनम् the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवचनम्
लोकः + -वचनम् a popular rumour or report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवर्तनम्
लोकः + -वर्तनम् the means by which the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">Page1373-2</a>]<BR> world subsists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवादः|लोकवाद
लोकः + -वादः public rumour; common talk, popular report; मां लोकवादश्रवणादहासीः R. 14. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवार्ता|लोकवार्त्ता
लोकः + -वार्ता popular report, public rumour; कश्चिदक्षधूर्तः कलासु<BR> कवित्वेषु लोकवार्तासु चातिवैचक्षण्यान्मया समसृज्यत Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविद्विष्ट
लोकः + -विद्विष्ट <i>a.</i> disliked by men, generally or universally disliked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविधिः|लोकविधि
लोकः + -विधिः<BR>—1 a mode of proceeding prevalent in the world.<BR>—2 the creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविनायकाः
लोकः + -विनायकाः a class of deities presiding over diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविभ्रमः
लोकः + -विभ्रमः see लोकव्यवहार; हृष्यत्तनुर्विस्मृतलोकविभ्रमः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 71. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविरुद्ध
लोकः + -विरुद्ध <i>a.</i> opposed to public opinion; यद्यपि शुद्धं लोकविरुद्धं<BR> नाकरणीयम् नाचरणीयम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुत
लोकः + -विश्रुत <i>a.</i> far-famed, universally known, famous, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविश्रुतिः|लोकविश्रुति
लोकः + -विश्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 world-wide fame.<BR>—2 unfounded rumour, mere report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकविसर्गः|लोकविसर्ग
लोकः + -विसर्गः<BR>—1 the end of the world; Mb.<BR>—2 the creation of the world; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवृत्तम्
लोकः + -वृत्तम्<BR>—1 the way of the world, a custom prevalent in the world; लोकवृत्तमनुष्ठेयं<BR> कृतं वो बाष्पमोक्षणम् Rām. 4. 25. 3.<BR>—2 an idle talk or gossip; न लोकवृत्तं वर्तेत वृत्तिहेतोः कथंचन Ms. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकवृत्तान्तः|लोकवृत्तान्त|लोकवृत्तांत
लोकः + -वृत्तान्तः, -व्यवहारः<BR>—1 the course or ways of the world, general custom; Ś. 5.<BR>—2 course of events.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकव्यवहारः|लोकव्यवहार
लोकः + -वृत्तान्तः, -व्यवहारः<BR>—1 the course or ways of the world, general custom; Ś. 5.<BR>—2 course of events.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकव्यवहार|लोकव्यवहारः
लोकः + -व्यवहार <i>a.</i> commonly used, universally current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकव्रतम्
लोकः + -व्रतम् general practice or way of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकश्रुतिः|लोकश्रुति
लोकः + -श्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a popular report.<BR>—2 world-wide fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसंसृतिः|लोकसंसृति
लोकः + -संसृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 fate, destiny.<BR>—2 course through the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसंकरः|लोकसङ्कर
लोकः + -संकरः general confusion in the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसंग्रहः|लोकसङ्ग्रह
लोकः + -संग्रहः<BR>—1 the whole universe.<BR>—2 the welfare of the world; लोकसंग्रहमेवापि संपश्यन् कर्तुमर्हसि Bg. 3. 20.<BR>—3 worldly experience.<BR>—4 propitiation of mankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसंपन्न|लोकसम्पन्न
लोकः + -संपन्न <i>a.</i> possessed of worldly wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसंबाधः
लोकः + -संबाधः a throng of men, going and coming; इतस्ततः प्रवेशनिर्गमप्रवृत्तलोकसंबाधम् Dk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसाक्षिक
लोकः + -साक्षिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the world as a witness; in the face of the world; प्रत्यक्षं<BR> फलमश्नन्ति कर्मणां लोकसाक्षिकम् Mb. 3. 32. 6.<BR>—2 attested by witnesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसाक्षिन्
लोकः + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसाधक
लोकः + -साधक <i>a.</i> creating worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसाधारण
लोकः + -साधारण <i>a.</i> common (as a topic); Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसिद्ध
लोकः + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 current among the people, usual, customary.<BR>—2 generally received or accepted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसीमातिवर्तिन्
लोकः + -सीमातिवर्तिन् <i>a.</i> extraordinary, supernatural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसुन्दर
लोकः + -सुन्दर <i>a.</i> generally admired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकस्थलम्
लोकः + -स्थलम् common occurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकस्थितिः|लोकस्थिति
लोकः + -स्थितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 existence or conduct of the universe, worldly existence; the stability<BR> or permanence of the world; ये चैवं पुरुषाः कलासु कुशलास्तेष्वेव लोकस्थितिः Bh. 2. 22.<BR>—2 a universal law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकहास्य
लोकः + -हास्य <i>a.</i> world-derided, the butt of general ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकहित
लोकः + -हित <i>a.</i> beneficial to mankind or to the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकहितम्
लोकः + -हित + .({@-तम्@}) general welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकनम्
लोकनम् Looking at, seeing, beholding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकसात्
लोकसात् <i>ind.</i> For the sake of the public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोकंपृण
लोकंपृण <i>a.</i> Filling or pervading the world; लोकंपृणैः परिमलैः<BR> परिपूरितस्य काश्मीरजस्य कटुतापि नितान्तरम्या Bv. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोक्य
लोक्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 World-wide.<BR>—2 Usual, customary.<BR>—3 Right, real.<BR>—4 Heavenly.<BR>—5 Granting free space.<BR>—6 Conducive to the attainment of a better world; यज्वानः पुत्रिणो लोक्याः<BR> कृतकृत्यास्तनुत्यजः Mb. 7. 17. 24;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1374-1" target="_blank">Page1374-1</a>]<BR> Bhāg. 3. 14. 36.<BR>—7 = लोकजित्; तस्मात् पुत्रमनुशिष्टं लोक्यमाहुः Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1373-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोगः|लोग
लोगः A clod, lump of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1374-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लोच्
