वडवा
वडवा<BR>—1 A mare; सैव भूत्वाथ वडवा नासत्यौ सुषुवे भुवि Bhāg. 6. 6. 40.<BR>—2 The nymph Aśvinī who in the form of a mare bore to the sun two sons,<BR> the Aśvins; see संज्ञा.<BR>—3 A female slave.<BR>—4 A harlot, prostitute.<BR>—5 A woman of the Brāhmaṇa caste (द्विजयोषित्).<BR>—6 A particular constellation represented by a horseʼs head.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वडवाग्निः, वडवानलः, वडवाभर्तृ, वडवामुखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1383-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

