वनम् + -स्थली a wood, forest ground; नखक्षतानीव वनस्थलीनाम् Ku. 3. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्रज्
वनम् + -स्रज् <i>f.</i> a garland of forest flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनहासः|वनहास
वनम् + -हासः, -हासकः<BR>—1 the Kāśa grass.<BR>—2 N. of the flower-plant Kunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनहासकः|वनहासक
वनम् + -हासः, -हासकः<BR>—1 the Kāśa grass.<BR>—2 N. of the flower-plant Kunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्पतिः|वनस्पति
वनस्पतिः [वनस्य पतिः नि˚ सुट्]<BR>—1 A large forest tree, especially one that bears fruit apparently without<BR> any blossoms; अपुष्पाः फलवन्तो ये ते वनस्पतयः स्मृताः Ms. 1. 47.<BR>—2 A tree in general; तमाशु विघ्नं तपसस्तपस्वी वनस्पतिं वज्र<BR> इवावभज्य Ku. 3. 74.<BR>—3 The Soma plant.<BR>—4 A stem, trunk.<BR>—5 A beam; pole, post.<BR>—6 A sacrificial post.<BR>—7 An offering to <i>Vanaspati</i>.<BR>—8 A wooden amulet.<BR>—9 A scaffold.<BR>—10 An ascetic.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वनस्पतिकायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्पतिकायः|वनस्पतिकाय
वनस्पतिः + -कायः the whole world of plants, vegetable kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वननम्
वननम् Ved. Wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनरः|वनर
वनरः (= वानरः); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनस्
वनस् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Loveliness or glory; आयाहि वनसा सह Rv. 10. 72. 1.<BR>—2 Wealth.<BR>—3 A wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायुः|वनायु
वनायुः [Uṇ. 1. 4] N. of a district; निद्रां विहाय वनजाक्ष<BR> वनायुदेश्याः R. 5. 73.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वनायुज<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनायुज|वनायुजः
वनायुः + -ज <i>a.</i> produced in Vanāyu, (as a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनाहिरः|वनाहिर
वनाहिरः A hog, wild boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिः|वनि
वनिः<BR>—1 N. of Agni.<BR>—2 A heap.<BR>—3 Asking, begging. ━<i>f.</i> Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिका
वनिका A little wood; as in अशोकवनिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिन्
वनिन् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Worshipping.<BR>—2 Desiring.<BR>—3 Giving, bestowing.<BR>—4 Abounding in water.<BR>—5 Living in a forest. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A tree.<BR>—2 The Soma plant.<BR>—3 A Brāhmaṇa in the third stage of his life, a Vānaprastha, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनी
वनी A forest, wood, grove or thicket (of trees); पूगवनी Mv. 7. 13;<BR> अवनीतलमेव साधु मन्ये न वनी माघवनी विलासहेतुः Jag.;<BR> वनीमिमां ते पृतना प्रतनीमतनीयसीम् Śiva B. 19. 10; कल्याणीं<BR> तु वनीमनीनयदहो कस्याप्यमृष्यन् वचः Viś. Guṇā. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेकिंशुकाः
वनेकिंशुकाः (pl.) ‘A Kiṃśuka in a wood’, anything found unexpectedly;<BR> also वनेबिल्वकाः in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचर|वनेचरः
वनेचर <i>a.</i> [वने चरति चर-ट अलुक् स˚] Dwelling in a wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनेचरः|वनेचर
वनेचर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A forester, woodman; वनेचराणां वनितासखानाम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">Page1387-2</a>]<BR> Ku. 1. 10; Ki. 1. 1.<BR>—2 An ascetic, a hermit.<BR>—3 A wild beast.<BR>—4 A sylvan, satyr.<BR>—5 A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनित|वनितः
वनित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Begged, asked, solicited &c.<BR>—2 Served, worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिता
वनिता<BR>—1 A woman in general; वनितेति वदन्त्येतां लोकाः सर्वे वदन्तु ते ।<BR> यूनां परिणता सेयं तपस्येति मतं मम ॥ Bv. 2. 117; पथिकवनिताः Me. 8.<BR>—2 A wife, mistress; वनेचराणां वनितासखानाम् Ku. 1. 10; R. 2. 19.<BR>—3 Any beloved woman.<BR>—4 The female of an animal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वनिताद्विष्, वनिताविलासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिताद्विष्
वनिता + -द्विष् <i>m.</i> a misogynist (woman-hater).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिताविलासः|वनिताविलास
वनिता + -विलासः wanton pastime of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्ठुः|वनिष्ठु
वनिष्ठुः [वन्-इष्ठुच् Uṇ. 4. 2] Ved.<BR>—1 Part of the entrails of an animal offered in sacrifice.<BR>—2 The rectum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनिष्णु
वनिष्णु <i>a.</i> Begging, requesting; (याचक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीकः|वनीक
वनीकः A beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीपकः|वनीपक
वनीपकः, वनीयकः A beggar, mendicant; वनीयकानां स<BR> हि कल्पभूरुहः N. 15. 60; Śi. 14. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीयकः|वनीयक
वनीपकः, वनीयकः A beggar, mendicant; वनीयकानां स<BR> हि कल्पभूरुहः N. 15. 60; Śi. 14. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीयति
वनीयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To beg (as alms).<BR>—2 To ask, entreat, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनीयस्
वनीयस् <i>a.</i> Very liberal; अन्यथा तेऽव्यक्तगतेर्दर्शनं नः<BR> कथं नृणाम् । नितरां म्रियमाणानां संसिद्धस्य वनीयसः ॥ Bhāg. 1. 19. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनुः|वनु
वनुः Ved.<BR>—1 A malicious person (हिंसक).<BR>—2 An assailant, enemy; त्वम् इन्द्र वनून् अहन् Rv. 4. 30. 5.<BR>—3 An adherent, a friend; वनुं वा ये सुश्रुणं सुश्रुतो धुः 10. 74. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वनुस्
वनुस् <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Eager, anxious for.<BR>—2 Devoted or attached to.<BR>—3 A worshipper, one who honours. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A plotter, an enemy (हिंसक).<BR>—2 Possessing, enjoying, using.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्|वंद्
वन्द् €1 Ā. (वन्दते, वन्दित)<BR>—1 To salute, greet respectfully, pay homage<BR> to; जगतः पितरौ वन्दे पार्वतीपरमेश्वरौ R. 1. 1, 13. 77, 14. 5.<BR>—2 To adore, worship.<BR>—3 To praise, extol. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि@} to salute, greet respectfully;<BR> मानोन्नतेनाप्यभिवन्द्य मूर्ध्ना R. 16. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दकः|वन्दक|वंदकः
वन्दकः<BR>—1 A praiser.<BR>—2 A parasitical plant; also वन्दका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दथः|वन्दथ|वंदथ|वंदथः
वन्दथः [वन्द्-अथः Uṇ. 3. 112]<BR>—1 A praiser, bard, panegyrist.<BR>—2 One who deserves praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनम्
वन्दनम् [वन्द्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Salutation, obeisance.<BR>—2 Reverence, adoration.<BR>—3 Obeisance paid to a Brāhmaṇa &c. (by touching his feet).<BR>—4 Praising, extolling.<BR>—5 A custaneous eruption, scrofula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दना|वंदना
वन्दनम् + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 Worship, adoration.<BR>—2 Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनी|वंदनी
वन्दनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 Worship, adoration.<BR>—2 Praise.<BR>—3 Solicitation.<BR>—4 A drug for reviving the dead.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वन्दनमाला, वन्दनमालिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमाला|वंदनमाला
वन्दनम् + -माला, -मालिका a garland suspended across gateways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनमालिका|वंदनमालिका
वन्दनम् + -माला, -मालिका a garland suspended across gateways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनकम्
वन्दनकम् Respectful salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1387-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनीय|वंदनीय|वन्दनीयः
वन्दनीय <i>a.</i> Fit to be saluted, adorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दनीया|वंदनीया
वन्दनीय + .{@-या@} Yellow pigment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दा|वंदा
वन्दा<BR>—1 A female beggar.<BR>—2 Parasitical plant ({@वन्दाकः, -की, -का, वन्दारः@} also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दारः|वन्दार
वन्दारः A parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दारु|वंदारु|वन्दारुः
वन्दारु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Praising.<BR>—2 Reverential, respectful, polite, civil; परमनुगृहीतो महामुनिवन्दारुः<BR> Mu. 7. ━<i>n.</i> Praise. ━<i>m.</i> A panegyrist, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिन्|वंदिन्
वन्दिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A panegyrist, bard, an encomiast, a herald; घर्मच्छेदात् पटुतरगिरो<BR> वन्दिनो नीलकण्ठाः V. 4. 13; (the bards form a distinct caste sprung<BR> from a Kṣatriya father and a Śūdra mother).<BR>—2 A captive, prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिः|वन्दि
वन्दिः, वन्दी <i>f.</i> [वन्द्-इन् Uṇ. 4. 128] See बन्दी.<BR>—1 A female prisoner.<BR>—2 Prey, booty, spoil.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वन्दिपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दी
वन्दिः, वन्दी <i>f.</i> [वन्द्-इन् Uṇ. 4. 128] See बन्दी.<BR>—1 A female prisoner.<BR>—2 Prey, booty, spoil.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वन्दिपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दिपालः
वन्दिः + -पालः a keeper of prisoners, jailer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्य|वंद्य
वन्द्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Adorable, venerable; शिशुत्वं स्त्रैणं वा भवतु ननु वन्द्यासि जगताम् U. 4. 11.<BR>—2 To be respectfully saluted; वन्द्यं युगं चरणयोर्जनकात्मजायाः<BR> R. 13. 78; Ku. 6. 83; Me. 12.<BR>—3 Laudable, commendable, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्द्या|वंद्या
वन्द्य + .{@-द्या@}<BR>—1 A parasitical plant.<BR>—2 Yellow pigment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दः|वन्द
वन्दः [वन्द्-रक् Uṇ. 2. 13] A worshipper, votary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्दम्
वन्दः + .{@-न्दम्@} Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्धुर|वंधुर
वन्धुर <i>a.</i> See बन्धुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्ध्य
वन्ध्य [Uṇ. 4. 121], वन्ध्या See बन्ध्य, बन्ध्या; यत्र<BR> बन्ध्यफला वृक्षा विपुष्पा पर्णवर्जिताः Rām. 4. 48. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्ध्या
वन्ध्य [Uṇ. 4. 121], वन्ध्या See बन्ध्य, बन्ध्या; यत्र<BR> बन्ध्यफला वृक्षा विपुष्पा पर्णवर्जिताः Rām. 4. 48. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्नः|वन्न
वन्नः [Uṇ. 2. 28] A co-partner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्य|वन्यं|वन्यः
वन्य <i>a.</i> [वने-भवः यत्]<BR>—1 Belonging to, growing or produced in, woods, wild; कल्पवित् कल्पयामास<BR> वन्यामेवास्य संविधाम् R. 1. 94; वन्यानां मार्गशाखिनाम् 45, 88.<BR>—2 Savage, not tamed or domesticated; वन्यान् विनेष्यन्निव दुष्टसत्त्वान्<BR> R. 2. 8, 37, 5. 43.<BR>—3 Wooden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्यः|वन्य|वन्यं
वन्य + .{@-न्यः@}<BR>—1 A wild animal.<BR>—2 A wild plant.<BR>—3 A monkey; शतशो नैरृतान् वन्या जध्नुर्वन्यांश्च नैरृताः । नैरृतास्तत्र<BR> वध्यन्ते प्रायेण न तु वानराः ॥ Rām. 3. 287. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्यम्
वन्य + .{@-न्यम्@} Forest-produce (such as fruits, roots, &c.); रामोऽपि सह<BR> वैदेह्या वने वन्येन वर्तयन् R. 12. 20.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वन्याश्रमः, वन्येतर, वन्यगजः, वन्यद्विपः, वन्यवृत्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्याश्रमः|वन्याश्रम
वन्य + -आश्रमः = वानप्रस्थाश्रमः q. v.; लोकमुख्येषु सत्कारं<BR> लिङ्गिमुख्येषु चासकृत् । कुर्वतस्तस्य कौन्तेय वन्याश्रमपदं भवेत् ॥ Mb. 12. 66. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्येतर
वन्य + -इतर <i>a.</i> tame, domesticated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्यगजः
वन्य + -गजः, -द्विपः a wild elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्यद्विपः|वन्यद्विप
वन्य + -गजः, -द्विपः a wild elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्यवृत्ति
वन्य + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> living on forest-food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वन्या
वन्या<BR>—1 A large forest, a number of thickets.<BR>—2 A mass of water, flood, deluge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्
वप् €1 U. (वपति, वपते, उप्त; <i>pass.</i> उप्यते; <i>desid.</i><BR> विवप्सति-ते)<BR>—1 To sow, scatter (as seed), plant; यथेरिणे बीजमुप्त्वा न वप्ता लभते<BR> फलम् Ms. 3. 142; न विद्यामिरिणे वपेत् 2. 113; यादृशं वपते<BR> बीजं तादृशं लभते फलम् Subhāṣ.; Ku. 2. 5; Ś. 6. 23.<BR>—2 To throw (as arrow); cast (as dice); शरान् वपन्तं निशितान् सुपुङ्खान् Mb. 6. 63. 28.<BR>—3 To beget,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">Page1388-2</a>]<BR> produce.<BR>—4 To weave.<BR>—5 To shear, shave (mostly Vedic). ━<i>Caus.</i> (वापयति-ते) To<BR> sow, plant, put into the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपः|वप
वपः<BR>—1 Sowing seed.<BR>—2 One who sows, a sower.<BR>—3 Shaving.<BR>—4 Weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपनम्
वपनम् [वप्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sowing seed.<BR>—2 Shaving, shearing; वपनं मेखला दण्डो भैक्षचर्या व्रतानि च Ms. 11. 152;<BR> प्रयागे भास्करक्षेत्रे पितृमातृवियोगतः । आधाने सोमपाने च<BR> वपनं पञ्चसु स्मृतम् ॥<BR>—3 Semen virile, seed.<BR>—4 A razor.<BR>—5 Placing, arranging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपनी
वपनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A barberʼs shop.<BR>—2 A weaving instrument.<BR>—3 A weaverʼs shop (तन्तुशाला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपा
वपा [वप्-अच्]<BR>—1 Fat, marrow; Y. 3. 94.<BR>—2 A hole, cavity; वल्मीकस्य वपायां च Mb. 13. 85. 49.<BR>—3 A mound of earth thrown up by ants.<BR>—4 The skin of the intestines; अगस्त्यस्याभिचारेण युष्माकं च वपा हुता<BR> Mb. 1. 118. 15.<BR>—5 A fleshy prominent navel.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वपाकृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपाकृत्
वपा + -कृत् <i>m.</i> marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपिलः|वपिल
वपिलः A procreator, father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुः|वपु
वपुः [उप्यन्ते सर्वदुःखानि अत्र, वप्-उसिः Uṇ. 2. 114] The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुनः|वपुन
वपुनः A god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष
वपुष <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Handsome.<BR>—2 Wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुषम्
वपुष + .{@-षम्@} Beauty (of form).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुस्
वपुस् <i>a.</i> [वप्-उसि] Handsome, beautiful (Ved.). ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Body, person; (स्मरं) वपुषा स्वेन नियोजयिष्यति Ku. 4. 42;<BR> नवं वयः कान्तमिदं वपुश्च R. 2. 47; Śi. 10. 50.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Form, figure, appearance; लिखितवपुषौ शङ्खपद्मौ च दृष्ट्वा<BR> Me. 82; परिघः क्षतजतुल्यवपुः Bṛ. S. 30. 25.<BR>—2 Essence, nature; अष्टानां लोकपालानां वपुर्धारयते नृपः Ms. 5. 96.<BR>—3 Beauty, a beautiful form or appearance; ‘वपुः क्लीबं तनौ शस्ताकृतावपि’<BR> इति मेदिनी; श्रमेण च विवर्णानां वक्त्राणां विप्लुतं वपुः Mb. 11. 20. 34.<BR>—4 Ved. A wonderful phenomenon, wonder.<BR>—5 Ved. Water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वपुर्गुणः, वपुष्प्रकर्षः, वपुर्धर, वपुःस्रवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुर्गुणः|वपुर्गुण
वपुस् + -गुणः, -प्रकर्षः excellence of form, personal beauty; संधुक्षयन्तीव<BR> वपुर्गुणेन Ku. 3. 52; वपुःप्रकर्षादजयद्गुरुं रघुः R. 3. 35; Ki. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्प्रकर्षः|वपुष्प्रकर्ष
वपुस् + -गुणः, -प्रकर्षः excellence of form, personal beauty; संधुक्षयन्तीव<BR> वपुर्गुणेन Ku. 3. 52; वपुःप्रकर्षादजयद्गुरुं रघुः R. 3. 35; Ki. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुर्धर
वपुस् + -धर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 embodied.<BR>—2 beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुःस्रवः|वपुःस्रव
वपुस् + -स्रवः a humour of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वपुष्मत्|वपुष्मन्त्
वपुष्मत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Embodied, incarnate, corporeal; ददृशे जगतीभुजा मुनिः स वपुष्मानिव<BR> पुण्यसंचयः Ki. 2. 56.<BR>—2 Beautiful, handsome; वपुष्मान् वीतभीर्वाग्मी दूतो राज्ञः प्रशस्यते Ms. 7. 64.<BR>—3 Well-built and fat (हृष्टपुष्ट); अरोगप्रसवा नार्यो वपुष्मन्तो<BR> हि मानवाः Rām. 7. 41. 19.<BR>—4 Complete, whole, unbroken (अक्षत); शतं वाहसहस्राणां तण्डुलानां<BR> वपुष्मताम् Rām. 7. 91. 19 (com. अभग्नस्वरूपाणाम्).<BR>—5 Materialist (देहात्मवादी); ततस्त्रेतायुगं नाम मानवानां वपुष्मताम्<BR> Rām. 7. 74. 11. ━<i>m.</i> N. of one of the Viśvedevas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्तृ
वप्तृ <i>m.</i> [वप्-तृच्]<BR>—1 A sower (of seed), planter, husbandman; न शालेः स्तम्बकरिता वप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते<BR> Mu. 1. 3; Ms. 3. 142.<BR>—2 A father, procreator.<BR>—3 A poet, an inspired sage. —4 A shaver, cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1388-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रः|वप्र|वप्रं
वप्रः, -प्रम्<BR> [उप्यते अत्र वप्-रन् Uṇ. 2. 27]<BR>—1 A rampart, earth-work, mud-wall; वेलावप्रवलयाम् (उर्वीम्) R. 1. 30;<BR> द्वितीयामिव मामत्र वप्रमालम्ब्य तिष्ठत Śiva B.<BR>—2 A bank or mound of any kind (against which bulls and elephants butt);<BR> शृङ्गाग्रलग्नाम्बुदवप्रपङ्कः R. 13. 47; see वप्रक्रीडा below.<BR>—3 The slope or declivity of a hill or rocky place; बृहच्छिलावप्रघनेन<BR> वक्षसा Ki. 14. 40.<BR>—4 A summit, peak, table-land on a mountain; तीव्रं महाव्रतमिवात्र<BR> चरन्ति वप्राः Śi. 4. 58, 3. 37; Ki. 5. 36, 6. 8.<BR>—5 The bank of a river, side, shore, bank in general; ध्वनयः प्रतेनुरनुवप्रमपाम्<BR> Ki. 6. 4, 7. 11, 17. 58.<BR>—6 The foundation of a building.<BR>—7 The gate of a fortified town.<BR>—8 A ditch.<BR>—9 The circumference of a sphere.<BR>—10 A field in general; विकासि वप्राम्भसि गन्धसूचितम् Ki. 4. 26.<BR>—11 The butting of an elephant or bull.<BR>—12 Dust.<BR>—13 A multitude, a heap; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रम्
वप्रः, -प्रम्<BR> [उप्यते अत्र वप्-रन् Uṇ. 2. 27]<BR>—1 A rampart, earth-work, mud-wall; वेलावप्रवलयाम् (उर्वीम्) R. 1. 30;<BR> द्वितीयामिव मामत्र वप्रमालम्ब्य तिष्ठत Śiva B.<BR>—2 A bank or mound of any kind (against which bulls and elephants butt);<BR> शृङ्गाग्रलग्नाम्बुदवप्रपङ्कः R. 13. 47; see वप्रक्रीडा below.<BR>—3 The slope or declivity of a hill or rocky place; बृहच्छिलावप्रघनेन<BR> वक्षसा Ki. 14. 40.<BR>—4 A summit, peak, table-land on a mountain; तीव्रं महाव्रतमिवात्र<BR> चरन्ति वप्राः Śi. 4. 58, 3. 37; Ki. 5. 36, 6. 8.<BR>—5 The bank of a river, side, shore, bank in general; ध्वनयः प्रतेनुरनुवप्रमपाम्<BR> Ki. 6. 4, 7. 11, 17. 58.<BR>—6 The foundation of a building.<BR>—7 The gate of a fortified town.<BR>—8 A ditch.<BR>—9 The circumference of a sphere.<BR>—10 A field in general; विकासि वप्राम्भसि गन्धसूचितम् Ki. 4. 26.<BR>—11 The butting of an elephant or bull.<BR>—12 Dust.<BR>—13 A multitude, a heap; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रः|वप्र|वप्रं
वप्रः, -प्रम् + .{@-प्रः@}<BR>—1 A father.<BR>—2 A Prajāpati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रम्
वप्रः, -प्रम् + .{@-प्रम्@}<BR>—1 Lead.<BR>—2 Gold; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रा
वप्रः, -प्रम् + .{@-प्रा@}<BR>—1 A flat bank of earth.<BR>—2 Garden-bed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वप्राभिघातः, वप्रावनी, वप्रक्रिया, वप्रक्रीडा, वप्रक्षेत्रफलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्राभिघातः|वप्राभिघात
वप्रः + -अभिघातः butting against the bank or side (as of a hill, river<BR> &c.); वप्राभिघातपरिमण्डलितोरुदेहः Ki. 5. 42; cf. तटाघात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रावनी
वप्रः + -अवनी cultivated land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रक्रिया
वप्रः + -क्रिया, -क्रीडा the playful butting of an elephant (or bull) against<BR> a bank or mound; वप्रक्रियामृक्षवतस्तटेषु R. 5. 44; बप्रक्रीडापरिणतगजप्रेक्षणीयं<BR> ददर्श Me. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रक्रीडा
वप्रः + -क्रिया, -क्रीडा the playful butting of an elephant (or bull) against<BR> a bank or mound; वप्रक्रियामृक्षवतस्तटेषु R. 5. 44; बप्रक्रीडापरिणतगजप्रेक्षणीयं<BR> ददर्श Me. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रक्षेत्रफलम्
वप्रः + -क्षेत्रफलम् the circumference of a sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रकः|वप्रक
वप्रकः The circumference of a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्रिः|वप्रि
वप्रिः<BR>—1 A field.<BR>—2 The ocean.<BR>—3 Difficult position (दुर्गति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वप्री
वप्री<BR>—1 A mound of earth, hillock.<BR>—2 Ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वभ्र्
वभ्र् €1 P. (वभ्रति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्
वम् €1 P. (वमति, वान्त; <i>caus.</i> वामयति, वमयति;<BR> but with prepositions only वमयति)<BR>—1 To vomit, spit out, eject from the mouth; रक्तं चावमिषुर्मुखैः<BR> Bk. 15. 62, 9. 10, 14. 30.<BR>—2 To send forth or out, pour out, give out, give off, give forth, emit<BR> (fig. also); किमाग्नेयग्रावा निकृत इव तेजांसि वमति U. 6. 14; Ś. 2. 7;<BR> R. 16. 66; Me. 20; अविदितगुणापि सत्कविभणितिः कर्णेषु वमति<BR> मधुधाराम् Vās.<BR>—3 To throw out or down; वान्तमाल्यः R. 7. 6.<BR>—4 To reject; अथैतद्वचः पणयो वमन्नित् Rv. 10. 108. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमः|वम
वमः Ejecting, vomiting, giving out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमथुः|वमथु
वमथुः<BR>—1 Ejecting, vomiting, spitting out; तेषां श्रमं च ग्लानिं च वमथुं<BR> वेपथुं व्रणान् सर्वं व्यपानुदत् कृष्णः Mb. 7. 100. 14.<BR>—2 Water ejected by an elephant from his trunk.<BR>—3 A cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमनम्
वमनम् [वम्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Ejecting, vomiting.<BR>—2 Drawing out, taking or getting out as in स्वर्गाभिष्यन्दवमनम्<BR> R. 15. 29; Ku. 6. 37.<BR>—3 An emetic; also वमनद्रव्यम्.<BR>—4 Offering oblations.<BR>—5 Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमनः|वमन|वमनं
वमनम् + .{@-नः@} Hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमनी
वमनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A leech.<BR>—2 The cotton shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमनीया
वमनीया A fly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमिः|वमि
वमिः [वम्-इन्]<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 A cheat, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमिः|वमि
वमिः + .{@-मिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Sickness, nausea.<BR>—2 An emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमिन्
वमिन् <i>a.</i> Vomiting, being sick; P. III. 2. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वमी
वमी Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्भः|वम्भ|वंभः
वम्भः A bamboo (वंश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्भारवः|वम्भारव|वंभारव|वंभारवः
वम्भारवः The lowing of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्रः|वम्र
वम्रः, -म्री<BR> An ant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वम्रकूटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्री
वम्रः, -म्री<BR> An ant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वम्रकूटम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वम्रकूटम्
वम्रः + -कूटम् an ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वय्
वय् €1 Ā. (वयते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयः|वय|वयं
वयः A weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयनम्
वयनम् Weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्
वयस् <i>n.</i> [अज्-असुन् वीभावः]<BR>—1 Age, any time or period of life; गुणाः पूजास्थानं गुणिषु न च लिङ्गं<BR> न च वयः U. 4. 11; नवं वयः R. 2. 47; पश्चिमे वयसि 19. 1;<BR> न खलु वयस्तेजसो हेतुः Bh. 2. 38; तेजसां हि न वयः समीक्ष्यते<BR> R. 11. 1; Ku. 5. 16; Bhāg. 10. 26. 4.<BR>—2 Youth, the prime of life; वयसि गते कः कामविकारः Carpaṭa. S. 10;<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 17; वयोगते किं वनिताविलासः Subhāṣ.; so<BR> अतिक्रान्तवयाः.<BR>—3 A bird in general; स्मरणीयाः समये वयं वयः N. 2. 62; मृगवयोगवयोपचितं<BR> वनम् R. 9. 53, 2. 9; Śi. 3. 55, 11. 47.<BR>—4 A crow; वयांसि किं न कुर्वन्ति चञ्च्वा स्वोदरपूरणम् Pt. 1. 23<BR> (here it may mean ‘a bird’ also.).<BR>—5 Ved. Sacrificial food or oblation.<BR>—6 Energy, strength.<BR>—7 Health, soundness of constitution.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वयोतिग, वयोतीत, वयोधिक, वयोवस्था, वयःकर, वयोगत, वयःपरिणतिः, वयःपरिणामः, वयःप्रमाणम्, वयोबाल, वयोवृद्ध, वयःसंधिः, वयःस्थ, वयःस्थानम्, वयोहानिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोतिग
वयस् + -अतिग, -अतीत <i>a.</i> (वयोतिग &c.) advanced in age, aged, decrepit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोतीत
वयस् + -अतिग, -अतीत <i>a.</i> (वयोतिग &c.) advanced in age, aged, decrepit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधिक
वयस् + -अधिक <i>a.</i> (वयोधिक) older in age, senior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोवस्था
वयस् + -अवस्था (वयोवस्था) stage or period of life, measure of<BR> age; वयोऽवस्थां तस्याः श्रुणुत Māl. 9. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःकर
वयस् + -कर <i>a.</i> causing health and vigour of life, prolonging life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोगत
वयस् + -गत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 come of age.<BR>—2 advanced in years; अयमितर आत्मा कृतकृत्यो वयोगतः प्रैति Ait. Up. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोगतम्
वयस् + -गत + .({@-तम्@}) the departure of youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःपरिणतिः|वयःपरिणति
वयस् + -परिणतिः, -परिणामः ripeness of age; advanced or old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःपरिणामः
वयस् + -परिणतिः, -परिणामः ripeness of age; advanced or old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःप्रमाणम्
वयस् + -प्रमाणम्<BR>—1 measure or length of life.<BR>—2 duration of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोबाल
वयस् + -बाल <i>a.</i> young in years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोवृद्ध
वयस् + -वृद्ध <i>a.</i> (वयोवृद्ध) old, advanced in years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःसंधिः|वयःसन्धि
वयस् + -संधिः<BR>—1 transition from one period of life to another; त्रयो वयःसंधयः.<BR>—2 puberty, maturity (period of coming of age).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्थ|वयःस्थः
वयस् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> (वयःस्थ or वयस्थ)<BR>—1 youthful; नानावर्णविभक्तानां वयःस्थानां तथैव च Rām. 1. 53. 20.<BR>—2 grown up, mature.<BR>—3 strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्थः|वयःस्थ
वयस् + -स्थ + .({@-स्थः@}) a friend; contemporary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्था
वयस् + -स्थ + .({@-स्था@})<BR>—1 a female companion.<BR>—2 the yellow myrobalan tree.<BR>—3 small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयःस्थानम्
वयस् + -स्थानम् firmness of youth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोहानिः|वयोहानि
वयस् + -हानिः <i>f.</i> ({@वयोहानिः@})<BR>—1 loss or decline of youth.<BR>—2 loss of youthful vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्य|वयस्यः
वयस्य <i>a.</i> [वयसा तुल्यः यत्]<BR>—1 Being of the same age.<BR>—2 Contemporary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्यः|वयस्य
वयस्य + .{@-स्यः@} A friend, companion, any associate (usually of the same age).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयस्या
वयस्य + .{@-स्या@} A female companion or friend, a womanʼs confidante.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयाकः|वयाक
वयाकः A little branch, a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1389-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयुनम्
वयुनम् [वय् उनन् Uṇ. 3. 60] (also used in adjectival sense)<BR>—1 Knowledge, wisdom, faculty of perception; सर्वानाचष्ट वैकुण्ठं चक्षुषा<BR> वयुनेन सः Bhāg. 10. 13. 38, 4. 9. 8.<BR>—2 A temple (said to be <i>m.</i> also in this sense in Uṇadisūtras).<BR>—3 A rule, precept, order.<BR>—4 Manner, custom.<BR>—5 Clearness.<BR>—6 Action, act (कर्म); अग्ने नय सुपथा राये अस्मान् विश्वानि देव<BR> वयुनानि विद्वान् Īśop. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधस्
वयोधस् <i>m.</i> A young or middle-aged man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधा
वयोधा <i>a.</i> [वयसि धाञः Uṇ. 4. 236] Ved.<BR>—1 Powerful, vigorous.<BR>—2 Giving strength or health.<BR>—3 Giving food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोधाः
वयोधा + .{@-धाः@} <i>f.</i> Strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वयोरङ्गम्
वयोरङ्गम् Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्
वर् €10 U. (वरयति-ते, strictly <i>caus.</i> of वृ, or वॄ of class €10)<BR> To ask for, choose, seek to get; see वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर|वरं|वरः
वर <i>a.</i> [वृ-कर्मणि अप्]<BR>—1 Best, excellent, most beautiful or precious, choicest, finest, royal,<BR> princely; with gen. or loc. or usually at the end of comp.; वदतां<BR> वरः R. 1. 59; वेदविदां वरेण 5. 23, 11. 54; Ku. 6. 18; नृवरः,<BR> तरुवराः, सरिद्वरा &c.<BR>—2 Better than, preferable to; ग्रन्थिभ्यो धारिणो वराः Ms. 12. 103; Y. 1. 352.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरः|वर|वरं
वर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 The act of choosing, selecting.<BR>—2 Choice, selection.<BR>—3 A boon, blessing, favour (तपोभिरिष्यते यस्तु देवेभ्यः स वरो मतः);<BR> वरं वृ or याच् ‘to ask a boon’; प्रीतास्मि ते पुत्र वरं वृणीष्व<BR> R. 2. 63; भवल्लब्धवरोदीर्णः Ku. 2. 32; (for the distinction between<BR> वर and आशिस् see आशिस्).<BR>—4 A gift, present, reward, recompense.<BR>—5 A wish, desire in general.<BR>—6 Solicitation, entreaty.<BR>—7 Charity, alms.<BR>—8 Surrounding, enclosing.<BR>—9 Obstructing, checking.<BR>—10 A bridegroom, husband; वरं वरयते कन्या; see under वधू (1) also.<BR>—11 A suitor, wooer.<BR>—12 A dowry.<BR>—13 A son-in-law; ‘वरो जामातरि श्रेष्ठे’ इति विश्वः; रथाङ्गभर्त्रेऽभिनवं<BR> वराय Śi. 3. 36.<BR>—14 A dissolute man, libertine.<BR>—15 A sparrow.<BR>—16 Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्
वर + .{@-रम्@} Saffron; (for वरम् see separately).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वराङ्ग, वराङ्गना, वरान्नम्, वरारणिः, वरार्ह, वरानना, वराजीविन्, वरारुहः, वरारोह, वरालिः, वरासनम्, वरेन्द्रः, वरेन्द्री, वरेश्वरः, वरोरुः, वरोरूः, वरक्रतुः, वरगात्र, वरचन्दनम्, वरतनु, वरतन्तुः, वरत्वचः, वरद, वरदक्षिणा, वरदानम्, वरदानिक, वरद्रुमः, वरधर्मः, वरनिमन्त्रणम्, वरनिश्चयः, वरपक्षः, वरपुरुषः, वरप्रद, वरप्रदा, वरप्रस्थानम्, वरयात्रा, वरफलः, वरबाह्लिकम्, वरयुवतिः, वरयुवती, वररुचिः, वरलक्षणम्, वरलब्ध, वरवत्सला, वरवर्णम्, वरवर्णिनी, वरवृद्धः, वरशीतम्, वरसुरत, वरस्रज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्ग|वरांग|वराङ्गं|वराङ्गः
वर + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> having an excellent form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गः|वराङ्ग|वरांग|वराङ्गं
वर + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गः@})<BR>—1 an elephant.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 N. of Cupid.<BR>—4 a Nakṣatra year consisting of 324 days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गी
वर + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गी@}) turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गम्
वर + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गम्@})<BR>—1 the head; वराङ्गानि महार्हाणि धनुषा शातयामि वः Rām. 1. 66. 10;<BR> वराङ्गमुर्व्यामपतच्चमूमुखे Mb. 8. 91. 53.<BR>—2 the best part.<BR>—3 an elegant form.<BR>—4 pudendum muliebre.<BR>—5 green cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराङ्गना|वरांगना
वर + -अङ्गना a lovely woman; वराङ्गनासेवनमल्पभोजनम् Lakṣmīcharitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरान्नम्
वर + -अन्नम् excellent dish; पक्वापक्वं दिवारात्रं वरान्नममृतोपमम् Mb. 7. 67. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारणिः|वरारणि
वर + -अरणिः a mother; ददर्श रावणस्तत्र गोवृषेन्द्रवरारणिम्<BR> Rām. 7. 23. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरार्ह
वर + -अर्ह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 worthy of a boon.<BR>—2 very worthy, highly esteemed; मत्कृतेऽद्य वरार्हायाः श्यामतां समुपागतम्<BR> (मुखम्) Mb. 3. 144. 11.<BR>—3 very expensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरानना
वर + -आनना a lovely-faced woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराजीविन्
वर + -आजीविन् <i>m.</i> an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारुहः
वर + -आरुहः an ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारोह|वरारोहः
वर + -आरोह <i>a.</i> having fine hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारोहः|वरारोह
वर + -आरोह + .({@-हः@})<BR>—1 an excellent rider.<BR>—2 a rider on an elephant or horse.<BR>—3 mounting, riding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारोहा
वर + -आरोह + .({@-हा@}) an elegant or a beautiful woman; कामं कुरु वरारोहे<BR> देहि मे परिरम्भणम् Māl. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालिः|वरालि
वर + -आलिः the moon.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">Page1390-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासनम्
वर + -आसनम्<BR>—1 an excellent seat.<BR>—2 the chief seat, a seat of honour.<BR>—3 the China rose.<BR>—4 a cistern, reservoir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासनः|वरासन|वरासनं
वर + -आसनम् + .({@-नः@})<BR>—1 a door-keeper.<BR>—2 a lover, paramour<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेन्द्रः|वरेन्द्र
वर + -इन्द्रः<BR>—1 a chief, sovereign.<BR>—2 Indra.<BR>—3 (also <i>n.</i>) N. of a part of Bengal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेन्द्री
वर + -इन्द्री the ancient Gaura or Gauda country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेश्वरः|वरेश्वर
वर + -ईश्वरः N. of a Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोरुः|वरोरु
वर + -उरुः, -उरूः <i>f.</i> a beautiful woman (lit. having beautiful thighs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोरूः
वर + -उरुः, -उरूः <i>f.</i> a beautiful woman (lit. having beautiful thighs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरक्रतुः|वरक्रतु
वर + -क्रतुः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरगात्र
वर + -गात्र <i>a.</i> fair-limbed, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरचन्दनम्
वर + -चन्दनम्<BR>—1 a kind of sandalwood.<BR>—2 the pine tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरतनु|वरतनुः
वर + -तनु <i>a.</i> fair-limbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरतनुः|वरतनु
वर + -तनु + .({@-नुः@} <i>f.</i>) a beautiful woman; वरतनुरथवासौ नैव दृष्टा<BR> त्वया मे V. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरतन्तुः|वरतन्तु|वरतंतु
वर + -तन्तुः N. of an ancient sage; कौत्सः प्रपेदे वरतन्तुशिष्यः R. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्वचः|वरत्वच
वर + -त्वचः the <i>Nimba</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरद|वरदः
वर + -द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 conferring a boon, granting or fulfilling a boon; आगच्छ वरदे देवि<BR> जपे मे संनिधौ भव Sandhyā.<BR>—2 propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदः|वरद
वर + -द + .({@-दः@})<BR>—1 a benefactor.<BR>—2 N. of a class of Manes. —3 fire for propitiatory burnt offerings. ˚चतुर्थी<BR> N. of the 4th day in the bright half of माघ, ˚हस्तः the boon-giving<BR> or beneficent hand (placed on the head of a suppliant by a deity &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदा
वर + -द + .({@-दा@})<BR>—1 N. of a river; वरद वरदारोधोवृक्षैः सहावनतो रिपुः M. 5. 1.<BR>—2 a maiden, girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदक्षिणा
वर + -दक्षिणा<BR>—1 a present made to the bridegroom by the father of the bride.<BR>—2 a term for expense incurred in fruitless endeavours to recover a loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदानम्
वर + -दानम् the granting of a boon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरदानिक
वर + -दानिक <i>a.</i> arising from the bestowal of a favour or boon;<BR> चतुर्दश वने वासं वर्षाणि वरदानिकम् Rām. 2. 107. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरद्रुमः|वरद्रुम
वर + -द्रुमः agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरधर्मः|वरधर्म
वर + -धर्मः a noble act of justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरनिमन्त्रणम्
वर + -निमन्त्रणम् a journey undertaken by the parents of the bride<BR> to recall the bridegroom (who pretends to go to Kāśī.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरनिश्चयः|वरनिश्चय
वर + -निश्चयः the choice of a bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरपक्षः|वरपक्ष
वर + -पक्षः the party of the bridegroom (at a wedding); प्रमुदितवरपक्षमेकतस्तत् R. 6. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरपुरुषः|वरपुरुष
वर + -पुरुषः the best of men; अहं वरपुरुषमनुष्यो वासुदेवः कामयितव्यः Mk. 1. 30/31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रद
वर + -प्रद <i>a.</i> granting wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रदा
वर + -प्रदा N. of Lopāmudrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरप्रस्थानम्
वर + -प्रस्थानम्, -यात्रा the setting out of the bridegroom in procession<BR> towards the house of the bride for the celebration of marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयात्रा
वर + -प्रस्थानम्, -यात्रा the setting out of the bridegroom in procession<BR> towards the house of the bride for the celebration of marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरफलः|वरफल
वर + -फलः the cocoa-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरबाह्लिकम्
वर + -बाह्लिकम् saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयुवतिः|वरयुवति
वर + -युवतिः, -युवती <i>f.</i> a beautiful young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयुवती
वर + -युवतिः, -युवती <i>f.</i> a beautiful young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वररुचिः|वररुचि
वर + -रुचिः N. of a poet and grammarian (one of the ‘nine gems’ at<BR> the court of king Vikrama; see नवरत्न; he is identified by some<BR> with Kātyāyana, the celebrated author of the Vārtikas on Pāṇiniʼs Sūtras).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरलक्षणम्
वर + -लक्षणम् the requisites of wedding. पाणिग्रहणमन्त्राश्च प्रथितं<BR> वरलक्षणम् Mb. 7. 55. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरलब्ध|वरलब्धः
वर + -लब्ध <i>a.</i> received as a boon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरलब्धः|वरलब्ध
वर + -लब्ध + .({@-ब्धः@}) the <i>Champaka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवत्सला
वर + -वत्सला a mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवर्णम्
वर + -वर्णम् gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवर्णिनी
वर + -वर्णिनी<BR>—1 an excellent or fair-complexioned woman; मया हीयं वृता पूर्वं भार्यार्थे<BR> वरवर्णिनी Mb. 1. 5. 23.<BR>—2 a woman in general.<BR>—3 turmeric.<BR>—4 lac.<BR>—5 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>—6 of Durgā.<BR>—7 of Sarasvatī.<BR>—8 the creeper called <i>Priyaṅgu</i>.<BR>—9 a yellow pigment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरवृद्धः|वरवृद्ध
वर + -वृद्धः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरशीतम्
वर + -शीतम् cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरसुरत
वर + -सुरत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 very wanton.<BR>—2 acquainted with the secrets of sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरस्रज्
वर + -स्रज् <i>f.</i> ‘the bridegroomʼs garland’, the garland put by the<BR> bride round the neck of the bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1390-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरकः|वरक|वरकं
वरकः [वृ-वुन् Uṇ. 5. 44]<BR>—1 A wish, request, boon.<BR>—2 A cloak.<BR>—3 A kind of wild bean.<BR>—4 One who asks a female in marriage, a suitor, wooer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरकम्
वरकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 The cover of a boat.<BR>—2 A towel, wiper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणम्
वरणम् [वृ-ल्युट् ल्यु वा Uṇ. 2. 71]<BR>—1 Choosing, selecting.<BR>—2 Begging, soliciting, requesting.<BR>—3 Surrounding, encircling.<BR>—4 Covering, screening, protecting.<BR>—5 The choice of a bride.<BR>—6 Worshipping (of priests &c.).<BR>—7 Keeping off, prohibiting, warding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणः|वरण|वरणं
वरणम् + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A rampart, surrounding wall; वरणः कनकस्य मानिनीं दिवमङ्कादमराद्रिरागताम्<BR> … … उवास N. 2. 86.<BR>—2 A bridge.<BR>—3 The tree called Varuṇa; Rām. 2. 94. 9; see वरुण (Mar. वायवर्णा).<BR>—4 A tree in general; इह सिन्धवश्च वरणावरणाः करिणां मुदे सनलदानलदाः Ki. 5. 25.<BR>—5 A camel.<BR>—6 A kind of ornament on a bow.<BR>—7 N. of Indra.<BR>—8 A particular magical formula recited over weapons.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वरणमाला, वरणस्रज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणमाला
वरणम् + -माला, -स्रज् See वरस्रज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणस्रज्
वरणम् + -माला, -स्रज् See वरस्रज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरटः|वरट|वरटं
वरटः [वृ-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 86]<BR>—1 Gander.<BR>—2 A kind of grain.<BR>—3 A kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरटा
वरटः + .{@-टा, -टी@}<BR>—1 A goose; नवप्रसूतिर्वरटा तपस्विनी N. 1. 135; कण्डूयमाना<BR> वरटा स्वचञ्चुपुटकोटिभिः । हंसं कामयमानं तु वारयेत् पक्षधूननैः ॥<BR> Kāśīkhaṇḍa. 3. 68.<BR>—2 A wasp or a variety of it; भो वयस्य, एते खलु दास्याः पुत्रा अर्थकल्यवर्ता<BR> वरटाभीता इव गोपालदारका अरण्ये यत्र यत्र न खाद्यन्ते तत्र तत्र<BR> गच्छन्ति Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरटी
वरटः + .{@-टा, -टी@}<BR>—1 A goose; नवप्रसूतिर्वरटा तपस्विनी N. 1. 135; कण्डूयमाना<BR> वरटा स्वचञ्चुपुटकोटिभिः । हंसं कामयमानं तु वारयेत् पक्षधूननैः ॥<BR> Kāśīkhaṇḍa. 3. 68.<BR>—2 A wasp or a variety of it; भो वयस्य, एते खलु दास्याः पुत्रा अर्थकल्यवर्ता<BR> वरटाभीता इव गोपालदारका अरण्ये यत्र यत्र न खाद्यन्ते तत्र तत्र<BR> गच्छन्ति Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरटम्
वरटः + .{@-टम्@} A jasmine flower (कुन्दपुष्प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणक
वरणक <i>a.</i> Obstructing; गुरु वरणकमेव तमः Sāṅ. K. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरणसी
वरणसी More usually written वाराणसी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डः|वरण्ड|वरंड|वरंडः
वरण्डः [वृ-अण्डच् Uṇ. 1. 120]<BR>—1 A multitude, group.<BR>—2 A pimple or eruption on the face.<BR>—3 A veranda.<BR>—4 A heap of grass.<BR>—5 The string of a fish-hook.<BR>—6 Pocket.<BR>—7 The middle part of the sacrificial altar (वेदी); see वरण्डक.<BR> (The word वरण्डलम्बुक in यदिदानीमहं वरण्डलम्बुक इव दूरमुत्क्षिप्य<BR> पातितः Mk. 1 is of doubtful meaning; it seems to mean ‘an over-hanging or projecting wall’<BR>, which, if raised high, is sure to topple down; so<BR> in the case of the Sūtradhāra whose expectations were raised very high<BR> only to be cruelly disappointed. वरण्ड may mean a contrivance for<BR> drawing water from a well (named आकती in Marathi) and लम्बुक<BR> is its handle.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डक|वरंडक|वरण्डकः
वरण्डक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Large, great, spacious.<BR>—2 Frightened.<BR>—3 Miserable, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डकः|वरण्डक|वरंडक
वरण्डक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A mound of earth.<BR>—2 The seat on an elephant, a <i>howdah</i>.<BR>—3 A wall.<BR>—4 An eruption on the face.<BR>—5 = वरण्डः (7); गतासुरन्तरा दन्ती वरण्डक इवाभवत् Śi. 19. 65<BR> (Com. ‘वरण्डकोऽन्तरावेदौ संदोहमुखरोगयोः’ इति विश्वः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डा
वरण्डा<BR>—1 A dagger, knife.<BR>—2 A kind of bird (सारिका).<BR>—3 The wick of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डालुः|वरण्डालु|वरंडालुः
वरण्डालुः The castor-oil tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरण्डी
वरण्डी <i>f.</i> A sheaf of grass; Cārudatta 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्रा
वरत्रा, -त्रम्<BR> [वृ-अत्रन् Uṇ. 3. 104]<BR>—1 A strap, thong, or girth (of leather); वंशः प्रांशुरसौ घुणव्रणमयो<BR> जीर्णा वरत्रा इमाः Udb.; Bhāg. 8. 24. 45; विततपृथुवरत्रातुल्यरूपैर्मयूखैः Śi. 11. 44.<BR>—2 The girth of an elephant or horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरत्रम्
वरत्रा, -त्रम्<BR> [वृ-अत्रन् Uṇ. 3. 104]<BR>—1 A strap, thong, or girth (of leather); वंशः प्रांशुरसौ घुणव्रणमयो<BR> जीर्णा वरत्रा इमाः Udb.; Bhāg. 8. 24. 45; विततपृथुवरत्रातुल्यरूपैर्मयूखैः Śi. 11. 44.<BR>—2 The girth of an elephant or horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरम्
वरम् <i>ind.</i> Rather or better than, preferably to, it is better<BR> that &c. It is sometimes used with the ablative; समुन्नयन् भूतिमनार्यसंगमाद्वरं<BR> विरोधोऽपि समं महात्मभिः Ki. 1. 8. But it is generally used absolutely,<BR> वरम् being used with the clause containing the thing preferred, and<BR> न च, न तु, or न पुनः with the clause containing the thing<BR> to which the first is preferred, (both being put in the nominative case);<BR> वरं मौनं कार्यं न च वचनमुक्तं यदनृतं … वरं भिक्षाशित्वं<BR> न च परधनास्वादनसुखम् H. 1. 116; वरं प्राणत्यागो न पुनरधमानामुपगमः<BR> <i>ibid.</i>; वरं गर्भस्रावो वरमृतुषु नैवाभिगमनम्, वरं जातप्रेतो<BR> वरमपि च कन्यैव जनिता । वरं वन्ध्या भार्या वरमपि च गर्भेषु वसतिर्न<BR> चाविद्वान् रूपद्रविणगुणयुक्तोऽपि तनयः ॥ Pt.; sometimes न is<BR> used without च, तु or पुनः; याच्ञा मोघा वरमधिगुणे नाधमे लब्धकामा Me. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरयितृ
वरयितृ <i>m.</i> A suitor, wooer, lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरलः|वरल
वरलः A kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरला
वरलः + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 A goose.<BR>—2 A kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरस्
वरस् <i>m.</i> Width, breadth (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरस्या
वरस्या Ved. Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरा
वरा<BR>—1 The three kinds of myrobalan.<BR>—2 A kind of perfume.<BR>—3 Turmeric.<BR>—4 N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराक|वराकः
वराक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Poor, pitiable, miserable, wretched, unhappy, unfortunate (often used<BR> to show pity); तन्मया न युक्तं कृतं यत् स वराकोऽपमानितः Pt. 1;<BR> तत् किमुज्जिहानजीवितां वराकीं नानुकम्पसे Māl. 10.<BR>—2 Low, vile.<BR>—3 Impure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराकः|वराक
वराक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटः|वराट
वराटः [वरमल्पम् अटति अट्-अण् Tv.]<BR>—1 A <i>cowrie</i>.<BR>—2 A rope, cord.<BR>—3 The seed vessel; वराटकिञ्जल्कनिभोष्ठदन्तः Rām. Ch. 1. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वराटराट्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटराट्
वराटः + -राट् the king of Vidarbha or Berar; वराटराट् चारुनितान्तचारुणोः<BR> N. 16. 111, 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटकः|वराटक
वराटकः<BR>—1 A <i>cowrie</i>; a kind of measure ¹⁄₈₀ of a Paṇa; प्राप्तः काणवराटकोऽपि<BR> न मया तृष्णेऽधुना मुञ्च माम् Bh. 3. 4.<BR>—2 The seed-vessed of the lotus-flower; औज्झि प्रियाङ्गैर्घृणयैव रूक्षा<BR> न वारिदुर्गात्तु वराटकस्य N. 7. 18, 11. 110.<BR>—3 A string, rope (<i>n.</i> also in this sense).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वराटकरजस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटकरजस्
वराटकः + -रजस् <i>m.</i> the tree called नागकेशर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटिका
वराटिका<BR>—1 A <i>cowrie</i>; लोभाद्वराटिकानां विक्रेतुं तक्रमानिशमटन्त्या (लब्धो … नीलमणिः)<BR> Bv. 2. 42.<BR>—2 A trifling; प्रयागे मूत्र्यते येन तस्य गङ्गा वराटिका Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराटी
वराटी, -डी<BR> (In music) A kind of Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराडी
वराटी, -डी<BR> (In music) A kind of Rāga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराणः|वराण
वराणः<BR>—1 An epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 The वरुण tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराणसी
वराणसी See वाराणसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1391-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरारकम्
वरारकम् A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालः|वराल
वरालः, वरालकः [वृ-आलच् Uṇ. 1. 110]<BR>—1 Cloves. (also <i>n.</i>).<BR>—2 A donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालकः|वरालक
वरालः, वरालकः [वृ-आलच् Uṇ. 1. 110]<BR>—1 Cloves. (also <i>n.</i>).<BR>—2 A donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराला
वरालः, वरालकः + .{@-ला@} A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरालिका
वरालिका An epithet of Durgā; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराशिः|वराशि
वराशिः, -सिः<BR> A coarse cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासिः|वरासि
वराशिः, -सिः<BR> A coarse cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासिः|वरासि
वरासिः A swordsman; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरासी
वरासी <i>f.</i> Bathing cloth or soiled cloth; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहः|वराह
वराहः [वराय अभीष्टाय मुस्तादिलाभाय आहन्ति भूमिम् आ-हन्-ड Tv.]<BR>—1 A boar, hog; विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षतिः पल्वले Ś. 2. 6.<BR>—2 A ram.<BR>—3 A bull.<BR>—4 A cloud.<BR>—5 A crocodile.<BR>—6 An array of troops in the form of a boar.<BR>—7 N. of Viṣṇu in the third or boar incarnation; cf. वसति दशनशिखरे<BR> धरणी तव लग्ना शशिनि कलङ्ककलेव निमग्ना । केशव धृतशूकररूप<BR> जय जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1.<BR>—8 A particular measure.<BR>—9 N. of Varāhamihira.<BR>—10 N. of one of the 18 Purāṇas.<BR>—11 A mountain; L. D. B.<BR>—12 A coin; L. D. B.<BR>—13 A kind of grass; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वराहावतारः, वराहकन्दः, वराहकर्णः, वराहकर्णिका, वराहकल्पः, वराहक्रान्ता, वराहद्वादशी, वराहनामन्, वराहपुराणम्, वराहमिहिरः, वराहशृङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहावतारः|वराहावतार
वराहः + -अवतारः the boar or third incarnation of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकन्दः|वराहकन्द
वराहः + -कन्दः a kind of esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकर्णः|वराहकर्ण
वराहः + -कर्णः a kind of arrow; वराहकर्णैर्नालोकैविकर्णैश्चाभ्यवीवृषत्<BR> Mb. 7. 166. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकर्णिका
वराहः + -कर्णिका a kind of missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहकल्पः|वराहकल्प
वराहः + -कल्पः the period of the boar incarnation, the period during<BR> which Viṣṇu assumed the form of a boar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहक्रान्ता
वराहः + -क्रान्ता the sensitive plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहद्वादशी
वराहः + -द्वादशी a festival held on the 12th day in the bright half of<BR> Māgha in honour of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहनामन्
वराहः + -नामन् <i>n.</i> an esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहपुराणम्
वराहः + -पुराणम् N. of one of the 18 major Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहमिहिरः|वराहमिहिर
वराहः + -मिहिरः N. of a celebrated astronomer, author of बृहत्संहिता<BR> (supposed to be one of the ‘nine gems’ at the court of king Vikrama).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहशृङ्गः|वराहशृङ्ग|वराहशृंग
वराहः + -शृङ्गः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहुः|वराहु
वराहुः Ved. A boar, hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिमन्
वरिमन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Excellence, superiority, pre-eminence; न ह्यस्य वर्ष्मणः पुंसां<BR> वरिम्णः सर्वयोगिनाम् Bhāg. 3. 25. 2, 4. 15. 26.<BR>—2 Ved. Circuit, compass.<BR>—3 Breadth, extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्
वरिवस् <i>n.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Worshipping, honouring.<BR>—2 Wealth.<BR>—3 Room, space.<BR>—4 Pleasure, happiness.<BR>—5 Ease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवसित|वरिवसितः
वरिवसि(स्यि)त <i>a.</i> Worshipped, honoured, adored, revered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्यित|वरिवस्यितः
वरिवसि(स्यि)त <i>a.</i> Worshipped, honoured, adored, revered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवसितृ
वरिवसितृ <i>a.</i> Worshipper; न तच्चित्रं तस्मिन् वरिवसितरि<BR> त्वच्चरणयोर्न कस्या उन्नत्यै भवति शिरसस्त्वय्यवनतिः Śivamahimna 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्यति
वरिवस्यति Den. P. To show favour; cherish; Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिवस्या
वरिवस्या<BR>—1 Worship, honour, adoration, devotion.<BR>—2 Service, attendance; क्षितिपतेः प्रसितो वरिवस्यया Rām. Ch. 4. 85.<BR> Hence वरिवस्यक <i>a.</i> engaged in worship; Cārudatta 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिशी
वरिशी A fish-hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिषम्
वरिषम् A year; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिषाः
वरिषाः <i>f.</i> (pl.) The rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं|वरिष्ठः
वरिष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Best, most excellent, most distinguished or pre-eminent; अयं च<BR> पार्थो बीभत्सुर्वरिष्ठो ज्याविकर्षणे Mb. 3. 35. 12.<BR>—2 Largest, greatest.<BR>—3 Widest.<BR>—4 Heaviest.<BR>—5 Worst, most wicked; (superl. of उरु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठः|वरिष्ठ|वरिष्ठं
वरिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठः@}<BR>—1 The francoline partridge.<BR>—2 The orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरिष्ठम्
वरिष्ठ + .{@-ष्ठम्@}<BR>—1 Copper.<BR>—2 Pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरी
वरी<BR>—1 N. of Chāyā, wife of the sun.<BR>—2 The plant called शतावरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीमन्
वरीमन् <i>m.</i> Excellence &c.; see वरिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीयस्
वरीयस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Better, more excellent, preferable; आरादुपकारकेभ्यः सामवायिकान्यङ्गानि<BR> वरीयांसि भवन्ति ŚB. on MS. 10. 1. 23.<BR>—2 Most excellent, very good; वरीयानन्योन्यप्रगुणगुणनिर्माणनिपुणः Māl. 1. 16.<BR>—3 Larger, wider, more extensive (compar. of उरु q. v.).<BR>—4 Extremely tender or younger. ━<i>m.</i> N. of one of the Yogas. ━<i>n.</i><BR> Ved. Rest, repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीवर्दः|वरीवर्द|वरीवर्द्द|वरीवर्द्दः
वरी(ली)वर्दः An ox, a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलीवर्दः|वलीवर्द|वलीवर्द्द|वलीवर्द्दः
वरी(ली)वर्दः An ox, a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरीषुः|वरीषु
वरीषुः N. of Cupid, the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुकः|वरुक
वरु(रू)कः [Uṇ. 4. 43] A species of inferior grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूकः|वरूक
वरु(रू)कः [Uṇ. 4. 43] A species of inferior grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुटः|वरुट
वरुटः N. of a class of Mlecchas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुडः|वरुड
वरुडः N. of a low caste; one of the 7 low castes, whose occupation<BR> is splitting canes (Mar. बुरुड); cf. Ms. 4. 215. Kull. (वेणः-वेणोर्भेदनेन<BR> यो जीवति, बुरुड इति विश्वरूपः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणः|वरुण
वरुणः [वृ-उनन् Uṇ. 3. 53]<BR>—1 N. of an <i>Āditya</i> (usually associated with Mitra); Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 11.<BR>—2 (In later mythology) The regent of the ocean and of the western quarter<BR> (represented with a noose in hand); यासां राजा वरुणो याति मध्ये सत्यानृत्ये<BR> अवपश्यञ्जनानाम्; वरुणो यादसामहम् Bg. 10. 29; त्वं विश्वेषां वरुणासि<BR> राजा ये च देवा ये च मर्ताः Rv. 2. 27. 10; प्रतीचीं वरुणः पाति<BR> Mb.; अतिसक्तिमेत्य वरुणस्य दिशा भृशमन्वरज्यदतुषारकरः Śi. 9. 7.<BR>—3 The ocean.<BR>—4 Firmament.<BR>—5 The Sun.<BR>—6 The Varuṇa tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वरुणाङ्गरुहः, वरुणात्मजः, वरुणात्मजा, वरुणालयः, वरुणावासः, वरुणेशम्, वरुणदेवम्, वरुणदैवतम्, वरुणपाशः, वरुणलोकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणाङ्गरुहः|वरुणाङ्गरुह|वरुणांगरुह
वरुणः + -अङ्गरुहः an epithet of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणात्मजः|वरुणात्मज
वरुणः + -आत्मजः N. of the sage Jamadagni; ततः सुतास्ते वरुणात्मजोपमाः<BR> Mb. 7. 155. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणात्मजा
वरुणः + -आत्मजा spirituous liquor (so called being produced from the sea).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणालयः|वरुणालय
वरुणः + -आलयः, -आवासः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणावासः|वरुणावास
वरुणः + -आलयः, -आवासः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणेशम्
वरुणः + -ईशम्, -देवम्, -दैवतम् the Nakṣatra Śatabhiṣaj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणदेवम्
वरुणः + -ईशम्, -देवम्, -दैवतम् the Nakṣatra Śatabhiṣaj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणदैवतम्
वरुणः + -ईशम्, -देवम्, -दैवतम् the Nakṣatra Śatabhiṣaj.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणपाशः|वरुणपाश
वरुणः + -पाशः<BR>—1 a shark.<BR>—2 the noose of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणलोकः|वरुणलोक
वरुणः + -लोकः<BR>—1 the world of Varuṇa.<BR>—2 water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणानी
वरुणानी Varuṇaʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुणाविः|वरुणावि
वरुणाविः <i>f.</i> N. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुत्रम्
वरुत्रम् A cloak, mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरुलम्
वरुलम् [वृ-उलच् Uṇ. 5. 8] Best, preeminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1392-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूतृ
वरूतृ <i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A protector, defender.<BR>—2 A god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूत्री
वरूतृ + .{@-त्री@} A guardian deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथम्
वरूथम् [वृ-ऊथन् Uṇ. 2. 6]<BR>—1 A sort of wooden fence or fender with which a chariot is provided as<BR> a defence against collision (<i>m.</i> also in this sense); वरूथो रथगुप्तिर्या<BR> तिरोधत्ते रथस्थितिम्; चक्रैः षोडशभिर्युक्तं सवरूथं सकूबरम् A. Rām. 6. 11. 2.<BR>—2 An armour, a coat of mail.<BR>—3 A shield.<BR>—4 A group, multitude, an assemblage; मथ्यमानात्तथा सिन्धोर्देवासुरवरूथपैः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 7. 16, 3. 1. 28.<BR>—5 Protection.<BR>—6 A family.<BR>—7 A house, residence (Ved. in the last 3 senses)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथः|वरूथ|वरूथं
वरूथम् + .{@-थः@}<BR>—1 The cuckoo.<BR>—2 Time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वरूथवती<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथवती
वरूथम् + -वती a host, army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथशस्
वरूथशस् <i>ind.</i> In multitude or heaps; खार्काररभसा मत्ताः<BR> पर्यधावन् वरूथशः Bhāg. 3. 17. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथिन्
वरूथिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wearing an armour, mailed.<BR>—2 Furnished with a fender or protecting plank; अवनिमेकरथेन वरूथिना<BR> जितवतः किल तस्य धनुर्भृतः R. 9. 11.<BR>—3 Protecting, sheltering.<BR>—4 Surrounded by a troop.<BR>—5 Being or seated in a carriage. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A chariot; वरूथिना विनिष्पत्य व्यचरत् पृतनामुखे Mb. 7. 13. 23; Śi. 17. 23.<BR>—2 A guard, defender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरूथिनी
वरूथिन् + .{@-नी@} An army; स्खलितसलिलामुल्लङ्घ्यैनां जगाम वरूथिनी Śi. 12. 77;<BR> R. 12. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्य|वरेण्यं|वरेण्यः
वरेण्य <i>a.</i> [वृ-एन्य Uṇ. 3. 98]<BR>—1 To be wished for, desirable, eligible; अनेन चेदिच्छसि गृह्यमाणं<BR> पाणिं वरेण्येन R. 6. 24.<BR>—2 (Hence) Best, most excellent, pre-eminent, most worthy or distinguished,<BR> chief; वेधा विधाय पुनरुक्तमिवन्दुबिम्बं दूरीकरोति न कथं विदुषां<BR> वरेण्यः Bv. 2. 158; तत् सवितुर्वरेण्यं भर्गो देवस्य धीमही Rv. 3. 62. 10;<BR> R. 6. 24, 84; Bk. 1. 4; Ku. 7. 90; A. Rām. 2. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्यः|वरेण्य|वरेण्यं
वरेण्य + .{@-ण्यः@} A particular class of deceased ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेण्यम्
वरेण्य + .{@-ण्यम्@} Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरेन्द्री
वरेन्द्री N. of Gauḍa or North Bengal; L. D. B. See वरेन्द्र under वर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोटः|वरोट|वरोटं
वरोटः The Marubaka plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोटम्
वरोटः + .{@-टम्@} Its flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वरोल|वरोलः
वरोल A kind of wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्करः|वर्कर
वर्करः [वृक्-अरन् Uṇ. 4. 3]<BR>—1 A lamb, kid.<BR>—2 A goat.<BR>—3 Any young domestic animal.<BR>—4 Mirth, sport, pastime.<BR>—5 Jest, joke.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वर्करकर्करः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्करकर्करः|वर्करकर्कर
वर्करः + -कर्करः a strap or rope of leather (कर्कर) to bind a lamb or goat with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कराटः|वर्कराट
वर्कराटः<BR>—1 A side-glance, leer.<BR>—2 The marks of a loverʼs fingernails on the bosom of a woman.<BR>—3 The rays of the ascending sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्कुटः|वर्कुट
वर्कुटः A pin, bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गः|वर्ग|वर्ग्ग
वर्गः [वृज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A class, division, group; company, society, tribe, collection (of similar<BR> things); न्यषेधि शेषोऽप्यनुयायिवर्गः R. 2. 4, 11. 7; so पौरवर्गः,<BR> नक्षत्रवर्गः &c.<BR>—2 A party, side; वर्गावुभौ देवमहीधराणाम् Ku. 7. 53.<BR>—3 A category.<BR>—4 A class of words grouped together; as मनुष्यवर्गः, वनस्पतिवर्गः &c.<BR>—5 A class of consonants in the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">Page1393-2</a>]<BR> alphabet; (as कवर्ग, चवर्ग etc.).<BR>—6 A section, chapter, division of a book.<BR>—7 Particularly, a subdivision of an Adhyāya in Ṛgveda.<BR>—8 The square power.<BR>—9 Strength.<BR>—10 Sphere, province.<BR>—11 The whole class of objects of worldly existence (धर्म, अर्थ and काम).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वर्गान्त्यम्, वर्गोत्तमम्, वर्गाष्टकम्, वर्गकर्मन्, वर्गघनः, वर्गपदम्, वर्गमूलम्, वर्गप्रकृतिः, वर्गवर्गः, वर्गस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गान्त्यम्
वर्गः + -अन्त्यम्, -उत्तमम् the last letter of each of the first five classes<BR> of consonants; <i>i. e.</i> a nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गोत्तमम्
वर्गः + -अन्त्यम्, -उत्तमम् the last letter of each of the first five classes<BR> of consonants; <i>i. e.</i> a nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गाष्टकम्
वर्गः + -अष्टकम् the eight groups of consonants <i>i. e.</i> the consonants collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गकर्मन्
वर्गः + -कर्मन् N. of an operation relating to square numbers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गघनः|वर्गघन
वर्गः + -घनः the cube of a square. ˚घातः the fifth power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गपदम्
वर्गः + -पदम्, -मूलम् the square root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गमूलम्
वर्गः + -पदम्, -मूलम् the square root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गप्रकृतिः|वर्गप्रकृति
वर्गः + -प्रकृतिः <i>f.</i> an affected square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गवर्गः|वर्गवर्ग
वर्गः + -वर्गः the square of a square.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गस्थ
वर्गः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> devoted to a party; partial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गणा
वर्गणा<BR>—1 Multiplication.<BR>—2 Accumulation; इति स्तुवन् हुङ्कृतिवर्गणाभिः N. 10. 65.<BR>—3 A division, class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गयति
वर्गयति Den. P. To multiply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गशस्
वर्गशस् <i>ind.</i> In groups, according to classes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गिन्
वर्गिन् <i>a.</i> Belonging to a class or party. ━<i>m.</i> A leader of<BR> a group; परिचर्यावतो द्वारे ये च केचन वर्गिणः (अभिघातयेत्)<BR> Mb. 12. 100. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीकृत
वर्गीकृत<BR>—1 Classified.<BR>—2 Squared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीण
वर्गीण <i>a.</i> Belonging to a class or category; P. IV. 3. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीय|वर्गीयः
वर्गीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to a class or category.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्गीयः|वर्गीय
वर्गीय + .{@-यः@} A class-fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग्य|वर्ग्यः
वर्ग्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to the same class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ग्यः|वर्ग्य
वर्ग्य + .{@-र्ग्यः@} One belonging to the same class or company, colleague,<BR> class-fellow, fellow-student (in learning); या यस्य युज्यते भूमिका तां<BR> खलु भावेन तथैव सर्वे वर्ग्याः पाठिताः Māl. 1; उद्बाहुना जुहुविरे<BR> मुहुरात्मवर्ग्याः Śi. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्च्|वर्च्च्
वर्च् €1 Ā. (वर्चते) To shine, be bright or splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चटी|वर्च्चटी
वर्चटी<BR>—1 A kind of rice.<BR>—2 A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्|वर्च्चस्
वर्चस् <i>n.</i> [वर्च्-असुन्]<BR>—1 Vigour, energy, power.<BR>—2 Light, lustre, brilliance, splendour; स्वरेण वर्चसा चैव प्रेक्षितेन<BR> च वानर … … व्यक्तिं वां नोपलक्षये Rām. 4. 12. 31.<BR>—3 Form, figure, shape.<BR>—4 Ordure, feces.<BR>—5 Semen virile.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वर्चोग्रहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चोग्रहः|वर्चोग्रह
वर्चस् + -ग्रहः constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्कः|वर्चस्क|वर्च्चस्क|वर्च्चस्कः
वर्चस्कः<BR>—1 Brightness, lustre.<BR>—2 Vigour.<BR>—3 Feces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्चस्विन्|वर्च्चस्विन्
वर्चस्विन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vigorous, energetic, active.<BR>—2 Bright, brilliant, radiant. ━<i>m.</i> The moon; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जः|वर्ज|वर्जं|वर्ज्ज
वर्जः Leaving, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जक|वर्ज्जक
वर्जक <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Exclusive of, excluding.<BR>—2 Leaving, avoiding, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जनम्
वर्जनम् [वृज्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Leaving, giving up, abandoning.<BR>—2 Renouncing.<BR>—3 Exception, exclusion; P. I. 4. 88.<BR>—4 Hurt, injury, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1393-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जम्|वर्ज्जम्
वर्जम् <i>ind.</i> To the exclusion of, excluding, except (at the end<BR> of comp.); रसवर्जं रसोऽप्यस्य परं दृष्ट्वा निवर्तते Bg. 2. 59;<BR> गौतमीवर्जमितरा निष्क्रान्ताः Ś. 4; प्रत्यग्रहीत् सर्वममन्त्रवर्जम् Ku. 7. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्जित|वर्ज्जित|वर्ज्जितः
वर्जित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left out, excepted.<BR>—2 Abandoned, relinquished.<BR>—3 Excluded.<BR>—4 Deprived of, destitute of, without; as in गुणवर्जित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्य|वर्ज्ज्यः
वर्ज्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be avoided or shunned.<BR>—2 To be excluded or left out.<BR>—3 With the exception of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ज्यम्
वर्ज्य + .{@-र्ज्यम्@} A point in each lunar mansion during which no business<BR> should be undertaken (कुयोग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्ण्
वर्ण् €10 U. (वर्णयति-ते, वर्णित)<BR>—1 To colour, paint, dye; यथा हि भरता वर्णैर्वर्णयन्त्यात्मनस्तनुम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 To describe, relate, explain, write, depict, delineate, illustrate;<BR> वर्णितं जयदेवेन हरेरिदं प्रणतेन Gīt. 3; Ki. 5. 18.<BR>—3 To praise; extol.<BR>—4 To spread, extend.<BR>—5 To illuminate.<BR>—6 To exert oneself.<BR>—7 To send, cast.<BR>—8 To pound, grind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णः|वर्ण|वर्णं|वर्ण्ण
वर्णः [वर्ण्-अच् Uṇ. 3. 10]<BR>—1 A colour, hue; अन्तःशुद्धस्त्वमपि भविता वर्णमात्रेण कृष्णः Me. 51.<BR>—2 A paint, dye, paint-colour; see वर्ण् (1).<BR>—3 Colour, complexion, beauty; विविक्तवर्णाभरणा सुखश्रुतिः Ki. 14. 3;<BR> त्वय्यादातुं जलमवनते शार्ङ्गिणो वर्णचौरे Me. 48; R. 8. 42.<BR>—4 Look, countenance; मध्यस्थवर्ण इव दृश्यते Madhyamavyāyoga 1;<BR> किं त्वं शङ्कितवर्ण इव Cārudatta 4; अवदातिका परशङ्कितवर्णेव<BR> दृश्यते Pratimā 1.<BR>—5 A class of men, tribe, caste (especially applied to the four principal<BR> castes, ब्राह्मण, क्षत्रिय, वैश्य and शूद्र); वर्णानामानुपूर्व्येण<BR> Vārt; न कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोऽपि भजते Ś. 5. 10; R. 5. 19.<BR>—6 A class, race, tribe, kind, species; as in सवर्णम् अक्षरम्; ब्रह्मणा<BR> पूर्वसृष्टं हि कर्मभिर्वर्णतां गतम् Mb. 12. 188. 10.<BR>—7<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A letter, character, sound; न मे वर्णविचारक्षमा दृष्टिः<BR> V. 5; Ki. 14. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A word, syllable; S. D. 9.<BR>—8 Fame, glory, celebrity, renown; राजा प्रजारञ्जनलब्धवर्णः R. 6. 21.<BR>—9 A good quality, merit, virtue; त्रिवर्णा वर्णिताऽस्माभिः किं भूयः<BR> श्रोतुमिच्छसि Bhāg. 11. 3. 16.<BR>—10 Praise; स्वगुणोच्चगिरो मुनिव्रताः परवर्णग्रहणेष्वसाधवः Śi. 16. 29.<BR>—11 Dress, decoration.<BR>—12 Outward appearance, form, figure.<BR>—13 A cloak, mantle.<BR>—14 A covering, lid.<BR>—15 The order or arrangement of a subject in a song (गीतक्रम); अभिध्यायन्वर्णरतिप्रमोदानतिदीर्घे<BR> जीविते को रमेत Kaṭh. 1. 28; उपात्तवर्णे चरिते पिनाकिनः Ku. 5. 56<BR> ‘celebrated in song, made the subject of a song’.<BR>—16 The housings of an elephant.<BR>—17 A quality, property; जङ्गमानामसंख्येयाः स्थावराणां च जातयः ।<BR> तेषां विविधवर्णानां कुतो वर्णविनिश्चयः ॥ Mb. 12. 188. 9.<BR>—18 A religious observance.<BR>—19 An unknown quantity.<BR>—20 The number ‘one’.<BR>—21 Application of perfumed unguents to the body.<BR>—22 Gold.<BR>—23 A musical mode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णा
वर्णः + .{@-र्णा@} Cajanus Indicus (Mar. तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्णम्
वर्णः + .{@-र्णम्@}<BR>—1 Saffron.<BR>—2 A coloured unguent or perfume.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वर्णाङ्का, वर्णाधिपः, वर्णानुप्रासः, वर्णान्तरम्, वर्णापसदः, वर्णापेत, वर्णावकृष्टः, वर्णार्हः, वर्णावर, वर्णागमः, वर्णात्मन्, वर्णाश्रमाः, वर्णोदकम्, वर्णकविः, वर्णकूपिका, वर्णक्रमः, वर्णगत, वर्णगुरुः, वर्णग्रथणा, वर्णचारकः, वर्णज्येष्टः, वर्णतर्णकम्, वर्णतर्णिका, वर्णतालः, वर्णतूलिः, वर्णतूलिका, वर्णतूली, वर्णद, वर्णदात्री, वर्णदूतः, वर्णदूषक, वर्णधर्मः, वर्णनाथः, वर्णपत्रम्, वर्णपरिचयः, वर्णपातः, वर्णपात्रम्, वर्णपुष्पम्, वर्णपुष्पकः, वर्णप्रकर्षः, वर्णप्रसादनम्, वर्णबुद्धिः, वर्णभेदिनी, वर्णमातृ, वर्णमातृका, वर्णमाला, वर्णराशिः, वर्णरेखा, वर्णलेखा, वर्णलेखिका, वर्णवर्तिः, वर्णवर्तिका, वर्णवादिन्, वर्णविक्रिया, वर्णविपर्ययः, वर्णविलासिनी, वर्णविलोडकः, वर्णवृत्तम्, वर्णव्यवस्थितिः, वर्णशिक्षा, वर्णश्रेष्ठः, वर्णसंयोगः, वर्णसंसर्गः, वर्णसंहारः, वर्णसंकरः, वर्णसंघातः, वर्णसमाम्नायः, वर्णस्थानम्, वर्णहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1394-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

