वर्य|वर्यः|वर्य्य|वर्य्यं|वर्य्यः
वर्य <i>a.</i> [वृ-यत्]<BR>—1 To be chosen or selected, eligible.<BR>—2 Best, most excellent, chief, principal (mostly at the end of comp.);<BR> अन्वीतः स कतिपयैः किरातवर्यैः Ki. 12. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्यः|वर्य|वर्य्य|वर्य्यं|वर्य्यः
वर्य + .{@-र्यः@} The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वर्या|वर्य्या
वर्य + .{@-र्या@}<BR>—1 A girl choosing her own husband.<BR>—2 A girl in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1397-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

