वल्लकी
वल्लकी [वल्ल् क्वुन् गौरा˚ ङीष् Uṇ. 5. 44] The (Indian) lute; अजस्रमास्फालितवल्लकीगुणक्षतोज्ज्वलाङ्गुष्टनखांशुभिन्नया<BR> Śi. 1. 9, 4. 57; Ṛs. 1. 8; R. 8. 41, 19. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभ|वल्लभः
वल्लभ <i>a.</i> [वल्ल्-अभच् Uṇ. 3. 124]<BR>—1 Beloved, desired, dear.<BR>—2 Supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभः|वल्लभ
वल्लभ + .{@-भः@} A lover; husband; (खेदः) त्वयि विलसति तुल्यं वल्लभालोकनेन<BR> Māl. 3. 8; Śi. 11. 33.<BR>—2 A favourite; करोति निर्विकल्पं यः स भवेद्राजवल्लभः Pt. 1. 53.<BR>—3 A superintendent, an overseer.<BR>—4 A chief herdsman.<BR>—5 A good horse (one with auspicious marks); मन्दुरापरिभ्रष्टवल्लभतुरङ्गमपर्याकुलीकृत … Ve. 2. 19/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभा
वल्लभ + .{@-भा@} A beloved female, mistress, wife; बहुवल्लभा राजानः श्रूयन्ते<BR> Ś. 3; Mu. 3. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वल्लभाचार्यः, वल्लभगणिः, वल्लभजनः, वल्लभपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभाचार्यः|वल्लभाचार्य|वल्लभाचार्य्य
वल्लभ + -आचार्यः N. of the celebrated founder of a Vaiṣṇava sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभगणिः|वल्लभगणि
वल्लभ + -गणिः N. of a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभजनः|वल्लभजन
वल्लभ + -जनः a mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभपालः|वल्लभपाल
वल्लभ + -पालः a groom; स्तोकेन नाक्रमत वल्लभपालमुच्चैः Śi. 5. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लभायितम्
वल्लभायितम् A mode of sexual enjoyment; cf. पुरुषायित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लरम्
वल्लरम् [वल्ल्-अरन्]<BR>—1 Aloe wood.<BR>—2 A bower.<BR>—3 A thicket (गहन).<BR>—4 A branching foot-stalk (मञ्जरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लरिः|वल्लरि
वल्लरिः, -री <i>f.</i><BR> [वल्ल्-अरि वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 A creeping plant; अनपायिनि संश्रयदुमे गजभग्ने पतनाय वल्लरी<BR> Ku. 4. 31; तमोवल्लरी Māl. 5. 7.<BR>—2 A branching foot-stalk; चित्रश्रीरलमलकाग्रवल्लरीभिः Śi. 8. 56.<BR>—3 Trigonella Foenum Graecum (Mar. मेथी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लरी
वल्लरिः, -री <i>f.</i><BR> [वल्ल्-अरि वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 A creeping plant; अनपायिनि संश्रयदुमे गजभग्ने पतनाय वल्लरी<BR> Ku. 4. 31; तमोवल्लरी Māl. 5. 7.<BR>—2 A branching foot-stalk; चित्रश्रीरलमलकाग्रवल्लरीभिः Śi. 8. 56.<BR>—3 Trigonella Foenum Graecum (Mar. मेथी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लवः|वल्लव
वल्लवः (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> See बल्लव. A cowherd; विश्रम्भस्तु न गन्तव्यो<BR> वल्लवानामिति स्मरे Mb. 3. 239. 6 (v. l.); पश्यन्कृतार्थैरपि वल्लवीजनः<BR> Śi. 12. 39 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लि|वल्लिः
वल्लि <i>f.</i> [वल्ल्-इन् Uṇ. 4. 135]<BR>—1 A creeper, creeping or winding plant; भूतेशस्य भुजङ्गवल्लिवलयस्रङ्नद्धजूटा<BR> जटाः Māl. 1. 2.<BR>—2 The earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वल्लिदूर्वा, वल्लिपाषाणसंभवम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लिदूर्वा|वल्लिदूर्व्वा
वल्लि + -दूर्वा a kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लिपाषाणसंभवम्
वल्लि + -पाषाणसंभवम् coral; also वल्लिकाग्रम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ली
वल्ली <i>f.</i> A creeping plant, winding plant, creeper.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वल्लीकर्णः, वल्लीगडः, वल्लीजम्, वल्लीपदम्, वल्लीवृक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीकर्णः|वल्लीकर्ण
वल्ली + -कर्णः a particular deformity of the ear, also वल्लूरकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीगडः|वल्लीगड
वल्ली + -गडः a kind of fish (भोला, बालिकडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीजम्
वल्ली + -जम् pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीपदम्
वल्ली + -पदम् a kind of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लीवृक्षः|वल्लीवृक्ष
वल्ली + -वृक्षः the <i>Śāla</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लुरम्
वल्लुरम्^1 [वल्ल्-उरन्]<BR>—1 A bower, an arbour.<BR>—2 A place overgrown with creepers, wood, thicket.<BR>—3 A branching foot-stalk.<BR>—4 An uncultivated field.<BR>—5 A desert, wild, wilderness.<BR>—6 Dried flesh.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: derivation supports short 'u", also other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1400-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लूरः|वल्लूर|वल्लूरं
वल्लूरः [वल्ल्-ऊरन् Uṇ. 4. 96]<BR>—1 Dried flesh; Kau. A. 1. 4; Ms. 5. 13.<BR>—2 The flesh of the (wild) hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्लूरम्
वल्लूरः + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A thicket.<BR>—2 A desert, wilderness.<BR>—3 An uncultivated field.<BR>—4 Ground impregnated with salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्वजः|वल्वज
वल्वजः, -जा<BR> See बल्वज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्वजा
वल्वजः, -जा<BR> See बल्वज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्शः|वल्श
वल्शः A branch, twig; अव्यक्तमूलं भुवनाङ्घ्रिपेन्द्रमहीन्द्रभोगैरधिवीतवल्शम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्ह्
वल्ह् I. €1 Ā. (वल्हते)<BR>—1 To be pre-eminent or excellent.<BR>—2 To cover.<BR>—3 To kill, hurt.<BR>—4 To speak.<BR>—5 To give. ━II. €10 U. (वल्हयति-ते)<BR>—1 To speak.<BR>—2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्हिक
वल्हिक, वल्हीक See बल्हिक, बल्हीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वल्हीक
वल्हिक, वल्हीक See बल्हिक, बल्हीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्
वश् €2 P. (वष्टि, उशित)<BR>—1 To wish, desire, long for; निःस्वो वष्टि शतं शती दशशतम् Śānti. 2. 6;<BR> अमी हि वीर्यप्रभवं भवस्य जयाय सेनान्यमुशन्ति देवाः Ku. 3. 15;<BR> Ś. 7. 26; वष्टि भागुरिरल्लोपमवाप्योरुपसर्गयोः Sk.<BR>—2 To favour.<BR>—3 To shine (कान्तौ).<BR>—4 To aver, maintain, declare for; यत् सात्वताः पुरुषरूपमुशन्ति सत्त्वम्<BR> Bhāg. 12. 8. 46, 1. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश|वशं|वशः
वश <i>a.</i> [वश् कर्तरि अच् भावे अप् वा]<BR>—1 Subject to, influenced by, under the influence or control of, usually<BR> in comp.; शोकवशः, मृत्युवशः &c.<BR>—2 Obedient, submissive, compliant.<BR>—3 Humbled, tamed.<BR>—4 Charmed, fascinated.<BR>—5 Subdued by charms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशः|वश|वशं
वश + .{@-शः, -शम्@}<BR>—1 Wish, desire, will; Ait. Up. 5. 2.<BR>—2 Power, influence, control, mastership, authority, subjection, submission;<BR> स्ववश ‘subject to oneself’, independent; परवश ‘under the influence of others’<BR>; अनयत् प्रभुशक्तिसंपदा वशमेको नृपतीननन्तरान्<BR> R. 8. 19; वशं नी, or आनी to reduce to subjection, subdue, win<BR> over; वशं गम्-इ-या &c. to become subject to, give way, yield, submit;<BR> विषमालोड्य पास्यामि मा कीचकवशं गमम् Mb. 4. 21. 48; न शुचो<BR> वशं वशिनामुत्तम गन्तुमर्हसि R. 8. 90; वशे कृ or वशीकृ<BR> to subdue, overcome, win over; to fascinate, bewitch; वशात् (abl.)<BR> is frequently used adverbially in the sense of ‘through the force, power or influence of’<BR>, ‘on account of’, ‘for the purpose of’; दैववशात्,<BR> वायुवशात्, कार्यवशात् &c.<BR>—3 Being tamed.<BR>—4 Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशम्
वश + .{@-शः, -शम्@}<BR>—1 Wish, desire, will; Ait. Up. 5. 2.<BR>—2 Power, influence, control, mastership, authority, subjection, submission;<BR> स्ववश ‘subject to oneself’, independent; परवश ‘under the influence of others’<BR>; अनयत् प्रभुशक्तिसंपदा वशमेको नृपतीननन्तरान्<BR> R. 8. 19; वशं नी, or आनी to reduce to subjection, subdue, win<BR> over; वशं गम्-इ-या &c. to become subject to, give way, yield, submit;<BR> विषमालोड्य पास्यामि मा कीचकवशं गमम् Mb. 4. 21. 48; न शुचो<BR> वशं वशिनामुत्तम गन्तुमर्हसि R. 8. 90; वशे कृ or वशीकृ<BR> to subdue, overcome, win over; to fascinate, bewitch; वशात् (abl.)<BR> is frequently used adverbially in the sense of ‘through the force, power or influence of’<BR>, ‘on account of’, ‘for the purpose of’; दैववशात्,<BR> वायुवशात्, कार्यवशात् &c.<BR>—3 Being tamed.<BR>—4 Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशः|वश|वशं
वश + .{@-शः@} The residence of harlots.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वशानुग, वशग, वशवर्तिन्, वशाढ्यकः, वशेन्द्रिय, वशोपनयनम्, वशकारक, वशक्रिया, वशग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशानुग
वश + -अनुग, -ग, -वर्तिन् (so वशंगत) <i>a.</i> obedient to the<BR> will of another, submissive, subject; नमस्यामो देवान्ननु हतविधेस्तेऽपि<BR> वशगाः Bh. 2. 94. ━(<i>m.</i>) a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशग
वश + -अनुग, -ग, -वर्तिन् (so वशंगत) <i>a.</i> obedient to the<BR> will of another, submissive, subject; नमस्यामो देवान्ननु हतविधेस्तेऽपि<BR> वशगाः Bh. 2. 94. ━(<i>m.</i>) a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशवर्तिन्|वशवर्त्तिन्
वश + -अनुग, -ग, -वर्तिन् (so वशंगत) <i>a.</i> obedient to the<BR> will of another, submissive, subject; नमस्यामो देवान्ननु हतविधेस्तेऽपि<BR> वशगाः Bh. 2. 94. ━(<i>m.</i>) a servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशाढ्यकः|वशाढ्यक
वश + -आढ्यकः a porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशेन्द्रिय
वश + -इन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> one who has the command of his senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशोपनयनम्
वश + -उपनयनम् an instrument to bring people under control; न<BR> ह्येवंविधं वशोपनयनमस्ति भूतानां यथा दण्डः Kau. A. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशकारक
वश + -कारक <i>a.</i> leading to subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशक्रिया
वश + -क्रिया winning over, subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशग
वश + -ग <i>a.</i> subject, obedient; नमस्यामो देवान्ननु हतविधेस्तेऽपि<BR> वशगाः Bh. 2. 94; Pt. 1. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशगा
वश + -ग + .({@-गा@}) an obedient wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशंवद|वशंवदः
वशंवद <i>a.</i> Obedient to the will of, compliant, submissive,<BR> subject, under the influence of (lit. and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">Page1401-2</a>]<BR> fig.); कोपस्य किं नु करभोरु वशंवदाऽभूः Bv. 3. 9, 2. 136, 157;<BR> N. 1. 33; सा ददर्श गुरुहर्षवशंवदवदनमनङ्गनिवासम् Gīt. 11;<BR> अभिसारयते कान्तं या मन्मथवशंवदा S. D.; कम्रामिच्छुर्वशंवदाम् Bk. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशका
वशका An obedient wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशा
वशा [वश्-अच्]<BR>—1 A woman.<BR>—2 A wife.<BR>—3 A daughter.<BR>—4 A husbandʼs sister.<BR>—5 A cow.<BR>—6 A barren woman; वशाऽपुत्रासु चैवं स्याद्रक्षणं निष्कुलासु च Ms. 8. 28.<BR>—7 A barren cow.<BR>—8 A female elephant; स्त्रीरत्नेषु ममोर्वशी प्रियतमा यूथे तवेयं वशा V. 4. 25.<BR>—9 A harlot; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वशापायिन्, वशालोभः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशापायिन्
वशा + -पायिन् <i>m.</i> a dog; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशालोभः
वशा + -लोभः A method of catching elephants by seducing them with females;<BR> Mātaṅga L. 10. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिः|वशि
वशिः<BR>—1 Subjugation.<BR>—2 Fascinating, bewitching. ━<i>n.</i> Subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिक|वशिकः
वशिक <i>a.</i> Void, empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिका
वशिक + .{@-का@} Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिता
वशिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Subjection, control.<BR>—2 Bewitching, fascinating.<BR>—3 The supernatural or magical power of subduing others to oneʼs own will<BR> (one of the अष्टसिद्धिs).<BR>—4 Self-command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशित्वम्
वशिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Subjection, control.<BR>—2 Bewitching, fascinating.<BR>—3 The supernatural or magical power of subduing others to oneʼs own will<BR> (one of the अष्टसिद्धिs).<BR>—4 Self-command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशितृ
वशितृ <i>a.</i> Independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिन्
वशिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [वशः अस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Powerful.<BR>—2 Being under control, subdued, subject, submissive.<BR>—3 One who has subdued his passions (used like a noun also); प्रस्थापयामास<BR> वशी वसिष्ठः R. 2. 70, 8. 90, 19. 1; Ś. 5. 28. ━<i>m.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 A ruler, lord.<BR>—2 A sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिनी
वशिनी<BR>—1 The Śamī tree.<BR>—2 A parasite plant.<BR>—3 A mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिरः|वशिर|वशिरं
वशिरः A sort of pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिरम्
वशिरः + .{@-रम्@} Sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिष्ठ|वशिष्ठः
वशिष्ठ See वसिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकरणम्
वशीकरणम्<BR>—1 Fascinating, attracting.<BR>—2 A cause of attraction or allurement; एकैकमेव हि वशीकरणं गरीयः Māl. 6. 17.<BR>—3 Subduing, subjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीकृत
वशीकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Subdued.<BR>—2 Bewitched, enchanted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशीभूत|वशीभूतः
वशीभूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Subject, obedient.<BR>—2 Become powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्य|वश्यं|वश्यः
वश्य <i>a.</i> [वश्-यत्]<BR>—1 Capable of being subdued, controllable, governable; आत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा<BR> प्रसादमधिगच्छति Bg. 2. 64.<BR>—2 Subdued, conquered, tamed, humbled; कृशपरिणति चेतः क्लेशवश्यं<BR> क्व चेदम् Śivamahimna 31; वश्यात्मना तु यतता शक्योऽवाप्तुमुपायतः Bg. 6. 36.<BR>—3 Under influence or control, subject, dependent, obedient; तस्य पुत्रो<BR> भवेद्वश्यः समृद्धो धार्मिकः सुधीः H. Pr. 18; oft. in comp.; (मनः)<BR> हृदि व्यवस्थाप्य समाधिवश्यम् Ku. 3. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यः|वश्य|वश्यं
वश्य + .{@-श्यः@} A servant, dependant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्या
वश्य + .{@-श्या@} An humble or obedient wife; यं ब्रह्माणमियं देवी वाग्वश्येवानुवर्तते<BR> U. 1. 2 (who has full command of language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यम्
वश्य + .{@-श्यम्@} Cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1401-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वश्यका
वश्यका See वश्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशना
वशना A neck-ornament of ladies; सारसनं सारशनं वसना वशना<BR> तथा Śabdaratnāvalī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्
वष् €1 P. (वषति) To injure, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्
वषट् <i>ind.</i> An exclamation used on making an oblation to a deity,<BR> (with dat. of the deity); इन्द्राय वषट्, पूष्णे वषट् &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वषट्कर्तृ, वषट्कारः, वषट्कृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कर्तृ|वषट्कर्त्तृ
वषट् + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> the priest who makes the oblation with the exclamation वषट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कारः|वषट्कार
वषट् + -कारः the formula or exclamation वषट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वषट्कृत|वषट्कृतं
वषट् + -कृत offered in fire (with वषट्); प्राज्यमाज्यमसकृद्वषट्कृतम् Śi. 14. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्क्
वष्क् €1 Ā. (वष्कते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कयः|वष्कय
वष्कयः A calf one year old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कयणी
वष्कयणी, वष्कयिणी A cow that has full-grown calves; (चिरप्रसूता गौः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वष्कयिणी
वष्कयणी, वष्कयिणी A cow that has full-grown calves; (चिरप्रसूता गौः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्
वस् I. €1 P. (वसति, sometimes वसते, उवास, अवात्सीत्, वत्स्यति,<BR> वस्तुम्, उषित)<BR>—1 To dwell, inhabit, live, stay, abide, reside (usually with loc.; but<BR> sometimes acc.); धीरसमीरे यमुनातीरे वसति वने वनमाली Gīt. 5.<BR>—2 To be, exist, be found in; वसन्ति हि प्रेम्णि गुणा न वस्तुनि Ki. 8. 37;<BR> यत्राकृतिस्तत्र गुणा वसन्ति; भूतिः श्रीह्रीर्धृतिः कीर्तिर्दक्षे<BR> वसति नालसे Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 To spend, pass (as time) (with acc.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to dwell, to dwell, lodge, people.<BR>—2 To receive hospitably.<BR>—3 To dwell, inhabit. ━<i>Desid.</i> (विवत्सति) To wish to dwell.<BR>━II. €2 Ā. (वस्ते) To wear, put on; वसने परिधूसरे वसाना<BR> Ś. 7. 21; Śi. 9. 75; R. 12. 8; Ku. 3. 54, 7. 9; Bk. 4. 10. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (वासयति-ते) To cause to put on. ━III. €4 P. (वस्यति)<BR>—1 To be straight.<BR>—2 To be firm.<BR>—3 To fix. ━IV. €10 P. (वसयति) To dwell; L. D. B. ━V. €10 U. (वासयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cut, divide, cut off.<BR>—2 To love.<BR>—3 To take, accept.<BR>—4 To hurt, kill.<BR>—5 To offer. ━VI. €10 U. (वसयति-ते) To scent, perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसतिः|वसति
वसतिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR> [वस्-अति वा ङीप् Uṇ. 4. 62]<BR>—1 Dwelling, residing, abiding; आश्रमेषु वसतिं चक्रे Me. 1 ‘fixed his residence in’<BR>; कमलवसतिमात्रनिर्वृतः Ś. 5. 1.<BR>—2 A house, dwelling, residence, habitation; हर्षो हर्षो हृदयवसतिः<BR> पञ्चबाणस्तु बाणः P. R. 1. 22; Ś. 2. 15.<BR>—3 A receptacle, reservoir, an abode (fig.); अलकामतिवाह्यैव वसतिं<BR> वसुसंपदाम् Ku. 6. 37; so विनयवसतिः, धर्मैकवसतिः.<BR>—4 A camp, halting place (शिबिर).<BR>—5 The time when one halts or stays to rest, <i>i. e.</i> night; तस्य<BR> मार्गवशादेका बभूव वसतिर्यतः R. 15. 11 (वसतिः = रात्रिः Malli.)<BR> ‘he halted at night’ &c.; तिस्रो वसतीरुषित्वा 7. 33, 11. 30.<BR>—6 A Jaina monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसती
वसतिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR> [वस्-अति वा ङीप् Uṇ. 4. 62]<BR>—1 Dwelling, residing, abiding; आश्रमेषु वसतिं चक्रे Me. 1 ‘fixed his residence in’<BR>; कमलवसतिमात्रनिर्वृतः Ś. 5. 1.<BR>—2 A house, dwelling, residence, habitation; हर्षो हर्षो हृदयवसतिः<BR> पञ्चबाणस्तु बाणः P. R. 1. 22; Ś. 2. 15.<BR>—3 A receptacle, reservoir, an abode (fig.); अलकामतिवाह्यैव वसतिं<BR> वसुसंपदाम् Ku. 6. 37; so विनयवसतिः, धर्मैकवसतिः.<BR>—4 A camp, halting place (शिबिर).<BR>—5 The time when one halts or stays to rest, <i>i. e.</i> night; तस्य<BR> मार्गवशादेका बभूव वसतिर्यतः R. 15. 11 (वसतिः = रात्रिः Malli.)<BR> ‘he halted at night’ &c.; तिस्रो वसतीरुषित्वा 7. 33, 11. 30.<BR>—6 A Jaina monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसथम्
वसथम् An abode, dwelling, nest (of birds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसनम्
वसनम् [वस्-आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Dwelling, residing, staying.<BR>—2 A house, residence.<BR>—3 Dressing, clothing, covering.<BR>—4 A garment, cloth, dress, clothes; वसने परिधूसरे वसाना Ś. 7. 21;<BR> उत्सङ्गे वा मलिनवसने सौम्य निक्षिप्य वीणाम् Me. 88, 43.<BR>—5 An ornament worn (by women)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">Page1402-2</a>]<BR> round the loins, (probably for रसना).<BR>—6 Siege.<BR>—7 A leaf of the cinnamon tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसना
वसनम् + .{@-ना@} (in comp.)<BR>—1 Clothed in.<BR>—2 Surrounded by; समुद्रवसने देवि पर्वतस्तनमण्डले. —3 Engrossed by.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वसनपर्यायः, वसनसद्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसनपर्यायः|वसनपर्याय
वसनम् + -पर्यायः change of clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसनसद्मन्
वसनम् + -सद्मन् a tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तः|वसन्त|वसंत|वसंतः
वसन्तः [वस्-झच् Uṇ. 3. 128]<BR>—1 The spring, vernal season (comprising the two months चैत्र and<BR> वैशाख); मधुमाधवौ वसन्तः Suśr.; सर्वं प्रिये चारुतरं वसन्ते<BR> Ṛs. 6. 2; विहरति हरिरिह सरसवसन्ते Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 Spring personified as a deity and regarded as a companion of Kāmadeva;<BR> सुहृदः पश्य वसन्त किं स्थितम् Ku. 4. 27.<BR>—3 Dysentery.<BR>—4 Smallpox.<BR>—5 (In dramas) A nickname for the Vidūṣaka or buffoon.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वसन्तावतारः, वसन्तोत्सवः, वसन्तकालः, वसन्तकुसुमः, वसन्तघोषिन्, वसन्तजा, वसन्ततिलकः, वसन्तकम्, वसन्तदूतः, वसन्तदूती, वसन्तद्रुः, वसन्तद्रुमः, वसन्तपञ्चमी, वसन्तबन्धुः, वसन्तयोधः, वसन्तसखः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तावतारः
वसन्तः + -अवतारः the advent or setting in of the spring; वसन्तावतारसमयेऽस्या<BR> उन्मादयितृकं रूपं प्रेक्ष्य Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तोत्सवः|वसन्तोत्सव|वसंतोत्सव
वसन्तः + -उत्सवः the vernal festival, spring-festivities, formerly held<BR> on the full-moon day of Chaitra, but now on the full-moon day of Phālguna,<BR> and identified with the <i>Holi</i> festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तकालः|वसन्तकाल|वसंतकाल
वसन्तः + -कालः the spring-tide, vernal season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तकुसुमः|वसन्तकुसुम
वसन्तः + -कुसुमः Cordia Latifolia (Mar. गोंधणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तघोषिन्|वसंतघोषिन्
वसन्तः + -घोषिन् <i>m.</i> a cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तजा|वसंतजा
वसन्तः + -जा<BR>—1 the Vāsantī or Mādhavī creeper.<BR>—2 the spring festival; see वसन्तोत्सव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्ततिलकः|वसन्ततिलक|वसंततिलक|वसन्ततिलकं
वसन्तः + -तिलकः, -कम् the ornament of the spring; फुल्लं वसन्ततिलकं<BR> तिलकं वनाल्याः Chand. M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तकम्
वसन्तः + -तिलकः, -कम् the ornament of the spring; फुल्लं वसन्ततिलकं<BR> तिलकं वनाल्याः Chand. M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्ततिलकः|वसन्ततिलक|वसंततिलक|वसन्ततिलकं
वसन्तः + -तिलकः, -कम् + .({@-कः, -का, -कम्@}) N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्ततिलका|वसंततिलका
वसन्तः + -तिलकः, -कम् + .({@-कः, -का, -कम्@}) N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्ततिलकम्
वसन्तः + -तिलकः, -कम् + .({@-कः, -का, -कम्@}) N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तदूतः|वसन्तदूत|वसंतदूत
वसन्तः + -दूतः<BR>—1 the cuckoo.<BR>—2 the month called Chaitra.<BR>—3 the musical mode हिन्दोल.<BR>—4 the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तदूती|वसंतदूती
वसन्तः + -दूती<BR>—1 the trumpet-flower.<BR>—2 the female cuckoo.<BR>—3 Bignonia Suaveolens (Mar. पाटला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तद्रुः|वसन्तद्रु|वसंतद्रु
वसन्तः + -द्रुः, -द्रुमः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तद्रुमः|वसन्तद्रुम|वसंतद्रुम
वसन्तः + -द्रुः, -द्रुमः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तपञ्चमी|वसंतपंचमी
वसन्तः + -पञ्चमी the fifth day in the bright half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तबन्धुः|वसन्तबन्धु|वसंतबंधु
वसन्तः + -बन्धुः, -योधः, -सखः epithets of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तयोधः|वसन्तयोध
वसन्तः + -बन्धुः, -योधः, -सखः epithets of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसन्तसखः|वसन्तसख|वसंतसख
वसन्तः + -बन्धुः, -योधः, -सखः epithets of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसा
वसा [वस्-अच्]<BR>—1 The marrow of the flesh, fat, marrow; adept, suet; निर्वान्त्यद्यापि<BR> नैते स्रुतबहलवसावाहिनो हव्यवाहाः Mu. 3. 28; R. 15. 16; Ve. 1. 27;<BR> शुद्धमांसस्य यः स्नेहः सा वसा परिकीर्तिता Suśr.<BR>—2 Any oily or fatty exudation.<BR>—3 Brain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वसाढ्यः, वसाढ्यकः, वसाकेतुः, वसाच्छटा, वसापायिन्, वसामेहः, वसारोहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसाढ्यः|वसाढ्य
वसा + -आढ्यः, -आढ्यकः the Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसाढ्यकः|वसाढ्यक
वसा + -आढ्यः, -आढ्यकः the Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसाकेतुः|वसाकेतु
वसा + -केतुः a particular comet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसाच्छटा|वसाछटा
वसा + -छटा the mass of the brain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसापायिन्
वसा + -पायिन् <i>m.</i> a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसामेहः|वसामेह
वसा + -मेहः a kind of diabetes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसारोहः|वसारोह
वसा + -रोहः a mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसान
वसान <i>a.</i> Dwelling; वसानस्तत्र वै पुर्यामदितेर्विप्रियंकरम्<BR> Mb. 12. 339. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिः|वसि
वसिः [वस्-इन् Uṇ. 4. 151]<BR>—1 Clothes.<BR>—2 A dwelling, an abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसित
वसित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Worn, put on.<BR>—2 Dwelling.<BR>—3 Stored (as grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसितम्
वसित + .{@-तम्@} Abode, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिन्
वसिन् <i>m.</i> An otter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिरम्
वसिरम् Sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिष्ठः|वसिष्ठ
वसिष्ठः (also written वशिष्ठ)<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated sage, the family priest of the solar race of kings,<BR> and author of several Vedic hymns, particularly of the seventh Maṇḍala<BR> of the Ṛgveda. He was the typical representative of true Brāhmanic dignity<BR> and power, and the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">Page1403-1</a>]<BR> efforts of Viśvāmitra to rise to his level form the subject of many<BR> legends; cf. विश्वामित्र. —2 N. of the author of a Smṛti (sometimes<BR> ascribed to the sage himself).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वशिष्ठ|वशिष्ठः
वसिष्ठः (also written वशिष्ठ)<BR>—1 N. of a celebrated sage, the family priest of the solar race of kings,<BR> and author of several Vedic hymns, particularly of the seventh Maṇḍala<BR> of the Ṛgveda. He was the typical representative of true Brāhmanic dignity<BR> and power, and the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">Page1403-1</a>]<BR> efforts of Viśvāmitra to rise to his level form the subject of many<BR> legends; cf. विश्वामित्र. —2 N. of the author of a Smṛti (sometimes<BR> ascribed to the sage himself).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसिष्ठम्
वसिष्ठः (also written वशिष्ठ) + .{@-ष्ठम्@} Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1402-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसु|वसुः
वसु <i>a.</i> Sweet.<BR>—2 Dry.<BR>—3 Ved. Wealthy, rich.<BR>—4 Ved. Good. ━<i>n.</i> [वस्-उन् Uṇ. 1. 10]<BR>—1 Wealth, riches; स्वयं प्रदुग्धेऽस्य गुणैरुपस्नुता वसूपमानस्य वसूनि<BR> मेदिनी Ki. 1. 18; R. 8. 31, 9. 6 वस्वीशाद् वसुनिकरं (लब्ध्वा)<BR> धृतानुरागा Rām. Ch. 7. 58.<BR>—2 A jewel, gem.<BR>—3 Gold.<BR>—4 Water; वसु काल उपादत्ते काले चायं विमुञ्चति Bhāg. 4. 16. 6.<BR>—5 A thing, substance; त्रात्वार्थितो जगति पुत्रपदं च लेभे दुग्धा वसूनि<BR> वसुधा सकलानि येन Bhāg. 2. 7. 9; Mb. 12. 98. 20.<BR>—6 A kind of salt.<BR>—7 A medicinal root (वृद्धि).<BR>—8 A yellow kind of kidney-bean.<BR>—9 The ghee (घृत); विधिना वेददृष्टेन वसोर्धारामिवाध्वरे Mb. 13. 2. 35.<BR>━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of a class of deities (usually pl. in this sense); सेयं भूरिवसोर्वसोरिव<BR> सुता मृत्योर्मुखे वर्तते Māl. 5. 24; Ki. 1. 18; (the <i>Vasus</i> are<BR> eight in number:− 1 आप, 2 ध्रुव, 3 सोम, 4 धर or धव,<BR> 5 अनिल, 6 अनल, 7 प्रत्यूष, and 8 प्रभास; sometimes<BR> अह is substituted for आप; धरो ध्रुवश्च सोमश्च अहश्चैवानिलोऽनलः ।<BR> प्रत्यूषश्च प्रभासश्च बसवोऽष्टाविति स्मृताः).<BR>—2 The number ‘eight’.<BR>—3 N. of Kubera.<BR>—4 Of Śiva.<BR>—5 Of Agni.<BR>—6 A tree.<BR>—7 A lake, pond.<BR>—8 A rein.<BR>—9 The tie of a yoke.<BR>—10 A halter.<BR>—11 A ray of light; निरकाशयद्रविमपेतवसुं वियदालयादपरदिग्गणिका<BR> Śi. 9. 10; शिथिलवसुमगाधे मग्नमापत् पयोधौ Ki. 1. 46 (in both<BR> cases वसु means ‘wealth’ also).<BR>—12 The sun.<BR>—13 The distance from the elbow to the closed fist. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 Light, radiance.<BR>—3 A medicinal root (वृद्धि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वसूत्तमः, वसूपमः, वस्वोकसारा, वस्वौकसारा, वसुकीटः, वसुकृमिः, वसुता, वसुतातिः, वसुदा, वसुदेवः, वसुदेवता, वसुदेव्या, वसुदेव्या, वसुद्रुमः, वसुधर्मिका, वसुधा, वसुधारा, वसुभारा, वसुधारिणी, वसुपालः, वसुप्रभा, वसुप्राणः, वसुभम्, वसुरण्व, वसुरेतस्, वसुरोचिस्, वसुव्रतम्, वसुश्रेष्ठम्, वसुषेणः, वसुस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूत्तमः|वसूत्तम
वसु + -उत्तमः N. of Bhīṣma; तान् समेतान् महाभागानुपलभ्य वसूत्तमः ।<BR> पूजयामास … … Bhāg. 1. 9. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसूपमः
वसु + -उपमः Natron (Mar. सज्जीखार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्वोकसारा
वसु + -ओकसारा, -औकसारा<BR>—1 N. of Amarāvatī, the city of Indra.<BR>—2 of Alakā, the city of Kubera; ‘वस्वौकसारा श्रीदस्य शक्रस्य नलिनी पुरी’ इति हरिः;<BR> वस्वौकसारां नलिनीमतीत्यैवोत्तरान् कुरून् Rām. 2. 94. 26;<BR> व्यक्तं वस्वोकसारेयम् Mb. 7. 67. 16 (com. वस्वोकसारा सलोप<BR> आर्षः । कनकमयानि ओकांसि सारो यस्याः सा तथा ।). —3 of a river attached<BR> to Amarāvatī and Alakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वस्वौकसारा
वसु + -ओकसारा, -औकसारा<BR>—1 N. of Amarāvatī, the city of Indra.<BR>—2 of Alakā, the city of Kubera; ‘वस्वौकसारा श्रीदस्य शक्रस्य नलिनी पुरी’ इति हरिः;<BR> वस्वौकसारां नलिनीमतीत्यैवोत्तरान् कुरून् Rām. 2. 94. 26;<BR> व्यक्तं वस्वोकसारेयम् Mb. 7. 67. 16 (com. वस्वोकसारा सलोप<BR> आर्षः । कनकमयानि ओकांसि सारो यस्याः सा तथा ।). —3 of a river attached<BR> to Amarāvatī and Alakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुकीटः|वसुकीट
वसु + -कीटः, -कृमिः a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुकृमिः|वसुकृमि
वसु + -कीटः, -कृमिः a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुता
वसु + -ता, -तातिः <i>f.</i> Ved. wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुतातिः|वसुताति
वसु + -ता, -तातिः <i>f.</i> Ved. wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदा
वसु + -दा the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1403-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वसुदेवः|वसुदेव
