वा
वा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 As an alternative conjunction it means ‘or’; but its position is different<BR> in Sanskrit, being used either with each word or assertion or only with<BR> the last, but it is never used at the beginning of a clause; cf. च.<BR>—2 It has also the following senses:−<BR>——(<i>a</i>) and, as well as, also; वायुर्वा दहनो वा G. M.; अस्ति ते<BR> माता स्मरसि वा तातम् U. 4.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) like, as; जातां मन्ये तुहिनमथितां पद्मिनीं वान्यरूपाम् Me. 85<BR> (v. l.); मणी वोष्ट्रस्य लम्बेते Sk.; हृष्टो गर्जति चातिदर्पितबलो<BR> दुर्योधनो वा शिखी Mk. 5. 6; स्नानीयवस्त्रक्रियया पत्रोर्णं वोपयुज्यते<BR> M. 5. 12; Śi. 3. 63, 4. 35, 7. 64; Ki. 3. 13.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) optionally; (in this sense mostly in grammatical rules as of<BR> Pāṇini); दोषो णौ वा चित्तविरागे P. VI. 4. 99, 91.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) possibility; (in this sense वा is usually added to the interrogative<BR> pronoun and its derivatives like इव or नाम), and may be translated<BR> by ‘possibly’, ‘I should like to know’; कस्य वान्यस्य वचसि मया स्थातव्यम्<BR> K.; परिवर्तिनि संसारे मृतः को वा न जायते Pt. 1. 27.<BR>——(<i>e</i>) sometimes used merely as an expletive.<BR>——(<i>f</i>) indeed, truly.<BR>——(<i>g</i>) only.<BR>—3 When repeated वा has the sense of ‘either━or’, ‘whether━or’;<BR> सा वा शंभोस्तदीया वा मूर्तिर्जलमयी मम Ku. 2. 60; तदत्र परिश्रमानुरोधाद्वा<BR> उदात्तकथावस्तुगौरवाद्वा नवनाटकदर्शनकुतूहलाद्वा भवद्भिरवधानं<BR> दीयमानं प्रार्थये Ve. 1; एक एव खगो मानी सुखं जीवति चातकः ।<BR> म्रियते वा पिपासायां याचते वा पुरंदरम् ॥ Subhāṣ. (अथवा or,<BR> or rather, or else); see under अथ; न वा not, neither, nor; यदि<BR> वा or if; यद्वा or, or else; किं वा whether, possibly &c.; किं<BR> वा शकुन्तलेत्यस्य मातुराख्या Ś. 7. 20/21; को वा or के वा followed<BR> by a negative means ‘everyone, all’; के वा न स्युः परिभवफला निष्फलारम्भयत्नाः Me. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
वा I. €2 P. (वाति, वात or वान)<BR>—1 To blow; वाता वाता दिशि दिशि न वा सप्तधा सप्तभिन्नाः Ve. 3. 6;<BR> दिशः प्रसेदुर्मरुतो ववुः सुखाः R. 3. 14; Me. 44; Bk. 7. 1, 8. 61.<BR>—2 To go, move.<BR>—3 To strike, hurt, injure.<BR>—4 To emit an odour, be diffused.<BR>—5 To smell. ━<i>Caus.</i> (वापयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to blow.<BR>—2 (वाजयति-ते) To shake. ━<i>With</i> {@आ@} to blow; बद्धां बद्धां<BR> भित्तिशङ्काममुष्मिन्नावानावान्मातरिश्वा निहन्ति Ki. 5. 36; Bk. 14. 97.<BR> ━{@प्र, वि@} to blow; वायुर्विवाति हृदयानि हरन्नराणाम् Ṛs. 6. 23.<BR>━II. €4 P. (वायति)<BR>—1 To be dried up, to dry.<BR>—2 To be extinguished. ━III. €10 U. (वापयति-ते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To be happy.<BR>—3 To worship, reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांश|वांशः
वांश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [वंश-अण्] Made of bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांशी
वांश + .{@-शी@} Bamboo-manna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांशिकः|वांशिक
वांशिकः [वंश-ठक]<BR>—1 A bamboo-cutter.<BR>—2 A flute-player, a piper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकम्
वाकम् A flght of cranes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकः|वाक|वाकं
वाकम् + .{@-कः@} [वच्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Speech, uttering; as in नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे U. 1. 1; सूक्तवाकेनातितरामुदितगुणगणावतारसुजयः<BR> Bhāg. 5. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Voice (वाणी); सर्वमिदमभ्यात्तोऽवाक्यनादरः Ch. Up. 3. 14. 2.<BR>—3 Text (संहिता); a Vedic portion containing mantras; यं वाकेष्वनुवाकेषु<BR> निषत्सूपनिषत्सु च (गुणन्ति) Mb. 12. 49. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाकोपवाकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकोपवाकम्
वाकम् + -उपवाकम् speech and reply, dialogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकुची
वाकुची, वागुजी Vernonia Anthelmintica (Mar. बावची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुजी
वाकुची, वागुजी Vernonia Anthelmintica (Mar. बावची).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकुल|वाकुलं
वाकुल See बाकुल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाकोवाक्यम्
वाकोवाक्यम् = तर्कशास्त्रम् q. v.; Ch. Up. 7. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यम्
वाक्यम् [वच्-ण्यत् चस्य कः]<BR>—1 Speech, words, a sentence, saying, what is spoken; शृणु मे वाक्यम्<BR> ‘hear my words’, ‘hear me’; वाक्ये न संतिष्टते ‘does not obey’; संक्षिप्तस्याप्यतोऽस्यैव<BR> वाक्यस्यार्थगरीयसः Śi. 2. 24.<BR>—2 A sentence, period (complete utterance of a thought); वाक्यं स्याद्योग्यताकाङ्क्षासत्तियुक्तः<BR> पदोच्चयः S. D. 6; पदसमूहो वाक्यम् Tarka K.; श्रौत्यार्थी च भवेद्वाक्ये<BR> समासे तद्धिते तथा K. P. 10.<BR>—3 An argument or syllogism (in logic).<BR>—4 A precept, rule, an aphorism.<BR>—5 (In astr.) The solar process for all astronomical computations.<BR>—6 An assertion, statement.<BR>—7 Command.<BR>—8 (In law) Declaration, legal evidence.<BR>—9 Betrothment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाक्याडम्बरः, वाक्यार्थः, वाक्यालापः, वाक्योपचारः, वाक्यखण्डनम्, वाक्यग्रहः, वाक्यपदम्, वाक्यपदीयम्, वाक्यपद्धतिः, वाक्यपरिसमाप्तिः, वाक्यप्रबन्धः, वाक्यप्रयोगः, वाक्यभेदः, वाक्यरचना, वाक्यविन्यासः, वाक्यविलेखः, वाक्यविशारद, वाक्यशेषः, वाक्यसारथिः, वाक्यस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्याडम्बरः|वाक्याडम्बर
वाक्यम् + -आडम्बरः bombastic language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यार्थः|वाक्यार्थ
वाक्यम् + -अर्थः<BR>—1 the meaning of a sentence.<BR>—2 (in Mīmāṃsā) the sense of a sentence derived on the strength of<BR> वाक्यप्रमाण as distinguished from श्रुति, लिङ्ग and other प्रमाणs.<BR> This is weaker than and hence sublated by the श्रुत्यर्थ or श्रुति;<BR> यत्र श्रुत्यर्थो न संभवति तत्र वाक्यार्थो गृह्यते ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 14;<BR> वाक्यार्थः श्रुत्या बाध्यते ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 14. According to Mīmāṃsā<BR> view the अर्थs of पदs are सामान्य and when these form a<BR> sentence to yield the वाक्यार्थ, they get restricted or modified. Hence<BR> वाक्यार्थ means the पदार्थs modified or restricted; सामान्येनाभिप्रवृत्तानां<BR> पदार्थानां यद्विशेषेऽवस्थानं स वाक्यार्थः ŚB. on MS. 3. 1. 12. ˚उपमा<BR> a variety of Upamā according to Daṇḍin; वाक्यार्थेनैव वाक्यार्थः कोऽपि<BR> यद्युपमीयते । एकानेकेवशब्दत्वात् सा वाक्यार्थोपमा द्विधा ॥ Kāv. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यालापः|वाक्यालाप
वाक्यम् + -आलापः conversation, discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्योपचारः|वाक्योपचार
वाक्यम् + -उपचारः speaking; Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यखण्डनम्
वाक्यम् + -खण्डनम् refutation of an assertion or argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यग्रहः|वाक्यग्रह
वाक्यम् + -ग्रहः paralysis of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यपदम्
वाक्यम् + -पदम् a word in a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यपदीयम्
वाक्यम् + -पदीयम् N. of a work attributed to Bhartṛhari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यपद्धतिः|वाक्यपद्धति
वाक्यम् + -पद्धतिः <i>f.</i> the manner of composing sentences, diction, style.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यपरिसमाप्तिः
वाक्यम् + -परिसमाप्तिः <i>f.</i> Completion of a sentence (<i>i. e.</i> the application<BR> of the sense expressed by a sentence). This occurs in two ways: (i) the<BR> sense of the sentence as a whole may be predicated of the things or persons<BR> mentioned in the उद्देशपद severally; or (ii) it may be predicated<BR> of them all combined together. The former is known as प्रत्येकं वाक्यपरिसमाप्तिः<BR> and is illustrated by देवदत्तयज्ञदत्तविष्णुमित्रा भोज्यन्ताम्; while<BR> the latter is known as समुदाये वाक्यपरिसमाप्तिः and illustrated<BR> by गर्गाः शतं दण्ड्यन्ताम्; see ŚB. on MS. 3. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यप्रबन्धः|वाक्यप्रबन्ध|वाक्यप्रबंध
वाक्यम् + -प्रबन्धः<BR>—1 a treatise, connected composition.<BR>—2 the flow of sentences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यप्रयोगः|वाक्यप्रयोग
वाक्यम् + -प्रयोगः employment of speech, use of language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यभेदः|वाक्यभेद
वाक्यम् + -भेदः a different assertion, a divergent statement; संदिग्धे<BR> तु व्यवायाद् वाक्यभेदः स्यात् MS. 3. 1. 21; वाक्यभेदान् बहूनगमत् Mu. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यरचना
वाक्यम् + -रचना, -विन्यासः arrangement of words in a sentence, syntax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविन्यासः|वाक्यविन्यास
वाक्यम् + -रचना, -विन्यासः arrangement of words in a sentence, syntax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविलेखः
वाक्यम् + -विलेखः An officer in charge of writing of accounts, orders etc.; ततो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">Page1407-1</a>]<BR> वाक्यविलेखाख्यैर्दत्तोपन्तैः स्वशक्तितः Parṇāl. 4. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1406-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यविशारद
वाक्यम् + -विशारद <i>a.</i> eloquent, skilled in speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यशेषः|वाक्यशेष
वाक्यम् + -शेषः<BR>—1 the remainder of a speech, an unfinished or incomplete sentence; सदोषावकाश<BR> इव ते वाक्यशेषः V. 3.<BR>—2 an elliptical sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यसारथिः|वाक्यसारथि
वाक्यम् + -सारथिः Spokesman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्यस्थ
वाक्यम् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> Obsequious; attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागरः|वागर
वागरः<BR>—1 A sage, holy man.<BR>—2 A learned Brāhmaṇa, scholar.<BR>—3 A brave man, hero.<BR>—4 A touchstone, whet-stone.<BR>—5 An impediment, obstacle.<BR>—6 Certainty, determination.<BR>—7 Submarine fire.<BR>—8 A wolf.<BR>—9 A water-vessel; L. D. B.<BR>—10 A horse of the sun; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागा
वागा A bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागारु|वागारुः
वागारु <i>a.</i> Breaking oneʼs promises, perfidious, faithless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागाशनिः|वागाशनि
वागाशनिः A Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरा
वागुरा [वा-हिंसने उरच् गन् च Uṇ. 1. 40] A trap, net, snare,<BR> toils, meshes; को वा दुर्जनवागुरासु पतितः क्षेमेण यातः पुमान् Pt. 1. 146.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वागुरावृत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरावृत्तिः|वागुरावृत्ति
वागुरा + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> livelihood obtained by catching wild animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरावृत्तिः|वागुरावृत्ति
वागुरा + -वृत्तिः + .({@-त्तिः@}) a fowler, huntsman; Ms. 10. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुरिकः|वागुरिक
वागुरिकः A fowler, hunter, deer-catcher; श्वगणिवागुरिकैः प्रथमास्थितम् R. 9. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्मिन्
वाग्मिन् <i>a.</i> [वाच् अस्त्यर्थे ग्मिनिः चस्य कः तस्य लोपः; cf. P. V. 2. 124]<BR>—1 Eloquent, oratorical.<BR>—2 Talkative.<BR>—3 Verbose, wordy. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An orator, an eloquent man; अनिर्लोडितकार्यस्य वाग्जालं वाग्मिनो वृथा<BR> Śi. 2. 27, 109; Ki. 14. 6; Pt. 3. 87.<BR>—2 N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—4 A parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्य|वाग्यः
वाग्य <i>a.</i> [वाचं यच्छति, यम्-ड]<BR>—1 Speaking little, speaking cautiously.<BR>—2 Speaking truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यः|वाग्य
वाग्य + .{@-ग्यः@}<BR>—1 Modesty, humility.<BR>—2 Doubt, alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यतस्
वाग्यतस् <i>ind.</i> Silently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्कः|वाङ्क|वांक|वांकः
वाङ्कः The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्क्ष्|वांक्ष्
वाङ्क्ष् €1 P. (वाङ्क्षति) To wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्
वाच् <i>f.</i> [वच्-क्विप् दीर्घोऽसंप्रसारणं च Uṇ. 2. 67]<BR>—1 A word, sound, an expression (opp. अर्थ); वागर्थाविव संपृक्तौ<BR> वागर्थप्रतिपत्तये R. 1. 1.<BR>—2 Words, talk, language, speech; वाचि पुण्यापुण्यहेतवः Māl. 4;<BR> लौकिकानां हि साधूनामर्थं वागनुवर्तते । ऋषीणां पुनराद्यानां वाचमर्थोऽनुधावति<BR> U. 1. 10; विनिश्चितार्थामिति वाचमाददे Ki. 1. 3 ‘spoke these words’,<BR> ‘spoke as follows’; R. 1. 49; Śi. 2. 13, 23; Ku. 2. 3.<BR>—3 A voice, sound; अशरीरिणी वागुदचरत् U. 2; मनुष्यवाचा R. 2. 33.<BR>—4 An assertion, a statement.<BR>—5 An assurance, a promise.<BR>—6 A phrase, proverb, saying.<BR>—7 N. of Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वागपहारकः, वागपेत, वागर्थः, वागसिः, वागाडम्बरः, वागात्मन्, वागीशः, वागीश्वरः, वागुत्तरम्, वागृषभः, वाक्कलहः, वाक्कीरः, वाक्केलिः, वाक्केली, वाग्गुदः, वाग्गुणः, वाग्गुम्फः, वाग्गुलिः, वाग्गुलिकः, वाक्चपल, वाक्चापल्यम्, वाक्छलम्, वाग्जालम्, वाग्जीवनः, वाग्डम्बरः, वाग्दण्डः, वाग्दत्त, वाग्दरिद्र, वाग्दलम्, वाग्दानम्, वाग्दुष्ट, वाग्देवता, वाग्देवी, वाग्दोषः, वाङ्निबन्धन, वाङ्निमित्तम्, वाङ्निश्चयः, वाङ्निष्ठा, वाक्पटु, वाक्पति, वाक्पथः, वाक्पाटवम्, वाक्पारीणः, वाक्पारुष्यम्, वाक्प्रचोदनम्, वाक्प्रतोदः, वाक्प्रलापः, वाग्बन्धनम्, वाग्भट, वाङ्मनस, वाङ्मात्रम्, वाङ्मुखम्, वाग्यत, वाग्यमः, वाग्यामः, वाग्युद्धम्, वाग्रोधः, वाग्वज्रः, वाग्विद्, वाग्विदग्ध, वाग्विनिःसृत, वाग्विभवः, वाग्विलासः, वाग्विलासिन्, वाग्विस्तरः, वाग्वीरः, वाग्व्ययः, वाग्व्यवहारः, वाग्व्यापारः, वाक्छलाका, वाक्छल्यम्, वाक्संतक्षणम्, वाक्संयमः, वाक्सारः, वाक्सिद्धम्, वाक्स्तम्भः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागपहारकः|वागपहारक
वाच् + -अपहारकः (वागपहारकः)<BR>—1 a ‘stealer of speech’, a reader of prohibited texts; Ms. 11. 51.<BR>—2 a liar (मिथ्यावादी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागपेत
वाच् + -अपेत (वागपेत) <i>a.</i> dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागर्थः|वागर्थ
वाच् + -अर्थः (वागर्थः) a word and its<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">Page1407-2</a>]<BR> meaning; वागर्थाविव संपृक्तौ R. 1. 1; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागसिः|वागसि
वाच् + -असिः cutting speech (cutting like a sword); स्फुरन्नसाधोर्विवृणोति<BR> वागसिः Ki. 14. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागाडम्बरः|वागाडम्बर|वागाडंबर
वाच् + -आडम्बरः (वागाडम्बरः) verbosity, bombast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागात्मन्
वाच् + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> (वागात्मन्) consisting of words; ऋषे प्रबुद्धोऽसि<BR> वागात्मनि ब्रह्मणि U. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीशः|वागीश
वाच् + -ईशः (वागीशः)<BR>—1 an orator, an eloquent man.<BR>—2 an epithet of Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods; वागीशाद्याः<BR> सुमनसः Nyāyamālā.<BR>—3 an epithet of Brahman; वागीशं (धातारं) वाग्भिरर्थ्याभिः प्रणिपत्योपतस्थिरे Ku. 2. 3.<BR>—4 the lunar mansion called Puṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीशा
वाच् + -ईशः + .({@-शा@}) N. of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीश्वरः|वागीश्वर
वाच् + -ईश्वरः (वागीश्वरः)<BR>—1 an orator, eloquent man.<BR>—2 an epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागीश्वरी
वाच् + -ईश्वरः + .({@-री@}) Sarasvatī, the goddess of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागुत्तरम्
वाच् + -उत्तरम् (वागुत्तरम्) end of a speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वागृषभः|वागृषभ
वाच् + -ऋषभः (वागृषभः) ‘eminent in speech’, an eloquent or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्कलहः|वाक्कलह
वाच् + -कलहः (वाक्कलहः) a quarrel, strife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्कीरः|वाक्कीर
वाच् + -कीरः (वाक्कीरः) a wifeʼs brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्केलिः|वाक्केलि
वाच् + -केलिः, -केली (वाक्केलिः, -ली) witty conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्केली
वाच् + -केलिः, -केली (वाक्केलिः, -ली) witty conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुदः|वाग्गुद
वाच् + -गुदः (वाग्गुदः) a kind of bird; Ms. 12. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुणः|वाग्गुण
वाच् + -गुणः (वाग्गुणः) a merit or excellence of speech; (35<BR> such merits are enumerated by Hemacandra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुम्फः|वाग्गुम्फ
वाच् + -गुम्फः (pl.) artificial language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुलिः|वाग्गुलि
वाच् + -गुलिः, -गुलिकः (वाग्गुलिः &c.) the betel-bearer of a king &c.;<BR> cf. ताम्बूलकरङ्कवाहिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्गुलिकः|वाग्गुलिक
वाच् + -गुलिः, -गुलिकः (वाग्गुलिः &c.) the betel-bearer of a king &c.;<BR> cf. ताम्बूलकरङ्कवाहिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्चपल
वाच् + -चपल <i>a.</i> (वाक्चपल) chattering, frivolous or inconsiderate in talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्चापल्यम्
वाच् + -चापल्यम् (वाक्चापल्यम्) idle or frivolous talk, chattering, gossiping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छलम्
वाच् + -छलम् (वाक्छलम्) ‘dishonesty in words’, an evasive reply,<BR> a prevarication; एतावदेवास्ति मे वाक्छलम् Mu. 2; केनेदममृतं मे<BR> वाक्छलाद् वृष्टम् K. 330.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्जालम्
वाच् + -जालम् (वाग्जालम्) bombast, empty talk; अनिर्लोडितकार्यस्य<BR> वाग्जालं वाग्मिनो वृथा Śi. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्जीवनः|वाग्जीवन
वाच् + -जीवनः (वाग्जीवनः) a buffoon; Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्डम्बरः|वाग्डम्बर|वाग्डंबर
वाच् + -डम्बरः (वाग्डम्बरः)<BR>—1 bombast.<BR>—2 eloquent language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दण्डः|वाग्दण्ड|वाग्दंड
वाच् + -दण्डः (वाग्दण्डः)<BR>—1 reproachful words, reprimand, reproof.<BR>—2 restraint of speech, control over words; cf. त्रिदण्ड Ms. 12. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दत्त
वाच् + -दत्त (वाग्दत्त) <i>a.</i> promised, affianced, betrothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दत्ता
वाच् + -दत्त + .({@-त्ता@}) an affianced or betrothed virgin; Kull. on Ms. 5. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दरिद्र|वाग्दरिद्रः
वाच् + -दरिद्र (वाग्दरिद्र) <i>a.</i> ‘poor in words’, <i>i. e.</i><BR> speaking little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दलम्
वाच् + -दलम् (वाग्दलम्) a lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दानम्
वाच् + -दानम् (वाग्दानम्) betrothal; Ms. 5. 72 (Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दुष्ट|वाग्दुष्टः
वाच् + -दुष्ट <i>a.</i> (वाग्दुष्ट)<BR>—1 abusive, scurrilous, using abusive words; Ms. 8. 345.<BR>—2 using ungrammatical language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दुष्टः|वाग्दुष्ट
वाच् + -दुष्ट + .({@-ष्टः@})<BR>—1 a defamer.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa not invested with the sacred thread at the proper time of his life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्देवता
वाच् + -देवता, -देवी (वाग्देवता, वाग्देवी) Sarasvatī, the goddess of<BR> speech; वाग्देवतायाः सांमुख्यमाधत्ते S. D. 1. ˚कुलम् science, learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्देवी
वाच् + -देवता, -देवी (वाग्देवता, वाग्देवी) Sarasvatī, the goddess of<BR> speech; वाग्देवतायाः सांमुख्यमाधत्ते S. D. 1. ˚कुलम् science, learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्दोषः|वाग्दोष
वाच् + -दोषः (वाग्दोषः)<BR>—1 the utterance of a (disagreeable) sound; द्वीपिचर्मपरिच्छन्नो वाग्दोषाद्<BR> गर्दभो हतः H. 3.<BR>—2 abuse, defamation.<BR>—3 an ungrammatical speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्निबन्धन
वाच् + -निबन्धन (वाग्निबन्धन) <i>a.</i> depending on words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्निमित्तम्
वाच् + -निमित्तम् (वाङ्निमित्तम्) Prognostications; तच्चाकर्ण्य<BR> वाङ्निमित्तज्ञः पितरि सुतरां जीविताशां शिथिलीचकार Hc. V.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्निश्चयः|वाङ्निश्चय
वाच् + -निश्चयः (वाङ्निश्चयः) affiance by word of mouth, marriage contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्निष्ठा
वाच् + -निष्ठा (वाङ्निष्ठा) faithfulness (to oneʼs word or promise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पटु
वाच् + -पटु <i>a.</i> (वाक्पटु) skilful in speech, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पति|वाक्पतिः
वाच् + -पति <i>a.</i> (वाक्पति) eloquent; oratorical.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">Page1408-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पतिः|वाक्पति
वाच् + -पति + .({@-तिः@})<BR>—1 N. of Bṛhaspati (in this sense वाचसांपतिः is also used).<BR>—2 the constellation Puṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1407-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पथः|वाक्पथ
वाच् + -पथः (वाक्पथः)<BR>—1 a moment fit for speech.<BR>—2 the range of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पाटवम्
वाच् + -पाटवम् (वाक्पाटवम्) eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पारीणः
वाच् + -पारीणः (वाक्पारीणः) beyond the range of speech; वाक्पारीणरुचिः<BR> स चेन्मुखमयं पद्मः प्रिये तावकम् N. 22. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्पारुष्यम्
वाच् + -पारुष्यम् (वाक्पारुष्यम्)<BR>—1 severity of language.<BR>—2 violence in words, abusive or scurrilous language, defamation; एवं<BR> दण्डविधिः प्रोक्तो वाक्पारुष्यस्य तत्त्वतः Ms. 8. 278.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्प्रचोदनम्
वाच् + -प्रचोदनम् (वाक्प्रचोदनम्) an order expressed in words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्प्रतोदः|वाक्प्रतोद
वाच् + -प्रतोदः (वाक्प्रतोदः) ‘the goad of words’, goading<BR> or taunting language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्प्रलापः|वाक्प्रलाप
वाच् + -प्रलापः (वाक्प्रलापः) eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्बन्धनम्
वाच् + -बन्धनम् (वाग्बन्धनम्) stopping the speech, silencing;<BR> व्रीडार्ता प्रकरोति दाडिमफलव्याजेन वाग्बन्धनम् Amaru. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्भट
वाच् + -भट (वाग्भटः) N. of a writer on medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मनस्
वाच् + -मनस्^1 <i>n.</i> (the dual<BR> वाङ्मनसी in Vedic language) speech and mind; अथैनं तुष्टुवुः<BR> स्तुत्यमवाङ्मनसगोचरम् R. 10. 15; अतीतः पन्थानं तव च महिमा<BR> वाङ्मनसयोः Śivamahimna 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मात्रम्
वाच् + -मात्रम् (वाङ्मात्रम्) mere words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मुखम्
वाच् + -मुखम् (वाङ्मुखम्) the beginning or introduction of a speech,<BR> an exordium, a preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यत|वाग्यतः
वाच् + -यत <i>a.</i> (वाग्यत) one who has controlled or curbed<BR> his speech, silent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यमः|वाग्यम
वाच् + -यमः (वाग्यमः) one who has controlled his speech, a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्यामः|वाग्याम
वाच् + -यामः (वाग्यामः) a dumb man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्युद्धम्
वाच् + -युद्धम् (वाग्युद्धम्) a war of words, (hot) debate or discussion, controversy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्रोधः|वाग्रोध
वाच् + -रोधः (वाग्रोधः) stopping the speech, silencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्वज्रः|वाग्वज्र
वाच् + -वज्रः (वाग्वज्रः)<BR>—1 adamantine words; अहह दारुणो वाग्वज्रः U. 1.<BR>—2 harsh or severe language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विद्
वाच् + -विद् <i>a.</i> (वाग्विद्) eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विदग्ध
वाच् + -विदग्ध <i>a.</i> (वाग्विदग्ध) skilled in speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विदग्धा
वाच् + -विदग्ध + .({@-ग्धा@}) a sweet-speaking or fascinating woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विनिःसृत
वाच् + -विनिःसृत <i>a.</i> (वाग्विनिःसृत) put forth by speech;<BR> वाच्यर्था नियताः सर्वे वाङ्मूला वाग्विनिःसृताः । तां तु यः स्तेनयेद्वाचं<BR> स सर्वस्तेयकृन्नरः ॥ Ms. 4. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विभवः|वाग्विभव
वाच् + -विभवः (वाग्विभवः) stock or provision of words, power<BR> of description, command of language; नास्ति मे वाग्विभवः प्रशंसितुम्<BR> V. 3; रघूणामन्वयं वक्ष्ये तनुवाग्विभवोऽपि सन् R. 1. 9; Māl. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विलासः|वाग्विलास
वाच् + -विलासः (वाग्विलासः) graceful or elegant speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विलासिन्
वाच् + -विलासिन् <i>m.</i> (वाग्विलासिन्) pigeon, dove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्विस्तरः|वाग्विस्तर
वाच् + -विस्तरः (वाग्विस्तरः) prolixity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्वीरः|वाग्वीर
वाच् + -वीरः (वाग्वीरः) master of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्व्ययः|वाग्व्यय
वाच् + -व्ययः (वाग्व्ययः) waste of breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्व्यवहारः|वाग्व्यवहार
वाच् + -व्यवहारः (वाग्व्यवहारः) verbal or oral discussion;<BR> प्रयोगप्रधानं हि नाट्यशास्त्रं किमत्र वाग्व्यवहारेण M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाग्व्यापारः|वाग्व्यापार
वाच् + -व्यापारः (वाग्व्यापारः)<BR>—1 the manner of speaking.<BR>—2 the style or habit of speaking.<BR>—3 customary phraseology or mode of talking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छलाका
वाच् + -शलाका (वाक्शलाका) injurious speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्छल्यम्
वाच् + -शल्यम् (वाक्शल्यम्) = वाक्शलाका. {@-शस्त्रम्@} (वाक्शस्त्रम्)<BR> a curse; वाक्शस्त्रं वै ब्राह्मणस्य तेन हन्यादरीन्<BR> द्विजः Ms. 11. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्संतक्षणम्
वाच् + -संतक्षणम् sarcastic remarks; असारस्य वाक्संतक्षणैः …<BR> अपवाहनम् Dk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्संयमः|वाक्संयम
वाच् + -संयमः (वाक्संयमः), {@-संवरः@}, (वाक्संवरः) restraint or control of speech.<BR> {@-संगः@} (वाक्संगः)<BR>—1 impeded or slow speech.<BR>—2 paralysis of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्सारः|वाक्सार
वाच् + -सारः (वाक्सारः) eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्सिद्धम्
वाच् + -सिद्धम् (वाक्सिद्धम्) supernatural perfection of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाक्स्तम्भः|वाक्स्तम्भ
वाच् + -स्तम्भः (वाक्स्तम्भः) paralysis of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मय|वाङ्मयं
वाङ्मय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Consisting of words; लिपेर्यथावद्ग्रहणेन वाङ्मयं नदीमुखेनेव<BR> समुद्रमाविशत् R. 3. 28; इत्येषा वाङ्मयी पूजा श्रीमच्छंकरपादयोः<BR> Śivamahimna 40.<BR>—2 Relating to speech or words; Ms. 12. 6; स्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं चैव वाङ्मयं<BR> तप उच्यते Bg. 17. 15.<BR>—3 Endowed with speech; अयमात्मा वाङ्मयो मनोमयः प्राणमयः Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 3.<BR>—4 Eloquent, rhetorical, oratorical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मयम्
वाङ्मय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 Speech, language; म्यरस्तजभ्नगैर्लान्तैरेभिर्दशभिरक्षरैः । समस्तं<BR> वाङ्मयं व्याप्तं त्रैलोक्यमिव विष्णुना Chand. M. 1. 7; द्विधाप्रयुक्तेन<BR> च वाङ्मयेन सरस्वती तन्मिथुनं नुनाव Ku. 7. 90; Śi. 2. 72.<BR>—2 Eloquence.<BR>—3 Rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाङ्मयी
वाङ्मय + .{@-यी@} The goddess Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचः|वाच|वाचं
वाचः<BR>—1 A kind of fish.<BR>—2 The plant मदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचंयम|वाचंयमः
वाचंयम <i>a.</i> Holding the tongue, maintaining perfect silence,<BR> silent, taciturn; उपस्थिता देवी तद्वाचंयमो भव V. 3; विद्वांसो<BR> वसुधातले परवचःश्लाघासु वाचंयमाः Bv. 4. 42; वाचंयमत्वात् R. 13. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचंयमः|वाचंयम
वाचंयम + .{@-मः@} A sage who maintains rigid silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचक|वाचकः
वाचक <i>a.</i> [वच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Speaking, declaring, explanatory; उन्नीय मे दर्शय वल्गुवाचकं<BR> यद्व्रीडया नाभिमुखं शुचिस्मिते Bhāg. 4. 25. 31.<BR>—2 Expressing, signifying, denoting directly (as a word, distinguished<BR> from लाक्षणिक and व्यञ्जक); साक्षात् संकेतितं योऽर्थमभिधत्ते<BR> स वाचकः K. P. 2.<BR>—3 Verbal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचकः|वाचक
वाचक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A speaker.<BR>—2 A reader.<BR>—3 A significant word.<BR>—4 A messenger.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाचकपदम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचकपदम्
वाचक + -पदम् a significant word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचक्नवी
वाचक्नवी N. of a preceptress (गार्गी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनम्
वाचनम् [वच्-णिच् स्वार्थे वा णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Reading, reciting.<BR>—2 Declaration, proclamation, utterance; as in स्वस्तिवाचनम्, पुण्याहवाचनम् qq. vv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचना
वाचनम् + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 A lesson.<BR>—2 A chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनकम्
वाचनकम्<BR>—1 A riddle.<BR>—2 A kind of sweetmeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचनिक
वाचनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [वचनेन निर्वृत्तं ठक्]<BR>—1 Verbal, expressed by words.<BR>—2 As expressed by the text (वचन); तस्माद् वाचनिक एषां क्रमः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचयितृ
वाचयितृ <i>a.</i> The director of a recitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पतिः|वाचस्पति
वाचस्पतिः [वाचः पतिः षष्टपलुक्]<BR>—1 ‘The lord of speech’, an epithet of Bṛhaspati, preceptor of the gods;<BR> अविज्ञातप्रबन्धस्य वचो वाचस्पतेरपि । व्रजत्यफलताम् Ki. 11. 43;<BR> also वाचसांपतिः.<BR>—2 The constellation Puṣya.<BR>—3 An orator.<BR>—4 The Veda; ततो वाचस्पतिर्जज्ञे तं मनः पर्यवेक्षते Mb. 14. 21. 9.<BR>—5 N. of a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचस्पत्यम्
वाचस्पत्यम् An eloquent speech, oration, a harangue; तदूरीकृत्य<BR> कृतिभिर्वाचस्पत्यं प्रतायते H. 3. 89 (= Śi. 2. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचा
वाचा<BR>—1 Speech.<BR>—2 A sacred text, a text or aphorism.<BR>—3 An oath.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाचाविरुद्ध, वाचासहायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाविरुद्ध
वाचा + -विरुद्ध <i>a.</i> not describable with words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचासहायः|वाचासहाय
वाचा + -सहायः a sociable companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाट|वाचाटः
वाचाट <i>a.</i> [वाच्-आटच् चस्य न कः]<BR>—1 Talkative, garrulous; talking much or idly; अरेरे वाचाट Ve. 3;<BR> Mv. 6; Bk. 5. 23.<BR>—2 Boastful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1408-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचाल|वाचालः
वाचाल <i>a.</i> [वाच्-आलच् चस्य न कः]<BR>—1 Noisy, making a sound, crying.<BR>—2 Talkative, garrulous; see वाचाट; तथापि वाचालतया युनक्ति मां मिथस्त्वदाभाषणलोलुपं<BR> मनः Śi. 1. 40.<BR>—3 Boasting, swaggering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचालना
वाचालना The act of making talkative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिक|वाचिकं|वाचिकः
वाचिक <i>a.</i> (-का, -की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [वाचा कृतं वाच्-ठक् चस्य न कः]<BR>—1 Consisting of or expressed by words; वाचिकं पारुष्यम्.<BR>—2 Oral, verbal, expressed by word of mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकः|वाचिक|वाचिकं
वाचिक + .{@-कः@} A declamatory speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकम्
वाचिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A message, an oral or verbal communication; वाचिकमप्यार्येण सिद्धार्थकाच्छ्रोतव्यमिति<BR> लिखितम् Mu. 5; निर्धारितेऽर्थे लेखेन खलूक्त्वा खलु वाचिकम् Śi. 2. 70;<BR> तव क्रीतसुतोऽस्मीति वाचिकेन व्यजिज्ञपत् Śiva B. 31. 32.<BR>—2 News, tidings, intelligence in general.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाचिकपत्रम्, वाचिकहारकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकपत्रम्
वाचिक + -पत्रम्<BR>—1 A letter.<BR>—2 A newspaper.<BR>—3 A written agreement, contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिकहारकः|वाचिकहारक
वाचिक + -हारकः<BR>—1 a letter.<BR>—2 a messenger, news-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचिन्
वाचिन् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Expressing, indicating, signifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचोयुक्ति|वाचोयुक्तिः
वाचोयुक्ति <i>a.</i> Skilled in speech, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाचोयुक्तिः|वाचोयुक्ति
वाचोयुक्ति + .{@-क्तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 ‘Arrangement of words’, a declaration, announcement, speech; यत्र<BR> खल्वियं वाचोयुक्तिः Māl. 1.<BR>—2 Good or clever speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्य|वाच्यं
वाच्य <i>a.</i> [वच्-कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be spoken, told or said, to be spoken to or addressed; वाच्यस्त्वया<BR> मद्वचनात् स राजा R. 14. 61 ‘say to the king in my name’; न वाच्यमित्थं<BR> पुरुषोत्तम त्वया Śi. 1. 31.<BR>—2 To be predicated, attributive.<BR>—3 Expressed (as the meaning of a word); cf. लक्ष्य and व्यङ्ग्य.<BR>—4 Blamable, censurable, reprehensible; अप्रदाता पिता वाच्यो वाच्यश्चानुपयन्<BR> पतिः । मृते भर्तरि पुत्रश्च वाच्यो मातुररक्षिता ॥ Mb. 3. 293. 35;<BR> Śi. 20. 34; एभिर्मुक्तो महीपालः प्राप्नोति खलु वाच्यताम् H. 3. 129, 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यम्
वाच्य + .{@-च्यम्@}<BR>—1 Blame, censure, reproach; प्रमदामनु संस्थितः शुचा नृपतिः सन्निति<BR> वाच्यदर्शनात् R. 8. 72, 84; चिरस्य वाच्यं न गतः प्रजापतिः Ś. 5. 15;<BR> Śi. 3. 58.<BR>—2 The expressed meaning, that derived by means of अभिधा q. v.; cf.<BR> लक्ष्य and व्यङ्ग्य; अपि तु वाच्यवैचित्र्यप्रतिभासादेव चारुताप्रतीतिः K. P. 10.<BR>—3 A predicate.<BR>—4 The voice of a verb.<BR>—5 A subject for expounding (प्रतिपाद्य-विषय); पुराणसंख्यासंभूतिमस्य<BR> वाच्यप्रयोजने Bhāg. 12. 13. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाच्यार्थः, वाच्यचित्रम्, वाच्यलिङ्ग, वाच्यवज्रम्, वाच्यवर्जितम्, वाच्यवाचकभाव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यार्थः|वाच्यार्थ
वाच्य + -अर्थः expressed meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यचित्रम्
वाच्य + -चित्रम् one of the two kinds of the third or lowest (अधम)<BR> division of <i>Kāvya</i> or poetry, in which the charm lies in the expression<BR> of a striking or fanciful idea (opp. शब्दचित्र); see चित्र also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यलिङ्ग
वाच्य + -लिङ्ग <i>a.</i> adjectival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यवज्रम्
वाच्य + -वज्रम् severe or harsh language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यवर्जितम्
वाच्य + -वर्जितम् an elliptical expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यवाचकभाव
वाच्य + -वाचकभाव the state of the signified and the signifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यता
वाच्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Blame, censure, reproach; सत्यं शौर्यं दया त्यागो नृपस्यैते महागुणाः ।<BR> एभिर्मुक्तो महीपालः प्राग्नोति खलु वाच्यताम् ॥ H. 3. 122.<BR>—2 Ill-repute, infamy.<BR>—3 Conjugation.<BR>—4 The being expressed or predicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाच्यत्वम्
वाच्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Blame, censure, reproach; सत्यं शौर्यं दया त्यागो नृपस्यैते महागुणाः ।<BR> एभिर्मुक्तो महीपालः प्राग्नोति खलु वाच्यताम् ॥ H. 3. 122.<BR>—2 Ill-repute, infamy.<BR>—3 Conjugation.<BR>—4 The being expressed or predicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजः|वाज|वाजं
वाजः [वज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A wing.<BR>—2 A feather.<BR>—3 The feather of an arrow; विचित्रवाजैर्निशितैः शिलीमुखैः Bhāg. 10. 59. 16.<BR>—4 Battle, conflict.<BR>—5 Sound.<BR>—6 Gain, reward.<BR>—7 N. of the month of चैत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजम्
वाजः + .{@-जम्@}<BR>—1 Clarified butter.<BR>—2 An oblation of rice offered at a Śrāddha or obsequial ceremony.<BR>—3 Food in general.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 A prayer or <i>mantra</i> with which a sacrifice is concluded.<BR>—6 A sacrifice.<BR>—7 Strength, power.<BR>—8 wealth.<BR>—9 Speed.<BR>—10 A month.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाजपेयः, वाजयम्, वाजभोजिन्, वाजवालः, वाजसनः, वाजसनिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजपेयः|वाजपेय|वाजपेयं
वाजः + -पेयः, -यम् N. of a particular sacrifice; Bhāg. 3. 12. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजयम्
वाजः + -पेयः, -यम् N. of a particular sacrifice; Bhāg. 3. 12. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजभोजिन्
वाजः + -भोजिन् <i>m.</i> (= -पेयः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजवालः|वाजवाल
वाजः + -वालः an emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनः|वाजसन
वाजः + -सनः<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनिः|वाजसनि
वाजः + -सनिः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 the food-giver (अन्नदाता); वरिष्ठ उग्रसेनानीः सत्यो वाजसनिर्गुहः Mb. 12. 43. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेयः|वाजसनेय
वाजसनेयः N. of Yājñavalkya, the author of the Vājasaneyi Samhitā<BR> or the Śukla Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेयिन्
वाजसनेयिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of the sage Yājñavalkya, the author and founder of the white or<BR> Śukla Yajurveda.<BR>—2 A follower of the white Yajurveda, one belonging to the sect of the Vājasaneyins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजसनेयिसंहिता
वाजसनेयिन् + .{@-संहिता@} the text of the शुक्लयजुर्वेद, ascribed to the Ṛṣi Yājñavalkya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजित
वाजित <i>a.</i> Feathered (as an arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिन्
वाजिन् <i>a.</i> [वाज-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>—1 Swift, quick.<BR>—2 Strong.<BR>—3 Winged; having anything for wings; मुष्णंस्तेज उपानीतस्तार्क्ष्येण<BR> स्तोत्रवाजिना Bhāg. 4. 7. 19. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A horse; न गर्दभा वाजिधुरं वहन्ति Mk. 4. 17; सत्यमतीत्य<BR> हरितो हरींश्च वर्तन्ते वाजिनः Ś. 1; R. 3. 43, 4. 25, 67; Śi. 18. 31.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR>—3 A follower of the Vājasaneyin branch of the Yajurveda; एतावदित्याह<BR> च वाजिनां श्रुतिः A. Rām. 7. 5. 21.<BR>—4 The sun; ऊर्ध्वपवित्रो वाजिनीव स्वमृतमस्मि T. Up. 1. 10.<BR>—5 N. of Indra, Bṛhaspati and other gods.<BR>—6 A bird; शूलव्यालसमाकीर्णां प्राणिवाजिनिषेविताम् Mb. 7. 14. 16.<BR>—7 The number ‘seven’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिनी
वाजिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A mare.<BR>—2 N. of Uṣas (dawn).<BR>—3 Food (Ved.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाजिगन्धः, वाजिदन्तः, वाजिदन्तकः, वाजिपृष्ठः, वाजिभक्षः, वाजिभूः, वाजिभूमिः, वाजिभोजनः, वाजिमेधः, वाजियोजकः, वाजिराजः, वाजिविष्ठा, वाजिशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिगन्धः|वाजिगन्ध
वाजिन् + -गन्धः Name of a tree, Physalis Flexuosa. (Mar. आसंध);<BR> Mātaṅga L. 11. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिदन्तः|वाजिदन्त
वाजिन् + -दन्तः, -दन्तकः Adhatoda Vasika (Mar. अडूळसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिदन्तकः|वाजिदन्तक
वाजिन् + -दन्तः, -दन्तकः Adhatoda Vasika (Mar. अडूळसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिपृष्ठः|वाजिपृष्ठ
वाजिन् + -पृष्ठः the globe-amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिभक्षः|वाजिभक्ष
वाजिन् + -भक्षः a chick-pea (Mar. चणा, हरभरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिभूः
वाजिन् + -भूः, -भूमिः a place abounding in horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिभूमिः|वाजिभूमि
वाजिन् + -भूः, -भूमिः a place abounding in horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिभोजनः|वाजिभोजन
वाजिन् + -भोजनः a kind of kidney-bean (Mar. मूग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिमेधः|वाजिमेध
वाजिन् + -मेधः a horse-sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजियोजकः|वाजियोजक
वाजिन् + -योजकः a driver, groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिराजः|वाजिराज
वाजिन् + -राजः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिविष्ठा
वाजिन् + -विष्ठा the Indian fig-tree (Mar. वड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिशाला
वाजिन् + -शाला a stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिनम्
वाजिनम्<BR>—1 Strength, heroism, prowess (Ved.).<BR>—2 A conflict.<BR>—3 The scum of curdled milk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाजिनन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजिनन्यायः
वाजिनम् + -न्यायः (Mīmāṃsā) The rule that of the various matters resulting<BR> from something, only the most important one is प्रयोजक while the<BR> rest are not प्रयोजक. This rule is established by जैमिनि and<BR> शबर discussing the text, MS. 4. 1. 22-24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजीकर
वाजीकर <i>a.</i> Stimulating amorous desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1409-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजीकरणम्
वाजीकरणम् Stimulating or exciting desire by aphrodisiacs; यद्<BR> द्रव्यं पुरुषं कुर्याद् वाजिवत्सुरतक्षमम् । तद्वाजीकरणं ख्यातम् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाजेभिस्
वाजेभिस् <i>ind.</i> (Ved.) Mightily, greatly; Rv. 1. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छ्|वांछ्
वाञ्छ् €1 P. (वाञ्छति, वाञ्छित)<BR>—1 To wish, desire; न संहतास्तस्य न भिन्नवृत्तयः प्रियाणि वाञ्छन्त्यसुभिः<BR> समीहितुम् Ki. 1. 19.<BR>—2 To seek for, pursue. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि, सम्@} to wish, desire or<BR> long for; समवाञ्छन्नथाऽऽशिषः Bk. 17. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छनम्
वाञ्छनम् Wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छा|वांछा
वाञ्छा A wish, desire, longing (usually with loc.); वाञ्छा सज्जनसंगमे<BR> Bh. 2. 62; Ki. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छित|वांछित|वाञ्छितं
वाञ्छित <i>p. p.</i> Wished, desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छितम्
वाञ्छित + .{@-तम्@} A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छिन्|वांछिन्
वाञ्छिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wishing.<BR>—2 Lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाञ्छिनी
वाञ्छिन् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 A libidinous woman.<BR>—2 A wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्
वाट् An exclamation uttered on making an oblation of butter &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट|वाटं|वाटः
वाट <i>a.</i> Made or consisting of the वट (Indian figtree) or<BR> its wood; क्षत्रियो वाटखादिरौ … दण्डानर्हन्ति धर्मतः Ms. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटः|वाट|वाटं
वाटः, -टम्<BR> [वट्-घञ्]<BR>—1 An enclosure, a piece of enclosed ground, court; स्ववाटकुक्कुटविजयहृष्टः<BR> Dk.; नीत्वा स्ववाटं कृतवत्यथोदयम् Bhāg. 10. 11. 20; विवेश … … मेघवाटम्<BR> Bhāg. so वेश˚, श्मशान˚ &c.<BR>—2 A garden, park, an orchard; Bhāg. 5. 5. 30.<BR>—3 A road.<BR>—4 The groin.<BR>—5 A sort of grain.<BR>—6 A district.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाटधानः, वाटशृङ्खला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटम्
वाटः, -टम्<BR> [वट्-घञ्]<BR>—1 An enclosure, a piece of enclosed ground, court; स्ववाटकुक्कुटविजयहृष्टः<BR> Dk.; नीत्वा स्ववाटं कृतवत्यथोदयम् Bhāg. 10. 11. 20; विवेश … … मेघवाटम्<BR> Bhāg. so वेश˚, श्मशान˚ &c.<BR>—2 A garden, park, an orchard; Bhāg. 5. 5. 30.<BR>—3 A road.<BR>—4 The groin.<BR>—5 A sort of grain.<BR>—6 A district.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाटधानः, वाटशृङ्खला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटधानः|वाटधान
वाटः + -धानः<BR>—1 the descendant of an outcast Brāhmaṇa by a Brāhmaṇa female; see Ms. 10. 21.<BR>—2 an officer who knows the disposition of his army.<BR>—3 a land-lord; Mb. 2. 49. 24 (com. वाटधानाः सस्यादिसंपन्नक्षेत्रादिवृत्तिमन्तः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटशृङ्खला
वाटः + -शृङ्खला a railing, fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटकः|वाटक
वाटकः, वाटिका<BR>—1 The site of a house.<BR>—2 An orchard, a garden; अये दक्षिणेन वृक्षवाटिकामालाप इव श्रूयते<BR> Ś. 1; so पुष्प˚, अशोक˚ &c.<BR>—3 A hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटिका
वाटकः, वाटिका<BR>—1 The site of a house.<BR>—2 An orchard, a garden; अये दक्षिणेन वृक्षवाटिकामालाप इव श्रूयते<BR> Ś. 1; so पुष्प˚, अशोक˚ &c.<BR>—3 A hut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाटी
वाटी<BR>—1 The site of a house.<BR>—2 A house, dwelling.<BR>—3 A court, an enclosure.<BR>—4 A garden, park, orchard; वाटीभुवि क्षितिभुजाम् Āśval. 5; Bhāg. 1. 6. 11.<BR>—5 A road.<BR>—6 The groin. —7 A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्य|वाट्यः
वाट्य <i>a.</i> Belonging to a park or garden.<BR>—2 Made of वट tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यः|वाट्य
वाट्य + .{@-ट्यः@} Fried barley; also वाट्टकः Mb. 8. 44. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाट्यपुष्पम्, वाट्यमण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यपुष्पम्
वाट्य + -पुष्पम्<BR>—1 sandal.<BR>—2 saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यपुष्पी
वाट्य + -पुष्पम् + .({@-ष्पी@}) the plant अतिबला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यमण्डः|वाट्यमण्ड
वाट्य + -मण्डः scum of fried barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्या
वाट्या, वाट्यालः, वाट्याली N. of the plant अतिबला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्यालः|वाट्याल
वाट्या, वाट्यालः, वाट्याली N. of the plant अतिबला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाट्याली
वाट्या, वाट्यालः, वाट्याली N. of the plant अतिबला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाड्
वाड् €1 Ā. (वाडते) To bathe, dive; cf. बाड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडः|वाड
वाडः An enclosure; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवः|वाडव|वाडवं
वाडवः [वडवाया अपत्यं वडवानां समूहो वा अण्]<BR>—1 Submarine fire.<BR>—2 A Brāhmaṇa; तस्मै बाडवाय प्रचुरतरं धनं दत्त्वा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">Page1410-2</a>]<BR> Dk. 1. 5.<BR>—3 A stud-horse.<BR>—4 N. of a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवः|वाडव|वाडवं
वाडवः + .{@-वः, -वम्@} The lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवम्
वाडवः + .{@-वः, -वम्@} The lower world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवम्
वाडवः + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 A stud or collection of mares.<BR>—2 A particular मुहूर्त.<BR>—3 A kind of coitus.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाडवाग्निः, वाडवानलः, वाडवहरणम्, वाडवहारकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवाग्निः|वाडवाग्नि
वाडवः + -अग्निः, -अनलः the submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवानलः|वाडवानल
वाडवः + -अग्निः, -अनलः the submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवहरणम्
वाडवः + -हरणम् the fodder given to a stud-horse; P. VI. 2. 65 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवहारकः|वाडवहारक
वाडवः + -हारकः a sea-monster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवेयः|वाडवेय
वाडवेयः [वडवा-ढक्]<BR>—1 A bull.<BR>—2 A stud-horse.<BR>—3 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडवेयौ
वाडवेयः + .{@-यौ@} (<i>m.</i> dual) The two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाडव्यम्
वाडव्यम् A collection of Brāhmaṇas; P. IV. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाढ
वाढ See बाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणः|वाण
वाणः<BR>—1 Sounding, sound; बाणैर्बाणैः समासक्तम् Ki. 15. 10.<BR>—2 An arrow; see बाण.<BR>—3 Music.<BR>—4 A harp with 100 strings.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाणशब्दः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणशब्दः|वाणशब्द
वाणः + -शब्दः the sound of a lute; नीहारे बाणशब्दे च Ms. 4. 113 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिः|वाणि
वाणिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Weaving.<BR>—2 A weaverʼs loom.<BR>—3 Speech, words.<BR>—4 N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>—5 A cloud.<BR>—6 Price, value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिजः|वाणिज
वाणिजः<BR>—1 A merchant.<BR>—2 The submarine fire.<BR>—3 The Libra sign of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिजिकः|वाणिजिक
वाणिजिकः<BR>—1 A merchant; Mb. 13. 126. 24; also वाणिजकः Ms. 3. 181.<BR>—2 A cheat, rogue.<BR>—3 The submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज्या
वाणिज्या, वाणिज्यम् Trade, traffic; धनमस्तीति वाणिज्यं<BR> किंचिदस्तीति कर्षणम् । सेवा न किंचिदस्तीति नाहमस्मीति साहसम् ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिज्यम्
वाणिज्या, वाणिज्यम् Trade, traffic; धनमस्तीति वाणिज्यं<BR> किंचिदस्तीति कर्षणम् । सेवा न किंचिदस्तीति नाहमस्मीति साहसम् ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणिनी
वाणिनी<BR>—1 A clever or intriguing woman.<BR>—2 A dancing girl, an actress.<BR>—3 A drunken woman (literally or figuratively), an amorous and wanton<BR> woman; यस्मिन् महीं शासति वाणिनीनां निद्रां विहारार्धपथे गतानाम् । वातोऽपि<BR> नास्रंसयदंशुकानि R. 6. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणी
वाणी<BR>—1 Speech, words, language; वाण्येका समलंकरोति पुरुषं या संस्कृता<BR> धार्यते Bh. 2. 19.<BR>—2 Power of speech.<BR>—3 Sound, voice; केका वाणी मयूरस्य Ak.; so आकाशवाणी.<BR>—4 A literary production, a work or composition; मद्वाणि मा कुरु विषादमनादरेण<BR> मात्सर्यमग्नमनसां सहसा खलानाम् Bv. 4. 41; U. 7. 20.<BR>—5 Praise.<BR>—6 Sarasavatī, the goddess of learning; तव करकमलस्थां स्फाटिकीमक्षमालां,<BR> नखकिरणविभिन्नां दाडिमीबीजबुद्धया । अनुलवमनुकर्षन् येन कीरो निषिद्धः,<BR> स भवतु मम भूत्यै वाणि ते मन्दहासः ॥.<BR>—7 Eloquent speech.<BR>—8 Music.<BR>—9 N. of a metre consisting only of long syllables.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाणीवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाणीवादः|वाणीवाद
वाणी + -वादः a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात्
वात् €10 P.<BR>—1 To blow.<BR>—2 To serve.<BR>—3 To go.<BR>—4 To make happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वात|वातः
वात <i>p. p.</i> [वा-क्त]<BR>—1 Blown.<BR>—2 Desired or wished for, solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातः|वात
वात + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Air, wind.<BR>—2 The god of wind, the deity presiding over wind.<BR>—3 Wind, as one of the three humours of the body.<BR>—4 Gout, rheumatism.<BR>—5 Inflammation of the joints.<BR>—6 A faithless lover (धृष्ट).<BR>—7 Wind emitted from the body; Mb.<BR>—8 Morbid<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">Page1411-1</a>]<BR> affection of the windy humour, flatulence.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वाताटः, वाताण्डः, वातातिसारः, वातादः, वाताध्वन्, वातायम्, वातायनः, वातायुः, वातारिः, वाताश्वः, वाताष्ठीला, वाताख्यम्, वातात्मजः, वाताप्यम्, वातामोदा, वातालिः, वाताली, वाताहत, वाताहतिः, वाताहार, वातोपसृष्ट, वातर्द्धिः, वातकण्टकः, वातकर्मन्, वातकुण्डलिका, वातकुम्भः, वातकेतुः, वातकेलिः, वातकोपन, वातक्षोभः, वातगामिन्, वातगुल्मः, वातघ्नी, वातचक्रम्, वातचटकः, वातजम्, वातज्वरः, वाततूलम्, वातथुडा, वातध्वजः, वातपटः, वातपण्डः, वातपातः, वातपित्तम्, वातपुत्रः, वातपोथः, वातपोथकः, वातप्रकोपः, वातप्रमी, वातप्रमेहः, वातप्रवाहिका, वातफुल्लान्त्रम्, वातमण्डली, वातमार्गः, वातमृगः, वातरक्तम्, वातशोणितम्, वातरङ्गः, वातरथः, वातरूषः, वातरेचकः, वातरोगः, वातव्याधिः, वातवस्तिः, वातवृद्धिः, वातवैरिन्, वातशीर्षम्, वातशूलम्, वातसंचारः, वातसह, वातसारथिः, वातस्कन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1410-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताटः|वाताट
वात + -अटः<BR>—1 an antelope (वातमृग).<BR>—2 a horse of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताण्डः|वाताण्ड|वातांड
वात + -अण्डः a disease of the testicles; वृषणौ दूषयेद्वायुः श्लेष्मणा<BR> यस्य संवृतः । तस्य मुष्कश्चलत्येको रोगो वाताण्डसंज्ञकः ॥ Mādhavakara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातातिसारः|वातातिसार
वात + -अतिसारः dysentery caused by some derangement or vitiation of<BR> the bodily wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातादः|वाताद
वात + -अदः the almond tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताध्वन्
वात + -अध्वन् <i>m.</i> an air hole, window; वाताध्वरोमविवरस्य च ते<BR> महित्वम् Bhāg. 10. 14. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायम्
वात + -अयम् a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायनः|वातायन|वातायनं
वात + -अयनः a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायनम्
वात + -अयनः + .({@-नम्@})<BR>—1 a window, an air-hole; कटाक्षैर्नारीणां कुवलयितवातायनमिव Māl. 2. 11;<BR> Ku. 7. 59; R. 6. 24, 13. 21.<BR>—2 a porch, portico.<BR>—3 a pavilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातायुः|वातायु
वात + -अयुः an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातारिः|वातारि
वात + -अरिः<BR>—1 the castor-oil tree.<BR>—2 N. of several plants:− शतमूली, शेफालिका, यवानी, भार्गी, स्नुही,<BR> विडंग, शूरण, जतुका &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताश्वः|वाताश्व
वात + -अश्वः a very fleet or swift horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताष्ठीला
वात + -अष्ठीला a hard globular swelling in the lower belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताख्यम्
वात + -आख्यम् a house with two halls (one looking south and the other east).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातात्मजः|वातात्मज
वात + -आत्मजः<BR>—1 N. of Hanumat; वातात्मजं वानरयूथमुख्यं श्रीरामदूतं शरणं<BR> प्रपद्ये Rāmarakṣā 33.<BR>—2 N. of Bhīmasena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताप्यम्
वात + -आप्यम्<BR>—1 fermentation.<BR>—2 Soma.<BR>—3 water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातामोदा
वात + -आमोदा musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातालिः|वातालि
वात + -आलिः, -आली <i>f.</i> a whirl-wind; एतेन वातालीपुञ्जितेन शुष्कपर्णपुटेन<BR> प्रच्छादयामि Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताली
वात + -आलिः, -आली <i>f.</i> a whirl-wind; एतेन वातालीपुञ्जितेन शुष्कपर्णपुटेन<BR> प्रच्छादयामि Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहत
वात + -आहत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 shaken by the wind.<BR>—2 affected by gout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहतिः|वाताहति
वात + -आहतिः <i>f.</i> a violent gust of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाताहार
वात + -आहार <i>a.</i> one who feeds only on air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातोपसृष्ट
वात + -उपसृष्ट <i>a.</i> rheumatic, gouty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातर्द्धिः|वातर्धि
वात + -ऋद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 excess of wind.<BR>—2 a mace, a club, stick tipped with iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकण्टकः|वातकण्टक
वात + -कण्टकः a particular pain in the ankle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकर्मन्|वातकर्म्मन्
वात + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> breaking wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुण्डलिका|वातकुंडलिका
वात + -कुण्डलिका scanty and painful flow of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकुम्भः|वातकुम्भ|वातकुंभ
वात + -कुम्भः the part of an elephantʼs forehead below the frontal sinuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकेतुः|वातकेतु
वात + -केतुः<BR>—1 dust.<BR>—2 cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकेलिः|वातकेलि
वात + -केलिः<BR>—1 amorous discourse, the low whispering of lovers.<BR>—2 the marks of finger-nails on the person of a lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातकोपन
वात + -कोपन <i>a.</i> exciting wind (in the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातक्षोभः|वातक्षोभ
वात + -क्षोभः disturbance of wind in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातगामिन्
वात + -गामिन् <i>m.</i> a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातगुल्मः|वातगुल्म
वात + -गुल्मः<BR>—1 a high wind, strong gale.<BR>—2 rheumatism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1411-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वातघ्नी
