वानायुः + -जः a Vānāyu horse <i>i. e.</i> a horse produced in the Vanāyu country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीरः|वानीर
वानीरः [वन्-ईरन् Uṇ. 4. 36] A sort of cane or ratan; वानीरमालिनी<BR> रम्या नदी पुलिनशोभिता Mb. 3. 95. 10; स्मरामि वानीरगृहेषु सुप्तः<BR> R. 13. 35; Me. 43; Māl. 9. 15; R. 13. 30, 16. 21; U. 2. 20; Mv. 5. 40;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">Page1413-2</a>]<BR> यमुनातीरवानीरनिकुञ्जे मन्दमास्थितम् Gīt.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वानीरजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीरजः|वानीरज|वानीरजं
वानीरः + -जः<BR>—1 the <i>Munja</i> grass.<BR>—2 Costus Speciosus (कुष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीरकः|वानीरक
वानीरकः The <i>Munja</i> grass, a kind of rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानेय|वानेयं
वानेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living or growing in a wood; प्रबृत्तमुदकं वायुं सर्वं वानेयमाश्रयेत्<BR> Mb. 14. 46. 12.<BR>—2 Relating or belonging to water; रक्तं शिरसि धार्यं तु तथा वानेयमित्यपि<BR> Mb. 13. 104. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानेयम्
वानेयम् N. of a fragrant grass (मुस्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्त|वांत|वान्तः
वान्त <i>p. p.</i> [वम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Vomited, spitted out; मलयभुजगवान्ता वान्ति वाताः कृतान्ताः Bv. 2. 28.<BR>—2 Emitted, ejected, effused.<BR>—3 Dropped; कयाचिदुद्वेष्टनवान्तमाल्यः R. 7. 6.<BR>—4 One who has vomited; वान्तो विरिक्तः स्नात्वा तु घृतप्राशनमाचरेत् Ms. 5. 144.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वान्तादः, वान्ताशिन्, वान्ताशिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तादः|वान्ताद|वांताद
वान्त + -अदः a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ताशिन्
वान्त + -अशिन्, -आशिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a foul-feeding demon.<BR>—2 a person who tells his गोत्र for obtaining food; न भोजनार्थं<BR> स्वे विप्रः कुलगोत्रे निवेदयेत् । भोजनार्थं हि ते शंसन्वान्ताशीत्युच्यते<BR> बुधैः ॥ Ms. 3. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ताशिन्
वान्त + -अशिन्, -आशिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a foul-feeding demon.<BR>—2 a person who tells his गोत्र for obtaining food; न भोजनार्थं<BR> स्वे विप्रः कुलगोत्रे निवेदयेत् । भोजनार्थं हि ते शंसन्वान्ताशीत्युच्यते<BR> बुधैः ॥ Ms. 3. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्ति|वांति|वान्तिः
वान्ति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Vomiting.<BR>—2 Ejecting, emitting.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वान्तिकृत्, वान्तिद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तिकृत्
वान्ति + -कृत्, -द <i>a.</i> emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तिद
वान्ति + -कृत्, -द <i>a.</i> emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्तीकृ
वान्तीकृ To reject, give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्य
वान्य <i>a.</i> Sylvan; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्या
वान्या A multitude of groves or woods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापः|वाप
वापः [वप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sowing seed.<BR>—2 Weaving.<BR>—3 Shaving, shearing; कृतवापो वसेद् गोष्ठे चर्मणा तेन संवृतः Ms. 11. 108.<BR>—4 A sower.<BR>—5 Seed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वापदण्डः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापदण्डः|वापदण्ड|वापदंड
वापः + -दण्डः a weaverʼs loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापनम्
वापनम्<BR>—1 Causing to sow.<BR>—2 Shaving; कृतवापनो निवसेद् ग्रामान्ते गोव्रजेऽपि वा Ms. 11. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापित|वापितं
वापित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sown.<BR>—2 Shaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापितम्
वापित + .{@-तम्@} A kind of corn; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापिः|वापि
वापिः, -पी <i>f.</i><BR> [वप्-इञ् वा ङीप्; Uṇ. 4. 125] A well, any large<BR> oblong or circular reservoir of water; कूपवापीजलानां च (हरणे)<BR> शुद्धिश्चान्द्रायणं स्मृतम् Ms. 11. 163; वापी चास्मिन् मरकतशिलाबद्धसोपानमार्गा Me. 78.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वापिजलम्, वापिविस्तीर्णम्, वापिहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापी
वापिः, -पी <i>f.</i><BR> [वप्-इञ् वा ङीप्; Uṇ. 4. 125] A well, any large<BR> oblong or circular reservoir of water; कूपवापीजलानां च (हरणे)<BR> शुद्धिश्चान्द्रायणं स्मृतम् Ms. 11. 163; वापी चास्मिन् मरकतशिलाबद्धसोपानमार्गा Me. 78.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वापिजलम्, वापिविस्तीर्णम्, वापिहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापिजलम्
वापिः + -जलम् (वापीजलम्) lake-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापिविस्तीर्णम्
वापिः + -विस्तीर्णम् a hole resembling a pond; Mk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापिहः|वापिह
वापिः + -हः the <i>Chātaka</i> bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापिका
वापिका = वापी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाप्यम्
वाप्यम् The Kuṣṭha tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम <i>a.</i> Left (opp. दक्षिण); विलोचनं दक्षिणमञ्जनेन संभाव्य<BR> तद्वञ्चितवामनेत्रा R. 7. 8; Me. 80, 98.<BR>—2 Being or situated on the left side; वामश्चायं नदति मधुरं चातकस्ते<BR> सगन्धः Me. 9; (वामेन is used adverbially in the same sense; <i>e. g.</i><BR> वामेनात्र वटस्तमध्वगजनः सर्वात्मना सेवते K. P. 10).<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Reverse, contrary, opposite, adverse, unfavourable; तदहो<BR> कामस्य वामा गतिः Gīt. 12; Māl. 9. 8; Bk. 6. 17.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Acting contrary, of an opposite nature; यान्त्येवं गृहिणीपदं<BR> युवतयो वामाः कुलस्याधयः Ś. 4. 18.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) Perverse, crooked-natured, refractory; Ś. 6.<BR>——(<i>d</i>) Coy (in love).<BR>——(<i>e</i>)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">Page1414-1</a>]<BR> Hard, cruel.<BR>—4 Vile, wicked, base low, bad; उवाच वामं चक्षुर्भ्यामभिवीक्ष्य दहन्निव<BR> Bhāg. 4. 2. 8; आसक्तास्तास्वमी मूढा वामशीला हि जन्तवः Ki. 11. 24.<BR>—5 Lovely, beautiful, charming; as in वामलोचना; वामोरू; वामभ्रूः वामस्वभाव q. v.<BR>—6 Short.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामः|वाम|वामं
वाम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 A sentient being, an animal.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Cupid, the god of love.<BR>—4 A snake.<BR>—5 An udder, a breast.<BR>—6 Prohibited or forbidden act or practice (as drinking wine).<BR>—7 The left hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामम्
वाम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth, possessions.<BR>—2 Any lovely or desirable thing.<BR>—3 Adversity, misfortune.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वामाङ्गी, वामाचारः, वाममार्गः, वामापीडनः, वामावर्तः, वामेतर, वामोरु, वामोरू, वामकुक्षिः, वामदृश्, वामदेवः, वामनयना, वामनी, वामनेत्रम्, वामभ्रूः, वामलोचना, वामशील, वामस्वभाव, वामहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1413-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाङ्गी
वाम + -अङ्गी <i>f.</i> a beautiful woman; वामाङ्गीकृतवामाङ्गि कुण्डलीकृतकुण्डलि Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामाचारः|वामाचार
वाम + -आचारः, -मार्गः the left-hand ritual or doctrine of the <i>Tantras</i>;<BR> the doctrine of resorting to मांस, मद्य, मत्स्य, मैथुन and मुद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाममार्गः|वाममार्ग
वाम + -आचारः, -मार्गः the left-hand ritual or doctrine of the <i>Tantras</i>;<BR> the doctrine of resorting to मांस, मद्य, मत्स्य, मैथुन and मुद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामापीडनः|वामापीडन
वाम + -आपीडनः the <i>Pilu</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामावर्तः|वामावर्त|वामावर्त्त
वाम + -आवर्तः —1 a conch-shell, the spiral of which runs from right to left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामेतर
वाम + -इतर <i>a.</i> right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामोरु
वाम + -ऊरु, -ऊरू <i>f.</i> a woman with handsome thighs; तदिदं विषहिष्यते<BR> कथं वद वामोरु चिताधिरोहणम् R. 8. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामोरू
वाम + -ऊरु, -ऊरू <i>f.</i> a woman with handsome thighs; तदिदं विषहिष्यते<BR> कथं वद वामोरु चिताधिरोहणम् R. 8. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामकुक्षिः|वामकुक्षि
वाम + -कुक्षिः left side of the abdomen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामदृश्
वाम + -दृश् <i>f.</i> a woman (with lovely eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामदेवः|वामदेव
वाम + -देवः<BR>—1 N. of a sage.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva; नाहं न यूयं यदृतां गतिं विदुर्न वामदेवः किमुतापरे<BR> सुराः Bhāg. 2. 6. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनयना
वाम + -नयना a fair-eyed woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनी
वाम + -नी <i>a.</i> bringing wealth; Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनेत्रम्
वाम + -नेत्रम् a mystical N. of the vowel ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामभ्रूः
वाम + -भ्रूः <i>f.</i> a beautiful-eyebrowed woman; केनेत्थं परमार्थतोऽर्थवदिव<BR> प्रेमास्ति वामभ्रुवाम् Pt. 1. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलोचना
वाम + -लोचना a woman with lovely eyes; विरूपाक्षस्य जयिनीस्ताः स्तुवे<BR> वामलोचनाः K. P. 10; R. 19. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामशील|वामशीलः
वाम + -शील <i>a.</i> of a perverse or crooked nature; cross-tempered;<BR> तदेहि वामशीलां मालतीं निर्भर्त्सयामः Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामशीलः|वामशील
वाम + -शील + .({@-लः@}) an epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामस्वभाव
वाम + -स्वभाव <i>a.</i> of noble character; निरीक्ष्य कृष्णाऽपकृतं गुरोः<BR> सुतं वामस्वभावा कृपया ननाम च Bhāg. 1. 7. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामहस्तः|वामहस्त
वाम + -हस्तः the dew-lap of a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामक|वामकः
वामक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Left.<BR>—2 Adverse, contrary; स्फुरता वामकेनापि दाक्षिण्यमवलम्ब्यते Māl. 8<BR> (where both senses are intended).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामकः|वामक
वामक + .{@-कः@} A particular mixed tribe; मागधो वामकश्चैव द्वौ वैश्यस्योपलक्षितौ ।<BR> ब्राह्मण्यां क्षत्रियायां च क्षत्रियस्यैक एव तु ॥ Mb. 13. 49. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामकम्
वामक + .{@-कम्@} A kind of gesture; Vikr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामतस्
वामतस् <i>ind.</i> From or on the left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामदेव्यम्
वामदेव्यम् (वामदेवेन दृष्टं साम इति वामदेवाड्डपड्डपौ P. IV. 2. 9)<BR> The name of a Sāma or Vedic chant, the cult of which involved<BR> promiscuous relations with women; एतद्वामदेव्यं मिथुने प्रोतम् Ch. Up. 2. 13. 1-2;<BR> कम्रं तत्रोपनम्राया विश्वस्या वीक्ष्य तुष्टवान् । स<BR> मम्लौ तं विभाव्याथ वामदेव्याभ्युपासकम् ॥ N. 17. 194. The Vāmadeva<BR> cult is personified by Ānandarāyamakhin in his allegorical play Vidyāpariṇayam ▪ Act 5━<BR> “इष्टाङ्गलक्षितरतिक्रमशोभितैषा, शृङ्गारिणी विजयते धुरि वामदेव्या ।<BR> हृद्यां च कीर्तिमियमातनुते हि विद्या ।”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामन|वामनः
वामन <i>a.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Short in stature, dwarfish, pigmy; छलवामनम् Śi. 13. 12.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) (Hence) Small, short, little, reduced in length; वामनार्चिरिव<BR> दीपभाजनम् R. 19. 51; कथं कथं तानि (दिनानि) च वामनानि N. 22. 57.<BR>—2 Bent down, bent low (नम्र); शिरसि स्म जिघ्रति सुरारिबन्धने छलवामनं<BR> विनयवामनं तदा Śi. 13. 12.<BR>—3 Vile, low, base.<BR>—4 Venerable;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">Page1414-2</a>]<BR> मध्ये वामनमासीनं विश्वेदेवा उपासते Kaṭh. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनः|वामन
वामन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A dwarf, pigmy; प्रांशुलभ्ये फले मोहादुद्बाहुरिव वामनः R. 1. 3, 10. 60;<BR> सहस्रं वामनान् कुब्जान् … … दृष्ट्वा ततोऽस्मयत वै तदा Mb. 7. 56. 8.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu in his fifth incarnation, when he was born as a dwarf<BR> to humble the demon Bali, (see बलि); छलयसि विक्रमणे बलिमद्भुतवामन<BR> पदनखनीरजनितजनपावन । केशव धृतवामनरूप जय जगदीश हरे ।<BR> Gīt. 1; Śi. 13. 12.<BR>—3 N. of the elephant that presides over the south.<BR>—4 N. of the author of the Kāśikāvṛtti, a commentary on Pāṇiniʼs Sūtras.<BR>—5 The tree called अङ्कोट.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वामनाकृति, वामनद्वादशी, वामननिघण्टुः, वामनपुराणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनाकृति
वामन + -आकृति <i>a.</i> dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनद्वादशी
वामन + -द्वादशी the 12th day in the light half of चैत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामननिघण्टुः|वामननिघण्टु
वामन + -निघण्टुः N. of a dictionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनपुराणम्
वामन + -पुराणम् N. of one of the 18 Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनिका
वामनिका A female dwarf; वादित्ररवसंघुष्टं कुब्जावामनिकायुतम्<BR> Rām. 2. 10. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनी
वामनी<BR>—1 A female dwarf.<BR>—2 A mare.<BR>—3 A kind of woman.<BR>—4 A disease of the vagina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनीकृत
वामनीकृत<BR>—1 Turned into a dwarf.<BR>—2 Pressed down, flattened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलूरः|वामलूर
वामलूरः An ant-hill, a mole-hill; वामलूरान्तरोद्गच्छद्दंदशूकजिघांसया<BR> Śiva B. 26. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामा
वामा<BR>—1 A woman.<BR>—2 A lovely woman; मधु द्राक्षा साक्षादमृतमथ वामाधरसुधा Bv. 4. 39, 42.<BR>—3 N. of Gaurī.<BR>—4 Of Lakṣmī.<BR>—5 Of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिः
वामिः [वम्-इञ् Uṇ. 4. 136] <i>f.</i> A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिल|वामिलः
वामिल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>—2 Proud, haughty.<BR>—3 Cunning, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1414-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

