विकल|विकलः
विकल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deprived of a part or member, defective, imperfect, maimed, mutilated;<BR> कूटकृद्विकलेन्द्रियाः Y. 2. 70; Ms. 8. 66; U. 4. 24.<BR>—2 Frightened, alarmed; नादस्तावद्विकलकुररीकूजितस्निग्धतारः Māl. 5. 20.<BR>—3 Devoid or destitute of (in comp.); आरामाधिपतिर्विवेकविकलः Bv. 1. 31;<BR> प्रसूति˚ Ś. 6. 24; Pt. 5. 8; Mk. 5. 41; न तु कुलविकलानां<BR> वर्तते वृत्तशुद्धिः Avimārakam 2. 5.<BR>—4 Agitated, weakened, dispirited, unnerved, drooping, sinking, languid;<BR> किमिति विषीदसि रोदिषि विकला विहसति युवतिसभा तव सकला Gīt. 9;<BR> विरहेण विकलहृदया Bv. 2. 71, 164; श्रुतियुगले पिकरुतविकले<BR> Gīt. 12; वहति विकलः कायो मोहं न मुञ्चति चेतनाम् U. 3. 31; Māl. 7. 1, 9. 12.<BR>—5 Ineffective, useless; विकलमिह पूर्वसुकृतम् Pt. 5. 9.<BR>—6 Wanting, failing.<BR>—7 Withered, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकला
विकल + .{@-ला, -ली@} A woman during her courses; (L. D. B. however says ‘A woman who has passed child-bearing’<BR>, ऋतुहीना).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकलाङ्ग, विकलेन्द्रिय, विकलकरण, विकलकरुण, विकलपाणिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकली
विकल + .{@-ला, -ली@} A woman during her courses; (L. D. B. however says ‘A woman who has passed child-bearing’<BR>, ऋतुहीना).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकलाङ्ग, विकलेन्द्रिय, विकलकरण, विकलकरुण, विकलपाणिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1423-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

