विकालिका
विकालिका A perforated copper-vessel which, placed in water, marks<BR> the time by gradually filling; cf. मानरन्ध्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश्
विकाश् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To appear, become visible.<BR>—2 To bloom, open.<BR>—3 To shine. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To display, manifest.<BR>—2 To illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशः|विकाश
विकाशः<BR>—1 Manifestation, display, exhibition.<BR>—2 Blowing, expanding (usually written विकास in this sense); बालेन्दुवक्राण्यविकाशभावाद्बभुः<BR> पलाशान्यतिलोहितानि Ku. 3. 29; विकाशः केषांचिन्नयनसुभगैर्विद्युदुदयैः Rāj. T.<BR>—3 An open or direct course; विकाशमीयुर्जगतीशमार्गणाः Ki. 15. 52.<BR>—4 An oblique course; Ki. 15. 52.<BR>—5 Joy, pleasure; Ki. 15. 52.<BR>—6 Sky, heaven (आकाश); Ki. 15. 52.<BR>—7 Eagerness, ardent desire; युगपद्विकासमुदयाद्गमिते शशिनः शिलीमुखगणोऽलभत<BR> Śi. 9. 41 (where it means ‘blowing’ also).<BR>—8 Retreat, solitude, privacy.<BR>—9 Brightness, radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशक
विकाशक <i>a.</i> (-शिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Displaying.<BR>—2 Opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशनम्
विकाशनम्<BR>—1 Manifestation, display, exhibition.<BR>—2 Blowing, expanding (of flowers &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशिन्
विकाशि(षि, सि)न् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Becoming visible, shining forth.<BR>—2 Expanding, opening, blowing.<BR>—3 Shining, resplendent; Pt. 3. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाषिन्
विकाशि(षि, सि)न् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Becoming visible, shining forth.<BR>—2 Expanding, opening, blowing.<BR>—3 Shining, resplendent; Pt. 3. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासिन्
विकाशि(षि, सि)न् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Becoming visible, shining forth.<BR>—2 Expanding, opening, blowing.<BR>—3 Shining, resplendent; Pt. 3. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिष्कुः|विकिष्कु
विकिष्कुः A carpenterʼs measure of 42 inches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुक्षि|विकुक्षिः
विकुक्षि, विकुक्षिक <i>a.</i> Having a prominent belly; वसाश्चैवापरे<BR> पीत्वा पर्यधावन् विकुक्षिकाः Mb. 10. 8. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुक्षिक
विकुक्षि, विकुक्षिक <i>a.</i> Having a prominent belly; वसाश्चैवापरे<BR> पीत्वा पर्यधावन् विकुक्षिकाः Mb. 10. 8. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुण्ठम्
विकुण्ठम् N. of Viṣṇuʼs heaven; प्रतिनन्द्य जगादेदं विकुण्ठनिलयो<BR> विभुः Bhāg. 3. 16. 1, 7. 9. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुण्ठा
विकुण्ठम् + .{@-ण्ठा@} N. of the mother of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुण्ठ|विकुंठ
विकुण्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sharp, penetrating.<BR>—2 Very blunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुण्ठित|विकुंठित
विकुण्ठित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Obtuse, blunt.<BR>—2 Weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुस्रः|विकुस्र
विकुस्रः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूजनम्
विकूजनम्<BR>—1 Cooing, humming.<BR>—2 Rumbling (as of the bowels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणनम्
विकूणनम्<BR>—1 A side-glance, leer.<BR>—2 Contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणिका
विकूणिका The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूबर
विकूबर <i>a.</i> Deprived of the shaft or pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृ
विकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To alter, change, affect; विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियन्ते येषां न चेतांसि<BR> त एव धीराः Ku. 1. 59; R. 13. 42.<BR>—2 To disfigure, deform; विकृताकृति Ms. 9. 52.<BR>—3 To create, produce, effect; मनः सृष्टिं विकुरुते चोद्यमानं सिसृक्षया<BR> Ms. 1. 75; नास्य विघ्नं विकुर्वन्ति दानवाः Mb.<BR>—4 To disturb, harm, injure (Ā.); हीनान्यनुपकर्तॄणि प्रवृद्धानि विकुर्वते R. 17. 58.<BR>—5 To utter (a sound); विकुर्वाणः स्वरानद्य Bk. 8. 20.<BR>—6 To be faithless (as a wife.).<BR>—7 To deprave, pervert, spoil.<BR>—8 To display.<BR>—9 To change for the worse, deteriorate (Ā.).<BR>—10 To rejoice (Ā.).<BR>—11 To feel aversion (Ā.).<BR>—12 To act in various ways (Ā.); विकुर्वन्तश्च तैः साकम् Bhāg. 10. 12. 9.<BR>—13 To decorate in various ways; प्रासादैः रत्नविकृतैः Rām. 1. 5. 15.<BR>—14 To exercise.<BR>—15 To distribute.<BR>—16 To destroy, ruin.<BR>—17 To spread, extend.<BR>—18 To become restless, move to and fro.<BR>—19 To act in a hostile manner.<BR>—20 To contend together.<BR>—21 To blame, revile; अनार्य इति मामार्याः … विकरिष्यन्ति रथ्यासु<BR> Rām. 2. 12. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारः|विकार
विकारः<BR>—1 Change of form or nature, transformation, deviation from the natural<BR> state; cf. विकृति.<BR>—2 A change, alteration, a modification; प्रमथमुखविकारैर्हासयामास<BR> गूढम् Ku. 7. 95; नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च लक्ष्यतेऽन्तर्गतं मनः Pt. 1. 44; Ś. 7.<BR>—3 Sickness, disease, malady; विकारं खलु परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वाऽनारम्भः<BR> प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 4; Ku. 2. 48.<BR>—4 Change of mind or purpose; मूर्च्छन्त्यमी विकाराः प्रायेणैश्वर्यमत्तेषु Ś. 5. 18.<BR>—5 A feeling, an emotion; विकारश्चैतन्यं भ्रमयति च संमीलयति<BR> च U. 1. 35, 3. 25, 36; Māl. 1. 30.<BR>—6 Agitation, excitement, perturbation; कुतः परस्मिन् पुरुषे विकारः Ki. 17. 23.<BR>—7 Contortion, contraction (as of the features of the face); प्रमथमुखविकारैर्हासयामास<BR> गूढम् Ku. 7. 95.<BR>—8 (In Sāṅ. phil.) That which is evolved<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">Page1425-1</a>]<BR> from a previous source or Prakṛti.<BR>—9 A wound.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकारहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1424-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारहेतुः|विकारहेतु
विकारः + -हेतुः a temptation, seduction, cause of perturbation; विकारहेतौ<BR> सति विक्रियन्ते येषां न चेतांसि त एव धीराः Ku. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारण
विकारण <i>a.</i> Causeless; तस्मात् स्यात् कलहो यत्र गृहे नित्यं<BR> विकारणः Pt. 5. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारित
विकारित <i>a.</i> Changed, perverted, corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारिन्
विकारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Liable to change, susceptible of emotions or impressions; भ्रमति<BR> भुवने कन्दर्पाज्ञा विकारि च यौवनम् Māl. 1. 17.<BR>—2 Changing, modifying.<BR>—3 Spoiling, corrupting.<BR>—4 Affected by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकार्यः|विकार्य|विकार्य्य
विकार्यः The sense of individuality (अहंकार); मनोमयं देवमयं<BR> विकार्यम् Bhāg. 2. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुर्वाण|विकुर्व्वाण|विकुर्व्वाणः
विकुर्वाण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Undergoing or causing a change; वायोरपि विकुर्वाणाद्विरोचिष्णु तमोनुदम् Ms. 1. 77.<BR>—2 Feeling glad, delighted, rejoiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृत|विकृतं
विकृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Changed, altered, modified.<BR>—2 Sick, diseased.<BR>—3 Mutilated, deformed, disfigured; दृष्ट्वा तथैव विकृतं रथं मृत्युसमन्वितम्<BR> Rām. 7. 22. 9; Ms. 9. 291.<BR>—4 Incomplete, imperfect.<BR>—5 Affected by passion or emotion.<BR>—6 Averse from, disgusted with.<BR>—7 Loathsome.<BR>—8 Strange, extraordinary.<BR>—9 Unnatural.<BR>—10 Perverted, spoiled.<BR>—11 Estranged, disloyal; Rām. 2. 39. 22; see विकृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृतम्
विकृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Change, modification.<BR>—2 Change for the worse, sickness.<BR>—3 Aversion, disgust.<BR>—4 Harm, misdeed; तच्छ्रुत्वा पार्थिवेन्द्रस्य रक्षसा विकृतं च तत्<BR> Rām. 7. 65. 34.<BR>—5 Abortion; बालाश्च न प्रमीयन्ते विकृतं न च जायते Ms. 9. 247.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृतिः|विकृति
विकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Change (as of purpose, mind, form &c.); चित्तविकृतिः; अङ्गुलीयकं<BR> सुवर्णस्य विकृतिः &c.; प्रकृतिविकृतिभिरनुसवनम् Bhāg. 5. 7. 5.<BR>—2 An unnatural or accidental circumstance, an accident; मरणं प्रकृतिः<BR> शरीरिणां विकृतिर्जीवितमुच्यते बुधैः R. 8. 87.<BR>—3 Sickness.<BR>—4 Excitement, perturbation, anger, rage; सावलेपमुपलिप्सिते परैरभ्युपैति<BR> विकृतिं रजस्यपि Ki. 13. 56; U. 5. 29; Śi. 15. 11, 40.<BR>—5 Emotion; सत्त्वानामपि लक्ष्यते विकृतिमच्चित्तं भयक्रोधयोः Ś. 2. 5.<BR>—6 A sudden seizure or affection.<BR>—7 Fermented liquor; see विकार and विक्रिया also.<BR>—8 Hostility.<BR>—9 A phantom, spectre.<BR>—10 Abortion.<BR>—11 (In gram.) A derivative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्
विकृष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To draw, pull.<BR>—2 To bend (as a bow); शरासनं तेषु विकृष्यतामिदम् Ś. 6. 28.<BR>—3 To deprive of, withhold, keep back.<BR>—4 To destroy, ruin.<BR>—5 To lead (an army).<BR>—6 To plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षः|विकर्ष
विकर्षः<BR>—1 Drawing asunder, pulling apart.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षणः|विकर्षण|विकर्षणं
विकर्षणः N. of one of the five arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षणम्
विकर्षणः + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Drawing, dragging, pulling asunder.<BR>—2 A cross throw.<BR>—3 Abstinence from food.<BR>—4 Searching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्ट|विकृष्टः
विकृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Dragged asunder, pulled hither and thither.<BR>—2 Drawn, pulled, drawn towards or attracted.<BR>—3 Extended, protracted.<BR>—4 Making a noise; (see कृष् with वि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकृष्टसीमान्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्टसीमान्त
विकृष्ट + -सीमान्त <i>a.</i> having extended boundaries; ग्रामान् विकृष्टसीमान्तान्<BR> Rām. 2. 49. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकॄ
विकॄ €6 P.<BR>—1 To scatter, throw about; strew or spread about; व्यकीर्यत त्र्यम्बकपादमूले<BR> पुष्पोच्चयः पल्लवभङ्गभिन्नः Ku. 3. 61; Ki. 2. 59; Bk. 1. 3, 14. 25.<BR>—2 To split, cut to pieces; असिर्गात्रं गात्रं सपदि लवशस्ते विकिरतु Māl. 5. 34.<BR>—3 To pollute, contaminate.<BR>—4 To dissolve; एतद्यो वेद निहितं गुहायां सोऽविद्याग्रन्थिं विकिरतीह<BR> Muṇḍ. 2. 1. 10.<BR>—5 To pour out.<BR>—6 To heave (a sigh).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरः|विकिर
विकिरः<BR>—1 A scattered portion or fallen bit.<BR>—2 One who tears or scatters, a bird; कङ्कोलीफलजग्धिमुग्धविकिरव्याहारिणस्तद्भुवो<BR> भागाः Māl. 6. 19.<BR>—3 A well.<BR>—4 A tree.<BR>—5 A scattered portion of rice (offered to hostile beings in a sacrifice);<BR> उच्छिष्टं भागधेयं स्याद्दर्भेषु विकिरश्च यः Ms. 3. 245.<BR>—6 Water trickled through; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरणम्
विकिरणम्<BR>—1 Scattering, throwing about, dispersing.<BR>—2 Spreading abroad.<BR>—3 Tearing up.<BR>—4 Killing (हिंसन).<BR>—5 Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरणः|विकिरण|विकिरणं
विकिरणम् + .{@-णः@} The <i>Arka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्ण|विकीर्णः
विकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scattered, dispersed.<BR>—2 Diffused.<BR>—3 Celebrated.<BR>—4 Dishevelled (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्णम्
विकीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} A particular fault in pronouncing vowels.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकीर्णकेश, विकीर्णमूर्धज, विकीर्णज्ञम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्णकेश
विकीर्ण + -केश, -मूर्धज <i>a.</i> tearing the hair, having dishevelled hair;<BR> विललाप विकीर्णमूर्धजा Ku. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्णमूर्धज
विकीर्ण + -केश, -मूर्धज <i>a.</i> tearing the hair, having dishevelled hair;<BR> विललाप विकीर्णमूर्धजा Ku. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्णज्ञम्
विकीर्ण + -ज्ञम् a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकॢप्
विकॢप् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To doubt, be doubtful; कथंचिन्न विकल्पन्ते विद्वद्भिश्चिन्तिता<BR> नयाः Pt. 1. 339.<BR>—2 To be optional. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To doubt, question; एवं कृष्णसखः कृष्णो भ्रात्रा राज्ञा विकल्पितः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 15. 1.<BR>—2 To consider, reflect upon; सखीनियोगोऽपि विकल्प्यते Ś. 3.<BR>—3 To presume, conjecture.<BR>—4 To prepare or arrange differently.<BR>—5 To make, form.<BR>—6 To exchange.<BR>—7 To admit as optional.<BR>—8 To state a dilemma.<BR>—9 To reflect upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पः|विकल्प
विकल्पः<BR>—1 Doubt, uncertainty, indecision, hesitation; तत् सिषेवे नियोगेन स<BR> विकल्पपराङ्मुखः R. 17. 49.<BR>—2 Suspicion; Mu. 1.<BR>—3 Contrivance, art; मायाविकल्परचितैः R. 13. 75.<BR>—4 Option, alternative (in gram.); तुल्यार्थयोर्हि तुल्यविषययोर्विकल्पो<BR> भवति न नानार्थयोः ŚB. on MS. 10. 6. 33.<BR>—5 Sort, variety; दण्डविकल्पः Ms. 9. 228; भूषणानां विकल्पम् Me. 76.<BR>—6 An error, a mistake, ignorance.<BR>—7 Distinction; एवं सुरासुरगणाः समदेशकालहेत्वर्थकर्ममतयोऽपि<BR> फलेऽविकल्पाः Bhāg. 8. 9. 28.<BR>—8 A division of Kalpa; यावान् कल्पो विकल्पो वा यथा कालोऽनुमीयते<BR> Bhāg. 2. 8. 12.<BR>—9 A god; वैकारिको विकल्पानाम् Bhāg. 10. 85. 11.<BR>—10 Origin (उत्पत्ति); आत्मा केवल आत्मस्थो विकल्पापायलक्षणः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 25. 27.<BR>—11 Admission, statement.<BR>—12 Fancy, imagination.<BR>—13 Mental occupation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकल्पोपहारः, विकल्पजालम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पोपहारः|विकल्पोपहार
विकल्पः + -उपहारः an optional offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पजालम्
विकल्पः + -जालम् a net-like indecision, a dilemma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पक
विकल्पक <i>a.</i> A distributor, apportioner; Mb. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1425-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पनम्
विकल्पनम्<BR>—1 Admitting of a doubt.<BR>—2 Allowing an option.<BR>—3 Indecision.<BR>—4 Inconsideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पित
विकल्पित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Prepared, arranged.<BR>—2 Divided, manifold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पिन्
विकल्पिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessing doubt.<BR>—2 Versed in the Mīmāṃsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेश
विकेश <i>a.</i> (-शी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Having loose hair.<BR>—2 Having no hair, bald (as head).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेशी
विकेश + .{@-शी@}<BR>—1 A woman with loose hair.<BR>—2 A woman without hair.<BR>—3 A small tress of hair tied up separately and then collected into the<BR> larger braid or <i>Veṇi</i>.<BR>—4 N. of the wife of Śiva in the form of the Earth (one of the 8 forms<BR> of Śiva; cf. यामाहुः सर्वभूतप्रकृतिः Ś. 1. 1.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विकेशतारका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेशतारका
विकेश + -तारका a comet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेशिका
विकेशिका Lint; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकोश
विकोश, -ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without husk.<BR>—2 Unsheathed, uncovered; विकोशनिर्धौततनोर्महासेः Ki. 17. 45; R. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकोष|विकोषः
विकोश, -ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without husk.<BR>—2 Unsheathed, uncovered; विकोशनिर्धौततनोर्महासेः Ki. 17. 45; R. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्कः|विक्क
विक्कः A young elephant (in the <i>tenth</i> (?) year). MW. gives<BR> twenty years old; विक्को विंशतिवर्षः स्यात् Abh. Cin. 1220;<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 11; विक्कैरिव महागजः Dharmābhyudayamahākāvya 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रम्
विक्रम् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To walk along or through; विष्णुस्त्रेधा विचक्रमे ‘took 3 steps’;<BR> जले विक्रममाणाया हनूमान् शतयोजनम् Bk. 8. 24.<BR>—2 To assail, overcome, conquer.<BR>—3 To cleave; split open (P.)<BR>—4 To advance, proceed. —5 To show prowess or valour; तत्प्रहरणान्याच्छिद्य<BR> विक्रामतः Māl. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमः|विक्रम
विक्रमः<BR>—1 A step, stride, pace; गतेषु लीलाञ्चितविक्रमेषु Ku. 1. 34; Ś. 7. 6;<BR> निष्पेषवन्त्यायतविक्रमाणि (सप्तपदानि) Bu. C. 1. 33;<BR> Mb. 7. 49. 5; cf. त्रिविक्रम.<BR>—2 Stepping over, walking; going, gait; ततः सुमन्त्रस्त्वरितं गत्वा<BR> त्वरितविक्रमः Rām. 1. 8. 5; गतैः सहावैः कलहंसविकमम् Ki. 8. 29.<BR>—3 Overcoming, overpowering.<BR>—4 Heroism, prowess, heroic valour; अनुत्सेकः खलु विक्रमालंकारः<BR> V. 1; R. 12. 87, 93.<BR>—5 N. of a celebrated king of Ujjayinī.<BR>—6 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 Strength, power.<BR>—8 Intensity.<BR>—9 Stability.<BR>—10 A kind of grave accent.<BR>—11 Non-change of the विसर्ग into an उष्मन्.<BR>—12 The third astrological house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विक्रमार्कः, विक्रमादित्यः, विक्रमकर्मन्, विक्रमशीलः, विक्रमस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमार्कः|विक्रमार्क
विक्रमः + -अर्कः, -आदित्यः see विक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमादित्यः|विक्रमादित्य
विक्रमः + -अर्कः, -आदित्यः see विक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमकर्मन्
विक्रमः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> a heroic deed, feat of valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमशीलः|विक्रमशील
विक्रमः + -शीलः N. of a monastery; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमस्थानम्
विक्रमः + -स्थानम् a promenade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमणम्
विक्रमणम्<BR>—1 A stride (of Viṣṇu); छलयसि विक्रमणे बलिमद्भुतवामन Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 Heroism.<BR>—3 (With Pāśupatas) Supernatural power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमितम्
विक्रमितम् Prowess; निष्पेततुः परमविक्रमितातिवेपस्कन्धप्रवालविटपौ<BR> कृतचण्डशब्दौ Bhāg. 10. 10. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमिन्
विक्रमिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Chivalrous, heroic.<BR>—2 Powerful, strong. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A lion.<BR>—2 A hero.<BR>—3 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्त|विक्रांत|विक्रान्तं|विक्रान्तः
विक्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Stepped or passed beyond.<BR>—2 Powerful, heroic, valiant, chivalrous; युधामन्युश्च विक्रान्तः Bg. 1. 6;<BR> Ki. 16. 2.<BR>—3 Victorious, overpowering (oneʼs enemies).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्तः|विक्रान्त|विक्रांत|विक्रान्तं
विक्रान्त + .{@-न्तः@}<BR>—1 A hero, warrior.<BR>—2 A lion.<BR>—3 N. of a kind of संधि which leaves विसर्ग unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्तम्
विक्रान्त + .{@-न्तम्@}<BR>—1 A pace, stride; तद्विक्रान्तैर्विजितानीह त्रीणि Mb. 13. 158. 20.<BR>—2 Heroism, valour, prowess.<BR>—3 The jewel called वैक्रान्त.<BR>—4 A kind of intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्तिः|विक्रान्ति|विक्रांति|विक्रांतिः
विक्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Stepping, striding.<BR>—2 A horseʼs gallop or canter.<BR>—3 Heroism, valour, prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रान्तृ|विक्रांतृ
विक्रान्तृ <i>a.</i> Valiant, victorious. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A lion.<BR>—2 A hero, victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रस्रः|विक्रस्र
विक्रस्रः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रिया
विक्रिया<BR>—1 Change, modification, alteration; श्मश्रुप्रवृद्धिजनिताननविक्रियान्<BR> R. 13. 71, 10. 17.<BR>—2 Agitation, excitement, perturbation, excitement of passion; अथ तेन<BR> निगृह्य विक्रियामभिशप्तः फलमेतदन्वभूत् Ku. 4. 41, 3. 34.<BR>—3 Anger, wrath, displeasure; साधोः प्रकोपितस्यापि मनो नायाति विक्रियाम्<BR> Subhāṣ.; लिङ्गैर्मुदः संवृतविक्रियास्ते R. 7. 30; किमकारणमस्मासु<BR> गतवानसि विक्रियाम् Bm. 1. 911.<BR>—4 Reverse, evil; विक्रियायै न कल्पन्ते संबन्धाः सदनुष्ठिताः Ku. 6. 29<BR> (विक्रियायै = वैकल्योत्पादनाय Malli.)<BR>—5 Knitting, contraction (of the eyebrows); भ्रूविक्रियायां विरतप्रसंगैः Ku. 3. 47.<BR>—6 Any sudden movement, as in रोमविक्रिया V. 1. 12 ‘thrill’.<BR>—7 A sudden affection or seizure, disease.<BR>—8 Violation, vitiation (of the proper duties); इत्याप्तवचनाद्रामो<BR> विनेष्यन् वर्णविक्रियाम् R. 15. 48.<BR>—9 A preparation or dish of rice &c.<BR>—10 Injury, harm.<BR>—11 Extinction (of a lamp).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विक्रियोपमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रियोपमा
विक्रिया + -उपमा a kind of Upamā mentioned by Daṇḍin; see चन्द्रबिम्बादिवोत्कीर्णं<BR> पद्मगर्भादिबोद्धृतम् । तव तन्वङ्गि वदनमित्यसौ विक्रियोपमा ॥ Kāv. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्री
विक्री €9 Ā.<BR>—1 To sell (Ātm. in this sense); गवां शतसहस्रेण विक्रीणीषे सुतं<BR> यदि Rām.; विक्रीणीत तिलाञ्शुद्धान् Ms. 10. 90, 8. 197, 222; Śānti. 1. 12.<BR>—2 To barter, exchange; नाकस्माच्छाण्डिलीमाता विक्रीणाति तिलैस्तिलान् Pt. 2. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयः|विक्रय|विक्रयं
विक्रयः<BR>—1 Sale, selling; यासां नाददते शुल्कं ज्ञातयो न स विक्रयः Ms. 3. 54.<BR>—2 The selling price; Ms. 7. 127.<BR>—3 The market; विक्रयाद्यो धनं किंचिद् गृह्णीयात् कुलसंनिधौ Ms. 8. 201.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विक्रयानुशयः, विक्रयपत्रम्, विक्रयवीथिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयानुशयः|विक्रयानुशय
विक्रयः + -अनुशयः rescission of a sale; Ms. 8. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयपत्रम्
विक्रयः + -पत्रम् a bill of sale, sale-deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयवीथिः
विक्रयः + -वीथिः market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिकः|विक्रयिक
विक्र(क्रा)यिकः, विक्रयिन् <i>m.</i> A dealer, seller, vendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रायिकः|विक्रायिक
विक्र(क्रा)यिकः, विक्रयिन् <i>m.</i> A dealer, seller, vendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिन्
विक्र(क्रा)यिकः, विक्रयिन् <i>m.</i> A dealer, seller, vendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रायक|विक्रायकः
विक्रायक <i>a.</i> Selling; पुत्रविक्रायकं ध्रुवम् Rām. 2. 12. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीत|विक्रीतः
विक्रीत <i>p. p.</i> Sold; विक्रीते करिणि किमङ्कुशे विवादः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीतम्
विक्रीत + .{@-तम्@} Sale; योगाधमनविक्रीतम् Ms. 8. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रेय|विक्रेयं
विक्रेय <i>a.</i> Saleable, vendible (as an article); Y. 2. 246.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रीडः|विक्रीड
विक्रीडः<BR>—1 A playing ground.<BR>—2 A play-thing, toy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1426-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुश्
विक्रुश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To call aloud, cry out loudly; आक्रोश विक्रोश लपाधिचण्डम् Mk. 1. 41;<BR> Bk. 14. 42, 16. 32.<BR>—2 To utter (with acc.).<BR>—3 To call out to (with acc.).<BR>—4 To resound.<BR>—5 To abuse, revile, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुष्ट|विक्रुष्टं
विक्रुष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Exclaimed, cried out.<BR>—2 Harsh, cruel, unkind.<BR>—3 Offensive; (परित्यजेत्) धर्मं चाप्यसुखोदर्कं लोकविक्रुष्टमेव च Ms. 4. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुष्टम्
विक्रुष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@}<BR>—1 A cry for help; विक्रुष्टे नाभिधावकः Y. 2. 234.<BR>—2 Abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोशः|विक्रोश
विक्रोशः, -विक्रोशनम्<BR>—1 Calling out, exclaiming; पृष्ठतो द्रौपदीं … सविक्रोशम् Mb. 14. 66. 13.<BR>—2 Abusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोशनम्
विक्रोशः, -विक्रोशनम्<BR>—1 Calling out, exclaiming; पृष्ठतो द्रौपदीं … सविक्रोशम् Mb. 14. 66. 13.<BR>—2 Abusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोष्टृ
विक्रोष्टृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who calls out for help; अकारणे च विक्रोष्टा Y. 2. 234.<BR>—2 A reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लव|विक्लवः
विक्लव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Overcome with fear, startled, alarmed, frightened; आचकाङ्क्ष घनशब्दविक्लवाः<BR> R. 19. 38; Ku. 4. 11.<BR>—2 Timid; तोयोत्सर्गस्तनितमुखरो मा च भूर्विक्लवास्ताः Me. 39.<BR>—3 Affected by, overcome with; निसर्गदुर्बोधमबोधविक्लवाः क्व भूपतीनां<BR> चरितं क्व जन्तवः Ki. 1. 6.<BR>—4 Agitated, excited, confused, bewildered; प्रतिषेधाक्षरविक्लवाभिरामम् Ś. 3. 24.<BR>—5 Distressed, afflicted; grieved; निराकरणविक्लवायाः प्रियायाः<BR> Ś. 6; Śi. 12. 63; Ku. 4. 39; सुतविक्लवाय राज्ञे Bu. C. 1. 86.<BR>—6 Disgusted with, averse from; मृगयाविक्लवं चेतः Ś. 2.<BR>—7 Faltering; प्रस्थानविक्लवगतेरवलम्बनार्थम् Ś. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लवम्
विक्लव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Agitation, bewilderment; किमिदं देवि करोषि हृदि विक्लबम् Rām. 2. 44. 25.<BR>—2 Fear; गतविक्लवः Rām. 7. 32. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लवता
विक्लवता Timidity; भवति हि विक्लवता गुणोऽङ्गनानाम् Śi. 7. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लवितम्
विक्लवितम् Despondent language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिन्न|विक्लिन्नः
विक्लिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Very moist, thoroughly wetted.<BR>—2 Decayed, withered up.<BR>—3 Old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिष्ट
विक्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Excessively afflicted, distressed.<BR>—2 Injured, destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिष्टम्
विक्लिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} A fault in pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लेदः|विक्लेद
विक्लेदः<BR>—1 Wetting thoroughly; पुरीषमूत्रविक्लेदम् (गर्भवासम्) Mb. 12. 213. 6.<BR>—2 Wetness, moisture.<BR>—3 Dissolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लेदनम्
विक्लेदनम् The act of softening (by cooking or boiling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लेशः|विक्लेश
विक्लेशः An incorrect pronunciation of the dentals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षत|विक्षतः
विक्षत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Torn asunder, wounded, hurt, struck; विक्षतं चायसैर्बाणैर्मत्प्रयुक्तैरजिह्मगैः<BR> Mb. 3. 173. 30.<BR>—2 Beaten, stamped; महीं महाककुत्कायः कम्पयन् खुरविक्षताम् Bhāg. 10. 36. 1.<BR>—3 Affected, seized; स राजा शापविक्षतः Rām. 7. 54. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षतम्
विक्षत + .{@-तम्@} Wounding, a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षावः|विक्षाव
विक्षावः<BR>—1 Cough, sneezing.<BR>—2 A sound; विक्षावैस्तोयविश्रावं तर्जयन्तो महोदधेः Bk. 7. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षित
विक्षित <i>a.</i> Miserable, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्
विक्षिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To throw about, scatter.<BR>—2 To throw, cast.<BR>—3 To divert.<BR>—4 To distract.<BR>—5 To extend, stretch out.<BR>—6 To reject, discard.<BR>—7 To press against.<BR>—8 To toss about.<BR>—9 To prepare, make up.<BR>—10 To bend (a bow); all these last four meanings can be seen in the following<BR> verse:− रक्षांसि वक्षांसि च विक्षिपन्ति गात्राणि कान्तासु च विक्षिपन्ति ।<BR> रूपाणि चित्राणि च विक्षिपन्ति दृढानि चापानि च विक्षिपन्ति ॥ Rām. 5. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्त|विक्षिप्तः
विक्षिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Scattered, thrown about, dispersed, cast about.<BR>—2 Discarded, dismissed.<BR>—3 Sent, despatched.<BR>—4 Distracted, bewildered, agitated; प्रविक्षिप्तं चेतः प्रविशति च<BR> मोहान्धतमसम् Māl. 9. 8.<BR>—5 Refuted; (see क्षिप् with वि).<BR>—6 Extended, spread out; विक्षिप्तौ राक्षसेन्द्रस्य भुजाविन्द्रध्वजोपमौ<BR> Rām. 5. 10. 15, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्तम्
विक्षिप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} One of the चित्तभूमिs in the Yogaśāstra; क्षिप्तं<BR> मूढं विक्षिप्तमेकाग्रं निरुद्धमिति चित्तभूमयः । Yogasūtrabhāṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपः|विक्षेप
विक्षेपः<BR>—1 Throwing away or asunder, scattering about.<BR>—2 Casting, throwing, discharging (opp. संहार); संहारविक्षेपसहस्रकोटीस्तिष्ठन्ति<BR> जीवाः Mb. 12. 280. 30; संहारविक्षेपलघुक्रियेण R. 5. 45.<BR>—3 Waving, moving about, shaking, moving to and fro; बाहुविक्षेपकरणां<BR> समुद्यम्य महागदाम् Rām. 7. 32. 41. लाङ्गूल˚ Ku. 1. 13.<BR>—4 Sending, despatching.<BR>—5 Distraction, confusion, perplexity; Māl. 1.<BR>—6 Alarm, fear.<BR>—7 Refutation of an argument.<BR>—8 Polar latitude.<BR>—9 Looking about vaguely or wildly.<BR>—10 Neglecting (time).<BR>—11 Extension, projection.<BR>—12 A kind of weapon.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विक्षेपध्रुवः, विक्षेपशक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपध्रुवः|विक्षेपध्रुव
विक्षेपः + -ध्रुवः (in astr.) the greatest inclination of a planetʼs orbit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपशक्तिः|विक्षेपशक्ति
विक्षेपः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> (in Vedānta phil.) the power of Māyā (अविद्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपणम्
विक्षेपणम्<BR>—1 Throwing, casting, discharging.<BR>—2 Despatching, sending.<BR>—3 Scattering, dispersing.<BR>—4 Confusion, perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीणकः|विक्षीणक
विक्षीणकः<BR>—1 N. of the chief of a class of beings attending on Śiva.<BR>—2 An assembly of the gods.<BR>—3 A destroyer.<BR>—4 A place from which flesh-eaters are excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीरः|विक्षीर
विक्षीरः The <i>Arka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षुभ्
विक्षुभ् €1 Ā., €4. €9 P.<BR>—1 To be greatly agitated or disturbed.<BR>—2 To confuse, disturb, perplex. ━<i>Caus.</i> To agitate, disturb, confuse &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षोभः|विक्षोभ
विक्षोभः<BR>—1 Shaking, agitation, movement; वीचि˚ R. 1. 43.<BR>—2 Agitation of mind, distraction, alarm.<BR>—3 Conflict, struggle.<BR>—4 Tearing open; सुरारिवक्षोविक्षोभजासृक् Śi. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख|विखः
विख, विखु, विख्य <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विखनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखु|विखुः
विख, विखु, विख्य <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विखनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्य|विख्यः
विख, विखु, विख्य <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विखनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखनस्
विख + -नस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Brahman; विखनसार्थितो विश्वगुप्तये सख उदेयिवान् सात्वतां कुले Bhāg. 10. 31. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्र|विख्रः
विख्र, विख्रु, विग्र [See विख]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्रु|विख्रुः
विख्र, विख्रु, विग्र [See विख]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्र|विग्रः
विख्र, विख्रु, विग्र [See विख]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखण्डित|विखंडित
विखण्डित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Broken up, divided.<BR>—2 Cleft in two.<BR>—3 Disfigured, mutilated; शस्त्रैरपि विखण्डिताः (न वशं योषितो<BR> यान्ति) Pt. 4. 89.<BR>—4 Refuted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1427-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखानसः|विखानस
विखानसः A kind of hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखासा
विखासा The tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखुरः|विखुर
विखुरः<BR>—1 A demon, goblin.<BR>—2 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखेद
विखेद <i>a.</i> Fresh, alert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्या
विख्या €2 P.<BR>—1 To be well-known or famous.<BR>—2 To look at, see.<BR>—3 To call, name.<BR>—4 To celebrate.<BR>—5 To make visible, illuminate. ━<i>Caus.</i> To proclaim, announce, publish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यात|विख्यातः
विख्यात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Renowned, well-known, celebrated, famous.<BR>—2 Called, named.<BR>—3 Avowed, confessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यातिः|विख्याति
विख्यातिः <i>f.</i> Celebrity, fame, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यापनम्
विख्यापनम्<BR>—1 Publishing, proclaiming.<BR>—2 Explanation.<BR>—3 Confessing, acknowledging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगण्
विगण् €10 P.<BR>—1 To number, compute; वायवीयैर्विगण्यन्ते विभक्ताः परमाणवः Y. 3. 104.<BR>—2 To regard, consider; नन्वात्मानं बहु विगणयन्नात्मनैवावलम्बे<BR> Me. 111; R. 1. 87.<BR>—3 To disregard, not to mind.<BR>—4 To reflect, think; विगणय्य कारणमनेकगुणम् Ki. 6. 37; किमपि<BR> विगणयन्तो बुद्धिमन्तः सहन्ते Pt. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणनम्
विगणनम्<BR>—1 Reckoning, computing, calculation.<BR>—2 Considering, deliberating.<BR>—3 Paying off a debt; P. I. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगद
विगद <i>a.</i> Healthy, well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगन्ध
विगन्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a bad smell.<BR>—2 Odourless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगन्धकः|विगन्धक|विगंधक|विगंधकः
विगन्धकः The tree called इङ्गुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगम्
विगम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To pass away (as time &c.); संध्ययापि सपदि व्यगमि Śi. 9. 17.<BR>—2 To go away, depart.<BR>—3 To vanish; disappear; सलज्जाया लज्जा व्यगमदिव दूरं मृगदृशः<BR> Gīt. 11; मोहोऽयं विगतो मम Bg. 11. 1.<BR>—4 To die. ━<i>Caus.</i> To spend, pass; विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः Ś. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगत|विगतः
विगत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Departed, gone away, disappeared.<BR>—2 Parted, separated.<BR>—3 Dead; विगतं तु विदेशस्थ शृणुयाद्यो ह्यनिर्दशम् Ms. 5. 75.<BR>—4 Destitute or devoid of, free from (in comp.); विगतमदः.<BR>—5 Lost.<BR>—6 Dark, obscured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगता
विगत + .{@-ता@} A girl in love with another (hence unfit for marriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतम्
विगत + .{@-तम्@} The flight of birds.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विगतासु, विगतार्तवा, विगतकल्मष, विगतक्लम, विगतभी, विगतलक्षण, विगतश्रीक, विगतस्पृह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतासु
विगत + -असु <i>a.</i> dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतार्तवा|विगतार्त्तवा
विगत + -आर्तवा a woman past child-bearing (in whom the menstrual discharge has ceased).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतकल्मष
विगत + -कल्मष <i>a.</i> sinless, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतक्लम
विगत + -क्लम <i>a.</i> relieved from fatigue; Ms. 7. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतभी
विगत + -भी <i>a.</i> fearless, intrepid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतलक्षण
विगत + -लक्षण <i>a.</i> unlucky, inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतश्रीक|विगतश्रीकः
विगत + -श्रीक <i>a.</i> unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगतस्पृह
विगत + -स्पृह <i>a.</i> indifferent, void of desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगमः|विगम
विगमः<BR>—1 Departure, disappearance, cessation, end; चारुनृत्यविगमे च तन्मुखम्<BR> R. 19. 15; ईतिविगम M. 5. 20; Ṛs. 6. 23.<BR>—2 Abandoning; करणाविगमात् Me. 57 (देहत्यागात्)<BR>—3 Loss, destruction.<BR>—4 Death.<BR>—5 Separation; यथा क्रीडोपस्कराणां संयोगविगमाविह Bhāg. 1. 13. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगरः|विगर
विगरः<BR>—1 A naked ascetic.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 An abstemious man (abstaining from eating).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्
विगर्ह् €1 U.<BR>—1 To blame, censure, reproach; तं विगर्हन्ति साधवः Ms. 9. 68, 3. 46, 11. 53.<BR>—2 To despise, contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणम्
विगर्हणम्, -णा, विगर्हा<BR> Censure blame, reproach, abuse; यदि भीष्मः स्त्रियं<BR> हन्यात् सन्तः कुयुर्विगर्हणम् Mb. 5. 192. 69; प्राप्ता नाम विगर्हणा<BR> स्थितिमतां मध्येऽनुजानामपि Ve. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणा
विगर्हणम्, -णा, विगर्हा<BR> Censure blame, reproach, abuse; यदि भीष्मः स्त्रियं<BR> हन्यात् सन्तः कुयुर्विगर्हणम् Mb. 5. 192. 69; प्राप्ता नाम विगर्हणा<BR> स्थितिमतां मध्येऽनुजानामपि Ve. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हा
विगर्हणम्, -णा, विगर्हा<BR> Censure blame, reproach, abuse; यदि भीष्मः स्त्रियं<BR> हन्यात् सन्तः कुयुर्विगर्हणम् Mb. 5. 192. 69; प्राप्ता नाम विगर्हणा<BR> स्थितिमतां मध्येऽनुजानामपि Ve. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हित|विगर्हितः
विगर्हित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Censured, reviled, abused.<BR>—2 Disdained.<BR>—3 Condemned, reprobated, prohibited.<BR>—4 Low, vile.<BR>—5 Bad, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हितम्
विगर्हित + .{@-तम्@} Censure.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विगर्हिताचार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हिताचार
विगर्हित + -आचार <i>a.</i> of reprehensible conduct; एतान् विगर्हिताचारानपाङ्क्तेयान्<BR> द्विजाधमान् Ms. 3. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगल्
विगल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To drop down, get loose; रतिविगलितबन्धे केशहस्ते सुकेश्याः V. 4. 10.<BR>—2 To ooze or trickle.<BR>—3 To vanish, disappear.<BR>—4 To melt away, be dissolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलित|विगलितः
विगलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Trickled, oozed.<BR>—2 Disappeared, gone away; मयि विगलितप्रत्याशत्वाद्विवाहविधेः पुरा Māl. 9. 11.<BR>—3 Fallen or dropped down.<BR>—4 Melted away, dissolved.<BR>—5 Dispersed.<BR>—6 Slackened, untied.<BR>—7 Loose, dishevelled, disordered (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाह्
विगाह् Ā.<BR>—1 To plunge or dive into, bathe; (दीर्धिकाः) स व्यगाहत विगाढमन्मथः R. 19. 9.<BR>—2 To enter, penetrate into, pervade (fig. also); विषमोऽपि विगाह्यते<BR> नयः कृततीर्थः पयसामिवाशयः Ki. 2. 3; R. 13. 1; Mu. 1. 26.<BR>—3 To stir about, agitate; विगाह्यमानां सरयूं च नौभिः R. 14. 30.<BR>—4 To follow, practise; तया मुनीनां चरितं व्यगाह्यत Ku. 5. 19.<BR>—5 To approach, set in (as season &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाढ|विगाढः
विगाढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Plunged into, bathed, immersed; पुरो विगाढाः सखिभिर्मरुत्वतः Ki. 8. 30, 31.<BR>—2 Deep, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाहः|विगाह
विगाहः Plunging into, bathing, diving; विगाहं तूर्णि तविषीभिरावृतम् Rv. 3. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगुण|विगुणः
विगुण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Destitute of merits, worthless, bad; श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः परधर्मात्<BR> स्वनुष्ठितात् Bg. 3. 35; Śi. 9. 12; Mu. 6. 11.<BR>—2 Destitute of qualities.<BR>—3 Having no string; विगुणीकृतकार्मुकोऽपि जेतुं भुवि जेतव्यमसौ समर्थ<BR> एव Mu. 7. 11.<BR>—4 Unfruitful; विगुणानि च पश्यन्ति Mb. 12. 269. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगूढ|विगूढः
विगूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Secret, concealed, hidden.<BR>—2 Reproached, censured.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विगूढचारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगूढचारिन्
विगूढ + -चारिन् <i>a.</i> proceeding or acting secretly; Ms. 9. 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगै
विगै €1 P.<BR>—1 To censure, reproach, blame; विगीयसे मन्मथदहदाहिना N. 1. 79;<BR> विगायति च यो लोके यवनानां विलोकनम् Śiva B. 19. 30.<BR>—2 To sing in a discordant tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगानम्
विगानम्<BR>—1 Censure, reproach, defamation, scandal.<BR>—2 A contradictory statement, contradiction, inconsistency; यत् पुनः<BR> कारणविषयं विगानं दर्शितं तत् परिहर्तव्यम् Ś. B. (and in several<BR> other places of the same work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1428-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीत
विगीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Censured, abused, reviled.<BR>—2 Contradictory, inconsistent; यश्चाधरोत्तरानर्थान् विगीतान्नावबुध्यते Ms. 8. 53.<BR>—3 Sung badly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीतिः|विगीति
विगीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Censure, abuse, reproach.<BR>—2 Contradictory statement, contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रह्
विग्रह् €9 P.<BR>—1 To hold or seize, catch hold of; विजगृहे तिसृणां जयिनं पुराम् Ki. 18. 12.<BR>—2 To quarrel, fight, contend; विगृह्य चक्रे नमुचिद्विषा बली य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्दिवं<BR> दिवः Śi. 1. 51; Bk. 6. 86, 17. 23; Ki. 14. 24.<BR>—3 To divide into parts, separate (into constituent members).<BR>—4 To dissolve, analyse, resolve in general.<BR>—5 To receive, welcome (as a guest).<BR>—6 To perceive, observe.<BR>—7 To stretch or spread out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृहीत
विगृहीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Divided, dissolved, analysed, resolved (as a compound).<BR>—2 Seized.<BR>—3 Encountered, opposed.<BR>—4 Obstructed, stopped; see विग्रह् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहः|विग्रह
विग्रहः<BR>—1 Stretching out, extension, expansion.<BR>—2 Form, figure, shape; यथा लोहस्य निःस्यन्दो निषिक्तो बिम्बविग्रहम् Mb. 14. 18. 9.<BR>—3 The body; त्रयी विग्रहवत्येव सममध्यात्मविद्यया M. 1. 14; गूढविग्रहः<BR> R. 3. 39, 9. 52; Ki. 4. 11, 12. 43.<BR>—4 Resolution, dissolution, analysis, separation (as of a compound word<BR> into its component parts); वृत्त्यर्थ- (समासार्थ) -बोधकं वाक्यं विग्रहः.<BR>—5 Quarrel, strife (often, love-quarrel or प्रणयकलह); विग्रहाच्च<BR> शयने पराङ्मुखीर्नानुनेतुमबलाः स तत्वरे R. 19. 38, 9. 47; Śi. 11. 35;<BR> शत्रौ मित्रे पुत्रे बन्धौ मा कुरु यत्नं विग्रहसन्धौ Śaṅkara.<BR>—6 War, hostilities, fighting, battle (opp. संधि); उग्राय विग्रहायास्मै<BR> त्वया प्रेषयता ह्यमुम् Śiva B. 17. 35; one of the six Guṇas or modes<BR> of policy; Ms. 7. 160; see गुण.<BR>—7 Disfavour; अनुग्रहं विग्रहं वा मन्यसे तद्विधेहि नः Bhāg. 10. 16. 59.<BR>—8 A part, portion, division; परिमाणं च कालस्य कल्पलक्षणविग्रहम्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विग्रहावरम्, विग्रहेच्छु, विग्रहग्रहणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहावरम्
विग्रहः + -अवरम् the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहेच्छु
विग्रहः + -इच्छु <i>a.</i> eager for combat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहग्रहणम्
विग्रहः + -ग्रहणम् the assumption of a form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहवत्|विग्रहवन्त्
विग्रहवत् <i>a.</i> Having body, incarnate, embodied; M. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहिन्
विग्रहिन् A minister of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रीव
विग्रीव <i>a.</i> Decapitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्
विघट् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To be disunited or separated.<BR>—2 To be spoiled or ruined.<BR>—3 To be stopped, break down.<BR>—4 To assume various shapes; उपरि विघटमानः प्रौढतापिच्छनीलः<BR> Māl. 9. 24; Mv. 5. 42. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To separate, disperse, tear apart; विघटयन्त्यग्रे नभोऽभोमुचः Māl. 5. 2.<BR>—2 To remove, displace.<BR>—3 To mar, frustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटनम्
विघटनम् Breaking up, ruin, destruction; भ्रातुर्वक्षःस्थलविघटने<BR> यच्च साक्षीकृतोऽसि Ve. 5. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटित
विघटित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Separated, severed.<BR>—2 Divided.<BR>—3 Broken, shattered; पौलस्त्यस्य जटायुषा विघटितः U. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटिका
विघटिका A measure of time equal to one-sixtieth part of a Ghaṭikā<BR> (or nearly equal to 24 seconds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्ट्
विघट्ट् €10 U.<BR>—1 To strike down, disperse, scatter, scare away; तदीयमातङ्गघटाविघट्टितैः<BR> Śi. 1. 64; Bh. 3. 54.<BR>—2 To rub, strike, rub against; कारण्डवाननविघट्टितवीचिमालाः Ṛs. 3. 8, 4. 9;<BR> विघट्टितानां सरलद्रुमाणाम् Ku. 1. 9; Ki. 8. 45; Śi. 8. 24, 13. 41.<BR>—3 To break, violate (as an agreement).<BR>—4 To break asunder, burst open (as a door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टनम्
विघट्टनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Striking asunder.<BR>—2 Striking against, friction.<BR>—3 Separating, undoing, untying.<BR>—4 Offending, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टना
विघट्टनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Striking asunder.<BR>—2 Striking against, friction.<BR>—3 Separating, undoing, untying.<BR>—4 Offending, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टित|विघट्टितं
विघट्टित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck apart, severed, separated, dispersed; आयुर्वायुविघट्टिताभ्रपटलीलीनाम्बुवद्भङ्गुरम् Bh. 3. 54.<BR>—2 Untied, loosened, opened.<BR>—3 Rubbed, touched.<BR>—4 Shaken about, churned.<BR>—5 Hurt, offended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघनः|विघन
विघनः<BR>—1 A mallet, hammer.<BR>—2 One who destroys, subdues or overpowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसः|विघस|विघसं
विघसः<BR>—1 Half-chewed morsel, the residue or leavings of food eaten; विघसो<BR> भुक्तशेषं तु Ms. 3. 285; तृप्यत्कालकरालवक्त्रविघसव्याकीर्यमाणा<BR> इव U. 5. 6; Māl. 5. 14; बकविघसपङ्कसारा न चिरात् कावेरि भवितासि Āryā. S.<BR>—2 Food in general; किमद्याश्वत्थामा तदरिरुधिरासारविघसं (कर्म<BR> विधातुं) Ve. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसम्
विघसः + .{@-सम्@} Beesʼ-wax.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विघसाशः, विघसाशिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसाशः|विघसाश
विघसः + -आशः, -आशिन् <i>m.</i> one who eats the remains of an offering or<BR> food eaten (a crow, dog); आमिषं विघसाशेन तद्वद्राज्यं हि नो हृतम् Mb. 3. 33. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसाशिन्
विघसः + -आशः, -आशिन् <i>m.</i> one who eats the remains of an offering or<BR> food eaten (a crow, dog); आमिषं विघसाशेन तद्वद्राज्यं हि नो हृतम् Mb. 3. 33. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसीकृतः
विघसीकृतः, -भूतः<BR> Reduced to dregs; निपीय देवैर्विघसीकृतायां घृणां विधोरस्य<BR> दधे सुधायाम् N. 22. 118; सोऽयं प्राक्कवलग्रहस्य विघसीभूतेष्वपि<BR> क्षत्रियक्षुद्रेषु क्षुधितश्चिरेण परशुस्तेनायमन्विष्यते A. R. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसीभूतः
विघसीकृतः, -भूतः<BR> Reduced to dregs; निपीय देवैर्विघसीकृतायां घृणां विधोरस्य<BR> दधे सुधायाम् N. 22. 118; सोऽयं प्राक्कवलग्रहस्य विघसीभूतेष्वपि<BR> क्षत्रियक्षुद्रेषु क्षुधितश्चिरेण परशुस्तेनायमन्विष्यते A. R. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातः|विघात
विघातः<BR>—1 Destruction, removing, warding off; क्रियादघानां मघवा विघातम् Ki. 3. 52.<BR>—2 Killing, slaying.<BR>—3 An obstacle, impediment, interruption; opposition, prevention; क्रियाविघाताय<BR> कथं प्रवर्तसे R. 3. 44; अध्वरविघातशान्तये 11. 1.<BR>—4 A blow, stroke.<BR>—5 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>—6 Failure, want of success.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विघातसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातसिद्धिः|विघातसिद्धि
विघातः + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> the removal of obstacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघूणिका
विघूणिका The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघूर्णनम्
विघूर्णनम् Swaying to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघूर्णित
विघूर्णित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rolled, shaken about, rolling (as eyes).<BR>—2 Agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघृष्ट
विघृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rubbed excessively.<BR>—2 Sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नः|विघ्न
विघ्नः [विहन्-क] (rarely <i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 An obstacle, interruption, impediment, a hindrance; कुतो धर्मक्रियाविघ्नः<BR> सतां रक्षितरि त्वयि Ś. 5. 14; मूर्तो विघ्नस्तपस इव नः Ś. 1. 32;<BR> हुंकारेणेव धनुषः स हि विघ्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1; Ku. 3. 40.<BR>—2 Difficulty, trouble.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विघ्नेशः, विघ्नेशानः, विघ्नेश्वरः, विघ्नकर, विघ्नकर्तृ, विघ्नकारिन्, विघ्नध्वंसः, विघ्नविघातः, विघ्ननायकः, विघ्ननाशकः, विघ्ननाशनः, विघ्नप्रतिक्रिया, विघ्नराजः, विघ्नविनायकः, विघ्नहारिन्, विघ्नसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नेशः|विघ्नेश
विघ्नः + -ईशः, -ईशानः, -ईश्वरः epithets of Gaṇeśa; विघ्नेशो वः स<BR> पायाद्विवृतिषु जलधीन् पुष्कराग्रेण पीत्वा. ˚वाहनम् a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नेशानः|विघ्नेशान
विघ्नः + -ईशः, -ईशानः, -ईश्वरः epithets of Gaṇeśa; विघ्नेशो वः स<BR> पायाद्विवृतिषु जलधीन् पुष्कराग्रेण पीत्वा. ˚वाहनम् a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नेश्वरः|विघ्नेश्वर
विघ्नः + -ईशः, -ईशानः, -ईश्वरः epithets of Gaṇeśa; विघ्नेशो वः स<BR> पायाद्विवृतिषु जलधीन् पुष्कराग्रेण पीत्वा. ˚वाहनम् a rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकर
विघ्नः + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> opposing, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकर्तृ
विघ्नः + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> opposing, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नकारिन्
विघ्नः + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> opposing, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1429-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

