विच्छाय + .{@-यः@} A gem, jewel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छायम्
विच्छाय + .{@-यम्@} The shadow of a flock of birds; also विच्छाया; विच्छायाभिः<BR> प्रधावन्तो गच्छन्तः साधुहंसकैः Bhāg. 10. 12. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिद्
विच्छिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To cut off, break, tear asunder, divide; यदर्धे विच्छिन्नं भवति<BR> कृतसंधानमिव तत् Ś. 1. 9; R. 16. 20; Bh. 1. 96.<BR>—2 To interrupt, break off, terminate, end, destroy, make extinct (as<BR> a family); विच्छिद्यमानेऽपि कुले परस्य Bk. 3. 52; विच्छिन्नेषु पथिष्वहःपरिणतौ<BR> ध्वान्ते समुत्सर्पति Amaru. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छित्तिः|विच्छित्ति
विच्छित्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Cutting off or asunder, tearing off; न ध्यातं पदमीश्वरस्य<BR> विधिवत् संसारविच्छित्तये Bh. 3. 11.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Breaking off, fracture.<BR>—2 Dividing, separating.<BR>—3 Disappearance, absence, loss, wanting; विच्छित्तिर्नवचन्दनेन वपुषः Śi. 16. 84.<BR>—4 Cessation.<BR>—5 Colouring the body with paints and unguents, painting colours, rouge;<BR> विच्छित्तिशेषैः सुरसुन्दरीणाम् Ś. 7. 5; Śi. 16. 84.<BR>—6 Limit, boundary (of a house &c.)<BR>—7 A pause in a verse, caesura.<BR>—8 A particular kind of amorous gesture, consisting in carelessness in<BR> dress and decoration (through pride of personal beauty); स्तोकाप्याकल्परचना<BR> विच्छित्तिः कान्तिपोषकृत् S. D. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्न|विच्छिन्नः
विच्छिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Torn asunder, cut off.<BR>—2 Broken, severed, divided, separated; यदर्धे विच्छिन्नं भवति कृतसंधानमिव<BR> तत् Ś. 1. 9.<BR>—3 Interrupted, prevented.<BR>—4 Ended, ceased, terminated.<BR>—5 Variegated.<BR>—6 Hidden.<BR>—7 Smeared or painted with unguents.<BR>—8 Crooked, curved.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विच्छिन्नप्रसर, विच्छिन्नमद्य, विच्छिन्नशरपातत्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्नप्रसर
विच्छिन्न + -प्रसर <i>a.</i> having its progress interrupted.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">Page1432-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्नमद्य
विच्छिन्न + -मद्य <i>a.</i> one who has long abstained from liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्नशरपातत्वम्
विच्छिन्न + -शरपातत्वम् excessive nearness of combatants to each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदः|विच्छेद
विच्छेदः<BR>—1 Cutting asunder, cutting, dividing, separation; किं वा भणामि विच्छेददारुणायासकारिणि Māl. 6. 11.<BR>—2 Breaking; विच्छेदः सहृदययेव हारयष्टपा Śi. 8. 51.<BR>—3 Break, interruption, cessation, discontinuance; विच्छेदमाप भुवि<BR> यस्तु कथाप्रबन्धः K.; पिण्डविच्छेददर्शिनः R. 1. 66.<BR>—4 Removal, prohibition.<BR>—5 Dissension.<BR>—6 A section, or division of a book.<BR>—7 Interval, space.<BR>—8 Interruption in family succession, failure of issue.<BR>—9 Distinction, difference, variety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदनम्
विच्छेदनम् Cutting off, breaking &c.; see विच्छेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुर्
विच्छुर् €6 P.<BR>—1 To smear, anoint, cover, coat; मनःशिलाविच्छुरिता निषेदुः Ku. 1. 55;<BR> C. P. 11; V. 4. 42.<BR>—2 To set, inlay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुरणम्
विच्छुरणम् Besprinkling, powdering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुरित|विछुरित
विच्छुरित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Covered, overspread, coated.<BR>—2 Inlaid.<BR>—3 Besmeared, anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्यु
विच्यु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To deviate or swerve from.<BR>—2 To fall to pieces.<BR>—3 To err, make mistake. ━<i>Caus.</i> To throw down or destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युत|विच्युतः
विच्युत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen down, slipped off.<BR>—2 Displaced, thrown down from.<BR>—3 Deviated or swerving from.<BR>—4 Separated from the living part, sloughed.<BR>—5 Failed, perished, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युतिः|विच्युति
विच्युतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Falling down from, severance, separation.<BR>—2 Decline, decay, downfall.<BR>—3 Deviation.<BR>—4 Miscarriage, failure; as in गर्भविच्युतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
विज् I. €3 U. (वेवेक्ति, वेविक्ते, विक्त)<BR>—1 To separate, divide.<BR>—2 To distinguish, discern, discriminate (usually with वि and allied<BR> to विच् with वि q. v.). ━II. €6 Ā., €7 P. (विजते, विनक्ति, विग्न)<BR>—1 To shake, tremble.<BR>—2 To be agitated, tremble with fear.<BR>—3 To fear, be afraid; चक्रन्द विग्ना कुररीव भूयः R. 14. 68.<BR>—4 To be distressed or afflicted. ━<i>Caus.</i> (वेजयति-ते) To<BR> terrify, frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्न
विग्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Trembling, agitated.<BR>—2 Frightened, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
विज् <i>m.</i> A bird; a die (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजग्ध
विजग्ध <i>p. p.</i> Eaten, devoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजङ्घ
विजङ्घ <i>a.</i> Having no wheels (a chariot).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजट
विजट <i>a.</i> Unplaited (hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितृ
विजितृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A discriminator, judge.<BR>—2 A partner, co-heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्
विजन् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To be born or produced.<BR>—2 To generate, produce.<BR>—3 To grow, arise, spring.<BR>—4 To be changed or transformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1432-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन|विजनः
विजन <i>a.</i> Lonely, retired, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजनम्
विजन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 A solitary place, retreat (विजने means ‘privately’).<BR>—2 Absence of witnesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजननम्
विजननम् Birth, procreation, delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्मन्
विजन्मन् <i>a.</i> or <i>m.</i> A bastard, one born illegitimately; Ms. 10. 23.<BR>━<i>n.</i> Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्या
विजन्या <i>a.</i> Pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजात|विजातः
विजात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Base-born, of mixed origin.<BR>—2 Born, produced.<BR>—3 Transformed.<BR>—4 Having good qualities, virtuous; यस्ते पुत्रो गमितोऽयं विजातः स्वर्णष्ठीवी<BR> यमदात् पर्वतस्ते Mb. 12. 29. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजाता
विजात + .{@-ता@} A mother, matron, a woman who has given birth to children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातिः|विजाति
विजातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Different origin.<BR>—2 Different kind, species or tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातीय|विजातीयः
विजातीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of a different kind or species, dissimilar, unlike.<BR>—2 Of different caste or tribe.<BR>—3 Of mixed origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजपिलम्
विजपिलम् Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयन्तः|विजयन्त|विजयंत|विजयंतः
विजयन्तः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजर|विजरः
विजर <i>a.</i> Young, fresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजरम्
विजर + .{@-रम्@} A stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल|विजलं
विजल <i>a.</i> Waterless; तोयाशया विजला सरितोऽपि Bṛ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजलम्
विजल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A sauce; also विजिलम्.<BR>—2 Drought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजर्जर
विजर्जर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Decrepit, infirm.<BR>—2 Rotten (as wood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्पः|विजल्प
विजल्पः<BR>—1 Prattle, idle or foolish talk.<BR>—2 Talk or speech in general.<BR>—3 A malignant or spiteful speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्पित
विजल्पित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spoken, talked; परिहासविजल्पितं सखे (वचः) Ś. 2. 19.<BR>—2 Prated, babbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातु
विजातु <i>n.</i> A particular mode of fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजि
विजि €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To conquer, defeat, overcome, subdue; व्यजेष्ट षड्वर्गम्<BR> Bk. 1. 2; प्रायस्त्वन्मुखसेवया विजयते विश्वं स पुष्पायुधः Gīt. 10;<BR> Bk. 2. 39, 15. 39.<BR>—2 To surpass, excel; चक्षुर्मेचकमम्बुजं विजयते Vb. 1. 33.<BR>—3 To win, acquire by conquest; भुजविजितविमान R. 12. 104; विजितारिपुरः 1. 59;<BR> Śānti. 2. 14.<BR>—4 To be victorious, be supreme or pre-eminent; विजयतां देवः Ś. 5;<BR> रहस्यं साधूनामनुपधि विशुद्धं विजयते U. 2. 2; Māl. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयः|विजय
विजयः<BR>—1 Overcoming, vanquishing, defeating.<BR>—2 Conquest, victory, triumph; दिग्विजयादारभ्य ‘conquest of the world’;<BR> प्रभवति न तदा परो विजेतुं भवति जितेन्द्रियता यदात्मरक्षा Ki. 10. 35;<BR> R. 12. 44; Ku. 3. 19; अस्याधिज्ये धनुषि विजयम् Ś. 2. 16.<BR>—3 A chariot of the gods, celestial chariot.<BR>—4 N. of Arjuna; Mb. (4. 44. 14) thus explains the name:− अभिप्रयामि<BR> संग्रामे यदहं युद्धदुर्मदान् । नाजित्वा विनिवर्तामि तेन मां विजयं विदुः ॥.<BR>—4 An epithet of Yama.<BR>—5 N. of the first year of Jupiterʼs cycle.<BR>—6 N. of an attendant of Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 Motion, march;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">Page1433-2</a>]<BR> L. D. B.<BR>—8 N. of a particular मुहूर्त; युक्ते मुहूर्ते विजये Rām. 1. 73. 9.<BR>—9 The third month.<BR>—10 A kind of military array.<BR>—11 A kind of measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयम्
विजयः + .{@-यम्@} A royal tent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विजयाभ्युपायः, विजयाह्वय, विजयेशः, विजयोर्जित, विजयकुञ्जरः, विजयच्छन्दः, विजयडिण्डिमः, विजयदण्डः, विजयद्वादशी, विजयनगरम्, विजयमर्दलः, विजयश्रीः, विजयसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयाभ्युपायः|विजयाभ्युपाय
विजयः + -अभ्युपायः a means of victory<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयाह्वय
विजयः + -आह्वय <i>a.</i> having the name Vijaya (<i>i. e.</i> Bijapur); तथा<BR> येदिलशाहोऽपि पत्तने विजयाह्वये Śiva B. 1. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयेशः|विजयेश
विजयः + -ईशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयोर्जित
विजयः + -ऊर्जित <i>a.</i> exalted by victory; स प्रविश्य दिवं देवानजयद्विजयोर्जितः Bm. 1. 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयकुञ्जरः|विजयकुञ्जर|विजयकुंजर
विजयः + -कुञ्जरः a war-elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयच्छन्दः|विजयच्छन्द|विजयछन्द
विजयः + -छन्दः a necklace of 500 strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयडिण्डिमः|विजयडिण्डिम|विजयडिंडिम
विजयः + -डिण्डिमः a large military drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयदण्डः|विजयदण्ड
विजयः + -दण्डः a particular detachment of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयद्वादशी
विजयः + -द्वादशी the 12th day of the light half of श्रावण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयनगरम्
विजयः + -नगरम् N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयमर्दलः|विजयमर्दल|विजयमर्द्दल|विजयमर्द्दलः
विजयः + -मर्दलः a large military drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयश्रीः
विजयः + -श्रीः the goddess of victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयसिद्धिः|विजयसिद्धि
विजयः + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> success, victory, triumph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजया
विजया<BR>—1 N. of Durgā; विजित्य पद्मनामानं दैत्यराजं महावलम् । विजया<BR> तेन सा देवी लोके चैवापराजिता ॥ Devī. P.<BR>—2 N. of one of her female attendants; Mu. 1. 1.<BR>—3 N. of a lore taught by Viśvāmitra to Rāma; विद्यामथैनं विजयां<BR> जयां च (अध्यापिपत्) Bk. 2. 21.<BR>—4 Hemp.<BR>—5 N. of a festival = विजयोत्सव, see below.<BR>—6 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विजयोत्सवः, विजयादशमी, विजयासप्तमी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयोत्सवः|विजयोत्सव
विजया + -उत्सवः a festival in honour of Durgā held on the 10th day of<BR> the bright half of Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयादशमी
विजया + -दशमी the tenth day of the bright half of Āśvina, observed<BR> as a great holiday and commonly known as Dasarā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयासप्तमी
विजया + -सप्तमी the seventh day of the bright half of a month falling on a Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन्
विजयिन् <i>m.</i> A conqueror, victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषा
विजिगीषा<BR>—1 Desire to conquer or overcome; भुवनविजिगीषोद्यते देवे कुसुमधन्वनि Dk. 2. 3.<BR>—2 Desire to surpass, emulation, competition, ambition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषु|विजिगीषुः
विजिगीषु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desirous of victory, wishing to conquer; यशसे विजिगीषूणाम् R. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Emulous, ambitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषुः|विजिगीषु
विजिगीषु + .{@-षुः@}<BR>—1 A warrior, a hero.<BR>—2 Antagonist, a disputant, an opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित|विजितः
विजित <i>p. p.</i> Subdued, conquered, overcome, defeated.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विजितात्मन्, विजितेन्द्रिय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितात्मन्
विजित + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> self-subdued, self-controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितेन्द्रिय|विजितेंद्रिय
विजित + -इन्द्रिय <i>a.</i> having the organs of sense subdued or controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितिः|विजिति
विजितिः <i>f.</i> Conquest, victory, triumph; क्षितिविजितिस्थितिविहितिव्रतरतयः<BR> परमतयः Kāv. 3. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिघत्स
विजिघत्स <i>a.</i> Not-liable to hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिज्ञासा
विजिज्ञासा<BR>—1 Desire of knowing distinctly.<BR>—2 Inquiry about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिज्ञासितव्य
विजिज्ञासितव्य, विजिज्ञास्य <i>a.</i> Wished to be known; विज्ञातं<BR> विजिज्ञास्यमविज्ञातमेत एव Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिज्ञास्य
विजिज्ञासितव्य, विजिज्ञास्य <i>a.</i> Wished to be known; विज्ञातं<BR> विजिज्ञास्यमविज्ञातमेत एव Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिनः|विजिन|विजिनं
विजिनः, -नम् (-लः, -लम्)<BR> A sauce (mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिनम्
विजिनः, -नम् (-लः, -लम्)<BR> A sauce (mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिलः|विजिल|विजिलं
विजिनः, -नम् (-लः, -लम्)<BR> A sauce (mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिलम्
विजिनः, -नम् (-लः, -लम्)<BR> A sauce (mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिहीर्षा
विजिहीर्षा Wish to roam about or sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1433-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्म|विजिह्मः
विजिह्म <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Crooked, bent, turned away; कृतं न वा कोपविजिह्ममाननम् Ki. 1. 21;<BR> R. 19. 35.<BR>—2 Dishonest.<BR>—3 Sidelong (as a glance).<BR>—4 Zero (शून्य); युगान्तसंशुष्कजलौ विजिह्मः Ki. 17. 39.<BR>—5 Pale (विच्छाय); प्रीतो विजिह्मश्च तदीयवृद्धपा Ki. 17. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजुलः|विजुल
विजुलः The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भ्|विजृंभ्
विजृम्भ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To yawn, gape, open the mouth; व्यजृम्भिषत चापरे Bk. 15. 108;<BR> विजृम्भितमिवान्तरिक्षेण Mk. 5. 51.<BR>—2 To open, expand (as a flower).<BR>—3 To spread every where, pervade, fill; सुखश्रवा मङ्गलतूर्यनिस्वनाः …<BR> न केवलं सद्मनि मागधीपतेः पथि व्यजृम्भन्त दिवौकसामपि R. 3. 19, 12. 72;<BR> रजोऽन्धकारस्य विजृम्भितस्य 7. 42.<BR>—4 To rise, appear, show, manifest oneself; तत्खल्विदं विजृम्भते Māl. 7.<BR>—5 To spring back (as a bow).<BR>—6 To display activity.<BR>—7 To become increased or developed.<BR>—8 To begin to feel well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भः|विजृम्भ
विजृम्भः Bending or knitting (the brows); प्रियविरहरुषा रोपितभ्रूविजृम्भत्रस्ताब्धिः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 10. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भणम्
विजृम्भणम्<BR>—1 Gaping, yawning.<BR>—2 Blossoming, budding, blowing, opening; वनेषु सायंतनमल्लिकानां<BR> विजृम्भणोद्गन्धिषु कुड्मलेषु R. 16. 47.<BR>—3 Exhibiting, displaying, unfolding.<BR>—4 Expanding.<BR>—5 Pastime, amorous sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भिका
विजृम्भिका<BR>—1 Gasping for breath.<BR>—2 Yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भित|विजृंभित|विजृम्भितं|विजृम्भितः
विजृम्भित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gaped, yawned; जलधरविवृद्धहनुना विजृम्भितमिवान्तरिक्षेण Mk. 5. 51.<BR>—2 Opened, blown, expanded; तदादिराजस्य यशोविजृम्भितम् Bhāg. 4. 21. 8.<BR>—3 Displayed, exhibited, manifested; विजृम्भितं च दिव्यस्य मङ्गलाय<BR> द्वयोरपि U. 6. 2.<BR>—4 Appeared.<BR>—5 Sported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृम्भितम्
विजृम्भित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Sport, pastime.<BR>—2 Wish, desire.<BR>—3 Display, exhibition; अज्ञानविजृम्भितमेतत्.<BR>—4 An act, action, conduct; उद्भूतभूरिफलशालि विजृम्भितं ते Māl. 10. 21.<BR>—5 Fruit, result.<BR>—6 Yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जनम्
विज्जनम्, -लम्<BR>—1 A kind of sauce; see विजुल.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जलम्
विज्जनम्, -लम्<BR>—1 A kind of sauce; see विजुल.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जिल|विज्जिलं
विज्जिल = विजिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जुलम्
विज्जुलम् Cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञा
विज्ञा €9 U.<BR>—1 To know, be aware of; विजानन्तोऽप्येते वयमिह विपज्जालजटिलान्न<BR> मुञ्चामः कामान् Bh. 3. 21.<BR>—2 To learn, comprehend, understand.<BR>—3 To ascertain, find out, learn from.<BR>—4 To regard, know to be, consider as.<BR>—5 To discern, discriminate, distinguish.<BR>—6 To be familiar with.<BR>—7 To become wise or learned; यथा यथा हि पुरुषः शास्त्रं समधिगच्छति ।<BR> तथा तथा विजानाति Ms. 4. 20.<BR>—8 To explain, declare. ━<i>Caus.</i> (विज्ञापयति)<BR>—1 To request, beg (opp. आज्ञापयति); सीता-आर्यपुत्र अस्ति मे विज्ञाप्यम्;<BR> रामः -नन्वाज्ञापय U. 1; R. 5. 20.<BR>—2 To communicate, inform.<BR>—3 To say, speak in general.<BR>—4 To teach, instruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञ|विज्ञः
विज्ञ, विजानत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Knowing, intelligent, wise, learned.<BR>—2 Clever, skilful, proficient; देशकालनयैर्युक्तो विज्ञः कार्यविनिश्चये<BR> Rām. 4. 40. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानत्
विज्ञ, विजानत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Knowing, intelligent, wise, learned.<BR>—2 Clever, skilful, proficient; देशकालनयैर्युक्तो विज्ञः कार्यविनिश्चये<BR> Rām. 4. 40. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञः|विज्ञ
विज्ञ, विजानत् + .{@-ज्ञः@} A wise or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञता
विज्ञता, विजानता Cleaverness, shrewdness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानता
विज्ञता, विजानता Cleaverness, shrewdness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्त
विज्ञप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Respectfully told, requested.<BR>—2 Made known, informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्तिः|विज्ञप्ति
विज्ञप्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A respectful statement or communication, a request, an entreaty.<BR>—2 An announcement.<BR>—3 Teaching, instruction (उपदेश); तत्त्वसंख्यानविज्ञप्त्यै जातं<BR> विद्वानजः स्वराट् Bhāg. 3. 24. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञात|विज्ञातः
विज्ञात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Known, understood, perceived.<BR>—2 Well-known, celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञातिः|विज्ञाति
विज्ञातिः <i>f.</i> Knowledge; न विज्ञातेर्विज्ञातारं विजानीयाः Bṛ. Up. 3. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानम्
विज्ञानम्<BR>—1 Knowledge, wisdom, intelligence, understanding; यज्जीव्यते क्षणमपि<BR> प्रथितं मनुष्यैर्विज्ञानशौर्यविभवार्यगुणैः समेतम् । तन्नाम जीवितमिह …<BR> Pt. 1. 24, 5. 3; विज्ञानमयः कोशः ‘the sheath of intelligence’<BR> (the first of the five sheaths of the soul).<BR>—2 Discrimination, discernment.<BR>—3 Skill, proficiency; प्रयोगविज्ञानम् Ś. 1. 2.<BR>—4 Worldly or profane knowledge, knowledge derived from worldly experience<BR> (opp. ज्ञान which is ‘knowledge of Brahma or Supreme Spirit’); ज्ञानं<BR> तेऽहं सविज्ञानमिदं वक्ष्याम्यशेषतः Bg. 7. 2, 3. 41, 6. 8; (the whole<BR> of the 7th Adhyāya of Bg. explains ज्ञान and विज्ञान).<BR>—5 Business, employment.<BR>—6 Music.<BR>—7 Knowledge of the fourteen lores.<BR>—8 The organ of knowledge; पञ्चविज्ञानचेतने (शरीरे) Mb. 12. 187. 12.<BR>—9 Knowledge beyond the cognisance of the senses (अतीन्द्रियविषय);<BR> विज्ञानं हि महद्भ्रष्टम् Rām. 3. 71. 30.<BR>—10 Information; लब्धविज्ञानम् Mb. 12. 44. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विज्ञानेश्वर, विज्ञानपादः, विज्ञानमातृकः, विज्ञानयोगः, विज्ञानवादः, विज्ञानस्कन्धः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानेश्वर
विज्ञानम् + -ईश्वर N. of the author of the Mitākṣarā, a commentary on<BR> Yājñavalkyaʼs Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानपादः|विज्ञानपाद
विज्ञानम् + -पादः N. of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानमातृकः|विज्ञानमातृक
विज्ञानम् + -मातृकः an epithet of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानयोगः
विज्ञानम् + -योगः means of arriving at correct knowledge (प्रमाण); केन<BR> विज्ञानयोगेन मतिश्चित्तं समास्थिता Mb. 14. 21. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानवादः|विज्ञानवाद
विज्ञानम् + -वादः the theory of knowledge, the doctrine taught by Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानस्कन्धः|विज्ञानस्कन्ध
विज्ञानम् + -स्कन्धः one of the five स्कन्धs postulated in the Buddhistic<BR> philosophy (रूपवेदनाविज्ञानसंज्ञासंस्काराः क्षणिकविज्ञानस्कन्धे स्मृतिरनुपपन्ना)<BR> ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानमय
विज्ञानमय <i>a.</i> Full of intelligence; एष विज्ञानमयः पुरुषः<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 6. ˚कोषः the soulʼs sheath of intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानिक|विज्ञानिकः
विज्ञानिक <i>a.</i> Wise, learned; see विज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापकः|विज्ञापक
विज्ञापकः<BR>—1 An informant.<BR>—2 A teacher, an instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापनम्
विज्ञापनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Respectful statement or communication, a request, an entreaty; कालप्रयुक्ता<BR> खलु कार्यविद्भिर्विज्ञापना भर्तृषु सिद्धिमेति Ku. 7. 93; R. 17. 40.<BR>—2 Information, representation.<BR>—3 Instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापना
विज्ञापनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Respectful statement or communication, a request, an entreaty; कालप्रयुक्ता<BR> खलु कार्यविद्भिर्विज्ञापना भर्तृषु सिद्धिमेति Ku. 7. 93; R. 17. 40.<BR>—2 Information, representation.<BR>—3 Instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापित
विज्ञापित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Respectfully told or communicated.<BR>—2 Requested.<BR>—3 Informed.<BR>—4 Instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाप्ति|विज्ञाप्तिः
विज्ञाप्ति See विज्ञप्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1434-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाप्यम्
विज्ञाप्यम् A request; U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञेय|विज्ञेयं
विज्ञेय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Knowable, cognizable.<BR>—2 To be learned.<BR>—3 To be regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्य
विज्य <i>a.</i> Stringless (as a bow); विज्ये बिभर्षि धनुषी सुहृदात्मनोऽर्थे<BR> Bhāg. 5. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्वर
विज्वर <i>a.</i> Free from fever, anxiety or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जामरम्
विञ्जामरम् The white of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जोलिः|विञ्जोलि
विञ्जोलिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> A line, row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विञ्जोली|विंजोली
विञ्जोलिः, -ली <i>f.</i><BR> A line, row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्
विट् €1 P. (वेटति)<BR>—1 To sound.<BR>—2 To curse, rail at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटः|विट
विटः [विट्-क]<BR>—1 A paramour; त्वद्वत्सलः क्व स तपस्विजनस्य हन्ता कन्याविटः<BR> पतिरसौ परिरक्षतु त्वाम् Māl. 8. 8; Śi. 4. 48.<BR>—2 A voluptuary, sensualist; प्रतिक्षणं नव्यवदच्युतस्य यत् स्त्रिया<BR> विटानामिव साधुवार्ता Bhāg. 10. 13. 2.<BR>—3 (In dramas) The companion of a prince or dissolute young man, or of<BR> a courtezan (who is described as being skilled in the arts of singing,<BR> music, and poetry and as a parasite on familiar terms with his associate<BR> to whom he nearly serves the purpose of the Vidūṣaka; see <i>inter alia</i><BR> Mk. acts 1, 5 and 8); for definition, see S. D. 78; अन्येभ्यश्च वसन्ति<BR> येऽस्य भवने लब्धप्रसादा विटाः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>—4 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—5 A catamite.<BR>—6 A rat.<BR>—7 The Khadira tree.<BR>—8 The orange tree.<BR>—9 A branch together with its shoot.<BR>—10 A mineral salt.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विटकान्ता, विटपेटकः, विटकम्, विटमाक्षिकम्, विटलवणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटकान्ता
विटः + -कान्ता turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपेटकः|विटपेटक
विटः + -पेटकः, -कम् a multitude of rogues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटकम्
विटः + -पेटकः, -कम् a multitude of rogues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटमाक्षिकम्
विटः + -माक्षिकम् a kind of mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटलवणम्
विटः + -लवणम् a medicinal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटकः|विटक
विटकः (= पिटकः) A boil, blister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्क|विटंक|विटंकः|विटङ्कः
विटङ्क <i>a.</i> Nice, handsome, beautiful; केयूरकुण्डलकिरीटविटङ्कवेषौ<BR> Bhāg. 3. 15. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्कः|विटङ्क|विटंक|विटंकः
विटङ्कः [विशेषेण टङ्कपते बध्यते इति]<BR>—1 An aviary, dove-cot; गुम्फितैरुशनसा सुभाषितैर्यस्य हाटकविटङ्कमङ्कितम्<BR> N. 18. 24; सभारण्यविटङ्कवान् Mb. 1. 1. 88; Mv. 5. 21.<BR>—2 The loftiest point, pinnacle, elevation; अयमेव महीधरविटङ्कः<BR> Māl. 10; Vikr. 5. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्कक|विटङ्ककः
विटङ्कक See विटङ्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटङ्कित|विटंकित
विटङ्कित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Marked, stamped.<BR>—2 Adorned; रोमोत्सवो मम यदङ्घ्निविटङ्कितायाः Bhāg. 1. 16. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपः|विटप
विटपः [विटं विस्तारं वा पाति पिबति पा˚ क Tv.]<BR>—1 A branch, bough (of a creeper or tree); कोमलविटपानुकारिणौ बाहू<BR> Ś. 1. 21, 31; यदनेन तरुर्न पातितः क्षपिता तद्विटपाश्रिता लता<BR> R. 8. 47; Śi. 4. 48; Ku. 6. 41.<BR>—2 A bush.<BR>—3 A new shoot or sprout; व्रज विटपममुं ददस्व तस्यै Śi. 7. 53.<BR>—4 A cluster, clump, thicket.<BR>—5 Extension.<BR>—6 The septum of the scrotum.<BR>—7 A creeper (लता); यो विस्फुरद्भ्रूविटपेन भूमेर्भारं कृतान्तेन<BR> तिरश्चकार Bhāg. 3. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपिन्
विटपिन् <i>m.</i> [विटप-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>—1 A tree; परितो दृष्टाश्च विटपिनः सर्वे Bv. 1. 21, 29.<BR>—2 The fig-tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विटपिमृगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपिमृगः|विटपिमृग
विटपिन् + -मृगः a monkey, an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटिः|विटि
विटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> Yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटी
विटिः, -टी <i>f.</i><BR> Yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्ठलः|विट्ठल
विट्ठ(ठ्ठ)लः^1 N. of a form of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (worshipped at<BR> Pandharpur in the Bombay presidency); ‘श्रुत्वा नामसहस्रं श्रीविठ्ठलस्य गुणान्वितम् ।’ -श्रीविठ्ठलाष्टोत्तरशतनामस्तोत्रम् 1;<BR> ‘शिरो मे विठ्ठलः पातु’ -विठ्ठलकवचम्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf Other dictionaries (AP90, MW, PWG).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठ्ठलः
विट्ठ(ठ्ठ)लः^1 N. of a form of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (worshipped at<BR> Pandharpur in the Bombay presidency); ‘श्रुत्वा नामसहस्रं श्रीविठ्ठलस्य गुणान्वितम् ।’ -श्रीविठ्ठलाष्टोत्तरशतनामस्तोत्रम् 1;<BR> ‘शिरो मे विठ्ठलः पातु’ -विठ्ठलकवचम्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf Other dictionaries (AP90, MW, PWG).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठङ्क|विठंक
विठङ्क <i>a.</i> Bad, vile, base, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठरः|विठर
विठरः<BR>—1 N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR>—2 [वदति अबद्धम्, वदेः अष्ठश्च, इत् च Uṇ. 5. 46] A fool.<BR>—3 An orator; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड् €1 P. (वेडति)<BR>—1 To curse, rail at, revile.<BR>—2 To cry out loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड्, विडः A fragment, bit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडः|विड|विडं
विड्, विडः A fragment, bit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्
विडम् A kind of artificial salt (Mar. बिडलोण); Mb. 13. 91. 40;<BR> विडं सक्षारमूर्ध्वाधः कफवातानुलोमनम् Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्ग|विडंग|विडङ्गं|विडङ्गः
विडङ्ग <i>a.</i> Clever, skilful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्गः|विडङ्ग|विडंग|विडङ्गं
विडङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गः, -ङ्गम्@} N. of a vegetable and medicinal substance (largely<BR> used as a vermifuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडङ्गम्
विडङ्ग + .{@-ङ्गः, -ङ्गम्@} N. of a vegetable and medicinal substance (largely<BR> used as a vermifuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्ब्|विडंब्
विडम्ब् €10 U.<BR>—1 To imitate, copy, resemble; (तं) ऋतुर्विडम्बयामास न पुनः<BR> प्राप तच्छ्रियम् R. 4. 17; वपुःप्रकर्षेण विडम्बितेश्वरः 3. 52, 13. 29, 16. 11;<BR> Ki. 5. 46, 12. 38; Śi. 1. 6, 12. 5, 16. 58.<BR>—2 To ridicule, deride, mock; संमोहयन्ति मदयन्ति विडम्बयन्ति निर्भर्त्सयन्ति<BR> रमयन्ति विषादयन्ति Bh. 1. 22; यथा न विडम्ब्यसे जनैः K. 109.<BR>—3 To cheat, deceive; एवमात्माभिप्रायसंभावितेष्टजनचित्तवृत्तिः प्रार्थयिता<BR> विडम्बयते Ś. 2.<BR>—4 To afflict, pain, molest.<BR>—5 To transform, distort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बः|विडम्ब|विडंब|विडंबः
विडम्बः<BR>—1 Imitation.<BR>—2 Distressing, afflicting, molesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बक
विडम्बक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Imitating.<BR>—2 Disgracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बनम्
विडम्बनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Imitation; न वेद कश्चिद् भगवंश्चिकीर्षितं तवेहमानस्य नृणां<BR> विडम्बनम् Bhāg. 1. 8. 29.<BR>—2 Disguise, imposture.<BR>—3 Deception, fraud.<BR>—4 Vexation, mortification.<BR>—5 Paining, distressing.<BR>—6 Disappointing.<BR>—7 Ridiculousness, mockery, a matter for laughter; इयं च तेऽन्या पुरतो<BR> विडम्बना Ku. 5. 70; असति त्वयि वारुणीमदः प्रमदानामधुना विडम्बना 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बना
विडम्बनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Imitation; न वेद कश्चिद् भगवंश्चिकीर्षितं तवेहमानस्य नृणां<BR> विडम्बनम् Bhāg. 1. 8. 29.<BR>—2 Disguise, imposture.<BR>—3 Deception, fraud.<BR>—4 Vexation, mortification.<BR>—5 Paining, distressing.<BR>—6 Disappointing.<BR>—7 Ridiculousness, mockery, a matter for laughter; इयं च तेऽन्या पुरतो<BR> विडम्बना Ku. 5. 70; असति त्वयि वारुणीमदः प्रमदानामधुना विडम्बना 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बित|विडंबित|विडम्बितः
विडम्बित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Imitated, copied.<BR>—2 Mocked, ridiculed.<BR>—3 Deceived.<BR>—4 Vexed, mortified.<BR>—5 Frustrated.<BR>—6 Low, abject, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्बितम्
विडम्बित + .{@-तम्@} An object of ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडम्ब्यम्
विडम्ब्यम् An object of ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडारकः|विडारक
विडारकः A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडाल|विडालः
विडाल, विडालक See बिडाल, बिडालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालक|विडालकं|विडालकः
विडाल, विडालक See बिडाल, बिडालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडीनम्
विडीनम् One of the several modes of flight of birds; see डीन;<BR> Mb. 8. 41. 27 (com. विडम्बितं बिडीनं स्यात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडुलः|विडुल
विडुलः A sort of cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1435-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडूरजम्
विडूरजम् <i>Lapis lazuli</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडोजस्
विडो(डौ)जस् <i>m.</i> N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडौजस्
विडो(डौ)जस् <i>m.</i> N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंसः|वितंस
वितंसः<BR>—1 A bird-cage.<BR>—2 A rope, chain, fetter &c. to confine beasts or birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितड्
वितड् €10 P. To strike, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितण्डः|वितण्ड|वितंडः
वितण्डः<BR>—1 An elephant.<BR>—2 A sort of lock or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितण्डा|वितंडा
वितण्डा<BR>—1 A captious objection, idle carping, a frivolous or fallacious argument<BR> or controversy (one of the sixteen <i>padārthas</i> or categories in Nyāya<BR> philosophy); स (जल्पः) प्रतिपक्षस्थापनाहीनो वितण्डा Gaut. S.<BR>—2 Wrangling, captious criticism in general.<BR>—3 A spoon, ladle.<BR>—4 Benzoin.<BR>—5 The oleander plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ|वितथं
वितथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untrue, false; आजन्मनो न भवता वितथं किलोक्तम् Ve. 3. 13, 5. 41; R. 9. 8.<BR>—2 Vain, futile; as in वितथप्रयत्न R. 2. 42.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वितथमर्याद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथमर्याद
वितथ + -मर्याद <i>a.</i> incorrect in behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ्य|वितथ्यं
वितथ्य <i>a.</i> False; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथयति
वितथयति Den. P. To make false; वितथयति न जातु मद्वचोऽसाविति Śi. 7. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितद्रुः|वितद्रु
वितद्रुः <i>f.</i> N. of a river in the Panjāb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्
वितन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To spread, stretch; स्फुरितविततजिह्वः Mk. 9. 12; Ki. 15. 53;<BR> Śi. 5. 38, 14. 53.<BR>—2 To cover, fill; प्रस्वेदबिन्दुविततं वदनं प्रियायाः C. P. 9;<BR> यो वितत्य स्थितः खम् Me. 60.<BR>—3 To form, make; श्रेणीबन्धाद् वितन्वद्भिरस्तम्भाम् तोरणस्रजम् R. 1. 41;<BR> Ki. 16. 51.<BR>—4 To stretch, string (as a bow); वितत्य किरतोः शरान् U. 6. 1; वितत्य<BR> शार्ङ्गम् Bk. 3. 47.<BR>—5 To cause, produce, create, give, bestow; V. 1. 4.<BR>—6 To write or compose (as a work); विराटपर्वप्रद्योती भावदीपो वितन्यते.<BR>—7 To do or perform (as a sacrifice or any other rite); यज्वभिः संभृतं<BR> हव्यं विततेष्वध्वरेषु सः Ku. 2. 46.<BR>—8 To unfold, manifest, exhibit, show; स्मरसि रुदितैः स्नेहाकूतं तथाप्यतनोदसौ Māl. 9. 11.<BR>—9 To perform, carry out, accomplish.<BR>—10 To prepare, make ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत|विततं
वितत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spread out, extended, stretched; अमुं यज्ञं विततमेयाय Ch. Up. 1. 10. 7.<BR>—2 Elongated, large, long, broad; विततवपुषा महाहिना Ki. 12. 22;<BR> भवति विततश्वासोन्नाहप्रणुन्नपयोधरम् Māl. 10. 15.<BR>—3 Performed, accomplished, effected; विततयज्ञः Ś. 7. 34.<BR>—4 Covered.<BR>—5 Diffused.<BR>—6 Gone away; शब्दवेध्यं च विततम् Rām. 1. 5. 20.<BR>—7 Drawn (as a bow string).<BR>—8 Bent (as a bow); (see तन् with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततम्
वितत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Any stringed instrument, such as a lute &c.<BR>—2 A shoot, tendril (प्रतान); विचिताश्च महागुल्मा लताविततसंतताः<BR> Rām. 4. 47. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विततोत्सव, विततधन्वन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततोत्सव
वितत + -उत्सव <i>a.</i> one who has arranged a festival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततधन्वन्
वितत + -धन्वन् <i>a.</i> one who has fully drawn or stretched his bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततिः|वितति
विततिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Extension, expansion; व्रततिविततिभिस्तिरोहितायाम् Śi. 7. 45; Ki. 6. 18.<BR>—2 Quantity, collection,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">Page1436-2</a>]<BR> cluster, clump; वंशविततिषु विषक्तपृथुप्रियबालाः Ki. 12. 47.<BR>—3 A line, row; यदकालमेघविततिर्व्ययूयुजत् Māl. 9. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितनु|वितनुः
वितनु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Delicate.<BR>—2 Beautiful.<BR>—3 Slender.<BR>—4 Bodiless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितनुः|वितनु
वितनु + .{@-नुः@} The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्तुः|वितन्तु|वितंतुः
वितन्तुः A good horse. ━<i>f.</i> A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्त्री
वितन्त्री A disordered or discordant lute; श्रोतुर्वितन्त्रीरिव ताड्यमाना Ku. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितप्
वितप् Ā.<BR>—1 To shine; रविर्वितपतेऽत्यर्थम् Bk. 8. 14.<BR>—2 To warm, heat.<BR>—3 To warm oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितमस्
वितमस्, वितमस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Light.<BR>—2 Free from darkness or the quality of ignorance (तमस्).<BR>—3 Pure, blemishless; ख्याते तस्मिन् वितमसि कुले जन्म कौलीनमेतत् Ve. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितमस्क
वितमस्, वितमस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Light.<BR>—2 Free from darkness or the quality of ignorance (तमस्).<BR>—3 Pure, blemishless; ख्याते तस्मिन् वितमसि कुले जन्म कौलीनमेतत् Ve. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्
वितर्क् €10 U.<BR>—1 To guess, conjecture.<BR>—2 To think, suppose, believe.<BR>—3 To reflect, reason.<BR>—4 To expect, anticipate.<BR>—5 To find out, discover, ascertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कः|वितर्क
वितर्कः<BR>—1 Argument, reasoning, inference.<BR>—2 Guess, conjecture, supposition, belief; शिरीषपुष्पाधिकसौकुमार्यौ<BR> बाहू तदीयाविति मे वितर्कः Ku. 1. 41.<BR>—3 Fancy, thought; रागग्राहवती वितर्कविहगा Bh. 3. 45.<BR>—4 Doubt; नुनोद तस्य स्थलपद्मिनीगतं वितर्कम् Ki. 4. 5, 13. 2.<BR>—5 Deliberation, discussion.<BR>—6 A teacher in divine knowledge.<BR>—7 False or adverse conjecture; वितर्कं निश्चयाज्जयेत् Mb. 12. 274. 11.<BR>—8 Purpose, intention.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वितर्कपदवी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कपदवी
वितर्कः + -पदवी the path of conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कणम्
वितर्कणम्<BR>—1 Reasoning.<BR>—2 Conjecturing, guessing.<BR>—3 Doubt.<BR>—4 Discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दिः|वितर्दि|वितर्द्दिः
वितर्दिः, -र्दी, वितर्दिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A raised seat of a quadrangular shape in a court-yard; वितर्दिशतशोभितम्<BR> (रामवेश्म) Rām. 2. 15. 31, 80. 20; बध्यन्ते च वितर्दिकाः प्रतिदिशं<BR> कृत्तै रदोमूर्धभिः Mv. 6. 24.<BR>—2 A balcony, verandah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्र्दी
वितर्दिः, -र्दी, वितर्दिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A raised seat of a quadrangular shape in a court-yard; वितर्दिशतशोभितम्<BR> (रामवेश्म) Rām. 2. 15. 31, 80. 20; बध्यन्ते च वितर्दिकाः प्रतिदिशं<BR> कृत्तै रदोमूर्धभिः Mv. 6. 24.<BR>—2 A balcony, verandah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दिका|वितर्द्दिका
वितर्दिः, -र्दी, वितर्दिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A raised seat of a quadrangular shape in a court-yard; वितर्दिशतशोभितम्<BR> (रामवेश्म) Rām. 2. 15. 31, 80. 20; बध्यन्ते च वितर्दिकाः प्रतिदिशं<BR> कृत्तै रदोमूर्धभिः Mv. 6. 24.<BR>—2 A balcony, verandah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धिः|वितर्धि
वितर्द्धिः, -र्द्धी, वितर्द्धिका <i>f.</i> See वितर्दि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धी
वितर्द्धिः, -र्द्धी, वितर्द्धिका <i>f.</i> See वितर्दि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धिका
वितर्द्धिः, -र्द्धी, वितर्द्धिका <i>f.</i> See वितर्दि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितलम्
वितलम् The second of the seven lower regions under the earth; see<BR> पाताल or लोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ता
वितस्ता N. of a river in the Punjab called Hydaspes by the Greeks<BR> and now called Jhelum or Betustā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्तिः|वितस्ति
वितस्तिः [वौ तसेः तिः Uṇ. 4. 189] A measure of length equal<BR> to 12 <i>aṅgulas</i> (being the distance between the extended thumb and<BR> the little finger); तेनेदमावृतं विश्वं वितस्तिमधितिष्ठति Bhāg. 2. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वितान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Vacant, empty.<BR>—2 Pithless.<BR>—3 Dismayed, sad; क्षितिपतिमण्डलमन्यतो वितानम् R. 6. 86.<BR>—4 Dull, stupid.<BR>—5 Wicked, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानः|वितान|वितानं
वितान + .{@-नः, -नम्@}<BR>—1 Spreading out, expansion, extension; ब्रह्मावर्ते यत्र यजन्ति यज्ञैर्यज्ञेश्वरं<BR> यज्ञवितानविज्ञाः Bhāg. 1. 17. 33; विलुलितकमलौघः कीर्णवल्लीवितानः<BR> Śi. 11. 28; Ki. 7. 19.<BR>—2 An awning, a canopy; विद्युलेखाकनकरुचिरं श्रीवितानं ममाभ्रम्<BR> V. 4. 13; R. 19. 39;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">Page1437-1</a>]<BR> Ki. 3. 42; Śi. 3. 50.<BR>—3 A cushion.<BR>—4 A collection, quantity, an assemblage; प्रस्तारस्थगिता इवोन्मुखमणिज्योतिर्वितानैर्दिशः<BR> Māl. 6. 5; Ki. 17. 61.<BR>—5 A sacrifice, an oblation; वितानेष्वप्येवं तव मम च सोमे विधिरभूत्<BR> Ve. 6. 30, 3. 16; Śi. 14. 10.<BR>—6 The sacrificial hearth or altar.<BR>—7 Season, opportunity.<BR>—8 Plenty, abundance.<BR>—9 Performance, accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानम्
वितान + .{@-नः, -नम्@}<BR>—1 Spreading out, expansion, extension; ब्रह्मावर्ते यत्र यजन्ति यज्ञैर्यज्ञेश्वरं<BR> यज्ञवितानविज्ञाः Bhāg. 1. 17. 33; विलुलितकमलौघः कीर्णवल्लीवितानः<BR> Śi. 11. 28; Ki. 7. 19.<BR>—2 An awning, a canopy; विद्युलेखाकनकरुचिरं श्रीवितानं ममाभ्रम्<BR> V. 4. 13; R. 19. 39;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">Page1437-1</a>]<BR> Ki. 3. 42; Śi. 3. 50.<BR>—3 A cushion.<BR>—4 A collection, quantity, an assemblage; प्रस्तारस्थगिता इवोन्मुखमणिज्योतिर्वितानैर्दिशः<BR> Māl. 6. 5; Ki. 17. 61.<BR>—5 A sacrifice, an oblation; वितानेष्वप्येवं तव मम च सोमे विधिरभूत्<BR> Ve. 6. 30, 3. 16; Śi. 14. 10.<BR>—6 The sacrificial hearth or altar.<BR>—7 Season, opportunity.<BR>—8 Plenty, abundance.<BR>—9 Performance, accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानम्
वितान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Leisure, rest.<BR>—2 A dual part of the elephantʼs head to which the hook is applied; Mātaṅga L. 12. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1436-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानकः|वितानक|वितानकं
वितानकः, -कम्<BR>—1 An expanse.<BR>—2 A heap, quantity collection, mass; बंहीयसा दीप्तिवितानकेन चकासयामासतुरुल्लसन्ती<BR> Śi. 3. 6, 6. 27.<BR>—3 An awning, a canopy.<BR>—4 The tree called Māḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानकम्
वितानकः, -कम्<BR>—1 An expanse.<BR>—2 A heap, quantity collection, mass; बंहीयसा दीप्तिवितानकेन चकासयामासतुरुल्लसन्ती<BR> Śi. 3. 6, 6. 27.<BR>—3 An awning, a canopy.<BR>—4 The tree called Māḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानायते
वितानायते Den. Ā. To act or serve as an awning; प्राग्भारेषु शिखण्डिताण्डवविधौ<BR> मेघैर्वितानाय्यते Māl. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानीकृ
वितानीकृ €8 U. To spread or extend over (as a canopy), overshadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितायमान
वितायमान <i>a.</i> [तनोतेः यकि शानच् P. VI. 4. 44] Being spread<BR> out; आसीदथर्वा त्रिवलित्रिवेदी मूलाद् विनिर्गत्य वितायमाना N. 10. 74;<BR> वितायमानयशसस्तदाश्रमपदं ययुः Bhāg. 4. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितार
वितार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Starless.<BR>—2 Without a nucleus (as a comet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विताल|वितालः
विताल <i>a.</i> Breaking time (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितालः|विताल
विताल + .{@-लः@} Wrong time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विताली
विताल + .{@-ली@} An instrument for beating time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्न|वितुन्नं
वितुन्न <i>a.</i> Pierced, torn; निष्फलेषु वितुन्नाङ्गो नङ्क्ष्यतीत्यत्र<BR> का प्रमा Pañcadaśī 7. 280.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नम्
वितुन्नम्<BR>—1 The pot-herb called सुनिषण्णक.<BR>—2 The plant called शैवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नकम्
वितुन्नकम्<BR>—1 Coriander-seed.<BR>—2 Blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नकः|वितुन्नक|वितुन्नकं
वितुन्नकम् + .{@-कः@} The plant called तामलकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृप्त
वितृप्त <i>p. p.</i> Satisfied, satiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुष्ट
वितुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Dissatisfied, displeased, discontented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्ण
वितृष्ण <i>a.</i> Free from desire, content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्णा
वितृष्ण + .{@-ष्णा@} Ardent desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितॄ
वितॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To cross or pass over, go beyond; आरूढमद्रीनुदधीन् वितीर्णम् R. 6. 77.<BR>—2 To give, grant, impart, confer or bestow on, vouchsafe, favour with;<BR> भगवान् मारीचस्ते दर्शनं वितरति Ś. 7; वितरति गुरुः प्राज्ञे<BR> विद्यां यथैव तथा जडे U. 2. 4; वितरति नृपो नोचितमहो Pt. 1. 11;<BR> U. 3. 48; निवासहेतोरुटजं वितेरुः R. 14. 81; Māl. 1. 3, 6. 7, 9. 5, 44.<BR>—3 To cause, produce; ज्योत्स्नाशङ्कामिह वितरति हंसश्रेणी Ki. 5. 31.<BR>—4 To carry over, ferry over.<BR>—5 To give (as medicine), apply a remedy.<BR>—6 To do, perform.<BR>—7 To forgive, pardon.<BR>—8 To increase, enhance. ━<i>Caus.</i> To carry through, accomplish (fig. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरणम्
वितरणम्<BR>—1 Crossing over.<BR>—2 A gift, donation, present; पूर्णाशा बहवः कृता वितरणैर्येन त्वया<BR> याचकाः Subhāṣ.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">Page1437-2</a>]<BR>—3 Giving up, leaving, abandoning.<BR>—4 Leading over, transference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितीर्ण
वितीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Crossed or passed over.<BR>—2 Given, bestowed, imparted; करकमलवितीर्णैः U. 3. 25; Śi. 7. 67, 17. 15.<BR>—3 Gone down, descended; R. 6. 77.<BR>—4 Conveyed.<BR>—5 Subdued, overcome (see तॄ with वि).<BR>—6 Fought (as a battle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त्
वित्त् €10 U. (वित्तयति-ते; वित्तापयति-ते also according to some)<BR> To give away, give as alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त <i>p. p.</i> [विद् लाभे क्त]<BR>—1 Found, discovered.<BR>—2 Gained, acquired.<BR>—3 Examined, investigated.<BR>—4 Known, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तम्
वित्त + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth, possessions, property, substance.<BR>—2 Power.<BR>—3 Gold; L. D. B.<BR>—4 The second astrological mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वित्तागमः, वित्तोपार्जनम्, वित्तेशः, वित्तपः, वित्तपतिः, वित्तपालः, वित्तेहा, वित्तजानि, वित्तदः, वित्तपेटा, वित्तपेटी, वित्तमात्रा, वित्तवर्धन, वित्तसमागमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तागमः|वित्तागम
वित्त + -आगमः, -उपार्जनम् acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तोपार्जनम्
वित्त + -आगमः, -उपार्जनम् acquisition of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तेशः|वित्तेश
वित्त + -ईशः, -पः, -पतिः, -पालः an epithet of Kubera; रुद्राणां शंकरश्चास्मि<BR> वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् Bg. 10. 23; Ms. 7. 4; Bhāg. 5. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तपः|वित्तप
वित्त + -ईशः, -पः, -पतिः, -पालः an epithet of Kubera; रुद्राणां शंकरश्चास्मि<BR> वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् Bg. 10. 23; Ms. 7. 4; Bhāg. 5. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तपतिः|वित्तपति
वित्त + -ईशः, -पः, -पतिः, -पालः an epithet of Kubera; रुद्राणां शंकरश्चास्मि<BR> वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् Bg. 10. 23; Ms. 7. 4; Bhāg. 5. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तपालः|वित्तपाल
वित्त + -ईशः, -पः, -पतिः, -पालः an epithet of Kubera; रुद्राणां शंकरश्चास्मि<BR> वित्तेशो यक्षरक्षसाम् Bg. 10. 23; Ms. 7. 4; Bhāg. 5. 10. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तेहा
वित्त + -ईहा <i>f.</i> a desire for wealth; धर्मार्थं यस्य वित्तेहा वरं<BR> तस्य निरीहता । प्रक्षालनाद्धि पङ्कस्य दूरादस्पर्शनं वरम् ॥ Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तजानि
वित्त + -जानि <i>a.</i> one who has married a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तदः|वित्तद
वित्त + -दः a donor, benefactor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तपेटा
वित्त + -पेटा, -पेटी money-receptacle, purse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तपेटी
वित्त + -पेटा, -पेटी money-receptacle, purse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तमात्रा
वित्त + -मात्रा property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तवर्धन
वित्त + -वर्धन <i>a.</i> profitable, lucrative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तसमागमः
वित्त + -समागमः acquisition of wealth, income; भूरिव्यया प्रचुरवित्तसमागमा<BR> च Pt. 1. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तवत्|वित्तवन्त्
वित्तवत् <i>a.</i> Rich, wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तिः|वित्ति
वित्तिः <i>f.</i> [विद्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Knowledge.<BR>—2 Judgment, discrimination, thought.<BR>—3 Gain, acquisition.<BR>—4 Likelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रस्
वित्रस् €1. €4 P. To be frightened or terrified; वित्रस्तमुग्धहरिणीसदृशैः<BR> कटाक्षैः Bh. 1. 9. ━<i>Caus.</i> To terrify, frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रासः|वित्रास
वित्रासः Fear, alarm, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रिभलग्नकम्
वित्रिभलग्नकम् The highest point of the ecliptic above the horizon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्सनः|वित्सन
वित्सनः An ox, a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्
विथ् €1 Ā. (वेथते) To beg, ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुरः|विथुर
विथुरः [व्यथ्-उरच् संप्रसारणं च Uṇ. 1. 40]<BR>—1 A demon.<BR>—2 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुरा
विथुरः + .{@-रा@} A widow; cf. विधुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् I. €2 P. (वेत्ति or वेद, विवेद-विदांचकार, अवेदीत्, वेत्स्यति,<BR> वेत्तुम्, विदित; <i>desid.</i> विविदिषति)<BR>—1 To know, understand, learn, find out, ascertain, discover; न चैतद्विमः<BR> कतरन्नो गरीयो यद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः Bg. 2. 5; तं मोहान्धः<BR> कथमयममुं वेत्तु देवं पुराणम् Ve. 1. 23, 3. 39; Ś. 5. 27; R. 3. 43;<BR> Bg. 4. 34, 18. 1.<BR>—2 To feel, experience; परायत्तः प्रीतेः कथमिव रसं वेत्ति पुरुषः Mu. 3. 4.<BR>—3 To look upon, regard, consider, know or take to be; य एनं वेत्ति<BR> हन्तारम् Bg. 2. 19; विद्धि व्याधिव्यालग्रस्तं लोकं शोकहतं च समस्तम्<BR> Moha M. 5; Bg. 2. 17; Ms. 1. 33; Ku. 6. 30. ━<i>Caus.</i> (वेदयति-ते)<BR>—1 To make known, communicate, inform, apprise, tell.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">Page1438-1</a>]<BR>—2 To teach, expound; वेदार्थं स्वानवेदयत् Sk.<BR>—3 To feel, experience; येन वेदयते सर्वं सुखं दुःखं च जन्मसु<BR> Ms. 12. 13. ━II. €4 Ā. (विद्यते, वित्त)<BR>—1 To be, to exist; अपापानां कुले जाते मयि पापं न विद्यते Mk. 9. 37;<BR> नासतो विद्यते भावो नाभावो विद्यते सतः Bg. 2. 16; (cf. the root (1) अस्).<BR>—2 To happen. ━III. €6 U. (विन्दति-ते, वित्त)<BR>—1 To get, obtain, acquire, gain; एकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विन्दते<BR> फलम् Bg. 5. 4; Y. 3. 192.<BR>—2 To find, discover, recognise; यथा धेनुसहस्रेषु वत्सो विन्दति मातरम्<BR> Subhāṣ.; Ms. 8. 109.<BR>—3 To feel, experience; R. 14. 56; Bg. 5. 21, 11. 24, 18. 45.<BR>—4 To marry; Ms. 9. 69. ━IV. €7 Ā. (विन्त्ते, वित्त or विन्न)<BR>—1 To know, understand.<BR>—2 To consider, regard, take for; न तृणेह्मीति लोकोऽयं विन्त्ते मां निष्पराक्रमम् Bk. 6. 39.<BR>—3 To find, meet with.<BR>—4 To reason, reflect.<BR>—5 To examine, inquire into. ━V. €10 Ā. (वेदयते)<BR>—1 To tell, declare, announce, communicate.<BR>—2 To feel, experience.<BR>—3 To dwell. (The following verse illustrates the root in some of its<BR> conjugations:− वेत्ति सर्वाणि शास्त्राणि गर्वस्तस्य न विद्यते । विन्त्ते<BR> धर्मं सदा सद्भिस्तेषु पूजां च विन्दति ॥ cf. also:− सत्तायां विद्यते<BR> ज्ञाते वेत्ति विन्त्ते विचारणे । विन्दते विन्दति प्राप्तौ श्यन्लुक् श्नम्शोष्विदं<BR> क्रमात् ॥) [cf. L. <i>video</i>; A. S. <i>witan</i>; Goth. <i>vait</i>].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1437-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.) Knowing, conversant with; वेदविद्<BR> &c.; यानि वेदविदां श्रेष्ठो भगवान् बादरायणः Bhāg. 1. 1. 7; Mv. 1. 26. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The planet Mercury.<BR>—2 A learned man, wise man. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Knowledge.<BR>—2 Understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदः|विद
विदः<BR>—1 A learned man, wise man or Paṇḍita.<BR>—2 The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदा
विदः + .{@-दा@}<BR>—1 Knowledge, learning.<BR>—2 Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदत्
विदत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Knowing.<BR>—2 Wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित|विदितं|विदितः
विदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Known, understood, learnt; अविदितगतयामा रात्रिरेव व्यरंसीत् U. 1. 27.<BR>—2 Informed.<BR>—3 Renowned, celebrated, well-known; भुवनविदिते वंशे Me. 6.<BR>—4 Promised, agreed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदितः|विदित|विदितं
विदित + .{@-तः@} A learned man, scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदितम्
विदित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Knowledge, information.<BR>—2 Celebrity, fame. —3 Acquisition, gaining.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विदितात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदितात्मन्
विदित + -आत्मन्<BR>—1 Celebrated; तस्य चिन्तयतो नित्यं धर्मेण विदितात्मनः Rām. 1. 42. 7.<BR>—2 One who knows oneself; ततो नित्यानुगस्तेषां विदितात्मा महामतिः<BR> Rām. 2. 103. 22. ━<i>m.</i> the almighty (परमेश्वर); सर्वमार्षं<BR> हि मन्यन्ते व्याहृतं विदितात्मनः Mb. 12. 268. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुषः|विदुष
विदुषः A learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुषी
विदुषः + .{@-षी@} A wise or learned woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदंशः|विदंश
विदंशः Pungent food such as excites thirst; स्वादितः सकृदिवासव<BR> एव प्रत्युत क्षणविदंशपदेऽभूत् Śi. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
विदग्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Burnt up, consumed by fire.<BR>—2 Cooked.<BR>—3 Digested.<BR>—4 Destroyed, decomposed.<BR>—5 Clever, shrewed, sharp, subtle; नाविदग्धः प्रियं ब्रूयात् Pt. 1. 164; U. 4. 21.<BR>—6 Crafty, artful, intriguing.<BR>—7 Unburnt or ill-digested.<BR>—8 Lovely, charming.<BR>—9 Respectable<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">Page1438-2</a>]<BR> (as dress &c.).<BR>—10 Mature (as a tumour).<BR>—11 Tawny, reddish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धः|विदग्ध
विदग्ध + .{@-ग्धः@}<BR>—1 A wise or learned man, scholar; वृद्धा विदग्धाः प्रविशन्त्यत्र विप्राः Mb. 3. 133. 5.<BR>—2 A libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धा
विदग्ध + .{@-ग्धा@} A shrewd and clever woman, an artful woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विदग्धपरिवृद्धता, विदग्धपरिषद्, विदग्धवचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धपरिवृद्धता
विदग्ध + -परिवृद्धता the turning acid and swelling (of food in the stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धपरिषद्
विदग्ध + -परिषद् <i>f.</i> an assembly of clever people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धवचन
विदग्ध + -वचन <i>a.</i> clever in speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धता
विदग्धता, -त्वम्<BR> Shrewdness, cleverness; skill, elegance &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धत्वम्
विदग्धता, -त्वम्<BR> Shrewdness, cleverness; skill, elegance &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदण्डः|विदण्ड
विदण्डः A door-key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथः|विदथ
विदथः [विदेः अथः कित् Uṇ. 3. 115]<BR>—1 A learned man, scholar.<BR>—2 An ascetic, a sage.<BR>—3 Ved. A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथम्
विदथः + .{@-थम्@} Ved.<BR>—1 Knowledge.<BR>—2 A sacrifice.<BR>—3 A battle (?).<BR>—4 A meeting, assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदरः|विदर|विदरं
विदरः<BR>—1 Breaking, bursting, rending.<BR>—2 A cavity, a slit; अदूरजाग्रद्विदरप्रणालीरेखा N. 8. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदरम्
विदरः + .{@-रम्@} The prickly pear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भाः
विदर्भाः (<i>m.</i> pl.) [विगताः दर्भाः कुशा यतः Tv.]<BR>—1 N. of a district, the modern Berar; अस्ति विदर्भो नाम जनपदः<BR> Dk.; अस्ति विदर्भेषु पद्मपुरं नाम नगरम् Māl. 1; R. 5. 40, 60; N. 1. 50.<BR>—2 The natives of Vidarbha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भः|विदर्भ
विदर्भाः + .{@-र्भः@}<BR>—1 A king of the Vidarbhas.<BR>—2 Any dry or desert soil.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विदर्भाजा, विदर्भातनया, विदर्भाराजतनया, विदर्भासुभ्रूः, विदर्भाजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

