विदर्भाः + -जा, -तनया, -राजतनया, -सुभ्रूः epithets of Damayantī, daughter<BR> of the king of the Vidarbhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भातनया
विदर्भाः + -जा, -तनया, -राजतनया, -सुभ्रूः epithets of Damayantī, daughter<BR> of the king of the Vidarbhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भाराजतनया
विदर्भाः + -जा, -तनया, -राजतनया, -सुभ्रूः epithets of Damayantī, daughter<BR> of the king of the Vidarbhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भासुभ्रूः
विदर्भाः + -जा, -तनया, -राजतनया, -सुभ्रूः epithets of Damayantī, daughter<BR> of the king of the Vidarbhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भाजा
विदर्भाः + -जा N. of the wife of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल्
विदल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To break, split, crack; त्वदिषुभिर्व्यदलिष्यदसावपि N. 4. 88.<BR>—2 To dig up.<BR>—3 To open, expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल|विदलं|विदलः
विदल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Split, rent asunder.<BR>—2 Opened, blown (as a flower &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलः|विदल|विदलं
विदल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 Dividing, separating.<BR>—2 Rending, splitting.<BR>—3 A cake.<BR>—4 Mountain ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलम्
विदल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A basket of split bamboos or any vessel of wicker-work; cf. Y. 1. 182.<BR>—2 The bark of pomegranate.<BR>—3 A twig; शिफाविदलरज्ज्वाद्यैर्विदध्यान्नृपतिर्दमम् Ms. 9. 230.<BR>—4 The chips of a substance.<BR>—5 Split peas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलनम्
विदलनम् Splitting, rending asunder, cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदश
विदश <i>a.</i> Having no border or fringe (a garment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदायः|विदाय
विदायः<BR>—1 Giving farewell (Persian word).<BR>—2 A division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारुः|विदारु
विदारुः A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदासिन्
विदासिन् <i>a.</i> Perishing; यथाऽविदासिनः कुल्याः सरसः स्युः सहस्रशः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 3. 26; see अविदासिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाहः|विदाह
विदाहः<BR>—1 Burning.<BR>—2 Great heat, inflammation.<BR>—3 Pungency, sharpness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाहिन्
विदाहिन् <i>m.</i> A substance causing inflammation; कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः Bg. 17. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिक्चङ्गः|विदिक्चङ्ग
विदिक्चङ्गः A kind of yellow bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1438-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिथः|विदिथ
विदिथः (= विदथः q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिश्
विदिश् <i>f.</i> An intermediate point of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिशा
विदिशा<BR>—1 N. of the capital of the district called दशार्ण; तेषां (दशार्णानां)<BR> दिक्षु प्रथितविदिशालक्षणां राजधानीम् Me. 24.<BR>—2 N. of a river in Mālvā.<BR>—3 = विदिश् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीपकः|विदीपक
विदीपकः A lantern; रथे रथे पञ्च विदीपकास्तु Mb. 7. 163. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुः|विदु
विदुः, -दूः<BR>—1 The middle of the frontal globes on an elephantʼs forehead (हस्तिकुम्भमध्यभागः);<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 4, 6. 7.<BR>—2 A hippopotamus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूः
विदुः, -दूः<BR>—1 The middle of the frontal globes on an elephantʼs forehead (हस्तिकुम्भमध्यभागः);<BR> Mātaṅga L. 5. 4, 6. 7.<BR>—2 A hippopotamus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुर|विदुरः
विदुर <i>a.</i> [विद्-कुरच् P. III. 2. 162] Wise, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुरः|विदुर
विदुर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A wise or learned man.<BR>—2 A crafty man, an intriguer.<BR>—3 N. of the younger brother of Paṇḍu. [When Satyavatī found that both<BR> the sons begotten by Vyāsa upon her two daughters-in-law were physically<BR> incapacitated for the throne −Dhṛtarāṣṭra being blind and Paṇḍu<BR> pale and sickly− she asked them to seek the assistance of Vyāsa once<BR> more. But being frightened by the austere look of the sage, the elder<BR> widow sent one of her slave-girls dressed in her own clothes, and this<BR> girl became the mother of Vidura. He is remarkable for his great wisdom,<BR> righteousness, and strict impartiality. He particularly loved the Pāṇḍavas,<BR> and saved them from several critical dangers.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विदुरनीतिः, विदुरप्रजागरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुरनीतिः|विदुरनीति
विदुर + -नीतिः, -प्रजागरः N. of chapters 33 to 40 in the 5th Parva of Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुरप्रजागरः|विदुरप्रजागर
विदुर + -नीतिः, -प्रजागरः N. of chapters 33 to 40 in the 5th Parva of Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुलः|विदुल
विदुलः<BR>—1 A kind of reed or ratan; विदुलस्येव तत् पुष्पं मोघं जनयितुः स्मृतम्<BR> Mb. 13. 105. 8.<BR>—2 Gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदून
विदून <i>p. p.</i> Afflicted, tormented, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूर|विदूरः
विदूर <i>a.</i> Remote, distant; सरिद् विदूरान्तरभावतन्वी R. 13. 48;<BR> U. 6. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरः|विदूर
विदूर + .{@-रः@} N. of a mountain or city from which the Vaidūrya jewel or<BR> <i>lapis lazuli</i> is brought; विदूरभूमिर्नवमेघशब्दादुद्भिन्नया रत्नशलाकयेव<BR> Ku. 1. 24; see Malli. thereon, as well as on Śi. 3. 45; तत्र तस्मै<BR> विदूराद्रिरविदूर इवाभवत् Śiva B. 30. 11. (The forms विदूरम्, विदूरेण,<BR> विदूरतस् or विदूरात् are often used adverbially in the sense of<BR> ‘from a distance’, ‘from afar’, ‘at a distance’, ‘far off’; वयं बत<BR> विदूरतः क्रमगता पशोः कन्यका Māl. 3. 18.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विदूराद्रिः, विदूरभूधरः, विदूरग, विदूरजम्, विदूरविगत, विदूरसंश्रव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूराद्रिः|विदूराद्रि
विदूर + -अद्रिः, -भूधरः See विदूरः; a legendary mountain located<BR> in Ceylon and supposed to produce jewels at the rumbling of clouds for<BR> the benefit of all comers; घनध्वानजरत्नमेदुरः तथा विदूराद्रिः<BR> N. 12. 55; यस्योत्थिताभिनवरत्नशलाकयेव लक्ष्मीरुरःस्थलविदूरभुवा<BR> विदध्रे Haravijaya 16. 25; रत्नाङ्कुररोमाञ्चकञ्चुकिनि विदूरभूधरे<BR> Yaśastilaka 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरभूधरः
विदूर + -अद्रिः, -भूधरः See विदूरः; a legendary mountain located<BR> in Ceylon and supposed to produce jewels at the rumbling of clouds for<BR> the benefit of all comers; घनध्वानजरत्नमेदुरः तथा विदूराद्रिः<BR> N. 12. 55; यस्योत्थिताभिनवरत्नशलाकयेव लक्ष्मीरुरःस्थलविदूरभुवा<BR> विदध्रे Haravijaya 16. 25; रत्नाङ्कुररोमाञ्चकञ्चुकिनि विदूरभूधरे<BR> Yaśastilaka 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरग|विदूरगः
विदूर + -ग <i>a.</i> spreading far and wide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरजम्
विदूर + -जम् the <i>lapis lazuli</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरविगत
विदूर + -विगत <i>a.</i> of lowest origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूरसंश्रव
विदूर + -संश्रव <i>a.</i> audible a long way off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषक|विदूषकः
विदूषक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Defiling, polluting, contaminating, corrupting.<BR>—2 Detracting, abusing.<BR>—3 Witty, humorous, jocular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषकः|विदूषक
विदूषक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A jester, buffoon.<BR>—2 Particularly,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">Page1439-2</a>]<BR> the humorous companion and confidential friend of the hero in a play,<BR> who excites mirth by his quaint dress, speeches, gestures, appearances<BR> &c., and by allowing himself to be made the butt of ridicule by almost<BR> every body; the S. D. thus defines him:− कुसुमवसन्ताद्यभिधः कर्मवपुर्वेशभाषाद्यैः ।<BR> हास्यकरः कलहरतिर्विदूषकः स्यात् स्वकर्मज्ञः ॥ 79; cf. also<BR> शृङ्गारस्य सहाया विटचेटविदूषकाद्याः स्युः । भक्ता नर्मसु निपुणाः कुपितवधूमानभञ्जनाः<BR> शुद्धाः ॥ <i>ibid.</i><BR>—3 A libertine, lecher.<BR>—4 A critic; an opponent; प्राशंसि संसद्गुरुणापि चार्वी चार्वाकता सर्वविदूषकेण N. 10. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषणम्
विदूषणम्<BR>—1 Pollution, corruption.<BR>—2 Abuse, reproach, detraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदृतिः|विदृति
विदृतिः A seam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदॄ
विदॄ €9 P. or €10 U.<BR>—1 To split, tear asunder, divide, cut to pieces; ऐन्द्रिः किल नखैस्तस्या<BR> विददार स्तनौ द्विजः R. 12. 22; न विदीर्ये कठिनाः खलु स्त्रियः<BR> Ku. 4. 5; R. 15. 33.<BR>—2 To rend (fig.); चित्तं विदारयति कस्य न कोविदारः Ṛs. 3. 6;<BR> स घोषो धार्तराष्ट्राणां हृदयानि व्यदारयत् Bg. 1. 19. ━<i>Pass.</i> To<BR> be rent or torn (with grief &c.). ━<i>Caus.</i> To rend, tear in pieces,<BR> tear or rip up; ततपृथुरसनोग्रमास्यगर्तं दधति विदार्य विवर्णदीर्घदेहाः<BR> Māl. 5. 15, 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारः|विदार
विदारः<BR>—1 Rending or cutting asunder, splitting.<BR>—2 War, battle.<BR>—3 An inundation, overflowing (of a tank, river &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारी
विदारः + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A swelling in the groin.<BR>—2 A species of medicinal plant (सालवण); विदारी वातपित्तघ्नी<BR> वल्या वृष्या रसायनी Rājavallabha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारकः|विदारक|विदारकं
विदारकः<BR>—1 A tearer, divider.<BR>—2 A tree or rock in the middle of a stream (which divides its course).<BR>—3 A hole sunk in water in the bed of a dry river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारकम्
विदारकः + .{@-कम्@} Alkaline earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारणः|विदारण|विदारणं
विदारणः<BR>—1 A tree or rock in the middle of a stream (to which a boat is fastened).<BR>—2 War, battle.<BR>—3 The Karṇikāra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारणा
विदारणः + .{@-णा@} War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारणम्
विदारणः + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Rending, splitting, tearing, ripping up, breaking, (often with the<BR> force of an adj. at the end of comp.); श्रुतं सखे श्रवणविदारणं वचः<BR> Mu. 5. 6; युवजनहृदयविदारणमनसिजनखरुचिकिंशुकजाले Gīt. 1; Ki. 14. 54.<BR>—2 Afflicting, tormenting.<BR>—3 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारिका
विदारिका, विदारिः <i>f.</i> A swelling in the groin; (also विदारी<BR> in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारिः|विदारि
विदारिका, विदारिः <i>f.</i> A swelling in the groin; (also विदारी<BR> in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्ण|विदीर्णः
विदीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Torn, split, rent asunder, split open.<BR>—2 Opened, expanded; (see दॄ with वि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विदीर्णमुख<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्णमुख
विदीर्ण + -मुख <i>a.</i> open-mouthed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1439-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदृतिः|विदृति
