विधवा + -आवेदनम् marrying a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवागामिन्
विधवा + -गामिन् <i>m.</i> one who has sexual intercourse with a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधस्
विधस् <i>m.</i> N. of Brahman, the creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधा
विधा €3 U.<BR>—1 To do, make, bring about, effect, accomplish, perform, cause, produce,<BR> occasion; यथाक्रमं पुंसवनादिकाः क्रिया धृतेश्च धीरः सदृशीर्व्यधत्त<BR> सः R. 3. 10; तन्नो देवा विधेयासुः Bk. 19. 2; विधेयासुर्देवाः परमरमणीयां<BR> परिणतिम् Māl. 6. 7; प्रायः शुभं च विदधात्यशुभं च जन्तोः सर्वंकषा<BR> भगवती भवितव्यतैव 1. 23; ये द्वे कालं विधत्तः Ś. 1. 1 ‘cause, produce, or regulate time’<BR>; तस्य तस्याचलां श्रद्धां तामेव विदधाम्यहम्<BR> Bg. 7. 21; R. 2. 38, 3. 66; Ve. 1. 1; Ki. 1. 3, 16. 62, 18. 28; (these<BR> senses may be further modified according to the noun with which विधा<BR> is used; cf. कृ).<BR>—2 To lay<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">Page1442-1</a>]<BR> down, ordain, prescribe, fix, settle, command, enjoin; प्राङ्नाभिवर्धनात्<BR> पुंसो जातकर्म विधीयते Ms. 2. 29, 3. 19; Y. 1. 72; शूद्रस्य तु सवर्णैव<BR> नान्या भार्या विधीयते Ms. 9. 157, 3. 118; पाणिनिश्च क्रियाफलस्य कर्तृगामित्वे<BR> सत्यात्मनेपदं विदधाति J. N. V.<BR>—3 To make, form, shape, create, manufacture; तं वेधा विदधे नूनं<BR> महाभूतसमाधिना R. 1. 29; अङ्गानि चम्पकदलैः स विधाय नूनं कान्ते<BR> कथं घटितवानुपलेन चेतः Ś. Til. 3.<BR>—4 To appoint, depute (as a minister).<BR>—5 To put on, wear; Pt. 1.<BR>—6 To fix upon, direct towards (as mind &c.); योगे धैर्यसमाधिसिद्धिसुलभे<BR> बुद्धिं विधद्ध्वं बुधाः Bh. 3. 54; व्यवसायात्मिका बुद्धिः समाधौ न<BR> विधीयते Bg. 2. 44.<BR>—7 To arrange, put in order.<BR>—8 To make ready, prepare.<BR>—9 To settle, fix, establish; चरणारविन्दयुगलं मनसा विदधत् Bhāg. 5. 9. 3.<BR>—10 To give, grant; अतीतसंख्या विहिता ममाग्निना शिलीमुखाः खाण्डवमत्तुमिच्छता Ki. 14. 10.<BR>—11 To procure, furnish.<BR>—12 To place, put, lay.<BR>—13 To engross, consume; धने सुखकला या तु साऽपि दुःखैर्विधीयते<BR> Mb. 12. 177. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1441-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधा
विधा<BR>—1 Mode, manner, form; मनः प्रत्यक् चित्ते सविधमवधायात्तमरुतः<BR> Śivamahimna 25.<BR>—2 Kind, sort.<BR>—3 Prosperity, affluence.<BR>—4 The food of elephants, horses &c.<BR>—5 Penetration.<BR>—6 Hire, wages.<BR>—7 Act, action.<BR>—8 Pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृ
विधातृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A maker, creator; यो विधाता च धाता च Rām. 7. 20. 31; प्रसिद्धनेपथ्यविधेर्विधाता Ku. 7. 36.<BR>—2 ‘The creator’, N. of Brahman; विधाता भद्रं नो वितरतु मनोज्ञाय विधये<BR> Māl. 6. 7; R. 1. 35, 6. 11, 7. 25.<BR>—3 A granter, giver, bestower; स्वयं विधाता तपसः फलानाम् Ku. 1. 57.<BR>—4 Fate, destiny; तावच्च तत्र च विधातृवशादुपैति H. 1. 40.<BR>—5 N. of Viśvakarman.<BR>—6 N. of Kāma, the god of love.<BR>—7 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—8 The illusion, Māyā; त्वं हि धाता विधाता च त्वं विष्णुः सुरसत्तमः Mb. 1. 23. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विधात्रायुस्, विधातृभूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्रायुस्
विधातृ + -आयुस् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 sunshine.<BR>—2 the sun flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृभूः
विधातृ + -भूः an epithet of Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्री
विधात्री Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानम्
विधानम्<BR>—1 Arranging, disposing; अपरं किं तु कृत्वैवं विधानं संविधास्यति<BR> Rām. 7. 20. 31.<BR>—2 Performing, making, doing, executing; नेपथ्यविधानम् Ś. 1; आज्ञा˚,<BR> यज्ञ˚ &c.; एवं कृत्वा विधानं स संनिवेश्य वसुं तदा Rām. 7. 54. 13.<BR>—3 Creation, creating; तस्मिन् विधानातिशये विधातुः कन्यामये नेत्रशतैकलक्ष्ये<BR> R. 6. 11, 7. 14; Ku. 7. 66; निधानं धर्माणां किमपि च विधानं नवमुदाम् G. L. 18.<BR>—4 Employment, use, application; प्रतिकारविधानम् R. 8. 40.<BR>—5 Prescribing, enjoining, ordering.<BR>—6 A rule, precept, ordinance, sacred rule or precept, sacred injunction;<BR> तन्न्यायत्वाद् विधानस्य MS. 1. 3. 16 (cf. विधीयते अनेनेति विधानं<BR> शब्दः ŚB. on MS.); Ms. 9. 148; ज्ञात्वा शास्त्रविधानोक्तं कर्म कर्तुमिहार्हसि<BR> Bg. 16. 24, 17. 24.<BR>—7 Mode, manner.<BR>—8 A means or expedient; वस्त्रैश्च सर्वैः सहितैर्विधानैर्नेयं वृता<BR> ते वरसंप्रदाने Rām. 2. 37. 36.<BR>—9 Performance of prescribed acts or rites.<BR>—10 A rite, ceremony.<BR>—11 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>—12 Affixing, prefixing (as terminations, suffixes &c.).<BR>—13 The food given to elephants<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">Page1442-2</a>]<BR> (to make them intoxicated); विधानसंपादितदानशोभितैः (where विधान<BR> means ‘rule’ also); उत्क्षिप्तहस्ततलदत्तविधानपिण्डस्नेहस्रुतिस्नपितबाहुरिभाधिराजम् Śi. 5. 51.<BR>—14 Wealth.<BR>—15 Pain, agony, torment, distress.<BR>—16 An act of hostility.<BR>—17 An act, doing; आशङ्कमानो नृपतेर्विधानम् Mb. 3. 113. 15.<BR>—18 An effort, attempt (यत्न); तथा विधानं क्रियतां समर्थाः साधनेष्विति<BR> Rām. 1. 8. 19.<BR>—19 Remedy (चिकित्सा); तेषामन्यतमोद्रेके विधानमुपदिश्यते Mb. 12. 16. 12.<BR>—20 Prevention (प्रतिकार); विधानं तत्र भगवन् कर्तुमर्हसि युक्तितः Mb. 5. 177. 8.<BR>—21 Granting; क्रतुभ्रेषस्त्वत्तः क्रतुफलविधानव्यसनिनः Śivamahimna 21.<BR>—22 The Veda; त्वमेको ह्यस्य सर्वस्य विधानस्य स्वयंभुवः Ms. 1. 3.<BR>—23 The fate, destiny (दैव); अहमद्योपयोक्ष्यामि विधानं पश्य यादृशम् Mb. 3. 179. 15.<BR>—24 A statement of the Vedas; तस्य शब्दं गुणं विद्यान्मूर्तिशास्त्रविधानवित् Mb. 12. 252. 3.<BR>—25 (In drama) Conflict of different feelings.<BR>—26 Worship.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विधानगः, विधानज्ञः, विधानयुक्त, विधानसप्तमी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानगः|विधानग
विधानम् + -गः, -ज्ञः a wise or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानज्ञः|विधानज्ञ
विधानम् + -गः, -ज्ञः a wise or learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानयुक्त
विधानम् + -युक्त <i>a.</i> in accordance with or conformable to sacred precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानसप्तमी
विधानम् + -सप्तमी the 7th day in the light half of माघ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानकम्
विधानकम् Distress, affliction, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायक|विधायकः
विधायक <i>a.</i> (-यीका <i>f.</i>), विधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Arranging, disposing.<BR>—2 Doing, making, performing, executing.<BR>—3 Creating.<BR>—4 Enjoying, prescribing, laying down. —5 Consigning, committing, delivering<BR> (to the care of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायीका
विधायक <i>a.</i> (-यीका <i>f.</i>), विधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Arranging, disposing.<BR>—2 Doing, making, performing, executing.<BR>—3 Creating.<BR>—4 Enjoying, prescribing, laying down. —5 Consigning, committing, delivering<BR> (to the care of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायिन्
विधायक <i>a.</i> (-यीका <i>f.</i>), विधायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Arranging, disposing.<BR>—2 Doing, making, performing, executing.<BR>—3 Creating.<BR>—4 Enjoying, prescribing, laying down. —5 Consigning, committing, delivering<BR> (to the care of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिः|विधि
विधिः [विधा-कि]<BR>—1 Doing, performance, practice, an act or action; ब्रह्मध्यानाभ्यसनविधिना<BR> योगनिद्रां गतस्य Bh. 3. 41; योगविधि R. 8. 22; अस्याः सर्गविधौ<BR> V. 1. 8; लेखाविधि Māl. 1. 35.<BR>—2 Method, manner, way, means, mode; निःसाराल्पफलानि ये त्वविधिना<BR> वाञ्छन्ति दण्डोद्यमैः Pt. 1. 376.<BR>—3 A rule, commandment, any precept which enjoins something for the first<BR> time (as distinguished from नियम and परिसंख्या qq. vv.);<BR> विधिरत्यन्तमप्राप्तौ; चिकीर्षाकृतिसाध्यत्वहेतुधीविषयो विधिः; वहति<BR> विधिहुतं या हविः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>—4 A sacred precept or rule, ordinance, injunction, law, a sacred command,<BR> religious commandment (opp. अर्थवाद which means ‘an explanatory statement coupled with legends and illustrations’<BR>; see अर्थवाद); प्रवृत्तिपरं<BR> वाक्यं विधिः, as ज्योतिष्टोमेन स्वर्गकामो यजेत; श्रद्धा वित्तं विधिश्चेति<BR> त्रितयं तत् समागतम् Ś. 7. 29; R. 2. 16.<BR>—5 Any religious act or ceremony, a rite, ceremony; स चेत् स्वयं कर्मसु<BR> धर्मचारिणां त्वमन्तरायो भवसि च्युतो विधिः R. 3. 45, 1. 34.<BR>—6 Behaviour, conduct.<BR>—7 Condition; V. 4.<BR>—8 Creation, formation; सामग्र्यविधौ Ku. 3. 28; कल्याणी विधिषु विचित्रता<BR> विधातुः Ki. 7. 7.<BR>—9 The creator.<BR>—10 Fate, destiny, luck; विधौ वामारम्भे मम समुचितैषा परिणतिः Māl. 4. 4.<BR>—11 The food of elephants.<BR>—12 Time.<BR>—13 A physician.<BR>—14 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—15 Use, application.<BR>—16 A means, expedient for; अक्षरं गन्तुमनसो विधिं वक्ष्यामि शीघ्रगम्<BR> Mb. 12. 236. 13.<BR>—17 Any act, action.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विध्यन्तः, विध्यादिः, विधिकर, विधिघ्न, विधिज्ञ, विधिदर्शकः, विधिदृष्ट, विधिविहित, विधिदेशकः, विधिद्वैधम्, विधिपूर्वकम्, विधिप्रयोगः, विधियज्ञः, विधियोगः, विधिलोपः, विधिवधूः, विधिविपर्ययः, विधिविभक्तिः, विधिहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यन्तः|विध्यन्त
विधिः + -अन्तः The end or the concluding portion of an injunctive text,<BR> all the other portion of the प्रयोगविधि (pertaining to an act) except<BR> the प्रधान or मुख्य विधि which is called विध्यादि;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">Page1443-1</a>]<BR> विध्यन्तो वा प्रकृतिवत्˚ MS. 7. 4. 10; सोमेन यजेत इति विध्यादिः ।<BR> सौमिकमपि ब्राह्मणं विध्यन्तः ŚB. on MS. ibid. Also see विध्यादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1442-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्यादिः|विध्यादि
विधिः + -आदिः <i>m.</i> the beginning of a विधि or injunction; the main<BR> or प्रधान injunction; वेदेऽपि दर्शपूर्णमासाभ्यां यजेत इति विध्यादिः ।<BR> विध्यन्तोऽपि प्रधानविधिवर्जितं कृत्स्नं पौरोडाशिकं ब्राह्मणम् ŚB. on MS. 7. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिकर
विधिः + -कर <i>a.</i> executing commands; विधिकरीरिमा वीर मुह्यतीरधरसीधुनाप्याययस्व<BR> नः Bhāg. 10. 31. 8. ━<i>m.</i> a servant; सोऽयं ते विधिकर ईश विप्रशप्तस्तस्येदं<BR> निधनमनुग्रहाय विद्मः Bhāg. 7. 8. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिघ्न
विधिः + -घ्न <i>a.</i> disregarding prescribed rites or rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिज्ञ|विधिज्ञः
विधिः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिज्ञः|विधिज्ञ
विधिः + -ज्ञ + .({@-ज्ञः@}) a Brāhmaṇa versed in the ritual, a ritualist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदर्शकः|विधिदर्शक
विधिः + -दर्शकः a priest at a sacrifice who sees that everything is<BR> done according to the precepts, and corrects any deviation from them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदृष्ट
विधिः + -दृष्ट, -विहित <i>a.</i> prescribed by rule, enjoined by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिविहित
विधिः + -दृष्ट, -विहित <i>a.</i> prescribed by rule, enjoined by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिदेशकः|विधिदेशक
विधिः + -देशकः<BR>—1 = विधिदर्शक above.<BR>—2 a preceptor, teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिद्वैधम्
विधिः + -द्वैधम् diversity of rules, variance of precept or commandment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिपूर्वकम्
विधिः + -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> according to rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिप्रयोगः|विधिप्रयोग
विधिः + -प्रयोगः application of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियज्ञः|विधियज्ञ
विधिः + -यज्ञः<BR>—1 a sacrifice performed according to rule; Ms. 2. 85-86.<BR>—2 a ceremonial act of worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधियोगः|विधियोग
विधिः + -योगः<BR>—1 the force or influence of fate.<BR>—2 the observance of a rule; अनेन विधियोगेन कर्तव्यांशप्रकल्पना Ms. 8. 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिलोपः|विधिलोप
विधिः + -लोपः transgression of a commandment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवधूः
विधिः + -वधूः <i>f.</i> an epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिविपर्ययः|विधिविपर्यय
विधिः + -विपर्ययः misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिविभक्तिः
विधिः + -विभक्तिः <i>f.</i> a potential termination; a termination which<BR> lays down an injunction; विधिविभक्तिं हि विधायिकां लिङं मन्यमानाः श्लोकमिमं<BR> समामनन्ति ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 3. The श्लोक referred to here is;<BR> कुर्यात् क्रियेत कर्तव्यं भवेत् स्यादिति पञ्चमम् । एतत् स्यात् सर्ववेदेषु<BR> नियतं विधिलक्षणम् ॥ This श्लोक speaks of the five forms which<BR> the विधिविभक्ति takes in the Vedic literature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिहीन
विधिः + -हीन <i>a.</i> devoid of rule, unauthorised, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सा
विधित्सा<BR>—1 Desire to do or perform; Mb. 12. 163. 1.<BR>—2 Design, purpose, desire in general; वाचो वेगं मनसः क्रोधवेगं<BR> विधित्सावेगमुदरोपस्थवेगम् । एतान् वेगान् यो विषहेदुदीर्णांस्तं मन्येऽहं<BR> ब्राह्मणं वै मुनिं च ॥ Mb. 12. 299. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सित
विधित्सित <i>a.</i> Intended to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सितम्
विधित्सित + .{@-तम्@} Intention. design.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवत्
विधिवत्, विधितः <i>ind.</i> According to law, agreeably to<BR> precept or rule, in conformity to prescribed rules, in due form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधितः
विधिवत्, विधितः <i>ind.</i> According to law, agreeably to<BR> precept or rule, in conformity to prescribed rules, in due form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवशात्
विधिवशात् <i>ind.</i> Through the power of fate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेय|विधेयः
विधेय <i>pot. p.</i><BR>—1 To be done or performed.<BR>—2 To be enjoyed or prescribed.<BR>—3<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Dependent on, at the disposal of; अथ विधिविधेयः परिचयः Māl. 2. 13.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Subject to, influenced or controlled by, subdued or overpowered<BR> by (usually in comp.); निद्राविधेयं नरदेवसैन्यम् R. 7. 62; संभाव्यमानस्नेहरसेनाभिसंधिना<BR> विधेयीकृतोऽपि Māl. 1; आत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति Bg. 2. 64;<BR> भ्रातुः सौहार्देन विधेयीकृतोऽस्मि Mv. 7; Mu. 3. 1; Śi. 3. 20;<BR> R. 19. 4; आज्ञाविधेया वयम् Pañc. 1. 57; विभीषणविधेयाः खलु राक्षसाः Pratimā 7.<BR>—4 Obedient, tractable, compliant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">Page1443-2</a>]<BR> submissive; अविधेयेन्द्रियः पुंसां गौरिवैति विधेयताम् Ki. 11. 33.<BR>—5 To be predicated (in gram. &c.); अत्र मिथ्यामहिमत्वं नानुवाद्यम्<BR> अपि तु विधेयम् K. P. 7.<BR>—6 A functionary, one who is in charge of anything; त्वं तस्य भव<BR> वश्यश्च विधेयश्च सदानघ Rām. 2. 30. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयम्
विधेय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 What ought to be done, a duty; विधीयतां तत्र विधेयमुत्तरम् Ki. 1. 25, 16. 62.<BR>—2 The predicate of a proposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयः|विधेय
विधेय + .{@-यः@} A servant, dependant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विधेयाविमर्शः, विधेयात्मन्, विधेयज्ञ, विधेयपदम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयाविमर्शः|विधेयाविमर्श
विधेय + -अविमर्शः a fault of composition which consists in assigning<BR> to the predicate a subordinate position or in expressing it imperfectly<BR> (अविमृष्टः प्राधान्येनानिर्दिष्टो विधेयांशो यत्र K. P. 7; see examples <i>ad loc.</i>)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयात्मन्
विधेय + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयज्ञ
विधेय + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> one who knows oneʼs duty; स भृत्यो यो विधेयज्ञः Pt. 1. 337.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेयपदम्
विधेय + -पदम्<BR>—1 the object to be accomplished.<BR>—2 the predicate; नात्रैषा वचनव्यक्तिः ये यजमाना इत्युद्देशपदम् ऋत्विजः<BR> इति विधेयपदम् ŚB. on MS. 6. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुः|विधु
विधुः [व्यघ्-कुः Uṇ. 1. 23]<BR>—1 The moon; सविता विधवति विधुरपि सवितरति दिनन्ति यामिन्यः K. P. 10.<BR>—2 Camphor.<BR>—3 A demon, fiend.<BR>—4 An expiatory oblation.<BR>—5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 N. of Brahman.<BR>—7 N. of Śiva.<BR>—8 Wind.<BR>—9 War, battle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विधुक्षयः, विधुदिनम्, विधुपञ्जरः, विधुपरिध्वंसः, विधुप्रिया, विधुमण्डलम्, विधुमासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुक्षयः|विधुक्षय
विधुः + -क्षयः waning of the moon, the period of the dark fortnight of<BR> a month; प्रथिता प्रेतकृत्यैषा पित्र्यं नाम विधुक्षये Ms. 3. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुदिनम्
विधुः + -दिनम् a lunar day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुपञ्जरः|विधुपञ्जर
विधुः + -पञ्जरः (also पिञ्जरः) a scimitar, sabre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुपरिध्वंसः|विधुपरिध्वंस
विधुः + -परिध्वंसः eclipse of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुप्रिया
विधुः + -प्रिया a <i>Nakṣatra</i> or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुमण्डलम्
विधुः + -मण्डलम् the moonʼs disc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुमासः|विधुमास
विधुः + -मासः a lunar month<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुत|विधुतः
विधुत See विधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुतिः|विधुति
विधुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Shaking, trepidation, tremor; वैनायक्यश्चिरं वो वदनविधुतयः<BR> पान्तु चीत्कारवत्यः Māl. 1. 1; पादन्यासैर्भुजविधुतिभिः Bhāg. 10. 33. 8.<BR>—2 Removal, destruction; मायाविवेकविधुतिस्रजि वाऽहिबुद्धिः Bhāg. 4. 22. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुननम्
विधुननम्<BR>—1 Shaking or tossing about, agitating.<BR>—2 Trembling, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुंतुदः|विधुन्तुद|विधुंतुद|विधुन्तुदः
विधुंतुदः N. of Rāhu; विधुमिव विकटविधुंतुददन्तदलनगलितामृतधारम्<BR> Gīt. 4; आभिमुख्यं शशाङ्कस्य यथाद्यापि विधुंतुदः Pt. 1. 326; N. 4. 71;<BR> Śi. 2. 61; ग्रस्तं विधुंतुदेनेव निखिलं विधुमण्डलम् Śiva B. 25. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर <i>a.</i> [विगता धूर्यस्य अच् समा˚ Uṇ. 1. 39]<BR>—1 Distressed, troubled, afflicted, overwhelmed with grief, miserable;<BR> अवस्थामापन्ना मदनदहनोद्दाहविधुराम् Māl. 2. 3, 9. 11; U. 3. 38, 6. 41;<BR> Ki. 11. 26; Śi. 9. 77, 17. 66; Bh. 3. 8, 134; नेत्राग्निप्लोषमूर्च्छाविधुरविनिपतत्सानलद्वादशार्कः Nāg. 5. 31.<BR>—2 Love-lorn, bereaved, suffering separation from a wife or husband; मयि<BR> च विधुरे भावः कान्ताप्रवृत्तिपराङ्मुखः V. 4. 20; विधुरां ज्वलनातिसर्जनान्ननु<BR> मां प्रापय पत्युरन्तिकम् Ku. 4. 32; विधुरबन्धुरबन्धुरमैक्षत<BR> Śi. 6. 29, 12. 8; निर्व्याजं विधुरेष्वधीर इति मां येनाभिधत्ते भवान् Nāg. 2. 3.<BR>—3 Devoid, deprived, or destitute of, free from; त्वामाद्यन्तान्तरवर्ती<BR> त्रयविधुरः Bhāg. 6. 16. 36; सा वै कलङ्कविधुरा मधुराननश्रीः Bv. 2. 5.<BR>—4 Adverse, hostile,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">Page1444-1</a>]<BR> unfriendly; कूपान्तः पतितः करोतु विधुरे किं वा विधौ पौरुषम् Pt. 2. 85.<BR>—5 Unable, helpless; प्रतिक्रियायै विधुरः Ki. 17. 41.<BR>—6 Incapable to perform (अनुष्ठानशून्य); अनुत्पन्नं ज्ञानं यदि<BR> यदि च संदेहविधुरम् Mv. 3. 36.<BR>—7 Infirm, drooping (विगलित); हयैश्च विधुरग्रीवै रथैश्च शकलीकृतैः<BR> Mb. 7. 146. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरः|विधुर|विधुरं
विधुर + .{@-रः@} A widower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरम्
विधुर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Alarm, fear, anxiety.<BR>—2 Separation from a wife or husband, bereavement suffered by a lover or mistress.<BR>—3 Calamity, distress; विधुरं किमतः परम् Ki. 2. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विधुरदर्शनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1443-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरदर्शनम्
विधुर + -दर्शनम्<BR>—1 the sight of danger or alarm; विना विधुरदर्शनं स्वामिनो मन्दादरा<BR> भवन्ति H. 2.<BR>—2 a feeling of agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर <i>a.</i> Destitute of a shaft (as a carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरा
विधुरा Curds mixed with sugar and spices (Mar. श्रीखंड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरित
विधुरित <i>a.</i> Pale; लज्जाविधुरिताननम् Ve. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधू
विधू €5. €10 U., €6 P.<BR>—1 To shake, move, cause to tremble; वायुर्विधूनयति चम्पकपुष्परेणून्<BR> K. R.; मृदुपवनविघूतान् Ṛs. 6. 29, 3. 10; दीर्धां वेणीं विधुन्वाना Mb.<BR>—2 To shake off, destroy, expel, drive away; कपेर्विधवितुं द्युतिम् Bk. 9. 28.<BR>—3 To spurn, despise, treat with contempt; ज्यानिघातकठिनत्वचो भुजान्<BR> स्वान् विधूय धिगिति प्रतस्थिरे R. 11. 40.<BR>—4 To leave, give up, abandon; द्रुतं विधूयान्यत् N. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवनम्
विधुवनम् Shaking, trembling, tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूत|विधूतं
विधूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shaken or tossed about, waved.<BR>—2 Tremulous.<BR>—3 Shaken off, dispelled, removed.<BR>—4 Unsteady.<BR>—5 Abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूतम्
विधूत + .{@-तम्@} Repugnance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विधूतकल्मष, विधूतकेश, विधूतनिद्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूतकल्मष
विधूत + -कल्मष <i>a.</i> free from sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूतकेश
विधूत + -केश <i>a.</i> one who has tossed about the hair; विधूतकेशाः<BR> परिलोलितस्रजः Ki. 8. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूतनिद्र
विधूत + -निद्र <i>a.</i> awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूतिः|विधूति
विधूतिः <i>f.</i>, विधूननम्<BR>—1 Shaking, tremor, agitation. स्तभ्ममुपहितविधूतिम् Śi. 15. 6.<BR>—2 Repulsion (as of love). See विधुतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूननम्
विधूतिः <i>f.</i>, विधूननम्<BR>—1 Shaking, tremor, agitation. स्तभ्ममुपहितविधूतिम् Śi. 15. 6.<BR>—2 Repulsion (as of love). See विधुतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनित|विधूनितं
विधूनित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Agitated, alarmed.<BR>—2 Harassed, annoyed, molested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूम
विधूम <i>a.</i> Smokeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूम्र
विधूम्र <i>a.</i> Quite grey; युधि तुरगरजोविधूम्रविष्वक् Bhāg. 1. 9. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृ
विधृ €10 U.<BR>—1 To seize, catch, catch or take hold of; अंशुकपल्लवेन विधृतः Amaru. 85.<BR>—2 To put on, wear, use; पर्णशालामथ क्षिप्रं विधृतासिः प्रविश्य सः<BR> R. 12. 40 (v. l.).<BR>—3 To maintain, bear, support, hold up; शिरसा विधृता नित्यम् Pt. 1. 82<BR> (where sense 2 is also intended); विधृतमपरैर्दत्तं चान्यैर्विजित्य<BR> तृणं यथा Bh. 3. 23.<BR>—4 To fix upon, direct towards.<BR>—5 To separate, divide.<BR>—6 To arrange, manage.<BR>—7 To withhold, obstruct, restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधारणम्
विधारणम् Stopping, detaining (a carriage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृत|विधृतं
विधृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seized, held, grasped.<BR>—2 Separated, kept asunder or separate.<BR>—3 Assumed, possessed.<BR>—4 Checked, restrained.<BR>—5 Supported, protected, borne up; (see धृ with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृतम्
विधृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Disregard of a command.<BR>—2 Dissatisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृतिः|विधृति
विधृतिः <i>f.</i> Arrangement, regulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्र
विध्र <i>a.</i> [विन्धेः क्रन्, नलोपश्च Uṇ. 2. 26] Clear, stainless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस्
विध्वंस् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To fall to pieces.<BR>—2 To be dispersed or scattered.<BR>—3 To perish, be destroyed or ruined. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To destroy, crush, annihilate.<BR>—2 To injure, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसः|विध्वंस
विध्वंसः<BR>—1 Ruin, destruction.<BR>—2 Enmity, aversion, dislike.<BR>—3 An insult, offence.<BR>—4 Cessation (of a disease).<BR>—5 Violation (of a woman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसिन्
विध्वंसिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Being ruined, falling to pieces.<BR>—2 Hostile, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वस्त
विध्वस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ruined, destroyed; दृश्यते मित्रविध्वस्तः कार्याद्वैरिप्ररक्षितः Pt. 2. 113.<BR>—2 Scattered about, tossed up.<BR>—3 Obscured, darkened.<BR>—4 Eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनग्न
विनग्न <i>a.</i> Quite naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनटनम्
विनटनम् Moving to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद्
विनद् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sound, resound; सिंहनादं विनद्योच्चैः शङ्खं दध्मौ प्रतापवान् Bg. 1. 12.<BR>—2 To roar, cry out.<BR>—3 To fill with cries. ━<i>Caus.</i> To cause to cry or utter notes;<BR> अम्बुदैः शिखिगणो विनाद्यते Ghaṭ. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनदः|विनद
विनदः<BR>—1 Sound, noise.<BR>—2 N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्
विनम् €1 P. To bend oneself, stoop, be bent; विनमन्ति चास्य तरवः<BR> प्रचये Ki. 6. 34; Bh. 1. 67; Bk. 7. 52. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To bend (a bow).<BR>—2 (In gram.) To change into a cerebral letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनत|विनतः
विनत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bent down, bowed.<BR>—2 Stooping, drooping, inclined; प्रकामविनतावंसौ Ś. 3. 9.<BR>—3 Sunk down, depressed.<BR>—4 Bent, crooked, curved.<BR>—5 Humble, modest.<BR>—6 Changed into a lingual letter; see विनाम.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनतानन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतानन
विनत + -आनन <i>a.</i> with downcast face, dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनता
विनता<BR>—1 N. of the mother of Aruṇa and Garuḍa, said to be one of the wives<BR> of Kaśyapa; see गरुड.<BR>—2 A kind of basket.<BR>—3 An abscess on the back or abdomen.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनतानन्दनः, विनतासुतः, विनतासूनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतानन्दनः|विनतानन्दन
विनता + -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -सूनुः epithets of Garuḍa or Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतासुतः|विनतासुत
विनता + -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -सूनुः epithets of Garuḍa or Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतासूनुः|विनतासूनु
विनता + -नन्दनः, -सुतः, -सूनुः epithets of Garuḍa or Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतिः|विनति
विनतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Bowing down, bending, stooping.<BR>—2 Modesty, humility.<BR>—3 A request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमनम्
विनमनम् Bending, bowing, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्र
विनम्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bent down, stooping; विनम्रशालिप्रसवौघशालिनीः Ki. 4. 2.<BR>—2 Depressed, sunk down.<BR>—3 Modest, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1444-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्रकम्
विनम्रकम् The flower of the <i>Tagara</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्द्
विनर्द् €1 U. To cry out, roar, thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनर्दिन्
विनर्दिन् <i>a.</i> Roaring (applied to a kind of mode of chanting Sāman);<BR> विनर्दि साम्नो वृणे पशव्यम् Ch. Up. 2. 22. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्
विनश् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be destroyed, perish, die.<BR>—2 To disappear, vanish.<BR>—3 To be lost or ruined.<BR>—4 To be frustrated or foiled. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To destroy, annihilate.<BR>—2 To suffer to be lost; स्थातुं नियोक्तुर्न हि शक्यमग्रे विनाश्य रक्ष्यं<BR> स्वयमक्षतेन R. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशनम्
विनशनम् Perishing, loss, destruction, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशनः|विनशन|विनशनं
विनशनम् + .{@-नः@} N. of the place where the river Sarasvatī is lost in the<BR> sand; cf. हिमवद्विन्ध्ययोर्मध्यं यत् प्राग्विनशनादपि । प्रत्यगेव प्रयागाच्च<BR> मध्यदेशः प्रकीर्तितः ॥ Ms. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्ट|विनष्टः
विनष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Perished, destroyed, ruined.<BR>—2 Disappeared, lost.<BR>—3 Spoiled, corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्टिः|विनष्टि
विनष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Utter ruin or destruction; न चेदिहावेदीन्महती विनष्टिः Ken. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Disappearance, vanishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशः|विनाश
विनाशः<BR>—1 Destruction, ruin, utter loss, decay.<BR>—2 Removal.<BR>—3 Death.<BR>—4 The perishable world; संभूतिं च विनाशं च यस्तद्वेदोभयं सह<BR> Īśop. 14 (it is called कार्यब्रह्म).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनाशोन्मुख, विनाशधर्मन्, विनाशधर्मिन्, विनाशहेतु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशोन्मुख|विनाशोन्मुखं
विनाशः + -उन्मुख <i>a.</i> about to perish, ripe to meet oneʼs doom; विनाशोन्मुखं<BR> दृष्ट्वा तत्प्रयुक्तं कार्यं कुर्वन्ति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशधर्मन्
विनाशः + -धर्मन्, -धर्मिन् <i>a.</i> subject to decay, perishable, transient;<BR> विषयेषु विनाशधर्मसु त्रिदिवस्थेष्वपि निःस्पृहोऽभवत् R. 8. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशधर्मिन्
विनाशः + -धर्मन्, -धर्मिन् <i>a.</i> subject to decay, perishable, transient;<BR> विषयेषु विनाशधर्मसु त्रिदिवस्थेष्वपि निःस्पृहोऽभवत् R. 8. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशहेतु
विनाशः + -हेतु <i>a.</i> being the cause of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशनम्
विनाशनम् Destruction, ruin, annihilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशनः|विनाशन|विनाशनं
विनाशनम् + .{@-नः@} A destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनस|विनसः
विनस <i>a.</i> (-सा, -सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Noseless; यद्यहं नाथ नायास्यं विनासा हतबान्धवा Bk. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विना
विना <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Without, except (with acc., instr. or abl.); यथा तानं विना रागो<BR> यथा मानं विना नृपः । यथा दानं विना हस्ती तथा ज्ञानं विना यतिः<BR> Bv. 1. 119; पङ्कैर्विना सरो भाति सदः खलजनैर्विना कटुवर्णैर्विना<BR> काव्यं मानसं विषयैर्विना 1. 116; विना वाहनहस्तिभ्यः क्रियतां सर्वमोक्षः<BR> Mu. 7; Śi. 2. 9. (विनाकृ means ‘to leave, abandon, bereave, deprive of’<BR>; मदनेन विनाकृता रतिः Ku. 4. 21 ‘bereft of Cupid’).<BR>—2 In the absence of; विना वचनेन अन्त्यलोप एव न्याग्यः ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 6.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनोक्तिः, विनाभवः, विनाभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोक्तिः|विनोक्ति
विना + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> a figure of speech in which विना is used in<BR> a poetically charming way; विनार्थसंबन्ध एव विनोक्तिः R. G.; see K. P. 10 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाभवः|विनाभव
विना + -भवः, -भावः separation; न सुहृद्भिर्विनाभवः Rām. 2. 94. 3;<BR> व्यक्तं दैवादहं मन्ये राघवस्य विनाभवम् 7. 50. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाभावः|विनाभाव
विना + -भवः, -भावः separation; न सुहृद्भिर्विनाभवः Rām. 2. 94. 3;<BR> व्यक्तं दैवादहं मन्ये राघवस्य विनाभवम् 7. 50. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाकृत|विनाकृतं
विनाकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deprived of, bereft of, destitute, free from.<BR>—2 Solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिः|विनाडि
विनाडिः, -विनाडिका<BR> A measure of time equal to one-sixtieth part of a Ghaṭikā<BR> or equal to 24 seconds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिका
विनाडिः, -विनाडिका<BR> A measure of time equal to one-sixtieth part of a Ghaṭikā<BR> or equal to 24 seconds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनामः|विनाम
विनामः<BR>—1 (In gram.) Change into a lingual or cerebral letter, the substitution<BR> of ष् for स् and ण् for न्.<BR>—2 Crookedness (of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायकः|विनायक
विनायकः<BR>—1 A remover (of obstacles).<BR>—2 N. of Gaṇeśa; विनायकं प्रकुर्वाणो रचयामास वानरम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 A Buddhist deified teacher.<BR>—4 N. of Garuḍa.<BR>—5 An obstacle, impediment.<BR>—6 A spiritual preceptor.<BR>—7 A leader, guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायिका
विनायिका The wife of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासक|विनासकः
विनास(सि)क <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासिक
विनास(सि)क <i>a.</i> Noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाहः|विनाह
विनाहः A cover for the mouth of a well; cf. वीनाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकृत
विनिकृत <i>p. p.</i> Ill-treated, injured, disabled; विश्वामित्रो विनिकृतो<BR> विनिःश्वस्येदमब्रवीत् Rām. 1. 56. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकॄ
विनिकॄ €6 Ā.<BR>—1 To throw, abandon, cast off; क्व नु मां त्वदधीनजीवितां विनिकीर्य<BR> क्षणभिन्नसौहृदः Ku. 4. 6.<BR>—2 To throw about, scatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकीर्ण
विनिकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i> Scattered, thrown about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकोचनम्
विनिकोचनम् Contraction (of the brow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्
विनिक्षिप् €6 Ā.<BR>—1 To entrust, deliver over.<BR>—2 To place in or upon.<BR>—3 To throw down, overthrow.<BR>—4 To engage in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षेपः|विनिक्षेप
विनिक्षेपः<BR>—1 Throwing down, sending forth.<BR>—2 Separation, isolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगड
विनिगड <i>a.</i> Without fetters, unrestrained, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगमना
विनिगमना <i>f.</i> Determination, definite conclusion, acceptance<BR> of something to the exclusion of the rest; न हि विनिगमनायां हेतुरस्ति<BR> एवंनिमित्तकं कर्तव्यं नैवंनिमित्तकमिति ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रह्
विनिग्रह् €9 U.<BR>—1 To restrain, check; obstruct, impede.<BR>—2 To lay hold of, seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रहः|विनिग्रह
विनिग्रहः<BR>—1 Restraining, curbing, subduing; Bg. 13. 7, 17. 16; न हि दण्डादृते<BR> शक्यः कर्तुं पापविनिग्रहः Ms. 9. 263.<BR>—2 Mutual opposition or antithesis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिघ्न
विनिघ्न <i>a.</i> Multiplied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्र|विनिद्रः
विनिद्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sleepless, awake (fig. also); तामेकतस्तव बिभर्ति गुरुर्विनिद्रः R. 5. 66.<BR>—2 Budded, opened, full-blown, expanded; विनिद्रमन्दाररजोरुणाङ्गुली Ku. 5. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपत्
विनिपत् €1 P.<BR>—1 To fly at, fall down, descend; विनिपतिततुषारः क्रौञ्चनादोपगीतः<BR> Ṛs. 4. 18 (v. l.).<BR>—2 To attack, assail. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to fall down, ruin, destroy; कटेन विनिपातितो यामि Mk. 2. 8.<BR>—2 To throw or pull down.<BR>—3 To kill, deprive of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपन्न
विनिपन्न <i>a.</i> Destroyed; एते चान्ये च बहवो बलवन्तो दुरासदाः ।<BR> विनिपन्ना मया दृष्टाः Rām. 7. 22. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1445-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातः|विनिपात
विनिपातः<BR>—1 Falling down, a fall.<BR>—2 A great fall, calamity, an evil, loss, ruin, destruction; विवेकभ्रष्टानां<BR> भवति विनिपातः शतमुखः Bh. 2. 10 (where it has sense 1 also); विधिहेतुरहेतुरागसां<BR> विनिपातोऽपि समः समुन्नतेः Ki. 2. 34.<BR>—3 Decay, death.<BR>—4 Hell, perdition; Ś. 5.<BR>—5 Occurrence, happening.<BR>—6 Pain, distress; जपतां जुह्वतां चैव विनिपातो न विद्यते Ms. 4. 146.<BR>—7 Disrespect.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनिपातगत, विनिपातशंसिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातगत
विनिपातः + -गत <i>a.</i> fallen into misfortune; भर्तारं नानुमन्यन्ते विनिपातगतं<BR> स्त्रियः Rām. 2. 39. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातशंसिन्
विनिपातः + -शंसिन् <i>a.</i> portentous, foreboding ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातनम्
विनिपातनम् Causing miscarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिबर्हण
विनिबर्हण <i>a.</i> Throwing down, crushing; अनुमन्त्र्याहमतुलं<BR> द्विषतां विनिबर्हणम् Mb. 3. 22. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमयः|विनिमय
विनिमयः [विनिमे-1 Ā.]<BR>—1 Exchange, barter; कार्यविनिमयेन M. 1; संपद्विनिमयेनोभौ दधतुर्भुवनद्वयम्<BR> R. 1. 26; वर्णयाकर्णितं मह्यमेह्यालि विनिमीयताम् N. 20. 113.<BR>—2 A pledge, deposit, security.<BR>—3 Transmutation (of letters).<BR>—4 Reciprocity; तेजोवारिमृदां यथा विनिमयः Bhāg. 1. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमित्त
विनिमित्त <i>a.</i> Having no real cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमेषः|विनिमेष
विनिमेषः<BR>—1 Twinkling (of the eyes).<BR>—2 A wink, sign; नयनविनिमेषविनोदिताः Ki. 12. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियम्
विनियम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To restrain, check, curb; मनसैवेन्द्रियग्रामं विनियम्य समन्ततः Bg. 6. 24.<BR>—2 To limit, restrict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियत
विनियत <i>p. p.</i> Controlled, checked, restrained, regulated; as<BR> in विनियताहार, विनियतवाच् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियमः|विनियम
विनियमः Control, restraint, check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुज्
विनियुज् €7 U.<BR>—1 To use, expend.<BR>—2 To appoint, employ.<BR>—3 To divide, apportion, distribute; प्रत्येकं विनियुक्तात्मा कथं न<BR> ज्ञास्यसि प्रभो Ku. 2. 31.<BR>—4 To disconnect, separate.<BR>—5 To discharge (an arrow). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To appoint, employ.<BR>—2 to enjoin, order, command; भृत्येषु विनियोजयेत् Ms. 7. 226.<BR>—3 To offer, present, give.<BR>—4 To perform, do, dispose of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुक्त
विनियुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Separated, loosed, detached.<BR>—2 Attached to, appointed.<BR>—3 Applied to.<BR>—4 Commanded, enjoined.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनियुक्तात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुक्तात्मन्
विनियुक्त + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> one who has his mind fixed on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोक्तृ
विनियोक्तृ <i>a.</i> Appointer, employer; तेषु तेषु हि कृत्येषु विनियोक्ता<BR> महेश्वरः Mb. 3. 32. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोगः|विनियोग
विनियोगः<BR>—1 Separation, parting, detachment.<BR>—2 Leaving, giving up, abandoning.<BR>—3 Employment, use, application, disposal; बभूव विनियोगज्ञः साधनीयेषु<BR> वस्तुषु R. 17. 67; प्राणायामे विनियोगः &c.; अनेनेदं तु कर्तव्यं<BR> विनियोगः प्रकीर्तितः ।; आर्षं छन्दश्च दैवत्यं विनियोगस्तथैव च<BR> Yogiyājñavalkya.<BR>—4 Appointment to a duty, commission, charge; विनियोगप्रसादा हि किङ्कराः<BR> प्रभविष्णुषु Ku. 6. 62.<BR>—5 An obstacle, impediment.<BR>—6 Relation, corelation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गम्
विनिर्गम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To go out.<BR>—2 To disappear, vanish.<BR>—3 To go away, depart.<BR>—4 To escape from, liberate oneself from.<BR>—5 To be beside oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गमः|विनिर्गम
विनिर्गमः<BR>—1 Disappearance.<BR>—2 Departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जि
विनिर्जि €1 P.<BR>—1 To conquer completely.<BR>—2 To subdue, overpower, master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जयः|विनिर्जय
विनिर्जयः Complete victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णी
विनिर्णी = निर्णी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णयः|विनिर्णय
विनिर्णयः<BR>—1 Complete settlement or ascertainment, full decision.<BR>—2 Certainty.<BR>—3 A settled rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्बन्धः|विनिर्बन्ध|विनिर्बंध|विनिर्बंधः
विनिर्बन्धः Persistence, pertinacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मा
विनिर्मा See निर्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मित
विनिर्मित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Formed or made of.<BR>—2 Made, created; विनिर्मितं छादनमज्ञतायाः (मौनम्) Bh. 2. 7.<BR>—3 Celebrated, observed (as a feast).<BR>—4 Determined, destined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मुच्
विनिर्मुच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To loosen, free from.<BR>—2 To set free, release, liberate.<BR>—3 To discharge, shoot off.<BR>—4 To abandon, give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मुक्तिः|विनिर्मुक्ति
विनिर्मुक्तिः <i>f.</i>, विनिर्मोक्षः Release, liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मोक्षः|विनिर्मोक्ष
विनिर्मुक्तिः <i>f.</i>, विनिर्मोक्षः Release, liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्वृत्
विनिर्वृत् See निर्वृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्वृत्त|विनिर्वृत्तः
विनिर्वृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Come forth, issued from; साक्षाद्रामाद्विनिर्वृत्तो धर्मश्चापि श्रिया<BR> सह Rām. 2. 2. 29.<BR>—2 Completed, finished (कृतकृत्य); त्वत्प्रसादाद्विनिर्वृत्तः समर्थः<BR> स्यामहं यथा Mb. 3. 40. 14; Y. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिविद्
विनिविद् See निविट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिविश्
विनिविश् €6 P. To be placed or be seated in. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To fix, place; सर्वोपमाद्रव्यसमुच्चयेन यथाप्रदेशं विनिवेशितेन<BR> (सा निर्मिता) Ku. 1. 49; R. 5. 63; मदुरसि कुचकलशं विनिवेशय Gīt. 12.<BR>—2 To populate or colonize.<BR>—3 To introduce.<BR>—4 To add, insert.<BR>—5 To draw up in array (as troops).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवेशः|विनिवेश
विनिवेशः<BR>—1 Entrance, settling down in a place; जनपदविनिवेशः Kau. A. 1.<BR>—2 An impression; स्विन्नाङ्गुलिविनिवेशो रेखाप्रान्तेषु दृश्यते मलिनः Ś. 6. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवेशनम्
विनिवेशनम् Erection, building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृ
विनिवृ €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To prevent, ward off, suppress; विनयं विनिवार्य Māl. 1. 18.<BR>—2 To prohibit, forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्
विनिवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To turn back, return.<BR>—2 To cease, come to an end; सपिण्डता तु पुरुषे सप्तमे विनिवर्तते<BR> Ms. 5. 60; विषया विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः Bg. 2. 59.<BR>—3 To desist, turn away, abstain (from); देवनात्, युद्धात् &c. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to cease or stop, withdraw; चापेन यस्यं विनिवर्तितकर्म<BR> जातम् Ś. 7. 26.<BR>—2 To restrain, withhold.<BR>—3 To renounce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1446-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्त|विनिवृत्तः
विनिवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Returned, turned away.<BR>—2 Stopped, ceased, desisted from.<BR>—3 Retired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्तिः|विनिवृत्ति
विनिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cessation, stopping, removing; शकाभ्यसूयाविनिवृत्तये R. 6. 74.<BR>—2 End, stop, termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चि
विनिश्चि €5 U. To determine, resolve, ascertain; विनिश्चेतुं शक्यो<BR> न सुखमिति वा दुःखमिति वा U. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चयः|विनिश्चय
विनिश्चयः<BR>—1 Fixing, settling, ascertainment.<BR>—2 A decision, resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्वासः|विनिश्वास
विनिश्वासः Hard breathing or respiration, sighing, a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पत्
विनिष्पत् P.<BR>—1 To fly forth, rush forth.<BR>—2 To run away; शशवच्च विनिष्पतेत् Ms. 7. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पेषः|विनिष्पेष
विनिष्पेषः Bruising, crushing, grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहत|विनिहतः
विनिहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck down, wounded.<BR>—2 Killed.<BR>—3 Completely overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहतः|विनिहत
विनिहत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Any great or unavoidable calamity, such as that inflicted by fate or heaven.<BR>—2 A portent, comet.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनिहतात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहतात्मन्
विनिहत + -आत्मन् one who has lost his soul; स त्वां विनिहतात्मानं … … जाने पापसमाचारम्<BR> Rām. 4. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहित
विनिहित <i>p. p.</i> [वि + नि + धा]<BR>—1 Put down, laid down.<BR>—2 Appointed.<BR>—3 Separated.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनिहितदृष्टि, विनिहितमनस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहितदृष्टि
विनिहित + -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> one who has the eyes fixed upon, eagerly looking at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहितमनस्
विनिहित + -मनस् <i>a.</i> intent upon, devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिह्नुत
विनिह्नुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Denied, disowned.<BR>—2 Hidden, concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनी
विनी €1 P.<BR>—1 To remove, take away, destroy (said to be Ā. only except where it<BR> has ‘a part of the body’ for its object); पटुपटहध्वनिभिर्विनीतनिद्रः<BR> R. 9. 71; विनीतखेदः 13. 35, 46, 15. 48; Śi. 10. 62; Ki. 7. 30;<BR> Ku. 1. 9, 5. 32.<BR>—2 To teach, instruct, educate, train; विनिन्युरेनं गुरवो गुरुप्रियम्<BR> R. 3. 29, 5. 101, 15. 69, 18. 51; Y. 1. 311; Ku. 1. 34.<BR>—3 To tame, subdue, govern, control (fig. also); वन्यान् विनेष्यन्निव<BR> दुष्टसत्त्वान् R. 2. 8, 6. 27, 14. 75; Ki. 2. 41; वनगज इव तस्मात्<BR> सोऽभ्युपायैर्विनेयः Mu. 3. 25.<BR>—4 To appease, pacify (anger) (Ātm.); शक्योऽस्य मन्युर्भवता विनेतुम् R. 2. 49.<BR>—5 To pass away, spend (as time); कथमपि यामिनी विनीय Gīt. 8.<BR>—6 To carry through, perform, complete, finish.<BR>—7 To spend, apply to use (Ātm.); शतं विनयते Sk.<BR>—8 To give, present, pay, pay off (as tribute) (Ātm.); करं विनयते Sk.<BR>—9 To lead or conduct towards; नार्यश्चतुष्काभिमुखं व्यनैषुः Ku. 7. 9.<BR>—10 To bid, direct, order; मा चापलायेति गणान् व्यनैषीत् Ku. 3. 41.<BR>—11 To bend down, incline.<BR>—12 To spread, stretch out.<BR>—13 To throw off, dispel; स त्वमुत्तिष्ठ युध्यस्व विनीय भयमात्मनः Mb. 9. 31. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
विनय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Cast, thrown.<BR>—2 Secret.<BR>—3 Ill-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयः|विनय
विनय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Guidance, discipline, instruction (in oneʼs duties), moral training;<BR> सर्वक्षत्त्रनिबर्हणस्य विनयं कुर्युः कथं क्षात्त्रियाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">Page1447-2</a>]<BR> Mv. 3. 37; प्रजानां विनयाधानात् R. 1. 24; Māl. 10. 5; विनयाधिकारिकं<BR> प्रथमाधिकरणम् Kau. A.<BR>—2 Sense of propriety, decorum, decency; अनुयास्यन् मुनितनयां सहसा<BR> विनयेन वारितप्रसरः Ś. 1. 28.<BR>—3 Polite conduct, gentleman-like bearing, good breeding or manners; गुणैश्च<BR> तैस्तैर्विनयप्रधानैः R. 6. 79; Māl. 1. 18.<BR>—4 Modesty, humility; सुष्ठु शोभसे आर्यपुत्र एतेन विनयमाहात्म्येन<BR> U. 1; विद्या ददाति विनयम्; तथापि नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत R. 3. 34, 10. 71<BR> (where Malli. renders विनय by इन्द्रियजय or restraint<BR> of passions, unnecessarily in our opinion).<BR>—5 Reverence, courtesy, obeisance.<BR>—6 Conduct in general.<BR>—7 Drawing off, taking away, removing; उत्तरीयविनयात् त्रपमाणा Śi. 10. 42.<BR>—8 A man who has subdued his senses.<BR>—9 A trader, merchant.<BR>—10 Chastisement (दण्ड); शीलवृत्तमविज्ञाय धास्यामि विनयं परम्<BR> Mb. 3. 306. 19.<BR>—11 An office, business; विफलविनययत्नाः कामिनीनां वयस्याः Śi. 11. 36.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनयावनत, विनयकर्मन्, विनयग्राहिन्, विनयभाज्, विनयवाच्, विनयस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयावनत
विनय + -अवनत <i>a.</i> stooping humbly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयकर्मन्
विनय + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयग्राहिन्
विनय + -ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i> tractable, obedient, submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयभाज्
विनय + -भाज् <i>a.</i> modest, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयवाच्
विनय + -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking mildly or affably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयस्थ|विनयस्थः
विनय + -स्थ <i>a.</i> modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयनम्
विनयनम्<BR>—1 Removing, taking away; वक्ष्यस्यध्वश्रमविनयने तस्य शृङ्गे निषण्णः Me. 54.<BR>—2 Education, instruction, training, discipline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीत|विनीतः
विनीत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Taken away, removed.<BR>—2 Well-trained, educated, disciplined.<BR>—3 Refined, well-behaved.<BR>—4 Modest, humble, meek, gentle.<BR>—5 Decent, decorous, gentlemanly.<BR>—6 Sent away, dismissed.<BR>—7 Tamed, broken in.<BR>—8 Plain, simple (as a dress).<BR>—9 Having the passions under control, self-subdued.<BR>—10 Chastised, punished.<BR>—11 Tractable, governable.<BR>—12 Lovely, handsome.<BR>—13 Stretched, spread; शष्पबृस्यां विनीतायामिच्छाम्यहमुपासितुम् Rām. 3. 43. 20.<BR> (See नी with वि also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतः|विनीत
विनीत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A trained horse.<BR>—2 A trader.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनीतात्मन्, विनीतवेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतात्मन्
विनीत + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> humble, lowly; विनीतात्मा हि नृपतिर्न विनश्यति<BR> कर्हिचित् Ms. 7. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतवेषः|विनीतवेष
विनीत + -वेषः plain dress; विनीतवेषेण प्रवेष्टव्यानि तपोवनानि Ś. 1. 15-16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतकम्
विनीतकम्<BR>—1 A vehicle or conveyance (a litter &c.).<BR>—2 A carrier, bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतिः|विनीति
विनीतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Training, good behaviour.<BR>—2 Respect, reverence, esteem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीयः|विनीय
विनीयः<BR>—1 Sediment, dregs.<BR>—2 Sin, crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीवि
विनीवि <i>a.</i> Denuded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेतृ
विनेतृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A leader, guide.<BR>—2 A teacher, an instructor; स तथेति विनेतुरुदारमतेः प्रतिगृह्य<BR> वचो विससर्ज मुनिम् R. 8. 91; राक्षसानां विनेत्रा Mv. 7. 1.<BR>—3 A king, ruler.<BR>—4 A chastiser, punisher; अयं विनेता दृप्तानाम् Mv. 3. 46, 4. 1; R. 6. 39, 14. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेयः|विनेय
विनेयः A pupil, disciple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनुद्
विनुद् €6 P.<BR>—1 To strike, pierce; चोदयामास तानश्वान् विनुन्नान् भीष्मसायकैः Mb. 6. 106. 45.<BR>—2 To play on a musical instrument (वीणाम्, आतोद्यम् &c.).<BR>—3 To remove,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">Page1448-1</a>]<BR> drive away, dispel. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To remove, drive away, dispel, cast off; तापं विनोदय दृष्टिभिः<BR> Gīt. 10; Śi. 4. 66; Ś. 3. 21; Māl. 9. 41.<BR>—2 To pass, spend (as time).<BR>—3 To divert, amuse, entertain; क्व नु खल्वात्मानं विनोदयामि Ś. 3;<BR> लतासु दृष्टिं विनोदयामि Ś. 6; R. 14. 77.<BR>—4 To amuse oneself with; लक्ष्मीर्विनोदयति येन दिगन्तलम्बी सोऽपि<BR> त्वदाननरुचिं विजहाति चन्द्रः R. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1447-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदः|विनोद
विनोदः<BR>—1 Removing, driving away; श्रमविनोद; विनोदमिच्छन्नथ दर्पजन्मनः<BR>—2 A diversion, an amusement, any interesting or amusing pursuit or occupation;<BR> प्रायेणैते रमणविरहेष्वङ्गनानां विनोदाः Me. 89; मिथ्यैव व्यसनं<BR> वदन्ति मृगयामीदृग्विनोदः कुतः Ś. 2. 5.<BR>—3 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>—4 Eagerness, vehement desire.<BR>—5 Pleasure, happiness, gratification; विलपनविनोदोऽप्यसुलभः U. 3. 30;<BR> जनयतु रसिकजनेषु मनोरमरतिरसभावविनोदम् Gīt. 12.<BR>—6 A particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR>—7 A kind of house.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विनोदरसिक, विनोदस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदरसिक
विनोदः + -रसिक <i>a.</i> addicted to pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदस्थानम्
विनोदः + -स्थानम् ground for pleasure or enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदनम्
विनोदनम्<BR>—1 Removing.<BR>—2 A diversion &c.; see विनोद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदित
विनोदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Diverted, delighted.<BR>—2 Dispelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्द|विन्दः
विन्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Finding, gaining.<BR>—2 One who has obtained; त्रैलोक्येनापि विन्दस्त्वं तां क्रीत्वा सुकृती भव Bk. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दः|विन्द
विन्द + .{@-न्दः@} A particular hour of the day (मुहूर्त); विन्दो नाम<BR> मुहूर्तोऽसौ Rām. 3. 68. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दु|विंदु|विन्दुः
विन्दु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intelligent, wise.<BR>—2 Liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्दुः|विन्दु|विंदु
विन्दु + .{@-न्दुः@} A drop; see बिन्दु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यः|विन्ध्य|विंध्यः
विन्ध्यः [विदधाति करोति भयम् Uṇ. 4. 121]<BR>—1 N. of a range of mountains which separates Hindustan proper from the<BR> Deccan or south; it is one of the seven <i>Kulaparvatas</i> (q. v.) and<BR> forms the southern limit of Madhyadeśa; see Ms. 2. 21. [According to<BR> a legend, the Vindhya mountain, being jealous of the mount Meru (or Himālaya)<BR> demanded that the sun should revolve round himself as about Meru, which<BR> the sun declined to do; whereupon the Vindhya began to rise higher and<BR> higher so as to obstruct the path of the sun and moon. The gods being<BR> alarmed sought the aid of the sage Agastya, who approached the mountain<BR> and requested that by bending down he would give him an easy passage to<BR> the south, and that he would retain the same position till his return.<BR> This Vindhya consented to do (because according to one account, he regarded<BR> Agastya as his teacher); but Agastya never returned from the south, and<BR> Vindhya never attained the height of Meru.]<BR>—2 A hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्या
विन्ध्यः + .{@-न्ध्या@}<BR>—1 N. of a plant (लवली).<BR>—2 Small cardamoms.<BR>—3 A measure of time (त्रुटि); L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विन्ध्याटवी, विन्ध्यकूटः, विन्ध्यकूटनम्, विन्ध्यगिरिः, विन्ध्यवासिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्याटवी
विन्ध्यः + -अटवी the great Vindhya forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यकूटः|विन्ध्यकूट
विन्ध्यः + -कूटः, -कूटनम् epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यकूटनम्
विन्ध्यः + -कूटः, -कूटनम् epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यगिरिः|विन्ध्यगिरि
विन्ध्यः + -गिरिः the Vindhya range of hills; also विन्ध्याचल, विन्ध्याद्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यवासिन्
विन्ध्यः + -वासिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of the grammarian व्याडि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्ध्यवासिनी
विन्ध्यः + -वासिन् + .({@-नी@}) an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्न|विन्नः
विन्न <i>p. p.</i> [विद् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Known.<BR>—2 Got, obtained.<BR>—3 Discussed, investigated.<BR>—4 Placed, fixed.<BR>—5 Married; (see विद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्नकः|विन्नक
विन्नकः N. of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्
विन्यस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To put down, deposit, place; विन्यस्यन्ती भुवि गणनया देहलीदत्तपुष्पैः<BR> Me. 89; Bk. 3. 3.<BR>—2 To fix in or on, direct towards; रामे विन्यस्तमानसाः Rām.<BR>—3 To deliver or make over, commit to the care of, entrust; सुतविन्यस्तपत्नीकः Y. 3. 45.<BR>—4 To arrange, dispose, adjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यसनम्
विन्यसनम् Putting down; पदविन्यसनम्. See न्यास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्त|विन्यस्तः
विन्यस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Placed or put down.<BR>—2 Inlaid, paved.<BR>—3 Fixed.<BR>—4 Arranged.<BR>—5 Delivered.<BR>—6 Presented, offered.<BR>—7 Deposited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्तम्
विन्यस्त + .{@-स्तम्@} Arrangement, placing; दान्ततोरणविन्यस्तं वज्रस्फटिकवेदिकम्<BR> Rām. 7. 13. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यासः|विन्यास
विन्यासः<BR>—1 Entrusting, depositing.<BR>—2 A deposit.<BR>—3 Arrangement, adjustment, disposition; अक्षरविन्यासः ‘inscribing letters’<BR>; प्रत्यक्षरश्लेषमयप्रबन्धविन्यासवैदग्धनिधिः Vās. ‘composition of a work &c.’<BR>—4 A collection, an assemblage.<BR>—5 A site or receptacle.<BR>—6 Putting on (ornaments).<BR>—7 Movement; position (of limbs); attitude.<BR>—8 Exhibition, display.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विन्यासरेखा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यासरेखा
विन्यासः + -रेखा a line drawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् €10 U. (वेपयति-ते) To throw, cast. See वेप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A praiser, singer of hymns.<BR>—2 A wise man. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Praise, a hymn.<BR>—2 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्ष|विपक्षः
विपक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hostile, inimical, adverse, contrary.<BR>—2 Impartial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षः|विपक्ष
विपक्ष + .{@-क्षः@}<BR>—1 An enemy, adversary, opponent; गुणास्तस्य विपक्षेऽपि गुणिनो लेभिरेऽन्तरम्<BR> R. 17. 75; Śi. 11. 59.<BR>—2 A rival or fellow wife; प्रेमगर्वितविपक्षमत्सरात् R. 19. 20.<BR>—3 A disputant; हृतोत्तरं तत्त्वविचारमध्ये वक्तेव दोषैर्गुरुभिर्विपक्षम् Ki. 17. 43.<BR>—4 (In logic) A negative instance, an instance on the opposite side, (<i>i. e.</i><BR> that in which the साध्य or major term is not found); निश्चितसाध्याभाववान्<BR> विपक्षः T. S.; Mu. 5. 10.<BR>—5 (In gram.) An exception.<BR>—6 Impartiality, indifference.<BR>—7 The day of transition from one-half of a lunar month to another.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपक्षभावः, विपक्षवृत्तिः, विपक्षरमणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षभावः|विपक्षभाव
विपक्ष + -भावः, -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> hostility; विपक्षभावे चिरमस्य तस्थुषः R. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षवृत्तिः
विपक्ष + -भावः, -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> hostility; विपक्षभावे चिरमस्य तस्थुषः R. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षरमणी
विपक्ष + -रमणी a female rival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1448-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

