विपणिन्
विपणिन् <i>m.</i> A trader, merchant, shop-keeper; (पण्य) पूर्णापणा<BR> विपणिनो विपणीर्विभेजुः Śi. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण्यु
विपण्यु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 One who has left occupation, practice etc.<BR>—2 Indifferent; विरजधियोऽन्वयन्त्यभिविपण्यव एकसरम् Bhāg. 10. 87. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपथः|विपथ
विपथः A wrong road, bad way (lit. and fig.); सत्पथं कथमुत्सृज्य<BR> यास्यामि विपथं पथः Mb. 12. 359. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To go badly; fail, miscarry (as a business &c.).<BR>—2 To fall into misfortune or bad state; स बन्धुर्यो विपन्नानामापदुद्धरणक्षमः H. 1. 29.<BR>—3 To be disabled or incapacitated.<BR>—4 To die, perish; नाथवन्तस्त्वया लोकास्त्वमनाथा विपत्स्यसे U. 1. 44;<BR> हा तात एष ते नरेन्द्रचित्ताराधनोपकरणं जनो विपद्यते Māl. 5; Mk. 1. 38.<BR>—5 To obstruct.<BR>—6 To come to naught; यदि त्वभिहितं राज्ञा त्वयि तन्न विपत्स्यते<BR> Rām. 2. 18. 26. ━<i>Caus.</i> To destroy, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तिः|विपत्ति
विपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A calamity, misfortune, disaster, mishap, adversity; संपत्तौ च<BR> विपत्तौ च महतामेकरूपता Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Death, destruction; अतिरभसकृतानां कर्मणामाविपत्तेर्भवति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">Page1449-2</a>]<BR> हृदयदाही शल्यतुल्यो विपाकः Bh. 2. 99; R. 19. 56; Ve. 4. 6; हिमसेकविपत्तिः<BR> नलिनी R. 8. 45.<BR>—3 Agony, torment (यातना).<BR>—4 Cessation, end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तिः|विपत्ति
विपत्तिः + .{@-त्तिः@} (<i>m.</i>) An excellent or distinguished footsoldier; स्यन्दना<BR> नो च तुरगाः सुरेभा वा विपत्तयः Ki. 15. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपत्तिकालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तिकालः|विपत्तिकाल
विपत्तिः + -कालः season of adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A calamity, misfortune, adversity, distress; तत्त्वनिकषग्रावा तु<BR> तेषां (मित्राणां) विपद् H. 1. 183.<BR>—2 Death; सिंहादवापद्विपदं नृसिंहः R. 18. 35.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपदुद्धरणम्, विपदुद्धारः, विपत्कालः, विपद्ग्रस्त, विपद्युक्त, विपत्सागरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदुद्धरणम्
