विपद्ग्रस्त
विपद् + -ग्रस्त, -युक्त <i>a.</i> overtaken by or involved in calamity, unhappy, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्युक्त
विपद् + -ग्रस्त, -युक्त <i>a.</i> overtaken by or involved in calamity, unhappy, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्सागरः|विपत्सागर
विपद् + -सागरः ‘sea of misery’, a very heavy calamity or disaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदा
विपदा See विपद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्न|विपन्नः
विपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Dead.<BR>—2 Lost, destroyed.<BR>—3 Unfortunate, afflicted, distressed, fallen into adversity.<BR>—4 Declined.<BR>—5 Disabled, incapacitated; बलिं विपन्नमादाय अस्तं गिरिमुपागमन्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 12. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्नः|विपन्न
विपन्न + .{@-न्नः@} A snake.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपन्नदीधिति, विपन्नदेह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्नदीधिति
विपन्न + -दीधिति <i>a.</i> one whose splendour is gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्नदेह
विपन्न + -देह <i>a.</i> dead, defunct; विपन्नदेहे मयि मन्दभाग्ये ममेति<BR> चिन्ता क्व गमिष्यसि त्वम् Mk. 1. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिक्रान्त
विपरिक्रान्त <i>a.</i> Courageous, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिगा
विपरिगा €3 P. To go over, be upset (as a cart).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणम्
विपरिणम् <i>Caus.</i> To change or transform into. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be changed into.<BR>—2 To undergo a change for the worse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणमनम्
विपरिणमनम्, विपरिणामः<BR>—1 A change, an alteration.<BR>—2 Change of form, transformation.<BR>—3 One of the modes of construing a sentence according to which a word<BR> or expression in the sentence is changed so as to suit the general trend<BR> in the context. This change may pertain to विभक्ति, लिङ्ग, वचन, पुरुष,<BR> काल, अर्थ etc.; ŚB. on MS. 1. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणामः|विपरिणाम
विपरिणमनम्, विपरिणामः<BR>—1 A change, an alteration.<BR>—2 Change of form, transformation.<BR>—3 One of the modes of construing a sentence according to which a word<BR> or expression in the sentence is changed so as to suit the general trend<BR> in the context. This change may pertain to विभक्ति, लिङ्ग, वचन, पुरुष,<BR> काल, अर्थ etc.; ŚB. on MS. 1. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिमर्शः
विपरिमर्शः Consideration; प्रकृतीनां सामवायित-विपरिमर्शः Kau. A. 3, 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवृत्
विपरिवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To turn round, revolve (fig. also); हेतुनानेन कौन्तेय जगद्विपरिवर्तते Bg. 9. 10.<BR>—2 To roll about; भूमौ विपरिवर्तेत Ms. 6. 22.<BR>—3 To wander about, move to and fro.<BR>—4 To return.<BR>—5 To surround; attend upon (with acc.); दुःखं सुतेन सततं जनान्<BR> विपरिवर्तते Mb. 12. 139. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तनम्
विपरिवर्तनम् Turning about, rolling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपरिवर्तनविद्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तनविद्या
विपरिवर्तनम् + -विद्या a magical formula for causing a person to return; Ks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिश्रमता
विपरिश्रमता The state of being without fatigue; उरु सत्त्वमाह<BR> विपरिश्रमता Ki. 6. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरी
विपरी [विपरि + इ] €2 P.<BR>—1 To turn in an opposite direction.<BR>—2 To be otherwise, fail, prove fruitless; कल्याणं विदधातु वा भगवतीनीतिर्विपर्येतु<BR> वा Māl. 6. 3.<BR>—3 To change for the worse.<BR>—4 To go round, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1449-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीत|विपरीतः
विपरीत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Reversed, inverted.<BR>—2 Contrary, opposite, reverse, inverse; राज्येन किं तद्विपरीतवृत्तेः R. 2. 53.<BR>—3 Wrong, contrary to rule.<BR>—4 False, untrue; विपरीतार्थविदो हि योषितः Bv. 2. 177.<BR>—5 Unfavourable, adverse.<BR>—6 Cross, acting in an opposite manner; विपरीतश्च वृद्धश्च विषयैश्च<BR> प्रधर्षितः Rām. 2. 21. 3.<BR>—7 Disagreeable, inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतः|विपरीत
विपरीत + .{@-तः@} A particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीता
विपरीत + .{@-ता@}<BR>—1 An unchaste or faithless wife.<BR>—2 A perverse woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपरीतकर, विपरीतकारक, विपरीतकारिन्, विपरीतकृत्, विपरीतचेतस्, विपरीतमति, विपरीतरतम्, विपरीतलक्षणा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतकर
विपरीत + -कर, -कारक, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> perverse, acting in a contrary<BR> manner; स्तौतिरत्र विपरीतकारकः Śi. 14. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतकारक
विपरीत + -कर, -कारक, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> perverse, acting in a contrary<BR> manner; स्तौतिरत्र विपरीतकारकः Śi. 14. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतकारिन्
विपरीत + -कर, -कारक, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> perverse, acting in a contrary<BR> manner; स्तौतिरत्र विपरीतकारकः Śi. 14. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतकृत्
विपरीत + -कर, -कारक, -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>a.</i> perverse, acting in a contrary<BR> manner; स्तौतिरत्र विपरीतकारकः Śi. 14. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतचेतस्
विपरीत + -चेतस्, -मति <i>a.</i> having a perverted mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतमति
विपरीत + -चेतस्, -मति <i>a.</i> having a perverted mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतरतम्
विपरीत + -रतम् inverted sexual intercourse; अद्यापि तत् कनककुण्डलघृष्टगण्डमास्यं<BR> स्मरामि विपरीतरताभियोगे C. P. 12; cf. पुरुषायित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतलक्षणा
विपरीत + -लक्षणा ironical description of a thing by mentioning its contrary properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतता
विपरीतता, -त्वम्<BR> Contrariety, inversion, opposition; लोके गुरुत्वं विपरीततां<BR> वा स्वचेष्टितान्येव नरं नयन्ति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतत्वम्
विपरीतता, -त्वम्<BR> Contrariety, inversion, opposition; लोके गुरुत्वं विपरीततां<BR> वा स्वचेष्टितान्येव नरं नयन्ति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यय|विपर्ययः|विपर्य्यय|विपर्य्ययः
विपर्यय <i>a.</i> Reversed, inverted, perverse; यदा वृश्चिकादिषु<BR> पञ्चसु वर्तते तदाहोरात्राणि विपर्ययाणि भवन्ति Bhāg. 5. 21. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्ययः|विपर्यय|विपर्य्यय|विपर्य्ययः
विपर्यय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 Contrariety, reverse, inversion; आहितो जयविपर्ययोऽपि मे श्लाघ्य<BR> एव परमेष्ठिना त्वया R. 11. 86; स्वशरीरशरीरिणावपि श्रुतसंयोगविपर्ययौ<BR> यदा 8. 89; नभसः स्फुटतारस्य रात्रेरिव विपर्ययः (न भाजनम्)<BR> Ki. 11. 44; विपर्यये तु Ś. 5 ‘if it be otherwise’, if contrary be<BR> the case; विपर्यये त्वस्याधिपतेरुल्लङ्घितः क्षान्रधर्मः स्यात् Ve. 5.<BR>—2 Change (of purpose, dress &c.); कथमेत्य मतिर्विपर्ययं करिणी<BR> पङ्कमिवावसीदति Ki. 2. 6; so वेषविपर्ययः Pt. 1.<BR>—3 Absence or non-existence; समुद्रगारूपविपर्ययेऽपि Ku. 7. 42;<BR> त्यागे श्लाघाविपर्ययः R. 1. 22.<BR>—4 Loss; राघवाणामयुक्तोऽयं कुलस्यास्य विपर्ययैः Rām. 1. 21. 2;<BR> निद्रा संज्ञाविपर्ययः Ku. 6. 44 ‘loss of consciousness’.<BR>—5 Complete destruction, annihilation; दुःशासनवधं श्रुत्वा कर्णस्य<BR> च विपर्ययम् Mb. 11. 1. 16; Rām. 7. 6. 50.<BR>—6 Exchange, barter.<BR>—7 Error, trespass, mistake, misapprehension.<BR>—8 A calamity, misfortune, adverse fate; प्रियं त्वत्कृतमिच्छामि मम<BR> गर्भविपर्यये Rām. 1. 47. 3.<BR>—9 Hostility, enmity.<BR>—10 Perverseness, opposition.<BR>—11 The destruction of the world (प्रलय); हरिं विशन्ति स्म शरा<BR> लोका इव विपर्यये Rām. 7. 7. 4.<BR>—12 Misapprehension; भयं द्वितीयाभिनिवेशतः स्यादीशादपेतस्य विपर्ययोऽस्मृतिः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 2. 37; Mv. 3. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यायः|विपर्याय|विपर्य्याय|विपर्य्यायः
विपर्यायः Reverse, contrariety; V. 4; see विपर्यय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्
विपर्यस् €4 P.<BR>—1 To overturn, reverse, invert.<BR>—2 To change, alter.<BR>—3 To take wrongly, misunderstand; प्रतीकारो व्याधेः सुखमिति विपर्यस्यति<BR> जनः Bh. 3. 92.<BR>—4 To undergo change, be affected (intrans.); दैवेनोपहतस्य बुद्धिरथवा<BR> सर्वा विपर्यस्यति Mu. 6. 8; (cf. the Latin adage ‘quem deus vult perdere prius dementat’<BR>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्त|विपर्य्यस्त
विपर्यस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Changed; विपर्यस्तं यथा नाम कुवलाश्वस्य धीमतः Mb. 3. 201. 7;<BR> inverted, reversed; हन्त विपर्यस्तः संप्रति जीवलोकः U. 1.<BR>—2 Opposite, contrary.<BR>—3 Wrongly considered to be real; अनुत्पन्नं ज्ञानं यदि यदि च संदेहविधुरं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">Page1450-2</a>]<BR> विपर्यस्तं वा स्यात् परिचर वसिष्ठस्य चरणौ Mv. 3. 36.<BR>—4 (In gram.) Interchanged.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपर्यस्तपुत्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्तपुत्रा
विपर्यस्त + -पुत्रा a woman bearing no male children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यासः|विपर्यास|विपर्य्यास|विपर्य्यासः
विपर्यासः<BR>—1 Change; कथं नाम विपर्यासाद्धुन्धुमारत्वमागतः Mb. 3. 201. 6;<BR> contrariety, reverse; विपर्यासं यातो घनविरलभावः क्षितिरुहाम् U. 2. 27.<BR>—2 Adverseness, unfavourableness; as in दैवविपर्यासात्.<BR>—3 Interchange, exchange; प्रवहणविपर्यासेनागता Mk. 8.<BR>—4 An error, a mistake.<BR>—5 Expiration, lapse (of time).<BR>—6 Deterioration, death.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपर्यासोपमा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यासोपमा
विपर्यासः + -उपमा an inverted comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलम्
विपलम् A moment, an extremely small division of time (said to be<BR> equal to one-sixth or one-sixtieth part of a <i>pala</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायनम्
विपलायनम् Running away, fleeing in different directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलाश
विपलाश <i>a.</i> Leafless (विपर्ण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्चित्
विपश्चित् <i>a.</i> Learned, wise; विपश्चितो विनिन्युरेनं गुरवो गुरुप्रियम्<BR> R. 3. 29. ━<i>m.</i> A learned or wise man, sage; भवन्ति ते सभ्यतमा<BR> विपश्चितां मनोगतं वाचि निवेशयन्ति ये Ki. 14. 4; Pt. 1. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाकः|विपाक
विपाकः<BR>—1 Cooking, dressing.<BR>—2 Digestion; रूपं चक्षुर्विपाकश्च त्रिधा ज्योतिर्विधीयते Mb. 12. 248. 10;<BR> also bad digestion.<BR>—3 Ripening, ripeness, maturity, development (fig. also); अमी पृथुस्तम्बभृतः<BR> पिशङ्गतां गता विपाकेन फलस्य शालयः Ki. 4. 26; वाचां विपाको मम<BR> Bv. 4. 42 ‘my mature, full-developed, or dignified words’.<BR>—4 Consequence, fruit, result, the result of actions either in this or<BR> in a former birth; अहो मे दारुणतरः कर्मणां विपाकः K. 354; ममैव<BR> जन्मान्तरपातकानां विपाकविस्फूर्जथुरप्रसह्यः R. 14. 62; Bh. 2. 99; Mv. 5. 56.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Change of state; कष्टं बतान्यदिव दैववशेन जाता दुःखात्मकं<BR> किमपि भूतमहो विपाकः U. 4. 6.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) An unexpected event or occurrence, a reverse, adverse turn of<BR> fate, distress, calamity; ईदृशानां विपाकोऽपि जायते परमाद्भुतः U. 3. 3;<BR> विपाके घोरेऽस्मिन्नथ खलु विमूढा तव सखी 4. 12.<BR>—6 Difficulty, embarrassment.<BR>—7 Flavour, taste.<BR>—8 Withering, fading.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपाककालः, विपाकदारुण, विपाकदोषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाककालः|विपाककाल
विपाकः + -कालः the time of maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाकदारुण
विपाकः + -दारुण <i>a.</i> terrible in results.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाकदोषः|विपाकदोष
विपाकः + -दोषः morbid affection of digestive powers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटल
विपाटल <i>a.</i> Very red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाठः|विपाठ
विपाठः A kind of large arrow; क्षुरनाराचभल्लानां विपाठानां च<BR> तत्त्ववित् Mb. 1. 139. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाण्डु|विपांडु
विपाण्डु <i>a.</i> Pale, pallid; परितो विपाण्डु दधदभ्रशिरः Śi. 9. 3;<BR> Ki. 5. 6; so विपाण्डुर; क्वचिज्जलापायविपाण्डुराणि Śi. 4. 5;<BR> विपाण्डुररुचम् Ratn. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादनम्
विपादनम् Destroying, killing, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादिका
विपादिका<BR>—1 A sore or tumour on the foot.<BR>—2 An enigma, a riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाल
विपाल <i>a.</i> Unguarded; विपालान् वारयेत् पशून् Ms. 8. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1450-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश्
विपाश्, विपाशा <i>f.</i> N. of one of the five rivers in the<BR> Panjab (now called Beas); एषा रम्या विपाशा च नदी परमपावनी Mb. 3. 130. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाशा
विपाश्, विपाशा <i>f.</i> N. of one of the five rivers in the<BR> Panjab (now called Beas); एषा रम्या विपाशा च नदी परमपावनी Mb. 3. 130. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिन|विपिनं
विपिन <i>a.</i> Thick, dense; अमुमतिविपिनं वेद दिग्व्यापिनम् Ki. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिनम्
विपिन + .{@-नम्@} [वप्-इनन् ह्रस्वश्च पृषो˚; cf. Uṇ. 2. 52]<BR>—1 A wood, forest, grove, thicket; वृन्दावनविपिने ललितं वितनोतु शुभानि यशस्यम् Gīt. 1;<BR> विपिनानि प्रकाशानि शक्तिमत्वाच्चकार सः R. 4. 31; Māl. 9. 2.<BR>—2 A multitude, quantity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपिनौकस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिनौकस्
विपिन + -ओकस् an ape, monkey; रक्षोभिर्विपिनौकसां परिवृढैश्चारादपास्तक्रमम् Mv. 6. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुंसक
विपुंसक <i>a.</i> Unmanly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुरुष
विपुरुष <i>a.</i> Void of men, empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुल|विपुलः
विपुल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Large, extensive, capacious, broad, wide, spacious; विपुलं नितम्बदेशे<BR> M. 3. 7; शिरसि तनुर्विपुलश्च मध्यदेशे Mk. 3. 22; कालो ह्ययं<BR> निरवधिर्विपुला च पृथ्वी Māl. 1. 6; क्वचिद् द्वीपाकारः पुलिनविपुलैर्भोगनिवहैः<BR> Nāg. 5. 26; so विपुलं पृष्ठम्, विपुलः कुक्षिः &c.<BR>—2 Much, ample, copious, abundant; तपसा तथा न मुदमस्य ययौ भगवान्<BR> यथा विपुलसत्त्वतया Ki. 18. 14.<BR>—3 Deep, profound; विपुलार्था च भारती Mv. 1. 2.<BR>—4 With the hair standing on end, thrilling; विपुलेन निपीडप निर्दयं<BR> मुदमायातु नितान्तमुन्मनाः Śi. 16. 3 (where it has sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलः|विपुल
विपुल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 N. of the mountain Meru.<BR>—2 Of Himālaya.<BR>—3 A respectable man.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विपुलग्रीव, विपुलच्छाय, विपुलजघना, विपुलप्रज्ञा, विपुलबुद्धि, विपुलमति, विपुलरसः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलग्रीव
विपुल + -ग्रीव <i>a.</i> long-necked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलच्छाय
विपुल + -छाय <i>a.</i> shady, umbrageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलजघना
विपुल + -जघना a woman with large hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलप्रज्ञा
विपुल + -प्रज्ञा, -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i> endowed with great talents or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलबुद्धि
विपुल + -प्रज्ञा, -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i> endowed with great talents or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलमति
विपुल + -प्रज्ञा, -बुद्धि, -मति <i>a.</i> endowed with great talents or understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुलरसः|विपुलरस
विपुल + -रसः the sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुला
विपुला The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुष्ट
विपुष्ट <i>a.</i> Ill-fed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुष्टिः|विपुष्टि
विपुष्टिः Perfect welfare; prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूयः|विपूय
विपूयः The <i>Munja</i> grass; P. III. 1. 117; विपूयैः कृतमेखलाम् Bk. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूयकम्
विपूयकम् Suppuration; an offensive smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रः|विप्र
विप्रः [वप्-रन् पृषो˚ अत इत्वम्; Uṇ. 2. 28]<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa; see the quotations under ब्राह्मण.<BR>—2 A sage, wise man; त्वं मुखं पद्मजो विप्रः Mb. 1. 23. 17.<BR>—3 The Aśvattha tree.<BR>—4 (In prosody) A foot of four short syllables.<BR>—5 A singer of hymns, praiser.<BR>—6 The month भाद्रपद.<BR>—7 Ficus Religiosa (Mar. पिंपळ).<BR>—8 Acacia Sirissa (Mar. शिरस).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विप्रर्षिः, विप्रकाष्ठम्, विप्रकुण्डः, विप्रग्रहः, विप्रप्रिय, विप्रसमागमः, विप्रस्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रर्षिः|विप्रर्षि
विप्रः + -ऋषिः = ब्रह्मर्षिः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकाष्ठम्
विप्रः + -काष्ठम् the cotton-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकुण्डः|विप्रकुण्ड
विप्रः + -कुण्डः an adulterous offspring of Brāhmaṇa parents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रग्रहः
विप्रः + -ग्रहः = ब्रह्मराक्षस q. v.; Bhāg. 6. 8. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रप्रिय|विप्रप्रियः
विप्रः + -प्रिय <i>a.</i> dear to Brāhmaṇas; विप्रप्रियं धार्मिकम् Rāmarakṣā 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रप्रियः|विप्रप्रिय
विप्रः + -प्रिय + .({@-यः@}) the Palāśa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रप्रियम्
विप्रः + -प्रिय + .({@-यम्@}) thick sour milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रसमागमः|विप्रसमागम
विप्रः + -समागमः a concourse or synod of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रस्वम्
विप्रः + -स्वम् the property of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकीर्ण
विप्रकीर्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Spread about, dispersed, scattered.<BR>—2 Loose, dishevelled (as hair).<BR>—3 Expanded, outstretched.<BR>—4 Wide, broad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृ
विप्रकृ €8 U.<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To tease, trouble, harass, harm; किं सत्त्वानि विप्रकरोषि Ś. 7;<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To oppress; तस्मिन् विप्रकृताः काले तारकेण दिवौकसः Ku. 2. 1.<BR>—2 To wrong, ill-treat, offend; भर्तुर्विप्रकृतापि रोषणतया मा स्म<BR> प्रतीपं गमः Ś. 4. 17.<BR>—3 To affect, cause a change in; कमपरमवशं न विप्रकुर्युर्विभुमपि<BR> तं यदमी स्पृशन्ति भावाः Ku. 6. 95.<BR>—4 To disfigure, deform; आभरणोचितं रूपमाश्रमसुलभैः प्रसाधनैर्विप्रकार्यते Ś. 4.<BR>—5 To appoint, admit (as a witness); Mb. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकारः|विप्रकार
विप्रकारः<BR>—1 Insult, contumely, abuse, treating with disrespect; उदीरितां तामिति<BR> याज्ञसेन्या नवीकृतोद्ग्राहितविप्रकाराम् Ki. 3. 55.<BR>—2 Injury, offence; शशंसुर्विप्रकारं तं तस्मै तारककारितम् Mb. 13. 86. 28.<BR>—3 Wickedness.<BR>—4 Opposition, counteraction.<BR>—5 Retaliation.<BR>—6 Various manner.<BR>—7 Wrong way, act; मत्स्यानां विप्रकारांस्ते बहूनस्मानकीर्तयन् Mb. 4. 47. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृत्
विप्रकृत् <i>a.</i> Hurting, offending; अस्मद्विधानां दुष्टानां निर्लज्जानां<BR> च विप्रकृत् Bhāg. 6. 17. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृत|विप्रकृतः
विप्रकृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Hurt, offended, injured; एवं विप्रकृते लोके दैत्येन्द्रानुचरैर्मुहुः<BR> Bhāg. 7. 2. 16.<BR>—2 Insulted, abused, treated with contumely.<BR>—3 Opposed.<BR>—4 Retaliated, requited.<BR>—5 Oppressed, troubled, disturbed.<BR>—6 Irritated, provoked; विप्रकृतः पन्नगः फणां कुरुते Ś. 6. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृतिः|विप्रकृति
विप्रकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Injury, offence.<BR>—2 An insult, abuse, contumely.<BR>—3 Retaliation, retort.<BR>—4 Change, variation; अभियुक्तं च नान्येन नोक्तं विप्रकृतिं नयेत् Y. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्
विप्रकृष् €1 P. To draw away, remove, counteract; कामं दुग्धे विप्रकर्षत्यलक्ष्मीम् U. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकर्षः|विप्रकर्ष
विप्रकर्षः<BR>—1 Distance, remoteness.<BR>—2 Difference, contrast; विप्रकर्षेण बुध्येत कृतकर्मा यथाफलम् Mb. 3. 32. 46.<BR>—3 Dragging away, carrying off; द्रौपद्या विप्रकर्षेण राज्यापहरणेन<BR> च Mb. 3. 2. 9.<BR>—4 (In gram.) The separation of two consonants by the insertion of a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्ट|विप्रकृष्टः
विप्रकृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Drawn away, removed.<BR>—2 Distant, remote.<BR>—3 Protracted, lengthened, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्टक|विप्रकृष्टकं
विप्रकृष्टक <i>a.</i> Remote, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रणश्
विप्रणश् See प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतारकः|विप्रतारक
विप्रतारकः An impostor, deceiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकारः|विप्रतिकार
विप्रतिकारः<BR>—1 Counteraction, opposition, contradiction.<BR>—2 Retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्
विप्रतिपद् €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To differ, be mutually opposed, conflict.<BR>—2 To waver, vacillate; मिथ्यावृत्तिरनार्यः सन्नद्य विप्रतिपद्यसे<BR> Mb. 5. 128. 18.<BR>—3 To reply falsely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपत्तिः|विप्रतिपत्ति
विप्रतिपत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Mutual discrepancy, contest, conflict, dispute, opposition (as of opinions or interests).<BR>—2 Dissent, objection.<BR>—3 Perplexity, confusion.<BR>—4 Mutual relation.<BR>—5 Conversancy.<BR>—6 Hostile feeling; इयं विप्रतिपत्तिस्ते यदा त्वं पिशिताशनः Mb. 12. 111. 9.<BR>—7 Error, mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1451-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपन्न
विप्रतिपन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Mutually opposed, opposite, dissentient; उवाच परया सूक्त्या बुद्ध्या<BR> विप्रतिपन्नया Rām. 2. 109. 1.<BR>—2 Confused, bewildered, perplexed; श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्ना ते यदा स्थास्यति<BR> निश्चला Bg. 2. 53.<BR>—3 Hindered, obstructed; नद्यो जलं विप्रतिपन्नमार्गाः Rām. 4. 28. 45.<BR>—4 Contested, disputed.<BR>—5 Mutually connected or related.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विप्रतिपन्नबुद्धि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपन्नबुद्धि
विप्रतिपन्न + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> having a false opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिषेधः|विप्रतिषेध
विप्रतिषेधः<BR>—1 Keeping under control, controlling; क्रव्याद्भ्य इव भूतानामदान्तेभ्यः<BR> सदा भयम् । तेषां विप्रतिषेधार्थं राजा सृष्टः स्वयंभुवा ॥ Mb.<BR>—2 The opposition of two courses of action which are equally important,<BR> the conflict of two even-matched interests; हरिर्विप्रतिषेधं तमाचचक्षे<BR> विचक्षणः Śi. 2. 6 (तुल्यबलविरोधो विप्रतिषेधः Malli.).<BR>—3 (In gram.) The conflict of two different grammatical operations become<BR> possible according to two different rules, conflict of two equally important<BR> rules; विप्रतिषेधे परं कार्यम् P. I. 4. 2; विरोधो विप्रतिषेधः ।<BR> यत्र द्वौ प्रसंगावन्यार्थावेकस्मिन् प्राप्नुतः सः विप्रतिषेधः Kāśi.; see Mbh. also.<BR>—4 Prohibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसारः|विप्रतिसार
विप्रति(ती)सारः<BR>—1 Repentance; प्रापि चेतसि सविप्रतिसारे सुभ्रुवामवसरः सरकेण Śi. 10. 20.<BR>—2 Anger, rage, wrath.<BR>—3 Wickedness, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतीसारः|विप्रतीसार
विप्रति(ती)सारः<BR>—1 Repentance; प्रापि चेतसि सविप्रतिसारे सुभ्रुवामवसरः सरकेण Śi. 10. 20.<BR>—2 Anger, rage, wrath.<BR>—3 Wickedness, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रत्ययः|विप्रत्यय
विप्रत्ययः Distrust; यदि विप्रत्ययो ह्येष तदिदं दर्शयाम ते<BR> Mb. 12. 111. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रथित
विप्रथित <i>p. p.</i> Celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदहः|विप्रदह
विप्रदहः Dry food consisting of fruits, roots etc.; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्ट
विप्रदुष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Vitiated, spoiled, dissolute.<BR>—2 Corrupt; very dissolute, bad; विप्रदुष्टां स्त्रियं भर्ता निरुन्ध्यादेकवेश्मनि Ms. 11. 176.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विप्रदुष्टभाव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्टभाव
विप्रदुष्ट + -भाव <i>a.</i> having a wicked disposition; न विप्रदुष्टभावस्य<BR> सिद्धिं गच्छन्ति कर्हिचित् Ms. 2. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रधर्षः|विप्रधर्ष
विप्रधर्षः Harassing, annoyance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रनष्ट
विप्रनष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Lost.<BR>—2 Vain, useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रपातः|विप्रपात
विप्रपातः A precipice, abyss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुच्
विप्रमुच् See प्रमुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुक्त
विप्रमुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Set free, liberated, loosened; पर्यायत्वरितगृहीतविप्रमुक्तः Mv. 1. 44.<BR>—2 Shot, discharged.<BR>—3 Free from (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुज्
विप्रयुज् €7 Ā. To separate, disjoin; to deprive (one) of. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR> To be separated from (with instr.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To deprive of, free from.<BR>—2 To separate, disjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुक्त|विप्रयुक्तः
विप्रयुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Separated, severed, detached.<BR>—2 Separated from, being absent or away from (with instr. or in comp.);<BR> अबलाविप्रयुक्तः स कामी Me. 2.<BR>—3 Freed or released from.<BR>—4 Deprived or destitute of, without (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोगः|विप्रयोग
विप्रयोगः<BR>—1 Disunion, severance, separation, dissociation; as प्रिय˚.<BR>—2 Especially, separation of lovers; मा भूदेवं क्षणमपि च ते विद्युता<BR> विप्रयोगः Me. 117, 10; सद्यस्त्वया सह कृशोदरि विप्रयोगः V. 5. 16;<BR> R. 13. 26, 14. 66.<BR>—3 Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>—4 Being fit or deserved.<BR>—5 Absence, want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलप्
विप्रलप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To dispute, contradict, wrangle, quarrel.<BR>—2 To discuss, debate.<BR>—3 To lament, bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलप्तम्
विप्रलप्तम्<BR>—1 Discussion, debate, controversy; futile talk; न चेन्मोघं विप्रलप्तं<BR> ममेदम् Mb. 12. 29. 145.<BR>—2 Bewailing, lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलापः|विप्रलाप
विप्रलापः<BR>—1 Idle or unmeaning talk, prattle, gibberish, nonsense.<BR>—2 Mutual contradiction, contradictory statement; P. I. 3. 50.<BR>—3 A dispute, wrangling.<BR>—4 Violation of oneʼs promise, breaking oneʼs word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलभ्
विप्रलभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To cheat, deceive, impose upon.<BR>—2 To recover, regain.<BR>—3 To insult, disrespect.<BR>—4 To violate, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्ध|विप्रलब्धः
विप्रलब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Deceived, cheated; ऐक्याद्वयस्य ऋतवानिति विप्रलब्धः Bhāg. 1. 15. 19.<BR>—2 Disappointed.<BR>—3 Hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्धा
विप्रलब्ध + .{@-ब्धा@} A woman disappointed by her loverʼs breaking his appointment;<BR> (one of the several classes of a Nāyikā in poetic composition); she<BR> is thus defined in S. D.:− प्रियः कृत्वापि संकेतं यस्या नायाति संनिधिम् ।<BR> विप्रलब्धेति सा ज्ञेया नितान्तमवमानिता ॥ 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्धृ
विप्रलब्धृ <i>a.</i> A deceiver; श्रद्धेया विप्रलब्धारः Ki. 11. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भः|विप्रलम्भ|विप्रलंभ|विप्रलंभः
विप्रलम्भः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Deceiving, deceit, tricking, disappointment; विप्रलम्भोऽयमत्यन्तं<BR> यदि स्युरफलाः क्रियाः Mb. 3. 31. 28; विप्रलम्भोऽपि लाभाय सति प्रियसमागमे Ki. 11. 27.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Delusion; अतिक्लामिता खलु प्रियसखी अनेनानुकूलविप्रलम्भेन Māl. 6.<BR>—2 Especially, deceiving by false statement or by not keeping promises;<BR> विप्रलम्भकृत्रिमप्रेमसहजसौहार्दवेदिनं तं विद्येश्वरं सबहुमानं<BR> विससर्ज Dk. 1. 5.<BR>—3 Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>—4 Disunion, separation, disjunction.<BR>—5 The separation of lovers; शुश्रुवे प्रियजनस्य कातरं विप्रलम्भपरिशङ्किनो<BR> वचः R. 19. 18; Ve. 2. 12.<BR>—6 (In Rhet.) The feeling or sentiment of love in separation, one of the<BR> two main kinds of शृङ्गार (opp. संभोग); अपरः (विप्रलम्भः)<BR> अभिलाषविरहेर्ष्याप्रवासशापहेतुक इति पञ्चविधः K. P. 4; यूनोरयुक्तयोर्भावो<BR> युक्तयोर्वाथवा मिथः । अभीष्टालिङ्गनादीनामनवाप्तौ प्रहृष्यते । विप्रलम्भः<BR> स विज्ञेयः −उज्ज्वलमणिः; cf. S. D. 212 <i>et seq.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भनम्
विप्रलम्भनम् Deception, fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलम्भित
विप्रलम्भित <i>p. p.</i> Insulted, violated; चतुर्भिरद्भुतैः सिद्धै<BR> राज्ञा ते विप्रलम्भिताः Bhāg. 6. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलयः|विप्रलय
विप्रलयः Complete destruction or dissolution; annihilation; विद्याकल्पेन<BR> मरुता मेघानां भूयसामपि । ब्रह्मणीव विवर्तानां क्वापि विप्रलयः कृतः ॥ U. 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलीन
विप्रलीन <i>a.</i> Dispersed, routed (as a defeated army).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1452-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुप्
विप्रलुप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To tear, snatch away.<BR>—2 To afflict, disturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुप्त
विप्रलुप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Carried away, snatched away.<BR>—2 Disturbed, interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुम्पक
विप्रलुम्पक <i>a.</i> Plunderer, robber, rapacious; Ms. 8. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलोभिन्
विप्रलोभिन् <i>m.</i> A species of plant like अशोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलोकः|विप्रलोक
विप्रलोकः A bird-catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवादः|विप्रवाद
विप्रवादः<BR>—1 Disagreement.<BR>—2 Different opinion; विप्रवादा बहवः श्रूयन्ते पुत्रकारिताः Mb. 13. 49. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवस्
विप्रवस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To sojourn, be absent from (oneʼs home); R. 12. 11.<BR>—2 To return from journey; विप्रोष्य तूपसंग्राह्या ज्ञातिसंबन्धियोषितः<BR> Ms. 2. 132. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To banish, expel.<BR>—2 To remove, take away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवसित
विप्रवसित <i>p. p.</i> Withdrawn, departed; भिक्षुभिर्विप्रवसिते<BR> Bhāg. 1. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासः|विप्रवास
विप्रवासः Staying abroad, dwelling in a foreign country (away from<BR> oneʼs home); क्व चासीद्विप्रवासस्ते किं चाकार्षीः प्रवासतः Mb. 3. 14. 1, 3. 273. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासनम्
विप्रवासनम्<BR>—1 Banishment; ततो दुःखतरं भूयः सीताया विप्रवासनम् Rām. 7. 50. 7.<BR>—2 Staying abroad, sojourn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषित|विप्रोषितः
विप्रोषित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Staying abroad, away from, absent; वनेषु मृगराजेषु व्याघ्नविप्रोषितेषु<BR> च Mb. 5. 120. 10.<BR>—2 Banished, being in exile; विप्रोषितकुमारं तद्राज्यमस्तमितेश्वरम् R. 12. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विप्रोषितभर्तृका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषितभर्तृका|विप्रोषितभर्त्तृका
विप्रोषित + -भर्तृका a woman whose husband is absent from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रश्निका
विप्रश्निका A female fortune-teller; विप्रश्निका त्वीक्षणिका दैवज्ञा Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रसन्न
विप्रसन्न <i>a.</i> Greatly pleased; शमात्मके चेतसि विप्रसन्ने Bu. C. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रस्थित
विप्रस्थित <i>p. p.</i> Departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रहत
विप्रहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck down, defeated.<BR>—2 Trodden; अविप्रहतमैक्ष्वाकः पप्रच्छ मुनिपुंगवम् Rām. 1. 24. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रहाणम्
विप्रहाणम् Disappearance, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रहीण
विप्रहीण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deprived or destitute of; इमं भौमं नरकं क्षीणपुण्यः प्रवेष्टुमुर्वी<BR> गगनाद्विप्रहीणः Mb. 1. 92. 7.<BR>—2 Disappeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रिय|विप्रियः
विप्रिय <i>a.</i> Disagreeable, disliked, unpleasant, distasteful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रियम्
विप्रिय + .{@-यम्@} Offence, wrong, a disagreeable act; मनसापि न विप्रियं<BR> मया कृतपूर्वं तव किं जहासि माम् R. 8. 52; Ku. 4. 7; Ki. 9. 39; Śi. 15. 11;<BR> U. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्
विप्रुष् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A drop (of water or any other liquid); संतापं नवजलविप्रुषो गृहीत्वा<BR> Śi. 8. 40; स्वेदविप्रुषः 2. 18.<BR>—2 A mark, dot, spot.<BR>—3 Drops falling from the mouth while speaking; Ms. 1. 133 (com. विप्रुषो<BR> मुखनिःसृता अल्पा जलकणाः).<BR>—4 A phenomenon; Rāj. T.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लु
विप्लु €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To float about, swing to and for, fluctuate.<BR>—2 To drift (in the sea), be scattered; यदि न स्यान्नरपतिः सम्यङ्नेता<BR> ततः प्रजा । अकर्णधारा जलधौ विप्लवेतेह नौरिव ॥ H. 3. 2; Pt. 3. 72.<BR>—3 To be confused (as mind).<BR>—4 To be ruined or destroyed.<BR>—5 To fail. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To cause to float or swim.<BR>—2 To divulge, spread abroad.<BR>—3 To teach (to unworthy persons); शरणागतं परित्यज्य वेदं विप्लाव्य<BR> च द्विजः Ms. 11. 198.<BR>—4 To cause to fail, spoil, mar; गुणानामायथातथ्यादर्थं विप्लावयन्ति<BR> ये Śi. 2. 56.<BR>—5 To confound, bewilder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लव|विप्लवः
विप्लव <i>a.</i> Perflexed, confused; मुमूर्षूणां हि मन्दात्मन्ननु<BR> स्युर्विप्लवा गिरः Bhāg. 7. 8. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लवः|विप्लव
विप्लव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Floating or drifting about, floating in different directions.<BR>—2 Opposition, contrariety.<BR>—3 Confusion, perplexity.<BR>—4 Tumult, scuffle, affray; M. 1.<BR>—5 Devastation, predatory warfare, danger from an enemy.<BR>—6 Extortion.<BR>—7 Loss, destruction; सत्त्वविप्लवात् R. 8. 41; तद्वाग्विसर्गो जनताघविप्लवः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 5. 11.<BR>—8 Adverseness, evil turn; अथवा मम भाग्यविप्लवात् R. 8. 47.<BR>—9 The rust on a mirror (dust accumulating on its surface); अपवर्जितविप्लवे<BR> शुचौ … मतिरादर्श इवाभिदृश्यते Ki. 2. 26 (where विप्लव also<BR> means प्रमाणबाधः ‘absence of reasoning’).<BR>—10 Transgression, violation; गुरूपदिष्टेन रिपौ सुतेऽपि वा निहन्ति<BR> दण्डेन स धर्मविप्लवम् Ki. 1. 13.<BR>—11 An evil, a calamity.<BR>—12 Sin, wickedness, sinfulness.<BR>—13 Terrifying an enemy by shouts and gestures.<BR>—14 Divulging, making public.<BR>—15 Profanation of the Veda by unseasonable study.<BR>—16 Shipwreck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लावः|विप्लाव
विप्लावः<BR>—1 Deluging, inundating.<BR>—2 Causing tumult.<BR>—3 A horseʼs canter or gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लावनम्
विप्लावनम् Abusing, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लावित
विप्लावित <i>p. p.</i> Confounded, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुत|विप्लुतः
विप्लुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Drifted about.<BR>—2 Drowned, submerged, deluged, overflowed.<BR>—3 Confounded, disturbed.<BR>—4 Ravaged, devastated.<BR>—5 Lost, disappeared.<BR>—6 Disgraced, dishonoured.<BR>—7 Ruined.<BR>—8 Obscured, disfigured.<BR>—9 Depraved, dissolute, profligate, guilty of lewdness; विप्लुतौ शूद्रवद्दण्ड्यौ Ms. 8. 377.<BR>—10 Contrary, reverse.<BR>—11 Turning out false; नैते वाचं विप्लुतां व्याहरन्ति U. 4. 18.<BR>—12 Agitated, troubled; भयविप्लुतमीक्षितो नभःस्थैर्जगतीं ग्राह इवापगां<BR> जगाहे Ki. 13. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुतम्
विप्लुत + .{@-तम्@} Springing, bursting asunder.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विप्लुतनेत्र, विप्लुतलोचन, विप्लुतभाषिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुतनेत्र
विप्लुत + -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> having the eyes suffused (with tears, joy etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुतलोचन
विप्लुत + -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> having the eyes suffused (with tears, joy etc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुतभाषिन्
विप्लुत + -भाषिन् <i>a.</i> speaking confusedly, stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुतिः|विप्लुति
विप्लुतिः Destruction, ruin, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुष्
विप्लुष् See विप्रुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्सा
विप्सा See वीप्सा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल|विफलं
विफल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fruitless, useless, vain, ineffectual, unprofitable; मम विफलमेतदनुरूपमपि<BR> यौवनम् Gīt. 7; जगता वा विफलेन किं फलम् R. G.; Śi. 9. 6;<BR> Ku. 7. 66; Me. 70.<BR>—2 Idle,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">Page1454-1</a>]<BR> unmeaning.<BR>—3 Having no testicles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफला
विफल + .{@-ला@} N. of a plant (केतकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलम्
विफल + .{@-लम्@} Fruitlessness, unprofitableness; नावमः कर्मकल्पोऽपि<BR> विफलायेश्वरार्पितः Bhāg. 8. 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1453-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीकृ
विफलीकृ €8 U. To frustrate, defeat, foil, render fruitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभू
विफलीभू €1 P. To become useless or unprofitable, be foiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्ध्|विबंध्
विबन्ध् €9 P.<BR>—1 To bind or fasten (on different sides).<BR>—2 To stretch out, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबद्ध
विबद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fastened, tied.<BR>—2 Obstructed, stopped.<BR>—3 Constipated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्धः|विबन्ध|विबंध|विबंधः
विबन्धः<BR>—1 Constipation.<BR>—2 Obstruction.<BR>—3 Encircling, a circular bandage; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबन्धु
विबन्धु <i>a.</i> Having no relations; भ्रातुर्यविष्ठस्य सुतान् विबन्धून्<BR> प्रवेश्य लाक्षाभवने ददाह Bhāg. 3. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाध्
विबाध् See बाध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाधा
विबाधा Pain, anguish, torment, agony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध्
विबुध् €1 P., €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To wake up, awake; निमील्य नेत्रे सहसा व्यबुध्यत Ku. 5. 57.<BR>—2 To become conscious.<BR>—3 To observe, perceive; find out. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To awaken, rouse.<BR>—2 To restore to consciousness; अथ मोहपरायणा सती विवशा कामवधूर्विवोधिता Ku. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुद्ध
विबुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Aroused, awakened, wide awake; Ś. 2.<BR>—2 Expanded, blossomed, full-blown; महाबलः कमलविबुद्धलोचनः<BR> Mb. 7. 155. 43.<BR>—3 Clever, skilful; अन्यथा प्रतिपन्नास्ते विबुद्धाः स्वेषु कर्मसु Mb. 14. 36. 29.<BR>—4 Unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधः|विबुध
विबुधः<BR>—1 A wise or learned man, sage; सख्यं साप्तपदीनं भो इत्याहुर्विबुधा<BR> जनाः Pt. 2. 47.<BR>—2 A god, deity; अभून्नृपो विबुधसखः परंतपः Bk. 1. 1; गोप्तारं<BR> न निधीनां महयन्ति महेश्वरं विबुधाः Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विबुधाधिपतिः, विबुधेन्द्रः, विबुधेश्वरः, विबुधानुचरः, विबुधावासः, विबुधेतरः, विबुधगुरुः, विबुधतटिनी, विबुधद्विष्, विबुधशत्रुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधाधिपतिः|विबुधाधिपति
विबुधः + -अधिपतिः, -इन्द्रः, -ईश्वरः epithets of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधेन्द्रः|विबुधेन्द्र
विबुधः + -अधिपतिः, -इन्द्रः, -ईश्वरः epithets of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधेश्वरः|विबुधेश्वर
विबुधः + -अधिपतिः, -इन्द्रः, -ईश्वरः epithets of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधानुचरः|विबुधानुचर
विबुधः + -अनुचरः a godʼs attendant; Ms. 11. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधावासः|विबुधावास
विबुधः + -आवासः a temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधेतरः|विबुधेतर
विबुधः + -इतरः a demon<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधगुरुः|विबुधगुरु
विबुधः + -गुरुः Brihaspati or the planet Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधतटिनी
विबुधः + -तटिनी the Gaṅgā river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधद्विष्
विबुधः + -द्विष्, -शत्रुः a demon; बन्दीकृता Vइबुधशत्रुभिरर्धमार्गे V. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधशत्रुः|विबुधशत्रु
विबुधः + -द्विष्, -शत्रुः a demon; बन्दीकृता Vइबुधशत्रुभिरर्धमार्गे V. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधानः|विबुधान
विबुधानः<BR>—1 A learned man.<BR>—2 A teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोधः|विबोध
विबोधः<BR>—1 Awakening, being awake.<BR>—2 Perceiving, discovering.<BR>—3 Intelligence.<BR>—4 Awaking, becoming conscious, one of the 33 or 34 subordinate feelings<BR> (or व्यभिचारिभाव) in Rhetoric; निद्रानाशोत्तरं जायमानो बोधो विबोधः R. G.<BR>—5 Inattention, absence of mind.<BR>—6 (In drama) The unfolding of the faculties in carrying out an object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुभूषा
विबुभूषा The wish to manifest oneʼs self; एकैकस्यां दशदश प्रकृतेर्विबुभूषया<BR> Bhāg. 3. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्बोकः|विब्बोक
विब्बोकः See बिब्बोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्रू
विब्रू €2 U.<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To speak of or about.<BR>—3 To speak falsely or wrongly; अब्रुवन् विब्रुवन् वापि नरो भवति किल्बिषी Ms. 8. 13.<BR>—4 To explain, expound, interpret; न विब्रूयान्नृपो धर्मं चिकीर्षन् हितमात्मनः Ms. 8. 390.<BR>—5 To quarrel, dispute, contend about.<BR>—6 To disagree with, contradict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्
विभज्<BR>—1 U. 1 To divide, distribute; विभज्य मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः N. 1. 16;<BR> पत्रिणां व्यभजदाश्रमाद्बहिः R. 11. 29, 10. 54; वपुर्विभक्तावयवं<BR> पुमानिति Śi. 1. 3; संध्यामङ्गलदीपिका विभजते शुद्धान्तवृद्धो जनः<BR> V. 3. 2 ‘distributes or places’.<BR>—2 To divide (as property, patrimony &c.); विभक्ता भ्रातरः ‘divided brothers’.<BR>—3 To distinguish, discriminate.<BR>—4 To honour, worship.<BR>—5 To separate from; विभक्तरक्षःसंबाधम् Rām. 5. 53. 37.<BR>—6 To open (a box or chest).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्त|विभक्तः
विभक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Divided, partitioned (as property &c.).<BR>—2 Divided, separated in interest, as in विभक्ता भ्रातरः; विभक्ताः<BR> सहजीवन्तो विभजेरन् पुनर्यदि Ms. 9. 210.<BR>—3 Parted, separated, made distinct; Śi. 1. 3; वायवीयैर्विगण्यन्ते<BR> विभक्ताः परमाणवः Y. 3. 104.<BR>—4 Different, multifarious.<BR>—5 Retired, secluded.<BR>—6 Regular, symmetrical.<BR>—7 Ornamented.<BR>—8 Measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तः|विभक्त
विभक्त + .{@-क्तः@} N. of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तम्
विभक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 Solitude, retirement.<BR>—2 A share.<BR>—3 Property (divided).<BR>—4 Separation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विभक्तजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तजः|विभक्तज
विभक्त + -जः a son born after partition of the family-property (between<BR> his parents and brothers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तिः|विभक्ति
विभक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Separation, division, partition, apportionment; कालं कालविभक्तीश्च<BR> Ms. 1. 24; कथं सृष्टानि भूतानि कथं वर्णविभक्तयः Mb. 12. 182. 3;<BR> कशापातेषु दृश्यन्ते नानावर्णविभक्तयः Pañc. 2. 4.<BR>—2 Division, separation in interest.<BR>—3 A portion or share of inheritance.<BR>—4 (In gram.) Inflection of nouns, a case or case-termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्य
विभज्य <i>ind.</i> By dividing, distinguishing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विभज्यपाठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्यपाठः|विभज्यपाठ
विभज्य + -पाठः the distinct pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभञ्ज्|विभंज्
विभञ्ज् €7 P. To break asunder, break to pieces, shatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्गः|विभङ्ग|विभंग|विभंगः
विभङ्गः<BR>—1 Breaking, fracture.<BR>—2 Stopping, obstruction, stoppage; तृष्णास्रोतोविभङ्गः Bh. 2. 26.<BR>—3 Bending, contraction (as of the eyebrows); भ्रूविभङ्गकुटिलं च वीक्षितम् R. 19. 17.<BR>—4 A fold, wrinkle; बलीविभङ्गचतुरं स्तनभारविनामितम् Mb. 4. 14. 22.<BR>—5 A step, stair; शिलाविभङ्गैर्मृगराजशावस्तुङ्गं नगोत्सङ्गमिवारुरोह R. 6. 3.<BR>—6 Breaking out, manifestation; विविधविकारविभङ्गम् Gīt. 11<BR>—7 Division; मसारगल्वर्कमयैर्विभङ्गैर्विभूषितं हेमनिबद्धचक्रम्<BR> Mb. 12. 46. 33.<BR>—8 A wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्गिः|विभङ्गि
विभङ्गिः Mere appearance or resemblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभङ्गुर
विभङ्गुर <i>a.</i> Unsteady (as a look).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभवः|विभव
विभवः<BR>—1 Wealth, riches, property; अतनुषु विभवेषु ज्ञातयः सन्तु नाम<BR> Ś. 5. 8; R. 8. 69.<BR>—2 Might, power, prowess, greatness; एतावान् मम मतिविभवः V. 2;<BR> वाग्विभवः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">Page1455-1</a>]<BR> Māl. 1. 26; R. 1. 9; Ki. 5. 21; विभवाद्वा प्रदीपवत् MS. 11. 1. 59.<BR>—3 Exalted position, rank, dignity.<BR>—4 Magnanimity.<BR>—5 Final beatitude, absolution; स भवान् सर्वलोकस्य भवाय विभवाय<BR> च अवतीर्णोऽशभागेन Bhāg. 10. 10. 35.<BR>—6 Protection (पालन); नियन्ता जन्तूनां निखिलजगदुत्पादविभवप्रतिक्षेपैः<BR> क्रीडन् Viś. Guṇā. 198.<BR>—7 Development; evolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1454-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा €2 P.<BR>—1 To shine; पयसा कमलेन विभाति सरः Bh. 2. 71.<BR>—2 To seem, appear.<BR>—3 To become visible, come to light.<BR>—4 To dawn; सुखमिव सा विबभौ विभावरी Rām. 1. 22. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा<BR>—1 Light, lustre.<BR>—2 A ray of light.<BR>—3 Beauty, splendour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विभानुगा, विभाकरः, विभावसुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभानुगा
विभा + -अनुगा shadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाकरः|विभाकर
विभा + -करः<BR>—1 the sun; बत बत लसत्तेजःपुञ्जो विभाति विभाकरः K. P. 10.<BR>—2 the <i>arka</i> plant.<BR>—3 the moon.<BR>—4 fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावसुः|विभावसु
विभा + -वसुः<BR>—1 the sun.<BR>—2 fire; रचयिष्यामि तनुं विभावसौ Ku. 4. 34; R. 3. 37, 10. 82; तेजश्चास्मि<BR> विभावसौ Bg. 7. 9.<BR>—3 the moon.<BR>—4 a kind of necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभातम्
विभातम्, -ती<BR> Day-break, dawn; भ्रमर इव विभाते कुन्दमन्तस्तुषारम् Ś. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाती
विभातम्, -ती<BR> Day-break, dawn; भ्रमर इव विभाते कुन्दमन्तस्तुषारम् Ś. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागः|विभाग
विभागः<BR>—1 Division, partition, apportionment (as of inheritance); समस्तत्र<BR> विभागः स्यात् Ms. 9. 120, 210; Y. 2. 114.<BR>—2 The share of an inheritance.<BR>—3 A part or share in general.<BR>—4 Division, separation, disjunction (regarded in Nyāya phil. as a Guṇa);<BR> Ku. 2. 4; तत्त्ववित्तु महाबाहो गुणकर्मविभागयोः Bg. 3. 28.<BR>—5 The numerator of a fraction.<BR>—6 A section.<BR>—7 Arrangement.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विभागकल्पना, विभागभावना, विभागधर्मः, विभागपत्रिका, विभागभाज्, विभागरेखा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागकल्पना
विभागः + -कल्पना, -भावना allotment of shares; विभागभावना ज्ञेया गृहक्षेत्रैश्च<BR> यौतकैः Y. 2. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागभावना
विभागः + -कल्पना, -भावना allotment of shares; विभागभावना ज्ञेया गृहक्षेत्रैश्च<BR> यौतकैः Y. 2. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागधर्मः|विभागधर्म
विभागः + -धर्मः the law of inheritance; Ms. 1. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागपत्रिका
विभागः + -पत्रिका a deed of partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागभाज्
विभागः + -भाज् <i>m.</i> one who shares in a property already distributed;<BR> विभक्तेषु सुतो जातः सवर्णायां विभागभाक् Y. 2. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागरेखा
विभागः + -रेखा partition-line, boundary between.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागतः
विभागतः <i>ind.</i> Proportionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागशः
विभागशः <i>ind.</i> Part by part, share by share, proportionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाजनम्
विभाजनम् Dividing, distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाज्य|विभाज्यं
विभाज्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Portionable, to be divided; वस्त्रं पत्रमलंकारं कृतान्नमुदकं<BR> स्त्रियः । योगक्षेमं प्रचारं च न विभाज्यं प्रचक्षते ॥ Ms. 9. 219.<BR>—2 Divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाण्डिका
विभाण्डिका, विभाण्डी The Senna plant (Mar. भुईतरवड, सोनामुखी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाण्डी
विभाण्डिका, विभाण्डी The Senna plant (Mar. भुईतरवड, सोनामुखी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावर
विभावर <i>a.</i> Brilliant, shining; विभावरीं सर्वभूतप्रतिष्ठां<BR> गङ्गां गता ये त्रिदिवं गतास्ते Mb. 13. 26. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावरी
विभावरी<BR>—1 Night; अपर्वणि ग्रहकलुषेन्दुमण्डला विभावरी कथय कथं भविष्यति<BR> M. 4. 15, 5. 7; Ku. 5. 44.<BR>—2 Turmeric.<BR>—3 A bawd.<BR>—4 A harlot.<BR>—5 A perverse woman.<BR>—6 A talkative woman (मुखरस्त्री); यशस्विनी मन्युमती कुले जाता<BR> विभावरी Mb. 5. 133. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाष्
विभाष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To lay down as an optional rule.<BR>—2 To abuse, revile, defame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषा
विभाषा<BR>—1 An option, alternative.<BR>—2 Optionality of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभास्
विभास् <i>f.</i> Brightness, splendour; सोर्मिविद्रुमवितानविभासा रञ्जितस्य<BR> जलधेः श्रियमूहे Ki. 9. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासा
विभासा Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्
विभिद् €7 U.<BR>—1 To break, tear down.<BR>—2 To pierce, penetrate.<BR>—3 To divide, separate.<BR>—4 To interrupt.<BR>—5 To scatter, unbind, disperse.<BR>—6 To loosen, untie.<BR>—7 To alienate, estrange.<BR>—8 To infringe, violate. ━<i>Pass.</i> To change, become changed. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To divide, separate.<BR>—2 To alienate, estrange.<BR>—3 To dispel, remove, drive away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिदा
विभिदा Division (भेद); विभिदामनयन्त कृत्यपक्षम् Śi. 20. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्न|विभिन्नः
विभिन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Broken asunder, divided, split.<BR>—2 Pierced, wounded.<BR>—3 Dispelled, driven away, dispersed.<BR>—4 Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>—5 Moved to and fro.<BR>—6 Disappointed.<BR>—7 Different, various.<BR>—8 Mixed, blended, variegated; विभिन्नवर्णा गरुडाग्रजेन सूर्यस्य रथ्याः<BR> परितः स्फुरन्त्या Śi. 4. 14.<BR>—9 Manifested, displayed.<BR>—10 Become faithless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्नः|विभिन्न
विभिन्न + .{@-न्नः@} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेदः|विभेद
विभेदः<BR>—1 Breaking asunder, dividing.<BR>—2 Division, separation.<BR>—3 Wounding.<BR>—4 Perplexing, bewildering.<BR>—5 Contradiction.<BR>—6 Enmity, opposition.<BR>—7 Variety, distinction.<BR>—8 Knitting, contraction (of the brows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभी
विभी <i>a.</i> Fearless; बिभीर्जप्यपरो मौनी वैराग्यं समुपाश्रितः<BR> Mb. 12. 278. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतः|विभीत|विभीतं
विभीतः, -तम्, विभीतकः, -कम्, विभीतकी, विभीता<BR> N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR> Belerica, one of the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतम्
विभीतः, -तम्, विभीतकः, -कम्, विभीतकी, विभीता<BR> N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR> Belerica, one of the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतकः|विभीतक|विभीतकं
विभीतः, -तम्, विभीतकः, -कम्, विभीतकी, विभीता<BR> N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR> Belerica, one of the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतकम्
विभीतः, -तम्, विभीतकः, -कम्, विभीतकी, विभीता<BR> N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR> Belerica, one of the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतकी
विभीतः, -तम्, विभीतकः, -कम्, विभीतकी, विभीता<BR> N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR> Belerica, one of the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीता
विभीतः, -तम्, विभीतकः, -कम्, विभीतकी, विभीता<BR> N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR> Belerica, one of the three myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषक
विभीषक <i>a.</i> Frightening, terrifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषा
विभीषा The wish of terrifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषिका
विभीषिका<BR>—1 Terror.<BR>—2 A means of terrifying, a scare (a scare-crow); नालं युद्धाय वै रक्षो<BR> महतीयं विभीषिका Rām. 6. 66. 6; यदि ते सन्ति सन्त्वेव केयमन्या<BR> विभीषिका U. 4. 28. [The etymology of this word as pointed out by Nārāyaṇa<BR> in his commentary on this word is apparently wrong. The correct word appears<BR> to be विभीषिका and not बिभीषिका for विभीषिकाशब्दस्य भीषिधातोर्ण्वुल्प्रत्ययनिष्पन्नत्वादन्तस्थवकारादित्वमेव<BR> समीचीनम् Mañjūṣā.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभु|विभुः
विभु <i>a.</i> (-भू, -भ्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Mighty, powerful.<BR>—2 Eminent, supreme.<BR>—3 Able to, capable of (with inf.); (धनुः) पूरयितुं भवन्ति विभवः<BR> शिखरमणिरुचः Ki. 5. 43.<BR>—4 Self-subdued, firm, self-controlled; कमपरमवशं न विप्रकुर्युर्विभुमपि<BR> तं यदमी स्पृशन्ति भावाः Ku. 6. 95.<BR>—5 (In Nyāya phil.) Eternal, existing everywhere, all-pervading, pervading<BR> all material things; सर्वमूर्तद्रव्यसंयोगित्वं विभुत्वम्.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">Page1456-1</a>]<BR>—6 Firm, hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुः|विभु
विभु + .{@-भुः@}<BR>—1 Ether.<BR>—2 Space.<BR>—3 Time.<BR>—4 The soul.<BR>—5 A lord, ruler, master, sovereign, king.<BR>—6 The supreme ruler; नादत्ते कस्यचित् पापं न चैव सुकृतं विभुः<BR> Bg. 5. 15, 10. 12; प्रकृतेर्विभुत्वयोगात् Sāṅ. K. 42.<BR>—7 A servant.<BR>—8 N. of Brahman.<BR>—9 Of Śiva; विभुमपि तं यदमी स्पृशन्ति भावाः Ku. 6. 95, 7. 31; Mu. 1. 1.<BR>—10 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1455-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुता
विभुता Power, supremacy, glory; विभुतानुषङ्गि भयमेति जनः Ki. 6. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभुग्न
विभुग्न <i>a.</i> Bent, curved; शयिता चापविभुग्नगात्रयष्टिः Bu. C. 5. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभू
विभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To appear, become manifest.<BR>—2 To be equal to, suffice for; एकमेव तदेकं सन्न व्यभवत् Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 11;<BR> Bhāg. 5. 1. 12.<BR>—3 To pervade; आत्मन्यदृच्छया प्राप्तं विबुभूषुरुपाददे Bhāg. 2. 5. 21.<BR>—4 To be able, be capable of, prevail. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To think of, reflect, contemplate.<BR>—2 To be aware of, know, perceive, discover, see; तामिन्दुसुन्दरमुखीं<BR> सुचिरं विभाव्य Māl. 1. 18, 5. 21; न विभाव्यन्ते लघवो वित्तविहीनाः<BR> पुरोऽपि निवसन्तः Pt. 5. 7; U. 2. 24.<BR>—3 To see or observe minutely, perceive carefully; V. 4.<BR>—4 To decide, settle, make clear.<BR>—5 To manifest, show, reveal; यशः परं जगति विभाव्य वर्तिता Mb. 7. 2. 15.<BR>—5 To separate.<BR>—6 To suppose, imagine.<BR>—7 To convince.<BR>—8 To establish, prove; तव सुचरितमङ्गुलीय नूनं प्रतनु ममेव<BR> विभाव्यते फलेन Ś. 6. 11.<BR>—9 To protect; लोकान् विभावयसि हंसि जगत्प्रतीपान् Bhāg. 7. 9. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावः|विभाव
विभावः<BR>—1 (In Rhet.) Any condition which produces or develops a particular state<BR> of body or mind; (one of the three main divisions of <i>Bhāvas</i>, the<BR> other two being अनुभाव and व्यभिचारिभाव qq. vv.); रत्याद्युद्बोधका<BR> लोके विभावाः काव्यनाट्ययोः S. D. 62; its chief subdivisions are आलम्बन<BR> and उद्दीपक; see आलम्बन.<BR>—2 A friend, an acquaintance.<BR>—3 Any exciting circumstance (as dress &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावक
विभावक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Manifesting, showing.<BR>—2 Discussing.<BR>—3 Procuring; त्वरमाणोऽभिनिर्यातु विप्रेभ्योऽर्थविभावकः Mb. 3. 33. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावनम्
विभावनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Clear perception or ascertainment, discrimination, judgment.<BR>—2 Discussion, investigation, examination.<BR>—3 Conception, imagination; यदन्यदन्यत्र विभाव्यते भ्रमात् A. Rām. 7. 5. 37.<BR>—4 Development.<BR>—5 Protection (पालन); यस्याङ्घ्रिपद्मं परिचर्य विश्वविभावनायात्तगुणाभिपत्तेः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 8. 20.<BR>—6 Looking, sight (दर्शन); पश्चिमां तु समासीनः सम्यगृक्षविभावनात् Ms. 2. 101.<BR>—7 Showing, manifesting; Ms. 9. 76 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावना
विभावनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Clear perception or ascertainment, discrimination, judgment.<BR>—2 Discussion, investigation, examination.<BR>—3 Conception, imagination; यदन्यदन्यत्र विभाव्यते भ्रमात् A. Rām. 7. 5. 37.<BR>—4 Development.<BR>—5 Protection (पालन); यस्याङ्घ्रिपद्मं परिचर्य विश्वविभावनायात्तगुणाभिपत्तेः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 8. 20.<BR>—6 Looking, sight (दर्शन); पश्चिमां तु समासीनः सम्यगृक्षविभावनात् Ms. 2. 101.<BR>—7 Showing, manifesting; Ms. 9. 76 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावना
विभावनम्, -ना + .{@-ना@} (In Rhet.) A figure of speech in which effects are represented<BR> as taking place though their usual causes are absent; क्रियायाः प्रतिषेधेऽपि<BR> फलव्यक्तिर्विभावना K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावित|विभावितः
विभावित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Manifested, made clearly visible.<BR>—2 Known, understood, ascertained; ततः शरीरीति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">Page1456-2</a>]<BR> विभाविताकृतिम् Śi. 1. 3.<BR>—3 Seen, conceived; अविभावितनिष्क्रमप्रयाणः Ki. 13. 27.<BR>—4 Judged, discriminated.<BR>—5 Inferred, indicated.<BR>—6 Proved, established.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विभावितैकदेश<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावितैकदेश
विभावित + -एकदेश <i>a.</i> ‘with whom a part has been discovered’, who has<BR> been found guilty with regard to a part (of what is in dispute); विभावितैकदेशेन<BR> देयं यदभियुज्यते V. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाव्य
विभाव्य <i>a.</i> Comprehensible; महतां हि धैर्यमविभाव्यवैभवम् Ki. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूत
विभूत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Arisen, produced.<BR>—2 Appeared, manifested.<BR>—3 Great, mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूतिः|विभूति
विभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Might, power, greatness; सा बिभूतिरनुभावसंपदां भूयसी तव<BR> Śi. 14. 5; Ku. 2. 61.<BR>—2 Prosperity, welfare; अघोपघातं मघवा विभूत्यै भवोद्भवाराधनमादिदेश Ki. 11. 80.<BR>—3 Dignity, exalted rank.<BR>—4 Riches, plenty, magnificence, splendour; ममैष कामो भूतानां यद्<BR> भूयासुर्विभूतयः Bhāg. 6. 4. 44; अहो राजाधिराजमन्त्रिणो विभूतिः<BR> Mu. 3; R. 8. 36.<BR>—5 Wealth, riches; (लोकान्) त्रीनत्यरोच उपलभ्य ततो विभूतिम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 16. 34; विभूतयस्तदीयानां पर्यस्ता यशसामिव R. 4. 19, 6. 76, 17. 43.<BR>—6 Superhuman power (which consists of eight faculties, अणिमन्, लघिमन्,<BR> प्राप्ति, प्राकाम्य, महिमन्, ईशिता, वशिता and कामावसायिता); Ku. 2. 11.<BR>—7 Ashes of cow-dung.<BR>—8 N. of Lakṣmī; हित्वेतरान् प्रार्थयतो विभूतिर्यस्याङ्घ्रिरेणुं जुषतेऽनभीप्सोः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 18. 20.<BR>—9 Expansion (विस्तार); एतां विभूतिं योगं च मम यो वेत्ति तत्त्वतः Bg. 10. 7.<BR>—10 Disposition; क्षेत्रज्ञ एता मनसो विभूतीर्जीवस्य मायारचितस्य नित्याः<BR> Bhāg. 5. 11. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूरसिः|विभूरसि
विभूरसिः The god of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूष्
विभूष् €10 U.<BR>—1 To adorn, decorate; केयूरा न विभूषयन्ति पुरुषम् Bh. 2. 19; Śi. 9. 33;<BR> Ku. 1. 28.<BR>—2 Ved. To shine forth, appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषणम्
विभूषणम् Ornament, decoration; विशेषतः सर्वविदां समाजे विभूषणं<BR> मौनमपण्डितानाम् Bh. 2. 7; R. 16. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषा
विभूषा<BR>—1 Ornament, decoration; संपेदे श्रमसलिलोद्गमो बिभूषा Ki. 7. 5; R. 4. 54.<BR>—2 Light, lustre.<BR>—3 Beauty, splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषित|विभूषितः
विभूषित <i>p. p.</i> Adorned, decorated, ornamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषितम्
विभूषित + .{@-तम्@} An ornament, decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत|विभृतः
विभृत <i>p. p.</i> Upheld, supported, maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंश्
विभ्रंश् €1 Ā., €4 P.<BR>—1 To drop or fall down.<BR>—2 To go to ruin, decay.<BR>—3 To fall, stray from, go astray.<BR>—4 To lose.<BR>—5 To disappear, vanish.<BR>—6 To fail. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To strike off, knock down.<BR>—2 To lead astray, seduce.<BR>—3 To destroy, ruin, annihilate.<BR>—4 To deprive (one) of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशः|विभ्रंश
विभ्रंशः<BR>—1 Falling away or off; slipping; अशर्करामविभ्रंशां समतीर्थामशैवलाम्<BR> Rām. 3. 73. 11.<BR>—2 Decay, decline, ruin.<BR>—3 A precipice; राज्यं चाप्युग्रविभ्रंशं संशयो जीवितस्य वा Mb. 5. 134. 28.<BR>—4 Diarrhoea, laxity of the bowels.<BR>—5 Perturbation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1456-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशित
विभ्रंशित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Led astray, seduced.<BR>—2 Deprived of.<BR>—3 Destroyed, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रष्ट
विभ्रष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fallen off or away, separated.<BR>—2 Decayed, lost, fallen, ruined.<BR>—3 Disappeared, vanished.<BR>—4 Deprived or devoid of.<BR>—5 Useless.<BR>—6 Vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम्
विभ्रम् €1. €4 P.<BR>—1 To roam, wander about.<BR>—2 To hover, whirl or wheel round.<BR>—3 To scare away, disperse, scatter about.<BR>—4 To be confused or disordered, be bewildered or perplexed; अनेकचित्तविभ्रान्ता<BR> मोहजालसमावृताः Bg. 16. 16.<BR>—5 To move about (the tail). ━<i>Caus.</i> To confuse, confound; प्रभामत्तश्चन्द्रो<BR> जगदिदमहो विभ्रमयति K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रमः|विभ्रम
विभ्रमः<BR>—1 Roaming or wandering about.<BR>—2 Whirling or going round, rolling about; निवृत्तसर्वेन्द्रियवृत्तिविभ्रमः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 9. 31.<BR>—3 Error, mistake, blunder.<BR>—4 Hurry, confusion, flurry, perturbation; especially, the flurry of mind<BR> caused by love; चित्तवृत्त्यनवस्थानं शृङ्गाराद्विभ्रमो भवेत्.<BR>—5 (Hence) Putting on ornaments &c. in wrong places through flurry; विभ्रमस्त्वरयाऽकाले<BR> भूषास्थानविपर्ययः; यश्चाप्सरोविभ्रममण्डनानां संपादयित्रीं शिखरैर्बिभर्ति<BR> Ku. 1. 4; (see Malli. thereon).<BR>—6 Any amorous or sportive action, amorous play or movement; Māl. 1. 26;<BR> नवप्रणयविभ्रमाकुलितमालतीदृष्टयः 9. 38.<BR>—7 Beauty, grace, charm; तदा तदङ्गस्य बिभर्ति विभ्रमम् N. 15. 25;<BR> U. 1. 20, 34, 6. 4; Śi. 6. 46, 7. 15, 16. 64; Māl. 7; क्रोधं स्मितं<BR> च कुसुमाभरणादि याच्ञा -तद्वर्जनं च सहसैव विमण्डनं च । आक्षिप्य<BR> कान्तवचनं लपनं सखीभिर्निष्कारणोत्थितगतं वद विभ्रमं तत् ॥<BR>—8 Doubt, apprehension; आमुक्तमिव पाखण्डं योऽधर्मे धर्मविभ्रमः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 19. 12.<BR>—9 Caprice, whim.<BR>—10 Disturbance, perturbation; ऊर्मिव्यतिकरविभ्रमप्रचण्डः Mv. 6. 26.<BR>—11 Pride; दीर्घमायुः स मे प्रादात्ततो मां विभ्रमोऽस्पृशत् Rām. 3. 71. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रमा
विभ्रमा Old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्त|विभ्रांत|विभ्रान्तः
विभ्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Whirled about.<BR>—2 Agitated, bewildered, confused, flurried.<BR>—3 Mistaken, erring.<BR>—4 Spread abroad (as fame).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विभ्रान्तनयन, विभ्रान्तशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्तनयन
विभ्रान्त + -नयन <i>a.</i> with rolling eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्तशील|विभ्रांतशील|विभ्रान्तशीलः
विभ्रान्त + -शील <i>a.</i><BR>—1 confused in mind.<BR>—2 intoxicated, drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्तशीलः|विभ्रान्तशील|विभ्रांतशील
विभ्रान्त + -शील + .({@-लः@})<BR>—1 a monkey.<BR>—2 the disc of the sun or moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रान्तिः|विभ्रान्ति|विभ्रांति|विभ्रांतिः
विभ्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Whirling, going round.<BR>—2 Flurry, error, confusion.<BR>—3 Hurry, precipitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् €1 Ā. To shine brilliantly or intensely; विभ्राजसे मकरकेतनमर्चयन्ती Ratn. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् <i>a.</i> Shining, splendid, bright, luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्सर
विमत्सर <i>a.</i> Free from jealousy, unenvious; Bg. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमथ्
विमथ्, -विमन्थ् €9 P.<BR>—1 To disperse, scatter.<BR>—2 To destroy, annihilate.<BR>—3 To confound, confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्थ्|विमंथ्
विमथ्, -विमन्थ् €9 P.<BR>—1 To disperse, scatter.<BR>—2 To destroy, annihilate.<BR>—3 To confound, confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमाथः|विमाथ
विमाथः Utter ruin or destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद्
विमद् €4 P.<BR>—1 To become perplexed or confused.<BR>—2 To be intoxicated or mad. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To confound, perplex.<BR>—2 To intoxicate, madden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्त
विमत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Intoxicated.<BR>—2 Ruttish; furious, in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद
विमद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from intoxication, pride or arrogance; यो बलात् प्रोन्नतं याति<BR> निहन्तुं सबलोऽप्यरिः । विमदः स निवर्तेत Pt. 1. 238.<BR>—2 Devoid of joy, sad, cheerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद्य
विमद्य <i>a.</i> Free from intoxicating drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्
विमन् <i>Caus.</i> To disrespect, dishonour, insult; त्वया नाम<BR> मुनिर्विमान्यः Ś. 5. 20; स्त्रीभिर्विमानितानां कापुरुषाणां विवर्धते<BR> मदनः Mk. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत|विमतः
विमत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Disagreeing, dissenting, differing in opinion.<BR>—2 At variance, inconsistent.<BR>—3 Slighted, despised, neglected; जहावसून् यद्विमतात्मजा सती मनस्विनी<BR> मानमभीक्ष्णमर्हति Bhāg. 4. 4. 29.<BR>—4 Dubious, doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमतः|विमत
विमत + .{@-तः@} An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमति|विमतिः
विमति <i>a.</i> Stupid, devoid of intelligence, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमतिः|विमति
विमति + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Dissent, disagreement, difference of opinion.<BR>—2 Dislike.<BR>—3 Stupidity.<BR>—4 A dispute; विधिं कलापौ विमतेरगाताम् N. 7. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमान|विमानं|विमानः
विमान <i>a.</i> Disgraced, devoid of honour; तन्मक्षिकाभिर्व्यथितो<BR> विमानः Bhāg. 5. 13. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानः|विमान|विमानं
विमानः, -नम्<BR>—1 Disrespect, dishonour; आक्रोशनविमानाभ्यां नाबुधान् बोधयेद् बुधः<BR> Mb. 12. 299. 25; Bhāg. 5. 10. 25.<BR>—2 A measure.<BR>—3 A balloon, a heavenly car (moving through the skies); पदं विमानेन<BR> विगाहमानः R. 13. 1, 7. 51; विमानीकृतराजहंसमण्डलः K.; R. 12. 104;<BR> Ku. 2. 45, 7. 40; V. 4. 43; Ki. 7. 11; विगते दिवसे ततो विमानं<BR> वपुषा सूर्य इव प्रदीप्यमानः (आरुरोह) Bu. C. 5. 43.<BR>—4 A vehicle or conveyance in general; स नौविमानादवतीर्य रेमे R. 16. 68.<BR>—5 A palace (with seven stories); ‘विमानोऽस्त्री देवयाने सप्तभूमौ च सद्मनि’ इति निघण्टुः;<BR> ‘विमानो व्योमयाने च सार्वभौमगृहेऽपि च’ इति मेदिनी;<BR> Rām. 1. 5. 16; नेत्रा नीताः सततगतिना यद्विमानाग्रभूमीः Me. 71.<BR>—7 A horse.<BR>—8 An open palanquin carried on menʼs shoulders; इमां विमानेन सभां<BR> विशन्तीं पपावपाङ्गैरथ राजराजिः N. 10. 107.<BR>—9 A ship, boat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमानगामिन्, विमानचारिन्, विमानयान, विमानराजः, विमानवाहः, विमानधुर्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानम्
विमानः, -नम्<BR>—1 Disrespect, dishonour; आक्रोशनविमानाभ्यां नाबुधान् बोधयेद् बुधः<BR> Mb. 12. 299. 25; Bhāg. 5. 10. 25.<BR>—2 A measure.<BR>—3 A balloon, a heavenly car (moving through the skies); पदं विमानेन<BR> विगाहमानः R. 13. 1, 7. 51; विमानीकृतराजहंसमण्डलः K.; R. 12. 104;<BR> Ku. 2. 45, 7. 40; V. 4. 43; Ki. 7. 11; विगते दिवसे ततो विमानं<BR> वपुषा सूर्य इव प्रदीप्यमानः (आरुरोह) Bu. C. 5. 43.<BR>—4 A vehicle or conveyance in general; स नौविमानादवतीर्य रेमे R. 16. 68.<BR>—5 A palace (with seven stories); ‘विमानोऽस्त्री देवयाने सप्तभूमौ च सद्मनि’ इति निघण्टुः;<BR> ‘विमानो व्योमयाने च सार्वभौमगृहेऽपि च’ इति मेदिनी;<BR> Rām. 1. 5. 16; नेत्रा नीताः सततगतिना यद्विमानाग्रभूमीः Me. 71.<BR>—7 A horse.<BR>—8 An open palanquin carried on menʼs shoulders; इमां विमानेन सभां<BR> विशन्तीं पपावपाङ्गैरथ राजराजिः N. 10. 107.<BR>—9 A ship, boat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमानगामिन्, विमानचारिन्, विमानयान, विमानराजः, विमानवाहः, विमानधुर्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानगामिन्
विमानः + -गामिन् a god; भयान्विता नभसि विमानगामिनः Mb. 1. 23. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानचारिन्
विमानः + -चारिन्, -यान <i>a.</i> moving in a balloon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानयान
विमानः + -चारिन्, -यान <i>a.</i> moving in a balloon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानराजः|विमानराज
विमानः + -राजः<BR>—1 an excellent heavenly car; U. 3.<BR>—2 the driver of a heavenly car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानवाहः
विमानः + -वाहः, -धुर्यः palanquin-bearer; तां राजसङ्घमनयन्त विमानवाहाः<BR> N. 11. 23; तां राजकादपगमप्य विमानधुर्या निन्युर्नलाकृतिधरानथ<BR> पञ्च वीरान् N. 13. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानधुर्यः
विमानः + -वाहः, -धुर्यः palanquin-bearer; तां राजसङ्घमनयन्त विमानवाहाः<BR> N. 11. 23; तां राजकादपगमप्य विमानधुर्या निन्युर्नलाकृतिधरानथ<BR> पञ्च वीरान् N. 13. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमाननम्
विमाननम्, -विमानना<BR>—1 Disrespect, dishonour, contempt, humiliation; विमानना सुभ्रु कुतः<BR> पितुर्गृहे Ku. 5. 43; अभवन्नास्य विमानना क्वचित् R. 8. 8.<BR>—2 Refusal, denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानना
विमाननम्, -विमानना<BR>—1 Disrespect, dishonour, contempt, humiliation; विमानना सुभ्रु कुतः<BR> पितुर्गृहे Ku. 5. 43; अभवन्नास्य विमानना क्वचित् R. 8. 8.<BR>—2 Refusal, denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानित
विमानित <i>p. p.</i> Disrespected, dishonoured; विमानिता विपथगतिं<BR> प्रयान्ति ते Mb. 1. 23. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1457-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्
विमनस्, -विमनस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sad, disconsolate, depressed in mind or spirits, sorry, discomposed;<BR> शिबिस्तथैवाविमना महित्वा कपालमभ्युद्धार्य भोक्तुमैच्छत् Mb. 3. 198. 22;<BR> देव्यास्ततो बिमनसः परिसान्त्वनाय धर्मासनाद्विशति वासगृहं नरेन्द्रः U. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Absent-minded.<BR>—3 Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>—4 Displeased.<BR>—5 Changed in mind or feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्क|विमनस्कः
विमनस्, -विमनस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sad, disconsolate, depressed in mind or spirits, sorry, discomposed;<BR> शिबिस्तथैवाविमना महित्वा कपालमभ्युद्धार्य भोक्तुमैच्छत् Mb. 3. 198. 22;<BR> देव्यास्ततो बिमनसः परिसान्त्वनाय धर्मासनाद्विशति वासगृहं नरेन्द्रः U. 1. 7.<BR>—2 Absent-minded.<BR>—3 Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>—4 Displeased.<BR>—5 Changed in mind or feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीकृत
विमनीकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Displeased.<BR>—2 Changed in mind or feeling.<BR>—3 Sad, discomposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्यु
विमन्यु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from anger.<BR>—2 Free from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमयः|विमय
विमयः Exchange, barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शः|विमर्श
विमर्शः<BR>—1 Thought, deliberation.<BR>—2 (In dramas) A change in the successful progress of a dramatic plot,<BR> a change in the prosperous course of a love-story caused by some unforeseen<BR> reverse or accident, one of the five <i>Sandhis</i> in a drama; it is thus<BR> defined in S. D.; यत्र मुख्यफलोपाय उद्भिन्नो गर्भतोऽधिकः । शापाद्यः<BR> सान्तरायश्च स विमर्श इति स्मृतः ॥ 336; कुर्वन् बुद्ध्या विमर्शं<BR> प्रसृतमपि पुनः संहरन् कार्यजातं कर्ता वा नाटकानामिममनुभवति क्लेशमस्मद्विधो वा Mu. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षः|विमर्ष
विमर्षः<BR>—1 Impatience, non-forbearance.<BR>—2 Dissatisfaction, displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षिन्
विम(र्शि)र्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, intolerant.<BR>—2 Averse, disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शिन्
विम(र्शि)र्षिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impatient, intolerant.<BR>—2 Averse, disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमल|विमलं|विमलः
विमल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Pure, stainless, spotless, clean (fig also).<BR>—2 Clear, limpid, pellucid, transparent (as water); विमलं जलम्.<BR>—3 White, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलः|विमल|विमलं
विमल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 An <i>Arhat</i>.<BR>—2 A magical formula recited over weapons.<BR>—3 A lunar year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलम्
विमल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Silver-gilt.<BR>—2 Talc.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमलाक्ष, विमलाद्रिः, विमलदानम्, विमलमणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलाक्ष
विमल + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> Having ten hair-curlings (आवर्त) (as a horse);<BR> तस्य सर्वगुणोपेता विमलाक्षा हयोत्तमाः Mb. 3. 161. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलाद्रिः|विमलाद्रि
विमल + -अद्रिः the mountain Girnār in Gujarāt (famous for its inscriptions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलदानम्
विमल + -दानम् an offering to a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमलमणिः|विमलमणि
विमल + -मणिः a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांसः|विमांस|विमांसं
विमांसः, -सम्<BR> Unclean meat (as of dogs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांसम्
विमांसः, -सम्<BR> Unclean meat (as of dogs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृ
विमातृ <i>f.</i> A step-mother.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमातृजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृजः|विमातृज
विमातृ + -जः a step-motherʼs son; (Kull. on Ms. 9. 118).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमात्र
विमात्र^1 <i>a.</i> Unequal^2 in measure.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260602. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/207.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260602. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गः|विमार्ग
विमार्गः<BR>—1 A bad road.<BR>—2 A wrong road, evil conduct or course, immorality.<BR>—3 A broom.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमार्गगा, विमार्गगामिन्, विमार्गप्रस्थित, विमार्गदृष्टि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गगा
विमार्गः + -गा an unchaste woman; विमार्गगायाश्च रुचिः स्वकान्ते Bv. 1. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गगामिन्
विमार्गः + -गामिन्, -प्रस्थित <i>a.</i> following evil courses; नियमयसि<BR> विमार्गप्रस्थितानात्तदण्डः Ś. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गप्रस्थित
विमार्गः + -गामिन्, -प्रस्थित <i>a.</i> following evil courses; नियमयसि<BR> विमार्गप्रस्थितानात्तदण्डः Ś. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गदृष्टि
विमार्गः + -दृष्टि <i>a.</i> looking in a wrong direction; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गणम्
विमार्गणम् Searching, looking out for, seeking for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्र
विमिश्र, विमिश्रित <i>a.</i> Mixed, blended, mingled (with instr.<BR> or in comp.); पुंभिर्विमिश्रा नार्यश्च Mb.; दम्पत्योरिह को न को<BR> न तमसि व्रीडाविमिश्रो रसः Gīt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्रित
विमिश्र, विमिश्रित <i>a.</i> Mixed, blended, mingled (with instr.<BR> or in comp.); पुंभिर्विमिश्रा नार्यश्च Mb.; दम्पत्योरिह को न को<BR> न तमसि व्रीडाविमिश्रो रसः Gīt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुख|विमुखः
विमुख <i>a.</i> (-खी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 With the face averted or turned away from.<BR>—2 Averse, disinclined, opposed; न क्षुद्रोऽपि प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया संश्रयाय<BR> प्राप्ते मित्रे भवति विमुखः किं पुनर्यस्तथोच्चैः Me. 17, 27; पुरन्ध्रीणां<BR> प्रज्ञा पुरुषगुणविज्ञानविमुखी Mu. 2. 7; (रघूणां) मनः परस्त्रीविमुखप्रवृत्ति<BR> R. 16. 8, 19. 47.<BR>—3 Adverse; अत्यन्तविमुखे दैवे व्यर्थे यत्ने च पौरुषे H. 1. 111.<BR>—4 Without, devoid of (in comp.); करुणाविमुखेन मृत्युना हरता त्वां<BR> वद किं न मे हृतम् R. 8. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्
विमुच् €6 P.<BR>—1 To free, liberate.<BR>—2 To loosen, unbind, unfasten, untie; ततो विमुक्त्वा सशरं शरासनम्<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 124; आसीद्विवृत्तवदना च विमोचयन्ती (वल्कलम्) Ś. 2. 13.<BR>—3 To give up, lay aside, abandon, quit; विमुच्य रोषं रिपुनिग्रहात्ततः<BR> Rām. 6. 111. 124; विमुच्य वासांसि गुरूणि सांप्रतम् Ṛs. 1. 7.<BR>—4 To let go, let loose; Bk. 7. 50.<BR>—5 To except, set aside, set apart; ननु मां कामवधे विमुञ्चता Ku. 4. 31.<BR>—6 To shed, pour down (tears); चिरमश्रूणि विमुच्य राघवः R. 8. 25.<BR>—7 To throw, cast.<BR>—8 To take off (clothes), undress oneself.<BR>—9 To stop, cease.<BR>—10 To take, assume; समाविशति संसृष्टस्तदा मूर्ति विमुञ्चति Ms. 1. 56.<BR>—11 To utter (a sound).<BR>—12 To lay (eggs). ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be deprived of, be freed from.<BR>—2 To drop, be expelled (as a foetus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्त|विमुक्तः
विमुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Set free, released, liberated.<BR>—2 Abandoned, given up, quitted, left, let loose; वाजिनः स्यन्दने भानोर्विमुक्तप्रग्रहा<BR> इव Bk. 7. 50.<BR>—3 Freed from.<BR>—4 Hurled, discharged; विमुक्तः सर्वपापेभ्यो विष्णुलोकं स गच्छति.<BR>—5 Given vent to.<BR>—6 = युक्त; कुसुमरसविमुक्तं वस्त्रमागुण्ठितेव Rām. 7. 59. 23 (com.).<BR>—7 Launched (as a ship).<BR>—8 Dispassionate.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमुक्तकण्ठ, विमुक्तमौनम्, विमुक्तशाप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्तकण्ठ
विमुक्त + -कण्ठ <i>a.</i> raising a loud cry, weeping bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्तमौनम्
विमुक्त + -मौनम् <i>ind.</i> breaking silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्तशाप
विमुक्त + -शाप <i>a.</i> released from the consequences of a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्तिः|विमुक्ति
विमुक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Release, liberation.<BR>—2 Separation.<BR>—3 Absolution, final liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुद्र|विमुद्रः
विमुद्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unsealed.<BR>—2 Opened, budded, blown (as a flower &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुह्
विमुह् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be confused, bewildered, or perplexed, be embarrassed; एषा ब्राह्मी<BR> स्थितिः पार्थ नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति Bg. 2. 72, 3. 6, 27.<BR>—2 To be foolish or infatuated. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To infatuate, bewilder.<BR>—2 To allure, tempt, seduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुग्ध
विमुग्ध <i>a.</i> Confused, confounded, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढ|विमूढः
विमूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Confounded, bewildered.<BR>—2 Seduced, tempted, beguiled; अप्रतिष्ठो महाबाहो विमूढो ब्रह्मणः पथि Bg. 6. 38.<BR>—3 Stupid.<BR>—4 Wise, learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढः|विमूढ
विमूढ + .{@-ढः@} A kind of divine being.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमूढात्मन्, विमूढसंज्ञ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढात्मन्
विमूढ + -आत्मन्, -संज्ञ <i>a.</i> perplexed, senseless; इद्रियार्थान् विमूढात्मा<BR> मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते Bg. 3. 6, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढसंज्ञ
विमूढ + -आत्मन्, -संज्ञ <i>a.</i> perplexed, senseless; इद्रियार्थान् विमूढात्मा<BR> मिथ्याचारः स उच्यते Bg. 3. 6, 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूर्च्छित
विमूर्च्छित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Full of, engrossed; मयूरकेकाभिरुतं मदान्धालिविमूर्च्छितम् Bhāg. 4. 6. 12.<BR>—2 Thickened, coagulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूर्च्छितम्
विमूर्च्छित + .{@-तम्@} Swoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1458-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूर्त
विमूर्त <i>a.</i> Coagulated, become solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृद्
विमृद् €9 P.<BR>—1 To press, squeeze.<BR>—2 To bruise, crush, pound.<BR>—3 To kill, destroy.<BR>—4 To lay waste, devastate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दः|विमर्द|विमर्द्द|विमर्द्दः
विमर्दः<BR>—1 Pounding, crushing, bruising.<BR>—2 Rubbing together, trituration (as of perfumes), friction; विमर्दसुरभिर्बकुलावलिका<BR> खल्वहम् M. 3; R. 5. 65; कस्तूरिका मृगविमर्दसुगन्धिरेति Śi. 4. 61, 11. 28.<BR>—3 Pressing together (as in embrace).<BR>—4 Spoiling, marring; कुतूहलविमर्दकारिणा परिश्रमेण Mk. 1.<BR>—5 Touch, contact.<BR>—6 Rubbing the person with saffron or other unguents.<BR>—7 War, battle, fight, encounter; विमर्दक्षमां भूमिमवतरावः U. 5, 3. 44.<BR>—8 Destruction, devastation; पुरा जनस्थानविमर्दशङ्की संधाय लङ्काधिपतिः<BR> प्रतस्थे R. 6. 62.<BR>—9 Conjunction of the sun and the moon.<BR>—10 An eclipse.<BR>—11 Weariness, tediousness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विमर्दार्धम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दार्धम्
विमर्दः + -अर्धम् the time from the apparent conjunction to the end of an eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दकः|विमर्दक|विमर्द्दकः
विमर्दकः<BR>—1 Grinding, pounding, bruising.<BR>—2 The trituration of perfumes.<BR>—3 An eclipse.<BR>—4 The conjunction of the sun and the moon.<BR>—5 Destroying.<BR>—6 Cassia Tora (Mar. टाकळा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दनम्
विमर्दनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Pounding, crushing, trampling.<BR>—2 Rubbing together, friction.<BR>—3 Destruction, killing; कौरव्य मह्यां द्विषतोर्विमर्दनम् Bhāg. 3. 18. 20.<BR>—4 An eclipse.<BR>—5 Fragrance, perfume.<BR>—6 Battle, war.<BR>—7 Trituration of perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दना
विमर्दनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Pounding, crushing, trampling.<BR>—2 Rubbing together, friction.<BR>—3 Destruction, killing; कौरव्य मह्यां द्विषतोर्विमर्दनम् Bhāg. 3. 18. 20.<BR>—4 An eclipse.<BR>—5 Fragrance, perfume.<BR>—6 Battle, war.<BR>—7 Trituration of perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दित
विमर्दित, विमृदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pounded, crushed, ground.<BR>—2 Rubbed.<BR>—3 Anointed, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृदित
विमर्दित, विमृदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pounded, crushed, ground.<BR>—2 Rubbed.<BR>—3 Anointed, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्
विमृश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To touch, feel.<BR>—2 To stroke, rub.<BR>—3 To think, consider, reflect, ponder (over); वृणते हि विमृश्यकारिणं<BR> गुणलुब्धाः स्वयमेव संपदः Ki. 2. 30; रामप्रवासे व्यमृशन्न दोषं<BR> जनापवादं सनरेन्द्रमृत्युम् Bk. 3. 7, 12. 24; Ku. 6. 87; इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातं<BR> गुह्याद् गुह्यतरं मया । विमृश्यैतदशेषेण Bg. 18. 63; Śi. 10. 56.<BR>—4 To perceive, observe.<BR>—5 To examine, test; तदत्रभवानिमं मां च शास्त्रे प्रयोगे च विमृशतु M. 1.<BR>—6 To hesitate, doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शः|विमर्श
विमर्शः, -र्शनम्<BR>—1 Deliberation, consideration, examination, discussion; कुर्वन् बुद्ध्या<BR> विमर्शम् Mu. 4. 3.<BR>—2 Reasoning.<BR>—3 A conflicting judgment.<BR>—4 Hesitation, doubt; कार्यस्य न विमर्शं च गन्तुमर्हसि सुव्रत<BR> Rām. 1. 18. 57, 2. 34. 44.<BR>—5 The impression left on the mind by past good or bad actions; see वासना.<BR>—6 Knowledge; अविद्वदधिकारित्वात् प्रायश्चित्तं विमर्शनम् Bhāg. 6. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शनम्
विमर्शः, -र्शनम्<BR>—1 Deliberation, consideration, examination, discussion; कुर्वन् बुद्ध्या<BR> विमर्शम् Mu. 4. 3.<BR>—2 Reasoning.<BR>—3 A conflicting judgment.<BR>—4 Hesitation, doubt; कार्यस्य न विमर्शं च गन्तुमर्हसि सुव्रत<BR> Rām. 1. 18. 57, 2. 34. 44.<BR>—5 The impression left on the mind by past good or bad actions; see वासना.<BR>—6 Knowledge; अविद्वदधिकारित्वात् प्रायश्चित्तं विमर्शनम् Bhāg. 6. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृशः|विमृश
विमृशः Reflection, deliberation; क्षेमस्य सध्र्यग्विमृशेषु हेतुः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 22. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्ट
विमृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Considered, reflected upon, pondered over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्टम्
विमृष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Reflection, thought; कतम उद्गीथ इति विमृष्टं भवति<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षः|विमोक्ष
विमोक्षः<BR>—1 Release, liberation, freeing; सा त्वं सर्वविमोक्षाय तत्त्वमाख्याहि<BR> पृच्छतः Mb. 5. 190. 19.<BR>—2 Discharging, shooting.<BR>—3 Final emancipation or beatitude.<BR>—4 Gift, bestowal (of wealth); वसूनां च विमोक्षस्य Rām. 2. 23. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षणम्
विमोक्षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Liberating, releasing, setting free.<BR>—2 Discharging.<BR>—3 Quitting, leaving, abandoning.<BR>—4 Laying (as eggs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षणा
विमोक्षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Liberating, releasing, setting free.<BR>—2 Discharging.<BR>—3 Quitting, leaving, abandoning.<BR>—4 Laying (as eggs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोघ
विमोघ <i>a.</i> Quite fruitless, idle, vain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचनम्
विमोचनम्<BR>—1 Unloosing, unyoking.<BR>—2 Release, freedom.<BR>—3 Liberation, emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहन|विमोहनं|विमोहनः
विमोहन <i>a.</i> (-ना or -नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Alluring, tempting, fascinating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहनः|विमोहन|विमोहनं
विमोहन + .{@-नः, -नम्@} N. of a division of Hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहनम्
विमोहन + .{@-नः, -नम्@} N. of a division of Hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहनम्
विमोहन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Seducing, tempting, fascinating.<BR>—2 Infatuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लान
विम्लान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Faded, withered.<BR>—2 Unfaded, fresh, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लापनम्
विम्लापनम्<BR>—1 Refreshing, reviving.<BR>—2 Cleaning, wiping.<BR>—3 Causing to wither or fade away, wasting away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बः|विम्ब|विंब|विंबं|विम्बं|विंबः
विम्बः, -म्बम्<BR> See बिम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बम्
विम्बः, -म्बम्<BR> See बिम्ब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बक|विंबक|विम्बकं
