विम्बा
विम्बा, -म्बी <i>f.</i><BR> N. of a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बी
विम्बा, -म्बी <i>f.</i><BR> N. of a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बिका|विंबिका
विम्बिका See बिम्बिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्बुः|विम्बु|विंबु|विंबुः
विम्बुः The betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत् <i>a.</i> Passing away, vanishing; कुटुम्बपोषाय वियन्निजायुर्न<BR> बुध्यतेऽर्थं विहतं प्रमत्तः Bhāg. 7. 6. 14, 9. 21. 3. ━<i>n.</i> The<BR> sky, atmosphere, ether; पश्योदग्रप्लुतत्वाद्वियति बहुतरं स्तोकमुर्व्यां<BR> प्रयाति Ś. 1. 7; R. 13. 40; हंसपङ्क्तिरपि नाथ संप्रति प्रस्थिता<BR> वियति मानसं प्रति Ghaṭ.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वियद्गङ्गा, वियच्चारिन्, वियत्पताका, वियत्पथः, वियद्भूतिः, वियन्मणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्गङ्गा|वियद्गंगा
वियत् + -गङ्गा<BR>—1 the heavenly Ganges.<BR>—2 the galaxy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियच्चारिन्
वियत् + -चारिन् (वियच्चारिन्) <i>m.</i> a kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्पताका
वियत् + -पताका lightning; सौदामिनी स्फुरति नाद्य वियत्पताका Ṛs. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्पथः|वियत्पथ
वियत् + -पथः the atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियद्भूतिः|वियद्भूति
वियत् + -भूतिः <i>f.</i> darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियन्मणिः|वियन्मणि
वियत् + -मणिः (वियन्मणिः), {@-मध्यहंसः@} (वियन्मध्यहंसः)<BR> the sun; Dk. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियतिः|वियति
वियतिः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम्
वियम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To spread out, extend.<BR>—2 To curb, restrain.<BR>—3 To give, grant, bestow.<BR>—4 To hold apart or asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियतम्
वियतम् <i>ind.</i> At intervals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियन्तृ
वियन्तृ <i>a.</i> Deprived of a guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियमः|वियम
वियमः<BR>—1 Restraint, check, control.<BR>—2 Distress, pain, affliction.<BR>—3 Cessation, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियवः|वियव
वियवः A kind of intestinal worm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियात|वियातः
वियात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bold (धृष्ट).<BR>—2 Audacious, shameless, impudent.<BR>—3 Abandoned, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1459-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियामः|वियाम
वियामः<BR>—1 See वियम.<BR>—2 A measure of length (two extended arms).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियु
वियु €3 P.<BR>—1 To be separated or dissolved (intran.).<BR>—2 To lose or be deprived of.<BR>—3 To exclude, deprive of.<BR>—4 To keep or ward off, prevent; उपवनं निरभर्त्सयत प्रियान् वियुवतीर्युवतीः<BR> शिशिरानिलः Śi. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुत
वियुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Deprived of, separated from; रथाङ्गनामन् वियुतो रथाङ्गश्रोणिबिम्बया V. 4. 37.<BR>—2 Without, devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुतिः|वियुति
वियुतिः (alg.) The difference between two quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुज्
वियुज् €7 Ā.<BR>—1 To leave, abandon; part with, forsake; मदमानसमुद्धतं नृपं न<BR> वियुङ्क्ते नियमेन मूढता Ki. 2. 49; R. 13. 63.<BR>—2 To separate; पुरो वियुक्ते मिथुने कृपावती Ku. 5. 26.<BR>—3 To relax, slacken.<BR>—4 To disjoin, divide, sever.<BR>—5 To free or deliver from, deprive of (with instr.); प्राणैर्न वियोजयति<BR> Pt. 1; असुभिर्न वियुज्यते K. 38.<BR>—6 To break (a vow); न व्रतेन वियुज्यते Ms. 5. 91.<BR>—7 To yield, give way. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To separate.<BR>—2 To free from, deprive of; अजानता मया सैव पत्रैः शाखा वियोजिता Mk. 4. 18.<BR>—3 To rob.<BR>—4 To subtract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुज्य
वियुज्य (absolutive of वि + युज् €4 Ā.) Separately, singly, individually,<BR> one at a time; प्रधानभूते आख्यातार्थे संहत्य विशेषणं भवति परार्थे<BR> पुनर्वियुज्येति ŚB. on MS. 6. 4. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुक्त|वियुक्तः
वियुक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Detached, severed, separated.<BR>—2 Separated from, deserted by; तया वियुक्तस्य विलग्नमध्यया V. 4. 66.<BR>—3 Free from, deprived of (with instr. or in comp.).<BR>—4 Failing, deficient.<BR>—5 Disunited (as husband and wife); यथा नाभिचरेतां तौ वियुक्तावितरेतरम् Ms. 9. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगः|वियोग
वियोगः<BR>—1 Separation, disunion; अयमेकपदे तया वियोगः सहसा चोपनतः सुदुःसहो<BR> मे V. 4. 10; त्वयोपस्थितवियोगस्य तपोवनस्यापि समवस्था दृश्यते<BR> Ś. 4; संधत्ते भृशमरतिं हि सद्वियोगः Ki. 5. 51; R. 12. 10; Śi. 12. 63.<BR>—2 Absence, loss.<BR>—3 Subtraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिन्
वियोगिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Separated.<BR>—2 Absent, apart. ━<i>m.</i> The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिनी
वियोगिनी<BR>—1 A woman separated from her lover or husband; गुरुनिःश्वसितैः कपिर्मनीषी<BR> निरणैषीदथ तां वियोगिनीति Bv. 4. 35.<BR>—2 N. of a metre; (see App.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजनम्
वियोजनम्<BR>—1 Separation from.<BR>—2 Subtraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजित|वियोजितः
वियोजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Separated.<BR>—2 Separated from, deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनिः|वियोनि
वियोनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Manifold birth.<BR>—2 The womb of animals; संभवांश्च वियोनीषु दुःखप्रायासु नित्यशः<BR> Ms. 12. 77 (Kull. on).<BR>—3 A debased or ignominious birth.<BR>—4 A woman of a different caste; ये तु मूढा दुराचारा वियोनौ मैथुने रताः<BR> Mb. 13. 145. 52. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of low origin; अयोनिं च वियोनिं च न गच्छेत विचक्षणः Mb. 13. 104. 133.<BR>—2 Destitute<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">Page1460-2</a>]<BR> of vulva. ˚जः an animal (पक्ष्यादि); वियोनिजानां च विजानते<BR> रुतं Mb. 13. 106. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनी
वियोनिः, -नी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Manifold birth.<BR>—2 The womb of animals; संभवांश्च वियोनीषु दुःखप्रायासु नित्यशः<BR> Ms. 12. 77 (Kull. on).<BR>—3 A debased or ignominious birth.<BR>—4 A woman of a different caste; ये तु मूढा दुराचारा वियोनौ मैथुने रताः<BR> Mb. 13. 145. 52. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of low origin; अयोनिं च वियोनिं च न गच्छेत विचक्षणः Mb. 13. 104. 133.<BR>—2 Destitute<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">Page1460-2</a>]<BR> of vulva. ˚जः an animal (पक्ष्यादि); वियोनिजानां च विजानते<BR> रुतं Mb. 13. 106. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरच्
विरच् €10 U.<BR>—1 To arrange; क्षितिविरचितशय्यं कौतुकागारमागात् Ku. 7. 94.<BR>—2 To compose, put together, write; इति विरचितवाग्भिर्वन्दिपुत्रैः<BR> R. 5. 75; मद्गोत्राङ्कं विरचितपदं गेयमुद्गातुकामा Me. 88, 105.<BR>—3 To effect, produce, cause, make; मालाकार व्यरचि भवता या तरोरस्य<BR> पुष्टिः Bv. 1. 30.<BR>—4 To put on.<BR>—5 To set, inlay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचनम्
विरचनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Arrangement, disposition; तारावलीविरचनैर्व्यरुचन्निवासाः Śi. 5. 21.<BR>—2 Contriving, constructing.<BR>—3 Formation, creation.<BR>—4 Composition, compilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचना
विरचनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Arrangement, disposition; तारावलीविरचनैर्व्यरुचन्निवासाः Śi. 5. 21.<BR>—2 Contriving, constructing.<BR>—3 Formation, creation.<BR>—4 Composition, compilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचित|विरचितः
विरचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Arranged, made, formed, prepared.<BR>—2 Contrived, constructed.<BR>—3 Written, composed.<BR>—4 Trimmed, dressed, embellished, ornamented.<BR>—5 Put on, worn.<BR>—6 Set, inlaid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरज|विरजः
विरज <i>a.</i> Free from dust or passion; pure; विधूतकल्मषाः<BR> स्थानं विरजेनात्मनैव हि Bhāg. 1. 15. 48, 8. 8. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजः|विरज
विरज + .{@-जः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजा
विरज + .{@-जा@}<BR>—1 Dūrvā grass; Mb. 13. 136. 25.<BR>—2 N. of the wife of Nahuṣa.<BR>—3 The Kapittha-tree.<BR>—4 N. of a river; मुण्डनं चोपवासश्च सर्वतीर्थेष्वयं विधिः । वर्जयित्वा<BR> गयां गङ्गां विशालां विरजां तथा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्
विरजस्, विरजस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from dust; विरजः पर आकाशादज आत्मा महान् ध्रुवः Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 20.<BR>—2 Free from passion; यथा लोकान् विरजाः संचरेयम् Mb. 3. 186. 3;<BR> असक्तदृष्टिर्विरजाः सदैव Śi. 20. 80.<BR>—3 Free from menstrual secretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्क
विरजस्, विरजस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from dust; विरजः पर आकाशादज आत्मा महान् ध्रुवः Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 20.<BR>—2 Free from passion; यथा लोकान् विरजाः संचरेयम् Mb. 3. 186. 3;<BR> असक्तदृष्टिर्विरजाः सदैव Śi. 20. 80.<BR>—3 Free from menstrual secretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्का
विरजस्का A woman in whom the menstrual secretion has ceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीकृ
विरजीकृ €8 U. To render free from dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीभू
विरजीभू €1 P. To become free from dust, be pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्चः|विरञ्च|विरंच|विरंचः
विरञ्चः, -ञ्चिः<BR> N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्चिः|विरञ्चि|विरंचि|विरंचिः
विरञ्चः, -ञ्चिः<BR> N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्ज्|विरंज्
विरञ्ज् €1. €4 U.<BR>—1 To grow discoloured or soiled, be coarse or rough; केशा अपि विरज्यन्ते<BR> निःस्नेहाः किं न सेवकाः Pt. 1. 82 (where it has sense 2 also).<BR>—2 To be discontented or disaffected, to dislike, hate; चिरानुरक्तोऽपि<BR> विरज्यते जनः Mk. 1. 53; Bh. 2. 2; श्रीर्निष्कुष्यति लङ्कायां विरज्यन्ति<BR> समृद्धयः Bk. 18. 22.<BR>—3 To become disgusted with the world and hence to renounce all worldly<BR> attachments. ━<i>Caus.</i> To colour, dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरञ्जित
विरञ्जित <i>p. p.</i> Cooled in affection, estranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
विरक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Very red, ruddy; विरक्तसंध्याकपिशं पुरस्तात् R. 13. 64.<BR>—2 Discoloured.<BR>—3 Changed in mind, disaffected, displeased; यां चिन्तयामि सततं मयि<BR> सा विरक्ता Bh. 2. 2.<BR>—4 Free from passion or worldly attachment, indifferent; विरक्तः प्रव्रजेद्<BR> धीमान् सरक्तस्तु गृहे वसेत् Nāradapari. Up. 3. 14.<BR>—5 Impassioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्ता
विरक्त + .{@-क्ता@} An unfortunate or unhappy woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरक्तचित्त, विरक्तप्रकृति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तचित्त
विरक्त + -चित्त <i>a.</i> estranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तप्रकृति
विरक्त + -प्रकृति <i>a.</i> having disaffected subjects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1460-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तिः|विरक्ति
विरक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Change of disposition, dissatisfaction, discontent, disaffection.<BR>—2 Estrangement.<BR>—3 Indifference, absence of desire, freedom from passion or worldly attachment;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 16. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरटः|विरट
विरटः<BR>—1 A kind of black agallochum.<BR>—2 The shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरणम्
विरणम् A kind of fragrant grass; cf. वीरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरण्य
विरण्य <i>a.</i> Vast, extensive; विरण्यशब्दो विस्तीर्णे भवति ।<BR> यथा विरण्यानि अरण्यानि विस्तीर्णानीति गम्यते ŚB. on MS. 10. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरथ्या
विरथ्या<BR>—1 A bad road.<BR>—2 A by-road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम्
विरम् €1 P.<BR>—1 To end, terminate, come to an end; अविदितगतयामा रात्रिरेव<BR> व्यरंसीत् U. 1. 27, 6. 33.<BR>—2 To cease, desist, stop, leave off (speaking &c.); एतावदुक्त्वा विरते<BR> मृगेन्द्रे R. 2. 51; Śi. 2. 13; oft. with abl.; हा हन्त किमिति चित्तं<BR> विरमति नाद्यापि विषयेभ्यः Bv. 4. 25; न स्थिरकर्मा विरराम कर्मणः<BR> R. 8. 22; वत्सैतस्माद्विरम विरमातःपरं न क्षमोऽस्मि U. 1. 33; Bh. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरत|विरतः
विरत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ceased or desisting from (with abl.).<BR>—2 Rested, stopped, ceased.<BR>—3 Ended, concluded, at an end; विरतं गेयमृतुर्निरुत्सवः R. 8. 66.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरतप्रसंग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरतप्रसंग|विरतप्रसङ्ग
विरत + -प्रसंग <i>a.</i> one who has ceased from being occupied in; भ्रूविक्रियायां<BR> विरतप्रसंगैः Ku. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरतिः|विरति
विरतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Cessation, stop, discontinuance.<BR>—2 Rest, end, pause.<BR>—3 Indifference to worldly attachments; विरतिवनितासंगमुदितः Bh. 3. 79;<BR> A. Rām. 2. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमः|विरम
विरमः<BR>—1 Cessation, stop.<BR>—2 Sunset; अभितिग्मरश्मि चिरमाविरमात् Śi. 9. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरामः|विराम
विरामः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Cessation, discontinuance; सुधां विना न प्रययुर्विरामम्<BR> Bh. 2. 80; प्रवृत्तस्याविरामे भवन्ती शासितव्या Mbh.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Rest, repose.<BR>—2 End, termination, conclusion; आरामः कल्पवृक्षाणां विरामः सकलापदाम्<BR> Rāmarakṣā 16; रजनिरिदानीमियमपि याति विरामम् Gīt. 5; U. 3. 16;<BR> Māl. 9. 34.<BR>—3 Pause, stop.<BR>—4 The stop or pause of the voice; वर्णानामपि मूर्च्छनान्तरगतं तारं<BR> विरामे मृदुम् Mk. 3. 5.<BR>—5 A small oblique stroke placed under a consonant, usually at the end of a sentence.<BR>—6 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरामणम्
विरामणम् A pause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having interstices, separated by intervals, thin, not thick or compact;<BR> विपर्यासं यातो घनविरलभावः क्षितिरुहाम् U. 2. 27, 1. 20; भवति<BR> विरलभक्तिर्म्लानपुष्पापहारः R. 5. 74.<BR>—2 Fine, declicate.<BR>—3 Loose, wide apart.<BR>—4 Rare, scarcely found, unfrequent; विरला हि तेषामुपदेष्टारः K.;<BR> स्तिमितोन्नतसंचारा जनसंतापहारिणः । जायन्ते विरला लोके जलदा<BR> इव सज्जनाः ॥ Pt. 1. 29.<BR>—5 Few, little (referring to number or quantity); तत्त्वं किमपि काव्यानां<BR> जानाति विरलो भुवि Bv. 1. 117; विरलातपच्छविः Śi. 9. 3.<BR>—6 Remote, distant, long (as time, distance &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलम्
विरल + .{@-लम्@} Curds, coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलम्
विरल + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i> Scarcely, rarely, not frequently.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">Page1461-2</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरलजानुक, विरलद्रवा, विरलपातक, विरलपार्श्वग, विरलभक्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलजानुक
विरल + -जानुक <i>a.</i> bandy-legged, bow-kneed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलद्रवा
विरल + -द्रवा a kind of gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलपातक
विरल + -पातक <i>a.</i> sinning rarely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलपार्श्वग
विरल + -पार्श्वग <i>a.</i> having scanty retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरलभक्ति
विरल + -भक्ति <i>a.</i> monotonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
विरस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Tasteless, insipid, flavourless.<BR>—2 Unpleasant, disagreeable, painful; तावत् कोकिल विरसान् यापय दिवसान्<BR> वनान्तरे निवसन् Bv. 1. 7; Māl. 1. 31, 6. 10.<BR>—3 Cruel, unfeeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरसः|विरस
विरस + .{@-सः@} Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहः|विरह
विरहः<BR>—1 Parting with, separation.<BR>—2 Especially, the separation of lovers; सा विरहे तव दीना Gīt. 4;<BR> क्षणमपि विरहः पुरा न सेहे <i>ibid.</i>; कः संनद्धे विरहविधुरां<BR> त्वय्युपेक्षेत जायाम् Me. 8, 12, 29, 87, 89.<BR>—3 Absence.<BR>—4 Want.<BR>—5 Desertion, abandonment, relinquishment.<BR>—6 The feeling of love in separation; see विप्रलम्भ (6).<BR>—7 Loneliness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरहानलः, विरहावस्था, विरहार्त, विरहोत्कण्ठ, विरहोत्सुक, विरहोत्कण्ठिता, विरहज्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहानलः|विरहानल
विरहः + -अनलः the fire of separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहावस्था
विरहः + -अवस्था the state of separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहार्त|विरहार्त्त
विरहः + -आर्त, -उत्कण्ठ, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> suffering from separation; pining<BR> away in separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहोत्कण्ठ|विरहोत्कंठ
विरहः + -आर्त, -उत्कण्ठ, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> suffering from separation; pining<BR> away in separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहोत्सुक
विरहः + -आर्त, -उत्कण्ठ, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> suffering from separation; pining<BR> away in separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहोत्कण्ठिता|विरहोत्कंठिता
विरहः + -उत्कण्ठिता a woman distressed by the absence of her lover or<BR> husband, one of the several classes of a Nāyikā in poetic compositions; see S. D. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहज्वरः|विरहज्वर
विरहः + -ज्वरः the fever or anguish of separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिणी
विरहिणी<BR>—1 A woman separated from her lover or husband.<BR>—2 Wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहित|विरहितः
विरहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Deserted, abandoned, forsaken.<BR>—2 Separated from.<BR>—3 Lonely, solitary.<BR>—4 Bereft of, devoid or destitute of, free from (mostly in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Absent from, being separated from a mistress or lover; नृत्यति युवतिजनेन<BR> समं सखि विरहिजनस्य दुरन्ते Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 Lonely, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागः|विराग
विरागः<BR>—1 Change of colour.<BR>—2 Change of disposition, disaffection, discontent, dissatisfaction; विरागकारणेषु<BR> परिहृतेषु Mu. 1.<BR>—3 Aversion, disinclination; Kau. A. 3.<BR>—4 Indifference to worldly attachments, freedom from passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज्<BR>—1 U. 1 To shine, glitter; शाखिनोऽन्ये विराजन्ते खण्ड्यन्ते चन्दनद्रुमाः Bv. 1. 88.<BR>—2 To appear or look like; तदन्तरे सा विरराज धेनुः R. 2. 20.<BR>—3 To be eminent or illustrious. ━<i>Caus.</i> To brighten, illuminate, irradiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Splendid, excellent; मृत्युर्भोजपतेर्विराडविदुषां तत्त्वं परं योगिनाम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 43. 17.<BR>—2 A ruler, chief. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Beauty, splendour.<BR>—2 A man of the Kṣatriya or warrior tribe; विराडायुषोऽर्धमथात्यगात्<BR> Bhāg. 4. 27. 6.<BR>—3 The first progeny of Brahman; cf. Ms. 1. 32; तस्मात् विराडजायत<BR> Rv. 10. 90. 5 (where विराज् is represented as born from <i>Puruṣa</i>).<BR>—4 The body.<BR>—5 (In Vedānta phil.) N. of ‘intellect’ considered as ruling over the<BR> aggregate of bodies.<BR>—6 The universe (ब्रह्माण्ड); नानावीर्याः पृथग्भूता विराजं जनयन्ति<BR> हि Bhāg. 10. 3. 15. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 N. of a Vedic metre.<BR>—2 Excellence, dignity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विराक्सुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराक्सुतः
विराज् + -सुतः (विराट्सुतः) a class of deceased ancestors; विराट्सुताः<BR> सोमसदः साध्यानां पितरः स्मृताः Ms. 3. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1461-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज|विराजः
विराज <i>a.</i> See विराज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजः|विराज
विराज + .{@-जः@} A particular form of a temple; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजित|विराजितः
विराजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Irradiated, illuminated.<BR>—2 Displayed, manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटः|विराट
विराटः<BR>—1 N. of a district in India.<BR>—2 N. of a king of the Matsyas. The Pāṇḍavas lived <i>incognito</i> in<BR> the service of this king for one year, (the thirteenth of their exile)<BR> having assumed different disguises. His daughter Uttarā was married to<BR> Abhimanyu and was mother of Parīkṣit who succeeded Yudhiṣṭhira to<BR> the throne of Hastināpura.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विराटजः, विराटपर्वन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटजः|विराटज
विराटः + -जः a sort of inferior diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटपर्वन्
विराटः + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> the fourth book of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटकः|विराटक
विराटकः A sort of inferior diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराणिन्
विराणिन् <i>m.</i> An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरात्रः|विरात्र
विरात्रः, -त्रम्<BR>—1 The end of night; day-break; तमेव गणयन् शोकं विरात्रे प्रत्यबुध्यत<BR> Bhāg. 13. 91. 8.<BR>—2 The dead of night (बहुरात्र, अपरात्र); विरात्रे चागतं कस्मात्<BR> कोऽनुबन्धस्तवाभवत् Mb. 3. 298. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरात्रम्
विरात्रः, -त्रम्<BR>—1 The end of night; day-break; तमेव गणयन् शोकं विरात्रे प्रत्यबुध्यत<BR> Bhāg. 13. 91. 8.<BR>—2 The dead of night (बहुरात्र, अपरात्र); विरात्रे चागतं कस्मात्<BR> कोऽनुबन्धस्तवाभवत् Mb. 3. 298. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध्
विराध् €4 P.<BR>—1 To hurt, injure, offend, wrong; क्रियासमभिहारेण विराध्यन्तं क्षमेत<BR> कः Śi. 2. 43; विराद्ध एवं भवता विराद्धा बहुधा च नः 2. 41.<BR>—2 To lose, be deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्ध
विराद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Opposed, counteracted.<BR>—2 Offended, injured, treated with contempt; see the quotations under<BR> राध् with वि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधः|विराध
विराधः<BR>—1 Opposition.<BR>—2 Annoyance, vexation, molestation.<BR>—3 N. of a powerful Rākṣasa slain by Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधनम्
विराधनम्<BR>—1 Opposing.<BR>—2 Hurting, injuring, offending.<BR>—3 Pain, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराल|विरालः
विराल See बिडाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिक्त|विरिक्तः
विरिक्त <i>p. p.</i> Evacuated, purged; वान्तो विरिक्तः स्नात्वा तु घृतप्राशनमाचरेत्<BR> Ms. 5. 144; विरिक्तस्य यथा सम्यग् घृतं भवति भेषजम् Mb. 12. 309. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिक्तिः|विरिक्ति
विरिक्तिः Purging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चः|विरिञ्च|विरिंच|विरिंचः
विरिञ्चः, विरिञ्चनः<BR>—1 N. of Brahman.<BR>—2 Of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चनः|विरिञ्चन|विरिंचन|विरिंचनः
विरिञ्चः, विरिञ्चनः<BR>—1 N. of Brahman.<BR>—2 Of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिञ्चिः|विरिञ्चि|विरिंचि|विरिंचिः
विरिञ्चिः [वौ रिञ्चेः इन् नुम् च Uṇ. 4. 131]<BR>—1 N. of Brahman; एवं समाकर्ण्य वचो विरिञ्चिः । … चुलुके मुमोच … विलोचनानि<BR> Vikr. 1. 46; N. 3. 44; Śi. 9. 9.<BR>—2 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिब्धः|विरिब्ध
विरिब्धः A note, sound; विधिविहितविरिब्धैः सामिधेनीरधीत्य Śi. 11. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरु
विरु €2 P.<BR>—1 To cry, bewail, lament; ननु सहचरीं दूरे मत्वा विरौषि समुत्सुकः<BR> V. 4. 20; Bk. 5. 54; Ṛs. 6. 27.<BR>—2 To make a sound, sound in general; न स विरौति न चापि स<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">Page1462-2</a>]<BR> शोभते Pt. 1. 75; जीर्णत्वाद् गृहस्य विरौति कपाटम् Mk. 3; एते<BR> त एव गिरयो विरुवन्मयूराः U. 2. 23.<BR>—3 To cry out, shout, scream. ━<i>Caus.</i> To roar or scream aloud;<BR> न च रक्तो विरावयेत् Ms. 4. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरावः|विराव
विरावः Clamour, noise, sound; आलोकशब्दं वयसां विरावैः R. 2. 9, 16. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरावण
विरावण <i>a.</i> Causing roar, clamour; विरावणं साधु तपस्विकण्टकं<BR> तपस्विनामुद्धर तं भयावहम् Rām. 1. 15. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविन्
विराविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Weeping, crying, shouting.<BR>—2 Lamenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविणी
विराविन् + .{@-णी@}<BR>—1 Weeping, crying.<BR>—2 A broom.<BR>—3 Sound, resound; गायनैश्च विराविण्यो वादनैश्च तथापरैः Rām. 1. 18. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुत
विरुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Screamed, shouted.<BR>—2 Resounding, filled with cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुतम्
विरुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Crying, shrieking, roaring &c.<BR>—2 Cry, sound, noise, clamour, din.<BR>—3 Singing, humming, chirping, buzzing; परभृतविरुतं कलं यथा प्रतिवचनीकृतमेभिरीदृशम् Ś. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुतिः|विरुति
विरुत + .{@-तिः@} Screaming, howling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुग्ण
विरुग्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Broken to pieces, shattered; तच्चित्रताण्डवविरुग्णफणातपत्रः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 16. 30.<BR>—2 Destroyed.<BR>—3 Bent.<BR>—4 Blunted, dulled; विरुग्णोदग्रधाराग्रः कुलिशो मम वक्षसि Bk. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुच्
विरुच् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To shine, be resplendent; सहस्रधात्मा व्यरुचद्विभक्तः पयोमुचां<BR> पङ्क्तिषु विद्युतेव R. 6. 5, 17. 14; Bk. 8. 66.<BR>—2 To be eminent or conspicuous.<BR>—3 To become visible, appear.<BR>—4 To illuminate, brighten (P.).<BR>—5 To please, delight. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To irradiate, illuminate.<BR>—2 To delight in.<BR>—3 To sport with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुक्मत्|विरुक्मन्त्
विरुक्मत् <i>m.</i> A bright weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुचः|विरुच
विरुचः A magic formula recited over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुज्
विरुज् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Violent pain.<BR>—2 A great disease; विन्देद्विरूपा विरुजा विमुच्यते Bhāg. 6. 19. 29.<BR>━<i>a.</i> Well, healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदः|विरुद|विरुदं
विरुदः, -दम्<BR>—1 Proclaiming.<BR>—2 Crying aloud.<BR>—3 A panegyric, laudatory poem; गद्यपद्यमयी राजस्तुतिर्विरुदमुच्यते<BR> S. D. 570; नदन्ति मददन्तिनः परिलसन्ति वाजिव्रजाः । पठन्ति विरुदावलीमहितमन्दिरे<BR> वन्दिनः ॥ R. G.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरुदावली, विरुदध्वजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदम्
विरुदः, -दम्<BR>—1 Proclaiming.<BR>—2 Crying aloud.<BR>—3 A panegyric, laudatory poem; गद्यपद्यमयी राजस्तुतिर्विरुदमुच्यते<BR> S. D. 570; नदन्ति मददन्तिनः परिलसन्ति वाजिव्रजाः । पठन्ति विरुदावलीमहितमन्दिरे<BR> वन्दिनः ॥ R. G.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरुदावली, विरुदध्वजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदावली
विरुदः + -आवली<BR>—1 a collection of epithets.<BR>—2 a particular collection of religious lyrics; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदध्वजः|विरुदध्वज
विरुदः + -ध्वजः a royal banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदितम्
विरुदितम् Loud cry or lamentation; तदद्याप्युच्छ्वासो भवति ननु<BR> लाभो विरुदितम् U. 3. 30, v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुध्
विरुध् €7 U. —1 To oppose, obstruct, hinder, prevent. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be opposed to, be inconsistent or at variance with.<BR>—2 To contend or quarrel with; एको दोषो विदेशस्य स्वजातिर्यद्विरुध्यते Pt. 4. 116.<BR>—3 To fail.<BR>—4 To be kept back or withheld.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्ध|विरुद्धः
विरुद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Hindered, checked, opposed, obstructed.<BR>—2 Blocked up, confined or shut up.<BR>—3 Besieged, blockaded.<BR>—4 Opposed to, inconsistent with,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">Page1463-1</a>]<BR> incongruous, inconsistent.<BR>—5 Contrary, opposite, opposed in quality.<BR>—6 Contradictory, proving the reverse, (as a <i>hetu</i> in Logic); साध्याभावव्याप्तो<BR> हेतुर्विरुद्धः Tarka K.; <i>e. g.</i> शब्दो नित्यः कृतकत्वात् T. S.<BR>—7 Hostile, adverse, inimical.<BR>—8 Unfavourable, unpropitious.<BR>—9 Prohibited, forbidden (as food).<BR>—10 Wrong, unlawful^1, improper.<BR>—11 Excluded.<BR>—12 Uncertain, doubtful.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20210320. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/512.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धम्
विरुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@}<BR>—1 Opposition, contrariety, hostility; स्वर्गे निवासे राजेन्द्र विरुद्धं<BR> चापि नश्यति Mb. 18. 1. 11.<BR>—2 Discord, disagreement.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरुद्धधी, विरुद्धभोजनम्, विरुद्धमतिकृत्, विरुद्धरूपकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1462-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धधी
विरुद्ध + -धी <i>a.</i> evil-minded, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धभोजनम्
विरुद्ध + -भोजनम् Unwholesome meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धमतिकृत्
विरुद्ध + -मतिकृत् <i>m.</i> a fault or defect in composition; विपरीतार्थधीर्यस्मात्<BR> विरुद्धमतिकृन्मतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्धरूपकम्
विरुद्ध + -रूपकम् a figure of speech in which an object compared to another<BR> object is not quite similar; अक्रिया चन्द्रकार्याणामन्यकार्यस्य च क्रिया ।<BR> अत्र सन्दिश्यते यस्माद्विरुद्धं नाम रूपकम् ॥ Kāv. 2. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधः|विरोध
विरोधः<BR>—1 Opposition, obstruction, impediment.<BR>—2 Blockade, siege, investment.<BR>—3 Restraint, check.<BR>—4 Inconsistency, incongruity, contradiction; विरोधो न विद्यते ब्रह्माद्वितीयमेव<BR> सत्यम् । (-त्रिपाद्विभूतिमहानारायणोपनिषत् 4. 2.)<BR>—5 Antithesis, contrast.<BR>—6 Enmity, hostility; विरोधो विश्रान्तः U. 6. 11; Pt. 1. 332; R. 10. 13.<BR>—7 A quarrel, disagreement.<BR>—8 A calamity, misfortune.<BR>—9 (In Rhet.) An apparent incongruity which is merely verbal and is explained<BR> away by properly construing the passage; it consists in representing objects<BR> as antithetical to one another though in the nature of things they are<BR> not so; representing things as being together though really they cannot<BR> be together; (this figure is largely used by Bāṇa and Subandhu; पुष्पवत्यपि<BR> पवित्रा, कृष्णोऽप्यसुदर्शनः, भरतोऽपि शत्रुघ्नः being familiar instances);<BR> it is thus defined by Mammaṭa:− विरोधः सोऽविरोधेऽपि विरुद्धत्वने<BR> यद्वचः K. P. 10; (this figure is also called विरोधाभास).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरोधोक्तिः, विरोधोपमा, विरोधकारिन्, विरोधकृत्, विरोधपरिहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधोक्तिः|विरोधोक्ति
विरोधः + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i>, {@-वचनम्@}<BR> contradiction, opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधोपमा
विरोधः + -उपमा (in Rhet.) a comparison founded on opposition; शतपत्रं<BR> शरच्चन्द्रस्त्वदाननमिति त्रयम् । परस्परविरोधीति सा विरोधोपमा मता ॥<BR> Kāv. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधकारिन्
विरोधः + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> fomenting quarrels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधकृत्
विरोधः + -कृत् <i>a.</i> opposing. ━(<i>m.</i>) an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधपरिहारः|विरोधपरिहार
विरोधः + -परिहारः reconciliation; Kull. on Ms. 7. 152.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधनम्
विरोधनम्<BR>—1 Hindering, opposing, obstructing.<BR>—2 Besieging, blockading.<BR>—3 Opposition, resistance.<BR>—4 Contradiction, inconsistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिन्
विरोधिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Resisting, opposing, obstructing.<BR>—2 Besieging.<BR>—3 Contradictory, opposed to, inconsistent with; तपोवन˚ Ś. 1.<BR>—4 Hostile, inimical, adverse; विरोधिसत्त्वोज्झितपूर्वमत्सरम् Ku. 5. 17.<BR>—5 Quarrelsome. ━<i>m.</i> An enemy; कलयन्त्युष्णकरं विरोधिनः Śi. 16. 64.<BR> ({@विरोधिनी@}) ━<i>f.</i> A woman who promotes quarrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुलः
विरुलः A kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुह्
विरुह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To grow, shoot up; गङ्गाप्रपातान्तविरूढशष्पं गौरीगुरोर्गह्वरमाविवेश<BR> R. 2. 26; Mk. 1. 9.<BR>—2 To mount,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">Page1463-2</a>]<BR> ascend.<BR>—3 To arise, proceed. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To heal (as a wound).<BR>—2 To plant.<BR>—3 To remove, expel; शशाप पुत्रं गान्धारे राज्याच्चापि व्यरोपयत् Mb. 5. 149. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढ|विरूढः
विरूढ <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Grown, germinated, shot up; तास्वेव संप्रति विरूढतृणाङ्कुरासु बीजाञ्जलिः<BR> पतति कीटमुखावलीढः Mk. 1. 9.<BR>—2 Produced, born, arisen.<BR>—3 Grown, increased.<BR>—4 Budded, blossomed.<BR>—5 Ascended, mounted.<BR>—6 Healed; जरासंधस्योरःस्थलमिव विरूढं पुनरपि.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरूढबोध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढबोध
विरूढ + -बोध <i>a.</i> one whose intelligence has matured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढकः|विरूढक
विरूढकः Grain that has begun to sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोपणम्
विरोप(ह)णम्<BR>—1 Healing (as a sore); व्रणविरोपणं तैलम् Ś. 4. 14.<BR>—2 Planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहणम्
विरोप(ह)णम्<BR>—1 Healing (as a sore); व्रणविरोपणं तैलम् Ś. 4. 14.<BR>—2 Planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहः|विरोह
विरोहः<BR>—1 Growing, shooting forth.<BR>—2 Source, origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूक्षणम्
विरूक्षणम्<BR>—1 Roughening.<BR>—2 Acting as an astringent.<BR>—3 Blame, censure.<BR>—4 A curse, an imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप|विरूपं|विरूपः
विरूप <i>a.</i> (-पा or -पी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Deformed, ugly, misshapen, disfigured; विरूपं रूपवन्तं वा पुमानित्येव<BR> भुञ्जते Pt. 1. 143.<BR>—2 Unnatural, monstrous.<BR>—3 Multiform, diverse; प्रकृतिसरूपं विरूपं च Sāṅ. K. 8.<BR>—4 Less by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपः|विरूप|विरूपं
विरूप + .{@-पः@}<BR>—1 Jaundice.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपा
विरूप + .{@-पा@}<BR>—1 Alhagi Maurorum (Mar. धमासा).<BR>—2 Aconitum Ferox (Mar. अतिविष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपम्
विरूप + .{@-पम्@}<BR>—1 Deformity, ugliness.<BR>—2 Variety of form, nature, or character.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरूपाक्ष, विरूपकरणम्, विरूपचक्षुस्, विरूपरूप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपाक्ष|विरूपाक्षः
विरूप + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> having deformed eyes; वपुर्विरूपाक्षम् Ku. 5. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपाक्षः|विरूपाक्ष
विरूप + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षः@}) N. of Śiva (having an unusual number of eyes); दृशा<BR> दग्धं मनसिजं जीवयन्ति दृशैव याः । विरूपाक्षस्य जयिनीस्ताः स्तुवे<BR> वामलोचनाः ॥ Vb. 1. 2; Ku. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपकरणम्
विरूप + -करणम्<BR>—1 disfiguring.<BR>—2 injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपचक्षुस्
विरूप + -चक्षुस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपरूप
विरूप + -रूप <i>a.</i> deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपक|विरूपकः
विरूपक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deformed, ugly.<BR>—2 Hideous, frightful, monstrous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपकः|विरूपक
विरूपक + .{@-कः@} A nickname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपिन्
विरूपिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Deformed, ugly, disfigured. ━<i>m.</i> A chameleon (Mar. सरडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेकः|विरेक
विरेकः<BR>—1 Evacuation of the bowels, purging.<BR>—2 A purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचनम्
विरेचनम् See विरेक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचित
विरेचित <i>a.</i> Purged, evacuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेफः|विरेफ
विरेफः<BR>—1 A river, stream.<BR>—2 Absence of the letter र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोकः|विरोक|विरोकं
विरोकः, -कम्<BR> A hole, pit, chasm; नासाविरोकपवनोल्लसितं तनीयो रोमाञ्चतामिव<BR> जगाम रजः पृथिव्याः Śi. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोकम्
विरोकः, -कम्<BR> A hole, pit, chasm; नासाविरोकपवनोल्लसितं तनीयो रोमाञ्चतामिव<BR> जगाम रजः पृथिव्याः Śi. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोकः|विरोक|विरोकं
विरोकः, -कम् + .{@-कः@} A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचनः|विरोचन
विरोचनः<BR>—1 The sun; दीप्तिनिर्जितविरोचनादयं गां विरोचनसुतादभीप्सतः Śi. 14. 74.<BR>—2 The moon; (सोममथाब्रवीत्) समं वर्तस्व भार्यासु मा त्वां शप्से<BR> विरोचन Mb. 9. 35. 57.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR>—4 N. of the son of Prarhāda and father of Bali; Śi. 14. 74.<BR>—5 A species of करञ्ज tree.<BR>—6 A species of श्योनाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचनम्
विरोचनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Light, lustre.<BR>—2 Propounding (आलोचन);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">Page1464-1</a>]<BR> विशुद्धविज्ञानविरोचनाञ्चिता विद्याऽत्मवृत्तिश्चरमेति भण्यते A. Rām. 7. 5. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विरोचनसुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1463-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचनसुतः|विरोचनसुत
विरोचनः + -सुतः an epithet of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचिष्णु
विरोचिष्णु <i>a.</i> Shining, bright; वायोरपि विकुर्वाणाद्विरोचिष्णु<BR> तमोनुदम् Ms. 1. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्
विल् I. €6 P. (बिलति)<BR>—1 To cover, conceal.<BR>—2 To break, divide. ━II. €10 U. (वेलयति-ते) To throw, send forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्
विलम् See बिलम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष्
विलक्ष् €10 U.<BR>—1 To see, observe, perceive, notice.<BR>—2 To characterize, distinguish.<BR>—3 To be confused, be bewildered; निर्व्यापारविलक्षितानि सान्त्वय बलानि<BR> U. 6; see विलक्ष below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष|विलक्षः
विलक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no characteristic or distinguishing marks, or fixed aim.<BR>—2 Bewildered, embarrassed.<BR>—3 Surprised, astonished.<BR>—4 Ashamed, abashed, disconcerted; गोत्रेषु स्खलितस्तदा भवति च व्रीडाविलक्षश्चिरम् Ś. 6. 5.<BR>—5 Forced, unnatural, embarrassed (as a smile); विलक्षस्मितस्फुरितैर्दशनांशुभिः<BR> K. 233; Ratn. 3. 14.<BR>—6 Missing the mark (as an arrow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
विलक्षण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having no characteristic or distinguishing marks.<BR>—2 Different, other; ततश्च कर्माणि विलक्षणानि Bhāg. 11. 23. 44.<BR>—3 Strange, extraordinary, unusual; तस्मै नमस्ते स्वविलक्षणात्मने<BR> Bhāg. 10. 70. 38.<BR>—4 Possessed of inauspicious marks.<BR>—5 Lustreless, bad-looking; उद्वीक्ष्योद्वीक्ष्य नयनैर्भयादिव विलक्षणैः<BR> Rām. 3. 52. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षणम्
विलक्षण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 A vain or useless state.<BR>—2 Perceiving, observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षित
विलक्षित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Distinguished, perceived, seen, discovered.<BR>—2 Discernible by.<BR>—3 Dismayed, perplexed, embarrassed, puzzled.<BR>—4 Vexed, annoyed.<BR>—5 Undistinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्
विलग् €1 P. To stick or adhere to, cling to; केचिद्विलग्ना दशनान्तरेषु Bg. 11. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्न|विलग्नं
विलग्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clinging or sticking to, resting on, fastened on; आकुटिलपक्ष्मविलग्नम्<BR> Ś. 7. 25; Śi. 9. 20.<BR>—2 Cast, fixed, directed; पुरोविलग्नैर्हरदृष्टिपातैः सुवर्णसूत्रैरिव<BR> कृष्यमाणः Ku. 7. 50.<BR>—3 Gone by, elapsed (as time).<BR>—4 Thin, slender, delicate; मध्येन सा वेदिविलग्नमध्या Ku. 1. 39; V. 4. 37.<BR>—5 Pendulous, flaccid (as breasts).<BR>—6 Caged (as a bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्नम्
विलग्न + .{@-ग्नम्@}<BR>—1 The waist.<BR>—2 The hips.<BR>—3 The rising of constellations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घ्|विलंघ्
विलङ्घ् €10 U.<BR>—1 To pass or spring over, traverse; निवेशयामास विलङ्घिताध्वा R. 5. 42, 16. 32;<BR> Śi. 12. 24, 8. 26.<BR>—2 To violate, transgress, overstep, disregard, neglect; गन्तुं प्रवृत्ते<BR> समयं विलङ्घ्य Ku. 3. 25; R. 5. 48; Ki. 2. 45; Śi. 17. 12.<BR>—3 To violate the limits of propriety; नृपतेः प्रतिषिद्धमेव तत् कृतवान्<BR> पङ्क्तिरथो विलङ्घ्य यत् R. 9. 74.<BR>—4 To rise towards, ascend or go up to; समुदितं न विलङ्घयितुं नभः<BR> Ki. 5. 1; N. 5. 2.<BR>—6 To give up, abandon, leave aside; मनो बबन्धान्यरसान् विलङ्घ्य सा R. 3. 4.<BR>—7 To surpass,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">Page1464-2</a>]<BR> excel; इति कर्णोत्पलं प्रायस्तव दृष्टपा विलङ्घ्यते Kāv. 2. 224.<BR>—8 To cause to fast.<BR>—9 To overcome, surmount.<BR>—10 To offend, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घनम्
विलङ्घनम्<BR>—1 Transgressing, overstepping.<BR>—2 Of fence, transgression, injury; केवलं न सहते विलङ्घनम् Ki. 13. 55.<BR>—3 (pl.) Fasting, abstension from food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घित|विलंघित
विलङ्घित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Passed over or beyond, gone over.<BR>—2 Transgressed.<BR>—3 Surpassed, excelled.<BR>—4 Overcome, defeated.<BR>—5 Baffled, defied (as efforts); विलङ्घिताधोरणतीव्रयत्नाः R. 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलङ्घितम्
विलङ्घित + .{@-तम्@} Fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज्
विलज्ज् €6 Ā. To be bashful or modest, to blush, feel ashamed; यत्रांशुकाक्षेपविलज्जितानाम्<BR> Ku. 1. 14; R. 14. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज|विलज्जः
विलज्ज <i>a.</i> Shameless, unabashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलप्
विलप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To say, speak.<BR>—2 To lament, moan, bewail, cry, weep; विललाप विकीर्णमूर्धजा Ku. 4. 4;<BR> विललाप स बाष्पगद्गदम् R. 8. 43, 70; Bk. 6. 11; तामिह<BR> वृथा किं विलपामि Gīt. 3.<BR>—3 To prattle, talk idly, babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपनम्
विलपनम्<BR>—1 Talking.<BR>—2 Talking idly, chattering, prattle.<BR>—3 Lamenting. wailing; विलपनविनोदोऽप्यसुलभः U. 3. 30.<BR>—4 The sediment of any oily substance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विलपनविनोदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपनविनोदः|विलपनविनोद
विलपनम् + -विनोदः removing grief by weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपितम्
विलपितम्<BR>—1 Lamentation, wailing.<BR>—2 A wail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलापः|विलाप
विलापः Wailing, lamentation, a wail, moan; लङ्कास्त्रीणां पुनश्चक्रे<BR> विलापाचार्यकं शरैः R. 12. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलापनम्
विलापनम् An act causing lamentation, ruin; मद्विलापनमेतत्तु<BR> प्रतिबुद्धोऽस्मि संत्यज Mb. 12. 177. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलभ्
विलभ् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To remove, take away.<BR>—2 To grant, bestow.<BR>—3 To choose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्ब्|विलंब्
विलम्ब् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To hang down, hang from, be suspended from; बिभ्रत्या कौस्तुभं न्यासं<BR> स्तनान्तरविलम्बिनम् R. 10. 62.<BR>—2 To set, decline (as the sun &c.).<BR>—3 To stay or lag behind, stay or remain, wait, stand still; तां प्राङ्मुखीं<BR> तत्र निवेश्य तन्वीं क्षणं व्यलम्बन्त पुरो निषण्णाः Ku. 7. 13.<BR>—4 To delay, be retarded; विलम्बितफलैः कालं निनाय स मनोरथैः<BR> R. 1. 33; किं विलम्ब्यते त्वरितं तं प्रवेशय U. 1.<BR>—5 To rest or depend upon; कर्माणि निर्वाणविलम्बितानि Bhāg. 1. 16. 24.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To delay, detain.<BR>—2 To put off, retard, procrastinate, postpone.<BR>—3 To waste, lose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बः|विलम्ब|विलंब|विलंबः
विलम्बः<BR>—1 Hanging over, pendulousness.<BR>—2 Tardiness, delay, procrastination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बनम्
विलम्बनम्<BR>—1 Hanging down, depending.<BR>—2 Delay, procrastination; न कुरु नितम्बिनि गमनविलम्बनम् Gīt. 5;<BR> or तन्मुग्धे विफलं विलम्बनमसौ रम्योऽभिसारक्षणः <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिका|विलंबिका
विलम्बिका Constipation; a form of indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बित|विलंबित|विलम्बितं
विलम्बित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Hanging, depending.<BR>—2 Pendent, pendulous.<BR>—3 Depending on, closely connected with.<BR>—4 Tardy, delayed, retarded.<BR>—5 Slow (as time in music opp. to द्रुत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बितम्
विलम्बित + .{@-तम्@} Delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बितम्
विलम्बित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Slowly, tardily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1464-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्बिन्|विलंबिन्
विलम्बिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Hanging down, depending, pendent; नवाम्बुभिर्दूरविलम्बिनो घनाः<BR> Ś. 5. 12; शिरीषमागण्डविलम्बि केशरम् 6. 17; अलघुविलम्बिपयोधरोपरुद्धाः<BR> Śi. 4. 29, 59; Ku. 1. 14; Ki. 5. 6; R. 16. 14, 18. 26; Mk. 5. 13.<BR>—2 Delaying, dilatory, being slow; भवति विलम्बिनि विगलितलज्जा विलपति<BR> रोदिति वासकसज्जा Gīt. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलम्भः|विलम्भ|विलंभ|विलंभः
विलम्भः<BR>—1 Liberality.<BR>—2 A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयः|विलय
विलयः<BR>—1 Dissolution, liquefaction.<BR>—2 Destruction, death, end; नयतु मामात्मनोऽङ्गेषु विलयमम्बा U. 7.<BR>—3 Destruction or dissolution of the world; (विलयं गम् to be dissolved,<BR> to end, to be terminated; दिवसोऽनुमित्रमगमद्विलयम् Śi. 9. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयनम्
विलयनम्<BR>—1 Dissolving, liquefying, dissolution.<BR>—2 Corroding.<BR>—3 Removing, taking away.<BR>—4 Attenuating.<BR>—5 An attenuant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलला
विलला N. of a plant (Mar. अतिबला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलस्
विलस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To shine, flash, glitter; वियति च विललास तद्वदिन्दुर्विलसति<BR> चन्द्रमसो न यद्वदन्यः Bk. 10. 69; Me. 49; R. 13. 76.<BR>—2 To appear, arise, become manifest; प्रेम विलसति महत्तदहो Śi. 15. 14, 9. 87.<BR>—3 To sport, amuse oneself, play, frolic about sportively; कापि चपला<BR> मधुरिपुणा विलसति युवतिरधिकगुणा Gīt. 7; or हरिरिह मुग्धवधूनिकरे<BR> विलासिनि विलसति केलिपरे Gīt. 1; पर्यङ्के तया सह विललास H. 1.<BR>—4 To sound, echo, reverberate.<BR>—5 To act upon, work upon, show oneself; (खेदः) त्वयि विलसति<BR> तुल्यं वल्लभालोकनेन Māl. 3. 8.<BR>—6 To move about, dart, shoot upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसत्|विलसन्त्
विलसत् <i>pres. p.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसन्ती
विलसत् + .({@-न्ती@} <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Glittering, shining, bright.<BR>—2 Flashing, darting.<BR>—3 Waving.<BR>—4 Sportive, playful; see विलस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसनम्
विलसनम्<BR>—1 Glittering, flashing, gleaming.<BR>—2 Sporting, dallying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसित
विलसित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Glittering, shining, gleaming.<BR>—2 Appeared, manifested; तया विलसितेष्वेषु गुणेषु गुणवानिव Bhāg. 1. 2. 31.<BR>—3 Sportive, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसितम्
विलसित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Glittering, gleaming.<BR>—2 A gleam, flash; रोघोभुवां मुहुरमुत्र हिरण्मयीनां भासस्तडिद्विलसितानि<BR> विडम्बयन्ति Ki. 5. 46; Me. 83; V. 4.<BR>—3 Appearance, manifestation; as in अज्ञानविलसितम् &c.<BR>—4 Sport, play; dalliance, amorous or wanton gesture (fig. also); अतिपिशुनानि<BR> चैकान्तनिष्ठुरस्य दैवहतकस्य विलसितानि K.<BR>—5 Action or gesture in general.<BR>—6 Effect, fruit, result; सुकृतविलसितानां स्थानमूर्जस्वलानाम् Māl. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासः|विलास
विलासः<BR>—1 Sport, play, pastime.<BR>—2 Amorous pastime, diversion, pleasure; as in विलासमेखला R. 8. 64;<BR> so विलासकाननम्, विलासमन्दिरम् &c.<BR>—3 Coquetry, dalliance, affectation, wantonness, graceful movement or<BR> play, any feminine gesture indicative of amorous sentiment; यातं यच्च<BR> नितम्बयोर्गुरुतया मन्दं विलासादिव Ś. 2. 2; कविकुलगुरुः कालिदासो<BR> विलासः P. R. 1. 22; Śi. 9. 26.<BR>—4 Grace, beauty,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">Page1465-2</a>]<BR> elegance, charm; सहजविलासनिबन्धनं शरीरम् Māl. 2. 6.<BR>—5 Flash, gleam.<BR>—6 Liveliness, joviality (considered as a masculine virtue); शोभा विलासो<BR> माधुर्यं … पौरुषा गुणाः Daśarūpaka 2. 10.<BR>—7 Lust.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विलासकाननम्, विलासगृहम्, विलासमन्दिरम्, विलासचेष्टितम्, विलासभित्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासकाननम्
विलासः + -काननम् a pleasure-grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासगृहम्
विलासः + -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् a pleasure-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासमन्दिरम्
विलासः + -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् a pleasure-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासचेष्टितम्
विलासः + -चेष्टितम् amorous movement; लतासु तन्वीषु विलासचेष्टितम् Ku. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासभित्तिः|विलासभित्ति
विलासः + -भित्तिः a wall (only) in appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासनम्
विलासनम्<BR>—1 Sport, play, pastime.<BR>—2 Wantonness, dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासवती
विलासवती A wanton or amorous woman; विलासवतीसखः R. 9. 48;<BR> विलासवत्यो मनसि प्रवासिनामनङ्गसंदीपनमाशु कुर्वते Ṛs. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिका
विलासिका A drama in one act full of love-incidents; it is thus defined<BR> in S. D.:− शृङ्गारबहुलैकाङ्का दशलास्याङ्गसंयुता । विदूषकविटाभ्यां<BR> च पीठमर्देन भूषिता । हीना गर्भविमर्शाभ्यां संधिभ्यां हीननायका ।<BR> स्वल्पवृत्ता सुनेपथ्या विख्याता सा विलासिका ॥ 552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिन्
विलासिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sportive, playful, dallying, wanton, coquettish;<BR> विस्रस्तमंसादपरो विलासी R. 6. 14. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A sensualist, voluptuary, an amorous person; उपमानमभूद्विलासिनां<BR> करणं यत्तव कान्तिमत्तया Ku. 4. 5.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR>—4 A snake.<BR>—5 An epithet of Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 Of Śiva.<BR>—7 Of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिनी
विलासिनी<BR>—1 A woman (in general).<BR>—2 A coquettish or wanton woman; हरिरिह मुग्धवधूनिकरे विलासिनि विलसति<BR> केलिपरे Gīt. 1; Ku. 7. 69; Śi. 8. 5; R. 6. 17.<BR>—3 A wanton, harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलागम्
विलागम् (= पिलाटम् q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलायः|विलाय|विलायं
विलायः, विलायनम् Dissolution, destruction, end; परीक्षितोऽथ<BR> राजर्षेर्जन्मकर्मविलायनम् Bhāg. 1. 7. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलायनम्
विलायः, विलायनम् Dissolution, destruction, end; परीक्षितोऽथ<BR> राजर्षेर्जन्मकर्मविलायनम् Bhāg. 1. 7. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलालः|विलाल
विलालः<BR>—1 A cat (= बिडाल).<BR>—2 An instrument, a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिख्
विलिख् €6 P.<BR>—1 To write, inscribe.<BR>—2 To draw, paint, delineate, portray; विलिखति रहसि कुरङ्गमदेन<BR> भवन्तमसमशरभूतम् Gīt. 4.<BR>—3 To scratch, scrape, tear up; निध्नन् प्रोथेन पृथिवीं विलिखंश्चरणैरपि<BR> Mb. 3. 167. 19; मन्दं शब्दायमानो विलिखति शयनादुत्थितः क्ष्मां खुरेण<BR> K. P. 10; व्यलिखच्चञ्चुपुटेन पक्षती N. 2. 2; पादेन हैमं विलिलेख<BR> पीठम् R. 6. 15; Ku. 2. 23.<BR>—4 To implant, infix; तावन्तोऽपि विलिख्यन्ते हृदये शोकशङ्कवः H. 4. 72 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिखनम्
विलिखनम्<BR>—1 Scratching, scraping, writing.<BR>—2 The course of a river.<BR>—3 Dividing, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखः|विलेख
विलेखः A hole, cavity; छायातपविलेखं च Mb. 14. 45. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखा
विलेखः + .{@-खा@}<BR>—1 A scratch, mark.<BR>—2 A written contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखनम्
विलेखनम्<BR>—1 Scratching, scraping, making a mark or furrow.<BR>—2 Digging.<BR>—3 Uprooting.<BR>—4 Dividing, splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1465-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिङ्ग
विलिङ्ग <i>a.</i> Of a different gender. ˚स्थ <i>a.</i> Not to be understood; Mb. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्
विलिप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To smear, anoint, rub on; तथा हि नृत्याभिनयक्रियाच्युतं विलिप्यते<BR> मौलिभिरम्बरौकसाम् Ku. 5. 79; Bk. 3. 20, 15. 6; Śi. 16. 62.<BR>—2 To pollute, defile, taint, contaminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्त
विलिप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Anointed, besmeared, smeared over.<BR>—2 Polluted, stained, defiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्ता
विलिप्ता, विलिप्तिका A second (= ¹⁄₃₆₀₀ of a degree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्तिका
विलिप्ता, विलिप्तिका A second (= ¹⁄₃₆₀₀ of a degree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिम्पित
विलिम्पित <i>a.</i> Smeared, anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपः|विलेप
विलेपः<BR>—1 An unguent, an ointment.<BR>—2 Mortar.<BR>—3 Plaster (in general).<BR>—4 Anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपनम्
विलेपनम्<BR>—1 Smearing, anointing.<BR>—2 An ointment, unguent, any cosmetic or perfume for the body (such as<BR> saffron, sandal &c.); न स्नानं न विलेपनं न कुसुमं नालंकृता मूर्धजाः<BR> Bh. 2. 19; यान्येव सुरभिकुसुमधूपविलेपनादीनि K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपनी
विलेपनी<BR>—1 A woman scented with perfumes.<BR>—2 A woman beautifully dressed or attired (सुवेशा).<BR>—3 Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिका
विलेपिका, विलेपी, विलेप्यः<BR> Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपी
विलेपिका, विलेपी, विलेप्यः<BR> Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप्यः|विलेप्य
विलेपिका, विलेपी, विलेप्यः<BR> Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिका
विलेपिका A female anointer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिन्
विलेपिन् <i>a.</i> Viscous, sticky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विली
विली I. €4 Ā.<BR>—1 To cling or stick to, adhere to.<BR>—2 To rest on, settle down or alight on; पुरोऽस्य यावन्न भुवि व्यलीयत Śi. 1. 12.<BR>—3 To be dissolved, to melt away, be absorbed in; विलिल्ये यत्कुक्षिस्थितशिखिनि<BR> वातापिवपुषा Mv. 6. 60, 7. 14.<BR>—4 To vanish, disappear.<BR>—5 To perish. ━II. €9 P. To melt, liquefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीन|विलीनः
विलीन <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sticking to, clung or attached to.<BR>—2 Perched or settled on, alighting on.<BR>—3 Contiguous to, in contact with.<BR>—4 Melted, dissolved, liquefied.<BR>—5 Disappeared, vanished.<BR>—6 Dead, perished.<BR>—7 Infused into the mind, imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुञ्चनम्
विलुञ्चनम् Tearing off, peeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुड्
विलुड् <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To agitate, stir up, toss about.<BR>—2 To disturb, confuse.<BR>—3 To turn over, upset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडनम्
विलोडनम्<BR>—1 Agitating, shaking about, stirring up, churning; तात नोदाधिविलोडनं<BR> प्रति त्वद्विनाथ वयमुत्सहामहे Śi. 14. 83.<BR>—2 Splashing, sporting in (water); कदाचिन्मद्विलोडनासहिष्णुर्मामशपत् Dk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडित|विलोडितं
विलोडित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shaken, churned, stirred, agitated.<BR>—2 Rolling on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडितम्
विलोडित + .{@-तम्@} Butter-milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुण्ठनम्
विलुण्ठनम् Robbing, plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्
विलुप् €6 P.<BR>—1 To break off, pull out, cut off.<BR>—2 To seize, plunder, rob, carry off; उपकारं ध्वजीकृत्य सर्वमेवावलुम्पति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">Page1466-2</a>]<BR> H. 2. 97.<BR>—3 To mar, spoil, impair.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To destroy, ruin, cause to disappear; प्रियमत्यन्तविलुप्तदर्शनम्<BR> Ku. 4. 2 ‘for ever lost to view’.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To eat up; क्रव्याद्भिरङ्गलतिका नियतं विलुप्ता U. 3. 28; Mk. 1. 9.<BR>—5 To wipe or rub off. ━<i>Pass.</i> To be destroyed or lost, to perish,<BR> disappear; जराविलुप्तमानावमानचिन्तः Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्त
विलुप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Broken or torn off; छायासुप्तमृगः शकुन्तनिवहैर्विष्वग्विलुप्तच्छदः Pt. 2. 2.<BR>—2 Seized, snatched away, carried off.<BR>—3 Robbed, plundered.<BR>—4 Destroyed, ruined.<BR>—5 Impaired, mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुम्पकः|विलुम्पक|विलुंपक|विलुंपकः
विलुम्पकः A thief, robber, ravisher; तदद्य नः पापमुपैत्यनन्वयं<BR> यन्नष्टनाथस्य वसोर्विलुम्पकात् Bhāg. 1. 18. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपः|विलोप
विलोपः<BR>—1 Taking away, carrying off, seizure, plunder.<BR>—2 Loss, destruction, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपनम्
विलोपनम्<BR>—1 Cutting off.<BR>—2 Carrying away.<BR>—3 Destroying, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोप्तृ
विलोप्तृ <i>m.</i> A robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभ्
विलुभ् €4 P. To be disturbed or deranged, be disordered; दधद्विलुभितं<BR> वातैः केशरं वह्निपिङ्गलम् Bk. 9. 40. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To allure, entice, attract; स्मर यावन्न विलोभ्यसे दिवि Ku. 4. 20;<BR> अङ्गनास्तमधिकं व्यलोभयन् (मुखैः) R. 19. 10.<BR>—2 To divert, amuse, entertain; क्व दृष्टिं विलोभयामि Ś. 6; ललितलताविलोभ्यमाननयनो<BR> भवानुत्कण्ठां विनोदयतु V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभित
विलुभित <i>p. p.</i> Disordered, agitated.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विलुभितप्लव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभितप्लव
विलुभित + -प्लव <i>a.</i> going in an agitated manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभः|विलोभ
विलोभः Attraction, seduction, allurement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभनम्
विलोभनम्<BR>—1 Enticing, alluring.<BR>—2 An allurement, a temptation, seduction; प्रयुज्य सामाचरितं विलोभनं<BR> भयं विभेदाय धियः प्रदर्शितम् Ki. 14. 7; R. 8. 60.<BR>—3 Praise, flattery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभनीय
विलोभनीय <i>a.</i> Alluring, enticing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुल्
विलुल् €1 P.<BR>—1 To move to and fro.<BR>—2 To shake, make tremulous.<BR>—3 To disorder, derange, dishevel (as hair). ━<i>Caus.</i> To agitate, stir, disturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुलित
विलुलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Moving to and fro, unsteady, shaken, tossed about, tremulous; U. 3. 23.<BR>—2 Disordered, disarranged; गलितकुसुमदलविलुलितकेशा Gīt. 7.<BR>—3 Waving, fickle, unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलून
विलून <i>p. p.</i> Cut off, lopped off, clipt, cut asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक्
विलोक् €10 U.<BR>—1 To see, behold, look at, perceive; विलोक्य वृद्धोक्षमधिष्ठितं त्वया<BR> महाजनः स्मेरमुखो भविष्यति Ku. 5. 70; R. 2. 11, 6. 59.<BR>—2 To search for, look out for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकः|विलोक
विलोकः, -विलोकनम्<BR>—1 Seeing, looking at, observing; नगविलोकनविस्मितमानसः Ki. 5. 16.<BR>—2 Sight, observation; विलोकनेनैव तवामुना मुने कृतः कृतार्थोऽस्मि<BR> निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनम्
विलोकः, -विलोकनम्<BR>—1 Seeing, looking at, observing; नगविलोकनविस्मितमानसः Ki. 5. 16.<BR>—2 Sight, observation; विलोकनेनैव तवामुना मुने कृतः कृतार्थोऽस्मि<BR> निबर्हितांहसा Śi. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1466-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकित|विलोकितं
विलोकित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Seen, observed, viewed, beheld.<BR>—2 Examined, thought about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकितम्
विलोकित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A look, glance; कृत इव मुग्धविलोकितोपदेशः Ś. 2. 3.<BR>—2 Observation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनम्
विलोचनम् The eye; R. 7. 8; Ku. 4. 1, 3. 67; तृष्णालोलविलोचने<BR> कलयति प्राचीं चकोरीगणे । Bv. 1. 4; also seeing, sight. ━<i>a.</i> Distorting<BR> the eyes (विपरीतदृष्टि); शत्रुर्मित्रमुखो यश्च जिह्मप्रेक्षी विलोचनः<BR> Mb. 12. 168. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विलोचनाम्बु, विलोचनपथः, विलोचनपातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनाम्बु|विलोचनांबु
विलोचनम् + -अम्बु <i>n.</i> tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनपथः|विलोचनपथ
विलोचनम् + -पथः the range of vision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनपातः|विलोचनपात
विलोचनम् + -पातः a glance, look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोटकः|विलोटक
विलोटकः A kind of fish; Clupea Cultrata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोम|विलोमं|विलोमः
विलोम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Inverted, reverse, inverse, contrary, opposite.<BR>—2 Produced in the reverse order.<BR>—3 Backward.<BR>—4 Hairless.<BR>—5 Refractory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमः|विलोम|विलोमं
विलोम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 Reverse order, inversion.<BR>—2 A dog.<BR>—3 A snake.<BR>—4 N. of a Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमम्
विलोम + .{@-मम्@} A water-wheel, machine for raising water from a well.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विलोमोत्पन्न, विलोमज, विलोमजात, विलोमवर्ण, विलोमक्रिया, विलोमविधिः, विलोमजिह्वः, विलोमरसनः, विलोमत्रैराशिकम्, विलोमपाठः, विलोमविधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमोत्पन्न
विलोम + -उत्पन्न, -ज, -जात, -वर्ण <i>a.</i> ‘born in the reverse order’;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> born of a mother whose caste is superior to the fatherʼs; cf.<BR> प्रतिलोमज also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमज
विलोम + -उत्पन्न, -ज, -जात, -वर्ण <i>a.</i> ‘born in the reverse order’;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> born of a mother whose caste is superior to the fatherʼs; cf.<BR> प्रतिलोमज also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमजात
विलोम + -उत्पन्न, -ज, -जात, -वर्ण <i>a.</i> ‘born in the reverse order’;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> born of a mother whose caste is superior to the fatherʼs; cf.<BR> प्रतिलोमज also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमवर्ण|विलोमवर्णः
विलोम + -उत्पन्न, -ज, -जात, -वर्ण <i>a.</i> ‘born in the reverse order’;<BR> <i>i. e.</i> born of a mother whose caste is superior to the fatherʼs; cf.<BR> प्रतिलोमज also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमक्रिया
विलोम + -क्रिया, -विधिः<BR>—1 a reverse action.<BR>—2 a rule of inversion (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमविधिः|विलोमविधि
विलोम + -क्रिया, -विधिः<BR>—1 a reverse action.<BR>—2 a rule of inversion (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमजिह्वः|विलोमजिह्व
विलोम + -जिह्वः, -रसनः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमरसनः|विलोमरसन
विलोम + -जिह्वः, -रसनः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमत्रैराशिकम्
विलोम + -त्रैराशिकम् rule of three inverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमपाठः|विलोमपाठ
विलोम + -पाठः recitation in reverse order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमविधिः|विलोमविधि
विलोम + -विधिः<BR>—1 reversed ceremony.<BR>—2 (Arith.) rule of inversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमी
विलोमी The emblic myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
विलोल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Shaking about, trembling, tremulous, unsteady, rolling, waving, tossing<BR> about; पृषतीषु विलोलमीक्षितम् R. 8. 59; Ku. 5. 8; Śi. 8. 8, 15. 62, 20. 42;<BR> Ve. 2. 24, 28; R. 7. 41, 16. 68.<BR>—2 Loose, disordered, dishevelled (as hair); दधती विलोलकबरीकमाननम् U. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलनम्
विलोलनम्<BR>—1 Shaking.<BR>—2 Stirring, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोहित|विलोहितः
विलोहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of a purple colour.<BR>—2 Reddish, red; धनुर्धरः कोपविलोहिताक्षः R. 16. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोहितः|विलोहित
विलोहित + .{@-तः@} N. of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोहिता
विलोहित + .{@-ता@} One of the tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्ल|विल्लं
विल्ल See बिल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्व|विल्वं|विल्वः
विल्व See बिल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षा
विवक्षा<BR>—1 A desire to speak.<BR>—2 Wish, desire.<BR>—3 Meaning, sense.<BR>—4 Intention, purpose.<BR>—5 Uncertainty, doubt, hesitation; किं ते विवक्षया वीर जहि भीष्मं<BR> महारथम् Mb. 6. 117. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षित|विवक्षितः
विवक्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Intended to be said or spoken; विवक्षितं ह्यनुक्तमनुतापं जनयति Ś. 3.<BR>—2 Meant, intended, purposed.<BR>—3 Wished, desired.<BR>—4 Favourite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षितम्
विवक्षित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Purpose, intention.<BR>—2 Sense, meaning.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवक्षितवचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षितवचन
विवक्षित + -वचन <i>a.</i> meant to express some sense, meant to be useful<BR> by expressing their sense; किं विवक्षितवचना मन्त्रा उताविवक्षितवचनाः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 1. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षु
विवक्षु <i>a.</i> Wishing or about to speak; पुनर्विवक्षुः स्फुरितोत्तराधरः Ku. 5. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवञ्चिषु|विवंचिषु
विवञ्चिषु <i>a.</i> Crafty, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवद्
विवद् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To quarrel, dispute; परस्परं विवदमानौ भ्रातरौ.<BR>—2 To be at variance, to conflict, be in opposition; परस्परं विवदमानानां<BR> शास्त्राणाम् H. 1.<BR>—3 To contend (as in a court of law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवदनम्
विवदनम् Quarrel, litigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादः|विवाद
विवादः<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A dispute, contest, contention, controversy, discussion, debate,<BR> quarrel, strife; अलं विवादेन Ku. 5. 82; एतयोर्विवाद एव मे न<BR> रोचते M. 1; एकाप्सरःप्रार्थितयोर्विवादः R. 7. 53; विक्रीते करिणि<BR> किमङ्कुशे विवादः Subhāṣ.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Argument, argumentation, discussion.<BR>—2 Contradiction; एष विवाद एव प्रत्याययति Ś. 7.<BR>—3 A litigation, law-suit, contest at law; सीमाविवादः, विवादपदम्<BR> &c.; (it is thus defined:− ऋणादिदायकलहे द्वयोर्बहुतरस्य वा विवादो<BR> व्यवहारश्च); see व्यवहार also.<BR>—4 Crying aloud, sounding.<BR>—6 An order, command; तस्याननादुच्चरितो विवादश्चस्खाल वेलास्वपि नार्णवानाम् R. 18. 43.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवादार्थिन्, विवादपदम्, विवादवस्तु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादार्थिन्
विवादः + -अर्थिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a litigant.<BR>—2 a plaintiff, complainant, prosecutor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादपदम्
विवादः + -पदम् a title of dispute; विवादपदनिबन्धः Kau. A. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादवस्तु
विवादः + -वस्तु <i>n.</i> the subject of dispute, the matter at issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादिन्
विवादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Disputing, contending, disputatious, quarrelling.<BR>—2 Litigating. ━<i>m.</i> A litigant, party in a law suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवत्सा
विवत्सा A calfless cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधः|विवध
विवधः<BR>—1 A yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>—2 A road, high-way.<BR>—3 A load, burden.<BR>—4 Storing grain; provisions.<BR>—5 A pitcher.<BR>—6 The income which a king obtains from his subjects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधिकः|विवधिक
विवधिकः<BR>—1 A carrier of loads, porter.<BR>—2 A pedlar, hawker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधा
विवधा<BR>—1 A yoke.<BR>—2 Chain of fetters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरम्
विवरम्<BR>—1 A fissure, hole, cavity, hollow, vacuity; यच्चकार विवरं शिलाघने<BR> ताडकोरसि स रामसायकः R. 11. 18, 9. 61, 19. 7; धीरनादभरितकर्णविवरं<BR> प्रिये मदयन्तिके इति व्याहरति Māl. 7.<BR>—2 An interstice, interval, intervening space; तानहं विवरं दृष्ट्वा<BR> प्राहिण्वं यमसादनम् Mb. 3. 171. 29; Bhāg. 5. 10. 12; अयमरविवरेभ्यश्चातकैर्निष्पतद्भिः Ś. 7. 7.<BR>—3 A solitary place; विवरेऽपि नैनमनिगूढमभिभवितुमेष पारयन् Ki. 12. 37.<BR>—4 A fault, flaw, defect, weak point.<BR>—5 A breach, wound.<BR>—6 The number ‘nine’.<BR>—7 Expansion, opening, widening.<BR>—8 The lower region (पाताल); ज्योतिषां विवराणां च यथेदमसृजद्विभुः<BR> Bhāg. 6. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरः|विवर|विवरं
विवरम् + .{@-रः@} Expansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवरनालिका, विवरप्रवेशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरनालिका
विवरम् + -नालिका a flute, fife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरप्रवेशः
विवरम् + -प्रवेशः entrance into a chasm (one of the means of getting oneʼs<BR> desired object); Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ण|विवर्णः
विवर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Colourless, pale, wan, pallid; नरेन्द्रमार्गाट्ट इव प्रपेदे विवर्णभावं<BR> स स भूमिपालः R. 6. 67.<BR>—2 Discoloured, deprived of water (as a gem.); विवर्णमणीकृतम् (कनकवलयम्) Ś. 3. 12.<BR>—3 Low, vile.<BR>—4 Ignorant, stupid, unlettered.<BR>—5 Bad-coloured; Mb. 12. 36. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्णः|विवर्ण
विवर्ण + .{@-र्णः@} An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">Page1468-1</a>]<BR> outcast, a man belonging to low caste.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवर्णभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1467-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्णभावः|विवर्णभाव
विवर्ण + -भावः paleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्णित
विवर्णित <i>p. p.</i> Disapproved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवल्ग्
विवल्ग् €1 P. To leap, jump, spring; कृतभुजध्वनि वल्गु विवल्गतोः Ki. 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवश|विवशः
विवश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uncontrolled, independent, unsubdued.<BR>—2 Having lost control over oneself, dependent, subject, under control<BR> (of another), helpless; विवशां धर्षयित्वा च कां त्वं प्रीतिमवाप्स्यसि<BR> Mb. 3. 281. 22; परीता रक्षोभिः श्रयति विवशा कामपि दशाम् Bv. 1. 83;<BR> मित्रस्नेहाद्विवशमधुना साहसे मां नियुङ्क्ते Mu. 6. 18; जातं<BR> जातमवश्यमाशु विवशं मृत्युः करोत्यात्मसात् Bh. 3. 105; Śi. 20. 58;<BR> सोद्योगं नरमायान्ति विवशाः सर्वसंपदः H. 1. 151; Mv. 6. 32, 63;<BR> Bhāg. 1. 1. 14.<BR>—3 Insensible, not master of oneself; विवशा कामवधूर्विबोधिता Ku. 4. 1.<BR>—4 Dead, perished; उपलब्धवती दिवश्च्युतं विवशा शापनिवृत्तिकारणम् R. 8. 82.<BR>—5 Desirous or apprehensive of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्
विवस् I. €1 P.<BR>—1 To dwell abroad.<BR>—2 To live, dwell.<BR>—3 To spend, pass (time).<BR>—4 To retire, withdraw; इच्छन्नितो विवसितुं गणयन् स्वमासान् Bhāg. 3. 31. 17.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> To banish, send into exile; अस्त्रहेतोर्महाबाहुरमितात्मा<BR> विवासितः Mb. 3. 86. 2; कृते सौभागिनेयस्य भरतस्य विवासितौ Bk. 4. 35.<BR>━II. €2 Ā.<BR>—1 To exchange clothes.<BR>—2 To wear, put on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासः|विवास
विवासः, -विवासनम्<BR>—1 Banishment, sending into exile, expulsion; रामस्य गात्रमसि दुर्वहगर्भखिन्नसीताविवासनपटोः<BR> करुणा कुतस्ते U. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Separation from; प्रियैर्विवासो बहुशः संवासश्चाप्रियैः सह Mb. 14. 16. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासनम्
विवासः, -विवासनम्<BR>—1 Banishment, sending into exile, expulsion; रामस्य गात्रमसि दुर्वहगर्भखिन्नसीताविवासनपटोः<BR> करुणा कुतस्ते U. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Separation from; प्रियैर्विवासो बहुशः संवासश्चाप्रियैः सह Mb. 14. 16. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासकाले
विवासः, -विवासनम् + .{@-विवासकाले@} <i>ind.</i> At the time of day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासित
विवासित <i>p. p.</i> Banished, exiled, expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवसन|विवसनः
विवसन <i>a.</i> Naked, unclothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवसनः|विवसन
विवसन + .{@-नः@} A Jaina mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वत्|विवस्वन्त्
विवस्वत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sun; त्वष्टा विवस्वतमिवोल्लिलेख Ki. 17. 48, 5. 48; R. 10. 30, 17. 48;<BR> एकः श्लाघ्यो विवस्वान् परहितकरणायैव यस्य प्रयासः Nāg. 3. 18.<BR>—2 N. of Aruṇa.<BR>—3 N. of the present Manu.<BR>—4 A god.<BR>—5 The <i>Arka</i> plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वती
विवस्वत् + .{@-ती@} <i>f.</i> The city of the sun; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवह्
विवह् €1 P.<BR>—1 To remove, take away, drive off.<BR>—2 To marry. ━<i>Caus.</i> To give in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवहः|विवह
विवहः N. of one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहः|विवाह
विवाहः Marriage; (Hindu lawgivers enumerate eight forms of marriage;<BR> ब्राह्मो दैवस्तथैवार्षः प्राजापत्यस्तथाऽऽसुरः । गांधर्वो राक्षसश्चैव<BR> पैशाचश्चाष्टमोऽधमः ॥ Ms. 3. 21; see Y. 1. 58-61 also; for explanation<BR> of these forms see s. v.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवाहचतुष्टयम्, विवाहदीक्षा, विवाहनेपथ्यम्, विवाहवेषः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहचतुष्टयम्
विवाहः + -चतुष्टयम् marrying four wives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहदीक्षा
विवाहः + -दीक्षा the marriage ceremony or rite; विवाहदीक्षां निरवर्तयद्<BR> गुरुः R. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहनेपथ्यम्
विवाहः + -नेपथ्यम्, -वेषः a marriage-dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहवेषः|विवाहवेष
विवाहः + -नेपथ्यम्, -वेषः a marriage-dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहित|विवाहितः
विवाहित <i>p. p.</i> Married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह्यः|विवाह्य
विवाह्यः<BR>—1 A son-in-law.<BR>—2 A bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाकः|विवाक
विवाकः A judge; cf. प्राड्विवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवारः|विवार
विवारः<BR>—1 Opening, expansion.<BR>—2 Expansion of the throat in the articulation of letters, (one of the<BR> Ābhyantara Prayatnas, opp. संवार); cf. विवृतमूष्मणां स्वराणां<BR> च Sk. on P. I. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविग्न
विविग्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Very much agitated or terrified; सकृद्विविग्नानपि हि प्रयुक्तं माधुर्यमीष्टे<BR> हरिणान् ग्रहीतुम् R. 18. 13; Ku. 1. 56.<BR>—2 Very angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविच्
विविच् €3. €7 U.<BR>—1 To separate, divide, remove from; विविनच्मि दिवः सुरान् Bk. 6. 36.<BR>—2 To discern, discriminate.<BR>—3 To judge, ascertain, determine; कर्मणां च विवेकार्थं धर्माधर्मौ<BR> व्यवेचयत् Ms. 1. 26; रे खल तव खलु चरितं विदुषामग्रे विविच्य<BR> वक्ष्यामि Bv. 1. 108.<BR>—4 To describe, treat of.<BR>—5 To tear up, rend asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्त|विविक्तं
विविक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Separated, detached, disjoined, abstracted; अपश्यमनेकानि गोसहस्राणि<BR> वर्णशो विविक्तानि Mb. 3. 198. 5; विविक्तवर्णाभरणा Ki. 14. 3.<BR>—2 Lonely, solitary, retired, sequestered; विविक्तदेशसेवित्वमरतिर्जनसंसदि Bg. 13. 10.<BR>—3 Single, alone.<BR>—4 Distinguished, discriminated; यथा विविक्तं यद्वक्त्रं गृह्णीमो युक्तिसंभवात्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 22. 9.<BR>—5 Judicious; वेदवित्सु विविक्तेषु प्रेत्य स्वर्गं समश्नुते Ms. 11. 6.<BR>—6 Pure, faultless; स्त्रीपुंभिदा न तु सुतस्य विविक्तदृष्टेः Bhāg. 1. 4. 5;<BR> प्रत्यग्रमज्जनविशेषविविक्तमूर्तिः Ratn. 1. 19.<BR>—7 Profound (as a judgment or thought).<BR>—8 Intent on.<BR>—9 Devoid of, free from; प्रसन्नदिक्पांसुविविक्तवातम् Ku. 1. 23.<BR>—10 Having the knowledge, known; विविक्तपरव्यथो व्यथामाचरति Bhāg. 5. 26. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तम्
विविक्त + .{@-क्तम्@} —1 A lonely or solitary place; विविक्तादृते नान्यदुत्सुकस्य<BR> शरणमस्ति V. 2; Ś. 5. 5; Śi. 8. 70; विविक्तसेवी Bg. 18. 52.<BR>—2 Loneliness, privacy, seclusion.<BR>—3 Clearness, purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्ता
विविक्त + .{@-क्ता@} An unlucky or ill-fated woman, one disliked by her husband (दुर्भगा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विविक्तसेविन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्तसेविन्
विविक्त + -सेविन् <i>a.</i> seeking solitude, lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवित्सा
विवित्सा Desire to know; प्रायो धर्मार्थकामेषु विवित्सायां च मानवाः ।<BR> हेतुनैव समीहन्ते आयुषो यशसः श्रियः ॥ Bhāg. 11. 7. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविध|विविधं
विविध <i>a.</i> Various, diverse, manifold, multiform, sundry; सोऽभिध्याय<BR> शरीरात् स्वात् सिसृक्षुर्विविधाः प्रजाः Ms. 1. 8, 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविधम्
विविध + .{@-धम्@} A variety of action or gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीतः|विवीत
विवीतः An enclosed or preserved spot of ground, such as pasture-land;<BR> पथि ग्रामविवीतान्ते क्षेत्रे दोषो न जायते Y. 2. 162; अकृष्यायां भूमौ<BR> पशुभ्यो विवीतानि प्रयच्छेत् Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवीताध्यक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीताध्यक्षः|विवीताध्यक्ष
विवीतः + -अध्यक्षः superintendent of pasture-lands; Kau. A.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृ
विवृ €5. €9 U.<BR>—1 To cover up, stop.<BR>—2 To open; स्वयं व्यवर्यन्त यथा तमो रवेः Bhāg. 10. 3. 50; स्वजनस्य<BR> हि दुःखमग्रतो विवृतद्वारमिवोपजायते Ku. 4. 26.<BR>—3 To unfold, disclose, reveal, show, display; द्वन्द्वानि भावं क्रियया<BR> विवव्रुः Ku. 3. 35; N. 9. 1; Bk. 7. 73; Śi. 16. 30.<BR>—4 To speak, utter; श्रवणकटु नृपाणामेकवाक्यं विवव्रुः R. 6. 85.<BR>—5 To teach, explain, expound; यस्मै मुनिर्ब्रह्म परं विवव्रे Mv. 2. 43.<BR>—6 To spread; दिशि दिशि निरपेक्षस्तावकीनं विवृण्वन् (परिमलम्)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">Page1469-1</a>]<BR> Bv. 1. 5.<BR>—7 To choose.<BR>—8 To unsheath a sword.<BR>—9 To part, comb (hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1468-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरणम्
विवरणम्<BR>—1 Displaying, expressing, unfolding, opening.<BR>—2 Exposing, laying bare or open.<BR>—3 Exposition, explanation, gloss, comment, interpretation.<BR>—4 Describing, description.<BR>—5 A sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत|विवृतं
विवृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Displayed, manifested, expressed.<BR>—2 Evident, clear, open.<BR>—3 Uncovered, exposed, laid bare; ज्ञातास्वादो विवृतजघनां को विहातुं<BR> समर्थः Me. 43.<BR>—4 Opened, unclosed, bare, open; कृष्णायसं च विवृतं धारयन् मुच्यते<BR> द्विजः Mb. 13. 136. 6.<BR>—5 Proclaimed.<BR>—6 Expounded, explained, commented upon; विवृत इव निरुक्तः Bhāg. 12. 11. 24.<BR>—7 Expanded, spread out.<BR>—8 Extensive, large, spacious.<BR>—9 Bare, barren (as ground).<BR>—10 Unhurt, woundless; Mb. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतम्
विवृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Open articulation.<BR>—2 Publicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृता
विवृत + .{@-ता@} A particular disease, ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतम्
विवृत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Openly.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवृताक्ष, विवृतद्वार, विवृतपौरुष, विवृतभाव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृताक्ष|विवृताक्षः
विवृत + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> large-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृताक्षः|विवृताक्ष
विवृत + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षः@}) a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतद्वार
विवृत + -द्वार <i>a.</i> with the gates thrown open; Ku. 4. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतपौरुष
विवृत + -पौरुष <i>a.</i> displaying valour; नित्यं विवृतपौरुषः Ms. 7. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतभाव
विवृत + -भाव <i>a.</i> candid, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतिः|विवृति
विवृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Display, manifestation.<BR>—2 Expansion.<BR>—3 Exposure, discovery.<BR>—4 Exposition, comment, interpretation, gloss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृज्
विवृज् €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To shun, avoid.<BR>—2 To make destitute of, deprive of.<BR>—3 To exclude.<BR>—4 To distribute, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जनम्
विवर्जनम् Leaving, excluding, abandoning; सर्वान् कामानवाप्नोति … … मुनिर्मांसविवर्जनात् Y. 1. 181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जित|विवर्ज्जित
विवर्जित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left, abandoned.<BR>—2 Shunned.<BR>—3 Deprived of, destitute of, without (usually in comp.); प्रधानोऽप्यप्रधानः<BR> स्याद्यदि सेवाविवर्जितः Pt. 1. 34.<BR>—4 Given, distributed.<BR>—5 That from which anything is subtracted; diminished by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्त
विवृक्त <i>p. p.</i> Left, abandoned, deserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्ता
विवृक्त + .{@-क्ता@} A woman disliked by her husband; cf. विविक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्
विवृत् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To turn round, roll, revolve, move round; अन्तर्बहिः परित एव विवर्तमानाम्<BR> (पश्यामि ताम्) Māl. 1. 40.<BR>—2 To turn or move about; संमार्जञ्जठरेणोर्वी विवर्तंश्च मुहुर्मुहुः<BR> Mb. 3. 167. 19.<BR>—3 To turn aside, bend; कश्चिद्विवृत्तत्रिकभिन्नहारः R. 6. 16; न<BR> विवृतो मदनो न च संवृतः Ś. 2. 12.<BR>—4 To become.<BR>—5 To turn away from, depart from, return.<BR>—6 To descend.<BR>—7 To attack, fall upon.<BR>—8 To take different forms; जीवितं च शरीरेण तेनैव सह जायते ।<BR> उभे सह विवर्तेते उभे सह विनश्यतः ॥ Mb. 12. 174. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तः|विवर्त|विवर्त्त|विवर्त्तः
विवर्तः<BR>—1 Turning round, revolving, whirling.<BR>—2 Rolling onward, moving about; संवर्तप्रकटविवर्तसप्तपाथोनाथोर्मिव्यतिकरविभ्रमप्रचण्डः Mv. 6. 26.<BR>—3 Rolling back, returning.<BR>—4 Dancing.<BR>—5 Alteration,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">Page1469-2</a>]<BR> modification, change of form, altered condition or state; शब्दब्रह्मणस्तादृशं<BR> विवर्तमितिहासं रामायणं प्रणिनाय U. 2; एको रसः करुण एव निमित्तभेदाद्भिन्नः<BR> पृथक् पृथगिवाश्रयते विवर्तान् U. 3. 47; अकाण्डशुष्काशनिपातरौद्रः<BR> क एष धातुर्विषमो विवर्तः Mv. 5. 57.<BR>—6 (In Vedānta phil.) An apparent or illusory form, an unreal appearance<BR> caused by अविद्या or human error; (this is a favourite doctrine of<BR> the Vedāntins according to whom the whole visible world is a mere illusion<BR> −an unreal and illusory appearance− while Brahman or Supreme Spirit<BR> is the only real entity; as a serpent (सर्प) is a <i>vivarta</i> of<BR> a rope (रज्जु), so is the world a <i>vivarta</i> of the real entity Brahman,<BR> and the illusion is removed by <i>Vidyā</i> or true knowledge; cf. Bhavabhūti:−<BR> विद्याकल्पेन मरुता मेघानां भूयसामपि । ब्रह्मणीव विवर्तानां क्वापि<BR> विप्रलयः कृतः ॥ U. 6. 6).<BR>—7 A heap, multitude, collection, an assemblage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवर्तवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तवादः|विवर्तवाद|विवर्त्तवाद
विवर्तः + -वादः the doctrine of the Vedāntins that the visible world is<BR> illusory and Brahman alone is the real entity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तनम्
विवर्तनम्<BR>—1 Revolving, revolution, whirling round.<BR>—2 Rolling about, turning round; शय्याप्रान्तविवर्तनैर्विगमयत्युन्निद्र<BR> एव क्षपाः Ś. 6. 5; Ve. 2. 8, 5. 40; Mv. 7. 5.<BR>—3 Rolling back, returning; लाङ्गूलचालनं क्ष्वेडा प्रतिवाचो विवर्तनम्<BR> Mb. 5. 72. 71; वप्रान्तस्खलितविवर्तनं पयोभिः Ki. 7. 11.<BR>—4 Rolling down, descending.<BR>—5 Existing, abiding.<BR>—6 Reverential salutation.<BR>—7 Passing through various states or existences.<BR>—8 An altered condition; पुनरकाण्डविवर्तनदारुणो प्रविशिनष्टि विधिर्मनसो<BR> रुजम् U. 4. 15; Māl. 4. 7.<BR>—9 Moving or wandering to and fro; तामिस्रादिषु चोग्रेषु नरकेषु विवर्तनम् Ms. 12. 75.<BR>—10 Transformation.<BR>—11 Circumambulating (प्रदक्षिणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तित|विवर्त्तित
विवर्तित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Turned or whirled round, revolved.<BR>—2 Moved round or about, rolling; विवर्तितभ्रूरियमद्य शिक्षते Ś. 1. 23.<BR>—3 Mangled, hacked, cut to pieces; संसक्तत्रुटितविवर्तितान्त्रजाल … Māl. 3. 17.<BR>—5 Unfolded.<BR>—6 Distorted, bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्त|विवृत्तं
विवृत्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Turned round.<BR>—2 Turning round, revolving, rolling, whirling; निहितविवृत्तलोचनेन Ki. 7. 34.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवृत्ताक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्ताक्षः|विवृत्ताक्ष
विवृत्त + -अक्षः a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्तिः|विवृत्ति
विवृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Turning round, whirling, revolution. मनोऽस्य जह्रुः शफरीविवृत्तयः<BR> Ki. 4. 3, 7. 12.<BR>—2 Going asunder; संवाता मुहुरनिलेन नीयमाने दिव्यस्त्रीजघनवरांशुके<BR> विवृत्तिम् Ki. 7. 14.<BR>—3 Expansion, development; विराजमतपत् स्वेन तेजसैषां विवृत्तये<BR> Bhāg. 3. 6. 10.<BR>—2 (In gram.) A hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृध्
विवृध् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To grow, increase.<BR>—2 To thrive, prosper.<BR>—3 To spring up, arise. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To increase, augment.<BR>—2 To promote, advance, further.<BR>—3 To raise, elevate.<BR>—4 To gratify, exhilarate.<BR>—5 To congratulate (one) upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धनम्
विवर्धनम्<BR>—1 Increasing.<BR>—2 Increase, augmentation, growth.<BR>—3 Enlargement, aggrandisement.<BR>—4 Cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1469-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धित
विवर्धित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Increased, augmented.<BR>—2 Advanced, promoted, furthered.<BR>—3 Gratified, satisfied.<BR>—4 Cut, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्ध
विवृद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Grown up. —2 Increased, augmented, heightened, enhanced, intensified<BR> (as grief, joy &c.).<BR>—2 Copious, large, plentiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्धिः|विवृद्धि
विवृद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Growth, increase, augmentation, development; ययुः शरीरावयवा विवृद्धिम्<BR> R. 18. 49; विवृद्धिमत्राश्नुवते वसूनि 13. 4; so शोक˚, हर्ष˚ &c.<BR>—2 Prosperity; लोकानां तु विवृद्धपर्थं मुखबाहूरुपादतः । ब्राह्मणं<BR> क्षत्रियं वैश्यं शूद्रं च निरवर्तयत् ॥ Ms. 1. 31.<BR>—3 Lengthening (of a vowel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकः|विवेक
विवेकः<BR>—1 Discrimination, judgment, discernment, discretion; काश्यपि यातस्तवापि<BR> च विवेकः Bv. 1. 68, 66; ज्ञातोऽयं जलधर तावको विवेकः 96;<BR> विवेकभ्रष्टानां भवति विनिपातः शतमुखः Bh. 2. 10.<BR>—2 Consideration, discussion, investigation; यच्छृङ्गारविवेकतत्त्वमपि<BR> यत् काव्येषु लीलायितम् Gīt. 12; so द्वैत˚, धर्म˚.<BR>—3 Distinction, difference, discriminating (between two things); नीरक्षीरविवेके<BR> हंसालस्यं त्वमेव तनुषे चेत् Bv. 1. 13; एकतामिव गतस्य विवेकः<BR> कस्यचिन्न महतोऽप्युपलेभे Ki. 9. 12; Bk. 17. 60.<BR>—4 (In Vedānta phil.) The power of distinguishing between the visible<BR> world and the invisible spirit, or of separating reality from mere semblance or illusion.<BR>—5 True knowledge. —6 A receptacle for water, basin, reservoir.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विवेकख्यातिः, विवेकज्ञ, विवेकज्ञानम्, विवेकदृश्वन्, विवेकपदवी, विवेकपरिपन्थिन्, विवेकभाज्, विवेकमन्थरता, विवेकविरहः, विवेकविश्रान्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकख्यातिः|विवेकख्याति
विवेकः + -ख्यातिः right knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकज्ञ
विवेकः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> judicious, discriminative; ते धन्यास्ते विवेकज्ञास्ते<BR> शस्या इह भूतले । आगच्छन्ति गृहे येषां कार्यार्थं सुहृदो जनाः ॥ Pt. 1. 262, 387.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकज्ञानम्
विवेकः + -ज्ञानम् the faculty of discrimination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकदृश्वन्
विवेकः + -दृश्वन् <i>m.</i> a discerning man; विवेकदृश्वत्वमगात् सुराणाम् Bk. 2. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकपदवी
विवेकः + -पदवी reflection, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकपरिपन्थिन्
विवेकः + -परिपन्थिन् obstructing right judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकभाज्
विवेकः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकमन्थरता
विवेकः + -मन्थरता feebleness of judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकविरहः|विवेकविरह
विवेकः + -विरहः ignorance, folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकविश्रान्त
विवेकः + -विश्रान्त <i>a.</i> foolish, unwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिन्
विवेकिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Discriminating, discreet, judicious; दम्भो भवति विवेकी Pt. 1. 418.<BR>—2 Separated. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A judge, discriminator.<BR>—2 A philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तृ
विवेक्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A judge.<BR>—2 A sage, philosopher.<BR>—3 A wise person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचनम्
विवेचनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Discrimination.<BR>—2 Discussion, consideration.<BR>—3 Settlement, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचना
विवेचनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Discrimination.<BR>—2 Discussion, consideration.<BR>—3 Settlement, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
विवोढृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A bridegroom, husband; आवरिष्ट विकटेन विवोढुर्वक्षसैव कुचमण्डलमन्या Śi. 10. 42.<BR>—2 A son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्वोक|विव्वोकः
विव्वोक See बिब्बोक; विव्वोकस्ते मुरविजयिनो वर्त्मपाती बभूव<BR> Ud. S. 43; गर्वाभिमानादिष्टेऽपि विव्वोकोऽनादरक्रिया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् €6 P. (विशति, विवेश, अविक्षत् वेक्ष्यति, वेष्टुम्, विष्ट)<BR>—1 To enter, go or enter into; यथा प्रदीप्तं ज्वलनं पतङ्गा विशन्ति<BR> नाशाय समृद्धवेगाः Bg. 11. 29; भोक्तुमन्तःपुरं विशेत् Ms. 7. 216;<BR> विवेश कश्चिज्जटिलस्तपोवनम् Ku. 5. 30; R. 6. 10; Me. 104; so दोलायमानेन<BR> चेतसा चिन्तां विवेश K. 199 ‘fell a-thinking’.<BR>—2 To go or come to, come into the possession of, fall<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">Page1470-2</a>]<BR> to the share of; उपदा विविशुः शश्वन्नोत्सेकाः कोशलेश्वरम् R. 4. 70.<BR>—3 To sit or settle down upon.<BR>—4 To penetrate, pervade.<BR>—5 To enter upon, undertake.<BR>—6 (In astr.) To come into conjunction with.<BR>—7 To appear on the stage.<BR>—8 To flow into (as a river or army); तत्सेना नरनाथानां पृतनाभिः<BR> पदे पदे । कुलापगेव कुल्याभिर्विशन्तीभिरवर्धत ॥ Rāj. T. 5. 140.<BR>—9 To befall (a death).<BR>—10 To belong to, exist for.<BR>—11 To mind, attend to (any business); Mb. 12. ━<i>Caus.</i> (वेशयति-ते)<BR> To cause to enter. ━<i>Desid.</i> (विविक्षति) To wish to enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशनम्
विशनम् Entering, entrance into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A man of the third caste, a Vaiśya.<BR>—2 A man in general. —3 People. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 People, subjects; शश्वद्येषु विशामनन्यविषयो रक्षाधिकारः स्थितः Mv. 1. 25.<BR>—2 A daughter; Ms. 3. 148.<BR>—3 Ved. Entrance.<BR>—4 A family, tribe, race.<BR>—5 A settlement, dwelling.<BR>—6 (pl.) Property, wealth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विट्पण्यम्, विट्पतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पण्यम्
विश् + -पण्यम् goods, merchandise; विट्पण्यमुद्धृतोद्धारं विक्रेयं वित्तवर्धनम् Ms. 10. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्पतिः|विट्पति
विश् + -पतिः (also विशांपतिः)<BR>—1 a king, lord of subjects.<BR>—2 a son-in-law; दौहित्रं विट्पतिं बन्धुमृत्विग्याज्यौ च भोजयेत् Ms. 3. 148.<BR>—3 a head-merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशम्
विशम् The fibres of the stalk of a lotus; cf. बिस.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशाकरः, विशकण्ठा, विशस्थूल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाकरः|विशाकर
विशम् + -आकरः a kind of plant (भद्रचूड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशकण्ठा|विशकंठा
विशम् + -कण्ठा a crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्थूल
विशम् + -स्थूल <i>a.</i> afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क्|विशंक्
विशङ्क् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To suspect, fear, have doubts or suspicions about; विशङ्कसे भीरु<BR> यतोऽवधीरणाम् Ś. 3. 14; सतीमपि ज्ञातिकुलैकसंश्रयां जनोऽन्यथा<BR> भर्तृमतीं विशङ्कते 5. 17.<BR>—2 To think to be, fancy, imagine; विशङ्कमाना रमितं कयापि जनार्दनं<BR> दृष्टवदेतदाह Gīt. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्क|विशंक|विशङ्कः
विशङ्क <i>a.</i> Fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्का
विशङ्क + .{@-ङ्का@} Fear, suspicion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कनीय
विशङ्कनीय <i>a.</i> Questionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कट|विशंकट|विशङ्कटः
विशङ्कट <i>a.</i> (-टा, -टी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Great, large, big; विशङ्कटो वक्षसि बाणपाणिः Bk. 2. 50; Śi. 13. 34.<BR>—2 Strong, vehement, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशङ्कटम्
विशङ्कट + .{@-टम्@} <i>ind.</i> Vehemently, intensely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद|विशदः
विशद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clear, pure, pellucid, clean, spotless; योगनिद्रान्तविशदैः पावनैरवलोकनैः<BR> R. 10. 14, 19. 39, 8. 3; प्रणयविशदां दृष्टिं वक्त्रे ददाति न शङ्किता<BR> Ratn. 3. 9; Ki. 5. 12.<BR>—2 White, of a pure white colour; निर्धौतहारगुलिकाविशदं हिमाम्भः<BR> R. 5. 70; Ku. 1. 44, 6. 25; Śi. 9. 26; Ki. 4. 23.<BR>—3 Bright, shining, beautiful; हिमव्यपायाद्विशदाधराणाम् Ku. 3. 33;<BR> ताम्बूलद्युतिविशदो विलासिनीनाम् Śi. 8. 70.<BR>—4 Clear, evident, manifest.<BR>—5 Calm, free from anxiety, at ease; जातो ममायं विशदः प्रकामम्<BR> (अन्तरात्मा) Ś. 4. 22; V. 3.<BR>—6 Tender, soft (to the touch).<BR>—7 Skilled in; fit for; Mk. 1, 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशदः|विशद
विशद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 A kind of smell (गन्ध); Mb. 12. 184. 28 (com. विशदः शाल्यन्नादौ).<BR>—3 A kind of touch (स्पर्श); Mb. 12. 184. 36 (com. विशदः उत्तमवस्त्रादेः).<BR> (विशदीकृ €8 U. ‘to explain, make clear, illustrate’.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1470-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशयः|विशय
विशयः<BR>—1 Doubt, uncertainty, the second of the five members of an Adhikaraṇa,<BR> q. v.; मुञ्चन्ति गुर्वशुचिताविशयेन किं न चक्राङ्कवैष्णवमनुग्रहणादि<BR> सर्वम् Viś. Guṇā. 368.<BR>—2 Refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशरः|विशर
विशरः<BR>—1 Splitting, bursting.<BR>—2 Slaughter, killing, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्य|विशल्यः
विशल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Free from trouble or anxiety, secure.<BR>—2 Free from thorns or darts; विशल्यौ चापि सुग्रीवः क्षणेनैतौ चकार<BR> ह । विशल्यया महौषध्या दिव्यमन्त्रप्रयुक्तया ॥ Mb. 3. 289. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्या
विशल्य + .{@-ल्या@} N. of several plants:− दन्ती, गुडूची, अजमोदा &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशल्यकरण, विशल्यकरणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्यकरण
विशल्य + -करण <i>a.</i> healing wounds inflicted by arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्यकरणी
विशल्य + -करणी a particular herb with medicinal properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्
विशस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To cut up, kill; U. 4.<BR>—2 To immolate, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसनम्
विशसनम्<BR>—1 Killing, slaughter, immolation; तस्यास्त्वं दुहितुस्तथा विशसनं<BR> किं दारुणेऽमृष्यथाः U. 4. 5; N. 19. 12.<BR>—2 Ruin.<BR>—3 Battle; शोणितोदां रथावर्तां कृत्वा विशसने नदीम् Mb. 7. 16. 43.<BR>—4 Cutting, dissecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसनः|विशसन|विशसनं
विशसनम् + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A sabre, crooked sword.<BR>—2 A sword in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसितृ
विशसितृ <i>m.</i> A dissector; Ms. 5. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त|विशस्तः
विशस्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cut up, hacked.<BR>—2 Rude, ill-mannered; P. VII. 2. 19.<BR>—3 Praised, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्तृ
विशस्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An immolator.<BR>—2 A Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त्र
विशस्त्र <i>a.</i> Weaponless, unarmed, defenceless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखः|विशाख
विशाखः<BR>—1 N. of Kārtikeya; वक्षो विशाखविशिखव्रणलाञ्छितं मे Mv. 2. 38.<BR>—2 An attitude in shooting (in which the archer stands with the feet a span apart).<BR>—3 A beggar, petitioner.<BR>—4 A spindle.<BR>—5 N. of Śiva.<BR>—6 N. of a god, frequently mentioned by Paṇini and Patañjali along with<BR> <i>Skanda</i>; <i>e. g.</i> see Mbh. on P. VI. 3. 26, VIII. 1. 15. ━<i>a.</i> also<BR> विशाखक; Branched, forked.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशाखजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखजः|विशाखज
विशाखः + -जः the orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखल|विशाखलं
विशाखल See विशाख (2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखा
विशाखा (usually in the dual) N. of the 16th lunar mansion consisting<BR> of two stars; किमत्र चित्रं यदि विशाखे शशाङ्कलेखामनुवर्तेते Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशातनम्
विशातनम्<BR>—1 Rending asunder, cutting off, destroying; नमस्ते देवदेवेश सनातन<BR> विशातन Mb. 7. 83. 18.<BR>—2 Setting free, delivering, releasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाप
विशाप <i>a.</i> Freed from a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशायः|विशाय
विशायः Sleeping in rotation, the rest enjoyed in rotation by the<BR> sentinels on watch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारणम्
विशारणम्<BR>—1 Splitting, rending.<BR>—2 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारद|विशारदः
विशारद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clever, skilful or proficient in, versed in, conversant with (usually<BR> in comp.); नानाशस्त्रप्रहरणाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">Page1471-2</a>]<BR> सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः Bg. 1. 9; मधुदानविशारदाः R. 9. 29, 8. 17.<BR>—2 Learned, wise.<BR>—3 Famous, celebrated.<BR>—4 Bold, confident.<BR>—5 Beautifully autumnal.<BR>—6 Lacking the gift of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारदः|विशारद
विशारद + .{@-दः@} The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाल|विशालः
विशाल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Large, great, extensive, spacious, broad, wide; गृहैर्विशालैरपि भूरिशालैः<BR> Śi. 3. 50; रथचरणविशालश्रोणिलोलेक्षणेन 11. 23, 17. 47; R. 2. 21, 6. 32;<BR> ते तं भुक्त्वा स्वर्गलोकं विशालम् Bg. 9. 21.<BR>—2 Rich or abounding in; श्रीविशालां विशालाम् Me. 30.<BR>—3 Eminent, illustrious, great, noble, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालः|विशाल
विशाल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A kind of deer.<BR>—2 A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाला
विशाल + .{@-ला@}<BR>—1 N. of the town Ujjayinī; पूर्वोद्दिष्टामनुसर पुरीं श्रीविशालां विशालाम् Me. 30.<BR>—2 N. of a river.<BR>—3 Colocynth (Mar. मोठी कंवडळ).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशालाक्ष, विशालकुलम्, विशालत्वच्, विशालविजयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालाक्ष|विशालाक्षः
विशाल + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> large-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालाक्षः|विशालाक्ष
विशाल + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षः@})<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Garuḍa.<BR>—3 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—4 N. of an ancient authority on the science of Govt. referred to by Kauṭilya; Kau. A. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालाक्षी
विशाल + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षी@}) an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालकुलम्
विशाल + -कुलम् a noble or eminent family; रुपयौवनसंपन्ना विशालकुलसंभवाः ।<BR> विद्याहीना न शोभन्ते निर्गन्धा इव किंशुकाः ॥ H.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालत्वच्
विशाल + -त्वच् <i>m.</i> Alstonia Scholaris (Mar. सातबीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालविजयः|विशालविजय
विशाल + -विजयः A kind of military array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालता
विशालता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Greatness, magnitude.<BR>—2 Eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालत्वम्
विशालता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Greatness, magnitude.<BR>—2 Eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिख|विशिखः
विशिख <i>a.</i> Crownless, crestless, pointless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिखः|विशिख
विशिख + .{@-खः@}<BR>—1 An arrow; माधव मनसिजविशिखभयादिव भावनया त्वयि लीना Gīt. 4;<BR> R. 5. 50; Mv. 2. 38.<BR>—2 A kind of reed.<BR>—3 An iron crow.<BR>—4 (In Math.) A versed sine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिखा
विशिखा<BR>—1 A spade.<BR>—2 A spindle.<BR>—3 A needle or pin.<BR>—4 A minute arrow.<BR>—5 A highway; विशिखायां सौवर्णिकप्रचारः Kau. A. 2; Śi. 15. 70.<BR>—6 A barberʼs wife.<BR>—7 A sick-room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशित
विशित <i>a.</i> Sharp, acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिपम्
विशिपम् [विशेः कपन् Uṇ. 3. 145]<BR>—1 A temple.<BR>—2 An abode, a house.<BR>—3 A palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्
विशिष् €7 P.<BR>—1 To particularize, individualize, specify, define.<BR>—2 To distinguish, discriminate.<BR>—3 To aggravate, heighten, enhance, intensify; पुनरकाण्डविवर्तनदारुणो<BR> विधिरहो विशिनष्टि मनोरुजम् Māl. 4. 7; U. 4. 15.<BR>—4 To surpass, excel; विशेषको वा विशिशेष यस्याः श्रियं त्रिलोकीतिलकः<BR> स एव Śi. 3. 63. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be different from; स्वदेहान्न व्यशिष्यत R. 17. 62.<BR>—2 To be better or higher than, surpass, excel, be preferable or superior<BR> to (often with abl.); तस्माद् दुर्गं विशिष्यते H. 3. 50; Mv. 7. 39;<BR> मौनात् सत्यं विशिष्यते Ms. 2. 83, 3. 203; (also with instr. and gen.);<BR> सर्वेषामेव दानानां ब्रह्मदानं विशिष्यते Ms. 4. 233. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To distinguish, particularize.<BR>—2 To surpass, excel; मदनमपि गुणैर्विशेषयन्ती Mk. 4. 4; M. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्ट|विशिष्टः
विशिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Distinguished, distinct.<BR>—2 Particular, special, peculiar, distinctive.<BR>—3 Characterized by, endowed with, possessed of, having.<BR>—4 Superior, best (of all), eminent, excellent, choice; विविष्टानि स्वकर्मसु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">Page1472-1</a>]<BR> Ms. 10. 80; विशिष्टाया विशेषेण संगमो गुणवान् भवेत् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टः|विशिष्ट
विशिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशिष्टाद्वैतवादः, विशिष्टकुल, विशिष्टबुद्धिः, विशिष्टवर्ण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1471-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टाद्वैतवादः|विशिष्टाद्वैतवाद
विशिष्ट + -अद्वैतवादः a doctrine of Rāmānuja which regards Brahman and<BR> Prakṛti as identical and real entities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टकुल
विशिष्ट + -कुल <i>a.</i> descended from an excellent race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टबुद्धिः|विशिष्टबुद्धि
विशिष्ट + -बुद्धिः <i>f.</i> a distinguishing knowledge, differentiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टवर्ण
विशिष्ट + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> of an eminent or excellent colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टता
विशिष्टता<BR>—1 Distinction, speciality.<BR>—2 Excellence, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष|विशेषः
विशेष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Peculiar.<BR>—2 Copious, abundant; आसीद्विशेषा फलपुष्पवृष्टिः R. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषः|विशेष
विशेष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 Discrimination, distinguishing between.<BR>—2 Distinction, difference; निर्विशेषो विशेषः Bh. 3. 50.<BR>—3 Characteristic difference, peculiar mark, special property, speciality,<BR> differentia; oft. in comp. and translated by ‘special’, ‘peculiar’ &c.;<BR> विशेषं नाधिगच्छामो गायतो राघवस्य च Rām. 7. 94. 14; प्रत्यादिष्टविशेषमण्डनविधिः Ś. 6. 5.<BR>—4 A favourable turn or crisis in sickness, a change for the better; अस्ति<BR> मे विशेषः Ś. 3 ‘I feel better’.<BR>—5 A limb, member; पुपोष लावण्यमयान् विशेषान् Ku. 1. 25.<BR>—6 A species, sort, variety, kind, mode (usually at the end of comp.);<BR> पञ्चत्वाय विशेषाय कल्पते भुवनैः सह Bhāg. 11. 23. 21; भूतविशेषः<BR> U. 4; परिमलविशेषान् Pt. 1; कदलीविशेषाः Ku. 1. 36.<BR>—7 A different or various object, various particulars (pl.); प्रासादास्त्वां<BR> तुलयितुमलं यत्र तैस्तैर्विशेषैः Me. 66, 59.<BR>—8 Excellence, superiority, distinction; usually at the end of comp. and<BR> translated by ‘excellent’, ‘distinguished’, ‘pre-eminent’, ‘choice’, &c.;<BR> अनुभावविशेषात्तु R. 1. 37; वपुर्विशेषेषु Ku. 5. 31; R. 2. 7, 6. 5;<BR> Ki. 9. 58; so आकृतिविशेषाः ‘excellent forms’, अतिथिविशेषः<BR> ‘a distinguished guest’ &c.<BR>—9 A peculiar attribute, the eternal distinguishing nature of each of<BR> the nine <i>dravyas</i>; अयमस्माद् व्यावृत्त इति व्यावृत्तिबुद्धिमात्रहेतुर्विशेषः<BR> Tarka K. (these viśeṣas are said to inhere in the atoms of the Earth,<BR> Water, Light, and Air and the five eternal substances, Ether, Time, Space,<BR> Soul and Mind.); पञ्च चैव विशेषा वै तथा पञ्चेन्द्रियाणि च Mb. 12. 306. 29;<BR> Bhāg. 2. 5. 29.<BR>—10<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Individuality, particularity.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A particular instance; उक्तिरर्थान्तरन्यासः स्यात् सामान्यविशेषयोः<BR>—11 A category, predicament.<BR>—12 A mark on the forehead with sandal, saffron &c.<BR>—13 A word which limits or qualifies the sense of another; see विशेषण.<BR>—14 N. of the mundane egg.<BR>—15 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech, said to be of three kinds; it is thus<BR> defined by Mammaṭa:− विना प्रसिद्धमाधारमाधेयस्य व्यवस्थितिः । एकात्मा<BR> युगपद्वृत्तिरेकस्यानेकगोचरा । अन्यत् प्रकुर्वतः कार्यमशक्यान्यस्य<BR> वस्तुनः । तयैव करणं चेति विशेषस्त्रिविधः स्मृतः ॥ K. P. 10.<BR>—16 (In geom.) The hypotenuse.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशेषातिदेशः, विशेषोक्तिः, विशेषकरणम्, विशेषगुणः, विशेषज्ञ, विशेषविद्, विशेषधर्मः, विशेषपतनीयम्, विशेषभावना, विशेषलक्षणम्, विशेषलिङ्गम्, विशेषवचनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषातिदेशः|विशेषातिदेश
विशेष + -अतिदेशः a special supplementary rule, special extended application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषोक्तिः|विशेषोक्ति
विशेष + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> a figure of speech in which an effect is represented<BR> as not taking place though the usual necessary causes exist; विशेषोक्तिरखण्डेषु<BR> कारणेषु फलावचः K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">Page1472-2</a>]<BR> हृदि स्नेहक्षयो नाभूत् स्मरदीपे ज्वलत्यपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकरणम्
विशेष + -करणम् improvement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषगुणः|विशेषगुण
विशेष + -गुणः<BR>—1 a special or distinguishing property.<BR>—2 (in phil.) such guṇa as is not produced (like संयोग, पृथक्त्व<BR> &c.) by the union of two things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषज्ञ
विशेष + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing distinctions, critical, connoisseur.<BR>—2 learned, wise; अज्ञः सुखमाराध्यः सुखतरमाराध्यते विशेषज्ञः Bh. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषविद्
विशेष + -ज्ञ, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 knowing distinctions, critical, connoisseur.<BR>—2 learned, wise; अज्ञः सुखमाराध्यः सुखतरमाराध्यते विशेषज्ञः Bh. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषधर्मः|विशेषधर्म|विशेषधर्म्म
विशेष + -धर्मः<BR>—1 A peculiar duty.<BR>—2 A special law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषपतनीयम्
विशेष + -पतनीयम् A particular crime; नीचाभिगमनं गर्भपातनं भर्तृहिंसनम् ।<BR> विशेषपतनीयानि स्त्रीणामेतान्यपि ध्रुवम् ॥ Y. 3. 297.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषभावना
विशेष + -भावना (in Arith.) a kind of method in extracting roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषलक्षणम्
विशेष + -लक्षणम्, -लिङ्गम् a special or characteristic mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषलिङ्गम्
विशेष + -लक्षणम्, -लिङ्गम् a special or characteristic mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषवचनम्
विशेष + -वचनम् a special text or precept. {@-विधिः, -शास्त्रम्@} a special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषक|विशेषकः
विशेषक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Distinguishing, distinctive.<BR>—2 Restrictive; ननु विशेषकः शब्दः श्रूयते ब्रह्मवर्चसकमिति ।<BR> नैष विशेषकः । उपाधिकर एषः । ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकः|विशेषक
विशेषक + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A distinguishing feature or characteristic, an attribute.<BR>—2 A discriminative or distinguishing quality.<BR>—3 A mark on the forehead with sandal, saffron &c.<BR>—4 Drawing lines of painting on the face and person with coloured unguents<BR> and cosmetics; प्रत्याख्यातविशेषकं कुरबकं श्यामावदातारुणम् M. 3. 5;<BR> स्वेदोद्गमः किंपुरुषाङ्गनानां चक्रे पदं पत्रविशेषकेषु Ku. 3. 33;<BR> R. 9. 29; Śi. 3. 63, 10. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकम्
विशेषक + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A distinguishing feature or characteristic, an attribute.<BR>—2 A discriminative or distinguishing quality.<BR>—3 A mark on the forehead with sandal, saffron &c.<BR>—4 Drawing lines of painting on the face and person with coloured unguents<BR> and cosmetics; प्रत्याख्यातविशेषकं कुरबकं श्यामावदातारुणम् M. 3. 5;<BR> स्वेदोद्गमः किंपुरुषाङ्गनानां चक्रे पदं पत्रविशेषकेषु Ku. 3. 33;<BR> R. 9. 29; Śi. 3. 63, 10. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकः|विशेषक
विशेषक + .{@-कः@} A particular form of speech; cf. विशेषोक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषकम्
विशेषक + .{@-कम्@} A group of three stanzas forming one grammatical sentence;<BR> द्वाभ्यां युग्ममिति प्रोक्तं त्रिभिः श्लोकैर्विशेषकम् । कलापकं चतुर्भिः<BR> स्यात्तदूर्ध्वं कुलकं स्मृतम् ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषण|विशेषणं
विशेषण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attributive.<BR>—2 Distinctive; सूक्ष्मं विशेषणं तेषामवेक्षेच्छास्त्रचक्षुषा Mb. 12. 217. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणम्
विशेषण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Distinguishing, discrimination, particularization; भावनं ब्रह्मणः<BR> स्थानं धारणं सद्विशेषणम् Bhāg. 3. 26. 46.<BR>—2 Distinction, difference; स्वानुभूत्या तिरोभूतमायागुणविशेषणम् Bhāg. 3. 33. 25.<BR>—3 A word which particularizes, qualifies, or defines another, an adjective,<BR> attribute, epithet (opp. विशेष्य); भक्षयतिश्च नञ्विशेषणम् Ś. B. on MS. 6. 2. 19<BR> उपपन्नमिदं विशेषणं वायोः V. 3; विशेषणैर्यत्<BR> साकूतैरुक्तिः परिकरस्तु सः K. P. 10. (विशेषण is said to be of<BR> three kinds व्यावर्तक, विधेय, and हेतुगर्भ).<BR>—4 A distinguishing feature or mark.<BR>—5 Species, kind.<BR>—6 Surpassing, excelling; अस्य काव्यस्य कवयो न समर्था विशेषणे<BR> Mb. 1. 1. 73; पराक्रमेऽन्योन्यविशेषणेन Ki. 17. 32.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशेषणासिद्धः, विशेषणपदम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणासिद्धः|विशेषणासिद्ध
विशेषण + -असिद्धः N. of a kind of हेत्वाभास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणपदम्
विशेषण + -पदम् a title of honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषतस्
विशेषतस्, विशेषेण, विशेषात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Especially, particularly.<BR>—2 In proportion to; निःस्वेभ्यो देयमेतेभ्यो दानं विद्याविशेषतः Ms. 11. 2.<BR>—3 Individually, singly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषेण
विशेषतस्, विशेषेण, विशेषात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Especially, particularly.<BR>—2 In proportion to; निःस्वेभ्यो देयमेतेभ्यो दानं विद्याविशेषतः Ms. 11. 2.<BR>—3 Individually, singly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषात्
विशेषतस्, विशेषेण, विशेषात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Especially, particularly.<BR>—2 In proportion to; निःस्वेभ्यो देयमेतेभ्यो दानं विद्याविशेषतः Ms. 11. 2.<BR>—3 Individually, singly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषित|विशेषितं
विशेषित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Distinguished.<BR>—2 Defined, particularized.<BR>—3 Distinguished by an attribute.<BR>—4 Superior, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्य|विशेष्यः
विशेष्य, -विशेषणीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be distinguished.<BR>—2 Chief, superior; उपपन्नं हि यच्चेष्टा विशिष्येत विशेष्यया Mb. 12. 237. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणीय
विशेष्य, -विशेषणीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be distinguished.<BR>—2 Chief, superior; उपपन्नं हि यच्चेष्टा विशिष्येत विशेष्यया Mb. 12. 237. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्यम्
विशेष्य, -विशेषणीय + .{@-ष्यम्@} The word qualified or limited by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">Page1473-1</a>]<BR> an adjective, the object to be defined or particularized by another word;<BR> a noun; विशेष्यं नाभिधा गच्छेत् क्षीणशक्तिर्विशेषणे K. P. 2.<BR>—2 A substantive, noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1472-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशील
विशील <i>a.</i> Ill-behaved, immoral, wicked; Ms. 5. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुध्
विशुध् €4 P. To be purified. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To purify.<BR>—2 To free from suspicion.<BR>—3 To justify.<BR>—4 (In alg.) To subtract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्ध|विशुद्धं
विशुद्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Purified, cleansed.<BR>—2 Pure, free from vice, sin, or imperfection.<BR>—3 Spotless, stainless.<BR>—4 Correct, accurate.<BR>—5 Virtuous, pious, straightforward; विशुद्धमुग्धः कुलकन्यकाजनः Māl. 7. 1.<BR>—6 Humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धम्
विशुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} A kind of mystical circle (चक्र) in the body.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशुद्धधिषण, विशुद्धधी, विशुद्धप्रकृति, विशुद्धसत्त्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धधिषण
विशुद्ध + -धिषण, -धी <i>a.</i> having the mind purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धधी
विशुद्ध + -धिषण, -धी <i>a.</i> having the mind purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धप्रकृति
विशुद्ध + -प्रकृति <i>a.</i> of virtuous disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धसत्त्व
विशुद्ध + -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> of a pure character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धिः|विशुद्धि
विशुद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Purification; तदङ्गसंसर्गमवाप्य कल्पते ध्रुवं चिताभस्मरजो<BR> विशुद्धये Ku. 5. 79; उपविश्यासने युञ्ज्याद्योगमात्मविशुद्धये Bg. 6. 12;<BR> Ms. 6. 69, 11. 53.<BR>—2 Purity, complete purity; हेम्नः संलक्ष्यते ह्यग्नौ विशुद्धिः श्यामिकापि<BR> वा R. 1. 10, 12. 48.<BR>—3 Correctness, accuracy.<BR>—4 Rectification, removal of error.<BR>—5 Similarity, equality.<BR>—6 (In alg.) A subtractive quantity.<BR>—7 Expiation, atonement; इयं विशुद्धिरुदिता प्रमाप्याकामतो द्विजम् Ms. 11. 89.<BR>—8 Settlement (of a debt).<BR>—9 Perfect knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधनम्
विशोधनम्<BR>—1 Cleaning, clearing (fig. also); राज्यकण्टकविशोधनोद्यतः Vikr. 5. 1.<BR>—2 Purifying, freeing from sin, defect &c.; घृतप्राशो विशोधनम् Ms. 11. 143.<BR>—3 Expiation, atonement.<BR>—4 A laxative; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधनी
विशोधनम् + .{@-नी, विशोधिनी@} Tiaridium Indicum (Mar. नाय, भुरुंडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधिनी
विशोधनम् + .{@-नी, विशोधिनी@} Tiaridium Indicum (Mar. नाय, भुरुंडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोध्य
विशोध्य <i>a.</i> To be purified, cleansed or corrected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोध्यम्
विशोध्य + .{@-ध्यम्@} A debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशून्य
विशून्य <i>a.</i> Perfectly empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशूल
विशूल <i>a.</i> Without (<i>i. e.</i> not possessing) a spear; दुर्जयो<BR> लवणः शूली विशूलः प्रार्थ्यतामिति R. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशृङ्खल|विशृंखल|विशृङ्खलः
विशृङ्खल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Without fetters (lit.).<BR>—2 Unfettered, unchecked, unrestrained, uncurbed (fig.); विशृङ्खलं<BR> शृङ्खलकाः प्रतिस्थिरे Śi. 12. 7; करिकुम्भतुलामुरोजयोः क्रियमाणां<BR> कविभिर्विशृङ्खलैः Bv. 2. 177.<BR>—3 Free from all moral bonds, dissolute; उद्भासिताखिलखलस्य विशृङ्खलस्य … गोचरगतैः<BR> सुखमाप्यते कैः Bh. 2. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशॄ
विशॄ <i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To be split in pieces, be shattered, विशीर्येत वनेऽथवा.<BR>—2 To crumble to pieces, be dissolved, decay.<BR>—3 To waste away, become emaciated.<BR>—4 To vanish, disappear; सर्वेषां मूर्ध्नि वा तिष्ठेद्विशीर्येत वनेऽथवा H. 1. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्ण|विशीर्णः
विशीर्ण^1 <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Shattered, broken to pieces; दधति विदार्य विशीर्णशुष्कदेहाः Māl. 5. 15.<BR>—2 Decayed, withered.<BR>—3 Dropped or fallen down; स्वयं विशीर्णद्रुमपर्णवृत्तिता Ku. 5. 28.<BR>—4 Shrunk, shrivelled.<BR>—5 Impaired, wasted,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">Page1473-2</a>]<BR> spoiled.<BR>—6 Squandered (as a treasure).<BR>—7 Rubbed off (as unguent).<BR>—8 Frustrated (as an enterprise).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विशीर्णधार, विशीर्णपर्णः, विशीर्णमूर्ति<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: cf. quotation and other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्णधार
विशीर्ण + -धार <i>a.</i> intermittent (as urine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्णपर्णः|विशीर्णपर्ण
विशीर्ण + -पर्णः the Nimba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्णमूर्ति|विशीर्णमूर्तिः
विशीर्ण + -मूर्ति <i>a.</i> having the body destroyed; (शिलीमुखः) इमां हृदि<BR> व्यायतपातमक्षिणोद्विशीर्णमूर्तेरपि पुष्पधन्वनः Ku. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्णमूर्तिः|विशीर्णमूर्ति
विशीर्ण + -मूर्ति + .({@-र्तिः@}) an epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोक|विशोकः
विशोक <i>a.</i> Free from grief, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोकः|विशोक
विशोक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Cessation of grief; सुहृदां च विशोकाय स्वसुश्च प्रियकाम्यया Bhāg. 1. 10. 7.<BR>—2 The Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोका
विशोक + .{@-का@} Exemption from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषः|विशोष
विशोषः Dryness, drought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषणम्
विशोषणम्<BR>—1 Drying up, dessication.<BR>—2 Healing (a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्चकद्रः|विश्चकद्र
विश्चकद्रः Ved.<BR>—1 A dog-dealer.<BR>—2 A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्नः|विश्न
विश्नः Lustre, splendour; P. III. 3. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रण्
विश्रण् €10 U. To give away, bestow; निःशेषविश्राणितकोशजातम्<BR> R. 5. 1, 14. 15; विश्राणितेषु विकचद्रुमकुड्मलेषु Rām. Ch. 5. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रणनम्
विश्रणनम्, -विश्राणनम्<BR> Giving away, bestowing, grant, gift, donation; विश्राणनाच्चान्यपयस्विनीनाम् R. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणनम्
विश्रणनम्, -विश्राणनम्<BR> Giving away, bestowing, grant, gift, donation; विश्राणनाच्चान्यपयस्विनीनाम् R. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्
विश्रम् €4 P.<BR>—1 To take rest, repose, stop; पितामहः प्रजासर्गे त्वयि विश्रान्तवान्<BR> प्रभुः Mb. 12. 156. 7; प्रसीद विश्राम्यतु वीर वज्रम् Ku. 3. 9.<BR>—2 To cease, stop, come to an end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रमः|विश्रम
विश्रमः, विश्रमणः<BR>—1 Rest, repose; तस्य विश्रमणादेष प्रसादो मत्कृतस्तव Mb. 12. 156. 8.<BR>—2 Relaxation, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रमणः|विश्रमण
विश्रमः, विश्रमणः<BR>—1 Rest, repose; तस्य विश्रमणादेष प्रसादो मत्कृतस्तव Mb. 12. 156. 8.<BR>—2 Relaxation, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्त|विश्रांत|विश्रान्तः
विश्रान्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ceased, stopped; स्वकालविरहाद्विश्रान्तपुष्पोद्गमा V. 4. 67.<BR>—2 Rested, reposed; रघुरिव स नरेन्द्रो यज्ञविश्रान्तकोशः Śiva B.<BR>—3 Calm, tranquil, composed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विश्रान्तकथ, विश्रान्तकर्णयुगल<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्तकथ
विश्रान्त + -कथ <i>a.</i> speechless, dumb; मुखं तव विश्रान्तकथं दुनोति<BR> माम् R. 8. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्तकर्णयुगल
विश्रान्त + -कर्णयुगल <i>a.</i> reaching to the ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्तिः|विश्रान्ति|विश्रांति|विश्रांतिः
विश्रान्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Rest, repose.<BR>—2 Cessation, stop.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विश्रान्तिभूमिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रान्तिभूमिः|विश्रान्तिभूमि
विश्रान्तिः + -भूमिः means of relaxation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रामः|विश्राम
विश्रामः<BR>—1 Cessation, stop.<BR>—2 Rest, repose; स्वमेव भवनं शौरिर्विश्रामार्थं जगाम ह Mb. 5. 147. 2;<BR> विश्रामो हृदयस्य यत्र U. 1. 39.<BR>—3 Tranquillity, calm, composure.<BR>—4 Deep breathing (after exertion).<BR>—5 Resting-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भ्|विश्रंभ्
विश्रम्भ् €1 Ā. To confide, place confidence in; विश्रम्भतस्त्वयि<BR> निवेशितसर्वकार्यम् Mu. 5. 7; see विश्रब्ध below. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> To inspire confidence in (a person), console, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्ध|विश्रब्धः
विश्रब्ध <i>p. p.</i> (also written विस्रब्ध)<BR>—1 Confided in, confided to, entrusted.<BR>—2 Confident, fearless, confiding; सुविश्रब्धैरङ्गैः पथिषु विषमेष्वप्यचलता<BR> Mu. 3. 3; Mb. 3. 189. 47.<BR>—3 Trusty, confidential.<BR>—4 Quiet, calm, tranquil, free from anxiety.<BR>—5 Firm, steady.<BR>—6 Meek, lowly.<BR>—7 Excessive, exceeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धम्
विश्रब्ध + .{@-ब्धम्@} <i>ind.</i> Confidently, fearlessly, without reserve, fear,<BR> or hesitation; विश्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षतिः पल्बले<BR> Ś. 2. 6; वृषल विश्रब्धं पृच्छ, ममापि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">Page1474-1</a>]<BR> बह्वाख्येयमत्र Mu. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विश्रब्धनवोढा, विश्रब्धप्रलापिन्, विश्रब्धसुप्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1473-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धनवोढा
विश्रब्ध + -नवोढा a confiding bride (one of the several classes of brides).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धप्रलापिन्
विश्रब्ध + -प्रलापिन् <i>a.</i> talking confidentially.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्धसुप्त
विश्रब्ध + -सुप्त <i>a.</i> sleeping peacefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भः|विश्रम्भ|विश्रंभ|विश्रंभः
विश्रम्भः<BR>—1 Trust, confidence, familiar confidence, perfect intimacy or familiarity;<BR> विश्रम्भादुरसि निपत्य लब्धनिद्राम् U. 1. 49; Māl. 3. 1.<BR>—2 A confidential matter, secret; विश्रम्भेष्वभ्यन्तरीकरणीया K.<BR>—3 Rest, relaxation.<BR>—4 An affectionate inquiry. —5 A love-quarrel, an amorous dispute.<BR>—6 Killing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विश्रम्भालापः, विश्रम्भकथा, विश्रम्भभाषणम्, विश्रम्भपात्रम्, विश्रम्भभूमिः, विश्रम्भस्थानम्, विश्रम्भप्रवण, विश्रम्भभृत्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भालापः|विश्रम्भालाप
विश्रम्भः + -आलापः, -कथा, -भाषणम् confidential or familiar conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भकथा
विश्रम्भः + -आलापः, -कथा, -भाषणम् confidential or familiar conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भभाषणम्
विश्रम्भः + -आलापः, -कथा, -भाषणम् confidential or familiar conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भपात्रम्
विश्रम्भः + -पात्रम्, -भूमिः, -स्थानम् an object of confidence, a confidant, trusty person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भभूमिः|विश्रम्भभूमि
विश्रम्भः + -पात्रम्, -भूमिः, -स्थानम् an object of confidence, a confidant, trusty person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भस्थानम्
विश्रम्भः + -पात्रम्, -भूमिः, -स्थानम् an object of confidence, a confidant, trusty person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भप्रवण
विश्रम्भः + -प्रवण <i>a.</i> trustful; विश्रम्भप्रबणः पुरा मम पिता नीतः<BR> कथाशेषताम् Mu. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भभृत्यः|विश्रम्भभृत्य
विश्रम्भः + -भृत्यः confidential servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भण|विश्रंभणं
विश्रम्भण <i>a.</i> Winning confidence; कृष्णस्त्वन्यतमं रूपं गोपविश्रम्भणं<BR> गतः Bhāg. 10. 24. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भणम्
विश्रम्भण + .{@-णम्@} Confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्भिन्|विश्रंभिन्
विश्रम्भिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Trusting, confiding.<BR>—2 Trustworthy, faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रयः|विश्रय
विश्रयः<BR>—1 A shelter, asylum.<BR>—2 Dependence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रवस्
विश्रवस् <i>m.</i> N. of a son of Pulastya, and father of Rāvaṇa,<BR> Kumbhakarṇa, Bibhīṣaṇa and Śūrpaṇakhā by his wife Kaikasī and<BR> of Kubera by his wife Iḍāviḍā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रावः|विश्राव
विश्रावः<BR>—1 Dropping, flowing forth (for विस्राव q. v.).<BR>—2 Celebrity, renown.<BR>—3 Noise; विक्षावैस्तोयविश्रावं तर्जयन्तो महोदधेः Bk. 7. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रिः|विश्रि
विश्रिः [विशेः क्रिन् Uṇ. 4. 68] Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुत|विश्रुतः
विश्रुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Well-known, renowned, celebrated.<BR>—2 Pleased, delighted, happy. —3 Flowing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुतम्
विश्रुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Fame, celebrity; त्वमप्यदभ्रश्रुतविश्रुतं विभोः Bhāg. 1. 5. 40.<BR>—2 Learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुतिः|विश्रुति
विश्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Fame, celebrity; एकशत्रुवधेनैव शूरो गच्छति विश्रुतिम् Mb. 5. 124. 23;<BR> Bhāg. 10. 82. 30.<BR>—2 Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुती
विश्रुती <i>f.</i> A cow; ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ
विश्लथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Loose, relaxed; untied; ऐरावतास्फालनविश्लथं यः संघट्टयन्नङ्गदमङ्गदेन R. 6. 73.<BR>—2 Languid, drooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्
विश्लिष् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be separated, to be away from.<BR>—2 To burst, fly asunder; शरबन्धा विशिश्लिषुः Bk. 14. 67. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To separate; संदेशं मे हर धनपतिक्रोधविश्लेषितस्य Me. 7.<BR>—2 To deprive of (instr.); बुद्ध्या विश्लेषयन्ति ते Pt. 3. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्ट
विश्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Disjoined, separated, disunited; गरुडापातविश्लिष्टमेघनादास्त्रबन्धनः R. 12. 76.<BR>—2 Loosened.<BR>—3 Dislocated (as limbs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषः|विश्लेष
विश्लेषः<BR>—1 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>—2 Especially separation of lovers, or of husband and wife.<BR>—3 Separation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">Page1474-2</a>]<BR> (in general); तनयाविश्लेषदुखैः Ś. 4. 6; चरणारविन्दविश्लेष R. 13. 23.<BR>—4 Absence, loss, bereavement.<BR>—5 A chasm.<BR>—6 (In Arith.) The converse of addition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विश्लेषजातिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषजातिः|विश्लेषजाति
विश्लेषः + -जातिः <i>f.</i> the reduction of fractional difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषण
विश्लेषण <i>a.</i> Dissolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषणम्
विश्लेषण + .{@-णम्@} Separation, dissolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषित
विश्लेषित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Severed, separated, disunited.<BR>—2 Torn, rent asunder.<BR>—3 Dissolved; Ku. 3. 38 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व <i>pron. a.</i> [विश्-व Uṇ. 1. 151]<BR>—1 All, whole, entire, universal; स सर्वनामा स च विश्वरूपः Bhāg. 6. 4. 28.<BR>—2 Every, every one.<BR>—3 All-pervading, omnipresent. ━<i>m.</i> <i>pl.</i> N. of a particular group of<BR> deities, ten in number and supposed to be sons of विश्वा; their names<BR> are:− वसुः सत्यः क्रतुर्दक्षः कालः कामो धृतिः कुरुः । पुरूरवा माद्रवश्च<BR> विश्वेदेवाः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥ देवाः साध्यास्तथा विश्वे तथैव च महर्षयः<BR> Mb. 3. 261. 6; Bg. 11. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वम्
विश्व + .{@-श्वम्@}<BR>—1 The universe, the (whole) world; इदं विश्वं पाल्यम् U. 3. 30; विश्वस्मिन्नधुनान्यः<BR> कुलव्रतं पालयिष्यति कः Bv. 1. 13.<BR>—2 Dry ginger.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वः|विश्व|विश्वं
विश्व + .{@-श्वः@}<BR>—1 The soul; Bhāg. 7. 15. 54; A. Rām. 7. 5. 49-50; the intellectual faculty.<BR>—2 A citizen (नागर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वा
विश्व + .{@-श्वा@}<BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 Asparagus Racemosus (Mar. शतावरी).<BR>—3 Dry ginger.<BR>—4 The plant अतिविषा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विश्वात्मन्, विश्वात्मना, विश्वाधारः, विश्वेन्वः, विश्वेशः, विश्वेश्वरः, विश्वौषधम्, विश्वकद्रु, विश्वकर्मन्, विश्वकारुः, विश्वकार्यः, विश्वकृत्, विश्वकेतुः, विश्वगः, विश्वगत, विश्वगन्धः, विश्वगन्धा, विश्वगोचर, विश्वगोप्तृ, विश्वग्रन्थिः, विश्वचक्रम्, विश्वचर्षणि, विश्वजनम्, विश्वजनीन, विश्वजन्य, विश्वजनीय, विश्वजित्, विश्वजीवः, विश्वदेव, विश्वदैवम्, विश्वदैवतम्, विश्वधारिणी, विश्वधारिन्, विश्वधेना, विश्वनाथः, विश्वपा, विश्वपावनी, विश्वपूजिता, विश्वप्सन्, विश्वबीजम्, विश्वबोधः, विश्वभावनः, विश्वभुज, विश्वभेषजम्, विश्वभोजस्, विश्वमूर्ति, विश्वयोनिः, विश्वराज्, विश्वरुची, विश्वरूप, विश्वरेतस्, विश्ववासः, विश्ववाह्, विश्वविभावनम्, विश्ववेदस्, विश्वव्यचस्, विश्वव्यापक, विश्वव्यापिन्, विश्वसंवननम्, विश्वसंहारः, विश्वसत्तम, विश्वसहा, विश्वसारकम्, विश्वसृज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वात्मन्
विश्व + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the Supreme Being (soul of the universe).<BR>—2 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—3 of Śiva; अथ विश्वात्मने गौरी संदिदेश मिथः सखीम् Ku. 6. 1.<BR>—4 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वात्मना
विश्व + -आत्मना <i>ind.</i> thoroughly; विश्वात्मना यत्र निवर्तते भीः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 2. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1474-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

