विषम + -चक्रवालम् (in math.) an ellipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमचतुरस्रः|विषमचतुरस्र
विषम + -चतुरस्रः, -चतुर्भुजः an unequal quadrilateral figure; trapezium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमचतुर्भुजः|विषमचतुर्भुज
विषम + -चतुरस्रः, -चतुर्भुजः an unequal quadrilateral figure; trapezium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमच्छदः|विषमच्छद|विषमछद
विषम + -छदः the tree सप्तपर्ण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमच्छाया|विषमछाया
विषम + -छाया the shadow of the gnomon at noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमज्वरः|विषमज्वर
विषम + -ज्वरः remittent fever; दोषोऽल्पोऽहितसंभूतो ज्वरोत्सृष्टस्य<BR> वा पुनः । धातुमन्यतमं प्राप्य करोति विषमज्वरम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमत्रिभुजः|विषमत्रिभुज
विषम + -त्रिभुजः a scalene triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमपत्रः
विषम + -पत्रः the Saptaparṇa tree; विषमपत्रमहीरुहसंभवम्<BR> Rām. Ch. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमबाणः|विषमबाण
विषम + -बाणः N. of the god of love; also विषमविशिखः, -शरः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमलक्ष्मी
विषम + -लक्ष्मी <i>f.</i> ill-luck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमविभागः|विषमविभाग
विषम + -विभागः unequal distribution (of property).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमवृत्तम्
विषम + -वृत्तम् a kind of metre with unequal Pādas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमशील
विषम + -शील <i>a.</i> cross-tempered, peevish, perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमस्थ|विषमस्थः
विषम + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being in an inaccessible position.<BR>—2 being in difficulty or misfortune; विश्वामित्रस्ततस्तां तु विषमस्थामनिन्दिताम् Mb. 1. 72. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमक
विषमक <i>a.</i> Rather uneven; not properly polished (as pearls).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमित
विषमित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Made rough, uneven or crooked; कोपविस्फुरणविषमिताग्राङ्गुली Mu. 3. 27.<BR>—2 Contracted, frowning.<BR>—3 Made difficult or inaccessible.<BR>—4 Hostile, unfavourable; क्वचित्कालविषमितराजकुलरक्षसापहृतप्रियतमधनासुः<BR> Bhāg. 5. 14. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमीभू
विषमीभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To become uneven. —2 To stumble, fall unevenly; मार्गे पदानि खलु<BR> ते विषमीभवन्ति Ś. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमीभावः|विषमीभाव
विषमीभावः Derangement of equilibrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयः|विषय
विषयः —1 An object of sense; (these are five, corresponding to the<BR> five organs of sense; रूप, रस, गन्ध, स्पर्श and शब्द corresponding<BR> to the eye, tongue, nose, skin, and ear); श्रुतिविषयगुणा या स्थिता व्याप्य<BR> विश्वम् Ś. 1. 1.<BR>—2 A worldly object or concern, an affair, a transaction.<BR>—3 The pleasures of sense, worldly or sensual objects (usually in pl.);<BR> यौवने विषयैषिणाम् R. 1. 8; शब्दादीन् विषयान् भोक्तुम् 10. 25; विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः<BR> V. 1. 9; निर्विष्टविषयस्नेहः 12. 1, 3. 70, 8. 10, 19. 49; विषया<BR> विनिवर्तन्ते निराहारस्य देहिनः Bg. 2. 59.<BR>—4 An object, a thing, matter; नार्यो न जग्मुर्विषयान्तराणि R. 7. 12, 8. 89.<BR>—5 An object or thing aimed at, mark, object; भूयिष्ठमन्यविषया न<BR> तु दृष्टिरस्याः Ś. 1. 30; Śi. 9. 40.<BR>—6 Scope, range, reach, compass; सौमित्रेरपि पत्रिणामविषये तत्र प्रिये<BR> क्वासि भोः U. 3. 45; यस्मिन्नीश्वर इत्यनन्यविषयः शब्दो यथार्थाक्षरः<BR> V. 1. 1; सकलवचनानामविषयः Māl. 1. 30, 36; U. 5. 19; Ku. 6. 17.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">Page1478-1</a>]<BR>—7 Department, sphere, province, field, element; सर्वत्रौदरिकस्याभ्यवहार्यमेव<BR> विषयः V. 3.<BR>—8 A subject, subject-matter, topic; अयि मलयज महिमायं कस्य गिरामस्तु<BR> विषयस्ते Bv. 1. 11; so शृङ्गारविषयको ग्रन्थः ‘treating of love’.<BR>—9 The topic or subject to be explained, general head; the first of the<BR> five members of an Adhikaraṇa q. v.<BR>—10 A place, spot; परिसरविषयेषु लीढमुक्ताः Ki. 5. 38.<BR>—11 A country, realm, domain, territory, district, kingdom; ‘विषयः स्यादिन्द्रियार्थे देशे जनपदेऽपि च’ इति विश्वः;<BR> अप्रविष्टविषयस्य रक्षसाम्<BR> R. 11. 18; Pt. 2. 2.<BR>—12 A refuge, an asylum.<BR>—13 A collection of villages.<BR>—14 A lover, husband.<BR>—15 Semen virile.<BR>—16 A religious observance.<BR>—17 A symbolical expression for the number ‘five’. (विषये means ‘with regard or reference to’<BR>, ‘in respect of’, ‘in the case of’, ‘regarding’,<BR> ‘concerning’; या तत्रास्ते युवतिविषये सृष्टिराद्येव धातुः Me. 84;<BR> स्त्रीणां विषये; धनविषये &c.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विषयाज्ञानम्, विषयाधिकृतः, विषयाधिपतिः, विषयाभिरतिः, विषयात्मक, विषयासक्त, विषयनिरत, विषयासक्तिः, विषयोपसेवा, विषयनिरतिः, विषयैषिन्, विषयकर्मन्, विषयग्रामः, विषयज्ञः, विषयनिरतिः, विषयनिह्नुतिः, विषयपतिः, विषयपराङ्मुख, विषयप्रवण, विषयलोलुप, विषयसंगः, विषयसुखम्, विषयस्नेहः, विषयस्पृहा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1477-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयाज्ञानम्
विषयः + -अज्ञानम् sleepiness, exhaustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयाधिकृतः|विषयाधिकृत
विषयः + -अधिकृतः the governor of a province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयाधिपतिः|विषयाधिपति
विषयः + -अधिपतिः the king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयाभिरतिः|विषयाभिरति
विषयः + -अभिरतिः —1 attachment to objects of sense or worldly pleasures;<BR> द्विषतां वधेन विषयाभिरतिम् (अभिलष्यति) Ki. 6. 44; so ˚अभिलाषः Ki. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयात्मक
विषयः + -आत्मक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 consisting of worldly objects.<BR>—2 carnal, sensual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयासक्त
विषयः + -आसक्त, -निरत <i>a.</i> addicted to sensual objects, sensualist,<BR> worldly-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयनिरत
विषयः + -आसक्त, -निरत <i>a.</i> addicted to sensual objects, sensualist,<BR> worldly-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयासक्तिः|विषयासक्ति
विषयः + -आसक्तिः, -उपसेवा, -निरतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-प्रसंगः@}<BR> addiction to pleasures of sense, sensuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयोपसेवा
विषयः + -आसक्तिः, -उपसेवा, -निरतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-प्रसंगः@}<BR> addiction to pleasures of sense, sensuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयनिरतिः|विषयनिरति
विषयः + -आसक्तिः, -उपसेवा, -निरतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-प्रसंगः@}<BR> addiction to pleasures of sense, sensuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयैषिन्
विषयः + -एषिन् <i>a.</i> addicted to worldly objects; यौवने विषयैषिणाम् R. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयकर्मन्|विषयकर्म्मन्
विषयः + -कर्मन् worldly business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयग्रामः|विषयग्राम
विषयः + -ग्रामः the collection of the objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयज्ञः|विषयज्ञ
विषयः + -ज्ञः a specialist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयनिरतिः|विषयनिरति
विषयः + -निरतिः attachment to sensual objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयनिह्नुतिः|विषयनिह्नुति
विषयः + -निह्नुतिः negation with regard to an object; शैशिर्यमभ्युपत्यैव<BR> परेष्वात्मनि कामिना । औष्ण्यप्रकाशनात्तस्य सैषा विषयनिह्नुतिः ॥ Kāv. 2. 306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयपतिः|विषयपति
विषयः + -पतिः the governor of a province.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयपराङ्मुख
विषयः + -पराङ्मुख <i>a.</i> averse from mundane affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयप्रवण
विषयः + -प्रवण <i>a.</i> attached to objects of sense; Kull. on Ms. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयलोलुप
विषयः + -लोलुप <i>a.</i> eager for sensual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयसंगः|विषयसङ्ग
विषयः + -संगः addiction to sensual objects; सोऽनुभूयासुखोदर्कान् दोषान्<BR> विषयसंगजान् Ms. 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयसुखम्
विषयः + -सुखम् the pleasures of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयस्नेहः|विषयस्नेह
विषयः + -स्नेहः, -स्पृहा desire for sensual objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयस्पृहा
विषयः + -स्नेहः, -स्पृहा desire for sensual objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयक
विषयक^1 <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to an object.<BR>—2 (At the end of comp.) Having for an object, treating of, relating to,<BR> as in दानविषयको ग्रन्थः.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयायिन्
विषयायिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One addicted to pleasures of sense, a sensualist.<BR>—2 A man of the world.<BR>—3 The god of love.<BR>—4 A king.<BR>—5 An organ of sense.<BR>—6 A materialist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयिन्
विषयिन् <i>a.</i> Sensual, carnal. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A man of the world, worldling.<BR>—2 A king.<BR>—3 The god of love.<BR>—4 A sensualist, voluptuary; विषयिणः कस्यापदोऽस्तं गताः Pt. 1. 146; Ś. 5.<BR>—5 (Rhet.) The object of a comparison. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 An organ of sense.<BR>—2 Knowledge (ज्ञान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयीकरणम्
विषयीकरणम् The making anything the object of thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्
विषह् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To bear, suffer, endure; दुर्वारं सा कथमपि परित्यागदुःखं<BR> विषेहे R. 14. 87, 3. 63, 8. 57.<BR>—2 To resist, oppose, withstand, be able to resist; तस्यामेव रघोः<BR> पाण्ड्याः प्रतापं न विषेहिरे R. 4. 49.<BR>—3 To be able; Śi. 14. 29, 17. 10.<BR>—4 To allow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्य
विषह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Endurable, bearable; अविषह्यव्यसनेन धूमिताम् Ku. 4. 30; R. 6. 47.<BR>—2 Possible to be settled or determined; सीमायामविषह्यायां स्वयं राजैव<BR> धर्मवित् Ms. 8. 265.<BR>—3 Possible.<BR>—4 Resistible, conquerable; किं नाम लोकेषु विषह्यमस्ति कृष्णस्य सर्वेषु<BR> सदेवकेषु Mb. 3. 120. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषलः|विषल|विषलं
विषलः Poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
विषा<BR>—1 Ordure, feces.<BR>—2 Intellect, understanding.<BR>—3 A tree (अतिविषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणः|विषाण|विषाणं
विषाणः, -णम्, -णी<BR> [विष्-बा˚ कानच्]<BR>—1 A horn; साहित्यसंगीतकलविहीनः साक्षात् पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः<BR> Bh. 2. 12; कदाचिदपि पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत् 2. 5.<BR>—2 The tusk of an elephant or boar; केचिद्भिन्ना विषाणाग्रैः Mb. 6. 94. 35;<BR> तप्तानामुपदधिरे विषाणभिन्नाः प्रह्रादं सुरकरिणां घनाः क्षरन्तः<BR> Ki. 7. 13; Śi. 1. 60; Bhāg. 10. 43. 15.<BR>—3 A horn (wind instrument).<BR>—4 The claws (of a crab).<BR>—5 A peak, top.<BR>—6 The nipple, (tip of the breast).<BR>—7 The chief or best of the kind.<BR>—8 A sword or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणम्
विषाणः, -णम्, -णी<BR> [विष्-बा˚ कानच्]<BR>—1 A horn; साहित्यसंगीतकलविहीनः साक्षात् पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः<BR> Bh. 2. 12; कदाचिदपि पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत् 2. 5.<BR>—2 The tusk of an elephant or boar; केचिद्भिन्ना विषाणाग्रैः Mb. 6. 94. 35;<BR> तप्तानामुपदधिरे विषाणभिन्नाः प्रह्रादं सुरकरिणां घनाः क्षरन्तः<BR> Ki. 7. 13; Śi. 1. 60; Bhāg. 10. 43. 15.<BR>—3 A horn (wind instrument).<BR>—4 The claws (of a crab).<BR>—5 A peak, top.<BR>—6 The nipple, (tip of the breast).<BR>—7 The chief or best of the kind.<BR>—8 A sword or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणी
विषाणः, -णम्, -णी<BR> [विष्-बा˚ कानच्]<BR>—1 A horn; साहित्यसंगीतकलविहीनः साक्षात् पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः<BR> Bh. 2. 12; कदाचिदपि पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत् 2. 5.<BR>—2 The tusk of an elephant or boar; केचिद्भिन्ना विषाणाग्रैः Mb. 6. 94. 35;<BR> तप्तानामुपदधिरे विषाणभिन्नाः प्रह्रादं सुरकरिणां घनाः क्षरन्तः<BR> Ki. 7. 13; Śi. 1. 60; Bhāg. 10. 43. 15.<BR>—3 A horn (wind instrument).<BR>—4 The claws (of a crab).<BR>—5 A peak, top.<BR>—6 The nipple, (tip of the breast).<BR>—7 The chief or best of the kind.<BR>—8 A sword or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिन्
विषाणिन् <i>a.</i> Having (big) horns or tusks; नाराजके जनपदे बद्धघण्टा<BR> विषाणिनः (अटन्ति) Rām. 2. 67. 20. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 Any animal having horns or tusks.<BR>—2 An elephant; भग्नो निवासोऽयमिहास्य पुष्पैः सदानतो येन विषाणिनागः<BR> Śi. 4. 63, 12. 77.<BR>—3 A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषारः|विषार
विषारः A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषालु
विषालु <i>a.</i> Poisonous, venomous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषासहि
विषासहि <i>a.</i> Victorious; विषासहिरिति वा अहमेतमुपास Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषु
विषु <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In two equal parts, equally.<BR>—2 Differently, variously.<BR>—3 Same, like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुण|विषुणः
विषुण <i>a.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Moving variously.<BR>—2 Having various forms.<BR>—3 Having uniform motion.<BR>—4 Adverse, hostile, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुणः|विषुण
विषुण + .{@-णः@} The equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुपम्
विषुपम् The equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवम्
विषुवम् The first point of <i>Aries</i> or <i>Libra</i> into which the<BR> sun enters at the vernal or autumnal equinox, the equinoctial point; अयने<BR> विषुवे कुर्याद्व्यतीपाते दिनक्षये Bhāg. 7. 14. 20.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विषुवच्छाया, विषुवदिनम्, विषुवरेखा, विषुवसंक्रान्तिः, विषुवसमयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवच्छाया|विषुवछाया
विषुवम् + -छाया the shadow of the gnomon at noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवदिनम्
विषुवम् + -दिनम् the day of the equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवरेखा
विषुवम् + -रेखा the equinoctial line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवसंक्रान्तिः|विषुवसङ्क्रान्ति|विषुवसंक्रान्ति|विषुवसंक्रांति
विषुवम् + -संक्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> the sunʼs equinoctial passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवसमयः|विषुवसमय
विषुवम् + -समयः the equinoctial season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवत्|विषुवन्त्
विषुवत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The equinox.<BR>—2 The central day in a sacrificial session.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विषुवद्दिनम्, विषुवद्दिवसः, विषुवद्वलयम्, विषुवद्वृत्तम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवद्दिनम्
विषुवत् + -दिनम्, -दिवसः the equinoctial day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवद्दिवसः|विषुवद्दिवस
विषुवत् + -दिनम्, -दिवसः the equinoctial day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवद्वलयम्
विषुवत् + -वलयम्, -वृत्तम् equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषुवद्वृत्तम्
विषुवत् + -वलयम्, -वृत्तम् equator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1478-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्क्
विष्क् €10 U. [विष्कयति-ते]<BR>—1 To kill, hurt, injure (Ātm. only in this sense).<BR>—2 To see, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषूचिः|विषूचि
विषूचिः Mind (मनस्); अन्तःपुरं च हृदयं विषूचिर्मन उच्यते<BR> Bhāg. 4. 29. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषूचिका
विषूचिका Cholera; also विषूचकम्; Mb. 12. 303. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषूचीन
विषूचीन <i>a.</i> Going in different directions, spreading everywhere;<BR> स यर्ह्यन्तःपुरगतो विषूचीनसमन्वितः Bhāg. 4. 25. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कः|विष्क
विष्कः An elephant twenty years old; विष्के नागः पर्यणंसीत् स्व<BR> एव Śi. 18. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्द्|विष्कंद्
विष्कन्द् P.<BR>—1 To go in different directions, roam, wander about.<BR>—2 To go away, disperse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कन्दः|विष्कन्द|विष्कंद|विष्कंदः
विष्कन्दः<BR>—1 Dispersing.<BR>—2 Going away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भ्|विष्कंभ्
विष्कम्भ् €5. €9 P.<BR>—1 To impede, obstruct.<BR>—2 To support, prop.<BR>—3 To fix firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भः|विष्कम्भ|विष्कंभ|विष्कंभः
विष्कम्भः<BR>—1 Obstacle, hindrance, impediment.<BR>—2 The bolt or bar of a door.<BR>—3 The supporting beam of a house<BR>—4 A post, pillar.<BR>—5 A tree.<BR>—6 (In dramas) An interlude between the acts of a drama and performed<BR> by one or more characters, middling or inferior, who connect the story<BR> of the drama and the subdivisions of the plot by briefly explaining to<BR> the audience what has occurred in the intervals of the acts or what is<BR> likely to happen later on:− S. D. thus defines it:− वृत्तवर्तिष्यमाणानां<BR> कथांशानां निदर्शकः । संक्षिप्तार्थस्तु विष्कम्भ आदावङ्कस्य दर्शितः ।<BR> मध्येन मध्यमाभ्यां वा पात्राभ्यां संप्रयोजितः । शुद्धः स्यात् स तु<BR> संकीर्णो नीचमध्यमकल्पितः ॥ 308.<BR>—7 The diameter of a circle.<BR>—8 A particular posture practised by Yogins.<BR>—9 Extension, length; तद्द्विगुणविष्कम्भं खाताद् वप्रं कारयेत् Kau. A. 1. 3;<BR> एषामन्तरविष्कम्भो योजनानि सहस्रशः Mb. 6. 6. 6.<BR>—10 The first of the twenty-seven astronomical periods (योग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भक|विष्कंभक
विष्कम्भक See विष्कम्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भित|विष्कंभित
विष्कम्भित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hindered, obstructed.<BR>—2 Richly furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कम्भिन्|विष्कंभिन्
विष्कम्भिन् <i>m.</i> The bolt of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्कलः|विष्कल
विष्कलः A hog (ग्राम्यशूकर); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्किरः|विष्किर
विष्किरः<BR>—1 Scattering about, tearing up.<BR>—2 A cock.<BR>—3 A bird, gallinaceous bird; छायापस्किरमाणविष्किरमुखव्याकृष्टकीटत्वचः U. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टप्
विष्टप् <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A place, region, world.<BR>—2 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टपः|विष्टप|विष्टपं
विष्टपः, पम् [विष्-कपन् Uṇ. 3. 145]<BR>—1 A world; अथ पुत्रस्य पौत्रेण ब्रध्नस्याप्नोति विष्टपम् Ms. 9. 137;<BR> R. 11. 19; सुराः समभ्यर्थयितार एते कार्यं त्रयाणामपि विष्टपानाम्<BR> Ku. 3. 20; cf. त्रिविष्टप.<BR>—2 A vessel, cup (Ved.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विष्टपहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पम्
विष्टपः, पम् [विष्-कपन् Uṇ. 3. 145]<BR>—1 A world; अथ पुत्रस्य पौत्रेण ब्रध्नस्याप्नोति विष्टपम् Ms. 9. 137;<BR> R. 11. 19; सुराः समभ्यर्थयितार एते कार्यं त्रयाणामपि विष्टपानाम्<BR> Ku. 3. 20; cf. त्रिविष्टप.<BR>—2 A vessel, cup (Ved.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विष्टपहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टपहारिन्
विष्टपः + -हारिन् <i>a.</i> one who pleases the world; तुष्टे विष्टपहारिणीष्टदहरौ<BR> संप्राप्यते देहिना Bh. 2. 25 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भ्|विष्टंभ्
विष्टम्भ् €5. €9 P.<BR>—1 To stop, obstruct; आहोस्वित् प्रसवो ममापचरितैर्विष्टम्भितो वीरुधाम् Ś. 5. 9.<BR>—2 To fix, plant, rest on; अत्युच्छ्रिते मन्त्रिणि पार्थिवे च विष्टभ्य पादावुपतिष्ठते<BR> श्रीः Mu. 4. 13.<BR>—3 To strengthen, to support; विष्टब्धं विद्रुमस्तम्भैर्वैदूर्यफलकोत्तमैः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 69. 9.<BR>—4 To pervade, permeate; विष्टभ्याहमिदं कृत्स्नमेकांशेन स्थितो जगत् Bg. 10. 42.<BR>—5 To ascertain, settle; पार्श्वतः करणं प्राज्ञो विष्टम्भित्वा प्रकारयेत्<BR> Mb. 12. 142. 9. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To obstruct.<BR>—2 To paralyse, benumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टब्ध
विष्टब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Fixed firmly; well supported.<BR>—2 Propped up, supported.<BR>—3 Obstructed, hindered.<BR>—4 Paralysed, made motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भः|विष्टम्भ|विष्टंभ|विष्टंभः
विष्टम्भः<BR>—1 Fixing firmly.<BR>—2 Obstruction, hindrance, an impediment.<BR>—3 Obstruction of the urine or ordure, constipation.<BR>—4 Paralysis.<BR>—5 Stopping, staying.<BR>—6 Stepping, placing the feet.<BR>—7 Prop, support.<BR>—8 Endurance, resistance; शीतोष्ण-वर्ष-पवन-विष्टम्भविभिन्नसर्वत्वचः<BR> Mb. 12. 192. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टम्भिन्|विष्टंभिन्
विष्टम्भिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Stopping, obstructing, impeding.<BR>—2 Making motionless, benumbing, chilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरः|विष्टर
विष्टरः<BR>—1 A seat (a stool, chair &c.); कुशपूतं प्रबंयास्तु विष्टरम् (आददे)<BR> R. 8. 18; वृक्षशाखां स्वयं छित्वा विष्टराय ददौ मुदा A. Rām. 4. 1. 32.<BR>—2 A layer, bed (as of Kuśa grass.).<BR>—3 A handful of Kuśa grass.<BR>—4 The seat of the presiding priest (or Brahman) at a sacrifice.<BR>—5 A tree.<BR>—6 An ascetic seat made of 25 Kuśa grass-shoots (‘पञ्चाशद्भिर्भवेद् ब्रह्मा तदर्धेन तु विष्टरः’);<BR> विष्टरासनयोग्यो हि कालेऽयं मामुपस्थितः<BR> Rām. 2. 20. 28.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विष्टरभाज्, विष्टरश्रवस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरभाज्
विष्टरः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> seated on or occupying a seat; तत्रेश्वरो विष्टरभाग्<BR> यथावत् Ku. 7. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टरश्रवस्
विष्टरः + -श्रवस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; तं वदन्तमिति<BR> विष्टरश्रवाः श्रावयन्नथ समस्तभूभृतः Śi. 14. 12; Mb. 14. 14. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टा
विष्टा Excrement, feces, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टिः|विष्टि
विष्टिः <i>f.</i> [विष्-क्तिन् क्तिच् वा]<BR>—1 Pervading.<BR>—2 An act, occupation.<BR>—3 Hire, wages.<BR>—4 Unpaid labour; दण्डविष्टिकराबाधै रक्षेदुपहतां कृषिम् Kau. A.<BR>—5 Sending.<BR>—6 Residence in hell to which one is condemned.<BR>—7 See विष्टिकारिन्; Mb. 12. 59. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विष्टिकरः, विष्टिकारिन्, विष्टिकर्मान्तिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टिकरः|विष्टिकर
विष्टिः + -करः the lord of slaves, of unpaid labourers; Mb. 3. 190. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टिकारिन्
विष्टिः + -कारिन् an unpaid forced labourer (Mar. वेठबिगार); भारयष्टिधरैश्चापि<BR> पुरुषैर्विष्टिकारिभिः Śiva B. 30. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्टिकर्मान्तिकः
विष्टिः + -कर्मान्तिकः (= विष्टिकारिन्); Rām. 2. 82. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठलम्
विष्ठलम् A remote place, one situated at a distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठा
विष्ठा<BR>—1 Feces, ordure, excrement; सोमविक्रयिणे विष्ठा भिषजे पूयशोणितम्<BR> Ms. 3. 180, 10. 91.<BR>—2 The belly.<BR>—3 Ved. Interval.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विष्ठाशिन्, विष्ठाभूः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठाशिन्
विष्ठा + -आशिन् a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठाभूः
विष्ठा + -भूः a worm living in ordure; नैकत्रास्ते सूतिवातैर्विष्ठाभूरिव<BR> सोदरः Bhāg. 3. 31. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1479-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्ठित
विष्ठित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Standing, being on or in; क्षमा यशः क्षमा धर्मः क्षमायां विष्ठितं<BR> जगत् Rām. 1. 33. 9.<BR>—2 Being present or near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुः|विष्णु
विष्णुः [विष् व्यापने नुक् Uṇ. 3. 39]<BR>—1 The second deity of the sacred Triad, entrusted with the preservation<BR> of the world, which duty he is represented to have duly discharged by<BR> his various incarnations; (for their descriptions see the several avatāras<BR> s. v. and also under अवतार); the word is thus popularly derived:−<BR> यस्माद्विश्वमिदं सर्वं तस्य शक्त्या महात्मनः । तस्मादेवोच्यते विष्णुर्विशधातोः<BR> प्रवेशनात् ॥.<BR>—2 N. of Agni; विष्णुर्नामेह योऽग्निः Mb. 3. 221. 12.<BR>—3 A pious man.<BR>—4 N. of a law-giver, author of a Smṛti called विष्णुस्मृति.<BR>—5 N. of one of the Vasus.<BR>—6 The lunar mansion called Śravaṇa (presided over by Viṣṇu).<BR>—7 N. of the month चैत्र.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विष्णुकाञ्ची, विष्णुक्रमः, विष्णुक्रान्ता, विष्णुगुप्तः, विष्णुग्रन्थिः, विष्णुजनः, विष्णुतिथिः, विष्णुतैलम्, विष्णुदत्तः, विष्णुदैवत्या, विष्णुधर्मः, विष्णुधर्मोत्तरपुराणम्, विष्णुपदम्, विष्णुपदी, विष्णुपुराणम्, विष्णुप्रिया, विष्णुप्रीतिः, विष्णुमाया, विष्णुमित्रः, विष्णुरथः, विष्णुरातः, विष्णुलिङ्गी, विष्णुलोकः, विष्णुवल्लभा, विष्णुवाहनः, विष्णुवाह्यः, विष्णुशक्तिः, विष्णुहिता<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुकाञ्ची|विष्णुकांची
विष्णुः + -काञ्ची N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुक्रमः|विष्णुक्रम
विष्णुः + -क्रमः the step or stride of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुक्रान्ता
विष्णुः + -क्रान्ता N. of various plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुगुप्तः|विष्णुगुप्त
विष्णुः + -गुप्तः N. of Cāṇakya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुग्रन्थिः|विष्णुग्रन्थि
विष्णुः + -ग्रन्थिः a particular joint of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुजनः
विष्णुः + -जनः a devotee, saint; अध्यगान्महदाख्यानं नित्यं विष्णुजनप्रियः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1480-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्णुतिथिः|विष्णुतिथि
