विहंगः + -इन्द्रः, -ईशवरः, -राजः epithets of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगम|विहङ्गम|विहंगमः|विहङ्गमः
विहंगम <i>a.</i> Moving in the sky, flying; प्रभुः संकल्पसिद्धोऽस्मि<BR> कामचारी विहंगमः Mb. 5. 192. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगमः|विहङ्गम|विहंगम|विहङ्गमः
विहंगम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 A bird; (गृहदीर्घिकाः) मदकलोदकलोलविहंगमाः R. 9. 37;<BR> Ms. 1. 39; H. 1. 34.<BR>—2 The sun; तथेत्युक्त्वा तु तां कुन्तीमाविवेश विहंगमः Mb. 3. 307. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगमा
विहंगमा, विहंगमिका, विहंगिका A pole for carrying burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगमिका
विहंगमा, विहंगमिका, विहंगिका A pole for carrying burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहंगिका|विहङ्गिका
विहंगमा, विहंगमिका, विहंगिका A pole for carrying burdens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत्
विहत् <i>f.</i> A barren cow (see वेहत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहन्
विहन् €2 P.<BR>—1 To kill, slay, destroy, destroy completely, annihilate; (अलं)<BR> सहसा संहतिमंहसां विहन्तुम् Ki. 5. 17, 14. 23.<BR>—2 To strike, beat violently.<BR>—3 To obstruct, impede, oppose, resist; विघ्नन्ति रक्षांसि वने क्रतूंश्च<BR> Bk. 1. 19; Śi. 14. 8; R. 5. 27.<BR>—4 To reject, refuse, decline; तद् भूतनाथानुग नार्हसि त्वं संबन्धिनो<BR> मे प्रणयं विहन्तुम् R. 2. 58; न व्यहन्यत कदाचिदर्थिता 11. 2.<BR>—5 To disappoint, foil, frustrate.<BR>—6 To separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहत|विहतः
विहत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Struck completely, killed.<BR>—2 Hurt.<BR>—3 Opposed, impeded, resisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहतः|विहत
विहत + .{@-तः@} A Jaina temple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहतिः|विहति
विहतिः A friend, companion. ━<i>f.</i><BR>—1 Killing, striking.<BR>—2 Failure.<BR>—3 Defeat, rout.<BR>—4 Repulse, frustration; मनोभिः सोद्वेगैः प्रणयविहतिध्वस्तरुचयः Ki. 10. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहननम्
विहननम्<BR>—1 Killing, striking.<BR>—2 Hurt, injury.<BR>—3 Obstruction, obstacle, impediment.<BR>—4 A bow for cleaning cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर्षः|विहर्ष
विहर्षः Great joy, rapture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्
विहस् €1 P.<BR>—1 To smile, laugh gently; किंचिद्विहस्यार्थपतिं बभाषे R. 2. 46.<BR>—2 To laugh at, deride, ridicule; किमिति विषीदसि रोदिषि विकला विहसति<BR> युवतिसभा तव सकला Gīt. 9; गौरीवक्त्रभ्रुकुटिरचनां या विहस्येव<BR> फेनैः Me. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसतिका
विहसतिका, विहसनम्, विहसितम्, विहासः A gentle laugh, smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसनम्
विहसतिका, विहसनम्, विहसितम्, विहासः A gentle laugh, smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहसितम्
विहसतिका, विहसनम्, विहसितम्, विहासः A gentle laugh, smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहासः|विहास
विहसतिका, विहसनम्, विहसितम्, विहासः A gentle laugh, smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्त|विहस्तः
विहस्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Handless.<BR>—2 Confounded, bewildered, overpowered, made powerless; मालतीमुखावलोकनविहस्ततया<BR> Māl. 1; R. 5. 49; पितामहस्तामालोक्य विहस्तामस्थिरां स्थिराम् Śiva B. 5. 47;<BR> शाहराजात्मज शिशो विहाय स्वां विहस्तताम् <i>ibid.</i> 21. 23.<BR>—3 Disabled, incapacitated (for doing the proper work); रुजाविहस्तचरणम् M. 4.<BR>—4 Adroit, skilled.<BR>—5 Learned, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहस्तः|विहस्त
विहस्त + .{@-स्तः@} A eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा <i>ind.</i> Heaven, paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहा
विहा €2 P. To leave, abandon, forsake, give up; विहाय लक्ष्मीपतिलक्ष्म<BR> कार्मुकं जटाधरः सन् जुहुधीह पावकम् Ki. 1. 44; ज्ञातास्वादो विवृतजघनां<BR> को विहातुं समर्थः Me. 43; R. 2. 40, 5. 67, 73, 6. 7, 12. 102, 14. 48, 69;<BR> Ku. 3. 1. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To give away.<BR>—2 To abandon, give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहापित|विहापितं
विहापित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Caused to abandon.<BR>—2 Extorted, caused to be given up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहापितम्
विहापित + .{@-तम्@} A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहाय|विहायः
विहाय <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 At a distance from.<BR>—2 More than.<BR>—3 Inspite of.<BR>—4 With the exception of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीन|विहीनः
विहीन <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Left, abandoned, forsaken.<BR>—2 Devoid of, destitute or deprived of, without (usually in comp.); विद्याविहीनः<BR> पशुः Bh. 2. 20.<BR>—3 Base, low, inferior.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विहीनजाति, विहीनयोनि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीनजाति
विहीन + -जाति, -योनि <i>a.</i> base-born, low-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहीनयोनि
विहीन + -जाति, -योनि <i>a.</i> base-born, low-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहानः|विहान
विहानः, -नम्<BR> Morning, dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहानम्
विहानः, -नम्<BR> Morning, dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस्
विहायस् <i>m., n.</i> Sky, atmosphere; गरुत्मतां संहतिभिर्विहायः<BR> क्षणप्रकाशाभिरिवावतेने Ki. 16. 43. ━<i>m.</i> A bird; अमोचि चञ्चूपुटमौनमुद्रा<BR> विहायसा तेन विहस्य भूयः N. 3. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहायस|विहायसं|विहायसः
विहायस See विहायस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहित|विहितः
विहित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Done, performed, made, acted.<BR>—2 Arranged, fixed, settled, appointed, determined.<BR>—3 Ordered, prescribed, decreed; विहिता व्यङ्गिता तेषाम् Pt. 1. 201.<BR>—4 Framed, constructed.<BR>—5 Placed, deposited.<BR>—6 Furnished with, possessed of.<BR>—7 Fit to be done.<BR>—8 Distributed, apportioned. (See धा with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितम्
विहित + .{@-तम्@} An order, a command, decree; परतो दैवविहितायत्तम् Pt. 1.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विहितक्षण, विहितप्रतिषिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितक्षण
विहित + -क्षण <i>a.</i> intent upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितप्रतिषिद्ध
विहित + -प्रतिषिद्ध <i>a.</i> enjoined and prohibited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहितिः|विहिति
विहितिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Performance, doing, action.<BR>—2 Arrangement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1484-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृ
विहृ €1 P.<BR>—1 To take away, seize away.<BR>—2 To remove, destroy.<BR>—3 To let fall, shed (as tears); as in बाष्पं विहरति.<BR>—4 To pass (as time).<BR>—5 To amuse, or divert oneself, sport, play; विहरति हरिरिह सरसवसन्ते<BR> Gīt. 1; गन्धमादनवनं विहर्तुं गता V. 4; U. 3. 6.<BR>—6 To go in various directions.<BR>—7 To live.<BR>—8 To change, alternate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरः|विहर
विहरः<BR>—1 Taking away, removing.<BR>—2 Separation, disunion.<BR>—3 Changing.<BR>—4 Play, pastime; विहर उदीक्षया यदि परस्य विमुक्त ततः Bhāg. 10. 87. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहरणम्
विहरणम्<BR>—1 Removing, taking away.<BR>—2 Taking a walk, airing, going about or rambling for pleasure.<BR>—3 Pleasure, pastime; क्वचिद्गतिज्ञानं क्वचिदपि परस्त्रीविहरणम्<BR> Viṣṇumahimna 12.<BR>—4 Opening, expanding; P. I. 3. 20.<BR>—5 Stepping out; P. I. 3. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहर्तृ|विहर्त्तृ
विहर्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A roamer.<BR>—2 A robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारः|विहार
विहारः<BR>—1 Removing, taking away.<BR>—2 Roaming or walking for pleasure, airing, a stroll, taking a walk.<BR>—3 Sport, play, pastime, recreation, diversion, pleasure; विहारशैलानुगतेव<BR> नागैः R. 16. 26, 67, 5. 41, 9. 68, 13. 38, 19. 37.<BR>—4 Tread, stepping, movement (of hands, feet &c.); विकर्षणैः पाणिविहारहारिभिः<BR> Ki. 4. 15; दरमन्थरचरणविहारम् Gīt. 11.<BR>—5 A park, garden; especially a pleasure-garden; आरामैश्च विहारैश्च<BR> शोभमानं समन्ततः Rām. 7. 70. 13.<BR>—6 The shoulder.<BR>—7 A Jaina or Buddhist temple, convent, monastery.<BR>—8 A temple in general.<BR>—9 Great expansion of the organs of speech.<BR>—10 Opening, expansion.<BR>—11 The palace or banner of Indra.<BR>—12 A palace in general.<BR>—13 A kind of bird.<BR>—14 (Mīmāṃsā) The triad of fires, viz. गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय and<BR> दक्षिण; विहारे लौकिकानामर्थ साधयेत् etc. MS. 12. 2. 1; (विहार<BR> इति गार्हपत्यादिरग्नित्रेता उच्यते विहरणात् ŚB. on MS. 12. 2. 1.).<BR>—15 N. of the country मगध (modern Bihar).<BR>—16 The sacrificerʼs house (यजमानगृह); Bhāg. 4. 5. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विहारगृहम्, विहारदासी, विहारभूमिः, विहारयात्रा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारगृहम्
विहारः + -गृहम् a pleasure-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारदासी
विहारः + -दासी a nun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारभूमिः|विहारभूमि
विहारः + -भूमिः a grazing ground, pasturage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारयात्रा
विहारः + -यात्रा a pleasure-walk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारणम्
विहारणम् Pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारिका
विहारिका A convent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारिन्
विहारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Diverting or amusing oneself by; मृगयाविहारिणः Ś. 1; Pt. 2. 20;<BR> व्योमैकान्तविहारिणोऽपि विहगाः संप्राप्नुवन्त्यापदम् H.<BR>—2 Expanding.<BR>—3 Beautiful, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहारवत्|विहारवन्त्
विहारवत् <i>a.</i> Delighting in; भक्षभोज्यविहारवान् Mb. 14. 59. 11; Ms. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृत|विहृतं
विहृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sported, played.<BR>—2 Expanded.<BR>—3 Transposed, varied.<BR>—4 Distributed, disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृतम्
विहृत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 One of the ten modes of indicating love used by women; see S. D. 125, 146;<BR> (written विकृत also in this sense).<BR>—2 Sport, play; Dk. 2. 6.<BR>—3 A walk.<BR>—4 Hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहृतिः|विहृति
विहृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Removal, taking away.<BR>—2 Sport, pastime, pleasure; अयं विन्ध्यो येनाहृतविहृतिराघ्मानमजहात् Mv. 7. 14.<BR>—3 Expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठः|विहेठ
विहेठः<BR>—1 Hurt, injury.<BR>—2 Afflicting, harassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठकः|विहेठक
विहेठकः<BR>—1 An injurer.<BR>—2 A reviler, calumniator; अतीवरूपसंपन्नो न कंचिदवमन्यते । अतीवजल्पन्<BR> दुर्वाचो भवतीह विहेठकः ॥ Mb. 1. 74. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेठनम्
विहेठनम्<BR>—1 Injuring, hurting.<BR>—2 Rubbing, grinding.<BR>—3 Afflicting.<BR>—4 Pain, sorrow, torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विहेल्
विहेल् <i>Caus.</i> Ā. (विहेलयते) To vex, annoy; Mb. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल्
विह्वल् €1 P. To stagger, tremble, shake about; अन्तर्भिन्नं भ्रमति<BR> हृदयं विह्वलत्यङ्गमङ्गम् Māl. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वल|विह्वलः
विह्वल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Agitated, disquieted, perturbed, confused; क्षणमात्रसखीं सुजातयोः<BR> स्तनयोस्तामवलोक्य विह्वला R. 8. 37.<BR>—2 Overcome with fear, alarmed.<BR>—3 Delirious, beside oneself.<BR>—4 Afflicted, distressed; वित्तव्याधिविकारविह्वलगिरां नामापि न श्रूयते<BR> Bh. 3. 59; Ku. 4. 4.<BR>—5 Desponding.<BR>—6 Fused, liquid.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: विह्वलचेतस्, विह्वलतनु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलचेतस्
विह्वल + -चेतस् <i>a.</i> low-spirited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विह्वलतनु
विह्वल + -तनु <i>a.</i> one whose body is exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वी
वी I. €2 P. (वेति, rarely used in classical literature)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To approach.<BR>—3 To pervade.<BR>—4 To bring, convey.<BR>—5 To throw, cast.<BR>—6 To eat, consume.<BR>—7 to obtain.<BR>—8 To conceive, bring forth.<BR>—9 To be born or produced.<BR>—10 To shine, be beautiful.<BR>—11 To desire, wish.<BR>—12 To shine. ━II. (वि + इ) €2 P.<BR>—1 To go away, depart; तस्यामहं त्वयि च संप्रति वीतचिन्तः Ś. 4. 13;<BR> so वीतभय, वीतक्रोध, etc.<BR>—2 To undergo a change; सदृशं त्रिषु लिङ्गेषु यन्न व्येति तदव्ययम् Sk.<BR>—3 To spend.<BR>—4 To be diffused, to spread.<BR>—5 To vanish, disappear.<BR>—6 To cross over, traverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीः
वीः<BR>—1 Act of going, motion.<BR>—2 A female bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीकः|वीक
वीकः<BR>—1 Wind.<BR>—2 A bird.<BR>—3 The mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीका
वीका = अक्षिमलम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीकाश|वीकाशः
वीकाश See विकाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्
वीक्ष् €1 Ā.<BR>—1 To see, behold; तं वीक्ष्य वेपथुमती Ku. 5. 85; सुभगं तथैव<BR> खलु सापि वीक्षते V. 4. 3.<BR>—2 To regard or consider as.<BR>—3 To think fit.<BR>—4 To study, peruse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षम्
वीक्षम्<BR>—1 A visible object.<BR>—2 Surprise, astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षः|वीक्ष|वीक्षं
वीक्षम् + .{@-क्षः, -क्षा@}<BR>—1 Seeing, gazing at.<BR>—2 Investigation.<BR>—3 Knowledge, intelligence.<BR>—4 Unconsciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षा
वीक्षम् + .{@-क्षः, -क्षा@}<BR>—1 Seeing, gazing at.<BR>—2 Investigation.<BR>—3 Knowledge, intelligence.<BR>—4 Unconsciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षणम्
वीक्षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Seeing, looking at, sight.<BR>—2 A glance.<BR>—3 Investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षणा
वीक्षणम्, -णा<BR>—1 Seeing, looking at, sight.<BR>—2 A glance.<BR>—3 Investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षणम्
वीक्षणम्, -णा + .{@-णम्@} An eye; आवव्राते वीक्षणे च क्षणेन Śi. 18. 30.<BR>—2 (In astrol.) Aspect of the planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्षितम्
वीक्षितम् A look, glance; अयुगपदुन्नमितभ्रु वीक्षितं च Ki. 10. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1485-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्य|वीक्ष्यं|वीक्ष्यः
वीक्ष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be looked at.<BR>—2 Visible, perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्यः|वीक्ष्य|वीक्ष्यं
वीक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यः@}<BR>—1 A dancer, an actor.<BR>—2 A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीक्ष्यम्
वीक्ष्य + .{@-क्ष्यम्@}<BR>—1 Anything to be looked at, a visible object.<BR>—2 Wonder, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीङ्खा|वींखा
वीङ्खा<BR>—1 Going, moving, progress.<BR>—2 One of the paces of a horse.<BR>—3 Dancing.<BR>—4 Junction, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचिः|वीचि
वीचिः <i>m., f.</i>, वीची [Uṇ. 4. 72]<BR>—1 A wave; समुद्रवीचीव चलस्वभावाः Pt. 1. 194; U. 3. 2; R. 6. 56, 12. 100;<BR> Me. 28.<BR>—2 Inconstancy, thoughtlessness.<BR>—3 Pleasure, delight.<BR>—4 Rest, leisure; कुतोऽवीचिर्वीचिस्तव यदि गता लोचनपथम् Gaṅgāṣṭaka (by Śaṃkarācārya) 6.<BR>—5 A ray of light.<BR>—6 Little.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीचिक्षोभः, वीचिमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीची
वीचिः <i>m., f.</i>, वीची [Uṇ. 4. 72]<BR>—1 A wave; समुद्रवीचीव चलस्वभावाः Pt. 1. 194; U. 3. 2; R. 6. 56, 12. 100;<BR> Me. 28.<BR>—2 Inconstancy, thoughtlessness.<BR>—3 Pleasure, delight.<BR>—4 Rest, leisure; कुतोऽवीचिर्वीचिस्तव यदि गता लोचनपथम् Gaṅgāṣṭaka (by Śaṃkarācārya) 6.<BR>—5 A ray of light.<BR>—6 Little.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीचिक्षोभः, वीचिमालिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचिक्षोभः|वीचिक्षोभ
वीचिः + -क्षोभः roughness of waves; वीचिक्षोभस्तनितविहगश्रेणिकाञ्चीगुणायाः Me. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीचिमालिन्
वीचिः + -मालिन् <i>m.</i> the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्
वीज् I. €1 Ā. (वीजते) To go. ━II. €10 U. (वीजयति-ते)<BR>—1 To fan, cool by fanning; खं वीज्यते मणिमयैरिव तालवृन्तैः Mk. 5. 13;<BR> Ku. 2. 42.<BR>—2 To stroke, caress. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि, उप, परि@} to fan; संलक्ष्यते पवनवेगचलैः<BR> पयोदै राजेव चामरवरैरुपवीज्यमानः Ṛs. 3. 4; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजनः|वीजन|वीजनं
वीजनः<BR>—1 The ruddy goose.<BR>—2 A sort of pheasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजनम्
वीजनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Fanning; तदनु ज्वलनं मदर्पितं त्वरयेर्दक्षिणवातबीजनैः<BR> Ku. 4. 36; Śi. 17. 6.<BR>—2 A fan.<BR>—3 A thing, substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज|वीजं
वीज, वीजक, वीजल See बीज, बीजक, बीजल,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजक|वीजकः
वीज, वीजक, वीजल See बीज, बीजक, बीजल,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजल
वीज, वीजक, वीजल See बीज, बीजक, बीजल,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिक
वीजिक, वीजिन्, वीज्य बीजिक, बीजिन्, and बीज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीजिन्
वीजिक, वीजिन्, वीज्य बीजिक, बीजिन्, and बीज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीज्य|वीज्यः
वीजिक, वीजिन्, वीज्य बीजिक, बीजिन्, and बीज्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटा
वीटा<BR>—1 A small piece of wood (about a span long) struck with a stick or bat<BR> in a game played by boys (called in Marāthī विटीदांडूचा खेळ); क्रीडन्तो<BR> वीटया तत्र वीराः पर्यचरन्मुदा । पपात कूपे सा वीटा तेषां वै क्रीडतां<BR> तदा ॥ Mb. 1. 131. 17.<BR>—2 A kind of metal or stone ball (held in the mouth as a form of penance);<BR> इत्येवं ब्रुवतस्तस्य जटी वीटामुखः कृशः Mb. 15. 26. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटिः|वीटि
वीटिः, वीटिका, वीटी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The betel-plant.<BR>—2 A preparation of betel (Mar. विडा = ताम्बूल q. v.).<BR>—3 A tie, fastening, knot (of a wearing garment).<BR>—4 The knot of a bodice; त्वं मुग्धाक्षि विनैव कञ्चुलिकया धत्से मनोहारिणीं<BR> लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि प्रियतमे तद्वीटिकासंस्पृशि । Amaru. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटिका
वीटिः, वीटिका, वीटी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The betel-plant.<BR>—2 A preparation of betel (Mar. विडा = ताम्बूल q. v.).<BR>—3 A tie, fastening, knot (of a wearing garment).<BR>—4 The knot of a bodice; त्वं मुग्धाक्षि विनैव कञ्चुलिकया धत्से मनोहारिणीं<BR> लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि प्रियतमे तद्वीटिकासंस्पृशि । Amaru. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीटी
वीटिः, वीटिका, वीटी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The betel-plant.<BR>—2 A preparation of betel (Mar. विडा = ताम्बूल q. v.).<BR>—3 A tie, fastening, knot (of a wearing garment).<BR>—4 The knot of a bodice; त्वं मुग्धाक्षि विनैव कञ्चुलिकया धत्से मनोहारिणीं<BR> लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि प्रियतमे तद्वीटिकासंस्पृशि । Amaru. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीडु
वीडु <i>a.</i> Ved. Strong, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणा
वीणा<BR>—1 The (Indian) lute; मूकीभूतायां वीणायाम् K.; उत्सङ्गे वा मलिनवसने<BR> सौम्य निक्षिप्य वीणाम् Me. 88.<BR>—2 Lightning.<BR>—3 A particular configuration of stars.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीणानुबन्धः, वीणास्यः, वीणादण्डः, वीणापाणिः, वीणाप्रसेवः, वीणावादः, वीणावादकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणानुबन्धः|वीणानुबन्ध
वीणा + -अनुबन्धः the tie of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणास्यः|वीणास्य
वीणा + -आस्यः an epithet of Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणादण्डः|वीणादण्ड|वीणादंड
वीणा + -दण्डः the neck of a lute; न हि तुम्बीफलविकलो वीणादण्डः<BR> प्रयाति महिमानम् Bv. 1. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणापाणिः|वीणापाणि
वीणा + -पाणिः N. of Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणाप्रसेवः|वीणाप्रसेव
वीणा + -प्रसेवः the damper on a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणावादः|वीणावाद
वीणा + -वादः, -वादकः a lutanist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणावादकः|वीणावादक
वीणा + -वादः, -वादकः a lutanist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीणिन्
वीणिन् <i>m.</i> A lute-player.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीत|वीतं|वीतः
वीत <i>p. p.</i> [वि˚ इ-क्त]<BR>—1 Gone, disappeared.<BR>—2 Gone away, departed.<BR>—3 Let go, loosed, set free.<BR>—4 Excepted, exempt.<BR>—5 Approved, liked.<BR>—6 Unfit for war.<BR>—7 Tame, quiet.<BR>—8 Freed from, devoid of (mostly in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">Page1486-2</a>]<BR> comp.); वीतचिन्त, वीतस्पृह, वीतभी, वीतशङ्क &c.<BR>—9 Desired, wished for.<BR>—10 Put on or worn; शुचिवल्कवीततनुः Ki. 6. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतः|वीत|वीतं
वीत + .{@-तः@} An elephant or horse unfit or untrained for war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतम्
वीत + .{@-तम्@} Pricking (an elephant) with the goad and striking with the<BR> legs; वीतवीतभया नागाः Ku. 6. 39 v. l. (see Malli. thereon); निर्धूतवीतमपि<BR> बालकमुल्ललन्तम् Śi. 5. 47.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीतदम्भ, वीतभय, वीतमत्सर, वीतमल, वीतराग, वीतशोकः, वीतसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतदम्भ|वीतदम्भः
वीत + -दम्भ <i>a.</i> humble, lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतभय|वीतभयः
वीत + -भय <i>a.</i> fearless, intrepid; वीतवीतभया नागाः Ku. 6. 39 (v. l.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतभयः|वीतभय
वीत + -भय + .({@-यः@}) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतमत्सर
वीत + -मत्सर <i>a.</i> free from envy; नियतो वीतमत्सरः Ms. 11. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतमल
वीत + -मल <i>a.</i> pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतराग|वीतरागः
वीत + -राग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 free from desire.<BR>—2 free from passion, calm, tranquil.<BR>—3 colourless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतरागः|वीतराग
वीत + -राग + .({@-गः@})<BR>—1 a sage who has subdued his passions; विशन्ति यद्यतयो वीतरागाः Bg. 8. 11.<BR>—2 a deified Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतशोकः|वीतशोक
वीत + -शोकः (= {@अशोकः@}) the Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतसूत्रम्
वीत + -सूत्रम् the sacred thread; V. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतंसः|वीतंस
वीतंसः<BR>—1 A cage, a cage or net for confining beasts or birds.<BR>—2 An aviary.<BR>—3 A place for preserving game.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतनौ
वीतनौ (<i>m.</i> dual) The sides of the larynx or throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतिः|वीति
वीतिः [वी-क्तिन्] A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतिः|वीति
वीतिः + .{@-तिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Going, motion.<BR>—2 Producing, production.<BR>—3 Enjoyment.<BR>—4 Eating.<BR>—5 Light, lustre.<BR>—6 Cleaning, purifying.<BR>—7 Separation; termination (निवृत्ति); भववीतये Ki. 6. 41, 44.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीतिहोत्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीतिहोत्रः|वीतिहोत्र
वीतिः + -होत्रः<BR>—1 fire.<BR>—2 the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथिः|वीथि
वीथिः, -थी <i>f.</i><BR> [विथ्-इन् वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 A road, way; पिपतिषतां विलङ्घ्य वीथीम् Ki. 7. 17; यदि रोहिण्याः<BR> शकटं भिनत्ति रविनन्दनो गगनबीथ्याम् Pt. 1. 211.<BR>—2 A row, line.<BR>—3 A market, stall, shop in a market; घनवीथिवीथिमवतीर्णवतः Śi. 9. 32.<BR>—4 A terrace in front of a house.<BR>—5 A variety of drama; it is thus defined in S. D.:− वीथ्यामेको भवेदङ्कः<BR> कश्चिदेकोऽत्र कल्प्यते । आकाशभाषितैरुक्तैश्चित्रां प्रत्युक्तिमाश्रितः । सूचयेद्<BR> भूरिशृङ्गारं किंचिदन्यान् रसानपि । मुखनिर्बहणे संधी अर्थप्रकृतयोऽखिलाः । 520.<BR>—6 A race-course; a training ground for horses; सिद्धं मुखे नवसु वीथिषु<BR> कश्चिदश्वम् Śi. 5. 60 (com. वीथयो नवाश्वानां सर्वत्र धारादार्ढ्यार्थाः<BR> परिमिताः प्रचारदेशाः).<BR>—7 A particular division of the planetary sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथी
वीथिः, -थी <i>f.</i><BR> [विथ्-इन् वा ङीप्]<BR>—1 A road, way; पिपतिषतां विलङ्घ्य वीथीम् Ki. 7. 17; यदि रोहिण्याः<BR> शकटं भिनत्ति रविनन्दनो गगनबीथ्याम् Pt. 1. 211.<BR>—2 A row, line.<BR>—3 A market, stall, shop in a market; घनवीथिवीथिमवतीर्णवतः Śi. 9. 32.<BR>—4 A terrace in front of a house.<BR>—5 A variety of drama; it is thus defined in S. D.:− वीथ्यामेको भवेदङ्कः<BR> कश्चिदेकोऽत्र कल्प्यते । आकाशभाषितैरुक्तैश्चित्रां प्रत्युक्तिमाश्रितः । सूचयेद्<BR> भूरिशृङ्गारं किंचिदन्यान् रसानपि । मुखनिर्बहणे संधी अर्थप्रकृतयोऽखिलाः । 520.<BR>—6 A race-course; a training ground for horses; सिद्धं मुखे नवसु वीथिषु<BR> कश्चिदश्वम् Śi. 5. 60 (com. वीथयो नवाश्वानां सर्वत्र धारादार्ढ्यार्थाः<BR> परिमिताः प्रचारदेशाः).<BR>—7 A particular division of the planetary sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथिका
वीथिका<BR>—1 A road &c.<BR>—2 A picture-gallery; or a large scroll of paper on which pictures are<BR> drawn (according to some); a wall (according to others); आर्यस्य चरित्रमस्यां<BR> वीथिकायामालिखितम् U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीथीकृत
वीथीकृत <i>a.</i> Placed or arranged in rows or heaps; कोटिशश्च<BR> सुवर्णं च तेषामकृतकं तथा । वीथीकृतममेयात्मा प्राहिणोन्मधुसूदनः ॥<BR> Mb. 1. 199. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीध्र|वीध्रं|वीध्रः
वीध्र^1 <i>a.</i> Pure, clean.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. note: alph. order; cf AP90 and MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीध्रम्
वीध्र + .{@-ध्रम्@}<BR>—1 The sky.<BR>—2 Wind, air.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीनाहः|वीनाह
वीनाहः The top or cover of a well; कूपवीनाहवेलायामपश्यत<BR> महागजम् Mb. 11. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीनाहिन्
वीनाहिन् <i>m.</i> A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीपा
वीपा Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1486-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीप्सा
वीप्सा<BR>—1 Pervasion.<BR>—2 Repetition of words to imply continuous or successive action; as in<BR> the example वृक्षं वृक्षं सिञ्चति; वीप्सायां द्विरुक्तिः.<BR>—3 Repetition in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीबुकोशः|वीबुकोश
वीबुकोशः A chowrie (चामर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीभ्
वीभ् €1 Ā. (वीभते) To boast, brag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर|वीरं|वीरः
वीर [अजेः रक् वीभावश्च Uṇ. 2. 13] <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Heroic, brave.<BR>—2 Mighty, powerful.<BR>—3 Excellent, eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरः|वीर|वीरं
वीर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A hero, warrior, champion; कोऽप्येष संप्रति नवः पुरुषावतारो वीरो<BR> न यस्य भगवान् भृगुनन्दनोऽपि U. 5. 33.<BR>—2 The sentiment of heroism (in rhetoric); अस्तोकवीरगुरुसाहसमद्भुतं<BR> च Mv. 1. 6; it is distinguished under four heads; दानवीर, धर्मवीर,<BR> दयावीर and युद्धवीर; (for explanation see these words s. v.).<BR>—3 An actor.<BR>—4 Fire.<BR>—5 The sacrificial fire.<BR>—6 A son; अस्य कुले वीरो जायते Ch. Up. 3. 13. 6; वीरं मे दत्त<BR> पितरः Śrāddhamantras.<BR>—7 A husband.<BR>—8 The Arjuna tree.<BR>—9 A Jaina.<BR>—10 The Karavīra tree.<BR>—11 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरम्
वीर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 A reed.<BR>—2 Pepper.<BR>—3 Rice-gruel.<BR>—4 The root of Uśīra q. v.<BR>—5 Iron; Gīrvāṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीराध्वन्, वीरमार्गः, वीराम्लः, वीराशंसनम्, वीरासनम्, वीरेशः, वीरेश्वरः, वीरोज्झः, वीरकाम, वीरकीटः, वीरगतिः, वीरजयन्तिका, वीरतरुः, वीरधन्वन्, वीरपट्टः, वीरपट्टिका, वीरपत्नी, वीरपानम्, वीरबाहुः, वीरभद्रः, वीरभवन्ती, वीरभावः, वीरमर्दलः, वीरमुद्रिका, वीररजस्, वीररसः, वीररेणुः, वीरलोकः, वीरवादः, वीरविप्लावकः, वीरवृक्षः, वीरव्रत, वीरव्रतम्, वीरशङ्कुः, वीरशयः, वीरशयनम्, वीरशय्या, वीरसूः, वीरसेनः, वीरसैन्यम्, वीरस्कन्धः, वीरस्थानम्, वीरहत्या, वीरहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराध्वन्
वीर + -अध्वन्, -मार्गः a heroic death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमार्गः|वीरमार्ग
वीर + -अध्वन्, -मार्गः a heroic death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराम्लः|वीराम्ल
वीर + -अम्लः a kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीराशंसनम्
वीर + -आशंसनम्<BR>—1 keeping watch.<BR>—2 the post of danger in battle.<BR>—3 a forlorn hope.<BR>—4 a field of battle; पयोदजालमिव तद्वीराशंसनमाबभौ Śi. 19. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरासनम्
वीर + -आसनम्<BR>—1 a kind of posture practised in meditation; एकं पादमथैकस्मिन् विन्यस्योरौ<BR> तु संस्थितम् । इतरस्मिस्तथैवोरुं वीरासनमिति स्मृतम् ॥ cf. पर्यङ्क.<BR>—2 kneeling on one knee.<BR>—3 a field of battle.<BR>—4 the station of a sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरेशः|वीरेश
वीर + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 epithets of Śiva.<BR>—2 a great hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरेश्वरः|वीरेश्वर
वीर + -ईशः, -ईश्वरः<BR>—1 epithets of Śiva.<BR>—2 a great hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरोज्झः|वीरोज्झ
वीर + -उज्झः a Brahmaṇa who omits to offer oblations to the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरकाम
वीर + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of male offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरकीटः|वीरकीट
वीर + -कीटः an insignificant or contemptible warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरगतिः|वीरगति
वीर + -गतिः Indraʼs heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरजयन्तिका|वीरजयंतिका
वीर + -जयन्तिका<BR>—1 a war-dance.<BR>—2 war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतरुः|वीरतरु
वीर + -तरुः<BR>—1 the Bilva tree.<BR>—2 the Arjuna tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरधन्वन्
वीर + -धन्वन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपट्टः|वीरपट्ट
वीर + -पट्टः a sort of military dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपट्टिका
वीर + -पट्टिका a gold band worn by men across the forehead; नलस्य<BR> भाले मणिवीरपट्टिकानिभेव लग्नः परिधिर्विधोर्बभौ N. 15. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपत्नी
वीर + -पत्नी the wife of a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरपानम्
वीर + -पानम् ({@णम्@}) an exciting or refreshing drink taken by<BR> soldiers either before or after a battle; मदोऽयं संप्रहारेऽस्मिन् वीरपानं<BR> समर्थ्यताम् Rām. 4. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरबाहुः|वीरबाहु
वीर + -बाहुः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभद्रः|वीरभद्र
वीर + -भद्रः<BR>—1 N. of a powerful hero created by Śiva from his matted hair; see दक्ष;<BR> महावीरोऽपि रे भद्र मम सर्वगणेष्विह । वीरभद्राख्यया हि त्वं प्रथितिं<BR> परमां व्रज । कुरु मे सत्वरं कर्म दक्षयज्ञं क्षयं नय ॥ Kāśīkhaṇḍa.<BR>—2 a distinguished hero.<BR>—3 a horse fit for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>—4 a kind of fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभवन्ती
वीर + -भवन्ती the elder sister; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरभावः|वीरभाव
वीर + -भावः heroic nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमर्दलः|वीरमर्दल
वीर + -मर्दलः a war-drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरमुद्रिका
वीर + -मुद्रिका a ring worn on the middle toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीररजस्
वीर + -रजस् <i>n.</i> red lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीररसः|वीररस
वीर + -रसः<BR>—1 the sentiment of heroism.<BR>—2 a warlike feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीररेणुः|वीररेणु
वीर + -रेणुः N. of Bhīmasena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरलोकः|वीरलोक
वीर + -लोकः Indraʼs heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवादः|वीरवाद
वीर + -वादः glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरविप्लावकः|वीरविप्लावक
वीर + -विप्लावकः a Brāhmaṇa who performs sacrifices by means of money<BR> got from the lowest<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">Page1487-2</a>]<BR> castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवृक्षः|वीरवृक्ष
वीर + -वृक्षः<BR>—1 the Arjuna tree.<BR>—2 the marking-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरव्रत
वीर + -व्रत <i>a.</i> adhering to oneʼs purpose; पूर्णः श्रुतधरो राजन्नाह<BR> वीरव्रतो मुनिः Bhāg. 10. 87. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरव्रतम्
वीर + -व्रतम् heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरशङ्कुः|वीरशङ्कु
वीर + -शङ्कुः an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरशयः|वीरशय
वीर + -शयः, -शयनम्, -शय्या<BR>—1 the couch of a dead or wounded hero in a battle; battlefield; कलेवरं योगरतो विजह्याद्यदग्रणीर्वीरशयेऽनिवृत्तः Bhāg. 6. 10. 33.<BR>—2 a particular posture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरशयनम्
वीर + -शयः, -शयनम्, -शय्या<BR>—1 the couch of a dead or wounded hero in a battle; battlefield; कलेवरं योगरतो विजह्याद्यदग्रणीर्वीरशयेऽनिवृत्तः Bhāg. 6. 10. 33.<BR>—2 a particular posture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरशय्या
वीर + -शयः, -शयनम्, -शय्या<BR>—1 the couch of a dead or wounded hero in a battle; battlefield; कलेवरं योगरतो विजह्याद्यदग्रणीर्वीरशयेऽनिवृत्तः Bhāg. 6. 10. 33.<BR>—2 a particular posture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसूः
वीर + -सूः <i>f.</i> the mother of a hero; (so वीरप्रसवा, -प्रसूः,<BR> -प्रसविनी); तस्यात्मनोऽर्ध पल्यास्ते नान्वगाद्वीरसूः कृपी Bhāg. 1. 7. 45.<BR>—2 the mother of a male child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसेनः|वीरसेन|वीरसेनं
वीर + -सेनः N. of the father of Nala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरसैन्यम्
वीर + -सैन्यम् garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरस्कन्धः|वीरस्कन्ध|वीरस्कंध
वीर + -स्कन्धः a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरस्थानम्
वीर + -स्थानम् = वीरासन (1); स्थाणुभूतो महातेजा वीरस्थानेन<BR> पाण्डव Mb. 3. 122. 2, 13. 142. 8; (= स्वर्ग) heaven; वीरासनं<BR> वीरशय्यां वीरस्थानमुपागतम् । अक्षयास्तस्य वै लोकाः सर्वकामगमास्तथा ॥<BR> Mb. 13. 7. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरहत्या
वीर + -हत्या the killing of a man; murder of a son; चान्द्रायणं चरेन्मासं<BR> वीरहत्यासमं हि तत् Ms. 11. 41; वीरहत्यामवाप्तोऽसि वह्नीनुद्वास्य<BR> यत्नतः Śāṅkaradigvijaya 8. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरहन्
वीर + -हन् <i>m.</i> a Brāhmaṇa who has neglected his domestic fire;<BR> तेनादृश्यन्त वीरध्ना न तु वीरहणो जनाः N. 17. 197; (cf. Note on<BR> N. 17. 197 given by the English translator Handiqui, p. 630.).<BR>—2 A child-murderer; वीरहा वा एष देवानां भवति योऽग्निमुद्वासयते Ts. 1. 5. 2.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरकः|वीरक
वीरकः<BR>—1 A hero.<BR>—2 The Karavīra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतरः|वीरतर|वीरतरं
वीरतरः<BR>—1 A great hero.<BR>—2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरतरम्
वीरतरः + .{@-रम्@} A kind of fragrant grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरंधरः|वीरन्धर|वीरंधर
वीरंधरः<BR>—1 A peacock.<BR>—2 Fighting with beasts.<BR>—3 A leather-jacket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवत्|वीरवन्त्
वीरवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Full of heroes.<BR>—2 Manly, heroic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरवती
वीरवत् + .{@-ती@} A woman whose husband and sons are living; स्त्रियो वीरवतीश्चार्चेत्<BR> स्रग्गन्धवलिमण्डनैः Bhāg. 6. 18. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरा
वीरा<BR>—1 The wife of a hero.<BR>—2 A wife.<BR>—3 A mother, matron.<BR>—4 A kind of perfume (called Murā).<BR>—5 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—6 An aloe.<BR>—7 The plantain tree.<BR>—8 A woman with a husband and a son living; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरायते
वीरायते (वीरयते) Den. Ā. To act like a hero, show heroism;<BR> इतोऽपि किं वीरयसे न कुर्वतः नृपान् धनुर्बाणगुणैर्वशंवदान् N. 12. 27;<BR> Ait. Br. 12. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरयते
वीरायते (वीरयते) Den. Ā. To act like a hero, show heroism;<BR> इतोऽपि किं वीरयसे न कुर्वतः नृपान् धनुर्बाणगुणैर्वशंवदान् N. 12. 27;<BR> Ait. Br. 12. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरणम्
वीरणम् N. of a fragrant grass, Andropogon Muricatus, (the root of<BR> which is used as a refrigerant); वीरणस्तम्बके लग्नाः सर्वतः परिभाक्षिते Mb. 1. 13. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरणी
वीरणी<BR>—1 A side-look.<BR>—2 A deep place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरिणम्
वीरिणम् See ईरिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुध्
वीरुध्, -धा <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A spreading creeper; लता प्रतानिनी वीरुत् Ak.; आहोस्वित् प्रसवो<BR> ममापचरितैर्विष्टम्भितो बीरुधाम् Ś. 5. 9; Ku. 5. 34; R. 8. 36.<BR>—2 A branch, shoot.<BR>—3 A plant which grows after being cut.<BR>—4 A creeper, a shrub in general; भृशं ददर्शाश्रममण्डपोपमाः सपुष्पहासाः<BR> स निवेशवीरुथः Ki. 4. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुधा
वीरुध्, -धा <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A spreading creeper; लता प्रतानिनी वीरुत् Ak.; आहोस्वित् प्रसवो<BR> ममापचरितैर्विष्टम्भितो बीरुधाम् Ś. 5. 9; Ku. 5. 34; R. 8. 36.<BR>—2 A branch, shoot.<BR>—3 A plant which grows after being cut.<BR>—4 A creeper, a shrub in general; भृशं ददर्शाश्रममण्डपोपमाः सपुष्पहासाः<BR> स निवेशवीरुथः Ki. 4. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1487-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीरुधः|वीरुध
वीरुधः A tree; तदा वैरे समुत्पन्ने न दग्धो वीरुधो यथा Rām. 7. 35. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यम्
वीर्यम् [वीर्-यत्, वीरस्य भावो यत् वा]<BR>—1 Heroism, prowess, valour; वीर्यावदानेषु कृतावमर्षः Ki. 3. 43;<BR> R. 2. 4, 3. 62, 11. 72; Ve. 3. 3.<BR>—2 Vigour, strength.<BR>—3 Virility; वीर्यशौर्याभ्यां च पिता ऋषभ इतीदं नाम चकार Bhāg. 5. 4. 2.<BR>—4 Energy, firmness, courage.<BR>—5 Power, potency; जाने तपसो वीर्यम् Ś. 3. 2.<BR>—6 Efficacy (of medicines); अतिवीर्यवतीव भेषजे बहुरल्पीयसि दृश्यते<BR> गुणः Ki. 2. 4; Ku. 2. 48.<BR>—7 Semen virile; अमी हि वीर्यप्रभवं भवस्य Ku. 3. 15; वसोर्वीर्योत्पन्नामभजत<BR> मुनिर्मत्स्यतनयाम् Pt. 4. 50.<BR>—8 Splendour, lustre.<BR>—9 The seed of plants.<BR>—10 Dignity, consequence.<BR>—11 Poison.<BR>—12 Gold (हिरण्य); अन्नं वीर्य ग्रहीतव्यं प्रेतकर्मण्यपातिते<BR> Mb. 12. 165. 39.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वीर्याधानम्, वीर्यकरः, वीर्यजः, वीर्यप्रपातः, वीर्यशालिन्, वीर्यशुल्क, वीर्यहीन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्याधानम्
वीर्यम् + -आधानम् impregnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यकरः|वीर्यकर
वीर्यम् + -करः marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यजः|वीर्यज|वीर्य्यजः
वीर्यम् + -जः a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यप्रपातः|वीर्यप्रपात
वीर्यम् + -प्रपातः seminal effusion, discharge of semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यशालिन्
वीर्यम् + -शालिन् <i>a.</i> strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यशुल्क
वीर्यम् + -शुल्क <i>a.</i> purchased by valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यहीन|वीर्य्यहीन
वीर्यम् + -हीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 cowardly, pusilanimous.<BR>—2 seedless.<BR>—3 impotent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्यवत्|वीर्यवन्त्|वीर्य्यवत्
वीर्यवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Strong, stout, vigorous.<BR>—2 Efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीर्या|वीर्य्या
वीर्या <i>f.</i> (= वीर्यम्); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवधः|वीवध
वीवधः<BR>—1 A yoke for carrying burdens.<BR>—2 A burden.<BR>—3 Store of corn etc.; रुध्यध्वं निर्विषासूञ्शिशुयुवतिजनान् वीवधांश्चाद्रियध्वम्<BR> Mv. 6. 16; Śi. 2. 64.<BR>—4 A way, road; अज्ञातवीवधासारतोयशस्यो व्रजेत्तु यः Pt. 3. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीवधिकः|वीवधिक
वीवधिकः<BR>—1 A man who carries loads by means of a yoke.<BR>—2 A general dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीशः|वीश
वीशः A kind of weight (= 20 Palas = ¹⁄₅ Tulā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वीहारः|वीहार
वीहारः<BR>—1 A Buddhist or Jaina convent.<BR>—2 A sanctuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुङ्ग्|वुंग्
वुङ्ग् €1 P. (वुङ्गति) To leave, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुण्ट्|वुंट्
वुण्ट् €10 U. (वुण्टयति-ते)<BR>—1 To hurt, kill.<BR>—2 To perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुन्ध्
वुन्ध् €10 P. (वुन्धयति) To kill, to hurt; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुवूर्षु
वुवूर्षु <i>a.</i> Desirous of choosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वुस्
वुस् See बुस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वूर्ण
वूर्ण <i>a.</i> Chosen, selected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृ
वृ I. €1. €5. €9 U. (वरति-ते, वृणोति-वृणुते, वृणाति-वृणीते, वृत;<BR> <i>pass.</i> व्रियते)<BR>—1 To choose, select as a boon; वृतं तेनेदमेव प्राक् Ku. 2. 56; ववार<BR> रामस्य वनप्रयाणम् Bk. 3. 6.<BR>—2 To choose for oneself (Ātm.); वृणते हि विमृश्यकारिणं गुणलुब्धाः<BR> स्वयमेव संपदः Ki. 2. 30; यदेव बव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतम् R. 3. 6.<BR>—3 To choose in marriage, woo, court; अयोनिजां राजसुतां वरीतुम् Mv. 3. 28;<BR> A. R. 3. 42.<BR>—4 To beg, solicit, ask for.<BR>—5 To cover, conceal, hide, screen, envelop; मेघैर्वृतश्चन्द्रमाः Mk. 5. 14.<BR>—6 To surround, encompass; वृतस्त्वं पात्रेसमितैः खट्बाऽऽरूढः प्रमादवान्<BR> Bk. 5. 10; U. 4. 18; R. 12. 61.<BR>—7 To ward off, keep away, restrain, check.<BR>—8 To hinder, oppose, obstruct.<BR>—9 To love, adore. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">Page1488-2</a>]<BR> (वारयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cover, conceal.<BR>—2 To avert from (with abl.).<BR>—3 To prevent, ward off, restrain, suppress, check, hinder; शक्यो वारयितुं<BR> जलेन हुतभुक् Bh. 2. 11. ━<i>Desid.</i> (वुवूर्षति-ते, विवरिषति-ते;<BR> विवरीषति-ते) To wish to choose. ━II. €10 U. (वरयति-ते)<BR>—1 To choose, select; वरं वरयते कन्या माता वित्तं पिता श्रुतम् Pt. 4. 68.<BR>—2 To choose in marriage.<BR>—3 To ask for, beg, solicit, (with two acc.); तां त्वां संवरणस्यार्थे<BR> वरयामि विभावसो Mb.; शैलेन्द्रं वरयामासुर्गङ्गां त्रिपथगां नदीम् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृत|वृतः
वृत <i>p. p.</i> [वृ-क्त]<BR>—1 Chosen, selected.<BR>—2 Covered, screened.<BR>—3 Hidden.<BR>—4 Surrounded, encompassed.<BR>—5 Agreed or assented to.<BR>—6 Hired.<BR>—7 Spoiled, vitiated.<BR>—8 Served.<BR>—9 Affected by.<BR>—10 Round, circular.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वृतार्चिस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतार्चिस्
वृत + -अर्चिस् night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिः|वृति
वृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Choosing, selecting.<BR>—2 Hiding, covering, concealing.<BR>—3 Asking, soliciting.<BR>—4 An entreaty, a request.<BR>—5 Surrounding, encompassing.<BR>—6 A hedge, fence, an enclosure; प्रत्यासन्नौ कुरबकवृतेर्माघवीमण्डपस्य<BR> Me. 80; Māl. 6. 19.<BR>—7 Cultivation (esp. that of the Piper Betel).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वृतिद्रुमः, वृतिमार्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिद्रुमः|वृतिद्रुम
वृतिः + -द्रुमः a boundary tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिमार्गः|वृतिमार्ग
वृतिः + -मार्गः a fenced road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिंकर|वृतिङ्कर|वृतिंकरः|वृतिङ्करः
वृतिंकर <i>a.</i> Surrounding, encompassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृतिंकरः|वृतिङ्कर|वृतिंकर|वृतिङ्करः
वृतिंकर + .{@-रः@} The tree called विकङ्कत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1488-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृक्
