वृषभगतिः|वृषभगति
वृषभः + -केतुः, -गतिः, -ध्वजः epithets of Śiva; पुत्रीकृतोऽसौ वृषभध्वजेन<BR> R. 2. 36; Ku. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभध्वजः|वृषभध्वज
वृषभः + -केतुः, -गतिः, -ध्वजः epithets of Śiva; पुत्रीकृतोऽसौ वृषभध्वजेन<BR> R. 2. 36; Ku. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभयानम्
वृषभः + -यानम् a car drawn by oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभषोडशा
वृषभः + -षोडशा (pl.) fifteen cows and a bull; ज्येष्ठस्तु जातो ज्येष्ठायां<BR> हरेद् वृषभषोडशाः Ms. 9. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभस्कन्ध
वृषभः + -स्कन्ध <i>a.</i> broad-shouldered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषभी
वृषभी <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A widow.<BR>—2 Mucuna Pruriens (कवच).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्यति
वृषस्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To long for a bull.<BR>—2 To long for sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषस्यन्ती|वृषस्यंती
वृषस्यन्ती<BR>—1 A woman longing for sexual intercourse (with acc. of male); रघुनन्दनं<BR> वृषस्यन्ती शूर्पणखा प्राप्ता Mv. 5; इति रामो वृषस्यन्तीं वृषस्कन्धः<BR> शशास ताम् R. 12. 34; Bk. 4. 30.<BR>—2 A libidinous or lascivious woman.<BR>—3 A cow in heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपायी
वृषाकपायी^1<BR>—1 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 Of Gaurī.<BR>—3 Of Śachī.<BR>—4 Of Svāhā, wife of Agni.<BR>—5 Of the dawn, wife of the sun.<BR>—6 Of the mother of Indra.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170713. note: confirm by alph. ordering and by MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषाकपिः|वृषाकपि
वृषाकपिः<BR>—1 An epithet of the sun.<BR>—2 Of Viṣṇu; तत्र गत्वा जगन्नाथं देवदेवं वृषाकपिम् Bhāg. 10. 1. 20;<BR> Mb. 12. 43. 10.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR>—4 Of Indra.<BR>—5 Of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायणः|वृषायण
वृषायणः<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषायते
वृषायते Den. Ā. Ved.<BR>—1 To act like a bull.<BR>—2 To roar like a bull.<BR>—3 To fertilize, sprinkle with water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषिन्
वृषिन् <i>m.</i> A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषी
वृषी, वृसी The seat of an ascetic or religious student (made<BR> of Kuśa grass); see बृशी(षी)सी; वृष्यामुपविवेश ह Mb. 15. 27. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृसी
वृषी, वृसी The seat of an ascetic or religious student (made<BR> of Kuśa grass); see बृशी(षी)सी; वृष्यामुपविवेश ह Mb. 15. 27. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्ट
वृष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Rained.<BR>—2 Raining.<BR>—3 Showering, pouring down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1493-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिः|वृष्टि
वृष्टिः <i>f.</i> [वृष्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Rain, a shower of rain; आदित्याज्जायते वृष्टिर्वृष्टेरन्नं ततः प्रजाः Ms. 3. 76.<BR>—2 A shower (of anything); अस्त्रवृष्टि R. 3. 58; पुष्पवृष्टि 2. 60;<BR> so शर˚, धन˚, उपल˚ &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वृष्टिकालः, वृष्टिघ्नी, वृष्टिजीवन, वृष्टिपातः, वृष्टिभूः, वृष्टिसंपातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिकालः|वृष्टिकाल
वृष्टिः + -कालः the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिघ्नी
वृष्टिः + -घ्नी small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिजीवन|वृष्टिजीवनः
वृष्टिः + -जीवन <i>a.</i> nourished or watered by rain (as a country); cf.<BR> देवमातृक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिजीवनः|वृष्टिजीवन
वृष्टिः + -जीवन + .({@-नः@}) the Chātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिपातः|वृष्टिपात
वृष्टिः + -पातः a shower of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिभूः
वृष्टिः + -भूः a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिसंपातः|वृष्टिसम्पात
वृष्टिः + -संपातः a shower of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्टिमत्|वृष्टिमन्त्
वृष्टिमत् <i>a.</i> Raining, rainy. ━<i>m.</i> A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्य|वृष्यं|वृष्यः
वृष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be rained or showered down.<BR>—2 Stimulating amorous desire, provocative of sexual vigour, aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्यः|वृष्य|वृष्यं
वृष्य + .{@-ष्यः@} A kind of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्यम्
वृष्य + .{@-ष्यम्@} Stimulating amorous desires (वाजीकरणम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषयः|वृषय
वृषयः<BR>—1 Refuge, shelter.<BR>—2 Asylum. ━<i>a.</i> Superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलः|वृषल
वृषलः [वृष् कलच्]<BR>—1 A Śudra.<BR>—2 A horse.<BR>—3 Garlic.<BR>—4 A sinner, wicked or irreligious man; वृषो हि भगवान् धर्मस्तस्य<BR> यः कुरुते ह्यलम् । वृषलं तं विदुर्देवास्तस्माद्धर्मं न लोपयेत् ॥<BR> Ms. 8. 16; वृषलो गृञ्जने शूद्रे चन्द्रगुप्ते च राजनि ।<BR>—5 An outcast.<BR>—6 N. of Chandragupta (particularly used by Chaṇakya, see <i>inter alia</i><BR> Mu. acts 1 and 3).<BR>—7 A man of one of the three highest classes who has lost his caste by<BR> the omission of prescribed duties.<BR>—8 A dancer.<BR>—9 An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलम्
वृषलः + .{@-लम्@} A long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलकः|वृषलक
वृषलकः A contemptible Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषली
वृषली<BR>—1 An unmarried girl twelve years old; particularly, a girl remaining<BR> unmarried at her fatherʼs house in whom menstruation has commenced; पितुर्गेहे<BR> च या नारी रजः पश्यत्यसंस्कृता । भ्रूणहत्या पितुस्तस्याः सा कन्या वृषली स्मृता ॥.<BR>—2 A woman during menstruation.<BR>—3 A barren woman.<BR>—4 The mother of a still-born child.<BR>—5 A Śūdra female, or the wife of a Śūdra.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वृषलीपतिः, वृषलीफेनः, वृषलीवृत्ति, वृषलीसेवनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलीपतिः|वृषलीपति
वृषली + -पतिः the husband of a Śūdra woman; Ms. 3. 155; Mb. 7. 73. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलीफेनः
वृषली + -फेनः the lip-moisture (अधररस) of a वृषली; वृषलीफेनपीतस्य<BR> … … निष्कृतिर्न विधीयते Ms. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलीवृत्ति
वृषली + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> brought up by वृषलs; Ms. 3. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृषलीसेवनम्
वृषली + -सेवनम् intercourse with a Śūdra female; यत् करोत्येकरात्रेण<BR> वृषलीसेवनाद् द्विजः Ms. 11. 178.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णि|वृष्णिः
वृष्णि [वृषेः निः किच्च Uṇ. 4. 50-51] <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Heretical; heterodox.<BR>—2 Angry, passionate.<BR>—3 Ved. Raining. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A cloud.<BR>—2 A ram.<BR>—3 A ray of light.<BR>—4 N. of an ancestor of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—5 N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—6 Of Indra.<BR>—7 Of Agni.<BR>—8 Air, wind.<BR>—9 A heretic.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वृष्णिगर्भः, वृष्णिपालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णिगर्भः|वृष्णिगर्भ
वृष्णि + -गर्भः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृष्णिपालः|वृष्णिपाल
वृष्णि + -पालः a shepherd; केनापि कृपालुना वृष्णिपालेन स्वकुटीरमावेश्य Dk. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

