वृहती
वृहती<BR>—1 The lute of Nārada.<BR>—2 The number ‘thirty-six’.<BR>—3 A mantle, cloak, wrapper.<BR>—4 Speech.<BR>—5 A reservoir (as of water); see बृहती also.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वृहतीपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहतीपतिः|वृहतीपति
वृहती + -पतिः An epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृहस्पति|वृहस्पतिः
वृहस्पति See बृहस्पति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वॄ
वॄ €9 U. (वृणाति, वृणीते, वूर्ण; <i>pass.</i> वूर्यते; <i>desid.</i><BR> वुवूर्षति-ते or विवरिषति-ते or विवरीषति-ते) To choose,<BR> select; (see वृ I.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वे
वे €1 U. (वयति-ते, उत; <i>Caus.</i> वाययति-ते)<BR>—1 To weave; सितांशुवर्णैर्वयति स्म तद्गुणैः N. 1. 12.<BR>—2 To braid, plait.<BR>—3 To sew.<BR>—4 To cover, overspread.<BR>—5 To make, compose, string together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेकटः|वेकट
वेकटः<BR>—1 A buffoon.<BR>—2 A jeweller.<BR>—3 A youth.<BR>—4 A kind of fish (Med. spells with ब); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेक्षणम्
वेक्षणम् Looking after, care about; पारिणाह्यस्य वेक्षणे (नियोजयेत्) Ms. 9. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगः|वेग
वेगः [विज्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Impulse, impetus.<BR>—2 Speed, velocity, rapidity.<BR>—3 Agitation.<BR>—4 Impetuosity, violence, force.<BR>—5 A stream, current; as in अम्बुवेगः; रुरोध नर्मदावेगं बाहुभिर्बहुभिर्वृतः<BR> Rām. 7. 32. 4, 6.<BR>—6 Energy, activity, determination.<BR>—7 Power, strength; ऊरू भग्नौ प्रसह्याजौ गदया भीमवेगया Mb. 1. 2. 288;<BR> मदनज्वरस्य वेगात् K.<BR>—8 Circulation, working, effect (as of poison); चिराद्वेगारम्भी प्रसृत<BR> इव तीव्रो विषरसः U. 2. 26; V. 5. 18.<BR>—9 Haste, rashness, sudden impulse; कृत्यं न कुरुते वेगान्न स संतापमाप्नुयात् Pt. 1. 109.<BR>—10 The flight of an arrow; घननीहार इवाविषक्तवेगः Ki. 13. 24.<BR>—11 Love, passion.<BR>—12 The external manifestation of an internal emotion.<BR>—13 Delight, pleasure.<BR>—14 Evacuation of the feces; स्वभावतः प्रवृत्तानां मलादीनां जिजीविषुः ।<BR> न वेगं धारयेद्धीरः कामादीनां च धारयेत् ॥ Rājanighaṇṭu.<BR>—15 Semen virile.<BR>—16 Pleasure, delight. —17 Attack, paroxysm (of a disease); Suśr.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेगानिलः, वेगाघातः, वेगदण्डः, वेगनाशनः, वेगरोधः, वेगवाहिन्, वेगविधारणम्, वेगसरः, वेगहरिणः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगानिलः|वेगानिल
वेगः + -अनिलः —1 blast caused by speed; यष्टपग्रे च समं स्थितो ध्वजपटः<BR> प्रान्ते च वेगानिलात् V. 1. 5.<BR>—2 a strong or violent wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगाघातः|वेगाघात
वेगः + -आघातः<BR>—1 sudden arresting of velocity, check of speed.<BR>—2 obstruction of excretion, constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगदण्डः|वेगदण्ड
वेगः + -दण्डः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगनाशनः|वेगनाशन
वेगः + -नाशनः the phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगरोधः|वेगरोध
वेगः + -रोधः = ˚आघातः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगवाहिन्
वेगः + -वाहिन् <i>a.</i> swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगविधारणम्
वेगः + -विधारणम्<BR>—1 checking of speed.<BR>—2 constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगसरः|वेगसर
वेगः + -सरः a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगहरिणः
वेगः + -हरिणः a kind of antelope; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगित|वेगितः
वेगित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Quickened, expedited, hastened.<BR>—2 Agitated, rough (as the sea).<BR>—3 Swift, rapid; तस्मिन् वालिनि दुर्वृत्ते निपतिष्यन्ति वेगिताः (शराः)<BR> Rām. 4. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिन्
वेगिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Swift, fleet, impetuous, violent, rapid. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A courier.<BR>—2 A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेगिनी
वेगिन् + .{@-नी@} A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेङ्काः
वेङ्काः N. of a people in the south of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेङ्कटः|वेङ्कट|वेंकट|वेंकटः
वेङ्कटः, वेङ्कटाद्रिः, -गिरिः N. of a mountain (तिरुपति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेङ्कटाद्रिः|वेङ्कटाद्रि
वेङ्कटः, वेङ्कटाद्रिः, -गिरिः N. of a mountain (तिरुपति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेङ्कटगिरिः|वेङ्कटगिरि
वेङ्कटः, वेङ्कटाद्रिः, -गिरिः N. of a mountain (तिरुपति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेङ्घरः|वेङ्घर
वेङ्घरः Pride of beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेचा
वेचा Hire, wages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेजित
वेजित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Agitated, frightened.<BR>—2 Enhanced, increased; Mb. 7. 188. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1494-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेडम्
वेडम् A kind of sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेडा
वेडा A boat. (See बेडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेण्
वेण्, वेन् €1 U. (वेणति-ते, वेनति-ते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To know, recognize, perceive.<BR>—3 To reflect, consider.<BR>—4 To take.<BR>—5 To play on an instrument.<BR>—6 To see.<BR>—7 To praise, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्
वेण्, वेन् €1 U. (वेणति-ते, वेनति-ते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To know, recognize, perceive.<BR>—3 To reflect, consider.<BR>—4 To take.<BR>—5 To play on an instrument.<BR>—6 To see.<BR>—7 To praise, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणः|वेण
वेणः<BR>—1 A musician by caste; cf. वैदेहकेन त्वम्बुष्ठपामुत्पन्नो वेण उच्यते<BR> Ms. 10. 19; वेणानां भाण्डवादनम् 10. 49.<BR>—2 N. of a king, son of Aṅga and said to be a descendant of Manu Svāyambhuva.<BR> [When he became king, he issued a proclamation prohibiting all worship<BR> and sacrifices. The sages strongly remonstrated with him, but when he<BR> turned a deaf ear to their words, they killed him with ‘blades of consecrated Kuśa grass’<BR>. The kingdom was now without a ruler. So they rubbed the<BR> thigh of the dead body, until a Niṣāda came forth, short in stature and<BR> with a flat face. They then rubbed the right arm, and from it sprang the<BR> majestic Pṛthu (see Pṛthu). According to the Padma Purāṇa, Veṇa<BR> began his reign well, but subsequently fell in to Jaina heresy. He is<BR> also said to have caused confusion of castes; cf. Ms. 7. 41, 9. 66-67.].<BR>—3 A worker in reed or bamboo; Ms. 4. 215 (com. वेणोर्भेदेन यो जीवति,<BR> बुरुड इति विश्वरूपः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणा
वेणा N. of a river (joining the Kṛṣṇā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिः|वेणि
वेणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [वेण्-इन्-वा डीप् Uṇ. 4. 18]<BR>—1 Braided hair, a braid of hair; तरङ्गिणी वेणिरिवायता भुवः Śi. 12. 75;<BR> Me. 18.<BR>—2 Hair twisted into a single unornamented braid and allowed to fall on<BR> the back (said to be worn by women whose husbands are absent from them);<BR> वनान्निवृत्तेन रघूत्तमेन मुक्ता स्वयं वेणिरिवावभासे R. 14. 12;<BR> अबलावेणिमोक्षोत्सुकानि Me. 101; Ku. 2. 61.<BR>—3 Continuous flow, current, stream; जलवेणिरम्यां रेवां यदि प्रेक्षितुमस्ति<BR> कामः R. 6. 43; Me. 20; प्रवृत्तबाष्पवेणिकं चक्षुः प्रमृज्य K.;<BR> cf. the word त्रिवेणि also.<BR>—4 The confluence of two or more rivers.<BR>—5 The confluence of the Ganges, Yamunā and Sarasvatī.<BR>—6 N. of a river.<BR>—7 The property re-united after it has been before divided.<BR>—8 A cascade.<BR>—9 A dam, bridge.<BR>—10 A ewe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेणिबन्धः, वेणिवेधनी, वेणिवेधिनी, वेणिसंहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणी
वेणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [वेण्-इन्-वा डीप् Uṇ. 4. 18]<BR>—1 Braided hair, a braid of hair; तरङ्गिणी वेणिरिवायता भुवः Śi. 12. 75;<BR> Me. 18.<BR>—2 Hair twisted into a single unornamented braid and allowed to fall on<BR> the back (said to be worn by women whose husbands are absent from them);<BR> वनान्निवृत्तेन रघूत्तमेन मुक्ता स्वयं वेणिरिवावभासे R. 14. 12;<BR> अबलावेणिमोक्षोत्सुकानि Me. 101; Ku. 2. 61.<BR>—3 Continuous flow, current, stream; जलवेणिरम्यां रेवां यदि प्रेक्षितुमस्ति<BR> कामः R. 6. 43; Me. 20; प्रवृत्तबाष्पवेणिकं चक्षुः प्रमृज्य K.;<BR> cf. the word त्रिवेणि also.<BR>—4 The confluence of two or more rivers.<BR>—5 The confluence of the Ganges, Yamunā and Sarasvatī.<BR>—6 N. of a river.<BR>—7 The property re-united after it has been before divided.<BR>—8 A cascade.<BR>—9 A dam, bridge.<BR>—10 A ewe.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेणिबन्धः, वेणिवेधनी, वेणिवेधिनी, वेणिसंहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिबन्धः|वेणिबन्ध
वेणिः + -बन्धः hair twisted into a braid; मोक्ष्यध्वे स्वर्गबन्दीनां<BR> वेणीबन्धानदूषितान् R. 10. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिवेधनी
वेणिः + -वेधनी a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिवेधिनी
वेणिः + -वेधिनी a comb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिसंहारः
वेणिः + -संहारः<BR>—1 tying the hair into a braid; Ve. 6.<BR>—2 N. of a drama by Bhaṭṭa Nārāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणिका
वेणिका<BR>—1 Braided hair.<BR>—2 A continuous line, uninterrupted stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेणुः|वेणु
वेणुः [वेण्-उण् Uṇ. 3. 38]<BR>—1 A bamboo; मलयेऽपि स्थितो वेणुर्वेणुरेव न चन्दनम् Subhāṣ.; R. 12. 41.<BR>—2 A reed, cane; प्राप्तापराधास्ताडपाः स्यू रज्ज्वा वेणुदलेन वा Ms. 8. 299.<BR>—3 A flute, pipe; वेणुं क्वणन्तीं क्रीडन्तीम् Bhāg. 10. 30. 18; नामसमेतं<BR> कृतसंकेतं वादयते मृदु वेणुम् Gīt. 5.<BR>—4 A banner; त्रिवेणुं पञ्चबन्धुरम् (रथम्) Bhāg. 4. 26. 1; cf. त्रिवेणु.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेणुकर्करः, वेणुजः, वेणुदलम्, वेणुध्मः, वेणुनिस्रुतिः, वेणुबीजम्, वेणुयवः, वेणुयष्टिः, वेणुवादः, वेणुवादकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1495-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

