वेथ् €1 Ā. (वेथते) To beg, solicit, ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदः|वेद
वेदः [विद्-अच् घञ् वा]<BR>—1 Knowledge.<BR>—2 Sacred knowledge, holy learning, the scriptures of the Hindus. (Originally<BR> there were only three <i>Vedas</i>:− ऋग्वेद, यजुर्वेद and सामवेद,<BR> which are collectively called त्रयी ‘the sacred triad’; but a fourth,<BR> the अथर्ववेद, was subsequently added to them, Each of the <i>Vedas</i><BR> has two distinct parts, the <i>Mantra</i> or <i>Samhitā</i> and <i>Brāhmaṇa</i>.<BR> According to the strict orthodox faith of the Hindus the Vedas are <i>a-pauruṣeya</i>,<BR> ‘not human compositions’, being supposed to have been directly revealed<BR> by the Supreme Being, Brahman, and are called ‘Śruti’ <i>i. e.</i> ‘what is heard or revealed’<BR>, as distinguished from ‘Smṛti’, <i>i. e.</i> ‘what is remembered or is the work of human origin’<BR>; see श्रुति, स्मृति also;<BR> and the several sages, to whom the hymns of the Vedas are ascribed, are,<BR> therefore, called द्रष्टारः ‘seers’, and not कर्तारः or स्रष्टारः ‘composers’.)<BR>—3 A bundle of Kuśa grass; पद्माक्षमालामुत जन्तुमार्जनं वेदं च<BR> साक्षात्तप एव रूपिणौ Bhāg. 12. 8. 34; Ms. 4. 36.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—5 A part of a sacrifice (यज्ञाङ्ग).<BR>—6 Exposition, comment, gloss.<BR>—7 A metre.<BR>—8 Acquisition, gain, wealth (Ved.).<BR>—9 N. of the number ‘four’.<BR>—10 The ritual (वेदयतीति वेदो विधिः); Karma-kāṇda; वेदवादस्य<BR> विज्ञानं सत्याभासमिवानृतम् Mb. 12. 10. 20 (see Nīlakaṇthaʼs commentary).<BR>—11 Smṛti literature; आम्नायेभ्यः पुनर्वेदाः प्रसृताः सर्वतोमुखाः<BR> Mb. 12. 260. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेदाग्रणीः, वेदाङ्गम्, वेदाधिगमः, वेदाध्ययनम्, वेदाधिपः, वेदाध्यापकः, वेदानध्ययनम्, वेदान्तः, वेदान्तिन्, वेदाभ्यासः, वेदार्थः, वेदावतारः, वेदाश्र, वेदादि, वेदोक्त, वेदोदयः, वेदोदित, वेदकार, वेदकौलेयकः, वेदगर्भः, वेदज्ञः, वेदत्रयम्, वेदत्रयी, वेददर्शिन्, वेददृष्ट, वेदनिन्दकः, वेदनिन्दा, वेदपारगः, वेदपुण्यम्, वेदबाह्य, वेदमातृ, वेदमूर्तिः, वेदवचनम्, वेदवाक्यम्, वेदवदनम्, वेदवादः, वेदवासः, वेदवाह्य, वेदविद्, वेदविद्वस्, वेदविहित, वेदव्यासः, वेदशास्त्रम्, वेदश्रुतिः, वेदसंन्यासः, वेदसंमत, वेदसंमित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाग्रणीः
वेदः + -अग्रणीः N. of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाङ्गम्
वेदः + -अङ्गम् ‘a member of the Veda’, N. of certain classes of works<BR> regarded as auxiliary to the Vedas and designed to aid in the correct pronunciation<BR> and interpretation of the text and the right employment of the <i>Mantras</i><BR> in ceremonials; (the <i>Vedāṅgas</i> are six in number:− शिक्षा कल्पो<BR> व्याकरणं निरुक्तं छन्दसां चयः । ज्योतिषामयनं चैव वेदाङ्गानि षडेव<BR> तु ॥; <i>i. e.</i> 1 शिक्षा ‘the science of proper articulation and pronunciation’<BR>; 2 छन्दस् ‘the science of prosody’; 3 व्याकरण<BR> ‘grammar’; 4 निरुक्त ‘etymological explanation of difficult Vedic words’<BR>; 5 ज्योतिष ‘astronomy’; and 6 कल्प ‘ritual or ceremonial’).<BR> A peculiar use of the word ‘वेदाङ्ग’ in masculine gender may here<BR> be noted; वेदांश्चैव तु वेदाङ्गान् वेदान्तानि तथा स्मृतीः । अधीत्य ब्राह्मणः<BR> पूर्वं शक्तितोऽन्यांश्च संपठेत् ॥ Bṛhadyogiyājñavalkya Smṛti 12. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाधिगमः|वेदाधिगम
वेदः + -आधिगमः, -अध्ययनम् holy study, study of the Vedas; काम्यो हि<BR> वेदाधिगमः कर्मयोगश्च वैदिकः Ms. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्ययनम्
वेदः + -आधिगमः, -अध्ययनम् holy study, study of the Vedas; काम्यो हि<BR> वेदाधिगमः कर्मयोगश्च वैदिकः Ms. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाधिपः|वेदाधिप
वेदः + -अधिपः<BR>—1 one who presides over the Veda;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">Page1496-2</a>]<BR> ऋग्वेदाधिपतिर्जीवो यजुर्वेदाधिपो भृगुः । सामवेदाधिपो भौमः शशिजोऽथर्ववेदपः ॥<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाध्यापकः|वेदाध्यापक
वेदः + -अध्यापकः a teacher of the Vedas, a holy preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदानध्ययनम्
वेदः + -अनध्ययनम् Remissness in the Vedic study; Ms. 3. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तः|वेदान्त|वेदांत
वेदः + -अन्तः<BR>—1 ‘the end of the Veda’, an <i>Upaniṣad</i> (which comes at the end<BR> of the Veda). Also -अन्तम् (See quotation from बृहद्योगियाज्ञवल्क्यस्मृति under -अङ्ग above).<BR>—2 the last of the six principal <i>Darśanas</i> or systems of Hindu philosophy;<BR> (so called because it teaches the ultimate aim and scope of the Veda,<BR> or because it is based on the <i>Upaniṣads</i> which come at the end of the<BR> Veda); (this system of philosophy is sometimes called उत्तरमीमांसा<BR> being regarded as a sequel to Jaiminiʼs पूर्वमीमांसा, but it is practically<BR> quite a distinct system; see मीमांसा. It represents the popular pantheistic<BR> creed of the Hindus, regarding, as it does, the whole world as synthetically<BR> derived from one eternal principle, the Brahman or Supreme Spirit; see<BR> ब्रह्मन् also). ˚गः, ˚ज्ञः a follower of the Vedanta philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदान्तिन्|वेदांतिन्
वेदः + -अन्तिन् <i>m.</i> a follower of the Vedanta philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाभ्यासः|वेदाभ्यास
वेदः + -अभ्यासः<BR>—1 the study of the Vedas; वेदाभ्यासो हि विप्रस्य तपः परमिहोच्यते Ms. 2. 166.<BR>—2 the repetition of the sacred syllable <i>Om</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदार्थः|वेदार्थ
वेदः + -अर्थः the meaning of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदावतारः|वेदावतार
वेदः + -अवतारः revelation of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदाश्र
वेदः + -अश्र <i>a.</i> quadrangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदादि
वेदः + -आदि <i>n.</i>, {@-आदिवर्णः, -आदिबीजम्@}<BR> the sacred syllable <i>Om</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोक्त|वेदोक्तः
वेदः + -उक्त <i>a.</i> scriptural, taught in the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोदयः|वेदोदय
वेदः + -उदयः N. of the sun (the Sāma Veda being said to have proceeded from him).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदोदित|वेदोदितः
वेदः + -उदित <i>a.</i> scriptural, ordained by the Vedas; वेदोदितं स्वकं<BR> कर्म नित्यं कुर्यादतन्द्रितः Ms. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदकार
वेदः + -कार the composer of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदकौलेयकः|वेदकौलेयक
वेदः + -कौलेयकः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदगर्भः|वेदगर्भ
वेदः + -गर्भः<BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman; कमण्डलुं वेदगर्भः कुशान् सप्तर्षयो ददुः<BR> Bhāg. 8. 18. 16.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa versed in the Vedas.<BR>—3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदज्ञः|वेदज्ञ
वेदः + -ज्ञः a Brāhmaṇa versed in the Vedas; तथा दहति वेदज्ञः<BR> कर्मजं दोषमात्मनः Ms. 12. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदत्रयम्
वेदः + -त्रयम्, -त्रयी the three Vedas collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदत्रयी
वेदः + -त्रयम्, -त्रयी the three Vedas collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेददर्शिन्
वेदः + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> one who discerns the sense of the Veda; तपोमध्यं<BR> बुधैः प्रोक्तं तपोऽन्तं वेददर्शिभिः Ms. 11. 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेददृष्ट
वेदः + -दृष्ट <i>a.</i> sanctioned by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनिन्दकः|वेदनिन्दक|वेदनिंदक
वेदः + -निन्दकः<BR>—1 an atheist, a heretic, an unbeliever (one who rejects the divine origin<BR> and character of the Vedas).<BR>—2 a Jaina or Buddhist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनिन्दा|वेदनिंदा
वेदः + -निन्दा unbelief, heresy; Ms. 11. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपारगः|वेदपारग
वेदः + -पारगः a Brāhmaṇa skilled in the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदपुण्यम्
वेदः + -पुण्यम् merit acquired by the study of the Veda; वेदपुण्येन<BR> युज्यते Ms. 2. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदबाह्य|वेदबाह्यः
वेदः + -बाह्य <i>a.</i> contrary to the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदबाह्यः|वेदबाह्य
वेदः + -बाह्य + .({@-ह्यः@}) a sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमातृ
वेदः + -मातृ <i>f.</i><BR>—1 N. of a very sacred Vedic verse called <i>Gāyatree</i> q. v.<BR>—2 N. of सरस्वती, सावित्री and गायत्री; सूतश्च मातरिश्वा वै कवचं<BR> वेदमातरः Mb. 5. 179. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदमूर्तिः|वेदमूर्ति
वेदः + -मूर्तिः (embodiment of the Veda) an honourable title before the<BR> names of learned Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवचनम्
वेदः + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम् a Vedic text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवाक्यम्
वेदः + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम् a Vedic text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवदनम्
वेदः + -वदनम् grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवादः|वेदवाद
वेदः + -वादः see वेदः (10); तदुक्तं वेदवादेषु गहनं वेददर्शिभिः<BR> Mb. 12. 238. 11 (com.); Vedic discussion; यामिमां पुष्पितां वाचं प्रवदन्त्यविपश्चितः ।<BR> वेदवादरताः Bg. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवासः|वेदवास
वेदः + -वासः a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवाह्य
वेदः + -वाह्य <i>a.</i> contrary to, or not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">Page1497-1</a>]<BR> founded on, the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1496-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्
वेदः + -विद् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a Brāhmaṇa versed in the Vedas.<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविद्वस्
वेदः + -विद्वस् <i>a.</i> conversant with the Vedas; ब्राह्मणान् वेदविदुषो<BR> यज्ञार्थ चैव दक्षिणाम् Ms. 11. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदविहित
वेदः + -विहित <i>a.</i> enjoined by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदव्यासः|वेदव्यास
वेदः + -व्यासः an epithet of Vyāsa who is regarded as the ‘arranger’<BR> of the Vedas in their present form; see व्यास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदशास्त्रम्
वेदः + -शास्त्रम् the doctrine of the Vedas; Ms. 4. 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदश्रुतिः|वेदश्रुति
वेदः + -श्रुतिः Vedic revelation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसंन्यासः|वेदसन्न्यास|वेदसंन्यास
वेदः + -संन्यासः giving up the ritual of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसंमत|वेदसम्मत
वेदः + -संमत, -संमित <i>a.</i> sanctioned by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदसंमित|वेदसम्मित
वेदः + -संमत, -संमित <i>a.</i> sanctioned by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदकम्
वेदकम्<BR>—1 Announcing, proclaiming.<BR>—2 Restoring to consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनम्
वेदनम्, वेदना [विद्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Knowledge, perception.<BR>—2 Feeling, sensation; सत्त्वं रजस्तमश्चैव प्राणिनां संश्रिताः सदा ।<BR> त्रिविधा वेदना चैव सर्वसत्त्वेषु दृश्यते ॥ Mb. 12. 194. 29. [also<BR> ‘sensitivity (to the driverʼs stimuli) of an elephant’. It is of 7 kinds:<BR> -अत्यर्थ, उत्तान, गम्भीर, अन्वर्थ, प्रत्यर्थ, कर्कश and सिद्ध].<BR>—3 Pain, torment, agony, anguish; अवेदनाज्ञं कुलिशक्षतानाम् Ku. 1. 20; R. 8. 50.<BR>—4 A cquisition, wealth, property.<BR>—5 Marriage; वसनस्य दशा ग्राह्या शूद्रयोत्कृष्टवेदने Ms. 3. 44, 9. 65;<BR> Y. 1. 62.<BR>—6 Presenting, giving.<BR>—7 The marriage of a Śūdra woman with a man of a higher caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदना
वेदनम्, वेदना [विद्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Knowledge, perception.<BR>—2 Feeling, sensation; सत्त्वं रजस्तमश्चैव प्राणिनां संश्रिताः सदा ।<BR> त्रिविधा वेदना चैव सर्वसत्त्वेषु दृश्यते ॥ Mb. 12. 194. 29. [also<BR> ‘sensitivity (to the driverʼs stimuli) of an elephant’. It is of 7 kinds:<BR> -अत्यर्थ, उत्तान, गम्भीर, अन्वर्थ, प्रत्यर्थ, कर्कश and सिद्ध].<BR>—3 Pain, torment, agony, anguish; अवेदनाज्ञं कुलिशक्षतानाम् Ku. 1. 20; R. 8. 50.<BR>—4 A cquisition, wealth, property.<BR>—5 Marriage; वसनस्य दशा ग्राह्या शूद्रयोत्कृष्टवेदने Ms. 3. 44, 9. 65;<BR> Y. 1. 62.<BR>—6 Presenting, giving.<BR>—7 The marriage of a Śūdra woman with a man of a higher caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदनी
वेदनी The true skin or cutis (that apprehends touch).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदस्
वेदस् <i>n.</i> Ved. Acquisition, gain, wealth; उशन् ह वै वाजश्रवसः<BR> सर्ववेदसं ददौ Kaṭh. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदापयति
वेदापयति Den. P. To impart knowledge, teach; cf. P. III. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदित|वेदितः
वेदित <i>p. p.</i> Made known, informed, communicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदितृ
वेदितृ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Knowing.<BR>—2 Wise, learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिन्
वेदिन् <i>a.</i> [विद्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Knowing; as in कृतवेदिन्.<BR>—2 Marrying. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A knower.<BR>—2 A teacher.<BR>—3 A learned Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—4 An epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेद्य|वेद्यं
वेद्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be known.<BR>—2 To be taught or explained.<BR>—3 To be married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदवती
वेदवती <i>f.</i> N. of the daughter of King Kuśadhvaja; कृते युगे<BR> वेदवती कुशध्वजसुता शुभा । त्रेतायां रामपत्नी सा सीतेति जनकात्मजा ॥ Brav. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदारः|वेदार
वेदारः A chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिः|वेदि
वेदिः [विद्-इन्] A learned man, sage; Paṇḍita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिः|वेदि
वेदिः + .{@-दिः, -दी@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An altar, especially one prepared for a sacrifice; उर एव वेदिः<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 18. 2; अमी वेदि परितः कॢप्तधिष्ण्याः (वह्नयः) Ś. 4. 8.<BR>—2 An altar of a particular shape, the middle points of which come very<BR> close to each other; मध्येन सा वेदिविलग्नमध्या Ku. 1. 39; (some<BR> propose to take वेदि in this passage as meaning ‘a seal-ring’).<BR>—3 A quadrangular spot in the court-yard of a temple or palace; विमानं<BR> नवमुद्वेदि चतुःस्तम्भप्रतिष्ठितम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">Page1497-2</a>]<BR> (कल्पयामासुः) R. 17. 9.<BR>—4 A seal-ring.<BR>—5 N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>—6 A tract or region.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेदीशः, वेदिजा, वेदिमेखला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदी
वेदिः + .{@-दिः, -दी@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 An altar, especially one prepared for a sacrifice; उर एव वेदिः<BR> Ch. Up. 5. 18. 2; अमी वेदि परितः कॢप्तधिष्ण्याः (वह्नयः) Ś. 4. 8.<BR>—2 An altar of a particular shape, the middle points of which come very<BR> close to each other; मध्येन सा वेदिविलग्नमध्या Ku. 1. 39; (some<BR> propose to take वेदि in this passage as meaning ‘a seal-ring’).<BR>—3 A quadrangular spot in the court-yard of a temple or palace; विमानं<BR> नवमुद्वेदि चतुःस्तम्भप्रतिष्ठितम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">Page1497-2</a>]<BR> (कल्पयामासुः) R. 17. 9.<BR>—4 A seal-ring.<BR>—5 N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>—6 A tract or region.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेदीशः, वेदिजा, वेदिमेखला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदीशः|वेदीश
वेदिः + -ईशः<BR>—1 N. of Agni.<BR>—2 of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिजा
वेदिः + -जा an epithet of Draupadī who was born from the midst of the<BR> sacrificial altar of king Drupada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिमेखला
वेदिः + -मेखला the cord which forms the boundary of the उत्तरवेदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेदिका
वेदिका<BR>—1 A sacrificial altar or ground; इति प्रिये वादिनि वेदिकोदरी Rām. Ch. 2. 57.<BR>—2 A raised seat; an elevated spot of ground (usually for sacred purposes);<BR> सप्तपर्णवेदिका Ś. 1; सदेवदारुद्रुमवेदिकायाम् Ku. 3. 44.<BR>—3 A seat in general.<BR>—4 An altar, a heap, mound; मन्दाकिनीसैकतवेदिकाभिः Ku. 1. 29 ‘by making altars or heaps of sand &c.’<BR>.<BR>—5 A quadrangular open shed in the middle of a court-yard; a pavilion,<BR> balcony; तप्तकाञ्चनवेदिकम् (जग्राह); Rām. 7. 15. 37; सुरवेश्मवेदिका Ki. 7. 12.<BR>—6 An arbour, a bower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधः|वेध
वेधः<BR>—1 Penetrating, piercing, perforation.<BR>—2 Wounding, a wound.<BR>—3 A hole, an excavation.<BR>—4 The depth (of an excavation).<BR>—5 A particular measure of time.<BR>—6 The ninth part of a <i>Paridhi</i>; परिधिनवमभागः शूकधान्येषु वेधः Līlā.<BR>—7 Fixing the position of the sun, planets or the stars.<BR>—8 Disturbance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेधमुख्यः, वेधमुख्यकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधमुख्यः|वेधमुख्य
वेधः + -मुख्यः, -मुख्यकः Curcuma Zerumbet (Mar. कचोरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधमुख्यकः|वेधमुख्यक
वेधः + -मुख्यः, -मुख्यकः Curcuma Zerumbet (Mar. कचोरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधकः|वेधक|वेधकं
वेधकः<BR>—1 N. of one of the divisions of hell.<BR>—2 Camphor.<BR>—3 A perforator (of gems etc.); Rām. 2. 83. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधकम्
वेधकः + .{@-कम्@} Rice in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनम्
वेधनम्<BR>—1 The act of piercing, perforating.<BR>—2 Penetration.<BR>—3 Excavation.<BR>—4 Pricking, wounding.<BR>—5 Depth (of an excavation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनिका
वेधनिका A sharp-pointed instrument for perforating shells and jewels, a gimblet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधनी
वेधनी<BR>—1 An instrument for piercing an elephantʼs ear.<BR>—2 A sharp-pointed instrument for perforating shells and jewels, a gimblet.<BR>—3 Depth (in measurement).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधित|वेधितः
वेधित <i>p. p.</i> Pierced, bored, perforated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधिन्
वेधिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Piercing, boring.<BR>—2 Hitting (a mark).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधिनी
वेधिन् + .{@-नी@} A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेध्यम्
वेध्यम् A butt, target.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधस्
वेधस् <i>m.</i> [विधा असुन् गुणः]<BR>—1 A creator; मदनश्च वेधाः Māl. 1. 21.<BR>—2 N. of Brahman, the creator; तं वेधा विदधे नूनं महाभूतसमाधिना<BR> R. 1. 29; Ku. 2. 16, 5. 41.<BR>—3 A secondary creator (such as Dakṣa, sprung from Brahman); विधाता<BR> वेधसामपि Ku. 2. 14.<BR>—4 N. of Śiva.<BR>—5 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 The sun.<BR>—7 The <i>Arka</i> plant.<BR>—8 A learned man.<BR>—9 A priest.<BR>—10 N. of Soma.<BR>—11 A poet. ━<i>a.</i> Performing, accomplishing; गम्भीरवेधा उपगुप्तवित्तः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 16. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1497-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेधसम्
वेधसम् The part of the hand under the root of the thumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्
वेन् €1 U. (वेनति-ते) See वेण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन|वेनः
वेन See वेण (2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेन्ना
वेन्ना See वेणा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेप्
वेप् €1 Ā. (वेपते, वेपित) To tremble, shake, quiver, quake;<BR> कृताञ्जलिर्वेपमानः किरीटी Bg. 11. 35; R. 11. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपः|वेप
वेपः Quivering, trembling; tremor; यस्मा अदादुदधिरूढभयाङ्गवेपः<BR> Bhāg. 2. 7. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपथुः|वेपथु
वेपथुः [वेप्-अथुच्] Tremor, trembling, heaving (of breasts &c.);<BR> अद्यापि स्तनवेपथुं जनयति श्वासः प्रमाणाधिकः Ś. 1. 29, 23; Śi. 9. 22, 73;<BR> R. 19. 23; Ku. 4. 17, 5. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेपनम्
वेपनम् [वेप्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Tremor, trembling.<BR>—2 Shaking, brandishing (the cord of a bow); Rām. 1. 67. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेमः|वेम
वेमः, -वेमन्<BR> [वेञः सर्वत्र इमनिन् Uṇ. 4. 163]. <i>m., n.</i> A loom;<BR> महासिवेम्नः सहकृत्वरी बहुम् N. 1. 12; तुरीवेमादिकम् T. S.;<BR> शुक्लं वयन्तो तरसा सुवेमौ Mb. 1. 3. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेमन्
वेमः, -वेमन्<BR> [वेञः सर्वत्र इमनिन् Uṇ. 4. 163]. <i>m., n.</i> A loom;<BR> महासिवेम्नः सहकृत्वरी बहुम् N. 1. 12; तुरीवेमादिकम् T. S.;<BR> शुक्लं वयन्तो तरसा सुवेमौ Mb. 1. 3. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरः|वेर|वेरं
वेरः, -रम्<BR> [अज्-रन् वीभावः Tv.]<BR>—1 The body.<BR>—2 Saffron.<BR>—3 The egg-plant.<BR>—4 The mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेरम्
