वेवी
वेवी €2 Ā. (वेवीते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To obtain.<BR>—3 To conceive, be pregnant.<BR>—4 To pervade.<BR>—5 To cast, throw.<BR>—6 To eat.<BR>—7 To wish, desire.<BR>—8 To shine; (seldom used in classical literature).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वेशः|वेश
वेशः [विश्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Entrance.<BR>—2 Ingress, access.<BR>—3 A house, dwelling; न वेशमाचक्रमुरस्य नीत्या Bu. C. 1. 3.<BR>—4 A house or residence of prostitutes; तरुणजनसहायश्चिन्त्यतां<BR> वेशवासः Mk. 1. 31.<BR>—5 Dress, apparel (also written वेष in this sense); मृगयावेषधारी;<BR> विनीतवेषेण Ś. 1; कृतवेशे केशवे Gīt. 11.<BR>—6 Disguise.<BR>—7 Hire, wages.<BR>—8 The prostitute-class (वेश्याजन); Mb. 5. 196. 26; Dk. 2. 6.<BR>—9 The wages of prostitutes; वेशेनैव च जीवताम् (न प्रतिगृह्णीयात्) Ms. 4. 84.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वेशदानः, वेशधारिन्, वेशनारी, वेशवधू, वेशवनिता, वेशवासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1498-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

