वैवक्षिक
वैवक्षिक <i>a.</i> Meant, intended to be said.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवधिकः|वैवधिक
वैवधिकः<BR>—1 A pedlar, hawker.<BR>—2 A carrier of loads on a pole.<BR>—3 A messenger doing various jobs; अथ वैवधिकस्तूर्णं विसृष्टः शिवभूभृता<BR> Śiva B. 31. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण
वैवर्ण <i>a.</i> Without any colour (like blue, yellow &c.); रूपं<BR> भवति वैवर्णम् Mb. 14. 21. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्णिक
वैवर्णिक <i>a.</i> Variegated (said especially of a variety of coral); Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण्यम्
वैवर्ण्यम् [विवर्णस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Change of colour or complexion, paleness; इदमाकर्ण्य वैवर्ण्याक्रान्तवक्त्रः Dk. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Difference, diversity.<BR>—3 Deviation from caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्तम्
वैवर्तम् Revolution, change of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वतः|वैवस्वत
वैवस्वतः [विवस्वतोऽपत्यम् अण्]<BR>—1 N. of the seventh Manu who is supposed to preside over the present<BR> age; see under Manu; वैवस्वतो मनुर्नाम माननीयो मनीषिणाम् R. 1. 11; U. 6. 18.<BR>—2 N. of Yama; यानं सस्मार कौबेरं वैवस्वतजिगीषया R. 15. 45.<BR>—3 N. of Agni.<BR>—4 One of the eleven Rudras.<BR>—5 The planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वतम्
वैवस्वतः + .{@-तम्@} The present age or Manvantara, as presided over by Manu Vaivasvata<BR> or the seventh Manu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वैवस्वतमन्वन्तरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वतमन्वन्तरम्
वैवस्वतः + -मन्वन्तरम् N. of the 7th (the present) मन्वन्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वती
वैवस्वती<BR>—1 The southern quarter.<BR>—2 N. of Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिक|वैवाहिकः
वैवाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [वीवाहाय हितं साधु वा ठक्] Relating to marriage,<BR> matrimonial, nuptial; वैवाहिको विधिः स्त्रीणां संस्कारो वैदिकः स्मृतः<BR> Ms. 2. 67; वैवाहिकैः कौतुकसंविधानैर्गृहे गृहे व्यग्रपुरंध्रिवर्गम् Ku. 7. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिकः|वैवाहिक
वैवाहिक + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A marriage, wedding.<BR>—2 Preparations for a wedding; nuptial festivities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिकम्
वैवाहिक + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A marriage, wedding.<BR>—2 Preparations for a wedding; nuptial festivities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिकः|वैवाहिक
वैवाहिक + .{@-कः@} The father of a sonʼs wife or daughterʼs husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाह्य
वैवाह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Nuptial.<BR>—2 Fit for marriage; अस्मद्वैवाह्यकुलजः कोऽपि विप्रदारकः Dk. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाह्यम्
वैवाह्य + .{@-ह्यम्@} Nuptial solemnity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैविक्त्यम्
वैविक्त्यम् Deliverance from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशद्यम्
वैशद्यम्<BR>—1 Clearness, purity (fig. also).<BR>—2 Perspicuity as in शिष्यबुद्धिवैशद्यार्थम्.<BR>—3 Whiteness.<BR>—4 Calmness, composure (of mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1504-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशम्पायनः|वैशम्पायन|वैशंपायन|वैशंपायनः
वैशम्पायनः N. of a celebrated pupil of Vyāsa; जनमेजयेन<BR> पृष्टः सन् ब्राह्मणैश्च सहस्रशः । शशास शिष्यमासीनं वैशम्पायनमन्तिके ॥<BR> Mb. [It was he who made Yājñavalkya disgorge the whole of the Yajurveda<BR> he had learnt from him which was picked up by his other pupils in the<BR> form of <i>Tittiris</i> or partridges; and hence the Veda was called ‘Taittirīya’.<BR> Vaīśampāyana was celebrated for his great skill in narrating Purāṇas,<BR> and is said to have recounted the whole of the Mahābhārata to king Janamejaya].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशल्यम्
वैशल्यम् Deliverence from a painful incumbrance (as that of the fetus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस|वैशसं
वैशस <i>a.</i> Causing death or destruction; द्रष्टाऽसि युधि सम्बाधे<BR> प्रवृत्ते वैशसेऽहनि Mb. 5. 76. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशसम्
वैशस + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 Destruction, slaughter, butchery; ददर्श यदुवीराणामापाने वैशसं<BR> महत् Mb. 1. 2. 58; विधिना कृतमर्धवैशसम् Ku. 4. 31; U. 4. 24, 6. 40.<BR>—2 Distress, torment, pain, suffering, hardship; सर्पवृश्चिकदंशाद्यैर्दशद्भिश्चात्मैवशसम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 30. 26, 8. 7. 37; उपरोधवैशसम् Mu. 2; धिगुच्छ्वसितवैशसम् Māl. 9. 35.<BR>—3 Violence (हिंसा); Bhāg. 5. 9. 15.<BR>—4 N. of a hell; Bhāg. 4. 25. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशसनम्
वैशसनम् = वैशसम्; see above; असुराणां प्लवङ्गानामत्र वैशसनं<BR> महत् A. Rām. 6. 14. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्रम्
वैशस्त्रम्<BR>—1 Defencelessness.<BR>—2 Government, rule.<BR>—3 The state of being unarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाखः|वैशाख|वैशाखं
वैशाखः<BR>—1 N. of the second lunar month (corresponding to April-May).<BR>—2 A churning-stick; द्रुततरकरदक्षाः क्षिप्तवैशाखशैले … कलशिमुदधिगुर्वी<BR> वल्लवा लोडयन्ति Śi. 11. 8; कालेन वैशाखधरं विधाय प्रभाकरं<BR> बिम्बममन्थि सिन्धुः Rām. Ch. 6. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाखम्
वैशाखः + .{@-खम्@} A kind of attitude in shooting; see विशाख.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाखी
वैशाखः + .{@-खी@} The full-moon day in the month of Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशारद
वैशारद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Experienced, skilled; वैशारदी धीः Bhāg. 7. 7. 17.<BR>—2 Learned; all-knowing; यद्येषोपरता देवी मायावैशारदी मतिः Bhāg. 1. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशारदम्
वैशारद + .{@-दम्@} Profound learning; नह्यस्य कश्चित् सदृशोऽस्ति शास्त्रे वैशारदे<BR> छन्दगतौ तथैव Rām. 7. 36. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशारद्यम्
वैशारद्यम् Skill, cleverness, proficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिक|वैशिकः
वैशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Practised by harlots; वैशिकीं कलाम् Mk. 1. 4<BR> ‘arts practised by harlots’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिकः|वैशिक
वैशिक + .{@-कः@} A person who associates with harlots; a kind of hero in erotic works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिकम्
वैशिक + .{@-कम्@} Harlotry, arts of harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्टम्
वैशिष्टम् = वैशिष्टप below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्ट्यम्
वैशिष्ट्यम्<BR>—1 Distinction, difference.<BR>—2 Peculiarity, speciality, particularity; वैशिष्टयादन्यमर्थं या बोधयेत्<BR> सार्थसंभवा S. D. 27<BR>—3 Excellence; S. D. 78.<BR>—4 Possession or endowment with some characteristic attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिक|वैशेषिकः
वैशेषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Characteristic, special; विषये वर्तमानानां यं तं वैशेषिकैर्गुणैः<BR> (प्राहुर्विषयगोप्तारम्) Mb. 12. 47. 70, 7. 5. 15.<BR>—2 Belonging to the Vaiśeṣika doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिकः|वैशेषिक
वैशेषिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">Page1505-2</a>]<BR> A follower of the Vaiśeṣika doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिकम्
वैशेषिक + .{@-कम्@} [विशेषं पदार्थभेदमधिकृत्य कृतो ग्रन्थः ठञ्] One<BR> of the six principal Darśanas or systems of Hindu philosophy founded by<BR> Kaṇāda; it differs from the Nyāya philosophy of Gautama in that it<BR> recognizes only seven instead of sixteen categories or heads of predicables<BR> (the earlier writers <i>e. g.</i> Kaṇāda recognizing only six), and lays<BR> particular stress upon Viśeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिन्
वैशेषिन् <i>a.</i> Specific, individual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेष्यम्
वैशेष्यम्<BR>—1 Excellence, pre-eminence, superiority; अन्योन्यगुणवैशेष्यान्न किंचिदतिरिच्यते Ms. 9. 296.<BR>—2 Specific or generic distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यः|वैश्य
वैश्यः A man of the third tribe, his business being trade and agriculture;<BR> a peasant; विशत्याशु पशुभ्यश्च कृष्यादावरुचिः शुचिः । वेदाध्ययनसंपन्नः<BR> स वैश्य इति संज्ञितः ॥ Padma P. (He is supposed to have sprung<BR> from the thighs of <i>Puruṣa</i>; cf. ऊरू तदस्य यद्वैश्यः Rv. 10. 90.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वैश्यकर्मन्, वैश्यभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यकर्मन्
वैश्यः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@वृत्तिः@} <i>f.</i> the business or occupation<BR> of a Vaīśya; trade, agriculture &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यभावः|वैश्यभाव
वैश्यः + -भावः the state or condition of a वैश्य; ब्राह्मणः सप्तरात्रेण<BR> वैश्यभावं नियच्छति Ms. 10. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रम्भक
वैश्रम्भक <i>a.</i> Inspiring confidence; वैश्रम्भकैरुपसृतानुपविश्रम्भय्य<BR> Bhāg. 5. 26. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणः|वैश्रवण
वैश्रवणः<BR>—1 N. of Kubera, the god of wealth; विभाति यस्यां ललितालकायां मनोहरा<BR> वैश्रवणस्य लक्ष्मीः Bv. 2. 10; यदाश्रोषं वैश्रवणेन सार्घम् Mb. 1. 1. 166.<BR>—2 N. of Rāvaṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: वैश्रवणालयः, वैश्रवणावासः, वैश्रवणोदयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणालयः|वैश्रवणालय
वैश्रवणः + -आलयः, -आवासः<BR>—1 the abode of Kubera.<BR>—2 the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणावासः|वैश्रवणावास
वैश्रवणः + -आलयः, -आवासः<BR>—1 the abode of Kubera.<BR>—2 the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणोदयः|वैश्रवणोदय
वैश्रवणः + -उदयः the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेव|वैश्वदेवः
वैश्वदेव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to the Viśvedevas, q. v.; Mb. 12. 301. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेवम्
वैश्वदेव + .{@-वम्@} [विश्वेभ्यो देवेभ्यो देयो बलिः अण्]<BR>—1 An offering made to the Viśvedevas.<BR>—2 An offering to all deities (made by presenting oblations to fire before meals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेवी
वैश्वदेव + .{@-वी@} The eighth day of the second half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वरूप
वैश्वरूप <i>a.</i> Multiform, manifold, diverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वरूपम्
वैश्वरूप + .{@-पम्@} The universe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1505-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वरूप्यम्
