व्रजनाथः|व्रजनाथ
व्रजः + -किशोरः, -नाथः, -मोहनः, -वरः, -वल्लभः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजमोहनः|व्रजमोहन
व्रजः + -किशोरः, -नाथः, -मोहनः, -वरः, -वल्लभः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजवरः|व्रजवर
व्रजः + -किशोरः, -नाथः, -मोहनः, -वरः, -वल्लभः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजवल्लभः|व्रजवल्लभ
व्रजः + -किशोरः, -नाथः, -मोहनः, -वरः, -वल्लभः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजभाषा
व्रजः + -भाषा the language current around Agra and Mathurā; old Hindi language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजसानः
व्रजः + -सानः a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजकः|व्रजक
व्रजकः A religious mendicant wandering about for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजनम्
व्रजनम् [वृजेः क्युः Uṇ. 2. 77]<BR>—1 Roaming, wandering, travelling.<BR>—2 Exile.<BR>—3 Ved. A way, road.<BR>—4 Sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजितम्
व्रजितम् Going, roaming; दुरासिताद् दुर्व्रजितात् Mb. 3. 233. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्या
व्रज्या<BR>—1 Wandering about as a religious mendicant.<BR>—2 An attack, invasion, a march.<BR>—3 A flock, multitude, tribe, class.<BR>—4 A theatre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण्
व्रण् I. €1 P. (व्रणति) To sound. ━II. €10 U. (व्रणयति-ते)<BR> To hurt; wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणः|व्रण|व्रणं
व्रणः, -णम्<BR> [व्रण्-अच्]<BR>—1 A wound, sore, bruise, hurt; आत्मनः सुमहत् कर्म व्रणैरावेद्य संस्थितः R. 12. 55.<BR>—2 A boil, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">Page1523-1</a>]<BR> ulcer; व्रणो रूढग्रन्थिः स्फुटित इव हृन्मर्मणि पुनः U. 2. 26.<BR>—3 A fracture, scar.<BR>—4 A flaw, blemish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रणारिः, व्रणकृत्, व्रणचिन्तकः, व्रणविरोपण, व्रणसंरोहण, व्रणशोधनम्, व्रणहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणम्
व्रणः, -णम्<BR> [व्रण्-अच्]<BR>—1 A wound, sore, bruise, hurt; आत्मनः सुमहत् कर्म व्रणैरावेद्य संस्थितः R. 12. 55.<BR>—2 A boil, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">Page1523-1</a>]<BR> ulcer; व्रणो रूढग्रन्थिः स्फुटित इव हृन्मर्मणि पुनः U. 2. 26.<BR>—3 A fracture, scar.<BR>—4 A flaw, blemish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रणारिः, व्रणकृत्, व्रणचिन्तकः, व्रणविरोपण, व्रणसंरोहण, व्रणशोधनम्, व्रणहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1522-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणारिः|व्रणारि
व्रणः + -अरिः gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणकृत्
व्रणः + -कृत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 wounding.<BR>—2 corroding. ━(<i>m.</i>) the marking-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणचिन्तकः|व्रणचिन्तक
व्रणः + -चिन्तकः a surgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणविरोपण
व्रणः + -विरोपण, -संरोहण <i>a.</i> sore-healing; यस्य त्वया व्रणविरोपणमिङ्गुदीनां<BR> तैलं न्यषिच्यत Ś. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणसंरोहण
व्रणः + -विरोपण, -संरोहण <i>a.</i> sore-healing; यस्य त्वया व्रणविरोपणमिङ्गुदीनां<BR> तैलं न्यषिच्यत Ś. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणशोधनम्
व्रणः + -शोधनम् the cleansing or dressing of a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणहः|व्रणह
व्रणः + -हः the castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणनम्
व्रणनम् Piercing, perforating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणित
व्रणित <i>a.</i> Wounded, bruised; विषक्तस्तीव्रेण व्रणितहृदयेन<BR> व्यथयता U. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतः|व्रत|व्रतं
व्रतः, -तम्<BR> [व्रज्-घ जस्य तः]<BR>—1 A religious act of devotion or austerity, vowed observance, a vow in<BR> general; अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारम् R. 13. 67, 2. 4, 25; (there are<BR> several <i>vratas</i> enjoined in the different Purāṇas; but their number<BR> cannot be said to be fixed, as new ones, <i>e. g.</i> सत्यनारायणव्रत,<BR> are being added every day).<BR>—2 A vow, promise, resolve; सोऽभूद् भग्नव्रतः शत्रूनुद्धृत्य प्रतिरोपयन्<BR> R. 17. 42; so सत्यव्रत, पुण्यव्रत, दृढव्रत &c.<BR>—3 Object of devotion or faith, devotion; as in पतिव्रता (पतिर्व्रतं<BR> यस्याः सा); यान्ति देवव्रता देवान् पितॄन् यान्ति पितृव्रताः Bg. 9. 25.<BR>—4 A rite, an observance, practice, as in अर्कव्रत q. v.; Śabaraswāmin<BR> defines it as पुरुषाणां क्रियार्थानां शरीरधारणार्थो बलकरणार्थश्चायं<BR> संस्कारो व्रतं नाम ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 8.<BR>—5 Mode of life, course of conduct; अथ तु वेत्सि शुचि व्रतमात्मनः Ś. 5. 27.<BR>—6 An ordinance, a law, rule.<BR>—7 Sacrifice.<BR>—8 An act, deed, work.<BR>—9 A design, plan.<BR>—10 Mental activity; व्रतमिति च मानसं कर्म उच्यते ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 20.<BR>—11 Celibacy; व्रतलोपनम् Ms. 11. 61 (com. ब्रह्मचारिणो भैथुनम्);<BR> Mb. 12. 11. 22 (com. व्रतं ब्रह्मचर्याद्युपेतमध्ययनम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रताचरणम्, व्रतादेशः, व्रतोपवासः, व्रतग्रहणम्, व्रतचर्यः, व्रतचर्या, व्रतधारणम्, व्रतपारणम्, व्रतपारणा, व्रतप्रतिष्ठा, व्रतभङ्गः, व्रतभिक्षा, व्रतरुचि, व्रतलोपनम्, व्रतवैकल्यम्, व्रतसंग्रहः, व्रतसंपादनम्, व्रतस्थ, व्रतस्थः, व्रतस्नात, व्रतस्नातकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतम्
व्रतः, -तम्<BR> [व्रज्-घ जस्य तः]<BR>—1 A religious act of devotion or austerity, vowed observance, a vow in<BR> general; अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारम् R. 13. 67, 2. 4, 25; (there are<BR> several <i>vratas</i> enjoined in the different Purāṇas; but their number<BR> cannot be said to be fixed, as new ones, <i>e. g.</i> सत्यनारायणव्रत,<BR> are being added every day).<BR>—2 A vow, promise, resolve; सोऽभूद् भग्नव्रतः शत्रूनुद्धृत्य प्रतिरोपयन्<BR> R. 17. 42; so सत्यव्रत, पुण्यव्रत, दृढव्रत &c.<BR>—3 Object of devotion or faith, devotion; as in पतिव्रता (पतिर्व्रतं<BR> यस्याः सा); यान्ति देवव्रता देवान् पितॄन् यान्ति पितृव्रताः Bg. 9. 25.<BR>—4 A rite, an observance, practice, as in अर्कव्रत q. v.; Śabaraswāmin<BR> defines it as पुरुषाणां क्रियार्थानां शरीरधारणार्थो बलकरणार्थश्चायं<BR> संस्कारो व्रतं नाम ŚB. on MS. 4. 3. 8.<BR>—5 Mode of life, course of conduct; अथ तु वेत्सि शुचि व्रतमात्मनः Ś. 5. 27.<BR>—6 An ordinance, a law, rule.<BR>—7 Sacrifice.<BR>—8 An act, deed, work.<BR>—9 A design, plan.<BR>—10 Mental activity; व्रतमिति च मानसं कर्म उच्यते ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 20.<BR>—11 Celibacy; व्रतलोपनम् Ms. 11. 61 (com. ब्रह्मचारिणो भैथुनम्);<BR> Mb. 12. 11. 22 (com. व्रतं ब्रह्मचर्याद्युपेतमध्ययनम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रताचरणम्, व्रतादेशः, व्रतोपवासः, व्रतग्रहणम्, व्रतचर्यः, व्रतचर्या, व्रतधारणम्, व्रतपारणम्, व्रतपारणा, व्रतप्रतिष्ठा, व्रतभङ्गः, व्रतभिक्षा, व्रतरुचि, व्रतलोपनम्, व्रतवैकल्यम्, व्रतसंग्रहः, व्रतसंपादनम्, व्रतस्थ, व्रतस्थः, व्रतस्नात, व्रतस्नातकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रताचरणम्
व्रतः + -आचरणम् the observance of a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतादेशः|व्रतादेश
व्रतः + -आदेशः investiture of a youth (of any one of the three classes)<BR> with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतोपवासः|व्रतोपवास
व्रतः + -उपवासः a fast for a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतग्रहणम्
व्रतः + -ग्रहणम् initiation into a vow for a religious performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतचर्यः|व्रतचर्य
व्रतः + -चर्यः a religious student; see ब्रह्मचारिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतचर्या
व्रतः + -चर्या observance or practice of a religious vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतधारणम्
व्रतः + -धारणम् the fulfilling of a religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतपारणम्
व्रतः + -पारणम्, -पारणा conclusion of a vow or fast, eating after a fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतपारणा
व्रतः + -पारणम्, -पारणा conclusion of a vow or fast, eating after a fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतप्रतिष्ठा
व्रतः + -प्रतिष्ठा performance of a religious vow voluntarily undertaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतभङ्गः|व्रतभङ्ग|व्रतभंग
व्रतः + -भङ्गः<BR>—1 breach of a vow.<BR>—2 breach of a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतभिक्षा
व्रतः + -भिक्षा begging alms as part of the ceremony of investiture with<BR> the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतरुचि
व्रतः + -रुचि <i>a.</i> delighting in religious observances, devout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतलोपनम्
व्रतः + -लोपनम् breaking a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतवैकल्यम्
व्रतः + -वैकल्यम् the incompletion of a religious vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतसंग्रहः|व्रतसङ्ग्रह
व्रतः + -संग्रहः initiation into a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतसंपादनम्
व्रतः + -संपादनम् fulfilling a religious vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्थ|व्रतस्थः
व्रतः + -स्थ <i>a.</i> practising any vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्थः|व्रतस्थ
व्रतः + -स्थः a celibate; व्रतस्थमपि दौहित्रं श्राद्धे यत्नेन भोजयेत् Ms. 3. 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्नात
व्रतः + -स्नात <i>a.</i> one who has bathed after completing a religious vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतस्नातकः|व्रतस्नातक
व्रतः + -स्नातकः a Brāhmaṇa who has completed the first stage of his<BR> religious life, <i>i. e.</i> that of a Brahmachārin or religious student;<BR> see स्नातक; Ms. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतयति
व्रतयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To observe a vow.<BR>—2 To fast in consequence of a vow.<BR>—3 To eat together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिक
व्रतिक, -व्रतिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Observing a vow, practising penance, devout, pious;<BR> नायज्वभिर्नाव्रतिकैः Mb. 3. 43. 5; व्रतिनः पापशीलानामसतीनां<BR> कुलस्त्रियः (द्वेध्याः) Pt. 1. 416. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A religious student; भैक्षेण वर्तयोन्नित्यं नैकान्नादी भवेद् व्रती ।<BR> भैक्षेण व्रतिनो वृत्तिरुपवाससमा स्मृता ॥ Ms. 2. 188.<BR>—2 An ascetic, a devotee; किं तावद् व्रतिनामुपोढतपसां विध्नैस्तपो<BR> दूषितम् Ś. 5. 9.<BR>—3 One who institutes a sacrifice; cf. यजमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिन्
व्रतिक, -व्रतिन् <i>a.</i><BR> Observing a vow, practising penance, devout, pious;<BR> नायज्वभिर्नाव्रतिकैः Mb. 3. 43. 5; व्रतिनः पापशीलानामसतीनां<BR> कुलस्त्रियः (द्वेध्याः) Pt. 1. 416. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A religious student; भैक्षेण वर्तयोन्नित्यं नैकान्नादी भवेद् व्रती ।<BR> भैक्षेण व्रतिनो वृत्तिरुपवाससमा स्मृता ॥ Ms. 2. 188.<BR>—2 An ascetic, a devotee; किं तावद् व्रतिनामुपोढतपसां विध्नैस्तपो<BR> दूषितम् Ś. 5. 9.<BR>—3 One who institutes a sacrifice; cf. यजमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रततिः|व्रतति
व्रततिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A creeper; पादाकृष्टव्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33; R. 14. 1.<BR>—2 Expansion, extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतती
व्रततिः, -ती <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A creeper; पादाकृष्टव्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33; R. 14. 1.<BR>—2 Expansion, extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रध्न
व्रध्न See ब्रध्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्च्
व्रश्च् €6 P. (वृश्चति, वृक्ण; <i>caus.</i> व्रश्चयति-ते;<BR> <i>desid.</i> विव्रश्चिषति or विव्रक्षति)<BR>—1 To cut, cut up or asunder, tear, lacerate.<BR>—2 To wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चनः|व्रश्चन|व्रश्चनं
व्रश्चनः<BR>—1 A small saw.<BR>—2 A fine file used by goldsmiths.<BR>—3 The juice trickling from an incision in a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चनम्
व्रश्चनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Cutting, tearing, wounding.<BR>—2 A cut, an incision.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रश्चनप्रभव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चनप्रभव
व्रश्चनः + -प्रभव <i>a.</i> flowing from an incision; लोहितान् वृक्षनिर्यासान्<BR> व्रश्चनप्रभवांस्तथा (विवर्जयेत्) Ms. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजः|व्राज
व्राजः<BR>—1 Going, motion.<BR>—2 A multitude (Ved.).<BR>—3 A domestic cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजिः|व्राजि
व्राजिः <i>f.</i> A gust or gale of wind, stormy wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातः|व्रात
व्रातः A multitude, group, flock, an assemblage; श्वपाकानां व्रातैः<BR> G. L. 29; R. 12. 94; Śi. 4. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातम्
व्रातः + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Bodily or manual labour.<BR>—2 Day-labour.<BR>—3 Casual employment.<BR>—4 The company or attendants at a marriage feast.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रातजीवन, व्रातपतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातजीवन
व्रातः + -जीवन <i>a.</i> see व्रातीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातपतिः|व्रातपति
व्रातः + -पतिः lord of an assemblage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीन|व्रातीनः
व्रातीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living by day-labour, a hired labourer, coolie; व्रातीनव्यालदीप्रास्त्रः<BR> सुत्वनः परिपूजयन् Bk. 4. 12.<BR>—2 One living by violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यः|व्रात्य
व्रात्यः [व्रातात् समूहात् च्यवति यत्]<BR>—1 A man of the first three classes who has lost his caste owing to the<BR> non-performance of the principal Saṃskāras or purificatory rites (especially<BR> investiture with the sacred thread) over him, an outcast; सावित्रीपतिता<BR> व्रात्या भवन्त्यार्याविगर्हिताः Ms. 2. 39; सौराष्ट्रावन्त्याभीराश्च शूरा<BR> अर्बुदमालवाः । व्रात्या द्विजा भविष्यन्ति शूद्रप्राया जनाधिपाः Bhāg. 12. 1. 38;<BR> भवत्या हि व्रात्याधमपतितपाखण्डपरिषत्परित्राणस्नेहः G. L. 37.<BR>—2 A low or vile person in general; vagrant.<BR>—3 A man of a particular inferior tribe (the descendant of a Śūdra father<BR> and Kṣatriya mother).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्या
व्रात्यः + .{@-त्या@} The daughter of an outcast.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रात्यचर्या, व्रात्यब्रुवः, व्रात्यस्तोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यचर्या
व्रात्यः + -चर्या the life and practice of a vagrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यब्रुवः|व्रात्यब्रुव
व्रात्यः + -ब्रुवः one who calls himself a Vrātya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यस्तोमः|व्रात्यस्तोम
व्रात्यः + -स्तोमः N. of a sacrifice performed to recover the rights forfeited<BR> by the non-performance of the due Saṃskāras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1523-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री I. €9 P. (व्रिणाति-व्रीणाति) To choose, select; cf. वृ.<BR>━II. €4 Ā. (व्रीयते, व्रीण)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To be chosen.<BR>—3 To cover, screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् €4 P. (व्रीडयति)<BR>—1 To be ashamed, feel shame.<BR>—2 To throw, cast, send forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडः|व्रीड
व्रीडः, -डा<BR>—1 Shame; व्रीडादिवाभ्यासगतैर्विलिल्ये Śi. 3. 40; व्रीडमावहति मे<BR> स (शब्दः) संप्रति R. 11. 73.<BR>—2 Modesty, bashfulness; व्रीडजाड्यमभजन्मधुपा सा Śi. 10. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रीडानत, व्रीडान्वित, व्रीडदानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडा
व्रीडः, -डा<BR>—1 Shame; व्रीडादिवाभ्यासगतैर्विलिल्ये Śi. 3. 40; व्रीडमावहति मे<BR> स (शब्दः) संप्रति R. 11. 73.<BR>—2 Modesty, bashfulness; व्रीडजाड्यमभजन्मधुपा सा Śi. 10. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रीडानत, व्रीडान्वित, व्रीडदानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडानत
व्रीडः + -आनत, -अन्वित <i>a.</i> modest, bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडान्वित
व्रीडः + -आनत, -अन्वित <i>a.</i> modest, bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडदानम्
व्रीडः + -दानम् (व्रीडादानम्) a gift offered out of modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडनम्
व्रीडनम्<BR>—1 Shame.<BR>—2 Modesty.<BR>—3 Lowering, depression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित (Sometimes व्रीलित also) <i>p. p.</i> Put to shame, ashamed,<BR> abashed; व्रीलित इवास्मि राजानं द्रष्टुम् Pañc. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीलः
व्रीलः Shame; व्रीलादिवाधोमुखम् Pratijñā. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् €1 P., €10 U. (व्रीसति, व्रीसयति-ते) To injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिः|व्रीहि
व्रीहिः [व्री-हि किच्च]<BR>—1 Rice; as in बहुव्रीहि q. v.<BR>—2 A grain of rice.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: व्रीह्यगारम्, व्रीहिकाञ्चनम्, व्रीहिमयः, व्रीहिमुखः, व्रीहिराजिकम्, व्रीहिवापम्, व्रीहिश्रेष्ठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीह्यगारम्
व्रीहिः + -अगारम् a granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिकाञ्चनम्
व्रीहिः + -काञ्चनम् a kind of pulse (Mar. मसुरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिमयः|व्रीहिमय
व्रीहिः + -मयः a sacrificial cake<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">Page1524-2</a>]<BR> made of grains (पुरोडाश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिमुखः|व्रीहिमुख
व्रीहिः + -मुखः a surgical instrument (resembling a grain of rice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिराजिकम्
व्रीहिः + -राजिकम् panic seed (= कङ्गू q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिवापम्
व्रीहिः + -वापम् Sowing rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिश्रेष्ठः|व्रीहिश्रेष्ठ
व्रीहिः + -श्रेष्ठः a kind of rice (शालिधान्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिक|व्रीहिकः
व्रीहिक <i>a.</i> Having or bearing rice; P. V. 2. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
व्रुड् €6 P. (व्रुडति)<BR>—1 To cover.<BR>—2 To be heaped or gathered.<BR>—3 To heap, accumulate.<BR>—4 To sink, go down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुडित
व्रुडित <i>p. p.</i> Immersed, sunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूष्
व्रूष्, -स् €1 P., €10 U.<BR> See व्रीस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
व्रूष्, -स् €1 P., €10 U.<BR> See व्रीस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [व्रीहि-ठक्]<BR>—1 Fit for rice.<BR>—2 Sown with rice; P. V. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेयम्
व्रैहेय + .{@-यम्@} A field of rice, one fit for growing rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली €9 P. (व्लिनाति rarely व्लीनाति, <i>Caus.</i> व्लेपयति)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To support, hold, maintain.<BR>—3 To choose, select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लीन
व्लीन <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Crushed, sunk down.<BR>—2 Held, supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष्
व्लेक्ष् €10 U. (व्लेक्षयति-ते) To see; cf. वेक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेष्कः|व्लेष्क
व्लेष्कः A snare, noose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शः|श|शं
शः<BR>—1 A cutter, destroyer.<BR>—2 A weapon.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शः + .{@-शम्@} Happiness; हर्तुर्याति न गोचरं किमपि शं पुष्णाति यत्<BR> सर्वदा Bh. 2. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु <i>a.</i> Happy, prosperous; कुर्वाणा पश्यतः शंयून् स्रग्विणी<BR> सुहसानना Bk. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयुः|शंयु
शंयु + .{@-युः@} A deity presiding over sacrifice; शंयोरभिस्रवन्ताय अथर्वाय<BR> नमो नमः Mb. 13. 14. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंव <i>a.</i> Happy, fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवः|शंव
शंव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 Ploughing in the regular direction.<BR>—2 The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—3 The iron head of a pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस् €1 P. (शंसति, शस्त; <i>pass.</i> शस्यते)<BR>—1 To praise, extol, approve of; साधु साध्विति भूतानि शशंसुर्मारुतात्मजम्<BR> Rām.; संन्यासं कर्मणां कृष्ण पुनर्योगं च शंससि Bg. 5. 1.<BR>—2 To tell, relate, express, declare, communicate, announce, report (with<BR> dat. or sometimes gen. of person or by itself); शशंस सीतापरिदेवनान्तमनुष्ठितं<BR> शासनमग्रजाय R. 14. 83; न मे ह्रिया शंसति किंचिदीप्सितम् 3. 5, 2. 68, 4. 72, 9. 77, 11. 84;<BR> Ku. 3. 60, 5. 51.<BR>—3 to indicate, bespeak, show; यः (अशोकः) सावज्ञो माधवश्रीनियोगे<BR> पुष्पैः शंसत्यादरं त्वत्प्रयत्ने M. 5. 8; Ki. 5. 23; Ku. 2. 22.<BR>—4 To repeat, recite; ओमिति शंसति Ch. Up. 1. 1. 9.<BR>—5 To hurt, injure.<BR>—6 To revile, traduce.<BR>—7 To praise in ऋक् verse not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">Page1524-a2</a>]<BR> set to music (as distinguished from स्तु €2 U.); प्रगीतेषु मन्त्रवाक्येषु<BR> स्तौतिशब्दः अप्रगीतेषु शंसतिशब्दः ŚB. on MS. 7. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसः|शंस
शंसः Ved.<BR>—1 Praise.<BR>—2 Recitation.<BR>—3 Calling, invocation.<BR>—4 A charm, spell.<BR>—5 Wishing well to.<BR>—6 A blessing.<BR>—7 A curse.<BR>—8 Calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसनम्
शंसनम् [शंस्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Praising.<BR>—2 Telling, relating.<BR>—3 Reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसनीय
शंसनीय <i>a.</i> To be praised, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा [शंस्-अ]<BR>—1 Praise.<BR>—2 Wish, desire, hope.<BR>—3 Repeating, narrating.<BR>—4 Reciting.<BR>—5 Conjecture, belief; मातास्य युगपद् वाक्यं विप्रियं प्रियशंसया<BR> Rām. 2. 72. 41 (com. प्रियशंसया प्रियशङ्कया).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित <i>p. p.</i> [शंस्-क्त]<BR>—1 Praised, extolled.<BR>—2 Told, said, spoken, declared.<BR>—3 Wished, desired.<BR>—4 Ascertained, established, determined.<BR>—5 Falsely accused, calumniated.<BR>—6 Observed (अनुष्टित); इदं शास्त्रमधीयानो ब्राह्मणः शंसितव्रतः Ms. 1. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
शंसिन् <i>a.</i> (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Praising.<BR>—2 Telling, announcing, communicating; प्रजावती<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">Page1525-1</a>]<BR> दोहदशंसिनी ते R. 14. 45.<BR>—3 Indicating, bespeaking; मूर्धानः क्षतहुंकारशंसिनः Ku. 2. 26;<BR> अभिमतफलशंसी चारु पुस्फोर बाहुः Bk. 1. 27; प्रार्थनासिद्धिशंसिनः<BR> R. 1. 42; Śi. 9. 77.<BR>—4 Presaging, foretelling; बभूव सर्वं शुभशंसि तत्क्षणम् R. 3. 14, 12. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1524-a2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A praiser, panegyrist.<BR>—2 A reciter of hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्य|शंस्यः
शंस्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Loudly read; (Dānasāgara, Bibl. Ind. 274, Fasc. 1, p. 63).<BR>—2 Praiseworthy.<BR>—3 Desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् I. €5 P. (शक्नोति, शक्त)<BR>—1 To be able, be competent for, have power to effect (usually with an<BR> inf. and translatable by ‘can’); अदर्शयन् वक्तुमशक्नुवत्यः शाखभिरावर्जितपल्लवाभिः<BR> R. 13. 24; Bk. 3. 6; Me. 20; sometimes, with acc. or dat.; दानेन वधनिर्णेकं<BR> सर्पादीनामशक्नुवन् Ms. 11. 139; with gen. also; see शक्त.<BR>—2 To bear, endure.<BR>—3 To be powerful. ━<i>Pass.</i> To be able, be possible or practicable (giving<BR> a passive sense to a following infinitive); तत् कर्तुं शक्यते ‘it can be done’<BR>. ━<i>Desid.</i> (शिक्षति)<BR>—1 To wish to be able.<BR>—2 To learn. ━II. €4 U. (शक्यति-ते, शक्त)<BR>—1 To be able, have power to effect.<BR>—2 To bear, endure.<BR>—3 To give.<BR>—4 To aid.<BR>—5 To know (mostly Ved. in these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकः|शक
शकः<BR>—1 N. of a king (especially applied to Śālivāhana; but scholars do<BR> not seem to have yet agreed as to the precise meaning and scope of the word).<BR>—2 An epoch, era (the term is especially applied to the era of Śālivāhana<BR> which commences 78 years after the Christian era).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकाः
शकः + .{@-काः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.)<BR>—1 N. of a country.<BR>—2 N. of a particular tribe or race of people (mentioned in Ms. 10. 44<BR> along with the Pauṇḍrakas &c.; see Mu. 5. 11 also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शकान्तकः, शकारिः, शकाब्दः, शककालः, शककर्तृ, शककृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकान्तकः|शकान्तक|शकांतक
शकः + -अन्तकः, -अरिः epithets of king Vikramāditya who is said to<BR> have exterminated the Śakas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकारिः|शकारि
शकः + -अन्तकः, -अरिः epithets of king Vikramāditya who is said to<BR> have exterminated the Śakas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकाब्दः|शकाब्द
शकः + -अब्दः, -कालः a year of the Śaka era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शककालः|शककाल
शकः + -अब्दः, -कालः a year of the Śaka era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शककर्तृ
शकः + -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the founder of an era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शककृत्
शकः + -कर्तृ, -कृत् <i>m.</i> the founder of an era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकम्
शकम् Dung, cow-dung (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटः|शकट|शकटं
शकटः, -टम्<BR> [शक्-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 81]<BR>—1 A cart, carriage, waggon; रोहिणीशकटम् Pt. 1. 213, 211, 212; Y. 3. 42.<BR>—2 Cart-stand; caravansary; कृष्णरामौ वृतौ गोपैः पुराच्छकटमीयतुः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 42. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटम्
शकटः, -टम्<BR> [शक्-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 81]<BR>—1 A cart, carriage, waggon; रोहिणीशकटम् Pt. 1. 213, 211, 212; Y. 3. 42.<BR>—2 Cart-stand; caravansary; कृष्णरामौ वृतौ गोपैः पुराच्छकटमीयतुः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 42. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटः|शकट|शकटं
शकटः, -टम् + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 A form of military array resembling a wedge; Ms. 7. 187.<BR>—2 A measure of capacity, cart-load equal to 2000 <i>palas</i>.<BR>—3 N. of a demon slain by Kṛṣṇa when quite a boy.<BR>—4 N. of a tree (तिनिश).<BR>—5 An implement for preparing grain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शकटाक्षः, शकटारिः, शकटहन्, शकटाह्वा, शकटोर्वी, शकटभेदः, शकटविलः, शकटव्यूहः, शकटव्रतम्, शकटसार्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाक्षः|शकटाक्ष
शकटः + -अक्षः the axle of a cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटारिः|शकटारि
शकटः + -अरिः, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटहन्
शकटः + -अरिः, -हन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटाह्वा
शकटः + -आह्वा the lunar asterism Rohiṇī (so called because it is figured by a cart).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटोर्वी
शकटः + -उर्वी even, flat space; Gīrvāṇa.; Mb. 13. 85. 50 (com. शकटोर्वी<BR> तु श्रुत्यन्तरात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटभेदः|शकटभेद
शकटः + -भेदः the division of Rohiṇī by a planet passing through it;<BR> cf. यदि रोहिण्याः शकटं भिनत्ति रविनन्दनो गगनबीथ्याम् । द्वादश<BR> वर्षणि तदा न हि वर्षति वासवो भूमौ ॥ Pt. 1. 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटविलः|शकटविल
शकटः + -विलः a gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटव्यूहः|शकटव्यूह
शकटः + -व्यूहः a particular form of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">Page1525-2</a>]<BR> military array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटव्रतम्
शकटः + -व्रतम् a particular observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटसार्थः|शकटसार्थ
शकटः + -सार्थः a train of carts; caravan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका A small cart, a toy-cart; as in मृच्छकटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् <i>n.</i> Ordure, feces, especially of animals; (this word has<BR> no forms for the first five inflections, and is optionally substituted<BR> for शकृत् after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकरम्
शकरम् See शकल (1); मांसान्यस्य शकराणि Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलः|शकल|शकलं
शकलः, -लम्<BR> [शक्-कलक् Uṇ. 1. 109]<BR>—1 A part, portion, piece, fragment, bit; ताभ्यां स शकलाभ्यां च दिवं<BR> भूमिं च निर्ममे Ms. 1. 13; उपलशकलमेतद्भेदकं गोमयानाम् Mu. 3. 15;<BR> R. 2. 46, 5. 73.<BR>—2 A pot-sherd; प्रतिगृह्य पुटेनैव पाणिना शकलेन वा Ms. 6. 28.<BR>—3 A spark; उद्यत्कृशानुशकलेषु खुराभिघातात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलम्
शकलः, -लम्<BR> [शक्-कलक् Uṇ. 1. 109]<BR>—1 A part, portion, piece, fragment, bit; ताभ्यां स शकलाभ्यां च दिवं<BR> भूमिं च निर्ममे Ms. 1. 13; उपलशकलमेतद्भेदकं गोमयानाम् Mu. 3. 15;<BR> R. 2. 46, 5. 73.<BR>—2 A pot-sherd; प्रतिगृह्य पुटेनैव पाणिना शकलेन वा Ms. 6. 28.<BR>—3 A spark; उद्यत्कृशानुशकलेषु खुराभिघातात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलम्
शकलः, -लम् + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Bark.<BR>—2 The scales (of a fish).<BR>—3 A half; as in चन्द्रशकलम्.<BR>—4 Cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलित
शकलित <i>a.</i> Reduced to fragments, shattered to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन् <i>m.</i> A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकृ
शकलीकृ €8 U. To reduce to fragments or pieces, cut to pieces, divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकारः|शकार
शकारः The brother of a kingʼs concubine, the brother-in-law of<BR> a king by a wife not regularly married (अनूढाभ्रातृ); (he is usually<BR> represented as a strange mixture of pride, folly, and vanity, of low family,<BR> and raised to power by reason of his relation to the king. In the Mṛcchakaṭika<BR> of Śūdraka where he plays a prominent part, his character is well exhibited<BR> in his lightness and frivolity of spirit, vain-glory, constant reference<BR> to his high connection, his blundering and ludicrous folly, but withal<BR> cruelty enough to throttle the heroine when she refused to yield to his<BR> desire; S. D. thus defines him:− मदमूर्खताभिमानी दुष्कुलतैश्वर्यसंयुक्तः ।<BR> सोऽयमनूढाभ्राता राज्ञः श्यालः शकार इत्युक्तः ॥) 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनः|शकुन|शकुनं
शकुनः [शक्-उनन् Uṇ. 3. 49]<BR>—1 A bird (in general); केनेदृशी जातु परा हि दृष्टा वागुच्यमाना शकुनेन<BR> संस्कृता Mb. 3. 197. 11; शकुनोच्छिष्टम् Y. 1. 168.<BR>—2 A kind of bird, a vulture or kite.<BR>—3 A kind of song (sung at festivals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनम्
शकुनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 An omen, a prognostic, any omen presaging good or evil; अशकुनेन<BR> स्खलितः किलेतरोऽपि Śi. 9. 83.<BR>—2 An auspicious omen.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शकुनज्ञ, शकुनज्ञानम्, शकुनशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञ
शकुनः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञा
शकुनः + -ज्ञ + .({@-ज्ञा@}) a small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनज्ञानम्
शकुनः + -ज्ञानम् knowledge of omens, augury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनशास्त्रम्
शकुनः + -शास्त्रम् ‘the science of omens’, N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिः|शकुनि
शकुनिः [शक्-उनि]<BR>—1 A bird; तरुशकुनिकुरङ्गान् मैथिली यानपुष्यत् U. 3. 25; Ms. 12. 63.<BR>—2 A vulture, kite or eagle.<BR>—3 A cock.<BR>—4 N. of a son of Subala, king of Gāndhāra and brother of Gāndharī,<BR> wife of Dhṛtarāṣṭra; he was thus the maternal uncle of Duryodhana<BR> whom he assisted in many of his wicked schemes to exterminate the Pāṇḍavas.<BR> The name is now usually applied to an old wicked-minded relative whose counsels tend<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">Page1526-1</a>]<BR> to ruin.<BR>—5 N. of a demon killed by Kṛṣṇa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शकुनीश्वरः, शकुनिप्रपा, शकुनिवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1525-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनीश्वरः|शकुनीश्वर
शकुनिः + -ईश्वरः N. of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिप्रपा
शकुनिः + -प्रपा a trough for watering birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिवादः|शकुनिवाद
शकुनिः + -वादः<BR>—1 the cry or sound of a bird.<BR>—2 the crowing of a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनी
शकुनी<BR>—1 A hen-sparrow.<BR>—2 A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तः|शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुंतः
शकुन्तः [शक्-उन्त]<BR>—1 A bird in general; अंसव्यापिशकुन्तनीडनिचितं बिभ्रज्जटामण्डलम् Ś. 7. 11.<BR>—2 The blue jay.<BR>—3 A kind of bird.<BR>—4 A sort of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तकः|शकुन्तक|शकुंतक|शकुंतकः
शकुन्तकः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तला|शकुंतला
शकुन्तला [शकुन्तैः लायते ला घञर्थे क] N. of the daughter<BR> of Viśvāmitra by the nymph Menakā who was sent down by Indra to disturb<BR> the sageʼs austerities. [When Menakā went up to the heaven she left the<BR> child in a solitary forest where she was taken care of by ‘Śakuntas’<BR> or birds, whence she was called “Śakuntalā”. She was afterwards found<BR> by the sage Kaṇva and brought up as his own daughter. When Duṣyanta<BR> in the course of his hunting came to the sageʼs hermitage, he was fascinated<BR> by her charms and prevailed on her to become his wife by the Gandharva<BR> form of marriage; (see Duṣyanta). She bore to him a son named Bharata,<BR> who became a universal monarch, and gave his name to India which came<BR> to be called Bharatavarṣa.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तिः|शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुंतिः
शकुन्तिः A bird; कलमविरलं रत्युत्कण्ठाः क्वणन्तु शकुन्तयः U. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुन्तिका|शकुंतिका
शकुन्तिका<BR>—1 A bird; छद्मना परिददामि मृत्यवे सौनिको गृहशकुन्तिकामिव U. 1. 45.<BR>—2 A kind of bird.<BR>—3 A locust, cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1526-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुर
