शत्वरी
शत्वरी Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्
शद् I. €1 P. (but Ā. in conjugational tenses) (शीयते, शन्न)<BR>—1 To fall, perish, decay, wither.<BR>—2 To go. ━<i>Caus.</i> (शादयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to go, impel.<BR>—2 (शातयति-ते)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To fell, throw down, cut down; किं भूभृत्कटकस्थितिव्यसनिना<BR> व्यर्थ खुराः शातिताः Subhāṣ.; Śi. 14. 80, 15. 24.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To kill, destroy. ━II. €1 P. (शदति) To go (usually with आ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शदः|शद
शदः<BR>—1 An eatable vegetable product (fruit, root &c.).<BR>—2 Produce, revenue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रिः|शद्रि
शद्रिः (शद्-क्रिन् Uṇ. 4. 67)<BR>—1 An elephant.<BR>—2 Cloud.<BR>—3 N. of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रिः|शद्रि
शद्रिः + .{@-द्रिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Lightning.<BR>—2 Candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रु|शद्रुः
शद्रु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Going, moving.<BR>—2 Falling, perishing, decaying, P. III. 2. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्न
शन्न <i>p. p.</i> Fallen, decayed, withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन
शन <i>a.</i> Quiet, soft, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकैस्
शनकैस् <i>ind.</i> Slowly; see शनैस्; विचिन्वन्तोऽथ शनकैर्जानकीं<BR> दक्षिणाम्बुधे A. Rām. 4. 7. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिः|शनि
शनिः [शो-अनि किच्च Tv.]<BR>—1 The planet Saturn (the son of the sun and represented as of a black<BR> colour or dressed in dark-coloured clothes).<BR>—2 Saturday.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शनिचक्रम्, शनिजम्, शनिप्रदोषः, शनिप्रसूः, शनिप्रियम्, शनिवारः, शनिवासरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिचक्रम्
शनिः + -चक्रम् Saturnʼs diagram (used for foretelling).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिजम्
शनिः + -जम् black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रदोषः|शनिप्रदोष
शनिः + -प्रदोषः a term for the (evening) worship of Śiva performed<BR> on the thirteenth day of a lunar fortnight when it falls on a Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रसूः
शनिः + -प्रसूः <i>f.</i> an epithet of Chāyā, wife of the sun; cf. संज्ञा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिप्रियम्
शनिः + -प्रियम् a sapphire or emerald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिवारः|शनिवार
शनिः + -वारः, -वासरः Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिवासरः|शनिवासर
शनिः + -वारः, -वासरः Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिर्भावः
शनिर्भावः<BR>—1 Slowness.<BR>—2 Graduality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिर्मेहः
शनिर्मेहः Dysuria.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैस्
शनैस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Slowly, gently, quietly.<BR>—2 Gradually, by degrees, little by little; धर्मं संचिनुयाच्छनैः;<BR> Ku. 3. 59; Ms. 3. 217.<BR>—3 Successively, in due order; विषयाणां ग्रहीतॄणि शनैः पञ्चेन्द्रियाणि<BR> च Ms. 1. 15.<BR>—4 Mildly, softly.<BR>—5 Tardily, sluggishly. —6 Independently. (शनैः शनैः slowly, by slow degrees).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शनैश्चर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैश्चर|शनैश्चरः
शनैस् + -चर <i>a.</i> going or moving slowly; शनैश्चराभ्यां पादाभ्यां<BR> रेजे ग्रहमयीव सा Bh. 1. 17 (where it means ‘Saturn’ also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैश्चरः|शनैश्चर
शनैस् + -चर + .({@-रः@}) the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्तनुः|शन्तनु|शंतनु|शंतनुः
शन्तनुः N. of a king of the lunar race. He married Gaṅgā and Satyavatī;<BR> by the former wife he had a son named Bhīṣma, and by the latter Chitrāṅgada<BR> and Vicitravīrya. Bhīṣma remained a celibate all his life, and his<BR> younger brothers died childless; cf. भीष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् A technical term used by Pāṇini for the conjugational sign<BR> अ inserted between the root and the terminations of the conjugational<BR> tenses in the first class of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् <i>ind.</i> A particle and prefix implying assent or compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् €1. €4 U. (शपति-ते, शप्यति-ते, शप्त)<BR>—1 To curse, execrate; अशपद् भव मानुषीति ताम् R. 8. 80; सोऽभूत्<BR> परासुरथ भूमिपतिं शशाप (वृद्धः) 9. 78, 1. 77.<BR>—2 To swear, take an oath, promise by oath, say on oath, (usually with<BR> dat. of the person to whom a promise &c. is made and instr. of the object<BR> by which it is made); भरतेनात्मना चाहं शपे ते मनुजाधिप । यथा<BR> नान्येन तुष्येयमृते रामविवासनात् ॥ Rām.; when used without an object<BR> it generally governs the instr. of the thing and dat. of the person by<BR> which or whom the oath is taken; सत्यं शपामि ते पादपङ्कजस्पर्शेन<BR> K.; Ghaṭ. 22; अशप्त निह्नुवानाऽसौ सीतायै स्मरमोहितः Bk. 8. 74;<BR> प्रेम जिज्ञासमानाभ्यस्ताभ्योऽशप्सत कामिनः 8. 33; sometimes शप्<BR> governs a cognate accusative; सहस्रशोऽसौ शपथानशप्यत् Bk. 3. 32; Ms. 8. 110.<BR>—3 To blame, scold, revile, abuse (with dat. or by itself); द्विषद्भपश्चा-शपंस्तथा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">Page1532-1</a>]<BR> Bk. 17. 4; प्रतिवाचमदत्त केशवः शपमानाय न चेदिभूभुजे Śi. 16. 25.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> (शापयति-ते)<BR>—1 To bind by an oath, conjure; शापितोऽसि गोब्राह्मणकाम्यया Mk. 3;<BR> शापितासि मम लवङ्गिकावलोकितयोश्च जीवितेन यदि वाचा न कथयसि Māl. 8.<BR>—2 To cause any one (acc.) to swear by (instr.); सत्येन शापयेद्विप्रं<BR> क्षत्रियं वाहनायुधैः Ms. 8. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1531-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपित
शपित <i>p. p.</i> Cursed; इति रोषवशादुभौ तदानीमन्योन्यं शपितौ<BR> नृपद्विजेन्द्रौ Rām. 7. 55. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपः|शप
शपः [शप्-अच्]<BR>—1 A curse, an imprecation.<BR>—2 An oath.<BR>—3 A corpse (wrong reading for शव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथः|शपथ
शपथः [शप्-अथन् Uṇ. 3. 112]<BR>—1 Cursing.<BR>—2 A curse, an imprecation, anathema.<BR>—3 An oath, swearing, taking or administering an oath, asseveration by<BR> oath or ordeal; आमोदो न हि कस्तूर्याः शपथेनानुभाव्यते Bv. 1. 120; Ms. 8. 109.<BR>—4 Conjuration, binding by oaths; सपदि शपथैः प्रत्यावृत्तिं प्रणम्य<BR> च याचते Māl. 3. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शपथोत्तरम्, शपथपूर्वकम्, शपथकरणम्, शपथपत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथोत्तरम्
शपथः + -उत्तरम्, -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> with oaths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथपूर्वकम्
शपथः + -उत्तरम्, -पूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> with oaths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथकरणम्
शपथः + -करणम् taking an oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथपत्रम्
शपथः + -पत्रम् an affidavit, a statement on oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपनम्
शपनम्<BR>—1 See शपथ; वृथा हि शपनं कुर्वन् प्रेत्य चेह च नश्यति Ms. 8. 111.<BR>—2 Reviling, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्त|शप्तः
शप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cursed; निशम्य शप्तमतदर्ह नरेन्द्रम् Bhāg. 1. 18. 41.<BR>—2 Sworn.<BR>—3 Reviled, abused; (see शप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफः|शफ|शफं
शफः, -फम्<BR> [शप्-अच् पृषो˚ पस्य फः]<BR>—1 A hoof; सुरभेर्महिषा गावो ये चान्ये द्विशफा नृप Bhāg. 6. 6. 27.<BR>—2 A claw; यज्ञायज्ञियं पुच्छं धिष्ण्यां शफाम् Vāj. 12. 4.<BR>—3 The root of a tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शफोरुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफम्
शफः, -फम्<BR> [शप्-अच् पृषो˚ पस्य फः]<BR>—1 A hoof; सुरभेर्महिषा गावो ये चान्ये द्विशफा नृप Bhāg. 6. 6. 27.<BR>—2 A claw; यज्ञायज्ञियं पुच्छं धिष्ण्यां शफाम् Vāj. 12. 4.<BR>—3 The root of a tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शफोरुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफोरुः|शफोरु
शफः + -ऊरुः <i>f.</i> a woman having thighs resembling the two divisions<BR> of a cowʼs hoof; see P. IV. 1. 70. The early commentators of Pāṇini<BR> or of other schools of grammar evidently think that the word is two well-known<BR> to require any explanation. Viṭṭhala, Bhaṭṭojī and others think that<BR> the word means ‘a woman whose thighs press together like hoofs’. But there<BR> is not the slightest doubt that the sense of similitude is present here<BR> and the word comes within the purview of the previous rule ऊरूत्तरपदादौपम्ये.<BR> Or it may mean a woman whose thighs are marked with the sign of hoofs.<BR> Sṛṣṭidhara the commentator on the Bhāṣāvṛtti gives the correct<BR> meaning. शफं खुरः । तच्चिह्नयुक्त ऊरुर्यस्याः ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफरः|शफर
शफरः (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शफं राति रा-क Tv.] A kind of small glittering<BR> fish; मोघीकर्तुं चटुलशफरोद्वर्तनप्रेक्षितानि Me. 42; मनोऽस्य<BR> जह्रुः शफरीविवृत्तयः Ki. 4. 3; Śi. 8. 24; Ku. 4. 39.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शफराधिपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफराधिपः|शफराधिप
शफरः + -अधिपः the fish called Ilīśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफरुकः|शफरुक
शफरुकः A box, pot; Hc. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरः|शबर
शब(व)रः<BR>—1 A mountaineer, barbarian, savage; राजन् गुञ्जाफलानां स्रज इति शबरा<BR> नैव हारं हरन्ति K. P 10.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 The hand.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 N. of a celebrated commentator and writer on Mīmāṃsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवरः|शवर
शब(व)रः<BR>—1 A mountaineer, barbarian, savage; राजन् गुञ्जाफलानां स्रज इति शबरा<BR> नैव हारं हरन्ति K. P 10.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 The hand.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 N. of a celebrated commentator and writer on Mīmāṃsā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरी
शब(व)रः + .{@-री@}<BR>—1 A Śabara female.<BR>—2 A female <i>Kirāta</i> who was an ardent devotee of Rāma.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शबरालयः, शबरकन्दः, शबरबलम्, शबरलोध्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरालयः|शबरालय
शबरः + -आलयः the abode of wild<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">Page1532-2</a>]<BR> mountaineers or barbarians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरकन्दः|शबरकन्द
शबरः + -कन्दः a sweet potato.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरबलम्
शबरः + -बलम् an army of mountaineers; वनमार्गेण दुर्गेण गच्छन्नधिकबलेन<BR> शबरबलेन रभसादभिहन्यमानः Dk. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरलोध्रः|शबरलोध्र
शबरः + -लोध्रः the wild <i>Lodhra</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबल|शबलः
शब(व)ल <i>a.</i> (शप्-अल, बश्च Uṇ. 1. 99)<BR>—1 Spotted, brindled, variegated; क्वचित् प्रभा चान्द्रमसी तमोभिश्छायाविलीनैः<BR> शबलीकृतेव R. 13. 56, 5. 44; Mv. 7. 26.<BR>—2 Varied, divided into various parts.<BR>—3 Articulate; imitative.<BR>—4 Mixed; आनन्दशोकशबलत्वमुपैति चेतः Māl. 9. 54.<BR>—5 Disfigured, pale; चिन्तया शबलं मुखम् Bhāg. 6. 14. 21.<BR>—6 Disturbed, afflicted; अत्युत्कण्ठः शबलहृदयोऽस्मद्विधो बाष्पधाराः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 90. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शब(व)ल <i>a.</i> (शप्-अल, बश्च Uṇ. 1. 99)<BR>—1 Spotted, brindled, variegated; क्वचित् प्रभा चान्द्रमसी तमोभिश्छायाविलीनैः<BR> शबलीकृतेव R. 13. 56, 5. 44; Mv. 7. 26.<BR>—2 Varied, divided into various parts.<BR>—3 Articulate; imitative.<BR>—4 Mixed; आनन्दशोकशबलत्वमुपैति चेतः Māl. 9. 54.<BR>—5 Disfigured, pale; चिन्तया शबलं मुखम् Bhāg. 6. 14. 21.<BR>—6 Disturbed, afflicted; अत्युत्कण्ठः शबलहृदयोऽस्मद्विधो बाष्पधाराः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 90. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबलः|शबल
शब(व)ल + .{@-लः@} A variegated colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबला
शब(व)ल + .{@-ला, -ली@}<BR>—1 A spotted or brindled cow.<BR>—2 The cow of plenty or Kāmadhenu q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबली
शब(व)ल + .{@-ला, -ली@}<BR>—1 A spotted or brindled cow.<BR>—2 The cow of plenty or Kāmadhenu q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबलम्
शब(व)ल + .{@-लम्@} Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबलिमन्
शबलिमन् Variegated condition or appearance; शबलिमा बलिमानमुषो<BR> वपुः Śi. 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द्
शब्द् €10 U. (शब्दयति-ते, शब्दित)<BR>—1 To sound, make a noise.<BR>—2 To speak, call out, call out to; विततमृदुकराग्रः शब्दयन्त्या वयोभिः<BR> परिपतति दिवोऽङ्के हेलया बालसूर्यः Śi. 11. 47. 3 To name, call;<BR> ब्रह्मेति परमात्मेति भगवानिति शब्द्यते Bhāg. 1. 2. 11; अत एव<BR> सागरिकेति शब्द्यते Ratn. 4. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि@} to name. ━{@प्र@} to explain.<BR> ━{@सं@} to call out to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दः|शब्द
शब्दः [शब्द्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sound (the object of the sense of hearing and property of आकाश);<BR> अथात्मनः शब्दगुणं गुणज्ञः पदं विमानेन विगाहमानः R. 13. 1.<BR>—2 Sound, note (of birds; men &c.), noise in general; विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः<BR> शब्दं सहन्ते मृगाः Ś. 1. 14; स शब्दस्तुमुलोऽभवत् Bg. 1. 13;<BR> Ś. 3. 1; Ms. 4. 31; Ku. 1. 45.<BR>—3 The sound of a musical instrument; वाद्यशब्दः Pt. 2; Ku. 1. 45.<BR>—4 A word, sound, significant word (for def. &c. see Mbh. introduction);<BR> एकः शब्दः सम्यगधीतः सम्यक् प्रयुक्तः स्वर्गे लोके कामधुग्भवति;<BR> so शब्दार्थौ.<BR>—5 A declinable word, a noun, substantive.<BR>—6 A title, an epithet; यस्यार्थयुक्तं गिरिराजशब्दं कुर्वन्ति बालव्यजनैश्चमर्यः<BR> Ku. 1. 13; Ś. 2. 15; नृपेण चक्रे युवराजशब्दभाक् R. 3. 35, 2. 53, 64, 3. 49, 5. 22, 18. 42;<BR> V. 1. 1.<BR>—7 The name, mere name as in शब्दपति q. v.<BR>—8 Verbal authority (regarded by the Naiyāyikas as a Pramāṇa.<BR>—9 Grammar); Dk. 1. 1.<BR>—10 Fame; लब्धशब्देन कौसल्ये कुमारेण धनुष्मता Rām. 2. 63. 11;<BR> स्वर्गाय शब्दं दिवमात्महेतोर्धर्मार्थमात्मस्थितिमाचकाङ्क्ष Bu. C. 2. 53;<BR>(cf. also ‘शब्दोऽक्षरे यशोगीत्योः’ -हैमः).<BR>—11 The sacred syllable ओम्.<BR>—12 A technical term.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शब्दाक्षरम्, शब्दातीत, शब्दाधिष्ठानम्, शब्दाध्याहारः, शब्दानुकृतिः, शब्दानुरूप, शब्दानुशासनम्, शब्दार्थः, शब्दालंकारः, शब्दाख्येय, शब्दाडम्बरः, शब्दादि, शब्देन्द्रियम्, शब्दकार, शब्दकोशः, शब्दग, शब्दगत, शब्दगतिः, शब्दगुण, शब्दगोचरः, शब्दग्रहः, शब्दग्रामः, शब्दचातुर्यम्, शब्दचित्रम्, शब्दचोरः, शब्दतन्मात्रम्, शब्दनेतृ, शब्दपतिः, शब्दपातिन्, शब्दप्रमाणम्, शब्दबोधः, शब्दब्रह्मन्, शब्दभाव्यत्वम्, शब्दभिद्, शब्दभेदिन्, शब्दयोनिः, शब्दलक्षण, शब्दवारिधिः, शब्दविद्या, शब्दशास्त्रम्, शब्दविरोधः, शब्दविशेषः, शब्दविशेषणम्, शब्दवृत्तिः, शब्दवेधिन्, शब्दवेध्य, शब्दवैलक्षण्यम्, शब्दशक्तिः, शब्दशासनम्, शब्दशुद्धिः, शब्दश्लेषः, शब्दसंग्रहः, शब्दसंज्ञ, शब्दसाधन, शब्दसाह, शब्दसौष्ठवम्, शब्दसौकर्यम्, शब्दस्मृतिः, शब्दहीनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाक्षरम्
शब्दः + -अक्षरम् the sacred syllable ओम् uttered aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दातीत
शब्दः + -अतीत <i>a.</i> beyond the power or reach of words, indescribable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाधिष्ठानम्
शब्दः + -अधिष्ठानम् the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाध्याहारः|शब्दाध्याहार
शब्दः + -अध्याहारः supplying a word (to complete an ellipsis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुकृतिः|शब्दानुकृति
शब्दः + -अनुकृतिः onomatopoeia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुरूप
शब्दः + -अनुरूप <i>a.</i> proportionate or corresponding to the sound; शब्दानुरूपेण<BR> पराक्रमेण भवितव्यम् Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दानुशासनम्
शब्दः + -अनुशासनम् the science of words; <i>i. e.</i> grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दार्थः|शब्दार्थ
शब्दः + -अर्थः the meaning of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दार्थौ
शब्दः + -अर्थः + .({@-र्थौ@} dual) a word and its meaning; अदोषौ शब्दार्थौ K. P. 1;<BR> न त्वयं शब्दार्थः, व्यामोहादेषा प्रतीतिः ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दालंकारः|शब्दालङ्कार|शब्दालंकार
शब्दः + -अलंकारः a figure of speech depending for its charmingness<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">Page1533-1</a>]<BR> on sound or words and disappearing as soon as the words which constitute<BR> the figure are replaced by others of the same meaning (opp. अर्थालंकार);<BR> <i>e. g.</i>; see K. P. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1532-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाख्येय
शब्दः + -आख्येय <i>a.</i> to be communicated in words; शब्दाख्येयं यदपि<BR> किल ते यः सखीनां पुरस्तात् Me. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाख्येयम्
शब्दः + -आख्येय + .({@-यम्@}) an oral or verbal communication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दाडम्बरः|शब्दाडम्बर|शब्दाडंबर
शब्दः + -आडम्बरः bombast, verbosity, high-sounding or grandiloquent words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दादि
शब्दः + -आदि <i>a.</i> beginning with शब्द (as the objects of sense);<BR> शब्दादीन् विषयान् भोक्तुं चरितुं दुश्चरं तपः R. 10. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्देन्द्रियम्
शब्दः + -इन्द्रियम् the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दकार|शब्दकारः
शब्दः + -कार <i>a.</i> sounding, sonorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दकोशः|शब्दकोश
शब्दः + -कोशः a lexicon, dictionary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दग
शब्दः + -ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 perceiving sounds.<BR>—2 uttering sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दगत
शब्दः + -गत <i>a.</i> inherent or residing in a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दगतिः|शब्दगति
शब्दः + -गतिः music, song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दगुण
शब्दः + -गुण <i>a.</i> having sound for its quality; अथात्मनः शब्दगुणं<BR> गुणज्ञः R. 13. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दगोचरः|शब्दगोचर
शब्दः + -गोचरः the aim or object of speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दग्रहः|शब्दग्रह
शब्दः + -ग्रहः<BR>—1 catching the sound.<BR>—2 the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दग्रामः|शब्दग्राम
शब्दः + -ग्रामः the range or reach of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचातुर्यम्
शब्दः + -चातुर्यम् cleverness of style, eloquence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचित्रम्
शब्दः + -चित्रम् one of the two subdivisions of the last (अवर or अधम)<BR> class of poetry (wherein the charm lies in the use of words<BR> which please the ear simply by their sound; see the example given under<BR> the word चित्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दचोरः|शब्दचोर
शब्दः + -चोरः ‘a word-thief’, a plagiarist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दतन्मात्रम्
शब्दः + -तन्मात्रम् the subtle element of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दनेतृ
शब्दः + -नेतृ <i>m.</i> N. of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दपतिः|शब्दपति
शब्दः + -पतिः a lord in name only, nominal lord; ननु शब्दपतिः क्षितेरहं<BR> त्वयि भे भावनिबन्धना रतिः R. 8. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दपातिन्
शब्दः + -पातिन् <i>a.</i> hitting an invisible mark the sound of which is<BR> only heard, tracing a sound; शब्दपातिनमिषुं विससर्ज R. 9. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दप्रमाणम्
शब्दः + -प्रमाणम् verbal or oral evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दबोधः|शब्दबोध
शब्दः + -बोधः knowledge derived from verbal testimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दब्रह्मन्
शब्दः + -ब्रह्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 the Vedas; शब्दब्रह्मणि निष्णातः परं ब्रह्माधिगच्छति Maitr. Up. 6. 22.<BR>—2 spiritual knowledge consisting in words, knowledge of the Supreme Spirit<BR> or the Spirit itself; शब्दब्रह्मणस्तादृशं विवर्तमितिहासम् U. 2, 7. 20.<BR>—3 a property of words called स्फोट q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दभाव्यत्वम्
शब्दः + -भाव्यत्वम् the state of becoming known through scriptural word<BR> only; कर्मणः शब्दभाव्यत्वात् … MS. 7. 1. 9 (on which Śabara writes<BR> अथेह कर्मणः शब्दभाव्यत्वम् । नान्यतः शक्यमेतज्ज्ञातुं कस्यापूर्वस्य<BR> धर्मा इति ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दभिद्
शब्दः + -भिद् <i>f.</i> perversion of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दभेदिन्
शब्दः + -भेदिन् <i>a.</i> hitting a mark merely by its sound. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 an epithet of Arjuna.<BR>—2 the anus.<BR>—3 a kind of arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दयोनिः|शब्दयोनि
शब्दः + -योनिः <i>f.</i> a root, radical word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दलक्षण
शब्दः + -लक्षण <i>a.</i> what is determined by the sacred word; इह शब्दलक्षणे<BR> कर्मणि यथाशब्दार्थं प्रवृत्तिः ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवारिधिः|शब्दवारिधि
शब्दः + -वारिधिः a vocabulary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दविद्या
शब्दः + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम् the science of words; <i>i. e.</i> grammar; अनन्तपारं<BR> किल शब्दशास्त्रम् Pt. 1; Śi. 2. 112, 14. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशास्त्रम्
शब्दः + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम् the science of words; <i>i. e.</i> grammar; अनन्तपारं<BR> किल शब्दशास्त्रम् Pt. 1; Śi. 2. 112, 14. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दविरोधः|शब्दविरोध
शब्दः + -विरोधः opposition of words (in a sentence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दविशेषः|शब्दविशेष
शब्दः + -विशेषः a variety of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दविशेषणम्
शब्दः + -विशेषणम् (in gram.) an adjective, adjectival word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवृत्तिः|शब्दवृत्ति
शब्दः + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the function of a word (in Rhet.).<BR>—2 the power of a word (to convey sense), indicative power (लक्षणा);<BR> अदृष्टार्थाच्छब्दवृत्तिर्लघीयसी ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवेधिन्
शब्दः + -वेधिन् <i>a.</i> hitting an invisible mark the sound of which is<BR> only heard; see शब्दपातिन्; अभ्याससाध्यं निखिलं मत्वा संतमसे व्यधात् ।<BR> इषुपातानभूद्येन शब्दवेधविशारदः ॥ Bm. 1. 632. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a kind of arrow.<BR>—2 an archer.<BR>—3 a warrior<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">Page1533-2</a>]<BR> who pierces his enemies by mere sounds; Rām. 2. 63. 11.<BR>—4 an epithet of king Daśaratha.<BR>—5 an epithet of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवेध्य
शब्दः + -वेध्य <i>a.</i> to be shot at without being seen; एवं मयाप्यविज्ञातं<BR> शब्दवेध्यमिदं फलम् Rām. 2. 63. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दवैलक्षण्यम्
शब्दः + -वैलक्षण्यम् verbal difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशक्तिः|शब्दशक्ति
शब्दः + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> the force or expressive power of a word; signification<BR> of a word; see शक्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशासनम्
शब्दः + -शासनम्<BR>—1 a rule of grammar.<BR>—2 the science of grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दशुद्धिः|शब्दशुद्धि
शब्दः + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 purity of words.<BR>—2 the correct use of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दश्लेषः|शब्दश्लेष
शब्दः + -श्लेषः a play or pun upon words, a verbal equivoque; (it differs<BR> from अर्थश्लेष in-as-much as the pun disappears as soon as the words<BR> which constitut it are replaced by others of the same signification whereas<BR> in अर्थश्लेष the pun remains unchanged; शब्दपरि वृत्तिसहत्वमर्थश्लेषः.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसंग्रहः|शब्दसङ्ग्रह
शब्दः + -संग्रहः a vocabulary, lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसंज्ञ
शब्दः + -संज्ञ (in gram.) a technical term; P. I. 1. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसाधन
शब्दः + -साधन, -साह <i>a.</i> See शब्दवेधिन्; ततोऽस्त्रं शब्दसाहं<BR> वै त्वरमाणो महारणे Mb. 3. 22. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसाह
शब्दः + -साधन, -साह <i>a.</i> See शब्दवेधिन्; ततोऽस्त्रं शब्दसाहं<BR> वै त्वरमाणो महारणे Mb. 3. 22. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसौष्ठवम्
शब्दः + -सौष्ठवम् elegance of words, a graceful or elegant style.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दसौकर्यम्
शब्दः + -सौकर्यम् ease of expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दस्मृतिः|शब्दस्मृति
शब्दः + -स्मृतिः <i>f.</i> philogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दहीनम्
शब्दः + -हीनम् the use of a word in a form or meaning not sanctioned by<BR> standard authors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दन|शब्दनः
शब्दन <i>a.</i> [शब्द् ल्यु-ल्युट् वा] Sounding, making a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दनम्
शब्दन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Sounding, making a noise, uttering a sound.<BR>—2 A sound, noise.<BR>—3 Calling out, calling.<BR>—4 Naming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दायते
शब्दायते Den. Ā.<BR>—1 To make a noise, sound; शब्दायन्ते मधुरमनिलैः कीचकाः पूर्यमाणाः Me. 58.<BR>—2 To cry, roar, scream, yell; शब्दायमानमव्यात्सीत् भयदं क्षणदाचरम्<BR> Bk. 5. 52, 17. 91.<BR>—3 To call, call out to; एते हस्तिनापुरगामिन ऋषयः शब्दायन्ते Ś. 4;<BR> Mu. 1; भवतु शब्दायिष्ये तावत् Ve. 3; Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दित
शब्दित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sounded, made to give out a sound, played upon (as a musical instrument).<BR>—2 Uttered, articulated.<BR>—3 Called, called out to.<BR>—4 Named, designated.<BR>—5 Taught, explained; ज्ञानेन वैयासकिशब्दितेन भेजे खगेन्द्रध्वजपादमूलम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 18. 16.<BR>—6 Made public, manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दितम्
शब्दित + .{@-तम्@} Noise, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् <i>ind.</i> A particle meaning welfare, happiness, prosperity, health,<BR> and generally used to express a blessing or pious wish, (with dat. or<BR> gen.); शं देवदत्ताय or देवदत्तस्य (often used in modern letters<BR> as an auspicious conclusion; इति शम्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शङ्कर, शन्तम, शन्ताति, शम्पाकः, शम्पातः, शम्भु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शङ्कर|शंकर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शम् + -कर see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्तम|शंतम
शम् + -तम most wholesome, salutary; तदोडुराजः ककुभः करैर्मुखं<BR> प्राच्या विलिम्पन्नरुणेन शन्तमैः Bhāg. 10. 29. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्ताति
शम् + -ताति <i>a.</i> conferring happiness, propitious, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पाकः|शम्पाक|शंपाक
शम् + -पाकः<BR>—1 lac, red dye.<BR>—2 cooking, maturing.<BR>—3 Cathartocarpus Fistula (शम्याक; Mar. बाहवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पातः|शम्पात
शम् + -पातः Cassia Fistula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भु|शंभु|शंभुः|शम्भुः
शम् + -भु see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् I. €4 P. (शाम्यति, शान्त)<BR>—1 To be calm, quiet or tranquil, be appeased or pacified (as a person);<BR> शाम्येत् प्रत्यपकारेण नोपकारेण दुर्जनः Ku. 2. 40; काकुत्स्थमुद्दिश्य<BR> समत्सरोऽपि शशाम तेन क्षितिपाललोकः R. 7. 3; शान्तो लवः U. 6. 7;<BR> Bh. 2. 75.<BR>—2 To cease, stop, come to an end; चिन्ता<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">Page1534-1</a>]<BR> शशाम सकलाऽपि सरोरुहाणाम् Bv. 3. 7; न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन<BR> शाम्यति Ms. 2. 94 ‘is not satisfied’.<BR>—3 To be quelled, be extinguished or quenched; शशाम वृष्टयापि विना<BR> दवाग्निः R. 2. 14; U. 5. 7.<BR>—4 To desist, leave off (speaking &c.).<BR>—5 To put an end to, destroy, kill (also €9 P. in this sense). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (शमयति-ते, but शामयतिते in the sense of ‘seeing’, see शम्<BR> II). —1 To appease, allay, calm, tranquillize, pacify, soothe; कः शीतलैः<BR> शमयिता वचनैस्तवाधिम् Bv. 3. 1; संरम्भं शमयामास R. 15. 85, 17. 55;<BR> Ś. 5. 7.<BR>—2 To put an end, to stop; वरेण शमितं लोकानलं दग्धुं हि तत्तपः Ku. 2. 56.<BR>—3 To remove, avert; प्रतिकूलं दैवं शमयितुम् Ś. 1.<BR>—4 To subdue, tame, defeat, conquer, vanquish; शमयति गजानन्यान् गन्धद्विपः<BR> कलभोऽपि सन् V. 5. 18; R. 9. 12, 11. 59.<BR>—5 To kill, destroy, slay; कर्णस्यात्मजमग्रतः शमयतः Ve. 5. 5.<BR>—6 To quench, extinguish; शमितकुरुवंशप्रसविता Pt. 4. 50; सुतप्तमपि<BR> पानीयं शमयत्येव पावकम् H. 1. 85; Me. 55.<BR>—7 To leave off, desist, cease. ━II. €10 U. (शामयति-ते)<BR>—1 To see, look at, inspect.<BR>—2 To show, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1533-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमः|शम
शमः [शम्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Quiet, tranquillity, calmness; धृतिं न विन्दामि शमं च विष्णो Bg. 11. 24.<BR>—2 Rest, calm, repose, cessation.<BR>—3 Absence or restraint of passions, mental quietness, quietism; शमरतेऽमरतेजसि<BR> पाथिंवे R. 9. 4; Ki. 10. 10, 16. 48; Śi. 2. 94; Bg. 10. 4.<BR>—4 Allayment, mitigation, alleviation, satisfaction, pacification (of<BR> grief, thirst, hunger &c.); शममुपयातु ममापि चित्तदाहः U. 6. 8;<BR> शममेष्यति मम शोकः कथं नु वत्से Ś. 4. 21.<BR>—5 Peace; as in अस्माकं शमकामा वै त्वं च पुत्रो ममेत्यथ Mb. 12. 1. 27;<BR> शमोपन्यास Ve. 5.<BR>—6 Final emancipation (from all worldly illusions and attachments).<BR>—7 The hand.<BR>—8 Cure of disease, convalescence.<BR>—9 Indifference, apathy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शमान्तकः, शमात्मक, शमोपन्यासः, शमपर, शमप्रधान, शमव्यसनिन्, शमशम<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमान्तकः|शमान्तक|शमांतक
शमः + -अन्तकः the god of love (a destroyer of mental tranquility).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमात्मक
शमः + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> calm, tranquil by nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमोपन्यासः|शमोपन्यास
शमः + -उपन्यासः overtures of peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमपर
शमः + -पर <i>a.</i> tranquil quiet, stoical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमप्रधान
शमः + -प्रधान <i>a.</i> in whom tranquillity or quietism predominates;<BR> शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु Ś. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमव्यसनिन्
शमः + -व्यसनिन् <i>a.</i> dissolute from indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमशम
शमः + -शम <i>a.</i> enjoying perpetual tranquillity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमथः|शमथ
शमथः [शम्-अथच्]<BR>—1 Tranquillity, calmness; especially mental calmness, absence of passion.<BR>—2 A counsellor, minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमन|शमनं|शमनः
शमन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शम् णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Quelling, allaying, subduing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनम्
शमन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Appeasing, allaying, soothing, conquering, alleviating, &c.<BR>—2 Calmness, tranquillity.<BR>—3 End, stop, cessation, destruction.<BR>—4 Hurting, injuring; destroying; सपत्नशमनम् Mb. 3. 85. 101.<BR>—5 Killing animals for sacrifice, immolation.<BR>—6 Swallowing, chewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनः|शमन|शमनं
शमन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A kind of deer, an antelope.<BR>—2 N. of Yama, the god of death; शतशस्तत्र यवनाः शमनातिथयोऽभवन्<BR> Śiva B. 14. 94.<BR>—3 A kind of pea.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शमनस्वसृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनस्वसृ
शमन + -स्वसृ <i>f.</i> ‘Yamaʼs sister’, epithet of the river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनी
शमनी Night.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शमनीसदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीसदः
शमनी + -सदः + ({@-षदः@}) a demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीषदः|शमनीषद
शमनी + -सदः + ({@-षदः@}) a demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीय
शमनीय <i>a.</i> Consolable, soothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनीयम्
शमनीय + .{@-यम्@} Sedative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमलम्
शमलम् [शम्-कलच् Uṇ. 1. 103]<BR>—1 Feces, ordure, excrement.<BR>—2 Impurity, sediment.<BR>—3 Sin, moral impurity; आशंसमानः शमलं गङ्गायां दुःखितोऽपतत्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 13. 32.<BR>—4 A calamity, misfortune. ━<i>a.</i> sinful; साध्व्यः कृताञ्जलिपुटाः शमलस्य<BR> भर्तुः Bhāg. 10. 16. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमाहः|शमाह
शमाहः A hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमित|शमितः
शमित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Appeased, allayed, soothed, calmed.<BR>—2 Alleviated, cured, relieved.<BR>—3 Relaxed.<BR>—4 Calm, sedate.<BR>—5 Moderated, tempered; अविभावितनिष्क्रमप्रयाणः शमितायाम इवातिरंहसा<BR> सः Ki. 13. 27.<BR>—6 Destroyed, killed; शमितकुरुवंशप्रसविता Pt. 4. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिता
शमित + .{@-ता@} Rice-powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमितृ
शमितृ <i>m.</i> A killer, slaughterer; यथाश्वमेधे पशवः शमित्रा Mb. 8. 84. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिन्
शमिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Calm, tranquil, pacific.<BR>—2 One who has subdued his passions, self-controlled; भ्रमी कदम्बसंभिन्नः<BR> पवनः शमिनामपि Bk. 7. 5; Mk. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमी
शमी [शम्-इन् वा ङीप्] (शमि sometimes)<BR>—1 N. of a tree (said to contain fire); अग्निगर्भां शमीमिव Ś. 4. 3;<BR> Ms. 8. 247; ध्रुवं स नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया शमीलतां छेत्तुमृषिर्व्यवस्यति<BR> Ś. 1. 18; Y. 1. 302.<BR>—2 A pod, legume.<BR>—3 A particular measure.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शमीकुणः, शमीगर्भः, शमीधान्यम्, शमीरोहः, शमीपत्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीकुणः|शमीकुण
शमी + -कुणः the time when the Śamī tree bears fruit; P. V. 2. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीगर्भः|शमीगर्भ
शमी + -गर्भः<BR>—1 an epithet of fire.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa, one belonging to the sacerdotal or priestly class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीधान्यम्
शमी + -धान्यम् any pulse or grain growing in pods, leguminous grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीरोहः
शमी + -रोहः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीपत्री
शमी + -पत्री Mimosa Pudica, a kind of sensitive plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीरः|शमीर
शमी(मि)रः A small variety of the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिरः|शमिर
शमी(मि)रः A small variety of the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्पा|शंपा
शम्पा [शम्-प Uṇ. 3. 28]<BR>—1 Lightning.<BR>—2 A girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्फली
शम्फली, शम्बली, शम्भली A procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बली
शम्फली, शम्बली, शम्भली A procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भली|शंभली
शम्फली, शम्बली, शम्भली A procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब्|शंब्
शम्ब् I. €1 P. (शम्बति) To go, move. ━II. €10 P. (शम्बयति)<BR> To collect, heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्ब|शंब|शम्बः
शम्ब(म्भ) <i>a.</i> [शम्ब् अच्]<BR>—1 Happy, fortunate.<BR>—2 Poor, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भ|शंभ|शंभः|शम्भः
शम्ब(म्भ) <i>a.</i> [शम्ब् अच्]<BR>—1 Happy, fortunate.<BR>—2 Poor, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बः|शम्ब|शंब
शम्ब(म्भ) + .{@-म्बः@},<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्भः|शम्भ|शंभ|शंभः
शम्ब(म्भ) + .{@-म्बः@} + .({@-म्भः@})<BR>—1 The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—2 The iron head of a pestle.<BR>—3 An iron chain worn round the loins.<BR>—4 Ploughing ‘with the grain’ or in the regular direction.<BR>—5 The second ploughing of a field.<BR>—6 A particular measure of length. (शम्बाकृ means ‘to plough twice’;<BR> त्वया शम्बाकृतं क्षतम् N. 20. 83, doubly pierced).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शम्बपाणिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बपाणिः
शम्ब + -पाणिः N. of Indra (having a thunderbolt in his hand); कण्ठेकालेन<BR> कैलासः स मेरुः शम्बपाणिना Śiva B. 16. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बर|शंबर|शम्बरं|शम्बरः
शम्बर <i>a.</i> [शम्ब् अरच्] Best, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बरः|शम्बर|शंबर|शम्बरं
शम्बर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 N. of a demon slain by Pradyumna, q. v.<BR>—2 A mountain.<BR>—3 A kind of deer.<BR>—4 A Jina.<BR>—5 N. of the trees चित्रक, लोध्र and अर्जुन.<BR>—6 A kind of fish.<BR>—7 War.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्बरम्
शम्बर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Water; किं विलम्बसे … शम्बरानयने Cola-Campū. p. 26.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR>—3 Wealth.<BR>—4 A rite or religious observance.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1535-1" target="_blank">Page1535-1</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शम्बरारिः, शम्बरसूदनः, शम्बरासुरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1534-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

