शशः|शश
शशः —1 A hare, rabbit; Ms. 3. 270, 5. 18.<BR>—2 The spots on the moon (which are popularly considered to resemble the<BR> form of a hare).<BR>—3 One of the four classes into which men are divided by erotic writers;<BR> thus defined:− मृदुवचनसुशीलः कोमलाङ्गः सुकेशः सकलगुणनिधानं<BR> सत्यवादी शशोऽयम् Śabdak.; see Ratimañjarī 35 also.<BR>—4 The Lodhra tree.<BR>—5 Gum-myrrh. —6 An antelope.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शशाङ्कः, शशलेखा, शशादः, शशादनः, शशोर्णम्, शशलोमन्, शशधरः, शशपदम्, शशप्लुतकम्, शशभृत्, शशरजस्, शशलक्ष्मणः, शशलाञ्छनः, शशबिन्दुः, शशविन्दुः, शशविषाणम्, शशशृङ्गम्, शशस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशाङ्कः|शशाङ्क|शशांक
शशः + -अङ्कः<BR>—1 the moon; रामाभिधानमपरं जगतः शशाङ्कम् Pratimā 4. 1.<BR>—2 camphor. ˚अर्धमुख <i>a.</i> crescent-headed (as an arrow). ˚मूर्तिः<BR> an epithet of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशलेखा
शशः + -लेखा the digit of the moon, lunar crescent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशादः|शशाद
शशः + -अदः<BR>—1 a hawk, falcon.<BR>—2 N. of a son of Ikṣvāku, father of पुरंजय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

