शशिन् + -लेखा<BR>—1 a digit of the moon.<BR>—2 N. of various plants (Mar. बांवची, काळें जिरें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिवाटिका
शशिन् + -वाटिका Boerhavia Procumbens (पुनर्नवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिनी
शशिनी N. of one of the sixteen digits of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वत्|शश्वन्त्
शश्वत् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Perpetually, eternally, for ever.<BR>—2 Constantly, repeatedly, always, frequently, again and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">Page1540-2</a>]<BR> again; जीवन् पुनः शश्वदुपप्लवेभ्यः (पासि) R. 2. 48, 4. 70;<BR> Mu. 3. 19; Bhāg. 10. 73. 14; Me. 57. (In comp. शश्वत् may be translated<BR> by ‘lasting, eternal’; as शश्वच्छान्ति eternal tranquillity.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्
शष् €1 P. (शषति) To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्कुली
शष्कु(स्कु)ली<BR>—1 The orifice of the ear, auditory passage; तथापि कर्णशष्कुल्यवच्छिन्नः<BR> सन् (आकाशः) शब्दग्राहकश्रोत्रेन्द्रियात्मकः Tarka K.; अवलम्बितकर्णशष्कुलीकलसीकं<BR> रचयन्नवोचत N. 2. 8; Y. 3. 96.<BR>—2 A kind of baked cake; संयावापूपशष्कुल्यः सर्वदोहश्च गृह्यताम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 24. 26; Y. 1. 173; Gaṇeśa P. 49 (verses 47-51).<BR>—3 Rice-gruel.<BR>—4 A disease of the ear.<BR>—5 A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्कुली
शष्कु(स्कु)ली<BR>—1 The orifice of the ear, auditory passage; तथापि कर्णशष्कुल्यवच्छिन्नः<BR> सन् (आकाशः) शब्दग्राहकश्रोत्रेन्द्रियात्मकः Tarka K.; अवलम्बितकर्णशष्कुलीकलसीकं<BR> रचयन्नवोचत N. 2. 8; Y. 3. 96.<BR>—2 A kind of baked cake; संयावापूपशष्कुल्यः सर्वदोहश्च गृह्यताम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 24. 26; Y. 1. 173; Gaṇeśa P. 49 (verses 47-51).<BR>—3 Rice-gruel.<BR>—4 A disease of the ear.<BR>—5 A sort of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पः|शष्प|शष्पं
शष्पः(स्पः) Loss of intellect or presence of mind (प्रतिभाक्षय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्पः|शस्प|शस्पं
शष्पः(स्पः) Loss of intellect or presence of mind (प्रतिभाक्षय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पम्
शष्पः(स्पः) + .{@-ष्पम्@} Young grass; शष्पाण्यात्ति U. 4. 26; गङ्गाप्रपातान्तनिरूढशष्पम्<BR> (गह्वरम्) R. 2. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शष्पबृसी, शष्पभुज्, शष्पभोजनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पबृसी
शष्पः + -बृसी a seat of Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पभुज्
शष्पः + -भुज्, -भोजनः a grass-eater, animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पभोजनः|शष्पभोजन
शष्पः + -भुज्, -भोजनः a grass-eater, animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् I. €1 P. (शसति) To cut up, kill, destroy. ━II. €2 P. (शस्ति)<BR> To sleep. Cf. शंस् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसनम्
शसनम् [शस्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Wounding, killing.<BR>—2 Immolation (of an animal at sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
शस्त <i>p. p.</i> [शंस्-क्त]<BR>—1 Praised, extolled.<BR>—2 Auspicious, happy; शस्ताः कुर्वन्ति मां सव्यं दक्षिणं पशवोऽपरे<BR> Bhāg. 1. 14. 13.<BR>—3 Right, best.<BR>—4 Repeated, recited.<BR>—5 Best, excellent.<BR>—6 Wounded, injured.<BR>—7 Killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तम्
शस्त + .{@-स्तम्@}<BR>—1 Happiness, welfare.<BR>—2 Excellence, auspiciousness.<BR>—3 The body.<BR>—4 A finger-guard (अङ्गुलित्राण q. v.; also शस्तकम् in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तः|शस्त|शस्तं
शस्त + .{@-स्तः@} A murderer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तिः|शस्ति
शस्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Praise, eulogy.<BR>—2 A hymn of praise (स्तोत्र).<BR>—3 A finger-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस्<BR>—1 A technical name for the termination of the acc. plural.<BR>—2 A Taddhita affix forming adverbs from nouns, especially from numerals;<BR> as द्विशः, शतशः, बहुशः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रम्
शस्त्रम् [शस्-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>—1 A weapon, arms; क्षमाशस्त्रं करे यस्य दुर्जनः किं करिष्यति<BR> Subhāṣ.; R. 2. 40, 3. 51, 62, 5. 28.<BR>—2 An instrument, a tool in general.<BR>—3 Iron; गृहीतशस्त्राः क्रोशन्ति चर्मिणो वाजिपृष्ठगाः Mb. 6. 2. 29.<BR>—4 Steel.<BR>—5 A hymn of praise (स्तोत्र).<BR>—6 Repetition, recitation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शस्त्राङ्गा, शस्त्राभ्यासः, शस्त्रायसम्, शस्त्रावपातः, शस्त्रास्त्रम्, शस्त्राख्यम्, शस्त्राजीवः, शस्त्रोपजीविन्, शस्त्रोद्यमः, शस्त्रोपकरणम्, शस्त्रकर्मन्, शस्त्रकारः, शस्त्रकोपः, शस्त्रकोषः, शस्त्रक्षारः, शस्त्रग्रहः, शस्त्रग्राहिन्, शस्त्रचिकित्सा, शस्त्रजीविन्, शस्त्रवृत्ति, शस्त्रदेवता, शस्त्रधरः, शस्त्रनिपातनम्, शस्त्रन्यासः, शस्त्रपाणि, शस्त्रपदम्, शस्त्रपूत, शस्त्रप्रहारः, शस्त्रभृत्, शस्त्रमार्जः, शस्त्रविद्या, शस्त्रशास्त्रम्, शस्त्रवृत्तिः, शस्त्रव्यवहारः, शस्त्रशास्त्रम्, शस्त्रसंहतिः, शस्त्रसंपातः, शस्त्रहत, शस्त्रहस्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राङ्गा
शस्त्रम् + -अङ्गा a kind of sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राभ्यासः|शस्त्राभ्यास
शस्त्रम् + -अभ्यासः the practice of arms, military exercise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रायसम्
शस्त्रम् + -अयसम्<BR>—1 steel.<BR>—2 iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रावपातः|शस्त्रावपात
शस्त्रम् + -अवपातः injury by weapon; शस्त्रावपाते गर्भस्य पातने चोत्तमो<BR> दमः Y. 2. 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रास्त्रम्
शस्त्रम् + -अस्त्रम्<BR>—1 weapons for striking and throwing, arms and missiles; शस्त्रास्त्रमृत्त्वं<BR> क्षत्रस्य Ms. 10. 79.<BR>—2 arms or weapons generally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राख्यम्
शस्त्रम् + -आख्यम् iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्राजीवः|शस्त्राजीव
शस्त्रम् + -आजीवः, -उपजीविन् <i>m.</i> a professional soldier; Kau. A. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोपजीविन्
शस्त्रम् + -आजीवः, -उपजीविन् <i>m.</i> a professional soldier; Kau. A. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोद्यमः|शस्त्रोद्यम
शस्त्रम् + -उद्यमः lifting up a weapon (to strike).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रोपकरणम्
शस्त्रम् + -उपकरणम् arms or instruments of war, military apparatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकर्मन्
शस्त्रम् + -कर्मन् any surgical operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकारः|शस्त्रकार
शस्त्रम् + -कारः an armourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकोपः|शस्त्रकोप
शस्त्रम् + -कोपः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">Page1541-1</a>]<BR> war, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1540-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकोषः|शस्त्रकोष
शस्त्रम् + -कोषः the sheath or scabbard of any weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रक्षारः|शस्त्रक्षार
शस्त्रम् + -क्षारः borax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रग्रहः|शस्त्रग्रह
शस्त्रम् + -ग्रहः battle, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रग्राहिन्
शस्त्रम् + -ग्राहिन् <i>a.</i> taking up or wearing arms (for battle); शस्त्रग्राही<BR> ब्राह्मणो जामदग्न्यः U. 5. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रचिकित्सा
शस्त्रम् + -चिकित्सा surgery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रजीविन्
शस्त्रम् + -जीविन्, -वृत्ति <i>m.</i> one living by the use of arms, a professonal soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रवृत्ति|शस्त्रवृत्तिः
शस्त्रम् + -जीविन्, -वृत्ति <i>m.</i> one living by the use of arms, a professonal soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रदेवता
शस्त्रम् + -देवता the deity presiding over weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रधरः|शस्त्रधर
शस्त्रम् + -धरः = शस्त्रभृत् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रनिपातनम्
शस्त्रम् + -निपातनम् a surgical operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रन्यासः|शस्त्रन्यास
शस्त्रम् + -न्यासः laying down arms; so शस्त्र (परि) त्यागः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपाणि|शस्त्रपाणिः
शस्त्रम् + -पाणि <i>a.</i> bearing arms, armed. ━(<i>m.</i>) an armed warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपदम्
शस्त्रम् + -पदम् incision; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रपूत
शस्त्रम् + -पूत <i>a.</i> ‘purified by arms’, rendered pure or absolved from<BR> guilt by being killed with a weapon on the battle-field; अशस्त्रपूतं<BR> निर्व्याजम् (महामांसम्) Māl. 5. 12; (see Jagaddharaʼs explanation<BR> of the word); अहमपि तस्य मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञावैलक्ष्यसंपादितमशस्त्रपूतं<BR> मरणमुपदिशामि Ve. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रप्रहारः|शस्त्रप्रहार
शस्त्रम् + -प्रहारः a wound inflicted with a weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रभृत्
शस्त्रम् + -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a soldier, warrior; रामः शस्त्रभृतामहम् Bg. 10. 31; न तद्<BR> यशः शस्त्रभृतां क्षिणोति R. 2. 40.<BR>—2 an armed man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रमार्जः|शस्त्रमार्ज|शस्त्रमार्ज्ज
शस्त्रम् + -मार्जः a weapon-cleaner, an armourer, a furbisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रविद्या
शस्त्रम् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम् the science of archery, see धनुर्वेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रशास्त्रम्
शस्त्रम् + -विद्या, -शास्त्रम् the science of archery, see धनुर्वेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रवृत्तिः|शस्त्रवृत्ति
शस्त्रम् + -वृत्तिः a professional soldier; पुरुषाः शस्त्रवृत्तयः Ms. 12. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रव्यवहारः|शस्त्रव्यवहार
शस्त्रम् + -व्यवहारः practice of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रशास्त्रम्
शस्त्रम् + -शास्त्रम् military science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसंहतिः|शस्त्रसंहति
शस्त्रम् + -संहतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a collection of arms.<BR>—2 an arsenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रसंपातः|शस्त्रसम्पात
शस्त्रम् + -संपातः a sudden fall of a number of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहत|शस्त्रहतः
शस्त्रम् + -हत <i>a.</i> killed by a weapon. ˚चतुर्दशी N. of a particular 14th<BR> day sacred to the memory of fallen warriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहस्त|शस्त्रहस्तः
शस्त्रम् + -हस्त <i>a.</i> armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रहस्तः|शस्त्रहस्त
शस्त्रम् + -हस्त + .({@-स्तः@}) an armed man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकम्
शस्त्रकम्<BR>—1 Steel.<BR>—2 Iron.<BR>—3 An instrument, a tool, weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिका
शस्त्रिका A knife, dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिन्
शस्त्रिन् <i>a.</i> Bearing arms or weapons, armed, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्री
शस्त्री A knife; पण्यस्त्रीषु विवेककल्पलतिकाशस्त्रीषु रज्येत कः<BR> Subhāṣ.; शस्त्रीश्यामैरंशुभिराशु द्रुतम् Śi. 4. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
शस्य <i>a.</i> (from शंस्)<BR>—1 Best, excellent.<BR>—2 Praiseworthy, laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्या
शस्य + .{@-स्या@} a ऋक् which is to be recited; योनिश्चासौ शस्या च योनिशस्या<BR> ŚB. on MS. 7. 2. 17; पुरोनुवाक्या च याज्या च शस्यैव तृतीया Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यम्
शस्यम् [शस्-यत्]<BR>—1 Corn or grain in general; दुदोह गां स यज्ञाय शस्याय मघवा दिवम् R. 1. 26.<BR>—2 The produce or fruit of a plant or tree; शस्यं क्षेत्रगतं प्राहुः<BR> सतुषं धान्यमुच्यते; see तण्डुल also.<BR>—3 A merit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शस्यक्षेत्रम्, शस्यभक्षक, शस्यमञ्जरी, शस्यमालिन्, शस्यशालिन्, शस्यसंपन्न, शस्यशूकम्, शस्यसंपद्, शस्यसम्बरः, शस्यसम्वरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यक्षेत्रम्
शस्यम् + -क्षेत्रम् a corn-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यभक्षक
शस्यम् + -भक्षक <i>a.</i> granivorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यमञ्जरी|शस्यमंजरी
शस्यम् + -मञ्जरी<BR>—1 an ear of corn.<BR>—2 a fruit-stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यमालिन्
शस्यम् + -मालिन् <i>a.</i> crowned with harvests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यशालिन्
शस्यम् + -शालिन्, -संपन्न <i>a.</i> abounding in corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यसंपन्न
शस्यम् + -शालिन्, -संपन्न <i>a.</i> abounding in corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यशूकम्
शस्यम् + -शूकम् a beard of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यसंपद्
शस्यम् + -संपद् <i>f.</i> abundance of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यसम्बरः|शस्यसम्बर|शस्यसंबर
शस्यम् + -सम्बरः, -सम्वरः the Śāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यसम्वरः
शस्यम् + -सम्बरः, -सम्वरः the Śāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकः|शाक|शाकं
शाकः, -कम्<BR> [शक्-घञ्] A vegetable, pot-herb, herb, any edible leaf,<BR> fruit or root used as a vegetable; दिल्लीश्वरो वा जगदीश्वरो वा मनोरथान्<BR> पूरयितुं समर्थः । अन्यैर्नृपालैः परिदीयमानं शाकाय वा स्याल्लवणाय<BR> वा स्यात् Jag.; वेत्रशाककुजे शैले<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">Page1541-2</a>]<BR> Ki. 15. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकम्
शाकः, -कम्<BR> [शक्-घञ्] A vegetable, pot-herb, herb, any edible leaf,<BR> fruit or root used as a vegetable; दिल्लीश्वरो वा जगदीश्वरो वा मनोरथान्<BR> पूरयितुं समर्थः । अन्यैर्नृपालैः परिदीयमानं शाकाय वा स्याल्लवणाय<BR> वा स्यात् Jag.; वेत्रशाककुजे शैले<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">Page1541-2</a>]<BR> Ki. 15. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकः|शाक|शाकं
शाकः, -कम् + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Power, strength, energy.<BR>—2 The teak tree.<BR>—3 The Śirīṣa tree; यस्मिन् शाको नाम महीरुहः Bhāg. 5. 20. 24.<BR>—4 N. of a people; see शक.<BR>—5 An era; especially the era of Śālivāhana.<BR>—6 N. of the sixth Dvīpa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाकाङ्गम्, शाकाम्लम्, शाकाष्टमी, शाकाख्यः, शाकाहारः, शाककलम्बकः, शाकचुक्रिका, शाकतरुः, शाकपणः, शाकपत्रः, शाकपात्रम्, शाकपार्थिवः, शाकप्रति, शाकयोग्यः, शाकरसः, शाकराज्, शाकराजः, शाकविन्दकः, शाकवृक्षः, शाकव्रतम्, शाकशाकटम्, शाकशाकिनम्, शाकश्रेष्ठा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाङ्गम्
शाकः + -अङ्गम् pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाम्लम्
शाकः + -अम्लम् hog-plum. ˚भेदनम् sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाष्टमी
शाकः + -अष्टमी the 8th day of the dark half of फाल्गुन (on which<BR> vegetables are offered to पितृs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाख्यः|शाकाख्य|शाकाख्यं
शाकः + -आख्यः the teak tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाख्यम्
शाकः + -आख्यः + .({@-ख्यम्@}) a vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकाहारः|शाकाहार
शाकः + -आहारः a vegetarian (living only on herbs &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाककलम्बकः|शाककलम्बक
शाकः + -कलम्बकः leek, garlic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकचुक्रिका
शाकः + -चुक्रिका the tamarind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकतरुः|शाकतरु
शाकः + -तरुः the teak tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपणः|शाकपण
शाकः + -पणः<BR>—1 a measure equal to a handful.<BR>—2 a handful of vegetables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपत्रः|शाकपत्र
शाकः + -पत्रः the <i>Śigru</i> tree (Mar. शेवगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपात्रम्
शाकः + -पात्रम् a vegetable dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपार्थिवः|शाकपार्थिव
शाकः + -पार्थिवः a king fond of an era; see मध्यमपदलोपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकप्रति
शाकः + -प्रति <i>ind.</i> a little of herbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकयोग्यः|शाकयोग्य
शाकः + -योग्यः coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकरसः|शाकरस
शाकः + -रसः edible vegetable juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकराज्
शाकः + -राज्, -राजः Chenododium (Mar. चाकवत); also शाकवीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकराजः|शाकराज
शाकः + -राज्, -राजः Chenododium (Mar. चाकवत); also शाकवीर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकविन्दकः|शाकविन्दक
शाकः + -विन्दकः see बिल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकवृक्षः|शाकवृक्ष
शाकः + -वृक्षः the teak tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकव्रतम्
शाकः + -व्रतम् a vow of abstinence from vegetables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकटम्
शाकः + -शाकटम्, -शाकिनम् a field of vegetables, a kitchen-garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकशाकिनम्
शाकः + -शाकटम्, -शाकिनम् a field of vegetables, a kitchen-garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकश्रेष्ठा
शाकः + -श्रेष्ठा the egg-plant (Mar. वांर्गें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

