शाकटी
शाकट <i>a.</i>^1 .<BR>—1 Relating to a cart.<BR>—2 Going in a cart.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174. note: content of 31802.001 (SAkawI) merged into SAkawa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटी
शाकट + ({@-टी@} <i>f.</i>) [शकटाय हितम् अण्]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटः|शाकट|शाकटं
शाकट + .{@-टः@}<BR>—1 A draught-ox.<BR>—2 The tree called श्लेष्मातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटम्
शाकट + .{@-टम्@} A field; cf. शाकशाकट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटायनः|शाकटायन
शाकटायनः N. of a philologist and grammarian often referred to<BR> by Pāṇini and Yāska; cf. व्याकरणे शकटस्य च तोकम् Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटिक|शाकटिकः
शाकटिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to a car.<BR>—2 Going in a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटिकः|शाकटिक
शाकटिक + .{@-कः@} A carter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटीनः|शाकटीन
शाकटीनः A cart-load, a measure of load equal to 20 <i>tulās</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपूणिः|शाकपूणि
शाकपूणिः, -र्णिः<BR> N. of an ancient expounder of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकपूर्णिः|शाकपूर्णि
शाकपूणिः, -र्णिः<BR> N. of an ancient expounder of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकरी
शाकरी = शाकारी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकंभरी|शाकम्भरी
शाकंभरी<BR>—1 An epithet of Durgā; ततो गच्छेत राजेन्द्र देव्याः स्थानं सुदुर्लभम् ।<BR> शाकंभरीति विख्याता त्रिषु लोकेषु विश्रुता ॥ Mb. 3. 84. 13.<BR>—2 N. of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकल|शाकलः
शाकल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शकल-अन्]<BR>—1 Relating to a piece (शकल).<BR>—2 Relating, belonging to or derived from the शाकलs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलः|शाकल
शाकल + .{@-लः@} A school of the Ṛgveda or the followers of this school (pl.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलम्
शाकल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 A brown variety of sandal; शाकलं कपिलमिति Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR>—2 A chip, piece.<BR>—3 The text or ritual of शाकल्य.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाकलप्रातिशाख्यम्, शाकलशाखा, शाकलहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलप्रातिशाख्यम्
शाकल + -प्रातिशाख्यम् N. of the Ṛgveda Prātiśākhya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलशाखा
शाकल + -शाखा the recension or traditional text of the Ṛgveda as represented<BR> by the Śākalas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलहोमः|शाकलहोम
शाकल + -होमः a particular kind of oblation; मन्त्रैः शाकलहोमीयैरब्दं<BR> हुत्वा घृतं द्विजः Ms. 11. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकलिक|शाकलिकः
शाकलिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to a piece, fragmentary.<BR>—2 Relating to शाकल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1541-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकल्यः|शाकल्य
शाकल्यः N. of an ancient grammarian mentioned by Pāṇini; (he is<BR> supposed to have arranged the <i>Pada</i> text of the Ṛgveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकारी
शाकारी One of the lowest forms of Prākṛta, the dialect spoken<BR> by the Śakas or Śakāra, as in the Mṛcchakaṭika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिनम्
शाकिनम् A field; as in शाकशाकिनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकिनी
शाकिनी [शाकमस्त्यस्या इनि]<BR>—1 A field of vegetables.<BR>—2 A kind of female being attendant on Durgā (supposed to be a demon or fairy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुण|शाकुणः
शाकुण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Repentent.<BR>—2 Afflicting others (परतापक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन|शाकुनः
शाकुन (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शकुन-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to birds; शाकुनेनाथ पञ्च वै (पितरः प्रीयन्ते) Ms. 3. 268.<BR>—2 Relating to omens.<BR>—3 Ominous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिकः|शाकुनिक
शाकुनिकः [शकुनेन पक्षिवधादिना जीवति ठञ्] A fowler, bird-catcher;<BR> Mk. 6; Ms. 8. 260.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिकम्
शाकुनिकः + .{@-कम्@} The interpretation of omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनेयः|शाकुनेय
शाकुनेयः A small owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुनिन्
शाकुनिन् <i>m.</i> A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तलः|शाकुन्तल|शाकुंतल|शाकुंतलः
शाकुन्तलः, -शाकुन्तलेयः<BR> A metronymic of Bharata (son of Śakuntalā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तलेयः|शाकुन्तलेय|शाकुंतलेयः
शाकुन्तलः, -शाकुन्तलेयः<BR> A metronymic of Bharata (son of Śakuntalā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तलम्
शाकुन्तलः, -शाकुन्तलेयः + .{@-लम्@} The drama called अभिज्ञानशकुन्तला of Kālidāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुन्तिकः|शाकुन्तिक
शाकुन्तिकः A fowler, bird-catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुल
शाकुल, शाकुलिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to fish; सप्त वै शाकुलेन<BR> तु (मासान् पितरः प्रीयन्ते) Mb. 13. 88. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुलिक|शाकुलिकः
शाकुल, शाकुलिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to fish; सप्त वै शाकुलेन<BR> तु (मासान् पितरः प्रीयन्ते) Mb. 13. 88. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकुलिकः|शाकुलिक
शाकुलिकः A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्करः|शाक्कर
शाक्करः An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्की
शाक्की N. of one of the five विभाषाs or corrupt dialects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त|शाक्तः
शाक्त <i>a.</i> (-क्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शक्तिर्देवताऽस्य अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to power.<BR>—2 Relating to <i>Śakti</i> or the female personification of divine energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तः|शाक्त
शाक्त + .{@-क्तः@} A worshipper of <i>Śakti</i>; (the <i>Śāktas</i> are generally<BR> worshippers of Durgā representing the female personification of divine<BR> energy, and the ritual enjoined to them is of two kinds, the pure or right<BR> hand ritual दक्षिणाचार, and impure or left-hand ritual वामाचार qq. vv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तिकः|शाक्तिक
शाक्तिकः<BR>—1 A worshipper of <i>Śakti</i>.<BR>—2 A spearman, lancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तीकः|शाक्तीक
शाक्तीकः A spearman, lancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्तेयः|शाक्तेय
शाक्तेयः, शाक्त्यः<BR>—1 A worshipper of <i>Śakti</i>.<BR>—2 N. of Parāśara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्त्यः|शाक्त्य
शाक्तेयः, शाक्त्यः<BR>—1 A worshipper of <i>Śakti</i>.<BR>—2 N. of Parāśara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यः|शाक्य
शाक्यः [शक्-घञ् तत्र साधुः यत्]<BR>—1 N. of the family of Buddha.<BR>—2 N. of Buddha.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाक्यपुत्रीयः, शाक्यभिक्षुः, शाक्यभिक्षुकः, शाक्यमुनिः, शाक्यसिंहः, शाक्यशासनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यपुत्रीयः|शाक्यपुत्रीय
शाक्यः + -पुत्रीयः a Buddhist<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">Page1542-2</a>]<BR> monk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यभिक्षुः|शाक्यभिक्षु
शाक्यः + -भिक्षुः, -भिक्षुकः a Buddhist religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यभिक्षुकः|शाक्यभिक्षुक
शाक्यः + -भिक्षुः, -भिक्षुकः a Buddhist religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यमुनिः|शाक्यमुनि
शाक्यः + -मुनिः, -सिंहः epithets of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यसिंहः|शाक्यसिंह
शाक्यः + -मुनिः, -सिंहः epithets of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्यशासनम्
शाक्यः + -शासनम् the doctrine of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्र
शाक्र <i>a.</i> Relating or belonging to Indra; प्रादुश्चक्रे ततः<BR> पार्थः शाक्रमस्त्रं महारथः Mb. 7. 93. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्रम्
शाक्र + .{@-क्रम्@} The ज्येष्ठा Nakṣatra (presided over by Indra).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाक्रदिश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्रदिश्
शाक्र + -दिश् the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्री
शाक्री<BR>—1 N. of Śachī, wife of Indra.<BR>—2 Of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाक्वरः|शाक्वर
शाक्वरः An ox; cf. शाक्कर; Hc. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाख्
शाख् €1 P. (शाखति) To pervade, fill completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखः|शाख
शाखः N. of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखा
शाखा —1 A branch (as of a tree); आवर्ज्य शाखाः R. 16. 19.<BR>—2 An arm.<BR>—3 A party, section, faction.<BR>—4 A part or subdivision of a work.<BR>—5 A school, branch, sect.<BR>—6 A part or division of an animal.<BR>—7 A school or traditional recension of the Veda, the traditional text<BR> followed by a school; as in शाकलशाखा, आश्वलायनशाखा, बाष्कलशाखा &c.<BR>—8 A branch of any science.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाखाध्येतृ, शाखान्तग, शाखाचङ्क्रमणम्, शाखाचन्द्रन्यायः, शाखानगरम्, शाखापुरम्, शाखापित्तम्, शाखाबाहुः, शाखाभृत्, शाखाभेदः, शाखामृगः, शाखारण्डः, शाखारथ्या, शाखावातः, शाखाविलीन, शाखाशिफा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाध्येतृ
शाखा + -अध्येतृ a follower of any particular text of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखान्तग
शाखा + -अन्तग <i>a.</i> one who has finished one शाखा; Ms. 3. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाचङ्क्रमणम्
शाखा + -चङ्क्रमणम् ‘leaping from branch to branch’, irregular study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाचन्द्रन्यायः|शाखाचन्द्रन्याय|शाखाचंद्रन्याय
शाखा + -चन्द्रन्यायः see under न्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखानगरम्
शाखा + -नगरम्, -पुरम् a suburb; प्रवेशयेच्च तान् सर्वान् शाखानगरकेष्वपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखापुरम्
शाखा + -नगरम्, -पुरम् a suburb; प्रवेशयेच्च तान् सर्वान् शाखानगरकेष्वपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखापित्तम्
शाखा + -पित्तम् inflammation of the extremities of the body, <i>e. g.</i><BR> hands, shoulders &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाबाहुः|शाखाबाहु
शाखा + -बाहुः a branch-like arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाभृत्
शाखा + -भृत् <i>m.</i> a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाभेदः|शाखाभेद
शाखा + -भेदः difference of (Vedic) school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखामृगः|शाखामृग
शाखा + -मृगः<BR>—1 a monkey, an ape; एतां दृष्ट्वा स्त्रियो मेऽन्या यथा शाखामृगस्त्रियः Mb. 3. 267. 3.<BR>—2 a squirrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखारण्डः|शाखारण्ड|शाखारंड
शाखा + -रण्डः ‘a traitor to his Śākhā’, a Brāhmaṇa who has changed<BR> his own school of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखारथ्या
शाखा + -रथ्या a branch-road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखावातः|शाखावात
शाखा + -वातः pain in the limbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाविलीन
शाखा + -विलीन <i>a.</i> sitting on branches (as a bird).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखाशिफा
शाखा + -शिफा a root growing from a branch (as of the fig-tree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखालः|शाखाल
शाखालः A sort of cane (वानीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखिन्
शाखिन् <i>a.</i> [शाखा अस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Having branches (fig. also).<BR>—2 Branching, ramifying.<BR>—3 Belonging to any branch or school (as of the Veda). ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A tree; कुल्याम्भोभिः पवनचपलैः शाखिनो धौतमूलाः Ś. 1. 15.<BR>—2 A Veda.<BR>—3 A follower of any Vedic school or recension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखीय
शाखीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to a school of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखोटः|शाखोट
शाखोटः, शाखोटकः N. of a tree; Trophis Aspera (Mar. हेदी);<BR> कस्त्वं भो कथयामि दैवहतकं मां विद्धि शाखोटकम् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाखोटकः|शाखोटक
शाखोटः, शाखोटकः N. of a tree; Trophis Aspera (Mar. हेदी);<BR> कस्त्वं भो कथयामि दैवहतकं मां विद्धि शाखोटकम् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्करः|शाङ्कर|शांकर|शाङ्करं|शांकरः
शाङ्करः<BR>—1 A bull.<BR>—2 A Śaivaite, a devotee of Śaṃkara; प्रतोषिताश्च शाङ्कराः Cola-Campū. p. 24, verse 59.<BR>—3 A follower of Śāṃkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्करिः|शाङ्करि|शांकरि|शांकरिः
शाङ्करिः<BR>—1 N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>—2 Of Gaṇeśa.<BR>—3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1542-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्कुची
शाङ्कुची The skate fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खम्
शाङ्खम् The sound of a conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खिकः|शाङ्खिक|शांखिक|शांखिकः
शाङ्खिकः [शङ्ख-ठञ्]<BR>—1 A shell-cutter, worker in shells.<BR>—2 N. of a mixed tribe.<BR>—3 A shell-blower; त्वरमाणशाङ्खिकसवेगवदनपवनाभिपूरितः Śi. 15. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाङ्खायनः|शाङ्खायन
शाङ्खायनः N. of a Vedic teacher (author of a Brāhmaṇa and two Sūtras).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाचि
शाचि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Distinguished, renowned.<BR>—2 Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटः|शाट
शाटः, शाटी<BR>—1 A garment, cloth; यस्मिन्नोतमिदं प्रोतं विश्वं शाटीव तन्तुषु Bhāg. 9. 9. 7.<BR>—2 A petticoat. —3 A particular female garment; स्फुरत् काच्ची शाटी पृथुकटितटे<BR> हाटकमयी Ā. L. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटी
शाटः, शाटी<BR>—1 A garment, cloth; यस्मिन्नोतमिदं प्रोतं विश्वं शाटीव तन्तुषु Bhāg. 9. 9. 7.<BR>—2 A petticoat. —3 A particular female garment; स्फुरत् काच्ची शाटी पृथुकटितटे<BR> हाटकमयी Ā. L. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटकः|शाटक|शाटकं
शाटकः, -कम्<BR> Cloth, garment, petticoat; रक्तोऽभिजायते भोग्यो नारीणां<BR> शाटको यथा Pt. 1. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाटकम्
शाटकः, -कम्<BR> Cloth, garment, petticoat; रक्तोऽभिजायते भोग्यो नारीणां<BR> शाटको यथा Pt. 1. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्यायनम्
शाट्यायनम् An oblation for remedying anything wrong in the performance of a rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाट्यायनः|शाट्यायन|शाट्यायनं
शाट्यायनम् + .{@-नः@} N. of a teacher and author of various works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाठ्यम्
शाठ्यम् [शठस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Dishonesty, perfidy, guile; trickery, fraud, villainy; आजन्मनः<BR> शाठ्यमशिक्षितो यः Ś. 5. 25; दाक्षिण्यं स्वजने दया परजने शाठ्यं<BR> सदा दुर्जने Bh. 2. 22.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Art, skill, cunning; देव्या निह्नोतुमिच्छेरिति सुरसरितं शाठ्यमव्याद्विभोर्वः Mu. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाड्
शाड् €1 Ā. To praise, extol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शणेन निर्वृत्तम् अण्] Hempen, flaxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणः|शाण|शाणं
शाण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A touch-stone; मणिः शाणोल्लीढः Bh. 2. 44; Bv. 1. 73.<BR>—2 A whetstone.<BR>—3 A saw.<BR>—4 A weight of four Māṣas; अष्टौ शाणाः शतमानं वहन्ति Mb. 3. 134. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणम्
शाण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Sack-cloth, coarse cloth.<BR>—2 A hempen garment; सर्वं च तान्तवं रक्तं शाणक्षौमाविकानि च<BR> Ms. 10. 87, 2. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाणाजीवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणाजीवः|शाणाजीव
शाण + -आजीवः an armourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणिः|शाणि
शाणिः A plant from the fibres of which a coarse cloth is prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणित|शाणितः
शाणित <i>p. p.</i> Whetted, ground, sharpened (on a whetstone).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणी
शाणी<BR>—1 A touchstone.<BR>—2 A white stone.<BR>—3 A saw.<BR>—4 A hempen garment; वस्त्राणां प्रवरा शाणी Mb. 3. 190. 19.<BR>—5 A ragged garment; शाणीवालपरीधानो व्याघ्रचर्मपरिच्छदः Mb. 12. 303. 13.<BR>—6 A small screen or tent.<BR>—7 Gesticulation, a sign made with the hands or eyes.<BR>—8 A weight of four Māṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणीरम्
शाणीरम् A bank or spot of ground in the Śoṇa river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्यः|शाण्डिल्य|शांडिल्य|शांडिल्यः
शाण्डिल्यः<BR>—1 N. of a sage, the author of a law-book.<BR>—2 The <i>Bilva</i> tree.<BR>—3 A form of Agni.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाण्डिल्यगोत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण्डिल्यगोत्रम्
शाण्डिल्यः + -गोत्रम् the family of Śāṇḍilya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात|शातं|शातः
शात <i>p. p.</i> [शो-क्त]<BR>—1 Sharpened, whetted; हास्यः पश्यन्नपि रिपुशिरःशाणशातं कुठारम्<BR> Mv. 3. 28; sharp; रामे शातकुठारभासुरकरे क्षत्रद्रुमोच्छेदिनि Ve. 6. 12.<BR>—2 Thin, slender; शय्यागतेन रामेण माता शातोदरी बभौ R. 10. 69.<BR>—3 Weak, feeble.<BR>—4 Beautiful, handsome.<BR>—5 Cut down.<BR>—6 Happy, thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातः|शात|शातं
शात + .{@-तः@} The Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातम्
शात + .{@-तम्@} Happiness, pleasure, delight; मानिनीजनजनितशातम् Gīt. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शातोदरी, शातशिख<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातोदरी
शात + -उदरी a woman with a slender waist; शातोदरी युवदृशां क्षणमुत्सवोऽभूत्<BR> Śi. 5. 23; R. 10. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातशिख
शात + -शिख <i>a.</i> sharp-pointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुम्भम्
शातकुम्भम्<BR>—1 Gold; द्रुतशातकुम्भनिभमंशुमतः Śi. 9. 9; Mb. 3. 172. 25; N. 16. 34.<BR>—2 The thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकौम्भम्
शातकौम्भम् Gold. ━<i>a.</i> Golden; शातकौम्भैश्च कवचैर्भूषणैश्च<BR> तमोऽभ्यगात् Mb. 7. 154. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातक्रतव
शातक्रतव <i>a.</i> Belonging or relating to Indra; त्वदुत्सङ्गे<BR> गङ्गे पतति यदि कायस्तनुभृतां तदा मातः शातक्रतवपदलाभोऽप्यतिलघुः<BR> Gaṅgāṣṭaka (by Śaṃkarācārya) 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातनम्
शातनम्<BR>—1 Whetting, sharpening.<BR>—2 Cutting down, destroyer; as in पर्वतपक्षशातनम् R. 3. 42.<BR>—3 Causing to fall or perish.<BR>—4 Causing to decay or wither.<BR>—5 Becoming thin or small, thinness.<BR>—6 Withering, decaying; वसन्ते सर्वशस्यानां जायते पत्रशातनम्<BR> Adhikaraṇamālā.<BR>—7 Polishing, planing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्रकः|शातपत्रक
शातपत्रकः, -की<BR> Moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्रकी
शातपत्रकः, -की<BR> Moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातभीरुः|शातभीरु
शातभीरुः A king of Mallikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमन्यव
शातमन्यव <i>a.</i> Belonging or relating to Indra; राजसे मुनिरपीह<BR> कारयन्नाधिपत्यमिव शातमन्यवम् Ki. 13. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमान|शातमानं
शातमान <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Bought for one hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातवाहनः|शातवाहन
शातवाहनः = शालिवाहनः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातह्रद
शातह्रद <i>a.</i> Relating or belonging to lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातित
शातित <i>p. p.</i> Destroyed, cut-off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रव|शात्रवं|शात्रवः
शात्रव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शत्रुरेव शत्रोरिदं वा अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to an enemy; नारिकेलासवं योधाः शात्रवं च पपुर्यशः R. 4. 42.<BR>—2 Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवः|शात्रव|शात्रवं
शात्रव + .{@-वः@} An enemy; तत्र नाभवदसौ महाहवे शात्रवादिव पराङ्मुखोऽर्थिनः<BR> Śi. 14. 44, 18. 20; Ve. 5. 1; Bk. 5. 81; Ki. 14. 2; देवः स्वर्गगतोऽपि<BR> शात्रववधेनाराधितः स्यादिति Mu. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवम्
शात्रव + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 A collection of enemies; त्वां तु दिष्टपा कुशलिनं पश्यामो हतशात्रवम्<BR> Rām. 7. 1. 17.<BR>—2 Enmity, hostility; त्रयीशात्रवशत्रवे R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवीय
शात्रवीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to an enemy.<BR>—2 Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादः|शाद
शादः [शद्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Young grass; सा शादहरिताप्युच्चैर्विशालाद्रेरुपत्यका Śiva B. 27. 39.<BR>—2 Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादा
शादः + .{@-दा@} Brick.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शादहरितः, शादहरितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादहरितः|शादहरित
शादः + -हरितः, -हरितम् a place green with young grass, a place clad in verdure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादहरितम्
शादः + -हरितः, -हरितम् a place green with young grass, a place clad in verdure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वल|शाद्वलः
शाद्वल <i>a.</i> [शादाः सन्त्यत्र वलच्]<BR>—1 Grassy.<BR>—2 Abounding in young green grass.<BR>—3 Green, verdant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वलः|शाद्वल
शाद्वल + .{@-लः, -लम्@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">Page1544-1</a>]<BR> A grass-plot, green, meadow; शय्या शाद्वलम् Śānti. 2. 21;<BR> R. 2. 17; रम्या नवद्युतिरपैति न शाद्वलेभ्यः Ki. 5. 37; Y. 3. 7;<BR> also शाद्वलस्थली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वलम्
शाद्वल + .{@-लः, -लम्@}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">Page1544-1</a>]<BR> A grass-plot, green, meadow; शय्या शाद्वलम् Śānti. 2. 21;<BR> R. 2. 17; रम्या नवद्युतिरपैति न शाद्वलेभ्यः Ki. 5. 37; Y. 3. 7;<BR> also शाद्वलस्थली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1543-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वलितम्
शाद्वलितम् The being covered with grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्
शान् €1 U. (शीशांसति-ते, strictly a desiderative of शान् used<BR> in a primitive sense) To sharpen, whet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानः|शान
शानः<BR>—1 A touch-stone.<BR>—2 A whet-stone.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शानपादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानपादः|शानपाद
शानः + -पादः<BR>—1 a stone for grinding sandal.<BR>—2 the Pāriyātra mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानच्
शानच् (In gram.) A technical term used by Paṇini for the Kṛt affix<BR> आन or मान used in forming present participles of the Ātm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानैश्चर
शानैश्चर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to Saturn.<BR>—2 Falling on a Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त|शांत|शान्तं|शान्तः
शान्त <i>p. p.</i> [शम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Appeased, allayed, calmed, satisfied, pacified; चचार सानुजः शान्तो<BR> वृद्धेक्ष्वाकुव्रतं युवा R. 12. 20.<BR>—2 Cured, alleviated; शान्तरोगः.<BR>—3 Abated, subsided, put an end to, removed, extinguished; शान्तरथक्षोभपरिश्रमम्<BR> R. 1. 58, 5. 47; शान्तार्चिषं दीपमिव प्रकाशः Ki. 17. 16.<BR>—4 Ceased, stopped; शान्तमृगप्रचारम् Ku. 3. 42.<BR>—5 Dead, deceased; तेषु सर्वेषु शान्तेषु गतेष्वविदितां गतिम्.<BR>—6 Stilled, hushed.<BR>—7 Calm, quiet, undisturbed, tranquil, still; शान्तमिदमाश्रमपदम्<BR> Ś. 1. 16, 4. 19.<BR>—8 Tamed; स्वमाश्रमं शान्तमृगं निनाय R. 14. 79.<BR>—9 Free from passions, at ease, contented; Bṛ. Up. 4. 4. 23.<BR>—10 Shaded.<BR>—11 Gentle; शान्तानुकूलपवनश्च शिवश्च पन्थाः Ś. 4. 11.<BR>—12 Purified.<BR>—13 Meek, humble.<BR>—14 Auspicious (in augury); (the phrase शान्तं पापम् which is sometimes<BR> repeated, means ‘oh no!’, ‘how can it be’, ‘God forbid such an untoward or unlucky event’<BR>; Ś. 5; Mu. 1).<BR>—15 Rendered ineffective, harmless (said of weapons).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तः|शान्त|शांत|शान्तं
शान्त + .{@-न्तः@}<BR>—1 A man who has subdued his passions, an ascetic.<BR>—2 Tranquillity, quietism, the sentiment of quietism, the predominant<BR> feeling of which is indifference to worldly objects and pleasures; see<BR> निर्वेद and रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तम्
शान्त + .{@-न्तम्@} Appeasing, pacifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तम्
शान्त + .{@-न्तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Enough, no more, not so, for shame, hush!, god<BR> (heaven) forbid!; शान्तं कथं दुर्जनाः पौरजानपदाः U. 1; तामेव<BR> शान्तमथवा किमिहोत्तरेण 3. 26.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शान्तात्मन्, शान्तचेतस्, शान्तगुण, शान्ततोय, शान्तरजस्, शान्तरव, शान्तरसः, शान्तलाभ, शान्तविवाद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तात्मन्
शान्त + -आत्मन्, -चेतस् <i>a.</i> calm, tranquil-minded, sedate or composed in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तचेतस्|शांतचेतस्
शान्त + -आत्मन्, -चेतस् <i>a.</i> calm, tranquil-minded, sedate or composed in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तगुण
शान्त + -गुण <i>a.</i> deceased; नृपे शान्तगुणे जाते Rām. 2. 65. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्ततोय
शान्त + -तोय <i>a.</i> having still water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरजस्
शान्त + -रजस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dustless.<BR>—2 passionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरव
शान्त + -रव <i>a.</i> uttering auspicious sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तरसः|शान्तरस|शांतरस
शान्त + -रसः the sentiment of quietism; see शान्त above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तलाभ
शान्त + -लाभ <i>a.</i> that which has ceased to bear interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तविवाद
शान्त + -विवाद <i>a.</i> reconciled, appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तक
शान्तक <i>a.</i> Allaying, appeasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनवः|शान्तनव|शांतनव|शांतनवः
शान्तनवः ‘The son of Śantanu’, N. of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तनुः|शान्तनु|शांतनु
शान्तनुः = शन्तनुः q. v.; शान्तनोः संततिं तन्वन् पुण्यकीर्तिर्महायशाः Mb. 1. 60. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्ता
शान्ता<BR>—1 N. of the daughter of Daśaratha, adopted by the sage Lomapāda and<BR> subsequently married by Ṛṣyaśṛṅga; कन्यां दशरथो राजा शान्तां<BR> नाम व्यजीजनत् । अपत्यकृतिकां राज्ञे रोमपादाय यां ददौ ॥ U. 1. 4;<BR> see ऋष्यशृङ्ग also.<BR>—2 (In music) A particular श्रति.<BR>—3 A kind of दूर्वा grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिः|शान्ति|शांति|शांतिः
शान्तिः <i>f.</i> [शम्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Pacification, allayment, alleviation, removal; अध्वरविघातशान्तये R. 11. 1, 62.<BR>—2 Calmness, tranquillity, quiet, ease, rest, repose; स्मर संस्मृत्य<BR> न शान्तिरस्ति मे Ku. 4. 17; शान्तिः कुतस्तस्य भुजङ्गशत्रोः Māl. 6. 1;<BR> यत् किंचिद् वस्तु संप्राप्य स्वल्पं वा यदि वा बहु । या तुष्टिर्जायते<BR> चित्ते सा शान्तिः कथ्यते बुधैः ॥ Padma P.<BR>—3 Cessation of hostility; सर्पस्य शान्तिः कुटिलस्य मैत्री विधातृसृष्टौ<BR> न हि दृष्टपूर्वा Bv. 1. 125.<BR>—4 Cessation, stop.<BR>—5 Absence of passion, quietism, complete indifference to all worldly<BR> enjoyments; तदुपहितकुटुम्बः शान्तिमार्गोत्सुकोऽभूत् R. 7. 71.<BR>—6 Consolation, solace.<BR>—7 Settlement of differences, reconciliation.<BR>—8 Satisfaction of hunger.<BR>—9 An expiatory rite, a propitiatory rite for averting evil; शान्तयश्चापि<BR> वर्धन्तां यथाकल्पं यथाविधि Rām. 1. 8. 16.<BR>—10 Good fortune, felicity, auspiciousness.<BR>—11 Exculpation or absolution from blame.<BR>—12 Preservation.<BR>—13 N. of Durgā.<BR>—14 Destruction, end, death.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शान्त्युदम्, शान्त्युदकम्, शान्तिजलम्, शान्तिकर, शान्तिकारिन्, शान्तिकर्मन्, शान्तिगृहम्, शान्तिमार्गः, शान्तिवाचनम्, शान्तिसलिलम्, शान्तिहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्युदम्
शान्तिः + -उदम्, -उदकम्, -जलम् soothing or propitiatory water; अहमपि<BR> वैतानिकं शान्त्युदकमस्यै गौतमीहस्ते विसर्जयिष्यामि Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्युदकम्
शान्तिः + -उदम्, -उदकम्, -जलम् soothing or propitiatory water; अहमपि<BR> वैतानिकं शान्त्युदकमस्यै गौतमीहस्ते विसर्जयिष्यामि Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिजलम्
शान्तिः + -उदम्, -उदकम्, -जलम् soothing or propitiatory water; अहमपि<BR> वैतानिकं शान्त्युदकमस्यै गौतमीहस्ते विसर्जयिष्यामि Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकर
शान्तिः + -कर, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> soothing, pacifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकारिन्
शान्तिः + -कर, -कारिन् <i>a.</i> soothing, pacifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकर्मन्
शान्तिः + -कर्मन् any action of averting evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिगृहम्
शान्तिः + -गृहम् a room for rest or retirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिमार्गः
शान्तिः + -मार्गः the life peaceful and leading to मोक्ष; तदुपहितकुटुम्बः<BR> शान्तिमार्गोत्सुकोऽभूत् R. 7. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिवाचनम्
शान्तिः + -वाचनम् reciting of a text for averting evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिसलिलम्
शान्तिः + -सलिलम् propitiatory water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिहोमः|शान्तिहोम|शांतिहोम
शान्तिः + -होमः a sacrifice or burnt offering to avert or remove an evil;<BR> सावित्राञ्छन्तिहोमांश्च कुर्यात् पर्वसु नित्यशः Ms. 4. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिक|शांतिक
शान्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Expiatory, propitiatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्तिकम्
शान्तिक + .{@-कम्@} Observances or ceremonies calculated to remove calamities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्त्व्|शांत्व्
शान्त्व् &c. See सान्त्व् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापः|शाप
शापः [शप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 A curse, an imprecation, anathema; शापेनास्तंगमितमहिमा वर्षभोग्येण<BR> भर्तुः Me. 1, 92; R. 1. 78, 5. 56, 59, 11. 14.<BR>—2 An oath, asseveration.<BR>—3 Abuse, calumny.<BR>—4 An interdiction, a ban.<BR>—5 Trouble, disturbance (उपद्रव); मुक्तशापं वनं तच्च तस्मिन्नेव<BR> तदाहनि Rām. 1. 26. 35.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शापान्तः, शापावसानम्, शापनिवृत्तिः, शापाम्बु, शापोदकम्, शापास्त्रः, शापोत्सर्गः, शापोद्धारः, शापमुक्तिः, शापग्रस्त, शापप्रदानम्, शापमुक्त, शापयन्त्रित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापान्तः|शापान्त|शापांत
शापः + -अन्तः, -अवसानम्, -निवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> the end of a curse; शापान्तो<BR> मे भुजगशयनादुत्थिते शाङ्र्गपाणौ Me. 112; R. 8. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापावसानम्
शापः + -अन्तः, -अवसानम्, -निवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> the end of a curse; शापान्तो<BR> मे भुजगशयनादुत्थिते शाङ्र्गपाणौ Me. 112; R. 8. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापनिवृत्तिः
शापः + -अन्तः, -अवसानम्, -निवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> the end of a curse; शापान्तो<BR> मे भुजगशयनादुत्थिते शाङ्र्गपाणौ Me. 112; R. 8. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापाम्बु
शापः + -अम्बु, -उदकम् water used in formularies of cursing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापोदकम्
शापः + -अम्बु, -उदकम् water used in formularies of cursing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापास्त्रः|शापास्त्र
शापः + -अस्त्रः ‘having a curse for a weapon’, a sage, saint; त्राणाभावे<BR> हि शापास्त्राः कुर्वन्ति तपसो व्ययम् R. 15. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापोत्सर्गः|शापोत्सर्ग
शापः + -उत्सर्गः the utterance of a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापोद्धारः|शापोद्धार
शापः + -उद्धारः, -मुक्तिः <i>f.</i>, {@-मोक्षः@}<BR> release or deliverance from a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापमुक्तिः|शापमुक्ति
शापः + -उद्धारः, -मुक्तिः <i>f.</i>, {@-मोक्षः@}<BR> release or deliverance from a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापग्रस्त
शापः + -ग्रस्त <i>a.</i> labouring under a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापप्रदानम्
शापः + -प्रदानम् uttering of a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापमुक्त
शापः + -मुक्त <i>a.</i> released from a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापयन्त्रित|शापयंत्रित
शापः + -यन्त्रित <i>a.</i> restrained by a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1544-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापित
शापित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bound by an oath, conjured.<BR>—2 Sworn, adjured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापठिकः|शापठिक
शापठिकः A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाफरिकः|शाफरिक
शाफरिकः A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबर|शाबरः
शाब(व)र <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शब(व)र-अण्]<BR>—1 Savage, barbarous.<BR>—2 Low, vile, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शाब(व)र <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शब(व)र-अण्]<BR>—1 Savage, barbarous.<BR>—2 Low, vile, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबरः|शाबर
शाब(व)र + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 An offence, a fault.<BR>—2 Sin, wickedness.<BR>—3 The tree called <i>Lodhra</i>.<BR>—4 N. of a teacher and author of a well-known commentary (शाबरभाष्य)<BR> on the Mīmāṃsā-sūtras; see शबर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबरी
शाब(व)र + .{@-री@} A low form of the Prākrita dialect (spoken by mountaineers &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाबरभेदाख्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबरभेदाख्यम्
शाबर + -भेदाख्यम् (also भेदाक्षम्) copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबरिका
शाबरिका A kind of leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबल्यम्
शाबल्यम्<BR>—1 Mixture, medley.<BR>—2 Apathy, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्द|शाब्दः
शाब्द <i>a.</i> (-ब्दी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शब्द-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to or derived from a word.<BR>—2 Relating to or depending on sound (opp. आर्थ).<BR>—3 Verbal, oral.<BR>—4 Sounding, sonorous.<BR>—5 Nominal (as inflection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दः|शाब्द
शाब्द + .{@-ब्दः@} A philologist, grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दी
शाब्द + .{@-ब्दी@} N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाब्दबोधः, शाब्दव्यञ्जना<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दबोधः|शाब्दबोध
शाब्द + -बोधः perception or apprehension of the sense of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दव्यञ्जना|शाब्दव्यंजना
शाब्द + -व्यञ्जना (in rhet.) insinuation founded on words (opp. to आर्थव्यञ्जना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिक|शाब्दिकः
शाब्दिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शब्द-ठक्]<BR>—1 Verbal, oral.<BR>—2 Relating to sounds or words.<BR>—3 Sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिकः|शाब्दिक
शाब्दिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A grammarian; अधःकरोत्यादिमशाब्दिकोरगम् Viś. Guṇā. 282.<BR>—2 A lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन्
शामन् <i>n.</i> Appeasing, conciliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामनः|शामन|शामनं
शामनः N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामनम्
शामनः + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>—2 Tranquillity, peace.<BR>—3 End.<BR>—4 Sedative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामनी
शामनः + .{@-नी@} The southern direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामित्रम्
शामित्रम्<BR>—1 Sacrificing.<BR>—2 Immolating, killing animals at a sacrifice; इहोपहूतो भगवान् मृत्युः<BR> शामित्रकर्मणि Bhāg. 1. 16. 7.<BR>—3 Typing up cattle for sacrifice.<BR>—4 A sacrificial vessel; न वैदिके शामित्रे मांसपाकः ŚB. on MS. 12. 2. 2.<BR>—5 A deadly blow.<BR>—6 A place of immolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामिली
शामिली A sacrificial ladle; (स्रुच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीनम्
शामीनम्<BR>—1 Ashes.<BR>—2 A sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीलम्
शामीलम् Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीली
शामीली A chaplet, garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बः|शाम्ब|शांबः
शाम्बः N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa and Jāmbavatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरम्
शाम्बरम् A kind of sandal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाम्बरशिल्पम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरशिल्पम्
शाम्बरम् + -शिल्पम् the art of jugglery, magic; see शाम्बरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरिकः|शाम्बरिक
शाम्बरिकः A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बरी|शांबरी
शाम्बरी<BR>—1 Jugglery, sorcery.<BR>—2 Magic illusion; शाम्बरीशिल्पमलक्षि दिक्षु N. 6. 14.<BR>—3 A sorceress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बविकः|शाम्बविक|शांबविक|शांबविकः
शाम्बविकः A dealer in shells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बुकः|शाम्बुक|शांबुक|शांबुकः
शाम्बु(म्बू)कः A bivalve-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्बूकः|शाम्बूक|शांबूक|शांबूकः
शाम्बु(म्बू)कः A bivalve-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भव|शांभव|शाम्भवं|शाम्भवः
शाम्भव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शम्भोरिदम् अण्] Belonging to Śiva; अत्तुं वाच्छति<BR> शाम्भवो गणपतेराखुं क्षुधार्तः फणी Pt. 1. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भवः|शाम्भव|शांभव|शाम्भवं
शाम्भव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A worshipper of Śiva.<BR>—2 A son of Śiva.<BR>—3 Camphor.<BR>—4 Bdellium.<BR>—5 A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भवम्
शाम्भव + .{@-वम्@} The <i>Devadāru</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भवी
शाम्भवी<BR>—1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—2 N. of a plant (नीलदूर्वा).<BR>—3 The opening in the crown of the head through which the soul is said to escape.<BR>—4 N. of a kind of Mudrā; अन्तर्लक्ष्यं बहिर्दृष्टिर्निमेषोन्मेषवर्जिता ।<BR> सा एषा शाम्भवी मुद्रा सर्वतन्त्रेषु गोपिता ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाम्भवीय|शांभवीय
शाम्भवीय <i>a.</i> Relating or belonging to Śiva; तस्य द्वैधं व्यधितधनुषः<BR> शाम्भवीयस्य रामः Mv. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायः|शाय
शायः Lying, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिका
शायिका<BR>—1 Repose, sleep.<BR>—2 The state of lying or reposing; कुर्यात्तृणमयं चापं शयीत मृगशायिकाम्<BR> Mb. 1. 140. 13; also शायिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिन्
शायिन् <i>a.</i> Reclining, sleeping, resting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायकः|शायक
शायकः<BR>—1 An arrow.<BR>—2 A sword; cf. सायक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्
शार् €10 U. (शारयति-ते)<BR>—1 To weaken.<BR>—2 To be weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार <i>a.</i> [शार्-अच् शॄ-घञ् वा]<BR>—1 Variegated, speckled, mottled, spotted; पक्ष्मोत्क्षेपादुपरिविलसत्कृष्णशारप्रभाणाम् Me. 49.<BR>—2 Yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारः|शार|शारं
शार + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A variegated colour.<BR>—2 Green colour.<BR>—3 Air, wind.<BR>—4 A piece used at chess, a chessman; कालः काल्या भुवनफलके क्रीडति<BR> प्राणिशारैः Bh. 3. 39.<BR>—5 Injuring, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारता
शारता<BR>—1 A variety of colour; शारतां गमितया शशिपादैः Ki. 9. 29.<BR>—2 Yellowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारङ्गः|शारङ्ग|शारंग|शारंगः
शारङ्गः<BR>—1 The <i>Chātaka</i> bird.<BR>—2 A peacock.<BR>—3 A bee.<BR>—4 A deer.<BR>—5 An elephant; cf. सारङ्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारङ्गी
शारङ्गी A particular musical instrument (played with a bow); cf. सारङ्गी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारणिक
शारणिक <i>a.</i> In need of protection, a refugee; Mb. 13. 104. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारतल्पिकः|शारतल्पिक
शारतल्पिकः (from शरतल्प) The epithet of Bhīṣma; शान्तिपर्वणि<BR> धर्माश्च व्याख्याताः शारतल्पिकाः Mb. 1. 2. 326.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद|शारदं|शारदः
शारद <i>a.</i> [शरदि भवम् अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to autumn, autumnal; (the <i>f.</i> is शारदी in this sense);<BR> विमलशारदचन्दिरचन्द्रिका Bv. 1. 113; R. 10. 9; Ms. 6. 11; मेघः<BR> शारद एव काशधवलः पानीयरिक्तोदरः Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Annual.<BR>—3 New, recent; P. VI. 2. 9.<BR>—4 Young, fresh.<BR>—5 Modest, shy, bashful.<BR>—6 Diffident, not bold.<BR>—7 Able, clever; शिखीव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">Page1546-1</a>]<BR> शारदः N. 9. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदः|शारद|शारदं
शारद + .{@-दः@}<BR>—1 A year.<BR>—2 An autumnal sickness.<BR>—3 Autumnal sunshine.<BR>—4 A kind of kidney-bean.<BR>—5 The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदी
शारद + .{@-दी@}<BR>—1 The full-moon day in the month of Āśvina (or Kārtika).<BR>—2 Alstonia Scholaris (Mar. सातवीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदम्
शारद + .{@-दम्@}<BR>—1 Corn, grain.<BR>—2 The white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदा
शारद + .{@-दा@}<BR>—1 A kind of Vīṇā or lute.<BR>—2 N. of Durgā.<BR>—3 Of Sarasvatī; (शरत्काले पुरा यस्मान्नवम्यां बोधिता सुरैः । शारदा<BR> सा समाख्याता पीठे लोके च नामतः ॥); लिखति यदि गृहीत्वा (लेखनीं)<BR> शारदा सार्वकालम् Śivamahimna 32. ˚अम्बा (शारदाम्बा) the<BR> goddess Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1545-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिकः|शारदिक|शारदिकं
शारदिकः<BR>—1 Autumnal sickness.<BR>—2 Autumnal sunshine or heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिकम्
शारदिकः + .{@-कम्@} An autumnal or annual Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदीय
शारदीय <i>a.</i> Autumnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद्यम्
शारद्यम् Autumnal grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद्वतः|शारद्वत
शारद्वतः N. of Kṛpa; Bhāg. 1. 13. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद्वती
शारद्वतः + .{@-ती@} Kṛpī, wife of Kṛpa; ते शरा रुधिराक्ताङ्गा भित्त्वा शारद्वतीसुतम्<BR> Mb. 7. 156. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिः|शारि
शारिः<BR>—1 A chessman, a piece at chess &c.; सुवर्णशारीः कपटेन भानां विहायसि<BR> द्यूतपटे वितत्य Rām. Ch. 6. 41.<BR>—2 A small round ball.<BR>—3 A kind of die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिः|शारि
शारिः + .{@-रिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 The bird called Sārikā.<BR>—2 Fraud, trick.<BR>—3 An elephantʼs housings or armour; शारिमशकदधिरोपयितुम् Śi. 15. 77.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शारिपट्टः, शारिफलम्, शारिफलकः, शारिकम्, शारिशृङ्खला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिपट्टः|शारिपट्ट
शारिः + -पट्टः, -फलम्, -फलकः, -कम् a chequered cloth for playing<BR> at chess, draughts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिफलम्
शारिः + -पट्टः, -फलम्, -फलकः, -कम् a chequered cloth for playing<BR> at chess, draughts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिफलकः|शारिफलक
शारिः + -पट्टः, -फलम्, -फलकः, -कम् a chequered cloth for playing<BR> at chess, draughts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिकम्
शारिः + -पट्टः, -फलम्, -फलकः, -कम् a chequered cloth for playing<BR> at chess, draughts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिशृङ्खला
शारिः + -शृङ्खला <i>f.</i> a kind of dice, chessman or a square on a chess-board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिका
शारिका<BR>—1 A kind of bird (Mar. मैना).<BR>—2 A bow or stick for playing any stringed instrument.<BR>—3 Playing at chess &c.<BR>—4 A chessman, a piece at chess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारित
शारित <i>a.</i> Variegated, coloured; स्थिरद्विरेफाञ्जनशारितोदरैः Ki. 8. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारी
शारी<BR>—1 A kind of bird.<BR>—2 Ved. An arrow.<BR>—3 Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीर|शारीरं|शारीरः
शारीर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शरीरस्येदम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to the body, bodily, corporeal.<BR>—2 Incorporate, embodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरः|शारीर|शारीरं
शारीर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 The incorporate or embodied spirit (जीवात्मन्); human or individual soul.<BR>—2 A bull.<BR>—3 A kind of drug.<BR>—4 Excrement; विनाद्भिरप्सु वाप्यार्तः शारीरं संनिवेश्य च Ms. 11. 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरम्
शारीर + .{@-रः, -रम्@}<BR>—1 The incorporate or embodied spirit (जीवात्मन्); human or individual soul.<BR>—2 A bull.<BR>—3 A kind of drug.<BR>—4 Excrement; विनाद्भिरप्सु वाप्यार्तः शारीरं संनिवेश्य च Ms. 11. 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरम्
शारीर + .{@-रम्@} Bodily constitution.<BR>—2 (In medic.) the science of the body and its parts; anatomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरक|शारीरकं
शारीरक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the body, corporeal; पश्यत्ययं धिषणया ननु सप्तवध्रिः<BR> शारीरके दमशरीर्यपरः स्वदेहे Bhāg. 3. 31. 19.<BR>—2 Incorporate, embodied (as the soul).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरकम्
शारीरक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 The embodied spirit.<BR>—2 The inquiry into the nature of that spirit (a term applied to the Bhāṣya<BR> of Śaṃkarācārya on the Brahma-sūtras).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शारीरकसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरकसूत्रम्
शारीरक + -सूत्रम् the aphorisms of the Vedānta philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरकीय
शारीरकीय <i>a.</i> Corporeal; embodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरिक|शारीरिकः
शारीरिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Bodily, corporeal, material.<BR>—2 Psychological.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारुक|शारुकः
