शार्दूलः|शार्दूल|शार्द्दूलः
शार्दूलः [शॄ-ऊलल् दुक् च Uṇ. 4. 97]<BR>—1 A tiger.<BR>—2 A leopard or panther.<BR>—3 A demon, <i>Rākṣasa</i>.<BR>—4 A kind of bird.<BR>—5 A kind of animal called शरभ.<BR>—6 A lion.<BR>—7 (at the end of comp.) An eminent or distinguished person, foremost;<BR> as in नरशार्दूल; cf. कुञ्जर.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शार्दूलचर्मन्, शार्दूलविक्रीडितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलचर्मन्
शार्दूलः + -चर्मन् <i>n.</i> a tigerʼs skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलविक्रीडितम्
शार्दूलः + -विक्रीडितम्<BR>—1 a tigerʼs play; कन्दर्पोऽपि यमायते विरचयन् शार्दूलविक्रीडितम् Gīt. 4.<BR>—2 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्मण्यः|शार्मण्य
शार्मण्यः, शार्मण्यदेशः The modern name of Germany.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1546-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्मण्यदेशः|शार्मण्यदेश
