शालवः The <i>Lodhra</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाला
शाला [शाल्-अच्]<BR>—1 An apartment, a room, saloon, hall; न तत्र च आरामविहारार्थाः शालाः<BR> स्युः Kau. A. 2. 1; गृहैर्विशालैरपि भूरिशालैः Śi. 3. 50; so संगीतशाला,<BR> रङ्गशाला &c.; निजमधिरुह्य विलोकनीयशालम् Śiva B. 26. 78.<BR>—2 A house, an abode; तस्यान्त इह भूयास्म महाशाला महाकुलाः ।<BR>—3 The upper or main branch of a tree.<BR>—4 The trunk of a tree.<BR>—5 A stable, stall; as in वाजिशाला, गर्दभशाला &c.; शालाविधिस्तम्भगतैश्च नागैः R. 16. 41.<BR>—6 A pavilion erected for making gifts; Dānasāgara, Bibl. Ind. 274, Fasc. 1. p. 146.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शालाजिरः, शालारम्, शालामुखम्, शालामृगः, शालावृकः, शालासद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाजिरः|शालाजिर
शाला + -अजिरः, -रम् a hollow earthen cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालारम्
शाला + -अजिरः, -रम् a hollow earthen cup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालामुखम्
शाला + -मुखम् the front of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालामुखः|शालामुख
शाला + -मुखम् + .({@-खः@}) a kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालामृगः|शालामृग
शाला + -मृगः a jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालावृकः|शालावृक
शाला + -वृकः<BR>—1 a dog; सिंहानां च सुखेन मूर्घसु पदं धास्यन्ति शालावृकाः Bv. 1. 72.<BR>—2 a wolf.<BR>—3 a deer.<BR>—4 a cat.<BR>—5 a jackal.<BR>—6 a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालासद्
शाला + -सद् <i>a.</i> one who stays at home; शालासदां प्रजानाम् Ait. Br. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाकिन्
शालाकिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A lancer, spear-man.<BR>—2 A surgeon.<BR>—3 A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाङ्की
शालाङ्की <i>f.</i> A doll.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक्यम्
शालाक्यम् A branch of surgery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक्यः|शालाक्य|शालाक्यं
शालाक्यम् + .{@-क्यः@} An occulist who uses sharp instruments.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शालाक्यशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक्यशास्त्रम्
शालाक्यम् + -शास्त्रम् the science of using sharp instruments for diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालातुरीयः|शालातुरीय
शालातुरीयः An epithet of Pāṇini (written also शालोत्तरीय;<BR> so called from शलातुर the place of his birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालारम्
शालारम्<BR>—1 A flight of steps, ladder.<BR>—2 A bird-cage.<BR>—3 The claw of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिः|शालि
शालिः<BR>—1 Rice; न शालेः स्तम्बकरिता वप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3; यवाः<BR> प्रकीर्णा न भवन्ति शालयः Mk. 4. 17.<BR>—2 The civet-cat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाल्योदनः, शालिनम्, शालिकूटम्, शालिकेदारः, शालिगोपी, शालिग्रामः, शालिचूर्णः, शालिचूर्णम्, शालिपिष्टम्, शालिभवनम्, शालिवाहः, शालिवाहनः, शालिशूकः, शालिहोत्रः, शालिहोत्रिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्योदनः|शाल्योदन
शालिः + -ओदनः, -नम् boiled rice (of a superior kind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिनम्
शालिः + -ओदनः, -नम् boiled rice (of a superior kind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिकूटम्
शालिः + -कूटम् a heap of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिकेदारः|शालिकेदार
शालिः + -केदारः a rice field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिगोपी
शालिः + -गोपी a female appointed to watch a rice field; इक्षुच्छायनिषादिन्यः<BR> शालिगोप्यो जगुर्यशः R. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिग्रामः|शालिग्राम
शालिः + -ग्रामः (s. v. शालग्रामः above); शालिग्रामशिलानां च दानानां<BR> च निरूपणम् Brav. P. ब्रह्मखण्ड 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिचूर्णः|शालिचूर्ण
शालिः + -चूर्णः, -चूर्णम् rice-flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिचूर्णम्
शालिः + -चूर्णः, -चूर्णम् rice-flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिपिष्टम्
शालिः + -पिष्टम् a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिभवनम्
शालिः + -भवनम् a rice-field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिवाहः|शालिवाह
शालिः + -वाहः an ox used for carrying rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिवाहनः|शालिवाहन
शालिः + -वाहनः N. of a celebrated sovereign of India whose era commences with 78 A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिशूकः|शालिशूक
शालिः + -शूकः an awn or beard of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्रः|शालिहोत्र
शालिः + -होत्रः<BR>—1 N. of a writer on veterinary subjects.<BR>—2 a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्रम्
शालिः + -होत्रः + .({@-त्रम्@}) Śālihotraʼs work on veterinary science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिहोत्रिन्
शालिः + -होत्रिन् <i>m.</i> a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिकः|शालिक
शालिकः<BR>—1 A weaver.<BR>—2 A toll, tax.<BR>—3 A village of artisans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन्
शालिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> (usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Endowed with, possessed of, possessing, shining or resplendent with;<BR> अलघूपलपङ्क्तिशालिनीः परितो रुद्धनिरन्तराम्बराः Śi. 16. 76; Ki. 2. 31, 7. 28, 55, 8. 17;<BR> विलासिनीनां स्तनशालिनीनामलंक्रियन्ते स्तनमण्डलानि Ṛs. 4. 2.<BR>—2 Domestic.<BR>—3 Well-behaved; दयालुः शालिनीमाह शुक्लाभिव्याहृतं स्मरन् Bhāg. 3. 24. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिनी
शालिनी<BR>—1 A mistress of the house, housewife.<BR>—2 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन <i>a.</i> [शालाप्रवेशमर्हति, शाला-ख]<BR>—1 Modest, bashful, shy, retiring; निसर्गशालीनः स्त्रीजनः M. 4;<BR> शशाक शालीनतया न वक्तुम् R. 6. 81, 18. 17; Śi. 16. 83.<BR>—2 Like, resembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनः|शालीन
शालीन + .{@-नः@} A householder. (शालीनीकृ ‘to make humble, humiliate’.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनम्
शालीन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Bashfulness, modesty.<BR>—2 Taking alms without begging (अयाचितवृत्ति); वार्ता सञ्चयशालीनशिलोञ्छ<BR> इति वै गृहे Bhāg. 3. 12. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनता
शालीनता, -त्वम्<BR> Bashfulness, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनत्वम्
शालीनता, -त्वम्<BR> Bashfulness, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनीकरणम्
शालीनीकरणम्<BR>—1 Humiliation; P. I. 3. 70.<BR>—2 Abuse, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीय
शालीय <i>a.</i> Belonging to a house or school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाली
शाली (from श्याली) A wifeʼs sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुः|शालु
शालुः [शाल्-उण्]<BR>—1 A frog.<BR>—2 A kind of perfume.<BR>—3 A kind of astringent substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालु|शालुः
शालुः + .{@-लु@} <i>n.</i> The root of the water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुकम्
शालु(लू)कम् [शल्-ऊकण् Uṇ. 4. 44]<BR>—1 The root of the water-lily.<BR>—2 Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूकम्
शालु(लू)कम् [शल्-ऊकण् Uṇ. 4. 44]<BR>—1 The root of the water-lily.<BR>—2 Nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुकः|शालुक|शालुकं
शालु(लू)कम् + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A frog.<BR>—2 The root of the water-lily (शालूक only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुरः|शालुर
शालु(लू)रः A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूरः|शालूर
शालु(लू)रः A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूरकः|शालूरक
शालूरकः A kind of worm infesting the intestines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1547-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेयम्
शालेयम् A field of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेयः|शालेय|शालेयं
शालेयम् + .{@-यः, -यम्@} Anethum Sowa (Mar. शोपा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेयम्
शालेयम् + .{@-यः, -यम्@} Anethum Sowa (Mar. शोपा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेयः|शालेय|शालेयं
शालेयम् + .{@-यः@} A kind of radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालोत्तरीयः|शालोत्तरीय
शालोत्तरीयः An epithet of Pāṇini; see शालातुरीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलः|शाल्मल
शाल्मलः [शाल्-मलच्]<BR>—1 The silk-cotton tree.<BR>—2 One of the seven great divisions of the earth.<BR>—3 The gum of the cotton-tree.<BR>—4 N. of a ṛṣi; V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिः|शाल्मलि
शाल्मलिः —1 The silk-cotton tree; आपातरम्यपुष्पश्रीशोभितः शाल्मलिर्यथा<BR> Bv. 1. 115; Ms. 8. 246.<BR>—2 One of the seven great divisions of the earth.<BR>—3 N. of a kind of hell.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाल्मलिपत्रकः, शाल्मलिस्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिपत्रकः|शाल्मलिपत्रक
शाल्मलिः + -पत्रकः Alstonia Scholaris (Mar. सातवीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिस्थः|शाल्मलिस्थ
शाल्मलिः + -स्थः<BR>—1 an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>—2 a vulture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिकम्
शाल्मलिकम् An inferior kind of Śālmali tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिन्
शाल्मलिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिनी
शाल्मलिनी The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मली
शाल्मली<BR>—1 The silk-cotton tree; शाल्मली शीतला स्वच्छा रसे पाके रसायनी ।<BR> श्लेष्मला स्निग्धबीजा च बृंहणी रक्तपित्तजित् ॥ Bhāva P.<BR>—2 N. of a river in Pātāla; लोहशङ्कुमृजीषं च पन्थानं शाल्मलीं<BR> नदीम् Ms. 4. 90.<BR>—3 A kind of hell.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शाल्मलीफलकम्, शाल्मलीवेष्टः, शाल्मलीवेष्टकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलीफलकम्
शाल्मली + -फलकम् a smooth board of Śālmalī wood (for washing clothes);<BR> शाल्मलीफलके श्लक्ष्णे नेनिज्यान्नेजकः शनैः Ms. 8. 396.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलीवेष्टः|शाल्मलीवेष्ट
शाल्मली + -वेष्टः, -वेष्टकः the gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलीवेष्टकः|शाल्मलीवेष्टक
शाल्मली + -वेष्टः, -वेष्टकः the gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्वः|शाल्व
शाल्वः<BR>—1 N. of a country.<BR>—2 A king of Śālva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्वणम्
शाल्वणम् A poultice, cataplasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शव-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a dead body; caused by the death (of a relative); दशाहं<BR> शावमाशौचं सपिण्डेषु विधीयते Ms. 5. 59, 61.<BR>—2 Tawny, dark-yellowish; जगाम तत्र यत्रास्या भर्तुः शावं कलेवरम् Mb. 3. 297. 62<BR>—3 Dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावः|शाव
शाव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 The young of any animal; a fawn, cub; क्व वयं क्व परोक्षमन्मथो<BR> मृगशावैः सममेधितो जनः Ś. 2. 18; मृगराजशावः R. 6. 3, 18. 37.<BR>—2 A dark-yellowish colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावम्
शाव + .{@-वम्@} Defilement caused by contact with a corpse or the death of a relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावः|शाव
शाव + .{@-वः, -वम्@} A corpse; अन्यदेहविषक्तं हि शावं काष्टत्वमागतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 153. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावम्
शाव + .{@-वः, -वम्@} A corpse; अन्यदेहविषक्तं हि शावं काष्टत्वमागतम्<BR> Mb. 12. 153. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावकः|शावक
शावकः The young of any animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शावर See शाबर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश
शाश <i>a.</i> Belonging to, or coming from a hare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शश्वद् भवः अण्]<BR>—1 Eternal, perpetual, everlasting; शाश्वतीः समाः Rām. 1. 2. 15<BR> (= U. 2. 5) ‘for eternal years’, ‘ever more’, ‘for all time to come’; श्रेयसे<BR> शाश्वतो देवो वराहः परिकल्पताम् U. 5. 27 (v. l.); R. 14. 14.<BR>—2 All.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतः|शाश्वत|शाश्वतं
शाश्वत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 Of Vyāsa.<BR>—3 The sun.<BR>—4 N. of a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतम्
शाश्वत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Heaven.<BR>—2 Eternity, continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतम्
शाश्वत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Eternally, perpetually, for ever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतिक
शाश्वतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Eternal, permanent, perpetual, constant; शाश्वतिको<BR> विरोधः ‘natural antipathy’; शाश्वतिकं विरोधमपहाय K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वती
शाश्वती The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Eating flesh (or fish).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुलिकम्
शाष्कुलिकम् A quantity of baked cakes (शष्कुली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास् €2 P. (शास्ति, शशास, अशिषत्, शासिष्यति, शासितुम्, शिष्ट)<BR>—1 To teach, instruct, train (govering two accusatives in this sense);<BR> माणवकं धर्मं शास्ति Sk.; Bk. 6. 10; शिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मां त्वां<BR> प्रपन्नम् Bg. 2. 7.<BR>—2 To rule, govern; अनन्यशासनामुर्वीं शशासैकपुरीमिव R. 1. 30, 10. 1, 14. 85, 19. 57;<BR> Ś. 1. 25; Bk. 3. 53.<BR>—3 To order, command, direct, enjoin; इति रामो वृषस्यन्तीं वृषस्कन्धः<BR> शशास ताम् R. 12. 34; त्वामागतः शासितुम् Mv. 6. 20; Ku. 6. 24; Bk. 9. 68.<BR>—4 To tell, communicate, inform (with dat.); तस्मिन्नायोधनं वृत्तं<BR> लक्ष्मणायाशिषन्महत् Bk. 6. 27; Ms. 11. 83.<BR>—5 To advise; स किंसखा साधु न शास्ति योऽधिपम् Ki. 1. 5.<BR>—6 To decree, enact.<BR>—7 To punish, chastise, correct; तान् शिष्याच्चौरदण्डेन धार्मिकः पृथिवीपतिः<BR> Ms. 8. 29, 4. 175; V. 5.<BR>—8 To tame, subdue; सौमित्रेश्चरणौ न चेत्तदिषुभिः शासिष्यसे दुर्मदः Mv. 6. 20.<BR>—9 To wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास् <i>m.</i> A reciter; as in उक्थशास्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासः|शास
शासः Ved.<BR>—1 An order, command.<BR>—2 Praise (स्तुति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासकः|शासक
शासकः [शास्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A ruler.<BR>—2 A chastiser, punisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासन|शासनं
शासन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Teaching, instructing; इति मे न तु बोधाय कल्पते शासनं वचः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 8. 50.<BR>—2 Punishing, chastising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनम्
शासन + .{@-नम्@} [शास्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Instruction, teaching, discipline.<BR>—2 Rule, sway, government; अनन्यशासनामुर्वीम् R. 1. 30; so अप्रतिशासन.<BR>—3 An order, a command, direction; तरुभिरपि देवस्य शासनं प्रमाणीकृतम्<BR> Ś. 6; R. 3. 69, 14. 83, 18. 28.<BR>—4 An edict, enactment, a decree.<BR>—5 A precept, rule.<BR>—6 A royal grant (of land &c.), charter; अहं त्वां शासनशतेन योजयिष्यामि<BR> Pt. 1; Y. 2. 240, 295.<BR>—7 A deed, writing, written agreement; शासनप्रधाना हि राजानः स्युः Kau. A. 2. 9.<BR>—8 Control of passions.<BR>—9 A written book of authority.<BR>—10 A (religious) doctrine.<BR>—11 A message. (At the end of comp. शासन often means ‘punisher, destroyer, killer’<BR>; as in स्मरशासनः, पाकशासनः).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शासनातिवृत्तिः, शासनदूषक, शासनधरः, शासनपत्रम्, शासनपराङ्मुख, शासनलङ्घनम्, शासनहरः, शासनहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनातिवृत्तिः|शासनातिवृत्ति
शासन + -अतिवृत्तिः <i>f.</i> violation of commands, disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनदूषक
शासन + -दूषक <i>a.</i> disobeying a command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनधरः|शासनधर
शासन + -धरः a messenger, envoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनपत्रम्
शासन + -पत्रम्<BR>—1 a plate (usually of copper) on which a grant of land &c. is inscribed.<BR>—2 a sheet of paper on which an order is written.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनपराङ्मुख
शासन + -पराङ्मुख <i>a.</i> disobedient to an order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनलङ्घनम्
शासन + -लङ्घनम् transgression of order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहरः|शासनहर
शासन + -हरः a royal messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनहारिन्
शासन + -हारिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an envoy, a messenger; तमभ्यनन्दत् प्रथमं प्रबोधितः प्रजेश्वरः<BR> शासनहारिणा हरेः R. 3. 68.<BR>—2 a conveyer of royal writs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनीय
शासनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be ruled, governed or directed.<BR>—2 Punishable; V. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Ruled, governed.<BR>—2 Punished.<BR>—3 Restrained, controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1548-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ <i>m.</i> [शास्-तृच्]<BR>—1 A ruler, governor.<BR>—2 A chastiser; कः पौरवे वसुमतीं शासति शासितरि दुर्विनीतानाम्<BR> Ś. 1. 24; Ms. 7. 17.<BR>—3 A teacher, instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तिः|शास्ति
शास्तिः <i>f.</i> [शास्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Governing, ruling.<BR>—2 An order, a command.<BR>—3 Correction, chastisement, punishment, especially the punishment inflicted<BR> by command of the king.<BR>—5 A sceptre, rod (of authority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ <i>m.</i> [शास्-तृच् इडभावः]<BR>—1 A teacher, an instructor<BR>—2 A ruler, king, sovereign.<BR>—3 A father.<BR>—4 A Buddha or Jina; or a deified teacher of the Bauddhas or Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रम्
शास्त्रम् [शिष्यतेऽनेन शास्-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>—1 An order, a command, rule, precept; अतिक्रामति यः शास्त्रं पितुर्धर्मार्थदर्शिनः<BR> Mb. 5. 148. 21.<BR>—2 A sacred precept or rule, scriptural injunction; तस्माच्छास्त्रं प्रमाणं<BR> ते कार्याकार्यव्यवस्थितौ Bg. 16. 24.<BR>—3 A religious or sacred treatise, sacred book, scripture; see comps. below.<BR>—4 Any department of knowledge, science; इति गुह्यतमं शास्त्रम् Bg. 15. 20;<BR> शास्त्रेष्वकुण्ठिता बुद्धिः R. 1. 19; often at the end of comp.<BR> after the word denoting the subject, or applied collectively to the whole<BR> body of teaching on that subject; वेदान्तशास्त्र, न्यायशास्त्र, तर्कशास्त्र,<BR> अलंकारशास्त्र &c.<BR>—5 What is learnt, knowledge; Śi. 5. 47.<BR>—6 A work, treatise; तन्त्रैः पञ्चभिरेतच्चकार सुमनोहरं शास्त्रम् Pt. 1.<BR>—7 Theory (opp. प्रयोग or practice); इमं मां च शास्त्रे प्रयोगे<BR> च विमृशतु M. 1.<BR>—8 The material and spiritual science together; तत्त्वाभेदेन यच्छास्त्रं<BR> तत्कार्यं नान्यथाविधम् Mb. 12. 267. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शास्त्रातिक्रमः, शास्त्राननुष्ठानम्, शास्त्रानुष्ठानम्, शास्त्रानुसारः, शास्त्रान्वित, शास्त्राभिज्ञ, शास्त्रार्थः, शास्त्राचरणम्, शास्त्रावर्तलिपिः, शास्त्रोक्त, शास्त्रकारः, शास्त्रकृत्, शास्त्रकोविद, शास्त्रगण्डः, शास्त्रचक्षुस्, शास्त्रचारणः, शास्त्रज्ञ, शास्त्रदर्शिन्, शास्त्रविद्, शास्त्रज्ञानम्, शास्त्रतत्त्वम्, शास्त्रदृष्ट, शास्त्रदृष्टिः, शास्त्रप्रसंगः, शास्त्रयोनिः, शास्त्रवक्तृ, शास्त्रवर्जित, शास्त्रवादः, शास्त्रविधानम्, शास्त्रविधिः, शास्त्रविप्रतिषेधः, शास्त्रविरोधः, शास्त्रविमुख, शास्त्रविरुद्ध, शास्त्रव्युत्पत्तिः, शास्त्रशिल्पिन्, शास्त्रसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रातिक्रमः|शास्त्रातिक्रम
शास्त्रम् + -अतिक्रमः, -अननुष्ठानम् violation of sacred precepts, disregard<BR> of religious authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राननुष्ठानम्
शास्त्रम् + -अतिक्रमः, -अननुष्ठानम् violation of sacred precepts, disregard<BR> of religious authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुष्ठानम्
शास्त्रम् + -अनुष्ठानम्, -अनुसारः conformity to or observance of sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रानुसारः|शास्त्रानुसार
शास्त्रम् + -अनुष्ठानम्, -अनुसारः conformity to or observance of sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रान्वित
शास्त्रम् + -अन्वित <i>a.</i> conformable to doctrine or rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राभिज्ञ
शास्त्रम् + -अभिज्ञ <i>a.</i> versed in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रार्थः|शास्त्रार्थ
शास्त्रम् + -अर्थः<BR>—1 the meaning of the sacred precept.<BR>—2 a scriptural precept or statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राचरणम्
शास्त्रम् + -आचरणम्<BR>—1 observance of sacred precepts.<BR>—2 the study of Śātras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्राचरणः|शास्त्राचरण
शास्त्रम् + -आचरणम् + .({@-णः@})<BR>—1 one versed in scriptures.<BR>—2 a student of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रावर्तलिपिः|शास्त्रावर्तलिपि
शास्त्रम् + -आवर्तलिपिः a particular mode of writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रोक्त
शास्त्रम् + -उक्त <i>a.</i> prescribed by sacred laws, enjoined by the Śāstras, lawful, legal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकारः|शास्त्रकार
शास्त्रम् + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the author of a Śāstra or sacred book.<BR>—2 an author in general.<BR>—3 a sage, saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकृत्
शास्त्रम् + -कारः, -कृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 the author of a Śāstra or sacred book.<BR>—2 an author in general.<BR>—3 a sage, saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रकोविद
शास्त्रम् + -कोविद <i>a.</i> versed in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रगण्डः|शास्त्रगण्ड|शास्त्रगंड
शास्त्रम् + -गण्डः a superficial reader of books, superficial scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रचक्षुस्
शास्त्रम् + -चक्षुस् <i>n.</i> grammar (as being the ‘eye’, as it were, with which<BR> to understand any Śāstra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रचारणः|शास्त्रचारण
शास्त्रम् + -चारणः one who deserves sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञ|शास्त्रज्ञः
शास्त्रम् + -ज्ञ, -दर्शिन्, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 well-versed in the Śāstras.<BR>—2 a mere theorist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रदर्शिन्
शास्त्रम् + -ज्ञ, -दर्शिन्, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 well-versed in the Śāstras.<BR>—2 a mere theorist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविद्
शास्त्रम् + -ज्ञ, -दर्शिन्, -विद् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 well-versed in the Śāstras.<BR>—2 a mere theorist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रज्ञानम्
शास्त्रम् + -ज्ञानम् knowledge of sacred books, conversancy with scriptures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रतत्त्वम्
शास्त्रम् + -तत्त्वम् truth as taught in the Śāstras, scriptural truth. ˚ज्ञः an astronomer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रदृष्ट
शास्त्रम् + -दृष्ट <i>a.</i> stated or enjoined in sacred books; तदहं प्रष्टुमिच्छामि<BR> शास्त्रदृष्टेन कर्मणा Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रदृष्टिः|शास्त्रदृष्टि
शास्त्रम् + -दृष्टिः <i>f.</i> scriptural point of view. ━<i>m.</i> an astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रप्रसंगः|शास्त्रप्रसङ्ग
शास्त्रम् + -प्रसंगः<BR>—1 the subject of the Śāstras.<BR>—2 any discussion on scriptural points.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रयोनिः|शास्त्रयोनि
शास्त्रम् + -योनिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">Page1549-2</a>]<BR> the source of the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवक्तृ
शास्त्रम् + -वक्तृ an expounder of sacred books or knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवर्जित
शास्त्रम् + -वर्जित <i>a.</i> free from all rule or law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रवादः|शास्त्रवाद
शास्त्रम् + -वादः a precept or statement of the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविधानम्
शास्त्रम् + -विधानम्, -विधिः a sacred precept, scriptural injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविधिः|शास्त्रविधि
शास्त्रम् + -विधानम्, -विधिः a sacred precept, scriptural injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविप्रतिषेधः|शास्त्रविप्रतिषेध
शास्त्रम् + -विप्रतिषेधः, -विरोधः<BR>—1 mutual contradiction of sacred precepts, inconsistency of precepts.<BR>—2 any act contrary to sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरोधः|शास्त्रविरोध
शास्त्रम् + -विप्रतिषेधः, -विरोधः<BR>—1 mutual contradiction of sacred precepts, inconsistency of precepts.<BR>—2 any act contrary to sacred precepts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविमुख
शास्त्रम् + -विमुख <i>a.</i> averse from study; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रविरुद्ध
शास्त्रम् + -विरुद्ध <i>a.</i> contrary to the Śāstras, illegal, unlawful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रव्युत्पत्तिः|शास्त्रव्युत्पत्ति
शास्त्रम् + -व्युत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> intimate knowledge of the sacred writings,<BR> proficiency in the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रशिल्पिन्
शास्त्रम् + -शिल्पिन् <i>m.</i> the country of Kāśmīra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रसिद्ध
शास्त्रम् + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> established by sacred authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शास्त्रं वेत्त्यधीते वा इनि] Versed or skilled<BR> in the Śāstras. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who has mastered the Śāstras, a learned man, a great Paṇḍit.<BR>—2 A teacher of sacred science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीय
शास्त्रीय <i>a.</i> [शास्त्रेण विहितः छ]<BR>—1 Scriptural.<BR>—2 Scientific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्य|शास्यः
शास्य <i>a.</i> [शास्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be taught or advised.<BR>—2 To be regulated or governed.<BR>—3 Deserving punishment, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि €5 U. (शिनोति, शिनुते)<BR>—1 To whet, sharpen.<BR>—2 To attenuate, make thin.<BR>—3 To excite.<BR>—4 To be attentive.<BR>—5 To be sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिः|शि
शिः<BR>—1 Auspiciousness, good fortune.<BR>—2 Composure, calm, tranquillity, peace.<BR>—3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा<BR>—1 N. of a tree (शिशु); शिंशपा कटुका तिक्ता कषाया शोषकारिणी ।<BR> उष्णवीर्या हरेन्मेदः कुष्ठचित्रवमिकृमीन् Bhāva P.<BR>—2 The Aśoka tree; (ददर्श) क्षामां स्वविरहव्याधिं शिंशपामूलमास्थिताम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्कु|शिक्कुः
शिक्कु <i>a.</i> Idle, lazy, indolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्थम्
शिक्थम् Beeʼs wax; cf. सिक्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यम्
शिक्यम्, -क्या<BR>—1 A loop or swing (made of rope); छिद्रं ह्यन्तर्निहितवयुनः शिक्यभाण्डेषु<BR> तद्वित् Bhāg. 10. 8. 30.<BR>—2 A burden or load carried in a sling.<BR>—3 The strings of a balance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिक्यपाशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्या
शिक्यम्, -क्या<BR>—1 A loop or swing (made of rope); छिद्रं ह्यन्तर्निहितवयुनः शिक्यभाण्डेषु<BR> तद्वित् Bhāg. 10. 8. 30.<BR>—2 A burden or load carried in a sling.<BR>—3 The strings of a balance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिक्यपाशः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यपाशः|शिक्यपाश
शिक्यम् + -पाशः (शिक्यपाशः) the string by which a vessel is suspended<BR> (Mar. फास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यित|शिक्यितं
शिक्यित <i>a.</i> Suspended or carried in a loop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्
शिक्ष् €1 Ā. (शिक्षते, शिक्षित)<BR>—1 To learn, study, acquire knowledge of;<BR> स्वं स्वं चरित्रं शिक्षेरन् पृथिव्यां सर्वमानवाः Ms. 2. 20; अशिक्षतास्त्रं<BR> पितुरेव मन्त्रवत् R. 3. 31; मरुत् किमद्यापि न तासु शिक्षते<BR> N. 1. 73, 1. 77, 4. 48.<BR>—2 €10 U. To teach (Ved.); अक्रोधं शिक्षयन्त्यन्यैः क्रोधना ये तपोधनाः N. 17. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षकः|शिक्षक
शिक्षकः (शिक्षका or शिक्षिका <i>f.</i>) [शिक्ष्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A learner.<BR>—2 A teacher, instructor; यस्योभयं (<i>i. e.</i> क्रिया and संक्रान्ति)<BR> साधु स शिक्षकाणां धुरि प्रतिष्ठापयितव्य एव ॥ M. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षणम्
शिक्षणम् [शिक्ष्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Learning, acquiring knowledge.<BR>—2 Teaching, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1549-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा [शिक्ष्-भावे अ]<BR>—1 Learning, study, acquisition of knowledge; पश्य मे हयसंयाने शिक्षां<BR> केशवनन्दन Mb. 3. 19. 5; Ki. 15. 36; शिक्षाविशेषलघुहस्ततया निमेषात् R. 9. 63.<BR>—2 Desire of being able to do anything, wish to prevail; पाण्डवः परिचक्राम<BR> शिक्षया रणशिक्षया Ki. 15. 37.<BR>—3 Teaching, instruction, training; काव्यज्ञशिक्षयाऽभ्यासः K. P. 1;<BR> अभूच्च नम्रः प्रणिपातशिक्षया R. 3. 25; M. 4. 9.<BR>—4 One of the six Vedāṅgas, the science which teaches the proper pronunciation<BR> of words and laws of euphony; वर्णस्वराद्युच्चारणप्रकारो यत्रोपदिश्यते<BR> सा शिक्षा Ṛgvedabhāṣya.<BR>—5 Modesty, humility.<BR>—6 Science; रणशिक्षा ‘military science’; Ki. 15. 37.<BR>—7 Giving, bestowing (Ved.).<BR>—8 Punishment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिक्षाक्षरम्, शिक्षाचार, शिक्षाकरः, शिक्षागुरुः, शिक्षानरः, शिक्षारसः, शिक्षाशक्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाक्षरम्
शिक्षा + -अक्षरम् a sound pronounced according to the rules of शिक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाचार
शिक्षा + -आचार <i>a.</i> conducting oneʼs self according to precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाकरः|शिक्षाकर
शिक्षा + -करः<BR>—1 a teacher, an instructor.<BR>—2 N. of Vyāsa<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षागुरुः|शिक्षागुरु
शिक्षा + -गुरुः a religious preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षानरः|शिक्षानर
शिक्षा + -नरः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षारसः|शिक्षारस
शिक्षा + -रसः desire of acquiring skill (in).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षाशक्तिः|शिक्षाशक्ति
शिक्षा + -शक्तिः <i>f.</i> skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित <i>p. p.</i> [शिक्षा जाताऽस्य तार˚ इतच् शिक्ष्-क्त वा]<BR>—1 Learnt, studied.<BR>—2 Taught, instructed; अशिक्षितपटुत्वम् Ś. 5. 22; शिक्षितासि मयैव<BR> यम् N. 20. 64.<BR>—3 Trained, disciplined.<BR>—4 Tame, docile.<BR>—5 Skilful, clever.<BR>—6 Modest, diffident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षितः|शिक्षित
शिक्षित + .{@-तः@} A pupil, scholar.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिक्षिताक्षरः, शिक्षितायुध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षिताक्षरः|शिक्षिताक्षर
शिक्षित + -अक्षरः<BR>—1 a teacher.<BR>—2 a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षितायुध
शिक्षित + -आयुध <i>a.</i> versed in the use of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षमाणः|शिक्षमाण
शिक्षमाणः A pupil, scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखकः|शिखक
शिखकः A scribe, writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डः|शिखण्ड|शिखंड|शिखंडः
शिखण्डः [शिखाममति अम्-ड् तस्य नेत्वम् Tv.]<BR>—1 A lock of hair left on the crown or sides of the head at tonsure.<BR>—2 A peacockʼs tail; केकाभिर्नीलकण्ठस्तिरयति वचनं ताण्डवादुच्छिखण्डः Māl. 9. 30.<BR>—3 A crest; आलोकयति पयोदान् प्रबलपुरोवातताडितशिखण्डः V. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिका
शिखण्डः + .{@-खण्डिका@} the चूडाकरण ceremony; Hc. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डकः|शिखण्डक|शिखंडक|शिखंडकः
शिखण्डकः [शिखण्ड इव-कन्]<BR>—1 A lock of hair left on the crown of the head at tonsure.<BR>—2 Locks or tufts of hair left on the sides of the head; (these are three<BR> or five in the case of the Kṣatriyas); कुवलयदलश्यामस्निग्धः शिखण्डकमण्डनः U. 4. 19.<BR>—3 A crest, tuft, plume.<BR>—4 A peacockʼs tail.<BR>—5 The fleshy part of the body below the buttocks.<BR>—6 (With Śaivas) One who attains a particular degree of emancipation;<BR> also शिखण्डिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिकः|शिखण्डिक|शिखंडिक|शिखंडिकः
शिखण्डिकः A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिका
शिखण्डिका See शिखण्ड (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिन्|शिखंडिन्
शिखण्डिन् <i>a.</i> [शिखण्डोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Crested, tufted. ━<i>m.</i> A peacock; नदति स एष वधूसखः शिखण्डी<BR> U. 3. 18; R. 1. 39; Ku. 1. 15.<BR>—2 A cock.<BR>—3 An arrow.<BR>—4 A peacockʼs tail.<BR>—5 A kind of jasmine.<BR>—6 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 N. of a son of Drupada; शिखण्डी च महारथः Bg. 1. 17. [Śikhaṇḍin<BR> was originally a female, being Ambā born in the family of Drupada for<BR> wreaking her revenge upon Bhīṣma; (see Ambā). But from her very birth<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">Page1550-2</a>]<BR> the girl was given out as a male child and brought up as such. In due<BR> course she was married to the daughter of Hiraṇyavarman, who was extremely<BR> sorry to find that she had got a veritable woman for her husband. Her<BR> father, therefore, resolved to attack the kingdom of Drupada for his having<BR> deceived him; but Śikhaṇḍin contrived, by practising austere penance<BR> in a forest, to exchange her sex with a Yakṣa and thus averted the calamity<BR> which threatened Drupada. Afterwards in the great Bhāratī war he proved<BR> a means of killing Bhīṣma, who declined to fight with a woman, when<BR> Arjuna put him forward as his hero. He was afterwards killed by Aśvatthāman.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डिनी
शिखण्डिनी<BR>—1 A pea-hen; बर्हाणामपरशिखण्डिनीं भरेण । आलोक्य व्यवदधतं पुरो<BR> मयूरम् ॥ Śi. 8. 11.<BR>—2 A kind of jasmine.<BR>—3 N. of the daughter of Drupada; see शिखण्डिन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखण्डी
शिखण्डी A lock on the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरः|शिखर|शिखरं
शिखरः, -रम्<BR> [शिखा अस्त्यस्य-अरच् आलोपः]<BR>—1 The top, summit, or peak of a mountain; जगाम गौरी शिखरं शिखण्डिमत्<BR> Ku. 5. 7, 4; Me. 18.<BR>—2 The top of a tree.<BR>—3 Crest, tuft.<BR>—4 The point or edge of a sword.<BR>—5 Top, peak, point in general.<BR>—6 The arm-pit.<BR>—7 Bristling of the hair.<BR>—8 The bud of the Arabian jasmine.<BR>—9 A kind of ruby-like gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरम्
शिखरः, -रम्<BR> [शिखा अस्त्यस्य-अरच् आलोपः]<BR>—1 The top, summit, or peak of a mountain; जगाम गौरी शिखरं शिखण्डिमत्<BR> Ku. 5. 7, 4; Me. 18.<BR>—2 The top of a tree.<BR>—3 Crest, tuft.<BR>—4 The point or edge of a sword.<BR>—5 Top, peak, point in general.<BR>—6 The arm-pit.<BR>—7 Bristling of the hair.<BR>—8 The bud of the Arabian jasmine.<BR>—9 A kind of ruby-like gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरा
शिखरः, -रम् + .{@-रा@} N. of a plant (मूर्वा).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिखरवासिनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरवासिनी
शिखरः + -वासिनी an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिणी
शिखरिणी<BR>—1 An excellent woman.<BR>—2 A dish of curds and sugar with spices.<BR>—3 A line of hair extending across the navel.<BR>—4 A kind of vine.<BR>—5 N. of a plant (मूर्वा).<BR>—6 A rabian jasmine.<BR>—7 N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिन्
शिखरिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शिखरम् अस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Crested, tufted.<BR>—2 Pointed, peaked; शिखरिदशना Me. 84. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A mountain; मेरुः शिखरिणामहम्; इतश्च शरणार्थिनां शिखरिणां गणाः<BR> शेरते Bh. 2. 76; Me. 13; R. 9. 12, 17.<BR>—2 A hill-fort.<BR>—3 A tree.<BR>—4 The lapwing.<BR>—5 The plant अपामार्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखा
शिखा [शी-खक् तस्य नेत्वम् पृषो˚; Uṇ. 5. 24]<BR>—1 A lock of hair left on the crown of the head; शिखां मोक्तुं बद्धामपि<BR> पुनरयं धावति करः Mu. 3. 30; Śi. 4. 50; Māl. 10. 6; the hair<BR> of the head; आसिञ्चदम्ब वत्सेति नेत्रोदैर्दुहितुः शिखाः Bhāg. 3. 22. 25.<BR>—2 A crest, top-knot.<BR>—3 Tuft, plume.<BR>—4 Top, summit, peak; अधिरुह्य पुष्पभरनम्नशिखैः परितः परिष्कृततलां<BR> तरुभिः Ki. 6. 17.<BR>—5 Sharp end, edge, point or end in general; ईषदीषच्चुम्बितानि भ्रमरैः<BR> सुकुमारकेसरशिखानि Ś. 1. 4; Bv. 1. 2.<BR>—6 The end of a garment; तोयाधारपथाश्च वल्कलशिखानिष्यन्दरेखाङ्किताः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>—7 A flame; प्रभामहत्या शिखयेव दीपः Ku. 1. 28; R. 17. 34; Ki. 16. 53.<BR>—8 A ray of light; ज्वलन्मणिशिखाश्चैनं वासुकिप्रमुखा निशि Ku. 2. 38.<BR>—9 A peacockʼs crest or comb.<BR>—10 A fibrous root.<BR>—11 A branch in general, especially one taking root.<BR>—12 The head or chief of anything.<BR>—13 The fever of love.<BR>—14 The point of the foot,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-1" target="_blank">Page1551-1</a>]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिखाकन्दम्, शिखातरुः, शिखादामन्, शिखाधर, शिखाधारः, शिखापित्तम्, शिखाबन्धः, शिखामणिः, शिखामूलम्, शिखावरः, शिखावल, शिखावृक्षः, शिखावृद्धिः, शिखासूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1550-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखाकन्दम्
शिखा + -कन्दम् a kind of turnip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखातरुः|शिखातरु
शिखा + -तरुः a lamp-stand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखादामन्
