शितशूकः|शितशूक
शित + -शूकः<BR>—1 barley.<BR>—2 wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितद्रुः|शितद्रु
शितद्रुः <i>f.</i> The river Sutlej; see शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिति|शितिः
शिति <i>a.</i> [शि-क्तिच्]<BR>—1 White.<BR>—2 Black; शितितारकानुमितताम्रनयनमरुणीकृतं क्रुधा Śi. 15. 48.<BR>—3 Blue, dark blue; शितिना गलेन विलसन् मरीचिना Ki. 12. 23.<BR>—4 Variegated; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिः|शिति
शिति + .{@-तिः@} The birch tree.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शितिकण्ठः, शितिकुम्भः, शितिचन्दनम्, शितिच्छदः, शितिपक्षः, शितिरत्नम्, शितिवासस्, शितिसारकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिकण्ठः|शितिकण्ठ|शितिकंठ
शिति + -कण्ठः<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva; तस्यात्मा शितिकण्ठस्य सैनापत्यमुपेत्य वः<BR> Ku. 2. 61, 6. 81; Bhāg. 4. 3. 12.<BR>—2 a peacock; अवनतशितिकण्ठकण्ठलक्ष्मीमिह दधति स्फुरिताणुरेणुजालाः Śi. 4. 56.<BR>—3 a gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिकुम्भः|शितिकुम्भ
शिति + -कुम्भः the oleander tree (Mar. कण्हेर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिचन्दनम्
शिति + -चन्दनम् musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिच्छदः|शितिच्छद|शितिछद
शिति + -छदः, -पक्षः a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिपक्षः|शितिपक्ष
शिति + -छदः, -पक्षः a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिरत्नम्
शिति + -रत्नम् a sapphire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिवासस्
शिति + -वासस् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Balarāma; विडम्बयन्तं शितिवाससस्तनुम् Śi. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितिसारकः|शितिसारक
शिति + -सारकः a kind of ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिर
शिथिर <i>a.</i> [शिथ्-किरच् Uṇ. 1. 52] Loose, slack, flexible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिल|शिथिलं
शिथिल <i>a.</i> [श्लथ्-किलच् पृषो˚ Uṇ. 1. 53]<BR>—1 Loose, loosened, slackened, relaxed. —2 Untied, unfastened; विश्रामं<BR> लभतामिदं च शिथिलज्याबन्धमस्मद्धनुः Ś. 2. 6.<BR>—2 Severed, fallen from the stalk; अर्कस्योपरि शिथिलं च्युतमिव नवमल्लिकाकुसुमम् Ś. 2. 8.<BR>—3 Languid, enfeebled, unnerved.<BR>—4 Weak, feeble; अशिथिलपरिरम्भ U. 1. 24 ‘fast or close embrace’; 1. 27.<BR>—5 Flaccid, flabby.<BR>—6 Dissolved.<BR>—7 Decayed.<BR>—8 Ineffective, futile, vain.<BR>—9 Inattentive,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">Page1552-1</a>]<BR> careless; सुभक्ष्याणि विचित्राणि शिथिलाश्चैव योषितः Pt. 4. 116.<BR>—10 Loosely done, not strictly or rigidly performed.<BR>—11 Cast off, abandoned.<BR>—12 Indistinct (as sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलम्
शिथिल + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Laxity, looseness.<BR>—2 Slowness. (शिथिलीकृ means<BR>—1 to loosen, unfasten, untie.<BR>—2 to relax, slacken; शिथिलीकृतेऽधिकृतकृत्यविधौ Ki. 6. 30.<BR>—3 to weaken, impair, enfeeble.<BR>—4 to give up, abandon; आत्मन्यवज्ञां शिथिलीचकार R. 2. 41. शिथिलीभू<BR>—1 to be slackened or relaxed.<BR>—2 to fall off from; एतत्तु मां दहति नष्टधनाश्रयस्य यत् सौहृदादपि<BR> जनाः शिथिलीभवन्ति Mk. 1. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1551-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलयति
शिथिलयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To relax, slacken, loosen; शिथिलितमानग्रहणो वाति दक्षिणपवनः Ratn. 1. 14.<BR>—2 To give up, abandon; शिथिलय क्षणमात्रं बाष्पमोक्षम् Ve. 5.<BR>—3 To lessen, allow to cool down; न सा इतोगतमनुरागं शिथिलयति V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलायते
शिथिलायते Den. Ā. To become loose or flaccid; गात्राणि शिथिलायन्ते Bh. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलित
शिथिलित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Loosed.<BR>—2 Relaxed, loosened.<BR>—3 Dissolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनिः|शिनि
शिनिः [शी-निः ह्रस्वश्च Uṇ. 4. 53]<BR>—1 N. of a warrior belonging to the side of the Yādavas. (शिनेर्नप्तृ<BR> <i>m.</i> N. of Sātyaki).<BR>—2 A class of people; शिनीनां दार्विहोमिको ब्राह्मणः ŚB. on MS. 8. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपिः|शिपि
शिपिः A ray of light. ━<i>f.</i> Skin, leather. ━<i>n.</i> Water; शौत्याच्छयनयोगाच्च<BR> शिपि वारि प्रचक्षते Vyāsa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिपिविष्ट<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपिविष्ट|शिपिविष्टः
शिपिः + -विष्ट <i>a.</i> (written शिपविष्ट or शिविपिष्ट also)<BR>—1 pervaded by rays.<BR>—2 bald, bald-headed.<BR>—3 leprous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपिविष्टः|शिपिविष्ट
शिपिः + -विष्ट + .({@-ष्टः@})<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu; नैकरूपो बृहद्रूपः शिपिविष्टः प्रकाशनः<BR> V. Sah.; पुरोडाशं निरवपन् शिपिविष्टाय विष्णवे Bhāg. 4. 13. 35.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 a bald man.<BR>—4 a man without prepuce.<BR>—5 a leper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रः|शिप्र
शिप्रः N. of a lake on the Himālaya; ततो हिमवतः प्रस्थे प्रतीच्यां<BR> तत्पुरस्य च । शिप्रो नाम सरः पूर्णं ददृशुर्द्रुहिणादयः ॥ Kālikā P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रम्
शिप्रः + .{@-प्रम्@} Ved.<BR>—1 A cheek; jaw.<BR>—2 The chin.<BR>—3 The nose.<BR>—4 A helmet or visor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रा
शिप्रा<BR>—1 N. of a river which issues from the Śipra lake and on the bank of<BR> which stands Ujjayinī; शिप्रावातः प्रियतम इव प्रार्थनाचाटुकारः Me. 31.<BR>—2 A visor or helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफः|शिफ
शिफः See शिफा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफा
शिफा<BR>—1 A fibrous root; नीरन्ध्रपल्लवशिफानिभृतप्रकाण्डं सायंतनाभ्रसमशोभमशोकसालम्<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 22; Ms. 9. 230.<BR>—2 The root of a water-lily.<BR>—3 A root in general.<BR>—4 A stroke with a whip; शिफाश्चैवाप्नुयाद्दश Ms. 8. 369.<BR>—5 A mother.<BR>—6 A river.<BR>—7 Turmeric.<BR>—8 Spikenard.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिफाकन्दः, शिफाकन्दम्, शिफाधरः, शिफारुहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाकन्दः|शिफाकन्द
शिफा + -कन्दः, -कन्दम् the root of a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाकन्दम्
शिफा + -कन्दः, -कन्दम् the root of a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाधरः|शिफाधर
शिफा + -धरः a branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफारुहः|शिफारुह
शिफा + -रुहः the (Indian) fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाकः|शिफाक
शिफाकः The root of a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिः|शिबि
शिबिः (-विः)<BR>—1 A beast of prey.<BR>—2 The birch tree.<BR>—3 N. of a country (pl.); Mb. 5. 195. 7.<BR>—4 N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">Page1552-2</a>]<BR> king (who is said to have saved <i>Agni</i> in the form of a dove from Indra<BR> in the form of a hawk by offering an equal quantity of his own flesh weighed<BR> in a balance); शिबेरिव समुद्भूतं शरणागतरक्षया Mu. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविः|शिवि
शिबिः (-विः)<BR>—1 A beast of prey.<BR>—2 The birch tree.<BR>—3 N. of a country (pl.); Mb. 5. 195. 7.<BR>—4 N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">Page1552-2</a>]<BR> king (who is said to have saved <i>Agni</i> in the form of a dove from Indra<BR> in the form of a hawk by offering an equal quantity of his own flesh weighed<BR> in a balance); शिबेरिव समुद्भूतं शरणागतरक्षया Mu. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिका
शिबि(वि)का<BR>—1 A palanquin, litter.<BR>—2 A bier.<BR>—3 A raised platform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिबि(वि)का<BR>—1 A palanquin, litter.<BR>—2 A bier.<BR>—3 A raised platform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिरम्
शिबि(वि)रम्<BR>—1 A camp; विद्रुते शिबिरे शून्ये Mb. 9. 30. 3, 4; धृष्टद्युम्नः स्वशिबिरमयं<BR> याति सर्वे सहध्वम् Ve. 3. 18; Śi. 5. 68.<BR>—2 A royal camp or residence.<BR>—3 An intrenchment for the protection of an army.<BR>—4 A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविरम्
शिबि(वि)रम्<BR>—1 A camp; विद्रुते शिबिरे शून्ये Mb. 9. 30. 3, 4; धृष्टद्युम्नः स्वशिबिरमयं<BR> याति सर्वे सहध्वम् Ve. 3. 18; Śi. 5. 68.<BR>—2 A royal camp or residence.<BR>—3 An intrenchment for the protection of an army.<BR>—4 A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिरथः
शिबि(वि)रथः A palanquin, litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविरथः
शिबि(वि)रथः A palanquin, litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बः|शिम्ब|शिंबः
शिम्बः A kind of large shrub (चक्रमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बा|शिंबा
शिम्बः + .{@-म्बा@} A pod, legume; (also शिम्बिः <i>f.</i> in this sense); तीराश्मन्तकशिम्बिचुम्बितमुखा<BR> धावन्त्यपः पूर्णिकाः Māl. 9. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बिका
शिम्बिका<BR>—1 A pod, legume.<BR>—2 A kind of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिम्बी|शिंबी
शिम्बी<BR>—1 A pod, legume.<BR>—2 A kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरम्
शिरम्<BR>—1 The head.<BR>—2 The root of the pepper plant (<i>m.</i> also according to some, in these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरः|शिर|शिरं
शिरम् + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A bed.<BR>—2 A large serpent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिरजम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरजम्
शिरम् + -जम् hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्
शिरस् <i>n.</i> [शॄ-असुन् निपातः Uṇ. 4. 193]<BR>—1 The head; शिरसा श्लाघते पूर्वं (गुणं) परं (दोषं)<BR> कण्ठे नियच्छति Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Skull.<BR>—3 A peak, summit, top (as of a mountain); हिमगौरैरचलाधिपः शिरोभिः<BR> Ki. 5. 17; Śi. 4. 54.<BR>—4 The top of a tree.<BR>—5 The head or top of anything; तेनाहतो महातालो वेपमानो बृहच्छिराः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 15. 33; शिरसि मसीपटलं दधाति दीपः Bv. 1. 74.<BR>—6 Pinnacle, acme, highest point.<BR>—7 Front, forepart, van (as of an army); पुत्रस्य ते रणशिरस्ययमग्रयायी<BR> Ś. 7. 26; U. 5. 3.<BR>—8 Chief, principal, head (usually at the end of comp.).<BR>—9 N. of the verse in the गायत्री (from आपो ज्योतिः to स्वरोम्);<BR> cf. T. Ār. 10. 27; Bhāg. 5. 9. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शिरोस्थि, शिरःकपालिन्, शिरःक्रिया, शिरोगृहम्, शिरोग्रहः, शिरश्छेदः, शिरश्छेदनम्, शिरस्तापिन्, शिरस्त्रम्, शिरस्त्राणम्, शिरोधरा, शिरोधिः, शिरोध्रः, शिरःपीठम्, शिरःपीडा, शिरःपुष्पम्, शिरःप्रणामः, शिरःप्रदानम्, शिरःप्रावरणम्, शिरःफलः, शिरोभूषणम्, शिरोमणिः, शिरोमर्मन्, शिरोमालिन्, शिरोरत्नम्, शिरोरुजा, शिरोरुह्, शिरोरोगः, शिरोवर्तिन्, शिरोवल्ली, शिरोवृत्तम्, शिरोवेष्टः, शिरोवेष्टनम्, शिरःशूलम्, शिरःस्थः, शिरःस्थानम्, शिरोहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरोस्थि
शिरस् + -अस्थि <i>n.</i> ({@शिरोस्थि@}) the skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरःकपालिन्
शिरस् + -कपालिन् <i>m.</i> an ascetic who carries about a human skull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1552-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

