शीता See सीता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतारु
शीतारु, -शीतालु <i>a.</i><BR> [शीतं न सहते शीत-आलुच्] Suffering from<BR> or shivering with cold, chilled, pinched; शीतालुः सलिलगतेन सिच्यते<BR> स्म Śi. 8. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतालु|शीतालुः
शीतारु, -शीतालु <i>a.</i><BR> [शीतं न सहते शीत-आलुच्] Suffering from<BR> or shivering with cold, chilled, pinched; शीतालुः सलिलगतेन सिच्यते<BR> स्म Śi. 8. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतीभावः|शीतीभाव
शीतीभावः<BR>—1 Perfect tranquillity of mind.<BR>—2 Final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतीभू
शीतीभू To become cold; मुहूर्तं सह्यतां दाहस्ततः शीतीभविष्यति<BR> Mb. 12. 318. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्य|शीत्यं
शीत्य See सीत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधु|शीधुः
शीधु <i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 Any spirituous liquor, rum; ह्रीप्रत्यूहप्रशमकुशलाः शीधवश्चक्रुरासाम् Śi. 9. 87.<BR>—2 Wine.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शीधुगन्धः, शीधुपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधुगन्धः|शीधुगन्ध|शीधुगंध
शीधु + -गन्धः the <i>Bakula</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधुपः|शीधुप
शीधु + -पः a drinker of spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन <i>a.</i> [श्यै-क्त] Thick, congealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीनः|शीन|शीनं
शीन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A dolt, blockhead.<BR>—2 A large snake (अजगर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीनम्
शीन + .{@-नम्@} Ice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीफर
शीफर <i>a.</i> Charming, delightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीफालिका
शीफालिका (= शेफालिका); The Nyctanthes Tristis (Mar. राननिर्गुडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्
शीभ् €1 Ā. (शीभते)<BR>—1 To boast.<BR>—2 To tell, say, speak (कथने ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभवः|शीभव
शीभवः A spray; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्यः|शीभ्य
शीभ्यः<BR>—1 A bull.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीरः|शीर
शीरः [शीड्-रक् Uṇ. 2. 13] A large snake; see सीर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ण|शीर्णं
शीर्ण [शॄ-क्त] <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Withered, decayed, rotten; शीर्णं च पतितं भूमौ पर्णं समुपयुक्तवान् Mb. 3. 38. 23.<BR>—2 Dry, sere.<BR>—3 Shattered, torn; shivered; क्रमशीर्णाकुलमूलसंततिः Ki. 2. 50.<BR>—4 Thin, emaciated; (see शॄ).<BR>—6 Small, slender.<BR>—6 Fallen, dropped; स्वयंशीर्ण Ms. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णम्
शीर्ण + .{@-र्णम्@} A kind of perfume.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शीर्णाङ्घ्रिः, शीर्णपादः, शीर्णपर्णम्, शीर्णवृन्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णाङ्घ्रिः|शीर्णाङ्घ्रि|शीर्णांघ्रि
शीर्ण + -अङ्घ्रिः, -पादः<BR>—1 epithets of Yama.<BR>—2 of the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपादः|शीर्णपाद
शीर्ण + -अङ्घ्रिः, -पादः<BR>—1 epithets of Yama.<BR>—2 of the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपर्णम्
शीर्ण + -पर्णम् a withered leaf; (so शीर्णपत्रम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णपर्णः|शीर्णपर्ण
शीर्ण + -पर्णम् + .({@-र्णः@}) the <i>Nimba</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्णवृन्तः|शीर्णवृन्त|शीर्णवृंत|शीर्णवृन्तं
शीर्ण + -वृन्तः a water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्य
शीर्य <i>a.</i> Destructible, perishable; शीर्यो न हि शीर्यते Bṛ. Up. 3. 9. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्वि|शीर्व्वि|शीर्व्विः
शीर्वि <i>a.</i> [शॄ-क्विन् Uṇ. 4. 56]<BR>—1 Destructive, hurtful, noxious, injurious.<BR>—2 Savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षम्
शीर्षम् [शिरस्-पृषो˚ शीर्षादेशः, शॄ-क सुक् च वा]<BR>—1 The head; शीर्षे सर्पो देशान्तरे वैद्यः Karpūr.; Mu. 1. 21.<BR>—2 The black variety of aloe-wood.<BR>—3 The upper part, tip, top; पञ्चशीर्षा यवाश्चापि शतशीर्षाश्च शालयः Mb. 6. 3. 19.<BR>—4 The fore-part, front.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शीर्षावशेषः, शीर्षामयः, शीर्षोदयः, शीर्षघातिन्, शीर्षच्छेदः, शीर्षच्छेदिक, शीर्षच्छेद्य, शीर्षत्राणम्, शीर्षरक्षम्, शीर्षपट्टकः, शीर्षवर्तनम्, शीर्षशोकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षावशेषः
शीर्षम् + -अवशेषः the head only as the remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षामयः|शीर्षामय
शीर्षम् + -आमयः any affection or disease of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षोदयः|शीर्षोदय
शीर्षम् + -उदयः an epithet of the zodiacal signs, Gemini, Leo, Virgo,<BR> Libra, Scorpio, Aquarius, and Pisces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षघातिन्
शीर्षम् + -घातिन् an executioner; P. III. 2. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेदः|शीर्षच्छेद|शीर्षछेद
शीर्षम् + -छेदः decapitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेदिक|शीर्षच्छेदिकः
शीर्षम् + -छेदिक, -छेद्य <i>a.</i> fit to be beheaded, deserving death by<BR> decapitation; शीर्षच्छेद्यः स ते राम तं हत्वा जीवय द्विजम् U. 2. 8; R. 15. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षच्छेद्य|शीर्षच्छेद्यः|शीर्षछेद्य
शीर्षम् + -छेदिक, -छेद्य <i>a.</i> fit to be beheaded, deserving death by<BR> decapitation; शीर्षच्छेद्यः स ते राम तं हत्वा जीवय द्विजम् U. 2. 8; R. 15. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षत्राणम्
शीर्षम् + -त्राणम्, -रक्षम् a helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षरक्षम्
शीर्षम् + -त्राणम्, -रक्षम् a helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षपट्टकः|शीर्षपट्टक
शीर्षम् + -पट्टकः a turban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षवर्तनम्
शीर्षम् + -वर्तनम् submission to punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षशोकः|शीर्षशोक
शीर्षम् + -शोकः pain in the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षकः|शीर्षक|शीर्षकं
शीर्षकः An epithet of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षकम्
शीर्षकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 The head.<BR>—2 Skull.<BR>—3 A helmet.<BR>—4 A head-dress, (cap, hat &c.).<BR>—5 Verdict, judgment, judicial sentence.<BR>—6 The top of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षणी
शीर्षणी The head of a couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1557-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्यः|शीर्षण्य
शीर्षण्यः [शीर्षन्-यत्] <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clean or unentangled hair.<BR>—2 White.<BR>—3 Produced in the head.<BR>—4 Beneficial to the head.<BR>—5 Chief; यद्यच्छीर्षण्याचरितं तत्तदनुवर्तते लोकः Bhāg. 5. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्यम्
शीर्षण्यः + .{@-ण्यम्@}<BR>—1 A helmet; वरशीर्षण्यशीर्षाणः Śiva B. 14. 49.<BR>—2 A head-dress (hat, cap &c.).<BR>—3 Ved. A head-rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षन्
शीर्षन् <i>n.</i> The head. (This word has no forms for the first five<BR> inflections, and is optionally substituted for शिरस् or शीर्ष<BR> after acc. dual); नाभ्यां कोष्ठेष्ववस्थाप्य हृदुरःकण्ठशीर्षणि Bhāg. 4. 23. 14;<BR> Śiva B. 14. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील्
शील् I. €1 P. (शीलति)<BR>—1 To meditate, contemplate.<BR>—2 To serve, honour, worship. —3 To do, practise. ━II. €10 U. (शीलयति-ते)<BR>—1 To honour, worship; स शीलयन् देवयानीं कन्यां संप्राप्तयौवनाम्<BR> Mb. 1. 76. 25.<BR>—2 To practise repeatedly, exercise, study, think of, ponder over; श्रुतिशतमपि<BR> भूयः शीलितं भारतं वा Bv. 2. 35; शीलयन्ति मुनयः सुशीलताम् Ki. 13. 43.<BR>—3 To put on, wear; चल सखि कुञ्जं सतिमिरपुञ्जं शीलय नीलनिचोलम् Gīt. 5.<BR>—4 To go to, visit, frequent; यदनुगमनाय निशि गहनमपि शीलितम्<BR> Gīt. 7; स्मेरानना सपदि शीलय सौधमौलिम् Bv. 2. 4. ━<i>With</i> {@अनु@}<BR> To practise in imitation; एवं लीलानरवपुर्नृलोकमनुशीलयन् Bhāg. 10. 23. 36, 11. 3. 32.<BR>━{@अनु, परि@} to practise repeatedly, cultivate, think of; शश्वच्छ्रुतोऽसि<BR> मनसा परिशीलितोऽपि Rāj. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलः|शील
शीलः [शील्-अच्] A large serpent (the boa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलम्
शीलः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 Disposition, nature, character, tendency, inclination, habit, custom;<BR> सा तस्य शीलमाज्ञाय तस्माच्छापाच्च बिभ्यती Mb. 3. 136. 4; समानशीलव्यसनेषु<BR> सख्यम् Subhāṣ.; frequently at the end of comp. in the sense of ‘disposed or habituated to’<BR>, ‘indulging in’, ‘prone to’, ‘addicted to’, ‘attached to’<BR> &c.; as कलहशील ‘disposed to quarrel, quarrelsome’; भावनशील<BR> ‘disposed or apt to think’; so दान˚, मृगया˚, दया˚, पुण्य˚, आश्वासन˚ &c.<BR>—2 Conduct, behaviour in general.<BR>—3 Good disposition or character, good nature; शीलं परं भूषणम्<BR> Bh. 2. 82; Pt. 5. 2.<BR>—4 Virtue, morality, good conduct, virtuous life, chastity, uprightness;<BR> दौर्मन्त्र्यान्नृपतिर्विनश्यति … शीलं खलोपासनात् Bh. 2. 42, 39;<BR> तथा हि ते शीलमुदारदर्शने तपस्विनामप्युपदेशतां गतम् Ku. 5. 36;<BR> Ki. 11. 25; Pt. 1. 169; R. 10. 70.<BR>—5 Beauty, good form.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शीलाङ्क, शीलाढ्य, शीलखण्डनम्, शीलगुप्त, शीलघारिन्, शीलभाज्, शीलभ्रंशः, शीलवञ्चना, शीलवृत्त, शीलवृत्तिः, शीलवृद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलाङ्क
शीलः + -अङ्क <i>a.</i> characterized by virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलाढ्य
शीलः + -आढ्य <i>a.</i> most honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलखण्डनम्
शीलः + -खण्डनम् violation of morality or chastity; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलगुप्त
शीलः + -गुप्त <i>a.</i> cunning, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलघारिन्
शीलः + -घारिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलभाज्
शीलः + -भाज् <i>a.</i> honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलभ्रंशः|शीलभ्रंश
शीलः + -भ्रंशः loss of virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवञ्चना
शीलः + -वञ्चना violation of chastity; प्राप्तेयं शीलवञ्चना Mk. 1. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृत्त
शीलः + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> well-behaved, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृत्तम्
शीलः + -वृत्त + .({@-त्तम्@}) good or virtuous conduct, good breeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृत्तिः|शीलवृत्ति
शीलः + -वृत्तिः <i>f.</i> virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलवृद्ध
शीलः + -वृद्ध <i>a.</i> honourable, moral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलनम्
शीलनम् (शील्-ल्युट्)<BR>—1 Repeated practice, exercise, study, cultivation; वेदान्तशीलनमपि<BR> प्रमितिं करोति Bhagavaccharaṇa S. 20.<BR>—2 Constant application.<BR>—3 Honouring, serving.<BR>—4 Wearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलित|शीलितं
शीलित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Practised, exercised.<BR>—2 Put on.<BR>—3 Frequented, visited.<BR>—4 Skilled in.<BR>—5 Endowed with, possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलितम्
शीलित + .{@-तम्@} Practice, conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलिन्
शीलिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Virtuous, moral.<BR>—2 Used to, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवन्
शीवन् <i>m.</i> (शीङ्-क्वनिप् Uṇ. 4. 124) A large snake, boa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवलम्
शीवलम्<BR>—1 Moss.<BR>—2 Benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु €1 P. (शवति) To go; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शु
शु, शकम् <i>ind.</i> Quickly, swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकम्
शु, शकम् <i>ind.</i> Quickly, swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंशुमारः|शुंशुमार
शुंशुमारः A porpoise, (a corruption of शिशुमार q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्
शुक् €1 P. (शोकति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकः|शुक|शुकं
शुकः [शुक्-क]<BR>—1 A parrot; आत्मनो मुखदोषेण बध्यन्ते शुकसारिकाः Subhāṣ.; तुण्डैराताम्रकुटिलैः<BR> पक्षैर्हरितकोमलैः । त्रिवर्णराजिभिः कण्ठैरेते मञ्जुगिरः शुकाः ॥ Kāv. 2. 9.<BR>—2 The Śirīṣa tree.<BR>—3 N. of a son of Vyāsa. [He is said to have been born from the seed<BR> of <i>Vyāsa</i> which fell at the sight of the heavenly nymph Ghṛtācī<BR> while roaming over the earth in the form of a female parrot. Śuka was<BR> a born philosopher, and by his moral eloquence successfully resisted all<BR> the attempts of the nymph Rambhā to win him over to the path of love.<BR> He is said to have narrated the Bhāgavata Purāṇa to king Parīkṣit.<BR> His name has become proverbial for the most rigid observer of continence.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकम्
शुकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Cloth, clothes.<BR>—2 A helmet.<BR>—3 A turban.<BR>—4 The end or hem of a garment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुकादनः, शुककूटः, शुकतरुः, शुकद्रुमः, शुकतुण्डः, शुकतुण्डकम्, शुकदेवः, शुकनास, शुकनासिका, शुकपुच्छः, शुकपुष्पः, शुकप्रियः, शुकवल्लभः, शुकवाहः, शुकसप्ततिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकादनः|शुकादन
शुकः + -अदनः the pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुककूटः|शुककूट
शुकः + -कूटः a garland fixed over two pillars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकतरुः|शुकतरु
शुकः + -तरुः, -द्रुमः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकद्रुमः|शुकद्रुम
शुकः + -तरुः, -द्रुमः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकतुण्डः|शुकतुण्ड
शुकः + -तुण्डः a particular position of hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकतुण्डकम्
शुकः + -तुण्डकम् a kind of cinnabar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकदेवः|शुकदेव
शुकः + -देवः N. of Śuka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनास|शुकनासः
शुकः + -नास <i>a.</i> having an aquiline nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनासः|शुकनास
शुकः + -नास + .({@-सः@})<BR>—1 N. of the minister of Tārāpīḍa.<BR>—2 a particular ornament on a house.<BR>—3 N. of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकनासिका
शुकः + -नासिका an aquiline nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपुच्छः|शुकपुच्छ
शुकः + -पुच्छः sulphur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकपुष्पः|शुकपुष्प|शुकपुष्पं
शुकः + -पुष्पः, -प्रियः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकप्रिया
शुकः + -पुष्पः, -प्रियः + .({@-या@}) the rose-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकप्रियः|शुकप्रिय
शुकः + -पुष्पः, -प्रियः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवल्लभः|शुकवल्लभ
शुकः + -वल्लभः the pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकवाहः|शुकवाह
शुकः + -वाहः an epithet of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकसप्ततिः|शुकसप्तति
शुकः + -सप्ततिः N. of 70 stories related by a parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त <i>p. p.</i> [शुच्-क्त]<BR>—1 Bright, pure, clean; बलिषष्ठेन शुक्तेन दण्डेनाथापराधिनाम् Mb. 12. 71. 10.<BR>—2 Acid, sour; स्त्रीक्षीरं चैव वर्ज्यानि सर्वशुक्तानि चैव हि Ms. 5. 9, 2. 177.<BR>—3 Harsh, rough, hard, severe.<BR>—4 United, joined.<BR>—5 Deserted, lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तम्
शुक्त + .{@-क्तम्@}<BR>—1 Flesh<BR>—2 Sour gruel.<BR>—3 A kind of acid liquid.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुक्तपाकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तपाकः|शुक्तपाक
शुक्त + -पाकः acidity of stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तकम्
शुक्तकम् Sour eructation; न भुक्तमात्रे नाजीर्णे न वमित्वा न शुक्तके Ms. 4. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिः|शुक्ति
शुक्तिः <i>f.</i> [शुच्-क्तिन् Uṇ. 4. 191]<BR>—1 An oyster shell, pearl-oyster; पात्रविशेषन्यस्तं गुणान्तरं व्रजति<BR> शिल्पमाधातुः । जलमिव समुद्रशुक्तौ मुक्ताफलतां पयोदस्य ॥ M. 1. 6;<BR> Bh. 2. 67; R. 13. 17.<BR>—2 A conchshell.<BR>—3 A small shell, muscle.<BR>—4 A portion of the skull.<BR>—5 A curl of hair on a horseʼs breast (or neck); आवर्तिनः शुभफलप्रदशुक्तियुक्ताः<BR> Śi. 5. 4; see<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">Page1559-1</a>]<BR> Malli. thereon.<BR>—6 A kind of perfume.<BR>—7 A particular weight equal to two <i>Karṣas</i>.<BR>—8 Hemorrhoids.<BR>—9 A bone; मुनेः शुक्तिभिरुत्सिक्तो भगवत्तेजसान्वितः Bhāg. 6. 10. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुक्त्युद्भवम्, शुक्तिजम्, शुक्तिकर्ण, शुक्तिखलति, शुक्तिचूर्णकः, शुक्तिपुटम्, शुक्तिपेशी, शुक्तिबीजम्, शुक्तिवीजम्, शुक्तिमणिः, शुक्तिवधूः, शुक्तिस्पर्शः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1558-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त्युद्भवम्
शुक्तिः + -उद्भवम्, -जम् a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिजम्
शुक्तिः + -उद्भवम्, -जम् a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिकर्ण
शुक्तिः + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> shell-eared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिखलति
शुक्तिः + -खलति <i>a.</i> completely bald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिचूर्णकः|शुक्तिचूर्णक
शुक्तिः + -चूर्णकः a variety of inferior gems looking like an oyster shell; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिपुटम्
शुक्तिः + -पुटम्, -पेशी a pearl-oyster shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिपेशी
