शुङ्गाकर्मन्|शुङ्गाकर्म्मन्
शुङ्गा + -कर्मन् a ceremony connected with पुंसवन at which the शुङ्गा<BR> of the वट tree is used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुङ्गिन्|शुंगिन्
शुङ्गिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 The (Indian) fig-tree.<BR>—2 The <i>Plakṣa</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच् I. €1 P. (शोचति)<BR>—1 To be sorry, grieve for, bewail, mourn; अरोदीद्रावणोऽशोचीन्मोहं चाशिश्रियत्<BR> परम् Bk. 15. 71, 21. 6; मा शुचः संपदं दैवीमभिजातोऽसि पाण्डव Bg. 16. 5.<BR>—2 To regret, repent. ━II. €4 U. (शुच्यति-ते)<BR>—1 To be sorry or afflicted.<BR>—2 To be wet.<BR>—3 To shine.<BR>—4 To be pure or clean.<BR>—5 To decay; become fetid.<BR>—6 To brighten, illuminate.<BR>—7 To burn, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच्, शुचा <i>f.</i> [शुच्-क्विप् टाप् वा]<BR>—1 Grief, sorrow, affliction, distress; विकलकरणः पाण्डुछायः शुचा<BR> परिदुर्बलः U. 3. 22; कामं जीवति मे नाथ इति सा विजहौ शुचम्<BR> R. 12. 75, 8. 72; Me. 90; Ś. 4. 18.<BR>—2 (pl.) Tears; भूतलेऽनुपतन्त्यस्मिन् विना ते प्राणिनां शुचः Bhāg. 1. 17. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचा
शुच्, शुचा <i>f.</i> [शुच्-क्विप् टाप् वा]<BR>—1 Grief, sorrow, affliction, distress; विकलकरणः पाण्डुछायः शुचा<BR> परिदुर्बलः U. 3. 22; कामं जीवति मे नाथ इति सा विजहौ शुचम्<BR> R. 12. 75, 8. 72; Me. 90; Ś. 4. 18.<BR>—2 (pl.) Tears; भूतलेऽनुपतन्त्यस्मिन् विना ते प्राणिनां शुचः Bhāg. 1. 17. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचि|शुचिः
शुचि <i>a.</i> [शुच्-कि]<BR>—1 Clean, pure, clear; सकलहंसगुणं शुचि मानसम् Ki. 5. 13.<BR>—2 White; अथ हिमशुचिभस्मभूषितम् Ki. 18. 15.<BR>—3 Bright, resplendent; प्रभवति शुचिर्बिम्बोद्ग्राहे मणिर्न मृदां चयः U. 2. 4.<BR>—4 Virtuous, pious, holy, undefiled, unsullied; अथ तु वेत्सि शुचिव्रतमात्मनः<BR> Ś. 5. 27; पथः शुचेर्दर्शयितार ईश्वराः R. 3. 46; Ki. 5. 13.<BR>—5 Purified, cleansed, hallowed; सुतां तदीयां सुरभेः कृत्वा प्रतिनिधिं<BR> शुचिः R. 1. 81; Ms. 4. 71.<BR>—6 Honest, upright, faithful, true,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">Page1560-1</a>]<BR> guileless; सभायां वक्ति सामर्षः सावष्टम्भो नरः शुचिः Pt. 1. 200.<BR>—7 Correct, accurate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिः|शुचि
शुचि + .{@-चिः@}<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 Purity, purification.<BR>—3 Innocence, virtue, goodness, uprightness.<BR>—4 Correctness, accuracy.<BR>—5 The condition of a religious student.<BR>—6 A pure man.<BR>—7 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—8 The hot season; कीडन् परिवृतः स्त्रीभिर्ह्रदिनीमाविशच्छुचौ Bhāg. 4. 25. 44;<BR> उपययौ विदधन्नवमल्लिकाः शुचिरसौ चिरसौरभसंपदः<BR> Śi. 6. 22, 1. 58; R. 3. 3; Ku. 5. 20.<BR>—9 The months of<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Jyeṣṭha; यथोग्ररश्मिः शुचिशुक्रमध्यगः Mb. 8. 79. 78 and<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Āṣāḍha; शुक्रश्चित्रस्वनश्चैव शुचिमासं नयन्त्यमी Bhāg. 12. 11. 36.<BR>—10 A faithful or true friend.<BR>—11 The sun.<BR>—12 The moon.<BR>—13 Fire; शुचीनां हृदयं शुचिः Mb. 12. 193. 18.<BR>—14 The sentiment of love (शृङ्गार).<BR>—15 The planet Venus.<BR>—16 The Chitraka tree.<BR>—17 Acquittal.<BR>—18 An oblation made to fire at the first feeding of an infant.<BR>—19 N. of Śiva.<BR>—20 The <i>Arka</i> plant.<BR>—21 The sky; हंसः शुचिषद् Kaṭh. 5. 2.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुचिद्रुमः, शुचिप्रणी, शुचिमणिः, शुचिमल्लिका, शुचिमानस, शुचियन्त्रम्, शुचिरोचिस्, शुचिव्रत, शुचिश्रवस्, शुचिषद्, शुचिसमाचार, शुचिस्मित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1559-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिद्रुमः|शुचिद्रुम
शुचि + -द्रुमः the sacred fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिप्रणी
शुचि + -प्रणी <i>a.</i> sipping water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिमणिः|शुचिमणि
शुचि + -मणिः<BR>—1 a crystal.<BR>—2 a jewel worn on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिमल्लिका
शुचि + -मल्लिका a kind of jasmine (Arabian).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिमानस
शुचि + -मानस <i>a.</i> pure-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचियन्त्रम्
शुचि + -यन्त्रम् a machine through which fire-work is shot; वियदग्रमुदग्रमाविशन्<BR> शुचियन्त्रस्फुरितस्फुलिङ्गकाः Śāhendra. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिरोचिस्
शुचि + -रोचिस् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिव्रत
शुचि + -व्रत <i>a.</i> holy, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिश्रवस्
शुचि + -श्रवस् N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिषद्
शुचि + -षद् <i>a.</i> abiding in the path of virtue; स्वर्गापवर्गद्वाराय<BR> नित्यं शुचिषदे नमः Bhāg. 4. 24. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिसमाचार
शुचि + -समाचार <i>a.</i> maintaining pure practices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्मित
शुचि + -स्मित <i>a.</i> having a sweet or pleasant smile; शुचिस्मिता मध्यगता<BR> सुमध्यमा Ku. 5. 20; R. 8. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचित
शुचित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Grieved, sad.<BR>—2 Pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिष्मत्|शुचिष्मन्त्
शुचिष्मत् <i>a.</i> Bright. ━<i>m.</i> An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्
शुचिस् <i>n.</i> Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचीयति
शुचीयति Den. P., शुचीभू €1 P.<BR>—1 To become pure.<BR>—2 To be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्य्
शुच्य् €1 P. (शुच्यति)<BR>—1 To bathe, perform ablutions.<BR>—2 To squeeze, express (as juice).<BR>—3 To distil.<BR>—4 To churn; (these senses may belong to शुच् €4 P. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीरः|शुटीर
शुटीरः A hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर्यम्
शुटीर्यम् Valour, heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुठ्
शुठ् I. €1 P. (शोठति)<BR>—1 To be impeded or hindered.<BR>—2 To limp, be lame.<BR>—3 To resist. ━II. €10 U. (शोठयतिते) To be idle, lazy, or dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्टम्
शुण्टम् The hair under the arm-pit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठ्|शुंठ्
शुण्ठ् €1 P., €10 U. (शुण्ठति, शुण्ठयति-ते)<BR>—1 To purify.<BR>—2 To become dry; see शुठ् 1 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठिः|शुण्ठि|शुंठि|शुंठिः
शुण्ठिः, -ठी <i>f.</i>, शुण्ठयम्<BR> Dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ठी
शुण्ठिः, -ठी <i>f.</i>, शुण्ठयम्<BR> Dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्ड्|शुंड्
शुण्ड् €1 P. (शुण्डति)<BR>—1 To break.<BR>—2 To molest, vex, trouble, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डः|शुण्ड|शुंड|शुंडः
शुण्डः<BR>—1 The juice issuing from the temples of an elephant in rut.<BR>—2 An elephantʼs trunk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुण्डमूषिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डमूषिका
शुण्डः + -मूषिका the musk rat (Mar. चिचुंदरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डकः|शुण्डक|शुंडक|शुंडकः
शुण्डकः<BR>—1 Distiller.<BR>—2 A kind of military music or musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डा
शुण्डा<BR>—1 An elephantʼs trunk.<BR>—2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>—3 A tavern, dram-shop.<BR>—4 The stalk of the lotus.<BR>—5 A courtezan, harlot.<BR>—6 A bawd, procuress.<BR>—7 The chin; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुण्डादण्डः, शुण्डापानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डादण्डः|शुण्डादण्ड
शुण्डा + -दण्डः an elephantʼs trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डापानम्
शुण्डा + -पानम् a tavern, dram-shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डारः|शुण्डार|शुंडार|शुंडारः
शुण्डारः<BR>—1 A distiller.<BR>—2 An elephantʼs trunk or proboscis; शुण्डारः कलभेन यद्वदचले वत्सेन<BR> दोर्दण्डकः Mv. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डालः|शुण्डाल|शुंडाल|शुंडालः
शुण्डालः An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिका|शुंडिका
शुण्डिका See शुण्डा.<BR>—1 The uvula or soft palate.<BR>—2 A swelling of a gland (also शुण्डी in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिन्|शुंडिन्
शुण्डिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A distiller.<BR>—2 An elephant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुण्डिमूषिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुण्डिमूषिका|शुंडिमूषिका
शुण्डिन् + -मूषिका the musk-rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रिः|शुतुद्रि
शुतुद्रिः, -द्रूः <i>f.</i><BR> The river Sutlej; cf. शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रूः
शुतुद्रिः, -द्रूः <i>f.</i><BR> The river Sutlej; cf. शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुदि
शुदि <i>ind.</i> In the light fortnight; Inscr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुध्
शुध् €4 P. (शुध्यति, शुद्ध)<BR>—1 To become pure or purified; (fig. also); मृत्तोयैः शुध्यते शोध्यं<BR> नदी वेगेन शुध्यति । अद्भिर्गात्राणि शुध्यन्ति मनः सत्येन शुध्यति ॥ Ms. 5. 108-9.<BR>—2 To be auspicious, favourable, or eligible; तिथिरेव तावन्न शुध्यति Mu. 5.<BR>—3 To be made clear, have the doubts removed; न शुध्यति मेऽन्तरात्मा Mk. 8.<BR>—4 To be defrayed or cleared; व्ययः शुध्यति Pt. 5. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (शोधयति-ते)<BR>—1 To purify, cleanse, wash off.<BR>—2 To clear, pay off (as a debt).<BR>—3 To refine, filter.<BR>—4 To correct.<BR>—5 To acquit.<BR>—6 To examine, investigate, inquire into. ━<i>With</i> {@परि, वि, सम्@} to be<BR> purified; रघुपतिरपि जातवेदोविशुद्धां प्रगृह्य प्रियाम् R. 12. 104; Ms. 5. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्ध|शुद्धं|शुद्धः
शुद्ध <i>p. p.</i> [शुध्-क्त]<BR>—1 Pure, clean, purified; अन्तःशुद्धस्त्वमपि भविता वर्णमात्रेण कृष्णः Me. 51.<BR>—2 Holy, undefiled, chaste, innocent; अन्वमीयत शुद्धेति शान्तेन वपुषैव<BR> सा R. 15. 77, 14. 14.<BR>—3 White, bright.<BR>—4 Stainless, spotless.<BR>—5 Innocent, simple, guileless.<BR>—6<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Genuine, true.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Honest, upright.<BR>—7 Correct, faultless, upright.<BR>—8 Cleared, acquitted.<BR>—9 Mere, only; शुद्धं हि दैवमेवेदं हठेनैवास्ति पौरुषम् Mb. 12. 177. 12.<BR>—10 Simple, pure, unmixed (opp. मिश्र).<BR>—11 Unequalled.<BR>—12 Authorized.<BR>—13 Whetted, sharpened; जघान शुद्धेषुरमन्दकर्षी Bk. 2. 31.<BR>—14 Not nasal.<BR>—15 Unmitigated (as capital punishment); तडागभेदकं हन्यादप्सु शुद्धवधेन<BR> वा Ms. 9. 279.<BR>—16 Tried, examined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धः|शुद्ध|शुद्धं
शुद्ध + .{@-द्धः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 The bright fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धम्
शुद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@}<BR>—1 Anything pure.<BR>—2 The pure spirit.<BR>—3 Rock-salt.<BR>—4 Black pepper.<BR>—5 A house built generally of one material; namely wood, brick or stone<BR> etc.; द्रुमेणेष्टकया वापि दृशदाद्यैरथापि वा । एतेन सहितं गेहं शुद्धमित्यभिधीयते<BR> Kāmikāgama. 45. 21.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुद्धाद्वैतम्, शुद्धान्तः, शुद्धान्ता, शुद्धानुमानम्, शुद्धापह्नुतिः, शुद्धात्मन्, शुद्धाभ, शुद्धौदनः, शुद्धकर्मन्, शुद्धकोटिः, शुद्धचैतन्यम्, शुद्धजङ्घः, शुद्धजडः, शुद्धधी, शुद्धभाव, शुद्धमति, शुद्धपक्षः, शुद्धबटुकः, शुद्धबोध, शुद्धभाव, शुद्धवधः, शुद्धवंश्य, शुद्धविष्कम्भकः, शुद्धशुक्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धाद्वैतम्
शुद्ध + -अद्वैतम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-1" target="_blank">Page1561-1</a>]<BR> the अद्वैत philosophy in which there is unity of जीव and ब्रह्म<BR> without माया (<i>i. e.</i> शुद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1560-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्तः|शुद्धान्त|शुद्धांत
शुद्ध + -अन्तः a kingʼs female apartments, harem, seraglio; शुद्धान्तदुर्लभमिदं<BR> वपुराश्रमवासिनो यदि जनस्य Ś. 1. 17; Ku. 6. 52.<BR>—2 a kingʼs wife. ˚चारिन् <i>m.</i> an attendant in the harem, a chamberlain;<BR> U. 1. ˚पालकः, ˚रक्षकः a guard of the harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धान्ता|शुद्धांता
शुद्ध + -अन्ता a kingʼs wife, queen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धानुमानम्
