शुन्ध् €1. €10 U. (शुन्धति-ते, शुन्धयति-ते)<BR>—1 To be purified or cleansed.<BR>—2 To cleanse, purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्ध्युः|शुन्ध्यु|शुंध्युः
शुन्ध्युः (शुन्ध्-युः Uṇ. 3. 20)<BR>—1 Air, wind.<BR>—2 N. of Agni (Ved.). ━<i>f.</i> A mare. ━<i>a.</i> holy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्य|शुन्यं
शुन्य <i>a.</i> Empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्यम्
शुन्य + .{@-न्यम्@}<BR>—1 A number of bitches.<BR>—2 A cypher; (more properly शून्य q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुप्
शुप् A technical term used by Pāṇini for उ the sign of the eighth<BR> class of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् I. €1 Ā. (शोभते)<BR>—1 To shine, be splendid, look beautiful or handsome; सुष्ठु शोभसे एतेन<BR> विनयमाहात्म्येन U. 1; R. 8. 6.<BR>—2 To appear to advantage; सुखं हि दुःखान्यनुभूय शोभते Mk. 1. 10.<BR>—3 To suit, become, befit (with gen.); रामभद्र इत्येवोपचारः शोभते<BR> तातपरिजनस्य U. 1.<BR>—4 To be gay or happy.<BR>—5 To be victorious. ━II. €6 P. (शुभति) To shine; L. D. B. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (शोभयति-ते) To decorate, adorn, grace. ━<i>With</i> {@परि, वि@} to shine, look splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् <i>f.</i> Ved.<BR>—1 Beauty, splendour.<BR>—2 Radiance, lustre.<BR>—3 Happiness.<BR>—4 Victory.<BR>—5 An ornament.<BR>—6 An auspicious offering.<BR>—7 Water.<BR>—8 A brilliant chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ <i>a.</i> [शुभ्-क]<BR>—1 Shining, bright.<BR>—2 Beautiful, handsome; जङ्घे शुभे सृष्टवतस्तदीये Ku. 1. 35.<BR>—3 Auspicious, lucky, happy, fortunate.<BR>—4 Eminent, good, virtuous; येन केनाप्युपायेन शुभेनाप्यशुभेन वा उद्धरेद्दीनमात्मानम् Pt. 1. 358.<BR>—5 Learned, versed in the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभः|शुभ|शुभं
शुभ + .{@-भः@}<BR>—1 N. of a yoga; L. D. B.<BR>—2 The Almighty (अज); L. D. B.<BR>—3 Water. —4 A he-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभम्
शुभ + .{@-भम्@}<BR>—1 Auspiciousness, welfare, good fortune, happiness, good prosperity;<BR> प्रायः शुभं च विदधात्यशुभं च जन्तोः सर्वंकषा भगवती भवितव्यतैव Māl. 1. 23.<BR>—2 An ornament.<BR>—3 Water.<BR>—4 A kind of fragrant wood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुभाक्षः, शुभाङ्ग, शुभापाङ्गा, शुभाशुभम्, शुभाचार, शुभानना, शुभावह, शुभेतर, शुभोदर्क, शुभकर, शुभकर्मन्, शुभग, शुभगन्धकम्, शुभग्रहः, शुभजानि, शुभद, शुभदः, शुभदन्ती, शुभदर्श, शुभदर्शन, शुभमङ्गलम्, शुभलग्नः, शुभलग्नम्, शुभवार्ता, शुभवासनः, शुभशंसिन्, शुभसूत्रम्, शुभस्थली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाक्षः|शुभाक्ष
शुभ + -अक्षः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाङ्ग
शुभ + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाङ्गी|शुभांगी
शुभ + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गी@})<BR>—1 a handsome woman.<BR>—2 N. of Rati, wife of Cupid.<BR>—3 N. of the wife of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभापाङ्गा|शुभापांगा
शुभ + -अपाङ्गा a beautiful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाशुभम्
शुभ + -अशुभम् weal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">Page1562-1</a>]<BR> and woe, good and evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1561-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभाचार
शुभ + -आचार <i>a.</i> virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभानना
शुभ + -आनना a handsome woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभावह
शुभ + -आवह <i>a.</i> tending to welfare, conducive to good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभेतर
शुभ + -इतर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 evil, bad.<BR>—2 inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभोदर्क
शुभ + -उदर्क <i>a.</i> having a happy end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकर
शुभ + -कर <i>a.</i> auspicious, propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकर्मन्|शुभकर्म्मन्
शुभ + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 a virtuous act.<BR>—2 an honourable occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभग
शुभ + -ग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 elegant, graceful.<BR>—2 propitious, fortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभगन्धकम्
शुभ + -गन्धकम् gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभग्रहः|शुभग्रह
शुभ + -ग्रहः an auspicious planet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभजानि
शुभ + -जानि <i>a.</i> having a beautiful wife; P. V. 4. 134 com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभद|शुभदः
शुभ + -द <i>a.</i> auspicious; गङ्गाष्टकं पठति यः प्रयतः प्रभाते<BR> वाल्मीकिना विरचितं शुभदं मनुष्यः । Gaṅgāṣṭaka 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभदः|शुभद
शुभ + -दः the sacred fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभदन्ती|शुभदंती
शुभ + -दन्ती a woman with good teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभदर्श
शुभ + -दर्श, -दर्शन <i>a.</i> beautiful; ददर्श पम्पां शुभदर्शकाननाम्<BR> Rām. 3. 75. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभदर्शन
शुभ + -दर्श, -दर्शन <i>a.</i> beautiful; ददर्श पम्पां शुभदर्शकाननाम्<BR> Rām. 3. 75. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभमङ्गलम्
शुभ + -मङ्गलम् good luck, welfare; मङ्गलानि महाबाहो दिशन्तु शुभमङ्गलम्<BR> Rām. 2. 25. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभलग्नः|शुभलग्न
शुभ + -लग्नः, -लग्नम् a lucky or auspicious moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभलग्नम्
शुभ + -लग्नः, -लग्नम् a lucky or auspicious moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभवार्ता|शुभवार्त्ता
शुभ + -वार्ता good news.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभवासनः|शुभवासन
शुभ + -वासनः perfume for the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभशंसिन्
शुभ + -शंसिन् <i>a.</i> presaging good, indicative of auspiciousness; बभूव<BR> सर्वं शुभशंसि तत् क्षणम् R. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभसूत्रम्
शुभ + -सूत्रम् a maṅgala-sūtra worn by married ladies round their necks;<BR> सुदृशः शुभसूत्रबन्धनं कृतवान् शाहविभुस्तदा Śāhendra. 2. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभस्थली
शुभ + -स्थली<BR>—1 a hall in which sacrifices are performed.<BR>—2 an auspicious place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंयु|शुभंयुः
शुभंयु <i>a.</i> [शुभम् अस्यास्ति युस्] Auspicious, lucky, fortunate,<BR> blessed; अधिकं शुशुभे शुभंयुना द्वितयेन द्वयमेव संगतम् R. 8. 6; Bk. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंकर|शुभङ्कर|शुभङ्करः
शुभंकर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Auspicious.<BR>—2 Promoting happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंकरी
शुभंकर + .{@-री@} N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंभावुक
शुभंभावुक <i>a.</i> Decorated, ornamented, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभकः|शुभक
शुभकः Mustard seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभा
शुभा<BR>—1 Lustre, light.<BR>—2 Beauty.<BR>—3 Desire.<BR>—4 Yellow pigment.<BR>—5 The Śamī tree.<BR>—6 An assembly of gods.<BR>—7 Dūrvā grass.<BR>—8 Bamboo-manna.<BR>—9 The Priyaṅgu creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्र|शुभ्रं|शुभ्रः
शुभ्र <i>a.</i> [शुभ्-रक् Uṇ. 2. 13] Shining, bright, radiant; बलानि<BR> राज्ञां शुभ्राणि प्रहृष्टानि चकाशिरे Rām. 1. 18. 4.<BR>—2 White; पश्यति पित्तोपहतः शशिशुभ्रं शङ्खमपि पीतम् K. P. 10; R. 2. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रः|शुभ्र|शुभ्रं
शुभ्र + .{@-भ्रः@}<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 Sandal (said to be <i>n.</i>).<BR>—3 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रम्
शुभ्र + .{@-भ्रम्@}<BR>—1 Silver.<BR>—2 Talc.<BR>—3 Rocksalt.<BR>—4 Green vitriol.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुभ्रांशुः, शुभ्रकरः, शुभ्रदन्तिन्, शुभ्रभानुः, शुभ्ररश्मिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रांशुः|शुभ्रांशु
शुभ्र + -अंशुः, -करः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रकरः|शुभ्रकर
शुभ्र + -अंशुः, -करः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रदन्तिन्
शुभ्र + -दन्तिन् <i>m.</i> the elephant presiding over the north-west quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रभानुः|शुभ्रभानु
शुभ्र + -भानुः, -रश्मिः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्ररश्मिः|शुभ्ररश्मि
शुभ्र + -भानुः, -रश्मिः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रा
शुभ्रा<BR>—1 The Ganges.<BR>—2 A crystal.<BR>—3 Bamboo-manna.<BR>—4 Alum.<BR>—5 Sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रिः|शुभ्रि
शुभ्रिः [शुभ्-क्रिन् Uṇ. 4. 67]<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 An epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भ्|शुंभ्
शुम्भ् €1 P. (शुम्भति)<BR>—1 To shine; प्राणन्ति शुम्भन्ति पुनन्ति वै जगत् Bhāg. 10. 38. 12.<BR>—2 To speak.<BR>—3 To hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुम्भः|शुम्भ|शुंभ|शुंभः
