शुल्क्
शुल्क् €10 U. (शुल्कयति-ते)<BR>—1 To gain.<BR>—2 To pay, give.<BR>—3 To create.<BR>—4 To tell, narrate.<BR>—5 To leave, forsake, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कः|शुल्क|शुल्कं
शुल्कः, -ल्कम्<BR> [शुल्क्यते अतिसृज्यते कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 A toll, tax, customs, duty; particularly levied at ferries, passes,<BR> roads &c.; कः सुधीः संत्यजेद्भाण्डं शुल्कस्यैवातिसाध्वसात् H. 3. 125;<BR> Ms. 8. 159; Y. 2. 47.<BR>—2 Gain, profit.<BR>—3 Money advanced to ratify a bargain.<BR>—4 Purchase price (of a girl); money given to the parents of a bride;<BR> पीडितो दुहितृशुल्कसंस्थया R. 11. 38; न कन्यायाः पिता विद्वान् गृह्णीयाच्छुल्कमण्वपि<BR> Ms. 3. 51, 8. 204, 9. 93, 98; Pratimā 1. 15.<BR>—5 A nuptial present.<BR>—6 Marriage settlement or dowry.<BR>—7 Present given by the bride-groom to his bride.<BR>—8 A dog; Uṇ. 3. 42.<BR>—9 Price, value.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शुल्काध्यक्षः, शुल्कखण्डनम्, शुल्कग्राहक, शुल्कग्राहिन्, शुल्कदः, शुल्कशाला, शुल्कस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1562-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

