शुष्
शुष् €4 P. (शुष्यति, शुष्क)<BR>—1 To be dried, become dry or parched up; तृषा शुष्यत्यास्ये पिबति सलिलं<BR> स्वादु सुरभि Bh. 3. 92.<BR>—2 To be withered.<BR>—3 To languish, become emaciated; अपि स्थाणुवदासीनः शुष्यन् परिगतः<BR> क्षुधा Pt. 1. 49.<BR>—4 To be afflicted or distressed. ━<i>Caus.</i> (शोषयति-ते)<BR>—1 To dry up, wither, parch; न शोषयति मारुतः Bg. 2. 23.<BR>—2 To emaciate.<BR>—3 To destroy.<BR>—4 To extinguish.<BR>—5 To drain, suck up, absorb.<BR>—6 To exhaust, empty. ━<i>With</i> {@उद्, परि@}<BR>—1 to be dried up, dry up; सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि मुखं च पीरशुष्यति<BR> Bg. 1. 29; स च विह्वलसत्त्वसंकुलः परिशुष्यन्नभवन् महाह्रदः Bk. 10. 42.<BR>—2 to pine, decay, wither; इमाः शून्यमया वाचः शुष्यमाणेन भाषिताः<BR> Rām. 3. 55. 36; अस्मत्कृते च परिशुष्यति काचिदन्या Bh. 2. 2.<BR>━{@वि, सम्@} to be dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1563-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषः|शुष
शुषः, शुषी<BR>—1 Drying, drying up.<BR>—2 A hole in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1563-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषी
शुषः, शुषी<BR>—1 Drying, drying up.<BR>—2 A hole in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1563-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

