शृङ्गाटकः|शृङ्गाटक|शृंगाटक|शृङ्गाटकं|शृंगाटकः
शृङ्गाटकः A mountain with three peaks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाटकम्
शृङ्गाटकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A place where four roads meet; तां शून्यशृङ्गाटकवेश्मरथ्यां Rām. 2. 71. 45;<BR> Mb. 4. 68. 25; इमां शृङ्गाटकस्थां विटसभां प्रविशामि Avimāraka 3;<BR> Bhāg. 9. 10. 17.<BR>—2 A kind of pastry.<BR>—3 A door; ‘शृङ्गाटकं भवेद् द्वारि कण्टके च चतुष्पथे’ इति मेदिनी;<BR> Bhāg. 8. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाटिका
शृङ्गाटिका A cross-road; Daṇḍaviveka, G. O. S. 52, p. 297.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारः|शृङ्गार|शृंगार|शृङ्गारं|शृंगारः
शृङ्गारः [शृङ्गं कामोद्रेकमृच्छत्यनेन ऋ-अण्]<BR>—1 The sentiment of love or sexual passion, the erotic sentiment (the<BR> first of the eight or nine sentiments in poetical compositions; it is of<BR> two kinds:− संभोगशृङ्गार and विप्रलम्भशृङ्गार qq. vv.);<BR> शृङ्गारः सखि मूर्तिमानिव मधौ मुग्धो हरिः क्रीडति Gīt. 1; (it is<BR> thus defined:− पुंसः स्त्रियां स्त्रियाः पुंसि संभोगं प्रति या स्पृहा ।<BR> स शृङ्गार इति ख्यातः क्रीडारत्यादिकारकः ॥ See S. D. 210 also).<BR>—2 Love, passion, sexual love; शृङ्गारैकरसः स्वयं नु मदनो मासो<BR> नु पुष्पाकरः V. 1. 10.<BR>—3 A dress suited to amorous interviews, an elegant dress.<BR>—4 Coition, sextual union.<BR>—5 Marks made with redlead on the body of an elephant; वर्षन्तः शममानयन्नुपलसच्छृङ्गारलेखायुधाः Śi. 17. 69.<BR>—6 A mark in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारम्
शृङ्गारः + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Cloves.<BR>—2 Red-lead.<BR>—3 Undried ginger.<BR>—4 A fragrant powder for the dress or body.<BR>—5 A gallochum.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शृङ्गारचेष्टा, शृङ्गारभाषितम्, शृङ्गारभूषणम्, शृङ्गारयोनिः, शृङ्गाररसः, शृङ्गारलज्जा, शृङ्गारविधिः, शृङ्गारवेशः, शृङ्गारसहायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारचेष्टा|शृंगारचेष्टा
शृङ्गारः + -चेष्टा an amorous or love-gesture; शृङ्गारचेष्टा विविधा बभूवुः R. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारभाषितम्
शृङ्गारः + -भाषितम् amorous talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारभूषणम्
शृङ्गारः + -भूषणम् red-lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारयोनिः|शृङ्गारयोनि|शृंगारयोनि
शृङ्गारः + -योनिः an epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गाररसः|शृङ्गाररस|शृंगाररस
शृङ्गारः + -रसः the sentiment of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारलज्जा
शृङ्गारः + -लज्जा shame or modesty caused by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारविधिः|शृङ्गारविधि|शृंगारविधि
शृङ्गारः + -विधिः, -वेशः a dress suited to amorous interviews and other purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारवेशः|शृङ्गारवेश|शृंगारवेश
शृङ्गारः + -विधिः, -वेशः a dress suited to amorous interviews and other purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारसहायः|शृङ्गारसहाय|शृंगारसहाय
शृङ्गारः + -सहायः an assistant in love-affairs, a confidant of the hero<BR> of a play; cf. नर्मसचिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारकः|शृङ्गारक|शृङ्गारकं|शृंगारकः
शृङ्गारकः Love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारकम्
शृङ्गारकः + .{@-कम्@} Red-lead. ━<i>a.</i> Horned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारित|शृंगारित
शृङ्गारित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Impassioned, affected by love.<BR>—2 Reddened.<BR>—3 Adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गारिन्|शृंगारिन्
शृङ्गारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Amorous, impassioned, enamoured.<BR>—2 Relating to love.<BR>—3 Stained with red-lead. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An impassioned lover.<BR>—2 A ruby.<BR>—3 An elephant.<BR>—4 Dress, decoration.<BR>—5 The betel-nut tree.<BR>—6 A preparation of betel-leaves and pieces of areca-nut; see ताम्बूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिः|शृङ्गि|शृंगि|शृंगिः
शृङ्गिः Gold for ornaments. ━<i>f.</i> The sheat-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिकम्
शृङ्गिकम् A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिका
शृङ्गिकम् + .{@-का@}<BR>—1 A kind of birch tree.<BR>—2 A kind of missile or catapult; लोहचर्मवती चापि साग्निः सगुडशृङ्गिका Mb. 3. 15. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिणः|शृङ्गिण|शृंगिण|शृंगिणः
शृङ्गिणः A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिणी
शृङ्गिणी<BR>—1 A cow.<BR>—2 The Arabian jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गिन्|शृंगिन्
शृङ्गिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शृङ्गमस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>—1 Horned.<BR>—2 Crested, peaked. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A mountain.<BR>—2 An elephant.<BR>—3 A ram.<BR>—4 A tree.<BR>—5 N. of Śiva.<BR>—6 N. of one of Śivaʼs attendants; शृङ्गी भृङ्गी रिटिस्तुण्डी Ak.<BR>—7 A bull; शङ्गयग्निदंष्ट्रयसिजलद्विजकण्टकेभ्यः Bhāg. 10. 8. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गी|शृंगी
शृङ्गी<BR>—1 Gold used for ornaments.<BR>—2 A kind of medicinal root.<BR>—3 A kind of poison.<BR>—4 The sheat-fish.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शृङ्गीकनकम्, शृङ्गीविषम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गीकनकम्
शृङ्गी + -कनकम् gold used for ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृङ्गीविषम्
शृङ्गी + -विषम् a kind of plant having a poisonous root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणिः|शृणि
शृणिः <i>f.</i> A hook for pricking an elephant, a goad; मदान्धकरिणां<BR> दर्पोपशान्त्यै शृणिः H. 2. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृत|शृतं
शृत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Cooked; अयं सर्वः समस्ताङ्गः शृतः कृष्णमृगो मया Rām. 2. 56. 28<BR> (some editions give श्रित for शृत).<BR>—2 Boiled (water, milk &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शृतपाक, शृतशीत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृतपाक
शृत + -पाक <i>a.</i> thoroughly cooked or boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृतशीत
शृत + -शीत <i>a.</i> boiled and cooked again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृदरः
शृदरः A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध्
शृध् I. €1 Ā. (but Paras. also in the Second Future, Aorist and Conditional)<BR> (शर्धते) To break wind downwards. ━II. €1 U. (शर्धति-ते)<BR>—1 To moisten, wet.<BR>—2 To cut off. ━III. €10 U. (शर्धयति-ते)<BR>—1 To strive.<BR>—2 To take, grasp.<BR>—3 To insult (as by breaking wind), mock, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृद्ध
शृद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Expelled from the body (as wind).<BR>—2 Moistened, wetted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधुः|शृधु
शृधुः<BR>—1 Intellect (बुद्धि).<BR>—2 The anus, also शृधू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शॄ
शॄ €9 P. (शृणाति, शीर्ण)<BR>—1 To tear asunder, tear to pieces;<BR>(-डिण्डीरपिण्ड)प्रायासृग्भारघोरं पशुमिव परशुः पर्वशस्त्वां<BR> शृणातु Mv. 3. 32.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure.<BR>—3 To kill, destroy; वनाश्रयाः कस्य मृगाः परिग्रहाः शृणाति यस्तान्<BR> प्रसभेन तस्य ते Ki. 14. 13. ━<i>Pass.</i> (शीर्यते)<BR>—1 To be shattered.<BR>—2 To wither, decay, waste away. ━<i>With</i> {@अव@} or {@वि@} to seize<BR> away. ━(<i>Pass.</i>) to fade or wither; मूर्ध्नि वा सर्वलोकस्य विशीर्येत<BR> वनेऽथवा Bh. 2. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेक्
शेक् €1 Ā. To go; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेकुः|शेकु
शेकुः A kind of grass; P. VIII. 3. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरः|शेखर|शेखरं
शेखरः<BR>—1 A crest, chaplet, tuft, a garland of flowers worn on the head; कपालि<BR> वा स्यादथवेन्दुशेखरम् Ku. 5. 78, 7. 42; नवकरनिकरेण स्पष्टबन्धूकसूनस्तबकरचितमेते<BR> शेखरं बिभ्रतीव Śi. 11. 46, 4. 50; मगधदेशशेखरीभूता पुष्पपुरी<BR> नाम नगरी Dk.; शीर्षे च शेखरको नित्यम् Nāg. 3. 2.<BR>—2 A diadem, crown.<BR>—3 A peak, summit.<BR>—4 The best or most distinguished of a class (at the end of comp.).<BR>—5 A kind of <i>Dhruva</i> or burden of a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1566-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

