शेपः + -स्तम्भः morbid rigidity and erection of the penis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपालः|शेपाल
शेपालः, -लम्<BR> Vitex Negundo (Mar. निर्गुंडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपालम्
शेपालः, -लम्<BR> Vitex Negundo (Mar. निर्गुंडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालिः|शेफालि
शेफालिः, -ली, शेफालिका <i>f.</i><BR> A kind of plant; शेफालिकाकुसुमगन्धमनोहराणि Ṛs. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफाली
शेफालिः, -ली, शेफालिका <i>f.</i><BR> A kind of plant; शेफालिकाकुसुमगन्धमनोहराणि Ṛs. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालिका
शेफालिः, -ली, शेफालिका <i>f.</i><BR> A kind of plant; शेफालिकाकुसुमगन्धमनोहराणि Ṛs. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेमुषी
शेमुषी<BR>—1 Intellect, understanding; स्वशेमुषीविशेषेण वशीकृतमहीतलम् Śiva B. 5. 3.<BR>—2 Resolve, purpose, intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेरुः
शेरुः [शी-उर Uṇ. 4. 112] Dozing, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेल्
शेल् €1 P. (शेलति)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेलुः|शेलु
शेलुः Cordia Myxa (Mar. भोकर); Ms. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेव्
शेव् €1 Ā. To worship; see सेव्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवः|शेव
शेवः [शुक्रपाते सति शेते, शी-वन् Uṇ. 1. 152, 154]<BR>—1 The penis.<BR>—2 A snake.<BR>—3 Height, elevation.<BR>—4 Happiness.<BR>—5 Wealth, treasure.<BR>—6 An epithet of Agni.<BR>—7 Of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवम्
शेवः + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 The penis (also शेवा).<BR>—2 Happiness.<BR>—3 Hail! (exclamation addressed to deities).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शेवधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवधिः|शेवधि
शेवः + -धिः<BR>—1 a valuable treasure; जानाम्यहं शेवधिरित्यनित्यम् Kaṭh. 2. 10;<BR> विद्या ब्राह्मणमेत्याह शेवधिस्तेऽस्मि रक्ष माम् Ms. 2. 144; सर्वे<BR> कामाः शेवधिर्जीवितं वा स्त्रीणां भर्ता धर्मदाराश्च पुंसाम् Māl. 6. 18;<BR> नाशेवधिर्बन्धुषु नाप्यदाता Bu. C. 2. 11.<BR>—2 one of the 9 treasures of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवलम्
शेवलम् [शी-विच् तथा भूतः सन् वलते वल्-अच् Tv.]<BR>—1 The green moss-like substance growing on the surface of water.<BR>—2 A kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवलिनी
शेवलिनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेवाल|शेवालं
शेवाल See शेवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेष|शेषं|शेषः
शेष <i>a.</i> [शिष्-अच्] Remaining, rest, all the other; न्यषेधि<BR> शेषोऽप्यनुयायिवर्गः R. 2. 4, 4. 64, 10. 29; Me. 30, 89; रम्भे निर्वर्त्यतां<BR> शेषो विधिः V. 5; शेषान् मासान् गमय चतुरो लोचने मीलयित्वा Me. 110<BR> (v. l.); Ms. 3. 47; Ku. 2. 44; oft. at the end of comp. in this sense;<BR> भक्षितशेष, आलेख्यशेष &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषः|शेष|शेषं
शेष + .{@-षः, -षम्@}<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Remainder, rest, residue; ऋणशेषोऽग्निशेषश्च व्याधिशेषस्तथैव<BR> च । पुनश्च वर्धते यस्मात्तस्माच्छेषं न कारयेत् ॥ Cāṇ. 40; अध्वशेष<BR> Me. 40; प्रतिकारविधानमायुषः सति शेषे हि फलाय कल्पते R. 8. 40;<BR> so शेषे वयसः समागतो मृत्युः Bv. 4. 30; त्रिभागशेष Ku. 5. 57;<BR> वाक्यशेषः V. 3 &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>)<BR>—1 Surplus, balance.<BR>—2 Anything left out or omitted to be said; (इति शेषः is often used<BR> by commentators in supplying an ellipsis or words necessary to complete<BR> the construction).<BR>—3 Escape, salvation, respite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषम्
शेष + .{@-षः, -षम्@}<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Remainder, rest, residue; ऋणशेषोऽग्निशेषश्च व्याधिशेषस्तथैव<BR> च । पुनश्च वर्धते यस्मात्तस्माच्छेषं न कारयेत् ॥ Cāṇ. 40; अध्वशेष<BR> Me. 40; प्रतिकारविधानमायुषः सति शेषे हि फलाय कल्पते R. 8. 40;<BR> so शेषे वयसः समागतो मृत्युः Bv. 4. 30; त्रिभागशेष Ku. 5. 57;<BR> वाक्यशेषः V. 3 &c.<BR>——(<i>b</i>)<BR>—1 Surplus, balance.<BR>—2 Anything left out or omitted to be said; (इति शेषः is often used<BR> by commentators in supplying an ellipsis or words necessary to complete<BR> the construction).<BR>—3 Escape, salvation, respite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषः|शेष|शेषं
शेष + .{@-षः@}<BR>—1 Result, effect.<BR>—2 End, termination, conclusion.<BR>—3 Death, destruction.<BR>—4 N. of a celebrated serpent,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">Page1567-2</a>]<BR> said to have one thousand heads, and represented as forming the couch<BR> of Viṣṇu or as supporting the entire world on his head; किं शेषस्य<BR> भरव्यथा न वपुषि क्ष्मां न क्षिपत्येष यत् Mu. 2. 18; Ku. 3. 13; R. 10. 13.<BR>—5 N. of Balarāma (supposed to be an incarnation of Śeṣa).<BR>—6 An elephant.<BR>—7 Subsidiary अङ्ग; something which is declared as being subservient<BR> to something else; शेषः परार्थत्वात् MS. 3. 1. 2 (यस्तु अत्यन्तं<BR> परार्थस्तं वयं शेष इति ब्रूमः ŚB. on MS.); शेषो हि सादनम् ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 76.<BR>—8 Favour (प्रसाद); ‘शेषः संकर्षणे वधे अनन्ते ना प्रसादे च’<BR> इति मेदिनी; नैवंशीलाः शेषमिहाप्नुवन्ति Mb. 1. 197. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषा
शेष + .{@-षा@} The remains of flowers or other offerings made to an idol<BR> and distributed among the worshippers as a holy relique; तस्यै स्त्रियस्ताः<BR> प्रददुः शेषां युयुजुराशिषः Bhāg. 10. 53. 50; तथेति शेषामिव भर्तुराज्ञामादाय<BR> मूर्ध्ना मदनः प्रतस्थे Ku. 3. 22; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषम्
शेष + .{@-षम्@} The remnants of food, remains of an offering. (शेषे is<BR> used adverbially in the sense of<BR>—1 at last, finally.<BR>—2 in other cases; as in शेषे षष्टी.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: शेषान्नम्, शेषावस्था, शेषकालः, शेषजातिः, शेषपतिः, शेषभागः, शेषभोजनम्, शेषरात्रिः, शेषरूपिन्, शेषशयनः, शेषशायिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषान्नम्
शेष + -अन्नम् leavings of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषावस्था
शेष + -अवस्था old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषकालः|शेषकाल
शेष + -कालः the time of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषजातिः|शेषजाति
शेष + -जातिः <i>f.</i> assimilation of residues; (in alg.) reduction of<BR> fractions of residues.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषपतिः|शेषपति
शेष + -पतिः a manager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभागः|शेषभाग
शेष + -भागः the remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषभोजनम्
शेष + -भोजनम् the eating of leavings; गृहस्थस्य … … त्यागः<BR> शेषभोजनम् Kau. A. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरात्रिः|शेषरात्रि
शेष + -रात्रिः the last watch of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषरूपिन्
शेष + -रूपिन् <i>a.</i> appearing to be secondary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषशयनः|शेषशयन
शेष + -शयनः, -शायिन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेषशायिन्
शेष + -शयनः, -शायिन् <i>m.</i> epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेष्य
शेष्य <i>a.</i> To be ignored, neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्य|शैक्यः
शैक्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Suspended in a loop.<BR>—2 Pointed, peaked; शैक्यां व्यालीमिवात्युग्रां वज्रकल्पामयोमयीम् Mb. 9. 11. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्यः|शैक्य
शैक्य + .{@-क्यः@}<BR>—1 A kind of sling (Mar. कावड, शिंकें); धारयन्ति महीं द्यां च<BR> शैक्यो वागमृतं तथा Mb. 12. 342. 17.<BR>—2 A pot kept in such sling; शैक्यं रुक्मसहस्रस्य बहुरत्नविभूषितम्<BR> Mb. 2. 49. 27 (see Nīlakaṇṭha com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्यायसम्
शैक्य + .{@-अयसम्@} Damasked steel; शक्रदेवाय चिक्षेप सर्वशैक्यायसीं<BR> गदाम् Mb. 6. 54. 24; शैक्यायसानि वर्माणि कांस्यानि च समन्ततः 7. 119. 42<BR> (com. शैक्यायसानि शोणितायोमयानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्षः|शैक्ष
शैक्षः [शिक्षां वेत्त्यधीते वा अण्]<BR>—1 A student who studies Śikṣā or the science of pronunciation, one<BR> who has just entered upon the study of the Vedas.<BR>—2 (Hence) A novice, tyro. ━<i>a.</i> Well familiar with the studies or sciences;<BR> expert; Mb. 6. 97. 28 (com. शैक्षं शस्त्रादिशिक्षासंपन्नम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्षिकः|शैक्षिक
शैक्षिकः One skilled in Śikṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैक्ष्यम्
शैक्ष्यम् Learning, proficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखः|शैख
शैखः The offspring of an outcaste (व्रात्य) Brāhmaṇa; Ms. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखरिकः|शैखरिक
शैखरिकः, -रेयः<BR> The Apāmārga tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखरेयः|शैखरेय
शैखरिकः, -रेयः<BR> The Apāmārga tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैखिन
शैखिन <i>a.</i> Relating to a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैख्य
शैख्य <i>a.</i> Pointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1567-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैघ्रम्
शैघ्रम्, शैघ्र्यम् [शीघ्र-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Quickness, rapidity.<BR>—2 The equation of the second epicycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैघ्र्यम्
शैघ्रम्, शैघ्र्यम् [शीघ्र-ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Quickness, rapidity.<BR>—2 The equation of the second epicycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैत्यम्
शैत्यम् [शीत-ष्यञ्] Cold, coldness, frigidity; शैत्यं हि यत्<BR> सा प्रकृतिर्जलस्य R. 5. 54; Ku. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैथिलिक
शैथिलिक <i>a.</i> Loose, lax, idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैथिल्यम्
शैथिल्यम् [शिथिलस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Looseness, laxity, relaxation of rule &c.<BR>—2 Slackness.<BR>—3 Dilatoriness, inattention.<BR>—4 Weakness; cowardice.<BR>—6 Unsteadiness.<BR>—6 Vacancy (of gaze).<BR>—7 Negligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैनेयः|शैनेय
