शैव्यः|शैव्य
शैव्यः<BR>—1 N. of one of the four horses of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>—2 N. of a king and warrior in the Pāṇḍava army.<BR>—3 A horse (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशवम्
शैशवम् [शिशोर्भावः अण्] Childhood, infancy (period under sixteen);<BR> शशैवात् प्रमृति पोषितां प्रियाम् U. 1. 45; शैशवेऽभ्यस्तविद्यानाम् R. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिर|शैशिरः
शैशिर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [शिशिर-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the cold or dewy (शिशिर) season; यस्य वै शैशिरे<BR> काले तडागे सलिलं भवेत् Mb. 13. 58. 13.<BR>—2 Icy, covered with ice (हिममय); ततोऽहं वचनात्तस्य गिरिमारुह्य<BR> शैशिरम् Mb. 3. 167. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1568-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिरः|शैशिर
