श्याव + -दत्, -दन्त, -दन्तक <i>a.</i> brown-toothed; तथा सूर्याभिनिर्मुक्तः<BR> कुनखी श्यावदन्नपि Mb. 12. 34. 3; प्रेष्यो ग्रामस्य राज्ञश्च कुनखी<BR> श्यावदन्तकः Ms. 3. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येत|श्येतः
श्येत <i>a.</i> (-ता or -नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> White; ज्योत्स्नाशङ्कामिह वितरति हंसश्येनी Ki. 5. 31<BR> (com. तकारस्य च नकारः-श्येतशब्दान् ङीप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येतः|श्येत
श्येत + .{@-तः@} The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1572-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनः|श्येन
श्येनः [श्यै-इनन् Uṇ. 2. 45]<BR>—1 The white colour.<BR>—2 Whiteness.<BR>—3 A hawk, falcon.<BR>—4 Violence.<BR>—5 Ved. A horse.<BR>—6 A kind of array in battle.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्येनावपातः, श्येनकपोतीय, श्येनकरणम्, श्येनकरणिका, श्येनचित्, श्येनजीविन्, श्येनपातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनावपातः|श्येनावपात
श्येनः + -अवपातः the swoop of a hawk; श्येनावपातचकिता वनवर्तिकेव Māl. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनकपोतीय
श्येनः + -कपोतीय <i>a.</i> (from Śibi story) sudden (calamity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनकरणम्
श्येनः + -करणम्, -करणिका<BR>—1 burning on a separate funeral pile.<BR>—2 a hawk-like, <i>i. e.</i> rash and desperate, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनकरणिका
श्येनः + -करणम्, -करणिका<BR>—1 burning on a separate funeral pile.<BR>—2 a hawk-like, <i>i. e.</i> rash and desperate, act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनचित्
श्येनः + -चित्, -जीविन् <i>m.</i> falconer; Ms. 3. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनजीविन्
श्येनः + -चित्, -जीविन् <i>m.</i> falconer; Ms. 3. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनपातः|श्येनपात
श्येनः + -पातः the swoop of a hawk or eagle; वडवे इव संयुक्ते श्येनपाते<BR> दिवौकसाम् Mb. 3. 133. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यै
श्यै €1 Ā. (श्यायते, श्यान, शीत or शीन)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To be congealed or coagulated.<BR>—3 To dry up, wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनंपाता|श्यैनम्पाता
श्यैनंपाता [श्येनस्य पातोऽत्र अण् मुम् च] Hawking, hunting, chase;<BR> इह विहरणैः श्यैनंपातां रवेरवधारयन् N. 19. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनिकशास्त्रम्
श्यैनिकशास्त्रम् The science of hunting; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योणाकः|श्योणाक
श्योणाकः, श्योनाकः N. of a tree, Bignonia Indica (Mar. दिंडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योनाकः|श्योनाक
श्योणाकः, श्योनाकः N. of a tree, Bignonia Indica (Mar. दिंडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रङ्क्|श्रंक्
श्रङ्क् €1 Ā. (श्रङ्कते) To go, creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रङ्ग्|श्रंग्
श्रङ्ग् €1 P. (श्रङ्गति) To go, move, creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रण्
श्रण् €1 P., €10 U. (श्रणति, श्राणयति-ते) To give, give away,<BR> bestow (usually with वि); विश्राणयन्तो रत्नानि विविधानि बहूनि च<BR> Rām. 4. 25. 31; निःशेषविश्राणितकोशजातम् R. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रत्
श्रत् <i>ind.</i> A prefix used with the root धा; see श्रद्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ्
श्रथ् I. €1. €9 P. (श्रथति, श्रथ्नाति) To hurt, injure, kill.<BR>━II. €1 P., €10 U. (श्रथति, श्राथयति-ते)<BR>—1 To hurt, kill.<BR>—2 To untie, loosen, liberate, release. ━III. €10 U. (श्रथयति-ते)<BR>—1 To make efforts, be occupied or busy.<BR>—2 To be weak or infirm.<BR>—3 To be glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथनम्
श्रथनम्<BR>—1 Killing, destruction.<BR>—2 Untying, loosening, release.<BR>—3 Effort, exertion.<BR>—4 Tying, binding.<BR>—5 Delighting repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्दधान|श्रद्दधानः
श्रद्दधान <i>a.</i> Having faith, trustful, believing; अज्ञश्चाश्रद्दधानश्च<BR> संशयात्मा विनश्यति Bg. 4. 40; Ms. 7. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रहानम्
श्रहानम् Faith, belief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धा
श्रद्धा €3 U.<BR>—1 To confide, believe, put faith in (with acc. of thing); कः श्रद्धास्यति<BR> भूतार्थम् Mk. 3. 24; कामिन्यः श्रदधुरनार्जवं नरेषु Śi. 8. 11, 9. 69;<BR> U. 7. 6; श्रद्दधे त्रिदशगोपमात्रके दाहशक्तिमिव कृष्णवर्त्मनि R. 11. 42.<BR>—2 To consent, assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्ध <i>a.</i> Believing, trusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धा
श्रद्धा<BR>—1 Trust, faith, belief, confidence.<BR>—2 Belief in divine revelation, religious faith; श्रद्धा वित्तं विधिश्चेति<BR> त्रितयं तत्समागतम् Ś. 7. 29; R. 2. 16; अयतिः श्रद्धयोपेतो योगात्<BR> चलितमानसः Bg. 6. 37, 7. 21, 17. 3.<BR>—3 Sedateness, composure<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">Page1573-2</a>]<BR> of mind.<BR>—4 Intimacy, familiarity.<BR>—5 Respect, reverence.<BR>—6 Strong or vehement desire; तथापि वैचित्र्यरहस्यलुब्धाः श्रद्धां<BR> विधास्यन्ति सचेतसोऽत्र Vikr. 1. 13; युद्धश्रद्धापुलकित इव प्राप्तसख्यः<BR> करेण Mu. 6. 18.<BR>—7 The longing of a pregnant woman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रद्धाजाड्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धाजाड्यम्
श्रद्धा + -जाड्यम् blind faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धापनम्
श्रद्धापनम् A means of inspiring faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालु|श्रद्धालुः
श्रद्धालु <i>a.</i> [श्रद्धा-आलुच्]<BR>—1 Believing, full of faith,<BR>—2 Desirous, longing or wishing for (anything); अकालकुसुमसमुद्गमश्रद्धालुना<BR> भर्त्रा Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालुः|श्रद्धालु
श्रद्धालु + .{@-लुः@} <i>f.</i> A pregnant woman longing for anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धेय
श्रद्धेय <i>a.</i> Trustworthy; श्रद्धेया विप्रलब्धारः Ki. 11. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थ्|श्रंथ्
श्रन्थ् I. €1 Ā. (श्रन्थते)<BR>—1 To be weak.<BR>—2 To be loose or relaxed.<BR>—3 To loosen, relax. ━II. €9 P. (श्रथ्नाति)<BR>—1 To loosen, liberate, release.<BR>—2 To delight repeatedly. ━III. €1. €10 P. To bind together, to compose; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थः|श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रंथः
श्रन्थः<BR>—1 Loosening, liberating.<BR>—2 Looseness.<BR>—3 Binding, tying together.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थनम्
श्रन्थनम्<BR>—1 Loosing, untying.<BR>—2 Hurting, killing, destroying.<BR>—3 Tying, binding.<BR>—4 Composing (a book).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रन्थित|श्रंथित|श्रन्थितः
श्रन्थित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Loosed, liberated, let loose.<BR>—2 Connected; strung or bound together.<BR>—3 Hurt, injured.<BR>—4 Overcome, overpowered.<BR>—5 Delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपणम्
श्रपणम्, -णा<BR> Causing to boil, boiling, seething.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपणा
श्रपणम्, -णा<BR> Causing to boil, boiling, seething.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपणः|श्रपण|श्रपणं
श्रपणम्, -णा + .{@-णः@} Cooking fire (आहवनीय or गार्हपत्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपित|श्रपितं
श्रपित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Boiled or caused to be boiled.<BR>—2 Seethed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपितम्
श्रपित + .{@-तम्@} Boiled meat &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपिता
श्रपित + .{@-ता@} Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्
श्रम् €4 P. (श्राम्यति, श्रान्त)<BR>—1 To exert oneself, take pains, toil, labour.<BR>—2 To perform austerities, mortify the body (by acts of penance); क्रियच्चिरं<BR> श्राम्यसि गौरि Ku. 5. 50.<BR>—3 To be wearied or fatigued, be exhausted; रतिश्रान्ता शेते रजनिरमणी<BR> गाढमुरसि K. P. 10; Śi. 14. 38; Bk. 14. 110.<BR>—4 To be afflicted or distressed; यो वृन्दानि त्वरयति पथि श्राम्यतां<BR> प्रोषितानाम् Me. 101. ━<i>Caus.</i> (श्र(श्रा)मयति-ते) To cause<BR> to be fatigued &c.<BR>—2 To overcome, conquer, subdue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमः|श्रम
श्रमः [श्रम्-घञ् न वृद्धिः]<BR>—1 Toil, labour, exertion, effort; अलं महीपाल तव श्रमेण R. 2. 34;<BR> जानाति हि पुनः सम्यक् कविरेव कवेः श्रमम् Subhāṣ.; R. 16. 75;<BR> Ms. 9. 208.<BR>—2 Weariness, fatigue, exhaustion; विनयन्ते स्म तद्योधा मधुभिर्विजयश्रमम्<BR> R. 4. 65, 67; Me. 17, 52; Ki. 5. 28.<BR>—3 Affliction, distress; देशकालविचारीदं श्रमव्यायामनिःस्वनम् Mb. 14. 45. 2.<BR>—4 Penance, austerity, mortification of the body; दिवं यदि प्रार्थयसे<BR> वृथा श्रमः Ku. 5. 45.<BR>—5<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Exercise; अयोदण्डेन च श्रममकरोत् K. 76.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Especially military exercise, drill.<BR>—6 Hard study.<BR>—7 = आश्रम q. v.; तदा स पर्याववृते श्रमाय Mb. 3. 114. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रमाम्बु, श्रमार्त, श्रमकर्षित, श्रमघ्नी, श्रमभञ्जनी, श्रमविनोदः, श्रमसाध्य, श्रमस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमाम्बु|श्रमांबु
श्रमः + -अम्बु <i>n.</i>, {@-जलम्, -सलिलम्@}<BR> perspiration, sweat; संपेदे श्रमसलिलोद्गमो<BR> विभूषाम् Ki. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमार्त|श्रमार्त्त
श्रमः + -आर्त <i>a.</i> oppressed by fatigue; Ms. 8. 67.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">Page1574-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1573-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमकर्षित
श्रमः + -कर्षित <i>a.</i> worn out by fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमघ्नी
श्रमः + -घ्नी Cucurbita Lagenaria (Mar. दुध्या भोपळा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमभञ्जनी
श्रमः + -भञ्जनी the Nāgavela plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमविनोदः|श्रमविनोद
श्रमः + -विनोदः the act of dispelling fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमसाध्य
श्रमः + -साध्य <i>a.</i> to be accomplished by dint of labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमस्थानम्
श्रमः + -स्थानम् a drill-ground, gymnasium &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमण|श्रमणः
श्रमण <i>a.</i> (-णा, -णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [श्रम्-युच्]<BR>—1 Labouring, toiling.<BR>—2 Low, base, vile.<BR>—3 Naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणः|श्रमण
श्रमण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 An ascetic, a devotee, religious mendicant in general; श्रमणोऽश्रमणः<BR> (भवति) Bṛ. Up. 4. 3. 22; Mb. 12. 154. 21; Bhāg. 5. 3. 20.<BR>—2 A Buddhist or Jain ascetic.<BR>—3 A beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणा
श्रमण + .{@-णा, -णी@}<BR>—1 A female devotee or mendicant.<BR>—2 A lovely woman.<BR>—3 A woman of low caste.<BR>—4 A hard-working woman.<BR>—5 Bengal madder.<BR>—6 The spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणी
श्रमण + .{@-णा, -णी@}<BR>—1 A female devotee or mendicant.<BR>—2 A lovely woman.<BR>—3 A woman of low caste.<BR>—4 A hard-working woman.<BR>—5 Bengal madder.<BR>—6 The spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणम्
श्रमण + .{@-णम्@} Toil, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणायते
श्रमणायते Den. Ā. To become a beggar, monk or ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमिन्
श्रमिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Laborious, toiling, diligent.<BR>—2 Undergoing fatigue or exertions.<BR>—3 Tiring, fatiguing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्भ्|श्रंभ्
श्रम्भ् €1 Ā. (श्रम्भते, श्रब्ध)<BR>—1 To be careless or inattentive, be negligent.<BR>—2 To err.<BR>—3 To trust, confide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयः|श्रय
श्रयः, श्रयणम् [श्रि-घञ् ल्युट् वा] Refuge, shelter, protection,<BR> asylum; (see आश्रय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयणम्
श्रयः, श्रयणम् [श्रि-घञ् ल्युट् वा] Refuge, shelter, protection,<BR> asylum; (see आश्रय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवः|श्रव
श्रवः [शृणोत्यनेन श्रु-अप्]<BR>—1 Hearing; as in सुखश्रव; अप्यदृष्टं श्रवादेव पुरुषं धर्मचारिणम्<BR> Mb. 13. 104. 10.<BR>—2 The ear; इन्द्रनीलोत्पलश्रवाः Rām. 3. 42. 16.<BR>—3 The hypotenuse of a triangle.<BR>—4 Flowing, oozing (for स्रव). —5 Fame, glory.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रवपत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवपत्रम्
श्रवः + -पत्रम् an ear-ring; सोऽस्याः श्रवः पत्रयुगे प्रणालीरेखैव<BR> धावत्यभिकर्णकूपम् N. 7. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणः|श्रवण|श्रवणं
श्रवणः, -णम्<BR> [शृणोत्यनेन श्रु-क्रणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The ear; ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे श्रवणमपिदवाति Gīt. 5; श्रवणाञ्जलिपुटपेयं<BR> विरचितवान् भारताख्यममृतं यः Ve. 1. 4.<BR>—2 The hypotenuse of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणम्
श्रवणः, -णम्<BR> [शृणोत्यनेन श्रु-क्रणे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The ear; ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे श्रवणमपिदवाति Gīt. 5; श्रवणाञ्जलिपुटपेयं<BR> विरचितवान् भारताख्यममृतं यः Ve. 1. 4.<BR>—2 The hypotenuse of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणः|श्रवण|श्रवणं
श्रवणः, -णम् + .{@-णः, -णा@} N. of a lunar mansion containing three stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणा
श्रवणः, -णम् + .{@-णः, -णा@} N. of a lunar mansion containing three stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणम्
श्रवणः, -णम् + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 The act of hearing; श्रवणसुभगम् Me. 11.<BR>—2 Study.<BR>—3 Fame, glory.<BR>—4 That which is heard or revealed, the Veda; इति श्रवणात् ‘because of such a Vedic text’<BR>.<BR>—5 Wealth.<BR>—6 Flowing, oozing.<BR>—7 (In phil.) The determining by means of the six signs the true doctrine<BR> of the Vedānta.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रवणाधिकारिन्, श्रवणेन्द्रियम्, श्रवणोत्पलम्, श्रवणोदरम्, श्रवणकातरता, श्रवणगोचर, श्रवणपथः, श्रवणविषयः, श्रवणपरुष, श्रवणपालिः, श्रवणपाली, श्रवणपाशः, श्रवणपुटकः, श्रवणपूरकः, श्रवणप्राघुणिकः, श्रवणभृत, श्रवणसुभग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणाधिकारिन्
श्रवणः + -अधिकारिन् <i>m.</i> a speaker, addresser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणेन्द्रियम्
श्रवणः + -इन्द्रियम् the sense of hearing, the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणोत्पलम्
श्रवणः + -उत्पलम् a lotus fastened in the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणोदरम्
श्रवणः + -उदरम् the hollow of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणकातरता
श्रवणः + -कातरता anxiety for hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणगोचर|श्रवणगोचरः
श्रवणः + -गोचर <i>a.</i> within the range of hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणगोचरः|श्रवणगोचर
