श्रवणभृत
श्रवणः + -भृत <i>a.</i> spoken of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणसुभग
श्रवणः + -सुभग <i>a.</i> pleasing to the ear; वचस्तस्याकर्ण्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">Page1574-2</a>]<BR> श्रवणसुभगं पण्डितपतेरधुन्वन् सूर्धानं नृपशुरथवायं पशुपतिः<BR> Jag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्
श्रवस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 The ear.<BR>—2 Fame, glory; बृहच्छ्रवाः (देवर्षिः) Bhāg. 1. 5. 1.<BR>—3 Wealth.<BR>—4 Hymn.<BR>—5 A praiseworthy action.<BR>—6 Sound; गन्धाकृतिः स्पर्शरसश्रवांसि Bhāg. 5. 11. 10.<BR>—7 A stream, channel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्यम्
श्रवस्यम् Fame, glory, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्यति
श्रवस्यति Den. P.<BR>—1 To wish for fame or glory.<BR>—2 To long for a sacrifice or oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

