श्राद्ध <i>a.</i> [श्रद्धा हेतुत्वेनास्त्यस्य अण्] Faithful, believing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धम्
श्राद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@}<BR>—1 A funeral rite or ceremony performed in honour of the departed spirits<BR> of dead relatives; श्रद्धया दीयते यस्मात्तस्माच्छ्राद्धं निगद्यते;<BR> it is of three kinds:− नित्य, नैमित्तिक, and काम्य; यः संगतानि<BR> कुरुते मोहाच्छ्राद्धेन मानवः Ms. 3. 140.<BR>—2 An obsequial oblation, a gift or offering at a Śrāddha; विहाय<BR> शोकं धर्मात्मा ददौ श्राद्धमनुत्तमम् Mb. 14. 62. 1; सर्वं श्रद्धया<BR> दत्तं श्राद्धम् Pratimā 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्राद्धकर्मन्, श्राद्धकृत्, श्राद्धदः, श्राद्धदिनः, श्राद्धदिनम्, श्राद्धदेवः, श्राद्धदेवता, श्राद्धभुज्, श्राद्धभुज्, श्राद्धभोक्तृ, श्राद्धमित्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकर्मन्|श्राद्धकर्म्मन्
श्राद्ध + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-क्रिया@}<BR> a funeral ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धकृत्
श्राद्ध + -कृत् <i>m.</i> the performer of a funeral rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदः|श्राद्धद
श्राद्ध + -दः the offerer of a Śrāddha or funeral oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदिनः|श्राद्धदिन
श्राद्ध + -दिनः, -दिनम् the anniversary of the death of a relative in whose<BR> honour a Śrāddha is performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदिनम्
श्राद्ध + -दिनः, -दिनम् the anniversary of the death of a relative in whose<BR> honour a Śrāddha is performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदेवः|श्राद्धदेव
श्राद्ध + -देवः, -देवता<BR>—1 a deity presiding over funeral rites.<BR>—2 an epithet of Yama.<BR>—3 a Viśvadeva q. v.<BR>—4 a Pitṛ or progenitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धदेवता
श्राद्ध + -देवः, -देवता<BR>—1 a deity presiding over funeral rites.<BR>—2 an epithet of Yama.<BR>—3 a Viśvadeva q. v.<BR>—4 a Pitṛ or progenitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धभुज्
श्राद्ध + -भुज् <i>a.</i> eating food prepared at a श्राद्ध; श्राद्धभुग्वृषलीतल्पं<BR> तदहर्योऽधिगच्छति Ms. 3. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धभुज्
श्राद्ध + -भुज्, -भोक्तृ <i>m.</i> a deceased ancestor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धभोक्तृ
श्राद्ध + -भुज्, -भोक्तृ <i>m.</i> a deceased ancestor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धमित्रः|श्राद्धमित्र
श्राद्ध + -मित्रः making friends through a श्राद्ध; cf. श्राद्धम् (1)<BR> above; स स्वर्गाच्छ्यवते लोकाच्छ्राद्धमित्रो द्विजाधमः Ms. 3. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिक|श्राद्धिकः
श्राद्धिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [श्राद्धे-देयम्, श्राद्धं तद्द्रव्यं भक्ष्यत्वेनास्त्यस्य<BR> वा ठन्] Relating to a Srāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिकः|श्राद्धिक
श्राद्धिक + .{@-कः@} The recipient of an obsequial offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिकम्
श्राद्धिक + .{@-कम्@} A present given at a Śrāddha; श्राद्धिकं प्रतिगृह्य च<BR> (नाधीयीत) Ms. 4. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धीय
श्राद्धीय <i>a.</i> Relating to a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धेय
श्राद्धेय <i>a.</i> Fit for श्राद्ध; अश्राद्धेयानि धान्यानि कोद्रवाः पुलकास्तथा<BR> Mb. 13. 91. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1574-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्त|श्रांत|श्रान्तः
श्रान्त <i>p. p.</i> [श्रम्-क्त]<BR>—1 Wearied, tired, fatigued, exhausted; आरभेतैव कर्माणि श्रान्तः श्रान्तः<BR> पुनः पुनः Ms. 9. 30.<BR>—2 Calmed, tranqil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्तः|श्रान्त|श्रांत
श्रान्त + .{@-तः@} An ascetic.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रान्तसंवाहनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्तसंवाहनम्
श्रान्त + -संवाहनम् soothing or relieving the wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रान्तिः|श्रान्ति|श्रांति|श्रांतिः
श्रान्तिः <i>f.</i> [श्रम्-क्तिन्] Fatigue, exhaustion, weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रामः|श्राम
श्रामः<BR>—1 A month.<BR>—2 Time.<BR>—3 A temporary shed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रायः|श्राय
श्रायः [श्रि-घञ्] Shelter, protection, refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावः|श्राव
श्रावः [श्रु-घञ्]<BR>—1 Hearing, listening.<BR>—2 Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावकः|श्रावक
श्रावकः [श्रि-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A hearer.<BR>—2 A pupil, disciple; श्रावकावस्थायाम् Māl. 10 ‘in their pupilage’.<BR>—3 A class of Buddhist saints or votaries.<BR>—4 A Buddhist votary in general.<BR>—5 A heretic.<BR>—6 A crow.<BR>—7 A sound audible from afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावण|श्रावणः
श्रावण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [श्रवण-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to the ear.<BR>—2 Born under the asterism Śravaṇa.<BR>—3 Enjoined in the Veda; विधिना श्रावणेनैव कुर्यात् कर्माण्यतन्द्रितः<BR> Mb. 12. 21. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणः|श्रावण
श्रावण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 N. of a lunar month (corresponding to July-August).<BR>—2 A heretic.<BR>—3 An impostor.<BR>—4 N. of a Vaiśya ascetic unwittingly shot dead by king Daśaratha who<BR> was in consequence cursed by his old parents that he would die of broken-heart<BR> separated from his sons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणम्
श्रावण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Causing to be heard.<BR>—2 Knowledge derived from hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिक|श्रावणिकः
श्रावणिक <i>a.</i> [श्रावणी अस्त्यस्मिन् मासे ठन्] Relating to the<BR> month Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिकः|श्रावणिक
श्रावणिक + .{@-कः@} The month called Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणी
श्रावणी<BR>—1 The day of full moon in Śrāvaṇa.<BR>—2 N. of an annual ceremony performed on this day when the sacred thread<BR> is put on anew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावित
श्रावित <i>a.</i> Told, narrated, related, made to hear, or learn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावितम्
श्रावित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 (In ritual) Call, exclamation.<BR>—2 Request; श्रोतुमर्हसि दीनस्य श्रावितं कृपया मुने Bhāg. 3. 22. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव्य
श्राव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be heard (opp. दृश्य).<BR>—2 Audible, distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावस्तिः|श्रावस्ति
श्रावस्तिः, -स्ती <i>f.</i><BR> N. of a city north of the Ganges (said to have been<BR> founded by king Śrāvasta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावस्ती
श्रावस्तिः, -स्ती <i>f.</i><BR> N. of a city north of the Ganges (said to have been<BR> founded by king Śrāvasta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रि
श्रि €1 U. (श्रयति-ते, शिश्राय-शिश्रिये, अशिश्रियत्-त, श्रयिष्यतिते,<BR> श्रयितुम्, श्रित; <i>Caus.</i> श्राययति-ते; <i>desid.</i> शिश्रीषति-ते,<BR> शिश्रयिषति-ते)<BR>—1 To go to, approach, resort to, have recourse to, approach for protection;<BR> यं देशं श्रयते तमेव कुरुते बाहुप्रतापार्जितम् H. 1. 150; R. 3. 70, 19. 1;<BR> श्रितासि चन्दनभ्रान्त्या दुर्विपाकं विषद्रुमम् U. 1. 46.<BR>—2 To go or attain to, reach, undergo, assume (as a state); परीता रक्षोभिः<BR> श्रयति विवशा कामपि दशाम् Bv. 1. 83; द्विपेन्द्रभावं कलभः श्रयन्निव R. 3. 32.<BR>—3 To cling to, lean or rest on, depend on; नीलः स्निग्धः श्रयति शिखरं<BR> नूतनस्तोयवाहः U. 1. 33.<BR>—4 To dwell in, inhabit.<BR>—5 To honour, serve, worship.<BR>—6 To use, employ.<BR>—7 To devote oneself to, be attached to.<BR>—8 To assist, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
श्रित <i>p. p.</i> [श्रि-क्त]<BR>—1 Gone to, approached, approached for refuse or protection.<BR>—2 Clung to, resting or sitting on.<BR>—3 United or joined with, connected with.<BR>—4 Protected.<BR>—5 Honoured, served.<BR>—6 Subservient, auxiliary.<BR>—7 Covered with, overspread.<BR>—8 Contained.<BR>—9 Assembled, collected.<BR>—10 Having, possessing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रितक्षम, श्रितसत्त्व<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रितक्षम
श्रित + -क्षम <i>a.</i> composed, tranquil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रितसत्त्व
श्रित + -सत्त्व <i>a.</i> one who has taken courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रितिः|श्रिति
श्रितिः <i>f.</i> Resort, recourse, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
श्रित = शृत q. v. Cooked; अयं सर्वः समस्ताङ्गः श्रितः कृष्णमृगो<BR> मया Rām. 2. 56. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष्
श्रिष् €1 P. (श्रेषति) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री €9 U. (श्रीणाति, श्रीणीते)<BR>—1 To cook, dress, boil, prepare.<BR>—2 To diffuse light; श्रीणन्नुप स्थाद् दिवं भुरण्युः Rv. 1. 68. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री <i>f.</i> [श्रि-क्विप् नि˚ Uṇ. 2. 57]<BR>—1 Wealth, riches, affluence, prosperity, plenty; अनिर्वेदः श्रियो मूलम्<BR> Rām.; साहसे श्रीः प्रतिवसति Mk. 4 ‘fortune favours the brave’;<BR> कर्माण्यारभमाणं हि पुरुषं श्रीर्निषेवते Ms. 9. 300; Ki. 7. 28.<BR>—2 Royalty, majesty, royal wealth; श्रियः कुरूणामधिपस्य पालनीम् Ki. 1. 1.<BR>—3 Dignity, high position, state; श्रीलक्षण Ku. 7. 45 ‘the marks or insignia of greatness or dignity’<BR>; दुराराध्याः श्रियो राज्ञां दुरापा<BR> दुष्परिग्रहाः Pt. 1. 67; विद्युल्लेखाकनकरुचिरं श्रीवितानं ममाभ्रम् V. 4. 13.<BR>—4 Beauty, grace, splendour, lustre; (मुखं) कमलश्रियं दधौ<BR> Ku. 5. 21, 7. 32; R. 3. 8.<BR>—5 Colour, aspect; तेषामाविरभूद् ब्रह्मा परिम्लानमुखश्रियाम् Ku. 2. 2.<BR>—6 The goddess of wealth, Laksmī, the wife of Viṣṇu; आसीदियं दशरथस्य<BR> गृहे यथा श्रीः U. 4. 6; Ś. 3. 14; Śi. 1. 1.<BR>—7 Any virtue or excellence.<BR>—8 Decoration.<BR>—9 Intellect, understanding.<BR>—10 Superhuman power.<BR>—11 The three objects of human existence taken collectively (धर्म,<BR> अर्थ and काम).<BR>—12 The Sarala tree.<BR>—13 The Bilva tree.<BR>—14 Cloves.<BR>—15 A lotus.<BR>—16 The twelfth digit of the moon.<BR>—17 N. of Sarasvatī, (the goddess of speech).<BR>—18 Speech.<BR>—19 Fame, glory. —20 The three Vedas (वेदत्रयी); श्रिया विहीनैरधनैर्नास्तिकैः<BR> संप्रवर्तितम् Mb. 12. 10. 20 (‘ऋचः सामानि यजूंषि । सा हि श्रीरमृता सताम्’ इति श्रुतेः । com.).<BR> ━<i>m.</i> N. of one of the six <i>Rāgas</i><BR> or musical modes. ━<i>a.</i> Splendid, radiant, adorning. (The word श्री<BR> is often used as an honorific prefix to the names of deities and eminent<BR> persons; श्रीकृष्णः, श्रीरामः, श्रीवाल्मीकिः, श्रीजयदेवः; also celebrated<BR> works, generally of a sacred character; श्रीभागवत, श्रीरामायण &c.;<BR> it is also used as an auspicious sign at the commencement of letters,<BR> manuscripts &c.; Māgha has used this word in the last stanza of each canto<BR> of his Śiśupālavadha, as Bhāravi has used लक्ष्मी).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्र्याह्वम्, श्रीशः, श्रीकण्ठः, श्रीकरः, श्रीकरणम्, श्रीकरणादिः, श्रीकान्तः, श्रीकारः, श्रीकारिन्, श्रीकृच्छ्रः, श्रीखण्डः, श्रीखण्डम्, श्रीगदितम्, श्रीगर्भः, श्रीग्रहः, श्रीग्रामरः, श्रीघनम्, श्रीचक्रम्, श्रीजः, श्रीतालः, श्रीदः, श्रीदयितः, श्रीधरः, श्रीनगरम्, श्रीनन्दनः, श्रीनिकेतनः, श्रीनिवासः, श्रीपञ्चमी, श्रीपतिः, श्रीपथः, श्रीपर्णम्, श्रीपर्णी, श्रीपर्वतः, श्रीपिष्टः, श्रीपुत्रः, श्रीपुष्पम्, श्रीप्रसूनम्, श्रीफलः, श्रीफला, श्रीफली, श्रीभ्रातृ, श्रीमकुटम्, श्रीमस्तकः, श्रीमुद्रा, श्रीमूर्तिः, श्रीयुक्त, श्रीयुत, श्रीरङ्गः, श्रीरसः, श्रीवत्सः, श्रीवत्सकिन्, श्रीवरः, श्रीवल्लभः, श्रीवर्धनः, श्रीवल्लभः, श्रीवासः, श्रीवासस्, श्रीवृक्षः, श्रीवेष्टः, श्रीसंज्ञम्, श्रीसहोदरः, श्रीसिद्धिः, श्रीसूक्तम्, श्रीहरिः, श्रीहस्तिनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1575-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

