श्री + -मुद्रा a particular mark on the forehead by the Vaiṣṇavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमूर्तिः|श्रीमूर्ति|श्रीमूर्त्ति|श्रीमूर्त्तिः
श्री + -मूर्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 an idol of Viṣṇu or Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 any idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयुक्त|श्रीयुक्तः
श्री + -युक्त, -युत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fortunate, happy.<BR>—2 wealthy, prosperous (often used as an honorific prefix to the names of men).<BR>—3 famous, illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीयुत|श्रीयुतः
श्री + -युक्त, -युत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 fortunate, happy.<BR>—2 wealthy, prosperous (often used as an honorific prefix to the names of men).<BR>—3 famous, illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीरङ्गः|श्रीरङ्ग|श्रीरंग
श्री + -रङ्गः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीरसः|श्रीरस
श्री + -रसः<BR>—1 turpentine.<BR>—2 resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सः|श्रीवत्स
श्री + -वत्सः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a mark or curl of hair on the breast of Viṣṇu; प्रभानुलिप्तश्रीवत्सं<BR> लक्ष्मीविभ्रमदर्पणम् R. 10. 10.<BR>—3 a hole in a wall made by a house-breaker. ˚अङ्कः, ˚धारिन्, ˚मृत्, ˚लक्ष्मन्,<BR> ˚लाञ्छन <i>m.</i> epithets of Viṣṇu; तमभ्यगच्छत् प्रथमो विधाता<BR> श्रीवत्सलक्ष्मा पुरुषश्च साक्षात् Ku. 7. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवत्सकिन्
श्री + -वत्सकिन् <i>m.</i> a horse having a curl of hair on his breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवरः|श्रीवर
श्री + -वरः, -वल्लभः epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवल्लभः|श्रीवल्लभ
श्री + -वरः, -वल्लभः epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवर्धनः|श्रीवर्धन
श्री + -वर्धनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवल्लभः|श्रीवल्लभ
श्री + -वल्लभः a favourite of fortune, a happy or fortunate person; Pt. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवासः|श्रीवास
श्री + -वासः<BR>—1 an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR>—3 a lotus.<BR>—4 turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवासस्
श्री + -वासस् <i>m.</i> turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवृक्षः|श्रीवृक्ष
श्री + -वृक्षः<BR>—1 the <i>Bilva</i> tree.<BR>—2 the Aśvattha or sacred fig-tree; वक्षः श्रीवृक्षकान्तं मधुकरनिकरश्यामलं<BR> शार्ङ्गपाणेः Viṣṇupāda. S. 28.<BR>—3 a curl of hair on the breast and forehead of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">Page1576-2</a>]<BR> horse. ˚किन् having such mark; श्रीवृक्षकी पुरुषकोन्नमिताग्रकायः Śi. 5. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीवेष्टः|श्रीवेष्ट
श्री + -वेष्टः<BR>—1 turpentine.<BR>—2 resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसंज्ञम्
श्री + -संज्ञम् cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसहोदरः|श्रीसहोदर
श्री + -सहोदरः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसिद्धिः|श्रीसिद्धि
श्री + -सिद्धिः N. of the 16th Yoga (in astrol.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीसूक्तम्
श्री + -सूक्तम् N. of a Vedic hymn (Rv. 1. 165).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीहरिः|श्रीहरि
श्री + -हरिः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीहस्तिनी
श्री + -हस्तिनी the sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियंमन्य
श्रियंमन्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thinking oneself worthy.<BR>—2 Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियापतिः
श्रियापतिः An epithet of Śiva; also श्रियावासिन् <i>m.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमत्|श्रीमन्त्
श्रीमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wealthy, rich.<BR>—2 Happy, fortunate, prosperous, thriving.<BR>—3 Beautiful, pleasing; श्रियः पतिः श्रीमति शासितुं जगत् Śi. 1. 1.<BR>—4 Famous, celebrated, glorious, dignified; (the word is often used as<BR> a respectful affix to celebrated or revered names of persons and things<BR> as श्रीमद्भागवत, श्रीमच्छंकराचार्य &c.). ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 Of Kubera.<BR>—3 Of Śiva.<BR>—4 The <i>Tilaka</i> tree.<BR>—5 The Aśvattha tree.<BR>—6 A parrot.<BR>—7 A bull kept for breeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रील|श्रीलः
श्रील <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Rich, wealthy.<BR>—2 Fortunate, prosperous.<BR>—3 Beautiful.<BR>—4 Famous, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
श्रु I. €1 P. (श्रवति) To go, move; cf. शु. ━II. €5 P. (शृणोति,<BR> शुश्राव, अश्रौषीत्, श्रोष्यति, श्रोतुम्, श्रुत)<BR>—1 To hear, listen to, give ear to; शृणु मे सावशेषं वचः V. 2;<BR> रुतानि चाश्रोषत षट्पदानाम् Bk. 2. 10; संदेशं मे तदनु जलद<BR> श्रोष्यसि श्रोत्रपेयम् Me. 13, 102.<BR>—2 To learn, study; द्वादशवर्षभिर्व्याकरणं श्रूयते Pt. 1.<BR>—3 To be attentive, to obey. (इति श्रूयते ‘it is so heard’, <i>i. e.</i><BR> is enjoined in the scriptures, such is the sacred precept.). ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (श्रावयति-ते) To cause to hear, communicate, tell, relate, inform;<BR> श्रावितोऽमात्यसंदेशं स्तनकलशः Mu. 4. ━<i>Desid.</i> (शुश्रूषते)<BR>—1 To wish to hear.<BR>—2 To be attentive or obedient, obey; वाक्यं नैव करोति बान्धवजनो<BR> पत्नी न शुश्रूषते Pt. 4. 78 (where the word may have the next sense also).<BR>—3 To serve, wait or attend upon; शुश्रूषस्व गुरून् Ś. 4. 17; Ku. 1. 59;<BR> Ms. 2. 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत|श्रुतं|श्रुतः
श्रुत <i>p. p.</i> [श्रु-क्त]<BR>—1 Heard, listened to.<BR>—2 Reported, heard of.<BR>—3 Learnt, ascertained, understood.<BR>—4 Wellknown, famous, celebrated, renowned; श्रुतानुभावं शरणं व्रज<BR> भावेन भाविनि Bhāg. 3. 32. 11; श्रुतस्य किं तत् सदृशं कुलस्य<BR> R. 14. 61, 3. 40.<BR>—5 Named, called.<BR>—6 Promised; तदवश्यं त्वया कार्यं यदनेन श्रुतं मम Rām. 2. 18. 21.<BR>—7 Vedic, like Vedas (वेदरूप); गिरः श्रुतायाः पुष्पिण्या मधुगन्धेन<BR> भूरिणा Bhāg. 4. 2. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतम्
श्रुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The object of hearing.<BR>—2 That which was heard by revelation <i>i. e.</i> the Veda, holy learning,<BR> sacred knowledge; श्रुतप्रकाशम् R. 5. 2.<BR>—3 Learning in general (विद्या); श्रोत्रं श्रुतेनैव न कुण्डलेन<BR> (विभाति) Bh. 2. 71; R. 3. 21, 5. 22; अग्निहोत्रफला वेदाः शीलवित्तफलं<BR> श्रुतम् Pt. 2. 150, 4. 68.<BR>—4 The act of hearing; योगे बुद्धिं, श्रुते सत्त्वं, मनो ब्रह्मणि धारयन्<BR> Mb. 12. 177. 31.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रुताध्ययनम्, श्रुतान्वित, श्रुतार्थः, श्रुतर्षिः, श्रुतकीर्ति, श्रुतदेवी, श्रुतधर, श्रुतश्रवस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुताध्ययनम्
श्रुत + -अध्ययनम् study of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतान्वित|श्रुतान्वितः
श्रुत + -अन्वित <i>a.</i> conversant with the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतार्थः|श्रुतार्थ
श्रुत + -अर्थः a fact verbally or orally communicated. ˚आपत्तिः see<BR> अर्थापत्तिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतर्षिः|श्रुतर्षि
श्रुत + -ऋषिः a class of sages like Śuśruta; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतकीर्ति|श्रुतकीर्त्ति|श्रुतकीर्त्तिः
श्रुत + -कीर्ति <i>a.</i> famous, renowned. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a generous man.<BR>—2 a divine sage.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">Page1577-1</a>]<BR>━(<i>f.</i>) N. of the wife of Śatrughna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1576-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतदेवी
श्रुत + -देवी N. of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतधर|श्रुतधरः
श्रुत + -धर <i>a.</i> remembering what is heard, retentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतधरः|श्रुतधर
श्रुत + -धर + .({@-रः@}) the ear; राष्ट्रमुत्तरपाञ्चालं याति श्रुतधरान्वितः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 25. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतश्रवस्
श्रुत + -श्रवस् <i>m.</i> N. of the father of Śiśupāla. ˚अनुजः the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतवत्|श्रुतवन्त्
श्रुतवत् <i>a.</i> Knowing the Veda, proficient in sacred knowledge<BR> or learning in general; अपथे पदमर्पयन्ति हि श्रुतवन्तोऽपि रजोनिमीलिताः R. 9. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिः|श्रुति
श्रुतिः <i>f.</i> [श्रु-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Hearing; चन्द्रस्य ग्रहणमिति श्रुतेः Mu. 1. 7; R. 1. 27.<BR>—2 The ear; श्रुतिसुखभ्रमरस्वनगीतयः R. 9. 35; Śi. 1. 1; Ve. 3. 23.<BR>—3 Report, rumour, news, oral intelligence.<BR>—4 A sound in general; सा तु वेदश्रुतिं श्रुत्वा दृष्ट्वा वै तपसो निधिम्<BR> Rām. 7. 2. 17; स वेत्ति गन्धांश्च रसान् श्रुतीश्च Mb. 12. 187. 19.<BR>—5 The Veda (known by revelation, opp. स्मृति; see under वेद); श्रुतिस्तु<BR> वेदो विज्ञेयो धर्मशास्रं तु वै स्मृतिः Ms. 2. 10, 14.<BR>—6 A Vedic or sacred text; इति श्रुतेः or इति श्रुतिः ‘so says a sacred text’.<BR>—7 Vedic or sacred knowledge, holy learning; यत्रैषा सात्वती श्रुतिः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 4. 7, 11. 3. 46.<BR>—8 (In music) A division of the octavo, a quarter tone or interval; रणद्भिराघट्टनया<BR> नभस्वतः पृथग्विभिन्नश्रुतिमण्डलैः स्वरैः Śi. 1. 10, 11. 1; (see<BR> Malli. <i>ad loc.</i>).<BR>—9 The constellation Śravaṇa.<BR>—10 The diagonal of a tetragon, the hypotenuse of a triangle; cf. कर्ण.<BR>—11 Direct or expressed signification (opp. लक्षणा); श्रुतिलक्षणाविशये<BR> च श्रुतिर्न्याय्या न लक्षणा ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 20.<BR>—12 Speech (वाक्); विविक्तवर्णाभरणा सुखश्रुतिः Ki. 14. 3.<BR>—13 Name, fame (कीर्ति); हैरण्यौ भवतो बाहू श्रुतिर्भवति पार्थिवी Mb. 3. 35. 9.<BR>—14 A word, saw, saying; Rām. 2. 72. 25.<BR>—15 An explanation of ब्रह्म from the उपनिषद्s; विविधाश्चौपनिषदीरात्मसंसिद्धये<BR> श्रुतीः Ms. 6. 29 (com. श्रुतीरुपनिषत्पठितब्रह्मप्रतिपादकवाक्यानि).<BR>—16 Advantage, gain (फलश्रुति); उपोष्य संशितो भूत्वा हित्वा वेदकृताः<BR> श्रुतीः Mb. 12. 265. 7.<BR>—17 Name, title; बिभ्रत्यनन्यविषयां लोकपाल इति श्रुतिम् Kāv. 2. 331.<BR>—18 Learning.<BR>—19 Scholarship.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रुत्यनुप्रासः, श्रुत्यर्थः, श्रुत्युक्त, श्रुत्युदित, श्रुतिकटः, श्रुतिकटु, श्रुतिकथित, श्रुतिचोदनम्, श्रुतिचोदनः, श्रुतिजातिंविशारद, श्रुतिजीविका, श्रुतिदूषक, श्रुतिद्वैधम्, श्रुतिधर, श्रुतिनिदर्शनम्, श्रुतिपथः, श्रुतिप्रसादन, श्रुतिप्रामाण्यम्, श्रुतिप्रामाण्यतः, श्रुतिमण्डलम्, श्रुतिमहत्, श्रुतिमूलम्, श्रुतिमूलक, श्रुतिवचनम्, श्रुतिवर्जित, श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्न, श्रुतिविवरम्, श्रुतिविशेषणार्थम्, श्रुतिविषयः, श्रुतिवेधः, श्रुतिशिखरम्, श्रुतिशिरस्, श्रुतिसुख, श्रुतिमनोहर, श्रुतिस्फोटा, श्रुतिस्मृति, श्रुतिहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्यनुप्रासः|श्रुत्यनुप्रास
श्रुतिः + -अनुप्रासः a kind of alliteration; see K. P. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्यर्थः
श्रुतिः + -अर्थः the sense of a sentence derived on the strength of the<BR> श्रुतिप्रमाण as distinguished from लिङ्ग, वाक्य and other प्रमाणs;<BR> यत्र श्रुत्यर्थो न सम्भवति तत्र वाक्यार्थो गृह्यते ŚB. on MS. 6. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्युक्त
श्रुतिः + -उक्त, -उदित <i>a.</i> enjoined by the Vedas; आचारः परमो धर्मः<BR> श्रुत्युक्तः स्मार्त एव च Ms. 1. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत्युदित
श्रुतिः + -उक्त, -उदित <i>a.</i> enjoined by the Vedas; आचारः परमो धर्मः<BR> श्रुत्युक्तः स्मार्त एव च Ms. 1. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकटः|श्रुतिकट
श्रुतिः + -कटः<BR>—1 a snake.<BR>—2 penance, expiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकटु|श्रुतिकटुः
श्रुतिः + -कटु <i>a.</i> harsh to hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकटुः|श्रुतिकटु
श्रुतिः + -कटु + .({@-टुः@}) a harsh or unmelodious sound, regarded as a fault of composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिकथित|श्रुतिकथितः
श्रुतिः + -कथित <i>a.</i> enjoined or prescribed by the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिचोदनम्
श्रुतिः + -चोदनम्, -चोदनः a scriptural injunction, Vedic precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिचोदनः|श्रुतिचोदन
श्रुतिः + -चोदनम्, -चोदनः a scriptural injunction, Vedic precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिजातिंविशारद
श्रुतिः + -जातिंविशारद <i>a.</i> familiar with different kinds of quarter<BR> tones; वीणावादनतत्त्वज्ञः श्रुतिजातिविशारदः । तालज्ञश्चाप्रयासेन<BR> मोक्षमार्गं नियच्छति ॥ Y. 3. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिजीविका
श्रुतिः + -जीविका a law-book or code of laws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिदूषक
श्रुतिः + -दूषक <i>a.</i> offending the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिद्वैधम्
श्रुतिः + -द्वैधम् disagreement or contradiction of Vedas or Vedic precepts;<BR> श्रुतिद्वैधं तु यत्र स्यात्तत्र धर्मावुभौ स्मृतौ Ms. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिधर|श्रुतिधरः
श्रुतिः + -धर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 hearing.<BR>—2 having a retentive memory; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिनिदर्शनम्
श्रुतिः + -निदर्शनम् evidence of the Vedas;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">Page1577-2</a>]<BR> कामकारकृतेऽप्याहुरेके श्रुतिनिदर्शनात् Ms. 11. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिपथः|श्रुतिपथ
श्रुतिः + -पथः<BR>—1 the range of the ear; तामाश्रित्य श्रुतिपथगतामास्थया लब्धमूलः M. 4. 1.<BR>—2 (pl.) tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिप्रसादन
श्रुतिः + -प्रसादन <i>a.</i> grateful to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिप्रामाण्यम्
श्रुतिः + -प्रामाण्यम् authority or sanction of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिप्रामाण्यतः
श्रुतिः + -प्रामाण्यतः <i>ind.</i> on the authority of the Veda; श्रुतिप्रामाण्यतो<BR> विद्वान् स्वधर्मे निविशेत वै Ms. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमण्डलम्
श्रुतिः + -मण्डलम्<BR>—1 the outer ear.<BR>—2 the whole circle of the quarter-tones; Śi. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमहत्|श्रुतिमहन्त्
श्रुतिः + -महत् <i>a.</i> rich in scriptural lore; सरस्वती श्रुतिमहतां<BR> महीयताम् Ś. 7. 35 (v. l. श्रुतमहताम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमूलम्
श्रुतिः + -मूलम्<BR>—1 the root of the ear; लपितुं किमपि श्रुतिमूले Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 a Vedic text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमूलक
श्रुतिः + -मूलक <i>a.</i> founded on the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिवचनम्
श्रुतिः + -वचनम् a Vedic precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिवर्जित|श्रुतिवर्ज्जित|श्रुतिवर्ज्जितः
श्रुतिः + -वर्जित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 deaf.<BR>—2 not knowing the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविप्रतिपन्न
श्रुतिः + -विप्रतिपन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 not recognizing the authority of the scriptures, disregarding the Vedas.<BR>—2 contrary to the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविवरम्
श्रुतिः + -विवरम् the auditory passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविशेषणार्थम्
श्रुतिः + -विशेषणार्थम् <i>ind.</i> for specialization in the Vedas; Svapna. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिविषयः|श्रुतिविषय
श्रुतिः + -विषयः<BR>—1 the object of the sense of hearing <i>i. e.</i> sound; श्रुतिविषयगुणा<BR> या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वम् Ś. 1. 1.<BR>—2 the reach or range of the ear; एतत् प्रायेण श्रुतिविषयमापतितमेव K.<BR>—3 the subject matter of the Veda.<BR>—4 any sacred ordinance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिवेधः|श्रुतिवेध
श्रुतिः + -वेधः boring the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिशिखरम्
श्रुतिः + -शिखरम्, -शिरस्<BR>—1 Upaniṣad or Vedānta; नमः सर्वेष्टाय श्रुतिशिखरदृष्टाय च नमः<BR> Viṣṇumahimna 30.<BR>—2 a leading text of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिशिरस्
श्रुतिः + -शिखरम्, -शिरस्<BR>—1 Upaniṣad or Vedānta; नमः सर्वेष्टाय श्रुतिशिखरदृष्टाय च नमः<BR> Viṣṇumahimna 30.<BR>—2 a leading text of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिसुख
श्रुतिः + -सुख, -मनोहर <i>a.</i> agreeable to the ear, melodious; श्रुतिसुखमुपवीणितं<BR> सहायैः Ki. 10. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिमनोहर
श्रुतिः + -सुख, -मनोहर <i>a.</i> agreeable to the ear, melodious; श्रुतिसुखमुपवीणितं<BR> सहायैः Ki. 10. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिस्फोटा
श्रुतिः + -स्फोटा Gynandropsis Pentaphylla (Mar. तिळवण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिस्मृति
श्रुतिः + -स्मृति <i>f.</i> (dual) revelation and legal institutes, Veda and<BR> law; श्रुतिस्मृतिपुराणोक्तफलप्राप्त्यर्थम् Pūjāmantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिहारिन्
श्रुतिः + -हारिन् <i>a.</i> captivating the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुती
श्रुती = श्रुति above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुवः|श्रुव
श्रुवः<BR>—1 A sacrifice.<BR>—2 A sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुवा
श्रुवा A sacrificial ladle; cf. स्रुवा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रुवावृक्षः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुवावृक्षः|श्रुवावृक्ष
श्रुवा + -वृक्षः the <i>Vikaṅkata</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1577-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्टिः|श्रुष्टि
