श्रोणी
श्रोणिः, -णी <i>f.</i><BR> [श्रोण्-इन् वा ङीप् Uṇ. 4. 53]<BR>—1 The hip or loins, the buttocks; श्रोणीभारादलसगमना Me. 84; श्रोणीभारस्त्यजति<BR> तनुताम् K. P. 10; Śi. 8. 31.<BR>—2 A road, way.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रोणितटः, श्रोणिफलकम्, श्रोणिबिम्बम्, श्रोणिसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणितटः|श्रोणितट
श्रोणिः + -तटः the slope of the hips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिफलकम्
श्रोणिः + -फलकम्<BR>—1 the broad hips.<BR>—2 the buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिबिम्बम्
श्रोणिः + -बिम्बम्<BR>—1 the round hips; रथाङ्गनामन् वियुतो रथाङ्गश्रोणिबिम्बया V. 4. 37.<BR>—2 a waist-band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिसूत्रम्
श्रोणिः + -सूत्रम्<BR>—1 a string worn round the loins.<BR>—2 a sword-belt; श्रोणिसूत्रं च खड्गं च विमलं कमलेक्षणः Rām. 7. 6. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
श्रोतस् <i>n.</i> [श्रु-असुन् तुट् च]<BR>—1 The ear.<BR>—2 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>—3 An organ of sense.<BR>—4 The stream or current (for स्रोतस् q. v.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रोतोरन्ध्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतोरन्ध्रम्
श्रोतस् + -रन्ध्रम् an aperture of the trunk, a nostril; श्रोतोरन्ध्रध्वनितसुभगं<BR> दन्तिभिः पीयमानः Me. 44; (also written स्रोतोरन्ध्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतृ
श्रोतृ <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A hearer.<BR>—2 A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रम्
श्रोत्रम् [श्रूयतेऽनेन श्रु-करणे-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>—1 The ear; श्रोत्रं श्रुतेनैव न कुण्डलेन Bh. 2. 71.<BR>—2 Proficiency in the Vedas.<BR>—3 The Veda.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रोत्रपदवी, श्रोत्रपरम्परा, श्रोत्रपालिः, श्रोत्रपुटः, श्रोत्रपेय, श्रोत्रमूलम्, श्रोत्रवादिन्, श्रोत्रसुख<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रपदवी
श्रोत्रम् + -पदवी the range of hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रपरम्परा
श्रोत्रम् + -परम्परा successive oral report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रपालिः|श्रोत्रपालि
श्रोत्रम् + -पालिः, -पुटः the lobe of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रपुटः|श्रोत्रपुट
श्रोत्रम् + -पालिः, -पुटः the lobe of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रपेय
श्रोत्रम् + -पेय <i>a.</i> to be imbibed by the ear, to be attentively heard;<BR> संदेशं मे तदनु जलद श्रोष्यसि श्रोत्रपेयम् Me. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रमूलम्
श्रोत्रम् + -मूलम् the root of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रवादिन्
श्रोत्रम् + -वादिन् <i>a.</i> obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रसुख
श्रोत्रम् + -सुख <i>a.</i> melodious, agreeable to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रिय|श्रोत्रियः
श्रोत्रिय <i>a.</i> [छन्दो वेदमधीते वेत्ति वा छन्दस् घ श्रोत्रादेशः;<BR> cf. P. V. 2. 84]<BR>—1 Proficient or versed in the Veda.<BR>—2 Teachable, tractable.<BR>—3 Modest, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रियः|श्रोत्रिय
श्रोत्रिय + .{@-यः@} A learned Brāhmaṇa, one well-versed in sacred learning;<BR> जन्मना ब्राह्मणो ज्ञेयः संस्कारैर्द्विज उच्यते । विद्यया याति विप्रत्वं<BR> त्रिभिः श्रोत्रिय उच्यते ॥; ते श्रोत्रियास्तत्त्वविनिश्चयाय भूरि श्रुतं शाश्वतमाद्रियन्ते<BR> Māl. 1. 5; R. 16. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रोत्रियस्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रियस्वम्
श्रोत्रिय + -स्वम् the property of a learned Brāhmaṇa; राजस्वं श्रोत्रियस्वं<BR> च न भोगेन प्रणश्यति Ms. 8. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत|श्रौतं|श्रौतः
श्रौत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [श्रुतौ विहितम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to the ear.<BR>—2 Relating to, founded on, or prescribed by, the Veda.<BR>—3 Sacrificial.<BR>—4 Audible, expressed in plain language (as a simile, opp. to आर्थ implied).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतम्
श्रौत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Any observance prescribed by the Vedas.<BR>—2 Ritual enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>—3 Preservation or maintenance of the sacred fire.<BR>—4 The three sacred fires collectively, (<i>i. e.</i> गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय<BR> and दक्षिण).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्रौतकर्मन्, श्रौतमार्गः, श्रौतसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतकर्मन्
श्रौत + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> Vedic rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतमार्गः|श्रौतमार्ग
श्रौत + -मार्गः hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौतसूत्रम्
श्रौत + -सूत्रम् N. of a class of Sūtra works based on the Veda (ascribed<BR> to आश्वलायन, सांख्यायन, कात्यायन &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत्रम्
श्रौत्रम् [श्रोत्र-स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>—1 The ear.<BR>—2 Proficiency in the Vedas. ━<i>a.</i> Relating to the ear; यश्चायमध्यात्मं<BR> श्रौत्रः प्रातिश्रुत्करतेजोमयोऽमृतमयः पुरुषः Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1578-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट् <i>ind.</i> An exclamation or formula used in making an offering<BR> with fire to the gods or departed spirits; cf. वषट् or वौषट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्ण|श्लक्ष्णं
श्लक्ष्ण <i>a.</i> [श्लिष्-क्स्न नि˚ Uṇ. 3. 19]<BR>—1 Soft, gentle, mild, bland (as words &c.); उवाच वचनं श्लक्ष्णं<BR> भूतभावनमव्ययम् Mb. 1. 7. 19.<BR>—2 Smooth, polished; यस्यामतिश्लक्ष्णतया गृहेषु विधातुमालेख्यमशक्नुवन्तः<BR> Śi. 3. 46; शाल्मलीफलके श्लक्ष्णे नेनिज्यान्नेजकः शनैः Ms. 8. 396.<BR>—3 Small. fine, thin, delicate; श्लक्ष्णं यत् परिहितमेतयोः किलान्तर्धानार्थं<BR> तदुदकसेकसक्तमूर्वोः Śi. 8. 65.<BR>—4 Beautiful, charming.<BR>—5 Candid, honest, frank.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लक्ष्णत्वच्, श्लक्ष्णपत्रकः, श्लक्ष्णपिष्ट, श्लक्ष्णवाच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णत्वच्
श्लक्ष्ण + -त्वच् <i>m.</i> Bauhinia Tomentosa (Mar. आपटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णपत्रकः|श्लक्ष्णपत्रक
श्लक्ष्ण + -पत्रकः ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णपिष्ट
श्लक्ष्ण + -पिष्ट <i>a.</i> ground fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णवाच्
श्लक्ष्ण + -वाच् kindly speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णक|श्लक्ष्णकं
श्लक्ष्णक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Smooth, soft.<BR>—2 Beautiful, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णकम्
श्लक्ष्णक + .{@-कम्@} The Areca-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लङ्क्|श्लंक्
श्लङ्क् €1 Ā. (श्लङ्कते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लङ्ग्|श्लंग्
श्लङ्ग् €1 Ā. (श्लङ्गते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ्
श्लथ् €1 P. (श्लथति)<BR>—1 To be loose or slackened; श्लथद्दुकूलं कबरीं च विच्युताम् Bhāg. 8. 12. 21.<BR>—2 To be weak or infirm.<BR>—3 To hurt, kill. ━<i>Caus.</i> (श्लथयति-ते) To slacken, loosen,<BR> relax (fig. also); श्लथयितुं क्षणमक्षमताङ्गना न सहसा सहसा कृतवेपथुः<BR> Śi. 6. 57; परित्राणस्नेहः श्लथयितुमशक्यः खलु यथा G. L. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Untied, unfastened.<BR>—2 Loose, relaxed, loosened, slipped off; वृन्ताच्छलथं हरति पुष्पमनोकहानाम्<BR> R. 5. 69, 19. 26.<BR>—3 Dishevelled (as hair).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लथोद्यम, श्लथबन्धनम्, श्लथलम्बिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथोद्यम
श्लथ + -उद्यम <i>a.</i> relaxing oneʼs efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथबन्धनम्
श्लथ + -बन्धनम् having the muscles relaxed; Ṛs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथलम्बिन्
श्लथ + -लम्बिन् <i>a.</i> hanging loosely down; श्लथलम्बिनीर्जटाः Ku. 5. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाख्
श्लाख् €1 P. (श्लाखति) To pervade, penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्
श्लाघ् €1 Ā. (श्लाघते)<BR>—1 To praise, extol, commend, applaud; शिरसा श्लाघते पूर्वं (गुणं)<BR> परं (दोषं) कण्ठे नियच्छति Subhāṣ.; यथैव श्लाघ्यते<BR> गङ्गा पादेन परमेष्ठिनः Ku. 6. 70 (some read श्लाघते for श्लाघ्यते<BR> and give it the next sense).<BR>—2 To boast of, be proud of; श्लाघिष्ये केन को बन्धून्नेष्यत्युन्नतिमुन्नतः Bk. 16. 4.<BR>—3 To flatter, coax (with dat.); गोपी कृष्णाय श्लाघते Sk.; श्लाघमानः<BR> परस्त्रीभ्यस्तत्रागाद्राक्षसाधिपः Bk. 8. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघनम्
श्लाघनम् [श्लाघ्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Praising, eulogizing.<BR>—2 Flattering. ━<i>a.</i> Boasting, a boaster; Mb. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघा
श्लाघा [श्लाघ्-अ]<BR>—1 Praise, eulogy, commendation; कर्णजयद्रथयोर्वा कात्र श्लाघा Ve. 2.<BR>—2 Self-praise, boast; हते जरति गाङ्गेये पुरस्कृत्य शिखण्डिनम् । या<BR> श्लाघा पाण्डुपुत्राणां सैवास्माकं भविष्यति ॥ Ve. 2. 4.<BR>—3 Flattery.<BR>—4 Service.<BR>—5 Wish, desire.<BR>—6 Pleasure, delight in anything.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लाघाविपर्ययः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघाविपर्ययः
श्लाघा + -विपर्ययः absence of boasting; त्यागे श्लाघाविपर्ययः R. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघित
श्लाघित <i>p. p.</i> Praised, eulogized, commended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघिन्
श्लाघिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Haughty; अभिगर्जन्ति हरयः श्लाघिनः परशङ्कया Bhāg. 8. 2. 6.<BR>—2 Proud, boasting.<BR>—3 Celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्य|श्लाघ्यः
श्लाघ्य [श्लाघ्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 Praised, praiseworthy; श्लाघ्यान्वयेति नयनोत्सवकारिणीति Māl. 6. 17;<BR> U. 4. 9, 13.<BR>—2 Respectable, venerable.<BR>—3 Laudable, commendable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिकुः|श्लिकु
श्लिकुः [श्लिष्-कु नेत्वम् पृषो˚ Uṇ. 1. 32]<BR>—1 A debauchee, libertine.<BR>—2 A slave, dependent. ━<i>n.</i> The science of astronomy, astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिक्युः|श्लिक्यु
श्लिक्युः<BR>—1 A libertine.<BR>—2 A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
श्लिष् I. €1 P. (श्लेषति) To burn. ━II. €4 P. (श्लिष्यति, श्लिष्ट)<BR>—1 To embrace; श्लिष्यति चुम्बति जलधरकल्पं हरिरुपगत इति तिमिरमनल्पम् Gīt. 6.<BR>—2 To stick, cling or adhere to.<BR>—3 To unite, join.<BR>—4 To grasp, take, understand; आश्लेषि न श्लेषकवेर्भवत्याः श्लोकद्वयार्थः<BR> सुधिया मया किम् N. 3. 69.<BR>—5 (Ā.) To result, be the consequence of anything. ━III. €10 U. (श्लेषयति-ते)<BR> To unite, join, connect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिषा
श्लिषा<BR>—1 An embrace.<BR>—2 Clinging, adherence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्ट|श्लिष्टः
श्लिष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [श्लिष्-क्त]<BR>—1 Embraced.<BR>—2 Clung, adhered to.<BR>—3 Resting or leaning on.<BR>—4 Involving a pun, susceptible of a double interpretation; अत्र विषमादयः<BR> शब्दाः श्लिष्टाः K. P. 10.<BR>—5 Fitting tight (as a coat of mail); विबभौ सर्वतः श्लिष्टम् (वर्म)<BR> Mb. 7. 127. 18.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लिष्टरूपकम्, श्लिष्टवर्त्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्टरूपकम्
श्लिष्ट + -रूपकम् ambiguity as a metaphor; राजहंसोपभोगार्हं भ्रमरप्रार्थ्यसौरभम् ।<BR> सखि वक्त्राम्बुजमिदं तवेति श्लिष्टरूपकम् ॥ Kāv. 2. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्टवर्त्मन्
श्लिष्ट + -वर्त्मन् the adhering together of the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्टिः|श्लिष्टि
श्लिष्टिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Embrace.<BR>—2 Adherence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषः|श्लेष
श्लेषः [श्लिष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 An embrace.<BR>—2 Clinging or adhering to.<BR>—3 Union, junction, contact; निरन्तरश्लेषघनाः K. (where it has<BR> the next sense also).<BR>—4 Pun, paronomasia, <i>double entendre</i>, susceptibility of a word or<BR> sentence to yield two or more interpretations (regarded as a figure of<BR> speech and very commonly used by poets; for def. see K. P. Kārikas 84 and 96);<BR> आश्लेषि न श्लेषकवेर्भवत्याः श्लोकद्वयार्थः सुधिया मया किम्<BR> N. 3. 69; see शब्दश्लेष also.<BR>—5 Burning.<BR>—6 Sexual union; ततो गर्भः संभवति श्लेषात् स्त्रीपुंसयोर्नृप Mb. 13. 111. 30.<BR>—7 A grammatical augment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लेषार्थः, श्लेषोपमा, श्लेषभित्तिक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषार्थः|श्लेषार्थ
श्लेषः + -अर्थः a pun, <i>double entendre</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषोपमा
श्लेषः + -उपमा a comparison containing double meanings; शिशिरांशुप्रतिद्वन्द्वि<BR> श्रीमत् सुरभिगन्धि च । अम्भोजमिव ते वक्त्रमिति श्लेषोपमा स्मृता ॥ Kāv. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषभित्तिक
श्लेषः + -भित्तिक <i>a.</i> trusting on (lit. having for its basis) a Śleṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषक
श्लेषक <i>a.</i> Attaching, connecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषिन्
श्लेषिन् <i>a.</i> Adhering, clinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषा
श्लेषा An embrace; अन्योन्यश्लेषयोत्तुङ्गनिरन्तरपयोधराम् Bhāg. 3. 20. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदम्
श्लीपदम् Swelled leg, elephantiasis.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लीपदापहः, श्लीपदप्रभवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदापहः|श्लीपदापह
श्लीपदम् + -अपहः removing elephantiasis, the पुत्रजीवी tree, Putrañjiva Roxburghii.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदप्रभवः|श्लीपदप्रभव
श्लीपदम् + -प्रभवः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1579-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदिन्
श्लीपदिन् <i>m.</i> A club-footed man<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लील|श्लीलः
श्लील <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Lucky, prosperous; see श्रील.<BR>—2 Decent; cf. अश्लील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मन्
श्लेष्मन् <i>m.</i> [श्लिष्-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 157]<BR>—1 Phlegmatic humour; गुडेन वर्धितः श्लेष्मा सुखं वृद्धया निपात्यते Pt. 3. 62.<BR>—2 Mucus (of the eye); स सुप्त इव चाण्डालः श्लेष्मापिहितलोचनः Mb. 12. 141. 44.<BR>━<i>n.</i> A band, cord.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लेष्मातिसारः, श्लेष्मौजस्, श्लेष्मकटाहकः, श्लेष्मघ्ना, श्लेष्मघ्नी, श्लेष्मधातुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातिसारः|श्लेष्मातिसार
श्लेष्मन् + -अतिसारः dysentery produced by vitiated phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मौजस्
श्लेष्मन् + -ओजस् <i>n.</i> the phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मकटाहकः|श्लेष्मकटाहक
श्लेष्मन् + -कटाहकः a spittoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मघ्ना
श्लेष्मन् + -घ्ना, -घ्नी<BR>—1 the Arabian jasmine.<BR>—2 the hog-weed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मघ्नी
श्लेष्मन् + -घ्ना, -घ्नी<BR>—1 the Arabian jasmine.<BR>—2 the hog-weed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मधातुः|श्लेष्मधातु
श्लेष्मन् + -धातुः the phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मकः|श्लेष्मक
श्लेष्मकः Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मण|श्लेष्मणः
श्लेष्मण <i>a.</i> Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मिक|श्लेष्मिकं
श्लेष्मिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Phlegmatic.<BR>—2 Producing phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातः|श्लेष्मात
श्लेष्मातः, श्लेष्मातकः A kind of tree; Cordia Latifolia (Mar. भोकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातकः|श्लेष्मातक
श्लेष्मातः, श्लेष्मातकः A kind of tree; Cordia Latifolia (Mar. भोकर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मिन्
श्लेष्मिन् Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्
श्लोक् €1 Ā. (श्लोकते)<BR>—1 To praise or compose in verse, versify.<BR>—2 To acquire.<BR>—3 To abandon, give up.<BR>—4 To heap together, collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकः|श्लोक
श्लोकः [श्लोक्-अच्]<BR>—1 Praising in verse, extolling.<BR>—2 A hymn or verse of praise.<BR>—3 Celebrity, fame, renown, name; as in पुण्यश्लोक q. v.; वैदेहि<BR> तावदमलो भुवनेषु पुण्यः श्लोकः प्रशस्तचरितैरुपगीयतां ते Mv. 7. 26;<BR> उत्तमश्लोक˚ Bhāg. 2. 1. 9.<BR>—4 An object of praise.<BR>—5 A proverb or saying.<BR>—6 A stanza or verse in general; श्लोकत्वमापद्यत यस्य शोकः R. 14. 70;<BR> समाक्षरैश्चतुर्भिर्यः पादैर्गीतो महर्षिणा । सोऽनुव्याहरणाद्भूयः<BR> शोकः श्लोकत्वमागतः ॥ Rām. 1. 2. 40.<BR>—7 A stanza or verse in the Anuṣṭubh metre.<BR>—8 The dear and beloved people (इष्टमित्र ?); यया ह वै पदेनानुविन्देदेवं<BR> कीर्ति श्लोकं विन्दते Bṛ. Up. 1. 4. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्लोककारः, श्लोकभू<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोककारः|श्लोककार
श्लोकः + -कारः a composer of Ślokas; P. III. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकभू
श्लोकः + -भू <i>a.</i> appearing in sound; Ait. Ār.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकयति
श्लोकयति Den. P. To celebrate or praise in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्य
श्लोक्य <i>a.</i> Praiseworthy; शरण्यो नावधीच्छ्लोक्य आह चेदं हसन्निव<BR> Bhāg. 1. 17. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण्
श्लोण् €1 P. (श्लोणति) To heap together, collect, gather; cf. श्रोण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोणः|श्लोण
श्लोणः A lame man, cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वङ्क्|श्वंक्
श्वङ्क् €1 Ā. (श्वङ्कते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वच्
श्वच्, श्वञ्च् €1 Ā. (श्वचते, श्वञ्चते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To be opened, gape, be split or cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वञ्च्|श्वंच्
श्वच्, श्वञ्च् €1 Ā. (श्वचते, श्वञ्चते)<BR>—1 To go, move.<BR>—2 To be opened, gape, be split or cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वज्
श्वज् €1 Ā. (श्वजते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ्
श्वठ् €10 U. (श्वठयति-ते)<BR>—1 To speak ill; (श्वाठयति only according to some).<BR>—2 (श्वाठयति-ते)<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To go, move.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To adorn.<BR>——(<i>c</i>) To finish, accomplish; (only श्वठयति in these senses according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वण्ठ्
श्वण्ठ् €10 U. (श्वण्ठयति) To speak ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वन्
श्वन् <i>m.</i> [श्वि-क्रनिन् नि˚ Uṇ. 1. 158] (Nom. श्वा, श्वानौ,<BR> श्वानः acc. pl. शुनः; शुनी <i>f.</i>) A dog; श्वा यदि क्रियते राजा<BR> स किं नाश्नात्युपानहम् Subhāṣ.; Bh. 2. 31; Ms. 2. 208.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: श्वादः, श्वाश्वः, श्वक्रीडिन्, श्ववत्, श्वगणः, श्वगणिकः, श्वजीविका, श्वदंष्ट्रा, श्वदयितम्, श्वधूर्तः, श्वनरः, श्वनिशम्, श्वनिशा, श्वपच्, श्वपदम्, श्वपाकः, श्वफलम्, श्वफल्कः, श्वभीरुः, श्वयूथ्यम्, श्ववृत्तिः, श्वव्याघ्रः, श्वहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वादः|श्वाद
श्वन् + -अदः = श्वपाकः q. v.; श्वादोऽपि सद्यः सवनाय कल्पते<BR> Bhāg. 3. 33. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वाश्वः|श्वाश्व
श्वन् + -अश्वः an epithet of Bhairava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वक्रीडिन्
