श्वनिशा
श्वन् + -निशम्, -निशा a night on which dogs bark; (the 14th day of the<BR> dark half of a month).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपच्
श्वन् + -पच् <i>m.</i>, {@-पचः@}<BR>—1 a man of a very low and degraded caste, an outcast, a Cāṇḍāla;<BR> Ms. 3. 92; श्वपचात्मभुवोर्निरन्तरा मम भूयात् परमात्मनि स्थितिः Bv. 4. 23.<BR>—2 a dog-feeder.<BR>—3 a public executioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपदम्
श्वन् + -पदम्<BR>—1 a dogʼs foot.<BR>—2 a mark like a dogʼs foot (to be branded on the forehead of a thief);<BR> स्तेये च श्वपदं कार्यम् Ms. 9. 237.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1580-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वपाकः|श्वपाक
