षष् + -ऊर्मिः the six waves of existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडूषणम्
षष् + -ऊषणम् (षडूषणम्) six spices taken collectively; पञ्चकोलं<BR> समरिचं षडूषणमुदाहृतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षडृतुः|षडृतु
षष् + -ऋतुः <i>m.</i> pl. the six seasons (<i>i. e.</i> वसन्त, ग्रीष्म,<BR> वर्षा, शरद्, हेमन्त and शिशिर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्ण|षट्कर्णः
षष् + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> (षट्कर्ण) heard by six ears; <i>i. e.</i><BR> by a third person other than the speaker and the person spoken to; told<BR> to more than one listener (as a counsel, secret &c.); षट्कर्णो भिद्यते<BR> मन्त्रः Pt. 1. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्णः|षट्कर्ण
षष् + -कर्ण + .({@-र्णः@}) a kind of lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कर्मन्|षट्कर्म्मन्
षष् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> (षट्कर्मन्)<BR>—1 the six acts or duties enjoined on a Brāhmaṇa; they are अध्यापनमध्ययनं<BR> यजनं याजनं तथा । दानं प्रतिग्रहश्चैव षट्कर्माण्यग्रजन्मनः ॥ Ms. 10. 75.<BR>—2 the six acts allowable to a Brāhmaṇa for his subsistence:− उञ्छं<BR> प्रतिग्रहो भिक्षा वाणिज्यं पशुपालनम् । कृषिकर्म तथा चेति षट्कर्माण्यग्रजन्मनः ॥.<BR>—3 the six acts that may be performed by means of magic:− शान्ति, वशीकरण,<BR> स्तम्भन, विद्वेष, उच्चाटन and मारण.<BR>—4 the six acts belonging to the practice of Yoga:− धौतिर्वस्ती तथा नेती<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">Page1583-2</a>]<BR> नौलिकी (नौलिकः) त्राटकस्तथा । कपालभाती चैतानि षट्कर्माणि समाचरेत् ॥ ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a Brāhmaṇa skilled in the above six acts.<BR>—2 one well-versed in the Tantra magical rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कोण|षट्कोणं
षष् + -कोण <i>a.</i> (षट्कोण) hexangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कोणम्
षष् + -कोण + .({@-णम्@})<BR>—1 a hexagon.<BR>—2 the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—3 a diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गया
षष् + -गया the sixfold <i>gayā</i>; गयागजो गयादित्यो गायत्री च गदाधरः ।<BR> गया गयासुरश्चैव षड्गया मुक्तिदायकाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गवम्
षष् + -गवम् (षड्गवम्)<BR>—1 a team or yoke of six oxen.<BR>—2 a yoke of six (sometimes after the names of other animals); <i>i. e.</i><BR> हस्ति˚, अश्व˚ ‘six elephants, horses &c.’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गवीय
षष् + -गवीय <i>a.</i> drawn by six oxen; न यद्वहेच्छकटं षड्गवीयम् Mb. 8. 76. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गुण
षष् + -गुण <i>a.</i> (षड्गुण)<BR>—1 sixfold.<BR>—2 having six attributes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्गुणम्
षष् + -गुण + .({@-णम्@})<BR>—1 an assemblage of six qualities.<BR>—2 the six expedients to be used by a king in foreign politics; see under<BR> गुण (21); cf. षाङ्गुण्य also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थः|षड्ग्रन्थ
षष् + -ग्रन्थः a kind of Karañja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थि
षष् + -ग्रन्थि <i>n.</i> (षड्ग्रन्थि) the root of long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्ग्रन्थिका|षड्ग्रंथिका
षष् + -ग्रन्थिका (षड्ग्रन्थिका) zedoary (शठी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चक्रम्
षष् + -चक्रम् (षट्चक्रम्) the six mystical circles of the body,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> मूलाधार, स्वाधिष्ठान, मणिपूर, अनाहत, विशुद्ध and आज्ञाख्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चत्वारिंशत्
षष् + -चत्वारिंशत् (षट्चत्वारिंशत्) forty-six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्चरणः|षट्चरण
षष् + -चरणः (षट्चरणः)<BR>—1 a bee.<BR>—2 a locust.<BR>—3 a louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्जः|षड्ज
षष् + -जः (षड्जः) the fourth (or first according to some)<BR> of the seven primary notes of the Indian gamut; so called because it is<BR> derived from the six ergans: नासां कण्ठमुरस्तालु जिह्वां दताञ्श्च संस्पृशन् ।<BR> षड्जः सञ्जायते (षड्भ्यः सञ्जायते) यस्मात्तस्मात् षड्ज इति स्मृतः ॥<BR> it is said to resemble the note of peacocks; षड्जं रौति मयूरस्तु<BR> Nārada.; षड्जसंवादिनीः केकाः द्विधा भिन्नाः शिखण्डिभिः R. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्तन्त्री
षष् + -तन्त्री N. of the six philosophical systems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्त्रिंशत्
षष् + -त्रिंशत् <i>f.</i> (षट्त्रिंशत्) thirty-six; ({@षट्त्रिंश@}<BR> <i>a.</i> thirty-sixth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्तिलिन्
षष् + -तिलिन् <i>m.</i> one performing six acts with sesamum seeds; तिलोद्वतीं<BR> तिलस्नायी तिलहोमी तिलप्रदः । तिलभुक् तिलवापी च षट्तिली नावसीदति ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्दर्शनम्
षष् + -दर्शनम् (षड्दर्शनम्) the six principal systems of Hindu philosophy;<BR> they are: सांख्य, योग, न्याय, वैशेषिक, मीमांसा and वेदान्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्दर्शनः|षड्दर्शन
षष् + -दर्शनम् + .({@-नः@}) one conversant with the above six systems.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्दीर्घः|षड्दीर्घ
षष् + -दीर्घः the six long vowels: आ, ई, ऊ, ऋ, ऐ, and औ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्दुर्गम्
षष् + -दुर्गम् (षड्दुर्गम्) the six kinds of forts taken collectively;<BR> धन्वदुर्गं महीदुर्गं गिरिदुर्गं तथैव च । मनुष्यदुर्गं मृद्दुर्गं<BR> वनदुर्गमिति क्रमात् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्नवतिः
षष् + -नवतिः <i>f.</i> (षण्णवतिः) ninety-six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पञ्चाशत्|षट्पंचाशत्
षष् + -पञ्चाशत् <i>f.</i> (षट्पञ्चाशत्) fifty-six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदः|षट्पद
षष् + -पदः (षट्पदः)<BR>—1 a bee; न पङ्कजं तद्यदलीनषट्पदं न षट्पदोऽसौ न जुगुञ्ज यः<BR> कलम् Bk. 2. 19; Ku. 5. 9; R. 6. 69.<BR>—2 a louse.<BR>—3 a verse consisting of six <i>padas</i>. ˚अथितिः<BR>—1 the mango tree.<BR>—2 the Champaka tree. ˚आनन्दवर्धनः the Aśoka or Kiṅkirāta tree.<BR> ˚ज्य <i>a.</i> having bees for the bow-string (as the bow of Cupid);<BR> प्रायश्चापं न वहति भयान्मन्मथः षट्पदज्यम् Me. 75. ˚प्रियः<BR> the tree called नागकेशर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पदी
षष् + -पदी (षट्पदी)<BR>—1 a stanza consisting of six lines.<BR>—2 a female bee.<BR>—3 a louse.<BR>—4 the six states (‘योऽशनायापिपासे शोकं मोहं जरां मृत्युमत्येति’<BR> इति श्रुत्युक्ताः Mb. 3. 314. 9 Com.):− hunger, thirst, sorrow, disordered<BR> intellect, old age and death; other version is:− कामक्रोधौ लोभमोहौ<BR> मदमानौ च षट्पदी ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्पादः|षट्पाद
षष् + -पादः (षट्पादः) a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्प्रज्ञः|षट्प्रज्ञ
षष् + -प्रज्ञः (षट्प्रज्ञः)<BR>—1 one who is well acquainted with six<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">Page1584-1</a>]<BR> subjects <i>i. e.</i> the four <i>Puruṣārthas</i> or objects of human existence,<BR> the nature of the world, and the nature of the Supreme Spirit; धर्मार्थकाममोक्षेषु<BR> लोकतत्त्वार्थयोरपि । षट्सु प्रज्ञा तु यस्यासौ षट्प्रज्ञः परिकीर्तितः ॥<BR>—2 a lustful or licentious man.<BR>—3 a good-hearted neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1583-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्बिन्दुः|षड्बिन्दु|षड्बिंदु
षष् + -बिन्दुः (षड्बिन्दुः) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भागः|षड्भाग
षष् + -भागः (षङ्भागः) a sixth part, one-sixth; तपःषङ्भागमक्षय्यं<BR> ददत्यारण्यका हि नः Ś. 2. 14; Ms. 7. 131, 8. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भाववादिन्
षष् + -भाववादिन् a maintainer of the theory of the six भावs (<i>i. e.</i><BR> द्रव्य, गुण, कर्मन्, सामान्य, विशेष and समवाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भुज|षड्भुजः
षष् + -भुज <i>a.</i> (षड्भुज)<BR>—1 six-armed.<BR>—2 six-sided, hexagonal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भुजः|षड्भुज
षष् + -भुज + .({@-जः@}) a hexagon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्भुजा
षष् + -भुज + .({@-जा@})<BR>—1 an epithet of Durgā.<BR>—2 the water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मतस्थापकः|षण्मतस्थापक
षष् + -मतस्थापकः (षण्मतस्थापकः) N. of Śaṃkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मासः|षण्मास
षष् + -मासः (षण्मासः) a period of six months. ˚निचय<BR> <i>a.</i> one who has a store (of food) sufficient for six months; Ms. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मासिक
षष् + -मासिक <i>a.</i> (षण्मासिक) half-yearly, occurring every six months.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मुखः|षण्मुख
षष् + -मुखः (षण्मुखः) an epithet of Kārtikeya; स गुणानां बलानां<BR> च षण्णां षण्मुखविक्रमः R. 17. 67; Mv. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षण्मुखा
षष् + -मुखः + .({@-खा@}) a water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रसम्
षष् + -रसम्, -रसाः (<i>m.</i> pl.) (षड्रसम् &c.) the six flavours<BR> taken collectively; see under रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रसाः
षष् + -रसम्, -रसाः (<i>m.</i> pl.) (षड्रसम् &c.) the six flavours<BR> taken collectively; see under रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रात्रम्
षष् + -रात्रम् (षड्रात्रम्) a period of six nights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्रेखा
षष् + -रेखा (षड्रेखा) a water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्वर्गः|षड्वर्ग
षष् + -वर्गः (षड्वर्गः)<BR>—1 an aggregate of six things.<BR>—2 especially, the six enemies of mankind; (also called षड्रिपु); कामः<BR> क्रोधस्तथा लोभो मदमोहौ च मत्सरः; कृतारिषड्वर्गजयेन Ki. 1 9;<BR> व्यजेष्ठ षड्वर्गम् Bk. 1. 2.<BR>—3 the five senses and Manas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विंशम्
षष् + -विंशम् N. of a Brāhmaṇa belonging to the Sāma Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विंशतिः|षड्विंशति
षष् + -विंशतिः <i>f.</i> (षड्विंशतिः) twenty-six; ({@षड्विंश@} twenty-sixth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्विध|षड्विधं
षष् + -विध (षड्विध) <i>a.</i> of six kinds, sixfold; षड्विधं<BR> बलमादाय प्रतस्थे दिग्जिगीषया R. 4. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्छास्त्रिन्
षष् + -शास्त्रिन् <i>m.</i> one conversant with the six Śāstras or darśanas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्षष्टिः|षट्षष्टि
षष् + -षष्टिः <i>f.</i> (षट्षष्टिः) sixty-six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्सप्ततिः|षट्सप्तति
षष् + -सप्ततिः (षट्सप्ततिः) seventy-six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्क|षट्कः
षट्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sixfold.<BR>—2 Bought for six &c.; P. V. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कः|षट्क
षट्क + .{@-कः@} Six.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्कम्
षट्क + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 An aggregate of six; मासषट्क, पूर्वषट्क, उत्तरषट्क &c.<BR>—2 The six passions collectively viz. (काम, मद, मान, लोभ, हर्ष, and रुषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्धा
षड्धा See षोढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिः|षष्टि
षष्टिः <i>f.</i> Sixty; Ms. 3. 177; Y. 3. 84. ˚तम sixtieth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: षष्टितन्त्रम्, षष्टिभागः, षष्टिमत्तः, षष्टियोजनी, षष्टिसंवत्सरः, षष्टिहायनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टितन्त्रम्
षष्टिः + -तन्त्रम् the doctrine of 60 conceptions (of the Sāṃkhya philosophy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिभागः|षष्टिभाग
षष्टिः + -भागः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिमत्तः|षष्टिमत्त
षष्टिः + -मत्तः an elephant who has reached the age of sixty and is in<BR> rut at that time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टियोजनी
षष्टिः + -योजनी <i>f.</i> a journey or extent of sixty <i>Yojanas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिसंवत्सरः|षष्टिसंवत्सर
षष्टिः + -संवत्सरः a period of sixty years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिहायनः|षष्टिहायन
षष्टिः + -हायनः<BR>—1 an elephant (sixty years old).<BR>—2 a kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक|षष्टिकः
षष्टिक <i>a.</i> Bought with sixty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिकः|षष्टिक
षष्टिक + .{@-कः, -का@} A kind of rice of quick growth; घृतक्षीरसमायुक्तं<BR> विधिवत् षष्टिकौदनम् Mb. 13. 64. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिका
षष्टिक + .{@-कः, -का@} A kind of rice of quick growth; घृतक्षीरसमायुक्तं<BR> विधिवत् षष्टिकौदनम् Mb. 13. 64. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक्यम्
षष्टिक्यम् A field sown with the above kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठ|षष्ठः
षष्ठ <i>a.</i> (-ष्ठी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sixth, the sixth; षष्ठं तु क्षेत्रजस्यांशं प्रदद्यात्<BR> पैतृकाद्धनात् Ms. 9. 164, 7. 130; षष्ठे भागे V. 2. 1; R. 17. 78;<BR> षष्ठे काले मयाऽऽहारः प्राप्तोऽयमनुजस्तव Mb. 3. 180. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: षष्ठांशः, षष्ठान्नम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठांशः|षष्ठांश
षष्ठ + -अंशः<BR>—1 a sixth part in general.<BR>—2 particularly, the sixth part of the produce of fields &c., which the<BR> king takes from his subjects as land-tax; ऊधस्यमिच्छामि तवोपभोक्तुं<BR> षष्ठांशमुर्व्या इव रक्षितायाः R. 2. 66; (the different kinds of produce,<BR> to the sixth part of which a king is entitled, are specified in Ms. 7. 131-132).<BR> ˚वृत्तिः a king (entitled to the sixth part of the produce);<BR> षष्ठांशवृत्तेरपि धर्म एषः Ś. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठान्नम्
षष्ठ + -अन्नम् the sixth meal. ˚कालः taking food once in three days,<BR> as an expiatory act; षष्ठान्नकालता मासं संहिताजप एव वा Ms. 11. 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठी
षष्ठी<BR>—1 The sixth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR>—2 The sixth or genitive case (in gram.).<BR>—3 An epithet of Durgā in the form of Kātyāyanī, one of the 16 divine mothers.<BR>—4 A goddess worshipped on the sixth day of child-birth (Mar. सटवाई);<BR> गणेशं जन्मदां षष्ठीं देवीं जीवन्तिकामपि Śiva B. 6. 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः, षष्ठीपूजनम्, षष्ठीपूजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठीतत्पुरुषः|षष्ठीतत्पुरुष
षष्ठी + -तत्पुरुषः the genitive Tatpuruṣa compound, one in which, when<BR> dissolved, the first member usually stands in the genitive case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठीपूजनम्
षष्ठी + -पूजनम्, -पूजा worship of the goddess षष्ठी performed on<BR> the sixth day after a womanʼs delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठीपूजा
षष्ठी + -पूजनम्, -पूजा worship of the goddess षष्ठी performed on<BR> the sixth day after a womanʼs delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षहसानुः|षहसानु
षहसानुः<BR>—1 A peacock.<BR>—2 A sacrifice. ━<i>a.</i> Full of forgiveness; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्
षाट् <i>ind.</i> A vocative particle; interjection of calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्कौशिक
षाट्कौशिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Incased or enveloped in six sheaths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्पौरुषिक
षाट्पौरुषिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to six generations (पुरुष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाडवः|षाडव
षाडवः<BR>—1 Passion, sentiment.<BR>—2 Singing, music.<BR>—3 (In music) A <i>Rāga</i> in which six of the seven primary notes are<BR> used; औडवः पञ्चभिः प्रोक्तः स्वरैः षङ्भिस्तु षाडवः ।<BR>—4 Confectionery, sweetmeats; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाडविकः|षाडविक
षाडविकः A confectioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाड्गुण्यम्
षाड्गुण्यम् [षड् गुणा एव ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 The collection of six qualities.<BR>—2 Six expedients to be used by a king, six measures of royal policy;<BR> षाड्गुण्यसमुद्देशः Kau. A. 6; षाड्गुण्यमुपयुञ्जीत शक्त्यपेक्षी रसायनम्<BR> Śi. 2. 93; see under गुण also; षाड्गुण्यस्य प्रयोगेण तत्तन्मन्त्रबलेन<BR> च Śiva B. 11. 3.<BR>—3 Multiplication of anything by six.<BR>—4 Six properties.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: षाड्गुण्यप्रयोगः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाड्गुण्यप्रयोगः|षाड्गुण्यप्रयोग
षाड्गुण्यम् + -प्रयोगः employment of the six expedients or measures of royal policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मातुरः|षाण्मातुर
षाण्मातुरः [षड् मातरोऽस्य] Having six mothers, an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मासिक
षाण्मासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Six monthly, half-yearly.<BR>—2 Six months old; मौक्तिकानां षाण्मासिकानाम् Vb. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1584-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाष्ठ|षाष्ठः
षाष्ठ (-ष्ठी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sixth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1585-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिड्गः|षिड्ग
षिड्गः<BR>—1 A lustful or libidinous man, libertine, lecher.<BR>—2 A gallant, an inconsistent lover (विट); षिड्गैरगद्यत ससंभ्रममेव<BR> काचित् Śi. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1585-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुः|षु
षुः Delivery, child-bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1585-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

