संज्वलनम् Fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्
सट् I. €1 P. (सटति) To form a part. ━II. €10 U. (साटयति-ते)<BR> To show, display, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटम्
सटम्, सटा<BR>—1 An asceticʼs matted hair.<BR>—2 The mane (of a lion); केनानेकपदानवासितसटः सिंहोऽर्पितः पञ्जरे<BR> Mu. 7. 6; Śi. 1. 47.<BR>—3 Bristles of a boar; विध्यन्तमुद्धृतसटाः प्रतिहन्तुमीषुः R. 9. 60.<BR>—4 A braid of hair.<BR>—5 A crest.<BR>—6 (Fig.) Lustre, light; जटां तडिद्वह्निसटोग्ररोचिषम् Bhāg. 4. 5. 2.<BR>—7 A multitude, number.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सटाङ्कः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटा
सटम्, सटा<BR>—1 An asceticʼs matted hair.<BR>—2 The mane (of a lion); केनानेकपदानवासितसटः सिंहोऽर्पितः पञ्जरे<BR> Mu. 7. 6; Śi. 1. 47.<BR>—3 Bristles of a boar; विध्यन्तमुद्धृतसटाः प्रतिहन्तुमीषुः R. 9. 60.<BR>—4 A braid of hair.<BR>—5 A crest.<BR>—6 (Fig.) Lustre, light; जटां तडिद्वह्निसटोग्ररोचिषम् Bhāg. 4. 5. 2.<BR>—7 A multitude, number.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सटाङ्कः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटाङ्कः|सटाङ्क|सटांक
सटम् + -अङ्कः a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटाल
सटाल <i>a.</i> Full of; Inscr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटिः|सटि
सटिः, -टी <i>f.</i>, सटिका<BR> Zedoary (Mar. कचोरा, आंबेहळद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटी
सटिः, -टी <i>f.</i>, सटिका<BR> Zedoary (Mar. कचोरा, आंबेहळद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटिका
सटिः, -टी <i>f.</i>, सटिका<BR> Zedoary (Mar. कचोरा, आंबेहळद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सटीक
सटीक <i>a.</i> Accompanied or explained by a commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्ट्
सट्ट् €10 U. (सट्टयति-ते)<BR>—1 To injure, kill.<BR>—2 To be strong.<BR>—3 To give.<BR>—4 To take.<BR>—5 To dwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्टम्
सट्टम् Two pieces of timber at the side of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्टकम्
सट्टकम् A kind of minor drama in Prākṛta; <i>e. g.</i> कर्पूरमञ्जरी; see S. D. 542.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सट्वा
सट्वा<BR>—1 A kind of bird.<BR>—2 A musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सठ्
सठ् €10 U. (साठयति-ते)<BR>—1 To finish, complete.<BR>—2 To leave unfinished.<BR>—3 To go, move.<BR>—4 To adorn, decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सठिः|सठि
सठिः <i>f.</i> The plant zedoary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सणसूत्रम्
सणसूत्रम् A hempen cord or thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सणिः|सणि
सणिः The smell of the breath of a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संटङ्कः|सण्टङ्क
संटङ्कः Connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्ड|संड|सण्डः
सण्ड See षण्ढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्डिशः|सण्डिश|संडिश|संडिशः
सण्डिशः A pair of tongs or nippers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संडीनम्
संडीनम् One of the several modes of flight of birds; Mb. 8. 41. 26<BR> (com. संडीनं ललितं गतम्); see डीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सण्ढिका
सण्ढिका A female camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्|सन्त्|संत्
सत् <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Being, existing, existent; सन्तः स्वतः प्रकाशन्ते गुणा न परतो<BR> नृणाम् Bv. 1. 120; सत्कल्पवृक्षे वने Ś. 7. 12.<BR>—2 Real, essential, true; Bṛ. Up. 2. 3. 1.<BR>—3 Good, virtuous, chaste; सती सती योगविसृष्टदेहा Ku. 1. 21; Ś. 5. 17.<BR>—4 Noble, worthy, high; as in सत्कुलम्.<BR>—5 Right, proper.<BR>—6 Best, excellent.<BR>—7 Venerable, respectable.<BR>—8 Wise, learned.<BR>—9 Handsome, beautiful.<BR>—10 Firm, steady. ━<i>m.</i> A good or virtuous man, a sage; आदानं हि<BR> विसर्गाय सतां वारिमुचामिव R. 4. 86; अविरतं परकार्यकृतां सतां<BR> मधुरिमातिशयेन वचोऽमृतम् Bv. 1. 113; Bh. 2. 78; R. 1. 10. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 That which really exists, entity, existence, essence.<BR>—2 The really existent truth, reality.<BR>—3 Good; as in सदसत् q. v.<BR>—4 Brahman or the Supreme Spirit.<BR>—5 Ved. Water.<BR>—6 The primary cause (कारण); य ईक्षिताऽहं रहितोऽप्यसत्सतोः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 38. 11.<BR>—7 (In gram.) The termination of the present participle. (सत्कृ means<BR>—1 to respect, treat with respect, receive hospitably.<BR>—2 to honour, worship, adore.<BR>—3 to adorn.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदञ्जनम्, सदर्थः, सदसत्, सदाचारः, सदात्मन्, सदानन, सदुत्तरम्, सत्करणम्, सत्कर्तृ, सत्कर्मन्, सत्काण्डः, सत्कारः, सत्कार्यम्, सत्कुल, सत्कुलीन, सत्कृत, सत्कृतिः, सत्क्रिया, सद्गतिः, सद्गुण, सद्घनः, सच्चरित, सच्चरित्र, सच्चारा, सच्चिद्, सज्जन, सद्धर्मः, सत्पतिः, सत्पत्रम्, सत्पथः, सत्परिग्रहः, सत्पशुः, सत्पात्रम्, सत्पुत्रः, सत्प्रतिपक्षः, सत्प्रमुदिता, सद्भाग्यम्, सत्फलः, सद्भावः, सन्मातुरः, सन्मात्रः, सन्मानः, सन्मित्रम्, सद्युवतिः, सद्वंश, सद्वचस्, सद्वस्तु, सद्वादिता, सद्विद्य, सद्वृत्त, सच्छील, सत्संसर्गः, सत्संनिधानम्, सत्संगः, सत्संगतिः, सत्समागमः, सत्संप्रदायः, सत्संप्रयोगः, सत्सहाय, सत्सार, सद्धेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदञ्जनम्
सत् + -अञ्जनम् (सदञ्जनम्) calx of brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदर्थः|सदर्थ
सत् + -अर्थः (सदर्थः) a matter in question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसत्|सदसन्त्
सत् + -असत् (सदसत्) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 existent and non-existent, being and not being.<BR>—2 real and unreal.<BR>—3 true and false.<BR>—4 good and bad, right and wrong.<BR>—5 virtuous and wicked. ━(<i>n.</i> <i>du.</i>)<BR>—1 entity and non-entity.<BR>—2 good and evil, right and wrong. ˚विवेकः discrimination between<BR> good and evil, or truth and falsehood. ˚व्यक्तिहेतुः the cause of discrimination<BR> between the good and bad; तं सन्तः श्रोतुमर्हन्ति सदसद्व्यक्तिहेतवः R. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाचारः|सदाचार
सत् + -आचारः (सदाचारः)<BR>—1 good manners, virtuous or moral conduct.<BR>—2 approved usage, traditionary observances, immemorial custom; यस्मिन्<BR> देशे य आचारः पारंपर्यक्रमागतः । वर्णानां सान्तरालानां स सदाचार<BR> उच्यते ॥ Ms. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदात्मन्
सत् + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> (सदात्मन्) virtuous, good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानन
सत् + -आनन (सदानन) <i>a.</i> fair-faced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदुत्तरम्
सत् + -उत्तरम्, (सदुत्तरम्) a proper or good reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्करणम्
सत् + -करणम् funeral obsequies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कर्तृ
सत् + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कर्मन्|सत्कर्म्मन्
सत् + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 a virtuous or pious act.<BR>—2 virtue, piety.<BR>—3 funeral obsequies.<BR>—4 expiation.<BR>—5 hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्काण्डः|सत्काण्ड|सत्कांड
सत् + -काण्डः a hawk, kite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कारः|सत्कार
सत् + -कारः<BR>—1 a kind or hospitable treatment, hospitable reception; सत्कारमानपूजार्थं<BR> तपो दम्भेन चैव यत् । क्रियते तदिह प्रोक्तं राजसं चलमध्रुवम् ॥ Bg. 17. 18.<BR>—2 reverence, respect.<BR>—3 care, attention.<BR>—4 a meal.<BR>—5 a festival, religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कार्यम्
सत् + -कार्यम् (in Sāṃkhya phil.) the necessary existence of an effect.<BR> ˚वाद the doctrine of the actual existence of an effect (in its cause).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कुल
सत् + -कुल a good or noble family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कुलीन|सत्कुलीनः
सत् + -कुलीन <i>a.</i> nobly born, of noble descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृत|सत्कृतः
सत् + -कृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 done well or properly.<BR>—2 hospitably received or treated.<BR>—3 revered, respected, honoured.<BR>—4 worshipped, adored.<BR>—5 entertained.<BR>—6 welcomed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृतः|सत्कृत
सत् + -कृत + .({@-तः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृतम्
सत् + -कृत + .({@-तम्@})<BR>—1 hospitality.<BR>—2 respect.<BR>—3 virtue, piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्कृतिः|सत्कृति
सत् + -कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 treating with respect, hospitality, hospitable reception.<BR>—2 virtue, morality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्क्रिया
सत् + -क्रिया<BR>—1 virtue, goodness; शकुन्तला मूर्तिमती च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">Page1612-1</a>]<BR> सत्क्रिया Ś. 5. 15.<BR>—2 charity, good or virtuous action.<BR>—3 hospitality, hospitable reception; सत्क्रियाविशेषात् Ś. 7.<BR>—4 courtesy, salutation.<BR>—5 any purificatory ceremony.<BR>—6 funeral ceremonies, obsequies.<BR>—7 Celebration, decoration; यावदादिशति पार्थिवस्तयोर्निर्गमाय पुरमार्गसत्क्रियाम् R. 11. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1611-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गतिः|सद्गति
सत् + -गतिः <i>f.</i> (सद्गतिः)<BR>—1 a good or happy state, felicity, beatitude. —2 The way of good men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गुण|सद्गुणः
सत् + -गुण <i>a.</i> (सद्गुण) possessed of good qualities, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्गुणः|सद्गुण
सत् + -गुण + .({@-णः@}) virtue, excellence, goodness, good quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्घनः|सद्घन
सत् + -घनः (सद्घनः) holy existence.<BR>—2 nothing but existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चरित
सत् + -चरित, -चरित्र <i>a.</i> (सच्चरित, -त्र) well-conducted,<BR> honest, virtuous, righteous; सूनुः सच्चरितः Bh. 2. 25. ━(<i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 good or virtuous conduct.<BR>—2 history or account of the good; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चरित्र
सत् + -चरित, -चरित्र <i>a.</i> (सच्चरित, -त्र) well-conducted,<BR> honest, virtuous, righteous; सूनुः सच्चरितः Bh. 2. 25. ━(<i>n.</i>)<BR>—1 good or virtuous conduct.<BR>—2 history or account of the good; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चारा
सत् + -चारा (सच्चारा) turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्चिद्
सत् + -चिद् (सच्चिद्) the Supreme Spirit. ˚अंशः a portion of existence<BR> and thought. ˚आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the soul consisting of entity and thought. ˚आनन्दः<BR>—1 ‘existence or entity, knowledge and joy’; an epithet of the Supreme<BR> Spirit or Brahman.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जन|सज्जनं|सज्जनः
सत् + -जन <i>a.</i> (सज्जन) good, virtuous, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सज्जनः|सज्जन|सज्जनं
सत् + -जन + .({@-नः@}) a good or virtuous man. ˚गर्हित despised by the virtuous;<BR> पुक्कस्यां जायते पापः सदा सज्जनगर्हितः Ms. 10. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्धर्मः|सद्धर्म
सत् + -धर्मः (सद्धर्मः) true justice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पतिः|सत्पति
सत् + -पतिः Ved.<BR>—1 a lord of good persons or heroes.<BR>—2 N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पत्रम्
सत् + -पत्रम् the new leaf of a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पथः|सत्पथ
सत् + -पथः<BR>—1 a good road.<BR>—2 the right path of duty, correct or virtuous conduct.<BR>—3 an orthodox doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्परिग्रहः|सत्परिग्रह
सत् + -परिग्रहः acceptance (of gifts) from a proper person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पशुः|सत्पशु
सत् + -पशुः a victim fit for a sacrifice, a good sacrificial victim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पात्रम्
सत् + -पात्रम् a worthy or virtuous person. ˚वर्षः bestowing favours<BR> on worthy recipients, judicious liberality. ˚वर्षिन् <i>a.</i> having<BR> judicious liberality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्पुत्रः|सत्पुत्र|सत्पुत्त्रः
सत् + -पुत्रः<BR>—1 a good or virtuous son.<BR>—2 a son who performs all the prescribed rites in honour of his ancestors.<BR>━<i>a.</i> one who has a son; यद्यपि स्यात्तु सत्पुत्रोऽप्यसत्पुत्रोऽपि वा<BR> भवेत् Ms. 9. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्प्रतिपक्षः|सत्प्रतिपक्ष
सत् + -प्रतिपक्षः (in logic) one of the five kinds of <i>hetvābhāsas</i><BR> or fallacious <i>hetus</i>, a counter-balanced <i>hetu</i>, one along which<BR> there exists another equal <i>hetu</i> on the opposite side; यत्र साध्याभावसाधकं<BR> हेत्वन्तरं स सत्प्रतिपक्षः; <i>e. g.</i> ‘sound is eternal because it is audible’<BR>; and also ‘sound is non-eternal, because it is a product’;<BR> नाप्रामाण्यं मतानां स्यात् केषां सत्प्रतिपक्षवत् N. 17. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्प्रमुदिता
सत् + -प्रमुदिता (in Sāṃkhya phil.) N. of one of the 8 perfections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भाग्यम्
सत् + -भाग्यम् (सद्भाग्यम्)<BR>—1 good fortune.<BR>—2 Felicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्फलः|सत्फल
सत् + -फलः the pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्भावः|सद्भाव
सत् + -भावः (सद्भावः)<BR>—1 existence, being, entity; सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत् प्रयुज्यते Bg. 17. 26.<BR>—2 actual existence, reality.<BR>—3 good disposition or nature, amiability.<BR>—4 quality of goodness.<BR>—5 obtainment (प्राप्ति); देहस्यान्यस्य सद्भावे प्रसादं कर्तुमर्हसि<BR> Rām. 7. 56. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मातुरः|सन्मातुर
सत् + -मातुरः (सन्मातुरः) the son of a virtuous mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मात्रः|सन्मात्र
सत् + -मात्रः (सन्मात्रः) ‘consisting of mere entity’, the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मानः|सन्मान
सत् + -मानः (सन्मानः) esteem of the good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्मित्रम्
सत् + -मित्रम् (सन्मित्रम्) a good or faithful friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्युवतिः|सद्युवति
सत् + -युवतिः <i>f.</i> (सद्युवतिः) a virtuous maiden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वंश
सत् + -वंश (सद्वंश) <i>a.</i> of high birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वचस्
सत् + -वचस् <i>n.</i> (सद्वचस्) an agreeable or pleasing speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वस्तु
सत् + -वस्तु <i>n.</i> (सद्वस्तु)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">Page1612-2</a>]<BR>—1 a good thing.<BR>—2 a good plot or story; प्रणयिषु वा दाक्षिण्यादथवा सद्वस्तुपुरुषबहुमानात् ।<BR> शृणुत मनोभिरवहितैः क्रियामिमां कालिदासस्य ॥ V. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वादिता
सत् + -वादिता (सद्वादिता) true counsel; सद्वादितेवाभिनिविष्टबुद्धौ Ki. 17. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्विद्य
सत् + -विद्य (सद्विद्य) well-educated, having good learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वृत्त|सद्वृत्तं
सत् + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> (सद्वृत्त)<BR>—1 well-behaved, well-conducted, virtuous, upright.<BR>—2 perfectly circular, well-rounded; सद्वृत्तः स्तनमण्डलस्तव कथं<BR> प्राणैर्मम क्रीडति Gīt. 3 (where both senses are intended).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वृत्तम्
सत् + -वृत्त + .({@-त्तम्@})<BR>—1 good or virtuous conduct.<BR>—2 an agreeable or amiable disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्छील
सत् + -शील (सच्छील) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 good-tempered.<BR>—2 benevolent, kindly disposed (towards others).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संसर्गः|सत्संसर्ग
सत् + -संसर्गः, -संनिधानम्, -संगः, -संगतिः, -समागमः company<BR> or society of the good, association with the good; तथा सत्संनिधानेन<BR> मूर्खो याति प्रवीणताम् H. 1; सत्संगजानि निधनान्यपि तारयन्ति U. 2. 11;<BR> सत्संगतिः कथय किं न करोति पुंसाम् Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संनिधानम्
सत् + -संसर्गः, -संनिधानम्, -संगः, -संगतिः, -समागमः company<BR> or society of the good, association with the good; तथा सत्संनिधानेन<BR> मूर्खो याति प्रवीणताम् H. 1; सत्संगजानि निधनान्यपि तारयन्ति U. 2. 11;<BR> सत्संगतिः कथय किं न करोति पुंसाम् Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संगः|सत्सङ्ग|सत्संग
सत् + -संसर्गः, -संनिधानम्, -संगः, -संगतिः, -समागमः company<BR> or society of the good, association with the good; तथा सत्संनिधानेन<BR> मूर्खो याति प्रवीणताम् H. 1; सत्संगजानि निधनान्यपि तारयन्ति U. 2. 11;<BR> सत्संगतिः कथय किं न करोति पुंसाम् Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संगतिः|सत्सङ्गति
सत् + -संसर्गः, -संनिधानम्, -संगः, -संगतिः, -समागमः company<BR> or society of the good, association with the good; तथा सत्संनिधानेन<BR> मूर्खो याति प्रवीणताम् H. 1; सत्संगजानि निधनान्यपि तारयन्ति U. 2. 11;<BR> सत्संगतिः कथय किं न करोति पुंसाम् Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्समागमः|सत्समागम
सत् + -संसर्गः, -संनिधानम्, -संगः, -संगतिः, -समागमः company<BR> or society of the good, association with the good; तथा सत्संनिधानेन<BR> मूर्खो याति प्रवीणताम् H. 1; सत्संगजानि निधनान्यपि तारयन्ति U. 2. 11;<BR> सत्संगतिः कथय किं न करोति पुंसाम् Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संप्रदायः|सत्सम्प्रदाय|सत्संप्रदाय
सत् + -संप्रदायः good tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्संप्रयोगः|सत्सम्प्रयोग|सत्संप्रयोग
सत् + -संप्रयोगः right application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सहाय|सत्सहायः
सत् + -सहाय <i>a.</i> having virtuous friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सहायः|सत्सहाय
सत् + -सहाय + .({@-यः@}) a good companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सार|सत्सारः
सत् + -सार <i>a.</i> having good sap or essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्सारः|सत्सार
सत् + -सार + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a kind of tree.<BR>—2 a poet.<BR>—3 a painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्धेतुः|सद्धेतु
सत् + -हेतुः (सद्धेतुः) a faultless or valid <i>hetu</i> or middle term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सती
सती<BR>—1 A virtuous or good woman (or wife); सती सती योगविसृष्टदेहा Ku. 1. 21;<BR> Ki. 11. 50; esp. applied to one who burns herself with her husbandʼs corpse.<BR>—2 A female ascetic.<BR>—3 N. of the goddess Durgā or Pārvatī; पर्यस्तं नन्दया सत्या स्नानपुण्यतरोदया ।<BR> विलोक्य भूतेशगिरिम् Bhāg. 4. 6. 22; Ku. 1. 21.<BR>—4 A kind of fragrant earth.<BR>—5 A wife or female (of an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीत्वम्
सतीत्वम् Chastity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतत|सततं
सतत <i>a.</i> Constant, eternal, everlasting, perpetual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततम्
सतत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Constantly, continuously, eternally, always; सुलभाः<BR> पुरुषा राजन् सततं प्रियवादिनः Rām.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सततगः, सततगतिः, सततदुर्गत, सततपरिग्रहम्, सततयायिन्, सततयुक्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततगः|सततग
सतत + -गः, -गतिः wind; सलिलतले सततगतीनन्तःसंचारिणः संनिगृह्य<BR> शय्या कार्या Dk.; सततगास्ततगानगिरोऽलिभिः Śi. 6. 50; नेत्रा<BR> नीताः सततगतिना यद्विमानाग्रभूमीः Me. 71; Mb. 5. 167. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततगतिः|सततगति
सतत + -गः, -गतिः wind; सलिलतले सततगतीनन्तःसंचारिणः संनिगृह्य<BR> शय्या कार्या Dk.; सततगास्ततगानगिरोऽलिभिः Śi. 6. 50; नेत्रा<BR> नीताः सततगतिना यद्विमानाग्रभूमीः Me. 71; Mb. 5. 167. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततदुर्गत
सतत + -दुर्गत <i>a.</i> always miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततपरिग्रहम्
सतत + -परिग्रहम् <i>ind.</i> continually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततयायिन्
सतत + -यायिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 always moving.<BR>—2 constantly tending to decay; घोरेऽस्मिन् भूतसंसारे नित्यं सततयायिनि Ms. 1. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततयुक्त
सतत + -युक्त <i>a.</i> constantly devoted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सततक
सततक <i>a.</i> Recurring twice a day (as fever).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतनम्
सतनम् A variety of sandal, red and smelling like earth; सतनं<BR> रक्तं भूमिगन्धि Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतर्क|सतर्कः
सतर्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Versed in reasoning.<BR>—2 Considerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतिः|सति
सतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A gift, donation.<BR>—2 End, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीकम्
सतीकम्, -सतीनम्<BR> Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीनम्
सतीकम्, -सतीनम्<BR> Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीनः|सतीन
सतीनः<BR>—1 A kind of pulse of pease.<BR>—2 A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थः|सतीर्थ
सतीर्थः, सतीर्थ्यः A fellow religious student, (a pupil<BR> of the same preceptor); यमात्मनः सतीर्थ्यं पितैव ते जानीते योऽसौ यादृशश्चेति<BR> Māl. 2. According to Pāṇini (VI. 3. 87)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">Page1613-1</a>]<BR> the latter word alone is correct. शब्दरत्नावली, however, says, “स्यात्<BR> सतीर्थः सतीर्थ्योऽपि तथैकगुरुरित्यपि.” Bohtlingk and Wackernagel<BR> say that the word सतीर्थ is approved to be correct by Vopadeva. But<BR> this is wrong because मुग्धबोधव्याकरण accepts सतीर्थ्य alone to be correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीर्थ्यः|सतीर्थ्य
सतीर्थः, सतीर्थ्यः A fellow religious student, (a pupil<BR> of the same preceptor); यमात्मनः सतीर्थ्यं पितैव ते जानीते योऽसौ यादृशश्चेति<BR> Māl. 2. According to Pāṇini (VI. 3. 87)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">Page1613-1</a>]<BR> the latter word alone is correct. शब्दरत्नावली, however, says, “स्यात्<BR> सतीर्थः सतीर्थ्योऽपि तथैकगुरुरित्यपि.” Bohtlingk and Wackernagel<BR> say that the word सतीर्थ is approved to be correct by Vopadeva. But<BR> this is wrong because मुग्धबोधव्याकरण accepts सतीर्थ्य alone to be correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1612-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीलः|सतील
सतीलः<BR>—1 A bamboo.<BR>—2 Air, wind.<BR>—3 Pease, pulse (<i>f.</i> also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतीलकः|सतीलक
सतीलकः Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतेरः|सतेर
सतेरः Husk, chaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सतोद
सतोद <i>a.</i> Attended with a pricking pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तम|सत्तमः
सत्तम <i>a.</i> Most beautiful, the best, excellent, the most respectable; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तलिका
सत्तलिका A carpet; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ता
सत्ता<BR>—1 Existence, entity, being.<BR>—2 Actual existence, reality.<BR>—3 The highest Jāti or generality; द्रव्यादित्रिकवृत्तिस्तु सत्ता परतयोच्यते.<BR>—4 Goodness, excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्तिः|सत्ति
सत्तिः<BR>—1 Sitting down.<BR>—2 Beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रम्
सत्त्रम् [सद्-ष्ट्रन्] (usually written सत्रम्)<BR>—1 A sacrificial session, especially one lasting from 13 to 100 days.<BR>—2 A sacrifice in general; त्रेतामपि निबोध त्वं यस्मिन् सत्रं प्रवर्तते<BR> Mb. 3. 149. 23.<BR>—3 A n oblation, offering, gift.<BR>—4 Liberality, munificence.<BR>—5 Virtue.<BR>—6 A house, residence.<BR>—7 Covering.<BR>—8 Wealth.<BR>—9 A wood, forest; अयमेव मृगव्यसत्रकामः Ki. 13. 9.<BR>—10 A tank, pond.<BR>—11 Fraud, cheating.<BR>—12 A place of refuge, asylum, covert.<BR>—13 Gifts made at all times; L. D. B.<BR>—14 Haughtiness, pride; L. D. B.<BR>—15 An assumed form or disguise; छन्नं तथा तं सत्रेण पाण्डवं प्रेक्ष्य<BR> भारत Mb. 4. 38. 40.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सत्त्रापश्रयः, सत्त्रायनम्, सत्त्रपरिवेषणम्, सत्त्रशाला<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रापश्रयः|सत्रापश्रय
सत्त्रम् + -अपश्रयः a place of refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रायनम्
सत्त्रम् + -अयनम् ({@णम्@}) a long sacrificial session.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रपरिवेषणम्
सत्त्रम् + -परिवेषणम् distribution of food at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रशाला
सत्त्रम् + -शाला an alms-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रायते
सत्रायते Den. Ā. To perform a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रिन्
सत्त्रिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who constantly performs sacrifices, a liberal householder; भूमिं<BR> वृत्तिकरीं दत्त्वा सत्री भवति मानवः Mb. 13. 62. 29; अत्यशेरत<BR> परस्परं धियः सत्त्रिणां नरपतेश्च संपदः Śi. 14. 32.<BR>—2 A priest superintending or performing a sacrifice; Bhāg. 4. 14. 7.<BR>—3 A class-mate, disciple; तदस्य गूढाः सत्त्रिणश्च संवादयेयुः<BR> Kau. A. 1. 11; स सत्रिभिः शपथपूर्वम् एकैकममात्यम् उपजापयेत् Kau. A. 1. 10.<BR>—4 An ambassador or agent in a foreign country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रा
सत्त्रा <i>ind.</i> With, together with; सत्त्रा पुत्रकलत्रमित्रनिवहैः<BR> Rām. Ch. 2. 94.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सत्त्राहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्राहन्
सत्त्रा + -हन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्रिः|सत्रि
सत्त्रिः<BR>—1 A cloud.<BR>—2 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वम्
सत्त्वम् [सतो भावः] (Said to be <i>m.</i> also in the first ten senses)<BR>—1 Being, existence, entity.<BR>—2 Nature, essence.<BR>—3 Natural character, inborn disposition; अच्योष्ट सत्त्वान्नृपतिश्च्युताशः Bk. 3. 20.<BR>—4 Life, spirit,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">Page1613-2</a>]<BR> breath, vitality, principle of vitality; उद्गतानीव सत्त्वानि वभूवुरमनस्विनाम्<BR> Rām. 2. 48. 2; चित्रे निवेश्य परिकल्पितसत्त्वयोगा Ś. 2. 10.<BR>—5 Consciousness, mind, sense; वाक्च सत्त्वं च गोविन्द बुद्धौ संवेशितानि<BR> ते Mb. 12. 46. 4; Bg. 16. 1; Bhāg. 7. 15. 41.<BR>—6 An embryo.<BR>—7 Substance, thing, wealth.<BR>—8 An elementary substance such as earth, air, fire &c.<BR>—9 (also <i>m.</i>) A living or sentient being, animal, beast; वन्यान् विनेष्यन्निव<BR> दुष्टसत्त्वान् R. 2. 8, 15. 15; किं नोऽपत्यनिर्विशेषाणि सत्त्वानि विप्रकरोषि<BR> Ś. 7; Māl. 9; यश्चासूनपि संत्यजेत् करुणया सत्त्वार्थमभ्युद्यतः Nāg. 2. 10.<BR>—10 An evil spirit, a demon, ghost; अद्य नूनं दशरथः सत्त्वमाविश्य<BR> भाषते Rām. 2. 33. 10.<BR>—11 Goodness, virtue, excellence.<BR>—12 Truth, reality, certainty.<BR>—13 Strength, energy, courage, vigour, power, inherent power, the stuff<BR> of which a person is made; निजमेव सत्त्वमुपकारि सताम् Ki. 18. 14;<BR> Mb. 12. 313. 17; क्रियासिद्धिः सत्त्वे भवति महतां नोपकरणे Subhāṣ.;<BR> R. 5. 31; Mu. 3. 22.<BR>—14 Wisdom, good sense.<BR>—15 The quality of goodness or purity regarded as the highest of the three<BR> Guṇas q. v.; (it is said to predominate most in gods and heavenly beings).<BR>—16 A natural property or quality, characteristic.<BR>—17 A noun, substantive.<BR>—18 Intellect (बुद्धि); अघ्राणमवितर्कं च सत्त्वं प्रविशते परम्<BR> Mb. 12. 204. 18.<BR>—19 The subtle body or individual soul (लिङ्गशरीर); गृहाणीव हि मर्त्यानामाहुर्देहानि<BR> पण्डिताः । कालेन विनियुज्यन्ते सत्त्वमेकं तु शाश्वतम् ॥ Mb. 11. 3. 8.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सत्त्वानुरूप, सत्त्वात्मन्, सत्त्वोत्साहः, सत्त्वोद्रेकः, सत्त्वगुणः, सत्त्वतनुः, सत्त्वधातुः, सत्त्वधामन्, सत्त्वयोगः, सत्त्वलक्षणम्, सत्त्वलोकः, सत्त्वविप्लवः, सत्त्वविहित, सत्त्वसंशुद्धिः, सत्त्वसंपन्न, सत्त्वसंप्लवः, सत्त्वसारः, सत्त्वस्थ, सत्त्वस्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वानुरूप
सत्त्वम् + -अनुरूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 according to oneʼs inborn disposition or inherent character; सर्वः<BR> कृच्छ्रगतोऽपि वाञ्छति जनः सत्त्वानुरूपं फलम् Bh. 2. 30.<BR>—2 according to oneʼs means or wealth; सत्त्वानुरूपाहरणीकृतश्रीः<BR> R. 7. 32 (Malli.ʼs interpretation does not appear to suit the context).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वात्मन्
सत्त्वम् + -आत्मन् <i>m.</i> the individual soul (लिङ्गदेह); वशे तिष्ठति<BR> सत्त्वात्मा सततं योगयोगिनाम् Mb. 12. 253. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वोत्साहः|सत्त्वोत्साह
सत्त्वम् + -उत्साहः<BR>—1 natural energy.<BR>—2 energy and courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वोद्रेकः|सत्त्वोद्रेक
सत्त्वम् + -उद्रेकः<BR>—1 excess of the quality of goodness.<BR>—2 pre-eminence in strength or courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वगुणः|सत्त्वगुण
सत्त्वम् + -गुणः the quality of purity or goodness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वतनुः
सत्त्वम् + -तनुः epithet of Viṣṇu; श्रेयांसि तत्र खलु सत्त्वतनोर्नृणां<BR> स्युः Bhāg. 1. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वधातुः|सत्त्वधातु
सत्त्वम् + -धातुः the animal sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वधामन्
सत्त्वम् + -धामन् epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वयोगः
सत्त्वम् + -योगः<BR>—1 dignity; Kau. A. 1. 9.<BR>—2 association with life; चित्रे निवेश्य परिकल्पितसत्त्वयोगा Ś. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वलक्षणम्
सत्त्वम् + -लक्षणम् signs of pregnancy; तत्कथमिमामभिव्यक्तसत्त्वलक्षणां … प्रतिपत्स्ये<BR> Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वलोकः|सत्त्वलोक
सत्त्वम् + -लोकः a world of living beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वविप्लवः|सत्त्वविप्लव
सत्त्वम् + -विप्लवः loss of consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वविहित
सत्त्वम् + -विहित<BR>—1 caused by nature.<BR>—2 caused by goodness.<BR>—3 virtuous, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसंशुद्धिः|सत्त्वसंशुद्धि
सत्त्वम् + -संशुद्धिः <i>f.</i> purity or uprightness of nature; अभयं सत्त्वसंशुद्धिः Bg. 16. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसंपन्न|सत्त्वसम्पन्न|सत्त्वसम्पन्नः
सत्त्वम् + -संपन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 endowed with goodness, virtuous.<BR>—2 equable, even-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसंप्लवः|सत्त्वसम्प्लव|सत्त्वसंप्लव
सत्त्वम् + -संप्लवः<BR>—1 loss of strength or vigour.<BR>—2 universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वसारः|सत्त्वसार
सत्त्वम् + -सारः<BR>—1 essence of strength.<BR>—2 a very powerful person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वस्थ|सत्त्वस्थः
सत्त्वम् + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 being in the nature of things.<BR>—2 inherent in animals.<BR>—3 animate.<BR>—4 characterized by goodness, good, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वस्थः|सत्त्वस्थ
सत्त्वम् + -स्थः a Yogi; कर्मस्था विषयं ब्रूयुः सत्त्वस्थाः समदर्शिनः<BR> Mb. 12. 238. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वकः|सत्त्वक
सत्त्वकः The spirit of a departed person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1613-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्वमेजय
सत्त्वमेजय <i>a.</i> Terrifying animals or living beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्ववत्|सत्त्ववन्त्
सत्त्ववत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living, existing.<BR>—2 Possessed of true essence.<BR>—3 Good, pure, virtuous.<BR>—4 Endowed with energy or courage; प्रकृतिरियं सत्त्ववताम् Subhāṣ. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The body (देह); सत्त्ववत्सु तथा सत्त्वं प्रतिरूपं स पश्यति Mb. 12. 253. 3.<BR>—2 epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्त्ववती
सत्त्ववत् + .{@-ती@} <i>a.</i> pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्य|सत्यं|सत्यः
सत्य <i>a.</i> [सते हितं यत्]<BR>—1 True, real, genuine; as in सत्यव्रत, सत्यसंध.<BR>—2 Honest, sincere, truthful, faithful.<BR>—3 Fulfilled, realized.<BR>—4 Virtuous, upright.<BR>—5 Unfailing; कच्चिच्छुश्रूषसे तात पितुः सत्यपराक्रम Rām. 2. 100. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यः|सत्य|सत्यं
सत्य + .{@-त्यः@}<BR>—1 The abode of Brahman and of truth, the uppermost of the seven worlds<BR> or <i>lokas</i> above the earth; see लोक.<BR>—2 The Aśvattha tree.<BR>—3 N. of Rāma.<BR>—4 Of Viṣṇu; सत्यव्रतं सत्यपरं त्रिसत्यं सत्यस्य योनिं निहितं<BR> च सत्ये । सत्यस्य सत्यमृतसत्यनेत्रं सत्यात्मकं त्वां शरणं प्रपन्नाः ॥<BR> Bhāg. 10. 2. 26.<BR>—5 The deity presiding over नान्दीमुखश्राद्ध q. v.<BR>—6 N. of Brahman; अव्ययस्याप्रमेयस्य सत्यस्य च तथाग्रतः Mb. 1. 37. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यम्
सत्य + .{@-त्यम्@}<BR>—1 Truth; मौनात्सत्यं विशिष्यते Ms. 2. 83; सत्यं ब्रू ‘to speak the truth’.<BR>—2 Sincerity.<BR>—3 Goodness, virtue, purity.<BR>—4 An oath, a promise, solemn asseveration; सत्याद् गुरुमलोपयन् R. 12. 9;<BR> Ms. 8. 113.<BR>—5 A truism, demonstrated truth or dogma.<BR>—6 The first of the four Yugas or ages of the world, the golden age, the<BR> age of truth and purity.<BR>—7 Water.<BR>—8 The Supreme Spirit; हिरण्मयेन पात्रेण सत्यस्यापिहितं मुखम् Īśop. 15.<BR>—9 Final emancipation (मोक्ष); इह चेदवेदीदथ सत्यमस्ति न चेदिहावेदीन्<BR> महती विनष्टिः Ken. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यम्
सत्य + .{@-त्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Truly, really, indeed, verily, forsooth; सत्यं<BR> शपामि ते पादपङ्कजस्पर्शेन K.; Ku. 6. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सत्याग्निः, सत्यानुरक्त, सत्यानृत, सत्याभिसंध, सत्यात्मन्, सत्याश्रमः, सत्योत्कर्षः, सत्योद्य, सत्योपयाचन, सत्यकामः, सत्यक्रिया, सत्यजित्, सत्यतपस्, सत्यदर्शिन्, सत्यधन, सत्यधर्मः, सत्यधृति, सत्यनारायणः, सत्यपुरम्, सत्यपुष्टिः, सत्यपूत, सत्यप्रतिज्ञ, सत्यप्रतिष्ठान, सत्यमूल, सत्यफलः, सत्यभामा, सत्यभारतः, सत्यभेदिन्, सत्यमानम्, सत्ययुगम्, सत्ययौवनः, सत्यरत, सत्यलौकिकम्, सत्यवचनम्, सत्यवचस्, सत्यवद्य, सत्यवाक्यम्, सत्यवाच्, सत्यवादिन्, सत्यव्यवस्था, सत्यव्रत, सत्यसंगर, सत्यसंध, सत्यश्रवसी, सत्यश्रावणम्, सत्यसंश्रवः, सत्यसंकल्प, सत्यसंकाश, सत्यसंगरः, सत्यसंधः, सत्यसाक्षिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याग्निः|सत्याग्नि
सत्य + -अग्निः N. of the sage Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानुरक्त
सत्य + -अनुरक्त <i>a.</i> devoted to truth, honest, upright, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानृत|सत्यानृतं
सत्य + -अनृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 true and false; सत्यानृता च परुषा H. 2. 183.<BR>—2 apparently true, but really false.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानृतम्
सत्य + -अनृत + .({@-तम्, -ते@})<BR>—1 truth and falsehood.<BR>—2 practice of truth and falsehood; <i>i. e.</i> trade, commerce; सत्यानृताभ्यामपि<BR> वा न श्ववृत्त्या कदाचन Ms. 4. 4 and 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यानृते
सत्य + -अनृत + .({@-तम्, -ते@})<BR>—1 truth and falsehood.<BR>—2 practice of truth and falsehood; <i>i. e.</i> trade, commerce; सत्यानृताभ्यामपि<BR> वा न श्ववृत्त्या कदाचन Ms. 4. 4 and 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याभिसंध
सत्य + -अभिसंध <i>a.</i> true to oneʼs promise, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यात्मन्
सत्य + -आत्मन् true. ━(<i>m.</i>) a virtuous or upright man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याश्रमः
सत्य + -आश्रमः renunciation of the world (संन्यास); दीक्षा बहुविधा<BR> राजन् सत्याश्रमपदं भवेत् Mb. 12. 66. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योत्कर्षः|सत्योत्कर्ष
सत्य + -उत्कर्षः<BR>—1 pre-eminence in truth.<BR>—2 true excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योद्य
सत्य + -उद्य <i>a.</i> speaking the truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्योपयाचन
सत्य + -उपयाचन <i>a.</i> fulfilling a request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यकामः|सत्यकाम
सत्य + -कामः a lover of truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यक्रिया
सत्य + -क्रिया a promise, oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यजित्
सत्य + -जित् N. of Indra in the third Manvantara; इन्द्रस्तु सत्यजित्<BR> Bhāg. 8. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यतपस्
सत्य + -तपस् <i>m.</i> N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यदर्शिन्
सत्य + -दर्शिन् <i>a.</i> truth-seeing, fore-seeing truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधन
सत्य + -धन <i>a.</i> rich in truth, exceedingly truthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधर्मः|सत्यधर्म
सत्य + -धर्मः the law of truth, eternal truth. ˚परायण <i>a.</i><BR> devoted to truth and virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यधृति|सत्यधृतिः
सत्य + -धृति <i>a.</i> strictly truthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यनारायणः|सत्यनारायण
सत्य + -नारायणः<BR>—1 A form of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 A form of divinity (called Satyapīr in Bengāli).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यपुरम्
सत्य + -पुरम्<BR>—1 the world of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 The city of Satya-nārayaṇa; अन्ते सत्यपुरं ययौ (सत्यनारायणव्रतकथा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यपुष्टिः|सत्यपुष्टि
सत्य + -पुष्टिः true or permanent prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यपूत
सत्य + -पूत <i>a.</i> purified by truth (as words); सत्यपूतां वदेद्वाणीम् Ms. 6. 46.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">Page1614-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यप्रतिज्ञ
सत्य + -प्रतिज्ञ <i>a.</i> true to oneʼs promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यप्रतिष्ठान
सत्य + -प्रतिष्ठान, -मूल <i>a.</i> grounded in truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यमूल
सत्य + -प्रतिष्ठान, -मूल <i>a.</i> grounded in truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यफलः|सत्यफल
सत्य + -फलः the <i>Bilva</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभामा
सत्य + -भामा N. of the daughter of Satrājit and the favourite wife of<BR> Kṛṣṇa; (it was for her that Kṛṣṇa fought with Indra and brought<BR> the Pārijāta tree from the Nandana garden and planted it in her garden).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभारतः|सत्यभारत
सत्य + -भारतः N. of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यभेदिन्
सत्य + -भेदिन् <i>a.</i> promise-breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यमानम्
सत्य + -मानम् a true measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ययुगम्
सत्य + -युगम् the golden age; the first or कृतयुग; see सत्यम् (6) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्ययौवनः|सत्ययौवन
सत्य + -यौवनः a Vidyādhara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यरत|सत्यरतः
सत्य + -रत <i>a.</i> devoted to truth, honest, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यरतः|सत्यरत
सत्य + -रत + .({@-तः@}) N. of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यलौकिकम्
सत्य + -लौकिकम् spiritual and worldly matters; मया प्रोक्तं हि लोकस्य<BR> प्रमाणं सत्यलौकिके Bhāg. 3. 24. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवचनम्
सत्य + -वचनम्<BR>—1 the speaking of truth.<BR>—2 a promise, solemn assurance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवचस्
सत्य + -वचस् <i>a.</i> truthful, veracious. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a saint, Ṛṣi.<BR>—2 a seer. ━(<i>n.</i>) truth, veracity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवद्य
सत्य + -वद्य <i>a.</i> veracious; सत्यवद्यो रघूत्तमः Bk. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवद्यम्
सत्य + -वद्य + .({@-द्यम्@}) truth, veracity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवाक्यम्
सत्य + -वाक्यम् truth-speaking, veracity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवाच्
सत्य + -वाच् <i>a.</i> truthful, veracious, candid. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 a saint, seer.<BR>—2 a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवादिन्
सत्य + -वादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 truth-speaking.<BR>—2 sincere, outspoken, candid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यव्यवस्था
सत्य + -व्यवस्था ascertainment of truth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यव्रत|सत्यव्रतः
सत्य + -व्रत, -संगर, -संध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 true or faithful to an agreement, promise or word, adhering to truth,<BR> veracious; Bhāg. 10. 2. 26; see सत्यः (4).<BR>—2 honest, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंगर|सत्यसङ्गर|सत्यसंगरः|सत्यसङ्गरः
सत्य + -व्रत, -संगर, -संध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 true or faithful to an agreement, promise or word, adhering to truth,<BR> veracious; Bhāg. 10. 2. 26; see सत्यः (4).<BR>—2 honest, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंध|सत्यसन्ध|सत्यसंधः|सत्यसन्धः
सत्य + -व्रत, -संगर, -संध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 true or faithful to an agreement, promise or word, adhering to truth,<BR> veracious; Bhāg. 10. 2. 26; see सत्यः (4).<BR>—2 honest, sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यश्रवसी
सत्य + -श्रवसी Ved. an epithet of Uṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यश्रावणम्
सत्य + -श्रावणम् taking a solemn oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंश्रवः|सत्यसंश्रव
सत्य + -संश्रवः a promise, vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंकल्प|सत्यसङ्कल्प
सत्य + -संकल्प <i>a.</i> true in purpose or resolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंकाश|सत्यसङ्काश|सत्यसङ्काशः
सत्य + -संकाश <i>a.</i> specious, plausible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंगरः|सत्यसङ्गर|सत्यसंगर|सत्यसङ्गरः
सत्य + -संगरः N. of Kubera. ━<i>a.</i> true to an agreement or promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंधः|सत्यसन्ध|सत्यसंध|सत्यसन्धः
सत्य + -संधः<BR>—1 an epithet of Rāma; राजेन्द्रं सत्यसंधं दशरथतनयम् Rāmarakṣā 26.<BR>—2 of Bharata.<BR>—3 of king Janamejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसंधा
सत्य + -संधः + .({@-धा@}) an epithet of Draupadī. ━<i>a.</i> keeping oneʼs promise, faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यसाक्षिन्
सत्य + -साक्षिन् <i>m.</i> a trustworthy witness; यथोक्तेन नयन्तस्ते पूयन्ते<BR> सत्यसाक्षिणः Ms. 8. 257.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यक|सत्यकं
सत्यक <i>a.</i> See सत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यकम्
सत्यक + .{@-कम्@} Ratification of a contract &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यंकारः|सत्यङ्कार|सत्यंकार|सत्यङ्कारः
सत्यंकारः<BR>—1 Making true or good, ratification of a contract or bargain.<BR>—2 Earnest money, advance payment, something given in advance as an earnest<BR> for the performance of a contract; उपाधत्त सपत्नेषु कृष्णाया गुरुसंनिधौ ।<BR> भावमानयने सत्याः सत्यंकारमिवान्तकः ॥ Ki. 11. 50.<BR>—3 A promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवत्|सत्यवन्त्
सत्यवत् <i>a.</i> Truthful, veracious. ━<i>m.</i> N. of a king, husband<BR> of Sāvitrī, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यवती
सत्यवत् + .{@-ती@}<BR>—1 N. of the daughter of a fisherman, who became mother of Vāysa by the<BR> sage Parāśara; व्यासः सत्यवतीपुत्र इदं वचनमब्रवीत् Mb. 1. 106. 16.<BR>—2 N. of the wife of Nārada.<BR>—3 Of the wife of Ṛchīka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्या
सत्या<BR>—1 Truthfulness, veracity.<BR>—2 N. of Sītā.<BR>—3 Of Draupadī.<BR>—4 Of Satyavatī, mother of Vyāsa; ऋषिमावाहयत् सत्या यथापूर्वमरिन्दम<BR> Mb. 1. 106. 14.<BR>—5 Of Durgā.<BR>—6 Of Satyabhāmā, wife of Kṛṣṇa^1; Bhāg. 3. 1. 35.<BR>—7 Of the mother of Viṣṇu; सत्यायामभवत् सत्यः सत्यरूपो जनार्दनः.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1614-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याकृ
सत्याकृ €8 U., सत्यापयति Den. P. To ratify a bargain or contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापयति
सत्याकृ €8 U., सत्यापयति Den. P. To ratify a bargain or contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्याकृतिः|सत्याकृति
सत्याकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Earnest money, advance payment.<BR>—2 Ratification of an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापनम्
सत्यापनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Speaking or observing the truth.<BR>—2 Ratification (of a contract, bargain &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्यापना
सत्यापनम्, -ना<BR>—1 Speaking or observing the truth.<BR>—2 Ratification (of a contract, bargain &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र्
सत्र् €10 Ā. To perform, to spread out; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्र|सत्त्रं|सत्रं
सत्र See सत्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रम्
सत्र + .{@-त्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> With, together; सार्धं साकं समं सत्रं सहार्थे<BR> संप्रकीर्तिताः<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सत्रन्यायः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रन्यायः
सत्र + -न्यायः the rule that at a सत्र, which is performed by several<BR> स्वामिन्s together, a प्रतिनिधि is admissible for a स्वामिन् if<BR> and when one of the स्वामिन्s commencing the सत्र is lost or dead<BR> before the completion of the सत्र. This is discussed and established<BR> by Jaimini and Śabara at MS. 6. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रप
सत्रप <i>a.</i> Ashamed, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्राजित्
सत्राजित् <i>m.</i> N. of a son of Nighna and father of Satyabhāmā.<BR> [He got the <i>Syamantaka</i> jewel from the Sun and always wore it round<BR> his neck. He afterwards gave it to his brother Prasena, from whom it passed<BR> into the hands of the monkey-chief Jāmbavat, who got possession of it<BR> after having killed Prasena. Kṛṣṇa, however, overtook Jāmbavat and<BR> vanquished him in fight after a long struggle. The monkey-chief thereupon<BR> presented it along with his daughter to Kṛṣṇa; see जाम्बवत्. Kṛṣṇa<BR> then gave the jewel back to its proper owner Satrājit, who out of gratitude<BR> presented it along with his daughter Satyabhāmā to him. Afterwards when<BR> Satyabhāmā was at her fatherʼs house with the jewel, Śatadhanvan, at<BR> the instigation of a Yādava named Akrūra who desired the jewel for himself,<BR> killed Satrājit and gave it to Akrūra. Śatadhanvan was afterwards killed<BR> by Kṛṣṇa, but when he found that the jewel was with Akrūra, he allowed<BR> him to retain it with himself after having once shown it to the people.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्रिन्
सत्रिन् <i>m.</i> A colleague, clan-mate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वर|सत्वरं
सत्वर <i>a.</i> Quick, speedy, expeditious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सत्वरम्
सत्वर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> Quickly, speedily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सथूत्कार|सथूत्कारः
सथूत्कार <i>a.</i> Sputtered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सथूत्कारः|सथूत्कार
सथूत्कार + .{@-रः@} Speech accompanied with sputtering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्
सद् €1 P. (€6 P. also according to some) (सीदति, सन्न; the स्<BR> of सद् is changed to ष् after any preposition ending in इ or उ except प्रति)<BR>—1 To sit, sit down, recline, lie, lie down, rest, settle; अमदाः सेदुरेकस्मिन्<BR> नितम्बे निखिला गिरेः Bk. 7. 58.<BR>—2 To sink down, plunge into; सीदन्ति च तदा यक्षाः कूला इव जलेन<BR> ह Rām. 7. 14. 18; तेन त्वं विदुषां मध्ये पङ्के गौरिव सीदसि<BR> H. Pr. 24; (where the word has sense 4 also).<BR>—3 To live, remain, reside, dwell.<BR>—4 To be dejected or low-spirited, despond, despair,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">Page1615-2</a>]<BR> sink into despondency; दृष्ट्वैव सागरं वीक्ष्य सीदन्तीं कपिवाहिनीम्<BR> Rām. 7. 35. 4; नाथ हरे जय नाथ हरे सीदति राधा वासगृहे Gīt. 6.<BR>—5 To decay, perish, go to ruin, waste away, be destroyed; विपन्नायां<BR> नीतौ सकलमवशं सीदति जगत् H. 2. 77; तं सन्नशत्रुं ददृशुः<BR> स्वयोधाः R. 7. 64; H. 2. 130.<BR>—6 To be in distress, be pained or afflicted, be helpless; सीदतामनुभवन्निवार्थिनां<BR> वेद यत्प्रणयभङ्गवेदनाम् Ki. 13. 60; Ms. 8. 21.<BR>—7 To be impeded or hindered; धर्मे सीदति सत्वरः Ms. 9. 94.<BR>—8 To be languid, be wearied or fatigued, droop, sink; सीदति मे हृदयम्<BR> K.; सीदन्ति मम गात्राणि Bg. 1. 29.<BR>—9 To go. ━<i>Caus.</i> (सादयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to sit down, rest.<BR>—2 To throw or cast down, place, put.<BR>—3 To weary, exhaust.<BR>—4 To cause to perish, destroy; बहुसमरनयज्ञः सादयिष्यन्नरातिम्.<BR>━<i>Desid.</i> (सिषत्सति) To wish to sit &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्
सद् <i>f.</i> An assembly; पृष्टः प्राह तमाभाष्य शृण्वत्यास्तत्सदः<BR> कथाः Bhāg. 7. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदनम्
सदनम् [सीदत्यस्मिन् सद् आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 A house, palace, mansion.<BR>—2 Sinking down, decaying, perishing.<BR>—3 Languor; exhaustion, fatigue.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 A sacrificial hall.<BR>—6 The abode of Yama.<BR>—7 Sitting, a seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदः|सद
सदः The fruit of trees; धान्ये सदे लवे बाह्ये नातिक्रामति पञ्चताम् Ms. 8. 151.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशः|सदंश
सदंशः A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदंशवदनः|सदंशवदन
सदंशवदनः A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदधन्
सदधन् <i>a.</i> Mixed with sour milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदय
सदय <i>a.</i> Kind, tender, merciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदयम्
सदय + .{@-यम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Kindly, mercifully.<BR>—2 Gently, softly; अधरस्य पिपासता मया ते सदयं सुन्दरि गृह्यते<BR> रसोऽस्य Ś. 3. 25, 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्
सदस् <i>n.</i> [सीदत्यस्यां सद्-असि]<BR>—1 Seat, abode, residence, dwelling; शापक्षयादिन्द्रसदो ययौ च Rām. 7. 56. 29.<BR>—2 An assembly; पङ्कैर्विना सरो भाति सदः खलजनैर्विना Bv. 1. 116;<BR> Bh. 2. 63. (the word is also feminine सदाः, सदसौ, सदसः L. D. B.).<BR>—3 The sky; रराज वै परमविमानमास्थितो निशाचरः सदसि गतो यथानलः<BR> Rām. 7. 15. 41. ━(du.) heaven and earth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदोजिरम्, सदोगत, सदोगृहम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदोजिरम्
सदस् + -अजिरम् a vestibule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदोगत
सदस् + -गत <i>a.</i> seated in an assembly; यथा च वृत्तान्तमिमं सदोगतस्त्रिलोचनैकांशतया<BR> दुरासदः R. 3. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदोगृहम्
सदस् + -गृहम् an assembly-hall, council-room; नृपस्य नातिप्रमनाः<BR> सदोगृहं सुदक्षिणासूनुरपि व्यवर्तत R. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदसस्पतिः|सदसस्पति
सदसस्पतिः The president of an assembly; सदसस्पतयोऽप्येके<BR> असन्तोषात् पतन्त्यधः Bhāg. 7. 15. 21, 10. 74. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदस्यः|सदस्य
सदस्यः [सदसि साधु वसति वा यत्]<BR>—1 Any person present at or belonging to an assembly, a member of an assembly<BR> (an assessor, a juror &c.); सदस्याग्न्यार्हणार्हं वै विमृशन्तः सभासदः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 74. 18.<BR>—2 An assistant at a sacrifice, a superintending or assisting priest;<BR> ऋषीणामार्त्विज्यं शरणद सदस्याः सुरगणाः Śivamahimna 21; सदस्यैरनुज्ञातः Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1615-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदा
सदा <i>ind.</i> Always, ever, perpetually, at all times.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदानन्द, सदोत्थायिन्, सदागतिः, सदातोया, सदानीरा, सदादान, सदानर्तः, सदापुष्प, सदाप्रसूनः, सदाफल, सदाभव, सदाभव्य, सदाभ्रम, सदायोगिन्, सदाशिवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानन्द|सदानंद|सदानन्दः
सदा + -आनन्द <i>a.</i> ever happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानन्दः|सदानन्द|सदानंद
सदा + -आनन्द + .({@-दः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदोत्थायिन्
सदा + -उत्थायिन् ever exerting; त्रिभिर्वर्षैः सदोत्थायी कृष्णद्वैपायनो<BR> मुनिः । महाभारतमाख्यानं कृतवानिदमद्भुतम् ॥ Mb. 1. 62. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदागतिः|सदागति
सदा + -गतिः<BR>—1 wind; पाशैः केन सदागतेरगतिता सद्यः समापादिता Mu. 7. 6.<BR>—2 the universal spirit.<BR>—3 the sun.<BR>—4 everlasting happiness, final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातोया
सदा + -तोया, -नीरा<BR>—1 N. of the <i>Karatoyā</i> river.<BR>—2 a river always bearing water, a running stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानीरा
सदा + -तोया, -नीरा<BR>—1 N. of the <i>Karatoyā</i> river.<BR>—2 a river always bearing water, a running stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदादान|सदादानः
सदा + -दान <i>a.</i> always making gifts or exuding rut; सदादानः परिक्षीणः<BR> शस्त एव करीश्वरः Pt. 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदादानः|सदादान
सदा + -दान + .({@-नः@})<BR>—1 a ruttish elephant.<BR>—2 a scent-elephant (= गन्धद्विप q. v.).<BR>—3 N. of the elephant of Indra.<BR>—4 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदानर्तः|सदानर्त|सदानर्त्त|सदानर्त्तः
सदा + -नर्तः a kind of bird, the wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदापुष्प|सदापुष्पः
सदा + -पुष्प <i>a.</i> ever-flowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदापुष्पः|सदापुष्प
सदा + -पुष्प + .({@-ष्पः@}) the cocoa-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाप्रसूनः|सदाप्रसून
सदा + -प्रसूनः N. of various plants:− रोहित, अर्क and कुन्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाफल|सदाफलः
सदा + -फल <i>a.</i> always bearing fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाफलः|सदाफल
सदा + -फल + .({@-लः@})<BR>—1 the Bilva tree.<BR>—2 the jack tree.<BR>—3 the glomerous fig-tree.<BR>—4 the cocoa-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभव
सदा + -भव <i>a.</i> perpetual, continual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभव्य
सदा + -भव्य <i>a.</i> always present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाभ्रम
सदा + -भ्रम <i>a.</i> always wandering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदायोगिन्
सदा + -योगिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदाशिवः|सदाशिव
सदा + -शिवः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातन|सदातनः
सदातन <i>a.</i> Incessant, perpetual, eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदातनः|सदातन
सदातन + .{@-नः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदुर्दिन
सदुर्दिन <i>a.</i> Enveloped in clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्ष|सदृक्षः
सदृक्ष (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), सदृश्, सदृश (-शी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Like, resembling, similar, of the same rank, (with gen. or loc., but<BR> usually in comp.); वज्रपातसदृश, कुसुमसदृश &c.; कश्चिद्धरेः<BR> सौम्य सुतः सदृक्षः (आस्ते) Bhāg. 3. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Fit, right, suitable, conformable; as in प्रस्तावसदृशं वाक्यम् H. 2. 51.<BR>—3 Worthy, befitting, becoming; श्रुतस्य किं तत्सदृशं कुलस्य R. 14. 61, 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदृक्षविनिमय, सदृक्षस्त्री, सदृक्षस्पन्दनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्षी
सदृक्ष (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), सदृश्, सदृश (-शी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Like, resembling, similar, of the same rank, (with gen. or loc., but<BR> usually in comp.); वज्रपातसदृश, कुसुमसदृश &c.; कश्चिद्धरेः<BR> सौम्य सुतः सदृक्षः (आस्ते) Bhāg. 3. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Fit, right, suitable, conformable; as in प्रस्तावसदृशं वाक्यम् H. 2. 51.<BR>—3 Worthy, befitting, becoming; श्रुतस्य किं तत्सदृशं कुलस्य R. 14. 61, 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदृक्षविनिमय, सदृक्षस्त्री, सदृक्षस्पन्दनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश्
सदृक्ष (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), सदृश्, सदृश (-शी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Like, resembling, similar, of the same rank, (with gen. or loc., but<BR> usually in comp.); वज्रपातसदृश, कुसुमसदृश &c.; कश्चिद्धरेः<BR> सौम्य सुतः सदृक्षः (आस्ते) Bhāg. 3. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Fit, right, suitable, conformable; as in प्रस्तावसदृशं वाक्यम् H. 2. 51.<BR>—3 Worthy, befitting, becoming; श्रुतस्य किं तत्सदृशं कुलस्य R. 14. 61, 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदृक्षविनिमय, सदृक्षस्त्री, सदृक्षस्पन्दनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृश|सदृशः
सदृक्ष (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), सदृश्, सदृश (-शी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Like, resembling, similar, of the same rank, (with gen. or loc., but<BR> usually in comp.); वज्रपातसदृश, कुसुमसदृश &c.; कश्चिद्धरेः<BR> सौम्य सुतः सदृक्षः (आस्ते) Bhāg. 3. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Fit, right, suitable, conformable; as in प्रस्तावसदृशं वाक्यम् H. 2. 51.<BR>—3 Worthy, befitting, becoming; श्रुतस्य किं तत्सदृशं कुलस्य R. 14. 61, 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदृक्षविनिमय, सदृक्षस्त्री, सदृक्षस्पन्दनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृशी
सदृक्ष (-क्षी <i>f.</i>), सदृश्, सदृश (-शी <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Like, resembling, similar, of the same rank, (with gen. or loc., but<BR> usually in comp.); वज्रपातसदृश, कुसुमसदृश &c.; कश्चिद्धरेः<BR> सौम्य सुतः सदृक्षः (आस्ते) Bhāg. 3. 1. 30.<BR>—2 Fit, right, suitable, conformable; as in प्रस्तावसदृशं वाक्यम् H. 2. 51.<BR>—3 Worthy, befitting, becoming; श्रुतस्य किं तत्सदृशं कुलस्य R. 14. 61, 1. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सदृक्षविनिमय, सदृक्षस्त्री, सदृक्षस्पन्दनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्षविनिमय
सदृक्ष + -विनिमय <i>a.</i> mistaking similar objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्षस्त्री
सदृक्ष + -स्त्री a wife of equal caste; सदृशस्त्रीषु जातानां पुत्राणामविशेषतः ।<BR> न मातृतो ज्यैष्ठयमस्ति जन्मतो ज्यैष्ठपमुच्यते Ms. 9. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदृक्षस्पन्दनम्
सदृक्ष + -स्पन्दनम् a regular or even palpitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदेश|सदेशः
सदेश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessing a country.<BR>—2 Belonging to the same place or country.<BR>—3 Proximate, neighbouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सदोष
सदोष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Defective, faulty.<BR>—2 Wrong, improper.<BR>—3 Objectionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्मन्
सद्मन् <i>n.</i> [सीदति अस्मिन् सद्-मनिन्]<BR>—1 A house, dwelling, abode; जगन्निवासो वसुदेवसद्मनि (वसन्)<BR> Śi. 1. 1; चकितनतनताङ्गी सद्म सद्यो विवेश Bv. 2. 32.<BR>—2 A place, station.<BR>—3 A temple.<BR>—4 An altar.<BR>—5 A seat.<BR>—6 Conflict.<BR>—7 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्
सद्यस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 To-day, the same day; गवादीनां पयोऽम्येद्युः सद्यो वा जायते दधि;<BR> पापस्य हि फलं सद्यः Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Instantly, forthwith, immediately, on a sudden; चकितनतनताङ्गी<BR> सद्म सद्यो विवेश Bv. 2. 32; Ku. 3. 29; Me. 16.<BR>—3 Quickly, promptly.<BR>—4 Recently, a short time back; as in सद्योहुताग्नीन् Ś. 4.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सद्यस्कार, सद्यःकालः, सद्यःकालीन, सद्यःकृतम्, सद्योजात, सद्यःपातिन्, सद्यःप्रक्षालक, सद्यःप्राणकर, सद्यःप्राणहर, सद्यःफल, सद्योभाविन्, सद्यःशुद्धिः, सद्यःशौचम्, सद्यःस्नेहनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्कार
सद्यस् + -कार <i>a.</i> being performed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">Page1616-2</a>]<BR> on the same day; सद्यस्कारां निरूप्येष्टिं सर्ववेदसदक्षिणाम् Mb. 12. 244. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःकालः|सद्यःकाल
सद्यस् + -कालः the present time. ━<i>a.</i> that which is to be performed<BR> on the same day (or in one day); तस्मात् सद्यस्काला एवंजातीयका विकृतयः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 5. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःकालीन
सद्यस् + -कालीन <i>a.</i> recent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःकृतम्
सद्यस् + -कृतम् name; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योजात|सद्योजातः
सद्यस् + -जात <i>a.</i> (सद्योजात) newly born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योजातः|सद्योजात
सद्यस् + -जात + .({@-तः@})<BR>—1 a calf.<BR>—2 an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःपातिन्
सद्यस् + -पातिन् <i>a.</i> quickly perishing, frail; सद्यःपाति प्रणयि हृदयं<BR> विप्रयोगे रुणद्धि Me. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःप्रक्षालक
सद्यस् + -प्रक्षालक <i>a.</i> providing for a day (or for a meal); सद्यःप्रक्षालको<BR> वा स्यान्माससंचयिकोऽपि वा Ms. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःप्राणकर|सद्यःप्राणकरः
सद्यस् + -प्राणकर <i>a.</i> quickly invigorating; सद्योमांसं नवान्नं<BR> च बाला स्त्री क्षीरभोजनम् । घृतमुष्णोदकं चैव सद्यःप्राणकराणि षट् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःप्राणहर|सद्यःप्राणहरः
सद्यस् + -प्राणहर <i>a.</i> quickly destroying life or vigour; शुष्कं<BR> मांसं स्त्रियो वृद्धा बालार्कस्तरुणं दधि । प्रभाते मैथुनं निद्रा सद्यःप्राणहराणि षट् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःफल
सद्यस् + -फल <i>a.</i> having immediate consequences.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्योभाविन्
सद्यस् + -भाविन् <i>a.</i> newly born. ━(<i>m.</i>) a newly born calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःशुद्धिः|सद्यःशुद्धि
सद्यस् + -शुद्धिः, -शौचम् immediate purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःशौचम्
सद्यस् + -शुद्धिः, -शौचम् immediate purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यःस्नेहनम्
सद्यस् + -स्नेहनम् a quickly operating emollient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्यस्क|सद्यस्कः
सद्यस्क <i>a.</i><BR>—1 New, recent.<BR>—2 Instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्रु
सद्रु <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Resting, staying.<BR>—2 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वन्द्व
सद्वन्द्व <i>a.</i> Quarrelsome, fond of strife, contentious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वसथः|सद्वसथ
सद्वसथः A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सद्वादित्वम्
सद्वादित्वम् The state of making a positive statement, being a सद्वादिन्;<BR> सद्वादित्वाच्च पाणिनेर्वचनं प्रमाणम् । असद्वादित्वान्न कात्यायनस्य<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मः|सधर्म
सधर्मः The same nature or qualities; गृहीतनरलोकसधर्मं<BR> भगवन्तम् Bhāg. 5. 4. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मन्|सधर्म्मन्
सधर्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having similar properties.<BR>—2 Having similar duties.<BR>—3 Of the same sect or caste.<BR>—4 Like, resembling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सधर्मचारिणी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मचारिणी|सधर्म्मचारिणी
सधर्मन् + -चारिणी a legal wife, a legally married wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मिणी|सधर्म्मिणी
सधर्मिणी See सधर्मचारिणी above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधर्मिन्|सधर्म्मिन्
सधर्मिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> See सधर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधिः|सधि
सधिः N. of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सधिस्
सधिस् <i>m.</i> An ox, a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्र्यञ्च्|सध्र्यंच्
सध्र्यञ्च् <i>a.</i> (सध्रीची <i>f.</i>) [सहाञ्चति; cf. P. VI. 3. 95]<BR>—1 Going along with, associated with, accompanying.<BR>—2 Right, correct; क्षेमस्य सध्र्यग्विमृशेषु हेतुः Bhāg. 4. 22. 21.<BR>━<i>m.</i> A companion (husband); सध्रीचा वलयितपद्मनालसूत्रः Śi. 8. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्रीची
सध्रीची A female companion, confidante, a wife; सीतां सौमित्रिणा<BR> त्यक्तां सध्रीचीं त्रस्नुमेकिकाम् Bk. 6. 7; सध्रीचीवदनसरोजसारमाध्वीम्<BR> (गिरम् आस्वाद्य) Rām. Ch. 7. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सध्रीचीन
सध्रीचीन <i>a.</i> Accompanying, associated with; सध्रीचीनेन वैराग्यं<BR> ज्ञानं च जनयिष्यति Bhāg. 4. 29. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्
सन् €1 P., €8 U. (सनति, सनोति, सनुते, सात; <i>pass.</i> सन्यते,<BR> सायते; <i>desid.</i> सिसनिषति; सिषासति)<BR>—1 To love, like.<BR>—2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">Page1617-1</a>]<BR> worship, honour.<BR>—3 To acquire, obtain.<BR>—4 To receive graciously.<BR>—5 To honour with gifts, give, bestow, distribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1616-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनः|सन
सनः<BR>—1 The flapping of an elephantʼs ears.<BR>—2 Presenting, offering; आदौ सनात् स्वतपसः च चतुःसनोऽभूत् Bhāg. 2. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनम्
सनः + .{@-नम्@} Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनकः|सनक
सनकः N. of one of the four sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्
सनत् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Brahman. ━<i>ind.</i> Always, perpetually.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सनत्कुमारः, सनत्सुजातः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्कुमारः|सनत्कुमार
सनत् + -कुमारः N. of one of the four sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनत्सुजातः|सनत्सुजात
सनत् + -सुजातः N. of one of the seven mind-born sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्दः|सनन्द
सनन्दः, सनन्दनः N. of one of the four sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनन्दनः|सनन्दन
सनन्दः, सनन्दनः N. of one of the four sons of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनय
सनय <i>a.</i> Ancient, old (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनसूत्र|सनसूत्रं
सनसूत्र See सणसूत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सना
सना <i>ind.</i> Always, perpetually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनात्
सनात् <i>ind.</i> Always.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातन|सनातनः
सनातन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Perpetual, constant, eternal, permanent; ज्वलन्मणिव्योमसदां सनातनम्<BR> Ki. 8. 1; एष धर्मः सनातनः.<BR>—2 Firm, fixed, settled; एष धर्मः सनातनः U. 5. 22. 3 Primeval, ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातनः|सनातन
सनातन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 The primeval being, Viṣṇu; सनातनः पितरमुपागमत् स्वयम् Bk. 1. 1.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Brahman.<BR>—4 A guest of the Manes.<BR>—5 N. of one of the sons of Brahman.<BR>—6 An ancient sage; द्विजातिचरितो धर्मः शास्त्रे दृष्टः सनातनैः<BR> Rām. 2. 61. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनातनी
सनातन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 Of Durgā or Pārvatī.<BR>—3 Of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथ
सनाथ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a master, lord or husband; त्वया नाथेन वैदेही सनाथा ह्यद्य<BR> वर्तते Rām.<BR>—2 Possessed of a guardian or protector; सनाथा इदानीं धर्मचारिणः<BR> Ś. 1; सनाथः संवृत्तः V. 5.<BR>—3 Occupied by, possessed by.<BR>—4 Provided or furnished with, having, possessing, endowed with, full<BR> of; usually in comp.; लतासनाथ इव प्रतिभाति Ś. 1; शिलातलसनाथो<BR> लतामण्डपः V. 2; Me. 100; Ku. 7. 94; R. 9. 42; V. 4. 10.<BR>—5 Crowded (as an assembly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथा
सनाथ + .{@-था@} A woman whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाथीकृ
सनाथीकृ Den. P.<BR>—1 To cause to possess a master; भुवनमिदं सनाथीकृतम् Dk. 2. 3.<BR>—2 To afford shelter, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभः|सनाभ
सनाभः A nearest kinsman, uterine brother; तस्माद्भवन्तो हृदयेन<BR> जाताः सर्वे महीयांसममुं सनाभम् Bhāg. 5. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभि|सनाभिः
सनाभि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Connected by the same navel or womb, uterine.<BR>—2 Kindred, related.<BR>—3 Like, resembling; गङ्गावर्तसनाभिर्नाभिः Dk.<BR>—4 Affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभिः|सनाभि
सनाभि + .{@-भिः@}<BR>—1 A uterine brother; a near kinsman; यो मे सनाभिवधतप्तहृदा ततेन<BR> लिप्ताभिशापमपमार्ष्टुमुपाजहार Bhāg. 10. 83. 9.<BR>—2 A relation, kinsman; अवलीढसनाभिरश्वसेनः Ki. 13. 11.<BR>—3 A relation as far as the seventh degree; यथोक्तेनैव कल्पेन शुद्धपन्ति<BR> तु सनाभयः Ms. 5. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनाभ्यः|सनाभ्य
सनाभ्यः A relation as far as the 7th degree; न च तत् कर्म कुर्वाणः<BR> सनाभ्योऽप्यशुचिर्भवेत् Ms. 5. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनामन्
सनामन्, -सनामक <i>a.</i><BR> Having the same name; सनाम्नी या भवित्री मे<BR> दित्सिता चैव बन्धुभिः Mb. 1. 13. 29; चन्द्रस्य ग्रहणमिति श्रुतेः<BR> सनाम्नो मौर्येन्दोर्द्विषदभियोग इत्यवैति Mu. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनामक|सनामकः
सनामन्, -सनामक <i>a.</i><BR> Having the same name; सनाम्नी या भवित्री मे<BR> दित्सिता चैव बन्धुभिः Mb. 1. 13. 29; चन्द्रस्य ग्रहणमिति श्रुतेः<BR> सनाम्नो मौर्येन्दोर्द्विषदभियोग इत्यवैति Mu. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिः|सनि
सनिः [सन्-इः Uṇ. 4. 151]<BR>—1 Worship, service.<BR>—2 A gift, donation.<BR>—3 An entreaty, a respectful solicitation (<i>f.</i> also in this sense).<BR>—4 Obtaining; तद्वां नरा सनये दंस उग्रमाविष्कृणोमि Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 16.<BR>—5 A quarter or point of the compass (<i>f.</i> also).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सनिवन्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिवन्य
सनिः + -वन्य <i>a.</i> what is obtained by begging; सनिवनिप्राप्तं सनिवन्यं<BR> याञ्चाप्राप्तमित्यर्थः ŚB. on MS. 10. 2. 27; सनिवन्येव भृतिवचनात् MS. 10. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिकार
सनिकार <i>a.</i> Degrading (as punishment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिग्रह
सनिग्रह <i>a.</i> Furnished with a handle; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिर्विशेष
सनिर्विशेष <i>a.</i> Indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिर्वेद
सनिर्वेद <i>a.</i> Dull (as conversation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिर्वेदम्
सनिर्वेद + .({@-दम्@}) <i>ind.</i> Despairingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनित|सनितः
सनित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Granted.<BR>—2 Gained, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठीवम्
सनिष्ठीवम्, -सनिष्ठेवम्<BR> Speech accompanied with emission of saliva, sputtered speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनिष्ठेवम्
सनिष्ठीवम्, -सनिष्ठेवम्<BR> Speech accompanied with emission of saliva, sputtered speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनी
सनी<BR>—1 A respectful entreaty.<BR>—2 A quarter or point of the compass.<BR>—3 Flapping of the elephantʼs ears.<BR>—4 Light, lustre.<BR>—5 An epithet of Gaurī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीड|सनीडः
सनीड(ल) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living in the same nest, dwelling together.<BR>—2 Near, proximate; एतल्लतागृहसनीडकृतस्वनीडाः (पारावताः)<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनील
सनीड(ल) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Living in the same nest, dwelling together.<BR>—2 Near, proximate; एतल्लतागृहसनीडकृतस्वनीडाः (पारावताः)<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीडः|सनीड
सनीड(ल) + .{@-नीडः, -डम्@} Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनीडम्
सनीड(ल) + .{@-नीडः, -डम्@} Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सनेमि
सनेमि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a felly.<BR>—2 Complete, perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतः|सन्त|संत|सन्तः
संतः The two hands opened and the palms joined together (संहतल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतक्ष्|सन्तक्ष्
संतक्ष् €1 P.<BR>—1 To pare off, chisel, chop.<BR>—2 To wound, hurt, strike; निस्त्रिंशाभ्यां सुतीक्ष्णाभ्यामन्योन्यं संततक्षतुः<BR> Mb.; Bṛ. S. 42. 29.<BR>—3 To hurt by words.<BR>—4 Ved. To compose (hymns &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतक्षणम्
संतक्षणम् Sarcastic or cutting language, sarcasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतन्|सन्तन्
संतन् €8 U.<BR>—1 To stretch over, cover over, cover with.<BR>—2 To make continuous, connect together.<BR>—3 To effect, accomplish.<BR>—4 To show, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतत|सन्तत|सन्ततं
संतत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Stretched, extended.<BR>—2 Uninterrupted, continual, constant, regular.<BR>—3 Lasting, eternal.<BR>—4 Much, many.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संततम्
संतत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Always, continually, constantly, eternally, perpetually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संततिः|सन्तति|संतति|सन्ततिः
संततिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Stretching across, spreading along.<BR>—2 Extent, expanse, extension; संतापसंततिमहाव्यसनाय तस्यामासक्तमेतदनपेक्षितहेतु<BR> चेतः Māl. 1. 23; Bhāg. 1. 4. 19.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">Page1618-1</a>]<BR>—3 Continuous line or flow, series, row, range, succession, continuity; चिन्तासंततितन्तुजालनिबिडस्यूतेव<BR> लग्ना प्रिया Māl. 5. 10; कुसुमसंततिसंततसंगिभिः Śi. 6. 36.<BR>—5 Perpetuation, uninterrupted continuance; निदानमिक्ष्वाकुकुलस्य संततेः R. 3. 1.<BR>—6 A race, lineage, family.<BR>—7 Offspring, progeny; संततिः शुद्धवंश्या हि परत्रेह च शर्मणे R. 1. 69.<BR>—8 A heap, mass; (अलं) सहसा संततिमंहसां विहन्तुम् Ki. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1617-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानः|सन्तान|संतान|संतानं|सन्तानः
संतानः, -नम्<BR>—1 Stretching, extending, extension, expanse, spread; चरामो वसुधां<BR> कृत्स्नां धर्मसंतानमिच्छवः Rām. 4. 18. 9; संतानैस्तनुभावनष्टसलिला<BR> व्यक्तिं व्रजन्त्यापगाः Ś. 7. 8.<BR>—2 Continuity, continuous flow or line, succession, continuance; अच्छिन्नामलसंतानाः<BR> Ku. 6. 69; संतानवाहीनि दुःखानि U. 4. 8.<BR>—3 Family, race.<BR>—4 Progeny, offspring, issue; संतानार्थाय विधये R. 1. 34; संतानकामाय<BR> राज्ञे 2. 65, 18. 52; Ms. 3. 185.<BR>—5 One of the five trees of Indraʼs paradise; सन्तानकुसुमशेखरकं<BR> च मम शीर्षे पिनद्धम् Nāg. 3 (between verses 2-3); सन्तानः कल्पवृक्षश्च<BR> पुंसि वा हरिचन्दनम् Ak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: संतानसंधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानम्
संतानः, -नम्<BR>—1 Stretching, extending, extension, expanse, spread; चरामो वसुधां<BR> कृत्स्नां धर्मसंतानमिच्छवः Rām. 4. 18. 9; संतानैस्तनुभावनष्टसलिला<BR> व्यक्तिं व्रजन्त्यापगाः Ś. 7. 8.<BR>—2 Continuity, continuous flow or line, succession, continuance; अच्छिन्नामलसंतानाः<BR> Ku. 6. 69; संतानवाहीनि दुःखानि U. 4. 8.<BR>—3 Family, race.<BR>—4 Progeny, offspring, issue; संतानार्थाय विधये R. 1. 34; संतानकामाय<BR> राज्ञे 2. 65, 18. 52; Ms. 3. 185.<BR>—5 One of the five trees of Indraʼs paradise; सन्तानकुसुमशेखरकं<BR> च मम शीर्षे पिनद्धम् Nāg. 3 (between verses 2-3); सन्तानः कल्पवृक्षश्च<BR> पुंसि वा हरिचन्दनम् Ak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: संतानसंधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानसंधिः|सन्तानसन्धि|संतानसंधि
संतानः + -संधिः a peace cemented by family alliance (as by giving a daughter<BR> in marriage &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानकः|सन्तानक|संतानक
संतानकः<BR>—1 One of the five trees of Indraʼs paradise or its flower; दधतः<BR> सन्तानकानां स्रजः Nāg. 3. 9. [It may be the tree Rhododendron Arborium.<BR> It is a tree which grows abundantly on the Himālaya. It gives good shade<BR> and bears beautiful flowers, having five united petals. The meaning of<BR> the word suggests a profuse growth both of the individual and its progeny.]<BR>—2 (pl.) N. of a particular world; लोकान् संतानकान्नाम यास्यन्तीमे समागताः<BR> Rām. 7. 110. 18; Ku. 6. 4, 7. 3; Śi. 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतानिका
संतानिका<BR>—1 Froth, foam.<BR>—2 Cream.<BR>—3 A cobweb.<BR>—4 The blade of a knife or sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतप्|सन्तप्
संतप् €1 P.<BR>—1 To heat, warm; संतप्तचामीकर Bk. 3. 3; संतप्तायसि संस्थितस्य<BR> पयसो नामापि न ज्ञायते Bh. 2. 67.<BR>—2 To parch, dry up.<BR>—3 To pain by heat, torture. ━<i>Pass.</i><BR>—1 To become hot or heated.<BR>—2 To be distressed, suffer pain, be sorry; संतप्तानां त्वमसि शरणम्<BR> Me. 7 ‘of the afflicted’; दिवापि मयि निष्क्रान्ते संतप्येते गुरू मम<BR> Mb.; Bh. 2. 87.<BR>—3 To repent, be stung with remorse; अवधूतप्रणिपाताः पश्चात् संतप्यमानमनसोऽपि V. 3. 5.<BR>—4 To undergo penance. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To heat, burn, inflame.<BR>—2 To provoke, exasperate, irritate.<BR>—3 To torment, torture, distress, afflict.<BR>—4 To burn up, consume.<BR>—5 To foment (quarrels &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतपनम्
संतपनम्<BR>—1 Heating, inflaming.<BR>—2 Torturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतप्त|सन्तप्त|सन्तप्तः
संतप्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Heated, inflamed, red-hot, glowing; संतप्तायसि संस्थितस्य पयसो<BR> नामापि न ज्ञायते Pt. 1. 250; संतप्तचामीकरवल्गुवज्रम् Bk. 3. 3;<BR> चुक्रुशुर्दुःखसंतप्ता मृत्योरिव भयागमे Rām. 2. 48. 32.<BR>—2 Distressed, afflicted, tormented.<BR>—3 Burnt, scorched.<BR>—4 Exhausted, fatigued, wearied.<BR>—5 Dry, faded; संतप्तपद्मा पद्मिन्यो लीनमीनविहंगमाः Rām. 2. 59. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतप्तम्
संतप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} Pain, grief, sorrow.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: संतप्तायस्, संतप्तवक्षस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतप्तायस्
संतप्त + -अयस् <i>n.</i> red-hot iron; Pt. 1. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतप्तवक्षस्
संतप्त + -वक्षस् <i>a.</i> short-breathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतापः|सन्ताप|संताप|सन्तापः
संतापः<BR>—1 Heat, great heat, inflammation; नष्टज्वलनसंतापा प्रशान्ताध्यायसत्कथा<BR> Rām. 2. 48. 34; संतापदग्धस्य शिखण्डियूनो वृष्टेः पुरस्तादचिरप्रभेव Māl. 3. 4.<BR>—2 Distress, torment, suffering, torture, agony, anguish; संतापसंततिमहाव्यसनाय<BR> तस्यामासक्तमेतदनपेक्षितहेतु चेतः Māl. 1. 23; न संतापच्छेदो<BR> हिमसरसि वा चन्द्रमसि वा 1. 31; Ś. 3.<BR>—3 Passion, rage.<BR>—4 Remorse, repentance; कृत्यं न कुरुते वेगान्न स संतापमाप्नुयात् Pt. 1. 109.<BR>—5 Penance, fatigues of penance, mortification of the body; संतापे<BR> दिशतु शिवः शिवां प्रसक्तिम् Ki. 5. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतापन|सन्तापन|संतापनः|सन्तापनः
संतापन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Burning, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतापनः|सन्तापन|संतापन|सन्तापनः
संतापन + .{@-नः@} N. of one of the 5 arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतापनम्
संतापन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Burning, scorching.<BR>—2 Paining, afflicting.<BR>—3 Exciting passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतापित|सन्तापित|सन्तापितः
संतापित <i>p. p.</i> Heated, afflicted, tormented &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतम्|सन्तम्
संतम् €4 P.<BR>—1 To become exhausted.<BR>—2 To pine away, languish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतमकः|सन्तमक|संतमक
संतमकः Oppression or distress (in breathing &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतमस्|सन्तमस्
संतमस् <i>n.</i>, संतमसम्<BR>—1 All-pervading or universal darkness, great darkness; निमज्जयन् संतमसे<BR> पराशयम् N. 9. 98; Śi. 9. 22; अकार्ष्टामायुधच्छायं रजःसंतमसे<BR> रणे Bk. 5. 2; प्रशान्ते च संतमसे Colacampū p. 25.<BR>—2 Great darkness or delusion of the mind (महामोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतमसम्
संतमस् <i>n.</i>, संतमसम्<BR>—1 All-pervading or universal darkness, great darkness; निमज्जयन् संतमसे<BR> पराशयम् N. 9. 98; Śi. 9. 22; अकार्ष्टामायुधच्छायं रजःसंतमसे<BR> रणे Bk. 5. 2; प्रशान्ते च संतमसे Colacampū p. 25.<BR>—2 Great darkness or delusion of the mind (महामोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतर्जनम्
संतर्जनम् Threatening, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतर्पणम्
संतर्पणम्<BR>—1 Satisfying, satiating.<BR>—2 Gratifying, delighting.<BR>—3 That which gives delight.<BR>—4 A kind of sweet dish. ━<i>a.</i> Refreshing, invigorating; संतर्पणानि<BR> सकलेन्द्रियमोहनानि (वचोमृतानि) Māl. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतर्पयाण
संतर्पयाण <i>a.</i> One who satisfies; योऽसौ त्वया खाण्डवे चित्रभानुं<BR> संतर्पयाणेन धनुर्धरेण Mb. 8. 90. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतिः|सन्ति|संति|सन्तिः
संतिः<BR>—1 End, destruction.<BR>—2 A gift; cf. सति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतुद्|सन्तुद्
संतुद् €6 U.<BR>—1 To goad, sting.<BR>—2 To recur (as a disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतुष्|सन्तुष्
संतुष् €4 P.<BR>—1 To be pleased, satisfied or contented; संतुष्टो भार्यया भर्ता भर्त्रा<BR> भार्या तथैव च Ms. 3. 60; तृष्णे जृम्भसि पापकर्मनिरते नाद्यापि संतुष्यसि<BR> Bh. 3. 5; Bg. 3. 17.<BR>—2 To have great pleasure in. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To satisfy, please, gratify.<BR>—2 To present with (anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतुष्ट|सन्तुष्ट|सन्तुष्टः
संतुष्ट <i>p. p.</i> Satisfied, pleased, contented; आत्मन्येव च<BR> संतुष्टस्तस्य कार्यं न विद्यते Bg. 3. 17; असंतुष्टा द्विजा नष्टाः<BR> संतुष्टाश्च महीभुजः Cāṇakyanītisāra 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतुष्टिः|सन्तुष्टि|संतुष्टि
संतुष्टिः <i>f.</i> Complete satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतोषः|सन्तोष|संतोष|सन्तोषः
संतोषः<BR>—1 Satisfaction, contentment; संतोषमूलं हि सुखम् Ms. 4. 12; संतोष<BR> एव पुरुषस्य परं निधानम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Pleasure, delight, joy.<BR>—3 The thumb and fore-finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतोषणम्
संतोषणम् Pleasing, gratifying, comforting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतृण्ण|सन्तृण्ण
संतृण्ण <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Joined, fastened together.<BR>—2 Covered; यथा शङ्कुना सर्वाणि पर्णानि संतृण्णानि Ch. Up. 2. 23. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1618-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतॄ|सन्तॄ
संतॄ €1 P.<BR>—1 To cross over, traverse, travel over.<BR>—2 To swim, float.<BR>—3 To get over, overcome, surmount, go to the end of.<BR>—4 To reach, attain to.<BR>—5 To escape from, be saved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतरणम्
संतरणम्<BR>—1 Crossing over.<BR>—2 Surmounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतारः|सन्तार|संतार
संतारः<BR>—1 Crossing, passing over; गङ्गायाश्चापि संतारं भरद्वाजस्य दर्शनम्<BR> Rām. 1. 3. 15.<BR>—2 A ford; नीयमानानि संतारे हृतान्यासन् वितस्तया Mb. 5. 119. 8.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: संतारनौ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संतारनौ
संतारः + -नौ <i>f.</i> a boat to cross over; यन्मेदिनी प्रचलिता पतिताग्रहर्म्या<BR> संचारनौरिव विकीर्णमहोर्मिमाला Bālacharitam 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संत्यज्|सन्त्यज्
संत्यज् €1 P.<BR>—1 To abandon; जायामदोषामुत संत्यजामि R. 14. 34; यश्चासूनपि<BR> संत्यजेत् करुणया Nāg. 2. 10.<BR>—2 To avoid, shun; Bh. 1. 81.<BR>—3 To give up, renounce; एतैर्विवादान् संत्यज्य सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते Ms. 4. 181.<BR>—4 To except, exclude; संत्यज्य विक्रमादित्यं धैर्यमन्यत्र दुर्लभम्<BR> Rāj. T. 3. 343.<BR>—5 To withdraw from (an obligation); प्रक्रान्ते सप्तमं भागं चतुर्थं<BR> पथि संत्यजन् Y. 2. 198. ━<i>Caus.</i> To deprive (one) of, rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संत्यक्त|सन्त्यक्त
संत्यक्त <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Completely deserted or abandoned.<BR>—2 Robbed, deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संत्यजनम्
संत्यजनम् Leaving, renouncing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संत्रस्|सन्त्रस्
संत्रस् €1. €4 P. To fear, be afraid or terrified; विचकार ततो<BR> रामः शरान् संतत्रसुर्द्विषः Bk. 14. 39. ━<i>Caus.</i> To frighten,<BR> terrify; भवति हि पापं कृत्वा स्वकर्मसंत्रासितः पुरुषः Pt. 1. 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संत्रासः|सन्त्रास|संत्रास
संत्रासः Fear, terror, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंश्|सन्दंश्
संदंश् €1 P.<BR>—1 To bite, sting; संदष्टेऽधरपल्लवे सचकितं हस्ताग्रमाधुन्वती Amaru. 36.<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To stick or adhere closely to, cling; उरसा संदष्टसर्पत्वचा<BR> Ś. 7. 11; संदष्टवस्त्रेष्वबलानितम्बेषु R. 16. 65, 48.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To press together, crush by pressure; संदष्टकुसुमशयनानि<BR> गात्राणि Ś. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंशः|सन्दंश|संदंश|सन्दंशः
संदंशः<BR>—1 A pair of tongs; अयस्मयैरग्निपिण्डैः संदंशैस्त्वचि निष्कुषन्ति<BR> Bhāg. 5. 26. 19.<BR>—2 Too great compression of the teeth in the pronunciation of vowels (or letters).<BR>—3 N. of those parts of the body used for grasping.<BR>—4 N. of a hell.<BR>—5 A chapter or section of a book.<BR>—6 The side of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंशकः|सन्दंशक|संदंशक
संदंशकः A pair of tongs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंशिका
संदंशिका<BR>—1 A pair of pincers.<BR>—2 An iron bill; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदंशित
संदंशित <i>a.</i> Armed, mailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदष्ट|सन्दष्ट
संदष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Bitten.<BR>—2 Pressed closely together, crushed; संदष्टकुसुमशयनानि (गात्राणि) Ś. 3. 17.<BR>—3 Nipped; pinched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदष्टम्
संदष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} A particular fault in pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदह्|सन्दह्
संदह् €1 P. To burn; अभिजनः संदह्यतां वह्निना Bh. 2. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदाहः|सन्दाह|संदाह|सन्दाहः
संदाहः Burning up, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदातृ
संदातृ <i>a.</i> One who ties up; असंदितानां संदाता Ms. 8. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानम्
संदानम्<BR>—1 A rope, cord.<BR>—2 A chain, fetter; ‘संदानं पशूनां पादबन्धनम्’ इति विश्वः.<BR>—3 Cutting, dividing.<BR>—4 That part of an elephantʼs temples whence the ichor (मद) exudes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानः|सन्दान|संदान|संदानं|सन्दानं|सन्दानः
संदानम् + .{@-नः@} That part of an elephant under the knee where the fetter<BR> is fastened; संदानान्तादस्त्रिभिः शिक्षितास्त्रैः Śi. 18. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानकम्
संदानकम् A pigeonʼs nest; अपनीतकपोतसंदानकम् Pratimā 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानिका|सन्दानिका
संदानिका A kind of sweetmeat; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानित|सन्दानित|सन्दानितः
संदानित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bound, tied; वक्षोजद्वन्द्वसंदानितमथ शिथिलीकृत्य गात्रं कथंचित्<BR> Rām. Ch. 7. 92.<BR>—2 Fettered, chained; Śiva B. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदानिनी|सन्दानिनी
संदानिनी A cow-pen (गोष्ठ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदायः|सन्दाय|संदाय
संदायः A rein, leash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदावः|सन्दाव|संदाव|सन्दावः
संदावः Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदित|सन्दित|सन्दितः
संदित <i>a.</i> Bound, chained, fettered; असंदितानां संदाता संदितानां<BR> च मोक्षकः Ms. 8. 342.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिश्|सन्दिश्
संदिश् €6 P.<BR>—1 To give, grant, assign, make over; राज्यं संदिश्य भोगांश्च ममार<BR> व्रणपीडितः Bk. 6. 141; Y. 2. 232.<BR>—2 To order, direct, instruct, advise, send as a message; किं नु खलु<BR> दुष्यन्तस्य युक्तरूपमस्माभिः संदेष्टव्यम् Ś. 4; Śi. 9. 56, 61.<BR>—3 To send as a messenger, entrust with a message; अथ विश्वात्मने गौरी<BR> संदिदेश मिथः सखीम् Ku. 6. 1.<BR>—4 To appoint.<BR>—5 To commission or depute in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिष्ट|सन्दिष्ट|सन्दिष्टं|संदिष्टः
संदिष्ट <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Pointed out, indicated.<BR>—2 Assigned.<BR>—3 Told, narrated, communicated.<BR>—4 Agreed to, promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिष्टः|सन्दिष्ट|संदिष्ट|सन्दिष्टं
संदिष्ट + .{@-ष्टः@} One entrusted with a message, a messenger, herald, courier<BR> (संदिष्टार्थ also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिष्टम्
संदिष्ट + .{@-ष्टम्@} Information, news, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशः|सन्देश|संदेश|सन्देशः
संदेशः<BR>—1 Information, news, tidings.<BR>—2 A message, an errand; संदेशं मे हर धनपतिक्रोधविश्लेषितस्य<BR> Me. 7, 13; R. 12. 63; Ku. 6. 2.<BR>—3 Commission, command; अनुष्ठितो गुरोः संदेशः Ś. 5.<BR>—4 A kind of sweetmeat.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: संदेशार्थः, संदेशपदानि, संदेशवाच्, संदेशहरः, संदेशहारकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशार्थः|सन्देशार्थ
संदेशः + -अर्थः the subject of a message; संदेशार्थाः क्व पटुकरणैः<BR> प्राणिभिः प्रापणीयाः Me. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशपदानि
संदेशः + -पदानि the words of a message.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशवाच्|सन्देशवाच्
संदेशः + -वाच् <i>f.</i> a message.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशहरः|सन्देशहर|संदेशहर|सन्देशहरः
संदेशः + -हरः, -हारकः<BR>—1 a news-bearer, messenger.<BR>—2 an envoy, ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1619-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशहारकः|सन्देशहारक|संदेशहारक|सन्देशहारकः
