समुन्दनम्
समुन्दनम्<BR>—1 Moistening.<BR>—2 Wetness, moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्न|समुन्नं
समुन्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wet, moist; यत्रोज्झिताभिर्मुहुरम्बुवाहैः समुन्नमद्भिर्न समुन्नमाद्भिः Śi. 4. 15.<BR>—2 Dirty, soiled; समुन्नानीव वस्त्राणि ययुर्दुर्दर्शतां पराम् Mb. 8. 21. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नम्
समुन्नम् €1 P. To rise, ascend. ━<i>Caus.</i> To raise or lift up, erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नत|समुन्नतः
समुन्नत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Upraised, lifted up.<BR>—2 Elevated, high, lofty.<BR>—3 Exalted, sublime.<BR>—4 Proud.<BR>—5 Projecting.<BR>—6 Upright, just.<BR>—7 Arched, vaulted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नतिः|समुन्नति
समुन्नतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Lifting up, raising.<BR>—2 Height, loftiness, elevation (mental also); मनसः शिखराणां च<BR> सदृशी ते समुन्नतिः Ku. 6. 66; R. 3. 10.<BR>—3 Eminence, high position or dignity, exaltation; उत्तमैः सह संगेन<BR> को न याति समुन्नतिम्; स जातो येन जातेन याति वंशः समुन्नतिम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—4 Rise, prosperity, increase, success; विनिपातोऽपि समः समुन्नतेः<BR> Ki. 2. 34; प्रकृतिः खलु सा महीयसः सहते नान्यसमुन्नतिं यया 2. 21.<BR>—5 Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नमनम्
समुन्नमनम् Raising, arching (as the brows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नह्
समुन्नह् €4 P.<BR>—1 To bind or tie up.<BR>—2 To raise or lift up.<BR>—3 To loosen, unfasten.<BR>—4 To liberate, release, set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समुन्नद्ध|समुन्नद्धः
समुन्नद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Elevated, exalted.<BR>—2 Swollen.<BR>—3 Full, excessive; परोक्षेण समुन्नद्धप्रणयौत्कण्ठ्यकातरः Bhāg. 1. 15. 3.<BR>—4 Proud, arrogant, overbearing.<BR>—5 Conceited, thinking oneself to be learned; अचिन्त्यं चापि तं ज्ञात्वा … विचरेद्योऽसमुन्नद्धः<BR> Mb. 12. 351. 12.<BR>—6 Unfettered.<BR>—7 Bound up.<BR>—8 Supreme.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1642-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

