सरण्डः|सरण्ड|सरंड|सरंडः
सरण्डः [सृ-अण्डन् Uṇ. 1. 120]<BR>—1 A bird.<BR>—2 A libertine, dissolute man.<BR>—3 A lizard.<BR>—4 A rogue.<BR>—5 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्युः|सरण्यु
सरण्युः [सृ-अन्युच् Uṇ. 3. 83]<BR>—1 Air, wind.<BR>—2 A cloud.<BR>—3 Water.<BR>—4 The spring.<BR>—5 Fire.<BR>—6 N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्
सरत् <i>m.</i> A thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्निः|सरत्नि
सरत्निः <i>m., f.</i> A kind of cubit-measure; cf. रलि or अरत्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथ|सरथः
सरथ <i>a.</i> Riding in the same car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथः|सरथ
सरथ + .{@-थः@} A warrior riding in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरद्वत्
सरद्वत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 N. of the sage Gautama.<BR>—2 N. of Gautamaʼs son (also spelt with श); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभस
सरभस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Speedy, quick,<BR>—2 Violent, impetuous.<BR>—3 Passionate.<BR>—4 Delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभसम्
सरभस + .{@-सम्@} <i>ind.</i> Impetuously, hurriedly &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा [सृ-अमः Uṇ. 4. 90]<BR>—1 A bitch.<BR>—2 The bitch of the gods.<BR>—3 N. of a daughter of Dakṣa.<BR>—4 N. of the wife of Bibhīṣaṇa, brother of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयुः|सरयु
सरयुः Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयुः|सरयु
सरयुः + .{@-युः, -यूः@} <i>f.</i> N. of a river on which stands Ayodhyā, or Oudh;<BR> तीर्थे तोयव्यतिकरभवे जह्नुकन्यासरय्वोः R. 8. 95, 13. 61, 63, 14. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयूः
सरयुः + .{@-युः, -यूः@} <i>f.</i> N. of a river on which stands Ayodhyā, or Oudh;<BR> तीर्थे तोयव्यतिकरभवे जह्नुकन्यासरय्वोः R. 8. 95, 13. 61, 63, 14. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरल|सरलः
सरल <i>a.</i> [सृ-अलच् Uṇ. 1. 105]<BR>—1 Straight, not crooked.<BR>—2 Honest, upright, sincere, candid. —3 Simple, artless, simple-minded;<BR> सरले साहसरागं परिहर Māl. 6. 10; अयि सरले किमत्र मया<BR> भगवत्या शक्यम् 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलः|सरल
सरल + .{@-लः@}<BR>—1 A kind of pine tree; विघट्टितानां सरलद्रुमाणाम् Ku. 1. 9; Me. 55;<BR> R. 4. 75; also सरला.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सरलाङ्गः, सरलद्रवः, सरलयायिनी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलाङ्गः|सरलाङ्ग|सरलांग
सरल + -अङ्गः ‘the exudation of Sarala’, resin, turpentine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलद्रवः|सरलद्रव
सरल + -द्रवः fragrant resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलयायिनी
सरल + -यायिनी a plant with an erect stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1653-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरलित
सरलित <i>a.</i> Straightened, straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरव्य|सरव्यं
सरव्य See शरव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्
सरस् <i>n.</i> [सृ-असुन्]<BR>—1 A lake, pond, pool, a large sheet of water; सरसामास्मि सागरः Bg. 10. 24.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 Speech; cf. सरस्-वती.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सरःकाकः, सरोजम्, सरोजन्मन्, सरोजः, सरोजिनी, सरोरुहिणी, सरोरक्षः, सरोरुह्, सरोवरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरःकाकः|सरःकाक
सरस् + -काकः + ({@-की@})<BR> A swan; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरःकाकी
सरस् + -काकः + ({@-की@})<BR> A swan; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजम्
सरस् + -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-रुहम्@} (सरोजम्, सरोजन्मन्, सरोरुहम्) also सरसिजम्, सरसिरुहम्<BR> a lotus; सरसिजमनुविद्धं शैवलेनापि रम्यम् Ś. 1. 20;<BR> [Shri Kṣītiśachandra Chatterji points out in Mañjūṣā (March, 1958)<BR> that the word सरसिजम् has been used in the sense of ‘a lotus’<BR> probably for the first time by Kālidāsa. According to lexicographers<BR> the word सरसिज is met with first in the Suśruta Saṃhitā (1. 46. 124)<BR> as an adjective qualifying मत्स्याः. Bhāravi uses the word<BR> in the sense of ‘a land lotus’ in उत्फुल्लस्थलनलिनीवनादमुष्मादुद्धूतः<BR> सरसिजसंभवः परागः. Three stages of being यौगिक, योगरूढ<BR> and रूढ are thus clearly seen in the history of the word.]; सरोरुहद्युतिमुषः<BR> पादांस्तवासेवितुम् Ratn. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजन्मन्
सरस् + -जम्, -जन्मन् <i>n.</i>, {@-रुहम्@} (सरोजम्, सरोजन्मन्, सरोरुहम्) also सरसिजम्, सरसिरुहम्<BR> a lotus; सरसिजमनुविद्धं शैवलेनापि रम्यम् Ś. 1. 20;<BR> [Shri Kṣītiśachandra Chatterji points out in Mañjūṣā (March, 1958)<BR> that the word सरसिजम् has been used in the sense of ‘a lotus’<BR> probably for the first time by Kālidāsa. According to lexicographers<BR> the word सरसिज is met with first in the Suśruta Saṃhitā (1. 46. 124)<BR> as an adjective qualifying मत्स्याः. Bhāravi uses the word<BR> in the sense of ‘a land lotus’ in उत्फुल्लस्थलनलिनीवनादमुष्मादुद्धूतः<BR> सरसिजसंभवः परागः. Three stages of being यौगिक, योगरूढ<BR> and रूढ are thus clearly seen in the history of the word.]; सरोरुहद्युतिमुषः<BR> पादांस्तवासेवितुम् Ratn. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजः|सरोज|सरोजं
सरस् + -जः (also {@सरसिजः@}) Sārasa bird. ({@सरोजिन्@} <i>m.</i><BR> an epithet of Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोजिनी
सरस् + -जिनी, -रुहिणी<BR>—1 a lotus-plant; भ्रमर कथं वा सरोजिनीं त्यजसि Bv. 1. 100.<BR>—2 a pond abounding in lotuses.<BR>—3 a multitude of lotuses.<BR>—4 A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुहिणी
सरस् + -जिनी, -रुहिणी<BR>—1 a lotus-plant; भ्रमर कथं वा सरोजिनीं त्यजसि Bv. 1. 100.<BR>—2 a pond abounding in lotuses.<BR>—3 a multitude of lotuses.<BR>—4 A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरक्षः|सरोरक्ष
सरस् + -रक्षः (सरोरक्षः) the guardian of a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोरुह्
सरस् + -रुह् (सरोरुह्) <i>n.</i> a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोवरः|सरोवर
सरस् + -वरः (सरोवरः) a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
सरस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Juicy, succulent.<BR>—2 Tasty, sapid.<BR>—3 Wet; सरसनखपदन्तर्दष्टकेशप्रमोकम् Śi. 11. 54.<BR>—4 Wet with perspiration; तं वीक्ष्य वेपथुमती सरसाङ्गयष्टिः Ku. 5. 85.<BR>—5 Full of love, impassioned; त्वयि चपलेऽपि च सरसां भ्रमर कथं<BR> वा सरोजिनीं त्यजसि Bv. 1. 100 (where it means ‘full of honey’ also).<BR>—6 Charming, lovely, agreeable, beautiful; सरसवसन्ते Gīt. 1;<BR> तन्मे मनः क्षिपति यत्सरसप्रहारम् Māl. 4. 8.<BR>—7 Fresh, new, blooming; सरसकुसुमक्षामैरङ्गैरनङ्गमहाज्वरः Māl. 9. 10.<BR>—8 Thick, solid (सान्द्र); निहितसरसयावकैर्बभासे चरणतलैः<BR> कृतपद्धतिर्वधूनाम् Ki. 10. 3.<BR>—9 Expressive of poetical sentiment; see रस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसम्
सरस + .{@-सम्@} A lake, pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिकः|सरसिक
सरसि(सी)कः The Sārasa bird (crane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीकः|सरसीक
सरसि(सी)कः The Sārasa bird (crane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसी
सरसी A lake, pool; आवर्तन्ते विवर्तन्ते सरसीषु मधुव्रताः<BR> Bv. 2. 154; Ki. 12. 51.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सरसीजम्, सरसीरुहम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीजम्
सरसी + -जम्, -रुहम् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीरुहः|सरसीरुह|सरसीरुहं
सरसी + -जम्, -रुहम् + .({@-हः@}) the Sārasa bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीरुहम्
सरसी + -जम्, -रुहम् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वत्|सरस्वन्त्
सरस्वत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having water, watery; सदैव सारस्य सरस्वतामुना Rām. Ch. 2. 85.<BR>—2 Juicy, succulent.<BR>—3 Elegant.<BR>—4 Sentimental.<BR>—5 Tasty, sapid. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The ocean; कार्ष्णिः प्रत्यग्रहीदेकः सरस्वानिव निम्नगाः Śi. 19. 10.<BR>—2 A lake; आह्लादनामनि सरस्वति सारसाक्षि क्वैतादृशस्तरुरशेषजनोपकारी<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 58.<BR>—3 A male river (नद).<BR>—4 A buffalo.<BR>—5 N. of Vāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वती
सरस्वती<BR>—1 N. of the goddess of speech and learning, and represented as the wife<BR> of Brahman; परस्परविरोधिन्योरेकसंश्रयदुर्लभम् । संगतं श्रीसरस्वत्योर्भूतयेऽस्तु<BR> सदा सताम् ॥ V. 5. 24.<BR>—2 Speech, voice, words; इति देहविमुक्तये स्थितां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">Page1654-2</a>]<BR> रतिमाकाशभवा सरस्वती … अन्वकम्पयत् Ku. 4. 39, 43; R. 15. 46.<BR>—3 N. of a river (which is lost in the sands of the great desert).<BR>—4 A river in general.<BR>—5 A cow; ŚB. on MS. 10. 3. 49; Vāj. 8. 43.<BR>—6 An excellent woman.<BR>—7 N. of Durgā.<BR>—8 N. of a female divinity peculiar to the Buddhists.<BR>—9 The Soma plant.<BR>—10 The plant called ज्योतिष्मती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसर
सरसर, सरासर <i>a.</i> Moving hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरासर
सरसर, सरासर <i>a.</i> Moving hither and thither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरहस्य
सरहस्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Mystical, magical.<BR>—2 Having or attended with mystical teaching or doctrine; तयोः किल<BR> सरहस्यानि जृम्भकास्त्राण्याजन्मसिद्धानि U. 2.<BR>—3 With Upaniṣads; सकल्पं सरहस्यं च तमाचार्यं प्रचक्षते Ms. 2. 140, 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराग
सराग <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Coloured, tinged, tinted; (अकारि) सरागमस्या रसनागुणास्पदम् Ku. 5. 10.<BR>—2 Dyed with red lac; निक्षिप्तवत्यश्चरणान् सरागान् R. 16. 15.<BR>—3 Impassioned, full of love, enamoured; मुनेरपि मनोऽवश्यं सरागं<BR> कुरुतेऽङ्गना Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराव|सरावः
सराव <i>a.</i> Sounding, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरावः|सराव
सराव + .{@-वः@}<BR>—1 A lid, cover.<BR>—2 A shallow dish, saucer; cf. शराव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिः|सरि
सरिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A spring, fountain.<BR>—2 A cascade (<i>m.</i>).<BR>—3 A quarter of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिका
सरिका<BR>—1 Going, proceeding.<BR>—2 A kind of drug (हिङ्गुपत्री).<BR>—3 A woman going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्
सरित् <i>f.</i> [सृ-इति]<BR>—1 A river; अन्यसरितां शतानि हि समुद्रगाः प्रापयन्त्यब्धिम् M. 5. 19.<BR>—2 A thread, string.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सरिन्नाथः, सरित्पतिः, सरिद्वरा, सरित्सुतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1654-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिन्नाथः|सरिन्नाथ
