सर्व + -संपातः all that remains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसरः|सर्वसर
सर्व + -सरः a kind of ulcer in the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसह|सर्वसहः|सर्व्वसह|सर्व्वसहः
सर्व + -सह <i>a.</i> all-forbearing, very patient; स त्वं जगत्त्राणखलप्रहाणये<BR> निरूपितः सर्वसहो गदाभृता Bhāg. 9. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसहः|सर्वसह|सर्व्वसह|सर्व्वसहः
सर्व + -सह + .({@-हः@}) bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसहा
सर्व + -सह + .({@-हा@}, also सर्वंसहा) the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसाक्षिन्
सर्व + -साक्षिन् <i>a.</i> all-witnessing. ━(<i>m.</i>)<BR>—1 N. of the Supreme Being.<BR>—2 N. of wind.<BR>—3 of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसाधनः|सर्वसाधन
सर्व + -साधनः Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसाधारण
सर्व + -साधारण, -सामान्य <i>a.</i> common to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">Page1657-1</a>]<BR> all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसामान्य
सर्व + -साधारण, -सामान्य <i>a.</i> common to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">Page1657-1</a>]<BR> all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1656-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वसिद्धिः|सर्वसिद्धि|सर्व्वसिद्धि|सर्व्वसिद्धिः
सर्व + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> universal success. ━(<i>m.</i>) the Bilva tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वस्वम्
सर्व + -स्वम्<BR>—1 everything, the whole of oneʼs possessions; as in सर्वस्वदण्डः,<BR> सर्वस्वहरणम् ‘confiscation of the whole property’.<BR>—2 the very essence, the all-in-all of anything; सर्वस्वं तदहो महाकविगिरां<BR> कामस्य चाम्भोरुह Subhāṣ.; see Ś. 1. 24, 6. 1; Māl. 8. 6; Bv. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वस्वारः|सर्वस्वार
सर्व + -स्वारः Vedic sacrifice (एकाह) in which the sacrificer commits<BR> suicide (usually a man suffering from some incurable desease with little<BR> hope of life); आननन्द निरीक्ष्यायं पुरे तत्रात्मघातिनम् । सर्वस्वारस्य<BR> यज्वानमेनं दृष्ट्वाथ विव्यथे । N. 17. 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वहर
सर्व + -हर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 appropriating everything.<BR>—2 inheriting a personʼs whole property.<BR>—3 all-destroying (as death); मृत्युः सर्वहरश्चाहम् Bg. 10. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वहरणम्
सर्व + -हरणम्, -हारः confiscating of oneʼs entire property; सर्वहारं<BR> हरेन्नृपः Ms. 8. 399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वहारः|सर्वहार|सर्व्वहार
सर्व + -हरणम्, -हारः confiscating of oneʼs entire property; सर्वहारं<BR> हरेन्नृपः Ms. 8. 399.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वहितम्
सर्व + -हितम् black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वक|सर्व्वक|सर्व्वकः
सर्वक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 All, every.<BR>—2 Whole, entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वके|सर्व्वके
सर्वक + .{@-के@} <i>ind.</i> Everywhere, universally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंकष
सर्वंकष <i>a.</i> ‘All-destroying’, all powerful; सर्वंकषा भगवती<BR> भवितव्यतैव Māl. 1. 23; Bv. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंकषः|सर्वङ्कष|सर्व्वङ्कष
सर्वंकष + .{@-षः@} A villain, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतस्|सर्व्वतस्
सर्वतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 From every side or quarter.<BR>—2 On all sides, everywhere, all round; सर्वतः पाणिपादं तत् सर्वतोऽक्षिशिरोमुखम् ।<BR> सर्वतः श्रुतिमल्लोके सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति ॥ Bg. 13. 13.<BR>—3 Completely, entirely.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सर्वतोगामिन्, सर्वतोदिशम्, सर्वतोभद्रः, सर्वतोमुख, सर्वतोवृत्त, सर्वतःशुभा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोगामिन्
सर्वतस् + -गामिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having access everywhere; वज्रं तपोवीर्यमहत्सु कुण्ठं त्वं सर्वतोगामि<BR> च साधकं च Ku. 3. 12.<BR>—2 all-pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोदिशम्
सर्वतस् + -दिशम् <i>ind.</i> from all sides; in all directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोभद्रः|सर्वतोभद्र|सर्व्वतोभद्र|सर्व्वतोभद्रं|सर्व्वतोभद्रः
सर्वतस् + -भद्रः<BR>—1 the car of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 a bamboo.<BR>—3 a kind of verse artificially arranged; <i>e. g.</i> see देवाकानिनि कावादे<BR> वाहिकास्वस्वकाहि वा । काकारेभभरे काका निस्वभव्यव्यभस्वनि ॥ Ki. 15. 25.<BR>—4 a temple or palace having openings on four sides; (<i>n.</i> also in this sense).<BR>—5 the <i>Nimba</i> tree.<BR>—6 a kind of military array.<BR>—7 a square mystical diagram (as a sort of altar); व्याघ्रचर्मोत्तरे<BR> शुक्ले सर्वतोभद्र आसने Mb. 12. 40. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोभद्रा|सर्व्वतोभद्रा
सर्वतस् + -भद्रः + .({@-द्रा@}) a dancing girl, an actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोमुख|सर्वतोमुखः|सर्व्वतोमुख|सर्व्वतोमुखं|सर्व्वतोमुखः
सर्वतस् + -मुख <i>a.</i> of every kind, complete, unlimited; उपपन्ना हि<BR> दारेषु प्रभुता सर्वतोमुखी Ś. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोमुखः|सर्वतोमुख|सर्व्वतोमुख|सर्व्वतोमुखं|सर्व्वतोमुखः
सर्वतस् + -मुख + .({@-खः@})<BR>—1 an epithet of Śiva.<BR>—2 of Brahman; अथ सर्वस्य धातारं ते सर्वे सर्वतोमुखम् (उपतस्थिरे)<BR> Ku. 2. 3 (having faces on all sides).<BR>—3 the Supreme Being.<BR>—4 the soul.<BR>—5 a Brāhmaṇa<BR>—6 fire.<BR>—7 heaven or Svarga (of Indra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोमुखम्
सर्वतस् + -मुख + .({@-खम्@})<BR>—1 water; पिपासतः काश्चन सर्वतोमुखं तवार्पयन्तामपि काममोदनम् N. 16. 49.<BR>—2 sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतोवृत्त
सर्वतस् + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> omnipresent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतःशुभा|सर्व्वतःशुभा
सर्वतस् + -शुभा the Priyaṅgu plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्र|सर्व्वत्र
सर्वत्र <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Everywhere, in all places; पदं हि सर्वत्र गुणैर्निधीयते R. 3. 62.<BR>—2 At all times.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सर्वत्रगः, सर्वत्रगामिन्, सर्वत्रगत, सर्वत्रसत्त्वम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्रगः|सर्वत्रग|सर्व्वत्रग|सर्व्वत्रगः
सर्वत्र + -गः, -गामिन् <i>m.</i> air, wind; वायुः सर्वत्रगो महान् Bg. 9. 6.<BR>━<i>a.</i> all-pervading, omnipresent; सर्वत्रगमचिन्त्यं च कूटस्थमचलं<BR> ध्रुवम् Bg. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्रगामिन्|सर्व्वत्रगामिन्
सर्वत्र + -गः, -गामिन् <i>m.</i> air, wind; वायुः सर्वत्रगो महान् Bg. 9. 6.<BR>━<i>a.</i> all-pervading, omnipresent; सर्वत्रगमचिन्त्यं च कूटस्थमचलं<BR> ध्रुवम् Bg. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्रगत
सर्वत्र + -गत <i>a.</i> universal, perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्रसत्त्वम्
सर्वत्र + -सत्त्वम् omnipresence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वथा|सर्व्वथा
सर्वथा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In every way, by all means; सर्वथा व्यवहर्तव्यं कुतो ह्यवचनीयता U. 1. 5.<BR>—2 At all, altogether<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">Page1657-2</a>]<BR> (usually with negation).<BR>—3 Completely, entirely, utterly.<BR>—4 At all times.<BR>—5 Exceedingly, very much.<BR>—6 In whatever way; सर्वथा वर्तमानोऽपि न स भूयोऽभिजायते Bg. 13. 23.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सर्वथाविषय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वथाविषय
सर्वथा + -विषय <i>a.</i> in whatever way appearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंदमः|सर्वन्दम|सर्व्वन्दम|सर्व्वन्दमः
सर्वंदमः = सर्वदमनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वद्र्यञ्च्|सर्वद्र्यंच्
सर्वद्र्यञ्च् <i>a.</i> Honouring or worshipping all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदा|सर्व्वदा
सर्वदा <i>ind.</i> At all times, always, for ever; सर्वदा सर्वदोऽसीति<BR> मिथ्या त्वं कथ्यसे बुधैः Bhojaprabandha 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वशस्|सर्व्वशस्
सर्वशस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Wholly, entirely, completely.<BR>—2 Everywhere.<BR>—3 On all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वरी|सर्व्वरी
सर्वरी See शर्वरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वला|सर्व्वला
सर्वला, -ली<BR> An iron club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वली|सर्व्वली
सर्वला, -ली<BR> An iron club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वस्विन्
सर्वस्विन् N. of a mixed caste (the offspring of a Gopa female and a barber).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वाणी|सर्व्वाणी
सर्वाणी See शर्वाणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षपः|सर्षप
सर्षपः [Uṇ. 3. 141]<BR>—1 Mustard; खलः सर्षपमात्राणि परच्छिद्राणि पश्यति Subhāṣ.; Māl. 10. 6.<BR>—2 A small measure of weight.<BR>—3 A sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षपी
सर्षपी<BR>—1 A kind of wag-tail. —2 A kind of eruption of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्
सल् €1 P. (सलति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलम्
सलम् Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलक्षण
सलक्षण <i>a.</i> Homogeneous, similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलग्नक
सलग्नक <i>a.</i> (A loan) Secured by surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्ज|सलज्जः
सलज्ज <i>a.</i> Bashful, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्जः|सलज्ज
सलज्ज + .{@-ज्जः@} Artemisia Indica (सुरपर्ण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिङ्ग
सलिङ्ग <i>a.</i> Corresponding to (अनुरूप); तत्सलिङ्गाभिराशीर्भिरिष्टाभिरभितः<BR> स्थिताम् Mb. 7. 55. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलम्
सलिलम् [सलति-गच्छति निम्नं सल्-इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54] Water; सुभगसलिलावगाहाः Ś. 1. 3.<BR>—2 The constellation उत्तराषाढा.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सलिलार्थिन्, सलिलाशयः, सलिलेन्द्रः, सलिलेन्धनः, सलिलोद्भवः, सलिलोपप्लवः, सलिलकर्मन्, सलिलकुन्तलः, सलिलक्रिया, सलिलचरः, सलिलजम्, सलिलधरः, सलिलनिधिः, सलिलराशिः, सलिलप्रियः, सलिलरयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलार्थिन्
सलिलम् + -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> thirsty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलाशयः|सलिलाशय
सलिलम् + -आशयः a tank, reservoir of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलेन्द्रः|सलिलेन्द्र
सलिलम् + -इन्द्रः N. of Varuṇa; सलिलेन्द्रपुरान्वेषी भ्रमति स्म रसातलम्<BR> Rām. 7. 23. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलेन्धनः|सलिलेन्धन|सलिलेंधन
सलिलम् + -इन्धनः the submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलोद्भवः|सलिलोद्भव
सलिलम् + -उद्भवः a shell, conch; ततस्तौ मृशसंक्रुद्धौ प्रध्माय सलिलोद्भवौ Mb. 9. 16. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलोपप्लवः|सलिलोपप्लव
सलिलम् + -उपप्लवः inundation, deluge, flood of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलकर्मन्
सलिलम् + -कर्मन् a libation of water (offered to a deceased person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलकुन्तलः|सलिलकुन्तल
सलिलम् + -कुन्तलः moss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलक्रिया
सलिलम् + -क्रिया the funeral rite of washing a corpse.<BR>—2 = उदकक्रिया q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलचरः|सलिलचर
सलिलम् + -चरः an aquatic animal (like मकर). ˚केतनः the god<BR> of love; सलिलचरकेतनशरासनानतां चिल्लिकालताम् Dk. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलजम्
सलिलम् + -जम् a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलधरः|सलिलधर
सलिलम् + -धरः<BR>—1 a cloud.<BR>—2 a god; विनाद्य खं दिवमपि चैव सर्वशस्ततो गताः सलिलधरा यथागतम्<BR> Mb. 1. 19. 30 (com. सलिलधरा अमृतभृतो देवाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलनिधिः|सलिलनिधि
सलिलम् + -निधिः, -राशिः the ocean; कामं दामोदरीयोदरसलिलनिधौ चित्तमत्स्यश्चिरं<BR> नः Viṣṇupāda. S. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलराशिः|सलिलराशि
सलिलम् + -निधिः, -राशिः the ocean; कामं दामोदरीयोदरसलिलनिधौ चित्तमत्स्यश्चिरं<BR> नः Viṣṇupāda. S. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलप्रियः|सलिलप्रिय
सलिलम् + -प्रियः a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलरयः|सलिलरय
सलिलम् + -रयः a current, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1657-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलील|सलीलः
सलील <i>a.</i> Sportive, wanton, amorous; सलीलयातानि न भर्तुरभ्रमोः Śi. 1. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलीलम्
सलील + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Playfully.<BR>—2 Affectionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलेशम्
सलेशम् Entire; सलेशमुल्लिङ्गितशात्रवेङ्गितः Ki. 14. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलोकता
सलोकता Being in the same world, residence in the same heaven with<BR> a particular deity, (one of the four states of <i>Mukti</i>); सायुज्यं<BR> सलोकतां जयति य एवमेतत् साम वेद Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लका
सल्लका, सल्लकि-की A kind of tree, Shorea Robusta; cf. शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लकि
सल्लका, सल्लकि-की A kind of tree, Shorea Robusta; cf. शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लकी
सल्लका, सल्लकि-की A kind of tree, Shorea Robusta; cf. शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवः|सव|सवं
सवः [सू-सु-अच्]<BR>—1 Extraction of Soma juice.<BR>—2 An offering, a libation.<BR>—3 A sacrifice; राजसूयाश्वमेधाद्यैः सोऽयजद्बहुभिः सवैः Mb. 1. 94. 26.<BR>—4 The sun.<BR>—5 The moon.<BR>—6 Progeny.<BR>—7 A generator.<BR>—8 The <i>Arka</i> plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवम्
सवः + .{@-वम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 The honey of flowers.<BR>—3 Extracting the Soma juice.<BR>—4 Making libations.<BR>—6 Command, order; युक्तेन मनसा वयं देवस्य सवितुः सवे Śvet. Up. 2. 2.<BR>—6 Instigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवनम्
सवनम् [सु-सू वा-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Extracting the Soma juice or drinking it.<BR>—2 A sacrifice; अथ तं सवनाय दीक्षितः R. 8. 75; Ś. 3. 26.<BR>—3 A libation, sacrificial libation; सवनशस्तदुपधार्य सुरेशाः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 35. 15.<BR>—4 Bathing, purificatory ablution; ‘सवनं सोमनिष्पेषे जननस्नानयोरपि’<BR> इति रत्नमाला; पित्र्यं तद्रक्तपूर्णह्लदसवनमहानन्दः … Mv. 2. 48.<BR>—5 Generation, bearing or bringing forth children.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सवनकर्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवनकर्मन्
सवनम् + -कर्मन् the sacred rite of libation; सायंतने सवनकर्मणि<BR> संप्रवृत्ते Ś. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवपुष
सवपुष <i>a.</i> Embodied; सवपुषमिव चित्तरागमूहुः Ki. 10. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवयस्
सवयस् <i>a.</i> Of the same age; अमात्यपुत्रैः सवयोभिरन्वितः<BR> R. 3. 28. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A contemporary, coeval.<BR>—2 A companion of the same age. ━<i>f.</i> A womanʼs female companion or confidante.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवरः|सवर
सवरः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्ण|सवर्णः
सवर्ण <i>a.</i> [समानो वर्णो यस्य]<BR>—1 Of the same colour.<BR>—2 Of like appearance, like, resembling; दुर्वर्णभित्तिरिह सान्द्रसुधासवर्णा<BR> Śi. 4. 28; Me. 18; R. 9. 51.<BR>—3 Of the same caste or tribe; उद्वहेत द्विजो भार्यां सवर्णां लक्षणान्विताम् Ms. 3. 4.<BR>—4 Of the same kind, similar.<BR>—5 Belonging to the same class of letters, requiring the same effort (of<BR> the organs of speech) in pronunciation; तुल्यास्यप्रयत्नं सवर्णम् P. I. 1. 9.<BR>—6 Having the same denominator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्णः|सवर्ण
सवर्ण + .{@-र्णः@} the son of a Brāhmaṇa and a Kṣatriya woman, a Māhiṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्णनम्
सवर्णनम् Reduction of fractions to the same denominator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवासस्
सवासस् <i>a.</i> With clothes, clothed; सवासा जलमाप्लुत्य शुद्धो<BR> भवति मानवः Ms. 5. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्प
सविकल्प, -सविकल्पक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Optional.<BR>—2 Doubtful.<BR>—3 Recognizing a distinction as that of subject and object, or of the<BR> knower and the known (opp. निर्विकल्पक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्पक
सविकल्प, -सविकल्पक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Optional.<BR>—2 Doubtful.<BR>—3 Recognizing a distinction as that of subject and object, or of the<BR> knower and the known (opp. निर्विकल्पक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकार
सविकार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 With its products.<BR>—2 Growing fond of.<BR>—3 Undergoing decomposition (as food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकाश|सविकाशः
सविकाश(स) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fully blown or expanded.<BR>—2 Extended, extensive; युगान्तकालप्रतिसंहृतात्मनो जगन्ति यस्यां<BR> सविकासमासत Śi. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकास
सविकाश(स) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fully blown or expanded.<BR>—2 Extended, extensive; युगान्तकालप्रतिसंहृतात्मनो जगन्ति यस्यां<BR> सविकासमासत Śi. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविग्रह
सविग्रह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessing a body, embodied; सविग्रहं ग्रहमिव विगृह्यानय दुर्ग्रहम्<BR> Śiva B. 17. 31.<BR>—2 Having meaning or import.<BR>—3 Engaged in strife, quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितर्क
सवितर्क, सविमर्श <i>a.</i> Thoughtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविमर्श
सवितर्क, सविमर्श <i>a.</i> Thoughtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितर्कम्
सवितर्क, सविमर्श + .{@-र्कम्, -र्शम्@} <i>ind.</i> Thoughtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविमर्शम्
सवितर्क, सविमर्श + .{@-र्कम्, -र्शम्@} <i>ind.</i> Thoughtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सू-तृच्] Generating, producing, yielding; सवित्री<BR> कामानां यदि जगति जागर्ति भवती G. L. 23. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The sun; अनन्यदृष्टिः सवितारमैक्षत Ku. 5. 20; उदेति सविता<BR> ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमेति च K. P. 7.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 Of Indra.<BR>—4 The <i>Arka</i> tree.<BR>—5 The creator of the world.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सवितृतनयः, सवितृदैवतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृतनयः|सवितृतनय
सवितृ + -तनयः the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृदैवतम्
सवितृ + -दैवतम् N. of the asterism Hasta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृल|सवितृलः
सवितृल <i>a.</i> Solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रम्
सवित्रम् Cause of generation; P. III. 2. 184.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रिय|सवित्रियः
सवित्रिय <i>a.</i> Solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्री
सवित्री<BR>—1 A mother; तया दुहित्रा सुतरां सवित्री (चकाशे) Ku. 1. 24.<BR>—2 A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविध|सविधः
सविध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Of the same kind or sort.<BR>—2 Near, adjacent, proximate; भूयो भूयः सविधनगरीरथ्यया पर्यटन्तम् Māl. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविधम्
सविध + .{@-धम्@} Proximity, vicinity; यस्य न सविधे दयिता दवदहनस्तुहिनदीधितिस्तस्य<BR> K. P. 9; किमासेव्यं पुंसां सविधमनवद्यं द्युसरितः 10; N. 2. 47;<BR> Śi. 14. 69; Bv. 2. 182; तस्य मत्तस्य सविधे ययौ साधुरसाधुताम् Śiva B. 8. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविधम्
सविध + .{@-धम्@} <i>ind.</i> According to rule or precept; सविधं जगृहे पाणीननुरूपः<BR> स्वमायया Bhāg. 3. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनय
सविनय <i>a.</i> Modest, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनयम्
सविनय + .{@-यम्@} <i>ind.</i> Modestly, respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविभक्तिक
सविभक्तिक <i>a.</i> Having a case termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविभ्रम
सविभ्रम, -सविलास <i>a.</i><BR> Sportive, coquettish, wanton; जल्पन्ति सार्धमन्येन<BR> पश्यन्त्यन्यं सविभ्रमाः Pt. 1. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलास
सविभ्रम, -सविलास <i>a.</i><BR> Sportive, coquettish, wanton; जल्पन्ति सार्धमन्येन<BR> पश्यन्त्यन्यं सविभ्रमाः Pt. 1. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलक्षम्
सविलक्षम् <i>ind.</i> With shame or embarrassment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेष
सविशेष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessing characteristic qualities.<BR>—2 Peculiar, extraordinary.<BR>—3 Special, particular; U. 4.<BR>—4 Pre-eminent, superior, excellent.<BR>—5 Discriminative. (सविशेषम् and सविशेषतस् are used adverbially<BR> in the sense of ‘especially’, ‘particularly’, ‘exceedingly’; अनेन धर्मः<BR> सविशेषमद्य मे त्रिवर्गसारः प्रतिभाति भामिनि Ku. 5. 38; oft. in comp.;<BR> द्विरेफमाला सविशेषसङ्गा Ku. 1. 27; R. 16. 53.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषक
सविशेषक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessing peculiar or distinguishing properties.<BR>—2 Discriminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषकम्
सविशेषक + .{@-कम्@} A distinguishing characteristic, peculiar property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1658-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्तर
सविस्तर <i>a.</i> Detailed, minute, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्तरम्
सविस्तर + .{@-रम्@} <i>ind.</i> In detail, <i>in extenso</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्मय|सविस्मयः
सविस्मय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Surprised, astonished.<BR>—2 Doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्मयम्
सविस्मय + .{@-यम्@} <i>ind.</i> With surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवीमन्
सवीमन् <i>m.</i> [सू-ईमनिच् Uṇ. 4. 161] Source, birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवृत्त
सवृत्त <i>a.</i> Well-conducted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवृद्धिक
सवृद्धिक <i>a.</i> Bearing interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेधम्
सवेधम् Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेश|सवेशः
सवेश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Decorated, ornamented, dressed.<BR>—2 Near, proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेष्टन
सवेष्टन <i>a.</i> Having a turban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवैलक्ष्य
सवैलक्ष्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Unnatural, forced; affected.<BR>—2 Embarrassed; सवैलक्ष्यस्मितम् ‘with a forced smile’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्य|सव्यः
सव्य <i>a.</i> [Uṇ. 4. 109]<BR>—1 Left, left-hand; सव्ये प्राचीनआवीती निवीती कण्ठसज्जने Ms. 2. 63.<BR>—2 Southern.<BR>—3 Contrary, backward, reverse; प्रदक्षिणं च सव्यं च ग्राममध्ये<BR> च नाचरेत् Mb. 12. 278. 7.<BR>—4 Right.<BR>—5 Dry, not sprinkled with ghee (अनभिघृत); सव्यशब्दो रूक्षे भाष्यते ।<BR> सव्या वपा इत्यनभिघृततां दर्शयति ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यः|सव्य
सव्य + .{@-व्यः@} An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यम्
सव्य + .{@-व्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> The usual position of the sacred thread when it<BR> hangs down over the left shoulder; cf. अपसव्य.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सव्यापसव्य, सव्येतर, सव्यजानु, सव्यबाहु, सव्यसाचिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यापसव्य
सव्य + -अपसव्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 left and right.<BR>—2 Wrong and right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येतर
सव्य + -इतर <i>a.</i> right; सव्येतरेण स्फुरता तदक्ष्णा R. 14. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यजानु
सव्य + -जानु <i>n.</i> a mode of fighting (by using the left knee).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यबाहु
सव्य + -बाहु <i>n.</i> a mode of fighting with the left arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यसाचिन्
सव्य + -साचिन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Arjuna; निमित्तमात्रं भव सव्यसाचिन्<BR> Bg. 11. 33; (the name is thus derived in Mb.:− उभौ मे दक्षिणौ पाणी<BR> गाण्डीवस्य विकर्षणे । तेन देवमनुष्येषु सव्यसाचीति मां विदुः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यपेक्ष
सव्यपेक्ष <i>a.</i> Connected with, dependent on; स्नेहश्च निमित्तसव्यपेक्षश्चेति<BR> विप्रतिषिद्धमेतत् Māl. 1; U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यभिचरण
सव्यभिचरण <i>a.</i> Liable to inaccuracy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यभिचारः|सव्यभिचार
सव्यभिचारः One of the five main divisions of <i>Hetvābhāsa</i> (in<BR> logic), a too general middle term; for explanation, see अनैकान्तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्याज
सव्याज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Artful, pretended.<BR>—2 Plausible, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्याजम्
सव्याज + .{@-जम्@} <i>ind.</i> Artfully, under a pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यापार
सव्यापार <i>a.</i> Engaged, employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्रण
सव्रण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wounded, sore.<BR>—2 Having a fault or flaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्रीड
सव्रीड <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bashful.<BR>—2 Ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्टृ
सव्येष्टृ, सव्येष्ठः, सव्येष्ठृ, सव्येष्ठातृ <i>m.</i><BR> A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठः|सव्येष्ठ
सव्येष्टृ, सव्येष्ठः, सव्येष्ठृ, सव्येष्ठातृ <i>m.</i><BR> A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठृ
सव्येष्टृ, सव्येष्ठः, सव्येष्ठृ, सव्येष्ठातृ <i>m.</i><BR> A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्ठातृ
सव्येष्टृ, सव्येष्ठः, सव्येष्ठृ, सव्येष्ठातृ <i>m.</i><BR> A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशब्द
सशब्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Sounding.<BR>—2 Proclaimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशब्दम्
सशब्द + .{@-ब्दम्@} <i>ind.</i> With a loud noise; भग्नं सशब्दं शिरः Bh. 2. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्कः|सशल्क
सशल्कः A kind of fish; Ms. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्य
सशल्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Thorny.<BR>—2 Pierced by darts or thorns.<BR>—3 Troublesome, difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशस्य
सशस्य <i>a.</i> Having or yielding corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशस्या
सशस्य + .{@-स्या@} A variety of sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशूकः|सशूक
सशूकः A believer in the existence of God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्च्
सश्च् €1 U. (सश्चति-ते) Ved.<BR>—1 To cling or stick to, follow.<BR>—2 To serve; worship, honour.<BR>—3 To pervade; see सच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्मश्रु|सश्मश्रुः
सश्मश्रु <i>a.</i> Bearded. ━<i>f.</i> A woman with a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्रीक
सश्रीक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Prosperous, fortunate.<BR>—2 Lovely, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्व्
सश्व् To go; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्
सस् €2 P. (सस्ति) To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्त्व
ससत्त्व <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of vitality, energy, vigour, courage &c. —2 Pregnant, big<BR> with child; नृपः ससत्त्वां महिषीममन्यत R. 3. 9.<BR>—2 Full of animals or creatures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्त्वा
ससत्त्व + .{@-त्त्वा@} A pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंदेह|ससन्देह|ससंदेहः
ससंदेह <i>a.</i> Doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंदेहः|ससन्देह|ससंदेह
ससंदेह + .{@-हः@} N. of a figure of speech; see संदेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससनम्
ससनम् Immolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंवित्क
ससंवित्क <i>a.</i> Sensible, having consciousness; ससंवित्कस्य<BR> कामेषु तथापि न रतिः क्षमा Bu. C. 4. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंहार
ससंहार <i>a.</i> Having the means of restraint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंध्य
ससंध्य <i>a.</i> Evening, vespertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंभ्रम|ससम्भ्रम
ससंभ्रम <i>a.</i> Flurried, agitated, hurried, confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंभ्रमम्|ससम्भ्रमम्
ससंभ्रम + .{@-मम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Hurriedly, hastily.<BR>—2 In fear or confusion, in great perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससाध्वस
ससाध्वस <i>a.</i> Alarmed, frightened, timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्ज्
सस्ज् See सञ्ज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्पृह
सस्पृह <i>a.</i> Desirous, longing, eager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्पृहम्
सस्पृह + .{@-हम्@} <i>ind.</i> Eagerly, wistfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्मित|सस्मितः
सस्मित <i>a.</i> Smiling, attended with a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यम्
सस्यम् [सस्-यत् Uṇ. 4. 119]<BR>—1 Corn, grain; (एतानि) सस्यैः पूर्णे जठरपिठरे प्राणिनां संभवन्ति<BR> Pt. 5. 97; see शस्य also.<BR>—2 Fruit or produce of any plant.<BR>—3 A weapon.<BR>—4 A good quality, merit.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सस्याद्, सस्यभक्षक, सस्येष्टिः, सस्यपालः, सस्यप्रद, सस्यमञ्जरी, सस्यमारिन्, सस्यमालिन्, सस्यवेदः, सस्यशूकम्, सस्यसंवरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्याद्
सस्यम् + -अद्, -भक्षक <i>a.</i> granivorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यभक्षक
सस्यम् + -अद्, -भक्षक <i>a.</i> granivorous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्येष्टिः|सस्येष्टि
सस्यम् + -इष्टिः <i>f.</i> a sacrifice made on the ripening of new grain; Ms. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यपालः|सस्यपाल
सस्यम् + -पालः a field-guarder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यप्रद
सस्यम् + -प्रद <i>a.</i> fertile; क्षेम्यां सस्यप्रदां नित्यं पशुवृद्धिकरीमपि Ms. 7. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यमञ्जरी
सस्यम् + -मञ्जरी an ear of corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यमारिन्
सस्यम् + -मारिन् <i>a.</i> destructive of grain. ━(<i>m.</i>) a kind of rat or mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यमालिन्
सस्यम् + -मालिन् <i>a.</i> abounding in corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यवेदः|सस्यवेद
सस्यम् + -वेदः the science of agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यशूकम्
सस्यम् + -शूकम् an awn of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यसंवरः|सस्यसंवर
सस्यम् + -संवरः the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1659-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
सस्यक <i>a.</i> Possessed of good qualities, meritorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यकः|सस्यक
सस्यक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A sword.<BR>—2 A weapon.<BR>—3 A kind of precious stone.<BR>—4 The inner part of a cocoa-nut; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेद
सस्वेद <i>a.</i> Covered over or moist with sweat, perspired; सस्वेदरोमाञ्चितकम्पिताङ्गी<BR> जाता प्रियस्पर्शसुखेन वत्सा U. 3. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेदा
सस्वेद + .{@-दा@} A girl recently deflowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
सह् I. €4 P. (सह्यति)<BR>—1 To satisfy.<BR>—2 To be pleased.<BR>—3 To endure, bear. ━II. €1 Ā. (सहते, epic. Paras. also; सोढ;<BR> the स् of सह् is changed to ष् after prepositions ending in<BR> इ, as नि, परि, वि, except when ह् is changed for ढ्)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To bear, endure, suffer, put up with; खलोल्लापाः सोढाः Bh. 3. 6;<BR> पदं सहेत भ्रमरस्य पेलवं शिरीषपुष्पं न पुनः पतत्रिणः<BR> Ku. 5. 4; so दुःखम्, संतापम्, क्लेशम् &c.; R. 12. 63, 11. 52; Bk. 17. 59.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To tolerate, allow; प्रकृतिः खलु सा महीयसः सहते नान्यसमुन्नतिं<BR> यया Ki. 2. 21; Me. 107; R. 14. 63.<BR>—2 To forgive, forbear; वारंवारं मयैतस्यापराधः सोढः H. 3; प्रियः<BR> प्रियायार्हसि देव सोढुम् Bg. 11. 44.<BR>—3 To wait, be patient; द्वित्राण्यहान्यर्हसि सोढुमर्हन् R. 5. 25, 15. 45.<BR>—4 To bear, support, bear up; क इदानीं सहकारमन्तरेण पल्लवितामतिमुक्तलतां<BR> सहेत Ś. 3.<BR>—5 To conquer, defeat, oppose, be able to resist.<BR>—6 To suppress, stop.<BR>—7 To be able (with inf.). ━<i>Caus.</i> (साहयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to bear or suffer.<BR>—2 To make bearable or supportable; गुर्वपि विरहदुःखमाशाबन्धः साहयति<BR> Ś. 4. 16. ━<i>Desid.</i> (सिसहिषते) To wish to bear &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह <i>a.</i> [सहते सह्-अच्]<BR>—1 Bearing, enduring, suffering.<BR>—2 Patient.<BR>—3 Able; see असह; चरतस्तपस्तव वनेषु सहा न वयं निरूपयितुमस्य<BR> गतिम् Ki. 6. 36.<BR>—4 Overpowering, vanquishing.<BR>—5 Defying, equal to.<BR>—6 Exerting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहः|सह|सहं
सह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 The month मार्गशीर्ष.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहः|सह|सहं
सह + .{@-हः, -हम्@} Power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहम्
सह + .{@-हः, -हम्@} Power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहम्
सह + .{@-हम्@} A kind of salt; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहक
सहक <i>a.</i> Patient, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन|सहनं|सहनः
सहन <i>a.</i> Bearing, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहनम्
सहन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Bearing, enduring.<BR>—2 Patience, forbearance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सहनशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहनशील
सहन + -शील <i>a.</i> patient, forgiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित्रम्
सहित्रम् Patience, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णु|सहिष्णुः
सहिष्णु <i>a.</i> [सह्-इष्णुच्]<BR>—1 Able to bear or endure, capable of enduring; राविकिरणसहिष्णु क्लेशलेशैरभिन्नम्<BR> Ś. 2. 4; उत्पतिष्णू सहिष्णू च चेरतुः खरदूषणौ Bk. 5. 1.<BR>—2 Patient, resigned, forbearing; सुकरस्तरुवत्सहिष्णुना रिपुरुन्मूलयितुं<BR> महानपि Ki. 2. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुता
सहिष्णुता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Power to bear or support.<BR>—2 Patience, resignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुत्वम्
सहिष्णुता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Power to bear or support.<BR>—2 Patience, resignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With, together with, along with, accompanied by (with instr.); शशिना<BR> सह याति कौमुदी सह मेघेन तडित् प्रलीयते Ku. 4. 33.<BR>—2 Together, simultaneously, at the same time; अस्तोदयौ सहैवासौ कुरुते<BR> नृपतिर्द्विषाम् Subhāṣ. (The following senses are given of this word:− साकल्य,<BR> सादृश्य, यौगपद्य, विद्यमानत्व, समृद्धि, संबन्ध and सामर्थ्य.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सहाध्ययनम्, सहाध्यायिन्, सहापवाद, सहार्थ, सहार्ध, सहालापः, सहासनम्, सहासिका, सहोक्तिः, सहोटजः, सहोत्थायिन्, सहोदरः, सहोपमा, सहोढः, सहोढजः, सहैकासनम्, सहकर्तृ, सहकारः, सहकारिन्, सहकृत्, सहकृत्वन्, सहकृत, सहक्रिया, सहखट्वासनम्, सहगमनम्, सहचर, सहचरित, सहचारः, सहचारिन्, सहज, सहजात, सहजित्, सहदार, सहदेवः, सहधर्मः, सहपथिन्, सहपांशुक्रीडिन्, सहपांशुकिलः,^1 सहभावः, सहभाविन्, सहभू, सहभोजनम्, सहमनस्, सहमरणम्, सहमृता, सहयुध्वन्, सहरक्षस्, सहवसतिः, सहवासः, सहवासिन्, सहवीर्यम्, सहसंसर्गः, सहसेविन्, सहस्थः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाध्ययनम्
सह + -अध्ययनम्<BR>—1 studying together; U. 2.<BR>—2 fellow-studentship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाध्यायिन्
सह + -अध्यायिन् <i>m.</i> a fellow-student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहापवाद
सह + -अपवाद <i>a.</i> disagreeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्थ|सहार्थः
सह + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the same object.<BR>—2 synonymous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्थः|सहार्थ
सह + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@}) the same or common object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्ध
सह + -अर्ध <i>a.</i> together with a half.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहालापः|सहालाप
सह + -आलापः conversation with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहासनम्
सह + -आसनम् sitting on the same seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहासिका
सह + -आसिका company, sitting together; समुद्रः सहासिकां यां सुमतिः<BR> प्रतीच्छति Rām. Ch. 2. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोक्तिः|सहोक्ति
सह + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> a figure of speech in Rhetoric; सा सहोक्तिः सहार्थस्य<BR> वलादेकं द्विवाचकम् K. P. 10; <i>e. g.</i> पपात भूमौ सह सैनिकाश्रुभिः R. 3. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोटजः|सहोटज
सह + -उटजः a hut made of leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोत्थायिन्
सह + -उत्थायिन् <i>a.</i> rising or conspiring together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोदरः|सहोदर
सह + -उदरः a uterine brother, brother of whole blood; जनन्यां<BR> संस्थितायां तु समं सर्वे सहोदराः Ms. 9. 92; सहोदरा कुङ्कुमकेसराणां<BR> भवन्ति नूनं कविताविलासाः Vikr. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोपमा
सह + -उपमा a kind of Upamā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढः|सहोढ
सह + -ऊढः, -ऊढजः the son of a woman pregnant at marriage; (one of<BR> the 12 kinds of sons recognized in old Hindu law); या गर्भिणी संस्क्रियते<BR> ज्ञाताज्ञातापि वा सती । वोढुः स गर्भो भवति सहोढ इति चोच्यते ॥ Ms. 9. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढजः|सहोढज
सह + -ऊढः, -ऊढजः the son of a woman pregnant at marriage; (one of<BR> the 12 kinds of sons recognized in old Hindu law); या गर्भिणी संस्क्रियते<BR> ज्ञाताज्ञातापि वा सती । वोढुः स गर्भो भवति सहोढ इति चोच्यते ॥ Ms. 9. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहैकासनम्
सह + -एकासनम् see सहासनम्; Y. 2. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकर्तृ
सह + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> a co-worker, assistant; तस्य कर्मानुरूपेण देयोंऽशः<BR> सहकर्तृभिः Ms. 8. 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारः|सहकार
सह + -कारः<BR>—1 co-operation.<BR>—2 a mango tree; क इदानीं सहकारमन्तरेण पल्लवितामतिमुक्तलतां<BR> सहेत Ś. 3. ˚भञ्जिका a kind of game.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकारिन्
सह + -कारिन्, -कृत्, -कृत्वन् <i>a.</i> co-operating. ━(<i>m.</i>) a coadjutor,<BR> associate, colleague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्
सह + -कारिन्, -कृत्, -कृत्वन् <i>a.</i> co-operating. ━(<i>m.</i>) a coadjutor,<BR> associate, colleague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत्वन्
सह + -कारिन्, -कृत्, -कृत्वन् <i>a.</i> co-operating. ━(<i>m.</i>) a coadjutor,<BR> associate, colleague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकृत
सह + -कृत <i>a.</i> co-operated with, assisted or aided by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहक्रिया
सह + -क्रिया simultaneous performance; स हि न्यायः संभूयकारिणां<BR> सहक्रियेति सर्वत्रैव ŚB. on MS. 11. 1. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहखट्वासनम्
सह + -खट्वासनम् sitting together on a bed; Ms. 8. 357; see सहैकासनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहगमनम्
सह + -गमनम्<BR>—1 accompanying.<BR>—2 a womanʼs burning herself with her deceased husbandʼs body, self-immolation of a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचर|सहचरः
सह + -चर <i>a.</i> accompanying, going or living with; यानि प्रियासहचरश्चिरमध्यवात्सम् U. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरः|सहचर
सह + -चर + .({@-रः@})<BR>—1 a companion, friend, associate; श्मशानेष्वाक्रीडा स्मरहर पिशाचाः<BR> सहचराः Śivamahimna 24.<BR>—2 a follower, servant.<BR>—3 a husband.<BR>—4 a surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरी
सह + -चर + .({@-री@} <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 a female companion.<BR>—2 a wife, mate; प्रेक्ष्य स्थितां सहचरीं व्यवधाय देहम् R. 9. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचरित
सह + -चरित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 accompanying, attending, associating with.<BR>—2 Congruent, homogeneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचारः|सहचार
सह + -चारः<BR>—1 accompaniment.<BR>—2 agreement, harmony.<BR>—3 (in logic) the invariable accompaniment of the <i>hetu</i> (middle term)<BR> by the <i>sādhya</i> (major term).<BR>—4 right course (opp. व्यभिचार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहचारिन्
सह + -चारिन् see सहचर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहज|सहजः
सह + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 inborn, natural, innate; सहजं कर्म कौन्तेय सदोषमपि न त्यजेत्<BR> Bg. 18. 48; सहजामप्यपहाय धीरताम् R. 8. 43.<BR>—2 hereditar; सहजं किल यद्विनिन्दितं न खलु तत्कर्म विवर्जनीयम् Ś. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजः|सहज
सह + -ज + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 a brother of whole blood; तृतीयो मे नप्ता रजनिचरनाथस्य सहजः Mv. 4. 7.<BR>—2 the natural state or disposition. ˚अरिः a natural enemy. ˚उदासीनः<BR> a born neutral. ˚मित्रम् a natural friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजात|सहजातः
सह + -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 natural; see सहज.<BR>—2 born together, twin-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहजित्
सह + -जित् <i>a.</i> victorious at once; स्वर्णेता सहजिद् बभ्रुरिति राजाभिधीयते<BR> Mb. 3. 185. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहदार
सह + -दार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 with a wife.<BR>—2 married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहदेवः|सहदेव
सह + -देवः N. of the youngest of the five Pāṇḍavas; the twin brother<BR> of Nakula, born of Mādrī by the gods Aśvins. He is regarded as the type of manly<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">Page1661-1</a>]<BR> beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1660-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहधर्मः|सहधर्म|सहधर्म्म
सह + -धर्मः same duties. ˚चारिन् <i>m.</i> a husband. ˚चारिणी<BR>—1 a lawful wife, one legally married (also सहधर्मिणी in this sense).<BR>—2 a fellow-worker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपथिन्
सह + -पथिन् <i>m.</i>, {@-पन्थाः@} <i>m., f.</i><BR> a fellow-traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपांशुक्रीडिन्
सह + -पांशुक्रीडिन्, -पांशुकिलः^1 <i>m.</i> a friend from the earliest childhood.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहपांशुकिलः|सहपांशुकिल
सह + -पांशुक्रीडिन्, -पांशुकिलः^1 <i>m.</i> a friend from the earliest childhood.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभावः|सहभाव
सह + -भावः<BR>—1 companionship.<BR>—2 concomitance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभाविन्
सह + -भाविन् <i>m.</i> a friend, partisan, follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभू
सह + -भू <i>a.</i> natural, innate; औत्सुक्येन कृतत्वरा सहभुवा व्यावर्तमाना<BR> ह्रिया Ratn. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहभोजनम्
सह + -भोजनम् eating in company with friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमनस्
सह + -मनस् <i>a.</i> with intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमरणम्
सह + -मरणम् see सहगमन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहमृता
सह + -मृता a woman who has burnt herself with her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहयुध्वन्
सह + -युध्वन् <i>m.</i> a brother in arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरक्षस्
सह + -रक्षस् <i>m.</i> one of the three kinds of sacrificial fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहवसतिः|सहवसति
सह + -वसतिः, -वासः dwelling together; सहवसतिमुपेत्य यैः प्रियायाः<BR> कृत इव मुग्धविलोकितोपदेशः Ś. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहवासः|सहवास
सह + -वसतिः, -वासः dwelling together; सहवसतिमुपेत्य यैः प्रियायाः<BR> कृत इव मुग्धविलोकितोपदेशः Ś. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहवासिन्
सह + -वासिन् <i>m.</i> a fellow-lodger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहवीर्यम्
सह + -वीर्यम् fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसंसर्गः|सहसंसर्ग
सह + -संसर्गः carnal contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसेविन्
सह + -सेविन् <i>a.</i> having intercourse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्थः|सहस्थ
सह + -स्थः a companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहता
सहता, -त्वम्<BR> Union, association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहत्वम्
सहता, -त्वम्<BR> Union, association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहकार|सहकारः
सहकार <i>a.</i> Having the sound ह; सहकारवृते समये सहका<BR> रहणस्य के न सस्मार पदम् । सहकारमुपरि कान्तैः सह का रमणी पुरः<BR> सकलवर्णमपि ॥ Nalod. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्ष|सहर्षः
सहर्ष <i>a.</i> Glad, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्षम्
सहर्ष + .{@-षम्@} <i>ind.</i> Gladly, delightedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्
सहस् <i>a.</i> Powerful, mighty; भीष्मो हि देवः सहसः सहीयान्<BR> Bhāg. 11. 23. 48. ━<i>m.</i> [सह्-असि]<BR>—1 The month called Mārgaśīrṣa; Śi. 6. 57, 16. 47; सहसि तत्र<BR> समृद्धिमुपागते Rām. Ch. 4. 83; Bhāg. 12. 11. 41.<BR>—2 The winter season. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 Power, might, strength.<BR>—2 Force, violence.<BR>—3 Victory, conquering.<BR>—4 Lustre, brightness.<BR>—5 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसा
सहसा <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With force, forcibly.<BR>—2 Rashly, precipitately, inconsiderately; सहसा विदधीत न क्रियामविवेकः<BR> परमापदां पदम् Ki. 2. 30.<BR>—3 Suddenly, all at once; मातङ्गनक्रैः सहसोत्पतद्भिः R. 13. 11.<BR>—4 With a smile, smiling.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सहसादृष्टः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसादृष्टः|सहसादृष्ट
सहसा + -दृष्टः an adopted son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसान|सहसानः
सहसान <i>a.</i> [सह्-असानच् Uṇ. 2. 84]<BR>—1 Patient.<BR>—2 Overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसानः|सहसान
सहसान + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A peacock.<BR>—2 A sacrifice, an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्यः|सहस्य
सहस्यः The month called Pauṣa; सहस्यरात्रीरुदवासतत्परा<BR> Ku. 5. 26; इति विभाति विभावितशीतले सहसहस्यसहस्यथ मैथिली Rām. Ch. 4. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रम्
सहस्रम् [समानं हसति हस्-र Tv.]<BR>—1 A thousand.<BR>—2 A large number.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सहस्रांशु, सहस्रार्चिस्, सहस्रकर, सहस्रकिरण, सहस्रदीधिति, सहस्रधामन्, सहस्रपाद, सहस्रमरीचि, सहस्ररश्मि, सहस्राक्ष, सहस्रारः, सहस्रारम्, सहस्राननः, सहस्राधिपतिः, सहस्रावरः, सहस्रकाण्डा, सहस्रकृत्वस्, सहस्रगु, सहस्रगुण, सहस्रणी, सहस्रघातिन्, सहस्रद, सहस्रदंष्ट्रः, सहस्रदृश्, सहस्रनयन, सहस्रनेत्र, सहस्रलोचनः,^1 सहस्रदोस्, सहस्रधारः, सहस्रपत्रम्, सहस्रपाद्, सहस्रपादः, सहस्रबाहुः, सहस्रभक्तम्, सहस्रभिद्, सहस्रभुजः, सहस्रमौलिः, सहस्रभुजा, सहस्रमूर्ति, सहस्रमूर्धन्, सहस्ररुच्, सहस्ररोमन्, सहस्रवदनः, सहस्रवीर्या, सहस्रवेधम्, सहस्रवेधिन्, सहस्रशिखरः, सहस्रशिरस्, सहस्रशीर्षन्, सहस्रशीर्ष, सहस्रश्रवणः, सहस्रहर्यश्वः, सहस्रहस्तः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रांशु|सहस्रांशुः
सहस्रम् + -अंशु, -अर्चिस्, -कर, -किरण, -दीधिति, -धामन्, -पाद, -मरीचि, -रश्मि<BR> <i>m.</i> the sun; तदण्डमभवद्धैमं सहस्रांशुसमप्रभम् Ms. 1. 9;<BR> तं चेत् सहस्राकिरणो धुरि नाकरिष्यत् Ś. 7. 4; पुनः सहस्रार्चिषि<BR> संनिधत्ते R. 13. 44; धाम्नातिशाययति धाम सहस्रधाम्नः Mu. 3. 17;<BR> सहस्ररश्मेरिव यस्य दर्शनम् Śi. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

