सहस्रबाहुः|सहस्रबाहु
सहस्रम् + -बाहुः<BR>—1 an epithet of king Kārtavīrya q. v.<BR>—2 of the demon Bāṇa.<BR>—3 of Śiva (or of Viṣṇu according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रभक्तम्
सहस्रम् + -भक्तम् a particular festival at which thousands are treated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रभिद्
सहस्रम् + -भिद् <i>m.</i> musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रभुजः|सहस्रभुज
सहस्रम् + -भुजः, -मौलिः <i>m.</i> epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रमौलिः|सहस्रमौलि
सहस्रम् + -भुजः, -मौलिः <i>m.</i> epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रभुजा
सहस्रम् + -भुजा <i>f.</i> N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रमूर्ति
सहस्रम् + -मूर्ति <i>a.</i> appearing in a thousand forms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रमूर्धन्
सहस्रम् + -मूर्धन् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्ररुच्
सहस्रम् + -रुच् the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्ररोमन्
सहस्रम् + -रोमन् <i>n.</i> a blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवदनः|सहस्रवदन
सहस्रम् + -वदनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवीर्या|सहस्रवीर्य्या
सहस्रम् + -वीर्या Dūrvā grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवेधम्
सहस्रम् + -वेधम्<BR>—1 sorrel<BR>—2 a kind of sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रवेधिन्
सहस्रम् + -वेधिन् <i>m.</i> musk. ━(<i>n.</i>) Asa-foetida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशिखरः|सहस्रशिखर
सहस्रम् + -शिखरः an epithet of the Vindhya mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशिरस्
सहस्रम् + -शिरस्, -शीर्षन्, -शीर्ष <i>a.</i> thousand-headed (epithet of Viṣṇu);<BR> सहस्रशीर्षा पुरुषः Rv. 10. 90. 1; सहस्रशीर्षापि ततो गरुत्मता Bhāg. 4. 1 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशीर्षन्
सहस्रम् + -शिरस्, -शीर्षन्, -शीर्ष <i>a.</i> thousand-headed (epithet of Viṣṇu);<BR> सहस्रशीर्षा पुरुषः Rv. 10. 90. 1; सहस्रशीर्षापि ततो गरुत्मता Bhāg. 4. 1 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशीर्ष
सहस्रम् + -शिरस्, -शीर्षन्, -शीर्ष <i>a.</i> thousand-headed (epithet of Viṣṇu);<BR> सहस्रशीर्षा पुरुषः Rv. 10. 90. 1; सहस्रशीर्षापि ततो गरुत्मता Bhāg. 4. 1 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रश्रवणः|सहस्रश्रवण
सहस्रम् + -श्रवणः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रहर्यश्वः|सहस्रहर्यश्व
सहस्रम् + -हर्यश्वः the car of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रहस्तः|सहस्रहस्त
सहस्रम् + -हस्तः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रक
सहस्रक <i>a.</i> Amounting to a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रतय
सहस्रतय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Thousand-fold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रतयम्
सहस्रतय + .{@-यम्@} A thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधा
सहस्रधा <i>ind.</i> In a thousand parts, a thousand-fold; दीर्ये<BR> किं न सहस्रधाहमथवा रामेण किं दुष्करम् U. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशस्
सहस्रशस् <i>ind.</i> By thousands; तत्र मल्लाः समापेतुर्दिग्भ्यो<BR> राजन् सहस्रशः Mb. 4. 13. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रिन्
सहस्रिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of a thousand; इच्छति शती सहस्रं सहस्री लक्षमीहते Pt. 5. 82.<BR>—2 Consisting of thousands.<BR>—3 Amounting to a thousand (as a fine); क्षत्रियं तु सहस्रिणम् Ms. 8. 376.<BR>━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A body of a thousand men &c.<BR>—2 The commander of a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्वत्|सहस्वन्त्
सहस्वत् <i>a.</i> Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहा
सहा<BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 The aloe-plant or flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायः|सहाय
सहायः [सह् एति इ-अच्]<BR>—1 A friend, companion; सहायसाध्यं राजत्वं चक्रमेकं न वर्तते<BR> Kau. A. 1. 7; सहायसाध्याः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">Page1662-1</a>]<BR> प्रदिशन्ति सिद्धयः Ki. 14. 44; Ku. 3. 21; Me. 11.<BR>—2 A follower, an adherent.<BR>—3 An ally.<BR>—4 A helper, patron.<BR>—5 The ruddy goose.<BR>—6 A kind of perfume.<BR>—7 N. of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सहायार्थम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1661-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायार्थम्
सहायः + -अर्थम् <i>ind.</i> for the sake of company; नामुत्र हि सहायार्थं<BR> पिता माता च तिष्ठतः Ms. 4. 239.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायता
सहायता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 A number of companions.<BR>—2 Companionship, union, friendship.<BR>—3 Help, assistance; कुसुमास्तरणे सहायतां बहुशः सौम्य गतस्त्वमावयोः<BR> Ku. 4. 35; R. 9. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायत्वम्
सहायता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 A number of companions.<BR>—2 Companionship, union, friendship.<BR>—3 Help, assistance; कुसुमास्तरणे सहायतां बहुशः सौम्य गतस्त्वमावयोः<BR> Ku. 4. 35; R. 9. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायनम्
सहायनम् Fellowship, company; नाना चित्राः कथाश्चान्या विश्वामित्रसहायने<BR> Rām. 1. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायवत्|सहायवन्त्
सहायवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a friend.<BR>—2 Befriended, assisted; नरस्त्वं पूर्वदेहे वै नारायणसहायवान् Mb. 3. 40. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहारः|सहार
सहारः<BR>—1 The mango tree.<BR>—2 Universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहार्द|सहार्द्द|सहार्द्दः
सहार्द <i>a.</i> Affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहाव
सहाव <i>a.</i> Employing amorous gestures, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
सहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Accompanied or attended by, together with, united or associated with;<BR> पवनाग्निसमागमो ह्ययं सहितं ब्रह्म यदस्त्रतेजसा R. 8. 4.<BR>—2 Borne, endured.<BR>—3 (In astr.) Being in conjunction with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितम्
सहित + .{@-तम्@} A bow weighing 300 Palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितम्
सहित + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i> Together with, with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितृ
सहितृ <i>a.</i> Enduring, patient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिम
सहिम <i>a.</i> Icy cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुरिः|सहुरि
सहुरिः [सह्-उरिन् Uṇ. 2. 70] The sun. ━<i>f.</i> The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृदय|सहृदयः
सहृदय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Good-hearted, kind, compassionate.<BR>—2 Sincere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृदयः|सहृदय
सहृदय + .{@-यः@}<BR>—1 A learned man.<BR>—2 An appreciator (of merits &c.), a man of taste, a man of critical faculty;<BR> इत्युपदेशं कवेः सहृदयस्य च करोति K. P. 1; परिष्कुर्वन्त्यन्ये<BR> सहृदयधुरीणाः कतिपये R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृल्लेख|सहृल्लेखं
सहृल्लेख <i>a.</i> Questionable, doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृल्लेखम्
सहृल्लेख + .{@-खम्@} Questionable food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृष्टकम्
सहृष्टकम् <i>ind.</i> With a thrill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेतु
सहेतु <i>a.</i> Well-founded, reasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेल
सहेल <i>a.</i> Sportive, playful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढः|सहोढ
सहोढः A thief caught with the stolen property in his possession;<BR> (चौरं) सहोढं सोपकरणं घातयेदविचारयन् Ms. 9. 270.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर <i>a.</i> Good, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोरः|सहोर
सहोर + .{@-रः@} A saint, sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bearable, supportable, endurable; अपि सह्या ते शिरोवेदना Mu. 5; M. 3. 4.<BR>—2 To be borne or endured; कथं तूष्णीं सह्यो निरवधिरिदानीं तु विरहः U. 3. 44.<BR>—3 Able to bear.<BR>—4 Adequate or equal to.<BR>—5 Sweet, agreeable.<BR>—6 Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्यः|सह्य|सह्यं
सह्य + .{@-ह्यः@} N. of one of the seven principal mountain ranges in India,<BR> a part of the western Ghāts at some distance from the sea;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">Page1662-2</a>]<BR> रामास्त्रोत्सारितोऽप्यासीत् सह्यलग्न इवार्णवः R. 4. 53, 52; Ki. 18. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्यम्
सह्य + .{@-ह्यम्@}<BR>—1 Health, convalescence.<BR>—2 Assistance.<BR>—3 Fitness, adequacy.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सह्यात्मजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्यात्मजा
सह्य + -आत्मजा N. of the river Kāverī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा<BR>—1 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 Of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयात्रिकः|सांयात्रिक
सांयात्रिकः A sea-trader, a merchant trading by sea (पोतवणिक्);<BR> यथा समुद्रेऽपि च पोतभङ्गे सांयात्रिको वाञ्छति तर्तुमेव Pt. 1. 316;<BR> सांयात्रिकाननेकांश्च कृतद्वीपान्तराश्रयान् Śiva B. 30. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयात्रिकम्
सांयात्रिकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Any vehicle.<BR>—2 The morning dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीन|सांयुगीनः
सांयुगीन <i>a.</i> [संयुगे साधुः ख] Warlike, skilled in war;<BR> भवांश्च सांयुगीनः सहायो नः V. 5; R. 11. 30; also सांयुग in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीनः|सांयुगीन
सांयुगीन + .{@-नः@} A great warrior, a soldier skilled in war; संयुगे सांयुगीनं<BR> तमुद्यतं प्रसहेत कः Ku. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांराविणम्
सांराविणम् [cf. P. III. 3. 44, V. 4. 15] A general or loud shout,<BR> tumultuous uproar; उत्तालाः कटपूतनाप्रभृतयः सांराविणं कुर्वते<BR> Māl. 5. 11; सांराविणं न कर्तव्यं यावन्नायाति दर्शनम् Bk. 7. 43; N. 19. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सर|सांवत्सरः
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Annual, yearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरी
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Annual, yearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरिक|सांवत्सरिकः
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Annual, yearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरिकी
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) <i>a.</i><BR> Annual, yearly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरः|सांवत्सर
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) + .{@-रः, -रकः, -रिकः@}<BR>—1 An astrologer.<BR>—2 An almanac-maker.<BR>—3 A lunar month.<BR>—4 Black rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्स्रकः
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) + .{@-रः, -रकः, -रिकः@}<BR>—1 An astrologer.<BR>—2 An almanac-maker.<BR>—3 A lunar month.<BR>—4 Black rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सरिकः|सांवत्सरिक
सांवत्सर (-री <i>f.</i>), सांवत्सरिक (-की <i>f.</i>) + .{@-रः, -रकः, -रिकः@}<BR>—1 An astrologer.<BR>—2 An almanac-maker.<BR>—3 A lunar month.<BR>—4 Black rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवर्तक|सांवर्तकः
सांवर्तक <i>a.</i> Relating to or appearing at the dissolution of<BR> the universe; लोकानामभवे युक्तं सांवर्तकमिवानलम् Rām. 3. 65. 1;<BR> Bhāg. 10. 25. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवर्तकः|सांवर्तक
सांवर्तक + .{@-कः@} the fire at the प्रलयकाल; दह्यमानाः प्रजाः सर्वाः सांवर्तकममंसत<BR> Bhāg. 1. 7. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिक|सांवादिकः
सांवादिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Colloquial.<BR>—2 Controversial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिकः|सांवादिक
सांवादिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A disputant.<BR>—2 A logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवास्यकम्
सांवास्यकम् Dwelling together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांविज्ञायिक
सांविज्ञायिक <i>a.</i> Conventional (as opposed to यौगिक); किं<BR> सांविज्ञायिकः स्विष्टकृच्छब्दः उत स्विष्टं करोतीति एतेन गुणेन प्रवृत्त<BR> इति गौणो न रूढः ŚB. on MS. 10. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवित्तिक
सांवित्तिक <i>a.</i> Subjective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवृत्तिक
सांवृत्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Illusory, phenomenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिक|सांशयिकः
सांशयिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Doubtful.<BR>—2 Uncertain, irresolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिकम्
सांशयिक + .{@-कम्@} A doubtful or dangerous deed; न हि सांशयिकं कुर्यादित्युवाच<BR> बृहस्पतिः Pt. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसर्गिक
सांसर्गिक <i>a.</i> Resulting from contact, contagious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसारिक
सांसारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Worldly, mundane; सांसारिकेषु च सुखेषु वयं रसज्ञाः U. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिक
सांसिद्धिक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Natural, existing naturally, innate, inherent; एवं सांसिद्धिके लोके<BR> किमर्थमनुशोचसि Mb. 11. 2. 7.<BR>—2 Effected naturally, spontaneous; परस्परभयादेके पापाः पापं न<BR> कुर्वते । एवं सांसिद्धिके लोके सर्वं दण्डे प्रतिष्ठितम् ॥ Mb. 12. 15. 6.<BR>—3 Absolute.<BR>—4 Effected by supernatural means.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सांसिद्धिकद्रवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिकद्रवः|सांसिद्धिकद्रव
सांसिद्धिक + -द्रवः natural fluidity (opp. नैमित्तिक ‘generated’) (belonging<BR> to water only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धव्यम्
सांसिद्धव्यम् Perfect attainment; सांसिद्धपमक्ष्णोस्तव दर्शनान्नः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 21. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1662-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसृष्टिक
सांसृष्टिक <i>a.</i> Immediately connected, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्कारिक
सांस्कारिक <i>a.</i> Relating to rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्थानिकः|सांस्थानिक
सांस्थानिकः A fellow-countryman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्राविणम्
सांस्राविणम् A general flow or stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांहत्यम्
सांहत्यम् Connection, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांहननिक
सांहननिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Bodily, corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम् A vegetable, herb; cf. शाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 With, together with (with instr.); यान्ती गुरुजनैः साकं स्मयमानाननाम्बुजा<BR> Bv. 2. 132, 1. 41; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>—2 At the same time, simultaneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकमेधीयन्यायः
साकमेधीयन्यायः The rule according to which an ectype (विकृति)<BR> sets aside a detail of its archetype (प्रकृतिधर्म) if it conflicts<BR> with some detail (धर्म) which is expressly enjoined with reference<BR> to it. This is discussed and established by Jaimini and Śabara in MS. 5. 1. 19-22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्यम्
साकल्यम् Entirety, totality, the whole or entire part of a thing;<BR> यावत्साकल्ये; Nalod. 3. 19. (साकल्येन ‘entirely, completely, thoroughly’<BR>; यो यदैषां गुणो देहे साकल्येनातिरिच्यते Ms. 12. 25.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्यक
साकल्यक <i>a.</i> Sick, unwell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकाङ्क्ष|साकांक्ष
साकाङ्क्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Desirous.<BR>—2 Having significance.<BR>—3 Requiring a complement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकार|साकारः
साकार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a definite shape or figure.<BR>—2 Beautiful.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साकारज्ञानवादः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकारज्ञानवादः|साकारज्ञानवाद
साकार + -ज्ञानवादः the doctrine that ideas consist of forms or images.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकुल
साकुल <i>a.</i> Perplexed, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूत
साकूत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having meaning, significant, meaning; साकूतस्मितम्^1 Gīt. 2; साकूतं वचनम् &c.<BR>—2 Intentional.<BR>—3 Amorous, wanton.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174. note: definition restructed; Comp. list removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूतम्
साकूत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Meaningly, significantly; as in साकूतं मां निर्वर्ण्य.<BR>—2 Amorously.<BR>—3 Feelingly, pathetically.<BR>—4 Attentively.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साकूतस्मितम्, साकूतहसितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूतस्मितम्
साकूत + -स्मितम्, -हसितम्^1 <i>n.</i> a significant smile, wanton glance.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174. note: headword change; -smita, -hasita to -smitam, -hasitam in body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूतहसितम्
साकूत + -स्मितम्, -हसितम्^1 <i>n.</i> a significant smile, wanton glance.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174. note: headword change; -smita, -hasita to -smitam, -hasitam in body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतम्
साकेतम् N. of the city of Ayodhyā; साकेतनार्योऽञ्जलिभिः प्रणेमुः<BR> R. 14. 13, 13. 79, 18. 36; अरुणद्यवनः साकेतम् Mbh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेताः
साकेतम् + .{@-ताः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) The inhabitants of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतकः|साकेतक
साकेतकः An inhabitant of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतकम्
साकेतकः + .{@-कम्@} = साकेतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुकम्
साक्तुकम् A quantity of fried grain (सक्तु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुकः|साक्तुक|साक्तुकं
साक्तुकम् + .{@-कः@} Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष
साक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having eyes; यथा साक्षः पुरुषः परेण चेन्नीयेत नूनमक्षिभ्यां न<BR> पश्यतीति गम्यते ŚB. on MS. 1. 2. 31.<BR>—2 Having the seeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्
साक्षात् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 In the presence of, before the very eyes, visibly, openly, evidently.<BR>—2 In person, actually<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">Page1663-2</a>]<BR> in bodily form; साक्षात् प्रियामुपगतामपहाय पूर्वम् Ś. 6. 15, 1. 6.<BR>—3 Directly. In comp. it is often translated by ‘incarnate’; साक्षाद्यमः;<BR> or by ‘open, direct’; तत्साक्षात् प्रतिषेधः कोपाय Māl. 1. 11. (साक्षात्कृ<BR>—1 to see with oneʼs own eyes, realize personally.<BR>—2 to have an intuitive perception or manifestation of; साक्षात्कृतधमर्ण ऋषयः U. 7.<BR>—3 To experience a result of or reward for; साक्षात्कृतं मे परिबर्हणं<BR> हि Bhāg. 5. 5. 27, 10. 22. 20.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साक्षात्करणम्, साक्षात्कारः, साक्षात्क्रिया<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्करणम्
साक्षात् + -करणम्<BR>—1 causing to be visibly present.<BR>—2 making evident to the senses.<BR>—3 intuitive perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्कारः|साक्षात्कार
साक्षात् + -कारः perception, apprehension, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्क्रिया
साक्षात् + -क्रिया<BR>—1 intuitive perception.<BR>—2 realization.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिन्
साक्षिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सह अक्षि अस्य; साक्षाद् द्रष्टा साक्षी वा P. V. 2. 91]<BR>—1 Seeing, observing, witnessing.<BR>—2 Attesting, testifying. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A witness, an observer, an eye-witness; फलं तपःसाक्षिषु दृष्टमेष्वपि<BR> Ku. 5. 60; साक्षित्वमस्य पुरुषस्य Sāṅ. K. 19; Ms. 8. 18.<BR>—2 The Supreme Being.<BR>—3 (In phil.) The Ego.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साक्षिद्वैधम्, साक्षिपरीक्षा, साक्षिप्रत्ययः, साक्षिभावित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिद्वैधम्
साक्षिन् + -द्वैधम् divergent evidence, discrepancy between witnessess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिपरीक्षा
साक्षिन् + -परीक्षा examination of a witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिप्रत्ययः|साक्षिप्रत्यय
साक्षिन् + -प्रत्ययः the evidence of witnesses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिभावित
साक्षिन् + -भावित <i>a.</i> borne out or proved by evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्यम्
साक्ष्यम्<BR>—1 Evidence, testimony; तमेव चाधाय विवाहसाक्ष्ये R. 7. 20.<BR>—2 Attestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षर|साक्षरं
साक्षर <i>a.</i> Eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिप्तम्
साक्षिप्तम् <i>ind.</i> Thoughtlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षेप
साक्षेप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Taunting, abusive.<BR>—2 Partial (पक्षपातिन्); पाण्डवेयेषु साक्षेपं द्रोणं जानाति ते सुतः Mb. 7. 12. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखिल्यम्
साखिल्यम् Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखेय|साखेयः
साखेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to a friend.<BR>—2 Friendly, amicable; P. IV. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साख्यम्
साख्यम् Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागम
सागम <i>a.</i> Legitimate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरः|सागर
सागरः [सगरेण निर्वृत्तः अण्]<BR>—1 The ocean, sea; सागरः सागरोपमः; (fig. also); दयासागर,<BR> विद्यासागर &c.; cf. सगर.<BR>—2 The number ‘four’ or ‘seven’.<BR>—3 A kind of deer.<BR>—4 N. of Bhagīratha; शंकरस्य जटाजूटाद् भ्रष्टां सागरतेजसा Rām. 2. 50. 25.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सागरानुकूल, सागरान्त, सागराम्बरा, सागरनेमिः, सागरमेखला, सागरालयः, सागरावर्तः, सागरोत्थम्, सागरगमा, सागरगा, सागरगामिनी, सागरनेमिः, सागरप्लवनम्, सागरमेखला, सागरसुता, सागरसूनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरानुकूल
सागरः + -अनुकूल <i>a.</i> situated along the sea-coast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरान्त|सागरांत
सागरः + -अन्त <i>a.</i> bounded by the sea, sea-girt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागराम्बरा|सागरांबरा
सागरः + -अम्बरा, -नेमिः, -मेखला the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरनेमिः|सागरनेमि
सागरः + -अम्बरा, -नेमिः, -मेखला the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरमेखला
सागरः + -अम्बरा, -नेमिः, -मेखला the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरालयः|सागरालय
सागरः + -आलयः N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरावर्तः|सागरावर्त
सागरः + -आवर्तः an island or bay of the sea; स मया सागरावर्ते दृष्ट<BR> आसीत् परीप्सता Mb. 3. 14. 19 (com. सागरस्य आसमन्ताद्वर्तो वर्तनं<BR> यस्मिन् सागरद्वीपे इत्यर्थः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरोत्थम्
सागरः + -उत्थम् sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरगमा
सागरः + -गमा, -गा<BR>—1 a river; दिवि वा सागरगमास्तेन वो मानयाम्यहम् Mb. 13. 146. 23.<BR>—2 the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरगा
सागरः + -गमा, -गा<BR>—1 a river; दिवि वा सागरगमास्तेन वो मानयाम्यहम् Mb. 13. 146. 23.<BR>—2 the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरगामिनी
सागरः + -गामिनी a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरनेमिः|सागरनेमि
सागरः + -नेमिः ({@मी@}) the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरप्लवनम्
सागरः + -प्लवनम् navigating (the ocean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरमेखला
सागरः + -मेखला the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरसुता
सागरः + -सुता N. of Lakṣmī; मनोवृत्तिस्तार्क्ष्यो मतिरियमथो सागरसुता<BR> Viṣṇumahimna 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरसूनुः|सागरसूनु
सागरः + -सूनुः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्नि
साग्नि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having fire.<BR>—2 Taking the sacred fire; साग्नयोऽनग्नयश्चेव सशिष्यगणबान्धवाः Mb. 3. 1. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1663-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्निक|साग्निकः
साग्निक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Maintaining, or possessing fire.<BR>—2 Attended by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्निकः|साग्निक
साग्निक + .{@-कः@} A house-holder who maintains the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्र
साग्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Entire; तेषां तु युद्धमानानां साग्रः संवत्सरो गतः Rām. 7. 23. 9.<BR>—2 With a surplus, more than.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्रम्
साग्र + .{@-ग्रम्@} <i>ind.</i> For a longer period, for a whole life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकथिक
सांकथिक <i>a.</i> Excellent in conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकथ्यम्
सांकथ्यम् Talk, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकर्यम्
सांकर्यम् Mixture, confusion, promiscuous or confused mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकल|साङ्कल|साङ्कलं
सांकल <i>a.</i> (-ली <i>f.</i>)<BR> Produced or effected by addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकाश्यम्
सांकाश्यम्, -श्या<BR> N. of the capital of Kuśadhvaja, brother of Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकाश्या|साङ्काश्या
सांकाश्यम्, -श्या<BR> N. of the capital of Kuśadhvaja, brother of Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकूजितम्
सांकूजितम् Loud commingled twittering; सांकूजितं पक्षिगणः करोति<BR> Rām. Ch. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकेतिक|साङ्केतिक
सांकेतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Symbolical, indicatory.<BR>—2 Conventional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकेत्यम्
सांकेत्यम्<BR>—1 Agreement; पाखण्डदेवताः कङ्कगृध्रवकवटप्राया आर्यसमयपरिहृताः<BR> साङ्केत्येनाभिधत्ते Bhāg. 5. 14. 29.<BR>—2 Appointment, assignment (with beloved person); अहो मयात्मा परितापितो<BR> वृथा साङ्केत्यवृत्त्यातिविगर्ह्यवार्तया Bhāg. 11. 8. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांक्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिकः
सांक्षेपिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Abridged, short, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्य|साङ्ख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
सांख्य <i>a.</i> [संख्यया निर्वृत्तम् अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to number.<BR>—2 Calculating, enumerating.<BR>—3 Discriminative.<BR>—4 Deliberating, reasoning, a reasoner; त्वं गतिः सर्वसांख्यानां योगिनां<BR> त्वं परायणम् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्यः|साङ्ख्य|सांख्य|सांख्यं|साङ्ख्यः
सांख्य + .{@-ख्यः, -ख्यम्@} N. of one of the six systems of Hindu philosophy,<BR> attributed to the sage Kapila; (this philosophy is so called because it<BR> ‘enumerates’ twenty-five <i>Tattvas</i> or true principles; and its chief<BR> object is to effect the final emancipation of the twenty-fifth <i>Tattva</i>,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> the <i>Puruṣa</i> or soul, from the bonds of this worldly<BR> existence −the fetters of phenomenal creation− by conveying a correct<BR> knowledge of the twenty-four other <i>Tattvas</i> and by properly discriminating<BR> the Soul from them. It regards the whole universe as a development of<BR> an inanimate principle called Prakṛti q. v., while the <i>Puruṣa</i> is<BR> altogether passive and simply a looker-on. It agrees with the Vedānta<BR> in being synthetical and so differs from the analytical Nyāya or Vaiśeṣika;<BR> but its great point of divergence from the Vedānta is that it maintains<BR> two principles which the Vedānta denies, and that it does not admit God<BR> as the creator and controller of the universe, which the Vedānta affirms);<BR> सांख्यमिव कपिलाधिष्ठितम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्यम्
सांख्य + .{@-ख्यः, -ख्यम्@} N. of one of the six systems of Hindu philosophy,<BR> attributed to the sage Kapila; (this philosophy is so called because it<BR> ‘enumerates’ twenty-five <i>Tattvas</i> or true principles; and its chief<BR> object is to effect the final emancipation of the twenty-fifth <i>Tattva</i>,<BR> <i>i. e.</i> the <i>Puruṣa</i> or soul, from the bonds of this worldly<BR> existence −the fetters of phenomenal creation− by conveying a correct<BR> knowledge of the twenty-four other <i>Tattvas</i> and by properly discriminating<BR> the Soul from them. It regards the whole universe as a development of<BR> an inanimate principle called Prakṛti q. v., while the <i>Puruṣa</i> is<BR> altogether passive and simply a looker-on. It agrees with the Vedānta<BR> in being synthetical and so differs from the analytical Nyāya or Vaiśeṣika;<BR> but its great point of divergence from the Vedānta is that it maintains<BR> two principles which the Vedānta denies, and that it does not admit God<BR> as the creator and controller of the universe, which the Vedānta affirms);<BR> सांख्यमिव कपिलाधिष्ठितम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्यः|साङ्ख्य|सांख्य|सांख्यं|साङ्ख्यः
सांख्य + .{@-ख्यः@}<BR>—1 A follower of the Sāṃkhya philosophy; ज्ञानयोगेन सांख्यानां कर्मयोगेण<BR> योगिनाम् Bg. 3. 3, 5. 5.<BR>—2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सांख्यकारिका, सांख्यप्रसादः, सांख्यमुख्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्यकारिका
सांख्य + -कारिका N. of a collection of 72 verses by Īśvara-Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्यप्रसादः|साङ्ख्यप्रसाद
सांख्य + -प्रसादः, -मुख्यः epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्यमुख्यः|साङ्ख्यमुख्य
सांख्य + -प्रसादः, -मुख्यः epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्ग|सांग
साङ्ग <i>a.</i> [सहाङ्गेन अङ्गैर्वा]<BR>—1 Having members.<BR>—2 Complete in every part.<BR>—3 Together with the six <i>aṅgas</i> or auxiliary members.<BR>—4 Concluded, finished.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साङ्गोपाङ्ग<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साङ्गोपाङ्ग
साङ्ग + -उपाङ्ग <i>a.</i> (the Vedas) with the अङ्गs and उपाङ्गs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांगतिक|साङ्गतिक|सांगतिकः
सांगतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to union or society, associating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांगतिकः|साङ्गतिक|सांगतिक
सांगतिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A visitor, guest, new-comer; नैकग्रामीणमतिथिं विप्रं साङ्गतिकं<BR> तथा Ms. 3. 103.<BR>—2 One who comes to transact business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांगत्यम्
सांगत्यम् Meeting, intercourse with; त्वत्सांगत्यसुखस्य नास्मि<BR> विषयस्तत् किं वृथा व्याहृतैः Mv. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांगमः|साङ्गम|सांगम|साङ्गमः
सांगमः Union, meeting; cf. संगम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्रामिक|साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिकः
सांग्रामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to war, warlike, martial; एष साङ्ग्रामिको<BR> न्याय एष धर्मः सनातनः U. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिक|साङ्ग्रामिकः
सांग्रामिक + .{@-कः@} A general, commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्रामिकम्
सांग्रामिक + .{@-कम्@} Implements of war; सर्वसाङ्ग्रामिकोपेतम् Bhāg. 8. 10. 17.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सांग्रामिकगुणः, सांग्रामिकपरिच्छदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्रामिकगुणः|साङ्ग्रामिकगुण
सांग्रामिक + -गुणः the martial qualities of a king (<i>i. e.</i> शाक्ति, षाड्गुण्य<BR> and अस्त्राद्याभ्यास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्रामिकपरिच्छदः|साङ्ग्रामिकपरिच्छद
सांग्रामिक + -परिच्छदः implements of war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्राहिक
सांग्राहिक <i>a.</i> Constipating; Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांघातिक
सांघातिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Greatly destructive, very deadly or fatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचार
साचार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Well-behaved.<BR>—2 Well-conducted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचि
साचि <i>ind.</i> Obliquely, crookedly, awry, in a sidelong manner; साचि<BR> लोचनयुगं नमयन्ती Ki. 9. 44, 10. 57.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साचिवाटिका, साचिविलोकितम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिवाटिका
साचि + -वाटिका the white-flowered hog-weed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिविलोकितम्
साचि + -विलोकितम् a side-long look, leer. (साचीकृ to turn or bend<BR> aside, make crooked; निनाय साचीकृतचारुवक्त्रः R. 6. 14; Ku. 3. 68;<BR> साचीकरोत्याननम् M. 4. 14.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचीन
साचीन <i>a.</i> Approaching sideways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्यम्
साचिव्यम्<BR>—1 The office of a minister, ministership.<BR>—2 Ministry, administration; अनभिज्ञश्च साचिव्यं गमितः केन हेतुना<BR> Mb. 13. 163. 7.<BR>—3 Friendship; assistance; तस्य मे कुरु साचिव्यं तस्य भार्यापहारणे<BR> Rām. 3. 31. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साचिव्याक्षेपः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्याक्षेपः|साचिव्याक्षेप
साचिव्यम् + -आक्षेपः (in rhet.) an objection under the form of assent; साचिव्याक्षेप<BR> एवैष यदत्र प्रतिषिध्यते । प्रियप्रयाणं साचिव्यं कुर्वत्येवानुरक्तया ॥<BR> Kāv. 2. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साजात्यम्
साजात्यम्<BR>—1 Sameness of caste, class, or kind; साजात्यशङ्कयाऽमी न त्वां निध्नन्ति<BR> निर्दयाः काकाः Bv. 1. 25.<BR>—2 Community of genus, homogeneousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साञ्जनः|साञ्जन|सांजनः
साञ्जनः A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्
साट् €10 U. (साटयति-ते) To show, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोप
साटोप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Elated or puffed up with pride, haughty.<BR>—2 Majestic, stately.<BR>—3 Swollen, filled or charged with (as with water); Pt. 1.<BR>—4 Rumbling (as clouds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोपम्
साटोप + .{@-पम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Proudly, arrogantly, in a stately manner, struttingly; as in साटोपं परिक्रामति.<BR>—2 Angrily, furiously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1664-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साण्ड
साण्ड <i>a.</i> Uncastrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् <i>ind.</i> A Taddhita affix added to a word to show that something<BR> is completely changed into the thing expressed by that word, or that it<BR> is left at the complete disposal or control of that thing; भस्मसात्<BR> भू ‘to be completely reduced to ashes’; अग्निसात् कृत्वा M. 5; भस्मसात्<BR> कृतवतः पितृद्विषः पात्रसाञ्च वसुधां ससागराम् R. 11. 86; विभज्य<BR> मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात् कृतः N. 1. 16; so ब्राह्मणसात्, राजसात् &c.; Śi. 14. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
सात <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Given.<BR>—2 Destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातम्
सात + .{@-तम्@} Pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातत्यम्
सातत्यम् Continuity, permanence; सातत्येनैव चेतोविषयमवतरत्<BR> पातु पीताम्बरस्य Viṣṇupāda. S. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातला
सातला<BR>—1 See सप्तला.<BR>—2 A soap-tree (Mar. शिकेकाई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातवाहनः|सातवाहन
सातवाहनः N. of king Śālivāhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिः|साति
सातिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Giving, a gift, donation.<BR>—2 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>—3 Help.<BR>—4 Destruction.<BR>—5 End, conclusion.<BR>—6 Sharp or acute pain.<BR>—7 Cessation.<BR>—8 Wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिशय
सातिशय <i>a.</i> Excessive, excellent; ज्वालाश्रियं सातिशयां दधन्ति Bk. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिना
सातिना A black variety of skin (चर्मजाति); Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीनः|सातीन
सातीनः, सातीनकः, सातीलकः<BR> Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीनकः|सातीनक
सातीनः, सातीनकः, सातीलकः<BR> Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीलकः|सातीलक
सातीनः, सातीनकः, सातीलकः<BR> Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्मीभावः|सात्मीभाव
सात्मीभावः Conduciveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्म्य|सात्म्यं|सात्म्यः
सात्म्य <i>a.</i> Wholesome, agreeable to nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्म्यः|सात्म्य|सात्म्यं
सात्म्य + .{@-त्म्यः@}<BR>—1 Suitableness.<BR>—2 Habit, habitation, diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्म्यम्
सात्म्य + .{@-त्म्यम्@} = सरूपता q. v.; नृपाश्चैद्यादयः सात्म्यं हरेस्तच्चिन्तया<BR> ययुः Bhāg. 7. 10. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विक|सात्त्विकः
सात्त्विक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सत्त्वगुणेन तत्कार्येण मनसा वा निर्वृत्तः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Real, essential.<BR>—2 True, genuine, natural.<BR>—3 Honest, sincere, good.<BR>—4 Virtuous, amiable.<BR>—5 Vigorous.<BR>—6 Endowed with the quality <i>Sattva</i> (goodness).<BR>—7 Belonging to or derived from the <i>Sattva</i> quality; ये चैव सात्त्विका<BR> भावाः Bg. 7. 12, 14. 16.<BR>—8 Caused by internal feeling or sentiment (as of love), internal; तद्भूरिसात्त्विकविकारमपास्तधैर्यमाचार्यकं<BR> विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विकः|सात्त्विक
सात्त्विक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 An external indication of (internal) feeling or emotion, one of the<BR> kinds of <i>Bhāvas</i> in poetry; (these are eight: स्तम्भः स्वेदोऽथ रोभाञ्चः<BR> स्वरभङ्गोऽथ वेपथुः । वैवर्ण्यमश्रुप्रलय इत्यष्टौ सात्त्विकाः स्मृताः ।<BR> see S. D. 164 also.)<BR>—2 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 N. of Brahman.<BR>—4 An autumn night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विकम्
सात्त्विक + .{@-कम्@} An oblation (without pouring water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विकी
सात्त्विक + .{@-की@} N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यकिः|सात्यकि
सात्यकिः N. of a Yādava warrior, who acted as charioteer to Kṛṣṇa,<BR> and took part with the Pāṇḍavas in the great war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवतः|सात्यवत
सात्यवतः, -सात्यवतेयः<BR> A metronymic of the sage Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवतेयः|सात्यवतेय
सात्यवतः, -सात्यवतेयः<BR> A metronymic of the sage Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत्|सात्वन्त्
सात्वत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A follower, worshipper (of Kṛṣṇa &c.); सूत जानामि भद्रं ते<BR> भगवान् सात्वतां पतिः Bhāg. 1. 1. 12.<BR>—2 A man of the Yādava tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वतः|सात्वत
सात्वतः<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu; Mb. 14. 52. 49.<BR>—2 Of Balarāma. —3 The son of an outcast Vaiśya; Ms. 10. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वताः
सात्वतः + .{@-ताः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) N. of a people; सुचिरं सह सर्वसात्वतैर्भव<BR> विश्वस्तविलासिनीजनः Śi. 16. 14. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to सात्वत, Vaiṣṇava; तन्त्रं सात्वतमाचष्ट नैष्कर्म्यं<BR> कर्मणां यतः Bhāg. 1. 3. 8.<BR>—2 A devotee (भक्त); सद्योऽन्तर्हृदये नित्यं मुनिभिः सात्वतैर्वृतः<BR> A. Rām. 1. 2. 17.<BR>—3 Belonging to Pāncharātra; सात्वतं विधिमास्थाय Mb. 12. 335. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वती
सात्वती<BR>—1 N. of one of the four dramatic styles; see S. D. 416.<BR>—2 N. of the mother of Śiśupāla; न दूये सात्वतीसूनुर्यन्मह्यमपराध्यति Śi. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादः|साद
सादः [सद्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sinking, settling down.<BR>—2 Exhaustion, weariness; उदितोरुसादमतिवेपथुमत् Śi. 9. 77.<BR>—3 Leanness, thinness, emaciation; शरीरसादादसमग्रभूषणा R. 3. 2.<BR>—4 Perishing, decay, loss, destruction, cessation; गतिविभ्रमसादनीरवा<BR> R. 8. 58; Nalod. 3. 24.<BR>—5 Pain, torment.<BR>—6 Clearness, purity.<BR>—7 Going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादनम्
सादनम्<BR>—1 Wearying, fatiguing.<BR>—2 Destroying; क्रोधलोभौ भयं दर्प एतेषां सादनाच्छुचिः Mb. 12. 213. 1.<BR>—3 Exhaustion.<BR>—4 A house, dwelling; तस्मात्त्वां पूर्वमेवाहं नेताऽद्य यमसादनम् Mb. 3. 39. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादनी
सादनम् + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 Exhaustion, decay, fatigue.<BR>—2 The plant कटुकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिः|सादि
सादिः [सद्-इण् Uṇ. 4. 136]<BR>—1 A charioteer.<BR>—2 A warrior.<BR>—3 A dispirited person.<BR>—4 Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादित|सादितः
सादित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Made to sit down.<BR>—2 Depressed, dispirited.<BR>—3 Wearied, exhausted; प्रसेहिरे सादयितुं न सादिताः Ki. 14. 57.<BR>—4 Destroyed, exterminated; समासदत् सादितदैत्यसंपदः Śi. 1. 11.<BR>—5 Wasted, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन् <i>a.</i> [सद्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Sitting down.<BR>—2 Exhausting, destroying &c.<BR>—3 Any one sitting or riding on; प्रतिप्रहाराक्षममश्वसादी R. 7. 47. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A horseman; ततो रथद्विपभटसादिनायकैः करालया परिवृत आत्मसेनया<BR> Bhāg. 10. 71. 14.<BR>—2 One riding on an elephant or seated in a car.<BR>—3 A charioteer; ततो वररथारूढाः कुमाराः सादिभिः सह Mb. 1. 138. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्यम्
सादृश्यम्<BR>—1 Likeness, resemblance, similarity; सन्ति पुनर्नामधेयसादृश्यानि<BR> Ś. 7; तवाक्षिसादृश्यमिव प्रयुञ्जते Ku. 5. 35, 7. 16; R. 1. 40, 15. 67.<BR>—2 A likeness, a portrait, an image; मत्सादृश्यं विरहतनु वा भावगम्यं<BR> लिखन्ती Me. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्य
साद्य <i>a.</i> New; मौलसाद्यसुभेदाभ्यां सारासारं पुनर्द्विधा Śukra. 4. 870.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यन्त|साद्यंत
साद्यन्त <i>a.</i> Entire, whole, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1665-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क <i>a.</i> (-स्की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Quick, instantaneous.<BR>—2 Resulting, taking place immediately (सद्यःफल); चत्वार्याह<BR> महाराज साद्यस्कानि बृहस्पतिः (पृच्छते) Mb. 5. 33. 71.<BR>—3 New, fresh; कार्यक्षमश्च प्राचीनः साद्यस्कः कति विद्यते Śukra. 2. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्कः|साद्यस्क
साद्यस्कः (also साद्यस्क्रः) A particular sacrifice; षट् साद्यस्काः<BR> सर्ववेदेषु दृष्टाः Mb. 3. 134. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क्रः|साद्यस्क्र
साद्यस्कः (also साद्यस्क्रः) A particular sacrifice; षट् साद्यस्काः<BR> सर्ववेदेषु दृष्टाः Mb. 3. 134. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् I. €5 P. (साध्नोति)<BR>—1 To complete, finish, accomplish.<BR>—2 To conquer. ━II. €4 P. (साध्यति) To be completed or accomplished. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR>—1 To accomplish, effect, bring about, perform; अपि साधय साधयेप्सितम्<BR> N. 2. 62; यावद्यते साधयितुं तवार्थम् R. 5. 25; Ku. 2. 33.<BR>—2 To complete, finish, conclude.<BR>—3 To gain, secure, obtain; किं तत्साध्यं यदुभये साधयेयुर्न संगताः<BR> R. 17. 38; Ms. 6. 75.<BR>—4 To prove, substantiate.<BR>—5 To subdue, overpower, conquer (as a foe &c.), win over; साधयस्व<BR> पितामहम् Mb. 6. 108. 60; न हि साम्ना न दानेन न भेदेन च पाण्डवाः ।<BR> शक्याः साधयितुम् Mb.<BR>—6 To kill, destroy; सुग्रीवान्तकमासेदुः साधयिष्याम इत्यरिम् Bk. 7. 31.<BR>—7 To learn, understand.<BR>—8 To cure, heal.<BR>—9 To go, depart, go oneʼs way; साधयाम्यहमविध्नमस्तु ते R. 11. 91;<BR> Ś. 1. 7; प्रायेण ण्यन्तकः साधिर्गमेरर्थे प्रयुज्यते S. D.<BR>—10 To recover (as a debt).<BR>—11 To make perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक <i>a.</i> [साध्-ण्वुल्, सिध्-णिच् ण्वुल् साधादेशः वा Tv.] (-धका or -धिका <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Accomplishing, fulfilling, effecting, completing.<BR>—2 Efficient, effective; त्वं सर्वतोगामि च साधकं च Ku. 3. 12.<BR>—3 Skilful, adept.<BR>—4 Effecting by magic, magical.<BR>—5 Assisting, helping.<BR>—6 Conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधकः|साधक
साधक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A magician.<BR>—2 One possessed of supernatural powers, a yogin; अविचलितमनोभिः साधकैर्मृग्यमाणः Māl. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधका
साधक + .{@-का@} N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन|साधनं
साधन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [साध् णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Accomplishing, effecting &c.<BR>—2 Procuring.<BR>—3 Conjuring up (a spirit).<BR>—4 Denoting, expressive of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनम्
साधन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Accomplishing, effecting, performing, as in स्वार्थसाधनम्.<BR>—2 Fulfilment, accomplishment, complete attainment of an object; प्रजार्थसाधने<BR> तौ हि पर्यायोद्यतकार्मुकौ R. 4. 16.<BR>—3 A means, an expedient, a means of accomplishing anything; असाधना<BR> अपि प्राज्ञा बुद्धिमन्तो बहुश्रुताः । साधयन्त्यशु कार्याणि Pt. 2. 1; शरीरमाद्यं<BR> खलु धर्मसाधनम् Ku. 5. 33, 52; R. 1. 19, 4. 36, 62.<BR>—4 An instrument, agent; कुठारः छिदिक्रियासाधनम्<BR>—5 The efficient cause, source, cause in general.<BR>—6 The instrumental case.<BR>—7 Implement, apparatus.<BR>—8 Appliance, materials.<BR>—9 Matter, ingredients, substance.<BR>—10 An army or a part thereof; व्यावृत्तं च विपक्षतो भवति यत्तत्साधनं<BR> सिद्धये Mu. 5. 10.<BR>—11 Aid, help, assistance (in general).<BR>—12 Proof, substantiation, demonstration.<BR>—13 The <i>hetu</i> or middle term in a syllogism, reason, that which leads<BR> to a conclusion; साध्ये निश्चितमन्वयेन घटितं बिभ्रत् सपक्षे स्थितिं ।<BR> व्यावृत्तं च विपक्षतो भवति यत्तत् साधनं सिद्धये ॥ Mu. 5. 10.<BR>—14 Subduing, overcoming.<BR>—15 Subduing by charms.<BR>—16 Accomplishing anything<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">Page1666-2</a>]<BR> by charms or magic.<BR>—17 Healing, curing.<BR>—18 Killing, destroying; फलं च तस्य प्रतिसाधनम् Ki. 14. 17.<BR>—19 Conciliating, propitiating, winning over.<BR>—20 Going out, setting forward, departure.<BR>—21 Going after, following.<BR>—22 Penance, self-mortification.<BR>—23 Attainment of final beatitude.<BR>—24 A medicinal preparation, drug, medicine.<BR>—25 (In law) Enforcement of the the delivery of anything, or of the payment<BR> of debt, infliction of fine.<BR>—26 A bodily organ.<BR>—27 The penis.<BR>—28 An udder.<BR>—29 Wealth.<BR>—30 Friendship.<BR>—31 Profit, advantage.<BR>—32 Burning a dead body.<BR>—33 Obsequies.<BR>—34 Killing or oxydation of metals.<BR>—35 Proof, argument.<BR>—36 Conflict, battle.<BR>—37 (In gram.) Instrument, agent.<BR>—38 Making ready, preparation.<BR>—39 Gain, acquisition.<BR>—40 Calculation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साधनाध्यक्षः, साधनार्ह, साधनक्रिया, साधनक्षम, साधननिर्देशः, साधनपत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनाध्यक्षः|साधनाध्यक्ष
साधन + -अध्यक्षः Superintendent or captain of the military forces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनार्ह
साधन + -अर्ह <i>a.</i> worthy of being proved or accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनक्रिया
साधन + -क्रिया<BR>—1 a finite verb.<BR>—2 an action connected with a <i>Kāraka</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनक्षम
साधन + -क्षम <i>a.</i> admitting proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधननिर्देशः|साधननिर्देश|साधननिर्द्देश
साधन + -निर्देशः production of proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनपत्रम्
साधन + -पत्रम् a document used as evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनता
साधनता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 The state of having means, possession of means to accomplish a desired<BR> object; प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ विफलत्वमेति बहुसाधनता Śi. 9. 6.<BR>—2 The state of perfection.<BR>—3 The being a proof or argument; Kull. on Ms. 8. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनत्वम्
साधनता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 The state of having means, possession of means to accomplish a desired<BR> object; प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ विफलत्वमेति बहुसाधनता Śi. 9. 6.<BR>—2 The state of perfection.<BR>—3 The being a proof or argument; Kull. on Ms. 8. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधना
साधना<BR>—1 Accomplishment, fulfilment, completion.<BR>—2 Worship, adoration.<BR>—3 Conciliation, propitiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनीकृ
साधनीकृ €8 P. To employ as a means for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनीभू
साधनीभू €1 P. To become a means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनीय
साधनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Useful for accomplishing a task; मांसान्योष्ठावलोप्यानि साधनीयानि<BR> देवताः Bk. 5. 14.<BR>—2 To be formed (as words).<BR>—3 To be acquired (as knowledge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिका
साधिका A skilful or accomplished woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधित|साधितः
साधित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Accomplished, effected, achieved.<BR>—2 Completed, finished.<BR>—3 Proved, demonstrated.<BR>—4 Obtained, secured.<BR>—5 Discharged.<BR>—6 Overcome, subdued.<BR>—7 Made good, recovered.<BR>—8 Fined.<BR>—9 Made to pay.<BR>—10 Awarded (as fine or punishment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य <i>a.</i> [साध्-णिच् यत्]<BR>—1 To be effected or accomplished, to be brought about; साध्ये सिद्धिर्विधीयताम् H. 2. 15.<BR>—2 Feasible, practicable, attainable.<BR>—3 To be proved or demonstrated; आप्तवागनुमानाभ्यां साध्यं त्वां प्रति<BR> का कथा R. 10. 28.<BR>—4 To be established or made good.<BR>—5 To be inferred or concluded; अनुमानं तदुक्तं यत् साध्यसाधनयोर्वचः K. P. 10.<BR>—6 To be conquered or subdued, conquerable; स च त्वदेकेषुनिपातसाध्यः<BR> Ku. 3. 15; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Pt. 3. 27.<BR>—7 Curable. —8 To be killed or destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यः|साध्य
साध्य + .{@-ध्यः@}<BR>—1 A particular class of celestial beings; साध्यानां च गणं सूक्ष्मम्<BR> Ms. 1. 22; विराट्सुताः सोमसदः साध्यानां पितरः स्मृताः Ms. 3. 195; Mb. 1. 1. 35.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">Page1667-1</a>]<BR>—2 A deity in general.<BR>—3 N. of a Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यम्
साध्य + .{@-ध्यम्@}<BR>—1 Accomplishment, perfection.<BR>—2 The thing to be proved or established, the matter at issue.<BR>—3 (In logic) The predicate of a proposition, the major term in a syllogism;<BR> साध्ये निश्चितमन्वयेन घटितं … &c.; यत् साध्यं स्वयमेव तुल्यमुभयोः<BR> पक्षे विरुद्धं च यत् Mu. 5. 10.<BR>—4 Silver.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साध्याभावः, साध्यर्षिः, साध्यपक्षः, साध्यव्यापक, साध्यसमः, साध्यसाधनम्, साध्यसिद्धिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1666-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्याभावः|साध्याभाव
साध्य + -अभावः the absence of the major term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यर्षिः|साध्यर्षि
साध्य + -ऋषिः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यपक्षः|साध्यपक्ष
साध्य + -पक्षः the plaint in a law-suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यव्यापक
साध्य + -व्यापक <i>a.</i> (in logic) invariably inherent in that which is to be proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसमः|साध्यसम
साध्य + -समः an assertion identical with the point to be proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसाधनम्
साध्य + -साधनम् effecting what has to be done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यसिद्धिः|साध्यसिद्धि
साध्य + -सिद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 accomplishment.<BR>—2 conclusion. ˚पादः judgment, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यता
साध्यता<BR>—1 Feasibility, practicability.<BR>—2 Curableness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साध्यतावच्छेदकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यतावच्छेदकम्
साध्यता + -अवच्छेदकम् that which marks out or measures the साध्य or<BR> major term, its characteristic property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यवत्|साध्यवन्त्
साध्यवत् <i>m.</i> The party on whom rests the <i>onus probandi</i> or<BR> burden of proof in a law-suit. ━<i>n.</i> That which contains the साध्य<BR> or the major term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधयन्तः
साधयन्तः [Uṇ. 3. 128 com.] A mendicant, beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्मिक
साधर्मिक <i>a.</i> One of the same faith or religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्यम्
साधर्म्यम्<BR>—1 Sameness or community of duty, office &c.; पञ्चमं लोकपालानामूचुः<BR> साधर्म्ययोगतः R. 17. 78.<BR>—2 Sameness of nature, common character, likeness, community of properties;<BR> साधर्म्यमुपमा भेदे K. P. 10; इदं ज्ञानमुपाश्रित्य मम साधर्म्यमागताः<BR> Bg. 14. 2; Bhāṣā P. 12.<BR>—3 Being of the same religion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साधर्म्यसमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्यसमः|साधर्म्यसम
साधर्म्यम् + -समः (in Nyāya) a sham objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण|साधारणः
साधारण <i>a.</i> (-णा or -णी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Common (to two or more), joint; साधारणोऽयं प्रणयः Ś. 3; साधारणो<BR> भूषणभूष्यभावः Ku. 1. 42; R. 16. 5; V. 2. 16.<BR>—2 Ordinary, common; साधारणी न खलु बाधा भवस्य Aśvad. 10.<BR>—3 General, universal; यत्सप्तान्नानि मेधया तपसाजनयत् पिता । एकमस्य<BR> साधारणम् Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 1.<BR>—4 Mingled, mixed with, in common with; उत्कण्ठासाधारणं परितोषमनुभवामि<BR> Ś. 4; वीज्यते स हि संसुप्तः श्वाससाधारणानिलैः Ku. 2. 42.<BR>—5 Equal, similar, like.<BR>—6 (In logic) Belonging to more than one instance alleged, one of the<BR> three divisions of the fallacy called अनैकान्तिक q. v.<BR>—7 Occupying a middle position, mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणम्
साधारण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 A common or general rule, a rule or precept generally applicable.<BR>—2 A generic property.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साधारणदेशः, साधारणधनम्, साधारणधर्मः, साधारणपक्षः, साधारणस्त्री<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणदेशः|साधारणदेश
साधारण + -देशः a wild marshy country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणधनम्
साधारण + -धनम् joint property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणधर्मः|साधारणधर्म|साधारणधर्म्म|साधारणधर्म्मः
साधारण + -धर्मः<BR>—1 a common or universal duty; (अहिंसा सत्यमस्तेयं शौचमिन्द्रियनिग्रहः ।<BR> दमः क्षमार्जवं दानं धर्मं साधारणं विदुः ॥).<BR>—2 the common duty of procreation; (प्रजनार्थं स्त्रियः सृष्टाः संतानार्थं<BR> च मानवाः । तस्मात् साधारणो धर्मः श्रुतौ पत्न्या सहोदितः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणपक्षः|साधारणपक्ष
साधारण + -पक्षः<BR>—1 common party.<BR>—2 the mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणस्त्री
साधारण + -स्त्री a common woman, harlot, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणता
साधारणता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Community, universality.<BR>—2 Joint interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणत्वम्
साधारणता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Community, universality.<BR>—2 Joint interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणी
साधारणी<BR>—1 A twig of bamboo.<BR>—2 A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणीकृ
साधारणीकृ €8 U. To share with, divide; केन वान्येन साधारणीकरोति दुःखम् K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणीभू
साधारणीभू €1 P. To become equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण्यम्
साधारण्यम्<BR>—1 Commonness; see साधारणता.<BR>—2 Equalness, analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिका
साधिका A deep or profound sleep (सुषुप्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु <i>a.</i> (-धु or -ध्वी <i>f.</i>; compar. साधीयस्; superl. साधिष्ठ)<BR> [साध्-उन्]<BR>—1 Good, excellent, perfect; यद्यत् साधु न चित्रे स्यात् क्रियते तत्तदन्यथा<BR> Ś. 6. 13; आ परितोषाद्विदुषां न साधु मन्ये प्रयोगविज्ञानम् 1. 2.<BR>—2 Fit, proper, right; as in साधुवृत्त, साधुसमाचार.<BR>—3 Virtuous, righteous, honourable, pious.<BR>—4<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Kind, well-disposed; तदीयमाक्रन्दितमार्तसाधोः R. 2. 28; Pt. 1. 247.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Well-behaved (with loc.); मातरि साधुः Sk.<BR>—5 Correct, pure, classical (as language).<BR>—6 Pleasing, agreeable, pleasant; अतोऽर्हसि क्षन्तुमसाधु साधु वा Ki. 1. 4.<BR>—7 Noble, well-born, of noble decent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुः|साधु
साधु + .{@-धुः@}<BR>—1 A good or virtuous man; प्रत्यर्पयिष्यत्यनघां स साधुः R. 13. 65, 2. 62;<BR> एभिः साधो हृदयनिहितैर्लक्षणैर्लक्षयेवाः Me. 82.<BR>—2 A sage, saint; साधोः प्रकोपितस्यापि मनो नायाति विक्रियाम् Subhāṣ.<BR>—3 A merchant; a jeweller; मुकुटे रोपितः काचश्चरणाभरणे मणिः ।<BR> न हि दोषो मणेरस्ति किं तु साधोरविज्ञता H. 2. 72.<BR>—4 A Jaina saint. —5 A usurer, money-lender. ━<i>n.</i><BR>—1 The good; तयोः श्रेय आददानस्य साधु भवति Kaṭh. 2. 1.<BR>—2 A good act or thing. ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Well, well-done, very nice, bravo; साधु गीतम् Ś. 1; साधु रे<BR> पिङ्गल वानर साधु M. 4.<BR>—2 Enough, away with.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साध्वाचार, साधुकारिन्, साधुकृत, साधुकृत्यम्, साधुज, साधुजात, साधुदर्शन, साधुदेवी, साधुधी, साधुपुष्पम्, साधुफल, साधुभावः, साधुमत, साधुमात्रा, साधुवादः, साधुवाहः, साधुवाहिन्, साधुवृक्षः, साधुवृत्त, साधुशील, साधुशुक्ल, साधुसंमत, साधुसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वाचार
साधु + -आचार <i>a.</i> well-conducted, pious, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुकारिन्
साधु + -कारिन् <i>a.</i> skilled, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुकृत
साधु + -कृत <i>a.</i> well-done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुकृत्यम्
साधु + -कृत्यम् compensation, requital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुज|साधुजः
साधु + -ज <i>a.</i> noble, of a noble family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुजात
साधु + -जात <i>a.</i> beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुदर्शन
साधु + -दर्शन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 good-looking.<BR>—2 thoughtful, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुदेवी
साधु + -देवी a mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुधी
साधु + -धी <i>a.</i> kind, well-disposed. ━(<i>f.</i>) a mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुपुष्पम्
साधु + -पुष्पम् a land-growing lotus; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुफल
साधु + -फल <i>a.</i> having good results.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुभावः|साधुभाव
साधु + -भावः kindness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुमत
साधु + -मत <i>a.</i> highly thought of or prized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुमात्रा
साधु + -मात्रा the right measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवादः|साधुवाद
साधु + -वादः a cry of ‘well done’, a cry of approbation; सिद्धा माल्यैः<BR> साधुवादैर्द्वयेऽपि (आकिरन्ति) Śi. 18. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवाहः|साधुवाह
साधु + -वाहः, -वाहिन् <i>m.</i> a well-trained horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवाहिन्
साधु + -वाहः, -वाहिन् <i>m.</i> a well-trained horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृक्षः|साधुवृक्ष
साधु + -वृक्षः the Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्त|साधुवृत्तः
साधु + -वृत्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 well-conducted, upright, virtuous; प्रायेण साधुवृत्तानामस्थायिन्यो<BR> विपत्तयः Bh. 2. 85 (where the next sense is also intended).<BR>—2 well-rounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्तः|साधुवृत्त
साधु + -वृत्त + ({@-त्तः@}) a virtuous man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुवृत्तम्
साधु + -वृत्त + .({@-त्तम्@}) good conduct, virtue, piety, righteousness; so साधुवृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशील
साधु + -शील <i>a.</i> virtuous, righteous; यः सप्तवर्षाणि जुहोति तार्क्ष्य<BR> हव्यं त्वग्नौ नियतः साधुशीलः Mb. 3. 186. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुशुक्ल
साधु + -शुक्ल <i>a.</i> quite white.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुसंमत|साधुसम्मत
साधु + -संमत <i>a.</i> approved by the good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुसिद्ध
साधु + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> quite finished, perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिमन्
साधिमन् <i>m.</i> Goodness, excellence, perfection; विहाय हा सर्वसुपर्वनायकं<BR> त्वया धृतः किं नरसाधिमभ्रमः N. 9. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1667-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Best, most excellent, most proper.<BR>—2 Very strong, hard or firm (superl. of साधु or बाढ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधीयस्
साधीयस् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Better, more excellent; नैर्गुण्यमेव साधीयो घिगस्तु गुणगौरवम् Bv. 1. 88.<BR>—2 Harder, stronger; (compar. of साधु or बाढ q. v.).<BR>—3 More handsome.<BR>—4 More proper or right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुता
साधुता, -त्वम्<BR> Goodness, purity, chastity &c.; यथा स्त्रीणां तथा वाचां<BR> साधुत्वे दुर्जनो जनः U. 1. 5; सत्संगाद्भवति हि साधुता खलानाम् Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुत्वम्
साधुता, -त्वम्<BR> Goodness, purity, chastity &c.; यथा स्त्रीणां तथा वाचां<BR> साधुत्वे दुर्जनो जनः U. 1. 5; सत्संगाद्भवति हि साधुता खलानाम् Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुकः|साधुक
साधुकः N. of a mixed caste; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुमत्
साधुमत्<BR>—1 Good.<BR>—2 Happy; देवानां प्रतिपत्तिश्च सत्यं साधुमता सताम् Mb. 5. 191. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधृतम्
साधृतम्<BR>—1 A stall, shop.<BR>—2 An umbrella.<BR>—3 A flock of peacocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वसम्
साध्वसम्<BR>—1 Fear, alarm, fright, terror; कुसुमस्तेयसाध्वसात् Ku. 2. 35, 3. 51.<BR>—2 Torpor.<BR>—3 Agitation, perturbation; प्रत्युज्जग्मू रथैर्हृष्टाः प्रणयागतसाध्वसाः<BR> Bhāg. 1. 11. 19, 10. 29. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वी
साध्वी<BR>—1 A virtuous or chaste woman.<BR>—2 A faithful wife. —3 N. of a kind of root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानन्द|सानंद|सानन्दः
सानन्द <i>a.</i> Happy, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानन्दम्
सानन्द + .{@-न्दम्@} <i>ind.</i> Joyfully, delightfully; सानन्दं नन्दिहस्ताहतमुरज … … Māl. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानलः|सानल
सानलः The resinous exudation of the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसिः|सानसि
सानसिः Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानाथ्यम्
सानाथ्यम् Assistance, aid; Dk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानिका
सानिका, सानियिका, सानेयी<BR> A pipe, flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानियिका
सानिका, सानियिका, सानेयी<BR> A pipe, flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयी
सानिका, सानियिका, सानेयी<BR> A pipe, flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानु|सानुः
सानु <i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 A peak, summit, ridge; सानूनि गन्धः सुरभीकरोति Ku. 1. 9; Me. 2; Ki. 5. 36.<BR>—2 A level ground on the top of a mountain, table-land.<BR>—3 A shoot, sprout.<BR>—4 A forest, wood; आसीद् विशालोत्तमसानुलक्ष्म्या पयोदपङ्क्त्येव परीतपार्श्वम् Bu. C. 1. 2.<BR>—5 A road.<BR>—6 Any surface, point, end.<BR>—7 A precipice.<BR>—8 A gale of wind.<BR>—9 A learned man.<BR>—10 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक
सानुक <i>a.</i> Elevated, arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमत्|सानुमन्त्
सानुमत् <i>m.</i> A mountain; द्रुमसानुमतां किमन्तरं यदि वायौ<BR> द्वितयेऽपि ते चलाः R. 8. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमती
सानुमत् + .{@-ती@} N. of an Apsaras; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुकम्प|सानुकंप
सानुकम्प^1 <i>a.</i> Feeling pity, sympathising, kind.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुकूल्यम्
सानुकूल्यम् Favour, assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक्रोश
सानुक्रोश <i>a.</i> Tender, compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुग
सानुग <i>a.</i> With followers; सानुगेभ्यो बलिं हरेत् Ms. 3. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुतर्षम्
सानुतर्षम् <i>ind.</i> Through thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनय
सानुनय <i>a.</i> Courteous, civil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनासिक
सानुनासिक<BR>—1 Nasalized.<BR>—2 Singing through the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुबन्ध|सानुबंध
सानुबन्ध <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Uninterrupted, continuous; सानुबन्धाः कथं न स्युः संपदो मे निरापदः R. 1. 64.<BR>—2 Having consequences.<BR>—3 Together with belongings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुराग
सानुराग <i>a.</i> Attached, enamoured, in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानूकर्ष
सानूकर्ष <i>a.</i> Having axle-beams; रथाः सानूकर्षाः कृतपरिकरा<BR> योधपुरुषाः Pañc. 2. 7 (com. रथस्य अधोधारणदारु अनूकर्षाख्यं तद्युक्ताः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तपनम्
सान्तपनम् A kind of rigid penance; cf. गोमूत्रं गोमयं क्षीरं<BR> दधि सर्पिः कृशोदकम् । एकरात्रोपवासश्च कृच्छ्रं सान्तपनं स्मृतम् ॥ Ms. 11. 212.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तर|सांतर|सान्तरं
सान्तर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having interstices or intervals.<BR>—2 Open in texture.<BR>—3 Not steadfast or firm; सान्तरं तु प्रतिज्ञाते राज्ञो द्रोणेन निग्रहे Mb. 7. 12. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तराल
सान्तराल <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having an interval.<BR>—2 Together with the mixed caste; वर्णानां सान्तरालानाम् Ms. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तानिक|सांतानिक|सान्तानिकः
सान्तानिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Stretching, spreading, extending (as a tree).<BR>—2 Relating to offspring or descendants.<BR>—3 Relating to the tree Santāna, q. v.<BR>—4 Desirous of offspring; नाहं त्वां भस्मसात् कुर्यां स्त्रियं सान्तानिकः<BR> सति Bhāg. 9. 14. 9.<BR>—5 Desirous of marriage; Ms. 11. 1 (com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्तानिकः|सान्तानिक|सांतानिक
सान्तानिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa who wishes to marry for the sake of issue.<BR>—2 (pl.) N. of particular worlds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्व्|सांत्व्
सान्त्व् €10 U. (सान्त्वयति-ते) To pacify, appease, conciliate, soothe,<BR> comfort; ताः सान्त्वयन्ती भरतप्रतीक्षा तं बन्धुता न्यक्षिपदाशु तैले Bk. 3. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वः|सान्त्व|सांत्व|सान्त्वं|सांत्वः
सान्त्वः, सान्त्वा, सान्त्वम्, सान्त्वनम्, -ना [सान्त्व् अच् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Appeasing, pacification, consolation.<BR>—2 Conciliation, mild or gentle means; Kau. A. 2. 10; सान्त्वं हि नाम<BR> दुर्विनीतानामौषधम् Pañc. 1; बबन्ध सान्त्वेन फलेन चैतान्<BR> Bu. C. 2. 42; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR> न संरम्भेण सिध्यन्ति सर्वेऽर्थाः सान्त्वया यथा Bhāg. 8. 6. 24; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>—3 Kind or conciliatory words; सान्त्वं बभाषे न च नार्थवद् यत् Bu. C. 2. 38.<BR>—4 Mildness.<BR>—5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वा
सान्त्वः, सान्त्वा, सान्त्वम्, सान्त्वनम्, -ना [सान्त्व् अच् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Appeasing, pacification, consolation.<BR>—2 Conciliation, mild or gentle means; Kau. A. 2. 10; सान्त्वं हि नाम<BR> दुर्विनीतानामौषधम् Pañc. 1; बबन्ध सान्त्वेन फलेन चैतान्<BR> Bu. C. 2. 42; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR> न संरम्भेण सिध्यन्ति सर्वेऽर्थाः सान्त्वया यथा Bhāg. 8. 6. 24; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>—3 Kind or conciliatory words; सान्त्वं बभाषे न च नार्थवद् यत् Bu. C. 2. 38.<BR>—4 Mildness.<BR>—5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

