सान्त्वः, सान्त्वा, सान्त्वम्, सान्त्वनम्, -ना [सान्त्व् अच् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Appeasing, pacification, consolation.<BR>—2 Conciliation, mild or gentle means; Kau. A. 2. 10; सान्त्वं हि नाम<BR> दुर्विनीतानामौषधम् Pañc. 1; बबन्ध सान्त्वेन फलेन चैतान्<BR> Bu. C. 2. 42; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR> न संरम्भेण सिध्यन्ति सर्वेऽर्थाः सान्त्वया यथा Bhāg. 8. 6. 24; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>—3 Kind or conciliatory words; सान्त्वं बभाषे न च नार्थवद् यत् Bu. C. 2. 38.<BR>—4 Mildness.<BR>—5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वनम्
सान्त्वः, सान्त्वा, सान्त्वम्, सान्त्वनम्, -ना [सान्त्व् अच् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Appeasing, pacification, consolation.<BR>—2 Conciliation, mild or gentle means; Kau. A. 2. 10; सान्त्वं हि नाम<BR> दुर्विनीतानामौषधम् Pañc. 1; बबन्ध सान्त्वेन फलेन चैतान्<BR> Bu. C. 2. 42; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR> न संरम्भेण सिध्यन्ति सर्वेऽर्थाः सान्त्वया यथा Bhāg. 8. 6. 24; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>—3 Kind or conciliatory words; सान्त्वं बभाषे न च नार्थवद् यत् Bu. C. 2. 38.<BR>—4 Mildness.<BR>—5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्त्वना
सान्त्वः, सान्त्वा, सान्त्वम्, सान्त्वनम्, -ना [सान्त्व् अच् ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Appeasing, pacification, consolation.<BR>—2 Conciliation, mild or gentle means; Kau. A. 2. 10; सान्त्वं हि नाम<BR> दुर्विनीतानामौषधम् Pañc. 1; बबन्ध सान्त्वेन फलेन चैतान्<BR> Bu. C. 2. 42; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सान्त्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR> न संरम्भेण सिध्यन्ति सर्वेऽर्थाः सान्त्वया यथा Bhāg. 8. 6. 24; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>—3 Kind or conciliatory words; सान्त्वं बभाषे न च नार्थवद् यत् Bu. C. 2. 38.<BR>—4 Mildness.<BR>—5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्दीपनिः|सान्दीपनि|सांदीपनि|सांदीपनिः
सान्दीपनिः N. of a sage. [According to ViṣṇuPurāṇa, he was the<BR> tutor of Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma, and asked as his preceptorʼs fee that<BR> his son, who was kept by a demon named Pañcajana underneath the waters,<BR> should be restored to him. Kṛṣṇa, having undertaken to get him up,<BR> plunged into the sea, killed the demon, and brought back the boy to his father.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांदृष्टिक|सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सांदृष्टिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to present perception, visible at the same time.<BR>—2 Evident, undeniable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांदृष्टिकम्
सांदृष्टिक + .{@-कम्@} Immediate consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्र|सांद्र|सान्द्रं|सान्द्रः
सान्द्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Close, compact, having no interstices.<BR>—2 Coarse, gross, thick, dense; दुर्वर्णभित्तिरिह सान्द्रसुधासवर्णा<BR> Śi. 4. 28, 64, 9. 15; R. 7. 41; Ṛs. 1. 20.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">Page1669-1</a>]<BR>—3 Clustered together, collected.<BR>—4 Stout, strong, robust.<BR>—5 Excessive, abundant, much; सान्द्रानन्दक्षुभितहृदयप्रस्रबेणावसिक्तः U. 6. 22.<BR>—6 Intense, strong, vehement; व्याप्तान्तराः सान्द्रकुतूहलानाम् R. 7. 11;<BR> Śi. 9. 37.<BR>—7 Unctuous, oily, viscid.<BR>—8 Bland, soft, smooth.<BR>—9 Pleasing, agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रम्
सान्द्र + .{@-द्रम्@}<BR>—1 A heap, cluster.<BR>—2 A thicket, wood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सान्द्रकुतूहल, सान्द्रस्पर्श<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1668-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रकुतूहल
सान्द्र + -कुतूहल <i>a.</i> greatly curious, seized with great curiosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रस्पर्श
सान्द्र + -स्पर्श <i>a.</i> soft to the touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्द्रीकृत
सान्द्रीकृत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Made thick or dense.<BR>—2 Increased, strengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांध
सांध <i>a.</i> Situated at the point of contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांधिकः|सान्धिक|सांधिक|सान्धिकः
सांधिकः A distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांधिविग्रहिकः|सान्धिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिक
सांधिविग्रहिकः A minister (or Secretary of State) for foreign affairs<BR> (deciding upon peace and war).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांध्य|सान्ध्य|सान्ध्यः
सांध्य <i>a.</i> (-ध्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to the twilight or evening; सांध्यं तेजः प्रतिनवजपापुष्परक्तं<BR> दधानः Me. 38; Ki. 5. 8; R. 11. 60; Śi. 9. 15.<BR>—2 Relating to the morning twilight or dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनहनिक|सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिकः
सांनहनिक, -सांनाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Bearing or putting on an armour; सांनाहिको यदा राजन् राजन्योऽथ<BR> पशुः शुचिः Bhāg. 9. 7. 14.<BR>—2 Calling to arms, encouraging to prepare for battle; शैलकटकतटभिन्नरवः<BR> प्रणनाद सांनहनिकोऽस्य बारिजः Śi. 15. 72; अकृतार्थश्च भीतश्च<BR> न च सांनाहिको हतः Mb. 7. 71. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनाहिक|सान्नाहिक
सांनहनिक, -सांनाहिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Bearing or putting on an armour; सांनाहिको यदा राजन् राजन्योऽथ<BR> पशुः शुचिः Bhāg. 9. 7. 14.<BR>—2 Calling to arms, encouraging to prepare for battle; शैलकटकतटभिन्नरवः<BR> प्रणनाद सांनहनिकोऽस्य बारिजः Śi. 15. 72; अकृतार्थश्च भीतश्च<BR> न च सांनाहिको हतः Mb. 7. 71. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिक|सान्नहनिकः
सांनहनिक, -सांनाहिक + .{@-कः@} An armour-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनाहुक
सांनाहुक <i>a.</i> Fit for wearing arms; Ait. Br. 7. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनाय्यः|सान्नाय्य|सांनाय्य|सान्नाय्यं
सांनाय्यः Any substance mixed with clarified butter and offered as<BR> an oblation to fire; पाय्य-सांनाप्य-निकाय्यधाष्याः मानहविर्निवाससामिधेनीषु<BR> (P. III. 1. 29; quoted by Śabara on MS. 5. 3. 5); Śi. 11. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनिध्यम्
सांनिध्यम्<BR>—1 Vicinity, proximity; वदनामलेन्दुसांनिध्यतः Māl. 3. 5.<BR>—2 Presence, attendance; परिकल्पितसांनिध्या काले काले च वन्दिषु<BR> R. 4. 6, 7. 3; Ku. 7. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनिपातिक|सान्निपातिक|सान्निपातिकः
सांनिपातिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [संनिपातात् त्रिदोषविकारात्<BR> आगतः तेन निर्वृत्तो वा अण्]<BR>—1 Miscellaneous.<BR>—2 Complicated.<BR>—3 Having a complicated derangement of the three bodily humours; वीर्यवन्त्यौषधानीव<BR> विकारे सांनिपातिके Ku. 2. 48; भिषजां सांनिपातिके कर्मणि व्यज्यते<BR> प्रज्ञा Pt. 1. 127.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सांनिपातिककर्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनिपातिककर्मन्
सांनिपातिक + -कर्मन् the treatment of the above illness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांन्यासिकः|सान्न्यासिक|सांन्यासिक|सान्न्यासिकः
सांन्यासिकः [संन्यासः प्रयोजनमस्य ठक्]<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa in the fourth order of his religious life; see संन्यासिन्.<BR>—2 A mendicant in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्वय
सान्वय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Hereditary.<BR>—2 Along with family or descendants; स जीवन्नेव शूद्रत्वमाशु गच्छति<BR> सान्बयः Ms. 2. 168.<BR>—3 Of kin, related to; अवहार्यो भवेच्चैव सान्वयः षट्शतं दमम् 8. 198.<BR>—4 Significant; Dk.<BR>—5 Having the same business; Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न
सापत्न <i>a.</i> (-त्नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Based on rivalry.<BR>—2 Born from or belonging to a rival wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्त्नाः
सापत्न + .{@-त्नाः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) The children of different wives of the same husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्नकम्
सापत्नकम् Rivalry, enmity, also सापत्न्यकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्यम्
सापत्न्यम्<BR>—1 The state or condition of a rival wife; सापत्न्यं क्षितिसुतविद्विषो महिष्यः.<BR>—2 Rivalry, ambition, enmity; तथापि देवाः सापत्न्यान्नोपेक्ष्या इति मन्महे<BR> Bhāg. 10. 4. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्यः|सापत्न्य|सापत्न्यं
सापत्न्यम् + .{@-त्न्यः@}<BR>—1 The son of a rival wife.<BR>—2 An enemy.<BR>—3 A half brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्य|सापत्यः
सापत्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having progeny.<BR>—2 Accompanied by children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्यः|सापत्य
सापत्य + .{@-त्यः@}<BR>—1 The son of a rival wife.<BR>—2 A half brother; see सापत्न्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापदेशम्
सापदेशम् <i>ind.</i> Under a pretence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापराध
सापराध <i>a.</i> Guilty, criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापवाद
सापवाद <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Spreading or indulging in scandal; देव्यामपि हि वैदेह्यां सापवादो<BR> यतो जनः U. 1. 6.<BR>—2 Attended with a scandal; U. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापवादम्
सापवाद + .{@-दम्@} <i>ind.</i> Censuringly, reproachfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापवादक
सापवादक <i>a.</i> Liable to exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापाश्रयम्
सापाश्रयम् A house with an open gallery at the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापिण्ड्यम्
सापिण्ड्यम् Connection by the offering of rice-balls to the same Manes,<BR> kindred, consanguinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापीड
सापीड <i>a.</i> Discharging a stream of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापेक्ष
सापेक्ष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having regard to, dependent on, (usually in comp.).<BR>—2 Favourable, partial; सुकेशं प्रति सापेक्षः प्राह देवगणान् प्रभुः Rām. 7. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपद
साप्तपद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>), साप्तपदीन <i>a.</i><BR> [cf. P. V. 2. 22] Formed by walking together seven steps, or by talking<BR> together seven words; यतः सतां संनतगात्रि संगतं मनीषिभिः साप्तपदीनमुच्यते<BR> Ku. 5. 39 (where the latter sense appears better); सतां साप्तपदं<BR> मैत्रमित्याहुर्विबुधा जनाः Pt. 2. 43, 4. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदी
साप्तपद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>), साप्तपदीन <i>a.</i><BR> [cf. P. V. 2. 22] Formed by walking together seven steps, or by talking<BR> together seven words; यतः सतां संनतगात्रि संगतं मनीषिभिः साप्तपदीनमुच्यते<BR> Ku. 5. 39 (where the latter sense appears better); सतां साप्तपदं<BR> मैत्रमित्याहुर्विबुधा जनाः Pt. 2. 43, 4. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदीन|साप्तपदीनं
साप्तपद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>), साप्तपदीन <i>a.</i><BR> [cf. P. V. 2. 22] Formed by walking together seven steps, or by talking<BR> together seven words; यतः सतां संनतगात्रि संगतं मनीषिभिः साप्तपदीनमुच्यते<BR> Ku. 5. 39 (where the latter sense appears better); सतां साप्तपदं<BR> मैत्रमित्याहुर्विबुधा जनाः Pt. 2. 43, 4. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदम्
साप्तपद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>), साप्तपदीन <i>a.</i> + .{@-दम्, -दीनम्@}<BR>—1 Circumambulation of the nuptial fire by the bride and bridegroom in<BR> seven steps (which makes the marriage tie irrevocable).<BR>—2 Friendship, intimacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपदीनम्
साप्तपद <i>a.</i> (-दी <i>f.</i>), साप्तपदीन <i>a.</i> + .{@-दम्, -दीनम्@}<BR>—1 Circumambulation of the nuptial fire by the bride and bridegroom in<BR> seven steps (which makes the marriage tie irrevocable).<BR>—2 Friendship, intimacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपौरुष
साप्तपौरुष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>) Extending to or including<BR> seven generations; पितॄणां तस्य तृप्तिः स्याच्छाश्वती साप्तपौरुषी Ms. 3. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साफल्यम्
साफल्यम्<BR>—1 Fruitfulness, usefulness, productiveness.<BR>—2 Profit, advantage.<BR>—3 Success.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साबाध
साबाध <i>a.</i> Disordered, deranged; प्रियायाः साबाधं तदपि कमनीयं<BR> वपुरिदम् Ś. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साब्दी
साब्दी A kind of grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभाव्यम्
साभाव्यम् Identity of nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1669-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिनयम्
साभिनयम् <i>ind.</i> With dramatic gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभिनिवेश
साभिनिवेश <i>a.</i> Attended with a great predilection for anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्यसूय
साभ्यसूय <i>a.</i> Envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्
साम् €10 U. (सामयति-ते) To appease, conciliate, soothe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम
साम <i>a.</i> Undigested, crude; Caraka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामम्
सामम् Likeness, similarity.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामस्थ्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामस्थ्यम्
सामम् + -स्थ्यम् comfort, ease, welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामकम्
सामकम् The principal of a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामकः|सामक|सामकं
सामकम् + .{@-कः@} A whet-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्री
सामग्री [समग्रस्य भावः ष्यञ् स्त्रीत्वपक्षे ङीषि यलोपः Tv.]<BR>—1 A collection or assemblage of materials, apparatus, furniture; इतीयं<BR> सामग्री भवति हरभक्तिं स्पृहयताम् Bh. 3. 155.<BR>—2 Effects, goods.<BR>—3 Stock, provision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्र्यम्
सामग्र्यम्<BR>—1 Entireness, perfection, completeness, totality; प्रायेण सामग्र्यविधौ<BR> गुणानां पराङ्मुखी विश्वसृजः प्रवृत्तिः Ku. 3. 28; पञ्चशरो भावरसानां<BR> सामग्र्यात् Dk. 2. 2.<BR>—2 Train, retinue.<BR>—3 A collection of implements, apparatus.<BR>—4 Stock, effects.<BR>—5 Welfare (क्षेम); अपि लक्ष्मण सीतायाः सामग्र्यं प्राप्नुयामहे Rām. 3. 57. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामञ्जस्यम्
सामञ्जस्यम्<BR>—1 Fitness, consistency, propriety; cf. असमञ्जस.<BR>—2 Accuracy, correctness; एकस्यां हि चितौ षष्ठीशब्दो न सामञ्जस्येन<BR> स्यात् ŚB. on MS. 4. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन् <i>n.</i> [सो-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 152]<BR>—1 Appeasing, calming, comforting, soothing.<BR>—2 Conciliation, pacific measures, negotiation, (the first of the four<BR> <i>upāyas</i> or expedients to be used by a king against an enemy); सामदण्डौ<BR> प्रशंसन्ति नित्यं राष्ट्राभिवृद्धये Ms. 7. 109.<BR>—3 Conciliatory or mild means; pacific or conciliatory conduct, gentle<BR> words; यो दुर्बलो ह्यण्वपि याच्यमानो बलीयसा यच्छति नैव साम्ना Pt. 4. 26, 48.<BR>—4 Mildness, gentleness.<BR>—5 A metrical hymn or song of praise; सप्तसामोपगीतं त्वाम् R. 10. 21;<BR> बृहत्साम तथा साम्नां गायत्री छन्दसामहम् Bg. 10. 35.<BR>—6 A verse or text of the Sāmaveda; सस्तोभस्वरकालाभ्यासविकारायां<BR> हिङ्कारप्रणवप्रस्तावोद्गीथप्रतिहारोपद्रवनिधनवत्यामृचि गीतौ सामशब्दोऽभियुक्तैरुपचर्यते<BR> ŚB. on MS. 7. 2. 1; स्तोभादिविशिष्टा ऋक् साम ibid.<BR>—7 The Sāmaveda itself (said to have been produced from the sun; cf. Ms. 1. 23).<BR>—8 Voice, sound; स्वरः सामशब्देन लोकेऽभिधीयते । सुसामा देवदत्त<BR> इति सुस्वरो देवदत्त इति । स्वरो घोषो नाद इति समानार्थाः । स सामशब्देनोच्यते ।<BR> ŚB. on MS. 7. 2. 7; त्रिःसामा हन्यतामेषा दुन्दुभिः शत्रुभीषणा Mb. 3. 20. 10.<BR>—9 A particular kind of sacred text or verse from the Vedas; प्रस्तौता<BR> साम प्रस्तौति; Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्ना
सामन् + .{@-साम्ना@} <i>ind.</i> Willingly, gladly; तत्र स्म गाथा गायन्ति साम्ना<BR> परमवल्गुना Mb. 3. 43. 28.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामोद्भवः, सामोपचारः, सामोपायः, सामकलम्, सामगः, सामगर्भः, सामगायनः, सामज, सामजात, सामप्रधान, सामयोनिः, सामवादः, सामविद्, सामविधानम्, सामवेदः, सामवेदिन्, सामवेदीयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोद्भवः|सामोद्भव
सामन् + -उद्भवः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोपचारः|सामोपचार
सामन् + -उपचारः, -उपायः mild or conciliatory means, gentle or pacific measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामोपायः|सामोपाय
सामन् + -उपचारः, -उपायः mild or conciliatory means, gentle or pacific measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामकलम्
सामन् + -कलम् <i>ind.</i> in a friendly tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामगः|सामग
सामन् + -गः a Brāhmaṇa who chants the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामगर्भः|सामगर्भ
सामन् + -गर्भः, -गायनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामगायनः|सामगायन
सामन् + -गर्भः, -गायनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामज|सामजः
सामन् + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 produced by the Sāmaveda.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">Page1670-2</a>]<BR>—2 produced by conciliatory means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामजात|सामजातः
सामन् + -ज, -जात <i>a.</i><BR>—1 produced by the Sāmaveda.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">Page1670-2</a>]<BR>—2 produced by conciliatory means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामजः|सामज
सामन् + -ज, -जात + .({@-जः, -तः@}) an elephant; नानाविधाविष्कृतसामजस्वरः Śi. 12. 11;<BR> दन्ता दन्तैराहताः सामजानां भङ्गं जग्मुर्न स्वयं सामजाताः 18. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामजातः|सामजात
सामन् + -ज, -जात + .({@-जः, -तः@}) an elephant; नानाविधाविष्कृतसामजस्वरः Śi. 12. 11;<BR> दन्ता दन्तैराहताः सामजानां भङ्गं जग्मुर्न स्वयं सामजाताः 18. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामप्रधान
सामन् + -प्रधान <i>a.</i> perfectly kind or friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयोनिः|सामयोनि
सामन् + -योनिः<BR>—1 Brahman.<BR>—2 an elephant; सुरद्विपानामिव सामयोनिर्भिन्नोऽष्टधा विप्रससार वंशः R. 16. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवादः|सामवाद
सामन् + -वादः kind words, conciliatory words; सामवादाः सकोपस्य<BR> तस्य प्रत्युत दीपकाः Śi. 2. 55; Pt. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

