सामविधानम्
सामन् + -विधानम् the employment of Sāmans (for religious purposes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवेदः|सामवेद
सामन् + -वेदः the third of the four Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवेदिन्
सामन् + -वेदिन् <i>m.</i> a Brāhmaṇa who has studied the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवेदीयः|सामवेदीय
सामन् + -वेदीयः a Chāndoga priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन
सामन <i>a.</i> Ved. Conciliatory, peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्यः|सामन्य
सामन्यः<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa versed in the Sāmaveda; ऋग्यजुषमधीयानान् सामन्यांश्च<BR> समर्चयन् Bk. 4. 9.<BR>—2 One skilful in chanting the verses of that Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन् <i>n.</i> Likeness, similarity; वर्णः स्वरः । मात्रा बलम् ।<BR> साम संतानः । T. Up. 2. 1; Bṛ. Up. 1. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामनी
सामनी, साम्नी A rope for tying cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्नी
सामनी, साम्नी A rope for tying cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्त|सामंत|सामन्तः
सामन्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Bordering, bounding, neighbouring.<BR>—2 Universal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तः|सामन्त|सामंत
सामन्त + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 A neighbour; राष्ट्रेषु रक्षाधिकृतान् सामन्तांश्चैव चोदितान् Ms. 9. 272.<BR>—2 A neighbouring king.<BR>—3 A feudatory or tributary prince; सामन्तमौलिमणिरञ्जितपादपीठम्<BR> V. 3. 19; R. 5. 28, 6. 33.<BR>—4 A prince with a revenue of 3 lacs Karṣa; सामन्तः स नृपः प्रोक्तो<BR> यावल्लक्षत्रयावधि Śukra. 1. 83.<BR>—5 A leader, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तम्
सामन्त + .{@-तम्@} Neighbourhood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामन्तचक्रम्, सामन्तप्रत्ययः, सामन्तवासिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तचक्रम्
सामन्त + -चक्रम् a circle of neighbouring princes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तप्रत्ययः|सामन्तप्रत्यय
सामन्त + -प्रत्ययः the evidence of near neighbours; सामन्तप्रत्ययो<BR> ज्ञेयः सीमासेतुविनिर्णयः Ms. 8. 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्तवासिन्
सामन्त + -वासिन् a neighbour; ग्रामाः सामन्तवासिनः Ms. 8. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयाचारिक
सामयाचारिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to conventional practice or usage (समयाचार).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामयाचारिकसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयाचारिकसूत्रम्
सामयाचारिक + -सूत्रम् N. of certain Sūtras, treating of conventional customs<BR> and rites sanctioned by the common agreement and practice of virtuous men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिक|सामयिकः
सामयिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [समय-ठञ्]<BR>—1 Customary, conventional.<BR>—2 Agreed upon, stipulated.<BR>—3 Conforming to agreement, keeping an appointment or engagement; देवि<BR> सामयिका भवामः M. 1.<BR>—4 Punctual, exact.<BR>—5 Reasonable, timely; किमसामयिकं वितन्वता मनसः क्षोभमुपात्तरंहसः Ki. 2. 40.<BR>—6 Periodical.<BR>—7 Temporary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिकः|सामयिक
सामयिक + .{@-कः@} Time, period.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामयिकाभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिकाभावः|सामयिकाभाव
सामयिक + -अभावः temporary non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामरिक
सामरिक <i>a.</i> Warlike, martial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्यम्
सामर्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Power, force, capacity, ability, strength; निन्दन्तस्तव सामर्थ्यं<BR> ततो दुःखतरं नु किम् Bg. 2. 36.<BR>—2 Sameness of aim or object.<BR>—3 Oneness of meaning or signification.<BR>—4 Adequacy, fitness.<BR>—5 The force or sense of words, the signifying power of a word.<BR>—6 Interest,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">Page1671-1</a>]<BR> advantage.<BR>—7 Wealth. (सामर्थ्यात्, सामर्थ्ययोगात् ‘by the force of, on the strength of, by dint of, by reason of, as a consequence of’<BR>.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1670-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्ष
सामर्ष <i>a.</i> Indignant, wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिक|सामवायिकः
सामवायिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [समवाये प्रसृतः ठञ्]<BR>—1 Belonging to an assembly or collection; P. IV. 4. 43.<BR>—2 Belonging to inseparable connection.<BR>—3 (An अङ्ग) that subserves the purpose of the principal act directly;<BR> आरादुपकारकेभ्यः सामवायिकानि गरीयांसि ŚB. on MS. 10. 4. 38; (see<BR> संनिपत्योपकारक), also 10. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिकः|सामवायिक
सामवायिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A minister, counsellor.<BR>—2 The chief of a company or corporation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामस्तम्
सामस्तम् Science of word-composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिक|सामाजिकः
सामाजिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [समाजः सभावेशनं प्रयोजनमस्य<BR> ठञ्] Belonging to an assembly; P. IV. 4. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिकः|सामाजिक
सामाजिक + .{@-कः@} A member of an audience or assembly, a spectator at an assembly<BR> or meeting; तेन हि तत्प्रयोगादेवात्रभवतः सामाजिकानुपास्महे Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानग्रामिक
सामानग्रामिक, सामानदेशिक Belonging to the same village,<BR> coming from the same village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानदेशिक
सामानग्रामिक, सामानदेशिक Belonging to the same village,<BR> coming from the same village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानाधिकरण्यम्
सामानाधिकरण्यम्<BR>—1 Being in the same predicament or situation.<BR>—2 Common office, function or government, common relationship (as of case).<BR>—3 The state of relating to the same object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानिक
सामानिक <i>a.</i> Of equal rank or dignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्य|सामान्यं
सामान्य <i>a.</i> [समानस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Common, general; सामान्यमेषां प्रथमावरत्वम् Ku. 7. 44; आहारनिद्राभयमैथुनं<BR> च सामान्यमेतत् पशुभिर्नराणाम् Subhāṣ.; R. 14. 67; Ku. 2. 26.<BR>—2 Alike, equal, same; सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकमियं दारेषु दृश्या त्वया Ś. 4. 17.<BR>—3 Ordinary, of an average or middle degree; सामान्यास्तु परार्थमुद्यमभृतः<BR> स्वार्थाविरोधेन ये Bh. 2. 74.<BR>—4 Vulgar, commonplace, insignificant.<BR>—5 Entire, whole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यम्
सामान्य + .{@-न्यम्@}<BR>—1 Community, generality, universality.<BR>—2 Common or generic property, general characteristic; नित्यमेकमनेकसमवेतं<BR> सामान्यम् Tarka K.<BR>—3 Totality, entireness.<BR>—4 Kind, sort.<BR>—5 Identity.<BR>—6 Equanimity, equability.<BR>—7 Public affairs.<BR>—8 A general proposition; उक्तिरर्थान्तरन्यासः स्यात् सामान्यविशेषयोः<BR> Candr. 5. 120.<BR>—9 (In Rhet.) A figure of speech thus defined by Mammaṭa:− प्रस्तुतस्य<BR> यदन्येन गुणसाम्यविवक्षया । ऐकात्म्यं बध्यते योगात्तत् सामान्यमिति स्मृतम् ॥<BR> K. P. 10. 10 A general statement or expression; न सामान्यं विशेषानभिवदति<BR> ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यम्
सामान्य + .{@-न्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> jointly, in common; तैः सार्धं चिन्तयेन्नित्यं<BR> सामान्यं संधिविग्रहम् Ms. 7. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्या
सामान्य + .{@-न्या@} A harlot, prostitute.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामान्यज्ञानम्, सामान्यपक्षः, सामान्यपदार्थः, सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकम्, सामान्यलक्षणम्, सामान्यवचन, सामान्यवनिता, सामान्यवाचिन्, सामान्यशासनम्, सामान्यशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यज्ञानम्
सामान्य + -ज्ञानम् knowledge or perception of generic properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यपक्षः|सामान्यपक्ष
सामान्य + -पक्षः the mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यपदार्थः|सामान्यपदार्थ
सामान्य + -पदार्थः the category called सामान्य or generality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकम्
सामान्य + -प्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकम् <i>ind.</i> with equal respect; Ś. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यलक्षणम्
सामान्य + -लक्षणम् a generic definition; इति द्रव्यसामान्यलक्षणानि Tarka K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यवचन
सामान्य + -वचन <i>a.</i> expressing a common property; P. II. 1. 55.<BR>—2 expressing a general notion; III. 4. 5.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">Page1671-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यवचनम्
सामान्य + -वचन + .({@-नम्@}) a substantive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यवनिता
सामान्य + -वनिता a common woman, prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यवाचिन्
सामान्य + -वाचिन् <i>a.</i> expressive of generality or genus; न हि सामान्यवाची<BR> शब्दो विशेषानभिवदति ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यशासनम्
सामान्य + -शासनम् an edict applicable to all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यशास्त्रम्
सामान्य + -शास्त्रम् a general rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यतः
सामान्यतः <i>ind.</i> Commonly, generally, usually.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामान्यतोदृष्टम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यतोदृष्टम्
सामान्यतः + सामान्यतोदृष्टम् (in logic) a kind of inference (neither deduced from the<BR> relation of cause to effect, nor from that of effect to cause); सामान्यतोदृष्टं<BR> च यदव्यभिचारि तत् प्रमाणम् ŚB. on MS. 7. 4. 12. ˚सम्बन्धम् variety<BR> of अनुमान where the connection between the लिङ्ग and the लिङ्गिन्<BR> or साध्य is not directly perceptible; सामान्यतोदृष्टसम्बन्धं यथा<BR> देवदत्तस्य गतिपूर्विकां देशान्तरप्राप्तिमुपलभ्य आदित्यगतिस्मरणम्<BR> ŚB. on MS. 1. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामायिकम्
सामायिकम्<BR>—1 Equanimity.<BR>—2 A deed (of property accrued from common business); मेलयित्वा स्वधनांशान्<BR> व्यवहाराय साधकाः । कुर्वन्ति लेखपत्रं यत्तच्च सामायिकं स्मृतम् ॥<BR> Śukra. 2. 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिक
सामासिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Comprehensive, comprehending the whole, collective.<BR>—2 Condensed, concise, brief; एष सामासिको नयः Ms. 7. 180.<BR>—3 Relating to a compound word.<BR>—4 Compounded, composite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिकम्
सामासिक + .{@-कम्@} The whole class of compounds; द्वन्द्वः सामासिकस्य च Bg. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामि
सामि <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Half <i>i. e.</i> unfinished; अभिवीक्ष्य सामिकृतमण्डनं यतीः कररुद्धनीविगलदंशुकाः<BR> स्त्रियः Śi. 13. 31; R. 19. 16.<BR>—2 Blamable, vile, contemptible.<BR>—3 Too soon, prematurely.<BR>—4 Imperfectly. [Cf. L. <i>semi-</i>; Gr. <i>hemi-</i>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिकः|सामिक
सामिकः A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामित
सामित <i>a.</i> Mixed with wheat-flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेनी
सामिधेनी [सम् + इन्ध् करणे ल्युट् नि˚]<BR>—1 A kind of prayer recited while the sacrificial fire is being kindled<BR> or fed with fuel; विधिविहितविरिब्धैः सामिधेनीरधीत्य Śi. 11. 41.<BR>—2 Fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिष
सामिष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of flesh.<BR>—2 Provided with meat; मध्यंदिनेऽर्धरात्रे च श्राद्धं भुक्त्वा च सामिषम् Ms. 4. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीची
सामीची<BR>—1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>—2 Decency, politeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीचीन्यम्
सामीचीन्यम् Propriety, fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्यम्
सामीप्यम्<BR>—1 Vicinity, nearness, proximity.<BR>—2 Nearness to the deity (one of the four states of beatitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्यः|सामीप्य|सामीप्यं
सामीप्यम् + .{@-प्यः@} A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्गः|सामुद्ग
सामुद्गः A joint with cup-like socket <i>e. g.</i> the shoulder-joint, hip-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्गम्
सामुद्गः + .{@-द्गम्@} Medicine taken before and after a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुदायिक
सामुदायिक <i>a.</i> Collective, belonging to a multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र <i>a.</i> (-द्री <i>f.</i>) [समुद्रे भवः अण्] Sea-born,<BR> marine, as in सामुद्रं लवणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रः|सामुद्र|सामुद्रं
सामुद्र + .{@-द्रः@} A mariner, voyager; a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">Page1672-1</a>]<BR> sea-faring merchant; कोट्यापरान्ताः सामुद्रा रत्नान्युपहरन्तु ते Rām. 2. 82. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रम्
सामुद्र + .{@-द्रम्@}<BR>—1 Sea-salt.<BR>—2 The cuttle-fish bone.<BR>—3 A mark or spot on the body.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सामुद्रनिष्कुटाः, सामुद्रबन्धुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1671-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रनिष्कुटाः
सामुद्र + -निष्कुटाः inhabitants of the sea-coast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रबन्धुः|सामुद्रबन्धु
सामुद्र + -बन्धुः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रकम्
सामुद्रकम्<BR>—1 Sea-salt.<BR>—2 The science of palmistry;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रकः|सामुद्रक|सामुद्रकं
सामुद्रकम् + .{@-कः@} See सामुद्रः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
सामुद्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) [समुद्रेण प्रोक्तं वेत्त्यधीते वा ठञ्]<BR>—1 Sea-born, oceanic.<BR>—2 Sea-faring; सामुद्रिकान् सवणिजस्ततोऽपश्यत् स्थितान् पथि Mb. 12. 169. 2.<BR>—2 Relating to marks on the body (which are supposed to indicate good<BR> or bad fortune).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिकः|सामुद्रिक
सामुद्रिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 One who is acquainted with palmistry, who knows how to interpret the<BR> various marks on the body.<BR>—2 A fortune-teller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिकम्
सामुद्रिक + .{@-कम्@} The science of palmistry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामूना
सामूना A black-coloured deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामूरम्
सामूरम् Leather from the Bahlava country; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामूली
सामूली A kind of leather from the Bahlava country; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामूहिक|सामूहिकः
सामूहिक <i>a.</i> Collected in masses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामूहिकः|सामूहिक
सामूहिक + .{@-कः@} a suffix forming collective nouns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामेधिक
सामेधिक <i>a.</i> One possessed of preternatural powers; असौ सिद्धः<BR> सामेधिकः Kau. A. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपराय|साम्पराय|सांपरायः
सांपराय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to war, warlike.<BR>—2 Relating to the other world, future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायः|साम्पराय|सांपराय
सांपराय + .{@-यः, -यम्@}<BR>—1 Conflict, contention.<BR>—2 Future life, the future; योगिनां सांपरायविधिमनुशिक्षयन् Bhāg. 5. 6. 6.<BR>—3 The means of attaining the future world.<BR>—4 Inquiry into the future; यस्य प्रमाणं भृगवः सांपराये Bhāg. 8. 19. 2.<BR>—5 Inquiry, investigation.<BR>—6 Uncertainty.<BR>—7 A helper; Mb. 1. 3. 58.<BR>—8 Need, distress, calamity; उक्तपूर्वं कुतो राजन् सांपराये स वक्ष्यति Mb. 1. 48. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायम्
सांपराय + .{@-यः, -यम्@}<BR>—1 Conflict, contention.<BR>—2 Future life, the future; योगिनां सांपरायविधिमनुशिक्षयन् Bhāg. 5. 6. 6.<BR>—3 The means of attaining the future world.<BR>—4 Inquiry into the future; यस्य प्रमाणं भृगवः सांपराये Bhāg. 8. 19. 2.<BR>—5 Inquiry, investigation.<BR>—6 Uncertainty.<BR>—7 A helper; Mb. 1. 3. 58.<BR>—8 Need, distress, calamity; उक्तपूर्वं कुतो राजन् सांपराये स वक्ष्यति Mb. 1. 48. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायिक|साम्परायिक|साम्परायिकं|सांपरायिकः
सांपरायिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Warlike; relating to or prepared for battle; पित्रा संवर्धितो नित्यं<BR> कृतास्रः सांपरायिकः R. 7. 62.<BR>—2 Military, strategic; सांपरायिकः (दुर्गः) Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR>—3 Calamitous.<BR>—4 Relating to the other world; द्वे चान्ते सांपरायिके Mb. 3. 314. 9.<BR>—5 Obsequial; भ्रातुर्ज्येष्ठस्य पुत्रेण यदुक्तं सांपरायिकम् (कुरु)<BR> A. Rām. 4. 3. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायिकम्
सांपरायिक + .{@-कम्@} War, battle, conflict; कुर्वाणानां सांपरायान्तरायम् Śi. 18. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायिकः|साम्परायिक|सांपरायिक|साम्परायिकं
सांपरायिक + .{@-कः@} A war-chariot.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सांपरायिककल्पः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायिककल्पः|साम्परायिककल्प|सांपरायिककल्प
सांपरायिक + -कल्पः a strategic array (of troops).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रत
सांप्रत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Fit, proper, suitable; रामाल्लब्धसमस्तहेतिगुरुणो वीर्यस्य यत्<BR> सांप्रतम् Ve. 3. 5.<BR>—2 Relevant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रतम्|साम्प्रतम्
सांप्रत + .{@-तम्@} <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Now, at this time; हन्त स्थानं क्रोधस्य सांप्रतं देव्याः Ve. 1.<BR>—2 Immediately.<BR>—3 Fitly, properly, seasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रतिक|साम्प्रतिक
सांप्रतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to the present time.<BR>—2 Fit, proper, right; U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रदायिक|साम्प्रदायिक
सांप्रदायिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Relating to he traditional<BR> doctrine, handed down by successive traditon, traditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रियक|साम्प्रियक
सांप्रियक <i>a.</i> Inhabited by people who are dear to one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बः|साम्ब|सांब|सांबः
साम्बः N. of Siva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांबन्धिक|साम्बन्धिक|सांबंधिक
सांबन्धिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Arising from relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांबन्धिकम्
सांबन्धिक + .{@-कम्@} Relationship, alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बरम्
साम्बरम् Salt produced in Sambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्बरी|सांबरी
साम्बरी<BR>—1 A sorceress.<BR>—2 Sorcery; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्भवी|सांभवी
साम्भवी<BR>—1 The red Lodhra tree.<BR>—2 Possibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांमुखी|साम्मुखी
सांमुखी A तिथि or lunar day lasting till evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांमुख्यम्
सांमुख्यम्<BR>—1 Presence.<BR>—2 Favour, countenance, propitiousness.<BR>—3 The state of being in front; न सांमुख्ये गुरोः स्थेयम् Śukra. 3. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यम्
साम्यम्, -ता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Equality, sameness, evenness; प्रवृत्तं कर्म संसेव्य देवानामेति<BR> साम्यताम् Ms. 12. 90; भवन्ति साम्येऽपि निविष्टचेतसाम् Ku. 5. 31.<BR>—2 Likeness, resemblance, similarity; स्पष्टं प्रापत् साम्यमुर्वीधरस्य<BR> Śi. 18. 38; H. 1. 45; Ki. 17. 51.<BR>—3 Equability.<BR>—4 Concord, harmony.<BR>—5 Indifference, impartiality, sameness of view; येषां साम्ये स्थितं<BR> मनः Bg. 5. 19.<BR>—6 Measure, time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साम्यग्राहः, साम्यतालविशारद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यता
साम्यम्, -ता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Equality, sameness, evenness; प्रवृत्तं कर्म संसेव्य देवानामेति<BR> साम्यताम् Ms. 12. 90; भवन्ति साम्येऽपि निविष्टचेतसाम् Ku. 5. 31.<BR>—2 Likeness, resemblance, similarity; स्पष्टं प्रापत् साम्यमुर्वीधरस्य<BR> Śi. 18. 38; H. 1. 45; Ki. 17. 51.<BR>—3 Equability.<BR>—4 Concord, harmony.<BR>—5 Indifference, impartiality, sameness of view; येषां साम्ये स्थितं<BR> मनः Bg. 5. 19.<BR>—6 Measure, time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साम्यग्राहः, साम्यतालविशारद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यत्वम्
साम्यम्, -ता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Equality, sameness, evenness; प्रवृत्तं कर्म संसेव्य देवानामेति<BR> साम्यताम् Ms. 12. 90; भवन्ति साम्येऽपि निविष्टचेतसाम् Ku. 5. 31.<BR>—2 Likeness, resemblance, similarity; स्पष्टं प्रापत् साम्यमुर्वीधरस्य<BR> Śi. 18. 38; H. 1. 45; Ki. 17. 51.<BR>—3 Equability.<BR>—4 Concord, harmony.<BR>—5 Indifference, impartiality, sameness of view; येषां साम्ये स्थितं<BR> मनः Bg. 5. 19.<BR>—6 Measure, time.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साम्यग्राहः, साम्यतालविशारद<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यग्राहः|साम्यग्राह
साम्यम् + -ग्राहः one who beats time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यतालविशारद
साम्यम् + -तालविशारद <i>a.</i> one versed in time and measure; गीतवादित्रकुशलाः<BR> साम्यतालविशारदाः Mb. 2. 4. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्यम्
साम्राज्यम्<BR>—1 Universal or complete sovereignty, imperial away; साम्राज्यशंसिनो<BR> भावाः कुशस्य च लवस्य च U. 6. 23; R. 4. 5.<BR>—2 Empire, dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राणिकर्दमम्
साम्राणिकर्दमम् A kind of fragrance, civet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायः|साय|सायं
सायः [सो-घञ्]<BR>—1 End, close, termination.<BR>—2 Close of day, evening.<BR>—3 An arrow, a missile. (साये ‘in the evening, at the close of the day’.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सायाशनम्, सायाहन्, सायारम्भ, सायधूर्तः, सायमण्डनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायाशनम्
सायः + -अशनम् an evening meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायाहन्
सायः + -अहन् <i>m.</i> (forming सायाह्नः) evening, evening time; सायाहनि<BR> प्रणयिनो भवनं व्रजन्त्याश्चेतो न कस्य हरते गतिरङ्गनायाः Bv. 2. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायारम्भ
सायः + -आरम्भ <i>a.</i> beginning in the evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायधूर्तः|सायधूर्त
सायः + -धूर्तः<BR>—1 a rogue, a cheat or deceiver in the form of evening.<BR>—2 The moon; आदत्त दीप्रं मणिमम्बरस्य दत्त्वा यदस्मै खलु सायधूर्तः N. 22. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायमण्डनम्
सायः + -मण्डनम् sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायंतन|सायन्तन|सायन्तनः
सायंतन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to the evening, evening; सायंतने सवनकर्मणि<BR> संप्रवृत्ते Ś. 3. 27; अलिनारमतालिनी शिलीन्ध्रे सह सायंतनदीपपाटलाभे Śi. 6. 72.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सायंतनमल्लिका, सायंतनसमयः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायंतनमल्लिका|सायन्तनमल्लिका
सायंतन + -मल्लिका evening jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायंतनसमयः|सायन्तनसमय
सायंतन + -समयः eventide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायम्
सायम् <i>ind.</i> In the evening; प्रयता प्रातरन्वेतु सायं प्रत्युद्व्रजेदपि R. 1. 90, 48.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सायकालः, सायधृतिः, सायप्रातर्, सायभोजनम्, सायमण्डनम्, सायसंध्या<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकालः
सायम् + -कालः evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायधृतिः
सायम् + -धृतिः <i>f.</i> the evening oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायप्रातर्
सायम् + -प्रातर् <i>ind.</i> in the evening and morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायभोजनम्
सायम् + -भोजनम् an evening meal; Kull. on Ms. 3. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायमण्डनम्
सायम् + -मण्डनम्<BR>—1 sunset.<BR>—2 the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायसंध्या
सायम् + -संध्या<BR>—1 the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">Page1673-1</a>]<BR> evening twilight.<BR>—2 the evening prayer.<BR>—3 the goddess to be worshipped in the evening. ˚देवता N. of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1672-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकः|सायक
सायकः [सो-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 An arrow; तत् साधुकृतसंधानं प्रतिसंहर सायकम् Ś. 1. 11.<BR>—2 A sword.<BR>—3 The number ‘five’.<BR>—4 The latitude of the sky.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सायकपुङ्खः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकपुङ्खः|सायकपुङ्ख|सायकपुंख
सायकः + -पुङ्खः the feathered part of an arrow; सक्ताङ्गुलिः सायकपुङ्ख<BR> एव R. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायणः|सायण
सायणः N. of a very learned Brāhmaṇa and a Vedic commentator,<BR> supposed to have flourished about 1370 A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायनम्
सायनम् The longitude of a planet reckoned from the vernal equinoctial point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायिका
सायिका <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Position in due order (= क्रमस्थितिः).<BR>—2 A dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायिन्
सायिन् <i>m.</i> A horseman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुज्यम्
सायुज्यम्<BR>—1 Intimate union, identification, absorption, especially into a deity<BR> (one of the four states of <i>Mukti</i>); सायुज्यं सलोकतां जयति य<BR> एवमेतत् साम वेद Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 22.<BR>—2 Similarity, likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुध
सायुध <i>a.</i> Armed.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सायुधप्रग्रह<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुधप्रग्रह
सायुध + -प्रग्रह <i>a.</i> holding weapons in the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार <i>a.</i> [सृ-घञ्, सार्-अच् वा]<BR>—1 Essential.<BR>—2 Best, highest, most excellent; एतद्वः सारफल्गुत्वं बीजयोन्योः प्रकीर्तितम्<BR> Ms. 9. 56; द्वयोः सारं तुल्यं द्वितयमभियुक्तेन मनसा Mu. 1. 13.<BR>—3 Real, true, genuine.<BR>—4 Strong, vigorous; सारबलम् Kau. A. 10; सुयुद्धकामुकं सारमसारं<BR> विपरीतकम् Śukra. 4. 872.<BR>—5 Sound, thoroughly proved.<BR>—6 Highest or best (at the end of comp.); त्रिवर्गसारः Ku. 5. 38.<BR>—7 Just, right; पृथोस्तत् सूक्तमाकर्ण्य सारं सुष्ठु मितं मधु Bhāg. 4. 22. 17.<BR>—8 Speckled, motley.<BR>—9 Driving away; सोऽयं दिधक्षोर्दावपावकस्य गरिमसारः सीकरासारः<BR> B. R. 2. 60/61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारः|सार|सारं
सार + .{@-रः, -रम्@} (but usually <i>m.</i> only except in the first 4 senses)<BR>—1 Essence, essential part, quintessence; स्नेहस्य तत् फलमसौ प्रणयस्य<BR> सारः Māl. 1. 9; U. 6. 22; असारे खलु संसारे सारमेतच्चतुष्टयम् ।<BR> काश्यां वासः सतां संगो गङ्गाम्भः शंभुसेवनम् ॥ Dharm. 14.<BR>—2 Substance, pith.<BR>—3 Marrow; निःशेषं शकलितवल्कलाङ्गसारैः Ki. 17. 62.<BR>—4 Real truth, main point.<BR>—5 The sap or essence of trees; as in खदिरसार, सर्जसार.<BR>—6 Summary, epitome, compendium.<BR>—7 Strength, vigour, power, energy; सारं धरित्रीधरणक्षमं च Ku. 1. 17;<BR> R. 2. 74.<BR>—8 Prowess, heroism, courage; राज्ञा हिमवतः सारो राज्ञः सारो हिमाद्रिणा R. 4. 79.<BR>—9 Firmness, hardness.<BR>—10 Wealth, riches; गामात्तसाराम् R. 5. 26.<BR>—11 Nectar.<BR>—12 Fresh butter.<BR>—13 Air, wind.<BR>—14 Cream, coagulum of curds.<BR>—15 Disease.<BR>—16 Matter, pus.<BR>—17 Worth, excellence, highest perception.<BR>—18 A man at chess.<BR>—19 Impure carbonate of soda.<BR>—20 A figure of speech corresponding to English ‘climax’; उत्तरोत्तरमुत्कर्षो<BR> भवेत् सारः परावधिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">Page1673-2</a>]<BR> K. P. 10.<BR>—21 The heart.<BR>—22 Course, motion.<BR>—23 Extension.<BR>—24 Any or chief ingredient.<BR>—25 (In Rhet.) A kind of climax.<BR>—26 Dung.<BR>—27 Pus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारम्
सार + .{@-रः, -रम्@} (but usually <i>m.</i> only except in the first 4 senses)<BR>—1 Essence, essential part, quintessence; स्नेहस्य तत् फलमसौ प्रणयस्य<BR> सारः Māl. 1. 9; U. 6. 22; असारे खलु संसारे सारमेतच्चतुष्टयम् ।<BR> काश्यां वासः सतां संगो गङ्गाम्भः शंभुसेवनम् ॥ Dharm. 14.<BR>—2 Substance, pith.<BR>—3 Marrow; निःशेषं शकलितवल्कलाङ्गसारैः Ki. 17. 62.<BR>—4 Real truth, main point.<BR>—5 The sap or essence of trees; as in खदिरसार, सर्जसार.<BR>—6 Summary, epitome, compendium.<BR>—7 Strength, vigour, power, energy; सारं धरित्रीधरणक्षमं च Ku. 1. 17;<BR> R. 2. 74.<BR>—8 Prowess, heroism, courage; राज्ञा हिमवतः सारो राज्ञः सारो हिमाद्रिणा R. 4. 79.<BR>—9 Firmness, hardness.<BR>—10 Wealth, riches; गामात्तसाराम् R. 5. 26.<BR>—11 Nectar.<BR>—12 Fresh butter.<BR>—13 Air, wind.<BR>—14 Cream, coagulum of curds.<BR>—15 Disease.<BR>—16 Matter, pus.<BR>—17 Worth, excellence, highest perception.<BR>—18 A man at chess.<BR>—19 Impure carbonate of soda.<BR>—20 A figure of speech corresponding to English ‘climax’; उत्तरोत्तरमुत्कर्षो<BR> भवेत् सारः परावधिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">Page1673-2</a>]<BR> K. P. 10.<BR>—21 The heart.<BR>—22 Course, motion.<BR>—23 Extension.<BR>—24 Any or chief ingredient.<BR>—25 (In Rhet.) A kind of climax.<BR>—26 Dung.<BR>—27 Pus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारा
सार + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 Dūrvā grass.<BR>—2 Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारम्
सार + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Fitness, propriety.<BR>—3 Wood, thicket.<BR>—4 Steel.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सारापराधौ, सारासार, सारगन्धः, सारगात्र, सारगुणः, सारगुरु, सारग्रीवः, सारजम्, सारतरुः, सारदा, सारद्रुमः, सारफल्गु, सारभङ्गः, सारभाण्डम्, सारमार्गणम्, सारमितिः, सारयोध, सारलोहम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारापराधौ
सार + -अपराधौ <i>m.</i> <i>du.</i> the ability (of a criminal to suffer) and<BR> the nature of crime; the greatness of the crime; सारापराधौ चालेक्य दण्डं<BR> दण्ड्येषु पातयेत् Ms. 8. 126; cf. 9. 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारासार
सार + -असार <i>a.</i> valuable and worthless, strong and weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारासारम्
सार + -असार + ({@-रम्@})<BR>—1 worth and worthlessness; सारासारं च भाण्डानाम् Ms. 9. 331.<BR>—2 substance and emptiness.<BR>—3 strength and weakness. ˚विचारः consideration of strong and weak points &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारगन्धः|सारगन्ध|सारगंध
सार + -गन्धः sandalwood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारगात्र
सार + -गात्र <i>a.</i> strong-limbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारगुणः|सारगुण
सार + -गुणः a principal virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारगुरु
सार + -गुरु <i>a.</i> heavy with weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1673-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारग्रीवः|सारग्रीव
