सार्प्यः|सार्प्य
सार्पः(र्प्यः) N. of the constellation Āśleṣā; सार्पे<BR> जातौ तु सौमित्री कुलीरेऽभ्युदिते रवौ Rām. 1. 18. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष|सार्पिषः
सार्पिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>), सार्पिष्क (-ष्की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Dressed or cooked with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिषी
सार्पिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>), सार्पिष्क (-ष्की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Dressed or cooked with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष्क|सार्पिष्कं
सार्पिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>), सार्पिष्क (-ष्की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Dressed or cooked with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष्की
सार्पिष <i>a.</i> (-षी <i>f.</i>), सार्पिष्क (-ष्की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Dressed or cooked with clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्य
सार्य <i>a.</i> That which may be dropped (in pronunciation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व|सार्वः|सार्व्व|सार्व्वः
सार्व <i>a.</i> (-र्वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 General, universal.<BR>—2 Fit or suitable for all; संभवन्ति यददोषदूषिते सार्व सर्वगुणसंपदस्त्वयि Śi. 14. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वः|सार्व|सार्व्व|सार्व्वः
सार्व + .{@-र्वः@} A Buddhist or Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकामिक|सार्व्वकामिक
सार्वकामिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Satisfying every desire, granting all wishes; तीर्थमस्ति<BR> न भवार्णवबाह्यं सार्वकामिकमृते भवतस्तत् Ki. 18. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकाल
सार्वकाल <i>a.</i> Taking place at all times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकालिक|सार्व्वकालिक
सार्वकालिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Eternal, everlasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वचर्मीण
सार्वचर्मीण <i>a.</i> Wholly made of leather; P. V. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिकः
सार्वजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), सार्वजनीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>), सार्वजन्य <i>a.</i><BR> Public, universal, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनिकी
सार्वजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), सार्वजनीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>), सार्वजन्य <i>a.</i><BR> Public, universal, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनीन|सार्व्वजनीन|सार्व्वजनीनः
सार्वजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), सार्वजनीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>), सार्वजन्य <i>a.</i><BR> Public, universal, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनीनी
सार्वजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), सार्वजनीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>), सार्वजन्य <i>a.</i><BR> Public, universal, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजन्य
सार्वजनिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>), सार्वजनीन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>), सार्वजन्य <i>a.</i><BR> Public, universal, general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वज्ञम्
सार्वज्ञम् Omniscience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वत्रिक|सार्व्वत्रिक
सार्वत्रिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to every place, general, applicable to<BR> all places or circumstances; as in सार्वत्रिको नियमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वधातुक|सार्व्वधातुक
सार्वधातुक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Applicable to the whole of<BR> a radical term, or to the complete form of the verbal base after the conjugational<BR> characteristics have been affixed, <i>i. e.</i> to the four conjugational<BR> or special tenses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वधातुकम्
सार्वधातुक + .{@-कम्@} N. of the verbal terminations of the four conjugational tenses<BR> (strictly, the personal terminations of all tenses and moods except the<BR> Perfect and Benedictive and the affixes distinguished by a mute श्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौतिक|सार्व्वभौतिक
सार्वभौतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging or relating to all elements or beings.<BR>—2 Comprising all animate beings; त्रिविधस्त्रिविधः कृस्त्नः संसारः<BR> सार्वभौतिकः Ms. 12. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौम|सार्वभौमः|सार्व्वभौम|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्वभौम <i>a.</i> (-मी <i>f.</i>) Relating to, consisting of,<BR> the whole earth, universal.<BR>—2 Relating to all conditions of the mind; Yoga S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौमः|सार्वभौम|सार्व्वभौम|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्वभौम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 An emperor, a universal monarch; नाज्ञाभङ्गं सहन्ते नृवर नृपतयस्त्वादृशाः<BR> सार्वभौमाः Mu. 3. 22.<BR>—2 N. of the elephant presiding over the north, the quarter of Kubera.<BR>—3 An emperor with a revenue of fifty crores (of कर्ष); पञ्चाशत्कोटिपर्यन्तः<BR> सार्वभौमस्ततः परम् । सप्तद्वीपा च पृथिवी यस्य वश्या भवेत् सदा ॥<BR> Śukra. 1. 186.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौमम्
सार्वभौमम् Universal empire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वयौगिक
सार्वयौगिक <i>a.</i> Useful in diseases of every kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वरात्रिक
सार्वरात्रिक <i>a.</i> Lasting the whole night (as a lamp).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिकः
सार्वलौकिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>) Known to all people, prevailing<BR> throughout the whole world, public, universal; अनुरागप्रवादस्तु वत्सयोः<BR> सार्वलौकिकः Māl. 1. 13; जिगाय तस्य हन्तारं स रामः सार्वलौकिकम् Bk. 5. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववर्णिक|सार्व्ववर्णिक
सार्ववर्णिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Of every kind or sort; सार्ववर्णिकमन्नाद्यं सन्नीयाप्लाव्य वारिणा Ms. 3. 244.<BR>—2 Belonging to every tribe or class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वविद्यम्
सार्वविद्यम् Omniscience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वविभक्तिक|सार्व्वविभक्तिक
सार्वविभक्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Applicable or belonging to all the cases of a noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेदसः|सार्ववेदस|सार्व्ववेदस
सार्ववेदसः One who gives away all his wealth at a sacrifice or sacred rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेदसम्
सार्ववेदसः + .{@-सम्@} A personʼs entire property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववैद्यः
सार्ववैद्यः A Brāhmaṇa conversant with all the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववैद्यम्
सार्ववैद्यः + .{@-द्यम्@} All the Vedas collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वसहः|सार्वसह
सार्वसहः A kind of salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षप|सार्षपः
सार्षप <i>a.</i> (-पी <i>f.</i>) Made of mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षपम्
सार्षप + .{@-पम्@} Mustard-oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1675-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टि
सार्ष्टि <i>a.</i> Possessing the same station, condition, or rank, having<BR> the same power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टिता
सार्ष्टिता<BR>—1 Equality in rank, condition, or power; देवतानां सलोकतां सार्ष्टितां<BR> सायुज्यं गच्छति Ch. Up. 2. 20. 2.<BR>—2 Equality with the Supreme Being in power and all the divine attributes,<BR> the last of the four states or grades of <i>Mukti</i>; ब्रह्मदो ब्रह्मसार्ष्टितां<BR> (प्राप्नोति) Ms. 4. 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्ट्यम्
सार्ष्ट्यम् The fourth grade of <i>Mukti</i>; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालः|साल
सालः<BR>—1 N. of a tree or its resin; Bhāg. 8. 2. 12.<BR>—2 A tree in general, as in कल्पसाल, रसालसाल; सायंतनाभ्रसमशोभमशोकसालम्<BR> Rām. Ch. 5. 22; आकाशमार्गेऽभिकुलायसालं मन्दं विचेलुर्मधुरं रुवन्तः<BR> <i>ibid.</i> 6. 4.<BR>—3 A rampart, a fence or wall round a building.<BR>—4 A wall in general.<BR>—5 A kind of fish. (For compounds see under शाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालंकार
सालंकार <i>a.</i> Decorated, adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालनः|सालन
सालनः<BR>—1 The resin of the Sāla tree.<BR>—2 Resin in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालस
सालस <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Languid, tired.<BR>—2 Indolent, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साला
साला<BR>—1 A wall, rampart.<BR>—2 A house, an apartment; see शाला.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सालाकरी, सालावृकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालाकरी
साला + -करी<BR>—1 a house-worker.<BR>—2 a male captive (particularly one taken in battle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालावृकः|सालावृक
साला + -वृकः see शालावृक; वृकसालावृकादिभ्यो भयमाशंसमानः Bhāg. 5. 8. 12, 8. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालारम्
सालारम् A peg projecting from a wall, bracket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालिका
सालिका A flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालूरः|सालूर
सालूरः A frog; see शालूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालेयम्
सालेयम् A kind of fennel; see शालेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्यम्
सालोक्यम्<BR>—1 Being in the same world or sphere with another.<BR>—2 Residence in the same heaven with any deity, (one of the four stages of beatitude).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोहितः|सालोहित
सालोहितः A kinsman; Buddh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्वः|साल्व
साल्वः<BR>—1 N. of a country, or its inhabitants (pl. in this sense).<BR>—2 N. of a demon slain by Viṣṇu.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साल्वहन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्वहन्
साल्वः + -हन् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्विकः|साल्विक
साल्विकः The bird called सारिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावः|साव
सावः A libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावक|सावकः
सावक <i>a.</i> (-विका <i>f.</i>)<BR> Productive, generative, causing birth, obstetric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावकः|सावक
सावक + .{@-कः@} The young of an animal; (for शावक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावकाश
सावकाश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having leisure, at leisure, unengaged.<BR>—2 Applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावकाशम्
सावकाश + .{@-शम्@} <i>ind.</i> Leisurely, at oneʼs convenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावग्रह
सावग्रह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having the mark called <i>avagraha</i> q. v.<BR>—2 Restrained, limited.<BR>—3 Analyzed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावज्ञ
सावज्ञ <i>a.</i> Despising, disdainful, feeling contempt; यः सावज्ञो<BR> माधवश्रीनियोगे पुष्पैः शंसत्यादरं त्वत्प्रयत्ने M. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावद्यम्
सावद्यम् (<i>i. e.</i> ऐश्वर्यम्) One of the three kinds of power<BR> attainable by an ascetic, (the other two being निरवद्य and सूक्ष्म).<BR>━<i>a.</i> Objectionable blamable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधान|सावधानः
सावधान <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Attentive, bestowing attention, careful, heedful.<BR>—2 Cautious.<BR>—3 Diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधानम्
सावधान + .{@-नम्@} <i>ind.</i> Carefully, attentively, cautiously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधारण
सावधारण <i>a.</i> Limited, restricted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधि
सावधि <i>a.</i> Having a bound or limit, limited, finite, defined,<BR> circumscribed; सावधिस्तोयराशिस्तें यशोराशेस्तु नावधिः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन|सावनं|सावनः
सावन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सवनं यागाङ्गं स्नानं सोमनिष्पीडनं वा तस्येदमण्]<BR> Relating to, or comprising, the three <i>savanas</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावनः|सावन|सावनं
सावन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 An institutor of a sacrifice, or one who employs priests at a sacrifice.<BR>—2 The conclusion of a sacrifice, or the ceremony by which it is concluded.<BR>—3 N. of Varuṇa.<BR>—4 A month of thirty solar days.<BR>—5 A natural day from sunrise to sunset.<BR>—6 A particular kind of year.<BR>—7 The Solar year; विचाली हि संवत्सरशब्दः सावनोऽपि गणितदिवसकः<BR> etc. ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावनम्
सावन + .{@-नम्@} The correct solar time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावमर्द
सावमर्द <i>a.</i> Disagreeable, contradictory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावयव
सावयव <i>a.</i> Composed of parts; सावयवत्वे चानित्यप्रसंगः,<BR> न ह्यविद्याकल्पितेन रूपभेदेन सावयवं वस्तु संपद्यते Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावरः|सावर
सावरः<BR>—1 Fault, offence.<BR>—2 Sin, wickedness, crime.<BR>—3 The Lodhra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावरण
सावरण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Clandestine, concealed, secret.<BR>—2 Covered, closed, shut; लब्धान्तरा सावरणेऽपि गेहे योगप्रभावो न<BR> च लक्ष्यते ते R. 16. 7.<BR>—3 Fenced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण|सावर्णः
सावर्ण <i>a.</i> (-र्णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating or belonging to one of the same colour,<BR> tribe or caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णः|सावर्ण
सावर्ण + .{@-र्णः@} A metronymic of the eighth Manu; see सावर्णि.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सावर्णलक्ष्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णलक्ष्यम्
सावर्ण + -लक्ष्यम्<BR>—1 a mark of the sameness of colour or caste.<BR>—2 skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णिः|सावर्णि
सावर्णिः A metronymic of the eighth Manu (son of the sun by Savarṇā);<BR> सावर्णिः सूर्यतनयो यो मनुः कथ्यतेऽष्टमः Mārk. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णिक
सावर्णिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the same tribe or caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण्यम्
सावर्ण्यम्<BR>—1 Sameness of colour.<BR>—2 Identity of class or caste.<BR>—3 The age or <i>Manvantara</i> presided over by the eighth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलेप
सावलेप <i>a.</i> Full of pride, proud, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलेपम्
सावलेप + .{@-पम्@} <i>ind.</i> Proudly, haughtily, arrogantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेष
सावशेष <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a remainder, leaving a remainder or residue.<BR>—2 Imperfect, incomplete, unfinished.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सावशेषजीवित, सावशेषबन्धन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेषजीवित
सावशेष + -जीवित <i>a.</i> having yet time to live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेषबन्धन
सावशेष + -बन्धन <i>a.</i> still bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1676-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टम्भ|सावष्टंभ
सावष्टम्भ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proud, dignified, noble, majestic.<BR>—2 Courageous, resolute.<BR>—3 Bold, vigorous, vehement; सावष्टम्भनिशुम्भसंभ्रमनमत् … … Māl. 5. 22.<BR>—4 Full of firmness; सभायां वक्ति सामर्षः सावष्टम्भो नरः शुचिः Pt. 1. 200.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टम्भम्
सावष्टम्भ + .{@-म्भम्@} <i>ind.</i> Resolutely, firmly, courageously.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सावष्टम्भवास्तु<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टम्भवास्तु
सावष्टम्भ + -वास्तु a house with an open side-gallery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेल
सावहेल <i>a.</i> Disdainful, disdaining, despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेलम्
सावहेल + .{@-लम्@} <i>ind.</i> Disdainfully, scornfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविका
साविका A midwife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्र|सावित्रं|सावित्रः
सावित्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सविता देवताऽस्य अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to the sun; Mb. 7. 157. 34.<BR>—2 Descended from the sun, belonging to the solar dynasty (of kings);<BR> यत् सावित्रैर्दीपितं भूमिपालैः U. 1. 42.<BR>—3 Accompanied by the <i>Gāyatree</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रः|सावित्र|सावित्रं
सावित्र + .{@-त्रः@}<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 An embryo or foetus.<BR>—3 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—4 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>—5 Of Karṇa; भ्राता भ्रातरमज्ञातं सावित्रः पाकशासनिम् (अब्रवीत्)<BR> Mb. 1. 136. 8, 13. 138. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रम्
सावित्र + .{@-त्रम्@}<BR>—1 The sacrificial thread (so called because the repetition of the <i>Gāyatree</i><BR> forms a principal part of the ceremony of putting on the sacred thread);<BR> शान्तिहोमांश्च कुर्वीत सावित्राणि च धारयेत् Mb. 13. 104. 60.<BR>—2 The initiation into membership of the द्विज classes (by performing<BR> the thread ceremony); Bhāg. 3. 12. 42.<BR>—3 N. of the constellation Hasta; पञ्चतारेण संयुक्तः सावित्रेणैव<BR> चन्द्रमाः Mb. 1. 135. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्री
सावित्री<BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 N. of a celebrated verse of the <i>Ṛgveda</i>, so called because it is<BR> addressed to the sun; it is also called गायत्री; q. v. for further information.<BR>—3 The ceremony of investiture with the sacred thread; आ षोडशाद् ब्राह्मणस्य<BR> सावित्री नातिवर्तते Ms. 2. 38.<BR>—4 N. of a wife of Brahman.<BR>—5 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>—6 N. of a wife of Kaśyapa.<BR>—7 An epithet of Sūryā (daughter of Savitṛ).<BR>—8 N. of the wife of Satyavat, king of Sālva. [She was the only daughter<BR> of king Aśvapati. She was so lovely that all the suitors that came to<BR> woo her were repulsed by her superior lustre, and thus though she reached<BR> a marriageable age, she found no one ready to espouse her. At last her<BR> father asked her to go and find out a husband of her own choice. She did<BR> so, and having made her selection returned to her father, and told him<BR> that she had chosen Satyavat, son of Dyumatsena, King of Sālva, who being<BR> driven out from his kingdom was then leading a hermitʼs life along with<BR> his wife. When Nārada, who happened to be present there, heard this,<BR> he told her as well as Aśvapati that he was very sorry to hear of the<BR> choice she had made, for though Satyavat was in every way worthy of her,<BR> yet he was fated to die in a year from that date, and in choosing him,<BR> therefore, Sāvitrī would be only choosing life-long widow-hood and misery.<BR> Her parents, therefore, naturally tried to dissuade her mind, but the<BR> high-souled maiden<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">Page1677-2</a>]<BR> told them that her choice was unalterably fixed. Accordingly the marriage<BR> took place in due time, and Sāvitrī laid aside her jewels and rich apparel,<BR> and putting on the coarse garments of hermits, spent her time in serving<BR> her old father and mother-in-law. Still, though outwardly happy, she could<BR> not forget the words of Nārada, and as she counted, the days seemed to<BR> fly swiftly like moments, and the fated time, when her husband was to<BR> die, drew near. ‘I have yet three days’ thought she, ‘and for these three days I shall observe a rigid fast’<BR>. She maintained her vow, and on the<BR> fourth day, when Satyavat was about to go to the woods to bring sacrificial<BR> fuel, she accompanied him. After having collected some fuel, Satyavat,<BR> being fatigued, sat down, and reposing his head on the bosom of Sāvitrī<BR> fell asleep. Just then Yama came down, snatched off his soul, and proceeded<BR> towards the south. Sāvitrī saw this and followed the god who told her<BR> to return as her husbandʼs term of life was over. But the faithful wife<BR> besought Yama in so pathetic a strain that he granted her boon after boon,<BR> except the life of her husband, until, being quite subdued by her devotion<BR> to her husband and the force of her eloquent appeal, the god relented<BR> and restored even the spirit of Satyavat to her. Delighted she returned,<BR> and found her husband as if roused from a deep sleep, and informing him<BR> of all that had occurred, went to the hermitage of her father-in-law who<BR> soon reaped the fruits of the boons of Yama. Sāvitrī is regarded as<BR> the <i>beau ideal</i> or highest pattern of conjugal fidelity, and a young<BR> married woman is usually blessed by elderly females with the words जन्मसावित्री<BR> भव, thus placing before her the example of Sāvitrī for life-long imitation.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सावित्रीपतितः, सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्टः, सावित्रीव्रतम्, सावित्रीसूत्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीपतितः|सावित्रीपतित
सावित्री + -पतितः, -परिभ्रष्टः a man of any one of the first three castes<BR> not invested with the sacred thread at the proper time; cf. व्रात्य;<BR> सावित्रीपतिता व्रात्या व्रात्यस्तोमादृते क्रतोः Y. 1. 38; Ms. 2. 39; तान्<BR> सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्टान् व्रात्यानिति विनिर्दिशेत् Ms. 10. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्टः|सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्ट
सावित्री + -पतितः, -परिभ्रष्टः a man of any one of the first three castes<BR> not invested with the sacred thread at the proper time; cf. व्रात्य;<BR> सावित्रीपतिता व्रात्या व्रात्यस्तोमादृते क्रतोः Y. 1. 38; Ms. 2. 39; तान्<BR> सावित्रीपरिभ्रष्टान् व्रात्यानिति विनिर्दिशेत् Ms. 10. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीव्रतम्
सावित्री + -व्रतम् N. of a particular fast kept by Hindu women on the last<BR> three days of the bright half of Jyeṣṭha to preserve them from widowhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्रीसूत्रम्
सावित्री + -सूत्रम् the sacred thread (यज्ञोपवीत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविनी
साविनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविष्कार
साविष्कार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Proud, haughty.<BR>—2 Manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावेगम्
सावेगम् <i>ind.</i> With excitement or agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशंस
साशंस <i>a.</i> Full of desire or passion, desirous, hopeful, expectant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशंसम्
साशंस + .{@-सम्@} <i>ind.</i> Wishfully, hopefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशङ्क|साशंक
साशङ्क <i>a.</i> Feeling fear, apprehensive, afraid, dismayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशङ्कता
साशङ्कता Fear, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1677-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशयन्दकः|साशयन्दक|साशयंदक|साशयंदकः
साशयन्दकः A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशूकः|साशूक
साशूकः A blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्य|साश्चर्य्य
साश्चर्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Wonderful, marvellous.<BR>—2 Struck with wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्यम्
साश्चर्य + .{@-र्यम्@} <i>ind.</i> With wonder or astonishment.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साश्चर्यचर्य<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्यचर्य
साश्चर्य + -चर्य <i>a.</i> of wonderful conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्र
साश्र(स्र) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having angles or corners, angular.<BR>—2 Tearful, weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्र
साश्र(स्र) <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having angles or corners, angular.<BR>—2 Tearful, weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रु
साश्रु <i>a.</i> Tearful, full of tears, shedding tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रुधी
साश्रुधी A wifeʼs or husbandʼs mother, a mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साष्टाङ्गम्|साष्टांगम्
साष्टाङ्गम् <i>ind.</i> With humble prostration of the body (by touching<BR> the earth with the eight members i. e. hands, breast, forehead, knees<BR> and feet); see अष्टाङ्गप्रणाम under अष्टन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास
सास^1 <i>a.</i> Having a bow; स सासिः सासुसूः सासो येयाययाययाययः Ki. 15. 5.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासहि
सासहि <i>a.</i> [सह्-यड्]<BR>—1 Able to bear; प्रयातु भारं स निवेश्य कस्मिन्नहिर्महीगौरवसासहिर्यः N. 10. 15.<BR>—2 Conquering, victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासार
सासार <i>a.</i> Rainy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासि
