सास्थिताम्रार्धम्
सास्थि + -ताम्रार्धम् a kind of amalgam of zinc and copper, bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्थिवधः|सास्थिवध
सास्थि + -वधः the killing of any animal having bones; किंचित् सास्थिवधे<BR> देयं प्राणायामस्त्वनस्थिके Y. 3. 275.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्थिस्वानम्
सास्थि + -स्वानम् <i>ind.</i> with the cracking sound of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्ना
सास्ना The dew-lap of an ox; गोः सास्नादिमत्त्वं लक्षणम् T. S.;<BR> रोमन्थमन्थरचलद्गुरुसास्नमासांचक्रे निमीलदलसेक्षणमौक्षकेण Śi. 5. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्यम्
साहचर्यम् Companionship, (constant) fellowship or association, living<BR> together, concomitance; किं न स्मरसि यदेकत्र नो विद्यापरिग्रहाय<BR> नानादिगन्तवासिनां साहचर्यमासीत् Māl. 1; Ku. 3. 21; R. 16. 87; Ve. 1. 20;<BR> Śi. 15. 24.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साहचर्यनियमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्यनियमः
साहचर्यम् + -नियमः a rule of invariable concomitance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहनम्
साहनम् Endurance, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसम्
साहसम् [सहसा बलेन निर्वृत्तम् अण्]<BR>—1 Violence, force, rapine; पैशून्यं साहसं द्रोहम् ईर्ष्यासूयार्थदूषणम् ।<BR> वाग्दण्डजं च पारुष्यं क्रोधजोऽपि गणोऽष्टकः ॥ Ms. 7. 48.<BR>—2 Any criminal act (such as robbery, rape, felony &c.), a heinous crime,<BR> an aggressive act.<BR>—3 Cruelty, oppression; न सहास्मि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">Page1678-2</a>]<BR> साहसमसाहसिकी Śi. 9. 59.<BR>—4 Boldness, daring, daring courage; साहसे श्रीः प्रतिवसति Mk. 4.<BR>—5 Precipitation, rashness, temerity, an inconsiderate or reckless act,<BR> a rash or daring act; तदपि साहसाभासम् Māl. 2; किमपरमतो निर्व्यूढं<BR> यत् करार्पणसाहसम् 9. 10; Pt. 1. 191; Ki. 17. 42.<BR>—6 Punishment, chastisement, fine (<i>m.</i> also in this sense); पणानां<BR> द्वे शते सार्धे प्रथमः साहसः स्मृतः Ms. 8. 138, 276; Y. 1. 66, 365.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साहसाङ्कः, साहसाधिपतिः, साहसाध्यवसायिन्, साहसैकरसिक, साहसकरणम्, साहसकारिन्, साहसदण्डः, साहसलाञ्छन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसाङ्कः|साहसाङ्क|साहसांक
साहसम् + -अङ्कः<BR>—1 an epithet of king Vikramāditya.<BR>—2 of a poet.<BR>—3 of a lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसाधिपतिः|साहसाधिपति
साहसम् + -अधिपतिः a police officer; साहसाधिपतिं चैव ग्रामनेतारमेव<BR> च Śukra. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसाध्यवसायिन्
साहसम् + -अध्यवसायिन् <i>a.</i> acting rashly or with inconsiderate haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसैकरसिक
साहसम् + -एकरसिक <i>a.</i> wholly intent on violence, ferocious, brutal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसकरणम्
साहसम् + -करणम् violence, force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसकारिन्
साहसम् + -कारिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 bold, audacious.<BR>—2 rash, inconsiderate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसदण्डः|साहसदण्ड
साहसम् + -दण्डः highest amerciament; पूर्वः साहसदण्ड आहर्तुः Kau. A. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसलाञ्छन
साहसम् + -लाञ्छन <i>a.</i> characterized by boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिक|साहसिकः
साहसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [साहसे प्रसृतः ठक्]<BR>—1 Using great force or violence, brutal, violent, rapacious, cruel, felonious.<BR>—2 Bold, daring, rash, inconsiderate, reckless; न सहास्मि साहसमसाहसिकी<BR> Śi. 9. 59; केचित्तु साहसिकास्त्रिलोचनमिति पेठुः Malli. on Ku. 3. 44.<BR>—3 Castigatory, punitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिकः|साहसिक
साहसिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A bold or adventurous person, an enterprising man; भयमतुलं गुरुलोकात्<BR> तृणमिव तुलयन्ति साधु साहसिकाः Pt. 5. 31.<BR>—2 A desperado, desperate or dangerous person; या किल विविधजीवोपहारप्रियेति<BR> साहसिकानां प्रवादः Māl. 1; साहसिकः खल्वेषः 6.<BR>—3 A felon, freebooter, robber.<BR>—4 An adulterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिकम्
साहसिक + .{@-कम्@} A bold, daring action; सुग्रीव एव विक्रान्तो वीर साहसिकप्रिय<BR> Rām. 4. 23. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिक्यम्
साहसिक्यम्<BR>—1 Rashness, temerity.<BR>—2 Violence, force; P. I. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिन्
साहसिन् <i>a.</i> [साहस-इनि]<BR>—1 Violent, ferocious; cruel.<BR>—2 Bold, daring, rash, impetuous; क्रियाफलमविज्ञाय यतते साहसी च सः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्र|साहस्रं|साहस्रः
साहस्र <i>a.</i> (-स्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सहस्र-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to a thousand.<BR>—2 Consisting of a thousand.<BR>—3 Bought with a thousand.<BR>—4 Paid per thousand (as interest &c.).<BR>—5 A thousand-fold.<BR>—6 Exceedingly numerous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्रः|साहस्र|साहस्रं
साहस्र + .{@-स्रः@} An army or detachment consisting of a thousand men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्रम्
साहस्र + .{@-स्रम्@} An aggregate of a thousand; किरीटसाहस्रमणिप्रवेकप्रद्योतिदोद्दामफणासहस्रम्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 6; (also साहस्रकम् in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्रिक
साहस्रिक <i>a.</i> Consisting of a thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहायकम्
साहायकम्<BR>—1 Assistance, help, aid; स कुलोचितमिन्द्रस्य साहायकमुपेयिवान् R. 17. 4.<BR>—2 Fellowship, alliance, friendship.<BR>—3 A number of companions or associates.<BR>—4 Auxiliary troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्यम्
साहाय्यम्<BR>—1 Assistance, help, succour.<BR>—2 Friendship, alliance.<BR>—3 (In drama) Helping another in danger; S. D.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साहाय्यकर, साहाय्यदानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्यकर
साहाय्यम् + -कर <i>a.</i> helping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्यदानम्
साहाय्यम् + -दानम् the giving of aid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1678-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्यम्
साहित्यम्<BR>—1 Association, fellowship, combination, society.<BR>—2 Literary or rhetorical composition; साहित्यसंगीतकलाविहीनः साक्षात्<BR> पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः Bh. 2. 12.<BR>—3 The science of rhetoric, art of poetry; साहित्यपाथोनिधिमन्थनोत्थं<BR> कर्णामृतं रक्षत हे कवीन्द्राः Vikr. 1. 11; साहित्यदर्पणम् &c.<BR>—4 A collection of materials for the production or performance of anything<BR> (a doubtful sense).<BR>—5 Agreement, harmony.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साहित्यशास्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्यशास्त्रम्
साहित्यम् + -शास्त्रम् see साहित्य (3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्यम्
साह्यम्<BR>—1 Conjunction, union, fellowship, society.<BR>—2 Assistance, help.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: साह्यकृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्यकृत्
साह्यम् + -कृत् <i>m.</i> a companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्न
साह्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Connected or terminating with a day.<BR>—2 Lasting a day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्व
साह्व <i>a.</i> Named, called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वयः|साह्वय
साह्वयः<BR>—1 Gambling with fighting animals.<BR>—2 Setting animals to fight for sport &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सि
सि €5. €9 U. (सिनोति, सिनुते, सिनाति, सिनीते)<BR>—1 To bind, tie, fasten; उभे नानार्थे पुरुषं सिनीतः Kaṭh. 2. 1.<BR>—2 To ensnare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
सित <i>p. p.</i> Joined with, accompanied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिः|सिति
सितिः Binding, fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहः|सिंह
सिंहः [हिंस्-अच् पृषो˚]<BR>—1 A lion; (it is said to be derived from हिंस्; cf. भवेद्वर्णागमाद्धंसः<BR> सिंहो वर्णविपर्ययात् Sk.); न हि सुप्तस्य सिंहस्य प्रविशन्ति मुखे<BR> मृगाः Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 The sign <i>Leo</i> of the zodiac. e. g. सिंहलग्न.<BR>—3 (At the end of comp.) Best, pre-eminent of a class; <i>e. g.</i> रघुसिंहः,<BR> पुरुषसिंहः; उद्योगिनं पुरुषसिंहमुपैति लक्ष्मीः Pt. 1. 361; U. 5. 22.<BR>—4 A particular place prepared for the building of a house.<BR>—5 (In music) A kind of tone.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सिंहावलोकनम्, सिंहाढ्य, सिंहासनम्, सिंहास्यः, सिंहकर्णः, सिंहकर्णी, सिंहकेशरः, सिंहकेसरः, सिंहगः, सिंहतलम्, सिंहतुण्डः, सिंहदंष्ट्रः, सिंहदर्प, सिंहद्वार्, सिंहध्वनिः, सिंहनादः, सिंहनर्दिन्, सिंहनादः, सिंहमलम्, सिंहयाना, सिंहरथा, सिंहलीलः, सिंहवाहनः, सिंहवाहिनी, सिंहविक्रमः, सिंहविक्रान्तः, सिंहविष्टरः, सिंहसंहनन, सिंहस्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहावलोकनम्
सिंहः + -अवलोकनम् the (backward) glance of a lion. ˚न्यायः the maxim<BR> of the lionʼs (backward) glance, generally used to mark the connection<BR> of a thing with what precedes and follows; (for explanation see under न्याय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाढ्य
सिंहः + -आढ्य <i>a.</i> abounding in lions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहासनम्
सिंहः + -आसनम् a throne, a seat of honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहासनः|सिंहासन|सिंहासनं
सिंहः + -आसनम् + .({@-नः@}) a particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहास्यः|सिंहास्य
सिंहः + -आस्यः a particular position of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकर्णः|सिंहकर्ण
सिंहः + -कर्णः a corner orifice containing lion-figures; यद्वेदिकातोरणसिंहकर्णै<BR> रत्नैर्दधानं प्रतिवेश्म शोभाम् Bu. C. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकर्णी
सिंहः + -कर्णी a particular position of the right hand in shooting an arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकेशरः|सिंहकेशर
सिंहः + -केशरः, -केसरः<BR>—1 the Bakula tree.<BR>—2 a lionʼs mane.<BR>—3 a kind of sweet-meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहकेसरः|सिंहकेसर
सिंहः + -केशरः, -केसरः<BR>—1 the Bakula tree.<BR>—2 a lionʼs mane.<BR>—3 a kind of sweet-meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहगः|सिंहग
सिंहः + -गः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतलम्
सिंहः + -तलम् the palms of the hands opened and joined together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहतुण्डः|सिंहतुण्ड|सिंहतुंड
सिंहः + -तुण्डः a kind of fish; Ms. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1679-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहदंष्ट्रः|सिंहदंष्ट्र
