सितिमन् <i>m.</i> Whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
सिध् I. €4 P. (सिध्यति, सिषेध, असिधत्, सेत्स्यति, सेद्धुम्, सिद्ध;<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> साधयति or सेधयति; <i>desid.</i> सिषित्सति)<BR>—1 To be accomplished or fulfilled; यत्ने कृते यदि न सिध्यति कोऽत्र<BR> दोषः H. Pr. 31; उद्यमेन हि सिध्यन्ति कार्याणि न मनोरथैः 36; Pt. 1. 158.<BR>—2 To be successful, succeed; सिध्यन्ति कर्मसु महत्स्वपि यन्नियोज्याः Ś. 7. 4.<BR>—3 To reach, hit, fall true on; उत्कर्षः स च धन्विनां यदिषवः सिध्यन्ति<BR> लक्ष्ये चले Ś. 2. 5.<BR>—4 To attain oneʼs object.<BR>—5 To be proved or established, to become valid; यदि वचनमात्रेणैवाधिपत्यं<BR> सिध्यति H. 3.<BR>—6 To be settled or adjudicated.<BR>—7 To be thoroughly prepared or cooked.<BR>—8 To be won or conquered; न विश्वासं विना शत्रुर्देवानामपि सिध्यति<BR> Pt. 2. 40. ━II. €1 P. (सेधति, सिद्ध; the स् of सिध् is generally<BR> changed to ष् after a preposition ending in इ or उ)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To ward or drive off.<BR>—3 To restrain, hinder, prevent.<BR>—4 To interdict, prohibit.<BR>—5 To ordain, command, instruct.<BR>—6 To turn out well or auspiciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध|सिद्धं|सिद्धः
सिद्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Accomplished, effected, performed, achieved, completed.<BR>—2 Gained, obtained, acquired.<BR>—3 Succeeded, successful; one who has attained his object; यातावला<BR> व्रजं सिद्धा मयेमा रंस्यथ क्षपाः Bhāg. 10. 22. 27.<BR>—4 Settled, established; नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः कुसुमस्य सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि<BR> स्थितिर्न चरणैरवताडनानि U. 1. 14.<BR>—5 Proved, demonstrated, substantiated; तस्मादिन्द्रियं प्रत्यक्षप्रमाणमिति<BR> सिद्धम् T. S.; साक्षिप्रत्ययसिद्धानि (कार्याणि) Ms. 8. 178.<BR>—6 Valid, sound (as a rule).<BR>—7 Admitted to be true.<BR>—8 Decided, adjudicated (as a law-suit).<BR>—9 Paid, discharged, liquidated (as debt).<BR>—10 Cooked, dressed (as food);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">Page1681-1</a>]<BR> अभ्रच्छाया खलप्रीतिः सिद्धमन्नं च योषितः । किंचित्कालोपभोग्यानि यौवनानि<BR> धनानि च ॥ Pt. 2. 117.<BR>—11 Matured, ripened.<BR>—12 Thoroughly prepared, compounded, cooked together (as drugs).<BR>—13 Ready (as money).<BR>—14 Subdued, won over, subjugated (as by magic).<BR>—15 Brought under subjection, become propitious.<BR>—16 Thoroughly conversant with or skilled in, proficient in; as in रससिद्ध q. v.<BR>—17 Perfected, sanctified (as by penance); अप्रमत्तोऽखिलस्वार्थे यदि<BR> स्यात् सिद्ध आत्मनि Bhāg. 11. 23. 29.<BR>—18 Emancipated.<BR>—19 Endowed with supernatural powers or faculties.<BR>—20 Pious, sacred, holy.<BR>—21 Divine, immortal, eternal.<BR>—22 Celebrated, well-known, illustrious; अथर्वशिरसि प्रोक्तैर्मन्त्रैः<BR> सिद्धां विधानतः Rām. 1. 15. 2; एवं तौ लोकसिद्धाभिः क्रीडाभिश्चेरतुर्वने Mb. 10. 18. 16.<BR>—23 Shining, splendid.<BR>—24 Hit (as a mark).<BR>—25 Peculiar, singular.<BR>—26 Invariable, unalterable. —27 Satisfied; Bhāg. 11. 23. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धः|सिद्ध|सिद्धं
सिद्ध + .{@-द्धः@}<BR>—1 A semi-divine being supposed to be of great purity and holiness, and<BR> said to be particularly characterized by eight supernatural faculties<BR> called <i>Siddhis</i> q. v.; उद्वेजिता वृष्टिभिराश्रयन्ते शृङ्गाणि यस्यातपवन्ति<BR> सिद्धाः Ku. 1. 5.<BR>—2 An inspired sage or seer (like Vyāsa).<BR>—3 Any sage or seer, a prophet; सिद्धादेश Ratn. 1.<BR>—4 One skilled in magical arts, a magician.<BR>—5 A law-suit, judicial trial.<BR>—6 A kind of hard sugar.<BR>—7 The dark thorn-apple.<BR>—8 One who has attained his object; सिद्धः कचो वत्स्यति मत्सकाशे Mb. 1. 76. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धम्
सिद्ध + .{@-द्धम्@} Sea-salt.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सिद्धाङ्गना, सिद्धयोषित्, सिद्धाञ्जनम्, सिद्धान्तः, सिद्धान्नम्, सिद्धार्थ, सिद्धादेशः, सिद्धापगा, सिद्धासनम्, सिद्धौषधम्, सिद्धकाम, सिद्धक्षेत्रम्, सिद्धगङ्गा, सिद्धनदी, सिद्धसिन्धुः, सिद्धग्रहः, सिद्धजलम्, सिद्धसलिलम्, सिद्धदेवः, सिद्धद्रव्यम्, सिद्धधातुः, सिद्धनरः, सिद्धपक्षः, सिद्धपथः, सिद्धपुरुषः, सिद्धपुष्पः, सिद्धप्रयोजनः, सिद्धमानस, सिद्धमोदकः, सिद्धयात्रिकः, सिद्धयोगः, सिद्धयोगिन्, सिद्धरस, सिद्धरूपम्, सिद्धलक्ष, सिद्धलोकः, सिद्धवस्तिः, सिद्धविद्या, सिद्धवेदनः, सिद्धव्यञ्जनः, सिद्धसंकल्प, सिद्धसंबन्ध, सिद्धसाधकः, सिद्धसाधनः, सिद्धसाधित, सिद्धसाध्य, सिद्धसिद्ध, सिद्धसेनः, सिद्धस्थाली, सिद्धहेमन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1680-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धाङ्गना
सिद्ध + -अङ्गना, -योषित् a beatified woman, a female siddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धयोषित्
सिद्ध + -अङ्गना, -योषित् a beatified woman, a female siddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धाञ्जनम्
सिद्ध + -अञ्जनम् magical ointment or collyrium; वसुपूर्णान् कलशान् सिद्धाञ्जनेन<BR> ज्ञात्वा Dk. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्तः|सिद्धान्त|सिद्धांत
सिद्ध + -अन्तः<BR>—1 the established end.<BR>—2 the demonstrated conclusion of an argument, established view of any<BR> question, the true logical conclusion (following on the refutation of<BR> the Pūrvapakṣa).<BR>—3 a proved fact, established truth, dogma, settled doctrine.<BR>—4 any established text-book resting on conclusive evidence; मध्येसभं<BR> दैवविदः सर्वसिद्धान्तपारगाः Śiva B. 6. 80. ˚कोटिः <i>f.</i> the<BR> point in an argument which is regarded as a logical conclusion. ˚कौमुदी<BR> N. of a celebrated commentary on Pāṇiniʼs grammar by भट्टोजीदीक्षित.<BR> ˚पक्षः the logically correct side of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्नम्
सिद्ध + -अन्नम् cooked food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थ|सिद्धार्थः
सिद्ध + -अर्थ <i>a.</i> one who has accomplished his desired object, successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थः|सिद्धार्थ
सिद्ध + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@})<BR>—1 white mustard; यन्त्रस्थसिद्धार्थपदाभिषेकं लब्ध्वाप्यसिद्धार्थममन्यत<BR> स्वम् N. 10. 6; अविरललग्नगौरसिद्धार्थकप्रकारतया काञ्चनरसखचितामिव<BR> मालाम् K. (Pūrvabhāga); Bhāg. 4. 9. 59.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 of the great Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धादेशः|सिद्धादेश
