सिद्ध + -विद्या the doctrine relating to perfect beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धवेदनः
सिद्ध + -वेदनः an elephant having perfect sensitivity; Mātaṅga L. 8. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धव्यञ्जनः
सिद्ध + -व्यञ्जनः an ascetic-spy; सिद्धव्यञ्जनैर्माणवप्रकाशनम् Kau. A. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसंकल्प
सिद्ध + -संकल्प <i>a.</i> one who has accomplished his desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसंबन्ध|सिद्धसम्बन्ध
सिद्ध + -संबन्ध <i>a.</i> one whose kindred are well known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधकः
सिद्ध + -साधकः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधनः|सिद्धसाधन|सिद्धसाधनं
सिद्ध + -साधनः white mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधनम्
सिद्ध + -साधनः + .({@-नम्@})<BR>—1 the performance of magical rites for the acquisition of supernatural powers &c.<BR>—2 the materials employed in mystical or chemical processes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाधित
सिद्ध + -साधित <i>a.</i> one who has learned by practice (not by study).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाध्य|सिद्धसाध्यः
सिद्ध + -साध्य <i>a.</i> accomplished, proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसाध्यम्
सिद्ध + -साध्य + .({@-ध्यम्@}) a dogma, demonstrated conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसिद्ध|सिद्धसिद्धः
सिद्ध + -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> thoroughly efficacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धसेनः|सिद्धसेन
सिद्ध + -सेनः N. of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धस्थाली
सिद्ध + -स्थाली the boiler or pot of a seer (it is supposed to be a vessel<BR> which is gifted with the property of overflowing with any kind of food<BR> at the desire of the possessor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धहेमन्
सिद्ध + -हेमन् purified gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धकः|सिद्धक
सिद्धकः The Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धता
सिद्धता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Accomplishment, fulfilment, perfection.<BR>—2 Validity of a rule or doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धत्वम्
सिद्धता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Accomplishment, fulfilment, perfection.<BR>—2 Validity of a rule or doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धान्तिन्|सिद्धांतिन्
सिद्धान्तिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 One who establishes a conclusion after noticing and answering objections<BR> (or पूर्वपक्ष).<BR>—2 One learned in scientific text-books.<BR>—3 A follower of the Mīmāṃsā philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थकः|सिद्धार्थक
सिद्धार्थकः White mustard; Dk. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धार्थकम्
सिद्धार्थकः + .{@-कम्@} A kind of ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिः|सिद्धि
सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> [सिध्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Accomplishment, fulfilment, completion, perfection, complete attainment<BR> (of an object); विरोधि सिद्धेरिति कर्तुमुद्यतः Ki. 14. 8; क्रियासिद्धिः<BR> सत्त्वे भवति महतां नोपकरणे Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 Success, prosperity, welfare, well-being.<BR>—3 Establishment, settlement.<BR>—4 Substantiation, demonstration, proof, indisputable conclusion.<BR>—5 Validity (of a rule, law &c.).<BR>—6 Decision, adjudication, settlement (of a law-suit); कार्यकारणसिद्धौ<BR> च प्रसन्ना बुद्धिरव्यया Rām. 4. 18. 47;<BR> तस्मान्न लेखसामर्थ्यात् सिद्धिरैकान्तिकी मता Śukra. 4. 726.<BR>—7 Certainty, truth, accuracy, correctness.<BR>—8 Payment, liquidation (of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">Page1682-1</a>]<BR> debt); अधमर्णार्थसिद्धपर्थमुत्तमर्णेन चोदितः Ms. 8. 47.<BR>—9 Preparing, cooking (as of drugs &c.).<BR>—10 The solution of a problem.<BR>—11 Readiness.<BR>—12 Complete purity or sanctification.<BR>—13 A superhuman power or faculty; (these faculties are eight:− अणिमा<BR> लघिमा प्राप्तिः प्राकाम्यं महिमा तथा । ईशित्वं च वशित्वं च तथा कामावसायिता ॥).<BR>—14 The acquisition of supernatural powers by magical means.<BR>—15 Marvellous skill or capability.<BR>—16 Good effect or result.<BR>—17 Final beatitude, final emancipation.<BR>—18 Understanding, intellect.<BR>—19 Concealment, vanishing, making oneself invisible.<BR>—20 A magical shoe (supposed to convey the wearer wherever he likes).<BR>—21 A kind of Yoga.<BR>—22 N. of Durgā.<BR>—23 Complete knowledge.<BR>—24 Advantage, use, good effect.<BR>—25 N. of Śiva (<i>m.</i> in this sense).<BR>—26 Efficacy, efficiency.<BR>—27 Becoming intelligible (as sounds or words).<BR>—28 (In Rhet.) The pointing out in the same person of various good qualities.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सिद्धिद, सिद्धिदात्री, सिद्धियोगः, सिद्धिविनायकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1681-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिद|सिद्धिदः
सिद्धिः + -द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 granting success or supreme felicity.<BR>—2 giving the eight superhuman faculties; हृदि विनिहितरूपः सिद्धिदस्तद्विदां<BR> यः Māl. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिदः|सिद्धिद
सिद्धिः + -द + .({@-दः@}) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिदात्री
सिद्धिः + -दात्री an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धियोगः|सिद्धियोग
सिद्धिः + -योगः a particular auspicious conjunction of planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिविनायकः|सिद्धिविनायक
सिद्धिः + -विनायकः a form of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मम्
सिध्मम्, सिध्मन् <i>n.</i> [सिध्-मन् किच्च Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>—1 Blotch, scab.<BR>—2 Leprosy.<BR>—3 A leprous spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मन्
सिध्मम्, सिध्मन् <i>n.</i> [सिध्-मन् किच्च Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>—1 Blotch, scab.<BR>—2 Leprosy.<BR>—3 A leprous spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मल|सिध्मलः
सिध्मल, सिध्मवत् <i>a.</i> Scabby, tainted with leprosy, leprous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मवत्|सिध्मवन्त्
सिध्मल, सिध्मवत् <i>a.</i> Scabby, tainted with leprosy, leprous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मला
सिध्मल, सिध्मवत् + .{@-ला@} See सिध्मम् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मा
सिध्मा<BR>—1 A blotch, scab, leprous spot.<BR>—2 Leprosy.<BR>—3 = कासश्वासः (according to Nīlakaṇṭha; cf. Mb. 12. 303. 6).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्यः|सिध्य
सिध्यः The asterism Puṣya; सिध्यतारामिव ख्यातां शबरीमापतुर्वने Bk. 6. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्र|सिध्रः
सिध्र <i>a.</i> [सिध्-रक् Uṇ. 2. 13]<BR>—1 Perfect, good.<BR>—2 Protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रः|सिध्र
सिध्र + .{@-ध्रः@}<BR>—1 A pious or virtuous man.<BR>—2 A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रकावणम्
सिध्रकावणम् N. of one of the celestial gardens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन|सिनं|सिनः
सिन <i>a.</i> [सि-नक् Uṇ. 3. 2]<BR>—1 White.<BR>—2 One-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनः|सिन|सिनं
सिन + .{@-नः@} A morsel, mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनम्
सिन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 The body.<BR>—2 Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1682-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनी
