सिवसः<BR>—1 A verse.<BR>—2 Cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिषाधयिषा
सिषाधयिषा<BR>—1 Wish to effect or accomplish.<BR>—2 Desire to establish, prove, or demonstrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिष्णासु
सिष्णासु <i>a.</i> (from स्ना) Wishing to bathe; सिष्णासुरभ्येति<BR> परं समुद्रम् Mb. 8. 94. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसिक्षा
सिसिक्षा (from सिच्) The desire of sprinkling; कन्दर्पप्रबणमनाः<BR> सखीसिसिक्षालक्ष्येण प्रतियुवमञ्जलिं चकार Śi. 8. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिसृक्षा
सिसृक्षा Desire to create; संभूतं षोडशकलमादौ लोकसिसृक्षया<BR> Bhāg. 1. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिहुण्डः|सिहुण्ड|सिहुंड|सिहुंडः
सिहुण्डः The milk-hedge plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्लः|सिह्ल
सिह्लः, सिह्लकः Benzoin, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्लकः|सिह्लक
सिह्लः, सिह्लकः Benzoin, incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्लकी
सिह्लकी, सिह्ली The olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिह्ली
सिह्लकी, सिह्ली The olibanum tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीक्
सीक् I. €1 Ā. (सीकते)<BR>—1 To sprinkle, scatter in small drops.<BR>—2 To go, move. ━II. €1 P., €10 U. (सीकति, सीकयति-ये)<BR>—1 To be impatient.<BR>—2 To be patient.<BR>—3 To touch. See शीक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीकरः|सीकर
सीकरः [सीक्यते सिच्यतेऽनेन, सीक्-अरन्]<BR>—1 Drizzling rain, drizzle, mist.<BR>—2 Spray, thin drops of water. See शीकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीता
सीता [सि-त पृषो˚ दीर्घः]<BR>—1 A furrow, track or line of a ploughshare.<BR>—2 (Hence) A tilled or furrowed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">Page1683-2</a>]<BR> ground, ploughed land; वृषेव सीतां तदवग्रहक्षताम् Ku. 5. 61.<BR>—3 Husbandry, agriculture; as in सीताद्रव्य q. v.<BR>—4 N. of the daughter of Janaka, king of Mithilā, and wife of Rāma;<BR> जनकानां कुले कीर्तिमाहरिष्यति मे सुता । सीता भर्तारमासाद्य रामं<BR> दशरथात्मजम् ॥ Rām. 1. 67. 22. [She was so called because she was<BR> supposed to have sprung from a furrow made by king Janaka while ploughing<BR> the ground to prepare it for a sacrifice which he had instituted to obtain<BR> progeny, and hence also her epithets, ‘Ayonijā’, ‘Dharāputrī’ &c. She<BR> was married to Rāma and accompanied him to the forest. While there she<BR> was once carried off by Rāvaṇa who tried to violate her chastity, but<BR> she scornfully rejected his suit. When Rāma came to know that she was<BR> in Lankā, he attacked the place, killed Rāvaṇa and his host of demons,<BR> and recovered Sītā. She had, however, to pass through the terrible ordeal<BR> of fire before she could be received by her husband as his wife. Though<BR> thus convinced of her chastity, he had afterwards to abandon her, when<BR> far advanced in pregnancy, because the people continued to suspect her<BR> fidelity. She however, found a protector in the sage Vālmīki, at whose<BR> hermitage she was delivered of Kuśa and Lava, and who brought them up.<BR> She was ultimately restored to Rāma by the sage.]<BR>—5 N. of a goddess, wife of Indra.<BR>—6 N. of Umā.<BR>—7 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>—8 N. of one of the four fabulous branches (the eastern branch) of the Ganges.<BR>—9 Spirituous liquor.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सीताध्यक्षः, सीताद्रव्यम्, सीतापतिः, सीताफलः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताध्यक्षः|सीताध्यक्ष
सीता + -अध्यक्षः superintendent of agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताद्रव्यम्
सीता + -द्रव्यम् implements of agriculture, tools of husbandry; सीताद्रव्यापहरणे<BR> शस्त्राणामौषधस्य च Ms. 9. 293.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतापतिः|सीतापति
सीता + -पतिः N. of Rāmachandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताफलः|सीताफल
सीता + -फलः the custard-apple tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीताफलम्
सीता + -फलः + .({@-लम्@}) its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्य|सीत्यं
सीत्य <i>a.</i> Measured out by furrows, tilled, ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्यम्
सीत्य + .{@-त्यम्@} Rice, corn, grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतानकः
सीतानकः, सीतीनकः Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीतीनकः|सीतीनक
सीतानकः, सीतीनकः Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कारः|सीत्कार
सीत्कारः, सीत्कृतिः <i>f.</i> A sound made by drawing in the<BR> breath, (expressive of sighing, shivering with cold, murmuring &c.); मया<BR> दष्टाधरं तस्याः ससीत्कारमिवाननम् V. 4. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीत्कृतिः|सीत्कृति
सीत्कारः, सीत्कृतिः <i>f.</i> A sound made by drawing in the<BR> breath, (expressive of sighing, shivering with cold, murmuring &c.); मया<BR> दष्टाधरं तस्याः ससीत्कारमिवाननम् V. 4. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीद्यम्
सीद्यम् Indolence, slothfulness, idleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधु|सीधुः
सीधु <i>m.</i> [सिध्-उ पृषो˚] Spirit distilled from molasses, rum;<BR> स्फुरदधरसीधवे तव वदनचन्द्रमा रोचयति लोचनचकोरम् Gīt. 10;<BR> Śi. 9. 87; R. 16. 52; ताम्बूलरज्जन्मुखसीधुदानादारक्तबिम्बोऽजनि<BR> युक्तमेतत् Rām. Ch. 6. 15.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सीधुगन्धः, सीधुप, सीधुपानम्, सीधुपुष्पः, सीधुरसः, सीधुसंज्ञः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुगन्धः|सीधुगन्ध|सीधुगंध
सीधु + -गन्धः —1 the Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुप
सीधु + -प <i>a.</i> drinking spirits; P. III. 2. 8. Vārt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुपानम्
सीधु + -पानम् the drinking of spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुपुष्पः|सीधुपुष्प
सीधु + -पुष्पः<BR>—1 the Kadamba tree.<BR>—2 the Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुरसः|सीधुरस
सीधु + -रसः the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीधुसंज्ञः|सीधुसञ्ज्ञ
सीधु + -संज्ञः the Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीध्रम्
सीध्रम् The anus (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीपः|सीप
सीपः A sacrificial vessel in the shape of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1683-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्
सीमन् <i>f.</i> [सि-इमनि पृषो˚ न गुणो दीर्घश्च Tv.]<BR>—1 A boundary &c.; see सीमा; सीमानमत्यायतयोऽत्यजन्तः Śi. 3. 57;<BR> see निःसीमन् also.<BR>—2 The scrotum; सीम्नि पुष्कलको हतः Sk.; (for other senses see सीमा below).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सीमलिङ्गम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमलिङ्गम्
सीमन् + -लिङ्गम् a boundary mark, land-mark; ग्रामीयककुलानां च समक्षं<BR> सीम्नि साक्षिणः । प्रष्टव्याः सीमलिङ्गानि तयोश्चैव विवादिनोः ॥ Ms. 8. 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तः|सीमन्त|सीमंत|सीमंतः
सीमन्तः [सीम्नोऽन्तः शकं˚]<BR>—1 A boundary-line, landmark.<BR>—2 The parting line of the hair; the hair parted on each side of the head<BR> so as to leave a line; सीमन्तः केशवेशे, सीमान्तोऽन्यः Sk. (Mar. भांग);<BR> सीमन्ते च त्वदुपगमजं यत्र नीपं वधूनाम् Me. 67; Śi. 8. 69; Mv. 5. 44.<BR>—3 A landmark.<BR>—4 See सीमन्तोन्नयनम् below; Y. 1. 11.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सीमन्तोन्नयनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तोन्नयनम्
सीमन्तः + -उन्नयनम् ‘parting of the hair’, one of the twelve Saṃskāras<BR> or purificatory rites observed by women in the fourth, sixth or eighth<BR> month of their pregnancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तकः|सीमन्तक|सीमंतक|सीमन्तकं|सीमंतकः
सीमन्तकः<BR>—1 N. of a particular kind of inhabitant of hell.<BR>—2 Hair-parting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तकम्
सीमन्तकः + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Red lead, vermilion.<BR>—2 A kind of ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तयति
सीमन्तयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To part as hair.<BR>—2 To part or mark by a line (in general); सेनां सीमन्तयन्नरेः Kīr. K. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तित|सीमंतित
सीमन्तित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Parted (as hair).<BR>—2 Parted or marked by a line; समीरसीमन्तितकेतकीकाः (प्रदेशाः)<BR> Śi. 3. 80; रथाङ्गसीमन्तितसान्द्रकर्दमान् (पथः) Ki. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमन्तिनी|सीमंतिनी
सीमन्तिनी A woman; मा स्म सीमन्तिनी काचिज्जनयेत् पुत्रमीदृशम्<BR> H. 2. 7; Me. 102; Bk. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमा
सीमा<BR>—1 Boundary, limit, border, margin, frontier.<BR>—2 A mound or ridge serving to mark the boundary of a field, village &c.;<BR> सीमां प्रति समुत्पन्ने विवादे Ms. 8. 245; Y. 2. 152.<BR>—3 A mark, land-mark.<BR>—4 A bank, shore, coast.<BR>—5 The horizon.<BR>—6 A suture (as of a skull).<BR>—7 The bounds of morality or decorum, limits of propriety.<BR>—8 The highest or utmost limit, highest point, climax; सीमेव पद्मासनकौशलस्य Bk. 1. 6.<BR>—9 A field.<BR>—10 The nape of the neck.<BR>—11 The scrotum.<BR>—12 An ornament of the hair; L. D. B.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सीमाज्ञानम्, सीमाधिपः, सीमान्तः, सीमोल्लङ्घनम्, सीमाकृषाण, सीमानिश्चयः, सीमाबन्धः, सीमालिङ्गम्, सीमावादः, सीमाविनिर्णयः, सीमाविवादः, सीमावृक्षः, सीमासंधिः, सीमासेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाज्ञानम्
सीमा + -अज्ञानम् ignorance of boundaries; सीमाज्ञाने नृणां वीक्ष्य नित्यं<BR> लोके विपर्ययम् Ms. 8. 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाधिपः|सीमाधिप
सीमा + -अधिपः<BR>—1 a neighbouring prince.<BR>—2 a keeper of borders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमान्तः|सीमान्त|सीमांत
सीमा + -अन्तः<BR>—1 a boundary-line, border, frontier-line.<BR>—2 the utmost limit. ˚पूजनम्<BR>—1 the ceremony of worshipping or honouring a village boundary.<BR>—2 worshipping the bridegroom when he arrives at the village boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमोल्लङ्घनम्
सीमा + -उल्लङ्घनम् transgressing or leaping over a boundary, crossing<BR> a frontier (now performed on the <i>Dasarā</i> day).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाकृषाण
सीमा + -कृषाण <i>a.</i> ploughing on the border of a land mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमानिश्चयः|सीमानिश्चय
सीमा + -निश्चयः a legal decision with respect to land-marks or boundaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाबन्धः|सीमाबन्ध
सीमा + -बन्धः a depository of rules of morality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमालिङ्गम्
सीमा + -लिङ्गम् a boundary-mark, land-mark; उपच्छन्नानि चान्यानि सीमालिङ्गानि<BR> कारयेत् Ms. 8. 249.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमावादः|सीमावाद
सीमा + -वादः a dispute<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">Page1684-2</a>]<BR> about boundaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाविनिर्णयः|सीमाविनिर्णय
सीमा + -विनिर्णयः settlement of disputed boundary-questions; सीमाविनिर्णयं<BR> कुर्युः प्रयता राजसंनिधौ Ms. 8. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमाविवादः|सीमाविवाद
सीमा + -विवादः litigation about boundaries. ˚धर्मः the law regarding<BR> disputes about boundaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमावृक्षः|सीमावृक्ष
सीमा + -वृक्षः<BR>—1 a tree serving as a boundary-mark; सीमावृक्षांश्च कुर्वीत न्यग्रोधाश्वत्थकिंशुकान् Ms. 8. 246.<BR>—2 (fig.) one whose example is followed by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमासंधिः|सीमासन्धि|सीमासंधि
सीमा + -संधिः the meeting of two boundaries; सीमासंधिषु कार्याणि देवतायतनानि<BR> च Ms. 8. 248, 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमासेतुः|सीमासेतु
सीमा + -सेतुः a ridge or causeway serving as a boundary; सामन्तप्रत्ययो<BR> ज्ञेयः सीमासेतुविनिर्णयः Ms. 8. 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमिकः|सीमिक
सीमिकः<BR>—1 A kind of tree.<BR>—2 An ant-hill.<BR>—3 An ant or a similar small insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीमिका
सीमिकः + .{@-का@} (<i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 An ant.<BR>—2 An ant-hill.<BR>—3 An abscess on the underside of the tongue; Uṇ. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरः|सीर
सीरः [सि-रक् पृषो˚ Uṇ. 2. 25]<BR>—1 A plough; सीरभेदैः कृषिः प्रोक्ता मन्वाद्यैर्ब्राह्मणादिषु Śukra. 4. 260;<BR> सद्यः सीरोत्कषणसुरभि क्षेत्रमारुह्य मालम् Me. 16.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 The <i>Arka</i> plant.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सीरायुधः, सीरध्वजः, सीरपाणिः, सीरभृत्, सीरयोगः, सीरवाहकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरायुधः|सीरायुध
सीरः + -आयुधः See सीरपाणिः; सीरायुधसमश्रियः Śiva B. 24. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरध्वजः|सीरध्वज
सीरः + -ध्वजः an epithet of Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1684-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीरपाणिः|सीरपाणि
