सुतात्मजः|सुतात्मज
सुत + -आत्मजः a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतात्मजा
सुत + -आत्मजः + .({@-जा@}) a grand-daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतोत्पत्तिः|सुतोत्पत्ति
सुत + -उत्पत्तिः <i>f.</i> birth of a son; शौनकस्य सुतोत्पत्त्या (पतति) Ms. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतनिर्विशेषम्
सुत + -निर्विशेषम् <i>ind.</i> not differently from a son, just like a son;<BR> संवर्धितानां सुतनिर्विशेषम् R. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवत्सलः|सुतवत्सल
सुत + -वत्सलः an affectionate father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवस्करा
सुत + -वस्करा the mother of seven children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतश्रेणी
सुत + -श्रेणी Salvinia Cucullata (Mar. बृहद्दंती, उंदीरकानी &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतस्नेहः|सुतस्नेह
सुत + -स्नेहः paternal affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतंगमः|सुतङ्गम|सुतंगम
सुतंगमः The father of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतवत्|सुतवन्त्
सुतवत् <i>a.</i> Having sons. ━<i>m.</i> The father of a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुता
सुता A daughter; तमर्थमिव भारत्या सुतया योक्तुमर्हसि Ku. 6. 79.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुतादानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतादानम्
सुता + -दानम् the gift (in marriage) of a daughter; अलंकृत्य सुतादानं<BR> दैवं धर्मं प्रचक्षते Ms. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिः|सुति
सुतिः <i>f.</i> Extraction of Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिन्
सुतिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Having a child or children. ━<i>m.</i> A father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतिनी
सुतिनी A mother; तेनाम्बा यदि सुतिनी वद वन्ध्या कीदृशी भवति Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतीयति
सुतीयति Den. P.<BR>—1 To long for progeny or son.<BR>—2 To treat like a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुतुस्
सुतुस् <i>a.</i> Well-sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्या
सुत्या<BR>—1 Extraction or preparation of Soma juice.<BR>—2 A sacrificial oblation.<BR>—3 Parturition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुत्याकालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्याकालः|सुत्याकाल
सुत्या + -कालः the time of the extraction of Soma; सुत्याकाले सुनिर्वृत्ते<BR> वेदिं गतरवामिव Rām. 2. 114. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्रामन्
सुत्रामन् <i>m.</i> N. of Indra; पुत्रा विठ्ठलराजस्य सुत्रामसमविक्रमाः<BR> Śiva B. 3. 4; सुत्रामबन्धुर्नृपः (दशरथः) Rām. Ch. 2. 94;<BR> Śivamahimna 13. ━<i>f.</i> The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुत्वन्
सुत्वन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 An offerer or drinker of Soma juice.<BR>—2 A student who has performed his ablutions (subsequent or preparatory<BR> to a sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुदि
सुदि <i>ind.</i> In the bright fortnight of a lunar month; cf. वदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधन्वाचार्यः|सुधन्वाचार्य|सुधन्वाचार्य्य|सुधन्वाचार्य्यः
सुधन्वाचार्यः The son of an outcast Vaiśya by a woman of the same<BR> class; वैश्यात्तु जायते व्रात्यात् सुधन्वाचार्य एव च Ms. 10. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधा
सुधा [सुष्ठु धीयते, पीयते धे-धा वा क Tv.]<BR>—1 The beverage of the gods, nectar, ambrosia; निपीय यस्य क्षितिरक्षिणः<BR> कथां तथाद्रियन्ते न बुधाः सुधामपि N. 1. 1.<BR>—2 The nectar or honey of flowers.<BR>—3 Juice.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">Page1693-1</a>]<BR> Ganges.<BR>—6 White-wash, plaster, mortar; कैलासगिरिणेव सुधासितेन प्राकारेण<BR> परिगता K.; कालान्तरश्यामसुधेषु नक्तम् R. 16. 18.<BR>—7 A brick.<BR>—8 Lightning.<BR>—9 The milk-hedge plant.<BR>—10 Emblic myrobalan.<BR>—11 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुधांशुः, सुधाङ्गः, सुधाकारः, सुधाधारः, सुधावासः, सुधोद्भवः, सुधाकण्ठः, सुधाकारः, सुधाक्षालित, सुधाजीविन्, सुधाद्रवः, सुधाधवलित, सुधानिधिः, सुधापाणिः, सुधाभवनम्, सुधाभित्तिः, सुधाभुज्, सुधाभूबिम्बम्, सुधाभृतिः, सुधामयम्, सुधामोदकः, सुधायोनिः, सुधावर्षः, सुधावर्षिन्, सुधावासः, सुधावासा, सुधाशर्करः, सुधासित, सुधासूतिः, सुधास्यन्दिन्, सुधास्रवा, सुधाहरः, सुधाहृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1692-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधांशुः|सुधांशु
सुधा + -अंशुः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor. ˚रत्नम् a pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाङ्गः|सुधाङ्ग
सुधा + -अङ्गः, -आकारः, -आधारः, -आवासः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाकारः|सुधाकार
सुधा + -अङ्गः, -आकारः, -आधारः, -आवासः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधारः|सुधाधार
सुधा + -अङ्गः, -आकारः, -आधारः, -आवासः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावासः|सुधावास
सुधा + -अङ्गः, -आकारः, -आधारः, -आवासः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधोद्भवः|सुधोद्भव
सुधा + -उद्भवः N. of Dhanvantari.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाकण्ठः|सुधाकण्ठ
सुधा + -कण्ठः the cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाकारः|सुधाकार
सुधा + -कारः the plasterer, white-washer; सूपकाराः सुधाकारा वंशचर्मकृतस्तथा<BR> (प्रतस्थिरे) Rām. 2. 80. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाक्षालित
सुधा + -क्षालित <i>a.</i> white-washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाजीविन्
सुधा + -जीविन् <i>m.</i> a plasterer, brick-layer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाद्रवः|सुधाद्रव
सुधा + -द्रवः<BR>—1 a nectarlike fluid.<BR>—2 white-wash, plaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाधवलित
सुधा + -धवलित <i>a.</i> plastered, white-washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधानिधिः|सुधानिधि
सुधा + -निधिः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधापाणिः|सुधापाणि
सुधा + -पाणिः an epithet of Dhanvantari, the physician of the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभवनम्
सुधा + -भवनम् a stuccoed house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभित्तिः|सुधाभित्ति
सुधा + -भित्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a plastered wall.<BR>—2 a brick-wall.<BR>—3 the fifth Muhūrta or hour after noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभुज्
सुधा + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभूबिम्बम्
सुधा + -भूबिम्बम् the lunar orb; अस्या मुखेन्दावधरः सुधाभूबिम्बस्य<BR> युक्तः प्रतिबिम्ब एषः N. 7. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाभृतिः|सुधाभृति
सुधा + -भृतिः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR>—3 a sacrifice, an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधामयम्
सुधा + -मयम्<BR>—1 a brick or stone building.<BR>—2 a royal palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधामोदकः|सुधामोदक
सुधा + -मोदकः<BR>—1 camphor.<BR>—2 a kind of sugar; L. D. B.<BR>—3 bamboo manna. ˚जः a kind of sugar prepared from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधायोनिः|सुधायोनि
सुधा + -योनिः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावर्षः|सुधावर्ष
सुधा + -वर्षः a shower of nectar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावर्षिन्
सुधा + -वर्षिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 the moon.<BR>—3 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावासः|सुधावास
सुधा + -वासः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधावासा
सुधा + -वासा a kind of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाशर्करः
सुधा + -शर्करः a lime-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधासित
सुधा + -सित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 white as mortar.<BR>—2 bright as nectar.<BR>—3 bound by nectar; जगतीशरणे युक्तो हरिकान्तः सुधासितः Ki. 15. 45<BR> (where it has senses 1 and 2 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधासूतिः|सुधासूति
सुधा + -सूतिः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 a sacrifice.<BR>—3 a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्यन्दिन्|सुधास्यंदिन्
सुधा + -स्यन्दिन् <i>a.</i> ambrosial, flowing with nectar; नेतुं वाञ्छति<BR> यः खलान् पथि सतां सूक्तैः सुधास्यन्दिभिः Bh. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधास्रवा
सुधा + -स्रवा uvula or soft palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहरः|सुधाहर
सुधा + -हरः, -हृत् an epithet of Garuḍa; see गरुड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधाहृत्
सुधा + -हरः, -हृत् an epithet of Garuḍa; see गरुड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधित
सुधित <i>a.</i> Nectar-like; गौप्यः स्फुरत्पुरटकुण्डलकुन्तलत्विड्गण्डश्रिया<BR> सुधितहासनिरीक्षणेन Bhāg. 10. 33. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुधितिः|सुधिति
सुधितिः <i>m., f.</i> An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनफा
सुनफा A particular configuration of the planets (when any one of<BR> the planets except the sun, occupies a secondary position to the moon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनारः|सुनार
सुनारः<BR>—1 The udder of a bitch.<BR>—2 The egg of a snake.<BR>—3 A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनासीरः|सुनासीर
सुनासी(शी)रः An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनाशीरः|सुनाशीर
सुनासी(शी)रः An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुनीथ|सुनीथः
सुनीथ <i>a.</i> [सुनी-क्थन् Uṇ. 2. 2] Of prudent behaviour, moral, good.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दः|सुन्द|सुंदः
सुन्दः N. of a demon and brother of Upasunda, who were sons of Nikumbha.<BR> [They got a boon from the Creator that they would not die until they should<BR> kill themselves. On the strength of this boon, they grew very oppressive<BR> and Indra had at last to send down a lovely nymph named Tilottamā, and<BR> while quarrelling for her, they killed each other.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दर|सुंदर|सुन्दरं|सुन्दरः
सुन्दर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सुन्द्-अरः Uṇ. 3. 133]<BR>—1 Lovely, beautiful, handsome, charming.<BR>—2 Right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दरः|सुन्दर|सुंदर|सुन्दरं
सुन्दर + .{@-रः@} N. of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दरी|सुंदरी
सुन्दर + .{@-री@} A beautiful woman; एका भार्या सुन्दरी वा दरी वा Bh. 2. 115;<BR> विद्याधरसुन्दरीणाम् Ku. 1. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुन्दरकाण्डम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुन्दरकाण्डम्
सुन्दर + -काण्डम्<BR>—1 a beautiful stalk.<BR>—2 the 5th book of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्
सुप्<BR>—1 A technical term used by Pāṇini for the termination of the Locative<BR> plural. —2 A name for any one of the several case-endings or terminations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्त|सुप्तं|सुप्तः
सुप्त <i>p. p.</i> [स्वप्-कर्तरि क्त] Slept, sleeping, asleep; न<BR> हि सुप्तस्य सिंहस्य प्रविशन्ति मुखे मृगाः H. Pr. 36.<BR>—2 Paralyzed, benumbed, insensible; see स्वप्.<BR>—3 Inactive, dull, latent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तम्
सुप्त + .{@-प्तम्@} Sleep, sound sleep.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुप्तजनः, सुप्तज्ञानम्, सुप्तघातक, सुप्तत्वच्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तजनः|सुप्तजन
सुप्त + -जनः<BR>—1 a sleeping person.<BR>—2 midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तज्ञानम्
सुप्त + -ज्ञानम् a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तघातक|सुप्तघातकः
सुप्त + -घातक <i>a.</i> ferocious; murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तत्वच्
सुप्त + -त्वच् <i>a.</i> paralytic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुप्तिः|सुप्ति
सुप्तिः <i>f.</i> [स्वप्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Sleep, sleepiness, drowsiness.<BR>—2 Insensibility, paralysis, numbness.<BR>—3 Trust, confidence.<BR>—4 A dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमः|सुम|सुमं
सुमः<BR>—1 The moon.<BR>—2 Camphor.<BR>—3 Sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुमम्
सुमः + .{@-मम्@} A flower; स्मरस्य स्वर्बालानयनसुममालार्चनपदम् Bv. 1. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्नम्
सुम्नम्<BR>—1 A hymn.<BR>—2 Joy, happiness.<BR>—3 Favour, protection.<BR>—4 A sacrifice.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुम्नयुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुम्नयुः|सुम्नयु
सुम्नम् + -युः a sacrificer. [Uṇ. 1. 37].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुयामुनः|सुयामुन
सुयामुनः<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 N. of Vatsarāja.<BR>—3 A palace.<BR>—4 N. of a mountain.<BR>—5 N. of a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुर्
सुर् I. €6 P. (सुरति)<BR>—1 To rule, govern.<BR>—2 To shine. ━II. €10 P. = स्वर् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरः|सुर
सुरः [सुष्ठु राति ददात्यभीष्टं सु-रा-क]<BR>—1 A god, deity; सुराप्रतिग्रहाद् देवाः सुरा इत्यभिविश्रुताः Rām.;<BR> सुधया तर्पयते सुरान् पितॄंश्च V. 3. 7; R. 5. 16.<BR>—2 The number ‘thirty-three’.<BR>—3 The sun.<BR>—4 A sage, learned man. —5 An idol.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सुराङ्गना, सुराद्रिः, सुराधिपः, सुराध्यक्षः, सुरारिः, सुरार्चनम्, सुरार्चावेश्मन्, सुरार्हम्, सुराचार्यः, सुरापगा, सुरालयः, सुराश्रयः, सुरास्पदम्, सुरेज्यः, सुरेज्या, सुरेन्द्रः, सुरेशः, सुरेश्वरः, सुरेभः, सुरेष्टः, सुरेशः, सुरेश्वरः, सुरोत्तमः, सुरोत्तरः, सुरोपम, सुरर्षिः, सुरकारुः, सुरकार्मुकम्, सुरगणः, सुरगण्डः, सुरगिरिः, सुरगुरुः, सुरग्रामणी, सुरजनः, सुरज्येष्ठः, सुरतरङ्गिणी, सुरतरुः, सुरतोषकः, सुरदारु, सुरदीर्धिका, सुरदुन्दुभी, सुरद्विपः, सुरद्विष्, सुरधनुस्, सुरधुनी, सुरधूपः, सुरनदी, सुरनिम्नगा, सुरपतिः, सुरपथम्, सुरपर्वतः, सुरपादपः, सुरप्रतिष्ठा, सुरप्रियः, सुरभूयम्, सुरभूरुहः, सुरभूषणम्, सुरमन्दिरम्, सुरमृत्तिका, सुरयुवतिः, सुरराज्यम्, सुरलासिका, सुरलोकः, सुरवर्त्मन्, सुरवल्लभा, सुरवल्ली, सुरविद्विष्, सुरवैरिन्, सुरशत्रुः, सुरविलासिनी, सुरवीथिः, सुरशाखिन्, सुरश्वेता, सुरसद्मन्, सुरसालः, सुरसरित्, सुरसिन्धुः, सुरसुन्दरी, सुरस्त्री, सुरस्थानम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराङ्गना|सुरांगना
सुरः + -अङ्गना a celestial woman or damsel, an <i>apsaras</i>; प्रजिघाय<BR> समाधिभेदिनीं हरिरस्मै हरिणीं सुराङ्गनाम् R. 8. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराद्रिः|सुराद्रि
सुरः + -अद्रिः the mountain Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराधिपः|सुराधिप
सुरः + -अधिपः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराध्यक्षः|सुराध्यक्ष
सुरः + -अध्यक्षः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरारिः|सुरारि
सुरः + -अरिः<BR>—1 an enemy of gods, a demon; गतं भयं भीरु सुरारिसंभवम् V. 1. 6.<BR>—2 the chirp of a cricket. ˚हन् <i>m.</i> N. of Śiva. ˚हन्तृ <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्चनम्
सुरः + -अर्चनम् the worship of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्चावेश्मन्
सुरः + -अर्चावेश्मन् <i>n.</i> a household temple, a chamber containing the<BR> idols of deities; ब्रह्मचारिपरिचारि सुरार्चावेश्म राजऋषिरेष विवेश N. 21. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरार्हम्
सुरः + -अर्हम्<BR>—1 gold.<BR>—2 saffron.<BR>—3 yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुराचार्यः|सुराचार्य|सुराचार्य्य|सुराचार्य्यः
सुरः + -आचार्यः an epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1693-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुरापगा
