सृप्रः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृप्रम्
सृप्रः + .{@-प्रम्@} Honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृभ्
सृभ्, -सृम्भ् €1 P. (सर्भत्-सृम्भति)<BR> To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृम्भ्|सृंभ्
सृभ्, -सृम्भ् €1 P. (सर्भत्-सृम्भति)<BR> To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृमर|सृमरः
सृमर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> Going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सृमरः|सृमर
सृमर + .{@-रः@} A kind of deer; Rām. 2. 29. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सॄ
सॄ €9 P. (सृणाति) To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सीर्णिः|सीर्णि
सीर्णिः <i>f.</i> Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्
सेक् €1 Ā. (सेकते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकः|सेक
सेकः [सिच्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sprinkling, watering (trees); सेकः सीकरिणा करेण विहितः कामम्<BR> U. 3. 16; R. 1. 51, 8. 45, 16. 30, 17. 16.<BR>—2 Emission, effusion.<BR>—3 Seminal effusion.<BR>—4 A libation, an offering.<BR>—5 Seminal fluid; कामतो रेतसः सेकं व्रतस्थस्य द्विजन्मनः Ms. 11. 120.<BR>—6 A drop of anything.<BR>—7 A shower-bath; Suśr.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेकपात्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकपात्रम्
सेकः + -पात्रम्<BR>—1 a pot for sprinkling water, a watering-pot.<BR>—2 a bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1701-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेकिमम्
सेकिमम् A radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्तृ
सेक्तृ <i>a.</i> (-क्त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> One who sprinkles &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A sprinkler; impregnator.<BR>—2 A husband.<BR>—3 A water-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेक्त्रम्
सेक्त्रम् A bucket, watering-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचक|सेचकः
सेचक <i>a.</i> (-चिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सिच्-ण्वुल्] Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचकः|सेचक
सेचक + .{@-कः@} A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचनम्
सेचनम् [सिच्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sprinkling, watering; वृक्षसेचने द्वे धारयसि मे Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Effusion, aspersion.<BR>—3 Oozing, dripping.<BR>—4 A bucket.<BR>—5 Emission. See सेकः.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेचनघटः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचनघटः|सेचनघट
सेचनम् + -घटः a watering-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचनकम्
सेचनकम् A shower-bath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेचनी
सेचनी A bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेगवः|सेगव
सेगवः A young crab; कुस्त्री खादति मांसानि माघमां सेगवा इव<BR> Mb. 12. 139. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेटुः|सेटु
सेटुः<BR>—1 Water-melon.<BR>—2 A kind of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतिका
सेतिका N. of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुः|सेतु
सेतुः [सि-तुन् Uṇ. 1. 69]<BR>—1 A ridge of earth, mound, bank, causeway, dam; नलिनीं क्षतसेतुबन्धनो<BR> जलसंघात इवासि विद्रुतः Ku. 4. 6; R. 16. 2.<BR>—2 A bridge in general; वैदेहि पश्या मलयाद्विभक्तं मत्सेतुना फेनिलमम्बुराशिम्<BR> R. 13. 2; सैन्यैर्बद्धद्विरदसेतुभिः 4. 38, 12. 70; Ku. 7. 53.<BR>—3 A landmark; ज्येष्ठे मासि नयेत् सीमां सुप्रकाशेषु सेतुषु Ms. 8. 245.<BR>—4 A defile, pass, a narrow mountain-road.<BR>—5 A boundary, limit.<BR>—6 A barrier, limitation, obstruction of any kind; दुष्येयुः सर्ववर्णाश्च<BR> भिद्येरन् सर्वसेतवः Subhāṣ.<BR>—7 A fixed rule or law, an established institution; सूचकाः सेतुभेत्तारः<BR> … … ते वै निरयगामिनः Mb. 13. 23. 66.<BR>—8 The sacred syllable <i>om</i>; मन्त्राणां प्रणवः सेतुस्तत्सेतुः<BR> प्रणवः स्मृतः । स्रवत्यनोङ्कृतं पूर्वं परस्ताच्च विदीर्यते ॥ Kālikā P.<BR>—9 A reservoir or a lake; सहोदकम् आहार्योदकं वा सेतुं बन्धयेत् Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR>—10 A bond, fetter.<BR>—11 An explanatory commentary.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेतुबन्धः, सेतुभेदिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुबन्धः|सेतुबन्ध|सेतुबंध
सेतुः + -बन्धः<BR>—1 the forming o construction of a bridge, cause-way &c.; Kau. A. 2. 1;<BR> वयोगते किं वनिताविलासो जले गते किं खलु सेतुबन्धः Subhāṣ.; Ku. 4. 6.<BR>—2 the ridge of rocks extending from the southern extremity of the Coromandel<BR> coast near Rameswaram towards Ceylon (said to have been built for Rāmaʼs<BR> passage to Laṅkā by Nala and the other monkeys); Bhāg. 7. 14. 31.<BR>—3 any bridge or cause-way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुभेदिन्
सेतुः + -भेदिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 breaking down barriers.<BR>—2 removing obstructions. ━(<i>m.</i>) N. of a tree (दन्ती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेतुकः|सेतुक
सेतुकः<BR>—1 A bank, cause-way, bridge.<BR>—2 A pass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेत्रम्
सेत्रम् A bond, fetter; P. III. 2. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेदिवस्
सेदिवस् <i>a.</i> (सेदुषी <i>f.</i>) Sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधः|सेध
सेधः<BR>—1 Going, reaching.<BR>—2 A tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेधा
सेधः + .{@-धा@}<BR>—1 A hedgehog.<BR>—2 A porcupine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन
सेन <i>a.</i> Having a lord, possessing a master or leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनम्
सेन + .{@-नम्@} The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेना
सेना [सि-न, सह इनेन प्रभुणा वा; Uṇ. 3. 10]<BR>—1 An army; सेना परिच्छदस्तस्य द्वयमेवार्थसाधनम् R. 1. 19.<BR>—2 Army personified as the wife of Kārtikeya, the god of war; cf. देवसेना.<BR>—3 A small army (consisting of 3 elephants, 3 chariots, 9 horse and 15 foot).<BR>—4 Any body of men.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेनाग्रम्, सेनाङ्गम्, सेनाकल्पः, सेनागोपः, सेनाचरः, सेनानिवेशः, सेनानी, सेनापतिः, सेनापत्यम्, सेनापरिच्छद्, सेनापृष्ठम्, सेनाभङ्गः, सेनामुखम्, सेनायोगः, सेनारक्षः, सेनावासः, सेनावाहः, सेनास्थः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाग्रम्
सेना + -अग्रम् the van or front of an army. ˚गः the leader or general of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाङ्गम्
सेना + -अङ्गम्<BR>—1 a component part of an army; (these are four:− हस्त्यश्वरथपादातं<BR> सेनाङ्गं स्याच्चतुष्टयम्).<BR>—2 a division of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाकल्पः
सेना + -कल्पः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनागोपः|सेनागोप
सेना + -गोपः the keeper of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाचरः|सेनाचर
सेना + -चरः<BR>—1 a soldier.<BR>—2 a camp-follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानिवेशः|सेनानिवेश
सेना + -निवेशः the camp. of an army; सेननिवेशं तुमुलं चकार R. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनानी
सेना + -नी <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a leader of an army, commander, general; सेनानीनामहं स्कन्दः<BR> Bg. 10. 24; Ku. 2. 51.<BR>—2 N. of Kārtikeya; अथैनमद्रेस्तनया शुशोच सेनान्यमालीढमिवासुरास्त्रैः R. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापतिः|सेनापति
सेना + -पतिः<BR>—1 a general.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>—4 A leader of ten पत्ति divisions; see पत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापत्यम्
सेना + -पत्यम् commandership, generalship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापरिच्छद्
सेना + -परिच्छद् <i>a.</i> surrounded by an army; (in R. 1. 19 सेनापरिच्छदः<BR> is sometimes taken as one word and is interpreted in this way, but it<BR> is much better to take them as separate words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनापृष्ठम्
सेना + -पृष्ठम् the rear of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनाभङ्गः|सेनाभङ्ग|सेनाभंग
सेना + -भङ्गः the breaking of an army, complete rout, disorderly flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनामुखम्
सेना + -मुखम्<BR>—1 a division of an army.<BR>—2 particularly, a division of an army consisting of three elephants,<BR> as many chariots, nine horse, and fifteen foot; पत्तिं तु त्रिगुणामेतामाहुः<BR> सेनामुखं बुधाः Mb. 1. 2. 20.<BR>—3 a mound in front of a city gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनायोगः|सेनायोग
सेना + -योगः the equipment of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनारक्षः|सेनारक्ष
सेना + -रक्षः a guard, sentinel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनावासः|सेनावास
सेना + -वासः a camp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनावाहः|सेनावाह
सेना + -वाहः the leader of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेनास्थः|सेनास्थ
सेना + -स्थः a soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेन्द्रिय
सेन्द्रिय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Together with the organs of sense; तमोऽयं तु समाश्रित्य चिरं तिष्ठति<BR> सेन्द्रियः Ms. 1. 55.<BR>—2 Organic (as chemistry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेफः|सेफ
सेफः The penis; cf. शेफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेमन्ती|सेमंती
सेमन्ती The Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरः|सेर
सेरः A kind of measure (Mar. शेर); it is thus defined in Līlāvatī:−<BR> पादोनगद्यानकतुल्यटङ्कैर्द्विसप्ततुल्यैः कथितोऽत्र सेरः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराल
सेराल <i>a.</i> Pale-yellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेराहः|सेराह
सेराहः A horse of a milk-white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेरु|सेरुः
सेरु <i>a.</i> Binding, fastening; P. III. 2. 159.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेर्ष्य
सेर्ष्य <i>a.</i> Full of envy or jealousy, envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेल्
सेल् €1 P. (सेलति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्
सेव् €1 Ā. (सेवते, सेवित; <i>caus.</i> सेवयति-ते; <i>desid.</i><BR> सिसेविषते; the स् of सेव् is generally changed to ष् after<BR> prepositions ending in इ such as नि, परि, वि)<BR>—1 To serve,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">Page1703-1</a>]<BR> wait or attend upon, honour, worship, obey; प्रायो भृत्यास्त्यजन्ति प्रचलितविभवं<BR> स्वामिनं सेवमानाः Mu. 4. 21; आचारपूतं पवनः सिषेवे R. 2. 13<BR> ‘served or refreshed’; ऐश्वर्यादनपेतमीश्वरमयं लोकोऽर्थतः सेवते Mu. 1. 14.<BR>—2 To go after, pursue, follow.<BR>—3 To use, enjoy; किं सेव्यते सुमनसां मनसापि गन्धः कस्तूरिकाजननशक्तिभृता मृगेण R. G.<BR>—4 To enjoy carnally; केतकीं सेवसे हन्त कथं रोलम्ब निस्त्रपः Bv. 1. 118.<BR>—5 To attach or devote oneself to, attend to, cultivate, practise, perform;<BR> विद्वद्भिः सेवितः (धर्मः) Ms. 2. 1; त्वया मनोनिर्विषयार्थकामया<BR> यदेक एव प्रतिगृह्य सेव्यते Ku. 5. 38; R. 17. 49.<BR>—6 To resort to, betake oneself to, dwell in, frequent, inhabit; तप्तं<BR> वारि विहाय तीरनलिनीं कारण्डवः सेवते V. 2. 23; Pt. 1. 9.<BR>—7 To watch over, guard, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1702-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव|सेवं
सेव See सेवन, सेवि (2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवक|सेवकः
सेवक <i>a.</i> [सेव्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Serving, worshipping, honouring.<BR>—2 Practising, following.<BR>—3 Dependent, servile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवकः|सेवक
सेवक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A servant, dependant; सेवया धनमिच्छद्भिः सेवकैः पश्य किं कृतम् ।<BR> स्वातन्त्र्यं यच्छरीरस्य मूढैस्तदपि हारितम् ॥ H. 2. 20.<BR>—2 A votary, worshipper.<BR>—3 A sewer.<BR>—4 A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनम्
सेवनम् [सिव्-सेव्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of serving, service, attendance upon, worship; पात्रीकृतात्मा<BR> गुरुसेवनेन R. 18. 30; Pt. 1. 11.<BR>—2 Following, practising, employing; इन्द्रियाणां प्रसङ्गेन धर्मस्यासेवनेन<BR> च । पापान् संयान्ति संसारानविद्वांसो नराधमाः ॥ Ms. 12. 52.<BR>—3 Using, enjoying.<BR>—4 Enjoying carnally; यत् करोत्येकरात्रेण वृषलीसेवनाद् द्विजः Ms. 11. 178.<BR>—5 Devotion to, fondness for.<BR>—6 Frequenting, dwelling in.<BR>—7 Binding, fastening.<BR>—8 Sewing, stitching.<BR>—9 A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवनी
सेवनी The Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवना
सेवना See सेवनम् (1); तानेव ते मदनुसेवनयावरुद्धान्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 23. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवती
सेवती<BR>—1 A needle.<BR>—2 A seam.<BR>—3 A suture or seam-like union of parts of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवा
सेवा [सेव्-अ]<BR>—1 Service, servitude, dependence; attendance; सेवां लाघवकारिणीं कृतधियः<BR> स्थाने श्ववृत्तिं विदुः Mu. 3. 14; हीनसेवा न कर्तव्या H. 3. 11.<BR>—2 Worship, homage, honouring.<BR>—3 Addiction or devotion to, fondness for.<BR>—4 Use, practice, employment, exercise.<BR>—5 Frequenting, resorting to. —6 Flattery, coaxing or flattering words;<BR> अलं सेवया मध्यस्थतां गृहीत्वा भण M. 3.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेवाकार, सेवाकाकुः, सेवाधर्मः, सेवाविलासिनी, सेवावृत्तिः, सेवाव्यवहारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाकार
सेवा + -आकार <i>a.</i> in the form of servitude; सेवाकारा परिणतिरहो<BR> स्त्रीषु कष्टोऽधिकारः V. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाकाकुः|सेवाकाकु
सेवा + -काकुः change of voice in service; (this is a variant in V. 3. 1<BR> for सेवाकारा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाधर्मः|सेवाधर्म
सेवा + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the duty of service; सेवाधर्मः परमगहनो योगिनामप्यगम्यः Pt. 1. 285.<BR>—2 the obligations of service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाविलासिनी
सेवा + -विलासिनी a female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवावृत्तिः|सेवावृत्ति
सेवा + -वृत्तिः a livelihood gained by service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवाव्यवहारः|सेवाव्यवहार
सेवा + -व्यवहारः the practice or law of service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवि
सेवि <i>n.</i><BR>—1 The jujube.<BR>—2 An apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवित|सेवितः
सेवित^1 <i>p. p.</i> [सेव्-क्त]<BR>—1 Served, attended upon, worshipped.<BR>—2 Followed, practised, pursued.<BR>—3 Frequented<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">Page1703-2</a>]<BR> by, resorted to, inhabited by, haunted by; वरं वनं व्याघ्रगजादिसोवितम् Pt. 5. 23.<BR>—4 Protected, preserved.<BR>—5 Enjoyed, used.<BR>—6 Abounding in.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. note: particple is adjective so no anusvAra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितम्
सेवित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 An apple.<BR>—2 The jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविता
सेवित + .{@-ता@} Service, attendance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेवितमन्मथ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितमन्मथ
सेवित + -मन्मथ <i>a.</i> addicted to love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवितृ
सेवितृ <i>m.</i> An attendant, a dependant; न सेव्यः सेविता रहः M. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविन्
सेविन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Serving, worshipping.<BR>—2 Following, using.<BR>—3 Inhabiting, dwelling.<BR>—4 Having sexual intercourse with.<BR>—5 Addicted to, fond of. ━<i>m.</i> A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्य|सेव्यं|सेव्यः
सेव्य <i>a.</i> [सेव्-ण्यत्]<BR>—1 To be served or waited upon.<BR>—2 To be used or employed.<BR>—3 To be enjoyed.<BR>—4 To be taken care of or guarded.<BR>—5 To be studied. —6 To be kept or hoarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यः|सेव्य|सेव्यं
सेव्य + .{@-व्यः@}<BR>—1 A master (opp. सेवक); भयं तावत् सेव्यादभिनिविशते सेवकजनम्<BR> Mu. 5. 12; M. 4. 12; Pt. 1. 48.<BR>—2 The Aśvattha tree.<BR>—3 A sparrow.<BR>—4 A kind of intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्या
सेव्य + .{@-व्या@}<BR>—1 The parasite plant वन्दा.<BR>—2 A kind of wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यम्
सेव्य + .{@-व्यम्@}<BR>—1 A kind of root.<BR>—2 Red sandal-wood.<BR>—3 Sea-salt.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेव्यसेवकौ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेव्यसेवकौ
सेव्य + -सेवकौ <i>m.</i> <i>dual</i> master and servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेवधि|सेवधिः
सेवधि See शेवधि under शेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेविका
सेविका<BR>—1 A maid servant.<BR>—2 A kind of sweetmeat (Mar. फेणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेश्वर
सेश्वर <i>a.</i> Theistical.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सेश्वरसांख्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सेश्वरसांख्यम्
सेश्वर + -सांख्यम् the theistical branch of the सांख्य school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सै
सै €1 P. (सायति) To waste away, decline, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंह|सैंहः
सैंह <i>a.</i> (-ही <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to a lion, leonine; द्युतिं सैंहीं किं<BR> श्वा धृतकनकमालोऽपि लभते H. 1. 154; Pt. 3. 154; Śi. 1. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहल
सैंहल <i>a.</i> Belonging to, growing or produced in, Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहली
सैंहल + .{@-ली@} A kind of pepper (Mar. पिंपळी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहलकः|सैंहलक
सैंहलकः Brass; Gīrvāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिकः|सैंहिक
सैंहिकः, -सैंहिकेयः<BR> A metronymic of Rāhu, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैंहिकेयः|सैंहिकेय
सैंहिकः, -सैंहिकेयः<BR> A metronymic of Rāhu, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैक
सैक <i>a.</i> Added to one, plus one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकत|सैकतं|सैकतः
सैकत <i>a.</i> (-ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सिकताः सन्त्यत्र अण्]<BR>—1 Consisting or made of sand, sandy, gravelly; तोयस्येवाप्रतिहतरयः<BR> सैकतं सेतुमोघः U. 3. 36.<BR>—2 Having sandy soil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतम्
सैकत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 A sand-bank; सुरगज इव गाङ्गं सैकतं सुप्रतीकः R. 5. 75, 5. 8, 10. 62, 13. 17, 62, 14. 76, 16. 21;<BR> Ku. 1. 29; Ś. 6. 16.<BR>—2 An island with sandy shores.<BR>—3 A bank or shore (in general).<BR>—4 A heap of sand (cf. Amarachandraʼs com. on Ṛs. 2. 9 ‘सैकतिनी सिकताया वालुकायाः समूहः सैकतं तेन युक्ता’).<BR> ━<i>m.</i> pl. N. of a family of<BR> Ṛṣis; अन्ये चापरिमेयाश्च ब्राह्मणा वनमाश्रिताः । वैखानसा वालखिल्याः<BR> सैकताश्च तथा परे ॥ Mb. 12. 244. 20 (some take सैकतः as a kind<BR> of वानप्रस्थ; see सैकतिकः).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सैकतेष्टम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतेष्टम्
सैकत + -इष्टम् ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1703-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिक|सैकतिकं|सैकतिकः
सैकतिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging or relating to a sand-bank.<BR>—2 Fluctuating, wavering, living in doubt and error (संदेहजीविन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिकः|सैकतिक|सैकतिकं
सैकतिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A religious mendicant.<BR>—2 An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिकम्
सैकतिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 A thread worn round the wrist or neck to secure good fortune (मङ्गलसूत्र).<BR>—2 मातृयात्रा (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैकतिनी
सैकतिनी <i>a.</i> Full of sand; समाचिता सैकतिनी वनस्थली Ṛs. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैक्षव
सैक्षव <i>a.</i> Sugared, sugary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैत्यम्
सैत्यम् Whiteness; तमालनीलानि तमांसि कामं पीत्वापि सैत्यं न<BR> जहाति चन्द्रः Rām. Ch. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैद्धान्तिक|सैद्धांतिक|सैद्धान्तिकः
सैद्धान्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सिद्धान्तं वेत्ति ठक्]<BR>—1 Relating to a dogma or demonstrated truth.<BR>—2 One who knows the real truth.<BR>—3 Relating to an astronomical or any other scientific work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनानिक
सैनानिक <i>a.</i> Belonging to the van of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सैनान्यम्
सैनान्यम्, -सैनापत्यम्<BR> The command of an army, generalship; तस्यात्मा शितिकण्ठस्य<BR> सैनापत्यमुपेत्य वः Ku. 2. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1704-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

