सोमधारा
सोमः + -धारा<BR>—1 the sky, heaven.<BR>—2 the milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमनाथः|सोमनाथ
सोमः + -नाथः N. of a celebrated <i>Liṅga</i> or the place where it<BR> was set up; (which by its splendour and enormous wealth attracted the<BR> attention of Mahmud of Ghazni who in 1024 A. D. destroyedthe image and<BR> carried off the treasures); तेषां मार्गे परिचयवशादर्जितं गुर्जराणां<BR> यः संतापं शिथिलमकरोत् सोमनाथं विलोक्य । Vikr. 18. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोमप|सोमपः
सोमः + -प, -पा <i>m.</i><BR>—1 one who drinks the Soma; त्रैविद्या मां सोमपाः पूतपापा यज्ञैरिष्ट्वा<BR> स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयन्ते Bg. 9. 20; Mb. 12. 284. 8.<BR>—2 a Soma-sacrificer.<BR>—3 a particular class of Pitṛs; सोमपा नाम विप्राणां (पितरः) Ms. 3. 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

