सोल्लुण्ठनम्
सोल्लुण्ठः, सोल्लुण्ठनम् Irony, ridicule, sarcasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठम्
सोल्लुण्ठः, सोल्लुण्ठनम् + .{@-ण्ठम्, -नम्@} <i>ind.</i> Ironically; U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लुण्ठनम्
सोल्लुण्ठः, सोल्लुण्ठनम् + .{@-ण्ठम्, -नम्@} <i>ind.</i> Ironically; U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोल्लेखम्
सोल्लेखम् <i>ind.</i> Distinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोवाल
सोवाल <i>a.</i> Blackish, smoky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोष्णीषम्
सोष्णीषम् A house with a verandah in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सोष्मन्
सोष्मन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Warm, hot.<BR>—2 (In gram.) Aspirated. ━<i>m.</i> An aspirate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1706-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर|सौकरः
सौकर (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> Hoggish, of a hog; दनुजं दधानमथ सौकरं वपुः Ki. 12. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकरिकः|सौकरिक
सौकरिकः<BR>—1 A boar-hunter.<BR>—2 pig-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकर्यम्
सौकर्यम् [सुकरस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>—1 Hoggishness.<BR>—2 Ease, facility; सौकर्यं च कार्यस्यानायासेन सिद्धपा साङ्गसिद्धपा च बोध्यम्.<BR>—3 Practicability, feasibility.<BR>—4 Adroitness, skill.<BR>—5 An easy or <i>extempore</i> preparation of food or medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौकुमार्यम्
सौकुमार्यम्<BR>—1 Softness, delicacy, tenderness; शिरीषपुष्पाधिकसौकुमार्यौ बाहू तदीयाविति<BR> मे वितर्कः Ku. 1. 41.<BR>—2 Youthfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्मकः|सौक्ष्मक
सौक्ष्मकः A small insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौक्ष्म्यम्
सौक्ष्म्यम् Minuteness, fineness, subtlety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखयानिकः|सौखयानिक
सौखयानिकः A bard or other officer who wishes a prince or any other<BR> guest a prosperous march.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखरात्रिक
सौखरात्रिक <i>a.</i> One who asks another whether he has had a good night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखशायनिकः|सौखशायनिक
सौखशायनिकः, सौखशायिकः [सुखशयनं पृच्छति ठक्]<BR> One who asks another person whether he has slept well or has had comfortable<BR> sleep; भृग्वादीननुगृह्णन्तं सौखशायनिकानृषीन् R. 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखशायिकः|सौखशायिक
सौखशायनिकः, सौखशायिकः [सुखशयनं पृच्छति ठक्]<BR> One who asks another person whether he has slept well or has had comfortable<BR> sleep; भृग्वादीननुगृह्णन्तं सौखशायनिकानृषीन् R. 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखसुप्तिकः|सौखसुप्तिक
सौख(प्र)सुप्तिकः [सुखसुप्तिं सुखेन शयनं पृच्छति ठञ्]<BR>—1 One who asks another person whether he has slept well.<BR>—2 A bard whose duty it is to waken a king or any other great personage<BR> with song and music; भ्रमरा … गुञ्जन्तः प्रतिकमलं प्रबभुः<BR> सौखप्रसुप्तिका इव ते Cola-Campū. p. 29, verse 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखप्रसुप्तिकः
सौख(प्र)सुप्तिकः [सुखसुप्तिं सुखेन शयनं पृच्छति ठञ्]<BR>—1 One who asks another person whether he has slept well.<BR>—2 A bard whose duty it is to waken a king or any other great personage<BR> with song and music; भ्रमरा … गुञ्जन्तः प्रतिकमलं प्रबभुः<BR> सौखप्रसुप्तिका इव ते Cola-Campū. p. 29, verse 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौखिक|सौखिकः
