सौख्यशायिकः|सौख्यशायिक
सौख्यम् + -शायनिकः, -शायिकः see सौखशायनिकः; Mb. 14. 70. 7 (com.<BR> सुखावहं सौख्यं शयनम् इति पृच्छन्ति ते सौख्यशायनिकाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगतः|सौगत
सौगतः A Buddhist; a follower of Sugata or Buddha; (the Buddhists<BR> are divided into four great schools; माध्यमिक, सौत्रान्तिक, योगाचार<BR> & वैभासिक); सौगतजरत्परिव्राजिकायास्तु कामन्दक्याः प्रथमां भूमिकां<BR> भाव एवाधीते Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगतिकः|सौगतिक
सौगतिकः<BR>—1 A Buddhist. —2 A Buddhist mendicant.<BR>—2 An atheist, a heretic, an unbeliever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगतिकम्
सौगतिकः + .{@-कम्@} Unbelief, heresy, atheism, scepticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध|सौगंध|सौगन्धं|सौगन्धः
सौगन्ध <i>a.</i> (-न्धी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sweet-scented, fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धम्
सौगन्ध + .{@-न्धम्@}<BR>—1 Sweet-scentedness, fragrance.<BR>—2 A kind of fragrant grass (कत्तृण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धः|सौगन्ध|सौगंध|सौगन्धं
सौगन्ध + .{@-न्धः@} A dealer in perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिक|सौगंधिक|सौगन्धिकं|सौगन्धिकः
सौगन्धिक <i>a.</i> (-का or -की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Sweet-scented, fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिकः|सौगन्धिक|सौगंधिक|सौगन्धिकं
सौगन्धिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A dealer in perfumes, perfumer.<BR>—2 Sulphur.<BR>—3 A sexually weak man (who is stimulated by the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">Page1707-2</a>]<BR> smell of the female organs).<BR>—4 A kind of worm infesting the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्धिकम्
सौगन्धिक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 The white water-lily; गृहेषु नानोपवनामलाम्भःसरस्सु सौगन्धिककाननेषु<BR> Bhāg. 9. 6. 45.<BR>—2 The blue lotus.<BR>—3 A kind of fragrant grass (कत्तृण).<BR>—4 A ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगन्ध्यम्
सौगन्ध्यम् Sweetness of odour, fragrance, perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौगम्यम्
सौगम्यम् Ease, facility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचिः|सौचि
सौचिः, सौचिकः A tailor; Kull. on Ms. 4. 214; प्रमाणतः<BR> सौचिकेन रञ्जनानि च वेत्ति यः Śukra. 2. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौचिकः|सौचिक
सौचिः, सौचिकः A tailor; Kull. on Ms. 4. 214; प्रमाणतः<BR> सौचिकेन रञ्जनानि च वेत्ति यः Śukra. 2. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजन्यम्
सौजन्यम्<BR>—1 Goodness, kindness of spirit, gentility; प्रसन्नं सौजन्याद्दयितकरुणैर्गाढकरुणम्<BR> U. 3. 13; Mk. 8. 38.<BR>—2 Magnanimousness, generosity.<BR>—3 Kindness, compassion, clemency.<BR>—4 Friendship, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजस्
सौजस्, सौजस्क <i>a.</i> Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौजस्क
सौजस्, सौजस्क <i>a.</i> Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौण्डी|सौंडी
सौण्डी Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौतिः|सौति
सौतिः<BR>—1 An epithet of Karṇa.<BR>—2 N. of a great sage; Mb. 1. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्य|सौत्यं
सौत्य <i>a.</i> Relating or devoted to Soma-pressing; बबन्ध वारुणैः<BR> पाशैर्बलिं सौत्येऽहनि क्रतौ Bhāg. 8. 21. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्यम्
सौत्यम्<BR>—1 The office of a charioteer; दीनानायतनस्थो नानायतनक्षमोऽस्य सौत्येऽधिकृतः<BR> Nalod. 4. 9; Bhāg. 1. 15. 17.<BR>—2 The sacrificial act called सवनीय; ऐकादशिनेषु सौत्यस्य द्वैरशन्यस्य<BR> दर्शनात् MS. 8. 1. 14; सौत्य इति सुत्याकालत्वात् सवनीयमाहुः ŚB. on MS. 8. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्र|सौत्रः
सौत्र <i>a.</i> (-त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सूत्र-अण्]<BR>—1 Belonging to or having a thread or string.<BR>—2 Belonging to, mentioned, occurring or declared in, a Sūtra q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रः|सौत्र
सौत्र + .{@-त्रः@}<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—2 An artificial root occurring in grammatical Sūtras which cannot be<BR> conjugated like a regular verb, but is used only to form derivative words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रान्तिकाः
सौत्रान्तिकाः <i>m.</i> pl. N. of one of the four great schools of Buddhism;<BR> cf. सौगत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रामणी
सौत्रामणी<BR>—1 The east; चकोरनयनारुणा भवति दिक् च सौत्रामणी Vb. 4. 1.<BR>—2 A kind of sacrifice involving the use of wine; मुमुदे मदिरादानं<BR> विदन्नेष द्विजन्मनः । दृष्ट्वा सौत्रामणीमिष्टिं तं कुर्वन्तमदूयत ॥<BR> N. 17. 182; Bhāg. 10. 23. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौत्रिकः|सौत्रिक
सौत्रिकः<BR>—1 A weaver.<BR>—2 A texture, anything woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदर्यम्
सौदर्यम्^1 <i>n.</i> Brotherhood. ━<i>a.</i> Brotherly or sisterly.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260501. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/174. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामनी
सौदामनी, सौदामिनी, सौदाम्नी<BR>—1 Lightning; सौदामन्या कनकनिकषस्निग्धया दर्शयोर्वीम् Me. 39; सौदामिनीव<BR> जलदोदरसंधिलीना Mk. 1. 35; Māl. 8. 14.<BR>—2 The female of Indraʼs elephant.<BR>—3 A kind of lightning (forked one); काञ्चनाभं नभश्चक्रे विद्युत्सौदामिनी<BR> यथा Rām. 7. 32. 56; Bhāg. 1. 6. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदामिनी
सौदामनी, सौदामिनी, सौदाम्नी<BR>—1 Lightning; सौदामन्या कनकनिकषस्निग्धया दर्शयोर्वीम् Me. 39; सौदामिनीव<BR> जलदोदरसंधिलीना Mk. 1. 35; Māl. 8. 14.<BR>—2 The female of Indraʼs elephant.<BR>—3 A kind of lightning (forked one); काञ्चनाभं नभश्चक्रे विद्युत्सौदामिनी<BR> यथा Rām. 7. 32. 56; Bhāg. 1. 6. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदाम्नी
सौदामनी, सौदामिनी, सौदाम्नी<BR>—1 Lightning; सौदामन्या कनकनिकषस्निग्धया दर्शयोर्वीम् Me. 39; सौदामिनीव<BR> जलदोदरसंधिलीना Mk. 1. 35; Māl. 8. 14.<BR>—2 The female of Indraʼs elephant.<BR>—3 A kind of lightning (forked one); काञ्चनाभं नभश्चक्रे विद्युत्सौदामिनी<BR> यथा Rām. 7. 32. 56; Bhāg. 1. 6. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदायिक|सौदायिकं
सौदायिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Whatever is given to a woman at her marriage by her<BR> parents, or a relative<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">Page1708-1</a>]<BR> in general, which becomes her own property; मातृपित्रादिभिर्दत्तं धनं<BR> सौदायिकं स्मृतम् Śukra. 4. 814.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौदायिकम्
सौदायिक + .{@-कम्@} A nuptial present so made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1707-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौध|सौधः
सौध <i>a.</i> (-धी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सुधया निर्मितं रक्तं वा अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to, or having, nectar.<BR>—2 Having plaster, or plastered; प्रासादमालासंयुक्ताः सौधप्राकारसंवृताः<BR> Rām. 2. 8. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधम्
सौध + .{@-धम्@}<BR>—1 A white-washed mansion, any stuccoed house; सितं सितिम्ना सुतरां<BR> मुनेर्वपुर्विसारिभिः सौधमिवाथ लम्भयन् Śi. 1. 25.<BR>—2 Any great mansion or palace, large house; सौधवासमुटजेन विस्मृतः<BR> संचिकाय फलनिःस्पृहस्तपः R. 19. 2, 7. 5, 13. 40.<BR>—3 Silver.<BR>—4 Opal.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौधोत्सङ्गः, सौधकारः, सौधमूर्धन्, सौधमौलिः, सौधरोहाधिपः, सौधवासः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधोत्सङ्गः|सौधोत्सङ्ग
सौध + -उत्सङ्गः the level roof of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधकारः|सौधकार
सौध + -कारः<BR>—1 a plasterer; संमार्जितं सौधकारैश्चित्रकारैश्च चित्रितम् Mb. 1. 128. 41.<BR>—2 a builder of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधमूर्धन्
सौध + -मूर्धन्, -मौलिः the top or turret of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधमौलिः|सौधमौलि
सौध + -मूर्धन्, -मौलिः the top or turret of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधरोहाधिपः
सौध + -रोहाधिपः an architect, building supervisor; आरामाधिपतिं चैव<BR> सौधरोहाधिपं पृथक् Śukra. 2. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधवासः|सौधवास
सौध + -वासः a palatial building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधन्वनः|सौधन्वन
सौधन्वनः N. of a caste slightly inferior to the त्रैवर्णिकs,<BR> but superior to the शूद्र; सौधन्वना नाम जातिरभिधीयते । हीनास्तु<BR> किंचित् त्रैवणिंकेभ्यः । जात्यन्तरं न तु शूद्रा न वैश्या न क्षत्रियाः<BR> ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौधर्म्यम्
सौधर्म्यम् Rectitude, honesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन|सौनः
सौन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Relating to butchery or a slaughter-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनम्
सौन + .{@-नम्@} Butcherʼs meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनः|सौन
सौन + .{@-नः@} A butcher. ˚पाल <i>a.</i> having a butcher for a keeper;<BR> कंसे जीवति दाशार्ह सौनपाला इवावयः Bhāg. 10. 38. 41.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौनधर्म्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनधर्म्यम्
सौन + -धर्म्यम् a state of deadly hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनिकः|सौनिक
सौनिकः<BR>—1 A butcher; cf. शौनिक; दश सूनासहस्राणि यो वाहयति सौनिकः Ms. 4. 86.<BR>—2 A hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्दम्
सौनन्दम् The club of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौनन्दिन्|सौनंदिन्
सौनन्दिन् <i>m.</i> An epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौन्दर्यम्
सौन्दर्यम् [सुन्दरस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Beauty, loveliness, gracefulness,<BR> elegance; सुधासौन्दर्यं ते सलिलमशिवं नः शमयतु G. L. 1; सौन्दर्यसारसमुदायनिकेतनं<BR> वा Māl. 1. 21; Ku. 1. 49, 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप
सौप <i>a.</i> Relating to the case terminations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्णम्
सौपर्णम्<BR>—1 Dry ginger.<BR>—2 Emerald. ━<i>a.</i> Relating to सुपर्ण bird or Garuḍa; सौपर्णमस्त्रं<BR> प्रतिसंजहार R. 16. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपर्णेयः|सौपर्णेय
सौपर्णेयः An epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपाकः|सौपाक
सौपाकः A particular mixed tribe; चण्डालेन तु सौपाकः चण्डालसमवृत्तिमान्<BR> Mb. 13. 48. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौपिक
सौपिक <i>a.</i> Sprinkled with sauce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिक|सौप्तिकं
सौप्तिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Connected with or relating to sleep.<BR>—2 Somniferous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिकम्
सौप्तिक + .{@-कम्@} A night-attack, an attack on sleeping men; कृते प्रतिकृतं<BR> पश्य हतपुत्रा हि पाण्डवाः । सौप्तिके शिबिरं तेषां हतं सनरवाहनम् ॥<BR> Mb. 10. 9. 51.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौप्तिकपर्वन्, सौप्तिकवधः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिकपर्वन्
सौप्तिक + -पर्वन् <i>n.</i> N. of the tenth <i>parvan</i> or book of the Mahābhārata<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">Page1708-2</a>]<BR> which relates how Aśvatthāman, Kṛtavarman and Kṛpa-the only surviving<BR> Kuru warriors-attacked by night the Pāṇḍava-camp and slaughtered thousands<BR> of warriors while asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्तिकवधः|सौप्तिकवध
सौप्तिक + -वधः the great nocturnal slaughter of Pāṇḍava-camp (above<BR> referred to); मार्गो ह्येष नरेन्द्रसौप्तिकवधे पूर्वं कृतो द्रौणिना Mk. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौप्रतीक
सौप्रतीक <i>a.</i> Relating to an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबलः|सौबल
सौबलः N. of Śakuni q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबली
सौबली, सौबलेयी N. of Gāndhārī, wife of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौबलेयी
सौबली, सौबलेयी N. of Gāndhārī, wife of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभम्
सौभम्<BR>—1 N. of Hariśchandraʼs city (said to be suspended in air); हतः सौभपतिः<BR> शाल्वस्त्वया सौभं च पाततम् Mb. 3. 12. 32.<BR>—2 N. of a town of the Śālvas; <i>ibid.</i>; Bhāg. 10. 76. 12.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौभपतिः, सौभराज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभपतिः|सौभपति
सौभम् + -पतिः, -राज् a Śālva king; <i>ibid.</i>; यथा सौभपतिर्हतः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 76. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभराज्
सौभम् + -पतिः, -राज् a Śālva king; <i>ibid.</i>; यथा सौभपतिर्हतः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 76. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभीकः
सौभीकः N. of Drupada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभगम्
सौभगम्<BR>—1 Good luck, happiness.<BR>—2 Prosperity, riches, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्रः|सौभद्र
सौभद्रः, सौभद्रेयः Epithets of Abhimanyu, son of Subhadrā;<BR> सौभद्रश्च महाबाहुः Bg. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभद्रेयः|सौभद्रेय
सौभद्रः, सौभद्रेयः Epithets of Abhimanyu, son of Subhadrā;<BR> सौभद्रश्च महाबाहुः Bg. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभरिः|सौभरि
सौभरिः N. of a Vedic seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेयः|सौभागिनेय
सौभागिनेयः The son of a favourite wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यम्
सौभाग्यम् [सुभगायाः सुभगस्य वा भावः ष्यञ् द्विपदवृद्धिः]<BR>—1 Good fortune or luck, fortunateness (chiefly consisting in a manʼs<BR> and womanʼs securing the favour and firm devotion of each other); प्रियेषु<BR> सौभाग्यफला हि चारुता Ku. 5. 1; सौभाग्यं ते सुभग विरहावस्थया व्यञ्जयन्ती<BR> Me. 29; (see Malli.ʼs remarks on सौभाग्य in both places); युज्यत<BR> आत्मनः सौभाग्यं प्रच्छादयितुम् V. 2.<BR>—2 Blessedness, auspiciousness; समृद्धं सौभाग्यं सकलवसुधायाः किमपि तत् G. L. 1.<BR>—3 Beauty, charm, grace; (यस्य) हिमं न सौभाग्यविलोपि जातम्<BR> Ku. 1. 3, 2. 53, 5. 49; R. 18. 19; U. 6. 27.<BR>—4 Grandeur, sublimity.<BR>—5 The auspicious state of wifehood (opp. widowhood).<BR>—6 Congratulation; good wishes.<BR>—7 Affection, favour.<BR>—8 Red-lead.<BR>—9 Borax.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौभाग्यचिह्नम्, सौभाग्यतन्तुः, सौभाग्यतृतीया, सौभाग्यदेवता, सौभाग्यवायनम्, सौभाग्यविलोपिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यचिह्नम्
सौभाग्यम् + -चिह्नम्<BR>—1 any mark of good fortune or happiness.<BR>—2 any sign of the blessed state of wifehood (such as the saffron mark<BR> on the forehead).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यतन्तुः|सौभाग्यतन्तु|सौभाग्यतंतु
सौभाग्यम् + -तन्तुः the marriage string (put round the neck of the bride by<BR> the bridegroom at the time of marriage and worn by her till widowhood;<BR> also called मङ्गलसूत्र q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यतृतीया
सौभाग्यम् + -तृतीया the third day of the bright half of Bhādrapada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यदेवता
सौभाग्यम् + -देवता an auspicious or tutelary deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवायनम्
सौभाग्यम् + -वायनम् an auspicious offering of sweetmeats &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यविलोपिन्
सौभाग्यम् + -विलोपिन् <i>a.</i> marring or impairing beauty; अनन्तरत्नप्रभवस्य<BR> यस्य हिमं न सौभाग्यविलोपि जातम् Ku. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवत्|सौभाग्यवन्त्
सौभाग्यवत् <i>a.</i> Fortunate, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवती
सौभाग्यवत् + .{@-ती@} A married woman whose husband is alive, a married unwidowed woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1708-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाञ्जनः|सौभाञ्जन
सौभाञ्जनः See शोभाञ्जनः (Mar. शेवगा); Mb. 13. 91. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभिकः|सौभिक
सौभिकः A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभिक्ष
सौभिक्ष <i>a.</i> Bringing security and abundance of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ्रात्रम्
सौभ्रात्रम् Good brotherhood, fraternity; सौभ्रात्रमेषां हि कुलानुसारि<BR> R. 16. 1, 10. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम
सौम <i>a.</i> Relating or belonging to Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमकिः|सौमकि
सौमकिः The king Drupada; पूर्वस्नेहानुरागित्वात् सदारः सौमकिं<BR> गतः Mb. 1. 132. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमङ्गल्यम्
सौमङ्गल्यम्<BR>—1 Welfare, prosperity.<BR>—2 Any object of the blessed state of wifehood (सौभाग्य); तथा राज्ञ्यपि<BR> वैदेही सौमङ्गल्यावशेषिता Bhāg. 9. 11. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस
सौमनस <i>a.</i> (-सा or -सी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सुमनस्-अण्]<BR>—1 Agreeable to the feelings, pleasing.<BR>—2 Relating to flowers, floral; मम न सौमनसौ मनसो मुदे Śi. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनसम्
सौमनस + .{@-सम्@}<BR>—1 Kindliness of spirit, benevolence, kindness.<BR>—2 Pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>—3 The nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनसा
सौमनसा The outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यम्
सौमनस्यम्<BR>—1 Satisfaction of mind, pleasure, delight; संतानश्रवणाद्भ्रातुः सौमित्रिः<BR> सौमनस्यवान् R. 15. 14, 17. 40; Pt. 5. 97.<BR>—2 A particular offering of flowers made to a Brāhmaṇa at a Śrāddha.<BR>—3 A flower; रत्नोदधारौषधिसौमनस्यवनस्रजो वेणुभुजाङ्घ्रिपाङ्घ्रेः<BR> Bhāg. 3. 8. 24. ━<i>a.</i> causing cheerfulness of mind; Bhāg. 4. 12. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यायनी
सौमनस्यायनी<BR>—1 The blossom of the Mālatī creeper.<BR>—2 The Mālatī creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमायनः|सौमायन
सौमायनः A patronymic of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Performed with or relating to the Soma juice.<BR>—2 Relating to the moon, lunar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमितिकम्
सौमितिकम् A variety of woollen cloth; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्रः|सौमित्र
सौमित्रः, -सौमित्रिः<BR> An epithet of Lakṣmaṇa; सौमित्रेरपि पत्रिणामविषये<BR> तत्र प्रिये क्वासि भोः U. 3. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्रिः|सौमित्रि
सौमित्रः, -सौमित्रिः<BR> An epithet of Lakṣmaṇa; सौमित्रेरपि पत्रिणामविषये<BR> तत्र प्रिये क्वासि भोः U. 3. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिल्लः|सौमिल्ल
सौमिल्लः N. of a dramatist who preceded Kālidāsa; भासकविसौमिल्लकविमिश्रादीनाम् M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमुख्यम्
सौमुख्यम् Gentle appearance; cheerfulness; सौमुख्यतस्तु श्रियमस्य<BR> केचिद् वैपुल्यमाशंसिषुरायुषश्च Bu. C. 3. 11; सौमुख्यमुख्यभवनं<BR> सौहार्दैकवितर्दिका Viś. Guṇā. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेचकम्
सौमेचकम् Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेधिकः|सौमेधिक
सौमेधिकः A sage, seer, one possessed of supernatural wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

