सौमेरव, -रुक + .({@-रवी, -रुकी@} <i>f.</i>) Relating to or coming from Sumeru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरवम्
सौमेरव, -रुक + .{@-रवम्, -रुकम्@} Gold; सौमेरवीमधिगतेन नितम्बशोभाम् Śi. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरुकम्
सौमेरव, -रुक + .{@-रवम्, -रुकम्@} Gold; सौमेरवीमधिगतेन नितम्बशोभाम् Śi. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्य|सौम्यः
सौम्य <i>a.</i> (-म्या or -म्यी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सोमो देवतास्य तस्येदं वा अण्]<BR>—1 Relating or sacred to the moon.<BR>—2 Having the properties of Soma.<BR>—3 Handsome, lovely, charming; pleasing, agreeable.<BR>—4 Gentle, soft, mild, placid; संरम्भं मैथिलीहासः क्षणसौम्यां निनाय<BR> ताम् R. 12. 36; सौम्यस्वभावोऽपि पृथुप्रतापः (where सौम्य means<BR> both ‘gentle’ and ‘lunar’) Bu. C. 1. 10; (the voc. सौम्य is often<BR> used in the sense of ‘good sir’, ‘gentle sir’, ‘good man’; प्रीतास्मि<BR> ते सौम्य चिराय जीव R. 14. 59; सौम्येति चाभाष्य यथार्थवादी 14. 44;<BR> Me. 51; Ku. 4. 35; Māl. 9. 25).<BR>—5 Auspicious.<BR>—6 Bright, brilliant.<BR>—7 Cool, moist.<BR>—8 Northern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यः|सौम्य
सौम्य + .{@-म्यः@}<BR>—1 N. of Budha or the planet Mercury.<BR>—2 A proper epithet by which a Brāhmaṇa should be addressed; आयुष्मान्<BR> भव सौम्येति वाच्यो विप्रोऽभिवादने Ms. 2. 125.<BR>—3 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—4 The Udumbara tree.<BR>—5 Blood before it becomes red, serum.<BR>—6 The gastric juice.<BR>—7 N. of one of the nine divisions of the earth.<BR>—8 An auspicious planet.<BR>—9 A Brāhmaṇa drinking the Soma juice.<BR>—10 A kind of penance (सौम्यकृच्छ्र).<BR>—11 An adherent, worshipper; पपुर्ज्ञानमयं सौम्या यन्मुखाम्बुरुहासवम्<BR> Bhāg. 2. 4. 24.<BR>—12 The left hand.<BR>—13 The month मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यम्
सौम्य + .{@-म्यम्@}<BR>—1 Gentleness.<BR>—2 The मृगशिरस् constellation.<BR>—3 The left eye.<BR>—4 The middle of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्या
सौम्य + .{@-म्या@}<BR>—1 N. of Durgā.<BR>—2 The moon-plant.<BR>—3 A pearl.<BR>—4 The मृगशिरस् constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यी
सौम्य + .{@-म्यी@} Moon-shine. ━<i>m.</i> pl.<BR>—1 N. of the five stars in Orionʼs head.<BR>—2 A particular class of Pitṛs or Manes; अग्निष्वात्तांश्च सौम्यांश्च<BR> विप्राणामेव निर्दिशेत् Ms. 3. 199.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौम्योपचारः, सौम्यकृच्छ्रः, सौम्यकृच्छ्रम्, सौम्यगन्धी, सौम्यगोलः, सौम्यग्रहः, सौम्यधातुः, सौम्यनामन्, सौम्यवारः, सौम्यवासरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्योपचारः|सौम्योपचार
सौम्य + -उपचारः a gentle measure, mild remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यकृच्छ्रः|सौम्यकृच्छ्र
सौम्य + -कृच्छ्रः, -कृच्छ्रम् a kind of religious penance; पिण्याकाचामतक्राम्बुसक्तूनां<BR> प्रतिवासरम् । एकरात्रोपवासश्च कृच्छ्रः सौम्योऽयमुच्यते ॥ Y. 3. 321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यकृच्छ्रम्
सौम्य + -कृच्छ्रः, -कृच्छ्रम् a kind of religious penance; पिण्याकाचामतक्राम्बुसक्तूनां<BR> प्रतिवासरम् । एकरात्रोपवासश्च कृच्छ्रः सौम्योऽयमुच्यते ॥ Y. 3. 321.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यगन्धी|सौम्यगंधी
सौम्य + -गन्धी the Indian white rose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यगोलः|सौम्यगोल
सौम्य + -गोलः the northern hemisphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यग्रहः|सौम्यग्रह
सौम्य + -ग्रहः a benign or auspicious planet (as बुध, गुरु, शुक्र<BR> and चन्द्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यधातुः|सौम्यधातु
सौम्य + -धातुः the phlegmatic humour, phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यनामन्
सौम्य + -नामन् <i>a.</i> having a pleasing or agreeable name; Ms. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यवारः|सौम्यवार
सौम्य + -वारः, -वासरः Wednesday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यवासरः|सौम्यवासर
सौम्य + -वारः, -वासरः Wednesday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यता
सौम्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Gentleness.<BR>—2 Benevolence.<BR>—3 Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्यत्वम्
सौम्यता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Gentleness.<BR>—2 Benevolence.<BR>—3 Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर|सौरः
सौर <i>a.</i> (-री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [सूरस्य इदं सूरो देवतास्य वा अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to the sun, solar.<BR>—2 Sacred or dedicated to the sun.<BR>—3 Worshipping the sun.<BR>—4 Celestial, divine.<BR>—5 Relating to spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरः|सौर
सौर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A worshipper of the sun; Mb. 7. 82. 16.<BR>—2 The planet Saturn.<BR>—3 A solar month.<BR>—4 A solar day.<BR>—5 The plant called Tumburu.<BR>—6 N. of Yama, the god of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरम्
सौर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 N. of a collection of hymns (extracted from the Ṛgveda) addressed to <i>Sūrya</i>.<BR>—2 The right eye.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: सौरनक्तम्, सौरमासः, सौरलोकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरनक्तम्
सौर + -नक्तम् a particular religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरमासः|सौरमास
सौर + -मासः a solar month (comprising thirty risings and settings of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरलोकः|सौरलोक
सौर + -लोकः the sunʼs sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरत|सौरतः
सौरत <i>a.</i> Relating to sexual enjoyment; स्मायावलोक. लवदर्शितभावहारिभ्रूमण्डलप्रहितसौरतमन्त्रशौण्डैः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 61. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">Page1710-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरतम्
सौरत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Sexual enjoyment; Bhāg. 5. 17. 12.<BR>—2 Seminal fluid (रेतस्); सिषेव आत्मन्यवरुद्वसौरतः Bhāg. 10. 33. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरतः|सौरत
सौरत + .{@-तः@} Mild wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1709-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरथः|सौरथ
सौरथः A hero, warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ|सौरभं
सौरभ <i>a.</i> (-भी <i>f.</i>) [सुरभिरस्यास्ति अण्] Fragrant;<BR> देवस्त्रीमज्जनामोदसौरभाम्ब्वनिलैर्युतः Bhāg. 8. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभम्
सौरभ + .{@-भम्@}<BR>—1 Fragrance; मधुप इव मारुतेऽस्मिन् मा सौरभलोभमम्बुजिनि मंस्थाः<BR> Bv. 1. 18, 121.<BR>—2 Saffron. (See grammatical note on सौरभ्य below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेय|सौरभेयः
सौरभेय <i>a.</i> (-यी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to <i>Surabhi</i>.<BR>—2 Fragrant; ननु नागा महावीर्याः सौरभेयास्तरस्विनः Mb. 12. 360. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेयः|सौरभेय
सौरभेय + .{@-यः@} An ox; मा सौरभेयानुशुचो व्येतु ते वृषलाद्भयम् Bhāg. 1. 17. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभी
सौरभी, सौरभेयी<BR>—1 A cow.<BR>—2 N. of the daughter of the cow called <i>Surabhi</i>; तां सौरभेयीं<BR> सुरभिर्यशोभिः R. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेयी
सौरभी, सौरभेयी<BR>—1 A cow.<BR>—2 N. of the daughter of the cow called <i>Surabhi</i>; तां सौरभेयीं<BR> सुरभिर्यशोभिः R. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्यः|सौरभ्य|सौरभ्यं
सौरभ्यः N. of Kubera; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्यम्
सौरभ्यम्<BR>—1 Fragrance, odour, sweet scent; सौरभ्यं भुवनत्रयेऽपि विदितम्<BR> Bv. 1. 38; पुनाना सौरभ्यैः G. L. 43; R. 5. 69.<BR>—2 Agreeableness, beauty.<BR>—3 Good character, reputation, glory, fame. [Dr. Kṣitīśachandra Chatterjee<BR> writes in Mañjūṣā, “Like चापल and चापल्य, both सौरभ<BR> and सौरभ्य are found in Sanskrit, but Pāṇini has made provision<BR> for both चापल and चापल्य by including the word चपल both<BR> in the युवादि group and in the ब्राह्मणादि group. सुरभि is<BR> included in neither of these groups but comes under the purview of the<BR> rule इगन्ताच्च लघुपूर्वात् and so the only form sanctioned by Pāṇini<BR> is सौरभ. It would appear that सौरभ्य came into use later on<BR> after the analogy of सौगन्ध्य.]”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसः|सौरस
सौरसः<BR>—1 Salted broth.<BR>—2 A kind of insect infesting the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसा
सौरसः + .{@-सा@} The mountain jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेनाः
सौरसेनाः <i>m.</i> pl. N. of a district and its people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेनी
सौरसेनाः + .{@-नी@} See शौरसेनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेयः|सौरसेय
सौरसेयः An epithet of Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैंधव|सौरसैन्धवः
सौरसैन्धव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to the celestial river or Ganges, Gangetic;<BR> पयसां प्रवाह इव सौरसैन्धवः Śi. 13. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैन्धवः|सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैंधव
सौरसैन्धव + .{@-वः@} A horse of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरस्यम्
सौरस्यम् Tastiness, savouriness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराज्यम्
सौराज्यम् Good government or rule; एको ययौ चैत्ररथप्रदेशान् सौराज्यरम्यानपरो<BR> विदर्भान् R. 5. 60; तन्वन् सौराज्यमधिकं नदीं भागीरथीमनु Śiva B. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरावः|सौराव
सौरावः Salted broth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्र|सौराष्ट्रः
सौराष्ट्र <i>a.</i> (-ष्ट्रा or -ष्ट्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> Coming from or relating to the district called Surāṣṭra (or Surat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रः|सौराष्ट्र
सौराष्ट्र + .{@-ष्ट्रः@} The district of Surāṣṭra. ━<i>m.</i> pl. The people of Surāṣṭra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रम्
सौराष्ट्र + .{@-ष्ट्रम्@} Brass, bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्री
सौराष्ट्र + .{@-ष्ट्री@} A kind of fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1710-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रकः|सौराष्ट्रक|सौराष्ट्रकं
