स्कन्धबन्धना|स्कंधबंधना
स्कन्धः + -बन्धना a sort of fennel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धमल्लकः|स्कन्धमल्लक|स्कंधमल्लक
स्कन्धः + -मल्लकः a heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धरुहः|स्कन्धरुह|स्कंधरुह
स्कन्धः + -रुहः the (Indian) figtree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाहः|स्कन्धवाह|स्कंधवाह
स्कन्धः + -वाहः, -वाहकः an ox trained to carry burdens, pack-bullock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धवाहकः|स्कन्धवाहक|स्कंधवाहक
स्कन्धः + -वाहः, -वाहकः an ox trained to carry burdens, pack-bullock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशाखा|स्कंधशाखा
स्कन्धः + -शाखा a principal branch, the forked branch issuing from the upper<BR> stem of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धशृङ्गः|स्कन्धशृङ्ग|स्कंधशृंग
स्कन्धः + -शृङ्गः a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्कन्धः|स्कन्धस्कन्ध|स्कंधस्कंध
स्कन्धः + -स्कन्धः every shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धस्|स्कंधस्
स्कन्धस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 The shoulder.<BR>—2 The trunk of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिकः|स्कन्धिक|स्कंधिक|स्कंधिकः
स्कन्धिकः An ox trained to carry burdens; cf. स्कन्धवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्धिन्|स्कंधिन्
स्कन्धिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Having shoulders.<BR>—2 Having branches or a branched stem. ━<i>m.</i> A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भ्|स्कंभ्
स्कम्भ् €1 Ā., €5. €9 P. (स्कम्भते, स्कभ्नोति, स्कभ्नाति)<BR>—1 To create.<BR>—2 To stop, hinder, impede, obstruct, curb, restrain; स्कभायत निरृतिं<BR> सेधतामतिम् Rv. 10. 76. 4.<BR>—3 To prop, support; चस्कम्भ यः स्वरभसाऽस्खलता त्रिपृष्ठम् Bhāg. 2. 7. 40.<BR>━<i>Caus.</i> (स्कम्भयति-ते or स्कम्भायति-ते) To stop &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कब्ध
स्कब्ध <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Supported, propped.<BR>—2 Stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भः|स्कम्भ|स्कंभ|स्कंभः
स्कम्भः<BR>—1 Support, prop, stay.<BR>—2 Fulcrum.<BR>—3 The Supreme Being.<BR>—4 N. of the Vedic deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कम्भनम्
स्कम्भनम्<BR>—1 The act of supporting.<BR>—2 A support, prop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कान्द|स्कांद|स्कान्दं
स्कान्द <i>a.</i> (-न्दी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्कन्द-अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to Skanda.<BR>—2 Relating to Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कान्दम्
स्कान्द + .{@-न्दम्@} The Skanda Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कु
स्कु €5. €9 U. (स्कुनोति, स्कुनुते, स्कुनाति, स्कुनीते)<BR>—1 To go up by leaps, jump, bound.<BR>—2 To raise, lift.<BR>—3 To cover, overspread; अस्कुनाच्चेषुवृष्टिभिः Bk. 17. 82.<BR>—4 To approach. ━<i>With</i> {@प्रति@} to cover; Bk. 18. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुन्द्|स्कुंद्
स्कुन्द् €1 Ā. (स्कुन्दते)<BR>—1 To jump.<BR>—2 To raise, lift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुम्भ्|स्कुंभ्
स्कुम्भ् €5. €9 P. (स्कुभ्ना-भ्नो-ति) To stop, hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कोटिका
स्कोटिका A kind of wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खद्
स्खद् €1 Ā. (स्खदते)<BR>—1 To cut, cut or tear to pieces.<BR>—2 To destroy.<BR>—3 To hurt, injure, kill.<BR>—4 To rout, defeat completely.<BR>—5 To fatigue, exhaust, trouble.<BR>—6 To make or be firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खदनम्
स्खदनम्<BR>—1 Cutting, tearing to pieces.<BR>—2 Hurting, injuring, killing.<BR>—3 Troubling, harassing.<BR>—4 Firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल्
स्खल् €1 P. (स्खलति, स्खलित)<BR>—1 To stumble, tumble, fall down, slip, trip; स्खलति चरणं भूमौ न्यस्तं<BR> न चार्द्रतमा मही Mk. 9. 13; Ku. 5. 24.<BR>—2 To totter, waver, shake, fluctuate.<BR>—3 To be disobeyed or violated (as an order); देवस्य शासनं पौरेषु<BR> कथं स्खलिष्यति Mu. 3, 3. 24; R. 18. 43.<BR>—4 To fall or deviate from the right course; मन्मथेन परिलुप्तमतीनां<BR> प्रायशः स्खलितमप्युपकारि Ki. 9. 37.<BR>—5 To be affected or excited; मात्सर्यरागोपहतात्मनां हि स्खलन्ति साधुष्वपि<BR> मानसानि Ki. 3. 53, 13. 6.<BR>—6 To err, blunder, commit mistakes; स्खलतो हि करालम्बः सुहृत्सचिवचेष्टितम्<BR> H. 3. 127 (where it has sense 1 also).<BR>—7 To stammer, lisp, falter; वदनकमलकं शिशोः स्मरामि स्खलदसमञ्जसमञ्जुजल्पितं<BR> ते U. 4. 4; R. 9. 76; Ku. 5. 56.<BR>—8 To fail, have no effect; राघवः स्खलितवीर्यमात्मनि R. 11. 83.<BR>—9 To drop, drip, trickle; विपङ्कतीरस्खलितोर्मिसंहतिः Ki. 8. 27.<BR>—10 To go, move.<BR>—11 To disappear.<BR>—12 To collect, gather. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्खलयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to stumble or trip.<BR>—2 To cause to err or blunder, cause to falter or stammer; वचनानि<BR> स्खलयन् पदे पदे Ku. 4. 12; स्खलयति वचनं ते संश्रयत्यङ्गमङ्गम् Māl. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलनम्
स्खलनम् [स्खल्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Stumbling, slipping, tripping, falling down.<BR>—2 Tottering.<BR>—3 Deviating from the right course.<BR>—4 Blundering, error, mistake.<BR>—5 Failure, disappointment, unsuccessfulness.<BR>—6 Stammering,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">Page1713-1</a>]<BR> blundering in speech or pronunciation, faltering.<BR>—7 Trickling, dripping.<BR>—8 Dashing against, clashing, collision; स्खलनमुखरभूरिस्रोतसो निर्झरिण्यः<BR> U. 2. 20; Mv. 5. 40.<BR>—9 Mutual striking or rubbing together.<BR>—10 Discharge, emission (of semen); Kull. on Ms. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1712-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित|स्खलितं
स्खलित <i>p. p.</i> [स्खल्-क्त]<BR>—1 Stumbled, slipped, tripped.<BR>—2 Fallen, dropped down.<BR>—3 Shaking, wavering, fluctuating, unsteady.<BR>—4 Intoxicated, drunk.<BR>—5 Stammering, faltering; सबाष्पकण्ठस्खलितैः पदैरियम् Ku. 5. 56.<BR>—6 Agitated, disturbed.<BR>—7 Erring, blundering; सर्वत्र स्खलितेषु दत्तमनसा यातं मया नोद्धतम् Ve. 2. 1<BR>—8 Dropped, emitted.<BR>—9 Dripping, trickling down.<BR>—10 Interrupted, stopped.<BR>—11 Confounded.<BR>—12 Gone.<BR>—13 Wounded; यद्यत्र स्खलितं गात्रं तत्र दम्भं प्रपातयेत् Śukra. 4. 970.<BR>—14 Incomplete, deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलितम्
स्खलित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Stumbling, tripping, a fall.<BR>—2 Deviation from the right course.<BR>—3 Error, blunder, mistake; गोत्रस्खलित Ku. 4. 8.<BR>—4 Fault, sin, transgression.<BR>—5 Deceit, treachery.<BR>—6 Circumvention, stratagem.<BR>—7 Loss, deprivation.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्खलितसुभगम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलितसुभगम्
स्खलित + -सुभगम् <i>ind.</i> dashing or flowing along in a charming manner;<BR> संसर्पन्त्याः स्खलितसुभगं दर्शितावर्तनाभेः Me. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खुड्
स्खुड् €6 P. (स्खुडति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तक्
स्तक् €1 P. (स्तकति)<BR>—1 To resist.<BR>—2 To strike against, repel, push back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तत्कः
स्तत्कः A drop; यथा पानीयस्य तैलस्य घृतस्य वा स्तत्का नानादेशेषु<BR> भिन्नाः समानदशे एकीभूता भवन्ति तद्वद् रश्मयः ŚB. on MS. 9. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्
स्तन् €1 P., €10 U. (स्तनति, स्तनयति-ते, स्तनित)<BR>—1 To sound, make a sound, resound, reverberate.<BR>—2 To groan, breathe hard, sigh.<BR>—3 To thunder, roar loudly; तस्तनुर्जज्वलुर्मम्लुर्जग्लुर्लुलुठिरे क्षताः<BR> Bk. 14. 30. ━<i>With</i> {@नि@}<BR>—1 to sound.<BR>—2 to sigh.<BR>—3 to mourn. ━<i>With</i> {@वि@} to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनः|स्तन
स्तनः [स्तन्-अच्]<BR>—1 The female breast; स्तनौ मांसग्रन्थी कनककलशावित्युपमितौ Bh. 3. 20;<BR> (दरिद्राणां मनोरथाः) हृदयेष्वेव लीयन्ते विधवास्त्रीस्तनाविव Pt. 2. 91.<BR>—2 The nipple of the breast.<BR>—3 The breast, udder, or dug of any female animal; अर्धपीतस्तनं मातुरामर्दक्लिष्टकेशरम् Ś. 7. 14.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तनांशुकम्, स्तनाग्रः, स्तनाङ्गरागः, स्तनान्तरम्, स्तनाभुज, स्तनाभोगः, स्तनावरणम्, स्तनोपपीडम्, स्तनकलशः, स्तनकुड्मलम्, स्तनकोटिः, स्तनग्रहः, स्तनचूचुकम्, स्तनतटः, स्तनतटम्, स्तनत्यागः, स्तनप, स्तनपा, स्तनपायक, स्तनपायिन्, स्तनपतनम्, स्तनपानम्, स्तनभरः, स्तनभवः, स्तनमध्यः, स्तनमुखम्, स्तनवृन्तम्, स्तनशिखा, स्तनरोहितः, स्तनरोहितम्, स्तनवेपथुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनांशुकम्
स्तनः + -अंशुकम् a cloth covering the breasts or bosom, breast-mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाग्रः|स्तनाग्र|स्तनाग्रं
स्तनः + -अग्रः a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाङ्गरागः|स्तनाङ्गराग|स्तनांगराग
स्तनः + -अङ्गरागः a paint or pigment smeared on the breasts of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनान्तरम्
स्तनः + -अन्तरम्<BR>—1 the heart.<BR>—2 the space between the breasts; (न) मृणालसूत्रं रचितं स्तनान्तरे<BR> Ś. 6. 17; R. 10. 62.<BR>—3 a mark on the breast (said to indicate future widowhood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाभुज
स्तनः + -आभुज <i>a.</i> feeding with the udder (said of cows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनाभोगः|स्तनाभोग
स्तनः + -आभोगः<BR>—1 fulness or expanding of the breasts.<BR>—2 the circumference or orb of the breast. —3 a man with large breasts<BR> like those of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनावरणम्
स्तनः + -आवरणम् a breast-cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनोपपीडम्
स्तनः + -उपपीडम् pressing the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनकलशः|स्तनकलश
स्तनः + -कलशः a jar-like breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनकुड्मलम्
स्तनः + -कुड्मलम् a womanʼs breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनकोटिः|स्तनकोटि
स्तनः + -कोटिः the nipple of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनग्रहः|स्तनग्रह
स्तनः + -ग्रहः the sucking or drawing of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनचूचुकम्
स्तनः + -चूचुकम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">Page1713-2</a>]<BR> the nipple of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनतटः|स्तनतट
स्तनः + -तटः, -तटम् the slope or projection of the breast; cf. तट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनतटम्
स्तनः + -तटः, -तटम् the slope or projection of the breast; cf. तट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनत्यागः|स्तनत्याग
स्तनः + -त्यागः weaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनप|स्तनपः
स्तनः + -प, -पा, -पायक, -पायिन् <i>a.</i> sucking the breast, suckling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपा
स्तनः + -प, -पा, -पायक, -पायिन् <i>a.</i> sucking the breast, suckling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपायक
स्तनः + -प, -पा, -पायक, -पायिन् <i>a.</i> sucking the breast, suckling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपायिन्
स्तनः + -प, -पा, -पायक, -पायिन् <i>a.</i> sucking the breast, suckling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपतनम्
स्तनः + -पतनम् flaccidity of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनपानम्
स्तनः + -पानम् sucking of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनभरः|स्तनभर
स्तनः + -भरः<BR>—1 the weight or heaviness of breasts; पादाग्रस्थितया मुहुः स्तनभरेणानीतया<BR> नम्रताम् Ratn. 1. 1.<BR>—2 a man having breasts like those of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनभवः|स्तनभव
स्तनः + -भवः a particular position in sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमध्यः|स्तनमध्य
स्तनः + -मध्यः a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमध्यम्
स्तनः + -मध्यः + .({@-ध्यम्@}) the space between the breasts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनमुखम्
स्तनः + -मुखम्, -वृन्तम्, -शिखा a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनवृन्तम्
स्तनः + -मुखम्, -वृन्तम्, -शिखा a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनशिखा
स्तनः + -मुखम्, -वृन्तम्, -शिखा a nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनरोहितः|स्तनरोहित
स्तनः + -रोहितः, -रोहितम् a particular part of the female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनरोहितम्
स्तनः + -रोहितः, -रोहितम् a particular part of the female breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनवेपथुः|स्तनवेपथु
स्तनः + -वेपथुः the heaving of the breast; अद्यापि स्तनवेपथुं जनयति<BR> श्वासः प्रमाणाधिकः Ś. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनथः|स्तनथ
स्तनथः Ved. Thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तननम्
स्तननम् [स्तन्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Sounding, a sound, noise.<BR>—2 Roaring, thundering, rumbling (of clouds).<BR>—3 Groaning.<BR>—4 Breathing hard.<BR>—5 The sound of a hollow cough; Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनंधय|स्तनन्धय|स्तनंधयः|स्तनन्धयः
स्तनंधय <i>a.</i> [स्तनं धयति धे-खश् मुम् च] Sucking the breast;<BR> यदि बुध्यते हरिशिशुः स्तनंधयो भविता करेणुपरिशेषिता मही Bv. 1. 53;<BR> तवाङ्कशायी परिवृत्तभाग्यया मया न दृष्टस्तनयः स्तनंधयः Māl. 10. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनंधयः|स्तनन्धय|स्तनंधय|स्तनन्धयः
स्तनंधय + .{@-यः@} An infant, a suckling; स्तनंधयप्रीतिमवाप्स्यसि त्वम्<BR> R. 14. 78; Śi. 12. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयित्नुः|स्तनयित्नु
स्तनयित्नुः [स्तन्-इत्नु]<BR>—1 Thundering, thunder, the muttering of clouds; मौर्वीघोषस्तनयित्नुः<BR> पृषत्कपृषतो महान् Mb. 6. 14. 27; Bhāg. 1. 14. 15.<BR>—2 A cloud; स्तनयित्नोर्मयूरीव चकितोत्कण्ठितं स्थिता U. 3. 7, 5. 8.<BR>—3 Lightning.<BR>—4 Sickness.<BR>—5 Death.<BR>—6 A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनित|स्तनितं
स्तनित <i>p. p.</i> [स्तन्-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>—1 Sounded, sounding, noisy; वीचिक्षोभस्तनितबिहगश्रेणिकाञ्चीगुणायाः Me. 28.<BR>—2 Thundering, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनितम्
स्तनित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The rattling of thunder, rumbling of thunder-clouds; तोयोत्सर्गस्तनितमुखरो<BR> मास्म भूर्विक्लवास्ताः Me. 39.<BR>—2 Thunder, noise.<BR>—3 The noise of clapping the hands.<BR>—4 The sound of a vibrating bow-string.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तनितकुमाराः, स्तनितफलः, स्तनितसुभगम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनितकुमाराः
स्तनित + -कुमाराः (with Jainas) a particular class of gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनितफलः|स्तनितफल
स्तनित + -फलः the Vikaṅkata tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनितसुभगम्
स्तनित + -सुभगम् <i>ind.</i> with pleasant rumbling sounds; तीरोपान्तस्तनितसुभगं<BR> पास्यसि स्वादु यत्र Me. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्यम्
स्तन्यम् [स्तने भवं यत्] Motherʼs milk, milk; स्मरति न भवान्<BR> पीतं स्तन्यं विभज्य सहामुना Ve. 5. 41; पिब स्तन्यं पोत Bv. 1. 60.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तन्यत्यागः, स्तन्यद, स्तन्यप<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्यत्यागः|स्तन्यत्याग
स्तन्यम् + -त्यागः leaving off the motherʼs milk, weaning; स्तत्यत्यागात्<BR> प्रभृति सुमुखी दन्तपाञ्चालिकेव Māl. 10. 5; स्तन्यत्यागं यावत् पुत्रयोरवेक्षस्व U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्यद
स्तन्यम् + -द <i>a.</i> producing (good) milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्यप
स्तन्यम् + -प <i>a.</i> suckling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तबकः|स्तबक
स्तबकः<BR>—1 A bunch, cluster; कुसुमस्तबकस्येव द्वे गती स्तो मनस्विनाम् Bh. 2. 104;<BR> R. 13. 32; Me. 77; Ku. 3. 39.<BR>—2 A feather of a peacockʼs tail.<BR>—3 A tassel.<BR>—4 A chapter or section of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभ्
स्तभ् See स्तम्भ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध|स्तब्धः
स्तब्ध <i>p. p.</i> [स्तम्भ् कर्मणि कर्तरि वा क्त]<BR>—1 Stopped, blocked up, obstructed.<BR>—2 Paralysed, senseless, stupefied, benumbed.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">Page1714-1</a>]<BR>—3 Motionless, immoveable; किंचित् किंचिच्छकृन्मुञ्चन् मूत्रयन् स्तब्धलोचनः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 36. 3.<BR>—4 Fixed, firm, hard, rigid, stiff.<BR>—5 Obstinate, stubborn, hard-hearted, stern; आत्मसंभाविताः स्तब्धा धनमानमदान्विताः Bg. 16. 17.<BR>—6 Coarse.<BR>—7 Solidified (as water).<BR>—8 Tardy, slack; inactive; सद्भिराचरितः पन्था येन स्तब्धेन दूषितः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 2. 10.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तब्धकर्ण, स्तब्धपाद, स्तब्धबाहु, स्तब्धमति, स्तब्धरोमन्, स्तब्धलोचन<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1713-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धकर्ण
स्तब्ध + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> pricking up the ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धपाद
स्तब्ध + -पाद <i>a.</i> stifflegged, lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धबाहु
स्तब्ध + -बाहु <i>a.</i> stiff-armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धमति
स्तब्ध + -मति <i>a.</i> dull-minded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धरोमन्
स्तब्ध + -रोमन् <i>m.</i> a hog, boar; स्तब्धरोमसमारब्धघर्घरस्वरघोषणाम्<BR> Śiva B. 31. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धलोचन
स्तब्ध + -लोचन <i>a.</i> having motionless or unwinking eyes (said of gods).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धता
स्तब्धता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Rigidity, firmness, hardness.<BR>—2 Stupor, insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धत्वम्
स्तब्धता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Rigidity, firmness, hardness.<BR>—2 Stupor, insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धिः|स्तब्धि
स्तब्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Fixedness, hardness, stiffness, rigidity.<BR>—2 Firmness, immoveableness.<BR>—3 Stupor, insensibility, numbness.<BR>—4 Obstinacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभः|स्तभ
स्तभः A goat, ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभिः|स्तभि
स्तभिः Rigidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभु
स्तभु <i>n.</i> = स्तम्भन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्
स्तम् €1 P. (स्तमति) To be confused or agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बः|स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तंबः
स्तम्बः [स्था-अम्बच् किच्च पृषो˚ Uṇ. 4. 96]<BR>—1 A clump of grass &c.; ब्रह्मस्तम्बनिकुञ्जपुञ्जितघनज्याघोषघोरं धनुः<BR> Mv. 3. 48; आरण्यकोपात्तफलप्रसूतिः स्तम्बेन नीवार इवावशिष्टः R. 5. 15.<BR>—2 A sheaf of corn; as in स्तम्बकरिता q. v.<BR>—3 A cluster, clump or bunch (in general); (कीचक) स्तम्बाडम्बरमूकमौकुलिकुलः<BR> क्रौञ्चावतोऽयं गिरिः U. 2. 29; R. 15. 19.<BR>—4 A bush, thicket.<BR>—5 A shrub or plant having no decided stem.<BR>—6 The post to which an elephant is tied.<BR>—7 A post; column; पांशुस्तम्बा बलानां तुरगखुरपुटक्षोदलब्धात्मलाभाः Mu. 5. 23.<BR>—8 Stupefaction, insensibility; (probably for स्तभ in these two senses).<BR>—9 A mountain.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तम्बकरि, स्तम्बकरिता, स्तम्बगहन, स्तम्बघनः, स्तम्बघ्नः, स्तम्बघातः, स्तम्बहन्, स्तम्बहननम्, स्तम्बहननी, स्तम्बपुरम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरि|स्तंबकरि|स्तम्बकरिः
स्तम्बः + -करि <i>a.</i> forming sheaves or clusters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरिः|स्तम्बकरि|स्तंबकरि
स्तम्बः + -करि + .({@-रिः@}) corn, rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकरिता|स्तंबकरिता
स्तम्बः + -करिता forming sheaves or clusters, abundant or luxuriant growth;<BR> न शालेः स्तम्बकरिता वप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बगहन
स्तम्बः + -गहन <i>a.</i> overgrown with thickets; Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघनः|स्तम्बघन|स्तंबघन
स्तम्बः + -घनः<BR>—1 a small hoe for weeding clumps of grass.<BR>—2 a sickle for cutting corn.<BR>—3 a basket for holding the heads of wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघ्नः|स्तम्बघ्न|स्तंबघ्न
स्तम्बः + -घ्नः, -घातः, -हन्, -हननम्, -हननी a sickle for cutting corn, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बघातः|स्तम्बघात
स्तम्बः + -घ्नः, -घातः, -हन्, -हननम्, -हननी a sickle for cutting corn, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बहन्
स्तम्बः + -घ्नः, -घातः, -हन्, -हननम्, -हननी a sickle for cutting corn, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बहननम्
स्तम्बः + -घ्नः, -घातः, -हन्, -हननम्, -हननी a sickle for cutting corn, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बहननी
स्तम्बः + -घ्नः, -घातः, -हन्, -हननम्, -हननी a sickle for cutting corn, a hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बपुरम्
स्तम्बः + -पुरम् N. of a city (ताम्रलिप्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बकः|स्तम्बक
स्तम्बकः A clump, bunch, tuft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्बेरमः|स्तम्बेरम|स्तंबेरम|स्तंबेरमः
स्तम्बेरमः An elephant; स्तम्बेरमा मुखरशृङ्खलकर्षिणस्ते R. 5. 72;<BR> Śi. 5. 34; Māl. 9. 33; स्तम्बेरमास्तमारुह्य पर्वतं पर्वता<BR> इव Śiva B. 20. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भ्|स्तंभ्
स्तम्भ् €1 Ā.; €5. €9 P. (स्तम्भते, स्तभ्नोति, स्तभ्नाति, स्तम्भित<BR> or स्तब्ध; the स् of the root being changed to ष् after prepositions<BR> ending in इ or उ and also after अब)<BR>—1 To stop, hinder, arrest, suppress; कण्ठः स्ताम्भितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषः Ś. 4. 5.<BR>—2 To make firm or stiff, to make immoveable.<BR>—3 To stupefy, paralyze, benumb; प्राणा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">Page1714-2</a>]<BR> दध्वंसिरे गात्रं तस्तम्भे च प्रिये हते Bk. 14. 55.<BR>—4 To prop, support, uphold, sustain.<BR>—5 To become stiff, rigid or immoveable.<BR>—6 To be proud or elated, be stiff-necked.<BR>—7 To occupy, spread; ततः पुण्याहघोषोऽभूद्दिवं स्तब्ध्वेव भारत<BR> Mb. 12. 38. 19. (The following verse illustrates the root in its different<BR> conjugations:− स्तम्भते पुरुषः प्रायो यौवनेन धनेन च । न स्तभ्नाति<BR> क्षितीशोऽपि न स्तभ्नोति युवाप्यसौ ॥). ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्तम्भयति-ते)<BR>—1 To stop, arrest.<BR>—2 To make firm or rigid.<BR>—3 To paralyze.<BR>—4 To prop, support. —5 To suppress, check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भः|स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तंभः
स्तम्भः [स्तम्भ्-अच्]<BR>—1 Fixedness, stiffness, rigidity, motionlessness; रम्भा स्तम्भं भजति<BR> Vikr. 18. 29; Ki. 12. 28; गात्रस्तम्भः स्तनमुकुलयोरुत्प्रबन्धः प्रकम्पः<BR> Māl. 2. 5; तत्संकल्पोपहितजडिम स्तम्भमभ्येति गात्रम् 1. 35, 4. 2.<BR>—2 Insensibility, stupefaction, stupor, numbness, paralysis.<BR>—3 Stoppage, obstruction, hindrance; सोऽपश्यत् प्रणिधानेन संततेः<BR> स्तम्भकारणम् R. 1. 74; वाक्स्तम्भं नाटयति Māl. 8.<BR>—4 Restraint, curbing, suppressing; कृतश्चित्तस्तम्भः प्रतिहतधियामञ्जलिरपि Bh. 3. 6.<BR>—5 Prop, support, fulcrum; नासिराबन्धनार्थाय न शराः स्तम्भहेतवः<BR> Rām. 2. 23. 30.<BR>—6 A pillar, column, post.<BR>—7 A stem, trunk (of a tree).<BR>—8 Stupidity.<BR>—9 Absence of feeling or excitability.<BR>—10 The suppression of any force or feeling by supernatural or magical means.<BR>—11 Stiff-neckedness; जन्मकर्मवयोरूपविद्यैश्वर्यधनादिभिः । यद्यस्य<BR> न भवेत् स्तम्भस्तत्रायं मदनुग्रहः Bhāg. 8. 22. 26.<BR>—12 Filling up, stuffing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तम्भोत्कीर्ण, स्तम्भकर, स्तम्भकारणम्, स्तम्भपूजा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भोत्कीर्ण|स्तंभोत्कीर्ण
स्तम्भः + -उत्कीर्ण <i>a.</i> carved out of a post of wood (as a statue).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकर|स्तंभकर|स्तम्भकरः
स्तम्भः + -कर <i>a.</i><BR>—1 paralysing, benumbing.<BR>—2 obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकरः|स्तम्भकर|स्तंभकर
स्तम्भः + -कर + .({@-रः@}) a fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकारणम्
स्तम्भः + -कारणम् cause of obstruction or impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भपूजा|स्तंभपूजा
स्तम्भः + -पूजा worship of the posts of temporary pavilions erected for<BR> marriages or other occasions of solemnity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भक
स्तम्भक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Stopping, arresting.<BR>—2 Styptic, astringent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भकिन्|स्तंभकिन्
स्तम्भकिन् <i>m.</i> A kind of musical instrument covered with leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भनम्
स्तम्भनम् [स्तम्भयति स्तम्भ्-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Stopping, obstructing, hindering, arresting, suppressing, restraining;<BR> लोलोल्लोलक्षुभितकरणोज्जृम्भणस्तम्भनार्थम् U. 3. 36.<BR>—2 Paralysing, benumbing, stupefying.<BR>—3 Quieting, composure; पराङ्मुखेऽपि दैवेऽत्र कृत्यं कार्यं विपश्चिता ।<BR> आत्मदोषविनाशाय खचित्तस्तम्भनाय च ॥ Pt. 1. 360.<BR>—4 Making firm or stiff, fixing firmly.<BR>—5 Propping, supporting.<BR>—6 Stopping the flow of blood.<BR>—7 Anything employed as an astringent.<BR>—8 A particular magical art or faculty; see स्तम्भ (10).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भनः|स्तम्भन|स्तंभन|स्तंभनं|स्तम्भनं
स्तम्भनम् + .{@-नः@} N. of one of the five arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भिः|स्तम्भि
स्तम्भिः The sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भिका
स्तम्भिका The leg of a chair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भित|स्तंभित|स्तम्भितः
स्तम्भित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Stopped, hindered.<BR>—2 Benumbed, paralyzed; द्वेधास्तम्भितपत्तिपङ्क्तिविकटः पन्थाः पुरस्तादभूत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">Page1715-1</a>]<BR> Māl. 8. 9.<BR>—3 Composed, collected; see स्तम्भ्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तम्भितबाष्पवृत्ति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1714-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भितबाष्पवृत्ति
स्तम्भित + -बाष्पवृत्ति <i>a.</i> suppressing the flow of tears; यास्यत्यद्य<BR> शकुन्तलेति हृदयं संस्पृष्टमुत्कण्ठया, कण्ठस्तम्भितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषम् Ś. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भिन्|स्तंभिन्
स्तम्भिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Supporting, stopping &c.<BR>—2 Provided with pillars.<BR>—3 Puffed up, arrogant. ━<i>m.</i> the sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्भिनी
स्तम्भिनी The earth (one of the five elements).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर <i>a.</i> [स्तृ-स्तॄ-घञ्] Spreading, extending, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरः|स्तर
स्तर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Anything spread, a layer, stratum.<BR>—2 A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरणम्
स्तरणम् [स्तृ-स्तॄ-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of spreading, strewing, scattering &c.<BR>—2 Plastering (of a wall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरिमन्
स्तरि(री)मन् <i>m.</i> A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरीमन्
स्तरि(री)मन् <i>m.</i> A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरी
स्तरी [स्तॄ कर्मणि ई]<BR>—1 Smoke, vapour.<BR>—2 A heifer.<BR>—3 A barren cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरीकृ
स्तरीकृ Den. (स्तरीकरोति) To render fruitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवः|स्तव
स्तवः [स्तु-अप्]<BR>—1 Praising, celebrating, eulogizing.<BR>—2 Praise, eulogium, panegyric; ततो गिरः पुरुषवरस्तवान्विता Mb. 12. 47. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवक|स्तवकः
स्तवक <i>a.</i> (-विका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्तु-वुन्] Praising, eulogizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकः|स्तवक
स्तवक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A panegyrist, praiser.<BR>—2 Praise, eulogium.<BR>—3 A cluster of blossoms.<BR>—4 Bunch of flowers, nosegay, tuft, bouquet.<BR>—5 A chapter or section of a book.<BR>—6 A multitude; cf. स्तबक also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकित
स्तवकित <i>a.</i> Full of blossoms or bunches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवनम्
स्तवनम् [स्तु-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Praising, praise.<BR>—2 A hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तविः|स्तवि
स्तविः A chanter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावः|स्ताव
स्तावः Praise, eulogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताव्य
स्ताव्य <i>a.</i> To be praised; P. III. 1. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावकः|स्तावक
स्तावकः A praiser, panegyrist, flatterer; स्तावकांस्तानभिप्रेत्य<BR> पुथुर्वैन्यः प्रतापवान् Bhāg. 4. 15. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

