स्तवेय्यः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवरकः|स्तवरक
स्तवरकः A fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताघ
स्ताघ <i>a.</i> Shallow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ताम्बेरम
स्ताम्बेरम <i>a.</i> Belonging to an elephant; रदं स्ताम्बेरमं तथा<BR> Śiva B. 30. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिघ्
स्तिघ् €5 Ā. (स्तिध्नुते)<BR>—1 To ascend.<BR>—2 To assail, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिप्
स्तिप् €1 Ā. (स्तेपते) To ooze, drop, drip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिभिः|स्तिभि
स्तिभिः<BR>—1 An obstacle, obstruction.<BR>—2 The ocean.<BR>—3 A cluster, bunch, clump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिभिनी
स्तिभिनी A clump, tuft &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्
स्तिम्, स्तीम् €4 P. (स्तिम्यति, स्तीम्यति)<BR>—1 To become wet or moist.<BR>—2 To become fixed or immoveable, be rigid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीम्
स्तिम्, स्तीम् €4 P. (स्तिम्यति, स्तीम्यति)<BR>—1 To become wet or moist.<BR>—2 To become fixed or immoveable, be rigid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमित|स्तिमितः
स्तिमित <i>a.</i> [स्तिम्-कर्तरि क्तः]<BR>—1 Wet, moist; स्तिमितोन्नतसंचारा जनसंतापहारिणः । जायन्ते विरला<BR> लोके जलदा इव सज्जनाः ॥ Pt. 1. 29 (here स्तिमित has two senses:−<BR> steady and moist).<BR>—2<BR>——(<i>a</i>) Still, unruffled, calm; क्षुभितमुत्कलिकातरलं मनः पयइव<BR> स्तिमितस्य महोदधेः Māl. 3. 10.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Fixed, rigid, unmoved, motionless, steady; वाचस्पतिः सन्नपि<BR> सोऽष्टमूर्तौ त्वाशास्यचिन्तास्तिमितो बभूव Ku. 7. 87, 2. 59; स्तिमितविकसितानाम्<BR> Māl. 1. 27; R. 2. 22, 3. 17, 13. 48, 79; U. 6. 25.<BR>—3 Closed, shut; इति विज्ञापितो राज्ञा ध्यानस्तिमितलोचनः R. 1. 73.<BR>—4 Benumbed, paralysed.<BR>—5 Soft, tender.<BR>—6 Gratified, satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितम्
स्तिमित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Moisture.<BR>—2 Fixity, steadiness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तिमितनयन, स्तिमितप्रवाह, स्तिमितवायुः, स्तिमितसमाधिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितनयन
स्तिमित + -नयन <i>a.</i> having the eyes intently fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितप्रवाह
स्तिमित + -प्रवाह <i>a.</i> flowing gently along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितवायुः|स्तिमितवायु
स्तिमित + -वायुः still air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितसमाधिः
स्तिमित + -समाधिः steady contemplation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितत्वम्
स्तिमितत्वम् Steadiness, stillness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्विः|स्तीर्वि|स्तीर्व्वि|स्तीर्व्विः
स्तीर्विः [स्तॄ क्विन्]<BR>—1 An officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR>—2 Grass.<BR>—3 Sky, atmosphere.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 Blood.<BR>—6 An epithet of Indra.<BR>—7 The body.<BR>—8 Fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तु
स्तु €2 U. (स्तौति-स्तवीति, स्तुते-स्तुवीते; तुष्टाव-तुष्टुवे, अस्तावीतस्तोष्ट,<BR> स्तोष्यति-ते, स्तोतुम्, स्तुत; <i>desid.</i> तुष्टूषति-ते; the स्<BR> of स्तु is changed to ष् after a preposition ending in इ or उ)<BR>—1 To praise, laud, eulogize, extol, glorify, celebrate; किं निन्दाम्यथवा<BR> स्तवामि कथय क्षीरार्णव त्वामहम् Bv. 1. 41; Mu. 3. 16; Bk. 8. 92, 15. 70.<BR>—2 To celebrate or praise in song, to hymn, worship by hymns.<BR>—3 To praise in ऋक् verses set to music; इह एतौ स्तौतिशंसतिशब्दौ<BR> समानेऽपि स्तुत्यर्थत्वे व्यवस्थितविषयौ । प्रगीतेषु मन्त्रवाक्येषु स्तौतिशब्दः<BR> अप्रगीतेषु शंसतिशब्दः ŚB. on MS. 7. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत|स्तुतः
स्तुत <i>p. p.</i> [स्तु-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Praised, lauded, eulogized.<BR>—2 Flattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतः|स्तुत
स्तुत + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 Praising.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिः|स्तुति
स्तुतिः <i>f.</i> [स्तु-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Praise, eulogy, commendation, laudation; स्तुतिभ्यो व्यतिरिच्यन्ते दूराणि<BR> चरितानि ते R. 10. 30.<BR>—2 A hymn of praise, panegyric; स्तुत्यं स्तुतिभिरर्थ्याभिरुपतस्थे सरस्वती R. 4. 6.<BR>—3 Adulation; flattery, empty or false praise; भूतार्थव्याहृतिः सा हि<BR> न स्तुतिः परमेष्ठिनः R. 10. 33.<BR>—4 N. of Durgā.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तुतिगीतम्, स्तुतिपदम्, स्तुतिपाठकः, स्तुतिवादः, स्तुतिव्रतः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिगीतम्
स्तुतिः + -गीतम् a panegyric, hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिपदम्
स्तुतिः + -पदम् an object of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिपाठकः|स्तुतिपाठक
स्तुतिः + -पाठकः a panegyrist, an encomiast, a minstrel, bard, herald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिवादः|स्तुतिवाद
स्तुतिः + -वादः a laudatory speech, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुतिव्रतः|स्तुतिव्रत
स्तुतिः + -व्रतः a bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्य|स्तुत्यः
स्तुत्य <i>a.</i> Laudable, commendable, praiseworthy; R. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्या
स्तुत्या<BR>—1 A particular fragrant bark.<BR>—2 Alumslate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुकः|स्तुक
स्तुकः A collection of hair, a knot or braid of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुका
स्तुका<BR>—1 A knot or braid of hair.<BR>—2 A bunch of curly hair between the horns of a bull.<BR>—3 Hip; thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुच्
स्तुच् €1 Ā. (स्तोचते)<BR>—1 To be bright, to shine, be pellucid.<BR>—2 To be propitious or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1715-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुनकः|स्तुनक
स्तुनकः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ्
स्तुभ् I. €1 P. (स्तोभति)<BR>—1 To praise.<BR>—2 To celebrate, extol, worship. ━II. €1 Ā. (स्तोभते)<BR>—1 To stop, suppress.<BR>—2 To paralyse, benumb, stupefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभः|स्तुभ
स्तुभः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुम्भ्|स्तुंभ्
स्तुम्भ् €5. €9 P. (स्तुभ्नोति; स्तुभ्नाति)<BR>—1 To stop.<BR>—2 To benumb, stupefy.<BR>—3 To expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुविः|स्तुवि
स्तुविः<BR>—1 A worshipper.<BR>—2 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुषेण्य
स्तुषेण्य, -स्तुषेय्य (Ved.)<BR> Best, excellent, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुषेय्य
स्तुषेण्य, -स्तुषेय्य (Ved.)<BR> Best, excellent, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप्
स्तूप् €4 P., €10 U. (स्तूप्यति, स्तूपयति-ते)<BR>—1 To heap up, accumulate, pile, collect.<BR>—2 To erect, raise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूपः|स्तूप
स्तूपः<BR>—1 A heap, pile, mound (of earth &c.); वटुभिरुपहृतानां बर्हिषां स्तूपमेतत् Mu. 3. 15.<BR>—2 A Buddhistic monument, or kind of Tope erected for keeping sacred relics,<BR> as those of Buddha.<BR>—3 A funeral pile.<BR>—4 Strength, power.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तूपपृष्ठः, स्तूपमण्डलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूपपृष्ठः|स्तूपपृष्ठ
स्तूपः + -पृष्ठः a turtle, tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूपमण्डलम्
स्तूपः + -मण्डलम् circumference of a tope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ I. €5 U. (स्तृणोति, स्तृणुते, स्तृत; <i>pass.</i> स्तर्यते)<BR>—1 To spread, strew, cover, spread on or over; (महीं) तस्तार सरघाव्याप्तैः<BR> स क्षौद्रपटलैरिव R. 4. 63, 7. 58.<BR>—2 To spread, expand, diffuse.<BR>—3 To scatter, spread about.<BR>—4 To clothe, cover, overspread, envelop.<BR>—5 To kill. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्तारयति-ते) To overspread, cover, strew;<BR> रक्तेनाचिक्लिदद्भूमिं सैन्यैश्चातस्तरद्धतैः Bk. 15. 48. ━<i>Desid.</i><BR> (तिस्तीर्षति-ते). ━II. €5 P. (स्तृणोति) To please, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ <i>m.</i> A star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृतिः|स्तृति
स्तृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Spreading, stretching, expansion.<BR>—2 Covering, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृक्ष्
स्तृक्ष् €1 P. (स्तृक्षति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृह्
स्तृह्, स्तॄह् €6 P. (स्तृहति, स्तॄहति) To strike, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄह्
स्तृह्, स्तॄह् €6 P. (स्तृहति, स्तॄहति) To strike, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄ
स्तॄ €9 U. (स्तृणाति, स्तृणीते, स्तीर्ण; <i>desid.</i> तिस्तरि(री)षति-ते,<BR> तिस्तीर्षति-ते) To cover, strew &c.; see स्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन्
स्तेन् €10 U. (Strictly a denom. from स्तेन; स्तेनयति-ते)<BR>—1 To steal, rob; यस्त्वेतान्युपकॢप्तानि द्रव्याणि स्तेनयेन्नरः Ms. 8. 333.<BR>—2 To be dishonest in speech; वाच्यर्था नियताः सर्वे Vआङ्मूला वाग्विनिःसृताः ।<BR> तां तु यः स्तेनयेद्वाचं स सर्वस्तेनकृन्नरः ॥ Ms. 4. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेनः|स्तेन|स्तेनं
स्तेनः [स्तेन्-कर्तरि अच्]<BR>—1 A thief, robber; न तं स्तेना न चामित्रा हरन्ति न च नश्यति<BR> Ms. 7. 83; यो भुङ्क्ते स्तेन एव सः Bg. 3. 12.<BR>—2 A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेनम्
स्तेनः + .{@-नम्@} Thieving, stealing.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तेननिग्रहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेननिग्रहः|स्तेननिग्रह
स्तेनः + -निग्रहः<BR>—1 the punishment of thieves.<BR>—2 suppression of theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयम्
स्तेयम् [स्तेनस्य भावः यत् नलोपः]<BR>—1 Theft, robbery; व्यावृत्तगतिरुद्याने कुसुमस्तेयसाध्वसात् Ku. 2. 35.<BR>—2 Anything stolen or liable to be stolen.<BR>—3 Anything private or secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयिन्
स्तेयिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A thief, robber.<BR>—2 A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैनम्
स्तैनम् Theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन्यम्
स्तैन्यम् [स्तेनस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन्यः|स्तैन्य|स्तैन्यं
स्तैन्यम् + .{@-न्यः@} A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेप्
स्तेप् I. €1 Ā. (स्तेपते) To ooze. ━II. €10 U. (स्येपयति-ते)<BR> To send, throw, cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेमः|स्तेम
स्तेमः Moisture, wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तै
स्तै €1 P. (स्तायति) To put on, adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैमित्यम्
स्तैमित्यम्<BR>—1 Fixedness, rigidity, immobility.<BR>—2 Numbness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोक|स्तोकः
स्तोक <i>a.</i> [स्तुच्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Little, small; स्तोकेनोन्नतिमायाति स्तोकेनायात्यधोगतिम् Pt. 1. 150;<BR> स्तोकं महद्वा धनम् Bh. 2. 49.<BR>—2 Short.<BR>—3 Few.<BR>—4 Low, abject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकः|स्तोक
स्तोक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A small quantity, drop; घृतवन्तः पावक ते स्तोकाश्चोतन्ति Ait. Br. 2. 12;<BR> अद्भ्यः स्तोका यान्ति यथा पृथक्त्वम् Mb. 7. 201. 75.<BR>—2 The Chātaka bird.<BR>—3 A spark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकम्
स्तोक + .{@-कम्@} <i>ind.</i> A little, less; पश्योदग्रप्लुतत्वाद्वियति बहुतरं<BR> स्तोकमुर्व्यां प्रयाति Ś. 1. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तोकायुस्, स्तोककाय, स्तोकतमस्, स्तोकनम्र, स्तोकपाण्डुर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकायुस्
स्तोक + -आयुस् <i>a.</i> short-lived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोककाय
स्तोक + -काय <i>a.</i> little-bodied, small, dwarfish, diminutive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकतमस्
स्तोक + -तमस् <i>a.</i> a little dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकनम्र
स्तोक + -नम्र <i>a.</i> a little bent down, slightly stooping or depressed;<BR> श्रोणीभारादलसगमना स्तोकनम्रा स्तनाभ्याम् Me. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकपाण्डुर
स्तोक + -पाण्डुर <i>a.</i> a little pale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोककः|स्तोकक
स्तोककः<BR>—1 The Chātaka bird; स्तोकको वारि (हृत्वा) Ms. 12. 67; स्तोककस्य<BR> खलु चञ्चुपुटेन म्लानिरुल्लसति तद्धनसड्घे N. 5. 127.<BR>—2 A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकशस्
स्तोकशस् <i>ind.</i> By little, sparingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतव्य
स्तोतव्य <i>a.</i> Fit to be praised, laudable, praiseworthy; स कस्य<BR> स्तोतव्यः कतिविधगुणः कस्य विषयः Śivamahimna 2; स्तोतव्यगुणसंपन्नः<BR> केषां न स्यात् प्रियो जनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतृ
स्तोतृ <i>m.</i> A praiser, panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रम्
स्तोत्रम् [स्तु-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>—1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>—2 A hymn of praise, panegyric; सकलगणवरिष्ठः पुष्पदन्ताभिधानो<BR> रुचिरमलघुवृत्तैः स्तोत्रमेतच्चकार Śivamahimna 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रियः|स्तोत्रिय
स्तोत्रियः, -या<BR> A particular kind of verse; कत्ययमद्योद्गाताऽस्मिन् यज्ञे<BR> स्तोत्रियाः स्तोष्यति Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रिया
स्तोत्रियः, -या<BR> A particular kind of verse; कत्ययमद्योद्गाताऽस्मिन् यज्ञे<BR> स्तोत्रियाः स्तोष्यति Bṛ. Up. 3. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभः|स्तोभ|स्तोभं
स्तोभः [स्तुभ्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Stopping, obstructing.<BR>—2 A stop, pause.<BR>—3 Disrespect, contumely.<BR>—4 A hymn, praise; साङ्केत्यं पारिहास्यं वा स्तोभं हेलनमेव वा । वैकुण्ठनामग्रहणमशेषाघहरं<BR> विदुः ॥ Bhāg. 6. 2. 14.<BR>—5 A division of the Sāmaveda.<BR>—6 Anything inserted; अस्तोभमनवद्यं च सूत्रं सूत्रविदो विदुः.<BR>—7 The sound or sounds dissimilar to and in excess of the letters of the<BR> Ṛk which is set to music; य ऋगक्षरेभ्योऽधिको न च तैः सवर्णः स<BR> स्तोभो नाम ŚB. on MS. 9. 2. 39.<BR>—8 A chanted interjection in a Sāman; सत्यं यज्ञस्तपो वेदाः स्तोभा<BR> मन्त्राः सरस्वती Mb. 12. 199. 68.<BR>—9 Torpor, paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्
स्तोम् €10 P. To praise; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1716-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमः|स्तोम
स्तोमः [स्तु-मन् Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>—1 Praise, eulogium, hymn.<BR>—2 A sacrifice, oblation; as in ज्योतिष्टोम, अग्निष्टोम.<BR>—3 A <i>Soma</i> libation.<BR>—4 A collection, multitude, number, group, assemblage; शस्त्रमिज्यां<BR> स्तुतिस्तोमं प्रायश्चित्तं व्यधात् क्रमात् Bhāg. 3. 12. 37; लवणत्रासितः<BR> स्तोमः शरण्यं त्वामुपस्थितः U. 1. 50.<BR>—5 A large quantity, mass; भस्मस्तोमपवित्रलाञ्छनमुरो धत्ते त्वचं<BR> रौरवीम् U. 4. 20; Mv. 1. 18.<BR>—6 A measure of 10 धन्वन्तरs or of 96 inches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमम्
स्तोमः + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 The head.<BR>—2 Riches, wealth.<BR>—3 Grain, corn.<BR>—4 An iron-pointed stick or shaft.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्तोमक्षारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमक्षारः|स्तोमक्षार
स्तोमः + -क्षारः soap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमयति
स्तोमयति Den. P. To praise, laud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्य
स्तोम्य <i>a.</i> Laudable, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौपिकम्
स्तौपिकम् A kind of Buddhist relic; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौभिकम्
स्तौभिकम् N. of the second portion of the Saṃhitā of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्येनः|स्त्येन
स्त्येनः [स्त्यै-इनच्]<BR>—1 Nectar.<BR>—2 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यै
स्त्यै €1 U. (स्त्यायति-ते)<BR>—1 To be collected into a heap or mass.<BR>—2 To spread about, be diffused; शिशिरकटुकषायः स्त्यायते सल्लकीनाम्<BR> Māl. 9. 6; U. 2. 21; Mv. 5. 41.<BR>—3 Sound, echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यान|स्त्यानं|स्त्यानः
स्त्यान <i>a.</i> [स्त्यै-क्त]<BR>—1 Collected into a mass; पर्यन्तप्रतिरोधिमेदुरचयस्त्यानं चिताज्योतिषाम्<BR> Māl. 5. 11; घनतरुशिखरे स्त्याननीलस्वरूपाम् (रक्तधाराम्) Nāg. 5. 8.<BR>—2 Thick, bulky, gross; स्त्यानेनार्द्रेण चाक्तः स्वयमनुभविता भूषणं<BR> भीममस्मि Ve. 5. 35.<BR>—3 Soft, bland, smooth, unctuous; स्त्यानावनद्धघनशोणितशोणपाणिः Ve. 1. 21.<BR>—4 Sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यानम्
स्त्यान + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Thickness, grossness, increase in magnitude or bulk; दधति कुहरभाजामत्र<BR> भल्लूकयूनामनुरसितगुरूणि स्त्यानमम्बूकृतानि Māl. 9. 6; U. 2. 21; Mv. 5. 41.<BR>—2 Unctuousness.<BR>—3 Nectar.<BR>—4 Sloth, idleness.<BR>—5 Echo, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यायनम्
स्त्यायनम् Collecting into a mass, crowding together, aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्री
स्त्री [स्त्यायेते शुक्रशोणिते यस्याम्]<BR>—1 A woman; श्रुतं दृष्टं स्पृष्टं स्मृतमपि नृणां ह्लादजननं न रत्नं<BR> स्त्रीभ्योऽन्यत् क्वचिदपि कृतं लोकपतिना । तदर्थं धर्मार्थौ विभववरसौख्यानि<BR> च ततो गृहे लक्ष्म्यो मान्याः सततमबला मानविभवैः ॥ Subh. Ratn.<BR>—2 A female of any animal; गजस्त्री, हरिणस्त्री &c.; स्त्रीणामशिक्षितपटुत्वममानुषीषु Ś. 5. 22.<BR>—3 A wife; स्त्रीणां भर्ता धर्मदाराश्च पुंसाम् Māl. 6. 18; Me. 28.<BR>—4 A white ant.<BR>—5 The Priyaṅgu plant.<BR>—6 The feminine gender, or a word used in that gender; आपः स्त्रीभूम्नि Ak.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्त्र्यगारः, स्त्र्यगारम्, स्त्र्यध्यक्षः, स्त्र्यभिगमनम्, स्त्र्याजीवः, स्त्रीकरणम्, स्त्रीकामः, स्त्रीकार्यम्, स्त्रीकितवः, स्त्रीकुमारम्, स्त्रीकुसुमम्, स्त्रीकृतम्, स्त्रीकोशः, स्त्रीक्षीरम्, स्त्रीग, स्त्रीगवी, स्त्रीगुरुः, स्त्रीगृहम्, स्त्रीग्राहिन्, स्त्रीघोषः, स्त्रीघ्नः, स्त्रीचरितम्, स्त्रीचरित्रम्, स्त्रीचिह्नम्, स्त्रीचौरः, स्त्रीजननी, स्त्रीजातिः, स्त्रीजितः, स्त्रीदेहार्धः, स्त्रीधनम्, स्त्रीधर्मः, स्त्रीधर्मिणी, स्त्रीधवः, स्त्रीध्वजः, स्त्रीनाथ, स्त्रीनिबन्धनम्, स्त्रीपण्योपजीविन्, स्त्रीपरः, स्त्रीपिशाची, स्त्रीपुंस्, स्त्रीपुंसौ, स्त्रीपुंसलक्षणा, स्त्रीपुंधर्मः, स्त्रीपुरम्, स्त्रीपुष्पम्, स्त्रीपूर्वः, स्त्रीप्रत्ययः, स्त्रीप्रसंगः, स्त्रीप्रसूः, स्त्रीप्रिय, स्त्रीबन्धः, स्त्रीबाध्यः, स्त्रीबुद्धिः, स्त्रीभोगः, स्त्रीमन्त्रः, स्त्रीमाया, स्त्रीमुखपः, स्त्रीयन्त्रम्, स्त्रीरजस्, स्त्रीरञ्जनम्, स्त्रीरत्नम्, स्त्रीराज्यम्, स्त्रीलम्पट, स्त्रीलिङ्गम्, स्त्रीलौल्यम्, स्त्रीवशः, स्त्रीवासः, स्त्रीविधेय, स्त्रीविवाहः, स्त्रीविषयः, स्त्रीव्रणः, स्त्रीशौण्ड, स्त्रीसंसर्गः, स्त्रीसंस्थान, स्त्रीसंगः, स्त्रीसंग्रहणम्, स्त्रीसभम्, स्त्रीसंबन्धः, स्त्रीसेवा, स्त्रीस्वभावः, स्त्रीहत्या, स्त्रीहन्तृ, स्त्रीहरणम्, स्त्रीहारिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्यगारः|स्त्र्यगार
स्त्री + -अगारः, -अगारम् a harem, the womenʼs apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्यगारम्
स्त्री + -अगारः, -अगारम् a harem, the womenʼs apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्यध्यक्षः|स्त्र्यध्यक्ष
स्त्री + -अध्यक्षः a chamberlain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्यभिगमनम्
स्त्री + -अभिगमनम् sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्र्याजीवः|स्त्र्याजीव
स्त्री + -आजीवः<BR>—1 one who lives by his wife.<BR>—2 one who lives by keeping women for prostitution; Ms. 11. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकरणम्
स्त्री + -करणम् sexual connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकामः|स्त्रीकाम
स्त्री + -कामः<BR>—1 desire of intercourse with women, fondness for women.<BR>—2 desire of a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकार्यम्
स्त्री + -कार्यम्<BR>—1 the business of women.<BR>—2 attendance on women or womenʼs apartments; वैदेहकानां स्त्रीकार्यं<BR> मागधानां वणिक्पथः Ms. 10. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकितवः|स्त्रीकितव
स्त्री + -कितवः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">Page1717-2</a>]<BR> deceiver or seducer of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकुमारम्
स्त्री + -कुमारम् a woman and child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकुसुमम्
स्त्री + -कुसुमम् menses, the menstrual excretion in women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकृतम्
स्त्री + -कृतम् sexual connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीकोशः|स्त्रीकोश
स्त्री + -कोशः a dagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीक्षीरम्
स्त्री + -क्षीरम् motherʼs milk; आरण्यानां च सर्वेषां मृगाणां माहिषं<BR> विना । स्त्रीक्षीरं चैव वर्ज्यानि … Ms. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीग
स्त्री + -ग <i>a.</i> cohabiting with women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीगवी
स्त्री + -गवी a milch-cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीगुरुः|स्त्रीगुरु
स्त्री + -गुरुः a female <i>Guru</i> or priestess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीगृहम्
स्त्री + -गृहम् = स्त्र्यगार q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीग्राहिन्
स्त्री + -ग्राहिन् (in law) accepting the guardianship over a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीघोषः|स्त्रीघोष
स्त्री + -घोषः dawn, day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीघ्नः|स्त्रीघ्न
स्त्री + -घ्नः the murderer of a woman; Ms. 9. 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचरितम्
स्त्री + -चरितम्, -चरित्रम् the doings of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचरित्रम्
स्त्री + -चरितम्, -चरित्रम् the doings of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचिह्नम्
स्त्री + -चिह्नम्<BR>—1 any mark or characteristic of the female sex.<BR>—2 the female organ, vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीचौरः|स्त्रीचौर
स्त्री + -चौरः a seducer of women, libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजननी
स्त्री + -जननी a woman who brings forth only daughters; Ms. 9. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजातिः|स्त्रीजाति
स्त्री + -जातिः <i>f.</i> woman-kind, female sex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीजितः|स्त्रीजित
स्त्री + -जितः a hen-pecked husband; स्त्रीजितस्पर्शमात्रेण सर्वं पुण्यं<BR> विनश्यति Śabdak.; मृष्यन्ति ये चोपपतिं स्त्रीजितानां च सर्वशः<BR> (तेषामन्नं न भुञ्जीत) Ms. 4. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीदेहार्धः|स्त्रीदेहार्ध
स्त्री + -देहार्धः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधनम्
स्त्री + -धनम् a womanʼs private property over which she exercises independent<BR> control; it is of six kinds:− अध्यग्न्यध्यावहनिकं दत्तं च प्रीतिकर्मणि ।<BR> भ्रातृमातृपितृप्राप्तं षड्विधं स्त्रीधनं स्मृतम् ॥ or according to<BR> others:− पितृमातृपतिभ्रातृदत्तमध्यग्न्युपायनम् । आधिवेदनिकाद्यं च<BR> स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम्; see also अन्वाधेयम्, बन्धुदत्तम्, यौतकम्, सौदायिकम्,<BR> शुल्कम्, पारिणाय्यम्, लावण्यार्जितम् and पादवन्दनिकम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्मः|स्त्रीधर्म|स्त्रीधर्म्म|स्त्रीधर्म्मः
स्त्री + -धर्मः<BR>—1 the duty of a woman or wife.<BR>—2 the laws concerning women; Ms. 1. 114.<BR>—3 menstruation.<BR>—4 copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधर्मिणी|स्त्रीधर्म्मिणी
स्त्री + -धर्मिणी a woman in her courses; स्त्रीधर्मिणी वेपमाना शोणितेन<BR> समुक्षिता । एकवस्त्रा विकृष्टास्मि दुःखिता कुरुसंसदि ॥ Mb. 3. 12. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीधवः|स्त्रीधव
स्त्री + -धवः a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीध्वजः|स्त्रीध्वज
स्त्री + -ध्वजः<BR>—1 the female of any animal.<BR>—2 an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीनाथ
स्त्री + -नाथ <i>a.</i> one protected by a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीनिबन्धनम्
स्त्री + -निबन्धनम् a womanʼs peculiar sphere of action or province; domestic<BR> duty, housewifery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपण्योपजीविन्
स्त्री + -पण्योपजीविन् <i>m.</i> see स्त्र्याजीवः above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपरः|स्त्रीपर
स्त्री + -परः a woman-lover, lecher, libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपिशाची
स्त्री + -पिशाची a fiend-like wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंस्
स्त्री + -पुंस् a woman who has become a man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंसौ
स्त्री + -पुंसौ <i>m.</i> du.<BR>—1 wife and husband.<BR>—2 male and female; स्त्रीपुंसावात्मभागौ ते भिन्नमूर्तेः सिसृक्षया Ku. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंसलक्षणा
स्त्री + -पुंसलक्षणा a hermaphrodite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुंधर्मः|स्त्रीपुन्धर्म|स्त्रीपुंधर्म्म|स्त्रीपुंधर्म्मः
स्त्री + -पुंधर्मः the law regulating the duties of man and wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुरम्
स्त्री + -पुरम् the womenʼs apartment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपुष्पम्
स्त्री + -पुष्पम् the menstrual excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीपूर्वः|स्त्रीपूर्व|स्त्रीपूर्व्वः
स्त्री + -पूर्वः = स्त्रीजितः q. v.; स्रीपूर्वाः काण्डपृष्टाश्च … …<BR> (श्राद्धे नार्हन्ति) Mb. 13. 23. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रत्ययः|स्त्रीप्रत्यय
स्त्री + -प्रत्ययः a feminine affix (in gram.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रसंगः|स्त्रीप्रसङ्ग|स्त्रीप्रसंग
स्त्री + -प्रसंगः (excessive) intercourse with women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रसूः
स्त्री + -प्रसूः <i>f.</i> a woman who brings forth only daughters; Y. 1. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रिय|स्त्रीप्रियः
स्त्री + -प्रिय <i>a.</i> loved by women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीप्रियः|स्त्रीप्रिय
स्त्री + -प्रिय + .({@-यः@}) the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीबन्धः|स्त्रीबन्ध
स्त्री + -बन्धः the sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीबाध्यः|स्त्रीबाध्य
स्त्री + -बाध्यः one who suffers himself to be troubled by a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीबुद्धिः|स्त्रीबुद्धि
स्त्री + -बुद्धिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the female understanding.<BR>—2 the counsel of a woman, female advice; स्त्रीबुद्धिः प्रलयंगता<BR> (प्रलयावहा) Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीभोगः|स्त्रीभोग
स्त्री + -भोगः sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमन्त्रः|स्त्रीमन्त्र|स्त्रीमंत्र
स्त्री + -मन्त्रः a female stratagem, womanʼs counsel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमाया
स्त्री + -माया womenʼs craft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीमुखपः|स्त्रीमुखप
स्त्री + -मुखपः the <i>Aśoka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीयन्त्रम्
स्त्री + -यन्त्रम् a machine-like woman, machine in the form of a woman;<BR> स्त्रीयन्त्रं केन लोके विषममृतमयं धर्मनाशाय सृष्टम् Pt. 1. 191.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरजस्
स्त्री + -रजस् menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरञ्जनम्
स्त्री + -रञ्जनम् betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीरत्नम्
स्त्री + -रत्नम्<BR>—1 an excellent woman; स्त्रीरत्नेषु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">Page1718-1</a>]<BR> ममोर्वशी प्रियतमा यूथे तवेयं वशा V. 4. 25.<BR>—2 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1717-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीराज्यम्
स्त्री + -राज्यम् the kingdom of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीलम्पट
स्त्री + -लम्पट <i>a.</i> desirous of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीलिङ्गम्
स्त्री + -लिङ्गम्<BR>—1 the feminine gender (in gram.)<BR>—2 any mark of the female sex (as breast &c.).<BR>—3 the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीलौल्यम्
स्त्री + -लौल्यम् fondness for women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीवशः|स्त्रीवश
स्त्री + -वशः submissiveness to a wife, subjection to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीवासः|स्त्रीवास
स्त्री + -वासः an ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविधेय
स्त्री + -विधेय <i>a.</i> governed by a wife, uxorious; संनिवेश्य सचिवेष्वतःपरं<BR> स्त्रीविधेयनवयौवनोऽभवत् R. 19. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविवाहः|स्त्रीविवाह
स्त्री + -विवाहः contracting marriage with a woman; अष्टाविमान् समानेन<BR> स्त्रीविवाहान्निबोधत Ms. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीविषयः|स्त्रीविषय
स्त्री + -विषयः sexual connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीव्रणः|स्त्रीव्रण
स्त्री + -व्रणः the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीशौण्ड
स्त्री + -शौण्ड <i>a.</i> fond of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंसर्गः|स्त्रीसंसर्ग
स्त्री + -संसर्गः female company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंस्थान
स्त्री + -संस्थान <i>a.</i> having a female shape; स्त्रीसंस्थानं चाप्यरस्तीर्थमारादुत्क्षिप्यैनां<BR> ज्योतिरेकं तिरोऽभूत् Ś. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंगः|स्त्रीसङ्ग
स्त्री + -संगः attachment to women, or intercourse with women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंग्रहणम्
स्त्री + -संग्रहणम्<BR>—1 the act of embracing a woman (improperly).<BR>—2 adultery, seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसभम्
स्त्री + -सभम् an assembly of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसंबन्धः|स्त्रीसम्बन्ध|स्त्रीसंबन्ध|स्त्रीसंबंध
स्त्री + -संबन्धः<BR>—1 matrimonial alliance with a woman.<BR>—2 connection by marriage.<BR>—3 relation to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीसेवा
स्त्री + -सेवा Devotion or addiction to women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीस्वभावः|स्त्रीस्वभाव
स्त्री + -स्वभावः<BR>—1 the nature of women.<BR>—2 a eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहत्या
स्त्री + -हत्या the murder of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहन्तृ
स्त्री + -हन्तृ the murderer of a woman; स्त्रीहन्तॄंश्च न संवसेत् Ms. 11. 190.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहरणम्
स्त्री + -हरणम्<BR>—1 the forcible abduction of women.<BR>—2 rape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीहारिन्
स्त्री + -हारिन् <i>m.</i> a ravisher or seducer (of women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीतमा
स्त्रीतमा, स्त्रीतरा A thorough woman, more thoroughly a woman; P. VI. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीतरा
स्त्रीतमा, स्त्रीतरा A thorough woman, more thoroughly a woman; P. VI. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीता
स्त्रीता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Womanhood.<BR>—2 Wifehood.<BR>—3 Effeminacy, feminineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीत्वम्
स्त्रीता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Womanhood.<BR>—2 Wifehood.<BR>—3 Effeminacy, feminineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैण|स्त्रैणं|स्त्रैणः
स्त्रैण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्त्रिया इदम् नञ् P. IV. 1. 88]<BR>—1 Female, feminine.<BR>—2 Suited or belonging to women.<BR>—3 Being among women.<BR>—4 Devoted to women; यदि स्त्रैणं देवी यमनिरत देहार्धघटनादवैति<BR> त्वामद्धा बत वरद मुग्धा युवतयः Śivamahimna 23; स इत्थमाचरन्कामान्स्त्रैणोऽपह्नवमात्मनः<BR> Bhāg. 9. 19. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैणम्
स्त्रैण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Womanhood, nature of women, feminineness; शिशुत्वं स्त्रैणं वा भवतु<BR> ननु वन्द्यासि जगतः U. 4. 11.<BR>—2 The female sex, womanhood; तृणे वा स्त्रैणे वा मम समदृशो यान्ति<BR> दिवसाः Bh. 3. 113; इदं तत्प्रत्युत्पन्नमति स्त्रैणमिति यदुच्यते<BR> Ś. 5; तस्य तृणमिव लघुवृत्ति स्त्रैणमाकलयतः K.<BR>—3 A collection of women; भूयिष्ठद्विजबालवृद्धविकलस्त्रैणश्च पौरो<BR> जनः U. 4. 24.<BR>—4 Ved. Sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैणता
स्त्रैणता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Feminineness, effeminacy.<BR>—2 Excessive fondness for women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैणत्वम्
स्त्रैणता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Feminineness, effeminacy.<BR>—2 Excessive fondness for women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थकरम्
स्थक(ग)रम् A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगरम्
स्थक(ग)रम् A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग्
स्थग् €1 P. or <i>Caus.</i> (स्थगति, स्थगयति)<BR>—1 To cover, conceal, hide, veil; पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि स्थगयति Māl. 1. 14.<BR>—2 To cover, pervade, fill; रवः श्रवणभैरवः स्थगितरोदसीकन्दरः K. P. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग <i>a.</i> [स्थग्-अच्]<BR>—1 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>—2 Abandoned, impudent, reckless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगः|स्थग
स्थग + .{@-गः@} A rogue, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगणा
स्थगणा The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगनम्
स्थगनम् Concealment, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगरः|स्थगर|स्थगरं
स्थगरः The plant पुत्रजीवक; Rām. 2. 94. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगिका
स्थगिका<BR>—1 A courtezan.<BR>—2 The office of betel-bearer.<BR>—3 A kind of bandage.<BR>—4 A box (for betel &c.); ततः प्रविशति लेखमलंकरणस्थगिकां मुद्रितां<BR> चादाय सिद्धार्थकः Mu. 5. 0/1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगित|स्थगितं
स्थगित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Covered, hidden, concealed.<BR>—2 Closed, shut.<BR>—3 Stopped, interrupted; विस्मृत्य भोः स्थगितगीरुपलक्ष्यसे नः Bhāg. 10. 90. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगी
स्थगी A betel-box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगु|स्थगुः
स्थगु <i>n.</i> A hump; तदेव स्थगु यद्दीर्घं रथघोणमिवायतम्<BR> Rām. 2. 9. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलम्
स्थण्डिलम् [स्थल्-इलच् नुक् लस्य डः Tv.]<BR>—1 A piece of ground (levelled, squared and prepared for a sacrifice),<BR> an altar; निषेदुषी स्थण्डिल एव केवले Ku. 5. 12; Bhāg. 11. 11. 45.<BR>—2 A barren field.<BR>—3 A heap of clods.<BR>—4 A limit, boundary.<BR>—5 A land-mark.<BR>—6 A place, ground (as before a house); इह तु स्थण्डिले शीघ्रं कुशानास्तर<BR> सारथे Rām. 2. 111. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थण्डिलशायिन्, स्थण्डिलसितकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलशायिन्|स्थंडिलशायिन्
स्थण्डिलम् + -शायिन् <i>m.</i>, also {@स्थण्डिलेशयः@} an ascetic who sleeps<BR> on the bare <i>Sthandila</i> or sacrificial ground; (मुनयः) आकाशनिलयाश्चैव<BR> तथा स्थण्डिलशायिनः Rām. 3. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थण्डिलसितकम्
स्थण्डिलम् + -सितकम् an altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपति|स्थपतिः
स्थपति <i>a.</i> [स्था-क तस्य पतिः] Chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपतिः|स्थपति
स्थपति + .{@-तिः@}<BR>—1 A king, sovereign; ‘स्थपतिरधिपतौ तक्ष्णि बृहस्पतिसचिवयोः’ इति<BR> वैजयन्ती; जगत्त्रयैकस्थपतिस्त्वमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 34.<BR>—2 An architect; स्थपतिर्बुद्धिसंपन्नो वास्तुविद्याविशारदः Mb. 1. 51. 15.<BR>—3 A wheel-wright, master-carpenter.<BR>—4 A charioteer.<BR>—5 One who offers a sacrifice to Bṛhaspati.<BR>—6 An attendant on the womenʼs apartments.<BR>—7 N. of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपत्यः
स्थपत्यः A chamberlain; स्थपत्यशुद्धान्तजनैः परीता Jānakīharaṇa. 7. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुट|स्थपुटः
स्थपुट <i>a.</i> [तिष्ठति स्था क, स्थं पुटं यत्र]<BR>—1 Being in distressed or difficult circumstances.<BR>—2 Unevenly raised, elevated and depressed. ━<i>m.</i> Protuberance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थपुटगत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुटगत
स्थपुट + -गत <i>a.</i> being in contracted or uneven parts, being in difficult<BR> places; अङ्कस्थादस्थिसंस्थं स्थपुटगतमपि क्रव्यमव्यग्रमत्ति Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुटीकृत
स्थपुटीकृत <i>p. p.</i> Made uneven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल्
स्थल् €1 P. (स्थलति) To stand firm, be firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलम्
स्थलम् [स्थल्-अच्]<BR>—1 Firm or dry ground, dry land, <i>terra firma</i> (opp. जल); भो<BR> दुरात्मन् (समुद्र) दीयतां टिद्दिभाण्डानि नो चेत्स्थलतां त्वां नयामि<BR> Pt. 1; प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना R. 4. 60; so स्थलकमलिनी or स्थलवर्त्मन् q. v.<BR>—2 Shore, strand, beach.<BR>—3 Ground, land, soil (in general).<BR>—4 Place, spot; उवाच वाग्मी दशनप्रभाभिः संवर्धितोरःस्थलतारहारः R. 5. 52.<BR>—5 Field, tract, district.<BR>—6 Station.<BR>—7 A piece of raised ground, mound; ततः स्थलमुपारुह्य पर्वतस्याविदूरतः । ख्यातः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">Page1719-1</a>]<BR> पञ्चवटीत्येव नित्यपुष्पितकाननः ॥ Rām. 3. 13. 22.<BR>—8 A topic, case, subject, the point under discussion; विवाद˚, विचार˚ &c.<BR>—9 A part (as of a book). —10 A tent.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थलान्तरम्, स्थलारूढ, स्थलारविन्दम्, स्थलकमलम्, स्थलकमलिनी, स्थलकमलः, स्थलकुमुदः, स्थलचर, स्थलच्युत, स्थलज, स्थलदेवता, स्थलपद्मम्, स्थलपद्मिनी, स्थलमार्गः, स्थलवर्त्मन्, स्थलविग्रहः, स्थलशुद्धिः, स्थलसीमन्, स्थलस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1718-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलान्तरम्
स्थलम् + -अन्तरम् another place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलारूढ
स्थलम् + -आरूढ <i>a.</i> alighted on the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलारविन्दम्
स्थलम् + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -कमलिनी a land-growing lotus; साभ्रेऽह्नीव<BR> स्थलकमलिनीं नप्रबुद्धां नसुप्ताम् Me. 94; Ku. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलकमलम्
स्थलम् + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -कमलिनी a land-growing lotus; साभ्रेऽह्नीव<BR> स्थलकमलिनीं नप्रबुद्धां नसुप्ताम् Me. 94; Ku. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलकमलिनी
स्थलम् + -अरविन्दम्, -कमलम्, -कमलिनी a land-growing lotus; साभ्रेऽह्नीव<BR> स्थलकमलिनीं नप्रबुद्धां नसुप्ताम् Me. 94; Ku. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलकमलः|स्थलकमल|स्थलकमलं
स्थलम् + -कमलः <i>m.</i> is also a plant of the lily-family (Gloriosa<BR> Superba). It is a red-flowered species traditionally called भूकमल.<BR> The plant goes by the name कळलावी in Marathi which seems to have<BR> been derived from Sanskrit स्थलकल्लारी. Kālidāsa pointedly refers<BR> to the peculiarity that it opens only in response to day-light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलकुमुदः|स्थलकुमुद
स्थलम् + -कुमुदः the Karavīra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलचर
स्थलम् + -चर <i>a.</i> land-going, not aquatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलच्युत
स्थलम् + -च्युत <i>a.</i> fallen or removed from a place or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलज
स्थलम् + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Growing or living on dry land; Ms. 1. 44.<BR>—2 accruing from land-transport (taxes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलदेवता
स्थलम् + -देवता a local or rural deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलपद्मम्
स्थलम् + -पद्मम् a land-lotus; सरोजलक्ष्मीं स्थलपद्महासैः Bk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलपद्मिनी
स्थलम् + -पद्मिनी the shrub <i>Hibiscus Mutabilis</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलमार्गः|स्थलमार्ग
स्थलम् + -मार्गः, -वर्त्मन् <i>n.</i> a road by land; स्थलवर्त्मना ‘by land’<BR>; पारसीकांस्ततो जेतुं प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना R. 4. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलवर्त्मन्
स्थलम् + -मार्गः, -वर्त्मन् <i>n.</i> a road by land; स्थलवर्त्मना ‘by land’<BR>; पारसीकांस्ततो जेतुं प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना R. 4. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलविग्रहः|स्थलविग्रह
स्थलम् + -विग्रहः a battle on level ground, a land-fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलशुद्धिः|स्थलशुद्धि
स्थलम् + -शुद्धिः <i>f.</i> purification or clearance of a place from impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलसीमन्
स्थलम् + -सीमन् <i>f.</i> a landmark, boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलस्थ
स्थलम् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> standing on dry ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थला
स्थला A spot of dry ground artificially raised and drained (opp.<BR> स्थली q. v. below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थली
स्थली<BR>—1 Dry ground, firm land.<BR>—2 A natural spot of ground, ground or land (as of a forest); विललाप<BR> विकीर्णमूर्धजा समदुःखामिव कुर्वती स्थलीम् Ku. 4. 4; Ki. 4. 2.<BR>—3 A deity of the soil; (= स्थलदेवता q. v.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थलीदेवता, स्थलीभूता, स्थलीशायिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीदेवता
स्थली + -देवता a deity of the soil, a tutelary deity; पश्यन्तीनां न<BR> खलु बहुशो न स्थलीदेवतानां मुक्तास्थूलास्तरुकिसलयेष्वश्रुलेशाः पतन्ति Me. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीभूत
स्थली + -भूत^1 <i>a.</i> high-lying (as a country).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलीशायिन्
स्थली + -शायिन् <i>a.</i> sleeping on the bare ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेशय|स्थलेशयः
स्थलेशय <i>a.</i> Sleeping on dry ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेशयः|स्थलेशय
स्थलेशय + .{@-यः@} Any amphibious animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविः|स्थवि
स्थविः<BR>—1 A weaver.<BR>—2 Heaven.<BR>—3 A moveable thing.<BR>—4 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविर|स्थविरं|स्थविरः
स्थविर <i>a.</i> [स्था-किरच् स्थवादेशः]<BR>—1 Fixed, firm, steady.<BR>—2 Old, aged, ancient; न तेन स्थविरो भवति येनास्य पलितं शिरः ।<BR> बालोऽपि यः प्रजानाति तं देवाः स्थविरं विदुः ॥ Mb. 3. 133. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविरः|स्थविर|स्थविरं
स्थविर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 An old man; ऊर्ध्वं प्राणा ह्युत्क्रामन्ति यूनः स्थविर आयति । प्रत्युत्थानाभिवादाभ्यां<BR> पुनस्तान् प्रतिपद्यते ॥ Ms. 2. 120.<BR>—2 A beggar.<BR>—3 N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविरा
स्थविर + .{@-रा@} An old woman; स्थविरे का त्वं, अयमर्भकः कस्य नयनानन्दकरः Dk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थविरद्युति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविरद्युति
स्थविर + -द्युति <i>a.</i> having the dignity of an elder; ऋषेः पुत्रो महातेजा<BR> बालोऽपि स्थविरद्युतिः Rām. 1. 50. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविष्ठ|स्थविष्ठः
स्थविष्ठ <i>a.</i> Greatest, very strong, largest (superl. of स्थूल<BR> q. v.) मनोमयं सूक्ष्ममुपेत्य रूपं मात्रा स्वरो वर्ण इति स्थविष्ठः<BR> Bhāg. 11. 12. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवीयस्
स्थवीयस् Greater, larger (compar. of स्थूल q. v.); सर्वसत्त्वात्मदेहाय<BR> विशेषाय स्थवीयसे (नमः) Bhāg. 4. 24. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्था
स्था €1 P. (Ātm. also in certain senses; तिष्ठतिते, तस्थौ-तस्थे,<BR> अस्थात्-अस्थित, स्थास्यति-ते, स्थातुं, स्थित; <i>pass.</i> स्थीयते;<BR> the स् of this root is changed to ष् after a preposition ending<BR> in इ or उ)<BR>—1 To stand; अयं स ते तिष्ठति संगमोत्सुकः Ś. 3. 13; चलत्येकेन<BR> पादेन तिष्ठत्येकेन बुद्धिमान् Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 To stay, abide, dwell, live; ग्रामे or गृहे तिष्ठति<BR>—3 To remain, be left; यावदेकानुदिष्टस्य गन्धो लेपश्च तिष्ठति. Ms. 4. 111;<BR> एको गङ्गदत्तस्तिष्ठति Pt. 4.<BR>—2 To delay, wait; किमिति स्थीयते Ś. 2.<BR>—5 To stop, cease, desist, stand still; तिष्ठत्येष क्षणमधिपतिर्ज्योतिषां<BR> व्योममध्ये V. 2. 1.<BR>—6 To be kept aside; तिष्ठतु तावत् पत्रलेखागमनवृत्तान्तः K. ‘never mind the account of’<BR> &c.<BR>—7 To be, exist, be in any state or position; often with participles;<BR> मेरौ स्थिते दोग्धरि दोहदक्षे Ku. 1. 2; व्याप्य स्थितं रोदसी V. 1. 1;<BR> या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वं Ś. 1. 1; कालं नयमाना तिष्ठति Pt. 1; Ms. 7. 8.<BR>—8 To abide by, conform to, obey (with loc.); शासने तिष्ठ भर्तुः<BR> V. 5. 17; R. 11. 65.<BR>—9 To be restrained; यदि ते तु न तिष्ठेयुरुपायैः प्रथमैस्त्रिभिः Ms. 7. 108.<BR>—10 To be at hand, be obtainable; न विप्रं खेषु तिष्ठत्सु मृतं शूद्रेण<BR> नाययेत् Ms. 5. 104.<BR>—11 To live, breathe; आः क एष मयि स्थिते चन्द्रगुप्तमभिभवितुमिच्छति Mu. 1.<BR>—12 To stand by or near, stand at oneʼs side, help; उत्सवे व्यसने चैव<BR> दुर्भिक्षे शत्रुसंकटे (राष्ट्रविप्लवे) । राजद्वारे श्मशाने च<BR> यस्तिष्ठति स बान्धवः ॥ H. 1. 71 (v. l.).<BR>—13 To rest or depend on; जहातु नैनं कथमर्थसिद्धिः संशय्य कर्णादिषु<BR> तिष्ठते यः Ki. 3. 14.<BR>—14 To do, perform, occupy oneself with; न तिष्ठति तु यः पूर्वां नोपास्ते<BR> यश्च पश्चिमाम् Ms. 2. 103.<BR>—15 (Ātm.) To resort or go to (as an umpire), be guided by the advice<BR> of; संशय्य कर्णादिषु तिष्ठते यः Ki. 3. 14.<BR>—16 (Ātm.) To offer oneself to (for sexual embrace), stand as a prostitute<BR> (with dat.); गोपी स्मरात् कृष्णाय तिष्ठते Sk. on P. I. 4. 34. ━<i>Caus.</i><BR> (स्थापयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to stand.<BR>—2 To lay, set, place, put.<BR>—3 To found, establish.<BR>—4 To stop.<BR>—5 To arrest, check.<BR>—6 To raise, erect.<BR>—7 To cause to last or continue, make durable.<BR>—8 To give in marriage; लोकश्रेष्ठे गुणवति वरे स्थापिता त्वं मयैव Māl. 10. 5.<BR>—9 To instruct in, initiate into. ━<i>Desid.</i> (तिष्ठासति) To wish to stand &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Standing, staying, abiding, being, existing &c.; तत्रस्थ, अङ्कस्थ,<BR> प्रकृतिस्थ, तटस्थ qq. vv.<BR>—2 Immovable (स्थावर); सृज्यन्ते जङ्गमस्थानि Mb. 12. 232. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थः|स्थ
स्थ + .{@-स्थः@} A place, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणव
स्थाणव <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to स्थाणुः.<BR>—2 Coming from the trunks or stems of trees; Hc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु <i>a.</i> [स्था-नु पृषो˚ णत्वम्] Firm, fixed, steady, stable,<BR> immoveable, motionless; नित्यः सर्वगतः स्थाणुरचलोऽयं सनातनः<BR> Bg. 2. 24; Mb. 1. 34. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुः|स्थाणु
स्थाणु + .{@-णुः@}<BR>—1 An epithet of Śiva; स स्थाणुः स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो निःश्रेयसायास्तु<BR> वः V. 1. 1.<BR>—2 A stake, post, pillar; अपि स्थाणुवदासीनः Pt. 1. 49; किं स्थाणुरयमुत पुरुषः.<BR>—3 A peg, pin; स्थाणौ निषङ्गिण्यनसि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">Page1720-1</a>]<BR> क्षणं पुरः Śi. 12. 26.<BR>—4 The gnomon of a dial.<BR>—5 A spear, dart.<BR>—6 A nest of white ants.<BR>—7 The drug or perfume called <i>Jeevaka</i>.<BR>—8 Stump, trunk; लता वल्लीश्च गुल्मांश्च स्थाणूनश्मन एव च Rām. 2. 80. 6.<BR>—9 A particular posture in sitting. ━<i>m., n.</i> A branchless trunk or<BR> stem, any bare stalk or stem, pollard.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थाणुच्छेदः, स्थाणुदिश्, स्थाणुभूत, स्थाणुभ्रमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1719-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुच्छेदः|स्थाणुच्छेद|स्थाणुछेद
स्थाणु + -छेदः one who cuts down the trunks of trees, one who clears away<BR> timber; स्थाणुच्छेदस्य केदारमाहुः शल्यवतो मृगम् Ms. 9. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुदिश्
स्थाणु + -दिश् <i>f.</i> the north-east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुभूत
स्थाणु + -भूत <i>a.</i> become motionless (as the trunk of a tree).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणुभ्रमः|स्थाणुभ्रम
स्थाणु + -भ्रमः mistaking anything for a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातृ
स्थातृ <i>a.</i> Standing, stationary, fixed. ━<i>m.</i> A guider, driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानम्
स्थानम् [स्था-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 The act of standing or remaining, stay, continuance, residence; न<BR> किल भवतां देव्याः स्थानं गृहेऽभिमतं ततः U. 3. 32.<BR>—2 Being fixed or stationary.<BR>—3 A state, condition; स्थानत्रयात्परं प्राप्तं ब्रह्मभूतमविक्रियम्<BR> Bhāg. 1. 18. 26.<BR>—4 A place, spot, site, locality; अक्षमालामदत्त्वास्मात्स्थानात्पदात्पदमपि<BR> न गन्तव्यम् K.<BR>—5 Station, situation, position.<BR>—6 Relation, capacity; पितृस्थाने ‘in the place or capacity of a father’;<BR> भक्ष्यस्थाने Pt. 2. 26.<BR>—7 An abode, a house, dwelling-house; स एव (नकः) प्रच्युतः<BR> स्थानाच्छुनापि परिभूयते Pt. 3. 46.<BR>—8<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A country, region, district.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A town, city.<BR>—9 Office, rank, dignity; अमात्यस्थाने नियोजितः.<BR>—10 Object; गुणाः पूजास्थानं गुणिषु न च लिङ्गं न च वयः U. 4. 11.<BR>—11 An occasion, a matter, subject, cause; पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि<BR> स्थगयति Māl. 1. 14; स्थानं जरापरिभवस्य तदेव पुंसाम् Subhāṣ;<BR> so कलह˚, कोप˚, विवाद˚ &c.<BR>—12 A fit or proper place; स्थानेष्वेव नियोज्यन्ते भृत्याश्चाभरणानि च Pt. 1. 72.<BR>—13 A fit or worthy object; स्थाने खलु सज्जति दृष्टिः M. 1; see स्थाने also.<BR>—14 The place or organ of utterance of any letter; (these are eight:−<BR> अष्टौ स्थानानि वर्णानामुरः कण्ठः शिरस्तथा । जिह्वामूलं च दन्ताश्च<BR> नासिकौष्ठौ च तालु च Śik. 13.)<BR>—15 A holy place.<BR>—16 An altar.<BR>—17 A place in a town, square, court.<BR>—18 The place or sphere assigned after death to persons according as they<BR> perform or neglect their prescribed duties.<BR>—19 (In politics, war &c.) The firm attitude or bearing of troops, standing<BR> firm so as to repel a charge; स्थाने युद्धे च कुशलानभीरूनविकारिणः Ms. 7. 190.<BR>—20 A halt.<BR>—21 A stationary condition, a neutral or middle state; स्थानं वृद्धिः<BR> क्षयश्चैव त्रिवर्गश्चैव दण्डजः Mb. 12. 59. 31.<BR>—22 That which constitutes the chief strength or the very existence of<BR> a kingdom, a stamina of a kingdom; <i>i. e.</i> army, treasure, town, and<BR> territory; Ms. 7. 56 (where Kull. renders स्थानं by दण्डकोषपुरराष्ट्रात्मकं चतुर्विधम्).<BR>—23 Likeness, resemblance.<BR>—24 Part or division of a work, section, chapter &c.<BR>—25 The character or part of an actor.<BR>—26 Interval, opportunity, leisure.<BR>—27 (In music) A note, tone, modulation of the voice; तौ तु गान्धर्वतत्त्वज्ञौ<BR> स्थानमूर्च्छनकोविदौ Rām. 1. 4. 10 (com.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">Page1720-2</a>]<BR> यदूर्ध्वं हृदयग्रन्थे कपोलफलकादधः । प्राणसंचारणस्थानं स्थानमित्यभिधीयते ॥<BR> … … इति शाण्डिल्यः).<BR>—28 A pose, posture (of archers etc.).<BR>—29 An order of the life (आश्रम); मैत्रेयीति होवाच याज्ञवल्क्य<BR> उद्यास्यन्वा अरेऽहमस्मात् स्थानादस्मि Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 1.<BR>—30 Ground (भूमि); स्थानासनिनो भूमि-पाषाण-सिकता-शर्करा-वालुका-भस्मशायिनः<BR> Mb. 12. 192. 1.<BR>—31 Sustenance, maintenance; यच्चेदं प्रभवः स्थानं भूतानां सयमो<BR> यमः । स्वभावेनैव वर्तन्ते द्वन्द्वसृष्टानि भूरिशः ॥ Mb. 12. 238. 20<BR> (com. स्थानं पोषणम्).<BR>—32 A mode or attitude in fighting; अस्त्रयन्त्राणि चित्राणि स्थानानि विविधानि<BR> च Mb. 9. 57. 18.<BR>—33 Storage (of goods); आगमं निर्गमं स्थानं तथा वृद्धिक्षयावुभौ ।<BR> विचार्य सर्वपण्यानां कारयेत् क्रयविक्रयौ ॥ Ms. 8. 401.<BR>—34 A state of perfect tranquillity.<BR>—35 Any organ of sense.<BR>—36 Shape, form, appearance (as of the moon).<BR>—37 An astronomical mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थानाधिकारः, स्थानाध्यक्षः, स्थानासनम्, स्थानासेधः, स्थानचञ्चला, स्थानकुटिकासनम्, स्थानचिन्तकः, स्थानच्युत, स्थानटिप्पटिका, स्थानदीप्त, स्थानपालः, स्थानभूमि, स्थानभ्रष्ट, स्थानमाहात्म्यम्, स्थानमृगः, स्थानयोगः, स्थानविभागः, स्थानस्थ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानाधिकारः|स्थानाधिकार
स्थानम् + -अधिकारः the superintendence of a shrine; Inscr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानाध्यक्षः|स्थानाध्यक्ष
स्थानम् + -अध्यक्षः<BR>—1 a local governor.<BR>—2 the superintendent of a place.<BR>—3 a watchman, police-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानासनम्
स्थानम् + -आसनम् <i>n.</i> du. standing and sitting down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानासेधः|स्थानासेध
स्थानम् + -आसेधः confinement to a place, imprisonment, arrest; cf. आसेध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानचञ्चला
स्थानम् + -चञ्चला Ocimum Pilosum (Mar. तुकुमराई).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानकुटिकासनम्
स्थानम् + -कुटिकासनम् leaving the house or any abode (स्थावरगृहत्याग);<BR> शिरसो मुण्डनाद्वापि न स्थानकुटिकासनात् Mb. 3. 200. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानचिन्तकः|स्थानचिन्तक|स्थानचिंतक
स्थानम् + -चिन्तकः a kind of quarter-master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानच्युत|स्थानच्युतः
स्थानम् + -च्युत see स्थानभ्रष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानटिप्पटिका
स्थानम् + -टिप्पटिका the daily account; Śukra. 3. 369.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानदीप्त
स्थानम् + -दीप्त (in augury) inauspicious on account of situation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानपालः|स्थानपाल
स्थानम् + -पालः a watchman, sentinel, policeman; Y. 2. 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानभूमि
स्थानम् + -भूमि <i>f.</i> a dwelling-place, mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानभ्रष्ट|स्थानभ्रष्टः
स्थानम् + -भ्रष्ट <i>a.</i> ejected from an office, displaced, dismissed, out of employ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानमाहात्म्यम्
स्थानम् + -माहात्म्यम्<BR>—1 the greatness or glory of any place.<BR>—2 a kind of divine virtue or uncommon sanctity supposed to be inherent<BR> in a sacred spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानमृगः|स्थानमृग
स्थानम् + -मृगः N. of certain animals (such as turtle, crocodile &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानयोगः|स्थानयोग
स्थानम् + -योगः assignment of proper places; द्रव्याणां स्थानयोगांश्च<BR> क्रयविक्रयमेवच Ms. 9. 332.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानविभागः|स्थानविभाग
स्थानम् + -विभागः (in alg.) subdivision of a number according to the position<BR> of its figures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानस्थ
स्थानम् + -स्थ <i>a.</i> being in oneʼs abode, at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानकम्
स्थानकम् [स्थान स्वार्थे क]<BR>—1 A position, situation.<BR>—2 A particular point or situation in dramatic action; <i>e. g.</i> पताकास्थानक<BR> q. v.; स्थानकेन अवलोक्य V. 4. 44/45; it may also mean ‘a kind of posture’.<BR>—3 A city, town.<BR>—4 A basin.<BR>—5 Froth, a kind of scum on spirits or wine.<BR>—6 A mode of recitation.<BR>—7 A division or section of the Taittirīya, a branch of the <i>Yajurveda</i>.<BR>—8 A temple in which the idol is kept in an erect posture.<BR>—9 The attitude of the body (in shooting &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानतस्
स्थानतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 According to oneʼs place or position.<BR>—2 From oneʼs proper place.<BR>—3 With reference to the organ of utterance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिक|स्थानिकः
स्थानिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to a place, local.<BR>—2 (In gram.) That which takes the place of a thing or is substituted for it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिकः|स्थानिक
स्थानिक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 Any one holding an office, a place-man.<BR>—2 The governor of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1720-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिन्
स्थानिन् <i>a.</i> [स्थानमस्यास्ति रक्ष्यत्वेन इनि]<BR>—1 Having a place.<BR>—2 Having fixedness, permanent. —3 Having a substitute. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The original form or primitive element, that for which anything else<BR> is substituted; स्थानिवदादेशोऽनल्विधौ P. I. 1. 56.<BR>—2 The form so substituted for anything.<BR>—3 That which has a place, or is actually expressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिवत्
स्थानिवत् <i>a.</i> Like the original or primitive element; P. I. 1. 56.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थानिवद्भावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिवद्भावः|स्थानिवद्भाव
स्थानिवत् + -भावः the state of being like the original form; किं स्थानिवद्भावमधत्त<BR> दुष्टं तादृक्कृतव्याकरणः पुनः सः N. 10. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीय|स्थानीयं
स्थानीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to a place, local.<BR>—2 Suitable to a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीयम्
स्थानीय + .{@-यम्@}<BR>—1 A town, city.<BR>—2 Capital; Kau. A. 2. 2.<BR>—3 A kind of fortress to defend 800 villages; अष्टशतग्राम्या मध्ये स्थानीयम् Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाने
स्थाने <i>ind.</i> (loc. of स्थान)<BR>—1 In the right or proper place, rightly, properly, justly, truly, appropriately;<BR> स्थाने हषीकेश तव प्रकीर्त्या जगत् प्रहृष्यत्यनुरज्यते च Bg. 11. 36;<BR> स्थाने वृता भूपतिभिः परोक्षैः R. 7. 13; स्थाने प्राणाः कामिनां<BR> दूत्यधीनाः M. 3. 14; Ku. 6. 67, 7. 65.<BR>—2 In place of, instead of, in lieu of, as a substitute for; धातोः स्थान<BR> इवादेशं सुग्रीवं संन्यवेशयत् R. 12. 58.<BR>—3 On account of, because of.<BR>—4 Similarly, like, as.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थानेपतित<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानेपतित
स्थाने + -पतित <i>a.</i> occupying the place of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापक|स्थापकः
स्थापक <i>a.</i> [स्थापयति स्था-णिच्-ण्वुल्] Causing to stand, fixing,<BR> founding, establishing, regulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापकः|स्थापक
स्थापक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 The director of the stage-business, a stage-manager.<BR>—2 The founder of a temple, or erector of an image.<BR>—3 A depositor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापनम्
स्थापनम्^1 [स्था-णिच्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) The act of causing to stand, fixing; founding, establishing,<BR> instituting; Mb. 12. 255. 3.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) Regulating, directing.<BR>—2 Fixing the thoughts, concentration of the mind, steady application, abstraction.<BR>—3 A dwelling, habitation.<BR>—4 A ceremony performed on a womanʼs perceiving the first signs of living<BR> conception; cf. पुंसवन.<BR>—5 Fastening, rendering immovable; उत्थापनैरुन्नयनैश्चालनैः स्थापनैरपि ।<BR> परस्परं जिगीषन्तावुपचक्रतुरात्मनः ॥ Bhāg. 10. 44. 5.<BR>—6 Founding, erecting (a temple, image &c.).<BR>—7 Preservation, prolongation (of life).<BR>—8 A means of stopping (the flow of blood), styptic.<BR>—9 Storage (of grain).<BR>—10 Establishment of a proposition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थापनवृत्त<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापनवृत्त
स्थापनम् + -वृत्त <i>a.</i> one who is past all restoration to strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापना
स्थापना<BR>—1 Placing, fixing, founding, establishing.<BR>—2 Arranging, regulating (as a drama), stage-management.<BR>—3 A prologue of the drama; (see plays of Bhāsa).<BR>—4 Storing, keeping, preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापनीय
स्थापनीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be fixed, established &c.<BR>—2 To be treated with tonics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापयितृ
स्थापयितृ <i>a.</i> Establisher, founder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापित|स्थापितं
स्थापित <i>p. p.</i> [स्था-णिच्-क्त]<BR>—1 Placed, fixed, located, deposited.<BR>—2 Founded, instituted.<BR>—3 Set up, raised, erected.<BR>—4 Directed, regulated, ordered, enacted.<BR>—5 Determined, settled, ascertained.<BR>—6 Appointed to, entrusted with any duty, post &c.<BR>—7 Wedded, married; Māl. 10. 5.<BR>—8 Firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्य|स्थाप्यः
स्थाप्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be placed or deposited.<BR>—2 To be founded, fixed or established.<BR>—3 To be appointed or installed.<BR>—4 To be shut up, confined in.<BR>—5 To be plunged (in grief &c.).<BR>—6 To be checked, restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्यम्
स्थाप्य + .{@-प्यम्@} A pledge, deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्यः|स्थाप्य
स्थाप्य + .{@-प्यः@} the image of a god.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थाप्यापहरणम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्यापहरणम्
स्थाप्य + -अपहरणम् the embezzlement of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामन्
स्थामन् <i>n.</i> [स्था-मनिन्]<BR>—1 Strength, power, stamina, as in the word अश्वत्थामन्, see the quotation<BR> from Mb. under अश्वत्थामन्.<BR>—2 The neighing of a horse; अश्वस्येवास्य यत्स्थाम नदतः प्रदिशो गतम्<BR> Mb. 1. 130. 48.<BR>—3 Fixity, stability.<BR>—4 Station, seat, place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामवत्|स्थामवन्त्
स्थामवत् <i>a.</i> Powerful, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायः|स्थाय
स्थायः A receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाया
स्थायः + .{@-या@} the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिता
स्थायिता<BR>—1 Constancy, stability.<BR>—2 Durableness, invariableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिन्
स्थायिन् <i>a.</i> [स्था-णिनि]<BR>—1 Standing, staying, being situated (at the end of comp.).<BR>—2 Enduring, continuing, lasting, abiding; शरीरं क्षणविध्वंसि कल्पान्तस्थायिनो<BR> गुणाः Subhāṣ.; कतिपयदिवसस्थायिनी यौवनश्रीः Bh. 3. 82; Mv. 7. 15.<BR>—3 Living, dwelling, remaining; संपत्स्यन्ते कतिपयदिनस्थायिहंसा<BR> दशार्णाः Me. 23.<BR>—4 Permanent, firm, steady, invariable, unchangeable. ━<i>m.</i> A lasting<BR> or permanent feeling; (see स्थायिभाव below); स्थायिनोऽर्थे प्रवर्तन्ते<BR> भावाः संचारिणो यथा Śi. 2. 87. ━<i>n.</i> Anything lasting, a permanent<BR> state or condition.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थायिभावः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिभावः|स्थायिभाव
स्थायिन् + -भावः a fixed or permanent condition of mind, a lasting or permanent<BR> feeling; (these feelings being said to give rise to the different <i>rasas</i><BR> or sentiments in poetry, each <i>rasa</i> having its own Sthāyibhāva);<BR> they are eight or nine; रतिर्हासश्च शोकश्च क्रोधोत्साहौ भयं तथा ।<BR> जुगुप्सा विस्मयश्चेत्थमष्टौ प्रोक्ताः शमोऽपि च S. D. 206; cf. व्यभिचारिभाव,<BR> भाव, विभाव also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायीभू
स्थायीभू €1 P. To become firm, fixed or permanent, take a strong or<BR> firm hold on; वचस्तत्र प्रयोक्तव्यं यत्रोक्तं लभते फलम् । स्थायीभवति<BR> चात्यन्तं रागः शुक्लपटे यथा ॥ Pt. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुक|स्थायुकः
स्थायुक <i>a.</i> (-का or -की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्था-उकञ्]<BR>—1 Likely to last, enduring.<BR>—2 Firm, steady, stationary; आयोधने स्थायुकमस्त्रजातम् Bk. 2. 22;<BR> अतीते वर्षुके काले, प्रमत्तः स्थायुको गृहे ibid. 7. 18. 3 Located,<BR> situated; कुम्भास्थिकूटावटस्थानस्थायुकमौक्तिकोत्करकिरः N. 12. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुकः|स्थायुक
स्थायुक + .{@-कः@} The superintendent or head of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1721-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर <i>a.</i> [स्था-वरच्]<BR>—1 Fixed to one spot, stable, stationary, immoveable, inanimate (opp.<BR> जङ्गम); शरीरिणां स्थावरजङ्गमानां सुखाय तज्जन्मदिनं बभूव<BR> Ku. 1. 23, 6. 67, 73.<BR>—2 Inert, inactive, slow. —3 Regular, established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरः|स्थावर|स्थावरं
स्थावर + .{@-रः@} A mountain; स्थावराणां हिमालयः Bg. 10. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरम्
स्थावर + .{@-रम्@}<BR>—1 Any stationary or inanimate object (such as clay, stones, trees &c.<BR> which formed the seventh creation of Brahman; cf. Ms. 1. 41); मान्यः<BR> स मे स्थावरजङ्गमानां सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारहेतुः R. 2. 44; Ku. 6. 58.<BR>—2 A bow-string.<BR>—3 Immoveable property, real estate.<BR>—4 A heir-loom.<BR>—5 A large body; (fig.) a gross or material body (स्थूलशरीर); गमनं<BR> निरपेक्षश्च पश्चादनवलोकयन् । ऋजुः प्रणिहितो गच्छंस्त्रसस्थावरवर्जकः Mb. 12. 9. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थावरास्थावरम्, स्थावरजङ्गमम्, स्थावरात्मन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरास्थावरम्
स्थावर + -अस्थावरम्, -जङ्गमम्<BR>—1 moveable and immoveable property.<BR>—2 animate and inanimate things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरजङ्गमम्
स्थावर + -अस्थावरम्, -जङ्गमम्<BR>—1 moveable and immoveable property.<BR>—2 animate and inanimate things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरात्मन्
स्थावर + -आत्मन् <i>a.</i> of immoveable form; स्थाने त्वां स्थावरात्मानं विष्णुमाहुस्तथाहि<BR> ते Ku. 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरता
स्थावरता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Fixedness, stability.<BR>—2 The state of a vegetable or mineral; शरीरजैः कर्मदोषैर्याति स्थावरतां<BR> नरः Ms. 12. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरत्वम्
स्थावरता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Fixedness, stability.<BR>—2 The state of a vegetable or mineral; शरीरजैः कर्मदोषैर्याति स्थावरतां<BR> नरः Ms. 12. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासकः|स्थासक
स्थासकः [स्था-स-स्वार्थादौ क]<BR>—1 Perfuming or smearing the body with fragrant unguents.<BR>—2 A bubble of water or any fluid; रौक्मा रेजुः स्थासका मूर्तिभाजो दर्पस्येव<BR> व्याप्तदेहस्य शेषाः Śi. 18. 5.<BR>—3 A bubble-shaped ornament on a horseʼs trappings.<BR>—4 A figure made with unguents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु <i>n.</i> Bodily strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नु|स्थास्नुः
स्थास्नु <i>a.</i> [स्था-स्नु]<BR>—1 Disposed to stand, firm, immoveable.<BR>—2 Permanent, eternal, lasting, durable; भवन्त्यस्यैवमङ्गानि स्थास्नूनि<BR> बलवन्ति च Śi. 2. 93; Ki. 2. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नुः|स्थास्नु
स्थास्नु + .{@-स्नुः@} A tree; अणुप्रायास्वोषधीषु शमीप्रायेषु स्थास्नुषु Bhāg. 12. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित|स्थितः
स्थित <i>p. p.</i> [स्था-क्त]<BR>—1 Stood, remained, stayed.<BR>—2 Standing.<BR>—3 Standing up, risen; स्थितः स्थितामुच्चलितः प्रयातां … छायेव<BR> तां भूपतिरन्वगच्छत् R. 2. 6.<BR>—4 Staying, resting, living, being, existing, situated; धन्या केयं<BR> स्थिता ते शिरसि Mu. 1. 1; Me. 7; oft, with gerunds merely as a copula;<BR> वेदान्तेषु यमाहुरेकपुरुषं व्याप्य स्थितं रोदसी V. 1. 1; Ś. 1. 1; Ku. 1. 1.<BR>—5 Happened, occurred; सुहृदः पश्य वसन्त किं स्थितम् Ku. 4. 27.<BR>—6 Stationed in, occupying, appointed to; अभिजनवतो भर्तुः श्लाघ्ये<BR> स्थिता गृहिणीपदे Ś. 4. 18.<BR>—7 Acting up to, abiding by, conforming to; किमत्र चित्रं यदि कामसूर्भूर्वृत्ते<BR> स्थितस्याधिपतेः प्रजानाम् R. 5. 33; धर्मे स्थिताः (राजानः) Māl. 10. 25.<BR>—8 Stood still, stopped, desisted.<BR>—9 Fixed on, firmly attached to; ममात्र भावैकरसं मनः स्थितम् Ku. 5. 82.<BR>—10 Steady, firm; as in स्थितधी or स्थितप्रज्ञ q. v.<BR>—11 Determined, resolved; इति देहविमुक्तये स्थिताम् (रतिम्) Ku. 4. 39.<BR>—12 Established, decreed.<BR>—13 Steadfast in conduct, steady-minded.<BR>—14 Upright, virtuous.<BR>—15 Faithful to a promise or agreement.<BR>—16 Agreed, engaged, contracted.<BR>—17 Ready, being close<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">Page1722-2</a>]<BR> or at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितम्
स्थित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Standing by itself (as a word).<BR>—2 Stopping, standing still.<BR>—3 Manner of standing. —4 Perseverance on the right path.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थितोपस्थित, स्थितधी, स्थितपाठव्यम्, स्थितप्रज्ञ, स्थितप्रेमन्, स्थितलिङ्ग, स्थितसंकेत, स्थितसंविद्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितोपस्थित
स्थित + -उपस्थित <i>a.</i> with and without the particle ‘इति’ (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितधी
स्थित + -धी <i>a.</i> firm-minded, steady-minded, cool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितपाठव्यम्
स्थित + -पाठव्यम् recitation in Prākṛta by a woman while standing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रज्ञ|स्थितप्रज्ञः
स्थित + -प्रज्ञ <i>a.</i> firm in judgment or wisdom, free from any hallucination,<BR> contented; प्रजहाति यदा कामान् सर्वान् पार्थ मनोगतान् । आत्मन्येवात्मना<BR> तुष्टः स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते Bg. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितप्रेमन्
स्थित + -प्रेमन् <i>m.</i> a staunch or faithful friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितलिङ्ग
स्थित + -लिङ्ग <i>a.</i> having the virile member erected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितसंकेत
स्थित + -संकेत, -संविद् <i>a.</i> keeping a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितसंविद्
स्थित + -संकेत, -संविद् <i>a.</i> keeping a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिः|स्थिति
स्थितिः <i>f.</i> [स्था-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Standing, remaining, staying, abiding, living, stay, residence; स्थितिं<BR> नो रे दध्याः क्षणमपि मदान्धेक्षण सखे Bv. 1. 52; रक्षोगृहे स्थितिर्मूलमग्निशुद्धौ<BR> त्वनिश्चयः U. 1. 6.<BR>—2 Stopping, standing still, continuance in one state; प्रस्थितायां प्रतिष्ठेथाः<BR> स्थितायां स्थितिमाचरेः R. 1. 89.<BR>—3 Remaining stationary, fixity, steadiness, firmness, steady application<BR> or devotion; मम भूयात् परमात्मनि स्थितिः Bv. 4. 23; Māl. 5. 22.<BR>—4 A state, position, situation, condition; एषा ब्राह्मी स्थितिः पार्थ<BR> नैनां प्राप्य विमुह्यति Bg. 2. 72.<BR>—5 Natural state, nature, habit; सपर्वतवनां कृत्स्नां व्यथयिष्यामि<BR> ते स्थितिम् Rām. 7. 98. 10; अथ वा स्थितिरियं मन्दमतीनाम् H. 4.<BR>—6 Stability, permanence, perpetuation, continuance; वंशस्थितेरधिगमान्महति<BR> प्रमोदे V. 5. 15; कन्यां कुलस्य स्थितये स्थितिज्ञः Ku. 1. 18; Mv. 7. 3;<BR> R. 3. 27.<BR>—7 Correctness of conduct, steadfastness in the path of duty, decorum,<BR> duty, moral rectitude, propriety; अमंस्त चानेन परार्ध्यजन्मना स्थितेरभेत्ता<BR> स्थितिमन्तमन्वयम् R. 3. 27, 11. 65, 12. 31; कन्यां कुलस्य स्थितये<BR> स्थितिज्ञः (विधिनोपयेमे) Ku. 1. 18; Ś. 5. 10.<BR>—8 Maintenance of discipline, establishment of good order (in a state);<BR> स्थित्यै दण्डयतो दण्ड्यान् R. 1. 25.<BR>—9 Rank, dignity, high station or rank.<BR>—10 Maintenance, sustenance; जग्धार्धैर्नवसल्लकीकिसलयैरस्याः स्थितिं<BR> कल्पयन् Māl. 9. 32; R. 5. 9.<BR>—11 Continuance in life, preservation (one of the three states of human<BR> beings); सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारहेतुः R. 2. 44; Ku. 2. 6.<BR>—12 Cessation, pause, stop, restriction; नासां कश्चिदगम्योस्ति नासां<BR> च वयसि स्थितिः Pt. 1. 143.<BR>—13 Wellbeing, welfare.<BR>—14 Consistency.<BR>—15 A settled rule, ordinance, decree, an axiom or maxim; अबान्धवं<BR> शवं चैव निर्हरेयुरिति स्थितिः Ms. 10. 55.<BR>—16 Settled determination.<BR>—17 Term, limit, boundary.<BR>—18 Inertia, resistance to motion.<BR>—19 Duration of an eclipse.<BR>—20 Regard, consideration, account; नासां च वयसि स्थितिः Pt. 1. 143.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थितिज्ञ, स्थितिपद्, स्थितिपदम्, स्थितिभिद्, स्थितिमार्गः, स्थितिस्थापक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिज्ञ
स्थितिः + -ज्ञ <i>a.</i> knowing the bounds of morality; कन्यां कुलस्य स्थितये<BR> स्थितिज्ञः Ku. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिपद्
स्थितिः + -पद् the epithet of Viṣṇu; पादेषु सर्वभूतानि पुंसः स्थितिपदो<BR> विदुः Bhāg. 2. 6. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिपदम्
स्थितिः + -पदम् the proper basin (for flow), the right path; अपामुद्वृत्तानां<BR> निजमुपदिशन्त्या स्थितिपदम् Mu. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिभिद्
स्थितिः + -भिद् <i>a.</i> violating the bounds of morality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिमार्गः
स्थितिः + -मार्गः the way to compose (the mind); मनसश्च स्थितिमार्गमाललम्बे Bu. C. 5. 9.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">Page1723-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1722-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिस्थापक|स्थितिस्थापकः
स्थितिः + -स्थापक <i>a.</i> fixing in the original position, having the power<BR> of restoring to a previous state, having elastic properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिस्थापकः|स्थितिस्थापक
स्थितिः + -स्थापक + .({@-कः@}) elasticity, capability of recovering the former position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिमत्|स्थितिमन्त्
स्थितिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Possessed of firmness, steady, firm; N. 5. 22.<BR>—2 Permanent; स्थितेरभेत्ता स्थितिमन्तमन्वयम् R. 3. 27.<BR>—3 Virtuous, upright.<BR>—4 Keeping within limits (as the ocean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाण्डिलः|स्थाण्डिल|स्थांडिल|स्थांडिलः
स्थाण्डिलः [स्थण्डिले शयिता अण्]<BR>—1 An ascetic who sleeps on the bare ground or on a place prepared for sacrifice.<BR>—2 A religious mendicant or beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्यः|स्थापत्य
स्थापत्यः [स्थपतिरेव स्वार्थे ष्यञ्] A guard of the womenʼs apartments,<BR> chamberlain; स्थापत्यैर्न स्म वित्तस्ते वर्षीयस्त्वचलत्करैः N. 20. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्यम्
स्थापत्यः + .{@-त्यम्@}<BR>—1 The office of the governor of a district.<BR>—2 Architecture, building, erecting; स्थांपंत्यं चासृजद्वेदं क्रमात्<BR> पूर्वादिभिर्मुखैः Bhāg. 3. 12. 38.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थापत्यवेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्यवेदः|स्थापत्यवेद
स्थापत्यः + -वेदः the science of architecture (one of the four उपवेदs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालम्
स्थालम् [स्थलति तिष्ठत्यन्नाद्यत्र आधारे घञ्]<BR>—1 A plate or dish.<BR>—2 A cooking-pot, any culinary vessel; स्थालानां चषकाणां च भृङ्गाराणां<BR> च भूरिशः Śiva B. 29. 58.<BR>—3 The hollow of a tooth.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थालपथ, स्थालपथिक, स्थालरूपम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालपथ
स्थालम् + -पथ, -पथिक <i>a.</i> imported by land; P. V. 1. 77. Vārt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालपथिक
स्थालम् + -पथ, -पथिक <i>a.</i> imported by land; P. V. 1. 77. Vārt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालरूपम्
स्थालम् + -रूपम् the form or representation of a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालकः|स्थालक
स्थालकः, -कम् (pl.)<BR> N. of particular bones on the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालकम्
स्थालकः, -कम् (pl.)<BR> N. of particular bones on the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालिकः|स्थालिक
स्थालिकः The smell of faeces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाली
स्थाली —1 An earthen pot or pan, a cooking-pot, caldron, kettle; न<BR> हि भिक्षुकाः सन्तीति स्थाल्यो नाधिश्रीयन्ते Sarva. S.; स्थाल्यां वैडूर्यमय्यां<BR> पचति तिलखलीमिन्धनैश्चन्दनाद्यैः Bh. 2. 100.<BR>—2 A particular vessel used in the preparation of Soma.<BR>—3 The trumpet-flower.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थालीद्रुमः, स्थालीपाकः, स्थालीपुरीषम्, स्थालीपुलाकः, स्थालीबिलम्, स्थालीबिलीयम्, स्थालीबिल्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीद्रुमः|स्थालीद्रुम
स्थाली + -द्रुमः Ficus Benjamina or Indica (Mar. नांदुरखी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपाकः|स्थालीपाक
स्थाली + -पाकः<BR>—1 a particular religious act performed by a householder.<BR>—2 a dish of rice boiled in milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपुरीषम्
स्थाली + -पुरीषम् the sediment or dirt sticking to a cooking-pot; स्थालीपुरीषादीन्यप्यमृतवदभ्यवहरति<BR> Bhāg. 5. 9. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीपुलाकः|स्थालीपुलाक
स्थाली + -पुलाकः boiled rice in a cooking-pot; यथा स्थालीपुलाकेन<BR> Ms. 7. 4. 12; अलिङ्गाखपि स्थालीपुलाकवत् सिद्धिः ŚB. on MS. 8. 1. 11.<BR> ˚न्यायः see under न्याय; also see तुल्यन्याय and तुल्यपाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीबिलम्
स्थाली + -बिलम् the interior or hollow of a caldron; P. V. 1. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीबिलीय|स्थालीबिलीयः
स्थाली + -बिलीय, -बिल्य^1 <i>a.</i> fit for cooking (rice etc.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालीबिल्य|स्थालीबिल्यः
स्थाली + -बिलीय, -बिल्य^1 <i>a.</i> fit for cooking (rice etc.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260429. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरादि
स्थावरादि <i>n.</i> A kind of poison; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविर|स्थाविरं
स्थाविर <i>a.</i> (-रा or -री <i>f.</i>)<BR> Thick, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविरम्
स्थाविर + .{@-रम्@} Old age (commencing after seventy); (वृद्धः स्यात्सप्ततेरूर्ध्वं<BR> वर्षीयान् नवतेः परम्); गार्हस्थ्येऽप्यथवा बाल्ये यौवने स्थाविरेऽपि<BR> वा Mb. 3. 200. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिकः|स्थिक
स्थिकः, (-क्कः)<BR> The buttocks; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिक्कः
स्थिकः, (-क्कः)<BR> The buttocks; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर <i>a.</i> [स्था-किरच्] (compar. स्थेयस्; superl. स्थेष्ठ)<BR>—1 Firm, steady, fixed; भावस्थिराणि जननान्तरसौहृदानि Ś. 5. 2;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-2" target="_blank">Page1723-2</a>]<BR> स स्थाणुः स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो निःश्रेयसायास्तु वः V. 1. 1; Ku. 1. 30; R. 11. 19.<BR>—2 Immoveable, still, motionless; स्थिरप्रदीपतामेत्य भुजङ्गाः पर्युपासते Ku. 2. 38.<BR>—3 Immoveably fixed; कालेनावरणात्ययात्परिणते यत्स्नेहसारे स्थितम् U. 1. 39.<BR>—4 Permanent, eternal, everlasting; कल्पिष्यन्ते स्थिरगणपदप्राप्तये<BR> श्रद्दधानाः Me. 57; Māl. 10. 25.<BR>—5 Cool, collected, composed, placid, calm.<BR>—6 Quiescent, free from passion.<BR>—7 Steady in conduct, steadfast.<BR>—8 Constant, faithful, determined.<BR>—9 Certain, sure.<BR>—10 Hard, solid.<BR>—11 Strong, intense.<BR>—12 Stern, relentless, hard-hearted; अहो स्थिरः कोऽपि तवेप्सितो युवा Ku. 5. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरः|स्थिर
स्थिर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A god, deity.<BR>—2 A tree.<BR>—3 A mountain.<BR>—4 A bull.<BR>—5 N. of Śiva.<BR>—6 N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>—7 Final beatitude or absolution.<BR>—8 The planet Saturn.<BR>—9 N. of certain zodiacal signs (<i>Taurus, Leo, Scorpio</i>, and <i>Aquarius</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरा
स्थिर + .{@-रा@}<BR>—1 The earth; पितामहस्तामालोक्य विहस्तामस्थिरां स्थिराम् Śiva B. 5. 47.<BR>—2 A strong-minded woman.<BR>—3 The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरम्
स्थिर + .{@-रम्@} Steadfastness, stubbornness. (स्थिरीकृ means<BR>—1 to confirm, strengthen, or to corroborate.<BR>—2 to stop, make fast.<BR>—3 to cheer up, console, comfort; Ś. 4.<BR>—4 To steel (the heart); Amaru. स्थिरीभू means<BR>—1 to become firm or steady.<BR>—2 to become calm or tranquil.)<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्थिराङ्घ्रिपः, स्थिरानुराग, स्थिरापाय, स्थिरात्मन्, स्थिरचित्त, स्थिरचेतस्, स्थिरधी, स्थिरबुद्धि, स्थिरमति, स्थिरायति, स्थिरायुस्, स्थिरजीविन्, स्थिरारम्भ, स्थिरकर्मन्, स्थिरकुट्टकः, स्थिरकुसुमः, स्थिरगतिः, स्थिरगन्धः, स्थिरच्छदः, स्थिरच्छायः, स्थिरजिह्वः, स्थिरजीवित, स्थिरजीविता, स्थिरदंष्ट्रः, स्थिरधामन्, स्थिरपत्रः, स्थिरपद, स्थिरपुष्पः, स्थिरप्रतिज्ञ, स्थिरप्रतिबन्ध, स्थिरप्रतिष्ठा, स्थिरफला, स्थिरयोनिः, स्थिरयौवन, स्थिररङ्गा, स्थिररागा, स्थिरलिङ्ग, स्थिरवाच्, स्थिरविक्रम, स्थिरश्री, स्थिरसङ्गर, स्थिरसौहृद, स्थिरस्थायिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1723-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

