स्नुध्निका Natron, mineral alkali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुषा
स्नुषा A daughter-in-law; समुपास्यत पुत्रभोग्यया स्नुषयेवाविकृतेन्द्रियः<BR> श्रिया R. 8. 14, 15. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुस्
स्नुस् €4 P. (स्नुस्यति)<BR>—1 To disappear, become invisible.<BR>—2 To take, accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह् €4 P. (स्नुह्यति, स्नुग्ध or स्नूढ) To vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह्^1, स्नुहा, -हिः <i>f.</i>, -ही<BR> The milk-hedge plant. [Raghunandana, the author of Kṛtyatattva<BR> (Jīvānandaʼs ed. of Smṛtitattva vol. II, 1895) quotes a verse from<BR> the Devīpurāṇa in connection with the worship of the goddess Manasā<BR> to get rid of the fear of snake-bite (cf. Dr. Kaneʼs History of Dharma-śāstra, vol. V. p. 125).<BR> He explains स्नुही as सिजुवृक्षः. The botanic<BR> name of the tree is Euphorbia Nerifolia (Mar. निवहुंग). It is a plant<BR> from the stem of which a sticky substance oozes out.]<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma. Cf. other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहा
स्नुह्^1, स्नुहा, -हिः <i>f.</i>, -ही<BR> The milk-hedge plant. [Raghunandana, the author of Kṛtyatattva<BR> (Jīvānandaʼs ed. of Smṛtitattva vol. II, 1895) quotes a verse from<BR> the Devīpurāṇa in connection with the worship of the goddess Manasā<BR> to get rid of the fear of snake-bite (cf. Dr. Kaneʼs History of Dharma-śāstra, vol. V. p. 125).<BR> He explains स्नुही as सिजुवृक्षः. The botanic<BR> name of the tree is Euphorbia Nerifolia (Mar. निवहुंग). It is a plant<BR> from the stem of which a sticky substance oozes out.]<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma. Cf. other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहिः|स्नुहि
स्नुह्^1, स्नुहा, -हिः <i>f.</i>, -ही<BR> The milk-hedge plant. [Raghunandana, the author of Kṛtyatattva<BR> (Jīvānandaʼs ed. of Smṛtitattva vol. II, 1895) quotes a verse from<BR> the Devīpurāṇa in connection with the worship of the goddess Manasā<BR> to get rid of the fear of snake-bite (cf. Dr. Kaneʼs History of Dharma-śāstra, vol. V. p. 125).<BR> He explains स्नुही as सिजुवृक्षः. The botanic<BR> name of the tree is Euphorbia Nerifolia (Mar. निवहुंग). It is a plant<BR> from the stem of which a sticky substance oozes out.]<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma. Cf. other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुही
स्नुह्^1, स्नुहा, -हिः <i>f.</i>, -ही<BR> The milk-hedge plant. [Raghunandana, the author of Kṛtyatattva<BR> (Jīvānandaʼs ed. of Smṛtitattva vol. II, 1895) quotes a verse from<BR> the Devīpurāṇa in connection with the worship of the goddess Manasā<BR> to get rid of the fear of snake-bite (cf. Dr. Kaneʼs History of Dharma-śāstra, vol. V. p. 125).<BR> He explains स्नुही as सिजुवृक्षः. The botanic<BR> name of the tree is Euphorbia Nerifolia (Mar. निवहुंग). It is a plant<BR> from the stem of which a sticky substance oozes out.]<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170124. note: missing virAma. Cf. other dictionaries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहः|स्नेह
स्नेहः [स्निह्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Affection, love, kindness, tenderness; स्नेहदाक्षिण्ययोर्योगात् कामीव<BR> प्रतिभाति मे V. 2. 4 (where it has sense 6 also); अस्ति मे सोदरस्नेहोऽप्येतेषु Ś. 1.<BR>—2 Oiliness, visicidity, unctuousness, lubricity (one of the 24 Guṇas<BR> according to the Vaiśeṣikas)<BR>—3 Moisture; तृष्णासंजननं स्नेह एष तेषां पुनर्भवः Mb. 12. 218. 33.<BR>—4 Grease, fat, any unctuous substance.<BR>—5 Oil; निर्विष्टविषयस्नेहः स दशान्तमुपेयिवान् R. 12. 1; Pt. 1. 82<BR> (where the word has sense 1 also), 221; R. 4. 75.<BR>—6 Any fluid of the body, such as semen.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्नेहाक्त, स्नेहाङ्कनम्, स्नेहानुवृत्तिः, स्नेहाशः, स्नेहकुम्भः, स्नेहकेसरिन्, स्नेहच्छेदः, स्नेहभङ्गः, स्नेहपक्व, स्नेहपानम्, स्नेहपूर्वम्, स्नेहप्रवृत्तिः, स्नेहप्रसरः, स्नेहप्रस्रवः, स्नेहप्रिय, स्नेहबीजः, स्नेहभाण्डम्, स्नेहभूः, स्नेहभूमिः, स्नेहरङ्गः, स्नेहरसनम्, स्नेहरेकभू, स्नेहवरम्, स्नेहवस्तिः, स्नेहविद्धः, स्नेहविमर्दित, स्नेहव्यक्तिः, स्नेहसंभाषः, स्नेहसार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1726-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

