स्फुलिङ्गा
स्फुलिङ्गः, -ङ्गम्, स्फुलिङ्गा<BR> [स्फुल्-इङ्गक् Uṇ. 1. 113] A spark of fire;<BR> स्फुलिङ्गावस्थया वह्निरेधापेक्ष इव स्थितः Ś. 7. 15; Ve. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिङ्गिनी|स्फुलिंगिनी
स्फुलिङ्गिनी One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्तिः|स्फूर्ति|स्फूर्त्ति|स्फूर्त्तिः
स्फूर्तिः <i>f.</i> [स्फुर्च्छ्-स्फुर् वा क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Throbbing, shaking, vibration.<BR>—2 Spring, bound.<BR>—3 Blooming, opening.<BR>—4 Manifestation, display.<BR>—5 Flashing on the mind.<BR>—6 Poetical inspiration.<BR>—7 Bragging, boasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्तिमत्|स्फूर्तिमन्त्|स्फूर्त्तिमत्
स्फूर्तिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Throbbing, tremulous, agitated.<BR>—2 Tender-hearted. ━<i>m.</i> A follower or worshipper of Śiva (पाशुपत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयस्
स्फेयस् <i>a.</i> More abundant, larger (compar. of स्फिर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेष्ठ|स्फेष्ठः
स्फेष्ठ <i>a.</i> Most abundant, largest (superl. of स्फिर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटः|स्फोट
स्फोटः [स्फुट् करणे घञ्]<BR>—1 Breaking forth, splitting open, bursting.<BR>—2 Disclosure; as in नर्मस्फोट.<BR>—3 A swelling, boil, tumour; अयमपरो गण्डस्योपरि स्फोटः Mu. 5.<BR>—4 The idea which bursts out or flashes on the mind when a sound is uttered,<BR> the impression produced on the mind at hearing a sound; बुधैर्वैयाकरणैः<BR> प्रधानभूतस्फोटरूपव्यङ्ग्यव्यञ्जकस्य शब्दस्य ध्वनिरिति व्यवहारः<BR> कृतः K. P. 1; also see Sarva. S. (पाणिनीयदर्शन).<BR>—5 The eternal sound recognised by the Mīmāṃsakas; दिशां त्वमवकाशोऽसि<BR> दिशः खं स्फोट आश्रयः Bhāg. 10. 85. 9; शृणोति य इमं स्फोटं सुप्तश्रोत्रे<BR> च शून्यदृक् 12. 6. 40.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्फोटकरः, स्फोटबीजकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटकरः|स्फोटकर
स्फोटः + -करः, -बीजकः the marking-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटबीजकः|स्फोटबीजक
स्फोटः + -करः, -बीजकः the marking-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटकः|स्फोटक
स्फोटकः A swelling, boil, tumour, pimple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटन|स्फोटनं|स्फोटनः
स्फोटन <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्फुट्-ल्युट्] Breaking asunder, manifesting, disclosing, making clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटनः|स्फोटन|स्फोटनं
स्फोटन + .{@-नः@} Separated utterance of a close combination of consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटनम्
स्फोटन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Rending, suddenly bursting, splitting, cracking.<BR>—2 Winnowing grain.<BR>—3 Cracking the finger-joints, snapping the fingers.<BR>—4 The separation of a double consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटनी
स्फोटनी The boring tool, an auger, a gimlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटा
स्फोटा The expanded hood of a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटिका
स्फोटिका A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोरणम्
स्फोरणम् See स्फुरणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्यम्
स्फ्यम्<BR>—1 A sword-shaped implement used in sacrifices; Ms. 5. 117; Y. 1. 184.<BR>—2 A kind of oar; (नौका) शुभस्फ्यवेगाभिहता शीघ्रं सलिलमत्यगात्<BR> Rām. 2. 52. 81.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्फ्यवर्तनिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्यवर्तनिः|स्फ्यवर्तनि|स्फ्यवर्त्तनि
स्फ्यम् + -वर्तनिः the furrow made by this implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्बृ
स्बृ See स्वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्म
स्म <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A particle added to the present tense of verbs (or to present participles)<BR> and giving them the sense of the past tense; भासुरको नाम सिंहः प्रतिवसति<BR> स्म Pt. 1; क्रीणन्ति स्म प्राणमूल्यैर्यशांसि Śi. 18. 15.<BR>—2 A pleonastic particle (generally added to the prohibitive particle<BR> मा q. v.); भर्तुर्विप्रकृतापि रोषणतया मास्म प्रतीपं गमः Ś. 4. 18;<BR> मास्म सीमन्तिनी काचिज्जनयेत् पुत्रमीदृशम् H. 2. 7.<BR>—3 A particle giving a sense of ‘ever’, ‘always’ or ‘indeed’, ‘verily’<BR> and like; उवाच विप्राः प्रतिनन्द्य पार्थिवं मुदा मुनीनां सदसि स्म<BR> शृण्वताम् Bhāg. 8. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरः|स्मर
स्मरः [स्मृ-भावे अप्]<BR>—1 Recollection, remembrance; स्मरो वावाकाशाद्भूयः Ch. Up. 7. 13. 1, 2.<BR>—2 Love; स्मर<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">Page1732-1</a>]<BR> एव तापहेतुर्निर्वापयिता स एव मे जातः Ś. 3. 11.<BR>—3 Cupid, the god of love; स्मर पर्युत्सुक एष माधवः Ku. 4. 28, 42, 43.<BR>—4 The 7th astrological mansion.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मराङ्कुशः, स्मरागारम्, स्मरकूपकः, स्मरगृहम्, स्मरमन्दिरम्, स्मराधिवासः, स्मरान्ध,^1 स्मराकुल, स्मरातुर, स्मरार्त, स्मरोत्सुक, स्मरासवः, स्मरोद्दीपनः, स्मरोन्मादः, स्मरोपकरणम्, स्मरकथा, स्मरकर्मन्, स्मरकार, स्मरगुरुः, स्मरचक्रः, स्मरचन्द्रः, स्मरच्छत्रम्, स्मरदशा, स्मरदुर्मद, स्मरध्वजः, स्मरप्रिया, स्मरभासित, स्मरमोहः, स्मरलेखः, स्मरलेखनी, स्मरवल्लभः, स्मरवीथिका, स्मरशासनः, स्मरशास्त्रम्, स्मरसखः, स्मरस्तम्भः, स्मरस्मर्यः, स्मरहरः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1731-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराङ्कुशः|स्मराङ्कुश|स्मरांकुश
स्मरः + -अङ्कुशः<BR>—1 a finger-nail.<BR>—2 a lover, lascivious person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरागारम्
स्मरः + -अगारम्, -कूपकः, -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकूपकः|स्मरकूपक
स्मरः + -अगारम्, -कूपकः, -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरगृहम्
स्मरः + -अगारम्, -कूपकः, -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमन्दिरम्
स्मरः + -अगारम्, -कूपकः, -गृहम्, -मन्दिरम् the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराधिवासः|स्मराधिवास
स्मरः + -अधिवासः the Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरान्ध|स्मरांध
स्मरः + -अन्ध^1 <i>a.</i> blinded by love, infatuated with passion.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मराकुल
स्मरः + -आकुल, -आतुर, -आर्त, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> pining with love, love-sick,<BR> smit with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरातुर
स्मरः + -आकुल, -आतुर, -आर्त, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> pining with love, love-sick,<BR> smit with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरार्त|स्मरार्त्त
स्मरः + -आकुल, -आतुर, -आर्त, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> pining with love, love-sick,<BR> smit with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरोत्सुक
स्मरः + -आकुल, -आतुर, -आर्त, -उत्सुक <i>a.</i> pining with love, love-sick,<BR> smit with love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरासवः|स्मरासव
स्मरः + -आसवः saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरोद्दीपनः|स्मरोद्दीपन
स्मरः + -उद्दीपनः a sort of hair-oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरोन्मादः|स्मरोन्माद
स्मरः + -उन्मादः amorous folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरोपकरणम्
स्मरः + -उपकरणम् implement of love (as perfumes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकथा
स्मरः + -कथा loversʼ prattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकर्मन्|स्मरकर्म्मन्
स्मरः + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> any amorous action, a wanton act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरकार
स्मरः + -कार <i>a.</i> exciting love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरगुरुः|स्मरगुरु
स्मरः + -गुरुः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरचक्रः|स्मरचक्र
स्मरः + -चक्रः, -चन्द्रः a kind of sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरचन्द्रः|स्मरचन्द्र
स्मरः + -चक्रः, -चन्द्रः a kind of sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरच्छत्रम्
स्मरः + -छत्रम् the clitoris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरदशा
स्मरः + -दशा a state of love, state of the body produced by being in<BR> love (these are ten).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरदुर्मद
स्मरः + -दुर्मद <i>a.</i> infatuated by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरध्वजः|स्मरध्वज|स्मरध्वजं
स्मरः + -ध्वजः<BR>—1 the male organ.<BR>—2 a fabulous fish.<BR>—3 N. of a musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरध्वजम्
स्मरः + -ध्वजः + .({@-जम्@}) the female organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरध्वजा
स्मरः + -ध्वजः + .({@-जा@}) a bright moon-light night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरप्रिया
स्मरः + -प्रिया an epithet of Rati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरभासित
स्मरः + -भासित <i>a.</i> inflamed by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमोहः|स्मरमोह
स्मरः + -मोहः infatuation of love, passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरलेखः|स्मरलेख
स्मरः + -लेखः a love-letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरलेखनी
स्मरः + -लेखनी the Sārikā bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवल्लभः|स्मरवल्लभ
स्मरः + -वल्लभः<BR>—1 an epithet of Spring.<BR>—2 of Aniruddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवीथिका
स्मरः + -वीथिका a prostitute, harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरशासनः|स्मरशासन
स्मरः + -शासनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरशास्त्रम्
स्मरः + -शास्त्रम् a manual of erotics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरसखः|स्मरसख
स्मरः + -सखः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 the spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्तम्भः|स्मरस्तम्भ
स्मरः + -स्तम्भः the male organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरस्मर्यः|स्मरस्मर्य|स्मरस्मर्य्य|स्मरस्मर्य्यः
स्मरः + -स्मर्यः a donkey, an ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरहरः|स्मरहर
स्मरः + -हरः an epithet of Śiva; श्मशानेष्वाक्रीडा स्मरहर पिशाचाः<BR> सहचराः Śivamahimna 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरमय
स्मरमय <i>a.</i> Produced by love; प्रकटयन्त्यनुरागमकृत्रिमं<BR> स्मरमयं रमयन्ति विलासिनः Śi. 6. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरवती
स्मरवती A woman in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणम्
स्मरणम् [स्मृ-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Remembering, remembrance, recollection; केवलं स्मरणेनैव पुनासि<BR> पुरुषं यतः R. 10. 29.<BR>—2 Thinking of or about; यदि हरिस्मरणे सरसं मनः Gīt. 1.<BR>—3 Memory.<BR>—4 Tradition, traditional precept; इति भृगुस्मरणात् (opp. श्रुति).<BR>—5 Mental recitation of the name of a deity.<BR>—6 Remembering with regret, regretting.<BR>—7 Rhetorical recollection, regarded as a figure of speech; thus defined:− यथानुभवमर्थस्य<BR> दृष्टे तत्सदृशे स्मृतिः स्मरणम् K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणी
स्मरणम् + .{@-णी@} A rosary of beads (for counting).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मरणानुग्रहः, स्मरणापत्यतर्पकः, स्मरणायौगपद्यम्, स्मरणपदवी<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणानुग्रहः|स्मरणानुग्रह
स्मरणम् + -अनुग्रहः<BR>—1 a kind remembrance.<BR>—2 the favour of remembrance; अद्य तूच्चैस्तरं ताभ्यां स्मरणानुग्रहात्तव Ku. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणापत्यतर्पकः|स्मरणापत्यतर्पक
स्मरणम् + -अपत्यतर्पकः a turtle, tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणायौगपद्यम्
स्मरणम् + -अयौगपद्यम् the non-simultaneousness of recollections.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणपदवी
स्मरणम् + -पदवी death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणीय
स्मरणीय, स्मर्तव्य, स्मर्य <i>a.</i> To be remembered, memorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्तव्य|स्मर्त्तव्य
स्मरणीय, स्मर्तव्य, स्मर्य <i>a.</i> To be remembered, memorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्य
स्मरणीय, स्मर्तव्य, स्मर्य <i>a.</i> To be remembered, memorable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मर्तृ
स्मर्तृ A teacher, preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार
स्मार <i>a.</i> Relating to Smara or the god of love; रूक्षस्मारेक्षुचापच्युतशरनिकरक्षीणलक्ष्मीकटाक्ष … …<BR> Viṣṇupāda. S. 43; स्मारं पुष्पमयं चापं बाणाः पुष्पमया<BR> अपि । तथाप्यनङ्गस्त्रैलोक्यं करोति वशमात्मनः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारम्
स्मार + .{@-रम्@} Recollection, memory; स सभाद्वारमागम्य विदुरः स्मारमोहितः Mb. 3. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारक
स्मारक <i>a.</i> (-रिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> Reminding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारकम्
स्मारक + .{@-कम्@} A memorial (a modern use).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारणम्
स्मारणम्<BR>—1 Calling to mind, reminding, causing to remember.<BR>—2 Calculating, checking; रमणीयेषु देशेषु घोषाः संप्रति कौरव ।<BR> स्मारणे समयः प्राप्तो वत्सानामपि चाङ्कनम् ॥ Mb. 3. 239. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त <i>a.</i> [स्मृतौ विहितः, स्मृतिं वेत्त्यधीते वा अण्]<BR>—1 Relating to memory, remembered, memorial.<BR>—2 Being within memory; स्मार्तमस्ति पुराणं मे यथैवाधिगतं तथा Mb. 3. 179. 20.<BR>—3 Based on or recorded in a Smṛti, prescribed in a code of laws; कर्म<BR> स्मार्तविवाहाग्नौ कुर्वीत प्रत्यहं गृही Y. 1. 97; Ms. 1. 108.<BR>—4 Legal.<BR>—5 Following or professing the law-books.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्तः|स्मार्त|स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त + .{@-र्तः@}<BR>—1 A Brāhmaṇa well-versed in traditional law.<BR>—2 One who follows the traditional law; धर्मोऽयं गृहमेधिनां निगदितः<BR> स्मार्तैर्लघुः स्वर्गदः Pt. 1. 253.<BR>—3 N. of a sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्तम्
स्मार्त + .{@-तम्@} An act or rite enjoined by the Smṛti, a legal act.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मार्तकालः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्तकालः|स्मार्तकाल|स्मार्त्तकाल
स्मार्त + -कालः<BR>—1 the period to which memory may extend.<BR>—2 a century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्तिक
स्मार्तिक <i>a.</i> Traditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मि
स्मि €1 Ā. (स्मयते, स्मित)<BR>—1 To smile, laugh (gently); काकुत्स्थ ईषत्स्मयमान आस्त Bk. 2. 11, 15. 8;<BR> स्मयमानं वदनाम्बुजं स्मरामि Bv. 2. 27.<BR>—2 To bloom, expand; Pt. 1. 136. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्माययति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause a smile by, cause to smile.<BR>—2 To laugh at, deride.<BR>—3 To astonish (स्माययते in this sense). ━<i>Desid.</i> (सिस्मयिषते)<BR> To wish to smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयः|स्मय
स्मयः [स्मि-अच्]<BR>—1 Astonishment, wonder, surprise.<BR>—2 Arrogance, pride, haughtiness, conceit; तस्मै स्मयावेशविवर्जिताय<BR> R. 5. 19; प्रभवः स्मयदूषिताः Bh. 3. 2, 69; Mu. 2. 22; विधृतायोधनस्मयां<BR> (सेनाम्) Śiva B. 25. 29.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मयदानम्, स्मयनुत्तिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयदानम्
स्मयः + -दानम् an ostentatious donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयनुत्तिः|स्मयनुत्ति
स्मयः + -नुत्तिः the pulling down of pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयनम्
स्मयनम् A smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयमान
स्मयमान <i>a.</i> One who wonders; तमगस्त्यं मुहुर्दृष्ट्वा स्मयमानोऽभ्यभाषत Rām. 7. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मायः|स्माय
स्मायः A gentle smile; स्मायावलोकलवदर्शितभावहारि … Bhāg. 10. 61. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मित|स्मितं
स्मित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Smiled, smiling.<BR>—2 Expanded, blown, blossomed; एकेन स्मितपाटलाधररुचो जल्पन्त्यनल्पाक्षरम् Pt. 1. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितम्
स्मित + .{@-तम्@} A smile, gentle laugh; सस्मितं ‘with a smile’; सविलक्षस्मितम् &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मितदृश्, स्मितपूर्वम्, स्मितमुख, स्मितवाच्, स्मितशालिन्, स्मितशोभिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितदृश्
स्मित + -दृश् <i>a.</i> having a smiling look. ━(<i>f.</i>) a handsome woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितपूर्वम्
स्मित + -पूर्वम् <i>ind.</i> smilingly, with a smile; सप्तर्षिभिस्तान् स्मितपूर्वमाह Ku. 7. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितमुख
स्मित + -मुख <i>a.</i> having a smiling face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितवाच्
स्मित + -वाच् <i>a.</i> speaking with a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितशालिन्
स्मित + -शालिन् <i>a.</i> smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितशोभिन्
स्मित + -शोभिन् <i>a.</i> smiling beautifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितिः|स्मिति
स्मितिः <i>f.</i> A smile, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिट्
स्मिट् €10 U. (स्मेटयति-ते)<BR>—1 To slight, scorn, despise.<BR>—2 To love.<BR>—3 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1732-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मील्
स्मील् €1 P. (स्मीलति) To wink, blink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
स्मृ I. €5 P. (स्मृणोति)<BR>—1 To please, gratify.<BR>—2 To protect, defend.<BR>—3 To live. ━II. €1 P. (Ātm. also in epic poetry) (स्मरति, स्मृत;<BR> <i>Pass.</i> स्मर्यते)<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) To remember, bear or keep in mind, recollect, call to mind, be<BR> aware of; स्मरसि सुरसनीरां तत्र गोदावरीं वा स्मरसि च तदुपान्तेष्वावयोर्वर्तनानि U. 1. 26.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) To call to mind, call upon mentally, think of; स्मरात्मनोऽभीष्टदेवताम्<BR> Pt. 1; R. 15. 45.<BR>—2 To recite mentally or call upon the name of a deity &c.; यः स्मरेत्<BR> पुण्डरीकाक्षं सबाह्याभ्यन्तरः शुचिः.<BR>—3 To lay down or record in a Smṛti; तथा च स्मरन्ति.<BR>—4 To declare, regard, consider; निरतिशयं गरिमाणं तेन जनन्याः<BR> स्मरन्ति विद्वांसः Pt. 1. 30.<BR>—5 To remember with regret, yearn after, long or desire for (oft. with<BR> gen.); स्मर्तुं दिशन्ति न दिवः सुरसुन्दरीभ्यः Ki. 5. 28; कच्चिद्भर्तुः<BR> स्मरसि रसिके त्वं हि तस्य प्रियेति Me. 87; Mu. 5. 14; भवत्याः स्मरतात्यर्थमर्पितः<BR> (अङ्गुलीयकः) सादरं मम Bk. 8. 118.<BR>—6 To teach. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्मारयति-ते, but स्मरयति-ते in<BR> the last sense)<BR>—1 To cause to remember, remind, put in mind of, call to mind; अनेन<BR> मत्प्रियाभियोगेन स्मारयसि मे पूर्वशिष्यां सौदामिनीम् Māl. 1; sometimes<BR> with two acc.; अपि चन्द्रगुप्तदोषा अतिक्रान्तपार्थिवगुणान् स्मारयन्ति<BR> प्रकृतीः Mu. 1; य एव दुःस्मरः कालस्तमेव स्मारिता वयम् U. 6. 34.<BR>—2 To give information.<BR>—3 To cause to remember with regret, cause to long or desire for; वरतनोः<BR> स्मरयत्यनिलोऽन्यदा Śi. 6. 56, 8. 64. ━<i>Desid.</i> (सुस्मूर्षते)<BR> To wish to recollect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत|स्मृतः
स्मृत <i>p. p.</i> [स्मृ-क्त]<BR>—1 Remembered, recollected, called to mind.<BR>—2 Regarded, laid down, recorded, mentioned; प्रसूतिभाजः सर्गस्य तावेव<BR> पितरौ स्मृतौ Ku. 2. 7.<BR>—3 Appointed, designed; तस्य त्वं रणशिरसि स्मृतो निहन्ता Ś. 6. 29.<BR>—4 Enjoined by a Smṛti or traditional law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतम्
स्मृत + .{@-तम्@} Remembrance, recollection; स्मृतं च तद्विदां राजन् येन<BR> चात्मा प्रसीदति Bhāg. 7. 11. 7.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मृतमात्र<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतमात्र
स्मृत + -मात्र <i>a.</i> only remembered or thought of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिः|स्मृति
स्मृतिः <i>f.</i> [स्मृ-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Remembrance; recollection, memory; अश्वत्थामा करधृतधनुः किं न<BR> यातः स्मृतिं ते Ve. 3. 21; संस्कारमात्रजन्यं ज्ञानं स्मृतिः T. S.;<BR> स्मृत्युपस्थितौ इमौ द्वौ श्लोकौ U. 6, 4. 2.<BR>—2 Thinking of, calling to mind.<BR>—3 What was delivered by human authors, law, traditional law, the body<BR> of traditional or memorial law (civil or religious) (opp. श्रुति).<BR>—4 A code of laws, law-book.<BR>—5 A text of Smṛti, canon, rule of law; इति स्मृतेः.<BR>—6 Desire, wish.<BR>—7 Discrimination, discretion; स्मृतौ हतायां भृतमानदुर्दृशः Bhāg. 4. 3. 17.<BR>—8 Understanding.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मृत्यन्तरम्, स्मृत्यपेत, स्मृत्युक्त, स्मृतिजातः, स्मृतितन्त्रम्, स्मृतिपत्रकम्, स्मृतिपथः, स्मृतिविषयः, स्मृतिपाठकः, स्मृतिप्रत्यवमर्शः, स्मृतिप्रबन्धः, स्मृतिभ्रंशः, स्मृतिरोधः, स्मृतिविनयः, स्मृतिविभ्रमः, स्मृतिविरुद्ध, स्मृतिविरोधः, स्मृतिविषयः, स्मृतिशास्त्रम्, स्मृतिशेष, स्मृतिशैथिल्यम्, स्मृतिसंमत, स्मृतिसाध्य, स्मृतिहीन, स्मृतिहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्यन्तरम्
स्मृतिः + -अन्तरम् another law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्यपेत|स्मृत्यपेतः
स्मृतिः + -अपेत <i>a.</i><BR>—1 forgotten.<BR>—2 inconsistent with Smṛti.<BR>—3 (hence) illegal, unjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत्युक्त
स्मृतिः + -उक्त <i>a.</i> prescribed or enjoined in the codes of law, canonical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिजातः|स्मृतिजात
स्मृतिः + -जातः the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतितन्त्रम्
स्मृतिः + -तन्त्रम् a law-book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिपत्रकम्
स्मृतिः + -पत्रकम् a register-book; राजाद्यङ्कितलेखस्य धारयेत् स्मृतिपत्रकम्<BR> Śukra. 2. 287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिपथः|स्मृतिपथ
स्मृतिः + -पथः, -विषयः the object of memory; स्मृतिपथं, स्मृतिविषयं<BR> गम् to be dead; सर्वं यस्य वशादगात् स्मृतिपथं कालाय तस्मै नमः Bh. 3. 37;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">Page1733-2</a>]<BR> समं यैः संवृद्धाः स्मृतिविषयतां तेऽपि गमिताः 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविषयः|स्मृतिविषय
स्मृतिः + -पथः, -विषयः the object of memory; स्मृतिपथं, स्मृतिविषयं<BR> गम् to be dead; सर्वं यस्य वशादगात् स्मृतिपथं कालाय तस्मै नमः Bh. 3. 37;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">Page1733-2</a>]<BR> समं यैः संवृद्धाः स्मृतिविषयतां तेऽपि गमिताः 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिपाठकः|स्मृतिपाठक
स्मृतिः + -पाठकः a lawyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिप्रत्यवमर्शः|स्मृतिप्रत्यवमर्श
स्मृतिः + -प्रत्यवमर्शः retentiveness of memory, accuracy of recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिप्रबन्धः|स्मृतिप्रबन्ध|स्मृतिप्रबंध
स्मृतिः + -प्रबन्धः a legal work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिभ्रंशः|स्मृतिभ्रंश
स्मृतिः + -भ्रंशः loss or failure of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिरोधः|स्मृतिरोध
स्मृतिः + -रोधः temporary interruption of memory; loss or failure of memory;<BR> शापादसि प्रतिहता स्मृतिरोधरूक्षे भर्तर्यपेततमसि प्रभुता तवैव । Ś. 7. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविनयः|स्मृतिविनय
स्मृतिः + -विनयः a reprimand given to a person by reminding him of his duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविभ्रमः|स्मृतिविभ्रम
स्मृतिः + -विभ्रमः confusion of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरुद्ध|स्मृतिविरुद्धः
स्मृतिः + -विरुद्ध <i>a.</i> illegal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविरोधः|स्मृतिविरोध
स्मृतिः + -विरोधः<BR>—1 opposition to law, illegality.<BR>—2 disagreement between two or more Smṛtis or legal texts; स्मृतिविरोधं<BR> परिहरति Ś. B.; cf. स्मृत्योर्विरोधे न्यायस्तु बलवान् व्यवहारतः Y. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिविषयः|स्मृतिविषय
स्मृतिः + -विषयः the range of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशास्त्रम्
स्मृतिः + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 a law-book, code, digest.<BR>—2 legal science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशेष
स्मृतिः + -शेष <i>a.</i> deceased, dead (as a person).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिशैथिल्यम्
स्मृतिः + -शैथिल्यम् loss of memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिसंमत|स्मृतिसम्मत
स्मृतिः + -संमत <i>a.</i> approved by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिसाध्य
स्मृतिः + -साध्य <i>a.</i> capable of being proved by law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिहीन
स्मृतिः + -हीन forgetful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिहेतुः|स्मृतिहेतु
स्मृतिः + -हेतुः a cause of recollection, impression on the mind, association of ideas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिमत्|स्मृतिमन्त्
स्मृतिमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having full consciousness.<BR>—2 Remembering a former life.<BR>—3 Prudent, discreet.<BR>—4 Versed in law.<BR>—5 Anything which causes recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर <i>a.</i> [स्मि-रन्]<BR>—1 Smiling; विलोक्य वृद्धोक्षमधिष्ठितं त्वया महाजनः स्मेरमुखो भविष्यति<BR> Ku. 5. 70; Bv. 2. 4, 3. 2; Māl. 10. 6.<BR>—2 Blown, expanded, dilated, blooming; अधिकविकसदन्तर्विस्मयस्मेरतारैः Māl. 1. 28.<BR>—3 Proud.<BR>—4 Evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरः|स्मेर
स्मेर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 A smile.<BR>—2 Manifestation, appearance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्मेरविष्किरः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेरविष्किरः|स्मेरविष्किर
स्मेर + -विष्किरः a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्द्|स्यंद्
स्यन्द् €1 Ā. (स्यन्दते, सस्यन्दे, अस्यदत्-अस्यन्त्त-अस्यन्दिष्ट, स्यन्त्स्यति-ते,<BR> स्यन्दिष्यते, स्यन्दितुं-स्यन्त्तुम्, स्यन्न; <i>desid.</i> सिस्यन्दिषते,<BR> सिस्यन्त्सति-ते; the स् of स्यन्द् is changed to ष् after a preposition<BR> ending in इ or उ)<BR>—1 To ooze, trickle, drop, drip, distil, flow; अयि दलदरविन्द स्यन्दमानं<BR> मरन्दं तव किमपि लिहन्तो मञ्जु गुञ्जन्तु भृङ्गाः Bv. 1. 5; Mu. 3. 7.<BR>—2 To shed, pour forth; स्यन्देते हि दिवा रुक्मं रात्रौ च द्विजसत्तम<BR> Mb. 14. 57. 25.<BR>—3 To run, flee.<BR>—4 Appear, occur; स्यन्दन्ति चाप्यनिष्टानि गात्रं सीदति चाप्युत Mb. 7. 72. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यदः|स्यद
स्यदः<BR>—1 Speed, rapid motion, rush, velocity; प्रतन्व्यः कोमला विन्ध्ये सहितारः<BR> स्यदं न ते Bk. 22. 5.<BR>—2 Driving, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दः|स्यन्द|स्यंद|स्यंदः
स्यन्दः [स्यन्द्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Flowing, trickling.<BR>—2 Going rapidly, moving.<BR>—3 A car, chariot.<BR>—4 Fluxion; Suśr.<BR>—5 Trickling perspiration; यत्र क्वचन स्यन्देनाभिपतति Bhāg. 5. 21. 9.<BR>—6 A particular eye-disease.<BR>—7 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दन|स्यंदन|स्यन्दनं|स्यन्दनः
स्यन्दन <i>a.</i> (-ना or -नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्यन्द्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>—1 Going quickly, fleet; flowing.<BR>—2 Quick, swift of foot, fleet; स्यन्दना नो चतुरगाः Ki. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनः|स्यन्दन|स्यंदन|स्यन्दनं
स्यन्दन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A war-chariot, a car or chariot in general; धर्मारण्यं प्रविशति<BR> गजः स्यन्दनालोक भीतः Ś. 1. 33; N. 15. 92; R. 1. 36.<BR>—2 Air, wind.<BR>—3 A kind of tree (तिनिश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनम्
स्यन्दन + .{@-नम्@}<BR>—1 Flowing, trickling, oozing.<BR>—2 Rushing, going or flowing quickly.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">Page1734-1</a>]<BR>—3 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनी|स्यंदनी
स्यन्दन + .{@-नी@}<BR>—1 Saliva.<BR>—2 The urinary passage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्यन्दनारोहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1733-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनारोहः|स्यन्दनारोह|स्यंदनारोह
स्यन्दन + -आरोहः a warrior who fights while seated in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दनिका|स्यंदनिका
स्यन्दनिका<BR>—1 A drop of saliva.<BR>—2 A brook, rivulet; यदन्तरं स्यन्दनिकासमुद्रयोः Rām. 3. 47. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दिन्|स्यंदिन्
स्यन्दिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Oozing, flowing, trickling; बाहुरैन्दवमयूखचुम्बितस्यन्दिचन्द्रमणिहारविभ्रमः<BR> Māl. 8. 3; U. 1. 35.<BR>—2 Rushing.<BR>—3 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्दिनी
स्यन्दिनी<BR>—1 Saliva.<BR>—2 A cow bearing two calves at the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्न|स्यन्नः
स्यन्न <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Oozed, trickled, dropped.<BR>—2 Dropping, trickling (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यम्
स्यम् €1 P., €10 U. (स्यमति, स्यमयति-ते)<BR>—1 To sound, to cry aloud, shout; वव्रश्चुराजुघूर्णुश्च स्येमुश्चुकूर्दिरे<BR> तथा Bk. 14. 77.<BR>—2 To go.<BR>—3 To consider, reflect (Ātm. only in this sense).<BR>—4 To guess, to reflect; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमन्तकः|स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमंतकः
स्यमन्तकः A kind of valuable gem (said to yield daily eight loads<BR> of gold and to preserve from all kinds of dangers and portents); Bhāg. 10. 56.<BR> (For some account, see the word सत्राजित्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमिकः|स्यमिक
स्यमि(मी)कः [स्यम्-ईकक्]<BR>—1 A cloud.<BR>—2 An anthill.<BR>—3 A kind of tree.<BR>—4 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमीकः|स्यमीक
स्यमि(मी)कः [स्यम्-ईकक्]<BR>—1 A cloud.<BR>—2 An anthill.<BR>—3 A kind of tree.<BR>—4 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमिका
स्यमिका Indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यात्
स्यात् <i>ind.</i> (Strictly 3rd pers. sing. of the Potential of अस्<BR> ‘to be’) It may be, perhaps, per chance.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्याद्वादः, स्याद्वादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याद्वादः|स्याद्वाद
स्यात् + -वादः an assertion of probability (in phil.), a form of scepticism of the Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्याद्वादिन्
स्यात् + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यालः|स्याल
स्यालः See श्याल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत|स्यूतः
स्यूत <i>p. p.</i> [सिव्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>—1 Sewn with a needle, stitched, woven (fig. also); चिन्तासंततितन्तुजालनिबिडस्यूतेव<BR> लग्ना प्रिया Māl. 5. 10.<BR>—2 Pierced.<BR>—3 Woven together, joined; नीलोपलस्यूतविचित्रधातुमसौ गिरिं रैवतकं<BR> ददर्श Śi. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूतः|स्यूत
स्यूत + .{@-तः@} A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूतिः|स्यूति
स्यूतिः <i>f.</i> [सिव्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Sewing, stitching.<BR>—2 Needle-work.<BR>—3 A sack.<BR>—4 Lineage, family.<BR>—5 Offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूनः|स्यून
स्यूनः [सिव् नक्]<BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 A bag, sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूना
स्यूनः + .{@-ना@}<BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 A girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योतः|स्योत
स्योतः A sack, bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमः|स्यूम|स्यूमं
स्यूमः A ray of light (also <i>n.</i>).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमम्
स्यूमः + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Water.<BR>—2 Happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योन|स्योनः
स्योन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>—2 Auspicious, propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योनः|स्योन
स्योन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A ray of light.<BR>—2 The sun. —3 A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योनम्
स्योन + .{@-नम्@} Happiness, pleasure.<BR>—2 A comfortable seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योनाकः|स्योनाक
स्योनाकः Bignonia Indica (Mar. दिंडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
स्रंस् €1 Ā. (स्रंसते, स्रस्त)<BR>—1 To fall, fall or drop down, slip off or down; नास्रसत् करिणां ग्रैवं<BR> त्रिपदीच्छेदिनामपि R. 4. 48; गाण्डीवं स्रंसते हस्तात् Bg. 1. 30;<BR> Bk. 14. 72, 15. 61.<BR>—2 To sink, drop, fall asunder; हा हा देवि स्फुटति हृदयं स्रंसते<BR> देहबन्धः U. 3. 38; Māl. 9. 20 v. l.<BR>—3 To hang down.<BR>—4 To go.<BR>—5 To be pleased.<BR>—6 To perish, cease. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्रंपयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to fall or slip down, move, disturb; वातोऽपि नास्रंसयदंशुकानि R. 6. 75.<BR>—2 To relax, loosen, slacken; स्खलयति वचनं ते स्रंसयत्यङ्गमङ्गम् Māl. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसः|स्रंस
स्रंसः Falling, slipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसनम्
स्रंसनम् [स्रंस्-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Falling.<BR>—2 Causing to fall, or bringing down.<BR>—3 Premature abortion.<BR>—4 A laxative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिन्
स्रंसिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्रंस्-णिनि]<BR>—1 Falling or slipping down, hanging down, being loosened, giving way;<BR> बन्धे स्रंसिनि चैकहस्तयमिताः पर्याकुला मूर्धजाः Ś. 1. 29.<BR>—2 Depending, pendulous, hanging loosely.<BR>—3 Miscarrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्त|स्रस्तं
स्रस्त <i>p. p.</i> [स्रंस्-क्त]<BR>—1 Fallen or dropped down, slipped off, fallen off; स्रस्तं शरं चापमपि<BR> स्वहस्तात् Ku. 3. 51; कनकवलयं स्रस्तं स्रस्तं मया प्रतिसार्यते<BR> Ś. 3. 12; Ki. 5. 33; Me. 65.<BR>—2 Drooping, hanging loosely down; विषादस्रस्तसर्वाङ्गी Mk. 4. 8;<BR> स्रस्तांसावतिमात्रलोहिततलौ बाहू घटोत्क्षेपणात् Ś. 1. 29.<BR>—3 Loosed.<BR>—4 Let go, relaxed.<BR>—5 Pendulous, hanging down.<BR>—6 Separated.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रस्ताङ्ग, स्रस्तगात्र, स्रस्तापान, स्रस्तहस्त<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्ताङ्ग|स्रस्तांग
स्रस्त + -अङ्ग, -गात्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the limbs relaxed.<BR>—2 swooning, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तगात्र
स्रस्त + -अङ्ग, -गात्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 having the limbs relaxed.<BR>—2 swooning, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तापान
स्रस्त + -अपान <i>a.</i> having prolapsus ani.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तहस्त
स्रस्त + -हस्त <i>a.</i> letting go the hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तिः|स्रस्ति
स्रस्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Falling, slipping.<BR>—2 A slip.<BR>—3 Loosening, slackening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंह्
स्रंह् €1 Ā. (स्रंहते) To confide or trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रक्तिः|स्रक्ति
स्रक्तिः <i>f.</i> A corner, edge; दिशो ह्यस्य स्रक्तयो द्यौरस्योत्तरं<BR> बिलम् Ch. Up. 3. 15. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्
स्रज् <i>f.</i> [सृज्यते सृज्-क्विन् नि˚]<BR>—1 A chaplet, wreath or garland of flowers (especially one worn on the<BR> head); स्रजमपि शिरस्यन्धः क्षिप्तां धुनोत्यहिशङ्कया Ś. 7. 24.<BR>—2 A garland (in general).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रग्दामन्, स्रग्धर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्दामन्
स्रज् + -दामन् (स्रग्दामन्) <i>n.</i> the tie or fillet of a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्धर
स्रज् + -धर <i>a.</i> wearing a garland; Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्धरा
स्रज् + -धर + .({@-रा@}) N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्वत्|स्रग्वन्त्
स्रग्वत्, स्रग्विन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> (compar. स्रजीयस्, superl. स्रजिष्ठ) Wearing<BR> a garland or chaplet; आमुक्ताभरणः स्रग्वी हंसचिह्नदुकूलवान् R. 17. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्विन्
स्रग्वत्, स्रग्विन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> (compar. स्रजीयस्, superl. स्रजिष्ठ) Wearing<BR> a garland or chaplet; आमुक्ताभरणः स्रग्वी हंसचिह्नदुकूलवान् R. 17. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजयति
स्रजयति Den. P. To furnish with a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्वन्
स्रज्वन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 A garland maker.<BR>—2 A cloth; Uṇ. 4. 106.<BR>—3 A rope.<BR>—4 N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्वा
स्रज्वा A rope, string, cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रद्धू
स्रद्धू <i>f.</i> Breaking wind downwards (अपानवायु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1734-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रम्भ्|स्रंभ्
स्रम्भ् €1 Ā. (स्रम्भते, स्रब्ध) To confide; see श्रम्भ.<BR>━<i>With</i> {@वि@}<BR>—1 to be confident.<BR>—2 to rest secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवः|स्रव
स्रवः [स्रु-अप्]<BR>—1 Trickling, oozing, flowing.<BR>—2 A drop flow, stream; विपुलौ स्नपयन्ती सा स्तनौ नेत्रजलस्रवैः Rām.<BR>—3 A fountain, spring.<BR>—4 Urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवणम्
स्रवणम् [स्रु-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Flowing, trickling, oozing.<BR>—2 Sweat.<BR>—3 Urine.<BR>—4 Premature abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्
स्रवत् <i>a.</i> (स्रवन्ती <i>f.</i>)<BR> Flowing, oozing, trickling &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रवद्गर्भा, स्रवन्मध्यः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवद्गर्भा
स्रवत् + -गर्भा<BR>—1 a woman that miscarries.<BR>—2 a cow miscarrying by accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवन्मध्यः|स्रवन्मध्य
स्रवत् + -मध्यः a gem appearing to pour water from its centre; Kau. A. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवन्ती
स्रवन्ती<BR>—1 A stream, river; वापीष्विव स्रवन्तीषु R. 17. 64; Māl. 9. 24.<BR>—2 The region of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवद्रङ्गः|स्रवद्रङ्ग
स्रवद्रङ्गः A fair, market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रष्टृ
स्रष्टृ <i>m.</i> [सृज्-तृच्]<BR>—1 A maker.<BR>—2 A creator, an epithet of Brahman; या सृष्टिः स्रष्टुराद्या Ś. 1. 1;<BR> तत्स्रष्टुरेकान्तरम् 7. 27.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तरः|स्रस्तर
स्रस्तरः A couch or sofa (for reclining), bed; शिलातले स्रस्तरमास्तीर्य<BR> निषसाद K.; Ms. 2. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राक्
स्राक् <i>ind.</i> Quickly, speedily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राम
स्राम <i>a.</i> One whose nose or eyes are always oozing; स्रामे स्रामः<BR> Ch. Up. 8. 9. 1; (according to MW. ‘lame’, ‘sick’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राम्यम्
स्राम्यम् Lameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावः|स्राव
स्रावः Flow, flowing, oozing, dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावक|स्रावकं
स्रावक <i>a.</i> (-विका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्रु-णिच्-ण्वुल्] Causing to flow, pouring out, exuding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावकम्
स्रावक + .{@-कम्@} Black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावित
स्रावित <i>a.</i> Liquefied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिध्
स्रिध् €1 U. (स्रेधति-ते) To injure, harm, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिभ्
स्रिभ् €1 P. (स्रेभति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिम्भ्|स्रिंभ्
स्रिम्भ् €1 P. (स्रिम्भति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिव्
स्रिव् €4 P. (स्रीव्यति)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु €1 P. (स्रवति, स्रुत)<BR>—1 To flow, stream, trickle, ooze, drop, exude; न हि निम्वात् स्रवेत् क्षौद्रम् Rām.<BR>—2 To pour out, shed, let flow; अलोठिष्ट च भूपृष्ठे शोणितं चाप्यसुस्रुवत्<BR> Bk. 15. 56, 17. 18.<BR>—3 To go, move.<BR>—4 To trickle or slip away, waste away, perish, come to nothing; स्रवते<BR> ब्रह्म तस्यापि भिन्नभाण्डात् पयो यथा Bhāg.; Bk. 6. 18; Ms. 2. 74.<BR>—5 To spread about, get abroad, transpire (as a secret).<BR>—6 To slip, issue out before the right time.<BR>—7 To accrue (as interest). ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्रावयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to flow, pour out, shed, spill (blood &c.); न गात्रात् स्रावयेदसृक् Ms. 4. 169.<BR>—2 To stir up, arouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत्
स्रुत् <i>a.</i> (Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>—1 Flowing, dropping, pouring forth; स्वरेण तस्याममृतस्रुतेव Ku. 1. 45;<BR> Śi. 9. 68.<BR>—2 Dissolved.<BR>—3 Become empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत|स्रुतं
स्रुत <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Flowed, trickled, dripping &c.<BR>—2 Gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुतिः|स्रुति
स्रुतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Flowing, oozing, distilling, trickling out; कीटक्षतिस्रुतिभिरस्रमिवोद्वमन्तः<BR> Mu. 6. 13; पदं तुषारस्रुतिधौतरक्तम् Ku. 1. 6; R. 16. 44; Ki. 5. 44, 16. 2;<BR> क्षीरस्रुतिसुरभयः (वाताः) Me. 109 ‘exudation or flow of the sap’.<BR>—2 Exudation, resin.<BR>—3 A stream.<BR>—4 Ved. A path, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्नः|स्रुघ्न
स्रुघ्नः N. of a district; पन्थाः स्रुध्नमुपतिष्ठते Sk.; (it was<BR> situated at some distance −at least one dayʼs journey− from Pātaliputra<BR> q. v.; cf. न हि देवदत्तः स्रुघ्ने संनिधीयमानस्तदहरेव पाटलिपुत्रे<BR> संनिधीयते युगपदनेकत्र वृत्तावनेकत्वप्रसंगात्) Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्नी
स्रुघ्नी Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रौघ्न|स्रौघ्नः
स्रौघ्न <i>a.</i> (-ध्नी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Belonging to, or coming from, Srughna.<BR>—2 Residing in Srughna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रौघ्नः|स्रौघ्न
स्रौघ्न + .{@-घ्नः@} An inhabitant of Srughna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रौघ्नम्
स्रौघ्न + .{@-घ्नम्@} The gate leading to Srughna; cf. P. IV. 3. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच् <i>f.</i> A sort of wooden ladle, used for pouring clarified butter<BR> on sacrificial fire; (usually made of trees like Palāśa or Khadira);<BR> ऋत्विजां च्युतविकङ्कतस्रुचाम् R. 11. 25; Ms. 5. 117; Y. 1. 183.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रुग्जिह्वः, स्रुक्प्रणालिका<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुग्जिह्वः|स्रुग्जिह्व
स्रुच् + -जिह्वः N. of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुक्प्रणालिका
स्रुच् + -प्रणालिका the spout of a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवः|स्रुव
स्रुवः, -वा<BR>—1 A sacrificial ladle; चरूणां स्रुक्स्रुवाणां च शुद्धिरुष्णेन वारिणा Ms. 5. 117.<BR>—2 A Soma ladle.<BR>—3 A spring, cascade.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रुवकर्ण, स्रुवतरुः, स्रुवप्रग्रहण, स्रुवहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवा
स्रुवः, -वा<BR>—1 A sacrificial ladle; चरूणां स्रुक्स्रुवाणां च शुद्धिरुष्णेन वारिणा Ms. 5. 117.<BR>—2 A Soma ladle.<BR>—3 A spring, cascade.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रुवकर्ण, स्रुवतरुः, स्रुवप्रग्रहण, स्रुवहस्तः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवकर्ण
स्रुवः + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> having ladle-mark on the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवतरुः|स्रुवतरु
स्रुवः + -तरुः Flacourtia Sapida (Mar. बेहकळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवप्रग्रहण
स्रुवः + -प्रग्रहण <i>a.</i> taking all to oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवहस्तः|स्रुवहस्त
स्रुवः + -हस्तः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A sacrificial ladle; स्रुवमुद्यम्य सक्रोधस्त्रिशङ्कुमिदमब्रवीत्<BR> Rām. 1. 60. 12.<BR>—2 A spring or fountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक्
स्रेक् €1 Ā. (स्रेकते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै €1 P. (स्रायति)<BR>—1 To boil.<BR>—2 To sweat; see श्रै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतम्
स्रोतम् A stream; see स्रोतस्.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रोतोद्भवम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोद्भवम्
स्रोतम् + -उद्भवम् antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस् <i>n.</i> [स्रु-तसि]<BR>—1<BR>——(<i>a</i>) A stream, current, flow or course of water; पुरा यत्र स्रोतः<BR> पुलिनमधुना तत्र सरिताम् U. 2. 27; Ms. 3. 163.<BR>——(<i>b</i>) A torrent, rapid stream; नदत्याकाशगङ्गायाः स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे<BR> R. 1. 78; स्रोतसेवोह्यमानस्य प्रतीपतरणं हि तत् V. 2. 5.<BR>—2 A stream, river (in general); स्रोतसामस्मि जाह्नवी Bg. 10. 31.<BR>—3 A wave.<BR>—4 Water.<BR>—5 The canal of nutriment in the body.<BR>—6 An organ of sense; निगृह्य सर्वस्रोतांसि Rām.; तद्वन्न रिक्तमतयो<BR> यतयोऽपि रुद्धस्रोतोगणास्तमरणं भज वासुदेवम् Bhāg. 4. 22. 39.<BR>—7 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>—8 Rush, onset; करालस्रोतो जगदाच्छिद्य धावत् Bhāg. 3. 21. 18.<BR>—9 The spout of a jar.<BR>—10 An aperture in animal body (रन्ध्र); स्नोतोभ्यो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">Page1736-1</a>]<BR> बहु रक्तं तु तस्य सुस्राव पात्यतः Rām. 4. 11. 46; Mb. 1. 3. 152.<BR>—11 Going; ऊर्ध्वस्रोतस इत्येते देवा वैकारिकाः स्मृताः Mb. 14. 38. 13.<BR>—12 Lineage.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्रोतोञ्जनम्, स्रोतईशः, स्रोतोरन्ध्रम्, स्रोतोवह्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1735-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोञ्जनम्
स्रोतस् + -अञ्जनम् (स्रोतोञ्जनम्) antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतईशः|स्रोतईश
स्रोतस् + -ईशः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोरन्ध्रम्
स्रोतस् + -रन्ध्रम् an aperture of the proboscis or trunk of an elephant,<BR> a nostril; स्रोतोरन्ध्रध्वनितसुभगं दन्तिभिः पीयमानः Me. 44 (see<BR> Malli. thereon); (written श्रोतोरन्ध्र also, q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतोवह्
स्रोतस् + -वह् <i>f.</i>, {@-वहा@}<BR> a river; स्रोतोवहां पथि निकामजलामतीत्य जातः सखे<BR> प्रणयवान् मृगतृष्णिकायाम् Ś. 6. 15, 2. 17; कार्या सैकतलीनहंसमिथुना<BR> स्रोतोवहा मालिनी 6. 16; R. 6. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्यः|स्रोतस्य
स्रोतस्यः<BR>—1 N. of Śiva.<BR>—2 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्वती
स्रोतस्वती, स्रोतस्विनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्विनी
स्रोतस्वती, स्रोतस्विनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व <i>pron. a.</i><BR>—1 Oneʼs own, belonging to oneself, often serving as a reflexive pronoun;<BR> स्वनियोगमशून्यं कुरु Ś. 2; प्रजाः प्रजाः स्वा इव तन्त्रयित्वा 5. 5;<BR> oft. in comp. in this sense; स्वपुत्र, स्वकलत्र, स्वद्रव्य.<BR>—2 Innate, natural, inherent, peculiar, inborn; सूर्यापाये न खलु कमलं<BR> पुष्यति स्वामभिख्याम् Me. 82; Ś. 1. 19; स तस्य स्वो भावः प्रकृतिनियतत्वादकृतकः U. 6. 14.<BR>—3 Belonging to oneʼs own caste or tribe; शूद्रैव भार्या शूद्रस्य सा<BR> च स्वा च विशः स्मृते Ms. 3. 13, 5. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वः|स्व|स्वं
स्व + .{@-स्वः@}<BR>—1 Oneʼs own self.<BR>—2 A relative, kinsman; एनं स्वा अभिसंविशन्ति भर्ता स्वानां श्रेष्ठः<BR> पुर एता भवति Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 18; (दौर्गत्यं) येन स्वैरपि मन्यन्ते<BR> जीवन्तोऽपि मृता इव Pt. 2. 100; Ms. 2. 109.<BR>—3 The soul.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वा
स्व + .{@-स्वा@} A woman of oneʼs own caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वः|स्व|स्वं
स्व + .{@-स्वः, -स्वम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth, property; as in निःस्व q. v.<BR>—2 (In alg.) The plus or affirmative quantity; cf. धन; स्वशब्दोऽयमात्मीयधनज्ञातीनां<BR> प्रत्येकं वाचको न समुदायस्य ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 2.<BR>—3 The Ego.<BR>—4 Nature (स्वभावः); वृत्तिर्भूतानि भूतानां चराणामचराणि च । कृता<BR> स्वेन नृणां तत्र कामाच्चोदनयापि वा ॥ Bhāg. 12. 7. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वाक्षपादः, स्वाक्षरम्, स्वाधिकारः, स्वाधिपत्यम्, स्वाधिष्ठानम्, स्वाधीन, स्वाध्यायः, स्वाध्यायिन्, स्वानुभवः, स्वानुभूतिः, स्वानुभावः, स्वानुरूप, स्वान्तम्, स्वार्जित, स्वार्थ, स्वानन्दः, स्वायत्त, स्वारब्ध, स्वारम्भक, स्वाहत, स्वेच्छा, स्वोत्थ, स्वोदयः, स्वोपधिः, स्वकम्पनः, स्वकर्मन्, स्वकर्मस्थ, स्वकर्मिन्, स्वकामिन्, स्वकार्यम्, स्वकुलक्षयः, स्वकृतम्, स्वकृतंभुज्, स्वगतम्, स्वगृहः, स्वगोचर, स्वचर, स्वच्छन्द, स्वज, स्वजनः, स्वजातिः, स्वज्ञातिः, स्वता, स्वतन्त्र, स्वदृश्, स्वदेशः, स्वधर्मः, स्वनिघ्न, स्वपक्षः, स्वपणः, स्वपरमण्डलम्, स्वप्रकाश, स्वप्रतिष्ठ, स्वप्रधान, स्वप्रयोगात्, स्वबीजः, स्वभटः, स्वभावः, स्वभूः, स्वमनीषा, स्वमनीषिका, स्वमात्रेण, स्वयुतिः, स्वयूथ्यः, स्वयोनि, स्वरसः, स्वराज्, स्वराज्यम्, स्वराष्ट्रम्, स्वरुचिः, स्वरूप, स्वलक्षणम्, स्वलोकः, स्ववत्, स्ववश, स्ववहित, स्ववासिनी, स्वविग्रहः, स्वविषयः, स्ववृत्तम्, स्ववृत्ति, स्वसंविद्, स्वसंवृत, स्वसंवेदनम्, स्वसंस्था, स्वस्थ, स्वस्थानम्, स्वस्वरूपम्, स्वहन्तृ, स्वहरणम्, स्वहस्तः, स्वहस्तिका, स्वहित, स्वहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वम्
स्व + .{@-स्वः, -स्वम्@}<BR>—1 Wealth, property; as in निःस्व q. v.<BR>—2 (In alg.) The plus or affirmative quantity; cf. धन; स्वशब्दोऽयमात्मीयधनज्ञातीनां<BR> प्रत्येकं वाचको न समुदायस्य ŚB. on MS. 6. 7. 2.<BR>—3 The Ego.<BR>—4 Nature (स्वभावः); वृत्तिर्भूतानि भूतानां चराणामचराणि च । कृता<BR> स्वेन नृणां तत्र कामाच्चोदनयापि वा ॥ Bhāg. 12. 7. 13.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वाक्षपादः, स्वाक्षरम्, स्वाधिकारः, स्वाधिपत्यम्, स्वाधिष्ठानम्, स्वाधीन, स्वाध्यायः, स्वाध्यायिन्, स्वानुभवः, स्वानुभूतिः, स्वानुभावः, स्वानुरूप, स्वान्तम्, स्वार्जित, स्वार्थ, स्वानन्दः, स्वायत्त, स्वारब्ध, स्वारम्भक, स्वाहत, स्वेच्छा, स्वोत्थ, स्वोदयः, स्वोपधिः, स्वकम्पनः, स्वकर्मन्, स्वकर्मस्थ, स्वकर्मिन्, स्वकामिन्, स्वकार्यम्, स्वकुलक्षयः, स्वकृतम्, स्वकृतंभुज्, स्वगतम्, स्वगृहः, स्वगोचर, स्वचर, स्वच्छन्द, स्वज, स्वजनः, स्वजातिः, स्वज्ञातिः, स्वता, स्वतन्त्र, स्वदृश्, स्वदेशः, स्वधर्मः, स्वनिघ्न, स्वपक्षः, स्वपणः, स्वपरमण्डलम्, स्वप्रकाश, स्वप्रतिष्ठ, स्वप्रधान, स्वप्रयोगात्, स्वबीजः, स्वभटः, स्वभावः, स्वभूः, स्वमनीषा, स्वमनीषिका, स्वमात्रेण, स्वयुतिः, स्वयूथ्यः, स्वयोनि, स्वरसः, स्वराज्, स्वराज्यम्, स्वराष्ट्रम्, स्वरुचिः, स्वरूप, स्वलक्षणम्, स्वलोकः, स्ववत्, स्ववश, स्ववहित, स्ववासिनी, स्वविग्रहः, स्वविषयः, स्ववृत्तम्, स्ववृत्ति, स्वसंविद्, स्वसंवृत, स्वसंवेदनम्, स्वसंस्था, स्वस्थ, स्वस्थानम्, स्वस्वरूपम्, स्वहन्तृ, स्वहरणम्, स्वहस्तः, स्वहस्तिका, स्वहित, स्वहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाक्षपादः|स्वाक्षपाद
स्व + -अक्षपादः a follower of the Nyāya system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाक्षरम्
स्व + -अक्षरम् oneʼs own hand-writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिकारः|स्वाधिकार
स्व + -अधिकारः oneʼs own duty or sway; स्वाधिकारात् प्रमत्तः Me. 1;<BR> स्वाधिकारभूमौ Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिपत्यम्
स्व + -अधिपत्यम् oneʼs own supremacy, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधिष्ठानम्
स्व + -अधिष्ठानम् one of the six Cakras or mystical circles of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाधीन|स्वाधीनः
स्व + -अधीन <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dependent on oneself, self-dependent.<BR>—2 independent.<BR>—3 oneʼs own subject.<BR>—4 in oneʼs own power; स्वाधीना ववनीयतापि हि वरं बद्धो न सेवाञ्जलिः<BR> Mk. 3. 11. ˚कुशल <i>a.</i> having prosperity in oneʼs own power; स्वाधीनकुशलाः<BR> सिद्धिमन्तः Ś. 4. ˚पतिका, ˚भर्तृका a woman who has full control<BR> over her husband, one whose husband is subject to her; अथ सा निर्गताबाधा<BR> राधा स्वाधीनभर्तृका । निजगाद रतिक्लान्तं कान्तं मण्डनवाञ्छया Gīt. 12;<BR> see S. D. 112. <i>et seq.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायः|स्वाध्याय
स्व + -अध्यायः<BR>—1 self-recitation, muttering to oneself.<BR>—2 study of the Vedas, sacred study, perusal of sacred books; स्वाध्यायेनार्चयेदृषीन्<BR> Ms. 3. 81; Bg. 16. 1; T. Up. 1. 9. 1.<BR>—3 the Veda itself.<BR>—4 a day on which sacred study is enjoined to be resumed after suspension.<BR> ˚अर्थिन् <i>m.</i> a student who tries to secure his own livelihood during<BR> his course of holy study; Ms. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाध्यायिन्
स्व + -अध्यायिन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a student of the Vedas.<BR>—2 a tradesman.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">Page1736-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुभवः|स्वानुभव
स्व + -अनुभवः, -अनुभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 self-experience.<BR>—2 self-knowledge; स्वानुभूत्येकसाराय नमः शान्ताय तेजसे Bh. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुभूतिः|स्वानुभूति
स्व + -अनुभवः, -अनुभूतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 self-experience.<BR>—2 self-knowledge; स्वानुभूत्येकसाराय नमः शान्ताय तेजसे Bh. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुभावः|स्वानुभाव
स्व + -अनुभावः love for property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानुरूप
स्व + -अनुरूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 natural, inborn.<BR>—2 worthy of oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वान्तम्
स्व + -अन्तम्<BR>—1 the mind; मम स्वान्तध्वान्तं तिरयतु नवीनो जलधरः Bv. 4. 5; Mv. 7. 17.<BR>—2 a cavern.<BR>—3 oneʼs own death, end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्जित
स्व + -अर्जित <i>a.</i> self-acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थ|स्वार्थः
स्व + -अर्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-interested.<BR>—2 having its own or true meaning.<BR>—3 having oneʼs own object or aim.<BR>—4 pleonastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वार्थः|स्वार्थ
स्व + -अर्थ + .({@-र्थः@})<BR>—1 oneʼs own interest, self-interest; सर्वः स्वार्थं समीहते Śi. 2. 65;<BR> स्वार्थात्सतां गुरुतरा प्रणयिक्रियैव V. 4. 15.<BR>—2 own or inherent meaning; स्वार्थे णिच्, स्वार्थे कप्रत्ययः &c.; परार्थव्यासङ्गादुपजहदथ<BR> स्वार्थपरताम् Bv. 1. 79 (where both senses are intended).<BR>—3 = पुरुषार्थः q. v.; Bhāg. 12. 2. 6. ˚अनुमानम् inference for<BR> oneself, a kind of inductive reasoning, one of the two main kinds of अनुमान,<BR> the other being परार्थानुमान. ˚पण्डित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 clever in oneʼs own affairs.<BR>—2 expert in attending to oneʼs own interests. ˚पर, ˚परायण <i>a.</i><BR> intent on securing oneʼs own interests, selfish; परार्थानुष्ठाने जडयति<BR> नृपं स्वार्थपरता Mu. 3. 4. ˚विघातः frustration of oneʼs object.<BR> ˚सिद्धिः <i>f.</i> fulfilment of oneʼs own object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानन्दः|स्वानन्द
स्व + -आनन्दः delight in oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायत्त
स्व + -आयत्त <i>a.</i> subject to, or dependent upon, oneself; स्वायत्तमेकान्तगुणं<BR> विधात्रा विनिर्मितं छादनमज्ञतायाः Bh. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारब्ध
स्व + -आरब्ध, -आरम्भक <i>a.</i> self-undertaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारम्भक
स्व + -आरब्ध, -आरम्भक <i>a.</i> self-undertaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहत
स्व + -आहत <i>a.</i> coined by oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेच्छा
स्व + -इच्छा self-will, own inclination. ˚आचारः acting as one likes;<BR> self-will. ˚मृत्युः an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोत्थ
स्व + -उत्थ <i>a.</i> innate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोदयः|स्वोदय
स्व + -उदयः the rising of a sign or heavenly body at any particular place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोपधिः|स्वोपधि
स्व + -उपधिः a fixed star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकम्पनः|स्वकम्पन|स्वकंपन
स्व + -कम्पनः air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्मन्|स्वकर्म्मन्
स्व + -कर्मन् oneʼs own duty (स्वधर्म); स्वकर्मनिरतः सिद्धिं<BR> यथा विन्दति तच्छृणु Bg. 18. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्मस्थ|स्वकर्म्मस्थ
स्व + -कर्मस्थ <i>a.</i> minding oneʼs own duty; अधीयीरंस्त्रयो वर्णाः<BR> स्वकर्मस्था द्विजातयः Ms. 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकर्मिन्
स्व + -कर्मिन् <i>a.</i> selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकामिन्
स्व + -कामिन् <i>a.</i> selfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकार्यम्
स्व + -कार्यम् oneʼs own business or interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकुलक्षयः|स्वकुलक्षय
स्व + -कुलक्षयः a fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकृतम्
स्व + -कृतम् a deed done by oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकृतंभुज्
स्व + -कृतंभुज् <i>a.</i> experiencing the results of former deeds (प्रारब्धकर्म);<BR> मा शोचतं महाभागावात्मजान् स्वकृतंभुजः Bhāg. 10. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगतम्
स्व + -गतम् <i>ind.</i> to oneself, aside (in theatrical language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगृहः|स्वगृह
स्व + -गृहः a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वगोचर
स्व + -गोचर <i>a.</i> subject to oneʼs self; स्वगोचरे सत्यपि चित्तहारिणा Ki. 8. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वचर
स्व + -चर <i>a.</i> self-moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छंद|स्वच्छन्दः|स्वछन्द
स्व + -छन्द <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-willed, uncontrolled, wanton.<BR>—2 spontaneous.<BR>—3 wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्दः|स्वच्छन्द|स्वच्छंद|स्वछन्द
स्व + -छन्द + .({@-न्दः@}) oneʼs own will or choice, own fancy or pleasure, independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छन्दम्|स्वच्छंदम्
स्व + -छन्द + .({@-न्दम्@}) <i>ind.</i> at oneʼs own will or pleasure, wantonly, voluntarily;<BR> स्वच्छन्दं दलदरविन्द ते मरन्दं विन्दन्तो विदधतु गुञ्जितं मिलिन्दाः Bv. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज|स्वजं|स्वजः
स्व + -ज <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-born.<BR>—2 natural (स्वाभाविक); आगता त्वामियं बुद्धिः स्वजा वैनायिकी च<BR> या Rām. 2. 112. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजः|स्वज|स्वजं
स्व + -ज + .({@-जः@})<BR>—1 a son or child.<BR>—2 sweat, perspiration. —3 a viper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजा
स्व + -ज + .({@-जा@}) a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजम्
स्व + -ज + .({@-जम्@}) blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजनः|स्वजन
स्व + -जनः<BR>—1 a kinsman, relative; इतःप्रत्यादेशात् स्वजनमनुगन्तुं व्यवसिता<BR> Ś. 6. 8; Pt. 1. 5.<BR>—2 oneʼs own people or kindred, oneʼs household. ˚गन्धिन् <i>a.</i> distantly<BR> related to. (स्वजनायते Den. P. ‘becomes or is treated as a relation’; Pt. 1. 5.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वजातिः|स्वजाति
स्व + -जातिः<BR>—1 oneʼs own kind.<BR>—2 oneʼs own family or caste.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">Page1737-1</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1736-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वज्ञातिः|स्वज्ञाति
स्व + -ज्ञातिः a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वता
स्व + -ता personal regard or interest; अस्यां मे महती स्वता Svapna. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्र|स्वतंत्र|स्वतन्त्रः
स्व + -तन्त्र <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-dependent, uncontrolled, independent, self-willed.<BR>—2 of age, full-grown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्रम्
स्व + -तन्त्र + .({@-न्त्रम्@}) oneʼs own (common group of) subsidiaries; जैमिनेः परतन्त्रापत्तेः<BR> स्वतन्त्रप्रतिषधः स्यात् MS. 12. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्रः|स्वतन्त्र|स्वतंत्र
स्व + -तन्त्र + .({@-न्त्रः@}) a blind man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदृश्
स्व + -दृश् <i>a.</i> seeing oneʼs self; ईयते भगवानेभिः सगुणो निर्गुणः<BR> स्वदृक् Bhāg. 3. 32. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदेशः|स्वदेश
स्व + -देशः oneʼs own country, native country. ˚जः, ˚बन्धुः a<BR> fellow countryman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधर्मः|स्वधर्म|स्वधर्म्म|स्वधर्म्मः
स्व + -धर्मः<BR>—1 oneʼs own religion.<BR>—2 oneʼs own duty, the duties of oneʼs own class; Ms. 1. 88, 91; स्वधर्मे<BR> निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो भयावहः Bg. 3. 35.<BR>—3 peculiarity, oneʼs own rights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिघ्न
स्व + -निघ्न <i>a.</i> depending on or subservient to oneself; (पुराणि<BR> च) निगृह्य निग्रहाभिज्ञो निन्ये नेता स्वनिघ्नताम् Śiva B. 25. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपक्षः|स्वपक्ष
स्व + -पक्षः<BR>—1 oneʼs own side or party.<BR>—2 a friend.<BR>—3 oneʼs own opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपणः|स्वपण
स्व + -पणः oneʼs own stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपरमण्डलम्
स्व + -परमण्डलम् oneʼs own and an enemyʼs country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रकाश
स्व + -प्रकाश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-evident.<BR>—2 self-luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रतिष्ठ
स्व + -प्रतिष्ठ <i>a.</i> astringent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रधान
स्व + -प्रधान <i>a.</i> independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्रयोगात्
स्व + -प्रयोगात् <i>ind.</i> by means of oneʼs own efforts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वबीजः|स्वबीज
स्व + -बीजः the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभटः|स्वभट
स्व + -भटः<BR>—1 oneʼs own warrior.<BR>—2 body-guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभावः|स्वभाव
स्व + -भावः<BR>—1 own state.<BR>—2 an essential or inherent property, natural constitution, innate or<BR> peculiar disposition, nature; स्वभावहेतुजा भावाः Mb. 12. 211. 3; पौरुषं<BR> कारणं केचिदाहुः कर्मसु मानवाः । दैवमेके प्रशंसन्ति स्वभावमपरे<BR> जनाः ॥ 12. 238. 4; Bg. 5. 14; स्वभावो दुरतिक्रमः Subhāṣ.;<BR> so कुटिल˚, शुद्ध˚, मृदु˚, चपल˚, कठिन˚ &c. ˚आत्मक <i>a.</i><BR> natural, inborn; स्वभावतः प्रवृत्तो यः प्राप्नोत्यर्थं न कारणात् । तत्<BR> स्वभावात्मकं विद्धि फलं पुरुषसत्तम ॥ Mb. 3. 32. 19. ˚उक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 spontaneous declaration.<BR>—2 (in Rhet.) a figure of speech which consists in describing a thing<BR> to the life, or with exact resemblance; स्वभावोक्तिस्तु डिम्भादेः स्वक्रियारूपवर्णनम्<BR> K. P. 10, or नानावस्थं पदार्थानां रूपं साक्षाद्विवृण्वती Kāv. 2. 8.<BR> ˚ज <i>a.</i> innate, natural. ˚भावः natural disposition. ˚वादः<BR> the doctrine that the universe was produced and is sustained by the natural<BR> and necessary action of substances according to their inherent properities,<BR> (and not by the agency of a Supreme Being). ˚सिद्ध <i>a.</i> natural,<BR> spontaneous, inborn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभूः
स्व + -भूः <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Śiva.<BR>—3 of Viṣṇu. ━<i>f.</i> oneʼs own country, home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमनीषा
स्व + -मनीषा own judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमनीषिका
स्व + -मनीषिका indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमात्रेण
स्व + -मात्रेण <i>ind.</i> by oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयुतिः|स्वयुति
स्व + -युतिः the line which joins the extremities of the perpendicular and diagonal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयूथ्यः|स्वयूथ्य
स्व + -यूथ्यः a relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयोनि
स्व + -योनि <i>a.</i> related on the motherʼs side. ━(<i>m., f.</i>) own womb,<BR> oneʼs own place of birth. ━(<i>f.</i>) a sister or near female relative;<BR> रेतःसेकः स्वयोनीषु कुमारीष्वन्त्यजासु च (गुरुतल्पसमं विदुः) Ms. 11. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसः|स्वरस
स्व + -रसः<BR>—1 natural taste.<BR>—2 proper taste or sentiment in composition.<BR>—3 a kind of astringent juice.<BR>—4 the residue of oily substances (ground on a stone.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराज्
स्व + -राज् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-luminons; त्वमकरणः स्वराडखिलकारकशक्तिधरः Bhāg. 10. 87. 28.<BR>—2 self-wise; Bhāg. 1. 1. 1. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 the Supreme Being.<BR>—2 one of the seven rays of the sun.<BR>—3 N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">Page1737-2</a>]<BR> Brahmā; दिदृक्षुरागादृषिभिर्वृतः स्वराट् Bhāg. 3. 18. 20.<BR>—4 N. of Viṣṇu; हस्तौ च निरभिद्येतां बलं ताभ्यां ततः स्वराट्<BR> Bhāg. 3. 26. 59.<BR>—5 a king with a revenue of 50 lacs to one crore Karṣas; ततस्तु कोटिपर्यन्तः<BR> स्वराट् सम्राट् ततः परम् Śukra. 1. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराज्यम्
स्व + -राज्यम्<BR>—1 independent dominion or sovereignty.<BR>—2 own kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराष्ट्रम्
स्व + -राष्ट्रम् own kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुचिः|स्वरुचि
स्व + -रुचिः oneʼs own pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूप|स्वरूपं|स्वरूपः
स्व + -रूप <i>a.</i><BR>—1 similar, like.<BR>—2 handsome, pleasing, lovely.<BR>—3 learned, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरूपम्
स्व + -रूप + .({@-पम्@})<BR>—1 oneʼs own form or shape, natural state or condition; तत्रान्यस्य<BR> कथं न भावि जगतो यस्मात् स्वरूपं हि तत् Pt. 1. 159.<BR>—2 natural character or form, true constitution.<BR>—3 nature.<BR>—4 peculiar aim.<BR>—5 kind, sort, species. ˚असिद्धि <i>f.</i> one of the three forms of fallacy<BR> called असिद्ध q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वलक्षणम्
स्व + -लक्षणम् a peculiar characteristic or property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वलोकः
स्व + -लोकः<BR>—1 oneʼs own form (आत्मरूप); व्यर्थोऽपि नैवोपरमत पुंसां मत्तः<BR> परावृत्तधियां स्वलोकात् Bhāg. 11. 22. 34.<BR>—2 self-knowledge; पुष्णन् स्वलोकाय न कल्पते वै Bhāg. 7. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववत्|स्ववन्त्
स्व + -वत् <i>a.</i> possessed of property; स्ववती श्रुत्यनुरोधात् ŚB. on MS. 6. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववश
स्व + -वश <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-controlled.<BR>—2 independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववहित
स्व + -वहित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-impelled.<BR>—2 alert, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववासिनी
स्व + -वासिनी a woman whether married or unmarried who continues to<BR> live after maturity in her fatherʼs house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वविग्रहः|स्वविग्रह
स्व + -विग्रहः oneʼs own body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वविषयः|स्वविषय
स्व + -विषयः oneʼs own country, home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववृत्तम्
स्व + -वृत्तम् oneʼs own business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ववृत्ति
स्व + -वृत्ति <i>a.</i> living by oneʼs own exertions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंविद्
स्व + -संविद् <i>f.</i> the knowledge of oneʼs own or the true essence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंवृत
स्व + -संवृत <i>a.</i> self-protected, self-guarded; मायां नित्यं स्वसंवृतः Ms. 7. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंवेदनम्
स्व + -संवेदनम् knowledge derived from oneʼs self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसंस्था
स्व + -संस्था<BR>—1 self-abiding.<BR>—2 self-possession.<BR>—3 absorption in oneʼs own self; उन्मत्तमत्तजडवत्स्वसंस्थां गतस्य<BR> मे वीर चिकित्सितेन Bhāg. 5. 10. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थ|स्वस्थः
स्व + -स्थ <i>a.</i><BR>—1 self-abiding.<BR>—2 self-dependent, relying on oneʼs own exertions, confident, firm, resolute;<BR> स्वस्थं तं सूचयन्तीव वञ्चितोऽसीति वीक्षितैः Bu. C. 4. 37.<BR>—3 independent.<BR>—4 doing well, well, in health, at ease, comfortable; स्वस्थ एवास्मि<BR> Māl. 4; स्वस्थे को वा न पण्डितः Pt. 1. 127; see अस्वस्थ also.<BR>—5 contented, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थम्
स्व + -स्थ + .({@-स्थम्@}) <i>ind.</i> at ease, comfortably, composedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्थानम्
स्व + -स्थानम् oneʼs own place or home, oneʼs own abode; नक्रः स्वस्थानमासाद्य<BR> गजेन्द्रमपि कर्षति Pt. 3. 46. ˚विवृद्धिः (Mīmāṃsā) augmentation<BR> in its own place (opp. दण्डकलितवत् आवृत्तिः); तत्र पूर्णे पुनरावृत्तिर्नास्तीति<BR> दण्डकलितवद् न स्यात् । न च वृद्धपा विना तदन्तरं पूर्यते इति स्वस्थानविवृद्धिरागतेति ŚB. on MS. 10. 5. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्वरूपम्
स्व + -स्वरूपम् oneʼs true character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहन्तृ
स्व + -हन्तृ <i>m.</i> suicide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहरणम्
स्व + -हरणम् confiscation of property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहस्तः|स्वहस्त
स्व + -हस्तः oneʼs own hand or handwriting, an autograph; see under हस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहस्तिका
स्व + -हस्तिका an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहित
स्व + -हित <i>a.</i> beneficial to oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहितम्
स्व + -हित + .({@-तम्@}) oneʼs own good or advantage, oneʼs own welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वहेतुः|स्वहेतु
स्व + -हेतुः oneʼs own cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक <i>a.</i> Oneʼs own, own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकः|स्वक|स्वकं
स्वक + .{@-कः@} A relation, friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकम्
स्वक + .{@-कम्@} Oneʼs own property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Oneʼs own, own.<BR>—2 Of oneʼs own family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीया
स्वकीय + .{@-या@} Oneʼs own wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1737-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतस्
स्वतस् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Of oneself, by oneself (used reflexively).<BR>—2 From oneself.<BR>—3 Out of own estate; दातव्यं बान्धवैस्तत्स्यात् प्रविभक्तैरपि स्वतः Ms. 8. 166.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वतःप्रमाणम्, स्वतःसिद्ध<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतःप्रमाणम्
स्वतस् + -प्रमाणम्, -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> self-evident, self-proved, axiomatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतःसिद्ध
स्वतस् + -प्रमाणम्, -सिद्ध <i>a.</i> self-evident, self-proved, axiomatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वता
स्वता Ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वम्
स्वत्वम्<BR>—1 Self-existence.<BR>—2 Ownership, proprietory right.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वत्वनिवृत्तिः, स्वत्वहानिः, स्वत्वबोधनम्, स्वत्वहेतुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वनिवृत्तिः|स्वत्वनिवृत्ति
स्वत्वम् + -निवृत्तिः, -हानिः loss of proprietory right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहानिः|स्वत्वहानि
स्वत्वम् + -निवृत्तिः, -हानिः loss of proprietory right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वबोधनम्
स्वत्वम् + -बोधनम् proof of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वहेतुः|स्वत्वहेतु
स्वत्वम् + -हेतुः cause of proprietory right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंग्|स्वङ्ग्
स्वं(क्)ग् €1 P. (स्वं-क-गति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंक्|स्वङ्क्
स्वं(क्)ग् €1 P. (स्वं-क-गति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
स्वच्छ <i>a.</i> [सुष्ठु अच्छः प्रा˚]<BR>—1 Very clear or transparent, pure, bright, pellucid; स्वच्छस्फटिक,<BR> स्वच्छमुक्ताफलम् &c.<BR>—2 White.<BR>—3 Beautiful.<BR>—4 Healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छः|स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं
स्वच्छ + .{@-च्छः@}<BR>—1 A crystal.<BR>—2 The jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छा
स्वच्छ + .{@-च्छा@} White Dūrvā grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छम्
स्वच्छ + .{@-च्छम्@}<BR>—1 A pearl.<BR>—2 Pure chalk.<BR>—3 An alloy of silver and gold.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वच्छपत्रम्, स्वच्छमणिः, स्वच्छवालुकम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छपत्रम्
स्वच्छ + -पत्रम् talc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छमणिः|स्वच्छमणि
स्वच्छ + -मणिः a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छवालुकम्
स्वच्छ + -वालुकम् pure chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छता
स्वच्छता<BR>—1 Perfect clearness.<BR>—2 Purity.<BR>—3 Transparency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वञ्ज्|स्वंज्
स्वञ्ज् €1 Ā. (स्वजते; the स् being changed to ष् after<BR> prepositions ending in इ or उ)<BR>—1 To embrace, clasp; कयाचिदाचुम्ब्य चिराय सस्वजे Bv. 2. 178; पर्यश्रुरस्वजत<BR> मूर्धनि चोपजघ्रौ R. 13. 70.<BR>—2 To encircle, twist round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वङ्गः|स्वङ्ग|स्वंग|स्वंगः
स्वङ्गः An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वञ्जनम्
स्वञ्जनम् The act of embracing, an embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ्
स्वठ् €10 U. (स्व(स्वा)ठयति-ते)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतन्त्रता
स्वतन्त्रता<BR>—1 Independence, freedom.<BR>—2 Originality.<BR>—3 Wilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् I. €1 Ā. (स्वदते, स्वदित)<BR>—1 To be liked, be sweet, be pleasant to the taste (with dat. of person);<BR> यज्ञदत्ताय स्वदतेऽपूपः Kāśi.; अपां हि तृप्ताय न वारिधारा<BR> स्वादुः सुगंधिः स्वदते तुषारा N. 3. 93; सस्वदे मुखसुरं प्रमदाभ्यः Śi. 10. 23.<BR>—2 To taste, relish, eat.<BR>—3 To please.<BR>—4 To sweeten. ━II. €10 U. or <i>Caus.</i> (स्वादयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to taste or eat.<BR>—2 To taste.<BR>—3 To sweeten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदनम्
स्वदनम् Tasting, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित <i>p. p.</i> Tasted, eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदितम्
स्वदित + .{@-तम्@} An exclamation meaning ‘may it be well tasted or relished’,<BR> uttered at a Śrāddha^1 ceremony after the presentation of rice-balls or<BR> oblations of food to the Manes; पृष्ट्वा स्वदितमित्येवं तृप्तानाचामयेत्ततः<BR> Ms. 3. 251, 254.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20260506. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्वधा [स्वद्-आ-पृषो˚ दस्य धः]<BR>—1 Oneʼs own nature or determination, spontaneity.<BR>—2 Oneʼs own will or pleasure.<BR>—3 The oblation of food offered to the Pitṛs or Manes of deceased ancestors;<BR> स्वधासंग्रहतत्पराः R. 1. 66; Ms. 9. 142; Y. 1. 102.<BR>—4 The food offered to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">Page1738-2</a>]<BR> Manes personified.<BR>—5 Food or oblation in general.<BR>—6 Oneʼs own portion or share.<BR>—7 A Śrāddha or funeral ceremony; Ms. 2. 142.<BR>—8 N. of Māyā or illusion. ━<i>ind.</i> An exclamation uttered on offering<BR> an oblation to the Manes (with dat.); पितृभ्यः स्वधा Sk.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वधाकर, स्वधाकारः, स्वधानिनयनम्, स्वधाप्रियः, स्वधाभुज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाकर
स्वधा + -कर <i>a.</i> offering oblations to the Pitṛs; यदपत्यं भवेदस्यां<BR> तन्मम स्यात् स्वधाकरम् Ms. 9. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाकारः|स्वधाकार
स्वधा + -कारः the exclamation Svadhā; पूतं हि तद्गृहं यत्र स्वधाकारः प्रवर्तते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधानिनयनम्
स्वधा + -निनयनम् a formula or sacred text used in making the oblations<BR> to the Pitṛs; नाभिव्याहारयेद्ब्रह्म स्वधानिनयनादृते Ms. 2. 172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाप्रियः|स्वधाप्रिय
स्वधा + -प्रियः<BR>—1 Agni or fire.<BR>—2 black sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधाभुज्
स्वधा + -भुज् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a deceased or deified ancestor.<BR>—2 a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधितिः|स्वधिति
स्वधितिः <i>m., f.</i>, स्वधिती An axe; सूदा महानसं नीत्वाऽवद्यन्स्वधितिनाद्भुतम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 55. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वधितिहेतिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधिती
स्वधितिः <i>m., f.</i>, स्वधिती An axe; सूदा महानसं नीत्वाऽवद्यन्स्वधितिनाद्भुतम्<BR> Bhāg. 10. 55. 5.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वधितिहेतिकः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधितिहेतिकः|स्वधितिहेतिक
स्वधितिः + -हेतिकः a soldier armed with an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधीतिः|स्वधीति
स्वधीतिः A good reciter (of the Veda); a Brahmachārin; स्विष्टिः<BR> स्वधीतिः सुतपा लोकाञ्जयति यावतः Mb. 12. 71. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् €1 P. (स्वनति)<BR>—1 To sound, make a noise; पूर्णाः पेराश्च सस्वनुः Bk. 14. 3; वेणवः<BR> कीचकास्ते स्युर्ये स्वनन्त्यनिलोद्धताः Bk.<BR>—2 To hum (as a bee); रहस्याख्यायीव स्वनसि मृदु कर्णान्तिकचरः Ś. 1. 24.<BR>—3 To sing. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्वनयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to resound.<BR>—2 To sound.<BR>—3 To adorn (स्वानयति in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनः|स्वन
स्वनः [स्वन्-अप्] Sound, noise; शिवाघोरस्वनां पश्चाद् बुबुधे<BR> विकृतेति ताम् R. 12. 39; शङ्खस्वनः &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वनचक्रः, स्वनोत्साहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनचक्रः|स्वनचक्र
स्वनः + -चक्रः a manner of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनोत्साहः|स्वनोत्साह
स्वनः + -उत्साहः a rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिः|स्वनि
स्वनिः<BR>—1 Sound, noise.<BR>—2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिक
स्वनिक <i>a.</i> Sounding; as in पाणिस्वनिकः ‘one who claps his hands’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित <i>a.</i> [स्वन्-कर्तरि क्त] Sounded, sounding, making a noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनितम्
स्वनित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 The noise of thunder, thunderclap; cf. स्तनित.<BR>—2 Noise, sound (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्
स्वप् €2 P. (स्वपिति, सुप्त; <i>pass.</i> सुप्यते; <i>desid.</i><BR> सुषुप्सति) (rarely €1 U. स्वपति-ते)<BR>—1 To sleep, fall asleep, go to sleep; असञ्जातकिणस्कन्धः सुखं स्वपिति<BR> गौर्गडिः K. P. 10; इतः स्वपिति केशवः Bh. 2. 76.<BR>—2 To recline, repose, lie down, rest.<BR>—3 To be absorbed in; स्वापं वाञ्छसि चेन्निरर्गलसुखे चेतः सखे सुप्यताम्<BR> Bv. 4. 19. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्वापयति-ते) To cause to sleep, rock to<BR> sleep. ━<i>With</i> {@अव, नि, प्र@}, or {@सम्@} to sleep, lie down; प्रसुप्तलक्षणः<BR> Māl. 7; वीज्यते स हि संसुप्तः Ku. 2. 42; तत् प्रसुप्तभुजगेन्द्रभीषणं<BR> वीक्ष्य दाशरथिराददे धनुः R. 11. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपनम्
स्वपनम्<BR>—1 Sleeping, dreaming, sleep.<BR>—2 Numbness (of the skin); Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नः|स्वप्न
स्वप्नः [स्वप्-भावे नक्]<BR>—1 Sleeping, sleep; अकाले बोधितो भ्रात्रा प्रियस्वप्नो वृथा भवान् R. 12. 81, 7. 61, 12. 70;<BR> Ku. 2. 8.<BR>—2 A dream, dreaming; स्वप्नेन्द्रजालसदृशः खलु जीवलोकः Śānti. 2. 2;<BR> स्वप्नो नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु Ś. 6. 10; R. 10. 60.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">Page1739-1</a>]<BR>—3 Sloth, indolence, sleepiness; Ms. 9. 13, 12. 33.<BR>—4 The state of ignorance (?); भावाद्वैतं क्रियाद्वैतं द्रव्याद्वैतं तथात्मनः ।<BR> वर्तयन् स्वानुभूत्येह त्रीन् स्वप्नान् धुनुते मुनिः ॥ Bhāg. 7. 15. 62.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वप्नान्तिकम्, स्वप्नावस्था, स्वप्नोपम, स्वप्नकर, स्वप्नकृत्, स्वप्नगृहम्, स्वप्ननिकेतनम्, स्वप्नज, स्वप्नतन्द्रिता, स्वप्नदर्शनम्, स्वप्नदृश्, स्वप्नदोषः, स्वप्नधीगम्य, स्वप्नप्रपञ्चः, स्वप्नविचारः, स्वप्नशील,^1 स्वप्नसृष्टिः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1738-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नान्तिकम्
स्वप्नः + -अन्तिकम् consciousness in dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नावस्था
स्वप्नः + -अवस्था a state of dreaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नोपम
स्वप्नः + -उपम <i>a.</i><BR>—1 resembling a dream.<BR>—2 unreal or illusory (like a dream).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नकर
स्वप्नः + -कर, -कृत् <i>a.</i> inducing sleep, soporific, narcotic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नकृत्
स्वप्नः + -कर, -कृत् <i>a.</i> inducing sleep, soporific, narcotic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नगृहम्
स्वप्नः + -गृहम्, -निकेतनम् a sleeping-room, bed-chamber; दुःखेन लोकः<BR> परवानिवागात् समुत्सुकः स्वप्ननिकेतनेभ्यः Bk. 11. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्ननिकेतनम्
स्वप्नः + -गृहम्, -निकेतनम् a sleeping-room, bed-chamber; दुःखेन लोकः<BR> परवानिवागात् समुत्सुकः स्वप्ननिकेतनेभ्यः Bk. 11. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज
स्वप्नः + -ज <i>a.</i> dreamt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नतन्द्रिता
स्वप्नः + -तन्द्रिता languor produced by drowsiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नदर्शनम्
स्वप्नः + -दर्शनम् dream-vision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नदृश्
स्वप्नः + -दृश् <i>a.</i> dreaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नदोषः|स्वप्नदोष
स्वप्नः + -दोषः involuntary seminal discharge, <i>pollutio nocturna</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नधीगम्य
स्वप्नः + -धीगम्य <i>a.</i> perceptible by the intellect only when it is in<BR> a state of sleep-like abstraction; रुक्माभं स्वप्नधीगम्यं विद्यात् तं<BR> पुरुषं परम् Ms. 12. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नप्रपञ्चः|स्वप्नप्रपञ्च|स्वप्नप्रपंच
स्वप्नः + -प्रपञ्चः the illusion of sleep, the world appearing in a dream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नविचारः|स्वप्नविचार
स्वप्नः + -विचारः interpretation of dreams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नशील
स्वप्नः + -शील^1 <i>a.</i> disposed to sleep, sleepy, drowsy; न चातिस्वप्नशीलस्य<BR> जाग्रतो नैव चार्जुन Bg. 6. 16.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नसृष्टिः|स्वप्नसृष्टि
स्वप्नः + -सृष्टिः <i>f.</i> the creation of dreams or illusions in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज् <i>a.</i> Sleepy, sleeping, drowsy; अहं स्वप्नक् प्रसादेन<BR> तव वन्दारुभिः सह Bk. 7. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नया
स्वप्नया, स्वप्न्यया <i>ind.</i> In dream; स यत्रैतत् स्वप्नया<BR> चरति Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्न्यया
स्वप्नया, स्वप्न्यया <i>ind.</i> In dream; स यत्रैतत् स्वप्नया<BR> चरति Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नालु
स्वप्नालु <i>a.</i> Sleepy, drowsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वभाजनम्
स्वभाजनम् Delighting, making happy; see सभाजनम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमेकः|स्वमेक
स्वमेकः A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Oneself, in oneʼs own person (used reflexively and applicable to all<BR> persons, such as myself, ourselves, thyself, himself &c. &c., and sometimes<BR> used with other pronouns for the sake of emphasis); विषवृक्षोऽपि संवर्ध्य<BR> स्वयं छेत्तुमसांप्रतम् Ku. 2. 55; यस्य नास्ति स्वयं प्रज्ञा शास्त्रं<BR> तस्य करोति किम् Subhāṣ.; R. 1. 70, 3. 20, 2. 56; Ms. 5. 39.<BR>—2 Spontaneously, of oneʼs own accord, without trouble or exertion; स्वयमेवोत्पद्यन्त<BR> एवंविधाः कुलपांशवो निःस्नेहाः पशवः K.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वयमधिगत, स्वयमनुष्ठानम्, स्वयमर्जित, स्वयमिन्द्रियमोचनम्, स्वयमीश्वरः, स्वयमीहितलब्ध, स्वयमुक्तिः, स्वयमुद्यत, स्वयमुपागतः, स्वयङ्कृत, स्वयङ्गुप्ता, स्वयङ्ग्रहः, स्वयङ्ग्राह, स्वयञ्जात, स्वयञ्ज्योतिस्, स्वयन्दत्त, स्वयन्दृश्, स्वयम्पाठः, स्वयम्प्रकाश, स्वयम्प्रभ, स्वयम्प्रभु, स्वयम्भुः, स्वयम्भुवः, स्वयम्भू, स्वयम्भूतः, स्वयम्भृत, स्वयंवरः, स्वयंवरा, स्वयंश्रेष्ठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमधिगत
स्वयम् + -अधिगत <i>a.</i> self-acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमनुष्ठानम्
स्वयम् + -अनुष्ठानम् oneʼs own achievement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमर्जित
स्वयम् + -अर्जित <i>a.</i> self-acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमिन्द्रियमोचनम्
स्वयम् + -इन्द्रियमोचनम् spontaneous emission of semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमीश्वरः|स्वयमीश्वर
स्वयम् + -ईश्वरः an absolute sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमीहितलब्ध
स्वयम् + -ईहितलब्ध <i>a.</i> gained by oneʼs own effort; अनुपघ्नन् पितृद्रव्यं<BR> श्रमेण यदुपार्जितम् । स्वयमीहितलब्धं तन्नाकामो दातुमर्हति ॥ Ms. 9. 208.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमुक्तिः|स्वयमुक्ति
स्वयम् + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 voluntary declaration.<BR>—2 information, deposition (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमुद्यत
स्वयम् + -उद्यत <i>a.</i> offered spontaneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयमुपागतः|स्वयमुपागत
स्वयम् + -उपागतः a son who offers himself voluntarily to an adoptive parent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्कृत|स्वयंकृत|स्वयङ्कृतः|स्वयंकृतः
स्वयम् + -कृत <i>a.</i> self-made, natural.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्कृतः|स्वयङ्कृत|स्वयंकृत|स्वयंकृतः
स्वयम् + -कृत + .({@-तः@}) an artificial or adopted son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्गुप्ता|स्वयंगुप्ता
स्वयम् + -गुप्ता Mucuna Pruritus (Mar. कुयली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्ग्रहः|स्वयङ्ग्रह
स्वयम् + -ग्रहः taking for one-self (without leave).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्ग्राह|स्वयङ्ग्राहः
स्वयम् + -ग्राह <i>a.</i><BR>—1 voluntary, self-choosing.<BR>—2 one who takes forcibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयङ्ग्राहः|स्वयङ्ग्राह
स्वयम् + -ग्राह + .({@-हः@}) self-choice, self-election; नितम्बिनीमिच्छसि मुक्तलज्जां<BR> कण्ठे स्वयंग्राहनिषक्तबाहुम् Ku. 3. 7; Māl. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयञ्जात
स्वयम् + -जात <i>a.</i> self-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयञ्ज्योतिस्
स्वयम् + -ज्योतिस् self-shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयंदत्त|स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयम् + -दत्त <i>a.</i> self-given.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">Page1739-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयन्दत्तः|स्वयन्दत्त|स्वयंदत्त|स्वयंदत्तः
स्वयम् + -दत्त + .({@-त्तः@}) a boy who has given himself to be adopted (by his adoptive<BR> parents); one of the twelve kinds of sons recognised in Hindu law; मातापितृविहीनो<BR> यस्त्यक्तो वा स्यादकारणात् । आत्मानं स्पर्शयेद्यस्मै स्वयंदत्तस्तु स स्मृतः ॥<BR> Ms. 9. 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयन्दृश्
स्वयम् + -दृश् <i>a.</i> self-evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्पाठः|स्वयम्पाठ|स्वयंपाठ
स्वयम् + -पाठः an original text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्प्रकाश
स्वयम् + -प्रकाश <i>a.</i> self-manifesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्प्रभ|स्वयंप्रभ|स्वयंप्रभः
स्वयम् + -प्रभ <i>a.</i> self-shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्प्रभु|स्वयंप्रभु
स्वयम् + -प्रभु <i>a.</i> self-powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भुः|स्वयम्भु|स्वयंभु
स्वयम् + -भुः N. of Brahman; शंभुस्वयंभुहरयो हरिणेक्षणानां येनाक्रियन्त<BR> सततं गृहकर्मदासाः Bh. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भुवः|स्वयम्भुव|स्वयंभुव
स्वयम् + -भुवः<BR>—1 the first Manu.<BR>—2 N. of Brahman.<BR>—3 of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भू|स्वयंभू
स्वयम् + -भू <i>a.</i> self-existent; त्वमेको ह्यस्य सर्वस्य विधानस्य<BR> स्वयंभुवः Ms. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भूः|स्वयंभूः
स्वयम् + -भू + .({@-भूः@})<BR>—1 N. of Brahman.<BR>—2 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 of Śiva.<BR>—4 of <i>Kāla</i> or time personified.<BR>—5 of Kāmadeva.<BR>—6 a Jaina deified saint.<BR>—7 the female breast.<BR>—8 the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भूतः|स्वयम्भूत
स्वयम् + -भूतः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्भृत|स्वयंभृत
स्वयम् + -भृत <i>a.</i> self-maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवरः|स्वयंवर
स्वयम् + -वरः self-choice, self-election (of a husband by the bride herself),<BR> choicemarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंवरा
स्वयम् + -वरा a maiden who chooses her own husband; ततस्ते शुश्रुवुः<BR> कृष्णां पञ्चालेषु स्वयंवराम् Mb. 1. 61. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयंश्रेष्ठः|स्वयंश्रेष्ठ
स्वयम् + -श्रेष्ठः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् €10 U. (स्वरयति-ते) To find fault, blame, reprove, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Heaven, paradise; as in स्वर्लोक, स्वर्वेश्या, स्वर्भानुः, &c.; त्वं<BR> कर्मणां मङ्गलमङ्गलानां कर्तुः स्म लोकं तनुषे स्वः परं वा Bhāg. 4. 6. 45.<BR>—2 The heaven of Indra and the temporary abode of the virtuous after death.<BR>—3 The sky, ether.<BR>—4 The space above the sun or between the sun and the polar star.<BR>—5 The third of the three Vyāhṛtis, pronounced by every Brāhmaṇa<BR> in his daily prayers; see व्याहृति.<BR>—6 Radiance, splendour.<BR>—7 Water. ━<i>ind.</i> (used in nom., acc., gen., or loc. case); स्वलंकृतैर्भवनवरैविभूषितां<BR> पुरंदरः स्वरिव यथामरावतीम् Rām. 7. 11. 50; साधोरपि स्वः खलु<BR> गामिताधो गमी स तु स्वर्गमितः प्रयाणे N. 6. 99 (herein abl. case,<BR> स्वर् = स्वर्गात्).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वरतिक्रमः, स्वरापगा, स्वर्गङ्गा, स्वरिङ्गणः, स्वर्गत, स्वर्गतिः, स्वर्गिरिः, स्वर्जित्, स्वस्तरुः, स्वर्दृश्, स्वर्धुनी, स्वर्नदी, स्वर्भानवः, स्वर्भानुः, स्वर्मणिः, स्वर्मध्यम्, स्वर्यात, स्वर्यातृ, स्वर्यानम्, स्वर्योषित्, स्वर्लोकः, स्वर्वधूः, स्वर्वापी, स्वर्वारवामभ्रू, स्वर्वेश्या, स्वर्वैद्यः,^1 स्वःषा, स्वःसिन्धु<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरतिक्रमः|स्वरतिक्रम
स्वर् + -अतिक्रमः reaching Vaikuṇṭha (beyond heaven).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरापगा
स्वर् + -आपगा, -गङ्गा<BR>—1 the celestial Ganges.<BR>—2 the galaxy or milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गङ्गा|स्वर्गंगा
स्वर् + -आपगा, -गङ्गा<BR>—1 the celestial Ganges.<BR>—2 the galaxy or milky way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरिङ्गणः|स्वरिङ्गण
स्वर् + -इङ्गणः a strong wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गत
स्वर् + -गत <i>a.</i> dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गतिः|स्वर्गति
स्वर् + -गतिः <i>f.</i>, {@-गमनम्@}<BR>—1 going to heaven, future felicity.<BR>—2 death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिरिः|स्वर्गिरि
स्वर् + -गिरिः Sumeru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्जित्
स्वर् + -जित् <i>m.</i> a kind of sacrifice; यजेत वाश्वमेधेन स्वर्जिता<BR> गोसवेन वा Ms. 11. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तरुः|स्वस्तरु
स्वर् + -तरुः (स्वस्तरुः) a tree of paradise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्दृश्
स्वर् + -दृश् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an epithet of Indra.<BR>—2 of <i>Agni</i>.<BR>—3 of <i>Soma</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्धुनी
स्वर् + -धुनी, -नदी (forming स्वर्णदी) the celestial Ganges; सद्यः<BR> पुनन्त्युपस्पृष्टाः स्वर्धुन्यापोनुसेवया Bhāg. 1. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्नदी
स्वर् + -धुनी, -नदी (forming स्वर्णदी) the celestial Ganges; सद्यः<BR> पुनन्त्युपस्पृष्टाः स्वर्धुन्यापोनुसेवया Bhāg. 1. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानवः|स्वर्भानव
स्वर् + -भानवः a kind of precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्भानुः|स्वर्भानु
स्वर् + -भानुः N. of Rāhu; तुल्येऽपराधे स्वर्भानुर्भानुमन्तं चिरेण<BR> यत् । हिमांशुमाशु ग्रसते तन्म्रदिम्नः स्फुटं फलम् Śi. 2. 49. ˚सूदनः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्मणिः|स्वर्मणि
स्वर् + -मणिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्मध्यम्
स्वर् + -मध्यम् the central point of the sky, the zenith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्यात|स्वर्यातः
स्वर् + -यात <i>a.</i> dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्यातृ
स्वर् + -यातृ <i>a.</i> dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्यानम्
स्वर् + -यानम् dying, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्योषित्
स्वर् + -योषित् a celestial woman, <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्लोकः|स्वर्लोक
स्वर् + -लोकः the celestial world, heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वधूः|स्वर्व्वधूः
स्वर् + -वधूः <i>f.</i> a celestial damsel, an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वापी|स्वर्व्वापी
स्वर् + -वापी the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वारवामभ्रू
स्वर् + -वारवामभ्रू (see -वधू above);<BR> स्वर्वारवामभ्रुवः नृत्यं चक्रुः Cola-Campū. p. 22, Verse 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वेश्या|स्वर्व्वेश्या
स्वर् + -वेश्या ‘a courtezan of heaven’, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">Page1740-1</a>]<BR> celestial nymph, an <i>apsaras</i>.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1739-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्वैद्यः|स्वर्वैद्य
स्वर् + -वैद्यः^1 <i>m.</i> du. an epithet of the two Aśvins.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वःषा
स्वर् + -षा<BR>—1 an epithet of <i>Soma</i>.<BR>—2 of the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वःसिन्धु|स्वःसिंधु
स्वर् + -सिन्धु = स्वर्गङ्गा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर|स्वरः
स्वर <i>a.</i> Going; one who goes (this meaning is given only by Gīrvaṇa.);<BR> असौ स्वर इतीममाचक्षते स्वर इति प्रत्यास्वर इत्यमुं … … चोद्गीथमुपासीत<BR> Ch. Up. 1. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरः|स्वर
स्वरः [स्वर्-अच्, स्वृ-अप् वा]<BR>—1 Sound, noise.<BR>—2 Voice; स्वरेण तस्याममृतस्रुतेव प्रजल्पितायामभिजातवाचि Ku. 1. 45.<BR>—3 A note of the musical scale or gamut, a tone, tune; (these are seven:− निषादर्षभगान्धारषडजमध्यमधैवताः<BR> ॥ पञ्चमश्चेत्यमी सप्त तन्त्रीकण्ठोत्थिताः स्वराः Ak.); सप्त स्वरास्त्रयो<BR> ग्रामा मूर्छनाश्चैकविंशतिः Pt. 5. 54.<BR>—4 The number ‘seven’.<BR>—5 A vowel.<BR>—6 An accent; (these are three; उदात्त, अनुदात्त and स्वरित qq. vv.);<BR> निहन्त्यरीनेकपदे य उदात्तः स्वरानिव Śi. 2. 95.<BR>—7 Air breathed through the nostrils.<BR>—8 Snoring.<BR>—9 Sweetness of tune or tone; तस्मादार्त्विज्यं करिष्यन् वाचि स्वरमिच्छेत<BR> तया वाचा स्वरसंपन्नयार्त्विज्यं कुर्यात् Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरा
स्वरः + .{@-रा@} N. of the chief wife of Brahman.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वरांशः, स्वराङ्कः, स्वरान्तरम्, स्वरोदय, स्वरोपघातः, स्वरोपध, स्वरकम्पः, स्वरकर, स्वरक्षयः, स्वरग्रामः, स्वरच्छिद्रम्, स्वरदीप्त, स्वरनाभिः, स्वरपत्तनम्, स्वरपरिवर्तः, स्वरबद्ध, स्वरब्रह्मन्, स्वरभक्तिः, स्वरभङ्गः, स्वरभेदः, स्वरभङ्गिन्, स्वरमञ्चनृत्यम्, स्वरमण्डलम्, स्वरमण्डलिका, स्वरमात्रा, स्वरयोगः, स्वरलासिका, स्वरविभक्तिः, स्वरशास्त्रम्, स्वरशुद्ध, स्वरशून्य, स्वरसंयोगः, स्वरसंक्रमः, स्वरसंदेहविवादः, स्वरसंधिः, स्वरसंपद्, स्वरसंपन्न, स्वरसामन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरांशः|स्वरांश
स्वरः + -अंशः a half or quarter tone (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वराङ्कः|स्वराङ्क
स्वरः + -अङ्कः a kind of musical composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरान्तरम्
स्वरः + -अन्तरम् the interval between two vowels, hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरोदय|स्वरोदयः
स्वरः + -उदय <i>a.</i> followed by a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरोदयः|स्वरोदय
स्वरः + -उदय + .({@-यः@})<BR>—1 the production of sound.<BR>—2 see स्वरशास्त्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरोपघातः|स्वरोपघात
स्वरः + -उपघातः hoarseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरोपध
स्वरः + -उपध <i>a.</i> preceded by a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरकम्पः|स्वरकम्प
स्वरः + -कम्पः trembling of tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरकर
स्वरः + -कर <i>a.</i> producing voice<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरक्षयः|स्वरक्षय
स्वरः + -क्षयः the loss of voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरग्रामः|स्वरग्राम
स्वरः + -ग्रामः the musical scale, gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरच्छिद्रम्
स्वरः + -च्छिद्रम् the sound-hole of a flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरदीप्त
स्वरः + -दीप्त <i>a.</i> (in augury) inauspicious with regard to voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरनाभिः|स्वरनाभि
स्वरः + -नाभिः a kind of flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरपत्तनम्
स्वरः + -पत्तनम् N. of the Sāma-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरपरिवर्तः|स्वरपरिवर्त
स्वरः + -परिवर्तः change of voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरबद्ध
स्वरः + -बद्ध composed in musical measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरब्रह्मन्
स्वरः + -ब्रह्मन् the Brahman as manifested in sound; स्वरब्रह्मणि निर्भातहृषीकेशपदाम्बुजे<BR> अखण्डं चित्तमावेश्य लोकाननुचरन् मुनिः ॥ Bhāg. 6. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभक्तिः|स्वरभक्ति
स्वरः + -भक्तिः <i>f.</i> a vowel-sound phonetically inserted in the pronunciation<BR> of र् or ल् when these letters are followed by a sibilant or any<BR> single consonant; (<i>e. g.</i> वर्ष pronounced as वरिष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभङ्गः|स्वरभङ्ग|स्वरभंग
स्वरः + -भङ्गः, -भेदः<BR>—1 indistinctness of utterance, broken articulation.<BR>—2 hoarseness or cracking of voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभेदः|स्वरभेद
स्वरः + -भङ्गः, -भेदः<BR>—1 indistinctness of utterance, broken articulation.<BR>—2 hoarseness or cracking of voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरभङ्गिन्
स्वरः + -भङ्गिन् <i>m.</i> a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमञ्चनृत्यम्
स्वरः + -मञ्चनृत्यम् a kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमण्डलम्
स्वरः + -मण्डलम् the circle of notes, arrangement of musical scales;<BR> सप्त स्वरास्त्रयो ग्रामा मूर्च्छनाश्चैकविंशतिः तानास्त्वेकोनपञ्चाशदित्येतत्स्वरमण्डलम् ॥<BR> Pt. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमण्डलिका|स्वरमंडलिका
स्वरः + -मण्डलिका a kind of lute (वीणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरमात्रा
स्वरः + -मात्रा strength of sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरयोगः|स्वरयोग
स्वरः + -योगः voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरलासिका
स्वरः + -लासिका a flute, pipe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरविभक्तिः|स्वरविभक्ति
स्वरः + -विभक्तिः separation of a vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरशास्त्रम्
स्वरः + -शास्त्रम्<BR>—1 the science of the modulation of sounds.<BR>—2 the science of the passage of the air through the nostrils (as bearing<BR> on the prognostication of future events).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरशुद्ध
स्वरः + -शुद्ध <i>a.</i> correct in musical measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरशून्य
स्वरः + -शून्य <i>a.</i> without musical notes, unmelodious, unmusical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंयोगः|स्वरसंयोग
स्वरः + -संयोगः<BR>—1 the junction of vowels.<BR>—2 the union of notes or sounds, <i>i. e.</i> voice; अन्य एवैष स्वरसंयागः<BR> Mk. 1, 3; U. 3; पण्डितकौशिक्या इव स्वरसंयोगः श्रूयते M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंक्रमः|स्वरसङ्क्रम
स्वरः + -संक्रमः<BR>—1 a transition or succession of notes; तं तस्य स्वरसंक्रमं मृदुगिरः<BR> श्लिष्टं च तन्त्रीस्वनम् Mk. 3. 5.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">Page1740-2</a>]<BR>—2 the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंदेहविवादः|स्वरसन्देहविवाद
स्वरः + -संदेहविवादः a kind of round game; K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंधिः|स्वरसन्धि
स्वरः + -संधिः the coalition of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंपद्
स्वरः + -संपद् <i>f.</i> melody of voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसंपन्न
स्वरः + -संपन्न <i>a.</i> having a melodious voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरसामन्
स्वरः + -सामन् <i>m.</i> pl. epithets of particular days in a sacrificial session.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरवत्|स्वरवन्त्
स्वरवत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having sound, sonorous.<BR>—2 Having a voice.<BR>—3 Vocal.<BR>—4 Having an accent, accented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित <i>a.</i> [स्वरो जातोऽस्य इतच्]<BR>—1 Sounded; caused to sound; स्वरितवेणुना सुष्ठु चुम्बितम् Bhāg. 10. 31. 14.<BR>—2 Sounded as a note, pitched.<BR>—3 Articulated.<BR>—4 Circumflexed.<BR>—5 Accented.<BR>—6 A dded, admixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरितः|स्वरित
स्वरित + .{@-तः@} The third or mixed tone lying between high and low; समाहारः<BR> स्वरितः P. I. 2. 31; see Sk. thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1740-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरितत्वम्
