स्वल्पदृश्
स्वल्प + -दृश् <i>a.</i> very short-sighted (lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पबल
स्वल्प + -बल <i>a.</i> very feeble or weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पवयस्
स्वल्प + -वयस् very young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पविषयः|स्वल्पविषय
स्वल्प + -विषयः<BR>—1 an insignificant matter.<BR>—2 a small part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्ययः|स्वल्पव्यय
स्वल्प + -व्ययः very little expenditure, stinginess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पव्रीड
स्वल्प + -व्रीड <i>a.</i> having little shame, shameless, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पशरीर
स्वल्प + -शरीर <i>a.</i> diminutive, dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पस्मृति
स्वल्प + -स्मृति <i>a.</i> having a short memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पक
स्वल्पक <i>a.</i> Very little, very small or few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पीयस्
स्वल्पीयस् <i>a.</i> Much less, smaller, more minute (compar. of स्वल्प<BR> q. v.); अतः स्वल्पीयसि द्रव्ये यः सोमं पिवति द्विजः Ms. 11. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पिष्ठ
स्वल्पिष्ठ <i>a.</i> Smallest, least, most minute (superl. of स्वल्प q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वशुरः|स्वशुर
स्वशुरः A father-in-law; cf. श्वशुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसा
स्वसा, स्वसृ <i>f.</i> [सू अस्-ऋन्; Uṇ. 2. 97]<BR>—1 A sister; तस्य शक्तिं रणे कार्ष्णिर्मृत्योर्घोरां स्वसामिव Mb. 6. 116. 3;<BR> स्वसारमादाय विदर्भनाथः पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R. 7. 1, 29.<BR>—2 A finger (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृ
स्वसा, स्वसृ <i>f.</i> [सू अस्-ऋन्; Uṇ. 2. 97]<BR>—1 A sister; तस्य शक्तिं रणे कार्ष्णिर्मृत्योर्घोरां स्वसामिव Mb. 6. 116. 3;<BR> स्वसारमादाय विदर्भनाथः पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R. 7. 1, 29.<BR>—2 A finger (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृत्
स्वसृत् <i>a.</i> Going or moving at will or pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्क्
स्वस्क् €1 Ā. (स्वस्कते) See ष्वस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्ति
स्वस्ति <i>f., n.</i> Welfare; समारम्भान्बुभूषेत हतस्वस्तिरकिच्चनः<BR> Mb. 12. 8. 6; जितं त आत्मविद्धुर्य स्वस्तये स्वस्तिरस्तु मे Bhāg. 4. 24. 33.<BR>━<i>ind.</i> A particle meaning ‘may it be well with (one)’, ‘fare-well’,<BR> ‘hail’, ‘adieu’ (with dat.); स्वस्ति तेऽस्त्वान्तरिक्षेभ्यः पार्थिवेभ्यश्च<BR> भारत Mb. 3. 37. 35; स्वस्ति भवते Ś. 2; स्वस्त्यस्तु ते R. 5. 17;<BR> it is also used in expressing oneʼs approbation; (often used at<BR> the beginning of letters).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वस्त्ययनम्, स्वस्तिकर्मन्, स्वस्तिकारः, स्वस्तिदः, स्वस्तिभावः, स्वस्तिमुखः, स्वस्तिवाचकः, स्वस्तिवाचनम्, स्वस्तिवाचनकम्, स्वस्तिवाचनिकम्, स्वस्तिवाच्यम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्त्ययनम्
स्वस्ति + -अयनम्<BR>—1 a means of securing prosperity.<BR>—2 the averting of evil by the recitation of <i>mantras</i> or performance<BR> of expiatory rites.<BR>—3 the benediction of a Brāhmaṇa after presentation of offerings; प्रास्थानिकं<BR> स्वस्त्ययनं प्रयुज्य R. 2. 70. ━<i>a.</i> Auspicious; इदं स्वस्त्ययनं<BR> श्रेष्ठम् Ms. 1. 106; Mb. 1. 75. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकर्मन्
स्वस्ति + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i> causing welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकारः|स्वस्तिकार
स्वस्ति + -कारः a bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिदः|स्वस्तिद
स्वस्ति + -दः, -भावः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिभावः|स्वस्तिभाव
स्वस्ति + -दः, -भावः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमुखः|स्वस्तिमुख
स्वस्ति + -मुखः<BR>—1 a letter.<BR>—2 a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>—3 a bard, panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाचकः|स्वस्तिवाचक
स्वस्ति + -वाचकः benediction, congratulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाचनम्
स्वस्ति + -वाचनम्, -वाचनकम्, -वाचनिकम्<BR>—1 a religious rite preparatory to a sacrifice or any religious or solemn observance.<BR>—2 a complimentary or congratulatory present of flowers &c. to any one<BR> attended with good wishes and blessings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाचनकम्
स्वस्ति + -वाचनम्, -वाचनकम्, -वाचनिकम्<BR>—1 a religious rite preparatory to a sacrifice or any religious or solemn observance.<BR>—2 a complimentary or congratulatory present of flowers &c. to any one<BR> attended with good wishes and blessings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाचनिकम्
स्वस्ति + -वाचनम्, -वाचनकम्, -वाचनिकम्<BR>—1 a religious rite preparatory to a sacrifice or any religious or solemn observance.<BR>—2 a complimentary or congratulatory present of flowers &c. to any one<BR> attended with good wishes and blessings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिवाच्यम्
स्वस्ति + -वाच्यम् congratulation, invoking blessings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकः|स्वस्तिक
स्वस्तिकः [स्वस्ति शुभाय हितं क]<BR>—1 A kind of mystical mark (卐) on persons or things denoting good luck.<BR>—2 A lucky object.<BR>—3 The meeting of four roads.<BR>—4 The crossing of the arms, making a sign like the cross; स्तनविनिहितहस्तस्वस्तिकाभिर्वधूभिः<BR> Māl. 4. 10; Śi. 10. 43.<BR>—5 A palace of particular form.<BR>—6 A particular symbol made with ground rice and shaped like a triangle.<BR>—7 A kind of cake.<BR>—8 A voluptuary, libertine.<BR>—9 Garlic.<BR>—10 A kind of bard (who utters words of eulogy); पुरःसरैः स्वस्तिकसूतमागधैः<BR> Rām. 2. 16. 46 (com. स्वस्तिका जयजयेति वादिनो वन्दिनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकः|स्वस्तिक
स्वस्तिकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A mansion or temple of a particular form with a terrace in front.<BR>—2 A particular mode of sitting practised by <i>Yogins</i> (in which<BR> the toes are placed in the inner hollow of the knees).<BR>—3 A seat (पीठ) prepared for a deity; Mb. 12. 40. 7 (com. स्वस्तिकान्<BR> सर्वतोभद्राद्यङ्कितानि देवतापीठानि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वस्तिककर्ण, स्वस्तिकपाणि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकम्
स्वस्तिकः + .{@-कः, -कम्@}<BR>—1 A mansion or temple of a particular form with a terrace in front.<BR>—2 A particular mode of sitting practised by <i>Yogins</i> (in which<BR> the toes are placed in the inner hollow of the knees).<BR>—3 A seat (पीठ) prepared for a deity; Mb. 12. 40. 7 (com. स्वस्तिकान्<BR> सर्वतोभद्राद्यङ्कितानि देवतापीठानि).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वस्तिककर्ण, स्वस्तिकपाणि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिककर्ण
स्वस्तिकः + -कर्ण <i>a.</i> marked on the ear with the figure स्वस्तिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकपाणि
स्वस्तिकः + -पाणि <i>a.</i><BR>—1 crossing hands like स्वस्तिक.<BR>—2 holding auspicious things in hands; श्रुत्वा चेदं वचनं पार्थिवस्य<BR> सर्वं पुरं स्वस्तिकपाणिभूतम् Mb. 4. 68. 27 (com. स्वस्तिकं मङ्गलारार्तिकादि<BR> दधिदूर्वादि च पाणौ यस्य तत् स्वस्तिकपाणिभ्तम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमत्|स्वस्तिमन्त्
स्वस्तिमत् <i>a.</i> Doing well, happy, safe; भूतानुकम्पा तव चेदियं<BR> गौरेका भवेत् स्वस्तिमती त्वदन्ते R. 2. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1741-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रीयः|स्वस्रीय
