स्वादु + -फलम् + .({@-ला@}) the jujube tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुमूलम्
स्वादु + -मूलम् a carrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुरसा
स्वादु + -रसा<BR>—1 the fruit of the hog-plum.<BR>—2 the Śatāvarī plant.<BR>—3 the root काकोली.<BR>—4 spirituous liquor.<BR>—5 a grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुलुङ्गी
स्वादु + -लुङ्गी the sweet citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादुशुद्धम्
स्वादु + -शुद्धम्<BR>—1 rock-salt.<BR>—2 marine-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्यम्
स्वाद्यम्<BR>—1 Astringent and salt taste.<BR>—2 = रसः q. v.; रूपं ज्योतिः शब्द आकाशवायुः स्पर्शः स्वाद्यं<BR> सलिलं गन्ध उर्वी Mb. 7. 201. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्वी
स्वाद्वी Vine, grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानः|स्वान
स्वानः Sound, noise; रामस्वनितसंकाशः स्वान इत्यवदत् स ताम् Bk. 5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापः|स्वाप
स्वापः [स्वप्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Sleep, sleeping; स्वापहेतुरनुपाश्रितो ऽन्यया रामबाहुरुपधानमेष<BR> ते U. 1. 37.<BR>—2 Dreaming, dream.<BR>—3 Sleepiness, sloth.<BR>—4 Paralysis, palsy, insensibility.<BR>—5 Temporary or partial loss of sensation from pressure on a nerve, numbness.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वापव्यसनम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापव्यसनम्
स्वापः + -व्यसनम्<BR>—1 Somnolency.<BR>—2 Lethargy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापक
स्वापक <i>a.</i> Soporiferous, soporific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापतेयम्
स्वापतेयम् [स्वपतेरागतं ढञ्] Wealth, property; स्वापतेयकृते<BR> मर्त्याः किं किं नाम न कुर्वते Pt. 2. 156; Śi. 14. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापदः|स्वापद
स्वापदः See श्वापद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाप्न
स्वाप्न <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Relating to sleep or dream.<BR>—2 Dreamy; तं सप्रपञ्चमधिरूढसमाधियोगः स्वाप्नं पुनर्न भजते<BR> प्रतिबुद्धवस्तुः Bhāg. 11. 13. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाविक|स्वाभाविकः
स्वाभाविक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्वभावादागतः ढञ्] Belonging to oneʼs own nature,<BR> innate, inherent, peculiar, natural; स्वाभाविकं विनीतत्वं तेषां विनयकर्मणा ।<BR> मुमूर्च्छ सहजं तेजो हविषेव हविर्भुजाम् R. 10. 79, 5. 69; Ku. 6. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाविकाः
स्वाभाविक + .{@-काः@} <i>m.</i> pl. A sect of Buddhists who accounted for all things<BR> by the laws of nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाव्यम्
स्वाभाव्यम् Naturalness, natural state or character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभास
स्वाभास <i>a.</i> Very illustrious or splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभील
स्वाभील <i>a.</i> Very formidable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिन्
स्वामिन् <i>a.</i> (-नी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [स्व-अस्त्यर्थे मिनि दीर्घः] Possessing proprietory<BR> rights. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A proprietor, an owner.<BR>—2 A lord, master; रघुस्वामिनः सच्चरित्रम् Vikr. 18. 107.<BR>—4 A sovereign, king, monarch.<BR>—5 A husband.<BR>—6 A spiritual preceptor.<BR>—7 A learned Brāhmaṇa, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">Page1743-1</a>]<BR> ascetic or religious man of the highest order; (in this sense usually<BR> added to proper names).<BR>—8 An epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>—9 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>—10 Of Śiva.<BR>—11 Of the sage Vātsyāyana.<BR>—12 Of Garuḍa.<BR>—13 The sacrificer, the owner (at a याग); योऽर्थी स्वत्यागेन ऋत्विजः<BR> परिक्रीणीते, यश्च स्वं प्रदेयं त्यजति स स्वामी ŚB. on MS. 6. 3. 21;<BR> तस्मान्न स्वामिनः प्रतिनिधिः ibid.<BR>—14 The image or temple of a god.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वाम्युपकारकः, स्वामिगुणः, स्वामिजङ्घिन्, स्वामिजनकः, स्वामिपालः,^1 स्वामिभट्टारकः, स्वामिभावः, स्वामिमूल, स्वामिवात्सल्यम्, स्वामिसद्भावः, स्वामिसेवा<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1742-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्युपकारकः|स्वाम्युपकारक
स्वामिन् + -उपकारकः a horse. {@कार्यम्@} the business of a king or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिगुणः|स्वामिगुण
स्वामिन् + -गुणः the virtue of a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिजङ्घिन्
स्वामिन् + -जङ्घिन् <i>m.</i> N. of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिजनकः|स्वामिजनक
स्वामिन् + -जनकः the father-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिपालः|स्वामिपाल
स्वामिन् + -पालः^1 <i>m.</i> du. the owner and the keeper (of cattle); क्रयविक्रयानुशयो<BR> विवादः स्वामिपालयोः Ms. 8. 5.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिभट्टारकः|स्वामिभट्टारक
स्वामिन् + -भट्टारकः a noble lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिभावः|स्वामिभाव
स्वामिन् + -भावः the state of a lord or owner, ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिमूल
स्वामिन् + -मूल <i>a.</i> originating in or derived from a master or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिवात्सल्यम्
स्वामिन् + -वात्सल्यम् affection for the husband or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिसद्भावः|स्वामिसद्भाव
स्वामिन् + -सद्भावः<BR>—1 existence of a master or owner.<BR>—2 goodness of a master or lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिसेवा
स्वामिन् + -सेवा<BR>—1 the service of a master.<BR>—2 respect for a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिता
स्वामिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Ownership, mastership, proprietory right.<BR>—2 Lordship, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामित्वम्
स्वामिता, -त्वम्<BR>—1 Ownership, mastership, proprietory right.<BR>—2 Lordship, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिनी
स्वामिनी A mistress, proprietress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्यम्
स्वाम्यम्<BR>—1 Mastership, lordship, ownership; स्वाम्यं च न स्यात् कस्मिंश्चित् प्रवर्तेताधरोत्तरम् Ms. 7. 21.<BR>—2 Right or title to property.<BR>—3 Rule, supremacy, dominion.<BR>—4 Sound state (of body and soul); स्वाम्ये प्रयत्नं कुर्वन्ति त्रयो वर्गा<BR> यथाविधि Mb. 12. 69. 78 (com. स्वाम्ये स्वास्थ्ये).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्नाय
स्वाम्नाय <i>a.</i> Well handed down by tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायत्त
स्वायत्त <i>a.</i> Dependent on oneʼs self, within oneʼs own control;<BR> स्वायत्तमेकान्तगुणं विधात्रा विनिर्मितं छादनमज्ञतायाः Bh. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायंभुव|स्वायम्भुव|स्वायंभुवः|स्वायम्भुवः
स्वायंभुव <i>a.</i> (-वी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Relating to Brahman; तुरासाहं पुरोधाय धाम स्वायंभुवं ययुः Ku. 2. 1.<BR>—2 Descended from Brahman; स्वायंभुवान्मरीचेर्यः प्रबभूव प्रजापतिः Ś. 7. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायंभुवः|स्वायम्भुव|स्वायंभुव|स्वायम्भुवः
स्वायंभुव + .{@-वः@} An epithet of the first Manu (as he was a son of Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारसिक
स्वारसिक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Possessing inherent flavour or sweetness (said of a poetical composition).<BR>—2 Voluntary, spontaneous; विधेरपि स्वारसिकः प्रयासः परस्परं योग्यसमागमाय N. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारस्यम्
स्वारस्यम्<BR>—1 Possessing natural flavour or excellence.<BR>—2 Elegance, fitness.<BR>—3 Naturalness, self-evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्
स्वाराज् <i>m.</i>, स्वाराज्यः An epithet of Indra; भवान् भक्तिमता<BR> लभ्यो दुर्लभः सर्वदेहिनाम् । स्वाराज्यस्याप्यभिमत एकान्तेनात्मविद्गतिः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 24. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्यः|स्वाराज्य|स्वाराज्यं
स्वाराज् <i>m.</i>, स्वाराज्यः An epithet of Indra; भवान् भक्तिमता<BR> लभ्यो दुर्लभः सर्वदेहिनाम् । स्वाराज्यस्याप्यभिमत एकान्तेनात्मविद्गतिः<BR> Bhāg. 4. 24. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्यम्
स्वाराज्यम्<BR>—1 The dominion of heaven, Indraʼs heaven; न वयं साध्वि साम्राज्यं<BR> स्वाराज्यं भोज्यमप्युत Bhāg. 10. 83. 41; Ait. Br.<BR>—2 Identification with the self-refulgent<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">Page1743-2</a>]<BR> (Brāhman) (ब्रह्मत्व); समं पश्यन्नात्मयाजी स्वाराज्यमधिगच्छति<BR> Ms. 12. 91; Bhāg. 7. 15. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिषः|स्वारोचिष
स्वारोचिषः, -स्वारोचिस् <i>m.</i><BR> N. of the second Manu; see under मनुः स्वारोचिषो<BR> द्वितीयस्तु मनुरग्नेः सुतोऽभवत् Bhāg. 8. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिस्
स्वारोचिषः, -स्वारोचिस् <i>m.</i><BR> N. of the second Manu; see under मनुः स्वारोचिषो<BR> द्वितीयस्तु मनुरग्नेः सुतोऽभवत् Bhāg. 8. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वालक्षण
स्वालक्षण <i>a.</i> Easily perceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वालक्षण्यम्
स्वालक्षण्यम् Peculiar characteristics, natural disposition; स्वालक्षण्यपरीक्षार्थं<BR> तासां श्रृणुत निष्कृतीः Ms. 9. 19; स्वालक्षण्यं वृत्तिः Sāṅ. K. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्प
स्वाल्प <i>a.</i> (-ल्पी <i>f.</i>)<BR>—1 Little, small.<BR>—2 Few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्पम्
स्वाल्प + .{@-ल्पम्@}<BR>—1 Littleness, smallness.<BR>—2 Smallness of number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वावश्यम्
स्वावश्यम् Self-determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाशित
स्वाशित <i>a.</i> Well fed or satiated; आशंसे स्वाशिता सेना वत्स्यत्येनां<BR> विभावरीम् Rām. 2. 84. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाश्लिष्
स्वाश्लिष् €4 P. To embrace closely; गुरुतल्प्यभिभाष्यैनस्तप्ते स्वप्यादयोमये ।<BR> सूर्मी ज्वलन्तीं स्वाश्लिष्येन्मृत्युना स विशुध्यति ॥ Ms. 11. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्तरः|स्वास्तर
स्वास्तरः Good straw for a couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्थ्यम्
स्वास्थ्यम्<BR>—1 Self-reliance, self-dependence.<BR>—2 Fortitude, resoluteness, firmness; स्वास्थ्यं भद्र भजस्वार्य त्यज्यतां<BR> कृपणा मतिः Rām. 4. 1. 120.<BR>—3 Sound state, health.<BR>—4 Prosperity, well-being, comfortableness.<BR>—5 Ease, satisfaction, spirits; लब्धं मया स्वास्थ्यम् Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा<BR>—1 An oblation or offering made to all gods indiscriminately.<BR>—2 N. of the wife of <i>Agni</i>; स्वाहा चैव विभावसोः (पतिदेवता)<BR> Mb. 13. 146. 5. ━<i>ind.</i> An exclamation used in offering oblations to<BR> the gods (with dat.); इन्द्राय स्वाहा; अग्नये स्वाहा &c.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वाहाकारः, स्वाहापतिः, स्वाहाप्रियः, स्वाहाभुज्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाकारः|स्वाहाकार
स्वाहा + -कारः utterance of the exclamation Svāhā; स्वाहास्वधाकारविवर्जितानि<BR> श्मशानतुल्यानि गृहाणि तानि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहापतिः|स्वाहापति
स्वाहा + -पतिः, -प्रियः <i>Agni</i> or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाप्रियः|स्वाहाप्रिय
स्वाहा + -पतिः, -प्रियः <i>Agni</i> or fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहाभुज्
स्वाहा + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् <i>ind.</i> A particle of interrogation or inquiry, often implying<BR> ‘doubt’, or ‘surprise’, and translatable by ‘what’, ‘hey’, ‘hallo’, ‘can it be that’<BR>. It is added to interrogative pronouns in this sense or to<BR> give an indefinite sense; कास्विदवगुण्ठनवती नातिपरिस्फुटशरीरलावण्या<BR> Ś. 5. 13; Me. 14. It is sometimes used disjunctively in the sense of<BR> ‘either’, ‘or’, with नु, उत, वा &c.; सरोजपत्रे नु विलीनषट्पदे<BR> विलोलदृष्टेः स्विदमू विलोचने । शिरोरुहाः स्विन्नतपक्ष्मसंततेर्द्विरेफवृन्दं<BR> नु निशब्दनिश्चलम् ॥ Ki. 8. 35, 12. 15, 13. 8, 14. 60; see आहो also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् I. €4 P. (स्विद्यति, स्विदित or स्विन्न) To sweat, perspire;<BR> तदा मोहमनुप्राप्तः सिष्विदे हि जनार्दनः Mb. 7. 27. 20; स्विद्यति<BR> कूणति वेल्लति K. P. 10; U. 3. 41; Ku. 7. 77; Māl. 1. 35; स त्वां<BR> पश्यति कम्पते पुलकयत्यानन्दति स्विद्यति Gīt. 11. ━II. €1 Ā. (स्वेदते,<BR> स्विन्न or स्वेदित)<BR>—1 To be anointed.<BR>—2 To be greasy or unctuous; निष्टापस्विद्यदस्थ्नः क्वथनपरिणमन्मेदसः प्रेतकायान्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">Page1744-1</a>]<BR> Māl. 5. 17.<BR>—3 To be disturbed. ━<i>Caus.</i> (स्वेदयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to perspire.<BR>—2 To heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1743-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् (In comp.) Sweating, perspiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विदित|स्विदितः
स्विदित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Sweated, perspired.<BR>—2 Melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विन्न|स्विन्नः
स्विन्न <i>p. p.</i> [स्विद्-क्त]<BR>—1 Perspiring, covered with sweat.<BR>—2 Seethed.<BR>—3 Cooked, boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विष्ट
स्विष्ट <i>a.</i> Much desired or loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विष्टि
स्विष्टि <i>a.</i> Sacrificing well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृ
स्वीकृ €8 U.<BR>—1 To make oneʼs own, appropriate, claim.<BR>—2 To take, accept.<BR>—3 To admit, grant, assume (in argument).<BR>—4 To assent or agree to, accede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरणम्
स्वीकरणम्, स्वीकारः, स्वीकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Taking, accepting.<BR>—2 Assenting, agreeing, promising, an assent, a promise.<BR>—3 Espousal, wedding, marriage; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकारः|स्वीकार
स्वीकरणम्, स्वीकारः, स्वीकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Taking, accepting.<BR>—2 Assenting, agreeing, promising, an assent, a promise.<BR>—3 Espousal, wedding, marriage; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृतिः|स्वीकृति
स्वीकरणम्, स्वीकारः, स्वीकृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Taking, accepting.<BR>—2 Assenting, agreeing, promising, an assent, a promise.<BR>—3 Espousal, wedding, marriage; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय <i>a.</i> Own, oneʼs own; लोकालोकविसारि तेन विहितं स्वीयं<BR> विशुद्धं यशः S. D. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वुर्च्छ्
स्वुर्च्छ् €1 P. (स्वूर्च्छति)<BR>—1 To spread, extend.<BR>—2 To forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ €1 P. (स्वरति; <i>desid.</i> सिस्वरिषति, सुस्वूर्षति)<BR>—1 To sound, recite; यदा वा ऋचमाप्नोत्योमित्येवातिस्वरति Ch. Up. 1. 4. 4.<BR>—2 To praise.<BR>—3 To pain or be pained.<BR>—4 To go. ━<i>With</i> {@अभि, प्र@} to sound. ━{@सम्@} to pain (Ātm.); द्रुतं<BR> संस्वरिषीष्ठास्त्वं निर्भयः प्रधनोत्तमे Bk. 9. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वॄ
स्वॄ €9 P. (स्वृणाति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेक्
स्वेक् €1 Ā. (स्वेकते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदः|स्वेद
स्वेदः [स्विद्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Sweat, perspiration; अङ्गुलिस्वेदेन दूष्येरन्नक्षराणि V. 2.<BR>—2 Heat, warmth.<BR>—3 Vapour.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वेदोदम्, स्वेदोदकम्, स्वेदजलम्, स्वेदचूषकः, स्वेदच्छिद, स्वेदज, स्वेदमातृ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदोदम्
स्वेदः + -उदम्, -उदकम्, -जलम् perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदोदकम्
स्वेदः + -उदम्, -उदकम्, -जलम् perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदजलम्
स्वेदः + -उदम्, -उदकम्, -जलम् perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदचूषकः|स्वेदचूषक
स्वेदः + -चूषकः a cooling breeze (sucking up sweat).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदच्छिद
स्वेदः + -च्छिद <i>a.</i> cooling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदज|स्वेदजः
स्वेदः + -ज <i>a.</i> generated by warm vapour or sweat (said of insects).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदमातृ
स्वेदः + -मातृ <i>f.</i> Chyle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनम्
स्वेदनम् [स्विद्-णिच्-ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Perspiration, sweat.<BR>—2 Causing to sweat.<BR>—3 A diaphoretic.<BR>—4 A kind of process to which quicksilver is subjected.<BR>—5 Mucus.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वेदनयन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनयन्त्रम्
स्वेदनम् + -यन्त्रम् a steam-bath (for metals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनिका
स्वेदनिका<BR>—1 A boiler, sauce-pan.<BR>—2 Kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनी
स्वेदनी A frying-pan, sauce-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदित
स्वेदित <i>a.</i> Fomented, softened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर <i>a.</i> [स्वस्य ईरम् ईर्-अच् वृद्धिः]<BR>—1 Following oneʼs own will or fancy, self-willed, wanton, uncontrolled,<BR> unrestrained; बद्धमिव स्वैरगतिर्जनमिह सुखसंगिनमवैमि Ś. 5. 11;<BR> अव्याहतैः स्वैरगतैः स तस्याः R. 2. 5.<BR>—2 Free, unreserved, confidential; सत्त्वभङ्गभयाद्राज्ञां कथयन्त्यन्यथा<BR> पुरः । अन्यथा विवृतार्थेषु स्वैरालापेषु मन्त्रिणः ॥ Mu. 4. 8.<BR>—3 Slow, mild, gentle; Mu. 1. 2.<BR>—4 Dull, lazy.<BR>—5 Dependent on oneʼs will, voluntary, optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरम्
स्वैर + .{@-रम्@} Wilfulness, wantonness; तत्रापि निरवरोधः स्वैरेण विहरन्<BR> Bhāg. 5. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरम्
स्वैर + .{@-रम्@} ━<i>ind.</i><BR>—1 At will or pleasure, as one likes, at perfect ease; सार्थाः स्वैरं<BR> स्वकीयेषु चेरुर्वेश्मस्विवाद्रिषु R. 17. 64.<BR>—2 Of oneʼs own accord, spontaneously.<BR>—3 Slowly, gently, mildly; मोहे मोहे रामभद्रस्य जीवं स्वैरं स्वैरं<BR> प्रेरितैस्तर्पयेति U. 3. 2.<BR>—4 Lowly, in an under-tone, inaudibly (opp. स्पष्ट); पश्चात्स्वैरं<BR> गज इति किल व्याहृतं सत्यवाचा Ve. 3. 9.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: स्वैरालापः, स्वैरकथा, स्वैरचारिन्, स्वैरविहारिन्, स्वैरवृत्त, स्वैरवृत्ति, स्वैराचार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरालापः|स्वैरालाप
स्वैर + -आलापः confidential talk. Mu. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरकथा
स्वैर + -कथा unreserved conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरचारिन्
स्वैर + -चारिन् <i>a.</i> free, independent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरविहारिन्
स्वैर + -विहारिन् <i>a.</i> unimpeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरवृत्त
स्वैर + -वृत्त, -वृत्ति, -आचार <i>a.</i> acting as one likes, following oneʼs<BR> own will, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरवृत्ति
स्वैर + -वृत्त, -वृत्ति, -आचार <i>a.</i> acting as one likes, following oneʼs<BR> own will, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैराचार
स्वैर + -वृत्त, -वृत्ति, -आचार <i>a.</i> acting as one likes, following oneʼs<BR> own will, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरकम्
स्वैरकम् <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 Freely.<BR>—2 Plainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरता
स्वैरता, -त्वम्<BR> Wantonness, freedom of will and action, independence; also<BR> स्वैरिता in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरत्वम्
स्वैरता, -त्वम्<BR> Wantonness, freedom of will and action, independence; also<BR> स्वैरिता in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिणी
स्वैरिणी<BR>—1 A loose or unchaste woman, a wanton woman, an adulteress; स्वैरिणी<BR> या पतिं हित्वा सवर्णं कामतः श्रयेत् Y. 1. 67.<BR>—2 A bat.<BR>—3 A line of ascetics; वाराणस्यामुपातिष्ठन्मैत्रेयं स्वैरिणीकुले Mb. 13. 120. 3<BR> (com. स्वम् ईरयति धर्माय प्रेरयति स्वैरिणी मुनिश्रेणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्
स्वैरिन् <i>a.</i> Self-willed, wanton, unrestrained, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्ध्री|स्वैरिंध्री
स्वैरिन्ध्री See सैरन्ध्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोरसः|स्वोरस
स्वोरसः<BR>—1 The residue or sediment of oily substances ground with a stone.<BR>—2 A husk, shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोवशीयम्
स्वोवशीयम् Happiness, prosperity (especially as regards future life).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1744-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह <i>ind.</i> An emphatic particle used to lay stress on the preceding<BR> word and translatable by ‘verily’, ‘indeed’, ‘certainly’, &c.; but it<BR> is often used expletively without any particular signification, especially<BR> in Vedic literature; तस्य ह शतं जाया बभूवुः; तस्य ह पर्वतनारदौ<BR> गृह ऊषतुः &c. Ait. Br.; द्वया ह प्राजापत्या देवाश्चासुराश्च Bṛ. Up. 1. 3. 1.<BR> It is sometimes used as a vocative particle and rarely of<BR> disdain or laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हः|ह|हं
ह + .{@-हः@}<BR>—1 A form of Śiva.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 Sky.<BR>—4 Blood.<BR>—5 A cipher.<BR>—6 Meditation.<BR>—7 Auspiciousness.<BR>—8 Paradise.<BR>—9 Heaven.<BR>—10 Drying.<BR>—11 Fear.<BR>—12 Knowledge.<BR>—13 The moon.<BR>—14 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—15 War, battle.<BR>—16 A horse.<BR>—17 Pride.<BR>—18 Horripilation.<BR>—19 A physician.<BR>—20 Cause, motive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्
ह + .{@-हम्@}<BR>—1 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>—2 Pleasure, delight.<BR>—3 A weapon.<BR>—4 The sparkling of a gem.<BR>—5 The sound of a lute. (<i>m.</i> also according to some in these senses.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसः|हंस
हंसः [हस्-अच्-पृषो˚ वर्णागमः] (said to be derived from हस्;<BR> cf. भवेद्वर्णागमाद् हंसः Sk.)<BR>—1 A swan, goose, duck; हंसाः संप्रति पाण्डवा इव वनादज्ञातचर्यां<BR> गताः Mk. 5. 6; न शोभते सभामध्ये हंसमध्ये बको यथा Subhāṣ.;<BR> R. 17. 25. (The description of this bird, as given by Sanskrit writers,<BR> is more poetical than real; he is described as forming the vehicle of<BR> the god Brahman, and as ready to fly towards the Mānasa lake at the approach<BR> of rains; cf. मानस. According to a very general poetical convention<BR> he is represented as being gifted with the peculiar power of separating<BR> milk from water <i>e. g.</i> सारं ततो ग्राह्यमपास्य फल्गु हंसो यथा<BR> क्षीरमिवाम्बुमध्यात् Pt. 1; हंसो हि क्षीरमादत्ते तन्मिश्रा वर्जयत्यपः<BR> Ś. 6. 28; नीरक्षीरविवेके हंसालस्यं त्वमेव तनुषे चेत् । विश्वस्मिन्नधुनान्यः<BR> कुलव्रतं पालयिष्यति कः Bv. 1. 13; see Bh. 2. 18 also).<BR>—2 The Supreme Soul, Brahman.<BR>—3 The individual soul (जीवात्मन्); प्रीणीहि हंसशरणं विरमक्रमेण<BR> Bhāg. 4. 29. 56.<BR>—4 One of the vital airs.<BR>—5 The sun; हंसः शुचिषद्वसुरन्तरिक्षसद्धोता वेदिषत् Kaṭh. 2. 5. 2;<BR> उषसि हंसमुदीक्ष्य हिमानिकाविपुलवागुरया परियन्त्रितम् Rām. Ch. 4. 91.<BR>—6 Śiva.<BR>—7 Viṣṇu.<BR>—8 Kāmadeva.<BR>—9 An unambitious monarch.<BR>—10 An ascetic of a particular order; Bhāg. 3. 12. 43.<BR>—11 A spiritual preceptor; Bhāg. 7. 9. 18.<BR>—12 One free from malice, a pure person.<BR>—13 A mountain.<BR>—14 Envy, malice.<BR>—15 A buffalo.<BR>—16 A horse.<BR>—17 A particular incantation; L. D. B.<BR>—18 The best of its kind (at the end of a compound; cf. कविहंस); L. D. B.<BR>—19 A temple of a particular form.<BR>—20 Silver. ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 moving, going (गतिमान्); नवद्वारं पुरं गत्वा हंसो हि नियतो<BR> वशी Mb. 12. 239. 31 (see com.).<BR>—2 Pure; हंसाय संयतगिरे निगमेश्वराय Bhāg. 12. 8. 47, 6. 4. 26.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">Page1745-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाः
हंसः + .{@-साः@} (<i>m.</i> pl.) N. of a tribe said to live in the Plakṣa-Dvīpa.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हंसांशु^1, हंसाङ्घ्रिः, हंसाधिरूढा, हंसाभिख्यम्, हंसारूढः, हंसोदकम्, हंसकान्ता, हंसकालीतनयः, हंसकीलकः, हंसनीलकः, हंसकूटः, हंसगति, हंसगद्गदा, हंसगामिनी, हंसगुह्यम्, हंसच्छत्रम्, हंसतूलः, हंसतूलम्, हंसदाहनम्, हंसनादः, हंसनादिनी, हंसपक्षः, हंसपदः, हंसपादम्, हंसबीजम्, हंसमाला, हंसयानम्, हंसयुवन्, हंसरथः, हंसवाहनः, हंसराजः, हंसलिपिः, हंसलोमशम्, हंसलोहकम्, हंसश्रेणी<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसांशु
हंसः + -अंशु^1 <i>a.</i> white.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8089dd2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाङ्घ्रिः|हंसाङ्घ्रि
हंसः + -अङ्घ्रिः vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाधिरूढा
हंसः + -अधिरूढा an epithet of Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसाभिख्यम्
हंसः + -अभिख्यम् silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसारूढः|हंसारूढ
हंसः + -आरूढः N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसोदकम्
हंसः + -उदकम् a kind of cordial liquor (prepared from infusion of cardamoms).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकान्ता|हंसकांता
हंसः + -कान्ता a female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकालीतनयः|हंसकालीतनय
हंसः + -कालीतनयः a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकीलकः|हंसकीलक
हंसः + -कीलकः, -नीलकः a particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनीलकः|हंसनीलक
हंसः + -कीलकः, -नीलकः a particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकूटः|हंसकूट
हंसः + -कूटः<BR>—1 N. of one of the peaks of the Himālaya.<BR>—2 the hump on the shoulder of an ox (for अंसकूट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगति
हंसः + -गति <i>a.</i> having a swanʼs gait, stalking in a stately manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगद्गदा
हंसः + -गद्गदा a sweetly speaking woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगामिनी
हंसः + -गामिनी<BR>—1 a woman having graceful gait like that of a swan; अव्यङ्गाङ्गीं सौम्यनाम्नीं<BR> हंसवारणगामिनीम् (उद्वहेत् स्त्रियम्) Ms. 3. 10.<BR>—2 N. of Brahmāṇi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसगुह्यम्
हंसः + -गुह्यम् N. of a particular hymn; अस्तौषीद्धंसगुह्येन भगवन्तमधोक्षजम्<BR> Bhāg. 6. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसच्छत्रम्
हंसः + -च्छत्रम् dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसतूलः|हंसतूल
हंसः + -तूलः, -तूलम् the soft feathers or down of a goose; रत्नखचितहेमपर्यङ्के<BR> हंसतूलगर्भशयनमानीय Dk. 1. 4, 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसतूलम्
हंसः + -तूलः, -तूलम् the soft feathers or down of a goose; रत्नखचितहेमपर्यङ्के<BR> हंसतूलगर्भशयनमानीय Dk. 1. 4, 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसदाहनम्
हंसः + -दाहनम् aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनादः|हंसनाद
हंसः + -नादः the cackling of a goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसनादिनी
हंसः + -नादिनी a woman of a particular class (described as having a slender<BR> waist, large hips, the gait of an elephant and the voice of a cuckoo;<BR> गजेन्द्रगमना तन्वी कोकिलालापसंयुता । नितम्बे गुर्विणी या स्यात् सा स्मृता<BR> हंसनादिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपक्षः|हंसपक्ष
हंसः + -पक्षः a particular position of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपदः|हंसपद
हंसः + -पदः a particular weight (कर्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसपादम्
हंसः + -पादम्<BR>—1 vermilion.<BR>—2 quick-silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसबीजम्
हंसः + -बीजम् a gooseʼs egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसमाला
हंसः + -माला a flight of swans; तां हंसमालाः शरदीव गङ्गाम् Ku. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसयानम्
हंसः + -यानम् a car drawn by swans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसयुवन्
हंसः + -युवन् <i>m.</i> a young goose or swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसरथः|हंसरथ
हंसः + -रथः, -वाहनः epithets of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसवाहनः|हंसवाहन
हंसः + -रथः, -वाहनः epithets of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसराजः|हंसराज
हंसः + -राजः a king of geese, a large gander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलिपिः|हंसलिपि
हंसः + -लिपिः a particular mode of writing (with Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोमशम्
हंसः + -लोमशम् green sulphate of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसलोहकम्
हंसः + -लोहकम् brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसश्रेणी
हंसः + -श्रेणी a line of geese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकः|हंसक
हंसकः<BR>—1 A goose, flamingo.<BR>—2 An ornament for the ankles (नूपुर or पादकटक); सरित<BR> इव सविभ्रमप्रपातप्रणदितहंसकभूषणा विरेजुः Śi. 7. 23 (where<BR> the word is used in the first sense also); Dk. 2. 5; पादलग्नेनेव कलहंसयुगेन<BR> हंसकयुगलेन परिष्कृताभ्यां पादकमलाभ्यां … … Cola-Campū. p. 6.<BR>—3 A particular beating of time in music; L. D. B. See हंस above<BR> for other senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिका
हंसिका, हंसी A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसी
हंसिका, हंसी A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिरः|हंसिर
हंसिरः A kind of mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A vocative particle corresponding to, ‘ho’, ‘hallo’; हंहो चिन्मयचित्तचन्द्रमणयः<BR> संवर्धयध्वं रसान् Candr. 1. 2.<BR>—2 A particle expressing haughtiness, contempt or wonder; तां गामृषिः<BR> स्यूमरश्मिः प्रविश्य यतिमब्रवीत् । हंहो वेदा यदि मता धर्माः केनापरे<BR> मताः ॥ Mb. 12. 268. 9.<BR>—3 A particle of interrogation. (In dramas it is mostly used as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1746-1" target="_blank">Page1746-1</a>]<BR> form of address by characters of the middling class; हंहो ब्राह्मण<BR> मा कुप्य Mu. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1745-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

