हनुस्वनः|हनुस्वन
हनु + -स्वनः sound made with the jaws.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1747-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुका
हनुका A jaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1747-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमत्|हनुमन्त्
हनुमत् (-नूमत्) <i>m.</i><BR> N. of a powerful monkey-chief. [He was the son<BR> of Añjanā by the god Wind or Marut and hence called Māruti. He is represented<BR> as a monkey of extraordinary strength and prowess which he manifested<BR> on several critical occasions on behalf of Rāma whom he regarded as the<BR> idol of his heart. When Sītā was carried off by Rāvaṇa, he crossed<BR> the sea and brought news about her to his lord. He played a very important<BR> part in the great war at Laṅkā.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हनुमत्कवचम्, हनुमज्जयन्ती<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1747-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूमत्|हनूमन्त्
हनुमत् (-नूमत्) <i>m.</i><BR> N. of a powerful monkey-chief. [He was the son<BR> of Añjanā by the god Wind or Marut and hence called Māruti. He is represented<BR> as a monkey of extraordinary strength and prowess which he manifested<BR> on several critical occasions on behalf of Rāma whom he regarded as the<BR> idol of his heart. When Sītā was carried off by Rāvaṇa, he crossed<BR> the sea and brought news about her to his lord. He played a very important<BR> part in the great war at Laṅkā.]<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हनुमत्कवचम्, हनुमज्जयन्ती<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1747-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमत्कवचम्
हनुमत् + -कवचम् N. of various hymns addressed to हनुमत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1747-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमज्जयन्ती
हनुमत् + -जयन्ती the day of the full moon of Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1747-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूषः|हनूष
हनूषः [हन्-ऊषन् Uṇ. 4. 75] A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्त|हंत
हन्त <i>ind.</i> A particle implying<BR>—1 Joy, surprise, flurry (oh!); हन्त भो लब्धं मया स्वास्थ्यम् Ś. 4;<BR> हन्त प्रवृत्तं संगीतकम् M. 1.<BR>—2 Compassion, pity; पुत्रक हन्त ते धानाकाः G. M.<BR>—3 Grief (oh!, alas!); हन्त धिङ् मामधन्यम् U. 1. 42; स्मरामि<BR> हन्त स्मरामि U. 1; काचमूल्येन विक्रीतो हन्त चिन्तामणिर्मया Śānti. 1. 12;<BR> Me. 106.<BR>—4 Good luck or benediction.<BR>—5 It is often used as an inceptive particle (expressive of an exhortation<BR> to do any thing, or asking attention); हन्तास्मिञ्जन्मनि भवान्न मां<BR> द्रष्टुमिहार्हति Bhāg. 1. 6. 22; Bṛ. Up. 2. 4. 1; हन्त ते कथयिष्यामि Rām.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हन्तोक्तिः, हन्तकारः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तोक्तिः|हन्तोक्ति|हंतोक्ति
हन्त + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> uttering the word ‘alas!’, tenderness, compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्तकारः|हन्तकार|हंतकार
हन्त + -कारः<BR>—1 the exclamation ‘hanta’.<BR>—2 an offering to be presented to a guest; निवीती हन्तकारेण मनुष्यांस्तर्पयेदथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

