हयः + -मेधः a horse sacrifice; सर्वान् कामानवाप्नोति हय-मेधफलं तथा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">Page1748-2</a>]<BR> Y. 1. 181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयवाहनः|हयवाहन
हयः + -वाहनः<BR>—1 an epithet of Kubera.<BR>—2 Revanta, the son of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयशाला
हयः + -शाला a stable for horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयशास्त्रम्
हयः + -शास्त्रम् the art or science of training and managing horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयशिक्षा
हयः + -शिक्षा hippology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयसंग्रहणम्
हयः + -संग्रहणम्, -संयानम् the restraining or curbing of horses;<BR> driving horses; पश्य मे हयसंयाने शिक्षां केशवनन्दन Mb. 3. 19. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयसंयानम्
हयः + -संग्रहणम्, -संयानम् the restraining or curbing of horses;<BR> driving horses; पश्य मे हयसंयाने शिक्षां केशवनन्दन Mb. 3. 19. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयंकषः|हयङ्कष|हयंकष|हयङ्कषः
हयंकषः<BR>—1 A driver, charioteer.<BR>—2 N. of Mātali, the charioteer of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हया
हया, हयी A female horse, mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयी
हया, हयी A female horse, mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयनः|हयन|हयनं
हयनः A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयनम्
हयनः + .{@-नम्@} A covered carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयिः|हयि
हयिः <i>m., f.</i> Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर <i>a.</i> (-रा, -री <i>f.</i>)<BR> [हृ-अच्]<BR>—1 Taking away, removing, depriving one of; as in खेदहर, शोकहर.<BR>—2 Bringing, conveying, carrying, taking; अपथहराः Ki. 5. 50; R. 12. 51.<BR>—3 Seizing, grasping.<BR>—4 Attracting, captivating.<BR>—5 Claiming, entitled to; as in रिक्थहर &c.; परिहृतमयशः पातितमस्मासु<BR> च घातितोऽर्धराज्यहरः Mu. 2. 19.<BR>—6 Occupying; समादिदेशैकवधूं भवित्रीं प्रेम्णा शरीरार्धहरां हरस्य Ku. 1. 50.<BR>—7 Dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरः|हर
हर + .{@-रः@}<BR>—1 Śiva; श्रुताप्सरोगीतिरपि क्षणेऽस्मिन् हरः प्रसंख्यानपरो बभूव<BR> Ku. 3. 40, 67, 1. 50; Me. 7.<BR>—2 N. of Agni or fire.<BR>—3 An ass.<BR>—4 A divisor.<BR>—5 The denominator of a fraction.<BR>—6 The act of seizing, taking.<BR>—7 A seizer, ravisher.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हराद्रिः, हरेश्वरः, हरगौरी, हरचूडामणिः, हरतेजस्, हरनेत्रम्, हरप्रियः, हरबीजम्, हरवल्लभः, हरवाहनः, हरशेखरा, हरसखः, हरसूनुः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हराद्रिः|हराद्रि
हर + -अद्रिः the Kailāsa mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेश्वरः|हरेश्वर
हर + -ईश्वरः Śiva and Viṣṇu forming one person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरगौरी
हर + -गौरी one of the forms of Śiva and Pārvatī conjoined (अर्धनारीनटेश्वर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरचूडामणिः|हरचूडामणि
हर + -चूडामणिः ‘Śivaʼs crest-gem’, the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरतेजस्
हर + -तेजस् <i>n.</i> quick-silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरनेत्रम्
हर + -नेत्रम्<BR>—1 Śivaʼs eye.<BR>—2 the number ‘three’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरप्रियः|हरप्रिय
हर + -प्रियः Nerium Odorum (करवीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरबीजम्
हर + -बीजम् ‘Śivaʼs seed’, quick-silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरवल्लभः
हर + -वल्लभः the white thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरवाहनः
हर + -वाहनः a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरशेखरा
हर + -शेखरा ‘Śivaʼs crest’, the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरसखः|हरसख
हर + -सखः N. of Kubera;<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरसूनुः|हरसूनु
हर + -सूनुः Skanda; व्याजहार हरसूनुसंनिभः R. 11. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरकः|हरक
हरकः<BR>—1 A stealer, thief.<BR>—2 A rogue.<BR>—3 A divisor.<BR>—4 N. of Śiva.<BR>—5 A long flexible sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरणम्
हरणम् [हृ-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>—1 Seizing, taking.<BR>—2 Carrying away, carrying off, removing, stealing; कन्याहरणम् Ms. 3. 33;<BR> धेनुवत्सहरणम् R. 11. 74.<BR>—3 Depriving of, destroying; as in प्राणहरणम्.<BR>—4 Dividing.<BR>—5 A gift to a student.<BR>—6 The arm.<BR>—7 Semen virile.<BR>—8 Gold.<BR>—9 A nuptial present. (= यौतक q. v.); आजग्मुः खाण्डवप्रस्थमादाय<BR> हरणं बहु Mb. 1. 221. 33.<BR>—10 A shell, cowrie.<BR>—11 Boiling water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि <i>a.</i> [हृ-इन्]<BR>—1 Green, greenish-yellow; हरिता हरिभिः शष्पैरिन्द्रगोपैश्च लोहिताः<BR> Bhāg. 10. 20. 11.<BR>—2 Tawny, bay, reddish-brown (कपिल); हरियुग्यं रथं तस्मै प्रजिघाय<BR> पुरंदरः R. 12. 84, 3. 43.<BR>—3 Yellow; महोरगवराहाद्य हरिकेश विभो जय Mb. 6. 65. 52, 3. 42. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिः|हरि
हरि + .{@-रिः@}<BR>—1 N. of Viṣṇu; हरिर्यथैकः पुरुषोत्तमः स्मृतः R. 3. 49.<BR>—2 N. of Indra; प्रजिघाय समाधि-भेदिनीं हरिरस्मै हरिणीं सुराङ्गनाम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">Page1749-1</a>]<BR> R. 8. 79, 3. 55, 68.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR>—4 N. of Brahman.<BR>—5 N. of Yama.<BR>—6 The sun; एवं स्तुतः स भगवान् वाजिरूपधरो हरिः Bhāg. 12. 6. 73.<BR>—7 The moon.<BR>—8 A man.<BR>—9 A ray of light.<BR>—10 Fire.<BR>—11 Wind; तासां तु वचनं श्रुत्वा हरिः परमकोपनः । प्रविश्य सर्वगात्राणि<BR> बभञ्ज भगवान् प्रभुः ॥ Rām. 1. 32. 23.<BR>—12 A lion; करिणामरिणा हरिणा हरिणाली हन्यतां नु कथम् Bv. 1. 50, 51.<BR>—13 A horse; ततः कदाचिद्धरिसंप्रयुक्तं महेन्द्रवाहं सहसोपयातम्<BR> Mb. 3. 165. 1; Śukra. 4. 946.<BR>—14 A horse of Indra; सत्यमतीत्य हरितो हरींश्च वर्तन्ते वाजिनः Ś. 1, 7. 7.<BR>—15 An ape, a monkey; व्यर्थं यत्र कपीन्द्रसख्यमपि मे वीर्यं हरीणां<BR> वृथा U. 3. 45; शत्रुर्वज्रधरात्मजेन हरिणा घोरेण घानिष्यते Mv. 4. 6; R. 12. 57.<BR>—16 The cuckoo.<BR>—17 A frog.<BR>—18 A parrot.<BR>—19 A snake.<BR>—20 The tawny green or yellow colour.<BR>—21 A peacock.<BR>—22 N. of the poet Bhartṛhari.<BR>—23 The sign of the zodiac, Leo.<BR>—24 An organ of sense (इन्द्रिय); युक्ता ह्यस्य हरयः शता दशेति<BR> Bṛ. Up. 2. 5. 19.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हर्यक्षः, हर्यश्वः, हरिकान्त, हरिकेलीयः, हरिकेशः, हरिगणः, हरिगन्धम्, हरिगोपकः, हरिचन्दनः, हरिचन्दनम्, हरिचापः, हरिचापम्, हरितालः, हरितालकः, हरितालिका, हरितुरंगमः, हरिदासः, हरिदिनम्, हरिदिश्, हरिदेवः, हरिद्रवः, हरिद्रुः, हरिद्वारम्, हरिनेत्रम्, हरिपदम्, हरिपर्णम्, हरिप्रियः, हरिप्रिया, हरिबीजम्, हरिभक्तः, हरिभुज्, हरिमन्थः, हरिमन्थकः, हरिमेधः, हरिमेधस्, हरिरोमन्, हरिलोचनः, हरिवंशः, हरिवर्षः, हरिवल्लभा, हरिवासरः, हरिवाहनः, हरिवीजम्, हरिशरः, हरिसखः, हरिसंकीर्तनम्, हरिसुतः, हरिसूनुः, हरिहयः, हरिहरः, हरिहेतिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1748-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यक्षः|हर्यक्ष|हर्य्यक्ष|हर्य्यक्षः
हरि + -अक्षः<BR>—1 a lion. … … हर्यक्षसमविक्रमान् Śiva B. 31. 53.<BR>—2 N. of Kubera.<BR>—3 of Śiva; सशूलमिव हर्यक्षं वने मत्तमिव द्विपम् Mb. 9. 12. 3.<BR>—4 N. of an Asura (हिरण्याक्ष); एवं गदाभ्यां गुर्वीभ्यां हर्यक्षो<BR> हरिरेव च Bhāg. 3. 18. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यश्वः|हर्यश्व|हर्य्यश्व|हर्य्यश्वः
हरि + -अश्वः<BR>—1 Indra; हयाश्च हर्यश्वतुरंगवर्णाः Bhāg. 8. 15. 5.<BR>—2 Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकान्त|हरिकांत
हरि + -कान्त <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dear to Indra.<BR>—2 beautiful as a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकेलीयः|हरिकेलीय
हरि + -केलीयः the country called वङ्ग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकेशः|हरिकेश
हरि + -केशः N. of Śiva; हरिकेशस्तथेत्युक्त्वा भूतानां दोषदर्शिवान्<BR> Mb. 10. 17. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिगणः|हरिगण
हरि + -गणः a troop of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिगन्धम्
हरि + -गन्धम् a kind of sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिगोपकः|हरिगोपक
हरि + -गोपकः cochineal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचन्दनः|हरिचन्दन|हरिचंदन|हरिचन्दनं
हरि + -चन्दनः, -चन्दनम्<BR>—1 a kind of yellow sandal (the wood or tree); ततः प्रकोष्ठे हरिचन्दनाङ्किते<BR> R. 3. 59, 6. 60; Ś. 7. 2; Ku. 5. 69.<BR>—2 one of the five trees of paradise; पञ्चैते देवतरवो मन्दारः पारिजातकः ।<BR> संतानः कल्पवृक्षश्च पुंसि वा हरिचन्दनम् ॥ Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचन्दनम्
हरि + -चन्दनः, -चन्दनम् + .({@-नम्@})<BR>—1 moonlight.<BR>—2 saffron.<BR>—3 the filament of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचन्दनम्
हरि + -चन्दनः, -चन्दनम्<BR>—1 a kind of yellow sandal (the wood or tree); ततः प्रकोष्ठे हरिचन्दनाङ्किते<BR> R. 3. 59, 6. 60; Ś. 7. 2; Ku. 5. 69.<BR>—2 one of the five trees of paradise; पञ्चैते देवतरवो मन्दारः पारिजातकः ।<BR> संतानः कल्पवृक्षश्च पुंसि वा हरिचन्दनम् ॥ Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचापः|हरिचाप
हरि + -चापः, -चापम् a rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिचापम्
हरि + -चापः, -चापम् a rainbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालः|हरिताल|हरितालं
हरि + -तालः (by some regarded as derived from हरित) a kind of<BR> yellow-coloured pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालम्
हरि + -तालः + .({@-लम्@}) yellow orpiment; अचल एष भवानिव राजते स हरितालसमाननवांशुकः<BR> Śi. 4. 21; Ku. 7. 23, 33; पारदं हरितालं च … … Śiva B. 30. 19; H. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताली
हरि + -तालः + .({@-ली@})<BR>—1 the Dūrvā grass.<BR>—2 a streak or line in the sky.<BR>—3 = हरितालिका (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालकः|हरितालक|हरितालकं
हरि + -तालकः a kind of yellow-coloured pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालकम्
हरि + -तालकः + .({@-कम्@})<BR>—1 yellow orpiment.<BR>—2 a theatrical decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितालिका
हरि + -तालिका<BR>—1 the third day of the bright half of Bhādrapada.<BR>—2 the Dūrvā plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितुरंगमः|हरितुरङ्गम
हरि + -तुरंगमः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदासः|हरिदास
हरि + -दासः a worshipper or votary of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदिनम्
हरि + -दिनम् the 11th day (एकादशी) in a fortnight sacred to Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदिश्
हरि + -दिश् <i>f.</i> ‘Indraʼs quarter’, the east.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदेवः|हरिदेव
हरि + -देवः the asterism Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रवः|हरिद्रव
हरि + -द्रवः<BR>—1 a green fluid.<BR>—2 powder of the blossoms of the Nāgakeśara tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रुः|हरिद्रु
हरि + -द्रुः a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्वारम्
हरि + -द्वारम् N. of a celebrated Tīrtha or sacred bathing-place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिनेत्रम्
हरि + -नेत्रम्<BR>—1 the eye of Viṣṇu.<BR>—2 the white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिनेत्रः|हरिनेत्र|हरिनेत्रं
हरि + -नेत्रम् + .({@-त्रः@}) an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिपदम्
हरि + -पदम् the vernal equinox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिपर्णम्
हरि + -पर्णम् a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिप्रियः|हरिप्रिय|हरिप्रियं
हरि + -प्रियः<BR>—1 the <i>Kadamba</i> tree.<BR>—2 a conch-shell.<BR>—3 a fool.<BR>—4 a madman.<BR>—5 Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिप्रियम्
हरि + -प्रियः + .({@-यम्@})<BR>—1 the root Uśīra.<BR>—2 a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">Page1749-2</a>]<BR> sort of sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिप्रिया
हरि + -प्रिया<BR>—1 Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 the sacred basil.<BR>—3 the earth.<BR>—4 the twelfth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिबीजम्
हरि + -बीजम् yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभक्तः|हरिभक्त
हरि + -भक्तः a worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिभुज्
हरि + -भुज् <i>m.</i> a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थः|हरिमन्थ
हरि + -मन्थः, -मन्थकः a chick-pea; Śukra. 4. 969.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्थकः|हरिमन्थक
हरि + -मन्थः, -मन्थकः a chick-pea; Śukra. 4. 969.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमेधः|हरिमेध
हरि + -मेधः, -मेधस् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu; नमो विशुद्धसत्त्वाय हरये<BR> हरिमेधसे Bhāg. 4. 30. 24, 11. 29. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमेधस्
हरि + -मेधः, -मेधस् <i>m.</i> N. of Viṣṇu; नमो विशुद्धसत्त्वाय हरये<BR> हरिमेधसे Bhāg. 4. 30. 24, 11. 29. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिरोमन्
हरि + -रोमन् <i>a.</i> having fair hair on the body, very young; सुवर्णशिरसोऽप्यत्र<BR> हरिरोम्णः प्रगायतः Mb. 5. 110. 12 (com. हरिरोम्णः अपलितस्य नित्यतरुणस्येत्यर्थः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिलोचनः|हरिलोचन
हरि + -लोचनः<BR>—1 a crab.<BR>—2 an owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवंशः|हरिवंश
हरि + -वंशः N. of a celebrated work by Vyāsa supplementary to the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवर्षः|हरिवर्ष|हरिवर्षं
हरि + -वर्षः N. of one of the nine divisions of Jambudvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवल्लभा
हरि + -वल्लभा<BR>—1 Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 the sacred basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवासरः|हरिवासर|हरिवासरं
हरि + -वासरः ‘Viṣṇuʼs day’, the eleventh day of a lunar fortnight (एकादशी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवाहनः|हरिवाहन
हरि + -वाहनः<BR>—1 Garuḍa.<BR>—2 Indra.<BR>—3 N. of the sun. ˚दिश् <i>f.</i> the east; अलकसंयमनादिव लोचने<BR> हरीत मे हरिवाहनदिङ्मुखम् V. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिवीजम्
हरि + -वीजम् yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिशरः|हरिशर
हरि + -शरः an epithet of Śiva (Viṣṇu having served Śiva as the<BR> shaft which burnt down ‘the three cities’ or cities of the demon Tripura).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसखः|हरिसख
हरि + -सखः a <i>Gandharva</i>; सपदि हरिसखैर्वधूनिदेशाद्ध्वनितमनोरमवल्लकीमृदङ्गैः Ki. 10. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसंकीर्तनम्
हरि + -संकीर्तनम् repeating the name of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसुतः|हरिसुत
हरि + -सुतः, -सूनुः N. of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिसूनुः|हरिसूनु
हरि + -सुतः, -सूनुः N. of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहयः|हरिहय
हरि + -हयः<BR>—1 Indra; रक्षसां रुवतां रावं श्रुत्वा हरिहयानुजः Rām. 7. 7. 41;<BR> हरिहयाग्रसरेण धनुर्भृता R. 9. 12.<BR>—2 the sun.<BR>—3 N. of Skanda.<BR>—4 of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहरः|हरिहर
हरि + -हरः a particular form of deity consisting of Viṣṇu and Śiva<BR> conjoined; see हरेश्वरः. ˚आत्मकः<BR>—1 N. of Garuḍa.<BR>—2 of Śivaʼs bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिहेतिः|हरिहेति
हरि + -हेतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 the rain-bow; कथमवलोकयेयमधुना हरिहेतिमतीः (ककुभः) Māl. 9. 18.<BR>—2 the discus of Viṣṇu. ˚हूतिः the ruddy goose; हरिहेतिहूति मिथुनं<BR> पततोः Śi. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकः|हरिक
हरिकः [हरि-संज्ञायां कन्]<BR>—1 A horse of a yellowish or tawny colour.<BR>—2 A thief.<BR>—3 A gambler (with dice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिण|हरिणः
हरिण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [हृ-इनन्]<BR>—1 Pale, whitish; न चाश्वेन विनिर्यासि विवर्णो हरिणः कृशः Mb. 1. 100. 61;<BR> रूपेण पश्ये हरिणेन पश्य N. 22. 134.<BR>—2 Reddish or yellowish white.<BR>—3 Having rays; विश्वरूपं हरिणं जातवेदसम् Praśna. Up. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणः|हरिण
हरिण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 A deer, an antelope; (said to be of five kinds:− हरिणश्चापि विज्ञेयः<BR> पञ्चभेदोऽत्र भैरव । ऋष्यः खड्गो रुरुश्चैव पृषतश्च मृगस्तथा Kālikā P.);<BR> अपि प्रसन्नं हरिणेषु ते मनः Ku. 5. 35.<BR>—2 The white colour.<BR>—3 A goose.<BR>—4 The sun.<BR>—5 Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 Śiva.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हरिणाक्ष, हरिणाङ्कः, हरिणकलङ्कः, हरिणधामन्, हरिणनयन, हरिणनेत्र, हरिणलोचन, हरिणनर्तकः, हरिणलाञ्छनः, हरिणहृदय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाक्ष|हरिणाक्षः
हरिण + -अक्ष <i>a.</i> deer-eyed, fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाक्षः|हरिणाक्ष
हरिण + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षः@}) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाक्षी
हरिण + -अक्ष + .({@-क्षी@} <i>f.</i>) ‘deer-eyed’, a woman with beautiful eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणाङ्कः|हरिणाङ्क|हरिणांक
हरिण + -अङ्कः<BR>—1 the moon.<BR>—2 camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणकलङ्कः|हरिणकलङ्क|हरिणकलंक
हरिण + -कलङ्कः, -धामन् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणधामन्
हरिण + -कलङ्कः, -धामन् <i>m.</i> the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनयन
हरिण + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> deer-eyed, fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनेत्र
हरिण + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> deer-eyed, fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणलोचन
हरिण + -नयन, -नेत्र, -लोचन <i>a.</i> deer-eyed, fawn-eyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणनर्तकः|हरिणनर्तक|हरिणनर्त्तक|हरिणनर्त्तकः
हरिण + -नर्तकः a Kinnara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणलाञ्छनः|हरिणलाञ्छन
हरिण + -लाञ्छनः the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणहृदय|हरिणहृदयः
हरिण + -हृदय <i>a.</i> deer-hearted, timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणकः|हरिणक
हरिणकः<BR>—1 A deer; क्व बत हरिणकानां जीवितं चातिलोलम् Ś. 1. 10.<BR>—2 A small deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1749-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणी
हरिणी<BR>—1 A female deer, doe; चकितहरिणीप्रेक्षणा Me. 84; R. 9. 55, 14. 69.<BR>—2 One of the four classes of women (also called चित्रिणी q. v.).<BR>—3 Yellow jasmine.<BR>—4 A good golden image.<BR>—5 N. of a metre.<BR>—6 The green colour.<BR>—7 Turmeric.<BR>—8 Madder.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हरिणीदृश्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणीदृश्
हरिणी + -दृश् <i>a.</i> deer-eyed. ━(<i>f.</i>) a deer-eyed woman; किमभवद्विपिने<BR> हरिणीदृशः U. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्
हरित् <i>a.</i> [हृ-इति]<BR>—1 Green, greenish.<BR>—2 Yellow, yellowish.<BR>—3 Greenish-yellow. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 The green or yellow colour.<BR>—2 A horse of the sun, a bay horse; सत्यमतीत्य हरितो हरींश्च वर्तन्ते<BR> वाजिनः Ś. 1; दिशो हरिद्भिर्हरितामिवेश्वरः R. 3. 30; Ku. 2. 43.<BR>—3 A swift horse.<BR>—4 A lion.<BR>—5 The sun.<BR>—6 Viṣṇu.<BR>—7 The kidney-bean. ━<i>m., n.</i><BR>—1 Grass.<BR>—2 A quarter, region.<BR>—3 A quarter or point of the compass; प्रायात् प्रतीचीं हरितं विचिन्वंश्च<BR> ततस्ततः Rām. 7. 75. 10; R. 3. 30.<BR>—4 Turmeric (usually <i>f.</i> only in the last 3 senses).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हरिदन्तः, हरिदन्तरम्, हरिदश्वः, हरिद्गर्भः, हरित्पर्णम्, हरित्पतिः, हरिन्मणिः, हरिद्रञ्जनी, हरिद्वर्ण<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदन्तः
हरित् + -अन्तः the end of the quarters (दिगन्त); दृगन्तानाधत्से<BR> किमिति हरिदन्तेषु परुषान् Bv. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदन्तरम्
हरित् + -अन्तरम् different regions, various quarters; आमोदानथ हरिदन्तराणि<BR> नेतुम् Bv. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिदश्वः|हरिदश्व
हरित् + -अश्वः<BR>—1 the sun; प्रविघाटयिता समुत्पतन् हरिदश्वः कमलाकरानिव Ki. 2. 46;<BR> R. 3. 22, 18. 23; Śi. 11. 56.<BR>—2 the <i>arka</i> plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्गर्भः|हरिद्गर्भ
हरित् + -गर्भः green or yellowish Kuśa grass with broad leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्पर्णम्
हरित् + -पर्णम् a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्पतिः|हरित्पति
हरित् + -पतिः the regent of a quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिन्मणिः|हरिन्मणि
हरित् + -मणिः (हरिन्मणिः) an emerald; हरिन्मणिश्यामतृणाभिरामैर्गृहाणि<BR> नीध्रैरिव यत्र रेजुः Śi. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रञ्जनी
हरित् + -रञ्जनी Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्वर्ण
हरित् + -वर्ण <i>a.</i> greenish, green-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित|हरितं|हरितः
हरित <i>a.</i> (-ता or हरिणी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [हृ-इतच्] Green, of a green<BR> colour, verdant; रम्यान्तरः कमलिनीहरितैः सरोभिः Ś. 4. 10; Ku. 4. 14;<BR> Me. 21; Ki. 5. 38.<BR>—2 Tawny.<BR>—3 Dark-blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितः|हरित|हरितं
हरित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 The green colour.<BR>—2 A lion.<BR>—3 A kind of grass.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हरिताश्मन्, हरितोपलः, हरितोपलेपनम्, हरितकपिश, हरितच्छद, हरितपण्यम्, हरितहरिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताश्मन्
हरित + -अश्मन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 an emerald.<BR>—2 blue vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितोपलः|हरितोपल
हरित + -उपलः an emerald; प्रेक्षां क्षिपन्तं हरितोपलाद्रेः Bhāg. 3. 8. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितोपलेपनम्
हरित + -उपलेपनम् green plastering or drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितकपिश
हरित + -कपिश <i>a.</i> yellowish brown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितच्छद|हरितछद
हरित + -छद <i>a.</i> green-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितपण्यम्
हरित + -पण्यम् trading in vegetables; Kau. A. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितहरिः|हरितहरि
हरित + -हरिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितकम्
हरितकम् —1 A pot-herb, green grass; अश्नन् पुरो हरितकं मुदमादधानः Śi. 5. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिता
हरिता<BR>—1 The Dūrvā grass.<BR>—2 Turmeric.<BR>—3 A brown-coloured grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताल|हरितालं|हरितालः
हरिताल &c. See under हरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रः|हरिद्र
हरिद्रः, हरिद्रकः The yellow sandal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रकः|हरिद्रक
हरिद्रः, हरिद्रकः The yellow sandal tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रा
हरिद्रा [हरिं पीतवर्णं द्रवति द्रु-गतौ-ड]<BR>—1 Turmeric.<BR>—2 The root of turmeric powdered; see Malli. on N. 22. 49.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हरिद्राङ्गः, हरिद्रांभ, हरिद्रागणपतिः, हरिद्रागणेशः, हरिद्राराग, हरिद्रारागक<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राङ्गः|हरिद्राङ्ग
हरिद्रा + -अङ्गः a kind of pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रांभ
हरिद्रा + -आंभ <i>a.</i> of a yellow colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रांभः|हरिद्राम्भ
हरिद्रा + -आंभ + .({@-भः@})<BR>—1 the yellow colour.<BR>—2 Zedoary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रागणपतिः|हरिद्रागणपति
हरिद्रा + -गणपतिः, -गणेशः a particular form of the god<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">Page1750-2</a>]<BR> Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रागणेशः|हरिद्रागणेश
हरिद्रा + -गणपतिः, -गणेशः a particular form of the god<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">Page1750-2</a>]<BR> Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्राराग|हरिद्रारागः
हरिद्रा + -राग, -रागक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 turmeric-coloured.<BR>—2 unsteady in attachment or affection, fickle-minded (as a lover); (thus<BR> defined by HalāyudhaH━ क्षणमात्रानुरागश्च हरिद्राराग उच्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रारागक
हरिद्रा + -राग, -रागक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 turmeric-coloured.<BR>—2 unsteady in attachment or affection, fickle-minded (as a lover); (thus<BR> defined by HalāyudhaH━ क्षणमात्रानुरागश्च हरिद्राराग उच्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रुः|हरिद्रु
हरिद्रुः<BR>—1 A tree.<BR>—2 A kind of plant (Mar. दारूहळद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
हरिमन् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 Yellowness.<BR>—2 Paleness.<BR>—3 Time.<BR>—4 Jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरियः|हरिय
हरियः A yellow-coloured horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चन्द्रः|हरिश्चन्द्र|हरिश्चंद्रः
हरिश्चन्द्रः N. of a king of the solar dynasty. [He was the son of<BR> Triśaṅku and was famous for his liberality, probity, and unflinching<BR> adherence to truth. On one occasion his family-priest Vasiṣṭha commended<BR> his qualities in the presence of Viśvāmitra, who refused to believe<BR> them. A quarrel thereupon ensued, and it was at last decided that Viśvāmitra<BR> should himself test the king. The sage accordingly subjected him to the<BR> most crucial test with a view to see if he could not be but once made<BR> to swerve from his plighted word. The king, however, stood the test with<BR> exemplary courage, adhering to his word though he had to forego the kingdom,<BR> to sell off his wife and son, and at last, even his own self to a low-caste<BR> man, and −as the last test, as it were, of his truthfulness and courage−<BR> to be even ready to put his own wife to death as a witch! Viśāmitra<BR> thereupon acknowledged himself vanquished, and the worthy king was elevated<BR> along with his subjects to heaven.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिषः|हरिष
हरिषः = हर्षः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीतकी
हरीतकी The yellow myrobalan tree (Mar. बाळहिरडा); सौवर्चलं<BR> यवक्षारं सर्जिकां च हरीतकीम् Śiva B. 30. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणुः|हरेणु
हरेणुः [हृ-एणुः Uṇ. 2. 1]<BR>—1 Pease, pulse.<BR>—2 A creeper serving as the boundary of a village.<BR>—3 N. of Laṅkā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणुः|हरेणु
हरेणुः + .{@-णुः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 A respectable woman.<BR>—2 A copper-coloured deer.<BR>—3 A fragrant drug; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणुकः|हरेणुक
हरेणुकः Pease, pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्तृ|हर्त्तृ
हर्तृ <i>a.</i> (-र्त्री <i>f.</i>)<BR> One who takes away, seizes, robs, accepts &c. ━<i>m.</i><BR>—1 A thief, robber; हर्तुर्याति न गोचरम् Bh. 2. 16.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मन्|हर्म्मन्
हर्मन् <i>n.</i> Gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मित|हर्म्मित|हर्म्मितं
हर्मित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Gaped; yawned.<BR>—2 Cast, thrown.<BR>—3 Burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मुटः|हर्मुट|हर्म्मुट|हर्म्मुटः
हर्मुटः<BR>—1 The sun.<BR>—2 A tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यम्
हर्म्यम् [हृ-यत् मुट् च]<BR>—1 A palace, mansion, any large or palatial building; हर्म्यपृष्ठं समारूढः<BR> काकोऽपि गरुडायते Subhāṣ.; वाह्योद्यानस्थितहरशिर श्चन्द्रिकाधौतहर्म्या Me. 7;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">Page1751-1</a>]<BR> Ṛs. 1. 28; Bk. 8. 36; R. 6. 47; Ku. 6. 42.<BR>—2 An oven, a fire-place, hearth.<BR>—3 A fiery pit, abode of evil spirits, the infernal regions.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हर्म्याङ्गनम्, हर्म्याङ्गणम्, हर्म्यतलम्, हर्म्यपृष्ठम्, हर्म्यवलभी, हर्म्यस्थलम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1750-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्याङ्गनम्
हर्म्यम् + -अङ्गनम्, -अङ्गणम् the court-yard of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्याङ्गणम्
हर्म्यम् + -अङ्गनम्, -अङ्गणम् the court-yard of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यतलम्
हर्म्यम् + -तलम्, -पृष्ठम्, -वलभी <i>f.</i> the upper room of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यपृष्ठम्
हर्म्यम् + -तलम्, -पृष्ठम्, -वलभी <i>f.</i> the upper room of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यवलभी
हर्म्यम् + -तलम्, -पृष्ठम्, -वलभी <i>f.</i> the upper room of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यस्थलम्
हर्म्यम् + -स्थलम् the room of a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मिका
हर्मिका <i>f.</i> A summer house on a Stūpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्|हर्य्य्
हर्य् €1 P. (हर्यति)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To worship.<BR>—3 To take.<BR>—4 To threaten.<BR>—5 To be weary or fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यतः|हर्यत|हर्य्यत|हर्य्यतः
हर्यतः<BR>—1 A horse.<BR>—2 A horse fit for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>—3 A sacrifice; Uṇ. 3. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षः|हर्ष
हर्षः [हृष्-घञ्]<BR>—1 Joy, delight, pleasure, satisfaction, gladness, rapture, glee, exultation;<BR> हर्षो हर्षो हृदयवसतिः पञ्चबाणस्तु बाणः P. R. 1. 22; सहोत्थितः<BR> सैनिकहर्षनिःस्वनैः R. 3. 61.<BR>—2 Thrilling, bristling, erection (of the hair of the body); as in रोमहर्ष<BR> q. v.; नेत्रे जलं गात्ररुहेषु हर्षः Bhāg. 2. 3. 24.<BR>—3 Joy, considered as one of the 33 or 34 subordinate feelings; हर्षस्त्विष्टावाप्तेर्मनःप्रसादोऽश्रुगद्गदादिकरः<BR> S. D. 195; or इष्टप्राप्त्यादिजन्मा सुखविशेषो हर्षः R. G.<BR>—4 The erection of the sexual organ; lustfulness.<BR>—5 Ardent desire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हर्षान्वित, हर्षाकुल, हर्षोत्कर्षः, हर्षोदयः, हर्षकर, हर्षकीलकः, हर्षगर्भ, हर्षजम्, हर्षजड, हर्षदोहलः, हर्षदोहलम्, हर्षवर्धनः, हर्षविवर्धन, हर्षसंपुटः, हर्षस्वनः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षान्वित
हर्षः + -अन्वित <i>a.</i> full of joy, happy; so हर्षाविष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षाकुल
हर्षः + -आकुल <i>a.</i> agitated with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षोत्कर्षः|हर्षोत्कर्ष
हर्षः + -उत्कर्षः excess of happiness or joy, ecstacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षोदयः|हर्षोदय
हर्षः + -उदयः rise of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षकर
हर्षः + -कर <i>a.</i> gratifying, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षकीलकः|हर्षकीलक
हर्षः + -कीलकः a kind of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षगर्भ
हर्षः + -गर्भ <i>a.</i> blissful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षजम्
हर्षः + -जम् semen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षजड
हर्षः + -जड <i>a.</i> dull or paralyzed with joy; परामृशन् हर्षजडेन<BR> पाणिना तदीयमङ्गं कुलिशव्रणाङ्कितम् R. 3. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षदोहलः|हर्षदोहल
हर्षः + -दोहलः, -दोहलम् lustful desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षदोहलम्
हर्षः + -दोहलः, -दोहलम् lustful desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षवर्धनः|हर्षवर्धन
हर्षः + -वर्धनः N. of a great king of Northern India and founder of<BR> an era, A. D. 605 or 606.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षविवर्धन
हर्षः + -विवर्धन <i>a.</i> increasing joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षसंपुटः|हर्षसम्पुट|हर्षसंपुट
हर्षः + -संपुटः a kind of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षस्वनः|हर्षस्वन
हर्षः + -स्वनः a cry or shout of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षक|हर्षकः
हर्षक <i>a.</i> (-र्षका or -र्षिका <i>f.</i>)<BR> [हृष्-णिच् ण्वुल्] Delighting, gladdening, delightful, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण <i>a.</i> (-णा or -णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [हृष्-णिच् ल्यु]<BR>—1 Causing delight, gladdening, delightful, pleasant.<BR>—2 Causing the hair of the body to stand erect; संवादमिममश्रौषमद्भुतं<BR> रोमहर्षणम् Bg. 18. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षणः|हर्षण|हर्षणं
हर्षण + .{@-णः@}<BR>—1 N. of one of the five arrows of Kāmadeva.<BR>—2 A morbid affection of the eyes.<BR>—3 A deity presiding over the funeral ceremonies.<BR>—4 A funeral and other rites; L. D. B.<BR>—5 One of the 27 yogas (Astr.); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षणम्
हर्षण + .{@-णम्@}<BR>—1 Joy, delight, happiness, gladdening, delighting; दुर्हृदामप्रहर्षाय<BR> सुहृदां हर्षणाय च Mb.<BR>—2 Raising the spirit (of an army); खातकव्यूहतत्त्वज्ञं बलहर्षणकोविदम्<BR> Mb. 12. 118. 11.<BR>—3 Erection of the sexual organ, sexual excitement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयित्नु|हर्षयित्नुः
हर्षयित्नु <i>a.</i> [हृष्-णिच् इत्नु] Gladdening, pleasing, delighting.<BR>━<i>n.</i> Gold. ━<i>m.</i> A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षित|हर्षितः
हर्षित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Delighted, happy.<BR>—2 Made happy, gladdened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षितम्
हर्षित + .{@-तम्@} Joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुलः|हर्षुल
हर्षुलः [हृष्-उलच् Uṇ. 1. 93]<BR>—1 A deer.<BR>—2 A lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुला
हर्षुलः + .{@-ला@} A girl with a beard (unfit for marriage). ━<i>a.</i><BR>—1 Jocular (परिहासशील); हयं वा दन्तिनं … … अभिहन्त्यनादृत्य<BR> हर्षुले पार्थिवे मुदौ Mb. 12. 56. 54.<BR>—2 Lustful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्
हल् €1 P. (हलति, हलित) To plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलः|हल|हलं
हलः, हलम्<BR>—1 A plough.<BR>—2 A weapon. —3 A land-measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलम्
हलः, हलम्<BR>—1 A plough.<BR>—2 A weapon. —3 A land-measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलम्
हलम् [हल् घञर्थे करणे क]<BR>—1 A plough; वहसि वपुषि विशदे वसनं जलदाभम् । हलहतिभीतिमिलितयमुनाभम्;<BR> or हलं कलयते Gīt. 1.<BR>—2 Deformity, ugliness; ततो मया रूपगुणैरहल्या स्त्री विनिर्मिता । हलं<BR> नामेह वैरूप्यं हल्यं तत्प्रभवं भवेत् ॥ Rām. 7. 30. 22.<BR>—3 Hindrance.<BR>—4 Quarrel.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हलाभः, हलायुधः, हलककुद्, हलगोलकः, हलदण्डः, हलधर, हलभृत्, हलभूतिः, हलभृतिः, हलमार्गः, हलमुखम्, हलवाहा, हलसीरः, हलहति<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलाभः|हलाभ
हलम् + -अभः a piebald horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलायुधः|हलायुध
हलम् + -आयुधः<BR>—1 an epithet of Balarāma.<BR>—2 N. of the author of अभिधान-रत्नमाला.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलककुद्
हलम् + -ककुद् <i>f.</i> the projecting beam of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलगोलकः|हलगोलक
हलम् + -गोलकः a kind of insect; फलं वा मूलकं हृत्वा अपूपं वा<BR> पिपीलिकाः । चोरयित्वा च निष्पावं जायते हलगोलकः ॥ Mb. 13. 111. 100<BR> (com. हलगोलकः दीर्धपुच्छो गोलरूपी कीटविशेषः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलदण्डः|हलदण्ड
हलम् + -दण्डः the shaft or pole of a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलधर|हलधरः
हलम् + -धर, -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a ploughman.<BR>—2 N. of Balarāma; केशव धृतहलधररूप जय जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1;<BR> अंसन्यस्ते सति हलमृतो मेचके वाससीव Me. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृत्
हलम् + -धर, -भृत् <i>m.</i><BR>—1 a ploughman.<BR>—2 N. of Balarāma; केशव धृतहलधररूप जय जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1;<BR> अंसन्यस्ते सति हलमृतो मेचके वाससीव Me. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभूतिः|हलभूति
हलम् + -भूतिः, -भृतिः <i>f.</i> ploughing, agriculture, husbandry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलभृतिः|हलभृति
हलम् + -भूतिः, -भृतिः <i>f.</i> ploughing, agriculture, husbandry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलमार्गः|हलमार्ग
हलम् + -मार्गः a furrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलमुखम्
हलम् + -मुखम् a ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलवाहा
हलम् + -वाहा a particular land-measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलसीरः|हलसीर
हलम् + -सीरः a ploughshare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलहति
हलम् + -हति <i>f.</i><BR>—1 striking or drawing along with a plough.<BR>—2 ploughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1751-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलदी
