हस्तिशाला
हस्तिन् + -शाला an elephant-stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिशुण्डा
हस्तिन् + -शुण्डा, -शुण्डी A kind of shrub (Mar. इंद्रवारुणी, कबंडळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिशुण्डी
हस्तिन् + -शुण्डा, -शुण्डी A kind of shrub (Mar. इंद्रवारुणी, कबंडळ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिश्यामाकः|हस्तिश्यामाक
हस्तिन् + -श्यामाकः a kind of millet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिषड्गवम्
हस्तिन् + -षड्गवम् a collection of six elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिस्नानम्
हस्तिन् + -स्नानम् = गजस्नानम् q. v.; अवशेन्द्रियचित्तानां हस्तिस्नानमिव<BR> क्रिया H. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिहस्तः|हस्तिहस्त
हस्तिन् + -हस्तः an elephantʼs trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनपुरम्
हस्तिन(ना)पुरम् N. of a city founded by king Hastin, said to be<BR> situated some fifty miles north-east of the modern Delhi; it forms a central<BR> scene of action in the Mahābhārata; itʼs other names are:− गजाह्वय,<BR> नागसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुरम्
हस्तिन(ना)पुरम् N. of a city founded by king Hastin, said to be<BR> situated some fifty miles north-east of the modern Delhi; it forms a central<BR> scene of action in the Mahābhārata; itʼs other names are:− गजाह्वय,<BR> नागसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनी
हस्तिनी<BR>—1 A female elephant.<BR>—2 A kind of drug and perfume.<BR>—3 A woman of a particular class, one of the four classes into which writers<BR> on erotical science divide women (described as having thick lips, thick<BR> hips, thick fingers, large breasts, dark complexion, and libidinous appetite);<BR> the Ratimañjarī thus describes her:− स्थूलाधरा स्थूलनितम्बबिम्बा<BR> स्थूलाङ्गुलिः स्थूलकुचा सुशीला । कामोत्सुका गाढरतिप्रिया च नितान्तभोक्त्री<BR> (नितम्बखर्वा) खलु हस्तिनी स्यात् (करिणी मता सा) 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तेकरणम्
हस्तेकरणम् Marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्य|हस्त्यः
हस्त्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Belonging to the hand.<BR>—2 Done with the hand, manual.<BR>—3 Given with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र <i>a.</i> [हस्-रक् Uṇ. 2. 12]<BR>—1 Smiling.<BR>—2 Stupid, foolish, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहलम्
हहलम् A kind of deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा <i>m.</i> A kind of Gandharva; cf. हाहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा <i>ind.</i> A particle expressing<BR>—1 Grief, dejection, pain, as expressed by ‘ah’, ‘alas!’, ‘woe me’, in<BR> English; हा प्रिये जानकि U. 3; हा हा देवि स्फुटति हृदयम् U. 3. 38;<BR> हा पितः क्वासि हे सुभ्रु Bk. 6. 11; हा वत्से मालति क्वासि Māl. 10 &c.;<BR> (in this sense हा is often used with the acc. of person; हा<BR> कृष्णाभक्तम् Sk.).<BR>—2 Surprise; हा कथं महाराजदशरथस्य धर्मदाराः प्रियसखी मे कौसल्या U. 4.<BR>—3 Anger or reproach.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हाकारः, हाहाकृत<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाकारः|हाकार
हा + -कारः the exclamation हा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाकृत
हा + -हाकृत <i>a.</i> filled with cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा I. €3 Ā. (जिहीते, हान; <i>pass.</i> हायते; <i>desid.</i> जिहासते)<BR>—1 To go, move; जिहीथा विख्यातां स्फुटमिह भवद्बान्धवरथम् H. D. 28;<BR> Ki. 13. 23; Nalod. 1. 38.<BR>—2 To get, attain. ━II. €3 P. (जहाति, हीन)<BR>—1 To leave, abandon, quit, give up, forsake, relinquish, dismiss; मूढ<BR> जहीहि धनागमतृष्णां कुरु तनुबुद्धे मनसि वितृष्णाम् Moha M. 1; सा<BR> स्त्रीस्वभावादसहा भरस्य तयोर्द्वयोरेकतरं जहाति Mu. 4. 13; R. 5. 72, 8. 52, 12. 24, 14. 61, 87, 15. 59;<BR> Ś. 4. 14; बुद्धियुक्तो जहातीह<BR> उभे सुकृतदुष्कृते Bg. 2. 50; Bk. 3. 53, 5. 91, 10. 71, 20. 10; Me. 51, 62;<BR> Bv. 2. 129; Ṛs. 1. 38.<BR>—2 To resign, forego.<BR>—3 To let fall.<BR>—4 To omit, disregard, neglect.<BR>—5 To remove.<BR>—6 To avoid, shun. ━<i>Pass.</i> (हीयते)<BR>—1 To be left or forsaken; भिन्नतिमिरनिकरं न जहे शशिरश्मिसंगमयुजा<BR> नभः श्रिया Ki. 12. 12.<BR>—2 To be excluded from, be deprived of, lose (with instr. or abl.); विरूपाक्षो<BR> जहे प्राणैः Bk. 14. 35; जनयित्वा सुतं तस्यां ब्राह्मण्यादेव हीयते<BR> Ms. 3. 17, 5. 161, 9. 211.<BR>—3 To be deficient or wanting in; usually with परि q. v.; धैर्यं<BR> यस्य न हीयते Pt. 1. 103.<BR>—4 To diminish, decrease, decay, decline, wane (fig. also); प्रवृद्धो<BR> हीयते चन्द्रः समुद्रोऽपि तथाविधः R. 17. 71; H. Pr. 42.<BR>—5 To fail (as in a law-suit); भूतमप्यनुपन्यस्तं हीयते व्यवहारतः Y. 2. 19.<BR>—6 To be left out or omitted.<BR>—7 To be weakened. ━<i>Caus.</i> (हापयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to leave, abandon &c.<BR>—2 To drive away, expel.<BR>—3 To lose.<BR>—4 To neglect, omit, delay the performance of; द्रुतमेतु न हापयिष्यते<BR> सदृशं तस्य विधातुमुत्तरम् Śi. 16. 33; Ms. 3. 71, 4. 21; Y. 1. 121.<BR>━<i>Desid.</i> (जिहासति) To wish to leave &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात
हात <i>a.</i> Given up, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हातुः|हातु
हातुः <i>m., f.</i><BR>—1 Death.<BR>—2 Road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानम्
हानम्<BR>—1 Leaving, abandoning, loss, failure; अज्ञानमेवास्य हि मूलकारणं<BR> तद्धानमेवात्र विधौ विधीयते A. Rām. 7. 5. 9.<BR>—2 Escaping.<BR>—3 Prowess, power.<BR>—4 Want, lack.<BR>—5 Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानिः|हानि
हानिः <i>f.</i> [हा-क्तिन् तस्य निः]<BR>—1 Abandonment, relinquishment.<BR>—2 Loss, failure, absence, non-existence; क्वचित्तु स्फुटालंकारविरहेऽपि<BR> न काव्यत्वहानिः K. P. 1 ‘it does not cease to be a Kāvya’ &c.<BR>—3 Loss, damage, detriment; ग्रासोद्गलितसिक्थेन का हानिः करिणो भवेत् Subhāṣ.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">Page1755-1</a>]<BR> का नो हानिः Sarva. S.<BR>—4 Decrease, deficiency; यथा हानिः क्रमप्राप्ता तथा वृद्धिः क्रमागता<BR> Hariv.; Y. 2. 207, 244.<BR>—5 Neglect, omission, breach; प्रतिज्ञा˚, कार्य˚.<BR>—6 Passing away, waste, loss; कालहानि R. 13. 16.<BR>—7 = गतिः (from हा €3 Ā.); हानिभङ्गविकल्पानां नवानां संचयेन<BR> च Mb. 12. 239. 33.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हानिकर<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1754-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानिकर
हानिः + -कर <i>a.</i> causing loss, detrimental, injurious; अनादिष्टोऽपि<BR> भूपस्य दृष्ट्वा हानिकरं च यः । यतते तस्य नाशाय स भृत्योऽर्हो महीभुजाम् ॥<BR> Pt. 1. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापनम्
हापनम् Causing to quit or abandon, expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाङ्गरः|हाङ्गर|हांगर|हांगरः
हाङ्गरः A large fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटक|हाटकं
हाटक <i>a.</i> (-की <i>f.</i>)<BR> Golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकम्
हाटक + .{@-कम्@}<BR>—1 Gold; नवहाटकेष्टकचितं ददर्श सः क्षितिपस्य पस्त्यमथ तत्र<BR> संसदि Śi. 13. 63.<BR>—2 The thorn-apple.<BR>—3 A kind of magical drink; या वै विलायनं प्रविष्टं पुरुषं रसेन<BR> हाटकाख्येन साधयित्वा Bhāg. 5. 24. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हाटकेशः, हाटकेशानः, हाटकेश्वरः, हाटकहाडिका, हाटकगिरिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकेशः|हाटकेश
हाटक + -ईशः, -ईशानः, -ईश्वरः N. of a form of Śiva; ततोऽधस्ताद्वितले<BR> हरो भगवान् हाटकेश्वरः स्वपार्षदभूतगणावृतः Bhāg. 5. 24. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकेशानः|हाटकेशान
हाटक + -ईशः, -ईशानः, -ईश्वरः N. of a form of Śiva; ततोऽधस्ताद्वितले<BR> हरो भगवान् हाटकेश्वरः स्वपार्षदभूतगणावृतः Bhāg. 5. 24. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकेश्वरः|हाटकेश्वर
हाटक + -ईशः, -ईशानः, -ईश्वरः N. of a form of Śiva; ततोऽधस्ताद्वितले<BR> हरो भगवान् हाटकेश्वरः स्वपार्षदभूतगणावृतः Bhāg. 5. 24. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकहाडिका
हाटक + -हाडिका An earthen pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटकगिरिः|हाटकगिरि
हाटक + -गिरिः the mountain Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्रम्
हात्रम् [हा-करणे त्रल्]<BR>—1 Wages, hire.<BR>—2 Injuring, killing.<BR>—3 Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्रः|हात्र|हात्रं
हात्रम् + .{@-त्रः@} A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्त्रः|हान्त्र|हांत्रः
हान्त्रः Death, dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हान्त्रम्
हान्त्रः + .{@-न्त्रम्@} A demon; Uṇ. 4. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापनम्
हापनम् The act of causing to quit or abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुत्री
हापुत्री, हापुत्रिका A kind of wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापुत्रिका
हापुत्री, हापुत्रिका A kind of wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाफिका
हाफिका Yawning, gaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायक
हायक <i>a.</i> Giving up, abandoning; नैव धर्मी न चाधर्मी पूर्वोपचितहायकः Mb. 14. 19. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायनः|हायन|हायनं
हायनः, -नम्<BR> A year; त्रस्तैकहायनकुरङ्गविलोलदृष्टेः U. 3. 28; Māl. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायनम्
हायनः, -नम्<BR> A year; त्रस्तैकहायनकुरङ्गविलोलदृष्टेः U. 3. 28; Māl. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायनः|हायन|हायनं
हायनः, -नम् + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A kind of rice.<BR>—2 A flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारः|हार|हारं
हारः [हृ-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>—1 Taking away, removal, seizing.<BR>—2 Conveying.<BR>—3 Abstraction, deprivation.<BR>—4 A carrier, porter.<BR>—5 A garland or necklace of pearls &c.; a necklace in general; हारोऽयं<BR> हरिणाक्षीणां लुठति स्तनमण्डले Amaru. 100; पाण्ड्योऽयमंसार्पितलम्बहारः<BR> R. 6. 60, 5. 52, 6. 16; Me. 74; Ṛs. 1. 4, 2. 18.<BR>—6 War, battle.<BR>—7 (In math.) The denominator of a fraction.<BR>—8 A divisor.<BR>—9 (In prosody) A long syllable.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हारावलिः, हारावली, हारगुटिका, हारगुलिका, हारफलम्, हारफलकम्, हारयष्टिः, हारहारा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारावलिः
हारः + -आवलिः, -आवली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a string of pearls; तरुणीस्तन एव शोभते मणिहारावलिरामणीयकम्<BR> N. 2. 44; हारावलीतरलकाञ्चितकाञ्चिदाम Gīt. 11.<BR>—2 N. of a vocabulary of uncommon words by पुरुषोत्तमदेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारावली
हारः + -आवलिः, -आवली <i>f.</i><BR>—1 a string of pearls; तरुणीस्तन एव शोभते मणिहारावलिरामणीयकम्<BR> N. 2. 44; हारावलीतरलकाञ्चितकाञ्चिदाम Gīt. 11.<BR>—2 N. of a vocabulary of uncommon words by पुरुषोत्तमदेव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारगुटिका
हारः + -गुटिका, -गुलिका the bead or pearl of a necklace;<BR> ताम्रोदरेषु पतितं तरुपल्लवेषु निर्धौतहारगुलिकाविशदं हिमाम्भः R. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारगुलिका
हारः + -गुटिका, -गुलिका the bead or pearl of a necklace;<BR> ताम्रोदरेषु पतितं तरुपल्लवेषु निर्धौतहारगुलिकाविशदं हिमाम्भः R. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारफलम्
हारः + -फलम्, -फलकम् a necklace of five strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारफलकम्
हारः + -फलम्, -फलकम् a necklace of five strings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारयष्टिः|हारयष्टि
हारः + -यष्टिः <i>f.</i> a necklace, string of pearls; दधति पृथुकुचाग्रैरुन्नतैर्हारयष्टिम्<BR> Ṛs. 2. 25, 1. 8; Ki. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहारा
हारः + -हारा a kind of reddish-brown grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारकः|हारक
हारकः [हृ-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 A thief, plunderer; लवणहारकः Y. 3. 215.<BR>—2 A cheat, rogue.<BR>—3 A string of pearls.<BR>—4 A divisor (in math.)<BR>—5 A kind of prose composition.<BR>—6 A gambler.<BR>—7 A kind of science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि <i>a.</i> Attracting, captivating, pleasing, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिः|हारि
हारि + .{@-रिः@} <i>f.</i><BR>—1 Defeat.<BR>—2 Losing a game.<BR>—3 A body of travellers, caravan.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हारिकण्ठः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिकण्ठः|हारिकण्ठ|हारिकंठ
हारि + -कण्ठः a cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
हारित <i>p. p.</i><BR>—1 Caused to be taken or seized.<BR>—2 Presented, offered.<BR>—3 Attracted.<BR>—4 Robbed, carried.<BR>—5 Lost; हतः शत्रुः कृतं मित्रं रत्नमाला न हारिता Pt. 5. 85.<BR>—6 Surpassed, exceeded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारितः|हारित
हारित + .{@-तः@}<BR>—1 The green colour.<BR>—2 A kind of pigeon; कांस्यं हृत्वा तु दुर्बुद्धिर्हारितो जायते नरः<BR> Mb. 13. 111. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारितकः|हारितक|हारितकं
हारितकः A green vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहूरः|हारहूर
हारहूरः Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहूरा
हारहूरः + .{@-रा@} A grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिण
हारिण <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> Belonging to a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणम्
हारिण + .{@-णम्@} Venison, flesh of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणिकः|हारिणिक
हारिणिकः A deer-catcher, hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
हारिन् <i>a.</i> (-णी <i>f.</i>)<BR> [हारो अस्त्यस्य इनि, हृ-णिनि वा]<BR>—1 Taking, conveying, carrying.<BR>—2 Robbing, taking away; वाजिकुञ्जराणां च हारिणः Y. 2. 273, 3. 208.<BR>—3 Seizing, disturbing; तद्रजो प्रतिपं विद्यात् सततं हारि देहिनाम् Ms. 12. 28.<BR>—4 Obtaining, securing.<BR>—5 Attracting, captivating, pleasing, delighting, ravishing; तवास्मि<BR> गीतरागेण हारिणा प्रसभं हृतः Ś. 1. 5; Śi. 10. 13, 69; विष्टपहारिणि<BR> हरौ Bh. 2. 25.<BR>—6 Surpassing, exelling.<BR>—7 Having a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्रः|हारिद्र
हारिद्रः<BR>—1 A yellow colour; हारिद्रवर्णं सुसुखं च शुक्लम् Mb. 12. 280. 33.<BR>—2 The Kadamba tree.<BR>—3 A kind of vegetable poison.<BR>—4 A kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्रम्
हारिद्रः + .{@-द्रम्@} Gold; तथापि नालोकि तदस्य रूपं हारिद्रभङ्गाय वितीर्णभङ्गम्<BR> N. 6. 45, 7. 13. ━<i>a.</i> yellow, yellow-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारी
हारी <i>f.</i> A pearl; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीतः|हारीत
हारीतः<BR>—1 A kind of pigeon; मारीचोद्भ्रान्तहारीता मलयाद्रेरुपत्यकाः R. 4. 46.<BR>—2 A rogue, cheat.<BR>—3 N. of a writer of a Smṛti or code of laws; Y. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्दम्
हार्दम् [हृदयस्य कर्म युवा˚ अण् हृदादेशः]<BR>—1 Affection, love; अमर्षशून्येन जनस्य जन्तुना न जातहार्देन न<BR> विद्विषादरः Ki. 1. 33; Śi. 9. 69; V. 5. 10.<BR>—2 Kindness, tenderness.<BR>—3 Will.<BR>—4 Intention, meaning; अर्जुनः सहसाऽऽज्ञाय हरेर्हार्दमथासिना Bhāg. 1. 7. 55.<BR>━<i>a.</i> Relating to or being in the heart; संछिद्य हार्दमनुमानसदुक्तितीक्ष्णज्ञानासिना<BR> भजत माखिलसंशयाधिम् Bhāg. 11. 13. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्दिक्यः|हार्दिक्य
हार्दिक्यः<BR>—1 N. of Kṛta-varman; Mb. 1. 2. 32; मुञ्च हार्दिक्य शङ्काम् । Ve. 3. 7.<BR>—2 Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्दिन्
हार्दिन् <i>n.</i> Anything greatly liked or desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1755-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्य|हार्यः|हार्य्य|हार्य्यः
हार्य <i>a.</i><BR>—1 To be taken or conveyed.<BR>—2 To be borne or carried on; यदूढया वारणराजहार्यया Ku. 5. 70.<BR>—3 To be taken away or snatched off; इतः परानर्भकहार्यशस्त्रान् वैदर्भि<BR> पश्यानुमता मयासि R. 7. 67.<BR>—4 To be displaced or borne away (as by wind); निःश्वासहार्यांशुकमाजगाम<BR> घर्मः प्रिया वेशमिवोपदेष्टुम् R. 16. 43.<BR>—5 To be shaken (as oneʼs resolution); विमुच्य सा हारमहार्यनिश्चया Ku. 5. 8.<BR>—6 To be secured or won over, to be attracted, conquered or influenced;<BR> वहसि हि धनहार्यं पण्यभूतं शरीरम् Mk. 1. 31; Ku. 5. 53; Ms. 7. 217.<BR>—7 To be seized or robbed; नहि तस्यास्ति किंचित् स्वं भर्तृहार्यधनो<BR> हि सः Ms. 8. 417.<BR>—8 To be destroyed; संनिबद्धमपहर्तुंमहार्यं भूरि दुर्गतिभयं भुवनानाम् Ki. 18. 30.<BR>—9 To be warded off; स संप्रधार्यैवमहार्यसारः सारं विनेष्यन् सगणस्य<BR> शत्रोः Ki. 16. 25.<BR>—10 Captivating, charming; हार्योऽयं विषयो ब्रह्मन् गान्धर्वो नाम् नामतः<BR> Mb. 13. 19. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्यः|हार्य|हार्य्य|हार्य्यः
हार्य + .{@-र्यः@}<BR>—1 A snake.<BR>—2 The tree called Bibhītaka.<BR>—3 The dividend (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्या
हार्य + .{@-र्या@} A kind of sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालः|हाल
हालः [हलो अस्त्यस्य अण्, हल एव वा अण्]<BR>—1 A plough.<BR>—2 N. of Balarāma.<BR>—3 N. of a king, Śālivāhana king.<BR>—4 A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाला
हालः + .{@-ला@} Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाली
हालः + .{@-ली@} A wifeʼs younger sister.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हालमृत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालमृत्
हालः + -मृत् <i>m.</i> an epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालकः|हालक
हालकः A horse of a yellowish-brown colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहलम्
हाल(ला)हलम्<BR>—1 A sort of deadly poison produced at the churning of the ocean; (being<BR> of a very virulent character it began to burn up everything when it was<BR> swallowed by the god Śiva); अहमेव गुरुः सुदारुणानामिति हालाहल मास्म<BR> तात दृप्यः । ननु सन्ति भवादृशानि भूयो भुवनेऽस्मिन् वचनानि दुर्जनानाम्<BR> Subhāṣ.; हालाहलं न विषं विषं रमा Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 (Hence) A deadly poison or poison in general; हालाहलं खलु पिपासति<BR> कौतुकेन Bv. 1. 95, 2. 73; मधु तिष्ठति वाचि योषितां हृदये हालहलं<BR> महद्विषम् Pt. 1. 188. (Also written हलाहल or हालहाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलम्
हाल(ला)हलम्<BR>—1 A sort of deadly poison produced at the churning of the ocean; (being<BR> of a very virulent character it began to burn up everything when it was<BR> swallowed by the god Śiva); अहमेव गुरुः सुदारुणानामिति हालाहल मास्म<BR> तात दृप्यः । ननु सन्ति भवादृशानि भूयो भुवनेऽस्मिन् वचनानि दुर्जनानाम्<BR> Subhāṣ.; हालाहलं न विषं विषं रमा Subhāṣ.<BR>—2 (Hence) A deadly poison or poison in general; हालाहलं खलु पिपासति<BR> कौतुकेन Bv. 1. 95, 2. 73; मधु तिष्ठति वाचि योषितां हृदये हालहलं<BR> महद्विषम् Pt. 1. 188. (Also written हलाहल or हालहाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहली
हालहली, हाला Wine, spirituous liquor; हित्वा हालामभिमतरसां<BR> रेवतीलोचनाङ्काम् Me. 51; Pt. 1. 58; Śi. 10. 21; हालया साकमज्ञातं<BR> हालाहलमदापयत् Śiva B. 28. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाला
हालहली, हाला Wine, spirituous liquor; हित्वा हालामभिमतरसां<BR> रेवतीलोचनाङ्काम् Me. 51; Pt. 1. 58; Śi. 10. 21; हालया साकमज्ञातं<BR> हालाहलमदापयत् Śiva B. 28. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलः|हालाहल|हालाहलं
हालाहलः<BR>—1 A kind of insect.<BR>—2 A kind of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहला
हालाहलः + .{@-ला@} A small mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहली
हालाहलः + .{@-ली@} Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलम्
हालाहलः + .{@-लम्@}<BR>—1 = हालहल (1).<BR>—2 Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिकः|हालिक
हालिकः [हलेन खनति हलः प्रहरणमस्य तस्येदं वा ठक् ठञ् वा]<BR>—1 A ploughman, an agriculturist; कस्मिश्चिंदधिष्ठाने हालिकदपम्ती<BR> प्रतिवसतः स्म Pt. 4. 92/93.<BR>—2 One that draws a plough (as a plough-ox).<BR>—3 One who fights with a plough. ━<i>a.</i> Relating or belonging to a plough; P. IV. 3. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिनी
हालिनी A kind of large house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाली
हाली A wifeʼs younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालुः|हालु
हालुः A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हावः|हाव
हावः [ह्वे-भावे घञ् नि˚ संप्र˚, हु-करणे घञ् वा]<BR>—1 A call, calling.<BR>—2 Any feminine coquettish gesture calculated to excite amorous sensations,<BR> dalliance (of love), blandishments; हावहारि हसितं वचनानां कौशलं<BR> दृशि विकारविशेषाः Śi. 10. 13; जगुः सरागं ननृतुः सहावम् Bk. 3. 43;<BR> गतैः सहावैः कलहंसविक्रमम् Ki. 8. 29. (हाव is thus<BR> defined by उज्ज्वलमणि:− ग्रीवारेचकसंयुक्तो भ्रूनेत्रादिविकासकृत् ।<BR> भावादीषत् प्रकाशो यः स हाव इति कथ्यते ॥) see S. D. 127 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हावकः|हावक
हावकः<BR>—1 One who calls or summons.<BR>—2 One who calls the bride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हावु
हावु [हा३वु] An exclamation of joy; T. Up. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासः|हास
हासः [हस्-भावे घञ्]<BR>—1 Laughter, laughing, smile; भासो हासः P. R. 1. 22.<BR>—2 Joy, mirth, merriment.<BR>—3 Laughter, as the prevailing feeling of the <i>rasa</i> called हास्य; see S. D. 207.<BR>—4 Derisive laughter; संरम्भं मैथिलीहासः क्षणसौम्यां निनाय ताम् R. 12. 36.<BR>—5 Opening, blowing, expanding (as of lotuses &c.); कूलानि सामर्षतयेव<BR> तेनुः सरोजलक्ष्मीं स्थलपद्महासैः Bk. 2. 3.<BR>—6 Pride, arrogance; अनन्यहेतुष्वथ मे गतिः स्यादात्यन्तिकी यत्र न<BR> मृत्युहासः Bhāg. 3. 27. 30.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हासशील<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासशील
हासः + -शील <i>a.</i> prone to mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासाः
हासाः (Ved.) कालाः; Uṇ. 4. 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासकः|हासक
हासकः A buffoon, merry-andrew (भण्ड); न नृत्यगीतशीलेषु<BR> हासकेषु च धार्मिकः Mb. 12. 36. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिका
हासिका<BR>—1 Laughter.<BR>—2 Mirth, merriment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासन
हासन <i>a.</i> Funny, comical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासनिकः|हासनिक
हासनिकः A play-fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्य|हास्यं|हास्यः
हास्य <i>a.</i> [हस्-ण्यत्] Laughable, ridiculous; संरुद्धचेष्टस्य<BR> मृगेन्द्र कामं हास्यं वचस्तद्यदहं विवक्षुः R. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यम्
हास्य + .{@-स्यम्@}<BR>—1 Laughter; क्रीडां शरीरसंस्कारं समाजोत्सवदर्शनम् । हास्यं परगृहे<BR> यानं त्यजेत् प्रोषितभर्तृका ॥ Y. 1. 84.<BR>—2 Mirth, amusement, sport; तस्माद्द्यूतं न सेवेत हास्यार्थमपि बुद्धिमान् Ms. 9. 227.<BR>—3 Jest, joke.<BR>—4 Derision, ridicule; तुष्टैर्बद्धं तदलघु रघुस्वामिनः सच्चरित्रं<BR> क्रुद्धैर्नीतस्त्रिभुवनजयी हास्यमार्गं दशास्यः Vikr. 18. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यः|हास्य|हास्यं
हास्य + .{@-स्यः@} The sentiment of mirth or humour, one of the eight or nine<BR> sentiments in poetry; it is thus defined:− विकृताकारवाग्वेषचेष्टादेः<BR> कुहकाद्भवेत् । हास्यो हासस्थायिभावः (so must the line be read instead<BR> of हासो हास्यस्थायिभावः) श्वेतः प्रमथदैवतः S. D. 228.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हास्यास्पदम्, हास्यकथा, हास्यकारः, हास्यपदवी, हास्यमार्गः, हास्यरसः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यास्पदम्
हास्य + -आस्पदम् a butt (of ridicule), laughing-stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यकथा
हास्य + -कथा a funny tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यकारः|हास्यकार
हास्य + -कारः = हासकः q. v.; तथोपविष्टं राजानमुपासन्ते विचक्षणाः ।<BR> कथानां बहुरूपाणां हास्यकाराः समन्ततः ॥ Rām. 7. 43. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यपदवी
हास्य + -पदवी, -मार्गः ridicule, derision; Vikr. 18. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यमार्गः
हास्य + -पदवी, -मार्गः ridicule, derision; Vikr. 18. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्यरसः|हास्यरस
हास्य + -रसः the sentiment of mirth or humour; see हास्य above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासस्
हासस् <i>m.</i> The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिकः|हास्तिक|हास्तिकं
हास्तिकः An elephant-driver or rider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिकम्
हास्तिकः + .{@-कम्@} A herd of elephants; खेदायत श्वसितवेगनिरस्तमुग्धमूर्धन्यरत्ननिकरैरिव<BR> हास्तिकानि Śi. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1756-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिनम्
हास्तिनम् N. of Hastināpura, q. v. ━<i>a.</i> Having the depth of an<BR> elephant (as water); सरस्तलं हास्तिनम् Dk. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहलम्
हाह(हा)लम् Deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहालम्
हाह(हा)लम् Deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहवः|हाहव
हाहवः A kind of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहस्
हाहस् <i>m.</i> A Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहा
हाहा <i>m.</i> N. of a Gandharva; हा हेति गायन् यदशोचि तेन नाम्नापि<BR> हाहा हरिगायनोऽभूत् N. 2. 27; हाहाहूहूभ्यां त्वा गन्धर्वाभ्यां परिददामि<BR> Kauś. 7. 56. 13. ━<i>ind.</i> An exclamation denoting pain, grief or surprise,<BR> (it is simply हा repeated for the sake of emphasis; see हा); हा<BR> हा देवि स्फुटति हृदयं ध्वंसते देहवन्धः U. 3. 38.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हाहाकारः, हाहारवः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहाकारः|हाहाकार
हाहा + -कारः<BR>—1 a grief, lamentation, loud wailing.<BR>—2 the din or uproar of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहारवः|हाहारव
हाहा + -रवः the cry हाहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि <i>ind.</i> (Never used at the beginning of a sentence) It has the<BR> following senses:−<BR>—1 For, because (expressing a strict or logical reason); अग्निरिहास्ति<BR> धूमो हि दृश्यते G. M.; R. 5. 10.<BR>—2 Indeed, surely; देव प्रयोगप्रधानं हि नाट्यशास्त्रम् M. 1; न<BR> हि कमलिनीं दृष्ट्वा ग्राहमवेक्षते मतङ्गजः M. 3.<BR>—3 For instance, as is well known; प्रजानामेव भूत्यर्थं स ताभ्यो बलिमग्रहीत् ।<BR> सहस्रगुणमुत्स्रष्टुमादत्ते हि रसं रविः R. 1. 18.<BR>—4 Only, alone (to emphasize an idea); मूढो हि मदनेनायास्यते K. 155.<BR>—5 Sometimes it is used merely as an expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि €5 P. (हिनोति, हित; <i>caus.</i> हाययति; <i>desid.</i> जिघीषति)<BR>—1 To send forth, impel.<BR>—2 To cast, throw, discharge, shoot; गदा शक्रजिता जिध्ये Bk. 14. 36.<BR>—3 To excite, incite, urge.<BR>—4 To promote, further.<BR>—5 To gratify, please, exhilarate.<BR>—6 To go or proceed.<BR>—7 To forsake, abandon; सर्वेषु भूतेष्वधियज्ञमीशं यजस्व योगेन च<BR> कर्म हिन्वन् Bhāg. 7. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्
हिंस् €1. €7 P., €10 U. (हिंसति, हिनस्ति, हिंसयति-ते, हिंसित)<BR>—1 To strike, hit.<BR>—2 To hurt, injure, harm; दीर्घौ बुद्धिमतो बाहू स ताभ्यां हन्ति हिंसितः Pt. 1. 307.<BR>—3 To afflict, torment; हिनस्ति प्रत्यङ्गं ज्वर इव गरीयानित इतो Māl. 2. 1.<BR>—4 To kill, slay, destroy completely; कीर्तिं सूते दुष्कृतं या हिनस्ति<BR> U. 5. 31; R. 8. 45; न हिनस्त्यात्मनात्मानं ततो याति परां गतिम् Bg. 13. 28;<BR> Bk. 6. 38, 14. 57, 15. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसक|हिंसकः
हिंसक <i>a.</i> [हिंस्-ण्वुल्]<BR>—1 Injurious, noxious, hurtful.<BR>—2 Hostile.<BR>—3 Ferocious, savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसकः|हिंसक
हिंसक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A savage animal, a beast of prey.<BR>—2 An enemy.<BR>—3 A Brāhmaṇa skilled in the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसनम्
हिंसनम्, -ना<BR> [हिंस्-ल्युट्] Striking, hurting, killing;<BR> वर्जयेत् … प्राणिनां चैव हिंसनम् Ms. 2. 177, 10. 48; Y. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसना
हिंसनम्, -ना<BR> [हिंस्-ल्युट्] Striking, hurting, killing;<BR> वर्जयेत् … प्राणिनां चैव हिंसनम् Ms. 2. 177, 10. 48; Y. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसनीय
हिंसनीय <i>a.</i> To be hurt or killed; पित्र्ये दैवे च कर्मणि श्राद्धादौ<BR> पशवो हिंसनीया नान्यत्रेति मनुरभिहितवान् Kull. on Ms. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसा
हिंसा [हिंस्-अ]<BR>—1 Injury, mischief, wrong, harm, hurt (said to be of three kinds:− कायिक<BR> ‘personal’, वाचिक ‘verbal’ and मानसिक ‘mental’); अहिंसा परमो धर्मः.<BR>—2 Killing, slaying, destruction; गान्धर्वमादत्स्व यतः प्रयोक्तुर्न<BR> चारिहिंसा विजयश्च हस्ते R. 5. 57, 3. 313; Ms. 10. 63.<BR>—3 Robbery, plunder.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हिंसात्मक, हिंसाकर्मन्, हिंसाप्राणिन्, हिंसाप्राय, हिंसारत, हिंसारुचि, हिंसासमुद्भव<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसात्मक
हिंसा + -आत्मक <i>a.</i> injurious, destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाकर्मन्|हिंसाकर्म्मन्
हिंसा + -कर्मन् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 any hurtful or injurious act.<BR>—2 magic used to effect the ruin or injury of an enemy. (= अभिचार q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाप्राणिन्
हिंसा + -प्राणिन् <i>m.</i> a noxious animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसाप्राय
हिंसा + -प्राय <i>a.</i> generally injurious; हिंसाप्रायां पराधीनां कृषिं<BR> यत्नेन वर्जयेत् Ms. 10. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारत
हिंसा + -रत <i>a.</i> delighting in mischief; हिंसारतश्च यो नित्यं<BR> नेहासौ सुखमेधते Ms. 4. 170; also हिंसाविहार in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारुचि
हिंसा + -रुचि <i>a.</i> intent on or delighting in mischief; व्याघ्राघ्रातमृगीकृपाकुलमृगन्यायेन<BR> हिंसारुचेः Māl. 5. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसासमुद्भव
हिंसा + -समुद्भव <i>a.</i> arising from injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारुः|हिंसारु
हिंसारुः<BR>—1 A tiger.<BR>—2 Any noxious animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालु|हिंसालुः
हिंसालु [हिंसा अस्त्यर्थे आलु]<BR>—1 Injurious, mischievous, hurtful.<BR>—2 Murderous. ━<i>m.</i> A mischievous or savage dog (हिंसालुक also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसित|हिंसितः
हिंसित <i>a.</i> Injured, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसितम्
हिंसित + .{@-तम्@} Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीनः|हिंसीन
हिंसीनः A savage animal, beast of prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीरः|हिंसीर
हिंसीरः [हिंस्-ईरन् Uṇ. 5. 22]<BR>—1 A tiger.<BR>—2 A bird (खग).<BR>—3 A mischievous fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्य
हिंस्य <i>a.</i> Liable to be injured or killed; मधुपर्के च यज्ञे<BR> च पितृदैवतकर्मणि । अत्रैव पशवो हिंस्या नान्यत्रेत्यब्रवीन्मनुः ॥<BR> Ms. 5. 41; R. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्र|हिंस्रः
हिंस्र <i>a.</i> [हिंस्-र्] Injurious, noxious, mischievous, hurtful,<BR> murderous; व्याधिता वाधिवेत्तव्या हिंस्रार्थघ्री च सर्वदा Ms. 9. 80, 12. 56.<BR>—2 Terrible.<BR>—3 Cruel, fierce, savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रः|हिंस्र
हिंस्र + .{@-स्रः@}<BR>—1 A fierce animal, beast of prey; सा दुष्प्रधर्षा मनसापि हिंस्रैः R. 2. 27.<BR>—2 A destroyer.<BR>—3 N. of Śiva.<BR>—4 N. of Bhīma.<BR>—5 A man who delights in injuring living creatures; Ms. 3. 164.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रम्
हिंस्र + .{@-स्रम्@} Cruelty; Ms. 1. 29.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हिंस्रजन्तुः, हिंस्रपशुः, हिंस्रयन्त्रम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1757-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रजन्तुः|हिंस्रजन्तु
