हिण्डुकः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हित|हितं|हितः
हित <i>a.</i> [धा-क्त, हि-क्त वा]<BR>—1 Put, laid, placed.<BR>—2 Held, taken.<BR>—3 Suitable, fit, proper, good (with dat.); गोभ्यो हितं गोहितम्.<BR>—4 Useful, advantageous.<BR>—5 Beneficial, advantageous, wholesome, salutary (said of words, diet<BR> &c.); हितं मनोहारि च दुर्लभं वचः Ki. 1. 4, 14. 63.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">Page1758-2</a>]<BR>—6 Friendly, kind, affectionate, well-disposed (generally with loc.); माता<BR> मित्रं पिता चेति स्वभावात् त्रितयं हितम् H. 1. 35.<BR>—7 Sent, impelled.<BR>—8 Gone, proceeded. —9 Auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितः|हित|हितं
हित + .{@-तः@} A friend, benefactor, friendly adviser; हितान्न यः संशृणुते<BR> स किंप्रभुः Ki. 1. 5; आपदामापतन्तीनां हितोऽप्यायाति हेतुताम् H. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिता
हित + .{@-ता@} A causeway, dike; Ms. 9. 274.<BR>—2 N. of particular veins; हिता नाम नाड्यो द्वासप्ततिसहस्राणि हृदयात्<BR> पुरीततमभिप्रतिष्ठन्ते Bṛ. Up. 2. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितम्
हित + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 Benefit, profit or advantage.<BR>—2 Anything proper or suitable.<BR>—3 Well-being, welfare, good.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हितानुबन्धिन्, हितान्वेषिन्, हितार्थिन्, हिताशंसा, हितेच्छा, हितेच्छु, हितोक्तिः, हितोपदेशः, हितैषिन्, हितकर, हितकर्तृ, हितकृत्, हितकारक, हितकाम, हितकाम्या, हितकारिन्, हितकृत्, हितपथ्य, हितप्रणी, हितप्रवृत्त, हितप्रेप्सु, हितबुद्धि, हितवचनम्, हितवाक्यम्, हितवादिन्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितानुबन्धिन्|हितानुबंधिन्
हित + -अनुबन्धिन् <i>a.</i> involving or causing welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितान्वेषिन्
हित + -अन्वेषिन्, -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> seeking anotherʼs welfare; स रामस्य<BR> हितान्वेषी त्वदर्थे हि स मावदत् Mb. 3. 280. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितार्थिन्
हित + -अन्वेषिन्, -अर्थिन् <i>a.</i> seeking anotherʼs welfare; स रामस्य<BR> हितान्वेषी त्वदर्थे हि स मावदत् Mb. 3. 280. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिताशंसा
हित + -आशंसा congratulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितेच्छा
हित + -इच्छा good will, good wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितेच्छु
हित + -इच्छु <i>a.</i> wishing well of, kindly disposed, a well-wisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितोक्तिः|हितोक्ति
हित + -उक्तिः <i>f.</i> salutary instruction, friendly or kind advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितोपदेशः|हितोपदेश
हित + -उपदेशः<BR>—1 friendly advice, salutary instruction.<BR>—2 N. of a celebrated collection of tales ascribed to Viṣṇu-Śarman;<BR> श्रुतो हितोपदेशोऽयं पाटवं संस्कृतोक्तिषु । वाचां सर्वत्र वैचित्र्यं<BR> नीतिविद्यां ददाति च ॥ H. Pr. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितैषिन्
हित + -एषिन् <i>a.</i> desiring anotherʼs welfare, well-wisher, benevolent;<BR> विमलं कलुषीभवच्च चेतः कथयत्येव हितैषिणं रिपुं वा Ki. 13. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकर|हितकरः
हित + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कृत्, -कारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing a kind act or service, friendly, favourable.<BR>—2 useful, rendering a service, serviceable; मूषिका गृहजातापि हन्तव्या<BR> सापकारिणी । उपप्रदानैर्मार्जारो हितकृत् प्रार्थ्यते जनैः ॥ Pt. 1. 95.<BR>—3 beneficial, doing good; दग्धानां किल वह्निना हितकरः सेकोऽपि तस्योद्भवः Pt. 1. 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकरः|हितकर
हित + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कृत्, -कारक + .({@-रः@}) a friend, benefactor; नरपतिहितकर्ता द्वेष्यतां याति<BR> लोके Pt. 1. 131; पण्डितोऽपि वरं शत्रुर्न मूर्खो हितकारकः 417.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकर्तृ
हित + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कृत्, -कारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing a kind act or service, friendly, favourable.<BR>—2 useful, rendering a service, serviceable; मूषिका गृहजातापि हन्तव्या<BR> सापकारिणी । उपप्रदानैर्मार्जारो हितकृत् प्रार्थ्यते जनैः ॥ Pt. 1. 95.<BR>—3 beneficial, doing good; दग्धानां किल वह्निना हितकरः सेकोऽपि तस्योद्भवः Pt. 1. 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकृत्
हित + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कृत्, -कारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing a kind act or service, friendly, favourable.<BR>—2 useful, rendering a service, serviceable; मूषिका गृहजातापि हन्तव्या<BR> सापकारिणी । उपप्रदानैर्मार्जारो हितकृत् प्रार्थ्यते जनैः ॥ Pt. 1. 95.<BR>—3 beneficial, doing good; दग्धानां किल वह्निना हितकरः सेकोऽपि तस्योद्भवः Pt. 1. 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकारक
हित + -कर, -कर्तृ, -कृत्, -कारक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 doing a kind act or service, friendly, favourable.<BR>—2 useful, rendering a service, serviceable; मूषिका गृहजातापि हन्तव्या<BR> सापकारिणी । उपप्रदानैर्मार्जारो हितकृत् प्रार्थ्यते जनैः ॥ Pt. 1. 95.<BR>—3 beneficial, doing good; दग्धानां किल वह्निना हितकरः सेकोऽपि तस्योद्भवः Pt. 1. 371.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम
हित + -काम <i>a.</i> desirous of befriending or benefiting; सुहृदां<BR> हितकामानां न करोतीह यो वचः Pt. 1. 315.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकाम्या
हित + -काम्या desire for anotherʼs welfare, goodwill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकारिन्
हित + -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>m.</i> a benefactor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकृत्
हित + -कारिन्, -कृत् <i>m.</i> a benefactor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितपथ्य
हित + -पथ्य <i>a.</i> useful and salutary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रणी
हित + -प्रणी <i>m.</i> a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रवृत्त
हित + -प्रवृत्त <i>a.</i> intent on the welfare of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितप्रेप्सु
हित + -प्रेप्सु <i>a.</i> = हितकाम; यो बन्धनवधक्लेशान् प्राणिनां न<BR> चिकीर्षति । स सर्वस्य हितप्रेप्सुः सुखमत्यन्तमश्नुते ॥ Ms. 5. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितबुद्धि
हित + -बुद्धि <i>a.</i> friendly-minded, a well-wisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवचनम्
हित + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम् friendly advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवाक्यम्
हित + -वचनम्, -वाक्यम् friendly advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितवादिन्
हित + -वादिन् <i>m.</i> a friendly counsellor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हितकः|हितक
हितकः<BR>—1 A child.<BR>—2 The young of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्तालः|हिन्ताल|हिंताल|हिंतालः
हिन्तालः A kind of palm; केसरहिन्तालबद्धबहलच्छायम् Bk. 13. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दुः|हिन्दु|हिंदुः
हिन्दुः also हिन्दू N. of the people of Hindusthan or Bhāratavarṣa.<BR> The name appears to have been derived from Sindhu, the name of the celebrated<BR> river where the Vedic Āryans recited their Vedic mantras. In the Avesta<BR> स् is pronounced as ह्; so सप्तसिन्धु was pronounced by the<BR> Persians as हप्तहिन्दु. The Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa speaks of हप्तहिन्दु.<BR> Here are a few references in a few Kośas and the Purāṇas:− (1) The<BR> Kālikā-Purāṇa says, “कलिना बलिना नूनमधर्माकलिते कलौ । यवनैर्धोरमाक्रान्ता<BR> हिन्दवो विन्ध्यमाविशन् ॥” (2) The Merutantra of the 8th century A. D.━ “हिन्दुधर्मप्रलोप्तारो<BR> जायन्ते चक्रवर्तिनः । हीनं च दूषयत्येष<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">Page1759-1</a>]<BR> हिन्दूरित्युच्यते प्रिये ॥” (3) The Rāmakośa━ “हिन्दुर्दुष्टो न भवति<BR> नानार्यो न विदूषकः । सद्धर्मपालको विद्वान् श्रौतधर्मपरायणः ॥”<BR> (4) The Hemantakavikośa━ “हिन्दुर्हि नारायणादिदेवताभक्तः” (5) The<BR> Adbhutarūpakośa. “हिन्दुर्हिन्दूश्च पुंसि द्वौ दुष्टानां च विघर्षणे ।”<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हिन्दुधर्मः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दू
हिन्दुः also हिन्दू N. of the people of Hindusthan or Bhāratavarṣa.<BR> The name appears to have been derived from Sindhu, the name of the celebrated<BR> river where the Vedic Āryans recited their Vedic mantras. In the Avesta<BR> स् is pronounced as ह्; so सप्तसिन्धु was pronounced by the<BR> Persians as हप्तहिन्दु. The Bhaviṣya-Purāṇa speaks of हप्तहिन्दु.<BR> Here are a few references in a few Kośas and the Purāṇas:− (1) The<BR> Kālikā-Purāṇa says, “कलिना बलिना नूनमधर्माकलिते कलौ । यवनैर्धोरमाक्रान्ता<BR> हिन्दवो विन्ध्यमाविशन् ॥” (2) The Merutantra of the 8th century A. D.━ “हिन्दुधर्मप्रलोप्तारो<BR> जायन्ते चक्रवर्तिनः । हीनं च दूषयत्येष<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">Page1759-1</a>]<BR> हिन्दूरित्युच्यते प्रिये ॥” (3) The Rāmakośa━ “हिन्दुर्दुष्टो न भवति<BR> नानार्यो न विदूषकः । सद्धर्मपालको विद्वान् श्रौतधर्मपरायणः ॥”<BR> (4) The Hemantakavikośa━ “हिन्दुर्हि नारायणादिदेवताभक्तः” (5) The<BR> Adbhutarūpakośa. “हिन्दुर्हिन्दूश्च पुंसि द्वौ दुष्टानां च विघर्षणे ।”<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हिन्दुधर्मः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1758-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दुधर्मः|हिन्दुधर्म
हिन्दुः + -धर्मः the Hindu religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोलः|हिन्दोल|हिंदोल|हिंदोलः
हिन्दोलः<BR>—1 A swing.<BR>—2 The swing on which the figures of Kṛṣṇa are carried about during<BR> the swing-festival in the bright half of Śrāvaṇa, or the festival itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोलकः|हिन्दोलक|हिंदोलक|हिंदोलकः
हिन्दोलकः, -हिन्दोला<BR>—1 A swing.<BR>—2 A cradle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिन्दोला|हिंदोला
हिन्दोलकः, -हिन्दोला<BR>—1 A swing.<BR>—2 A cradle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिबुकम्
हिबुकम् The fourth astrological house (पाताल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिम|हिमं|हिमः
हिम <i>a.</i> [हि-मक्] Cold, frigid, frosty, dewy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमः|हिम|हिमं
हिम + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 The cold season, winter.<BR>—2 The moon.<BR>—3 The Himālaya mountain.<BR>—4 The sandal tree.<BR>—5 Camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमम्
हिम + .{@-मम्@}<BR>—1 Frost, hoar-frost; हिमनिर्मुक्तयोर्योगे चित्राचन्द्रमसोरिव R. 1. 46, 9. 25, 9. 28, 15. 66, 16. 44;<BR> Ki. 5. 12; अनन्तरत्नप्रभवस्य<BR> यस्य हिमं न सौभाग्यविलोपि जातम् Ku. 1. 3, 11.<BR>—2 Cold, coldness.<BR>—3 A lotus.<BR>—4 Fresh butter.<BR>—5 A pearl.<BR>—6 Night.<BR>—7 Tin.<BR>—8 Sandal wood.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हिमांशुः, हिमाङ्कः, हिमाचलः, हिमाद्रिः, हिमाम्बु, हिमाम्भस्, हिमानिलः, हिमापहः, हिमाब्जम्, हिमाभ्रः, हिमारातिः, हिमारिः, हिमागमः, हिमानद्ध, हिमार्त, हिमालयः, हिमाह्वः, हिमाह्वयः, हिमोत्तरा, हिमोत्पन्ना, हिमोद्भवा, हिमोस्रः, हिमर्तुः, हिमकरः, हिमकूटः, हिमखण्डम्, हिमगिरिः, हिमगुः, हिमगृहम्, हिमजः, हिमजा, हिमज्योतिस्, हिमज्वरः, हिमझटिः, हिमझण्टिः, हिमतैलम्, हिमदीधितिः, हिमदुर्दिनम्, हिमद्युतिः, हिमद्रुमः, हिमद्रुह्, हिमधातुः, हिमधामन्, हिमध्वस्त, हिमपातः, हिमप्रस्थः, हिमभानुः, हिमभास्, हिमरश्मि, हिमशर्करा, हिमशीतल, हिमशौलः, हिमश्रथः, हिमसंहतिः, हिमसरस्, हिमस्रुतः,^1 हिमस्रुतिः, हिमहासकः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/8ab1240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमांशुः|हिमांशु
हिम + -अंशुः<BR>—1 the moon; प्राचीमूले तनुमिव कलामात्रशेषां हिमांशोः Me. 91; मलिनमपि<BR> हिमांशोर्लक्ष्म लक्ष्मीं तनोति Ś. 1. 20; R. 5. 16, 6. 47, 14. 80; Śi. 2. 49.<BR>—2 camphor. ˚अभिख्यम् silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाङ्कः|हिमाङ्क
हिम + -अङ्कः camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाचलः|हिमाचल
हिम + -अचलः, -अद्रिः the Himālaya mountain; प्रस्थं हिमाद्रेर्मृगनाभिगन्धि<BR> किंचित् क्वणत् किंनरमध्युवास Ku. 1. 54; R. 4. 79, 4. 3. ˚जा, ˚तनया<BR>—1 Pārvatī.<BR>—2 the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाद्रिः|हिमाद्रि
हिम + -अचलः, -अद्रिः the Himālaya mountain; प्रस्थं हिमाद्रेर्मृगनाभिगन्धि<BR> किंचित् क्वणत् किंनरमध्युवास Ku. 1. 54; R. 4. 79, 4. 3. ˚जा, ˚तनया<BR>—1 Pārvatī.<BR>—2 the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाम्बु|हिमांबु
हिम + -अम्बु, -अम्भस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 cold water.<BR>—2 dew; निर्धौतहारगुलिकाविशदं हिमाम्भः R. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमाम्भस्|हिमांभस्
हिम + -अम्बु, -अम्भस् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 cold water.<BR>—2 dew; निर्धौतहारगुलिकाविशदं हिमाम्भः R. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिमानिलः|हिमानिल
हिम + -अनिलः a cold wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

