हिरण्मयम्
हिरण्मय + .{@-यम्@} One of the nine divisions of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यम्
हिरण्यम् [हिरणमेव स्वार्थे यत्]<BR>—1 Gold; Ms. 2. 246.<BR>—2 Any vessel of gold; मन्त्रवत् प्राशनं चास्य हिरण्यमधुसर्पिषाम्<BR> Ms. 2. 29 (some take in the first sense).<BR>—3 Silver; (ददौ) हिरण्यस्य सुवर्णस्य मुक्तानां विद्रुमस्य च<BR> Rām. 1. 74. 5; Mb. 13. 57. 34.<BR>—4 Any precious metal.<BR>—5 Wealth, property; अपदेश्यैश्च संन्यस्य हिरण्यं तस्य तत्त्वतः Ms. 8. 182.<BR>—6 Semen virile.<BR>—7 A <i>cowrie</i>.<BR>—8 particular measure.<BR>—9 A substance.<BR>—10 The thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्या
हिरण्यम् + .{@-ण्या@} One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हिरण्याक्षः, हिरण्यकक्ष, हिरण्यकर्तृ, हिरण्यकवच, हिरण्यकशिपुः, हिरण्यकारः, हिरण्यकेशी, हिरण्यकोशः, हिरण्यगर्भः, हिरण्यद, हिरण्यनाभः, हिरण्यबाहुः, हिरण्यबिन्दुः, हिरण्यरेतस्, हिरण्यवर्चस्, हिरण्यवर्णा, हिरण्यवाहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्याक्षः|हिरण्याक्ष
हिरण्यम् + -अक्षः N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">Page1760-1</a>]<BR> a celebrated demon, twin brother of Hiraṇyakaśipu; अंशे हिरण्याक्षरिपोः<BR> स जाते हिरण्यनाभे तनवे नयज्ञः R. 18. 25. [On the strength of a<BR> boon from Brahman, he became insolent and oppressive, seized upon the<BR> earth, and carried it with him into the depths of the ocean. Viṣṇu therefore<BR> became incarnate as a boar, killed the demon and lifted up the earth.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1759-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकक्ष
हिरण्यम् + -कक्ष <i>a.</i> wearing a golden girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकर्तृ
हिरण्यम् + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> goldsmith; यथा हिरण्यकर्ता वै रूप्यमग्नौ विशोधयेत्<BR> Mb. 12. 280. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकवच
हिरण्यम् + -कवच <i>a.</i> having golden armour (said of Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकशिपुः|हिरण्यकशिपु
हिरण्यम् + -कशिपुः N. of a celebrated king of demons. [He was a son of Kaśyapa<BR> and Diti, and by virtue of a boon from Brahman, he became so powerful<BR> that he usurped the sovereignty of Indra and oppressed the three worlds.<BR> He freely blasphemed the great god and subjected his son Prahrāda to<BR> untold cruelties for acknowledging Viṣṇu as the Supreme deity. But he<BR> was eventually torn to pieces by Viṣṇu in the form of Narasimha; see प्रह्राद].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकारः|हिरण्यकार
हिरण्यम् + -कारः a goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकेशी
हिरण्यम् + -केशी a branch (शाखा) of Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यकोशः|हिरण्यकोश
हिरण्यम् + -कोशः gold and silver (whether wrought or unwrought).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यगर्भः|हिरण्यगर्भ
हिरण्यम् + -गर्भः<BR>—1 N. of Brahman (as born from a golden-egg).<BR>—2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>—3 the soul invested by the subtitle body or सूक्ष्मशरीर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यद|हिरण्यदः
हिरण्यम् + -द <i>a.</i> giving or granting gold; भूमिदो भूमिमाप्नोति दीर्घमायुर्हिरण्यदः Ms. 4. 230.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिरण्यदः|हिरण्यद
