हिल्वलाः <i>f.</i> pl. N. of five small stars in the head of the lunar<BR> mansion called मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ही
ही <i>ind.</i> An interjection of<BR>—1 Surprise (ah!); ही वीर कुरुराजेति ही भीम इति जल्पताम् Mb. 1. 135. 2;<BR> हतविधिलसितानां ही विचित्रो विपाकः Śi. 11. 64; or आः,<BR> कष्टम्, बत, ही, चित्रम् … … Bk. 6. 11 and ही चित्रं लक्ष्मणेनोचे<BR> Bk. 14. 39; (often repeated in theatrical language in this sense).<BR>—2 Fatigue, despondency or sorrow.<BR>—3 Reason (cf. हि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन|हीनः
हीन <i>p. p.</i> [हा-क्त तस्य नः ईत्वम्]<BR>—1 Left, abandoned, forsaken &c.; यो वैश्यः स्याद् बहुपशुर्हीनक्रतुरसोमपः ।<BR> कुटुम्बात् तस्य तद् द्रव्यमाहरेद्यज्ञसिद्धये ॥ Ms. 11. 12.<BR>—2 Destitute or deprived of, bereft of, without; (with instr. or in comp.);<BR> तया (संतत्या) हीनं विधातर्मां कथं पश्यन्न दूयसे R. 1. 70;<BR> गुणैर्हीना न शोभन्ते निर्गन्धा इव किंशुकाः Subhāṣ.; so द्रव्य˚,<BR> मति˚, उत्साह˚ &c.; अन्नहीनो दहेद्राष्ट्रं मन्त्रहीनस्तु ऋत्विजः ।<BR> दीक्षितं दक्षिणाहीनो नास्ति यज्ञसमो रिपुः Ms. 11. 40 (v. l.)<BR>—3 Excluded, shut out from (with abl.).<BR>—4 Decayed, wasted.<BR>—5 Deficient, defective; हीनातिरिक्तगात्रो वा तमप्यपनयेत्ततः Ms. 3. 242.<BR>—6 Subtracted.<BR>—7 Less, lower; हीनान्नवस्त्रवेषः स्यात् सर्वदा गुरुसंनिधौ Ms. 2. 194;<BR> हीना हीनान् प्रसूयन्ते 10. 31.<BR>—8 Low, base, mean, vile.<BR>—9 Defeated (in a law-suit).<BR>—10 Lost, strayed from (a caravan).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनः|हीन
हीन + .{@-नः@}<BR>—1 A defective witness.<BR>—2 A faulty respondent; (Nārada enumarates five kinds:− अन्यवादी क्रियाद्वेषी<BR> नोपस्थायी निरुत्तरः । आहूतप्रपलायी च हीनः पञ्चविधः स्मृतः ॥).<BR>—3 Substraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीना
हीन + .{@-ना@} A female mouse; cf. दीना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनम्
हीन + .{@-नम्@} Deficiency, want.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हीनाङ्ग, हीनकर्मन्, हीनक्रिय, हीनकुल, हीनज, हीनक्रतु, हीनजाति, हीनपक्ष, हीनप्रतिज्ञा, हीनयानम्, हीनयोनिः, हीनरोमन्, हीनवर्ण, हीनवादः, हीनवादिन्, हीनसख्यम्, हीनसामन्तः, हीनसन्धिः, हीनसेवा<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनाङ्ग|हीनांग|हीनाङ्गः
हीन + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> deficient in a limb, crippled, maimed, defective;<BR> हीनाङ्गी वाधिकाङ्गी वा या भवेत् कन्यका नृणाम् । भर्तुः स्यात् सा विनाशाय<BR> स्वशीलनिधनाय च ॥ Pt. 5. 95; Ms. 4. 141; Y. 1. 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनाङ्गी
हीन + -अङ्ग + .({@-गी@}) a small ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनकर्मन्|हीनकर्म्मन्
हीन + -कर्मन्, -क्रिय <i>a.</i> neglecting the customary religious rites; Ms. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनक्रिय
हीन + -कर्मन्, -क्रिय <i>a.</i> neglecting the customary religious rites; Ms. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनकुल
हीन + -कुल, -ज <i>a.</i> baseborn, of low family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनज
हीन + -कुल, -ज <i>a.</i> baseborn, of low family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनक्रतु
हीन + -क्रतु <i>a.</i> one who neglects his sacrifice; Ms. 11. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनजाति|हीनजातिः
हीन + -जाति <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of a low caste.<BR>—2 excommunicated, outcaste, degraded; हीनजातिस्त्रियं मोहादुद्वहन्तो<BR> द्विजातयः । कुलान्येव नयन्त्याशु ससंतानानि शूद्रताम् ॥ Ms. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनपक्ष
हीन + -पक्ष <i>a.</i> unprotected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनप्रतिज्ञ
हीन + -प्रतिज्ञ^1 <i>a.</i> faithless.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by . Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/6b5cd78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनयानम्
हीन + -यानम् N. of the earliest system of Buddhist doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनयोनिः|हीनयोनि
हीन + -योनिः <i>f.</i> low birth or origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनरोमन्
हीन + -रोमन् <i>a.</i> bald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवर्ण|हीनवर्णः
हीन + -वर्ण <i>a.</i><BR>—1 of low caste.<BR>—2 of inferior rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवादः|हीनवाद
हीन + -वादः a defective statement, contradictory evidence, prevarication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनवादिन्
हीन + -वादिन् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 making a defective statement.<BR>—2 prevaricating.<BR>—3 dumb, speechless.<BR>—4 cast in law, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसख्यम्
हीन + -सख्यम् associating with low persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसामन्तः
हीन + -सामन्तः a deposed king; Śukra. 1. 189.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसन्धिः|हीनसन्धि|हीनसंधि
हीन + -सन्धिः an agreement made by an inferior king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनसेवा
हीन + -सेवा attendance on base persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनक
हीनक <i>a.</i> Deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीनित
हीनित <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Deprived of oneʼs own.<BR>—2 Separated from.<BR>—3 Subtracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन्तालः|हीन्ताल|हींताल|हींतालः
हीन्तालः The marshy date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरः|हीर|हीरं
हीरः [हृ-क नि]<BR>—1 A snake.<BR>—2 A necklace.<BR>—3 A lion.<BR>—4 N. of the father of Srīharṣa, the author of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">Page1761-1</a>]<BR> Naishadha-charita. —5 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरः|हीर|हीरं
हीरः + .{@-रः, -रम्@} The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—2 A diamond; (occurring in the concluding stanza of each canto of नैषधचरित).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हीराङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरम्
हीरः + .{@-रः, -रम्@} The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>—2 A diamond; (occurring in the concluding stanza of each canto of नैषधचरित).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हीराङ्गः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1760-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीराङ्गः|हीराङ्ग|हीरांग
हीरः + -अङ्गः the thunder-bolt of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरकः|हीरक
हीरकः A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरा
हीरा<BR>—1 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>—2 An ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलम्
हीलम् Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलना
हीलना Injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलुकम्
हीलुकम् A kind of rum (distilled from molasses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीही
हीही <i>ind.</i> A particle expressive of surprise or merriment; see ही.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु €3 P. (जुहोति, हुत; <i>pass.</i> हूयते; <i>caus.</i><BR> हावयति-ते; <i>desid.</i> जुहूषति)<BR>—1 To offer or present (as oblation to fire); make an offering to or in<BR> honour of a deity (with acc.); sacrifice; यो मन्त्रपूतां तनुमप्यहौषीत्<BR> R. 13. 45; जटाधरः सन् जुहुधीह पावकम् Ki. 1. 44; हविर्जुहुधि<BR> पावकम् Bk. 20. 11; Ms. 3. 87; Y. 1. 99.<BR>—2 To perform a sacrifice. —3 To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत|हुतं|हुतः
हुत <i>p. p.</i> [हु-क्त]<BR>—1 Offered as an oblation to fire, burnt as a sacrificial offering; हुतं<BR> च दत्तं च तथैव तिष्ठति Karṇabhāra 1. 22.<BR>—2 One to whom an oblation is offered; Ś. 4; R. 2. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतः|हुत|हुतं
हुत + .{@-तः@} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतम्
हुत + .{@-तम्@}<BR>—1 An oblation, offering.<BR>—2 An Oblation to fire; द्वे देवानभाजयदिति हुतं च प्रहुतं च<BR> Bṛ. Up. 1. 5. 2; Bg. 9. 16.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हुताग्नि, हुताशः, हुताशनः, हुताशनी, हुताशः, हुतजातवेदस्, हुतभुज्, हुतवहः, हुतहोमः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताग्नि
हुत + -अग्नि <i>a.</i> who has made an oblation to fire; हुताग्निर्ब्राह्मणांश्चार्च्य<BR> प्रविशेत् स शुभां सभाम् Ms. 7. 145; यथाविधिहुताग्नीनाम् R. 1. 6.<BR>━(<i>m.</i>) a sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशः|हुताश
हुत + -अशः<BR>—1 fire.<BR>—2 N. of the number ‘three’. —3 Plumbago Ceylanica (Mar. चित्रक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशनः|हुताशन
हुत + -अशनः<BR>—1 fire; समीरणो नोदयिता भवेति व्यादिश्यते केन हुताशनस्य Ku. 3. 21;<BR> R. 4. 1.<BR>—2 N. of Śiva.<BR>—3 the Chitraka tree. ˚सहायः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशनी
हुत + -अशनी the full-moon day in the month of Phālguna (होलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुताशः|हुताश
हुत + -आशः fire; प्रदक्षिणीकृत्य हुतं हुताशम् R. 2. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतजातवेदस्
हुत + -जातवेदस् <i>a.</i> one who has made an oblation to fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतभुज्
हुत + -भुज् <i>m.</i> fire; शक्यो वारयितुं जलेन हुतभुक् Bh. 2. 11;<BR> नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव च्छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 7; U. 5. 9. ˚प्रिया<BR> Svāhā, the wife of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतवहः|हुतवह
हुत + -वहः fire; जनाकीर्णं मन्ये हुतवहपरीतं गृहमिव Ś. 5. 10;<BR> शीतांशुस्तपनो हितो हुतवहः Gīt. 9; Me. 45; Ṛs. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतहोमः|हुतहोम
हुत + -होमः a Brāhmaṇa who has offered oblations to fire; आश्रमादाश्रमं<BR> गत्वा हुतहोमो जितेन्द्रियः Ms. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतहोमम्
हुत + -होमः + .({@-मम्@}) a burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतिः|हुति
हुतिः <i>f.</i> Offering oblations; यज्ञो न मेऽस्ति हुतिदानदयादियुक्तः<BR> Bhagavaccharaṇa S. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड्
हुड् I. €1 P. (होडै) To go. ━II. €6 P. (हुडति)<BR>—1 To collect.<BR>—2 To dive, sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडः|हुड
हुडः<BR>—1 A ram.<BR>—2 An iron stake for keeping out thieves.<BR>—3 A kind of fence.<BR>—4 An iron club.<BR>—5 A kind of bulwark or fence.<BR>—6 A place for voiding excrement on a chariot.<BR>—7 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुः|हुडु
हुडुः A ram; जम्बुको हुडुयुद्धेन Pt. 1. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुक्कः|हुडुक्क
हुडुक्कः<BR>—1 A small hour-glass-shaped drum or small cymbal; न ते हुडुक्केन न<BR> सोऽपि ढक्कया न मर्दलैः सापि न तेऽपि ढक्कया. N. 15. 17.<BR>—2 A kind of bird (दात्यूह).<BR>—3 The bolt of a door.<BR>—4 A drunken man.<BR>—5 A stick bound with iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुत्
हुडुत् <i>n.</i><BR>—1 Noise of a bull.<BR>—2 A sound of threat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुम्बः|हुडुम्ब
हुडुम्बः Parched rice (called हुडुम्); L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्ड्|हुंड्
हुण्ड् €1 Ā. (हुण्डते)<BR>—1 To collect.<BR>—2 To select, choose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डः|हुण्ड|हुंड|हुंडः
हुण्डः<BR>—1 A tiger.<BR>—2 A ram.<BR>—3 A blockhead.<BR>—4 A village-hog.<BR>—5 A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डनम्
हुण्डनम् Becoming benumbed or paralyzed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डिः|हुण्डि
हुण्डिः <i>m., f.</i> A heap or lump of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुण्डिका
हुण्डिका<BR>—1 A bill of exchange, bond (Mar. हुंडी); Rāj. T.<BR>—2 Assignment (for the maintenance of soldiers); <i>ibid.</i><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्
हुम् <i>ind.</i> A particle (originally an imitative sound) expressing<BR>—1 Remembrance or recollection; हुं ज्ञातम् or रामो नाम बभूव हुं<BR> तदबला सीतेति हुम्.<BR>—2 Doubt; चैत्रो हुं मैत्रो हुम्.<BR>—3 Assent; U. 5. 35.<BR>—4 Anger.<BR>—5 Aversion.<BR>—6 Reproach.<BR>—7 Interrogation. (In spells and incantations हुम् is often found used<BR> with dat.; <i>e. g.</i> ॐ कवचाय हुम्). (हुंकृ means ‘to utter the sound <i>hum</i>’<BR>, ‘to roar, grunt, bellow’, as in अनुहुंकृ ‘to roar in return’<BR>; अनुहुंकुरुते घनध्वनिं न हि गोमायुरुतानि केसरी Śi. 16. 25.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हुङ्कारः, हुङ्कृतिः, हुङ्कृतम्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कारः|हुङ्कार|हुंकार
हुम् + -कारः, -कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 uttering the sound ‘hum’; पृष्टा पुनः पुनः कान्ता हुंकारैरेव भाषते.<BR>—2 a menacing sound, sound of defiance; क्षतहुंकारशंसिनः Ku. 2. 26;<BR> हुंकारेणेव धनुषः स हि विध्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1; R. 7. 58; Ku. 5. 54.<BR>—3 roaring, bellowing in general.<BR>—4 the grunting of a boar.<BR>—5 the twang of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कृतिः|हुङ्कृति
हुम् + -कारः, -कृतिः <i>f.</i><BR>—1 uttering the sound ‘hum’; पृष्टा पुनः पुनः कान्ता हुंकारैरेव भाषते.<BR>—2 a menacing sound, sound of defiance; क्षतहुंकारशंसिनः Ku. 2. 26;<BR> हुंकारेणेव धनुषः स हि विध्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1; R. 7. 58; Ku. 5. 54.<BR>—3 roaring, bellowing in general.<BR>—4 the grunting of a boar.<BR>—5 the twang of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुङ्कृतम्
हुम् + -कृतम्<BR>—1 an incantation.<BR>—2 the grunt of a wild boar.<BR>—3 the roar of thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुंभा|हुम्भा
हुंभा = हंबा; तस्या हुंभारवोत्सृष्टाः पह्लवाः शतशो नृप Rām. 1. 54. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुरुट्टकः|हुरुट्टक
हुरुट्टकः A kind of bolt or hook (for elephants).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्च्छ्
हुर्च्छ् €1 P. (हूर्च्छति)<BR>—1 To be crooked.<BR>—2 To act dishonestly, deceive.<BR>—3 To escape; L. D. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्च्छनम्
हुर्च्छनम् Dishonesty, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुल्
हुल् €1 P. (होलति)<BR>—1 To go.<BR>—2 To cover or conceal.<BR>—3 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलः|हुल
हुलः A kind of implement or knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलहुली
हुलहुली A kind of inarticulate sound, uttered by women on joyful occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलिहुली
हुलिहुली<BR>—1 Nuptial music.<BR>—2 Roaring, howling; Mk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलुः|हुलु
हुलुः A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहु|हुहुः
हुहु(हू), हूहू <i>m.</i> A kind of Gandharva; मुक्तो<BR> देवलशापेन हूहूर्गन्धर्वसत्तमः Bhāg. 8. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहू
हुहु(हू), हूहू <i>m.</i> A kind of Gandharva; मुक्तो<BR> देवलशापेन हूहूर्गन्धर्वसत्तमः Bhāg. 8. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूहू
हुहु(हू), हूहू <i>m.</i> A kind of Gandharva; मुक्तो<BR> देवलशापेन हूहूर्गन्धर्वसत्तमः Bhāg. 8. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हू
हू <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 An interjection of calling.<BR>—2 Of contempt.<BR>—3 Of pride.<BR>—4 Of grief (oh! ah! alas &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूड्
हूड् €1 Ā. (हूडते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1761-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूणः|हूण
हूणः (-नः)<BR>—1 A barbarian, foreigner; सद्यो मण्डितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि नारङ्गकम्;<BR> ग्रासं ग्रासं चरति परितः कश्चिदेणाङ्कहूणः Rām. Ch. 6. 96.<BR>—2 A kind of golden coin, (probably current in the country of the Hūṇas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूनः|हून
हूणः (-नः)<BR>—1 A barbarian, foreigner; सद्यो मण्डितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि नारङ्गकम्;<BR> ग्रासं ग्रासं चरति परितः कश्चिदेणाङ्कहूणः Rām. Ch. 6. 96.<BR>—2 A kind of golden coin, (probably current in the country of the Hūṇas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूणाः
हूणः (-नः) + .{@-णाः@} <i>m.</i> pl. N. of a country or its people; हूणावरोधानाम् R. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत|हूतं
हूत <i>p. p.</i> [ह्वे-क्त संप्रसारणम्] Called, summoned, invited<BR> &c.; see ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूतम्
हूतम् The act of calling; P. VIII. 2. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूतिः|हूति
हूतिः <i>f.</i> [ह्वे-क्तिन् संप्रसारणम्]<BR>—1 Calling, inviting.<BR>—2 Challenging.<BR>—3 A name; as in हरिहेतिहूति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूम्
हूम् &c. See हुम्; (a particle expressing anger); … हूं मातर्,<BR> दैवतानि धिक् Bk. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूरवः|हूरव
हूरवः A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ €1 U. (हरति-ते, जहार, जह्रे, अहार्षीत्, अहृत, हरिष्यति-ते,<BR> हर्तुम्, हृत; <i>pass.</i> ह्रियते)<BR>—1 To take, carry, convey, lead, (often used with two accusatives in this<BR> sense); अजां ग्रामं हरति Sk.; संदेशं मे हर धनपतिक्रोधविश्लेषितस्य<BR> Me. 7; Ms. 4. 74.<BR>—2 To carry off or away, take or draw to a distance; हरामि रामसौमित्री<BR> मृगो भूत्वा मृगद्युवौ Bk. 5. 47.<BR>—3 To take away, rob, plunder, steal; दुर्वृत्ता जारजन्मानो हरिष्यन्तीति<BR> शङ्कया Bv. 4. 45; R. 3. 39; Ku. 2. 47; Bk. 2. 39; Ms. 7. 43.<BR>—4 To strip off, deprive of, despoil, take away; वृन्तात्श्लथं हरति<BR> पुष्पमनोकहानाम् R. 5. 69; Bk. 15. 116; Ms. 8. 334.<BR>—5 To take away, cure, destroy; उत्कण्ठां तां हरिष्यामि मेघलेखामिवानिलः<BR> Rām. 7. 40. 19; तथापि हरते तापं लोकानामुन्नतो घनः Bv. 1. 39;<BR> R. 15. 24; Me. 31.<BR>—6 To attract, captivate, win over, influence, subdue, enchant; चेतो<BR> न कस्य हरते गतिरङ्गनायाः Bv. 2. 157; ये भावा हृदयं हरन्ति 1. 103;<BR> तवास्मि गीतरागेण हारिणा प्रसभं हृतः Ś. 1. 5; हरति<BR> मे हरिवाहनदिङ्मुखम् V. 3. 6; मृगया जहार चतुरेव कामिनी R. 9. 69, 10. 83;<BR> Ṛs. 6. 21; इन्द्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरन्ति प्रसभं मनः<BR> Bg. 2. 60, 6. 44; Ms. 6. 59.<BR>—7 To gain, acquire, obtain; ततो विंशं नृपो हरेत् Ms. 8. 391, 153;<BR> Y. 2. 123; स हरतु सुभगपताकाम् Dk.<BR>—8 To have, possess; अङ्गैः सुकुमारतरैः सा कुसुमानां श्रियं हरति Bv. 2. 163.<BR>—9 To surpass, eclipse; त्वां हरन्तीं श्रियं श्रियः Bk. 5. 71.<BR>—10 To marry; पित्रे न दद्याच्छुल्कं तु कन्यामृतुमतीं हरन् Ms. 9. 93.<BR>—11 To divide.<BR>—12 To cast, throw (as an arrow).<BR>—13 To accept, receive, inherit.<BR>—14 To offer. ━<i>Caus.</i> (हारयति-ते)<BR>—1 To cause to take, carry or convey, send (something) by one, (with acc.<BR> or instr.); भृत्यं भृत्येन वा भारं हारयति Sk.; जीमूतेन स्वकुशलमयीं<BR> हारयिष्यन् प्रवृत्तिम् Me. 4; Ms. 8. 114; Ku. 2. 39.<BR>—2 To cause to be taken away, to lose, be deprived of.<BR>—3 To give away. ━<i>Desid.</i> (जिहीर्षति-ते) To wish to take &c.<BR>━II. €3 P. (जिहर्ति) To take by force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्
हृत् <i>a.</i> (At the end of comp. only) Taking away, seizing, removing,<BR> carrying off, attracting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत|हृतं
हृत <i>p. p.</i> [हृ-क्त]<BR>—1 Taken or carried away.<BR>—2 Seized.<BR>—3 Captivated.<BR>—4 Accepted.<BR>—5 Divided; see हृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतम्
हृत + .{@-तम्@} A portion, share.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हृताधिकार, हृतोत्तर, हृतोत्तरीय, हृतदार, हृतद्रव्य, हृतधन, हृतप्रसाद, हृतमानस, हृतशिष्ट, हृतसर्वस्व, हृतसार<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृताधिकार
हृत + -अधिकार <i>a.</i><BR>—1 dismissed from authority, turned out.<BR>—2 deprived of oneʼs<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-2" target="_blank">Page1762-2</a>]<BR> due rights.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतोत्तर
हृत + -उत्तर <i>a.</i> deprived of an answer; हृतोत्तरं तत्त्वविचारमध्ये Ki. 17. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतोत्तरीय
हृत + -उत्तरीय <i>a.</i> having the upper garments stripped off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतदार
हृत + -दार <i>a.</i> bereft of oneʼs wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1762-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतद्रव्य
