हृषु + .{@-षुः@}<BR>—1 Fire.<BR>—2 The sun.<BR>—3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्ट|हृष्टः
हृष्ट <i>p. p.</i> [हृष्-क्त]<BR>—1 Pleased, rejoiced (= हृषित).<BR>—2 Bristling, erect, standing on end.<BR>—3 Rigid, stiff.<BR>—4 Blunted.<BR>—5 Surprised.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हृष्टचित्त, हृष्टमानस, हृष्टतनु, हृष्टतनूरुह, हृष्टरोमन्, हृष्टरूप, हृष्टवदन, हृष्टसंकल्प, हृष्टहृदय<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टचित्त
हृष्ट + -चित्त, -मानस <i>a.</i> rejoiced in mind, glad at heart, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टमानस|हृष्टमानसः
हृष्ट + -चित्त, -मानस <i>a.</i> rejoiced in mind, glad at heart, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टतनु
हृष्ट + -तनु, -तनूरुह, -रोमन् <i>a.</i> having the hair on the body bristling<BR> or thrilling (with joy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टतनूरुह
हृष्ट + -तनु, -तनूरुह, -रोमन् <i>a.</i> having the hair on the body bristling<BR> or thrilling (with joy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टरोमन्
हृष्ट + -तनु, -तनूरुह, -रोमन् <i>a.</i> having the hair on the body bristling<BR> or thrilling (with joy).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टरूप
हृष्ट + -रूप <i>a.</i> in a happy mood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टवदन
हृष्ट + -वदन <i>a.</i> having a cheerful countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टसंकल्प
हृष्ट + -संकल्प <i>a.</i> contented, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टहृदय
हृष्ट + -हृदय <i>a.</i> joyous-hearted, cheerful, merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टिः|हृष्टि
हृष्टिः <i>f.</i> [हृष्-क्तिन्]<BR>—1 Delight, happiness, joy, pleasure; वस्ताण्डवं देवि भूयादभीष्टपै<BR> च हृष्टपै च नः Māl. 5. 23.<BR>—2 Pride.<BR>—3 Knowledge.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हृष्टियोनिः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टियोनिः|हृष्टियोनि
हृष्टिः + -योनिः a kind of semi-impotent man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हे
हे <i>ind.</i><BR>—1 A vocative particle (oh!, oh!); हे कृष्ण हे यादव हे सखेति<BR> Bg. 11. 41; हे राजानस्त्यजत सुकविप्रेमवन्धे विरोधम् Vikr. 18. 107.<BR>—2 A particle used in challenging.<BR>—3 An interjection expressing defiance, envy, ill-will or disapprobation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1763-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेक्का
हेक्का Hiccough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ्
हेठ् €1 P. (हेठति)<BR>—1 To be wicked.<BR>—2 To vex, trouble, harass.<BR>—3 To strike, hurt, injure.<BR>—4 To be born or produced.<BR>—5 To purify.<BR>—6 To cause prosperity, produce happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठः|हेठ
हेठः<BR>—1 Vexation.<BR>—2 Hindrance, obstruction, opposition.<BR>—3 Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड्
हेड् I. €1 Ā. (हेड्ते) To disregard, slight, neglect; अहेडमानास्त्वरया<BR> स्म दूता रात्र्यां तु ते तत्पुरमेव याताः Rām. 2. 68. 22. ━II. €1 P. (हेडति)<BR>—1 To surround.<BR>—2 To attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडः|हेड
हेडः Disregard, slight.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हेडजः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडजः|हेडज
हेडः + -जः anger, displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडाबुक्कः|हेडाबुक्क
हेडाबु(वु)क्कः A horse-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडावुक्कः|हेडावुक्क
हेडाबु(वु)क्कः A horse-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतिः|हेति
हेतिः <i>m., f.</i> [हन्-करणे क्तिन् नि˚]<BR>—1 A weapon, a missile; समरविजयी हेतिदलितः Bh. 2. 44; R. 10. 12;<BR> Ki. 3. 56, 14. 30.<BR>—2 A stroke, injury.<BR>—3 A ray of the sun.<BR>—4 Light, splendour.<BR>—5 Flame; वहन्ति सर्वभूतानि त्वत्तो निष्क्रम्य हेतयः Mb. 5. 16. 6; Śi. 14. 25.<BR>—6 An implement, instrument; सध्यड् नियम्य यतयो यमकर्तहेतिं जहपुः<BR> स्वराडिव निपानखनित्रमिन्द्रः Bhāg. 2. 7. 48.<BR>—7 Shot, impact (of a bow-string).<BR>—8 A young sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुः|हेतु
हेतुः [हि-तुन् Uṇ. 1. 73]<BR>—1 Cause, reason, object, motive; इति हेतुस्तदुद्भवे K. P. 1; Māl. 1. 23;<BR> R. 1. 10; नीचैराख्यं गिरिमधिवसेस्तत्र विश्रामहेतोः Me. 25; Ś. 3. 12.<BR>—2 Source, origin; स पिता पितरस्तासां केवलं जन्महेतवः R. 1. 24<BR> ‘authors of their being’.<BR>—3 A means or instrument.<BR>—4 The logical reason, the reason for an inference, middle term (forming<BR> the second member of the five-membered syllogism).<BR>—5 Logic, science of reasoning.<BR>—6 Any logical proof or argument.<BR>—7 A rhetorical reason (regarded by some writers as a figure of speech);<BR> it is thus defined:− हेताहतुमता सार्धमभेदो हेतुरुच्यते.<BR>—8 (In gram.) The agent of the causal verb; P. I. 4. 55.<BR>—9 (with Buddhists) Primary cause.<BR>—10 (with Pāśupatas) The external world and senses (that cause the bondage of the soul).<BR>—11 Mode, manner.<BR>—12 Condition.<BR>—13 Price, cost; दीन्नाराणां दशशती पञ्चाशदधिकाभवत् । धान्यखारीक्रये<BR> हेतुर्देशे दुर्भिक्षविक्षते Rāj. T. 5. 71. (<i>N. B.</i> The forms हेतुना,<BR> हेतोः, rarely हेतौ, are used adverbially in the sense of ‘by reason of’<BR>, ‘on account of’, ‘because of’, with gen. or in comp.; तमसा बहुरूपेण<BR> वेष्टिताः कर्महेतुना Ms. 1. 49; शास्त्रविज्ञानहेतुना; अल्पस्य हेतोर्बहु<BR> हातुमिच्छन् R. 2. 47; विस्मृतं कस्य हेतोः Mu. 1. 1 &c.).<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हेत्वपदेशः, हेत्ववधारणम्, हेत्वाक्षेप, हेत्वाभासः, हेतूत्प्रेक्षा, हेतूपमा, हेतूपक्षेपः, हेतूपन्यासः, हेतुकर्तृ, हेतुदुष्ट, हेतुदृष्टिः, हेतुबलिक, हेतुयुक्त, हेतुरूपकम्, हेतुवादः, हेतुवादिन्, हेतुविशेषोक्तिः, हेतुशास्त्रम्, हेतुहेतुमत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्वपदेशः|हेत्वपदेश
हेतुः + -अपदेशः adducing the <i>hetu</i> (in the form of the five-membered syllogism).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्ववधारणम्
हेतुः + -अवधारणम् (in dram.) reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्वाक्षेप
हेतुः + -आक्षेप (in Rhet.) an objection accompanied with reasons; न<BR> स्तूयसे नरेन्द्र त्वं ददासीति कदाचन । स्वमेव मत्वा गृह्णन्ति यतस्त्वद्धनमर्थिनः<BR> ॥ इत्येवमादिराक्षेपो हेत्वाक्षेप इति स्मृतः । Kāv. 2. 167-168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेत्वाभासः|हेत्वाभास
हेतुः + -आभासः ‘the semblance of a reason’, a fallacious middle term,<BR> fallacy; (it is of five kinds:− सव्यभिचार or अनैकान्तिक, विरुद्ध,<BR> असिद्ध, सत्प्रतिपक्ष and बाधित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतूत्प्रेक्षा
हेतुः + -उत्प्रेक्षा, -उपमा a simile accompanied with reasons.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">Page1764-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतूपमा
हेतुः + -उत्प्रेक्षा, -उपमा a simile accompanied with reasons.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">Page1764-2</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतूपक्षेपः
हेतुः + -उपक्षेपः, -उपन्यासः adducing a reason, statement of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतूपन्यासः|हेतूपन्यास
हेतुः + -उपक्षेपः, -उपन्यासः adducing a reason, statement of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुकर्तृ
हेतुः + -कर्तृ <i>m.</i> the causal subject; याजयेदिति हेतुकर्तुरेवैतत्<BR> प्रत्यक्षं वचनम्, लक्षणया यजेः कर्तुः ŚB. on MS. 10. 8. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुदुष्ट
हेतुः + -दुष्ट <i>a.</i> unreasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुदृष्टिः|हेतुदृष्टि
हेतुः + -दृष्टिः scepticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुबलिक
हेतुः + -बलिक <i>a.</i> strong in argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुयुक्त
हेतुः + -युक्त <i>a.</i> well-founded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुरूपकम्
हेतुः + -रूपकम् a metaphor accompanied with reasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुवादः|हेतुवाद
हेतुः + -वादः<BR>—1 disputation, controversy.<BR>—2 fraud (कपट); न हेतुवादाल्लोभाद्वा धर्मं जह्यां कथंचन Mb. 5. 91. 24.<BR>—3 assigning a cause (sceptically); न यक्ष्यन्ति न होष्यन्ति हेतुवादविमोहिताः<BR> Mb. 3. 190. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुवादिन्
हेतुः + -वादिन्<BR>—1 a disputant.<BR>—2 a sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुविशेषोक्तिः|हेतुविशेषोक्ति
हेतुः + -विशेषोक्तिः a mention of difference accompanied with reasons;<BR> एकचक्रो रथो यन्ता विकलो विषमा हयाः । आक्रामत्येव तेजस्वी तथाप्यर्को<BR> नभस्तलम् ॥ सैषा हेतुविशेषोक्तिस्तेजस्वीति विशेषणात् ॥ Kāv. 2. 328-329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुशास्त्रम्
हेतुः + -शास्त्रम् a logically-treated work, any heretical work questioning<BR> the authority of Smṛtis or revelation; योऽवमन्येत ते मूले हेतुशास्त्राश्रयाद्<BR> द्विजः Ms. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुहेतुमत्
हेतुः + -हेतुमत् <i>m.</i> du. cause and effect. ˚भावः the relation<BR> existing between cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुक|हेतुकः
हेतुक <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Causing, producing (at the end of comp.).<BR>—2 Destined for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुकः|हेतुक
हेतुक + .{@-कः@}<BR>—1 A cause, reason.<BR>—2 An instrument.<BR>—3 A logician; Ms. 12. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुता
हेतुता, -त्वम्<BR> Causation, the existence of cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुत्वम्
हेतुता, -त्वम्<BR> Causation, the existence of cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुमत्|हेतुमन्त्
हेतुमत् <i>a.</i><BR>—1 Having a reason or cause.<BR>—2 Having the <i>hetu</i>. ━<i>m.</i> An effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुवन्निगदः
हेतुवन्निगदः A prose (Vedic) statement supplying or stating the<BR> purpose; असति हेतौ न ह्यत्रानुयाजान् यक्ष्यन् भवतीति हेतुवन्निगदो<BR> नोपपद्येत । ŚB. on MS. 4. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमम्
हेमम् [हि-मन्]<BR>—1 Gold.<BR>—2 The thorn-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमः|हेम|हेमं
हेमम् + .{@-मः@}<BR>—1 A dark or brown-coloured horse.<BR>—2 A particular weight of gold.<BR>—3 The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमा
हेमम् + .{@-मा@}<BR>—1 The earth.<BR>—2 A handsome woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
हेमन् <i>n.</i> [हि-मनिन्]<BR>—1 Gold; हेम्नः संलक्ष्यते ह्यग्नौ विशुद्धिः श्यामिकापि वा R. 1. 10.<BR>—2 Water.<BR>—3 Snow.<BR>—4 The thorn-apple.<BR>—5 The Keśara flower.<BR>—6 Winter, the cold season.<BR>—7 The planet Mercury.<BR>—8 The Dhattūra plant; हेमनामकतरुप्रसवेन त्र्यम्बकस्तदुपकल्पितपूजः N. 21. 34.<BR>.━{@Comp.@}: हेमाङ्क^1, हेमाङ्ग, हेमाङ्गदम्, हेमाद्रिः, हेमाम्भोजम्, हेमाम्भोरुहम्, हेमाह्वः, हेमकक्ष, हेमक्षः, हेमकन्दलः, हेमकरः, हेमकर्तृ, हेमकारः, हेमकारकः, हेमकलशः, हेमकिंजल्कम्, हेमकुम्भः, हेमकूटः, हेमकेतकी, हेमकेलिः, हेमकेशः, हेमगन्धिनी, हेमगर्भ, हेमगिरिः, हेमगौरः, हेमघ्नम्, हेमघ्नी, हेमचन्द्रः, हेमच्छन्न, हेमज्वालः, हेमतरुः, हेमतारम्, हेमदुग्धः, हेमदुग्धकः, हेमधान्यकः, हेमधारणम्, हेमपर्वतः, हेमपुष्पः, हेमपुष्पकः, हेमपुष्पिका, हेमपृष्ठ, हेमबलम्, हेमवलम्, हेममाला, हेममक्षिकम्, हेममालिन्, हेमयूथिका, हेमरागिणी, हेमरेणुः, हेमवलम्, हेमव्याकरणम्, हेमशङ्खः, हेमशृङ्गम्, हेमसारम्, हेमसूत्रम्, हेमसूत्रकम्<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्क
हेमन् + -अङ्क^1 <i>a.</i> adorned with gold; Mu. 2. 10 (v. l.); see next word.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260502. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/commit/5f7cee5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्ग|हेमांग|हेमाङ्गः
हेमन् + -अङ्ग <i>a.</i> golden; सुगाङ्गे हेमाङ्गं नृवर तव सिंहासनमिदम् Mu. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्गः|हेमाङ्ग|हेमांग
हेमन् + -अङ्ग + .({@-ङ्गः@})<BR>—1 Garuḍa.<BR>—2 a lion.<BR>—3 the mountain <i>Sumeru</i>.<BR>—4 N. of Brahman.<BR>—5 of Viṣṇu.<BR>—6 the <i>Champaka</i> tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाङ्गदम्
हेमन् + -अङ्गदम् a gold bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमाद्रिः|हेमाद्रि
हेमन् + -अद्रिः<BR>—1 the mountain <i>Sumeru</i>.<BR>—2 N. of an author of the encyclopaedic work चतुर्वर्गचिन्तामणि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP&page=1764-2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap" target="_blank">Correction</a>

